COLLDATA("mujamkabir","en",[[1,"Abu Bakr As-Siddiq, his name is Abdullah bin Uthman bin Amer bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah. He witnessed the Battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . The mother of Abu Bakr, the mother of goodness, Salma bint Sakhr bin Amer bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah bin Kaab bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fehr bin Malik. The mother of the mother of goodness, Dilaaf, she is Ummamah bint Ubaid bin An-Naqid Al-Khuzaiyyi. The grandmother of Abu Bakr, Umm Abu Quhafa, Aminah bint Abdul Uzza bin Huthan bin Awf bin Ubaid bin Uwaid bin Adi bin Kaab."],[2,"The mother of Abu Bakr ؓ was called Umm al-Khayr bt. Sakhr b. Amir. Abu Bakr died and both his parents inherited from him; they had both embraced Islam. Abu Bakr's mother died before his father."],[3,"It is also said: Atiq b. Uthman. He was named Atiq because of the beauty of his face."],[4,"Abu Bakr ؓ was named Atiq because of the beauty of his face. His name was Abdullah b. Uthman."],[5,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Atiq from the Fire."],[6,"Abdullah. I said, \"But people say Atiq.\" She said, \"Abu Quhafa had three sons, and he named one Atiq, one Mu'aytiq, and one Mu'taq.\""],[7,"Abu Bakr's name was Abdullah b. Uthman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Atiq from the Fire."],[8,"I heard Abdullah b. al-Zubayr say, \"Abu Bakr's ؓ name was Abdullah b. Uthman.\""],[9,"I entered upon Aisha, the Mother of the Believers ؓ, and she said, \"Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to him, 'You are Atiq from the Fire.' From that day on he was called Atiq.\""],[10,"\"That Abu Bakr passed by the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Whoever wants to see a person freed from Hellfire, should look at this (referring to himself).'\" She said, and his name given by his family is Abdullah ibn Uthman.\""],[11,"We do not know of four generations who met the Prophet ﷺ, along with their sons, except these four: Abu Quhafa, Abu Bakr, Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, and Abu Atiq b. Abd al-Rahman. Abu Atiq's name was Muhammad ؓ."],[12,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"After me there will be twelve caliphs. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq will remain after me only a short time. The owner of a turning millstone will live praiseworthily and die as a martyr.\" It was said, \"Who is he, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Umar b. al-Khattab\" ؓ. Then he turned to Uthman and said, \"And you: the people will ask you to take off a shirt that Allah ﷻ has clothed you with. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you take it off you will not enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle.\""],[13,"From Safina, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The caliphate is thirty years, then it will be kingship.\" He said, \"Abu Bakr held it for two years, Umar for ten, Uthman for twelve, and Ali for six\" ؓ."],[14,"I heard Ali ؓ swear: By Allah, Allah sent down the name of Abu Bakr from heaven as al-Siddiq."],[15,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he was taken on the Night Journey, \"I want to go out to the Quraysh and inform them.\" So he informed them, but they rejected him and Abu Bakr confirmed him (believed him), so he was called \"As-Siddiq\" that day."],[16,"Three men of Quraysh had the brightest faces, the best character, and the firmest modesty. If they told you something, they would not lie to you; and if you told them something, they would not accuse you of lying: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ."],[17,"Abu Bakr ؓ dyed his hair with henna and katam."],[18,"Abu Bakr ؓ dyed his beard with henna and katam, while Umar ؓ dyed his hair with henna alone."],[19,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to dye his hair with henna and katam, and Umar ؓ used to dye his hair with henna."],[20,"She saw a man passing by while she was in her howdah and said, \"I have never seen a man more resembling Abu Bakr than this one.\" It was said to her, \"Describe Abu Bakr for us.\" She said, \"He was a fair-skinned, slender man with light hair on his temples, slightly stooped; his waist-wrapper would not stay up and would slip from his hips; he had a lean face, deep-set eyes, a prominent forehead, and thin forearms. This is his description.\""],[21,"I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, while he was the caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with a reddish beard, deep red in color."],[22,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to dye his hair with henna."],[23,"I saw Abu Bakr ؓ during the campaign of Dhat al-Salasil, and his beard was like the flame of the arfaj plant, on a white camel of his, light and slender."],[24,"I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ say: I said, \"O Messenger of God, do we act upon a matter already decreed or upon a matter newly initiated?\" He said, \"Rather upon a matter already decreed.\" I said, \"Then what is the point of action, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Everyone is facilitated for what he was created for.\""],[25,"Muawiyah ؓ said, \"I entered with my father upon Abu Bakr ؓ, and I saw Asma standing at his head, fair-skinned. I saw Abu Bakr ؓ as fair-skinned and slender. He mounted me and my father on two horses, then we were presented to him and he granted us rewards.\""],[26,"The Prophet ﷺ died at the age of sixty-three."],[27,"The Prophet ﷺ died at the age of sixty-three."],[28,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[29,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ mentioned their birth dates in my presence, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was older than Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was sixty-three, and Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three, two and a half years after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[30,"I was with Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan ؓ and I heard him say: \"The Prophet ﷺ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three, and 'Umar ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three.\" Abu Ishaq said: Mu'awiya ؓ also said: \"This [age] for me is fifty-seven, then he lived about twenty years.\""],[31,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[32,"Abu Bakr was taken when he was sixty-three."],[33,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[34,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr ruled for two years. He was buried at night, and 'Umar ؓ prayed over him."],[35,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old, and Abu Bakr ؓ was at the same age."],[36,"When Abu Bakr ؓ intended to appoint 'Umar as his successor, he sent for him and called him. He came to him and he said: \"I am calling you to a matter that is exhausting for the one who undertakes it. So fear Allah, O 'Umar, through obedience to Him, and obey Him through fear of Him, for the God-fearing is secure and protected. Then indeed the affair is presented [as a test]; none deserves it except the one who acts upon it. Whoever commands the truth but acts upon falsehood, and commands the right but acts upon the wrong, his hope is about to be cut off and his deeds to be nullified. If you are given authority over them, then if you are able to keep your hand dry from their blood, to keep your stomach empty of their wealth, and to keep your tongue from their honors, then do so. And there is no power except with Allah.\""],[37,"When Abu Bakr was on his deathbed, he said, \"Oh Aisha, look at the container from which we used to drink its milk, and the slaughter tool from which we used to slaughter animals, and the garment that we used to wear. We used to benefit from these things when we were in the service of the Muslims. So when I die, return them to Umar.\" When Abu Bakr passed away, I sent them to Umar, and Umar said, \"May Allah be pleased with you, Abu Bakr. You have really exhausted those who came after you.\""],[38,"In the sermon of Abu Bakr ؓ it was said: \"Do you not know that you go out in the morning and return in the evening for a fixed term? Whoever is able to have his term expire while he is in the work of Allah ﷻ, let him do so. You will never attain that except with Allah ﷻ. Indeed some people have made their terms for other than Him, so Allah has forbidden you to be like them: {And be not like those who forgot Allah, so He made them forget} [Quran 59:19]. Where are those of your brothers whom you knew? They have sent forth what they sent forth in the days of their predecessors, and they have fallen therein into misery or felicity. Where are the first tyrants who built cities and surrounded them with walls? They have become beneath rocks and wells. This is the Book of Allah ﷻ; its wonders never cease. So enjoin one another to follow it for a day of darkness, and illuminate yourselves with its light and its clarity. Indeed Allah ﷻ praised Zakariyya and his household, saying: {They used to hasten to good deeds and supplicate Us in hope and fear, and they were humbly submissive to Us} [Quran 21:90]. There is no good in a saying by which the face of Allah is not intended, no good in wealth that is not spent in the path of Allah, no good in one whose ignorance overcomes his forbearance, and no good in one who fears the blame of a blamer for the sake of Allah.\""],[39,"Abu Bakr ؓ died on Tuesday night and was buried at night."],[40,"I heard my grandfather say: \"Abu Bakr ؓ died while he had a touch of consumption, and he ruled for two and a half years.\""],[41,"Abu Bakr ؓ was appointed as successor on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. Abu Bakr ؓ died in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year thirteen, and his age on the day he died, as 'A'isha ؓ mentioned, was the age of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which is sixty-three."],[42,"I entered upon Abu Bakr ؓ to visit him during the illness in which he died. I greeted him and asked him how he was and he sat up straight. I said, \"By the praise of God, you are recovering.\" He said, \"Indeed, as you see, I am in pain, and you have made a distraction for me along with my pain. I made a covenant for you after me and chose for you the best of you in my own judgment, so every one of you has his nose swollen at that, hoping that the matter will be his. And I saw that the world has turned towards you, and it has not yet turned, and it is coming. You will adorn your houses with silk curtains and brocade cushions, and you will feel pain from lying on coarse wool as if one of you is on the thorns of Saʿdan. By God, if one of you were to come forward and have his neck struck without hadd punishment, it would be better for him than to roam in the flood of the world.\" Then he said, \"Indeed, I regret nothing except three things I did that I wish I had not done, three things I did not do that I wish I had done, and three things I wish I had asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about. As for the three things I wish I had not done: I wish I had not uncovered the house of Fatimah and left it, and had not closed the war upon myself. I wish that on the day of the Saqifah of Banu Saʿidah I had thrown the matter upon the neck of one of the two men, Abu ʿUbaydah or ʿUmar, so that he would have been the Commander of the Believers and I would have been a minister. And I wish that when I dispatched Khalid b. al-Walid to the people of apostasy, I had stayed at Dhu al-Qassah, so if the Muslims prevailed, they prevailed, and if not, I would have been a support or a reinforcement. As for the things I wish I had done: I wish that on the day al-Ashʿath was brought to me as a prisoner I had struck his neck, for it seems to me that he will be an evil frame around him. I wish that on the day al-Fuja'ah al-Sulami was brought to me, I had not burned him but had killed him quickly or released him successfully. And I wish that when I dispatched Khalid b. al-Walid to Syria, I had dispatched ʿUmar to Iraq, so that I would have stretched out both my hands, right and left, in the way of God ﷻ. As for the three things I wish I had asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about: I wish I had asked him to whom this matter belongs, so that its people would not dispute it. I wish I had asked him whether the Ansar have a share in this matter. And I wish I had asked him about the paternal aunt and the brother's daughter, for I have a need in my heart concerning them.\""],[43,"Ali and al-Abbas brought a dispute before Abu Bakr ؓ concerning the inheritance of the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"I will not transfer it from the place where the Messenger of God ﷺ put it.\""],[44,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the Ansar: \"Accept from their doers of good and overlook their doers of evil.\""],[45,"\"That the Messenger of God ﷺ consulted concerning the matter of war.\" Stick to that."],[46,"Al-Shifa' bt. Abd Allah, who was among the first emigrant women, informed me that Labid b. Rabi'ah and Adi b. Hatim came to Madinah and went to the mosque. They found Amr b. al-As and said, \"O Ibn al-As, seek permission for us to see the Commander of the Believers.\" He said, \"By God, you two have hit upon his name: he is the commander and we are the believers.\" Amr went in to Umar and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers.\" Umar said to him, \"What is this?\" He said, \"You are the commander and we are the believers.\" And the title has been used from that day on."],[47,"Al-Shifa', the daughter of Abdullah, informed me that Labid ibn Rabiah and Adi ibn Hatim, who were among the first immigrants, came to the Medina and entered the mosque. They found Amr ibn al-'As and said, \"O son of al-'As, ask permission for us to meet the Commander of the Believers.\" He replied, \"By Allah, you have both got his name right. He is the Commander, and we are the believers.\" Then Amr ibn al-'As went to Umar and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers.\" Umar asked, \"What is this?\" He said, \"You are the Commander, and we are the believers.\" From that day onwards, the title spread."],[48,"\"I was reciting poetry to him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, and I did not recognize his Companions until a man came who was broad between the shoulders and bald.\" It was said to me, \"Be quiet! Be quiet!\" I said, \"Alas, who is this for whom I must be quiet in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ?\" It was said to me, \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[49,"The people of Madinah went out for a gathering of theirs, and there I saw a bald man, left-handed but using his right, who towered above the people by a forearm's length, wearing a coarse loincloth and a striped cloak, saying: \"O people, emigrate and do not abandon, and let none of you throw a stone or stick at a rabbit and then eat it; let spears, lances, and arrows be of service to you.\" I said, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[50,"\"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was bald, severely bald.\""],[51,"That he will expel us from our land."],[52,"\"When Umar b. al-Khattab got angry, he would twist his mustache and blow.\""],[53,"\"Umar ؓ would take hold of his ear, meaning his own ear, then leap onto the horse.\""],[54,"Umar ؓ was offered by a freedwoman of his that he dye his beard. He said, “Do you want to extinguish my light as so-and-so extinguished his light?”"],[55,"I heard Abu 'Amir Sulaym b. 'Amir say, “I saw Umar not changing anything of his beard.”"],[56,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection,” and I will not change my gray hair."],[57,"I was in Madinah when there was a dark brown man, left-handed on one side and right-handed on the other, huge; when he appeared before the people it was as if he were on a mount. Then it was Umar ؓ."],[58,"I saw Umar ؓ as a huge man, as if he were one of the men of Banu Sadus."],[59,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Jibril ﷺ said to me: Let Islam weep over the death of Umar ؓ.”"],[60,"When Umar ؓ was struck, I heard a voice: “Let him weep for Islam who would weep; they have nearly perished. The covenant has not arrived, and the world has turned its back, and its good has turned away; those who believed in the promise have grown weary of it.”"],[61,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ held authority for ten years, then he died."],[62,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ died when he was sixty-six years old."],[63,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[64,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, Abu Bakr ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, and Umar was taken when he was sixty-three years old."],[65,"Umar ؓ was killed when he was sixty-one years old."],[66,"Umar ؓ died at the beginning of fifty-five."],[67,"Umar ؓ passed away when he was fifty-five years old."],[68,"Umar ؓ died when he was fifty-five years old."],[69,"And he said: \"Gray hair came to me quickly from the side of my maternal uncles, Banu al-Mughira.\""],[70,"Umar ؓ was buried on Wednesday, when four nights remained of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year twenty-three."],[71,"Umar was appointed in the month of Rajab in the thirteenth year and he was killed in the month of Dhul-Hijjah in the twenty-third year. He remained alive for three days after being stabbed, then he died in the end of Dhul-Hijjah. Suhaib led the funeral prayer for him, and his son Abdullah ibn Umar washed his body and shrouded him in five garments. He was buried next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . Umar was stabbed on Wednesday, the ninth day of the remaining days of Dhul-Hijjah. Some people say he died on that day, and his age on the day he died was what I have heard from Malik ibn Anas, who mentioned that the Prophet's ﷺ age when he died was sixty-three. Some people say it was fifty-nine, and others say it was fifty-three. Some people say it was forty-five, and his caliphate lasted for ten years, four months, and some days."],[72,"The Commander of the Faithful, Umar ؓ, was killed at the return of the pilgrims, and that was in the year twenty-three."],[73,"He was fifty-eight years old."],[74,"Umar died in the year twenty-three, and his caliphate lasted ten years."],[75,"He was accused of practicing sorcery, and it was Abu Lu'lu'a, the servant of Al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, who stabbed him. He was a Zoroastrian."],[76,"Umar was stabbed. They sent for a physician, and a man from the Ansar came and gave him milk to drink. The milk came out white from the stab wound below the navel. The physician said to him: \"Make your will, for I do not think you will live until evening.\" He said: \"He has told me the truth.\""],[77,"I witnessed the death of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and the sun was eclipsed on that day."],[78,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"May one of us sleep while he is in a state of major ritual impurity?\" He said: \"Yes, and he should perform ablution as he does for prayer.\""],[79,"The Prophet ﷺ heard me saying: \"By my father,\" and he said: \"Allah ﷻ forbids you to swear by your fathers.\""],[80,"He said: O people, do not judge based on opinion in matters of religion. Indeed, you have seen me opposing the orders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own opinion as an effort. By Allah, that has not diverted me from the truth. This happened on the day of Abu Jandal, when the message was between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people of Makkah. He said: \"Write in the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\" They said: \"Do you see that we have believed you in what you say?\" However, you write in your own name, so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will be satisfied. I refused until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do you see that I am satisfied and you refuse?\" I said: \"I am satisfied.\""],[81,"I said to Abī, \"Who is the man who freed you from the polytheists on the day they beat you?\" He said, \"That was al-ʿĀṣ b. Wāʾil al-Sahmī.\""],[82,"ʿUmar ؓ went out to pray for rain and took al-ʿAbbās with him to pray for rain, saying, \"O Allah, we used to seek intercession with You through our Prophet ﷺ when we suffered drought during the time of our Prophet ﷺ , and now we seek intercession with You through the uncle of our Prophet ﷺ, so accept it from him.\""],[83,"I heard ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say on the pulpit, \"Gold for gold is ribā unless equal for equal, with no increase; whatever exceeds that is ribā.\" Ibn ʿUmar said, \"If you are in doubt, ask Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī about that.\" So he went and asked Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, and he told him that he had heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn ʿAbbās was told what Ibn ʿUmar and Abū Saʿīd had said, so he sought forgiveness and said, \"This is an opinion I held.\""],[84,"\"Are you satisfied with your father?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So we gathered before the Commander of the Faithful, and Saʿd said to him, \"I urinated, performed ablution, wiped over my leather socks, and then prayed.\" He said, \"You have done well and followed the Sunnah.\" He said, \"But your son ʿAbdullāh criticized me for that.\" He said, \"O Saʿd, you are older and more knowledgeable than him.\""],[85,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The price of a singing slave-girl is unlawful, her singing is forbidden, looking at her is forbidden, her price is like the price of a dog, and the price of a dog is unlawful. Whoever's flesh grows on unlawful gain, the Fire is more fitting for him.\""],[86,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to marry one of his women, he would come to her from behind the veil and say to her, \"O my daughter, so-and-so has proposed to you. If you dislike him, say no, for no one should be ashamed to say no. And if you accept, then your silence is consent.\""],[87,"Allah ﷻ to His Prophet ﷺ”"],[88,"He is also called Abū ʿAbdullāh. The mother of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān is Arwā bt. Kurayz b. Rabīʿa b. Ḥabīb b. ʿAbd Shams. Arwā's mother is Umm Ḥakīm al-Bayḍāʾ bt. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umm Ḥakīm's mother is Fāṭima bt. ʿAmr b. ʿĀʾidh b. ʿImrān b. Makhzūm, who is the paternal grandmother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[89,"\"The mother of ʿUthmān ؓ, Arwā bt. Kurayz, accepted Islam.\""],[90,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ on Friday on the pulpit wearing a thick ʿAdanī lower garment worth four or five dirhams and a Kufan dyed cloak, of sturdy build, with a long beard and a handsome face.\""],[91,"\"On Friday, Uthman used to lean on a walking stick. He was the most beautiful of people and he wore two yellow garments, an undergarment and a cloak, until he would reach the pulpit and sit on it.\""],[92,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ, and I have never seen any male or female with a more beautiful face than his.\""],[93,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ with a white beard.\""],[94,"I saw Uthman b. Affan ؓ with a yellow beard."],[95,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Uthman ؓ with a dish containing meat. I entered upon him while Ruqayyah was sitting, and I never saw two people more beautiful than them ؓ. I found myself looking once at Ruqayyah and once at Uthman. When I returned, the Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"Did you enter upon them?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Did you see a couple more beautiful than them?\" I said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah, I kept looking once at Ruqayyah and once at Uthman.\" Abu al-Qasim, may Allah have mercy on him, said, \"This was before the revelation of the verse of hijab.\""],[96,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon his daughter while she was washing Uthman's ؓ head and said, \"O my dear daughter, be kind to Abu Abd Allah, for he is the closest of my Companions to me in character.\""],[97,"I entered upon Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wife of Uthman ؓ, with a comb in her hand. She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me a little while ago after I combed his hair. He said, 'How do you find Abu Abd Allah?' I said, 'Well.' He said, 'Honor him, for he is among the closest of my Companions to me in character.'\""],[98,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ was killed in the middle of the days of tashriq."],[99,"I heard Zubayr ibn Bakkar say, \"Uthman ibn Affan was killed on Friday, in the eighteenth day of Dhu al-Hijjah, in the year thirty-six, after 'Asr prayer. He was eighty-two years old at that time and was fasting.\""],[100,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[101,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[102,"Uthman was killed when he was ninety or eighty-eight years old."],[103,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[104,"The caliphate of Uthman ؓ was twelve years."],[105,"The shura was held, and the people agreed upon Uthman ؓ with three nights remaining in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year twenty-three. Then Uthman ؓ was killed on Friday, eighteen nights having passed in Dhu al-Hijjah, at the completion of the year thirty-five. He was eighty-eight years old. He used to dye his beard yellow, and the reign of Uthman ؓ was twelve years."],[106,"Uthman ؓ was killed when he was ninety or eighty-eight years old."],[107,"I heard Malik say: Uthman ؓ was killed, and he lay cast aside on the rubbish heap of the Banu Fulān for three days. Then twelve men came to him, among them my grandfather Malik b. Abi Amir, Huwaytib b. Abd al-Uzza, Hakim b. Hizam, Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, and Aisha bt. Uthman, with a lamp inside a small box. They carried him on a door, and his head kept knocking against the door: tap, tap. Then they brought him to al-Baqi`, and they differed about praying over him, so Hakim b. Hizam or Huwaytib b. Abd al-Uzza prayed over him — Abd al-Rahman was unsure. Then they wanted to bury him, but a man from the Banu Mazin stood up and said: By Allah, if you bury him with the Muslims, I will tell the people. So they carried him until they brought him to the orchard of Kawkab. When they lowered him into his grave, Aisha bt. Uthman cried out, and Ibn al-Zubayr said to her: Be quiet, for by Allah, if you do it again, I will strike the part where your eyes are. When they had buried him and leveled the earth over him, Ibn al-Zubayr said to her: Cry now, as much as you want. Malik said: Before that, Uthman b. Affan ؓ used to pass by the orchard of Kawkab and say: A righteous man will surely be buried here. Abu al-Qasim said: al-hushsh means the garden."],[108,"When evening came, I said: If you leave your companion until morning, they will mutilate him, so take him to Baqi al-Gharqad, and make it possible for us in the middle of the night. Then we carried him, and a blackness came over us from behind, and we feared them until we almost dispersed from around him. Then a caller called out: Do not be afraid; stand firm, for we have come to witness him with you. Ibn Hubaysh used to say: They were, by Allah, the angels."],[109,"O Commander of the Faithful, what do you say about Uthman? The two men hastened to answer and said: Why do you ask? About a man who disbelieved in Allah after his faith and acted as a hypocrite? The man said to them: I am not asking you two, and I did not come to you two. Ali said to him: \"I do not say what they say.\" They both said to him: Then why did we kill him? He said: He was put in authority over you and ruled badly in his final days, and you became distressed and behaved badly in your distress. By Allah, I hope that I and Uthman will be as Allah ﷻ said: {And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts; they will be brothers, on couches facing one another}."],[110,"Ali ؓ addressed the people and said: O people, by Allah, if no one enters the Fire except those who killed Uthman, I will not enter it; and if no one enters Paradise except those who killed Uthman, I will not enter it. When he came down, it was said to him: You have spoken a word that has divided your companions against you. So he addressed them and said: \"O people, indeed Allah ﷻ caused Uthman to be killed, and I am with him.\" Hammad said: And Habib b. al-Shahid narrated to us from Muhammad b. Sirin: A Qurayshi expression that has two meanings. Abu al-Qasim said: It is as if he meant, \"Allah, exalted is He, caused him to be killed, and I too will be killed with him ؓ.\""],[111,"Ali ؓ addressed them, but they interrupted his sermon. He said: I was only weakened the day Uthman ؓ was killed. And he struck for them a parable: the parable of three bulls and a lion who met in a thicket — a black one, a red one, and a white one. Whenever the lion wanted one of them, they gathered together against him and resisted him. So the lion said to the black one and the red one: The one who disgraces us in our thicket and exposes us is this white one. Let me eat him, so that your color will match mine and my color will match yours. The lion attacked him, and it was not long before he killed him. Then he said to the black one: The one who disgraces us and exposes us in our thicket is this red one. Let me eat him, so that my color will match yours and your color will match mine. He attacked him and killed him. Then he said to the black one: I will eat you. He said: Let me cry out three cries. So he cried out: Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was only weakened the day Uthman was killed."],[112,"\"By Allah, you have killed him while he was one who fasted much and prayed much.\" Al-Ashtar went and informed Ammar ؓ, so Ammar came to Masruq and said: By Allah, Ammar will be flogged, Abu Dharr will be exiled, and the protected pasture will be guarded, and you say, 'You have killed him while he was one who fasted much and prayed much.' Masruq said to him: \"By Allah, you have not done one of two things: you have not been punished as you have been punished, nor have you been patient, and patience is better for the patient.\" It was as if he had thrust a stone into his mouth. He said: And al-Shabi said: \"No woman of Hamdan has given birth to one like Masruq.\""],[113,"We gathered in the house of Makhrama after Uthman ؓ was killed, wanting to pledge allegiance. Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfa said: Whoever of you we give allegiance to, we will not stand in the way of retaliation. Ammar b. Yasir said: Not for the blood of Uthman. Abu Jahm said: O son of Sumayya, by Allah, retaliation will be taken from you for the lashes you were given, but no retaliation will be taken for the blood of Uthman ؓ. So they departed that day without pledging allegiance."],[114,"Waththab, who was one of those whom Uthman ؓ had freed and who used to stand before Uthman, informed me: Uthman sent me and I summoned al-Ashtar for him. Ibn Awn said: I think he said: I placed a cushion for the Commander of the Faithful, and he had a cushion. He said: \"O Ashtar, what do the people want from me?\" He said: Three things, one of which is unavoidable. He said: \"What are they?\" He said: They give you the choice between handing over their affair to them, saying, 'This is your affair, so choose for it whom you will,' and between exacting retribution from yourself. If you refuse these two, then the people will fight you. He said: \"Is one of them unavoidable?\" He said: One of them is unavoidable. He said: \"As for handing over their affair to them, I would never remove a garment with which I have been clothed.\" He said: And al-Hasan said: By Allah, to be brought forward and have my neck struck is dearer to me than to remove the affair of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ from one another. Ibn Awn said: This is more like the words of Uthman. As for exacting retribution from myself, by Allah, I know that my two companions before me were punished, and my body cannot withstand retaliation. As for killing me, by Allah, if you kill me, you will never love one another after me, and you will never fight an enemy together after me. Then al-Ashtar stood up and left. We waited and said: Perhaps the people... Then a man came who looked like a wolf, peered in from a door, and then went back. Then Muhammad b. Abi Bakr came with thirteen men and reached Uthman ؓ. He grabbed his beard and said with it, and said with it, until I heard the chattering of his teeth, and said: What did Muawiya avail you? What did Ibn Amir avail you? What did your letters avail you? He said: \"Let go of my beard, O son of my brother. Let go of my beard, O son of my brother.\" He said: I saw him summon a man from the group with his eye, and the man went to him with a small spear and struck him with it on his head. I said: Then what? He said: Then they all attacked him, by Allah, until they killed him."],[115,"Muhammad said: O Kab, do you not find this ship of ours in the Torah, how it sails? He said: \"No, but I find in it a man, the most wretched of the young men of Quraysh, who leaps into the turmoil as a donkey leaps. Do not be that one.\" Ibn Sirin said: They claimed that it was indeed him."],[116,"A man of the Ansar entered upon Uthman, and he said: Go back, O son of my brother, for you are not my killer. He said: How do you know that? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day, and he chewed a date for you and blessed you.\" Then another man of the Ansar entered upon him, and he said: Go back, O son of my brother, for you are not my killer. He said: How do you know that? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day, and he chewed a date for you and blessed you.\" Then Muhammad b. Abi Bakr entered upon him, and he said: You are my killer. He said: How do you know, O Nathal? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day so that he might chew a date for you and bless you, but you defecated on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So he leaped onto his chest and grabbed his beard, saying: If you do that, it would be hard for your father that you upset him. Then he struck him in the throat with small spears that were in his hand."],[117,"It was the first hand that wrote the Mufassal."],[118,"\"A righteous ruler who is not deterred from the cause of Allah by the blame of any blamer.\" He said: Then what? He said: \"Then after you there will be a caliph whom a sinful faction will kill.\" He said: Then what? He said: \"Then there will be the tribulation.\""],[119,"to collapse"],[120,"had the people not sought the blood of Uthman, they would have been stoned from the sky"],[121,"I heard al-Hasan say: “The corrupt Muhammad b. Abi Bakr was seized in a ravine among the ravines of Egypt, then put inside a donkey’s belly and burned.”"],[122,"\"I sought refuge with my Lord for ten days. Indeed, I am the fourth among four in Islam. I have not intended or desired anything, nor have I ever placed my right hand on my private parts since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Every Friday that has passed since I embraced Islam, I have freed a slave in it, except that if I did not have one, then I would continue to do so afterwards. I have never committed adultery, neither during the period of ignorance nor after embracing Islam.\""],[123,"As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, Uthman is occupied with Your need and the need of Your Messenger,” so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him his arrow."],[124,"Uthman b. Affan stayed behind in Madinah with his wife, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was ill, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him his arrow. He said: And my reward, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “And your reward.”"],[125,"And Talhah ؓ was washing one side of his head, so he did not answer her. So she put her hands into the sleeve of her garment and brought out her breasts and said: I ask you by what I carried you and nursed you: do it. So he got up, twisted the side of his hair until he tied it while it was washed, then went out until he came to Ali ؓ while he was sitting beside his house. Talhah ؓ, with his mother and the mother of Abdullah b. Rafi’, said: If only you would ease this man’s siege, for it has become severe. He said: He tapped with a cup in his hand three times, then raised his head and said: “By Allah, I do not love anything of this that you dislike.” He said: And Abu Khalifah recited to us, saying: Al-Abbas b. al-Faraj al-Riyashi recited to us for Layla al-Akhyaliyyah."],[126,"It is by Hassan b. Thabit."],[127,"“Welcome to those who speak justly, and by prayer, welcome and family.”"],[128,"The wife of Uthman ؓ said when they surrounded him intending to kill him: “If you kill him or spare him, he used to keep the whole night alive in a single rak’ah, gathering the Quran in it.”"],[129,"I heard al-Hasan say: I reached the time of Uthman ؓ when I was then near puberty, and I heard him delivering a sermon, and I witnessed him saying: “O people, what do you hold against me?” He said: And there was no day but they would share in some good. He would say: “O people, come in the morning for your gifts,” so they would come and take them in full. Then it would be said: “O Muslims, come in the morning for your clothing,” so fine robes would be brought and divided among them. Al-Hasan said: “The enemy is repelled, gifts are flowing, harmony is good, and good is abundant. No believer on earth fears another believer. Whomever he meets, from whatever tribe he is, he is his brother, his friend, and his supporter. The tribulation is that someone draws a sword against him.”"],[130,"“To fall from the sky and be torn apart would be dearer to me than to have shared in the blood of Uthman ؓ.”"],[131,"And who is the man? I said: From the people of Basra. She said: From which people of Basra? I said: From Bakr b. Wa’il. She said: From which Bakr b. Wa’il? I said: From Banu Qays b. Tha’labah. She said: Are you from the household of so-and-so? I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, for what reason was Uthman, the Commander of the Believers ؓ, killed? She said: “By Allah, he was killed unjustly. May Allah curse his killers. May Allah exact retribution for him from Ibn Abi Bakr. May Allah drive humiliation into the eyes of Banu Tamim in his house. May Allah shed the blood of Banu Budayl upon error. May Allah send to al-Ashtar an arrow from His arrows.” For by Allah, there was no man among those people but her supplication struck him."],[132,"The majority of the riders who marched against Uthman went mad."],[133,"Why do I see that you have kept away from the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman ؓ? Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ said: Shall I tell him that I did not stay behind from Badr? Uthman ؓ was informed of that, so he said: As for his saying that I did not stay behind from Badr, I was nursing Ruqayya bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until she died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted me a share, and whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share to has indeed attended."],[134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The caliphate after me in my community is thirty years. He said: So we calculated and found Abu Bakr two years, Umar ten, Uthman twelve, and Ali six ؓ."],[135,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, they claim that you said, 'A people will disbelieve after their faith.' He said, 'Yes, and you are not among them.' Abu al-Darda died before the killing of Uthman ؓ."],[136,"Uthman, possessor of the two lights, was killed wrongfully."],[137,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, you got his name right; Umar, a horn of iron; Uthman, possessor of the two lights, you got his name right, killed wrongfully, he was given two portions of reward."],[138,"From its highest, one with above."],[139,"I heard Abdullah say when allegiance was given to Uthman: We did not hold back from its highest, one with above."],[140,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There will be after me twelve caliphs: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who will not remain except a little; and the companion of the millstone of the Arab abode, who will live praiseworthy and be killed as a martyr. A man said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said, 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' Then he turned to Uthman and said, 'And you, the people will ask you to take off a shirt with which Allah has clothed you. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you take it off, you will not enter Paradise until the camel enters the eye of the needle.'"],[141,"Uthman ؓ went out as an emigrant to the land of Abyssinia, and with him was Ruqayya bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. News of them was withheld from the Prophet ﷺ, and he would go out looking for news of them. A woman came and told him. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Uthman is the first to emigrate to Allah with his family after Lot.'"],[142,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Uthman to the people of Makkah and then his companions pledged the pledge of al-Ridwan, he pledged for Uthman with one of his hands on the other. The people said: Congratulations to Abu Abdullah, he will circumambulate the House in safety. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'If he stayed such and such, he would not circumambulate until I circumambulate.'"],[143,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ, while delivering a sermon on the pulpit: I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Nothing prevented me from telling you except concern for you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A night of guard duty in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights in which its night is spent in prayer and its day is spent in fasting.'"],[144,"Uthman ؓ adjured the people one day and said: Do you know that the Prophet ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ and I, and Uhud trembled, and upon it were Muhammad the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ؓ? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be still, Uhud, for upon you are none but a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs.\""],[145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Anything that exceeds the shade of a house, a crust of bread, and a garment that covers a man's private parts\"—or he said, \"the private parts of the son of Adam\"—\"and anything that exceeds that, the son of Adam has no right to it.\""],[146,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays the later Isha in congregation, it is as if he prayed the whole night; and whoever prays the morning prayer in congregation, it is as if he prayed the whole day.\""],[147,"I heard Uthman ؓ—and he narrated little from the Messenger of God ﷺ—say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs wudu as he has been commanded and prays as he has been commanded, his sins depart him as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[148,"Abu Talib's name was Abd Manaf b. Abd al-Muttalib; Abd al-Muttalib's name was Shaybah b. Hashim; Hashim's name was Amr b. Abd Manaf b. Qusayy; and Qusayy's name was Zayd."],[149,"It is said that she was the first Hashimite woman to give birth to a Hashimite. She embraced Islam, emigrated to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah, died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ buried her. Her mother was Fatimah bt. Harim b. Rawahah b. Hujr b. Abd Mu'arrid b. Amir b. Lu'ayy."],[150,"\"O Amr, look at the Commander of the Believers for me.\" He said: \"I did not see that he had dyed his beard; he had a large head.\""],[151,"\"I saw Ali ؓ with a white head and beard, wearing a lower garment and a cloak.\""],[152,"\"I saw Ali ؓ on the pulpit with a white head and beard.\""],[153,"I went out with my father to the Friday prayer when I was a boy. When Ali ؓ came out and ascended the pulpit, my father said to me: \"Get up, O Amr, and look at the Commander of the Believers.\" He said: \"I got up, and there he was standing on the pulpit, white of beard and head, wearing a lower garment and a cloak, no shirt on him.\" He said: \"I did not see him sit on the pulpit until he descended from it.\" We said to Abu Ishaq: \"Did he perform qunut?\" He said: \"No.\""],[154,"When Ali ؓ married Fatimah ؓ, she said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"You have married me to a bleary-eyed man with a big belly.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have married you to him, and he is the first of my companions in submission, the most knowledgeable of them, and the greatest of them in forbearance.\""],[155,"\"I saw Ali ؓ on the pulpit, white of beard, which had filled what was between his shoulders.\" Yahya b. Sa'id added in his narration: \"on his head there were small hairs.\""],[156,"It is said, \"Ali ibn Abi Talib was a stout and robust man, with broad shoulders, long beard, bald head, big belly, thick eyebrows, and white hair and beard.\""],[157,"I asked Abu Ishaq, \"Are you older than al-Sha'bi?\" He said to me, \"Al-Sha'bi is older than me by a year or two.\" He said: And Abu Ishaq saw Ali ؓ and used to describe him to us as \"large-bellied, bald-headed.\" Shu'ba said, \"Abu Ishaq was older than Abu al-Bakhtari, but Abu al-Bakhtari did not meet Ali and did not see him.\""],[158,"I mentioned to Ibn Mas'ud the saying of Ali ؓ, and he said, \"Do you not see his head? It is like a basin, and around it is only a rim.\""],[159,"\"I saw Ali ؓ as fat, with thinning hair, as if on his side was the hide of a sheep.\""],[160,"\"Ali b. Abi Talib accepted Islam when he was eight years old.\""],[161,"\"The first to believe was Ali b. Abi Talib, when he was fifteen or sixteen years old.\""],[162,"\"Ali b. Abi Talib was killed on Friday, the seventeenth of the month of Ramadan, in the year forty.\""],[163,"\"Ali ؓ died when he was sixty-three years old.\""],[164,"\"Ali died when he was fifty-eight.\""],[165,"When Abd al-Rahman b. Muljam struck Ali ؓ and he was carried to his house, visitors came to him. He praised God (glorified and exalted be He) and extolled Him, and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said: Every person will meet what he flees from in his flight, and the appointed term drives the soul, and flight from its calamities does not avail. How many days have I pursued, examining their hidden depths about the secret of this matter, but God (glorified and exalted be He) willed only to conceal it. Alas, it is hidden knowledge. As for my testament to you: fear God (glorified and exalted be He) and associate nothing with Him, and do not neglect the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ. Uphold these two pillars, and you will be free of blame as long as they are not dispersed. Each person will be burdened according to his effort, and the ignorant will be shown leniency by a merciful Lord, a sound religion, and a knowledgeable Imam. We were among winds and the scattering of branches, under the shade of a cloud whose center has vanished, and a captive neighbor will drive it away, bringing days in succession, then it fell. After him you will be left with a hollow corpse, still after motion, silent after speech. Indeed, that is a greater admonition for those who reflect than the speech of the eloquent. Your caller is a caller on the watch for the meeting. Tomorrow you will see my days, and my secrets will be revealed. God (glorified and exalted be He) will not show me favor unless I draw near to Him through piety, so that He forgives excess. Peace be upon you until the day of inevitability. If I remain, I am the guardian of my own blood; if I perish, then annihilation is my appointed time. Forgiveness for me is a means of nearness to God, and for you it is a good deed, so forgive, may God forgive us and you. {Do you not love that God should forgive you? And God is Forgiving, Merciful.} Then he said:"],[167,"\"Its most wretched one will not be held back. By the One in whose hand is my soul, this will surely be dyed from this,\" and he recited these two lines of poetry."],[168,"He said, \"Did anything bring you here other than this?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, {That is a nation which has passed away. It will have what it earned, and you will have what you earned, and you will not be asked about what they used to do.}"],[169,"\"Ali ؓ was killed in the year forty.\""],[170,"Ali was killed in the year forty, and his caliphate was five years and six months."],[171,"He visited Ali ؓ during an illness he was suffering from. I said to him, \"We feared for you, O Abu al-Hasan, in this illness of yours.\" He said, \"But by Allah, I did not fear for myself from it, because I heard the truthful, the believed one ﷺ say: 'You will be struck with a blow here and a blow here'—and he pointed to his temples—'and its blood will flow until it dyes your beard, and the one who strikes it will be its most wretched, just as the hamstringer of the she-camel was the most wretched of Thamud.'\""],[172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed the banner to Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ when he was twenty years old."],[173,"I married Fatimah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, arrange my marriage?\" He said, \"Do you have anything to give her?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Where is your Hutama armor?\" I said, \"With me.\" He said, \"Give it to her.\""],[174,"Ali used to say during the life of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , that Allah says, \"If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?\" By Allah, we will not turn back on our heels after Allah has guided us. And by Allah, if he dies or is killed, I will surely fight for what he fought for until I die. And by Allah, I am his brother, his guardian, his cousin, and his inheritor. So, who is more entitled to him than me?"],[175,"\"Shall I not inform you of the good of this nation after its Prophet ﷺ ?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Abu Bakr.\" Then he said, \"Shall I not inform you of the good of this nation after Abu Bakr?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Umar, and if I wanted, I would inform you about the third.\""],[176,"He was sitting on the pulpit and mentioned Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and said: \"The best of this nation after its Prophet ﷺ is Abu Bakr, and the second is Umar. And if I wished to mention the third, I would mention him.\""],[177,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Exalted, for three qualities for my nation, and He granted me two and withheld one. I said, 'O Lord, do not destroy my nation by hunger.' He said, 'This is granted.' I said, 'O Lord, do not set over them an enemy from other than them'—meaning the people of polytheism—'and make them need him.' He said, 'That is granted to you.' I said, 'O Lord, do not make their might between themselves,' and He withheld this one from me.\""],[178,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said, 'O people of the gathering, lower your gazes until Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ passes.' So she passes, and upon her are two green cloaks, ؓ.\""],[179,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah curse Suhayl three times, for he used to tithe the people in the land, so Allah transformed him into a meteor.\""],[180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: \"Allah becomes angry for your anger and pleased for your pleasure.\""],[181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Use ithmid, for it grows the hair, removes the speck, and clears the vision.\""],[182,"\"I do not know but that we set out as pilgrims, proclaiming the Hajj, and neither the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor Umar ؓ exited the state of ihram until they circumambulated the House on the Day of Sacrifice and between al-Safa and al-Marwa.\""],[183,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to observe continuous fasting from pre-dawn to pre-dawn.\""],[184,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Whoever frees a Muslim or believing slave, God will shield, for every limb of that slave, a limb of his from the Fire.\""],[185,"Because he was in the lands of Hadramawt, where ʿAmr b. Nāhiḍ al-Ḥimyarī was killed. Then he fled to Makkah and became an ally of Ḥarb b. Umayya. The Ḥaḍramī’s name was ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmmār b. Rabīʿa b. Akbar b. ʿAwf b. Mālik b. ʿUwayf b. Khazraj b. Iyād b. al-Ṣadaf b. Ḥaḍramawt b. Qaḥṭān b. Kinda. Al-Ṣaʿba was the sister of al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī, and her mother was ʿĀtika bt. Wahb b. ʿAbd b. Quṣayy b. Kilāb b. Murra b. Kaʿb."],[186,"\"Umm Ṭalḥa bt. ʿUbayd Allāh accepted Islam.\""],[187,"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAmr b. Kaʿb b. Saʿd b. Taym b. Murra. He was in Syria, then he arrived and spoke to the Messenger of God ﷺ about his share, so he assigned him his share. He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And your reward,\" meaning on the day of Badr."],[188,"\"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh is given the kunya Abū Muḥammad ؓ\""],[189,"\"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh ؓ was fair-skinned with a reddish tinge, of medium height, closer to short, broad-chested, wide-shouldered; when he turned, he turned his whole body; he had large feet.\""],[190,"\"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh ؓ was fair-skinned with a reddish tinge, of medium height, closer to short, broad-chested, wide-shouldered; when he turned, he turned his whole body; he had large feet.\""],[191,"\"I saw the hand of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh paralyzed; he had shielded the Messenger of God ﷺ with it on the day of Uḥud.\""],[192,"\"The finger of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh ؓ was paralyzed.\""],[193,"Sufyān, and his family used to say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Fayyāḍ.\""],[194,"Ṭalḥa visited me one day and I noticed heaviness in him. I said, \"What is the matter with you? Has something from us upset you, so that we may make amends?\" He said, \"No, and what a good wife of a Muslim man you are. But wealth has accumulated with me, and I do not know what to do with it.\" She said, \"What distresses you about it? Call your people and divide it among them.\" He said, \"O boy, bring my people to me.\" I then asked the treasurer how much he had distributed. He said, \"Four hundred thousand.\""],[195,"\"The daily income of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh was one thousand complete.\""],[196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me on the day of Uhud Talhah al-Khayr, and in the expedition of Dhu al-‘Ushayrah Talhah al-Fayyad, and on the day of Hunayn Talhah al-Jud. Abu al-Qasim said: with both sīn and shīn; with sīn it is from ‘usrah (difficulty), and with shīn it is a place."],[197,"Talhah slaughtered a camel and dug a well on the day of Dhu Qarad, and he fed them and gave them to drink. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Talhah al-Fayyad!” So he was called Talhah al-Fayyad."],[198,"Al-Waqidi said: “He was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada of the year thirty-six.”"],[199,"Al-Waqidi said: “He was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada of the year thirty-six.”"],[200,"“Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah ؓ was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada of the year thirty-six, and his age was fifty-two or fifty-four years. Al-Zubayr was older than him, and he was given the kunyah Abu Muhammad.”"],[201,"\"That he died.\""],[202,"From his face and his beard while he was asking for mercy for him and saying, “Would that I had died twenty years before this day.”"],[203,"I heard ‘Ali ؓ on the Day of the Camel say to his son Hasan: “O Hasan, I wish I had died twenty years ago.”"],[204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[205,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, part of humility before Allah is contentment with a lowly seat in gatherings of honor.”"],[206,"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: “One who marries among his own people is like one who plants fresh pasture in his own land.”"],[207,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There has never been prophethood except that after it came killing and crucifixion.”"],[208,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Amr b. al-‘As is among the righteous of Quraysh.”"],[209,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O ‘Amr, you are indeed a man of sound judgment in Islam.”"],[210,"“Should I lead you in prayer, are you pleased with my prayer?” They said, “Yes, and who would dislike that, O disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Any man who leads a people in prayer while they dislike him, his prayer will not pass beyond his ears.’”"],[211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is granted a favor should mention it. Whoever mentions it has thanked it, and whoever conceals it has denied it.”"],[212,"The mount and perfume of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were in my charge. A man came to him asking for one of them, and he said: “That is up to Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah.” The man came to me and informed me, but I refused him. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he replied to him with the same thing. He came to me and informed me, but I refused him. He went back to the Prophet ﷺ and said the same thing, then returned to me. I said to myself: He would not have sent him to me unless he wanted his need to be fulfilled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was hardly ever asked for something without doing it. I said: That I should take charge of the Prophet’s own saddle is dearer to me than that I should take charge of his mount. So I handed it over to him. The Prophet ﷺ then intended to travel and ordered that a mount be saddled for him. He came to me and said: Which of the two saddles was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: The one from Ta’if. So he saddled it for him, then brought it close to him. When it bolted with him, it stumbled, and he said: “Who saddled this?” They said: So-and-so. He said: “Return it to Talhah.” So it was returned to me. Talhah said: By Allah, I did not deceive anyone in Islam except him, so that the saddle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come back to me."],[213,"On the day of Uhud, I placed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my back until he stood upright and was on the rock, shielded from the polytheists. He said: “Like this,” and gestured with his hand behind my back, “this is Jibril ﷺ . He has informed me that he will not see you on the Day of Resurrection in any terror except that he will rescue you from it.”"],[214,"On the day of Uhud, an arrow struck me and I said: “Hiss!” He said: “If you had said: In the name of Allah, the angels would have flown with you while the people were looking at you.”"],[215,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he would say: “Whoever would like to look at a martyr walking on the face of the earth, let him look at Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah.”"],[216,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he would say: “My predecessor in this world and my predecessor in the Hereafter.”"],[217,"When the Prophet ﷺ returned from Uhud, he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, and then recited this verse: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah” — the entire verse. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these? I approached wearing two green garments, and he said: “O questioner, this is one of them.”"],[218,"On the day of Uhud the Prophet ﷺ named me Talhah al-Khayr (Talhah of Goodness), on the day of the expedition of Dhat al-‘Ushayrah Talhah al-Fayyad (Talhah the Generous), and on the day of Hunayn Talhah al-Jud (Talhah of Bounty)."],[219,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was among a group of his companions, holding a quince in his hand, turning it over. When I sat down beside him, he rolled it toward me and said: “Take it, Abu Muhammad, for it strengthens the heart, purifies the soul, and removes the heaviness of the chest.”"],[220,"From ‘Urwah, regarding those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza: al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam b. Khuwaylid b. Asad."],[221,"Al-Zubayr was given the kunyah Abu Abdullah."],[222,"When it was the battle of Yarmuk, they said to al-Zubayr, O Abu Abdullah."],[223,"I heard Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Urwah b. al-Zubayr say: Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was fair-skinned, tall, with a trimmed beard, light on the sides."],[224,"Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was tall; his feet would touch the ground when he mounted a riding beast. He had much hair, and sometimes I would grasp the hair on his shoulders."],[225,"Ibn Umar heard a man say, 'I am the son of the disciple of the Prophet ﷺ.' Ibn Umar said, 'If you are from the family of al-Zubayr, then yes; otherwise, no.'"],[226,"The first to draw a sword in the path of Allah was al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam."],[227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Trench, 'Who will bring us news of Banu Qurayzah?' He called them a second time, then a third time, and al-Zubayr volunteered. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.'"],[228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.'"],[229,"I covered him, so I covered him. It occurred to me to glance at him, and I saw him mutilated with swords. I said, 'By Allah, I have seen marks on you that I have never seen on anyone else.' He said, 'And you have seen that?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'By Allah, there is no wound among them except that it was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in the path of Allah, may He be exalted.'"],[230,"Gabriel ﷺ descended on the day of Badr in the appearance of al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, wearing a yellow turban."],[231,"On the day of Badr, there were two horsemen with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam on a horse on the right flank, and al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad on a horse on the left flank."],[232,"That I entrust it to him: al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, for he is a pillar among the pillars of the religion."],[233,"Do you hear what he says to me? Zubayr struck him until he fell."],[234,"Abdullah said to him, \"Will you make my mother a target for your oath?\" So he rushed upon him and freed her from him, and she became separated from him. He said, \"I was a boy who sometimes grabbed the hair on Zubayr's shoulders.\""],[235,"\"O my sons, do not marry your daughters except to suitable matches.\" They said, \"O our father, who are the suitable matches?\" He said, \"The descendants of Zubayr b. al-Awwam.\""],[236,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say, \"Zubayr was killed at the age of sixty-four, and he was killed in the year thirty-six.\""],[237,"\"Zubayr embraced Islam at the age of sixteen and was killed at the age of sixty-something.\""],[238,"\"Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada—I do not know whether it was the first or the second—in the year thirty-six.\""],[239,"\"Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada—I do not know whether it was the first or the second—in the year thirty-six.\""],[240,"Zubayr b. al-Awwam embraced Islam at the age of eight, and he emigrated at the age of eighteen. Zubayr's uncle would hang Zubayr in a mat and smoke him with fire, saying, \"Return to disbelief,\" and Zubayr would say, \"I will never disbelieve.\""],[241,"\"When Umar ؓ was killed, Zubayr erased his name from the register.\""],[242,"The killer of Zubayr approached Zubayr, and Zubayr turned to face him. He said, \"I remind you of Allah,\" and Zubayr refrained from him until he did that several times. Then Zubayr said, \"May Allah fight him—he reminds by Allah ﷻ yet forgets Him.\""],[243,"On the Day of the Camel, Ali ؓ saw heads being severed. He took al-Hasan ؓ by the hand and placed it on his belly, then said, \"O my son, what good is there after this?\""],[244,"I was sitting with Ali ؓ when the head of Zubayr ؓ was brought. Ali ؓ said, \"Give news of Hellfire to the killer of the son of Safiyyah. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Zubayr.'\""],[245,"About a military expedition that the Messenger of God ﷺ undertook, and he was killed at the age of sixty-something, and he was from al-Basra, at about a barid away."],[246,"Al-Zubayr was killed in the year thirty-six. Ibn Jurmuz killed him, and with him were al-Nu'man b. Zimam and Abu al-Madrahi, two men from Banu Tamim. He was killed in Wadi al-Siba' and buried there."],[247,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, Uthman, al-Miqdam b. al-Aswad, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Muti' b. al-Aswad made their wills to al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam."],[248,"Ali, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas were of the same age."],[249,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A single suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.\""],[250,"\"On the day of Uhud, it was as if I was seeing servants on her thighs encouraging people.\""],[251,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The earth is God's earth and the servants are God's servants. Wherever one of you finds good, let him fear God and stay.\""],[252,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The earth is God's earth and the servants are God's servants. Wherever one of you finds good, let him fear God and stay.\""],[253,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The earth is God's earth and the servants are God's servants. Wherever one of you finds good, let him fear God and stay.\""],[254,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the morning prayer in the mosque of Madinah. When he finished, he said: \"Which of you will follow me to the delegation of the jinn tonight?\" The people fell silent, and none of them spoke. He said that three times. Then he passed by me walking, took me by the hand, and I walked with him until all the mountains of Madinah receded from us, and we were led to a flat land. There were tall men, as if they were spears, having tucked their garments between their legs. When I saw them, a severe trembling seized me until my legs could not hold me from fear. When we drew near to them, the Messenger of God ﷺ drew a line with the big toe of his foot on the ground and said to me: \"Sit in the middle of it.\" When I sat down, everything I felt of apprehension left me. The Prophet ﷺ went between me and them and recited the Qur'an in a raised voice until dawn broke. Then he came back, passed by me, and said: \"Follow.\" I walked with him, and we went a short distance. Then he said to me: \"Look back and see if you can see anyone where those had been.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I see many dark shapes.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ lowered his head to the ground, strung a bone with dung, threw it at them, and said: \"Those were rightly guided from the delegation of a people—they are the delegation of Nasibin. They asked me for provision, so I made for them every bone and dung.\" Al-Zubayr said: \"So it is not permissible for anyone ever to clean oneself with bone or dung.\""],[255,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. Abd Awf b. Abd al-Harith b. Zuhrah b. Kilab."],[256,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ was called Abd al-Ka'bah in the pre-Islamic era, so the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Abd al-Rahman."],[257,"My name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of God ﷺ named me Abd al-Rahman."],[258,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. Abd Awf b. Abd al-Harith b. Zuhrah, whose kunya is Abu Muhammad, was present at Badr."],[259,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr, concerning those who were present at Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ from the Banu Zuhrah b. Kilab b. Murrah: Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. al-Harith b. Zuhrah."],[260,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ, “How did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in touching the corner?”—meaning the Black Stone. Abd al-Rahman said, “I touched it and left off.” The Messenger of God said, “You have done correctly.”"],[261,"A companion of mine [said]: The Commander of the Faithful did not give you a good ruling until he asked the man. Umar ؓ heard part of his speech, so Umar struck him with the whip as a beating. Then he turned to me to strike me, so I said, “O Commander of the Faithful, I did not say anything; he said it.” So he left me. He said: Then he said, “You wanted to kill what is sacred and transgress the fatwa.” Then he said, “In a person there are ten traits: nine good and one evil. That evil one corrupts it.” Then he said, “Beware of the company of young men.”"],[262,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ used to wear a shirt of karabisi cloth reaching to the middle of his calf, and his cloak would strike his buttocks."],[263,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf had lost his two front teeth, was gap-toothed, left-handed, and lame. He was injured at Uhud, so his teeth were broken, and he received twenty wounds or more, some of which affected his leg, so he became lame."],[264,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ was born ten years after the Elephant, and he died in the year thirty-one or thirty-two, aged seventy-five. Uthman b. Affan ؓ prayed over him."],[265,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ was born ten years after the Elephant, and he died in the year thirty-one or thirty-two, aged seventy-five. Uthman b. Affan ؓ prayed over him."],[266,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ was born ten years after the Elephant, and he died in the year thirty-one or thirty-two, aged seventy-five. Uthman b. Affan ؓ prayed over him."],[267,"While Aisha ؓ was in her house, she heard a sound from which Madinah trembled. She said, “What is this?” They said, “A caravan has arrived for Abd al-Rahman b. Awf from Syria, consisting of seven hundred camels.” Aisha ؓ said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘I saw Abd al-Rahman b. Awf entering Paradise crawling.’” This reached Abd al-Rahman, so he came to her and asked her about what had reached him, and she told him. He said, “I call you to witness that it, with its loads, its saddle-frames, and its saddle-cloths, is for the sake of God.”"],[268,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf gave half his wealth in charity during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ—four thousand. Then he gave forty thousand [dirhams]. Then he gave forty thousand dinars. Then he equipped five hundred horses in the path of God. Then he equipped one thousand five hundred camels in the path of God. Most of his wealth came from trade."],[269,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “If the plague breaks out in a land and you are in it, do not leave it, fleeing from it. If it breaks out in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it.” Abu al-Qasim said: Thus it was narrated by Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid b. Tamim and Sufyan b. Husayn, and Ibn Abi Dhiʾb differed from them."],[270,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “This pain, or this illness, is a punishment with which those before you were punished. So if it is in a land where you are not, do not go down upon it; and if it is in a land where you are, do not leave fleeing from it.” He said: Then ‘Umar ؓ turned the people back that year."],[271,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[272,"Al-Qa‘nabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ‘Abd al-Ḥamīd b. ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb, from ‘Abd Allāh b. al-Ḥārith b. Nawfal, from ‘Abd Allāh b. ‘Abbās, from ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. ‘Awf ؓ, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[273,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of this epidemic in a town, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[274,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, fleeing from it must not make you leave.”"],[275,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This epidemic is a punishment with which Allah destroyed some nations, and some of it remains on the earth, coming at times and going at times. So if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave it; and if you hear of it in a land, do not go there.”"],[277,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “This pain, or sickness, is a punishment with which some nations before you were punished; then it remained afterwards on the earth, going one time and coming another. So whoever hears of it in a land, they should not advance upon it, and whoever is in a land where it occurs, fleeing from it must not make him leave.” And the wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Layth."],[278,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “It is a punishment that befell those before you, or a torment that befell those before you. So if you hear of it in a town, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a town, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This epidemic is something with which the nations before you were punished, and there remains on the earth a remnant of it. It occurs at times and goes at times. So if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land where you are not, do not enter upon it.”"],[280,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “It is a defilement that befell those before you. So if you hear of it in a town, do not enter it upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a town, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear of it in a land, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[282,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, 'Which part of the night is best for hearing (prayers)?' He said, 'The last part of the night. Then prayer is accepted until you pray the dawn. Then there is no prayer until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands as a spear. Then there is no prayer until the sun declines. Then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then there is no prayer until the sun sets.'"],[283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, 'Which part of the night is best for hearing (prayers)?' He said, 'The last part of the night. Then prayer is accepted until you pray the dawn. Then there is no prayer until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands as a spear. Then there is no prayer until the sun declines. Then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then there is no prayer until the sun sets.'"],[284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ missed a man from his companions. He said, 'Where were you? For I did not see you. Did you not attend the prayer?' He said, 'Yes, but I came when the people had already settled, and I disliked stepping over people's necks.' He said, 'You did well.'"],[285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The official, when he is appointed and takes what is right and gives what is right, is like the one striving in the way of God until he returns to his home.'"],[286,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The midday prayer is from the night prayer.' So I asked Abd al-Rahman b. Humayd about the midday. He said, 'When the sun declines.'"],[287,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ heard a man from Banu Hashim saying, 'I am the closest of people to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said, 'Another is closer to him than you, but you have his lineage.'"],[288,"Umama bt. Abi al-As became critically ill. Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ saying to him, 'My daughter is critically ill.' He sent to his daughter, 'To God belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He leaves.' She became critically ill a second time, and she sent to him, 'My daughter is critically ill.' He sent to his daughter, 'To God belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He leaves.' Then it was the third time, and the Prophet ﷺ came to her. She brought the child out to him, and her soul was rattling in her chest. With the Prophet ﷺ were some of his companions. His eyes shed tears until he grasped his beard. He noticed them while they were looking at him, and he said, 'What is with you that you look?' They said, 'O Messenger of God, we saw you become tender.' He said, 'It is a mercy that God ﷻ places wherever He wills. And God will have mercy tomorrow on the merciful among His servants.'"],[289,"Sleep was cast upon us on the day of Uhud."],[290,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'A little understanding is better than much worship, and the best of your deeds are the easiest.'"],[291,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Gently, O Talha, for he witnessed Badr as you did. And the best of you is the best to his clients.'"],[292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Satan, may God curse him, said, \"The owner of wealth will never be safe from me through one of three things: I will come to him with them morning and evening – his taking wealth without its right, spending it without its right, and making it beloved to him so that he withholds it from its right.\"'"],[293,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, who am I?' He said, 'Sa'd b. Malik b. Uhayb b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhra. Whoever says otherwise, upon him is the curse of God.'"],[294,"To Saʿd: \"Thus is the thought concerning you, O Abū Isḥāq.\""],[295,"Saʿd said: O Messenger of God, who am I? He said: \"You are Saʿd b. Mālik b. Ahyab b. ʿAbd Manāf b. Zuhrah, so whoever says otherwise, upon him is the curse of God.\""],[296,"The mother of Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ was Ḥamnāh bt. Abī Sufyān b. Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams b. ʿAbd Manāf, and her mother was the daughter of Abī Sarḥ b. Ḥabīb b. Jadhīmah b. Naṣr b. Mālik b. Ḥasal b. ʿĀmir b. Luʾayy b. Ghālib."],[297,"\"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ had curly hair, a hairy body, was tall, dark-skinned, and flat-nosed.\""],[298,"\"My father was a short, stout, thick-set man with a large head and coarse fingers, and he had witnessed Badr.\""],[299,"\"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ used to dye his hair black.\""],[300,"\"Saʿd used to dye his hair black.\""],[301,"\"On the day of Badr, I, ʿAmmār, and Saʿd shared in the spoils. Saʿd got two captives, while I and ʿAmmār got nothing.\""],[302,"I heard Saʿd say: \"No one embraced Islam except on the day I embraced it, and indeed I remained for seven days while I was one-third of Islam.\""],[303,"\"Saʿd was the last of the Emigrants to die ؓ.\""],[304,"My father said: \"He died at the age of eighty-three, and he died ten miles from Madinah, and was carried on the shoulders of men to Madinah. Marwān was the governor of it at that time. He embraced Islam when he was nineteen years old.\""],[305,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Saʿd died while Marwān was governor of Madinah, and he prayed over him. He died in the year fifty-five.\""],[306,"Sa'd died in al-ʿAqīq, in his palace, ten miles from Madinah, and was carried on the shoulders of men to Madinah. It is said that he died when he was seventy-some years old."],[307,"He said, “I embraced Islam when I was nineteen years old, and he died in the year fifty-five.”"],[308,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ died in the time of Muʿāwiyah ؓ after his first Hajj, when he was eighty-three years old."],[309,"Saʿd was the last of the Muhājirūn to die ؓ."],[310,"Ibn Masʿūd had a claim of money against Saʿd ؓ. Ibn Masʿūd said, “Pay the money that you owe.” Saʿd said, “Woe to you! What is between me and your money?” He said, “Pay the money that you owe.” Saʿd said, “By Allah, I see that you will meet evil from me. Are you anything but Ibn Masʿūd, a slave of the Banū Hudhayl?” He said, “Yes, by Allah, I am Ibn Masʿūd and you are Ibn Ḥamnah.” Hāshim b. ʿUtbah said to them, “You are both companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. People look to you.” Saʿd threw down a stick that was in his hand, then raised his hands and said, “O Allah, Lord of the heavens...” ʿAbdullāh said to him, “Say words, and do not curse.” So he fell silent. Then Saʿd said, “By Allah, were it not for fear of Allah, I would call upon you with a supplication that would not miss you.”"],[311,"While Saʿd was walking, he passed by a man who was reviling ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, and al-Zubayr. Saʿd said to him, “You are reviling people for whom Allah has already decreed what He has decreed. By Allah, you must stop reviling them, or I will supplicate Allah ﷻ against you.” The man said, “You frighten me as if you were a prophet.” Saʿd said, “O Allah, this man reviles people for whom You have already decreed what You have decreed, so make him an example today.” Then a Bactrian camel came, the people made way for it, and it trampled him. I saw the people following Saʿd, saying, “May Allah answer your supplication, O Abū Isḥāq.”"],[312,"The people of Kufa complained about Saʿd to ʿUmar ؓ. He sent men to ask about him in Kufa. They did not come to any mosque of the people of Kufa except that they praised him and spoke well of him, until they came to a mosque of the Banū ʿAbs. A man called Abū Saʿdah stood up and said, “Since you have asked us, he does not lead raiding parties, he does not judge fairly, and he does not distribute equally.” Saʿd said, “O Allah, if he is lying, blind him, prolong his poverty, and expose him to trials.” ʿAbd al-Malik said, “I saw him accosting slave women in the streets. When they asked him, ‘How are you, Abū Saʿdah?’ he would say, ‘Old, blind, poor, and afflicted. The supplication of Saʿd has overtaken me.’” Abū al-Qāsim said, “Abū Saʿdah is the grandfather of Abū Bakr b. Abī Shaybah.”"],[313,"She was called Zīrā, and she was wearing a new shirt. The wind uncovered her, so ʿUmar ؓ struck her with a whip. Saʿd came to stop him, and he struck him with the whip. Saʿd went to supplicate against ʿUmar, but ʿUmar handed him the whip and said, “Take retribution.” So he forgave ʿUmar ؓ."],[314,"A Muslim man satirized Saʿd, and he said..."],[315,"A cousin of ours on the day of al-Qādisiyyah."],[316,"To his son when death came to him: “O my son, you will never meet anyone more sincere to you than I am. When you want to pray, perform your ablution well, then pray a prayer such that you do not think you will pray after it. Beware of greed, for it is present poverty. And cling to despair [of what people have], for that is wealth. Beware of doing or saying anything for which you would have to apologize. Do what seems right to you.”"],[317,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ: “No one embraced Islam on the day I did, and I remained for seven days while I was a third of Islam.”"],[318,"I heard Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas say: \"Indeed, I am the first Muslim man to shoot an arrow in the cause of God, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[319,"The Prophet ﷺ combined his parents for him. He said: \"A man from the polytheists had incited the Muslims, so the Prophet ﷺ said to Sa'd: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'\" He said: \"So I drew a blunt arrow and struck his side. He fell, and his private parts were exposed, and the Prophet ﷺ laughed until I saw his molars.\""],[320,"\"Shroud me in it, for in it I faced the polytheists on the day of Badr, and I was keeping it for this.\""],[321,"\"When my father prayed in the mosque, he was brief but completed the bowing and prostration; when he prayed at home, he prolonged the bowing, prostration, and prayer.\" I said: \"O father, when you pray in the mosque you are brief, but when you are alone at home you lengthen it.\" He said: \"O my son, we are leaders who are followed.\""],[322,"On the day of Badr, I was shooting before the Prophet ﷺ. I placed the arrow on the bowstring and said: 'O God, make their feet slip, terrify their hearts, and do to them such and such.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O God, answer Sa'd.'"],[323,"\"You disobeyed me concerning this arbitration.\" A dark-complexioned youth stood up to him and said: \"By God, you did not forbid us; rather, you commanded us and destroyed us. When something you disliked happened, you absolved yourself and saddled us with your sin.\" 'Ali ؓ said to him: \"What have you to do with this speech? May God disfigure you! By God, there was a community and you were insignificant in it. When the strife appeared, you emerged in it like the horns of a goat.\" Then he turned to the people and said: \"For God is the standing of Sa'd b. Malik and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar. By God, if it was a sin, it is small and forgiven; and if it was a good deed, it is great and appreciated.\""],[324,"When 'Umar ؓ was wounded, he began advising the people of the council: \"If Sa'd is chosen, then that is it; otherwise let the one appointed seek his help, for I did not remove him out of incapacity or betrayal.\""],[325,"He said: \"Sit here for the people.\" Sa'd apologized to him and swore that he had not spoken the word that had reached the Commander of the Faithful."],[326,"\"I will not fight until you bring me a sword with two eyes, a tongue, and lips that recognizes the believer from the disbeliever, for I have struggled while knowing jihad.\""],[327,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas approached. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This is my maternal uncle; let a man show me his uncle.\""],[328,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Killing a Muslim is disbelief, insulting him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days.\""],[329,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.\""],[330,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My father used to maintain ties of kinship, and he was, and he was—so where is he?\" He said, \"In the Fire.\" It was as if the bedouin was hurt by that, so he said, \"O Messenger of God, then where is your father?\" He said, \"Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him tidings of the Fire.\" The bedouin later accepted Islam, and he said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ tasked me with a burden; I never passed by the grave of a disbeliever except that I gave him tidings of the Fire.\""],[331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever desires humiliation for Quraysh, God will humiliate him.\""],[332,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.\""],[333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, part of happiness is a righteous wife, a good dwelling, and a good mount. And indeed, part of misery is a bad wife, a bad dwelling, and a bad mount.\""],[334,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"It is a punishment that afflicted those before you. If it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if it occurs in a land, do not enter it.\""],[335,"Three verses from the Book of God (Mighty and Sublime) were revealed concerning me. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, I had been drinking with a man; I opposed him and he opposed me, and I became rowdy with him and wounded him. Then God (Exalted is He) revealed, {O you who believe, wine and gambling...} up to His saying {So will you desist?} And there was revealed concerning me, {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents. His mother carried him with hardship} to the end of the verse. And there was revealed, {O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, give charity before your private consultation.} So I offered a barley grain, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You are indeed frugal.\" Then the other was revealed, {Are you afraid to give charities before your private consultation?} the entire verse."],[336,"Three verses from the Book of God (Mighty and Sublime) were revealed concerning me. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, I had been drinking with a man; I opposed him and he opposed me, and I became rowdy with him and wounded him. Then God (Exalted is He) revealed, {O you who believe, wine and gambling...} up to His saying {So will you desist?} And there was revealed concerning me, {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents. His mother carried him with hardship} to the end of the verse. And there was revealed, {O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, give charity before your private consultation.} So I offered a barley grain, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You are indeed frugal.\" Then the other was revealed, {Are you afraid to give charities before your private consultation?} the entire verse."],[337,"Three verses from the Book of God (Mighty and Sublime) were revealed concerning me. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, I had been drinking with a man; I opposed him and he opposed me, and I became rowdy with him and wounded him. Then God (Exalted is He) revealed, {O you who believe, wine and gambling...} up to His saying {So will you desist?} And there was revealed concerning me, {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents. His mother carried him with hardship} to the end of the verse. And there was revealed, {O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, give charity before your private consultation.} So I offered a barley grain, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You are indeed frugal.\" Then the other was revealed, {Are you afraid to give charities before your private consultation?} the entire verse."],[338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.\""],[339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[340,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Rabah b. 'Abd Allah b. Qurt b. Razah b. 'Adi b. Ka'b; his kunya is Abu al-A'war, and his mother is Fatimah bt. Na'jah b. Umayyah b. Khuwaylid, from Khuza'ah."],[341,"Sa'id b. Zayd was tall, dark-skinned, and hairy."],[342,"I heard Abu Hafs Amr b. Ali say: Sa'id b. Zayd was dark-skinned, tall, and very hairy."],[343,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl arrived from Syria after the Messenger of God ﷺ had returned from Badr. He spoke to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he allotted him his share. He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God, as they claim?\" He said, \"And your reward.\""],[344,"Sa'id b. Zayd arrived from Syria after the Prophet ﷺ had arrived from Badr. He spoke to the Prophet ﷺ about his share, so he said to him, \"Your share.\" He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And your reward.\""],[345,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl died in the year fifty-one, or in the seventies, and was buried in Madinah. He died at al-Aqiq, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas and Ibn Umar went down into his grave. His kunya was Abu al-A'war."],[346,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas washed Sa'id b. Zayd at al-Sajara."],[347,"She stole my land and incorporated it into her land. Sa'id said, \"I would not steal from her after I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever steals a span of land will be collared with it down to the seven earths.'\" She said, \"I will not dispute with you after this.\" Sa'id said, \"O God, if she is lying, take away her sight and kill her in her land.\" Her sight was taken away, and she fell into a pit in her land and died."],[348,"I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr saying, \"Sa'id ibn Zaid died in the year fifty-one in Medina.\""],[349,"I did not wash from the washing of Sa'id; I washed only because of the heat."],[350,"A man from Syria said, \"What is holding you back?\" He said, \"Until Sa'id b. Zayd comes and gives allegiance, for he is the most noble of the people of the land. When he gives allegiance to the people, the people give allegiance.\""],[351,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There will be after me trials, and in them there will be, and there will be.\" We said, \"If we live to see that, we will perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for my Companions.\""],[352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the trials, so we said, \"O Messenger of God, will everyone tried in them perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for you.\""],[353,"He mentioned a tribulation — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — like patches of dark night. He said, \"People will go in it in the quickest going.\" It was said, \"Will all of them perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for them.\""],[354,"Indeed, the one you seek will appear in your land. He turned back saying: \"At Your service, truly, truly, in worship and servitude. I seek piety, not the transient. Is an emigrant like one who said: I seek refuge in what Ibrahim sought refuge, while he was standing? I disown for You, O God, a submissive, compelled one. Whatever You burden me with, I will bear.\" Then he fell down and prostrated to the Kaaba. He said: Zayd b. Amr passed by the Prophet ﷺ and Zayd b. Haritha while they were eating from a traveling provision of theirs. They invited him, so he said, \"O son of my brother, I do not eat from what is slaughtered on the stone altars.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ was not seen eating from what is slaughtered on the stone altars from that day until he was sent as a prophet. He said: Sa'id b. Zayd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Zayd was as you saw, or as you have heard. Pray for forgiveness for him.\" He said, \"Yes,\" so he prayed for forgiveness for him, \"for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone.\""],[355,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced Hasan and said: “O Allah, I have loved him, so love him.”"],[356,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[357,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in defense of his property until he is killed is a martyr.”"],[358,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[359,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever unjustly diminishes even a handspan of the earth, Allah will encircle him on the Day of Judgment from seven earths.\""],[360,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on Hira. It shook, so he struck it with his foot and said: “Be still, Hira, for upon you is none but a prophet, a siddiq, or a martyr.” And these people were with him: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and myself—meaning himself."],[361,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Among the worst forms of usury is a man’s attack on the honor of a Muslim without right. Indeed this womb-relationship is a branch of the Most Merciful; whoever severs it, Allah forbids him Paradise.”"],[362,"Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah—he is Amir b. Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah b. Hilal b. Uhayb b. Dabbah b. al-Harith b. Fihr—left no descendants. The mother of Abu Ubaydah was Umm Ghanm bt. Jabir b. Abd b. al-Ala b. Amir b. Umayrah b. Wadi'ah b. al-Harith b. Fihr."],[363,"“Abu Ubayd Amir b. Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah.”"],[364,"The father of Abu Ubaydah kept confronting Abu Ubaydah on the Day of Badr, but Abu Ubaydah kept avoiding him. When he persisted, Abu Ubaydah headed for him and killed him. Then Allah ﷻ revealed about him, when he killed his father, this verse: {You will not find a people who believe in Allah and the Last Day} to the end of the verse."],[365,"Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah was present at Badr from the Banu al-Harith b. Fihr."],[366,"Syria was under two commanders: Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Yazid b. Abi Sufyan. Abu Ubaydah died and appointed as his successor his maternal uncle Iyad b. Ghanm, one of the Banu al-Harith b. Fihr, and Umar ؓ confirmed him. Then Iyad died, and he appointed in his place Sa'id b. 'Amir b. Judhaym. Then Sa'id b. 'Amir died, and he appointed in his place 'Umayr b. Sa'd."],[367,"He got ahead of him. Indeed I saw the two forelocks of Abu Ubaydah bobbing as he galloped behind him on an Arabian horse."],[368,"It is said that Mu'adh b. Jabal prayed over him."],[369,"Its matter concerning al-Harith himself, and he feared for it when he saw it. Abu Ubaydah swore to him by Allah that he would not love to have in exchange for it red camels."],[370,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among the prayers, there is no prayer more excellent than the Fajr prayer on Friday in congregation, and I do not think anyone among you who attends it but will be forgiven.\""],[371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, this matter (Islam) began as mercy and prophethood, then it will become mercy and caliphate, then it will become a cruel monarchy, then it will become tyrannical rule, and finally corruption on the earth. They will make silk, sex trade, and alcohol permissible, and they will be provided sustenance based on that, and they will be victorious until they meet Allah.\""],[372,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, entrust me to a man of good teaching. He entrusted me to Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, then said: I have entrusted you to a man who will teach you well and discipline you. I went to Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah while he and Bashir b. Sa'd, Abu al-Nu'man b. Bashir, were conversing. When they saw me, they fell silent. I said: O Abu Ubaydah, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not tell me this. He said: You came while we were speaking of a hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so sit until we tell you. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among you is prophethood, then there will be a caliphate upon the pattern of prophethood, then there will be kingship and tyranny.\""],[373,"I passed by the mosque and found Ali and al-Abbas ؓ sitting. They said: O Usama, ask permission for us to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali and al-Abbas are at the door wanting to enter upon you. He said: \"Do you know what brought them?\" I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what brought them. He said: \"But I know what brought them. Give them permission.\" They entered upon him, and Ali said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you which of your family is most beloved to you? He said: \"Fatimah daughter of Muhammad\" ﷺ. Ali said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I am not asking you about your family. He said: \"The most beloved of my family to me is the one whom Allah has blessed and whom I have blessed: Usama.\" He said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Then you.\" Al-Abbas said: You have made your uncle the last of them? He said: \"Ali preceded you in the Hijrah.\""],[374,"Usama went to a palm tree, tapped it, and extracted its heart, then fed it to his mother. They said to him: What led you to do this when you see the palm tree has reached a thousand? He said: \"My mother asked me for it, and she does not ask me for anything I am able to give but that I give it to her.\""],[375,"Usama b. Zayd was called to the command until he died. They said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him, then did not remove him until he died."],[376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Usama is the most beloved of people to me.\""],[377,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr regarding his lineage: Usama b. Zayd b. Harithah b. Sharahil b. Ka'b b. Abd al-Uzza b. Yazid b. Imri al-Qays, the Kalbi, and Allah and His Messenger ﷺ blessed him."],[378,"I heard our elders say: The inscription on the ring of Usama b. Zayd was 'the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[379,"\"I saw people among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapping their lower garments midway up their shins. He mentioned Ibn Umar, Zayd b. Arqam, Usama b. Zayd, and al-Bara b. Azib ؓ.\""],[380,"The Prophet ﷺ clothed him with a Coptic garment from what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted him. I clothed my wife with it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with you that you do not wear the Coptic garment?\" I said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: \"Tell her to put a lining under it, for I fear it may reveal the outline of her bones.\""],[381,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, I descended and the people descended to Madinah. I entered upon him while he had become silent and was not speaking. He began raising his hand to the sky and lowering it upon me, and I knew that he was supplicating for me."],[382,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ja'far: \"Your physical form is like my physical form, and you are from me, and you, O 'Ali, are from me and the father of my child.\""],[383,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Jam' (Muzdalifah), he prayed Maghrib and 'Isha there."],[384,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military expedition to Al-Hurqu'at.\""],[385,"He informed him (the Prophet), saying, \"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Indeed, I have divorced and remembered the hadith.'\""],[386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, this plague is a punishment,\" then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[387,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, this plague is a punishment,\" then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[388,"He informed him: \"I rode with the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey, on a packsaddle, on a velvet cloth,\" then he mentioned the hadith in full."],[389,"He departed with the Prophet ﷺ on the evening of 'Arafah. He went to a narrow pass, made his mount kneel, relieved himself, then came and performed ablution while Usamah poured water for him. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the prayer?' He said: 'The prayer place is ahead of you.'"],[390,"Gloom entered upon the Prophet ﷺ. I said: 'What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Jibril ﷺ promised me that he would come to me, but he has not come to me for three days.' He said: And there was a dog. Usamah said: I put my hand on my head and shouted. He said: 'What is the matter with you, O Usamah?' I said: 'A dog.' So the Prophet ﷺ ordered it and it was killed. Then Jibril came to him and said: 'What is the matter with you that you did not come to me? When you promise me, you do not break it.' He said: 'We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images.'"],[391,"The Messenger of Allah said, \"Is there anyone eager for Paradise? By the Lord of the Kabah, it is a radiant light, a [breezes] of sweet fragrances, a steady flowing river, a lovely and beautiful spouse in an everlasting garden and an abode of joy.\""],[392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions used to accept pardon from the polytheists and the People of the Book as Allah, Mighty and Sublime, commanded them, and they were patient in the face of harm. Allah, Mighty and Sublime, said: 'You will surely hear from those who were given the Scripture before you and from those who associate others with Allah much abuse' [Quran 3:186]. The Prophet ﷺ used to interpret the command of pardon as Allah had commanded him until Allah gave permission concerning them. When the Prophet ﷺ raided Badr and Allah killed those He killed of the disbelievers among the leaders of Quraysh, Ibn Ubayy and those with him among the polytheists said: 'This is a matter that has taken hold. So pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam.' And they became Muslims."],[393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to visit 'Abdullah b. Ubayy during the illness in which he died, and I was with him. He recognized death in him and said: 'I used to forbid you from loving the Jews.' He said: 'As'ad b. Zurarah died, so what?' When he died, his son 'Abdullah came to him and said: 'Abdullah has died, so give me your shirt to shroud him in it.' He removed his shirt and clothed him with it."],[394,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim, nor does a Muslim inherit from a disbeliever, and the people of two religions do not inherit from each other.'"],[395,"I thrust a spear into a man while he was saying 'There is no god but Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said to Usamah: 'What will you do with \"There is no god but Allah\" on the Day of Resurrection?' He repeated that several times until I wished that I had not become Muslim before that moment."],[396,"I sought permission for some people from among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he granted them permission. There he was, with his head covered with a striped Yemeni cloak of his. He uncovered his head and then said: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[397,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to al-Huraqat.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[398,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “A man will be brought” and then he mentioned the hadith."],[399,"That he “saw the Prophet ﷺ enter the House” — the hadith."],[400,"\"The Prophet wiped over the Khuff and the Khimar.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 101)"],[401,"“The daughters of the Prophet ﷺ were sent” — the hadith."],[402,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Indeed Allah, exalted be He, does not love the obscene and the one who acts obscenely.”"],[403,"From Usama: “The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to raid the people of Ibna’ in the morning and to burn.”"],[404,"A man arrived from one of the rural areas and was afflicted with pain, so he returned. The Prophet ﷺ said: “I hope that its mountain pass will not appear to us,” meaning the mountain pass of Madinah."],[405,"Indeed, I do not say to a man, “You are the best of people,” after I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection” — the hadith."],[406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This plague is a punishment and torment with which those before you were punished. So if it is in a land, do not leave it, and if it falls in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it.”"],[407,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, Allah does not like obscenity and vulgarity.\""],[408,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed Allah, exalted be He, hates the obscene and foul-mouthed.”"],[409,"That the Prophet ﷺ “entered the House and walked until he reached its middle, drew near to the wall, and entered between Usama and Bilal” — the hadith."],[410,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House and saw images. He called for water and began wiping them out, saying, “May Allah fight a people who depict what they do not create.”"],[411,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zhuhr in the intense heat."],[412,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Deeds are presented to Allah (mighty and sublime be He) on Monday and Thursday, and Allah forgives except whatever is between two people bearing mutual hatred or one who severs family ties.”"],[413,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"All of them are from this Ummah.\""],[414,"The Prophet ﷺ said during his final illness: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[415,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.” Ma‘mar, Sufyan b. Husayn, and Salih b. Kaysan added in their narration that the Prophet ﷺ said, “And did ‘Aqil leave us any house?”"],[416,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, where will we stay tomorrow?” He said, “And did ‘Aqil leave us any house or property? Our place is at Khayf of Banu Kinanah where Quraysh swore an oath upon disbelief.”"],[417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued riding in his usual manner after departing from Jam‘."],[418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[420,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[421,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left among people any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have not left behind me any trial more harmful to men than women.\""],[424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I saw that the people of hard work were held back from entering, except for those who were from the people of hell, as they were ordered to be taken to the fire.\""],[425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever abandons three Friday prayers without an excuse is written among the hypocrites.\""],[426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had Umm Salamah with him when Jibril ﷺ came and spoke as was decreed. When he stood up, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Umm Salamah, who is this?\" She said: \"Dihyah.\" She said: \"By Allah, I did not think he was anyone but Dihyah until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon about the news of Jibril ﷺ.\" Mu'tamir said: My father said to Abu 'Uthman: \"From whom did you hear it?\" He said: \"From Usamah.\""],[427,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When a believer is praised to his face, faith grows in his heart.\""],[428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The most grateful of people to Allah are the most grateful of them to people.\""],[429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of Hamal, he and Bilal, and Bilal came out to them and informed them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks.\""],[431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[432,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[435,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[436,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in the deferred sale (nasīʾa).”"],[437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale.”"],[438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale or in a delay (naẓira).”"],[439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt.”"],[440,"He narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt.”"],[441,"“It is lawful with an increase or decrease if it is hand to hand.” Abu Salih said: I asked Abu Saʿid al-Khudri about that, and he said: “It is unlawful except equal for equal.” So I informed Abu Saʿid of what Ibn Abbas said, and I informed Ibn Abbas of what Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said. They met while I was with them. Abu Saʿid al-Khudri began and said: Ibn Abbas, what is this fatwa you give to people about selling gold for silver? You command them to buy it with an increase or a decrease, hand to hand. Ibn Abbas said: I have not accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ longer than you, and this is Zayd b. Arqam and al-Baraʾ b. ʿAzib; they say: We heard the Prophet ﷺ…"],[442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is in the deferred sale.”"],[443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale.”"],[444,"I heard Usama b. Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt,” or he said, “in the deferred sale.”"],[445,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no riba in a hand-to-hand transaction; riba is only in debt.”"],[446,"He said to Ibn Abbas ؓ: Did you accompany the Prophet ﷺ longer than I did? I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Gold for gold, equal for equal, and silver for silver, equal for equal.” Ibn Abbas said: Usama narrated to me that that was a deferred sale."],[447,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in the deferred sale.”"],[448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in deferred payment.\""],[449,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[450,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no riba in what is hand to hand.\""],[452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in deferred payment.\""],[453,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[454,"\"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah.\""],[455,"\"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah.\""],[456,"He was with Abu al-Minhal, saying: A partner of mine in Kufah sold dirhams for dirhams with a difference between them. I said: I do not think this is permissible. He said: I sold them in the market and no one found fault with me for that. So I went to al-Bara' b. 'Azib and asked him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while our trade was like this, and he said: \"Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm in it; whatever is deferred, there is no good in it.\" And I went to Zayd b. Arqam, for he was a greater trader than me. I went to him and mentioned that to him, and he said: Al-Bara' spoke the truth. Al-Humaydi said: \"This is abrogated; it is not to be acted upon.\""],[457,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri met Ibn 'Abbas and testified concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Gold for gold and silver for silver, like for like. Whoever increases has committed riba.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"I repent to Allah ﷻ from what I used to give as a legal opinion.\" Then he retracted."],[458,"\"I see no harm in what is hand to hand.\" Then I came to Makkah the following year, and he had \"forbidden it.\""],[459,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: O Allah, I repent to You from exchange; this is only my opinion, and here is Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating it from the Prophet ﷺ."],[460,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and I turn to Him in repentance from sarf.\""],[461,"Abu Sa'id said to Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah have mercy on him: \"Repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\" He said: \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and I turn to Him in repentance.\" He said: \"Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold for gold and silver for silver, and said: 'Indeed I fear for you riba?'\" I said to 'Atiyyah: \"What is riba?\" He said: \"Increase and surplus between them.\""],[462,"O people, there is no harm in sarf as long as it is hand to hand; riba is only in nasi'ah. So a word spread among the people of the east and the west until when the season ended, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri entered upon him and said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, have you consumed riba and fed it to others?\" He said: \"Did I do that?\" He said: \"Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba. Silver for silver, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba. Barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, like for like; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba.'\" Until when the next year came, Ibn 'Abbas came and I came with him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O people, last year I spoke a word from my own opinion, and I seek forgiveness from Allah for it and turn to Him in repentance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba.'\" And he repeated to them these six types."],[463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When zina and riba appear in a town, they have made lawful for themselves the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not appoint the death of a servant in a land except that He has made for him a need therein.\""],[465,"That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his mount did not lift its foot at a run until he came to Jam'.\""],[466,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ at 'Arafat and greeted him. The birds were on the heads of his companions. The Bedouins came to him from here and there: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in such and such? Is there any harm upon us in such and such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O servants of Allah, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from a Muslim man wrongfully; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said: \"Seek treatment, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He placed for it a cure, except old age.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best of what people have been given?\" He said: \"People have not been given anything better than good character.\""],[467,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Bedouins came to him, many people from here and there. The people fell silent, no one speaking but them. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in such and such?\" Regarding things from people's affairs that are not objectionable. He said: \"O servants of Allah, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from a man wrongfully; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in seeking treatment?\" He said: \"Seek treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not place a disease except that He placed for it a cure, except old age.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best of what a person is given?\" He said: \"Good character.\""],[468,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when the Bedouins came and asked him, \"What is the best thing that people are given?\" He said, \"Good character.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?\" He said, \"Yes, you should seek medical treatment, for indeed Allah ﷻ has not created any illness except that he has also created its cure, except for one illness.\" They asked, \"What is it?\" He said, \"Old age.\""],[469,"\"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ , and the Bedouins came to him saying, 'We are facing difficulty in such and such matter, we are facing difficulty in such and such matter, is there any harm in it?' He said, 'O servants of Allah, Allah has removed all difficulty except for the one who borrows from someone and intends to repay him back. That person is the one who faces difficulty and destruction.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?' He said, 'Yes, seek medical treatment. Indeed, Allah has not revealed a disease except that He has also revealed its cure, except for one disease.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a person can be given?' He said, 'Good manners.'\""],[470,"I attended the Prophet ﷺ and he was asked which actions are the best. He said, \"Having good character.\""],[471,"“I saw the Bedouins asking the Prophet ﷺ: ‘Is there any harm in such and such, is there any harm in such and such?’ He said to them: ‘O slaves of Allah! Allah has only made harm in that which transgresses the honor of one’s brother. That is what is sinful.’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! Is there any sin if we do not seek treatment?’ He said: ‘Seek treatment, O slaves of Allah! For Allah does not create any disease but He also creates with it the cure, except for old age.’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing that a person may be given?’ He said: ‘Good manners.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3436)"],[472,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is the most excellent of what a Muslim is given?\" He said: \"Good character.\""],[473,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ as if birds were on our heads; none of us was speaking. Then people came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about such and such; give us a ruling about such and such.\" He said: \"O people, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from his brother a loan; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed. Should we seek treatment, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down for it a cure, except one disease.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and what is it?\" He said: \"Old age.\" They said: \"Then who is the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah?\" He said: \"The best of them in character.\""],[474,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ as a pilgrim, and the people would come to him. A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did sa'i before tawaf\" or \"I delayed something.\" He said to them: \"No harm, except upon a man who borrows from the honor of a Muslim man while he is wronging; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\""],[475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who shaved before slaughtering. He said: \"No harm; let him shave.\""],[476,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when some people came to him and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed, Allah ﷻ has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure.\""],[477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked during his Hajj: What is the best thing people have been given? He said, \"Good character.\""],[478,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while people were asking him, and someone said, \"I shaved before sacrificing,\" and another said, \"I did this and that before Fajr.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no harm, there is no harm.\""],[479,"The Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him if there was any difficulty in something for them. The Prophet replied, \"Allah has only placed difficulty on a man who borrows from his brother's wealth. That is what causes difficulty and destruction.\" He also said, \"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down a cure for it, except for one disease, old age.\""],[480,"The Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?\" He said, \"Those with the best character.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said, \"Yes, seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure.\""],[481,"The Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such? Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" He said, \"There is no sin. Allah has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from the honor of his brother; that is the sin.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said, \"Seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure, except old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a human being has been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[482,"Some Bedouin people came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing swords, and they crowded around him asking him questions. We feared for the Prophet ﷺ, so we drew near to them. He said: I heard them saying, \"Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such? Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O people, Allah has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from the honor of his Muslim brother; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment for such-and-such? Should we seek treatment for such-and-such?\" He said, \"Seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a remedy, except old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a Muslim servant has been given in this world?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[483,"A Bedouin said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is best for a Muslim man?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[484,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when some Bedouin people came to him asking him from his right and from his left, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" twice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ has removed the sin except for one who borrows from a Muslim man wrongfully\" or he said \"with wrong.\" \"That is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment for such-and-such?\" twice. He said, \"Yes, seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure, except for one disease: old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing people have been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[485,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the Bedouins came from all directions, until they surrounded him, and the people became silent. They called out, \"O Messenger of Allah, can you cure?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed Allah has not created any disease except that He has also created its cure, except for one disease.\" They asked, \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Old age.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing that can be given to a person?\" He replied, \"Good manners.\" They called out, \"O Messenger of Allah, we face difficulties in various matters. What should be done about that?\" He said, \"O servants of Allah, Allah has not created any difficulty except for those who borrow from others, for that is what causes difficulty and loss.\""],[486,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Hajj saying, \"Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then your nearest.\" Then some people came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Banu Yarbu' have killed some of us.\" He said, \"No soul bears the sin of another.\" Then a man asked him about forgetting to throw the pebbles. He said, \"Throw, and there is no sin.\" Then another man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I forgot the circumambulation.\" He said, \"Circumambulate, and there is no sin.\" Then another came who had shaved before slaughtering. He said, \"Slaughter, and there is no sin.\" He said: They did not ask him about anything that day but that he said, \"No sin, no sin.\" Then he said, \"Allah ﷻ has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from a Muslim; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" And he said, \"Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a remedy, except old age.\""],[487,"When the Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ, we took advantage of their roughness to ask him questions. They came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" He said, \"There is no sin. The sin has been removed from the servants of Allah, except for one who borrows from the honor of his brother wrongfully; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a human being has been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\" This is how Wahb b. Isma'il narrated it from Muhammad b. Qays, and he erred in it. The correct version is from Usamah b. Sharik."],[488,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and his companions we as if they birds were perched on their heads (i.e. they were still and attentive)."],[489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Any man who goes out to divide my community, strike his neck.\" This is how Zayd b. 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib narrated it from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah from Usamah, but the correct version is from 'Arfajah. Likewise, Muhammad b. Bishr narrated it from Mujalid."],[490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever divides my community while they are united, strike his head, whoever he may be.\""],[491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah's hand is with the community. If anyone deviates from it, Satan snatches him as a wolf snatches a sheep from the flock.\""],[492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, \"My Companions were weighed last night. Abu Bakr ؓ was weighed, then 'Umar ؓ was weighed, then 'Uthman ؓ was weighed.\" This is how Yazid b. Harun narrated it. Sa'dawayh narrated it from 'Abd al-A'la b. Abi al-Masawir from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah from Qutbah b. Malik from 'Arfajah."],[493,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death.\""],[494,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and nights; and for the resident, one day and night.\""],[495,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one enters Paradise by his deeds.\" We said, \"Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, not even me, unless Allah ﷻ envelops me in mercy from Him.\" And he placed his hand on his head."],[496,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is none of you but with him is a devil.\" We said, \"And with you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And with me, except that Allah ﷻ helped me against him, so he submitted.\""],[497,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral bier was brought near to him so that he could pray over it. He turned and saw a woman approaching, and he said, \"Turn her back.\" So they turned her back repeatedly until she disappeared. When he saw that she had disappeared, he said the takbir over it."],[498,"We prayed Isha in Basra and were rained upon. Then I came and sought to open [the door]. My father Usamah said to me: \"I saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we were rained upon, and the sky did not wet the bottoms of our sandals. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: 'Pray in your dwellings.'\""],[499,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a rainy day, and he ordered a caller who called out: \"The prayer is in the dwellings.\""],[500,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we set out to Hunayn when seventeen nights of Ramadan had passed. It coincided with a Friday, a rainy day. The Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called out among the people: \"The prayer is in the dwellings.\""],[501,"I witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a light rain—meaning a drizzle—fell upon us. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: \"Whoever wishes to pray in his dwelling, let him pray.\""],[502,"I went out one rainy night to the mosque. When I returned and sought to open [the door], my father said to me: \"I saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah, and a rain fell upon us that did not wet the bottoms of our sandals. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pray in your dwellings.'\""],[503,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a rainy Friday. He ordered a caller who called out: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[504,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"If a nation among the nations testifies, and they are forty or more, Allah accepts their testimony—or he said: He confirms their testimony.\""],[505,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There is no man over whom one hundred pray except that he is forgiven.\""],[506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fast from one brightness to the next.\""],[507,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement.\""],[508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement.\""],[509,"A man freed a share of a slave, so the Prophet ﷺ allowed his emancipation and said: \"Allah has no partner.\""],[510,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the skins of beasts of prey.\" Yazid b. Harun added: \"to be used as floor coverings.\""],[511,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[512,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[513,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[514,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I complain to you about whispers that I feel in my chest. When I am in prayer, I do not know whether to finish my prayer in a sitting position (after two units) or in a prostrating position (after one unit).\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you experience this, raise your right index finger and stab it in your left thigh and say, 'In the name of Allah,' for it is the weapon of the Satan.\""],[515,"From his father, who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: There were two women, one of whom struck the other with a tent pole, killing her and what was in her womb. The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the blood money for the woman was to be paid, and for the fetus a ghurra, a male or female slave, or a horse, or two camels, or such and such from sheep. A man from the clan of the killer said: \"How can we pay blood money, O Messenger of Allah, for one who did not eat, drink, or cry out? Such a one should be disregarded.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Are you a rhymester?\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the inheritance of the woman belonged to her husband and her child, and that the blood money was upon the male relatives of the killer."],[516,"It is said that Haml ibn Malik had two wives, one of them was Hudhayyah and the other was 'Amirayah. Hudhayyah struck the stomach of 'Amirayah with a thin stick or a whip, causing her to miscarry a dead fetus. Hudhayyah then went to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ with her brother, 'Imran ibn 'Uwaymir, and they told him the story. The Prophet said, \"Leave it,\" and 'Imran said, \"O Prophet of Allah, should the one who has not eaten, drunk, or shouted be blamed? She committed such an act.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Leave the wrath of the Bedouins to me, in return there will be a slave or a servant, or five hundred sheep, or a horse, or twenty camels.\" 'Imran said, \"O Prophet of Allah, she has two sons who are the leaders of the community and it is more appropriate for them to be compensated by their mother.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have more right to make a decision regarding your sister than her children do.\" 'Imran said, \"I have nothing to decide on.\" The Prophet said, \"O Haml ibn Malik, who was at that time responsible for such charity, being the husband of both wives and the father of the killed fetus, take from the charity under your supervision twenty and one hundred sheep.\" And so he did."],[517,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when our camel stumbled. I said: \"May the devil perish!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not say 'May the devil perish,' for he then grows until he becomes like a house and says: 'By my power.' Say: 'In the name of Allah,' for he then becomes like a fly.\""],[518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Delay the evening prayer, and you will increase in clemency.\""],[519,"The angels descended on the day of Badr wearing turbans, and on that day al-Zubayr had a yellow turban."],[520,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “Allah does not thank one who does not thank people.”"],[521,"He prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr with the Prophet ﷺ, and he prayed near him, so he prayed two light rak'ahs, and I heard him say, “O Allah, Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, Israfil, and Muhammad, I seek refuge in You from the Fire,” three times."],[522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the owner of the plot that was added to the Mosque of Madinah, and its owner was a man from the Ansar. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “You will have for it a house in Paradise.” He said: Then 'Uthman came and said to him, “You will have for it ten thousand,” and he bought it from him. Then 'Uthman ؓ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, buy from me the plot that I bought from the Ansari.” So he bought it from him for a house in Paradise. 'Uthman said, “I bought it for ten thousand dirhams.” The Prophet ﷺ placed a brick, then he called Abu Bakr ؓ and he placed a brick, then he called 'Umar ؓ and he placed a brick, then 'Uthman ؓ came and placed a brick, then he said to the people, “Place [bricks],” and they placed them."],[523,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say, “The name of Abu al-Malih is 'Amir b. Usama.”"],[524,"He was called Asram. He was among the group who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He brought him an Abyssinian slave boy of his whom he had purchased in that region and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I bought this one and I would like you to name him and supplicate for blessing for him.” He said, “What is your name?” He said: He said, “Asram.” He said, “Rather, you are Zur'ah.” He said, “What do you want for him?” He said, “I want him as a shepherd.” He said, “Then he is 'Asim.” And the Prophet ﷺ closed his hand."],[525,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He recited {You have reached from my presence} with tashdid (doubling)."],[526,"From 'Urwah: Among those who witnessed Badr was Ubayy b. Ka'b b. Qays b. 'Ubayd b. Zayd b. Mu'awiya b. 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[527,"I saw Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ with white hair and beard; he did not dye them."],[528,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “May knowledge be pleasant for you, Abu al-Mundhir.”"],[529,"Ubayy had some harshness in his character."],[530,"The companions of judicial authority among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were six: 'Umar, 'Ali, 'Abd Allah, Ubayy, Zayd, and Abu Musa."],[531,"Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, whose kunya was Abu al-Mundhir, died in Madinah in the year twenty-two, though one says in the year thirty, during the caliphate of 'Uthman ؓ."],[532,"Ibn Numayr, and some of them say, “during the caliphate of Uthman ؓ.”"],[533,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of the son of Adam has been set as a parable for this world. Consider what comes out of the son of Adam, even if he seasons it and salts it, he knows what it becomes.”"],[534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see a man expressing grief with the grief of Jahiliyyah, then rebuke him and do not use kunyah.”"],[535,"The last verse revealed to the Prophet ﷺ was {There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves} to the end of the verse."],[536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wishes that a building be raised for him and that his rank be elevated, let him pardon those who wrong him, and give to those who deprive him, and maintain ties with those who cut him off.”"],[537,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at the watering place of Banu Ghifar and said, “O Muhammad, Allah ﷻ commands you to teach your community the Quran in one mode.” Then he said, “In two modes,” until he reached seven modes. So whoever recites any one of them, it is as he said."],[538,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say concerning {And He bound them to the word of God-consciousness}, “There is no god but Allah.”"],[539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes to reveal a mountain of gold, for which nine-tenths of them will fight.”"],[540,"The verdict that water (bath) is necessary when there is emission given by the people (in the early days of Islam) was due to the concession granted by the Messenger of Allah in the beginning of Islam. He then commanded to take a bath (in such a case). Abu Dawud said : By Abu Ghassan is meant Muhammad b. mutarrif. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 215)"],[541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abu al-Mundhir, I have been commanded to present the Quran to you.” Ubayy said, “In Allah I have believed, at your hand I have submitted, and from you I have learned.” He said, so the Prophet ﷺ repeated the statement, “O Messenger of Allah, and I was mentioned there?” He said, “Yes, by your name and lineage in the highest assembly.” He said, “Then recite, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[542,"He said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever?” He said, “Good deeds continue to flow for its bearer as long as a foot twitches or a vein throbs.” Ubayy said, “O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me from going out in Your path, nor from going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet.” He said, and from then on Ubayy was never without fever."],[543,"He had a store of dates that was decreasing, so he guarded it one night and found an animal resembling a young man who had reached puberty. He greeted it and it returned the greeting. He said, “Are you a jinn or a human?” It said, “No, rather a jinn.” He said, “Then give me your hand.” It gave him its hand, and its hand was like a dog’s paw and its hair was like a dog’s hair. He said, “This is how the jinn are created.” It said, “The jinn know that there is no man among them stronger than me.” He said, “Then what brought you here?” It said, “It reached us that you love charity, so we came to get some of your food.” He said, “Then what protects us from you?” It said, “This verse in Surat al-Baqarah: {Allah—there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer}. Whoever says it in the evening is protected from us until morning, and whoever says it in the morning is protected from us until evening.” When morning came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, “The evil one told the truth.”"],[544,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If a human being had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of a human being except dust. Then Allah ﷻ turns in mercy to those who repent.”"],[545,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, \"Whoever attains his parents or one of them and then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him.\""],[546,"From Ibn 'Umarah al-Ansari, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed in his house facing both qiblahs. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may I wipe over the leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes, for a day.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and two days?\" He said, \"Yes, and three.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and three?\" He said, \"Yes, and as long as you wish.\""],[547,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in his house. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may I wipe over the leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"For a day?\" He said, \"Yes, and two days.\" He said: I said, \"And three, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes, and as much as appears to you.\""],[548,"From 'Urwah concerning those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge: Usayd b. Hudayr b. Simak b. 'Ubayd b. Rafi' b. Imri' al-Qays b. Zayd b. 'Abd al-Ashhal, and he was a naqib (leader)."],[549,"\"Usayd b. Hudayr died, whose kunyah was Abu Yahya, in the year twenty, and 'Umar ؓ carried him between the two posts of the bier until he placed him in al-Baqi' and prayed over him.\""],[550,"\"Usayd b. Hudayr died in the year twenty, in Sha'ban.\""],[551,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar from Banu Sa'idah: Usayd b. Yarbu'."],[552,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal: Usayd b. Hudayr, and he was a naqib (leader)."],[553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will see after me selfishness (atharah).\" They said, \"What do you command us?\" He said, \"Be patient until you meet me at the Hawd (basin).\""],[554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. People will increase, but they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.\""],[555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. People will increase, but they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.\""],[556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Ansar are my inner circle and my trusted confidants. People will increase, but they will decrease, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.\""],[557,"From his mother Fatimah bt. Husayn ؓ, from 'A'ishah ؓ, that she said: Usayd b. Hudayr was among the most virtuous of people, and he used to say: If I could always be as I am in any one of three states, I would be of the people of Paradise, and I have no doubt about that: when I recite the Qur'an, or when I listen to it being recited, and when I hear a sermon of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when I attend a funeral. And I have never attended a funeral but that I told myself nothing except what is done to it and what it is becoming."],[558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that if you find it with a man who is not suspected, then if its master wishes he may take it for the price, and if he wishes he may pursue its thief. Then Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman ؓ ruled accordingly after him. Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah sent to Marwan: You are not the one to pass judgment against me, nor is Usayd, in what I have been entrusted with. Rather, I pass judgment upon you two, so carry out what I have commanded you. So Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter to me, and I said: By God, I will never rule by it."],[559,"While he was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he had jest in him, he was telling people things to make them laugh. The Messenger of God ﷺ poked him in his side, so he said: Let me get even with you. He said: Get even. He said: You are wearing a shirt and I am not wearing a shirt. So the Messenger of God ﷺ lifted his shirt, and he embraced him and began kissing his flank, saying: I only wanted this, O Messenger of God."],[560,"A man was making people laugh in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ pointed with his finger at his side. He said: You have killed me, O Messenger of God. He said: Retaliate. He said: You are wearing a shirt and I was not wearing a shirt. So the Messenger of God ﷺ lifted his shirt until his flank showed, and he embraced him and began kissing his flank, saying: May my father and mother be your ransom; this is what I wanted."],[561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution with the meat of camels.\""],[562,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Pray in sheep pens, and do not perform wudu' from their milk, and do not pray at camel resting places, and perform wudu' from their milk.'"],[563,"\"He was reading Surah Al-Baqarah while his horse was tied.\""],[564,"When something like a cloud covered me, in which there were things like lamps, while a woman was sleeping beside me and she was pregnant, and a horse was tied in the house, I feared that the horse would bolt and the woman would be startled and miscarry her child. So I stopped my prayer, and I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning, and he said: 'Recite it, O Usayd, for that was an angel who listened to the Qur'an.'"],[565,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, last night I was reciting Surat al-Kahf when something came and covered my mouth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'That was the Sakinah; it came to listen to the Qur'an.'"],[566,"I was praying on a moonlit night, and I had tied up my horse, and it moved suddenly, and I was startled. Then it moved again, and I raised my head, and there was a canopy that had covered me, and it had come between me and the moon, and I was startled, so I entered the house. In the morning I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Those were the angels; they came to listen to your recitation of the Qur'an at the end of the night: Surat al-Baqarah.' And Usayd had a beautiful voice."],[567,"He said: O Messenger of God, while I was reciting Surat al-Baqarah, I heard a thud behind me, and I thought my horse had been set loose. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Recite it, O Abu 'Atik.' He said: I turned around, and there were lamps hanging between heaven and earth, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was saying: 'Recite it, O Abu 'Atik.' He said: O Messenger of God, I could not continue. He said: 'Those were the angels who descended for the recitation of Surat al-Baqarah. Indeed, if you had continued, you would have seen wonders.'"],[568,"The people of two households from my people came to me and said: Speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ for us, that he may distribute to us from these dates. So I went to him and spoke to him, and he said: 'Yes, we will distribute to each household a half, and if God gives us more, we will give them more.' I said: May God reward you well on our behalf. He said: 'And you, may God reward you well on my behalf, O company of the Ansar, for you are, as far as I know, chaste and patient. Indeed, you will meet after me preference being given to others, so be patient until you meet me.'"],[569,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God ﷺ considered Rafi' b. Khadij too young. His uncle Zuhayr, may God have mercy on him, said to him: O Messenger of God, he is a man who can shoot. So the Messenger of God ﷺ allowed him. Then an arrow struck him in his throat, and his uncle brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My brother's son has been struck by an arrow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If you wish, we will remove it, and if you wish, we will leave it; for if he dies while it is in him, he dies as a martyr.'"],[570,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A prayer in the mosque of Quba' is like an 'umrah.'"],[571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land."],[572,"From 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those killed on the Day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar from Banu Sa'idah: Usayd b. Yarbu'."],[573,"And in it [i.e., that year], Abu 'Amrah al-Mazini died in the year thirty-seven."],[574,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition he undertook. The people suffered severe hunger, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to slaughter some of their riding camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was about to grant them permission for that, when 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"Consider, O Messenger of Allah, if we slaughter our riding camels and then meet our enemy tomorrow while we are hungry and on foot?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you think, O 'Umar?\" He said: \"Call the people to bring the remnants of their provisions, then supplicate to Allah for us for blessing in them, for Allah ﷻ will surely suffice us through your supplication, if Allah wills.\" He said: \"It was as if a covering had been upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was removed.\" So he called for a cloth and ordered it to be spread. Then he called the people to bring the remnants of their provisions. They came with what they had; some people brought a large bowl of food or a handful, and some brought something like an egg. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered it to be placed on that cloth. Then he supplicated for blessing in it and spoke as Allah willed him to speak. Then he called out in the army, and they came. Then he ordered them, and they ate and were satisfied, and they filled their vessels and their provision bags. Then he called for a small water skin and placed it in front of him. Then he called for water and poured it into it. Then he spat into it and spoke as Allah willed him to speak. Then he inserted his little finger into it. I swear by Allah, I saw the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gushing forth springs of water. Then he ordered the people, and they drank and gave water to their mounts and filled their water skins and their water vessels. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars appeared. Then he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. No one meets Allah with these two on the Day of Resurrection except that he enters Paradise, no matter what he has done.\""],[575,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who believe in you but have not seen you, and affirm you but have not seen you? What will they have?\" He said: \"Blessedness be to them, twice. Those are of us, those are with us.\""],[576,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar: Abu Salit Usayr b. 'Amr."],[577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys, and the cooking pots were boiling, so we overturned them."],[578,"The people suffered severe hunger during the Battle of Khaybar, so they went to their donkeys in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and slaughtered them, then threw the meat into cooking pots. While they were boiling, the prohibition of them came down upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prohibition of the donkeys you are cooking has come down,\" so the pots were overturned."],[579,"The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against eating the flesh of donkeys came to us while the cooking pots were boiling with them, so we overturned them."],[580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs the full ritual bath on Friday, and goes early and arrives early, and draws near to the imam and listens attentively, he will have for every step he takes the reward of fasting for a year and standing in prayer for a year, and that is easy for Allah.\""],[581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs the full ritual bath and goes early and arrives early, then sits close to the imam and listens and remains silent, he will have for every step he takes the reward of a year's fasting and standing in prayer.\""],[582,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ that he said on Friday: “Whoever bathes and washes himself, comes early, draws near and listens, for every step he takes from his house to the mosque he will have the reward of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[583,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then goes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, and does not engage in idle talk, a year’s deeds will be written for him.” Ibn Jabir said: I narrated this hadith to Yahya b. al-Harith al-Dhimari, and he said: I heard Abu al-Ash‘ath narrate it from Aws b. Aws from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he said: “For every step he will have the deeds of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.” Ibn Jabir said: “Yahya remembered and I forgot.” Al-Walid said: I mentioned that to Abu ‘Amr al-Awza‘i, and he said: “The hadith is established that for every step he will have the deeds of a year.”"],[584,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then comes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, draws near and listens, and does not engage in idle talk, for every step he takes he will have the deeds of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself, goes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, draws near to the imam, and does not engage in idle talk, he will have the reward of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[586,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ he said: “When Friday comes, and one of you washes his head and bathes, then goes early and arrives early, draws near, listens, and remains silent, for every step he takes he will have a year of fasting and a year of standing in prayer.”"],[587,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then goes early or leaves or arrives early, then draws near, remains silent, and listens, for the measure of every step he takes he will have like the reward of standing in prayer for a year and fasting for a year.”"],[588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the best of your days is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it the trumpet will be blown, and on it the blast will occur. So increase your prayers upon me on it, for your prayers are presented to me.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our prayers be presented to you when you have decayed? He said: He says: “You have become worn out.” He said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.”"],[589,"\"Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, 'Jesus, son of Mary, will descend near the white minaret to the east of Damascus.'\""],[590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever lies about his Prophet, or about his own eyes, or about his parents will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[591,"I heard Aws b. Aws al-Thaqafi say: I came to the Prophet ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif. He said: I was at the lower part of the qiblah, in which there was no one except the Prophet ﷺ sleeping, when a man came to him and whispered to him. Then he said: “Go and kill him.” Then he said: “Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me, except by its right.”"],[592,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while we were in a tent in the mosque of Madinah. He took hold of something from the tent, and a man came to him and whispered something that could not be known what he said. Then he said: “Go and tell them to kill him.” Then he said: “Perhaps he testifies that there is no god but Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Go and tell them to release him, for I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me, except by a rightful matter, and their reckoning is with Allah ﷻ.”"],[593,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while his hair was disheveled and I was listening. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Go to them and say to them, 'Kill him.' Then, he called him back after he had left and said, 'Perhaps he will say, 'There is no god but Allah.' \" The man said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Tell them to release him, for I have been commanded to fight against people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth become inviolable to me, except for its right, and their account is with Allah.\""],[594,"He informed him, saying: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was narrating to us and reminding us, when a man came to him and whispered to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Go and kill him.” When the man turned away, he called him and said: “Does he testify that there is no god but Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Take him and let him go, for I have only been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they do that, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.”"],[595,"“We stayed with the Prophet ﷺ for half a month. I saw him turn to his right and I saw him turn to his left, and I saw his sandals had two straps.”"],[596,"I stayed with the Prophet ﷺ for half a month and saw him praying while wearing two unlined sandals, and I saw him spit to his right and to his left."],[597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: While I was sitting, Jibril ﷺ came to me and carried me and entered me into the Garden of my Lord ﷻ. While I was sitting, an apple was placed in my hand, and the apple split into two halves, and out of it came a maiden the like of whose beauty I had never seen and the like of whose loveliness I had never seen. She was glorifying Allah with a glorification the like of which the first and the last had never heard. I said, 'Who are you, O maiden?' She said, 'I am from the hūr al-ʿīn. Allah ﷻ created me from the light of His Throne.' I said, 'For whom are you?' She said, 'For the wronged caliph, ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ.'"],[598,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a delegation of Thaqīf, and we were lodged with him in a tent of his. Our brothers from the allies lodged with al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us after the evening prayer and talk to us, and most of his talk was complaining about the Quraysh. He would say, 'It is not equal: we were in Makkah despised and oppressed, but when we came to Madinah, the war was alternately for us and against us.' One night he was late in coming to us and stayed away long, so we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you have been late.' He said, 'A portion of the Qur'an came upon me, and I disliked to go out until I had completed it.' We asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divide the Qur'an into portions?' They said, 'He divided it into threes, fives, sevens, nines, elevens, thirteens, and the portion of the Mufaṣṣal.'"],[599,"\"We arrived at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us every night and tell us stories. One night, he came to us later than usual, so we asked him, \"What's the matter with you?\" He replied, \"I received a portion of the Quran, and I wanted to finish it before I leave.\""],[600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man's recitation of the Qur'an without looking at the mushaf is a thousand degrees, and his recitation in the mushaf is multiplied over that up to two thousand degrees.'"],[601,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and asked for water to be poured over his hands three times. Shuʿbah said: He was an Arab man, so I said to him, 'What does istawkaf mean?' He said, 'He washed his hands three times.'"],[602,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come to a water outlet, meaning a purification place, and perform ablution and wipe over his feet."],[603,"He would say, 'Hand me my sandals,' and he would put them on and pray in his sandals. He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.'"],[604,"I saw my father wiping over the sandals. I said, 'Do you wipe over them?' He said, 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ do it.'"],[605,"We passed by some water of the Bedouins, and my father stood and urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his sandals. I said, 'Will you not take them off?' He said, 'I will not add to what I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[606,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his sandals.\""],[607,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his sandals, then stand for prayer."],[608,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in his sandals."],[609,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in his sandals."],[610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me, and with him was Abu Bakr ؓ, at Khadawat between al-Juhfah and Harsha, both of them on a single camel, heading to al-Madinah. Ibn al-Rida' mounted them on a stud camel of his, and he sent with them a servant of his called Mas'ud. He said to him: \"Take them by the hidden passes of the roads which you know, and do not leave them until they have fulfilled their need from you and from your camel.\" So he took them through Thaniyyat al-Zamha', then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Kubah, then he brought them to Ahya', then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then he brought them from the mountain pass of Dhat Kasht, then he took them through al-Mudlajah, then he took them through al-'Ishalah, then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then he brought them into al-Madinah, and they had fulfilled their need from him and from his camel. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mas'ud back to his master Aws b. 'Abd Allah. He was negligent, not branding the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to tell Aws to brand them on their necks with the mark of a horse's fetter.\" Sakhr b. Malik said: \"And it is, by Allah, our brand today. The fetter of a horse, as I see it, is two rings and a line drawn between them.\""],[611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Hadathan during the days of Tashriq, and they called out: \"None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.\""],[612,"From Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of whoever witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj, or Aws ibn al-Samit."],[613,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Give Zakat al-Fitr as a sa' of food.\" Our food that day was wheat, dates, and raisins. This is the wording of Zayd b. Akhzam. Sha'tham said: \"Our food that day was dates, raisins, and dried curd.\""],[614,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Asram b. Fihr b. Ghanm b. 'Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Aws b. al-Samit and his brother 'Ubadah."],[615,"One day he came in to me and spoke to me about something while he was somewhat irritable about it, so I answered him back. He said: \"You are to me like the back of my mother.\" Then he went out and sat in the gathering of his people. Then he returned to me and wanted me for himself, but I refused him. He struggled with me and I struggled with him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said: \"No, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach it until Allah judges between me and you with His judgment.\" So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining to him of what I had suffered from him. He said: \"Your husband and your cousin? Fear Allah.\" And Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah has indeed heard the statement of the woman who pleads with you concerning her husband} up to the mention of the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tell him to free a slave.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no slave to free.\" He said: \"Then let him fast two consecutive months.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he is not capable of fasting.\" He said: \"Then let him feed sixty poor people.\" She said: \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing to feed them with.\" He said: \"We will help him with a basket of dates.\" A basket holds thirty sa's. I said: \"And I will help him with another basket.\" He said: \"You have done well. Tell him to give it in charity.\""],[616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When it is the day of Fitr, the angels stand at the gates of the roads and call out: 'Go forth, O assembly of Muslims, to a Generous Lord who bestows good and then rewards abundantly for it. You were commanded to pray at night and you prayed; you were commanded to fast during the day and you fasted; you obeyed your Lord, so receive your prizes.' When they have prayed, a caller announces: 'Indeed your Lord has forgiven you, so return rightly guided to your mounts.' It is the day of prizes, and that day is called in heaven the Day of Prizes.\""],[617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When it is the morning of Fitr, the angels stand at the mouths of the roads and call out: 'O assembly of Muslims, go forth to a Merciful Lord who bestows good and rewards abundantly for it. You were commanded to fast during the day and you fasted; you obeyed your Lord, so receive your prizes.' When they have prayed the Eid prayer, a caller from heaven announces: 'Return to your homes rightly guided; I have forgiven all your sins.' That day is called in heaven the Day of Prizes.\""],[618,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever walks with an oppressor to help him, knowing that he is an oppressor, has left Islam.\""],[619,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever drinks wine, flog him. If he repeats—he said it three times—on the fourth, kill him.\""],[620,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah: Aws b. Mu'adh b. Aws al-Ansari.\""],[621,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Aws b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir, who had no surviving offspring."],[622,"Ali b. Abi Talib, al-Fadl and Qutham the two sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended into the burial niche of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Abu Layla Aws b. Khawli said to Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, \"I adjure you by Allah and by our share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Ali ؓ said, \"Descend,\" and he descended."],[623,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Aws b. Mu'adh b. Aws, no offspring for him."],[624,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who witnessed al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar, and who witnessed Badr: Aws b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir, a Badri."],[625,"From Urwah regarding naming those of the Ansar who were martyred on the day of Uhud, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. al-Mundhir."],[626,"About Ibn Shihab's account of the names of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr among the Ansar, then from the Banu Auf bin Al-Khazraj, Aws bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Khauliy."],[627,"\"Those who descended into the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were al-Fadl, Qutham, Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Aws b. Khawli.\""],[628,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, and Aishah and Hafsah were with him, Ali ؓ entered. When he saw him, he raised his head and said, \"Draw near to me.\" So he leaned against him and remained with him until he ﷺ passed away. When he died, Ali ؓ rose and locked the door. Al-Abbas ؓ came with the Banu Abd al-Muttalib and stood at the door. Ali ؓ began to say, \"May my father be ransomed for you, pure in life and pure in death.\" A sweet fragrance spread that they had never smelled the like of before. Ali ؓ said, \"Let al-Fadl b. Abbas enter to me.\" The Ansar said, \"We adjure you by Allah concerning our share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So they brought in a man from among them called Aws b. Khawli, carrying a water jar in one of his hands. They heard a voice in the house: \"Do not strip the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; wash him as he is in his shirt.\" So Ali ؓ washed him, inserting his hand beneath the shirt while al-Fadl held the cloth away from him, and the Ansari poured the water. On Ali's ؓ hand there was a cloth, and he inserted his hand."],[629,"It is said: Sulaym Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Daws. Muhammad b. Ishaq mentioned him among those who witnessed Badr."],[630,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. Yazid b. Asram."],[631,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. Thabit."],[632,"From Urwah regarding naming those of Quraysh who were killed at Ajnadayn, then from the Banu Abd Shams b. Abd Manaf: Aban b. Sa'id b. al-As."],[633,"\"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ abolished every blood claim that existed in the time of ignorance.\""],[634,"From Aban al-Muharibi, who was one of the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Abd al-Qays, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no servant who says in the morning, 'Praise belongs to Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' except that he remains forgiven of his sins until evening. And if he says it in the evening, he passes the night forgiven of his sins until morning.\""],[635,"Madaan had a dispute with a man over some land, and they brought the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. He ruled that one of them should take an oath. The other said, \"Will he take away my land?\" He said, \"If he swears by Allah falsely,\" Ibn Awn said, \"he said something severe.\""],[636,"A man from Kindah and a man from Hadramawt brought a dispute before the Prophet ﷺ concerning a piece of land in Yemen. The Hadrami said, 'O Messenger of God, it is my land; this man's father usurped it from me.' He said to the Kindi, 'What do you say?' He said, 'I say it is my land, in my possession; I inherited it from my father.' He said to the Hadrami, 'Do you have any proof?' He said, 'No, but let him swear, O Messenger of God, by the One besides whom there is no god, that he does not know it is my land which his father usurped.' The Kindi prepared to take the oath, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'No man seizes property but that he will meet God ﷻ on the Day of Resurrection with it as a leper.' So the Kindi returned it."],[637,"A man of the Hadramis disputed with a man of ours called al-Hafshish before the Prophet ﷺ concerning a piece of land belonging to the latter. The Prophet ﷺ said to the Hadrami, 'Bring your witnesses to prove your right; otherwise, he will swear to you.' He said, 'My land is too great a matter for him not to swear concerning it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The oath of a Muslim stands behind what is greater than that.' He went to swear, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'If he swears falsely, God ﷻ will admit him to the Fire.' Al-Ash'ath went and informed him, and he said, 'Make peace between me and him.' So he made peace between them."],[638,"I once bought my oath for seventy thousand, because I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim by an oath will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him.'"],[639,"In this verse, it was revealed to me that I had a piece of land in the possession of my paternal uncle. So, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"Do you want me to arbitrate or shall I uphold his oath?\" I said, \"If he has taken an oath, then you should arbitrate, O Messenger of Allah.\" So, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes an oath, while he is still a sinner and uses it to wrongfully take the wealth of a Muslim, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\" So, Allah revealed the verse: \"Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their [own] oaths for a small price...\" until the end of the verse."],[640,"This verse was revealed concerning me. I had a dispute with a man before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...}"],[641,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever swears a patient oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim will meet God while He is angry with him.' Then al-Ash'ath entered and said, 'What did Abu 'Abd al-Rahman tell you?' We said, 'Such and such.' He said, 'It was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over some land of ours. I brought the case to the Prophet ﷺ, but I had no proof. He said, \"Shall I make him swear?\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, then he will swear.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever swears an oath to seize thereby the property of a person while he is lying in it will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him.\" And the verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...} to the end of the verse."],[642,"This verse was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over some property or land. I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, 'Do you have proof?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Then your opponent will be made to swear.' I said, 'Then he will swear.' So this verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...} to the end of the verse."],[643,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Whoever swears a patient oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him, whether He pardons him or punishes him.'"],[644,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ in a group from Kindah, and they did not consider me the best of them. I said, 'O Messenger of God, we claim that you are one of us.' He said, 'No, we are Banu al-Nadr b. Kinanah; we do not follow our mother nor disown our father.' Al-Ash'ath b. Qays said, 'O Prophet of God, I will not hear anyone deny that Quraysh is from Kinanah except that I will flog him.'"],[645,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ among the delegation of Kindah. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you have any children?' He said, 'None except a newborn who was born when I set out to you. I would wish that in his place the people had been filled.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not say that, for in them is joy for the eyes and reward when they die. And if you say that, they are indeed a cause of cowardice, grief, and stinginess.'"],[646,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'A child was born to me from the daughter of Jamd b. Wali'ah al-Kindi. I wished that in his place we had a bowl of tharid.' He said, 'Indeed, children are a cause of stinginess, cowardice, and grief.'"],[647,"Regarding the first fighting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against the polytheists: \"If Allah lets me witness it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah will surely see what I do.\" When the day of Uhud came, he met the polytheists and the people were defeated. He said, \"O Allah, I seek excuse to You for what these—meaning the Muslims—have done, and I declare my innocence to You from what those—meaning the polytheists—have brought.\" Then he took the sword and met Saʿd b. Muʿadh. He said, \"O Saʿd, I truly find the scent of Paradise before Uhud.\" He went on and was killed. He was not recognized until his sister identified him by the beauty of his fingertips. He had eighty-some wounds from spear thrusts, sword strikes, and arrow shots."],[648,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred from the Ansar on the day of the Trench: Anas b. Muʿadh b. Aws b. ʿAbd ʿAmr."],[649,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred from the Ansar on the day of the Bridge, then from the Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Anas b. Aws."],[650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The most grateful of you to God ﷻ is the most grateful of you to people.'"],[651,"And he said: 'By God, I have not disbelieved; rather, this man married me to his sister. If we were in our own land, we would have had a wedding feast other than this. O people of Madinah, slaughter and eat; and O owners of camels, come and take its equivalent.'"],[652,"I had a debt owed to me by a man from Kindah, and I used to frequent him before dawn. The Fajr prayer overtook me in the mosque of al-Ash'ath, so I prayed. When the imam said the salam, he placed before every person a fine garment, a pair of sandals, and five hundred dirhams. I said, 'I am not one of the people of the mosque.' He said, 'Even if you are not one of the people of the mosque?' I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'Al-Ash'ath b. Qays has arrived from Makkah.'\""],[653,"\"What do you have to do with him, O Ash'ath? By Allah, if you were to wrestle with the servant of Thaqif, the little hairs of your buttocks would stand on end.\" It was said to him, \"O Commander of the Believers, and who is the servant of Thaqif?\" He said, \"A young man who will rule over them; he will not leave any household of the Arabs but he will bring them humiliation.\" It was said, \"How long will he reign?\" He said, \"Twenty years, if he reaches that.\""],[654,"Muhammad b. Sallam said: Nobility is only counted from a short time before the Prophet ﷺ to the era of the Prophet ﷺ and continued in Islam. The house of Yemen that is in the courtyard near the honor, in Kindah, is al-Ash'ath b. Qays; its horseman among the Banu Zubayd is 'Amr b. Ma'dikarib; and its poet Imru' al-Qays, from Kindah; there is no disagreement about this."],[655,"\"Have you prevented me because of these two, O Commander of the Believers? You know that their companion came to us and filled us with lies,\" meaning 'Ali. Ibn 'Abbas said, \"Do you think I will insult you because of Ibn Abi Talib?\" He said, \"No Arab better than me has been insulted.\" Ibn 'Abbas said, \"The servant of Mahrah killed your grandfather and stabbed your father in the buttocks.\" He said, \"Do you not hear what he says to me, O Commander of the Believers?\" He said, \"You began it.\""],[656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Hamzah."],[657,"I asked Anas b. Malik, saying, 'O Abu Hamzah...'"],[658,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a kunya when I was a young boy.\" He said, \"And he gave me a kunya because of a herb I used to gather.\""],[659,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik with a white head and beard; he dyed his head with henna.\""],[660,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ dyeing with henna.\""],[661,"\"Anas b. Malik used to dye his beard yellow with wars.\""],[662,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ dyeing with red.\""],[663,"And he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me.\""],[664,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, “O you with two ears.”"],[665,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to me, “O you with two ears.”"],[666,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ touching his forearms with perfume made from whiteness that was on him."],[667,"I saw Anas b. Malik wearing a dark-colored silk-blend jubba, a dark silk-blend cloak, and a black turban with a hanging end behind him, dyeing with yellow."],[668,"I saw on Anas b. Malik a yellow silk-blend garment."],[669,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ with his sons carrying him around the House on their arms, and they had fastened his teeth with gold."],[670,"He saw Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah, ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ, Abu Usayd al-Badri, Rafiʿ b. Khadij, and Anas b. Malik ؓ trimming their moustaches closely like shaving and letting their beards grow, and plucking their armpits."],[671,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ leaning on a staff with a silver ferrule on its top."],[672,"I accompanied my grandfather Anas b. Malik for thirty years and never saw him drink nabidh at all."],[673,"Anas' wine was sweet, causing the lips to stick together."],[674,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ drinking tila' (reduced grape juice)."],[675,"Anas b. Malik had a servant who prepared fine delicate dishes for him, cooked two kinds of food, baked white bread for him, and kneaded it with clarified butter."],[676,"When Anas b. Malik completed the Quran, he would gather his family and children and supplicate for them."],[677,"He resolved to fast before his death for a year, so he broke it and fed a poor person each day."],[678,"\"I performed Hajj with Anas b. Malik, and I saw him stop saying the talbiyah when he descended from the mountain pass when he saw the houses of Makkah.\""],[679,"Anas used to hasten breaking the fast and not wait for the call to prayer."],[680,"And we heard him reciting: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\"."],[681,"Anas used to sit and a bed was laid for him to sit on. He would hold his son between his hands and play with him. One day, he came out while we were playing and said, \"O my sons! How bad what you throw is!\" Then he took something and threw it, and it did not miss the target."],[682,"We approached with Anas from Kufah until when we were at Uthth, morning came while the ground was mud and water, and he prayed the prescribed prayer on his mount. Then he said, \"I never prayed the prescribed prayer on my mount before today.\""],[683,"I went out with Anas to the land of Baythaq Sirin until when we were at the Tigris, the noon prayer arrived, \"and he led us sitting on a mat in the boat while the boat was pulling us along strongly.\""],[684,"He stayed with Anas in Naysabur for two years, and he used to pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."],[685,"\"He saw Anas b. Malik going between Safa and Marwah on a donkey.\""],[686,"that the imam should pray."],[687,"about his sons the slaughtered camel."],[688,"\"Anas used to wipe over the socks.\""],[689,"from his side, and open the gates of heaven for his soul, and replace for him a home better than his home."],[690,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik prostrating on his turban.\""],[691,"\"That Anas had loudly pronounced during noon or afternoon prayer and did not prostrate.\""],[692,"\"I saw Anas ibn Malik volunteering to travel.\""],[693,"That I should die on my bed — by Allah, that will never be. Allah has tried me, and I have killed a hundred of the polytheists, some of whom I killed alone and some of whom I shared in killing.\""],[694,"Anas said to him: \"Remember Allah, my brother.\" So he sat up straight and said: \"O Anas, do you think I would die on my bed when I have killed a hundred polytheists in single combat, besides those whose killing I shared in?\""],[695,"\"I stayed with Anas b. Malik for two months and he never performed qunut in the dawn prayer.\""],[696,"and on his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[697,"\"I gave Anas b. Malik walking medicine.\""],[698,"\"Anas b. Malik used to pass by us, and we were women, but he did not greet us.\""],[699,"\"This is a place where permission is not sought.\""],[700,"\"He was a governor over Naysabur, and a dihqan brought him khabis in a silver vessel, but he disliked it and returned it to him. Then he transferred it and came again with it, and he ate it.\""],[701,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — we heard it from him, but we would not lie to one another.\""],[702,"Anas ؓ said to us: \"Bind knowledge with writing.\""],[703,"that he would not leave it night or day, so Anas made peace among them for every day and night at six."],[704,"to bathe at midday and at nightfall.\""],[705,"I entered the house of Abu Talhah while he had locked the door on Umm Sulaym and was beating her, and she is the mother of Anas. I called out from behind the door, \"What do you want with this old woman that you beat her?\" She called out to me from behind the door and said, \"You call me an old woman? May Allah weaken your support.\""],[706,"Al-Hajjaj: It is you I mean; may Allah make your hearing deaf. Anas ؓ sought return (said: \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return\"), then went out from him and said, \"Had I not remembered my children and feared for them, I would have spoken to him in my place with words after which he would never respond to me again.\""],[707,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty years old.\""],[708,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[709,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[710,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[711,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for seven years.\""],[712,"Umm Sulaym: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for Anas. He said, \"O Allah, increase his wealth and children and bless him in it.\" Anas said, \"I have indeed buried from my loins, apart from my grandchildren, one hundred and twenty-five, and my land yields fruit twice a year, and there is nothing in the town that yields fruit twice other than it.\""],[713,"A'ishah: \"What knowledge do Abu Sa'id and Anas have of the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They were only two young boys.\""],[714,"\"I had a lock of hair, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pull it and take hold of it.\""],[715,"I heard Anas b. Malik say, \"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was eight years old.\" Yazid said, \"This shaykh Hammad b. Salamah directed me to this.\""],[716,"I washed Anas b. Malik, and when I reached his private area, I said to his sons, \"You are more entitled to wash his private area. Here, you wash it.\" The one who washed it put a cloth on his hand, and over it was a garment. Then he washed the private area from beneath the garment."],[717,"\"Anas b. Malik died, and in his embalming perfume was placed a small amount of sukk or musk containing sweat of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[718,"The last of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to die in Kufa was Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, and in Basra Anas b. Malik."],[719,"Anas b. Malik died in the year ninety-three."],[720,"In the year ninety."],[721,"Muwarriq al-Ijli said: \"Today half of knowledge has gone.\" It was said: \"And how is that, O Abu al-Mu'tamir?\" He said: \"When a man of the people of whims differed with us about a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would say to him, 'Come to someone who heard it from him.'\""],[722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do good throughout your entire life, and expose yourselves to the breezes of Allah's mercy, for Allah has breezes of His mercy with which He touches whom He wills of His servants. And ask Allah to conceal your faults and to secure your fears.\""],[723,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appoint as miqat for the people of the garrison towns al-Aqiq, for the people of Basra Dhat Irq, for the people of Madinah Dhul-Hulayfah, and for the people of Sham al-Juhfah."],[724,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"An Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj with me.\""],[725,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.\""],[726,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are three things that if a person possesses, he has tasted the sweetness of faith: to love nothing more than Allah, to love being thrown into the fire more than turning back on his religion, and to love for the sake of Allah and to hate for the sake of Allah.\""],[727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in a house, and each one of us moved back from his seat so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might sit next to him. He stood at the door and said: \"The leaders are from Quraysh, and they have a right, and I have a right over them as long as they do three things: if they judge, they are just; if they make a covenant, they fulfill it; and if they are asked for mercy, they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[728,"The Prophet ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still completing it."],[729,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would stand up immediately upon giving the greeting of peace. Then I prayed with Abu Bakr ؓ, and when he gave the greeting of peace, he would spring up as if he were rising from a hot stone."],[730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Helpers, and he made brothers of Sa'd b. al-Rabi' and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. Sa'd said to him: \"I have wealth, so it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them you like, and I will divorce her, and when her waiting period is over, marry her.\" He said: \"I have no need of your wealth or your family; show me the market.\" So he went, then returned with dates and dried curd, having profited. He came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces of yellow perfume on him, and the Prophet said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I have married a woman from the Helpers.\" He said: \"What did you give her as a dowry?\" He said: \"The weight of a date stone of gold, or a date stone of gold.\" He said: \"Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep.\""],[731,"I attended a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that had no bread and no meat. I said: What was it then, O Abu Hamza? He said: Barley porridge and dates."],[732,"A bird was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he placed it before him and said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me. Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ came and knocked on the door. I said: Who is it? He said: I am Ali. I said: The Prophet ﷺ is occupied. So he went back. He came three times, each time coming back like that. Then he struck the door with his foot and entered. The Prophet ﷺ said: What kept you? He said: I came three times, and each time it was said: The Prophet ﷺ is occupied. The Prophet ﷺ said: What made you do that? I said: I wanted it to be a man from my people."],[733,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and put his eye to a gap in a hut. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and aimed at him with a stick or an iron tool to pierce his eye with it. When the Bedouin saw the Prophet ﷺ, he withdrew. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Indeed, had you remained, I would have pierced your eye."],[734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Madinah will shake three times, and every hypocrite and disbeliever will leave it."],[735,"There is no ruqya except for the evil eye, or a fever, or blood that does not stop."],[736,"The most beloved fragrance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was faghiya."],[737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the children of the children of the Ansar, and the daughters-in-law and the neighbors."],[738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not enter upon women, even if they are daughters-in-law. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the brother-in-law? He said: The brother-in-law is death."],[739,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered the pots on the day of Khaybar to be overturned because of donkey meat."],[740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Quran is a richness with no poverty after it, and there is no richness without it."],[741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' silently, and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ did the same."],[742,"\"O Messenger of Allah! Can I go out with you for battle?\" Umm Salamah said. He replied, \"O Umm Salamah, it is not required for women to engage in warfare.\" She responded, \"But I will take care of the wounded, treat the sick, and provide water.\" He said, \"Indeed, that would be excellent.\""],[743,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Four things are not attained except with wonder: patience, which is the first form of worship; humility; remembrance of Allah; and having little."],[744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prayer of one sitting is equivalent to half the prayer of one standing.\""],[745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was sent and the Hour are like these two.\""],[746,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: \"Jibril ﷺ took out his entrails in a golden basin and washed them, then packed them with wisdom and light, or wisdom and knowledge.\""],[747,"Zainab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ passed away, so we went out with him and saw Rasul Allah ﷺ extremely saddened and distressed. We did not speak to him until we reached the grave. He had not finished burying her yet, so Rasul Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat around him. He sighed and looked up at the sky for a moment, then he finished burying her. Rasul Allah ﷺ descended into the grave, and I saw him becoming even more sorrowful. Then he finished and came out, and I saw him relieved and smiling ﷺ . We said, \"O Rasul Allah, we saw you deeply saddened and distressed, and we could not speak to you, but then we saw you relieved and smiling. Why is that?\" He said, \"I remembered the narrowness, darkness, and weakness of the grave, and it caused me difficulty because of Zainab. So I supplicated to Allah to ease her burden, and He did. He made her grave narrow, and only jinn and humans can hear its constriction.\""],[748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the call to prayer is given in a town, Allah grants it safety from His punishment on that day.\""],[749,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday between the afternoon prayer and the setting of the sun, and it is about this much,\" indicating a handful."],[750,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father died without performing Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"What if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would that settle it for him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community.\""],[752,"Fatimah ؓ brought a piece of bread to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is this?\" She said: \"A loaf I baked, and I was not comfortable until I brought you this piece.\" He said: \"This is the first food that has entered your father's mouth in three days.\""],[753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He does not believe in me who goes to bed full while his neighbor next to him is hungry, and he knows it.\""],[754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in building mosques.\""],[755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him before his death.\""],[756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A servant may, through good character, reach the highest ranks of the Hereafter and the noblest stations, even though he is weak in worship; and through bad character he may reach the lowest level of Hell.\""],[757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a woman performs ghusl after her menstruation, she should undo her hair and wash it with marshmallow and potash. And when she performs ghusl after janabah, she should pour water over her head and wring it.\""],[758,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom.\""],[759,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command giving gifts as a means of connection between people, and he would say: \"If people were to embrace submission, they would exchange gifts without hunger.\""],[760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Jibril ﷺ comes to me in the form of Dihyah al-Kalbi.\" Anas said: \"Dihyah was a handsome, fair-skinned man.\""],[761,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: \"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\""],[762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you.\""],[763,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Set prices for us, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the rise and fall of your prices is in the hand of Allah, may He be exalted. I hope to meet Allah, may He be exalted, while none of you has a grievance against me concerning wealth or blood.\""],[764,"I arrived to the Prophet ﷺ from a journey, and the Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Have lunch.\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Shall I inform you about the traveler? Indeed, Allah has relieved him of fasting and half of the prayer.\""],[765,"He arrived in Madinah and entered upon the Prophet ﷺ for a need of his, and found the Prophet ﷺ eating. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Come close.\" The man said: \"I am fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of fasting and half of the prayer, and likewise the pregnant and the nursing woman.\""],[766,"Abu Qilabah said to me: \"He is alive, so meet him and hear the hadith from him.\" Ayyub said: \"I met al-Amiri, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out cavalry, and they raided the camels of a neighbor of ours and took them away. So he set out regarding that—either my father said, or my paternal uncle, or he said a close relative of his—and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. He said: I came to him while he was eating, and he said: 'Come to lunch.' I said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'Come, and I will tell you about that. Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, has relieved the traveler of fasting and half of the prayer, and likewise the pregnant woman'—or he said 'the nursing woman.' And he ordered the camels, and they were returned. And whenever he narrated this hadith, he would lament and say: 'Would that I had eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[767,"Cavalry belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided us, so I went to him while he was eating. He said: \"Sit and eat from this food of ours.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am fasting.\" He said: \"Sit, and I will tell you about prayer and fasting. Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of half—or half of the prayer—and has relieved the traveler, the sick, and the pregnant woman of fasting.\" By Allah, he said all of them or one of them. So I reproached myself for not having eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[768,"Cavalry belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided us, so I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was eating. He said: \"Sit and eat from our food.\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Sit, and I will tell you about prayer and fasting. Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of half the prayer, and has relieved the traveler and the nursing woman of fasting.\" So I reproached myself for not having eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[769,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Come.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Come, let me tell you: Allah has relieved the traveler of the fast and half of the prayer.\""],[770,"His paternal aunt, al-Rubayyiʿ bt. al-Nadr, slapped a girl and broke her tooth. They offered them compensation, but they refused; they sought pardon, but they refused. So they came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered them to exact retaliation. Her brother Anas b. al-Nadr came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will the tooth of al-Rubayyiʿ be broken? No, by the One who sent you with the truth, her tooth shall not be broken.\" He said, \"O Anas, the Book of Allah prescribes retaliation.\" The people then pardoned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Among Allah's servants are those who, if they swore by Allah, He would fulfill their oath.\""],[771,"Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah narrated to him that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar. He mentioned the hadith—its completion is to be written in the chapter of Sīn, under Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah; and in the chapter of Zāy, under Zayd b. Rāfiʿ, the story of stoning."],[772,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in naming those who were killed on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from the Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then from Banu Zaʿuraʾ: Aws b. ʿAtīk b. ʿĀmir."],[773,"The first thing that called me to Islam was that we were a group of Arabs, and then affliction struck us. I carried my mother"],[774,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who were killed on the day of the Bridge of al-Madaʾin from the Ansar, from the Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu Zaʿuraʾ: Unays b. ʿAtīk b. ʿĀmir."],[775,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from the Banu ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Najjār, then from the Banu Qays b. ʿUbayd b. Zayd b. Muʿāwiyah b. ʿAmr b. Mālik: Unays b. Muʿādh b. Qays."],[776,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from the Banu Zurayq: Unays b. Qatādah."],[777,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws: Unays b. Qatādah."],[778,"His freed slave used to seek permission for him—meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[779,"From 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[780,"From Ibn Shihāb, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[781,"From Iyās b. 'Abd al-Muzanī, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of water.\""],[782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not strike the female servants of Allah.\" So they stopped striking them. Then 'Umar came and said: \"By Allah, the women have become defiant toward their husbands.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they strike them. Then many women came to the family of Muhammad ﷺ, and when morning came he said: \"Seventy women came to the family of Muhammad last night, all of them complaining of the beating. By Allah, I do not think those are among the best of you.\""],[783,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Nabit: Iyas b. Aws."],[784,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim b. 'Awf: Iyas b. Wadhqah."],[785,"“He had a ringworm on his face – meaning qawba' – and I disliked his nose.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and wiped his face, and on that day it was not touched and there was no trace of it."],[786,"Ahmar b. Jaz', a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to us. He said: “We used to seek shelter for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from what kept his hand away from his sides when he prostrated.”"],[787,"A captive was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “O God, I repent to You, but I do not repent to Muhammad.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “He has acknowledged the truth for its people.”"],[788,"I came to the Prophet of God ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of God, I composed poetry in which I praised God ﷻ and praised you.” He said, “As for what you praised God with, bring it; and as for what you praised me with, leave it.” So I began to recite, and a tall, aquiline-nosed man entered, and he said to me, “Stop.” When he left, he said, “Go on.” So I resumed reciting, and before long he returned, and he said to me, “Stop.” When he left, he said, “Go on.” I said, “Who is this who entered, O Prophet of God, that you said ‘Stop,’ and when he left you said ‘Go on’?” He said, “This is Umar b. al-Khattab, and he has nothing to do with falsehood.”"],[789,"“No. My father and my uncle witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but God. So if you bring me proof of immunity from the Fire, I will fight with you.” He said, “Go, for we have no need of you.” Ayman said, “...”"],[790,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of water.\""],[791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not strike the female servants of Allah.\" He said: So the women became defiant and their behavior toward their husbands worsened. 'Umar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the women have become defiant and their behavior toward their husbands has worsened since you forbade striking them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Then strike them.\" So the people struck their wives that night, and many women came complaining of the beating. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seventy women came to the family of Muhammad ﷺ last night, all of them complaining of the beating. By Allah, you will not find those among the best of you.\""],[792,"Al-Qa'nabī and Ibrāhīm b. Bashshār al-Ramādī narrated to us, saying: Sufyān b. 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from 'Abd Allāh b. 'Abd Allāh b. 'Umar, from Iyās b. 'Abd Allāh, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not strike the female servants of Allah.\" Then 'Umar ؓ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the women have become defiant toward their husbands since you forbade striking them.\" So he permitted them, and they struck them. Then many women came to the family of Muhammad ﷺ — seventy women, each one complaining about her husband — and you will not find those among the best of you."],[793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There must be some prayer at night, even if it be the milking of a camel or the milking of a ewe. Whatever is after the late night prayer ('Ishā') is part of the night.\""],[794,"I left the mosque and suddenly there was a man wearing white clothes, a shirt and a cloak. He said to me: \"Your grandfather Abū Umāmah b. Tha'labah informed me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'Humbleness in dress is part of faith, humbleness in dress is part of faith, humbleness in dress is part of faith.'\""],[795,"We were in a gathering discussing worldly matters when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: \"Humbleness in dress is part of faith,\" three times."],[796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Humbleness in dress is part of faith, humbleness in dress is part of faith.\""],[797,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \"Humbleness in dress is part of faith,\" meaning austerity."],[798,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed them about marching out to Badr and he resolved to march out with him.” His maternal uncle Abu Burdah b. Niyar said to him, “Stay with your mother, O son of my sister.” Abu Umamah said, “Rather, you stay with your sister.” That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, “so he commanded Abu Umamah to stay with his mother, and he set out with Abu Burdah. Then the Prophet ﷺ arrived while she had died, and he prayed over her.”"],[799,"Abdullah b. al-Munib b. Abdullah b. Abi Umamah al-Balawi—whose name was Iyas b. Tha'labah, and he had been a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—narrated to us, from his grandfather Abdullah b. Abi Umamah, from his father, who said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution from [a vessel licked by] a dog, and that we should not harm one another.”"],[800,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sit in the qurfusa' position.”"],[801,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes as allies other than his rightful patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him. Whoever swears a false oath by this pulpit of mine to seize the property of a Muslim unjustly, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory act will be accepted from him. Whoever introduces an innovation in this city of mine or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him either an obligatory or a supererogatory act.”"],[802,"That he heard Abu Umamah b. Tha'labah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: “Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim man by his [false] oath, Allah has made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise to him.” A man said, “Even if it is something insignificant, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Even if it is a stick of arak.”"],[803,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim man by his [false] oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him.” They said, “Even if it is something insignificant, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Even if it is a stick of arak.” He said it three times."],[804,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever seizes by his oath the right of a Muslim man, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and made the Fire obligatory for him.” A man stood and said, “Even if it is something insignificant?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Even if it is a stick of arak.”"],[805,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No man seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him.” A man from the people said, “Even if it is insignificant, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Even if it is a toothstick of arak.”"],[806,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No man seizes the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him.” A man from the people said, “O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something insignificant?” He said, “Even if it is a toothstick of arak.”"],[807,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever wrongfully takes the wealth of a Muslim by lying, it will be a black spot in his heart that cannot be changed until the Day of Judgment.\""],[808,"From 'Urwah, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu Mu'awiyah b. 'Awf: Iyas b. Aws."],[809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of them and came to them and sat with them and said, “Would you like something better than what you came for?” They said, “And what is that?” He said, “I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sent me to the servants to call them to worship Him and not associate anything with Him, and Allah sent down the Book to me.” Then he began to teach them Islam and recited the Qur'an to them. Iyas b. Mu'adh, who was a young boy, said, “O my people, this, by Allah, is better than what you came for.” He said: Then Abu al-Haysar Anas b. Rafi' took a handful of pebbles from the ground and threw it in the face of Iyas and said, “Leave us alone, for by my life we have come for something other than this.” He said: Iyas fell silent, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and left them, and they returned to Madinah. Then the Battle of Bu'ath took place between the Aws and the Khazraj. Then Iyas b. Mu'adh did not remain long before he died. Mahmud b. Labid said: “One of his people who was present at his death informed me that they kept hearing him declaring the oneness of Allah, magnifying Him, praising Him, and glorifying Him until he died. They had no doubt that he had died a Muslim. He had embraced Islam in that gathering when he heard what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[810,"He spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the sadaqah when he came to him as a delegate in Madinah, and he said, “O brother of Saba', there must be a sadaqah.” He said, “We only grew cotton, O Messenger of Allah. Saba' has scattered, and none remain of them except a few in Ma'rib.” So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ made a peace agreement with Abyad b. Hammal for seventy suits of the finest value of the Ma'afir garments every year on behalf of those who remained of Saba' in Ma'rib, and they continued to pay it until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died."],[811,"The workers revolted against them when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken by death regarding what \"Salih Abiad ibn Hammal, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the seventy ornaments\" had decided. Abu Bakr affirmed what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had established until Abu Bakr died, and when Abu Bakr died, that was revoked and became the responsibility of charity."],[812,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to grant him the salt that is called Shadda in Ma'rib, and he granted it to him. Then al-Aqra' b. Habis al-Tamimi said, “O Prophet of Allah, I came to the salt in the Jahiliyyah, and it is in a land where whoever comes to it takes it, and it is like standing water.” He said: So the Prophet ﷺ asked Abyad b. Hammal to revoke his grant. Abyad said, “I have revoked it from him on condition that you make it sadaqah from me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is sadaqah from you, and it is like standing water: whoever comes to it takes it.” He said: So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ granted him land and pasture in al-Jawf, the Jawf of Murad, in its place when he revoked it from him. And he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the protected area of the arak tree. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no protected area in the arak.” He said, “An arak tree in my enclosure.” He said, “There is no protected area in the arak.” Faraj said: “Meaning, Abyad, in my enclosure is the land that contains the crops and is surrounded by it.”"],[813,"He came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ to request the salt, and he granted it to him. A man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you have granted him? You have granted him standing water.” So he took it back from him. I asked him about what may be protected of the arak. He said, “What the hooves of camels do not reach.”"],[814,"He came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, and he granted him the salt. When he turned away, a man said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you have granted him? You have only granted him standing water.” He said: So he took it back. He said: I asked him about what may be protected of the arak. He said, “What the hooves of camels do not reach.”"],[815,"He came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for the salt that is in Ma'rib, and he granted it to him. A man said, “Do you know, O Messenger of Allah, what you have granted him? You have granted him standing water.” He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it back from me. He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what may be protected of the arak. He said, “What the hooves of camels do not reach may be protected.”"],[816,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and gave him the oath of allegiance, and he said, “Whoever gets to something that no Muslim has gotten to before, it is his.” So the people went out racing and drawing lines."],[817,"He informed him that his father al-Aswad attended the Prophet ﷺ while the people were giving him the oath of allegiance at Qarn Masqalah. He said: Qarn Masqalah is next to the houses of Abu Thumamah, and it is what faces the house of Ibn 'Amir and what is behind it toward the house of Ibn Samurah and its surroundings. Al-Aswad said: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ taking the oath of allegiance from the people. Men, women, young, and old came to him and gave him the oath of allegiance on Islam and the shahadah.” I said: And what is the shahadah? Muhammad b. al-Aswad informed me, he said: “On the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.”"],[818,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to renew the boundary markers of the Haram in the year of the conquest.”"],[819,"He brought some fat camels to Madinah at a time of drought and barrenness of the land. When the people of Madinah saw them, they marveled at their fatness. I mentioned that to the Messenger ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for them, and they were brought to him. He went out to them and looked at them and said, “Why did you bring these camels of yours?” He said, “I wanted a servant for them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who has a servant?” Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ said, “I have one, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Bring her.” So Uthman brought her. When Aswad saw her, he said, “I want one like her.” He said, “You have her, so take her.” So Aswad took her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received his camels. Then Aswad said, “O Messenger of Allah, give me advice.” He said, “Do you control your tongue?” He said, “What do I control if I do not control it?” He said, “Do you control your hand?” He said, “What do I control if I do not control my hand?” He said, “Do not say with your tongue anything but good, and do not extend your hand to anything but good.”"],[820,"I said: O Messenger of God, give me advice. He said: \"Do you control your hand?\" I said: What do I control if I do not control my hand? He said: \"Do you control your tongue?\" He said: Then what do I control if I do not control my tongue? He said: \"Do not extend your hand except toward good, and do not say with your tongue except what is right.\""],[821,"I was reciting poetry to him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, and I did not recognize his companions until a man came who was broad between the shoulders, bald. It was said to me: Be quiet, be quiet. I said: O my bereavement! Who is this for whom I should be quiet in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ? It was said: He is Umar b. al-Khattab. By God, I knew thereafter that it would have been easy for him, had he heard me, not to speak to me until he took hold of my foot and dragged me to al-Baqi."],[822,"I was a poet and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, shall I recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Exalted is He? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask me for more."],[823,"\"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask him for more than that."],[824,"O Prophet of God, shall I let you hear praises with which I praised my Lord? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise, or there is nothing more beloved to Him than praise from God, Exalted is He.\""],[825,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have praised my Lord with praises. He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask him to recite."],[826,"O Messenger of God, shall I recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Exalted is He? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask me for more."],[827,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I praised you with praises. He said: \"Indeed, God, Exalted is He, loves to be praised.\" And he did not ask him to recite."],[828,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a military expedition and it was reported to him that they killed the children of the polytheists. When the Prophet ﷺ received this news, he said, \"What is the matter with people who reach the point of killing the children of the polytheists?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah! And he mentioned a statement after that.\" He ﷺ said, \"Isn't it your best among you the children of the polytheists? By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, no newborn is born but upon the natural disposition until his parents make him Jewish or Christian.\""],[829,"When they killed the offspring, the Prophet ﷺ was informed about it. He said, \"Are not the best of you those who are born to the polytheists? Every newborn is born on the fitrah (natural inclination towards Islam) until his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian.\""],[830,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Every child is born upon Fitrah (innate goodness), until his language expresses something else. His parents raise him as a Jew or a Christian.\""],[831,"\"I participated in a battle alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he achieved victory over our enemies. Some people started killing infants, and when the Prophet ﷺ was informed about this, he said, 'What has happened to people that they have gone so far as to kill children?' Then a man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, they are the sons of the idolaters.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'The best among you are the children of the idolaters. Do not kill children, for every child is born on the natural disposition (fitrah) until his tongue expresses it. His parents make him Jewish or Christian'.\""],[832,"\"We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and killing continued until they killed the offspring. When the Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, he said, 'What is the matter with people who have killed the offspring?' A man said, 'Are they not the children of the polytheists?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Are not the best of you those who were born from the polytheists, and then their parents made them Jews, Christians, or Magians?' (This is the wording of the hadith narrated by Al-Muqaddimiy)\""],[833,"About Aswad ibn Sari'a, they fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and encountered the enemy, killing them until they reached the women and children. They asked the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Every child is born on Al-Fitrah (the natural inclination towards monotheism), and it is his parents who convert him to Judaism or Christianity.\""],[834,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sent a detachment and they killed the children. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , asked them, \"What is the matter with the children?\" They replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, are they not from their fathers?\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Are not the best of you those who are born to polytheists? Indeed, every newborn child is born on the natural inclination (fitrah) until their tongue expresses it.\""],[835,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, every child is born upon the Fitrah (natural inclination), and it is only his parents who turn him into a Jew or a Christian or a Magian.\""],[836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and they encountered the enemy and engaged in fighting until they reached the children. When the expedition returned, they informed the Prophet ﷺ about what happened. He asked them, \"Didn't they tire you?\" They replied, \"They were the children of the polytheists.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Are not the best among you those who are born to polytheists?\" Then he called for a crier and announced, \"Indeed, every newborn is born on the fitrah (natural inclination towards monotheism).\""],[837,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ hastened in killing until it reached killing children. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian.\""],[838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No one loves praise more than God, Exalted is He, and no one makes more excuses than God, Exalted is He.\""],[839,"When Uthman b. Maz'un died, the Muslims feared for him. When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, he said: \"He has been joined to our righteous predecessor, Uthman b. Maz'un.\""],[840,"It was said: O Messenger of God, who is in Paradise? He said: \"The prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn is in Paradise.\""],[841,"A captive was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “I repent to God, but I do not repent to Muhammad.” He said, “He has acknowledged the truth for its people.”"],[842,"On the Day of Resurrection, there will be four types of people who will present their excuses. The first is a deaf person who cannot hear, and he will say, \"O Lord, I came and the children threw me with stones.\" The second is a foolish person who lacks understanding, and he will say, \"Certainly Islam came, but I did not comprehend.\" The third is an old person who will say, \"Indeed, Islam came, but my mind failed to grasp it.\" And the fourth is a person who died during the interval between the messengers, and he will say, \"O Lord, Your messenger did not come to me, nor did he take their covenants, so that I may follow them.\" Then a messenger will be sent to them, instructing them to enter the Fire. But by the One in Whose hand is my soul, if they enter it, it will be a cool and peaceful place for them."],[843,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I praised God with one praise and I praised you with one praise.” He said, “Bring it, and begin with praise of God.”"],[844,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from the Khazraj, from Banu Salama: Aswad b. Zayd b. Tha'laba b. Ghanm."],[845,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Hunayn: Ayman b. Ubayd."],[846,"Sa'd said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, “I saw Ayman while he was fleeing from the fighting,” and I recognized dislike in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Sa'd said, “I said, ‘I have not seen a speech farther from every good.’” Then after that they were on the verge of fighting, and Sa'd said, “I saw Ayman, the most obstinate of the people, and that pleased the Prophet ﷺ.” He said: And Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said to Ayman, “I have been told that you do not stand between the two ranks out of cowardice.” He said, “I hope to stand in a station that God and His Messenger love.” Umar said, “You are worthy to do that.”"],[847,"Ayman was in charge of the Prophet's ﷺ ablution water and his sandals, and he would hand him what he needed."],[848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The minimum for which the thief's hand is cut off is the price of a shield.” He said: It used to be valued at a dinar."],[849,"Hands were cut off in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ for the price of a shield."],[850,"My father and my uncle witnessed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and they commanded me not to fight. Then he recited, saying..."],[851,"From his paternal uncle, Umayyah b. Makhshiyy, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting while a man was eating. The man did not pronounce Allah's name until only one morsel of his food remained. He said, \"In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and then said, \"The devil kept eating with you, and when you mentioned Allah's name, he vomited what was in his belly.\""],[852,"\"Umayyah b. 'Abd Allāh b. Khālid b. Usayd led us in prayer in Khurasan, and he recited these two sūrahs: 'Indeed, we seek Your help and Your forgiveness.'\" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth."],[853,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turn away from his left side toward his house when he gave the greeting of peace."],[854,"We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is swift in fighting.' He said, 'He is in the Fire.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so, with his worship, effort, and gentle manner, is in the Fire, then where are we?' He said, 'That is the humility of hypocrisy, and he is in the Fire.' He said: We used to watch him in battle: no horseman or foot soldier passed by him but he would leap upon him, and his wounds multiplied. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has been martyred.' He said, 'He is in the Fire.' When the pain of his wounds became severe, he took his sword, placed it between his breasts, and leaned on it until it came out through his back. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise, yet he is among the people of the Fire, and a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire, yet he is among the people of Paradise. Wretchedness or happiness overtakes him at the departure of his soul, and he is sealed with it.'"],[855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath.'"],[856,"I was saddling the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was afflicted by major ritual impurity on a cold night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to depart, and I disliked saddling his camel while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and I feared that if I bathed with cold water I would die or become ill. So I ordered a man from the Ansar to saddle it, and I placed stones and heated water with them, then bathed. Then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. He said, 'O Asla', why do I see that your saddle has changed?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not saddle it; a man from the Ansar saddled it.' He said, 'Why?' I said, 'I was afflicted by major ritual impurity, and I feared the cold for myself, so I ordered him to saddle it. I placed stones and heated water with them, and bathed with it.' Then Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated} until {Indeed, Allah is ever Pardoning and Forgiving}."],[857,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have woken up and have not performed the Witr prayer.\" The Prophet replied, \"Verily, Witr is performed at night.\" The man persisted and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have woken up and have not performed the Witr prayer.\" The Prophet said, \"Then, perform the Witr prayer.\""],[858,"From 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Qarabūs b. Ghanm b. Sālim: Umayyah b. Lawdhān b. Sālim b. Thābit b. Hazzāl b. 'Amr b. Qarabūs b. Ghanm."],[859,"In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end. So I asked him about that and he said, \"My grandfather, Umayyah ibn Makhshiyya, narrated to me that he was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ . There was a man who used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ but he would not mention the name of Allah before eating. Then, when he was in the last morsel, he would say, 'In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The devil was eating with him until he mentioned the name of Allah at the beginning and at the end, and then the devil vomited out everything he had eaten.'\""],[860,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ sent him as a spy to Quraysh. I came to the wood of Khubayb while I was wary of being seen. I climbed upon it and untied him, and he fell to the ground. I left him not far away, then I turned around and could not see the wood of Khubayb—it was as if the earth had swallowed it. No trace of Khubayb has been mentioned until now.\""],[861,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek victory through the poor among the Muhājirūn.\""],[862,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek victory through the poor among the Muhājirūn.\""],[863,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek victory and help through the poor among the Muslims.\""],[864,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he granted me al-Ghamīm, stipulating for me and for the wayfarer the first watering. He granted Sā'idah, a man from among us, a well in the desert called al-Ja'ūniyyah—a well in which water is stored, and it is not sweet water. And he granted Iyās b. Qatādah al-'Anazī al-Jābiyah, which is on this side of al-Yamāmah. We had all come to him together, and he wrote for each one of us that grant on leather."],[865,"\"Do not shroud me in a sewn garment.\" So when he died and was washed, they sent to me, saying, \"Send the shroud.\" I sent them the shroud. They said, \"A shirt?\" I said, \"My father forbade me to shroud him in a sewn shirt.\" So I sent to the fuller—my father had a shirt with the fuller. It was brought and put on him, and he was taken away. I locked my door and followed him. When I returned, the shirt was in the house. I sent to those who had washed my father and asked, \"Did you shroud him in a shirt?\" They said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Is this it?\" They said, \"Yes.\""],[866,"\"Will you not come out and help me against these people?\" He said, \"Yes, if you wish. O girl, hand me the sword.\" She handed him the sword, and he placed it in his lap. Then he drew part of it and said, \"My close friend and your cousin ﷺ commanded me, when there is fighting between two tribes of the Muslims, to make a sword of wood.\" He drew part of it while it was in his lap and said, \"If you wish, I will go out with you with this.\" He said, \"I have no need of you.\""],[867,"My close friend—meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—advised me, saying: \"There will be tribulation and division. When that happens, break your sword and make a sword of wood.\" And when he became gravely ill, he commanded his family to shroud him but not to put a shirt on him. We put a shirt on him, and in the morning the shirt was on the clothes rack."],[868,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When you see two men of my community fighting over wealth, then prepare a sword of wood.\""],[869,"When Ali ؓ came to Basra, he came to us at the house and said, 'Is Abu Muslim here?' We said, 'Yes.' He came out to him, and Ali said to him, 'Will you not help us in this matter?' He said, 'Yes. O slave girl, bring me that sword.' She brought his sword, and he unsheathed it, and it was a sword of wood. Abu Muslim said to him, 'Your cousin, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, enjoined upon me that if there is a trial among the Muslims, I should take a sword of wood.' Ali turned away angry and said, 'We have no need of you or your sword.' Yazid b. Zuray' said: Yunus b. Ubayd narrated this hadith to me from this shaykh before I met him."],[870,"That Ali ؓ came to her father, stood at the door, asked permission to enter, and said, 'O Abu Muslim, what prevents you from striving in this matter and taking your share of it?' He said, 'What prevents me from that is a covenant which my close friend and your cousin ﷺ made with me: \"He commanded me that if tribulation occurs, I should take a sword of wood.\" Here it is with me, so if you wish, I will fight with it.'"],[871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see differences among my companions. If you live to that day, make your sword from palm branches.' He said: So I made my sword from palm branches. Then Ali ؓ came to me, grasped the two side-posts of the door, then gave the greeting of peace and said, 'O Uhban, will you not come out?' I said, 'By my father and mother, O Abu al-Hasan, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me' or 'commanded me' or 'enjoined me' or 'instructed me' – Ibn Zahdam was uncertain – and he said: 'O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see differences among my companions. If you live to that day, make your sword from palm branches.' So I brought out my sword to him, and Ali ؓ turned away."],[872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on the day of Ashura and said, 'Go to your people and command them to fast this day.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not think I will reach them until they have eaten.' He said, 'Command whoever among them has eaten to fast the rest of his day.'"],[873,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ placing his hand, I think, on his thigh, pointing with his finger during the tashahhud."],[874,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have purchased a slave, so pray to Allah for blessing for him and name him.' He said, 'What is your name?' He said, 'Asram.' He said, 'Rather, you are Zur'ah.' He said, 'What do you want him to be?' He said, 'A farmer.' He said, 'Then he is Asim.'"],[875,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ and saddle his mount. One night he said to me, 'O Asla', get up and saddle the mount.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been afflicted by major ritual impurity.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him with the verse of tayammum. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum.' He said: So I got up and performed tayammum, then saddled the mount for him. He traveled until he passed by some water and said to me, 'O Asla', touch – or 'touch this' – your skin.' He said: My father showed me how to perform tayammum just as his father showed him: 'One strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.'"],[876,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, 'O Asla', get up and show me how such-and-such is done.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been afflicted by major ritual impurity.' He remained silent for a while until Jibril ﷺ came to him with tayammum using earth. He said, 'Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum.' He said: Then he showed me, Asla', how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him tayammum. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the earth with both palms, then shook them off, then wiped his face with them until they passed over his beard, then returned them to the earth and wiped the earth with his palms, rubbing one with the other, then shook them off, then wiped his forearms, both their outer and inner sides."],[877,"He called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from behind the chambers, saying, “O Muhammad, my praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace.” He said, “That is Allah, exalted be He.”"],[878,"He informed him that al-Agharr, a man from Muzaynah who had companionship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, had several wasqs of dates owed by a man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. He went back and forth to him several times. He said, “So I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ with me.” He said, “Everyone we met greeted us with salam, so Abu Bakr ؓ said, ‘Do I not see people greeting you first, so the reward is theirs? So greet them first, and the reward will be yours.’”"],[879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ordered a portion of dates for me from a man among the Ansar, but he delayed paying me. So I spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Go early with him, O Abu Bakr, and take his dates for him.” Abu Bakr ؓ promised to meet me at the mosque after we prayed the dawn prayer. I found him where he had promised, and we set off. Whenever a man saw Abu Bakr from afar, he greeted him. Abu Bakr said, “Do you not see what reward the people earn because of you? Let no one beat you to the greeting.” So whenever a man appeared, we hurried to greet him before he greeted us.”"],[880,"From al-Agharr, one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited Surah al-Rum."],[881,"He narrated to us from al-Agharr, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that he heard the Prophet say, “Indeed I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times a day.”"],[882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O people, repent to your Lord, for by Allah, I repent to my Lord one hundred times a day.”"],[883,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “O people, repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day.”"],[884,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “O people, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for I seek forgiveness and repent to Him one hundred times a day, or every day, or more than once.”"],[885,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, so that I seek forgiveness one hundred times a day.”"],[886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, and I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times every day.”"],[887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, and I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times.”"],[888,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from Banu Sa'idah: As'ad b. Harithah b. Lawdhan."],[889,"\"O my son, the happiest person who ever joined us in the city before the Prophet's arrival was during the defeat of a group from the Banu Bayadha tribe in the valleys of Naki'in. I asked, 'How many of you were there then?' He said, 'We were forty men.'\""],[890,"The first person to pray al-Duha was a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ known as Abu al-Zawa'id."],[891,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: As'ad b. Zayd b. al-Fakih b. Zayd b. Khalda b. Amir b. Ajlan."],[892,"In the year one, Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah died; the quinsy seized him while the mosque was being built."],[893,"As'ad b. Zurarah was one of the Naqibs on the night of al-Aqabah."],[894,"Abu Umamah was afflicted with a pain that the people of Madinah call quinsy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I shall strive or excuse myself concerning Abu Umamah.\" He said, \"So he cauterized him with his own hand, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'An evil death for the Jews. They will say: Why did he not protect his companion? I possess no power for him or for myself from Allah.'\""],[895,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah, and he was a Naqib."],[896,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ relates that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to al-Dahhak b. Qays to give inheritance to the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi from the blood money of her husband."],[897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever wishes for Allah to shade him on the day when there is no shade except His shade, then let him ease the difficulty of someone in hardship, or help someone in need.\""],[898,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: As'ad b. Salamah."],[899,"I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Nu'mayr say, \"Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf died in the year one hundred.\""],[900,"I was tending sheep at al-Qa' in Namira, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alight there. He established the prayer and prayed with his companions, and I prayed with them. It was as if I could see the whiteness beneath the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was prostrating."],[901,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraysh, then from Banu Makhzum b. Nuqta b. Murra b. Ka'b: al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam. The name of Abu al-Arqam was Abd Manaf, and he was called Abu Khindif b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Makhzum."],[902,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam."],[903,"From his grandfather al-Arqam, who was a Badri. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took shelter in his house near al-Safa until forty men had become Muslims, the last of them to accept Islam being Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. When they reached forty, they went out to the polytheists. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to bid him farewell, intending to go to Jerusalem. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Where do you intend to go?\" I said, \"I intend to go to Jerusalem.\" He said, \"What takes you there? Is it for trade?\" I said, \"No, but I wish to pray there.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers there.\""],[904,"On the authority of his father al-Arqam, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who steps over people’s necks on Friday and separates them is like one dragging his own intestines into the Fire.”"],[905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr: “Put aside whatever spoils you have taken.”"],[906,"“Aslam, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died after the killing of ʿUthmān ؓ in the year thirty-five.”"],[907,"The name of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was Aslam."],[908,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the call to prayer in the ear of al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ when they were born, and he commanded it. The wording is that of al-Himmani."],[909,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub b. Muhammad b. Tahla' narrated to us from Abu al-Rijal from Salim b. 'Abd Allah from Abu Rafi', who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to kill dogs. I went out killing every dog I met until I came to al-'Asiyya. There was a dog around a house. I moved toward it to kill it, and a woman from the house called out to me: 'What do you want?' I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to kill dogs.' She said: 'Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that I am a woman whose sight has gone, and it alerts me to those who approach and drives away wild beasts from me.' So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: 'Go back and kill it.' So I went back and killed it."],[910,"A book fell into my hands containing the opening supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he would say: 'I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With that I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. Glory be to You and praise. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. No partner has You. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins except You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' Then he would recite."],[911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever washes a dead body and conceals its faults, forty major sins will be forgiven for him. Whoever digs a grave for his brother until he buries him, it is as if he has given him a dwelling until he is resurrected.'"],[912,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, who said: \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ being brought a shoulder, and he ate it, then prayed without touching a drop of water.\""],[913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the middle of the night to supplicate at al-Baqi', and Abu Rafi' was with him. He supplicated as Allah willed, then turned back and passed by a grave. He said, \"Uff, uff, uff.\" Abu Rafi' said to him, \"O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. No one is with you except me, so did you say 'uff' because of me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but I said 'uff' because of the occupant of this grave who was asked about me and doubted me.\""],[914,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Baqi' al-Gharqad, walking behind him, he suddenly said, 'You are not guided, you are not guided.' Abu Rafi' said: I turned around but saw no one. I said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the matter with me?' He said, 'I do not mean you; rather I mean the occupant of this grave. He is being asked about me and he claims that he does not know me.' Then there was a grave that had been sprinkled with water when its occupant was buried."],[915,"\"I testify that I used to cook the sheep's belly for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he would eat from it and then pray without performing ablution.\""],[916,"'A sheep was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I roasted some of it. He ate from it, then stood and prayed without touching water.'"],[917,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to al-'Abbas: 'O uncle, shall I not maintain ties with you? Shall I not gift you? Shall I not benefit you?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Pray, O uncle, four rak'ahs. In each rak'ah recite the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation, say: Allahu akbar, wal-hamdu lillah, wa subhan Allah, wa la ilaha illa Allah – fifteen times before you bow. Then bow and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then stand up. That is seventy-five in each rak'ah and three hundred in four rak'ahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea, God would forgive you.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, who can say it every day?' He said, 'If you cannot pray it in a day, then pray it in a week.' Until he said, 'Pray it in a month.' Until he said, 'Pray it in a year.'"],[918,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Baqi' and said, 'Uff, uff, uff,' with no one with him except me. That alarmed me, so I said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom.' He said, 'The occupant of this grave – I appointed him over Banu so-and-so, and he betrayed a cloak. I was shown it upon him, blazing.'"],[919,"He saw Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, pass by Husayn b. Ali while Husayn was praying standing and had pinned his braid at the nape of his neck. Abu Rafi' untied it, and al-Husayn turned around angrily. Abu Rafi' said, 'Attend to your prayer and do not be angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"That is the devil's share\" – meaning the devil's seat, that is, the place where his braid was pinned.'"],[920,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali to Yemen and tied a banner for him. When he set off, he said, 'O Abu Rafi', catch up with him and do not leave him; let him stop and not turn around until I come to him.' He came to him and enjoined upon him several things, then said, 'O Ali, if Allah guides one man through your hands, it is better for you than all that the sun has risen upon.'"],[921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ, 'There will be an affair between you and A'ishah ؓ.' He said, 'Me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Me, from among my companions?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then I am the most wretched of them.' He said, 'No, but when that happens, return her to her place of safety.'"],[922,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, be one who raises dust and pours down [abundantly].'"],[923,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ at Mina speaking to the people, saying to them, 'Face the sandals.'"],[924,"We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits indecencies; should I report his matter to the ruler? He said, 'I killed ninety-nine polytheists in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it would not please me to kill the like of them in number if I had [instead] unveiled the private affair of a Muslim.'"],[925,"The Prophet ﷺ came to them in the company of the Muhajirun, and a man asked him, 'Which verse in the Quran is greatest?' The Prophet ﷺ said, '{Allah – there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep.}'"],[926,"On the authority of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I was a servant of al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. I had accepted Islam, Umm al-Faḍl had accepted Islam, and al-ʿAbbās had accepted Islam, but he concealed his Islam out of fear of his people. Abū Lahab had stayed behind from Badr and sent al-ʿĀṣ b. Hishām in his place, for he owed him a debt. He said to him: “Suffice for me in this campaign, and I will leave for you what you owe me.” So he did. When the news came and Allah humiliated Abū Lahab, I—being a weak man—was carving these wooden bowls in a chamber. By Allah, I was sitting in the chamber carving my bowls, with Umm al-Faḍl near me, when the wicked Abū Lahab came dragging his feet—I think he said—until he sat by the chamber’s rope, with his back to my back. The people said: “This is Abū Sufyān b. al-Ḥārith.” Abū Lahab said: “Come to me, O son of my brother.” Abū Sufyān came and sat with him, and the people came and stood over them. He said: “O son of my brother, how were the affairs of the people?” He replied: “Nothing, by Allah. It was only that when we met them, we offered them our shoulders; they killed us as they wished and took us captive as they wished. By Allah, I do not blame the people.” He said: “And why?” He replied: “I saw white men on piebald horses—by Allah, nothing withstands them, and nothing can stand before them.” He said: I raised the chamber’s rope and said: “Those, by Allah, are the angels.” Abū Lahab raised his hand and slapped my face. I sprang at him, but he overpowered me and threw me to the ground, then he got on top of me. Umm al-Faḍl stood up, tucked up her garment, took a pillar from the chamber’s pillars, and struck him with it, splitting open a severe wound in his head. She said: “O enemy of Allah, have you deemed him weak because you saw his master absent from him?” He rose humiliated. By Allah, he lived only seven nights until Allah struck him with the ‘adasa (plague) and it killed him. His two sons left him for two or three nights without burying him until he stank. A man of Quraysh said to his two sons: “Are you not ashamed? Your father has stunk in his house.” They replied: “We fear this ulcer—’al-‘adasa’—for Quraysh used to fear the ‘adasa’ as they feared the plague.” A man said: “Go, and I will be with you.” He said: By Allah, they did not wash him except by throwing water on him from a distance. Then they carried him and threw him to the top of Makkah against a wall, and threw stones upon him."],[927,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Zayd b. Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ b. Yasār, from Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed a young camel. Then the camels of zakāh came to him. Abū Rāfiʿ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to repay the man his young camel. I went and found nothing among the camels but excellent mature camels, a six-year-old. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give it to him, for the best of Muslims are the best of them in repaying.”"],[928,"the Prophet ﷺ asked a man to give as a loan a young camel and said: “When the camels of the Sadaqah come, we will pay you back.” When the camels came, he said: \" O Abu Rafi', pay this man back for his Young camel.\" But all I could find was a seven-year-old camel or that which is better. I told the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"Give it to him, for the best of People are those who are best in repaying.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2285)"],[929,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymūnah while in a state of iḥrām, and consummated the marriage with her while in a state of iḥrām, and I was the messenger between them.”"],[930,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not order me to halt there—meaning al-Abṭaḥ—but I pitched his tent, and he came and halted.” Sufyān said: ʿAmr b. Dīnār used to narrate this ḥadīth from Ṣāliḥ b. Kaysān. When he came to us, ʿAmr b. Dīnār said to us: “Go to this man and ask him about this ḥadīth.”"],[931,"When Fāṭimah gave birth to Ḥasan ؓ, she said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall I not offer an ʿaqīqah for my son?” He said: “No, but shave his head and give in charity the weight of his hair in silver”—or he said “in silver”—“to the poor.” When she gave birth to Ḥusayn, she did the same for him. Mūsā b. Dāwūd said in his ḥadīth: “to the destitute and the poor.”"],[932,"That she should offer an ʿaqīqah on his behalf with a great ram. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Do not offer an ʿaqīqah on his behalf with anything, but shave the hair of his head, then give in charity the weight of it in silver for the sake of Allah ﷻ to the destitute.” Then she gave birth to al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī ؓ the following year, and she did the same for him."],[933,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever guards what is between his two jaws and his two thighs will enter Paradise.”"],[934,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered a sacrifice, he would buy two fat, horned, black-and-white rams. After he had given the sermon and prayed, one of them would be brought to him while he was standing in his place of prayer, and he would slaughter it himself with a knife. Then he would say: “This is on behalf of my entire ummah—whoever bears witness to Your oneness and bears witness to my conveyance.” Then the other would be brought, and he would slaughter it himself. Then he would say: “O Allah, this is on behalf of Muḥammad and the family of Muḥammad.” He would give them all to the poor, and he and his family would eat from them."],[935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he offered a sacrifice, would bring two fat, horned, black-and-white rams that were valuable. When he had addressed the people, greeted, and finished, he would bring one of them while standing in his place of prayer and slaughter it himself. Then he would say: 'O Allah, this is on behalf of my community, those who bore witness to Your oneness and to my conveyance of the message.' Then the other would be brought, and he would slaughter it himself. Then he would say: 'O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' He and his family would eat from both, and he would feed both of them to the poor. We remained for years with no man of Banu Hashim offering a sacrifice, for Allah, Exalted is He, had sufficed them the burden through the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he intended to offer a sacrifice, would buy two horned, black-and-white rams. When he prayed and delivered the sermon, he would call for one of them while in his place of prayer and slaughter it. Then he would say: 'O Allah, this is on behalf of my entire community, those who bore witness to Your oneness and bore witness to my conveyance of the message.' Then he would bring the other and slaughter it. Then he would say: 'O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and his household.'"],[937,"The Prophet ﷺ offered as sacrifice two black-and-white, horned rams."],[938,"When the muezzin gave the call to prayer, the Prophet ﷺ would say as he said. When he said 'Hayya 'ala al-salah' (Come to prayer), he would say: 'There is no might and no power except with Allah.'"],[939,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that no religion other than the religion of Islam should be left in Madinah except that it be expelled."],[940,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'For Allah, Exalted is He, to guide through your hands a man is better for you than what the sun has risen and set upon.'"],[941,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the call to prayer in the ear of al-Hasan b. 'Ali when Fatimah ؓ gave birth to him."],[942,"From his father, who was a client of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Banu Makhzum to collect zakat. He said: 'Accompany me so that you may receive some of it.' I said: 'Wait until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So I came to him and asked him. He said: 'The client of a people is one of them, and indeed zakat is not lawful for us.'"],[943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Banu Makhzum to collect sadaqah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no sadaqah on less than five wasqs, no sadaqah on less than five camels, and no sadaqah on less than five uqiyahs.”"],[944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I should not find any one of you reclining on his couch and when an instruction comes to him from what I have commanded or forbidden, he says, ‘We do not know; whatever we find in the Book of Allah we follow.’”"],[945,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Abi ʿAmr, from ʿUbayd Allah ibn Abi Rafiʿ, from Abu Rafiʿ, who said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution three times, three times.” Al-Qaʿnabi added in his hadith: “and twice, and once.”"],[946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a glowing complexion, and joy was recognized in his face. He said: “I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said to me: ‘O Muhammad, do you know in what the highest assembly disputes?’ I said: ‘O Lord, in expiations.’ He said: ‘And what are expiations?’ I said: ‘Conveying ablution to its places despite dislikes, walking on foot to the prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.’”"],[947,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apply ithmid kohl while fasting.”"],[948,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed a scorpion while praying.”"],[949,"When ʿAli ؓ killed the standard-bearers on the day of Uhud, Jibril ﷺ said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is indeed consolation.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He is from me and I am from him.” Jibril said: “And I am from both of you, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[950,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.”"],[951,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to go out to the two Eids walking, and he would pray without an adhan or an iqamah, then return walking by another route.”"],[952,"“We slaughtered a young she-goat for the Prophet ﷺ and he ate, without performing ablution, without touching water, and without rinsing his mouth.”"],[953,"“I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a wooden spit and roasted it. He ate without rinsing his mouth and without performing ablution.”"],[954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAli on an expedition. When he returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Allah, His Messenger, and Jibril (peace be upon them) are pleased with you.”"],[955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Whoever loves him has loved me, whoever loves me has loved Allah, whoever hates him has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah.\""],[956,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, \"You and your followers will come to me at the Pool (of Kawthar) as radiant as pure white camels. Whereas, your enemies will come to me as disheveled and humiliated.\""],[957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Are you not pleased that you are my brother and I am your brother?\""],[958,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said to Ali, \"The first four who will enter Paradise are me, you, Hasan, and Husayn, and our descendants following our backs, and our spouses behind our descendants, and our Shia (followers) are from our faith and our traits.\""],[959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not that factions of my community would say concerning you what the Christians said concerning 'Isa ibn Maryam, I would say about you today a statement such that no Muslim would pass by you except that he would take the dust from the traces of your feet, seeking blessing thereby.\""],[960,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on Monday morning, Khadija ؓ prayed on Monday at the end of the day, and 'Ali prayed on Tuesday. 'Ali remained praying in concealment for seven years and some months before anyone else prayed."],[961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a place and said: \"What an excellent site for a bathhouse this is,\" so a bathhouse was built there."],[962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ammar ibn Yasir ؓ: \"The transgressing party will kill you.\""],[963,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sleeping or receiving revelation, and there was a snake in the side of the house. I disliked killing it and waking him, so I lay down between him and the snake, so that if anything happened it would be to me rather than him. He woke up while reciting this verse: {Your guardian is only Allah and His Messenger and those who believe} up to the end of the verse. He said: \"Praise be to Allah.\" Then he saw me beside him and said: \"What made you lie down here?\" I said: \"Because of this snake.\" He said: \"Get up to it and kill it.\" So I killed it, and he praised Allah. Then he took my hand and said: \"O Abu Rafi', there will be after me people who fight 'Ali; it is a duty upon Allah to fight them. Whoever cannot fight them with his hand, then with his tongue; whoever cannot with his tongue, then with his heart. There is nothing beyond that.\""],[964,"Ibrahim ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', the client of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Rafi': \"When the Prophet ﷺ performed his ablution for prayer, he would move his ring on his finger.\""],[965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered a ram and then said: \"This is on behalf of me and on behalf of my community.\""],[966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you's ear rings, let him remember me and invoke blessings upon me, and let him say: 'May Allah remember with good the one who remembered me.'\""],[967,"He said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a shoulder of a sheep and then pray without touching water.\""],[968,"Manbudh, a man from the family of Abu Rafi', narrated to me, from al-Fadl b. Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', who said: When the Prophet ﷺ prayed 'Asr, he would sometimes go to Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal and converse with them, and sometimes he would converse until Maghrib prayer. While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Maghrib prayer and he was hurrying, we passed by al-Baqi'. He said, \"Uff, uff, for you.\" I thought he meant me, so he said to me, \"Walk. What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, have I done something?\" He said, \"What is that?\" I said, \"You said 'uff' because of me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but this is the grave of so-and-so. I sent him as a collector for Banu So-and-so, and he stole a coat of mail. Now he has been made to wear the like of it from the Fire.\""],[969,"He informed him that he came with a letter from Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Islam was cast into my heart. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will never return to them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I do not break a covenant, nor do I detain messengers. But return, and if what is in your heart now remains, then come back.\" So I returned to them, then came back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accepted Islam."],[970,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kept handing me, you would continue handing me.\""],[971,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kept handing me, you would continue handing me.\""],[972,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Fa'id, the mawla of Ubayd Allah b. Ali b. Abi Rafi', narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Ali, from his grandfather, who said: \"I cooked the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ate from it, then prayed 'Isha' and did not perform wudu'.\""],[973,"I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg.\" He said, \"Eat it.\""],[974,"While the Prophet ﷺ was walking in Baqi' al-Gharqad and I was walking behind him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May you not be guided, may you not be guided,\" three times. Abu Rafi' said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with me?\" He said, \"It is not you I mean. I mean the occupant of this grave. He is asked about me and claims that he does not know me.\" And there was a grave upon which water had been sprinkled when its occupant was buried."],[975,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to roast a sheep for him. I roasted it for him. He said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how many forelegs does it have?\" He said, \"If you had remained silent, you would have found it as long as I called you.\""],[976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us and we had cooked mutton with us. He said, \"O Abu Rafi', give me the forearm.\" So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said, \"Give me the forearm.\" So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said, \"Give me the forearm.\" So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, does the mutton have anything other than two forearms?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you had remained silent, I would have continued to eat forearms as long as I wished.\""],[977,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us from this community that you commanded to be killed?\" meaning dogs. Then Allah, Mighty and Sublime, revealed: {They ask you what is lawful for them} the verse."],[978,"Gabriel came asking permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He gave him permission, but he delayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his cloak and stood up to him while he was standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We have given permission.\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\" Then they found a puppy in one of their houses. Abu Rafi' said: So he commanded me when morning came, and I did not leave in Madinah any dog except that I killed it. Then there was a woman far away who had a dog that barked at her. I felt compassion for her and left it, then came back. He commanded me, so I returned to the dog and killed it. The people said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us from this community that you commanded to be killed?\" Then Allah, Mighty and Sublime, revealed: {They ask you what is lawful for them. Say: Lawful for you are good things}"],[979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to all his wives in one night, performing a complete ghusl after each of them. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why not make it a single ghusl?\" He said, \"This is purer and better.\""],[980,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, with people around him: 'Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch when a command of mine comes to him, saying: We do not find it in the Book of God, so we act upon it [only if it is there].'"],[981,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent.'"],[982,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us; and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us; they said: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Maysarah narrated to us; he said: I heard 'Amr b. al-Sharid say: Al-Miswar b. Makhramah took me by the hand and said, 'Come with us to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas.' So I went out with him, his hand on one of my shoulders. Then Abu Rafi' came and said to al-Miswar, 'Will you not command this one' – meaning Sa'd – 'to buy from me my two houses that are in his dwelling?' Sa'd said, 'No, by God, I will not give you more than four hundred dinars,' either in installments or deferred. Abu Rafi' said, 'By God, I would sell them for five hundred dinars in cash, and were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent,\" I would not sell to you.' The wording is that of al-Humaydi."],[983,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent.'"],[984,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'He roasted some meat for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[985,"\"I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he ordered me to prepare its stomach for him. He ate from it, then he stood up and performed prayer without performing ablution.\""],[986,"'The Prophet ﷺ ate from the meat of a sheep and did not perform ablution.'"],[987,"'The Messenger of God ﷺ ate meat, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[988,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'I roasted the belly of a sheep for the Prophet ﷺ, and he ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[989,"\"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he passed by a pot where some of his family members were cooking meat. Some of them handed him a shoulder from it, and he ate it while standing. Then he performed the prayer without performing ablution.\""],[990,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited a guest, but he did not find anything suitable at the Prophet's ﷺ house. So he sent a message to a Jewish man, saying to him \"Muhammad ﷺ asked you to lend him some dates until the month of Rajab.\" The man replied, \"Only if you give me something as collateral.\" So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, \"By Allah, I am trustworthy in the heavens and trustworthy on earth. If he lent me or sold me something, I would fulfill my obligation to him.\" When I left him, the following verse was revealed to me, until the end of the verse, as a consolation to him regarding worldly matters: \"And do not extend your eyes toward that by which We have given enjoyment to [some] categories of them\" (Quran 20:131)."],[991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hair tied back."],[992,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was in prostration, and I had unkempt hair. He straightened it and advised me against doing that.\""],[993,"A shaykh from the people of Ta'if, whose kunya was Abu Sa'id, narrated to me from Abu Rafi' that he saw al-Husayn b. Ali prostrating with his hair tied back, and Abu Rafi' said, 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"None of you should ever pray while he has tied back his hair.\"'"],[994,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he placed him in charge of the captives of Qurayzah. He would look at the private part of a boy; if he saw that pubic hair had grown, he struck his neck, and whoever had not grown pubic hair he took and placed among the spoils of the Muslims."],[995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Asad b. Kurz, you will not enter Paradise by your deeds, but by the mercy of Allah.' I said, 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Not even I, unless Allah encompasses me or covers me with mercy from Him.'"],[996,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Indeed, illness removes sins just as leaves fall off a tree.'"],[997,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a drinker while he was at Khaybar, and he threw dust in his face. Then he ordered his companions, and they struck him with their sandals and with whatever was in their hands, until he said to them, “Lift him,” so they lifted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and that was his Sunnah. Then Abu Bakr lashed forty for wine, then Umar ؓ lashed forty in the beginning of his rule, then he lashed eighty at the end of his caliphate. Then Uthman ؓ lashed the prescribed punishment of forty, then Mu'awiyah ؓ eighty."],[998,"That his father al-Firasi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, shall I ask?” He said, “No, but if you must ask, then ask the righteous.”"],[999,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr, a client of Abu Bakr ؓ."],[1000,"About the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr, Bilal, the slave of Abu Bakr, was mentioned.\""],[1001,"It is said that he was the contemporary of Abu Bakr ؓ in Damascus during the plague and was buried near Bab al-Saghir, and his kunya is Abu Abdullah, in the year seventeen or eighteen. He was among those born in al-Sarat. It is also said that Bilal was given the kunya Abu Amr."],[1002,"“Abu Bakr ؓ freed seven of those who were tortured for the sake of Allah, among them Bilal and Amir b. Fuhayrah.”"],[1003,"“...from my evil deeds and excuse me for my faults.”"],[1004,"Bilal said to Abu Bakr when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, ؓ: “If you bought me for yourself, then keep me; but if you freed me for Allah, then let me work for Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[1005,"Bilal came to Umar ؓ while he was in Syria, and the commanders of the armies were sitting around him. He said, “O Umar!” He said, “Here I am, Umar.” Bilal said, “You are between Allah and these people, and there is no one between you and Allah. So look to your right, to your left, in front of you, and behind you. These people around you eat nothing but the flesh of birds.” He said, “You have spoken the truth. By Allah, I will not rise from this seat of mine until you guarantee for every Muslim man his food and his share of oil and vinegar.” They said, “This is up to you, O Commander of the Faithful, for Allah has expanded our provision and increased the good.”"],[1006,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “I heard a soft sound in front of me when I entered Paradise, so I said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Bilal.'” He informed him, and he said, “How do you precede me to Paradise?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I never perform ablution except that I pray, and I never pray except that I pray two rak'ahs after the ablution.”"],[1007,"From their forefathers they said: Bilal came to Abu Bakr ؓ and said, “O successor of the Messenger of Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The best deed of a believer is jihad in the path of Allah,' and I want to bind myself in the path of Allah until I die.” Abu Bakr said, “I adjure you by Allah, O Bilal, and by my sanctity and my right: my age has become advanced, my strength has weakened, and my term has drawn near.” So Bilal stayed with him. When Abu Bakr ؓ died, Umar came and said to him something similar to what Abu Bakr said, but Bilal refused. Umar ؓ said, “Then to whom, O Bilal?” He said, “To Sa'd, for he called the adhan at Quba during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So Umar assigned the adhan to Sa'd and his descendants."],[1008,"I passed by Bilal while he was sitting at the time of the morning prayer. I said, “What keeps you, O Abu Abdullah?” He said, “I am waiting for the sun to rise.”"],[1009,"Umar said, “Abu Bakr is our master, and he freed our master,” meaning Bilal."],[1010,"I had dates of low quality, so I purchased with them from the market better dates for half their measure. I presented them to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “I have not seen today dates better than these. Where did you get these, O Bilal?” He said: I told him what I had done. He said: “Go and return them to their owner, take your dates, sell them for wheat or barley, then buy these dates with that, then bring them to me.” He said: I did so. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Dates for dates, equal for equal; wheat for wheat, equal for equal; barley for barley, equal for equal; salt for salt, equal for equal; gold for gold, equal for equal, weight for weight; silver for silver, equal for equal, weight for weight. Whatever is in excess is ribā.”"],[1011,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1012,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I had some dates. He said: “What is this?” I said: We stored it for our winter. He said: “Do you not fear that you will see a vapor for it in Hell?”"],[1013,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the head covering (khimār).\""],[1014,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The best deed of a believer is striving in the path of Allah.\""],[1015,"'We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and they slept until the sun rose. He ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer, then they prayed the two rak'ahs of dawn, then they prayed the morning prayer.'"],[1016,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, people engage in business and pursue their livelihoods, but we are unable to do so.\" He said, \"Don't you want the muadhin (caller to prayer) to have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection?\""],[1017,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. When you see that, hasten to prayer.”"],[1018,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs and the head covering."],[1019,"A shaykh from Banu Taym, whose kunya is Abu ‘Abd Allah, told me, from Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was with ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf when Bilal passed by. They asked him about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “He would relieve himself, then come and perform ablution, and wipe over the head covering and the muqs.”"],[1020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1022,"I met Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said: O Bilal, tell me how was the expenditure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He had nothing. I was the one who took charge of that for him from the time Allah, may He be exalted, sent him until he passed away. When a Muslim man came to him and he saw him unclothed, he would order me concerning him, and I would go and borrow and buy a cloak, clothe him and feed him. This continued until a man from the polytheists came in my way and said: O Bilal, I have ample means, so do not borrow from anyone except me. So I did that. Then one day I performed ablution and then stood to call the adhan for prayer, and there was the polytheist approaching with a group of merchants. When he saw me, he said: O Abyssinian! I said: At your service. He scowled at me and said harsh words to me. He said: Do you know how much time is between you and the month? I said: It is near. He said: It is only four days, and I will seize you for what you owe me, for I did not give you what I gave you out of respect for you or for your companion; rather, I gave it to you to make you my slave, and I will return you to herding sheep as you were before. Then something took hold of my soul as it takes hold of people's souls. I departed, then called the adhan for prayer, until when I had prayed the evening prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his family. I asked permission to enter upon him, and he gave me permission. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheist from whom I used to borrow said such-and-such to me. You do not have anything to pay on my behalf, and I do not have anything, and he will disgrace me. So permit me to flee to some of those Arab tribes that have accepted Islam until Allah provides His Messenger ﷺ with something to settle my debt. So I went out until I reached my dwelling. I placed my sword, my provision bag, my shield, and my sandals at my head, and I faced the horizon with my face. Whenever I slept for a while I would wake up, and when I saw that night was still upon me I would sleep until the first column of dawn broke. Then I wanted to depart, and there was a man running and calling: O Bilal, answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So I went until I came to him, and there were four mounted camels with their loads upon them. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Rejoice, for Allah has brought you the means to settle your debt.\" I praised Allah, may He be exalted, and he said: \"Did you not pass by the four mounted camels?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"You have their necks and what is on them—clothing and food—as a gift sent to me by the chief of Fadak. Take them and pay your debt.\" I did so. I unloaded their burdens, then hobbled them, then went to give the call for the dawn prayer, until when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed, I went out to al-Baqi' and put my fingers in my ears and called out: Whoever has a debt owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him come forward. I kept selling and paying until no debt remained owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on earth, until there remained in my hand two uqiyyahs or one and a half uqiyyahs. Then I went to the mosque, and most of the day had passed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting alone in the mosque. I greeted him, and he said to me: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: Allah has settled everything that was owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and nothing remains. He said: \"Is there any surplus?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"See that you relieve me of it, for I will not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it.\" No one came to us until evening. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed the evening prayer, he called me and said: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: It is with me; no one came to us. He spent the night in the mosque until morning, and remained the second day until near the end of the day, when two riders came. I went with them and fed them and clothed them, until when he had prayed the evening prayer, he called me and said: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah. He said takbir and praised Allah, may He be exalted, out of fear that death might overtake him while he still had that. Then I followed him until he came to his wives, and he greeted each wife one by one until he reached his sleeping place. That is what you asked me about."],[1023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not give the call to prayer until you see the dawn like this,\" and he gestured with his hand and then opened it."],[1024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.\""],[1025,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Do not precede me in saying Amin.\""],[1026,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Bilal, commence the dawn prayer early in the morning, for that is better for you.”"],[1027,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had dates with me, and they became spoiled. I took them out to the market and sold two sāʿs for one sāʿ. When I brought some of them near to him, he said: “What is this, O Bilal?” I informed him. He said: “Wait, return the sale, then sell dates for gold, silver, or wheat, then buy dates with it.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Dates for dates, equal for equal; wheat for wheat, equal for equal; gold for gold, weight for weight; silver for silver, weight for weight. But when the two types differ, there is no harm in one for ten.”"],[1028,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Bilal while he had a heap of dates. He said: “What is this, O Bilal?” He said: O Messenger of God, I stored it for you and for your guests. He said: “Do you not fear that it will have a vapor from Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Possessor of the Throne.”"],[1029,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O Bilal, die poor and do not die rich.” I said: And how is that? He said: “Whatever provision you receive, do not hoard it; and whatever you are asked for, do not withhold it.” I said: O Messenger of God, how can I do that? He said: “It is that, or the Fire.”"],[1030,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks."],[1031,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Bilal and found a heap of dates with him. He said: “What is this, O Bilal?” He said: Dates I am storing. He said: “Woe to you, O Bilal! Do you not fear that it will have a vapor in the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Possessor of the Throne.”"],[1032,"The Prophet ﷺ visited Bilal, and he brought out a heap of dates for him. He said: “What is this, O Bilal?” He said: I stored it for you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Do you not fear that a vapor will be made for you in the Fire of Hell? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Possessor of the Throne.”"],[1033,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to the Mosque of Qubāʾ. The Anṣār came to greet him. I said to Bilal: How did the Messenger of God ﷺ respond to them? He said: “Like this,” gesturing with his hand."],[1034,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a guest come to him, so he ordered him to bring him food. He brought him dates, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was impressed by those dates. He said: “Where did you get these dates?” He said: I exchanged one sāʿ for two sāʿs. He said: “Return our dates to us.” So he returned them."],[1035,"I heard Ibn Umar say: \"The Prophet ﷺ came walking between Usamah and Bilal until they entered the Kaaba, and inside was a wooden beam placed across.\" When Bilal came out, I asked him how he [the Prophet] prayed. He said: \"He left two-thirds of the beam on his right and prayed in the remaining third.\" I said: \"How many [rak'ahs] did he pray?\" He said: \"I did not ask Bilal about that.\""],[1036,"[Ibn Umar asked Bilal] about the Prophet's ﷺ prayer inside the House, and he informed him \"that he prayed two rak'ahs in the middle of the House, and he placed the pillar on his right, moved forward a little, and put the Maqam behind his back.\""],[1037,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Kaaba and Bilal stood at the door.\" Ibn Umar said: I asked Bilal, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said: \"Yes, two rak'ahs in the middle of the House.\""],[1038,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs inside it.\""],[1039,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed inside the Kaaba.\""],[1040,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed inside the House.\""],[1041,"Abdullah b. Umar ؓ: \"The Prophet ﷺ came on the day of the conquest riding a camel belonging to Usamah b. Zayd, with Usamah as the Prophet's ﷺ riding companion, and with him were Bilal and Uthman b. Talhah. The Prophet ﷺ, Usamah b. Zayd, Uthman b. Talhah, and Bilal entered, and they stayed in the House for a long time, and they closed the door on themselves. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out, and the people rushed to the door.\" Abdullah b. Umar got ahead of them, along with another man with him. Abdullah b. Umar asked Bilal: \"Where did the Prophet ﷺ pray?\" He showed him where he prayed, but he did not ask him how many [rak'ahs] he prayed."],[1042,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed in the House facing the front, then he stood and supplicated for a while, then he left.\""],[1043,"I asked Bilal, \"Where did the Prophet ﷺ pray when he entered the Kaaba?\" He said: \"Between the two columns.\""],[1044,"I said to Bilal, \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" meaning inside the House. He said: \"Between the two front columns; he prayed two rak'ahs.\""],[1045,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived and stopped in the courtyard of the Kaaba. Then he sent for Uthman b. Talhah, who came with the key. The Prophet ﷺ, Bilal, Usamah b. Zayd, and Uthman b. Talhah entered.\" When they came out, the people rushed to them. I said to Bilal, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray inside the House?\" He said: \"Yes, between the two columns, facing straight ahead.\""],[1046,"I said to Bilal, \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said: \"Between the two columns.\""],[1047,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar ؓ: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, he and Usamah b. Zayd, 'Uthman b. Talhah al-Hajabi, and Bilal, and he closed it upon them and stayed inside.\" 'Abdullah b. 'Umar said: \"When he came out, I asked Bilal what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.\" He said: \"He placed one pillar to his left, two pillars to his right, and three pillars behind him, and at that time the House was on six pillars, then he prayed.\""],[1048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came on the day of the Conquest on a she-camel belonging to Usamah b. Zayd, with Usamah riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him were Bilal and 'Uthman b. Talhah. When he came to the House, he sent 'Uthman b. Talhah, who brought him the key of the House and opened it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, along with Usamah, 'Uthman b. Talhah, and Bilal. They stayed inside for a long time, having closed the House upon themselves. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, and the people rushed toward the House. 'Abdullah b. 'Umar and another man with him got there first. 'Abdullah b. 'Umar asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. Bilal showed him the place where he prayed, but he did not ask how many units he prayed."],[1049,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, and with him were Bilal, Usamah, and 'Uthman, and he had closed the door upon them. I came and sat on the ground, and they remained inside for a long while. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, I went up the steps and entered the House. I said: \"Where did the Prophet ﷺ pray?\" They said: \"Here.\" And I forgot to ask how many units he prayed."],[1050,"I asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed when he entered the House. He said: \"Between the two pillars that are adjacent to the door.\""],[1051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah with Usamah b. Zayd, Bilal, and 'Uthman b. Talhah, and he stayed in the House for a long time. Then he came out, and 'Abdullah b. 'Umar entered right behind him, ahead of the people. He asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He said: \"Between the two front pillars.\" And I forgot to ask him how many units he prayed."],[1052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, he and Usamah b. Zayd, 'Uthman b. Talhah, and Bilal, and he stayed in the House for a long time, then he came out. 'Abdullah entered right behind him, ahead of the people. He asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He said: \"Between the two pillars.\""],[1053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah on the day of the Conquest, and with him were Bilal and 'Uthman b. Talhah b. Shaybah, and they closed it upon themselves from inside. When they came out, I asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He told me that he prayed facing forward as soon as he entered, putting the two pillars to his right. He said: \"Then I blamed myself for not asking him how many units he prayed.\""],[1054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came riding with Usamah behind him on al-'Adba', and with him were Bilal and 'Uthman b. Talhah, until he made his camel kneel at the House. He said to 'Uthman: \"Bring us the key.\" So he brought him the key and opened the door for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, along with Usamah, Bilal, and 'Uthman b. Talhah. Then they closed the House upon themselves and stayed inside for a long time. Then he came out, and the people rushed to enter. I got ahead of them and found Bilal standing behind the people. I said: \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said: \"He prayed between the two front pillars, keeping the people behind his back and facing straight ahead in the direction you are facing when you enter.\""],[1055,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ enter the House, and with him were a group: Usamah b. Zayd, al-Fadl b. 'Abbas, 'Uthman b. Talhah, and Bilal. He closed the door. I stood at the door, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, the first person I met was Bilal. I said: \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said: \"Between the two columns.\""],[1056,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Ka'bah with Usamah b. Zayd, 'Uthman b. Talhah, and Bilal, and he stayed inside for a long time. I was the first of the people to enter right after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said to Bilal: \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said: \"Two rak'ahs between the two front pillars.\""],[1057,"I asked Bilal where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He said: \"Two rak'ahs between the two pillars.\""],[1058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah, and with him were Usamah b. Zayd, Bilal, and the custodian of the Ka'bah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, I was the first to enter, and I found Bilal at the door. I asked him where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He said: \"Between the two front pillars.\""],[1059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, and with him entered al-Fadl b. Abbas, Usamah b. Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman b. Talhah. He prolonged his stay, then came out. I hurried ahead of the people and was among the first to enter. I met Bilal and asked, “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said, “Between the two front pillars.” Ibn Umar said, “I forgot to ask him how many (rakahs) he prayed.”"],[1060,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House: he, Usamah b. Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman b. Talhah. They closed it behind them.” When they opened it, I was among the first to enter. I met Bilal and asked him, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray inside it?” He said, “Yes, he prayed between the two Yemeni pillars.”"],[1061,"I hear where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed when he entered the House? Ibn Umar said, “The Prophet ﷺ entered between Usamah and Bilal.” When they came out, I asked them where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. They said, “Facing it.”"],[1062,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the Kaaba, so I hurried off and met Bilal and asked, “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in the House?” He said, “Yes, he prayed two rakahs between the two pillars, and he placed the right pillar on his right.”"],[1063,"Muawiyah ؓ asked Ibn Umar ؓ where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed when he entered the House. Ibn Umar said, “I did not reach him while he was praying; I came when he had finished, so I asked Bilal, and he told me that the Prophet ﷺ prayed between two pillars.”"],[1064,"“The Prophet ﷺ had a servant named Rabah.”"],[1065,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the turban.”"],[1066,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban.”"],[1067,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban.”"],[1068,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the thin socks.”"],[1069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of Hamal, he and Bilal. Bilal came out to them and informed them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[1070,"“The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks.”"],[1071,"I called the adhān on a cold night, and no one came; then I called again, and no one came—three times. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is wrong with them?\" I said, \"The cold kept them away.\" He said, \"O Allah, remove the cold from them.\" Bilāl said, \"And I bear witness that I saw them fanning themselves in the morning because of the heat.\""],[1072,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Bilāl, begin the morning prayer at the break of dawn, for that is better for you.\""],[1073,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Wipe over the leather socks and over the head covering (khimār).\""],[1074,"Regarding prayer at any time except when the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, or upon the two horns of a devil.\""],[1075,"He used to call the adhān for the dawn prayer, saying, \"Come to the best of deeds (ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal).\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that in its place be said, \"Prayer is better than sleep (al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm),\" and he left out \"Come to the best of deeds.\""],[1076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you give the adhān, put your fingers in your ears, for it raises your voice.\""],[1077,"He used to give the adhān for the Prophet ﷺ. He would say: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar; ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh, ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Then he would turn to the right of the qiblah and say: ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh, ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh. Then he would turn and face away from the qiblah and say: ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh, ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Then he would turn to his left and say: ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ, ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Then he would face the qiblah and say: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar, lā ilāha illā Allāh. And he used to pronounce the iqāmah for the Prophet ﷺ in single statements, saying: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar; ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh; ashhadu anna Muḥammadan rasūlu Allāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh; ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ; qad qāmat al-ṣalāh; Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar; lā ilāha illā Allāh."],[1078,"The last words of Bilāl's adhān were, \"There is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great.\""],[1079,"\"That he used to give the adhān for the Messenger of Allah on Friday when the shade was the length of a sandal strap, when the Prophet ﷺ sat on the pulpit.\""],[1080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah ﷻ has placed the truth upon the tongue and heart of ʿUmar.\""],[1081,"Bilal came to the Prophet ﷺ to call him to prayer once, and it was said that he was sleeping, so he called out: 'Prayer is better than sleep.' And it was established in the dawn prayer."],[1082,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ to call him to the morning prayer and found him sleeping, so he said: 'Prayer is better than sleep' twice. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'How excellent this is, O Bilal! Put it in your call to prayer.'"],[1083,"'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to call him to prayer while he was intending to fast, and he drank, then handed it to me and I drank, then he went out to the prayer and led us.'"],[1084,"'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to call him to prayer while he was intending to fast, so he called for a vessel and drank, then handed it to me and I drank, then he went out to the prayer.'"],[1085,"On the authority of Bilal, who traced it back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: he raised his gaze to the sky and said: 'Glory be to Allah, who sends poverty upon them like the sending of rain.'"],[1086,"He saw a man praying badly, not completing its bowing or its prostration, so he said: 'If you were to die now, you would die upon other than the religion of Jesus ﷺ .'"],[1087,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and over the turban.'"],[1088,"'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1089,"'The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and the turban.'"],[1090,"'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and over the turban.'"],[1091,"'The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1092,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the khuffs."],[1093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the iqamah for Fajr, and he forbade me from calling the iqamah for Isha."],[1094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the iqamah for Fajr, and he forbade me from calling the iqamah for Isha."],[1095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs and the head covering."],[1096,"I had some dates belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I found better dates than them, a sa‘ for two sa‘s, so I bought them and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “What is this?” I said, “I took a sa‘ for two sa‘s.” He said, “Return our dates to us.”"],[1097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Feed us, O Bilal, some dates.” So I scooped handfuls for him. He said, “Give us more, O Bilal.” I added three more and said, “Nothing remains except a little I had stored for the Prophet ﷺ.” He said, “Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Owner of the Throne.”"],[1098,"He heard ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf ask Bilal how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his khuffs. Bilal said: “He went to relieve himself, then called for a vessel of water with a small bucket, washed his face and hands, then wiped over his khuffs and over his head covering as a substitute for the turban.”"],[1099,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-fourth.”"],[1100,"“Wipe over the head coverings and the muq,” tracing it back to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1101,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Wipe over the turban and the leather socks.'"],[1102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1103,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Wipe over the leather socks and the leather socks.'"],[1104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1105,"He and a man from Quraysh were performing ablution from the water container of the mosque, and they disputed about wiping over the leather socks. Bilal said: 'The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1106,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1107,"Bilal, the freed slave of Abu Bakr ؓ, reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he came from relieving himself on the day of the Battle of Tabuk and called for water for ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[1108,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the turban."],[1109,"That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the turban and the leather socks."],[1110,"Bilal wiped over his leather socks, and it was said to him: 'What is this?' He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the turban.' Ma'mar did not mention Abu Idris in his hadith, and likewise Yahya b. Abi Ishaq narrated it from Abu Qilabah."],[1111,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1112,"He was sitting in Damascus on a cold day performing ablution when Bilal, the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, passed by him. He said: 'O Bilal, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution?' He said: 'He would wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1113,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Bilal, announce among the people: Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah' before his death by a year, or a month, or a week, or a day, or an hour, will enter Paradise.\" Bilal said: \"Then they will rely on that.\" He said: \"Even if they rely on it.\""],[1115,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Do not precede me in saying Amin.\""],[1116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every act of kindness is charity.\""],[1117,"Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani died in the year sixty, and his age was eighty years."],[1118,"Bilal ibn al-Harith is known by the kunyah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman."],[1119,"«Bilal b. al-Harith is given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.»"],[1120,"«Bilal b. al-Harith is given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.»"],[1121,"«Bilal b. al-Harith is given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.»"],[1122,"«Bilal b. al-Harith is given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.»"],[1123,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, «A man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath without realizing how far it will reach, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the Day of Resurrection. And a man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure without realizing how far it will reach, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1124,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, «A man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure without thinking it will reach what it has reached, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath without thinking it will reach what it has reached, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1125,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. (H) And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik reported to us. (H) And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Abi al-Hakam narrated to us: Malik b. Anas reported to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr b. 'Alqama, from his father, from Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, «A man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure, not thinking it would reach what it has reached, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath, not thinking it would reach what it has reached, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.» Abu al-Qasim said: \"Malik and Muhammad b. 'Ajlan omitted 'Alqama b. Waqqas, the grandfather of Muhammad b. 'Amr, from the chain, and Hammad b. Salama narrated it, and the people differed with him in this.\""],[1126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man may speak a word that angers Allah without realizing its severity, so Allah writes His anger against him until the day they meet. And indeed, a man may speak a word that pleases Allah without realizing its significance, so Allah writes His satisfaction with him until the day they meet.\""],[1127,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, «A man may utter a word of goodness without knowing how far it will reach, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word of evil without knowing how far it will reach, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1128,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal b. al-Harith, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said, «The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.»"],[1129,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, is the termination of Hajj for 'Umrah specific to us or for all people generally?' He said, «Rather, it is specific to us.»"],[1130,"«The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath along with a witness.»"],[1131,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ granted him all of al-'Aqiq as a fief.»"],[1132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him this piece of land and wrote for him: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, gave Bilal b. al-Harith: He gave him the minerals of al-Qabilah, its lowland and its highland, Ghashayah, Dhat al-Nusub, and wherever cultivation is suitable from Quds, if he is truthful.” Muawiyah wrote [it]."],[1133,"When the Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away."],[1134,"We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on some of his journeys, and he went out to relieve himself. Whenever he went out to relieve himself, he would go far away. I came to him with water for purification, and he set off. I heard some men arguing and making noise by him, like nothing I had ever heard before. He came and said, \"Bilal.\" I said, \"Bilal.\" He asked, \"Do you have water?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have done well.\" So he took it from me and performed ablution. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard some men arguing and making noise near you. I have never heard anyone speak like them before.\" He said, \"The Muslim and non-Muslim jinn disputed with me, asking me to accommodate them. So I accommodated the Muslim jinn in the lowlands and the non-Muslim jinn in the mountains.\" Abdullah ibn Kathir said, \"I asked Kathir, 'What are the lowlands and mountains?' He said, 'The lowlands are the villages and the mountains are the places between the mountains and the seas.' Kathir said, 'We have never seen anyone afflicted with the lowlands except that they were safe, and we have never seen anyone afflicted with the mountains except that they were barely safe.'\""],[1135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Ramadan in Madinah is better than a thousand Ramadans elsewhere, and a Friday in Madinah is better than a thousand Fridays elsewhere.”"],[1136,"Abu Musa: “And Buraydah b. Husayb is called Abu Abd Allah.”"],[1137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Buraydah, there will be expeditions. You must join the expedition of Khurasan, then you must go to the city of Marw, for no harm will befall its people because Dhu al-Qarnayn built it.”"],[1138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter. I had forbidden you [to use] gourds, but now make nabidh in any vessel and avoid every intoxicant. I had forbidden you to eat the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, but now eat, store, and keep provisions.”"],[1139,"A group of the Ansar said to Ali ؓ: “Fatimah is with you.” So he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him. He said: “What is the need of the son of Abu Talib?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have thought of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Welcome and family!” He added nothing more. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ went out to that group of Ansar who were waiting for him. They said: “What happened?” He said: “I don't know, except that he said to me: ‘Welcome and family!’” They said: “One of the two from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is enough for you. He gave you family and welcome.” Then later, after he married him, he said: “O Ali, a bridegroom must have a walimah.” Sa'd said: “I have a ram.” And a group of the Ansar collected for him measures of corn. On the wedding night he said: “Do not do anything until you meet me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, performed ablution with it, then poured it over Ali and said: “O Allah, bless them and bless their union.”"],[1140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who judges unjustly while knowing it—that one is in the Fire. A judge who judges while not knowing and thereby destroys people's rights—that one is in the Fire. And a judge who judges with truth—that one is in Paradise.”"],[1141,"We prayed Zuhr behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he finished his prayer, he turned to us angrily and called out in a voice that made the women in their chambers hear: “O assembly of those who have submitted but faith has not entered their hearts! Do not disparage Muslims, do not seek their faults. For whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will expose his own faults and reveal his private matters even if he is in the innermost part of his house.”"],[1142,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who judges unjustly while knowing it—he is in the Fire. A judge who judges unjustly while not knowing it—he is in the Fire. And a judge who judges with truth while knowing it—he is in Paradise.” Abu al-Qasim said: Abd Allah b. Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, disagreed with the people about this man. He said Abbad, and al-Mutayyan, Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah, al-Tirmidhi and others narrated from him, saying Ubadah b. Ziyad."],[1143,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the market, he would say: “O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from incurring a false oath or a losing deal in it.”"],[1144,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A stone the size of seven pregnant camels will be thrown into Hell and it will fall for seventy autumns without reaching its bottom.”"],[1145,"While the Prophet ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he came upon a man turning over on the burning ground, on his back and on his belly, saying, “O soul, sleep at night and vanity by day, and you hope to enter Paradise?” When the man had finished his own prayer, he came over to us and said, “Here is your brother for you.” We said, “Supplicate Allah for us, may Allah have mercy on you.” He said, “O Allah, unite their affair upon guidance.” We said, “More.” He said, “O Allah, make piety their provision.” We said, “More.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “Give them more. O Allah, grant him success.” He said, “O Allah, make Paradise their final abode.”"],[1146,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he gestured to us with his hand to sit down."],[1147,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black, and his standard was white."],[1148,"Al-Samad is the One who has no hollow."],[1149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade naming a dog Kalb or Kulayb."],[1150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The inviolability of the wives of the mujahidun over those who stay behind is like that of their mothers. Whoever among those who stay behind is left in charge of any mujahid's family and betrays him regarding them will be brought to a halt for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: ‘This one betrayed you regarding your family, so take from his deeds whatever you wish.’”"],[1151,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr."],[1152,"Ibn Umar and I were presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr, and we were deemed too young, but we were present at Uhud."],[1153,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr."],[1154,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr, so we did not witness it."],[1155,"We were sitting waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Eid al-Adha. He came, greeted the people, and said, “The first rite of this day of yours is the prayer.” He then went forward and prayed two rak'ahs with the people, then said the salam, then faced the people, and then was given a bow or a staff. He leaned on it, praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, commanded them, and forbade them."],[1156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he entered the morning and the evening: “We have entered the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. O Allah, we ask You for the good of this day and the good of what comes after it, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil of what comes after it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the evil of pride, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire.”"],[1157,"A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about loneliness, so he said: \"Say: Glory be to the King, the Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit. You have clothed the heavens and the earth with might and dominion.\" The man said it, and Allah ﷻ removed the loneliness from him."],[1158,"Al-Bara' b. 'Azib said to me: \"Shall I not teach you a supplication that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me?\" He said: \"When you see people competing for gold and silver, supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and I ask You for determination upon guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessings and patience in Your trials and excellence in worshiping You and contentment with Your decree. I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.\""],[1159,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"What is your name?\" He said: \"Nu'm.\" He said: \"Rather you are 'Abd Allah.\""],[1160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night for wiping over the leather socks.\""],[1161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fast upon seeing it, and break your fast upon seeing it. If it is obscured to you, then complete thirty.\" And he said with his hand: \"The month is like this and like this,\" meaning twenty-nine."],[1162,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, the earnings of a cupper, the payment of a soothsayer, and the stud fee of a stallion.\" And al-Bara' had a he-goat that anyone who wanted would bring to it for breeding, without preventing anyone, and he would not accept a fee for the stallion."],[1163,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we came to a well with little water. Sulayman said: \"Al-dhamma means little water.\" He said: \"Six of us went down, I being the sixth, or seven, I being the seventh, to draw water.\" Sulayman said: \"Al-maha are those who draw water.\" He said: \"We lowered a bucket while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the edge of the well. We filled it halfway, or nearly two-thirds, or about that. Then I raised it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Bara' said: \"I searched my vessel to see if I could find anything to put in my throat, but I found nothing.\" He said: \"Then I raised it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he dipped his hand into it and said whatever Allah willed him to say. The bucket was returned to the well with the water in it. I saw one of us brought out with a garment for fear of drowning. Then it overflowed,\" or he said \"it gushed,\" and the wording is from the hadith of al-Muqri'."],[1164,"Anas said to him: \"O my brother,\" so he sat up and said: \"O Anas, do you think I will die on my bed when I have killed one hundred of the polytheists in single combat, besides those I participated in killing?\""],[1165,"\"O my brother, Allah has taught you what is better for you than that.\" He said: \"Yes.\" Al-Bara' said to him: \"Do you fear that I will die on my bed? By Allah, that will not be a trial from Allah to me, for I have killed one hundred of the polytheists whom I killed alone, and among them those I shared in killing.\""],[1166,"To Abu Talha: \"We used not to give a fifth of the spoils, but the spoils of al-Bara' have reached a great amount of wealth, so I think we should give a fifth of it.\""],[1167,"\"A tall man with a white sword in his hand.\" He said: \"Al-Bara' was a short man. Al-Bara' struck his legs with the sword, and it seemed to miss him, and he fell on his back.\" He said: \"I took his sword and sheathed my own, and I struck only once until it broke, so I threw it away and took my sword.\""],[1168,"While Anas b. Malik and his brother al-Bara' b. Malik were at a fortress of the enemy's fortresses, the enemy was throwing hooks attached to heated chains that would catch a person and lift him up to them. One of those hooks caught Anas b. Malik, and they lifted him until he was raised off the ground. His brother al-Bara' b. Malik came, and it was said: \"Catch up to your brother!\" He was fighting among the people, so he came running until he leaped onto the wall, then he grabbed the chain with his hand while it was being turned. He kept pulling them while his hands were smoking until he cut the rope. Then he looked at his hands, and the bones were showing; the flesh on them had gone. And Allah ﷻ saved Anas b. Malik by that."],[1169,"From ʿUrwa: “Regarding the naming of the Companions of al-ʿAqaba who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Salima b. Yazid b. Jusham: al-Bara' b. Maʿrur b. Sakhr b. Khansa', and he was a naqib (leader), and he was the first to bequeath a third of his wealth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approved it.”"],[1170,"From Ibn Shihab: “Among those who attended al-ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Salima: al-Bara' b. Maʿrur. He was the first to bequeath a third of his wealth and to face the Kaʿba while he was in his own land, and he was a naqib (leader).”"],[1171,"That al-Bara' b. Maʿrur “bequeathed a third of his wealth to the Prophet ﷺ to dispose of as he wished, but the Prophet ﷺ returned it to his children.”"],[1172,"That the Prophet ﷺ proposed to the wife of al-Bara' b. Maʿrur, and she said: “I stipulated to my husband that I would not marry after him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is not appropriate.”"],[1173,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered into an alliance on the day of al-Hudaybiya with Khuzaʿa and wrote to them and to Budayl b. Warqa' and the leaders of Banu ʿAmr: “Peace be upon you. I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not harbored ill intentions toward you nor neglected your side. The most honored people of Tihama to me are you and those of the Mutayyabin who follow you. I have secured for those of you who emigrate the same as I have secured for myself, even if he emigrates in his own land without residing in Makkah. You shall not fear from me nor be made to fear.” This or similar."],[1174,"And he said: “O my son, this is the letter of the Prophet ﷺ, so follow its instructions. You will remain in good as long as it is among you. In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Budayl b. Warqa', Busr, and the leaders of Banu ʿAmr. I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not harbored ill intentions toward you nor neglected your side. The most honored of my people from Tihama to me are you, and the closest of them to me in kinship, and those of the Mutayyabin who follow you. I have secured for those of you who emigrate the same as I have secured for myself, even if he emigrates in his own land without residing in Makkah except as a pilgrim for ʿumra or hajj. I have not placed any burden upon you since I made peace, and you shall not fear from me nor be confined. To proceed: ʿAlqama b. ʿUlatha and the two sons of Hawdha have embraced Islam and pledged allegiance and emigrated on behalf of those who followed them from ʿIkrima, and he secured for those of you who followed them the same as he secured for himself. And some of you are from some others forever in the sacred and non-sacred territory.” Abu Muhammad said: My father narrated to me: “I heard our elders say: This is the handwriting of ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ.”"],[1175,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “ordered Budayl to detain the captives and the spoils at al-Jiʿrana until he came to him, so they were detained.”"],[1178,"That he heard his father Busr say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday.” He said: “If one of you finds nothing but to chew the bark of a tree, he should not fast that day.” And ʿAbdullah b. Busr said: “If you doubt, ask my sister.” So Khalid b. Maʿdan went to her and asked her about what ʿAbdullah had mentioned, and she narrated that to him."],[1179,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them riding a mule that we used to call a Syrian donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions entered upon them. My mother stood and placed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a velvet cloth over a mat in the house, preferring it for him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on it, I pressed down the mat. ʿAbdullah b. Busr said: My father Busr brought them dates to occupy them with, and he ordered my mother, so she prepared for them a dish of crushed wheat. ʿAbdullah said: I was the servant between my father and mother, and my father was the one standing over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. When my mother finished the crushed wheat, I came carrying it until I placed it before them, and they ate. Then he gave them a drink of fadikh (a beverage made from dates), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank and gave to the one on his right. Then I took the cup until what was in it was finished, so I filled it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Give it to the one to whom the cup came.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the food, he supplicated for us and said: “O Allah, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless their provision.” And we continued to recognize from Allah ﷻ abundance in provision."],[1180,"That the Prophet ﷺ spat one day on his palm and placed his finger on it, then said: “O son of Adam, Allah ﷻ says: You will never frustrate Me, for I created you from something like this. Then when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, and the earth resounded from your heavy tread. Then you gathered and withheld until when it reached the collarbones, you said, 'Should I give charity?' But how, when it is the time of charity?”"],[1181,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended his hand and spat into it, then looked at it and said: “Allah says: How will you frustrate Me, O son of Adam, when I created you from something like this, then I fashioned you and proportioned you, and you walked between two garments, and the earth resounded from your heavy tread? Then you gathered and withheld until when it reached the collarbones, you said, 'Should I give charity now?' But how, when it is the time of charity?”"],[1182,"That he said on the pulpit when he flogged the two men who had stolen from the people's spoils: “Nothing prevented me from cutting off their hands except that Busr b. Arta'a found a man stealing during a military expedition, so he flogged him and did not cut off his hand, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from amputation during a military expedition.'”"],[1183,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O Allah, make my final outcome good in all matters, and protect me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.”"],[1184,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O Allah, make my final outcome good in all matters, and protect me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.” And he said: “Whoever makes this his supplication will die before affliction befalls him.”"],[1185,"He used to supplicate: “O Allah, make our final outcome good in all matters, and protect us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.”"],[1186,"From 'Urwah: “In naming the companions of al-'Aqabah who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah b. Yazid b. Jusham: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, and he was present at Badr.”"],[1187,"From Ibn Shihab: “Among those who were present at al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, and he is the one who ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the sheep that was poisoned on the day of Khaybar.”"],[1188,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who were present at Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Ubayd b. 'Adi: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.”"],[1189,"A Jewish woman gave the Prophet ﷺ a roasted sheep as a gift. He ate from it, then said: “It has informed me that it is poisoned.” Bishr b. al-Bara' died from it. He sent for her and said: “What prompted you to do what you did?” She said: “I wanted to know if you were a prophet, it would not harm you, and if you were a king, I would relieve the people of you.” So he ordered her and she was killed."],[1190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is your chief, O Banu 'Ubayd?” They said: “Al-Jadd b. Qays, although he has some miserliness.” He said: “What disease is worse than miserliness? Rather, your chief is Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.”"],[1191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him, so he announced at Mina during the days of Tashriq, \"None will enter Paradise except a submitting soul, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1192,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Constantinople will surely be conquered, and excellent is its commander, and excellent is that army!\" Then Maslama b. 'Abd al-Malik called me and asked me about this hadith, so I narrated it to him, and he campaigned that year."],[1193,"From Bishr b. 'Isma, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Azd are from me and I am from them; I am angry for them when they are angry, and pleased for them when they are pleased.\" Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him, said, \"He only said that about Quraysh.\" Bishr said, \"Would I then lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? If I were to lie about him, I would have made it for my own people.\""],[1194,"Abu Ma'shar al-Bara' narrated to us: al-Nawwar bt. 'Umar narrated to me, she said: Fatima bt. Muslim narrated to me, she said: Khalifa b. Bishr narrated to me from his father Bishr that when he embraced Islam, the Prophet ﷺ returned to him his wealth and his children. Then the Prophet ﷺ met him and saw him and his son Talq tied together with a rope. He said, \"What is this, O Bishr?\" He said, \"I swore that if Allah returned my wealth and my children to me, I would perform the pilgrimage to the House of Allah tied together.\" So the Prophet ﷺ took the rope and cut it, and said to them, \"Perform the pilgrimage, for this is from Satan.\""],[1195,"When Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, granted victory at Khaybar to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he killed those he killed among them, Zaynab bt. al-Harith the Jewess, the daughter of Marhab's brother, gave him a roasted sheep as a gift, and she put poison in it, adding more to the shoulder and foreleg, because she was told that those were the parts of the sheep most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and with him was Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, the brother of Banu Salimah, she presented it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he took the shoulder and foreleg and bit into them, and Bishr took another bone and bit into it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swallowed his mouthful, Bishr swallowed what was in his mouth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Raise your hands, for the shoulder of the sheep tells me that treachery has been intended in it.” Bishr b. al-Bara' said: “By the One who honored you, I found that in the morsel I ate; if I did not spit it out, it was only because I disliked spoiling your food. When you ate what was in your mouth, I did not prefer my own life over yours, and I hoped that I had not swallowed it while it contained treachery.” Bishr did not rise from his place until his color turned like a black cloak, and pain lingered in him until he could not move except when moved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained alive for three years after that, until the illness in which he died."],[1196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us during the days of tashriq and said: “These are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only a believing soul will enter Paradise, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1198,"“The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on the days of Tashriq and said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer, and these days are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1200,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on the days of Tashriq and said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the days of Mina and said, \"Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them.\""],[1202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, the days of Mina.\""],[1203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to announce on the days of Tashriq, \"Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1204,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to announce on the days of Tashriq, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer; indeed, these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1207,"From 'Urwa, \"In the naming of the Aqaba participants from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. Sa'd, and he witnessed Badr.\""],[1208,"From 'Urwa, \"Among those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Zayd b. Malik b. Tha'laba b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. Sa'd b. Tha'laba b. Jilas.\""],[1209,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"Regarding the naming of the participants of the ʿAqaba pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Bashīr b. Saʿd Abū al-Nuʿmān.\""],[1210,"From Bashīr b. Saʿd, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The position of the believer to the believer is like the position of the head to the body: whenever the body complains, the head complains for it; and whenever the head complains, the rest of the body complains.\""],[1211,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever delivers a speech seeking nothing but ostentation and reputation, God ﷻ will make him stand in a position of ostentation and reputation.\""],[1212,"There was an uprising among Banu Mu'awiyah. The Prophet ﷺ went to reconcile between them. He turned to a grave and said, “You did not know.” It was said to him, so he said, “Indeed this one is being asked about me,” and he said, “I do not know.”"],[1213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of Dhu Qar: “This is the first day on which the Arabs obtained justice from the Persians.”"],[1214,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those killed on the Day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. 'Abd Allah.”"],[1215,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and became Muslims, and we asked him to waive the 'atamah for us. He said, “The 'atamah prayer.” We said, “We are occupied with milking our camels.” He said, “You will, if Allah wills, milk and pray.”"],[1216,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Buhayr b. al-Haytham.”"],[1217,"The Prophet ﷺ used to use the siwak horizontally, drink by sipping, and breathe three times, and he would say, “It is more wholesome, more palatable, and more healing.”"],[1218,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Sa'idah b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, an ally of theirs.”"],[1221,"From his father, who had companionship with the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this vegetable—meaning garlic—let him not approach our mosque.\""],[1222,"When the Muhājirūn arrived in Madinah, they found the water unpleasant. A man from Banū Ghifār had a spring called Rūmah, and he would sell a waterskin of it for a mudd. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Sell it to me for a spring in Paradise.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have nothing besides it for myself and my dependents; I cannot do that.\" This reached ʿUthmān ؓ, so he bought it for thirty-five thousand dirhams. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, will you give me the like of what you gave him—a spring in Paradise—if I buy it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I have bought it and made it for the Muslims.\""],[1223,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever delivers a speech seeking nothing but ostentation and reputation, God ﷻ will make him stand in a position of ostentation and reputation.\""],[1224,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"A fire is about to emerge that will illuminate the necks of camels in Buṣrā, moving at the pace of a slow camel: it will travel by day and halt by night. It will go forth in the morning and return in the evening. It will be said: 'The fire has set out, O people, so set out!' The fire will say: 'O people, take your midday rest!' It will return, saying: 'O people, return!' Whoever it overtakes, it will consume.\""],[1225,"The Messenger of God ﷺ—his name in the pre-Islamic era was Zaḥm, and when he migrated the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Bashīr—said: While I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said to me: \"O Ibn al-Khaṣāṣiyyah, what have you come to resent about God?\" He said: \"I have not come to resent anything about God; all good has been done to me.\" He said: Then he came upon the graves of the Muslims and said: \"These attained much good\"—he said it three times. Then he came upon the graves of the polytheists and said: \"These missed much good\"—he said it three times. Then a glance occurred from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and there was a man walking on the graves wearing two sandals. The Prophet ﷺ called out to him: \"O owner of the two sandals, remove your sandals!\" The man looked and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he removed his sandals and threw them away. The wording is that of Muslim's hadith."],[1226,"And he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from this. He said: \"Only the Christians do that. Rather, my fasting is as God ﷻ commanded; then complete the fast until night, and when night comes, break the fast.\""],[1227,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Should I fast on Friday and not speak to anyone that day?\" He said: \"Do not fast on Friday except as part of days of which it is the last. As for not speaking to anyone, by my life, to speak and command good and forbid evil is better than to remain silent.\""],[1228,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He stipulated for me: \"You must testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger, perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, give zakāh, perform the pilgrimage to the House, and strive in the path of God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, as for two of them, I cannot bear them: zakāh—for by God, I have only ten camels that are the means of transport for my family and their baggage—and jihād—for they claim that whoever flees has incurred wrath from God, and I fear that if fighting confronts me, my soul will be frightened and I will hate death.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew his hand and shook it, then said: \"No charity and no jihād—will you enter Paradise?\" So I pledged allegiance to him on all of them."],[1229,"The Prophet ﷺ said, relating from his Lord, Exalted is He: \"Fasting is a shield with which My servant shields himself from the Fire. Fasting is for Me, and I reward it: he leaves his food and his desire for My sake. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person is sweeter to God ﷻ on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk.\""],[1232,"I married a virgin woman in her chamber, and I found her pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said, “As for the child, he is a slave for you. When she gives birth, flog her one hundred lashes, and she has the dower because of what he made lawful from her private part.”"],[1233,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Tarif b. al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, their ally."],[1234,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar b. al-Najjar: Bujayr b. Bujayr, an ally of theirs.”"],[1235,"Narrated Abu Huraira: \"The first person who saddled a ride in the mosque was Tamim al-Dari.\""],[1236,"“Tamim al-Dari bought a cloak for one thousand and used to pray in it.”"],[1237,"Tamim al-Dari asked 'Umar for permission to tell stories. He refused to grant him permission. Then he asked him again, and he refused to grant him permission. Then he asked him again, and he said, “If you wish,” and he gestured with his hand, meaning slaughter."],[1238,"A man of the people of Makkah said to me, 'This is the standing place of your brother Tamim al-Dari. I saw him stand in prayer one night until morning, or nearly until morning, reciting a verse from the Book of Allah ﷻ, then bowing, prostrating, and weeping: {Or do those who commit evil deeds think that We will make them like those who believe and do righteous deeds, equal in their life and their death? Evil is what they judge.}'"],[1239,"Tamim al-Dari kept repeating this verse until morning: {Or do those who commit evil deeds think...}"],[1240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, the devout obedience of a night is recorded for him.'"],[1241,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Whoever recites ten verses in a night, a qintar is recorded for him, and the qintar is better than this world and all it contains. On the Day of Resurrection, your Lord ﷻ will say: \"Recite and ascend; for every verse there is a degree,\" until he reaches the last verse he has with him. Your Lord ﷻ will say to the servant: \"Take hold.\" The servant will say, gesturing with his hand: \"My Lord, You know best.\" He will say: \"With this one, eternity; with this one, bliss.\"'"],[1242,"I entered upon Tamim al-Dari while he was governor of Jerusalem and he was cleaning barley for his horse. I said, 'O governor, is there no one to take care of this for you?' He said, 'No, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever cleans barley for his horse and then carries it until he hangs it on the horse, Allah records for every barley grain a good deed.\"'"],[1243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing the servant is brought to account for is the prayer; then the rest of the deeds.'"],[1244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing the servant is brought to account for is the prayer; then the rest of the deeds.'"],[1245,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The Friday prayer is obligatory except upon a woman, a child, a sick person, a slave, or a traveler.'"],[1246,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The right of the husband over the wife is that she not forsake his bed, that she keep his oath, that she obey his command, that she not leave except with his permission, and that she not admit into his presence anyone he dislikes.'"],[1247,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every ambiguous matter is forbidden; there is no ambiguity in the religion.'"],[1248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel.' It was asked, 'To whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'To Allah, to His Book, to the leaders of the believers, and to their common folk.'"],[1249,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'Religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel.' They said, 'To whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims and the believers, and to their common folk.'"],[1250,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. I said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common folk.\""],[1254,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the believers, and to their common folk.\""],[1255,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His angels, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the believers, or the Muslims, and to their common folk.\""],[1256,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel.\" They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Messenger, to His Book, to the leaders of the believers, and to the believers generally.\""],[1257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the good city, al-Madinah, and any of its mountain passes are guarded by an angel with an unsheathed sword. The Dajjal will never enter it.\" Abu Kurayb 'Uthman b. Zayd also said it."],[1258,"I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , calling for the congregational prayer. I left with a group of Ansar women until we reached the mosque. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , prayed the Dhuhr prayer with us, then he ascended the pulpit and faced us with a smiling face. Then he said, \"By Allah, I did not gather you out of desire or fear except for a story that Tamim ad-Dari told me. He came to me, embraced Islam, and pledged his allegiance. He informed me that he rode with thirty men from Lakhm and Juzam, who were two tribes from the Arab tribes of Yemen. They encountered the sea and were captured by the waves for a month. Then the waves cast them near the sunset to an island from the islands of the sea. There they encountered a creature that resembled neither its face nor its back. We asked, \"What are you, O creature?\" It spoke to us by the permission of Allah with a swift and fluent tongue, saying, \"I am Al-Jassasah.\" We asked, \"And what is Al-Jassasah?\" It said, \"You should go to that monastery in the farthest part of the island. There is a man who is eagerly awaiting news from you.\" So we went to the monastery and found the greatest man we had ever seen, with a beautiful physique. His eyes were wiped as if they had kohl on them, and his hands were tied to his neck. His feet were tied with shackles. We said to him, \"Who are you, O man?\" He replied, \"You should know that I am Al-Masih ad-Dajjal (the Anti-Christ). It will soon be announced for me to emerge, and as soon as I exit, I will step on every land of Arabia except Makkah and Madinah. Whenever I intend to approach them, an angel with a drawn sword prevents me from doing so.\" Abu Al-Ashhab said, \"Amir said, Fatimah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , raising his hands until his armpits were visible. Then he said, 'Shall I not inform you of the mystery of this matter?' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Shall I not inform you of its location?' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Rather, it is in Yemen.' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Rather, it is towards ash-Sham (Syria).' Then he fell unconscious for a while. Then he woke up and said, 'Rather, it is in Iraq. Rather, it is in Iraq. Rather, it is in Iraq.' He will emerge from a village called Asbahān, from a village named Rastqabath. He will emerge with seventy thousand people, and they will have banners with them, and there will be two"],[1259,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, a man who accepts Islam at my hands and then dies?\" He said, \"You have the most right among the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1260,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the Sunnah regarding a man from the people of disbelief who accepts Islam at the hands of a man from the Muslims?\" He said, \"He is the closest of the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1261,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, a man from the polytheists who accepts Islam at the hands of a man from the Muslims?\" He said, \"He is the closest of the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1262,"He used to give the Prophet ﷺ a container of wine every year. When the year in which it was forbidden came, he gave him a container, and the Prophet ﷺ smiled and said, \"It has been forbidden.\" He said, \"Shall I sell it?\" He said, \"Its buying and its price are unlawful.\""],[1263,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"There are people who cut off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep.\" He said, \"Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead.\""],[1264,"They said, \"O Messenger of God, there are people who cut off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep while they are alive.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion.\""],[1265,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, One, Single, Eternal, who has not taken a consort or a child, and there is none equal to Him, ten times, God will record for him forty thousand good deeds.\""],[1266,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to grant me land in Syria before it was conquered, and he gave it to me. Then Umar conquered it in his time, so I went to him and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me land from such-and-such to such-and-such.' So Umar ؓ made one third of it for the wayfarer, one third for its development, and one third for us."],[1267,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"This religion will continue to prevail until it reaches the houses of mud and houses of camel hair, until Allah makes Islam triumph and humiliates the disbelievers.\" Tameem said, \"I have witnessed that in my family, those who embraced Islam found goodness, honor, and prestige, while those who remained steadfast on disbelief suffered humiliation, servitude, and taxation.\""],[1268,"Tamim al-Dari reported—or I was informed about him—that Tamim al-Dari prayed two rak'ahs after Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ had prohibited prayer after Asr. So Umar came to him and struck him with the whip. Tamim gestured to him to sit while he was still in prayer, and Umar sat until Tamim finished. Then he said to Umar, 'Why did you strike me?' He said, 'Because you prayed these two rak'ahs, and I have prohibited them.' He said, 'Indeed I prayed them with one better than you—with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Umar ؓ said, 'It is not you, O group, that I fear for, but I fear that after you there will come a people who pray between Asr and Maghrib until they pass the hour in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited praying, just as they join between Zuhr and Asr. Then they will say: We saw so-and-so and so-and-so praying after Asr.'"],[1269,"Abu Rifa'ah used to heat water for his companions and say, 'Make your ablution excellent with this, for I will make mine excellent with this,' then he would perform ablution with cold water."],[1270,"It is the path of Abu Rifa'ah: I take it, and I strive in work after him with great striving."],[1271,"Abu Rifa'ah al-Adawi: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a stranger has come asking about his religion; he does not know what his religion is.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and left his sermon, then a chair was brought whose legs I thought were iron. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed it and began teaching me from what Allah had taught him. Then he returned to his sermon and completed it."],[1272,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution. He began by washing his face and forearms, then rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nostrils, then wiped his head."],[1273,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe with water over his beard and his feet."],[1274,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do you enter upon me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would command them to use the siwāk at every prayer.”"],[1275,"Abu al-Hasan al-Mazini: 'The grandfather of Amr b. Yahya, whose name was Tamim b. Amr. Ali b. Abi Talib appointed him over Madinah when he went to Iraq, when Sahl b. Hunayf went to him.'"],[1276,"From Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Khudrah b. Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Tamim b. Yu'ar b. Qays b. Adiy."],[1277,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Tamim b. Yu'ar b. Qays b. Adiy b. Umayyah."],[1278,"From Urwah: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Tamim, the mawla of Banu Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws b. Harithah.'"],[1279,"From Ibn Shihab: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Tamim, the mawla of Banu Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws.'"],[1280,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Anṣār: Tamīm, the freedman of Khirāsh b. al-Ṣimma.”"],[1281,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Khazraj, then from Banū Salama: Tamīm, the freedman of Khirāsh b. al-Ṣimma.”"],[1282,"From ʿUrwa, in naming those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Ajnādayn, then from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm b. Huṣayṣ: Tamīm b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays."],[1283,"From Ibn Shihāb, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Ajnādayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: Tamīm b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays."],[1284,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to feed me and measure out for me a mudd, and I would set it aside and eat with the people until it became food. He said: And al-Talib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: You fed me a mudd on such-and-such a day, and I collected it until today. He said: “So the Prophet ﷺ borrowed it from him, and he had from him what he used to measure out for him before that.”"],[1285,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Hospitality is a binding right for three days; whatever is after that is charity.”"],[1286,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, seek forgiveness for me. He said: “When permission is given to you – or until permission is given to you.” He said: So he waited as long as God willed, then he called him and wiped his hand over his face and said: “O God, forgive al-Talib and have mercy on him,” three times."],[1287,"“I accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and I did not hear any prohibition regarding the small creatures of the earth.”"],[1288,"“A man manumitted a portion of a slave he owned, and the Prophet ﷺ did not make him liable for the remainder.”"],[1289,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do I see you coming to me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have made the siwāk obligatory upon them just as prayer has been made obligatory upon them.”"],[1290,"From Abū ʿAlī al-Ṣayqal, the freedman of Banū Asad, from Jaʿfar b. Tammām b. ʿAbbās, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do you enter upon me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would command them to use the siwāk at every purification.”"],[1291,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say during his march to Khaybar to 'Amir b. al-Akwa'—and al-Akwa's name was Sinan—\"Take for us some of your songs.\" So he dismounted and recited rajaz poetry for the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1292,"\"Urwa narrated that the person who was killed on the day of Yamama from the Ansar, and then from the Banu Harith bin Khazraj, was Thabit bin Qais bin Shammass.\""],[1293,"\"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas was martyred on that day, in the year twelve.\""],[1294,"\"O God, I declare myself innocent before You of what these people have brought, and I apologize for what these people have done.\" Then he was killed. He had a coat of mail that was stolen. A man saw him in a dream, and he said, \"My coat of mail is in a pot under the brazier in such-and-such a place,\" and he charged him with some instructions. They sought the coat of mail and found it, and they carried out the instructions."],[1295,"\"Thabit b. Qays was the orator of the Ansar.\""],[1296,"The Prophet ﷺ missed Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas. A man said, \"I know his news, O Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He went to him and found him in his house with his head bowed, weeping. He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has been missing you.\" He said, \"I raised my voice above the voice of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so my deeds are nullified and I am among the people of the Fire.\" The man came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Go back to him and tell him that he is not of the people of the Fire and that he is of the people of the Garden.\""],[1297,"Thabit came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God forbade us to be praised for what we have not done, and I am a man who loves praise; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice; and He forbade us arrogance, and I am a man who loves beauty.\" He said, \"O Thabit, would you not like to live praised and be killed as a martyr?\" So he was killed on the day of al-Yamama."],[1298,"He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of God, by God, I fear that I have been destroyed.' He said, 'By what?' I said, 'God forbade a man to be praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; God forbade arrogance, and I find myself loving arrogance; and God forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' So he lived praised and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima.\""],[1299,"He said, \"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"By what?\" He said, \"God forbids us to be praised for what we have not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I am a man who loves beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O Thabit b. Qays, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\""],[1300,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said to him, \"Why?\" He said, \"God forbade a man to love to be praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I find myself loving beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" So he lived praised and was killed on the day of Musaylima."],[1301,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God, the Exalted, forbade us praise—that we be praised for what we have not done—and I love praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I love beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" So he lived praised and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima the Liar."],[1302,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God prevents a man from being praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbids arrogance, and I find myself loving beauty; and God forbids us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am loud-voiced.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, do you not want to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\""],[1303,"When this verse was revealed: \"{Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet}\" (Q 49:2), Thabit sat in the road weeping. 'Asim b. 'Adi passed by him and said, \"What makes you weep, O Thabit?\" He said, \"I have a loud voice, and I fear that this verse was revealed concerning me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O my son, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"I am content with the good tidings of God and His Messenger. I will never raise my voice above the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Then it was revealed: \"{Indeed, those who lower their voices}\" (Q 49:3), the verse."],[1304,"Pride was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke sternly about it, saying, “Indeed, Allah does not love any arrogant boaster.” A man among the people said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I wash my clothes and their whiteness pleases me, and the strap of my sandal and the thong of my whip please me.” He said, “That is not pride. Pride is only to reject the truth and to scorn people.”"],[1305,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he recited this verse: “Indeed, Allah does not love any arrogant boaster.” He mentioned pride and magnified it, and Thabit b. Qays wept. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him, “What makes you weep?” He replied, “O Prophet of Allah, I love beauty, so much so that I would be pleased if the strap of my sandal were fine.” He said, “Then you are one of the people of Paradise. Pride is not that you make your mount and your saddle fine; rather pride is one who rejects the truth and despises people.”"],[1306,"I came to the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer. When the Prophet ﷺ said the salutation, he turned to me while I was praying. The Prophet ﷺ kept looking at me as I prayed. When I finished, he said, “Did you not pray with us?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then what is this prayer?” I replied, “O Messenger of Allah, the two rak‘ahs of Fajr. I left my house and had not prayed them.” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not find fault with me for that.”"],[1307,"I heard my father say when the following verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Indeed, Allah does not like everyone self-deluded and boastful\" (Quran 57:23), the difficulty intensified for Thabit. He closed the door and started crying. He was informed about the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ, who sent for him and asked him about the hardship he was going through. Thabit explained that he was a man who loved beauty and being from a black-skinned people, he was feeling dejected. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You are not one of them. Instead, you will live well, die well, and Allah will admit you into Paradise.\" When Allah revealed the verse, \"O you who have believed, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet or be loud to him in speech\" (Quran 49:2), Thabit started practicing it. He informed the Prophet ﷺ, who sent for him and told him that he had been too loud and that he was concerned his deeds might go to waste. The Prophet ﷺ assured him, \"You are not one of them. Instead, you will live well, die well, and Allah will admit you into Paradise.\" When Abu Bakr mobilized the Muslims against the apostates of Al-Riddah, the Battle of Yamama, and Musaylima the Liar, Thabit bin Qais joined the campaign. They faced Musaylima and the Banu Hanifa three times, and the Muslims were defeated each time. Thabit said, \"O Saeed, my servant of Abu Hudhaifa, this is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" They dug a trench for themselves and fought until they were both killed. I dreamt of a Muslim man, Thabit bin Qais, who said, \"Yesterday, after I was killed, a Muslim man passed by me and took a beautiful shield from me. He has his tent in the furthest part of the camp, and there is a horse tied in front of it, with a saddle placed on the horse's back.\" Thabit asked Saeed to inform Khalid bin Walid and ask him to collect the shield and inform the Caliph, Abu Bakr, about his debt, his share of the money, and the enslaved person who served him. He advised him not to say it was a dream. Saeed went to Khalid bin Walid and described the shield as Thabit had mentioned. He also went to Abu Bakr and informed him about what was said. After the death of Abu Bakr, his testament became known, and we do not know of anyone whose testament was carried out after their death except Thabit bin Qais bin Shammash."],[1308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you.”"],[1309,"We fight the enemy facing them, and how evil is what you have accustomed your peers to. By Allah, this is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[1310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping."],[1311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition before the Umrah to Najd, whose commander was Thabit b. Aqram. Thabit b. Aqram was killed in it."],[1312,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from Banu Amr b. Mabdhul: Thabit b. Atik."],[1313,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"Concerning the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar: Thabit b. al-Jidh'.\""],[1314,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit b. Hazzal b. 'Amr."],[1315,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit b. Rabi'a."],[1316,"From Ibn Shihab: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. 'Amr b. Zayd b. 'Adi.\""],[1317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted on the day of Khaybar to Sahla bt. 'Asim b. 'Adi and to a daughter of hers who was born."],[1318,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he entered upon him and said, \"Remove the hardship, O Lord of the people, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas.\" Then he took some soil from a plate containing water and poured it on him."],[1319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever kills himself with poison will be punished with it. Whoever testifies against a Muslim — or he said, against a believer — of disbelief, it is like killing him. Whoever curses him, it is like killing him. Whoever falsely swears by a religion other than Islam, he is as he swore.”"],[1320,"Hammad said, “Even if you said it is marfu‘, I would not mind.” He said, “Whoever falsely swears by a religion other than Islam, he is as he said.”"],[1321,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever falsely swears by a religion other than Islam, he is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it in the Fire of Hell. Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever charges a believer with disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever falsely swears by a religion other than Islam, he is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something, he will be killed with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever deliberately kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection in the Fire of Hell. Whoever deliberately and falsely swears by a religion other than Islam, he is as he said. Whoever charges a believer with disbelief is like killing him. Whoever curses a believer is like killing him.”"],[1325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever accuses a believing man or woman of disbelief is like killing him. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A servant has no vow in what he does not possess.”"],[1326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no vow concerning what one does not possess, and cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said, and whoever says to a believer, ‘O disbeliever,’ it is like killing him.”"],[1327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1328,"He informed him that he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under the tree, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess.”"],[1329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter.”"],[1331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess.”"],[1332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said. The son of Adam is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever curses a believer is like killing him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1333,"The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely and deliberately is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something, Allah will punish him with it in the fire of Hell.”"],[1334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no oath in disobedience to Allah, nor concerning what the son of Adam does not possess. Whoever curses a Muslim is like killing him. Whoever calls a Muslim a disbeliever has indeed disbelieved. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely and deliberately is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something by which he dies is in the Fire.”"],[1335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever declares a Muslim a disbeliever, one of them incurs it.” Abu al-Qasim said: “This Abu Abdullah is called Khalid al-Hadhdha’, and Khalid has two kunyas: Abu Munazil and Abu Abdullah.”"],[1336,"A man made a vow during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to slaughter a camel at Buwana. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I vowed to slaughter at Buwana.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Was there any idol among the idols of the Jahiliyyah worshipped there?” He said, “No.” He said, “Was there any festival among their festivals held there?” He said, “No.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fulfill your vow, for there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in severing ties of kinship, nor concerning what the son of Adam does not possess.”"],[1337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping."],[1338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, wearing a cloak wrapped around him, placing his hand on it to protect himself from the cold of the pebbles."],[1339,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Thabit b. Aqram b. Tha'labah b. Adiyy b. al-Ajlan."],[1340,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Ajlan: Thabit b. Aqram."],[1341,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Adiyy b. Malik b. al-Najjar b. Aws: Thabit b. al-Mundhir b. Haram b. Amr b. Zayd Manat b. Adiyy b. Amr."],[1342,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who were killed on the day of al-Yamamah from the Muslims, then from the Ansar, then from Banu Malik b. Taym Allah: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man b. Khansa'."],[1343,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man."],[1344,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man b. Khansa'."],[1345,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the Bridge of al-Mada'in with Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas from the Ansar, then from Banu Amr b. Mabdhul: Thabit b. Atik."],[1346,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those killed on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar: Thabit b. Atik."],[1347,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended the 'Aqaba pledge from the Ansar: Thabit b. Ajda'."],[1348,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salama, then from Banu Haram: Thabit b. Tha'laba b. Zayd b. al-Harith b. Haram."],[1349,"He was called al-Jidh'.\""],[1350,"From Ibn Shihab: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Adi b. al-Najjar: Thabit b. Hassan b. 'Amr; he had no descendants.\""],[1351,"A lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"A nation that was transformed—and Allah knows best.\""],[1352,"A man from Banu Fazarah brought the Prophet ﷺ some lizards he had hunted. He began turning one of them over in front of him, and the Prophet said: \"A nation that was transformed.\" And the best of my knowledge is that he said: \"I do not know what happened to it, and I do not know—perhaps this is one of them.\""],[1353,"A roasted lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ took a stick and began counting its toes, then said: \"A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I do not know which beasts they are.\" So he did not eat from it, nor did he forbid it."],[1354,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people caught some lizards, roasted them, and ate them. I caught one of them, roasted it, then brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He took a palm branch and began counting its toes with it, then said: \"A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I think it may be that.\" I said: \"The people have roasted them and eaten them.\" He neither ate nor forbade."],[1355,"The Jews used to say that if a small child of theirs died, they would say he is a truthful one (siddiq). That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: \"The Jews have lied. There is no soul that Allah creates in its mother's womb except that it is either wretched or blessed.\" So Allah ﷻ then revealed this verse: {He is most knowing of you when He produced you from the earth and when you were fetuses in the wombs of your mothers} – the entire verse."],[1356,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Thabit b. 'Amr b. Zayd b. 'Adi b. Sawwad b. 'Usaymah, or 'Usayyah, an ally of theirs from Ashja'."],[1357,"We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar, and the people plundered them. The Prophet ﷺ came while their cooking pots were boiling. He said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"Plunder, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Overturn them, for plunder is not permissible.\" So they overturned what remained in them."],[1358,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass by cooking pots containing meat of sheep they had plundered. He ordered them to be overturned and said: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\""],[1359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plunder."],[1360,"We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar and plundered them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while their cooking pots were boiling. They said: \"It is plunder.\" He said: \"Overturn the cooking pots, for plunder is not permissible.\""],[1361,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me captive when I was a young man, and I heard him ﷺ forbidding plunder and ordering that the cooking pots of domestic donkey meat be overturned."],[1362,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"We do not eat plunder, for it is not permissible.\" I said to Simak: \"What is this plunder that the Prophet ﷺ forbade?\" He said: \"Tha'labah said: It is sheep they plundered on the day of Khaybar before it was distributed. So the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Overturn the cooking pots.'\""],[1363,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\" A group plundered sheep, and they informed him. So the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Overturn the cooking pots and what is in them.\""],[1364,"We captured sheep belonging to the enemy and plundered them. We set up our cooking pots, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by the cooking pots and ordered them to be overturned. Then he said: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\""],[1365,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and I heard him forbidding plunder and ordering that the cooking pots be overturned."],[1366,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God (mighty and majestic is He) will say to the scholars on the Day of Resurrection, when He sits on His throne to judge His servants: 'I did not place My knowledge and My wisdom among you except that I intend to forgive you for what is in you, and I do not care.'"],[1367,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, plunder is not permissible.\""],[1368,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever withholds the right of a person by making a false oath, a black spot will be written on his heart. And as long as that spot remains on his heart, it will not be changed by anything till the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1369,"A man from Banu Tha'labah b. Yarbu' came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, and he was saying: \"The upper hand is the giving hand. Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then your nearest, then your nearest.\" A man from the Ansar stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, these Banu Tha'labah b. Yarbu' struck so-and-so in the pre-Islamic period.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ shouted: \"No soul shall bear the burden of another.\""],[1370,"The Jews are disbelievers who did not believe in Muhammad, and none followed him except our evil ones. Even if they were among our best, they would not have abandoned their religion of their forefathers. So Allah revealed concerning them from His saying, \"They are not equal to the people of the Book\" to His saying \"from the righteous.\""],[1371,"That the Prophet ﷺ stood as a preacher and commanded the zakat al-fitr for the young and the old, the free and the slave: one sa' of dates or one sa' of barley for each individual, or for each head, and one sa' of wheat between two."],[1372,"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us in the hadith of Ibn Abi Rafi': \"Tha'labah b. Qayzi b. Sakhr b. Salamah, a Badri.\""],[1373,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim, then from Banu Haram: Tha'labah, the one called al-Jidh'.\""],[1374,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled, the last person of his household he would bid farewell to was Fatimah, and when he returned, the first person he would visit was her. He said: He arrived from a military expedition or journey of his, and behold, Fatimah had hung a cloth on her door and adorned al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two silver bracelets. He turned back. She thought he turned back only because of what he saw, so she removed the curtain and removed the bracelets from the two boys and cut them off, then gave them to the two boys. They came to the Prophet ﷺ crying, and he said, “O Thawban, take these two and go with them to a household in Madinah” – I think he said – “who are needy, for these are my household, and I dislike that they consume their good things in their worldly life.” Then he said, “O Thawban, buy for Fatimah a necklace of ‘asab (beads) and two bracelets of ivory.”"],[1375,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever you see reciting poetry in the mosque, say to him, ‘May Allah break your mouth,’ three times; and whoever you see announcing a lost item in the mosque, say to him, ‘May you not find it,’ three times; and whoever you see buying and selling in the mosque, say to him, ‘May Allah not make your trade profitable.’” Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed us."],[1376,"I heard Ma‘n b. Yazid say, “I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled in my favor, delivered a sermon on my behalf, and married me; and I and my grandfather pledged allegiance to him.”"],[1377,"That 'Amr b. Habib b. 'Abd Shams came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I stole a camel belonging to Banu So-and-so.\" The Prophet ﷺ sent to them, and they said, \"We have indeed missed a camel of ours.\" The Prophet ﷺ ordered, and his hand was cut off. Tha'labah said: I was looking at him when his hand fell, and he was saying, \"Praise be to God who purified me through you. I wanted you to enter my body into the Fire.\""],[1378,"A dispute was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning the flood channel of Banu Qurayzah, Mahzur. The Messenger of God ﷺ judged among them that water should be allowed to reach the ankles, and it should not be held back except by the lowest landowner."],[1379,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no harm and no reciprocating harm.\""],[1380,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no harm and no reciprocating harm.\""],[1381,"From Ibn Shihab, \"in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from the Aws, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Umayyah b. Zayd: Tha'labah b. Hatib.\""],[1382,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then Banu Sa'idah: Tha'labah b. Sa'idah b. Malik b. Khalid b. Tha'labah b. Harithah b. 'Amr b. al-Khazraj."],[1383,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu Sa'idah: Tha'labah b. Sa'd b. Malik."],[1384,"From 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Tha'labah b. Mihsan b. 'Amr b. 'Ubayd.\""],[1385,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who were killed on the day of the Bridge of al-Mada'in with Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. Mabdhul: Tha'labah b. 'Amr b. Mihsan.\""],[1386,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In the naming of those who were killed on the day of the Bridge in the year fifteen: Tha'labah b. 'Amr b. Mihsan.\""],[1387,"He was called al-Jidh'."],[1388,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salamah, then from Banu Haram: Tha'labah, the one called al-Jidh'.\""],[1389,"\"My brother Tha'labah b. Sa'd witnessed Badr and was killed on the day of Uhud, and he left no offspring.\""],[1390,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Tha'labah b. 'Anamah b. 'Adi.\""],[1391,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In the naming of those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge from the Ansar: Tha'labah b. 'Anamah b. 'Adi.\""],[1392,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Khandaq from the Ansar, then from Banu Salamah: Tha'labah b. 'Anamah.\""],[1393,"He was called Thumamah. He was in charge of San'a'. When 'Uthman ؓ was killed, he gave a sermon and wept profusely. When he regained consciousness and composure, he said: \"Today the caliphate of prophethood has been wrested from the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ and has become kingship and tyranny. Whoever takes something overpowers it.\""],[1394,"He said, \"There was a prince in Sana'a. Abu Qahtham, also known as Thumamah bin Adiy, was his companion. When the news of the death of so-and-so came, he cried intensely. When he woke up, he said, 'This is when the caliphate of prophethood was removed and became a monarchy and tyranny, whoever becomes dominant over something becomes its ruler.'\""],[1395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[1396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever begs when he has what suffices him, there will be a blemish on his face on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1397,"ﷺ said: “Whoever leaves a treasure, it will be represented to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed venomous serpent with two fangs, which will pursue him and say: ‘I am your treasure that you left behind you.’ It will keep pursuing him until it forces him to put his hand [into its mouth], and it will chew it, then it will pursue the rest of his body.”"],[1398,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the turban.” — meaning the head covering."],[1399,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he said, \"Indeed, this journey is laborious and burdensome. So, when one of you wants to sleep, let him pray two units of prayer. If he wakes up, then it will be for him. Otherwise, they will be for him.\""],[1400,"The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered his sacrificial animal and said: “Prepare some of it for us.” So we prepared some for him, and I kept feeding him from it until we reached Madinah."],[1401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “For every act of forgetfulness there are two prostrations after the salutation.”"],[1402,"I heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying: \"Verily, my Lord has promised me seventy thousand from my Ummah (nation), who will not be held accountable with every seventy thousand.\""],[1403,"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a rabbi from among the Jewish scholars came and said: “Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.” I pushed him with a shove that nearly knocked him over. He said: “Why do you push me?” I said: “Why don’t you say: O Messenger of God?” The Jew said: “We call him only by the name his family gave him.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “My name is Muhammad, the name my family gave me.” The Jew said: “I have come to ask you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Will anything benefit you if I tell you?” He said: “I will listen with my ear.” So he made marks on the ground with a stick he had and said: “Ask.” The Jew said: “Where will people be on the day when the earth is changed to another earth and the heavens too?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They will be in darkness before the bridge.” He said: “Who will be the first people to cross?” He said: “The poor among the emigrants.” The Jew said: “What will be their greeting when they enter Paradise?” He said: “A portion of the liver of the whale.” He said: “What will be their food after that?” He said: “The bull of Paradise, which eats from its pastures, will be slaughtered for them.” He said: “What will they drink after it?” He said: “From a spring called Salsabil.” He said: “You have spoken the truth. I have come to ask you about something that no one on earth knows except a prophet or one or two men.” He said: “Will it benefit you if I tell you?” He said: “I will listen with my ear.” He said: “I have come to ask you about the child.” He said: “The man’s fluid is white and the woman’s fluid is yellow. When they meet and the man’s fluid prevails over the woman’s fluid, it is a male by God’s permission, and when the woman’s fluid prevails over the man’s fluid, it is a female by God’s permission.” The Jew said: “You have spoken the truth, and you are a prophet.” Then he left and went away. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “This man asked me about that which he asked me, and I had no knowledge of any of it until God informed me.”"],[1404,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the bribe-taker, the bribe-giver, and the one who goes between them.”"],[1405,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are performing deeds that are not recognized, and soon the unmarried man will return to his family, either happy or distressed.”"],[1406,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man who was cupping during Ramadan while he was lending money to another man, and he said: “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.”"],[1407,"I heard Thawban say: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade “wearing gold rings, al-qassi garments, dyed garments of yellow, and animal-skin mats.”"],[1408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now visit them, and make your visit to them a prayer for them and a request of forgiveness for them. I had forbidden you to eat the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, but now eat from them and store some. I had forbidden you from that which is fermented in gourds, green jars, and pitch-covered vessels, but now ferment in them and make use of them.”"],[1409,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Three things with which no deed benefits: associating partners with God, disobedience to parents, and fleeing from the battlefield.”"],[1410,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Compeller, Exalted is He, will come on the Day of Resurrection, place His foot on the bridge, and say: 'By My might and majesty, no wrongdoer shall pass Me.' Then He will render justice to the creation, some from others, to the extent that He will even render justice for the hornless sheep against the horned one by a butt that it butted.\""],[1411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping performed, gave the cupper his wage, and said: \"Feed it to the water-carrying camel.\""],[1412,"Forty men from the Companions gathered to discuss fate and predestination. Among them were Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. Then the trustworthy spirit, Jibril ﷺ , descended and said, \"O Muhammad, go out to your nation, for they have innovated.\" So he went out to them in a moment in which he had never gone out before, and they denied this from him. He came out with a reddish complexion, and his cheeks seemed as if they were sprinkled with sour pomegranate. They hurriedly approached the Messenger of Allah with their hearts throbbing, their palms trembling, and their arms shivering. They said, \"Seek forgiveness for us from Allah and His Messenger.\" The Prophet, ﷺ , replied, \"I am closer to you. If you were about to force me to divulge information, then indeed, the trustworthy spirit came to me and said, 'Go out to your nation, O Muhammad, for they have fabricated falsehood.'\""],[1413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Banu al-Abbas will have two banners; its highest is disbelief and its center is misguidance. If you reach it, do not go astray.\""],[1414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was shown Banu Marwan taking turns on my pulpit, and that grieved me. And I saw Banu al-Abbas taking turns on my pulpit, and that pleased me.\""],[1415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do I have to do with Banu al-Abbas? They led my Ummah astray, shed its blood, and clothed it in black garments. May Allah clothe them in garments of fire.\""],[1416,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When my Companions are mentioned, refrain; when the stars are mentioned, refrain; when divine decree is mentioned, refrain.\""],[1417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He had struck his sister at the beginning of the night while she was reciting: \"Read in the name of your Lord who created\" (Quran 96:1) until I thought he had killed her. Then he got up before dawn and heard her voice reciting: \"Read in the name of your Lord who created.\" He said: \"By Allah, this is not poetry or muttering.\" So he went until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Bilal at the door. He pushed the door. Bilal said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said: \"Until I ask permission for you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Bilal said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Umar is at the door.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If Allah wills good for Umar, He will admit him into the religion.\" Then he said to Bilal: \"Open.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his upper arms, shook him, and said: \"What do you want, and what have you come for?\" Umar said to him: \"Present to me what you call to.\" He said: \"You testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" Umar embraced Islam on the spot, and he said: \"Go out.\""],[1418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the millstone of Islam is turning.\" He was asked: \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Present my hadith to the Book. Whatever agrees with it is from me, and I said it.\""],[1419,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Allah has pardoned my Ummah for three things: mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do.\""],[1420,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"There will be peoples from my Ummah whose jurists engage in complex questions. Those are the worst of my Ummah.\""],[1421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is forbidden by suckling is forbidden by lineage.\""],[1422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who will guarantee me that he will not ask people for anything, and I will guarantee him Paradise?\" Thawban said: \"I will.\" And Thawban never asked anyone for anything after that."],[1423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will guarantee me one quality, and I will guarantee him Paradise?” I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Do not ask people for anything.” He (the narrator) said: “Indeed, Thawban’s whip would fall while he was on his camel, and a man would go to hand it to him, but he would make his camel kneel and take his whip himself.”"],[1424,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and said: “We are traveling by night, so let no weak or unruly (mount) enter with us.” A man set off on a difficult she-camel, and it threw him, and his thigh was broken, and he died. The Prophet ﷺ ordered the funeral prayer over him, then ordered Bilal, who called out three times: “Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient person.”"],[1425,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “My cistern is between Aden and Oman. Its water is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey, and those who come to it most are the poor among the Emigrants.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the poor among the Emigrants? He said: “Those with disheveled hair and soiled clothes, who do not marry women who are inaccessible, for whom the doors of the great are not opened, who give the right that is upon them and are not given what is due to them.”"],[1426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things do not break the fast: cupping, vomiting, and nocturnal emission, but the fasting person should not vomit deliberately.”"],[1427,"I heard Thawban ؓ say: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man among his companions who had a ring of copper on his hand, and he said: “What is this?” He said: For the pain of the vein (wāhina). He said: “Remove it from you.”"],[1428,"He narrated to us from the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ vomit, and he broke his fast.”"],[1429,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.”"],[1430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nothing repels fate except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness. Indeed, a man is deprived of provision because of a sin he commits.”"],[1431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, my cistern is between Aden and Oman. Its cups are as numerous as the stars, and its water is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey. The first to come to it are the poor among the Emigrants.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: “Those with disheveled hair and soiled clothes, who do not marry inaccessible women, for whom the doors of the great are not opened, who give what is upon them and are not given what is due to them.”"],[1432,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that among the best of your deeds is prayer and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 278)"],[1433,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person remains in the khurfa of Paradise.” It was said: What is the khurfa of Paradise? He said: “Its picked fruit.”"],[1434,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person remains in the khurfa of Paradise until he returns.”"],[1435,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.”"],[1436,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “When a man plucks (a fruit) from Paradise, another grows in its place.”"],[1437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you is afflicted (by it), fever is a piece of the fire of Hell, so let him extinguish it from himself with cold running water, facing the flow of the water, and let him say after dawn before sunrise: ‘O Allah, confirm Your Messenger and heal Your servant.’ Let him immerse himself in it three times. If he is not cured in five (days), then in seven; and if he is not cured in seven, then in nine, for it will hardly exceed nine by Allah’s permission.”"],[1438,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six (days) of Shawwal, that is the fasting of a year.”"],[1439,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The nations are about to call one another against you,” and he mentioned the hadith."],[1440,"And among those killed on the day of Khaybar from Quraysh, then from Banu ‘Abd Manaf, was Thaqif b. ‘Amr, an ally of theirs from Banu Asad b. Jazimah."],[1441,"“The Prophet ﷺ sent Ja‘far to Mu’tah in Jumada of the year eight.”"],[1442,"“Ja‘far b. Abi Talib wore a ring on his right hand.”"],[1443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the companions of Mu’tah from the pulpit, one by one: he began with Zayd b. Harithah, then Ja‘far b. Abi Talib, then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah, may Allah have mercy on them. He said, “Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the banner, and he is a sword among the swords of Allah.”"],[1444,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of Zaid and his companions before receiving the news, and his eyes were filled with tears."],[1445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army and appointed Zayd b. Harithah over them, saying, “If he is killed or martyred, your commander is Ja‘far b. Abi Talib; and if he is killed or martyred, your commander is ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah.” They set out and met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Ja‘far b. Abi Talib took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the banner, and Allah ﷻ granted victory through him. Their news reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he came out, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: your brothers met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Ja‘far took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah granted victory through him.” Then he gave the family of Ja‘far three days before coming to them. Then he came to them and said, “Do not weep for him after today.” Then he said, “Bring me the sons of my brother.” We were brought to him as if we were chicks. He said, “Call the barber for me,” and ordered him, and he shaved our heads. Then he said, “As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib; and as for ‘Awn, he resembles my physical appearance and character.” Then he took my hand and raised it, saying, “O Allah, be a successor for Ja‘far in his family, and bless ‘Abd Allah in the transaction of his right hand.” He said it three times. Then our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?”"],[1446,"From his sorrel horse, then he fought the people until he was killed."],[1447,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Zayd b. Harithah as commander during the expedition of Mu'tah and said, \"If Zayd is killed, then Ja'far; and if Ja'far is killed, then 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah.\" 'Abd Allah said, \"I was with them in that expedition, and we sought Ja'far and found that he had received something over ninety wounds between stabs and shots.\""],[1448,"\"We missed Ja'far b. Abi Talib, so we searched for him and found him among the slain. We found in him more than ninety wounds between sword strikes, spear stabs, and arrow shots, and we found that all of them were in the front of his body.\""],[1449,"He informed him that he stood over Ja'far that day while he was slain. He said, \"I counted in him fifty wounds between stabs and strikes, none of which was in his back.\""],[1450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I entered Paradise last night and looked around in it, and there was Ja'far flying with the angels.\""],[1451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib as an angel flying in Paradise, possessing two wings with which he flies wherever he wishes, the leading feathers of his wings dyed with blood.\""],[1452,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was shown them in a dream and saw Ja'far as an angel with two wings stained with blood, and Zayd opposite him on the couch.\""],[1453,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after conquering Khaybar, it was said to him, \"Ja'far has arrived from the Negus.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not know which of the two makes me happier: the arrival of Ja'far or the conquest of Khaybar.\" Then he kissed him between his eyes."],[1454,"When Ja'far came from the emigration to Abyssinia, the Prophet ﷺ met him, embraced him, kissed him between his eyes, and said, \"I do not know which of the two makes me more joyful: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja'far.\""],[1455,"\"When the death of Ja'far came, we recognized grief in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them something that preoccupy them.\""],[1457,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shown in a dream the companions of Mu'tah, and he saw Ja'far as an angel with two wings stained with blood, meaning dyed.\""],[1458,"Peace be upon you, O son of the one with two wings."],[1459,"Ja'far b. Abi Talib was killed on the day of Mu'tah in al-Balqa'."],[1460,"I used to ask 'Ali ؓ for something and he would refuse me, so I would say, 'By the right of Ja'far,' and when I said, 'By the right of Ja'far,' he gave it to me."],[1461,"Washing from major ritual impurity was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"As for me, I pour water over my head three times.\""],[1462,"Ja'far used to love the poor, sitting with them, talking to them and they talking to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call him Abu al-Masakin (the father of the poor)."],[1463,"And he said, \"What do you say?\" So we said, \"Indeed, our people worship idols, and indeed Allah has sent a Messenger to us, so we believed in him and affirmed him.\" So Najashi said to them, \"Are they your slaves?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then they are free from any debt from you?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"So leave them alone.\" So we left his presence. 'Amr bin Al-Aas said, \"Indeed, these people say about 'Isa (Jesus) what you do not say.\" He said, \"If they do not say about 'Isa what I say, I will not leave them in my land for a moment of the day.\" He said, \"So he sent for us, and his invitation was tougher on us than the first. So he said, \"What does your companion say about 'Isa ibn Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary)?\" So we said, \"He says he is the Spirit of Allah and His word, which He bestowed upon the Virgin Mary.\" He said, \"So he sent for them and said, \"Summon this priest and this monk.\" So people from among them came to him, and he said, \"What do you say about 'Isa ibn Maryam?\" They said, \"You know best.\" He said, \"So what do you say?\" Najashi took something from the ground, and said, \"This is what 'Isa says. He does not exceed what these people say.\" Then he said to them, \"Does anyone harm you?\" They said, \"Yes.\" So he commanded a caller to announce, \"Whoever harms any of them will be granted an allowance of four dirhams.\" Then he said, \"Is this enough for you?\" They said, \"No.\" So he doubled it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated to Al-Madinah and appeared there, we said to Najashi, \"Indeed, our companion has left for Al-Madinah and has appeared there, and he emigrated and killed those whom we informed you about, and we wanted to join him.\" So he provided us with what we needed and said, \"Inform your companion of what I have done for you, and this is my Messenger with you, and I testify that there is no god but Allah, and that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" So tell him to seek forgiveness for me.\" Ja'far said, \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, performed ablution, then he prayed three times, 'O Allah, forgive Najashi.' And the Muslims said, 'Ameen.' Ja'far said, \"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , 'Leave now and inform your companion about what you have seen of the Prophet ﷺ .' And the wording is that of the hadith of Muhammad bin Adam.\""],[1464,"A messenger was sent among us whose tongue, truthfulness, and fidelity we knew. He called us to worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, and to abandon what our people and others besides them worshipped besides Him. He commanded us to do what is right and forbade us from what is wrong, and commanded us to pray, fast, give charity, and maintain family ties. He called us to what we knew, and he recited to us a revelation that came from Allah, which nothing else resembles. We believed him, had faith in him, and knew that what he brought was the truth from Allah. At that point our people parted from us, harmed us, and overpowered us. When they had reached with us what we detested and we were unable to defend ourselves against them, we went out to your land and chose you over anyone else. Al-Najashi said, 'Go, for you are sayūm (secure) in my land. Whoever insults you will pay a fine.'"],[1465,"They mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.' Then he gestured with his hand as if pouring with both of them over his head."],[1466,"Washing from janabah was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.'"],[1467,"We learned from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ how to perform the ritual purification after sexual impurity (janabah). The Prophet ﷺ said, \"As for me, I pour water on my head three times and then I wash my head to purify it from janabah.\""],[1468,"We learned about performing the ritual of washing after sexual impurity from the Prophet Muhammad (PBUH). One of us asked, \"What should we do?\" The Prophet (PBUH) answered, \"As for me, I take a handful of water and pour it on my head, and then I pour water on the rest of my body.\""],[1469,"From Jubayr b. Mut'im that they mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times,' and he gestured with both of his hands."],[1470,"We argued about washing in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour three handfuls of water over my head.'"],[1471,"They argued in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about washing from janabah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.'"],[1472,"Washing was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, it suffices me to pour over my head three times a handful of water from janabah.'"],[1473,"We mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'As for me, I perform wudu' as I do for prayer, then I take a handful of water three times and pour it over my head, then I wash.'"],[1474,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A Qurashi has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh.\" A questioner asked Ibn Shihab what he meant by that, and he said, \"Soundness of judgment.\""],[1475,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1476,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, who said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1477,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the ransom of the people of Badr, and I heard him recite in the Maghrib prayer: \"By the Mount, and a Book inscribed\" (Q 52:1-2)."],[1478,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, and Muad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, and Musaddad said: They said, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Muhammad ibn Jubair ibn Mut'im from his father that he heard the Prophet saw reciting in al-Maghrib \"At-Tur\". And the wording is for al-Humaidi."],[1479,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer."],[1480,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting al-Tur(surah lii) in the sunset prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 811)"],[1481,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the Maghrib prayer: 'By the Mount, and a Book inscribed' (Q 52:1-2).\""],[1482,"It is mentioned in the Fida' of the captives of Badr that I happened to coincide with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer and the Surah at-Tur that is written in a parchment spread out. He then took me from his recitation with such pain. This was the first thing I heard about the matter of Islam."],[1483,"\"Hushaim, and I think I have only heard it from Al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubair ibn Mut'im, from his father Jubair ibn Mut'im, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to speak to him about the prisoners of Badr. I met him while he was praying Maghrib or Isha with his companions. I heard him say or recite, and his voice came from the mosque, 'Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur. There is none who can avert it.' It was as if my heart was torn apart.\""],[1484,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1485,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1486,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying with his companions the Isha or Maghrib prayer, and I heard him reciting, his voice coming out of the mosque: \"Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur; of it there is no repeller\" (Q 52:7-8), and it was as if my heart was cracked open."],[1487,"\"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the captives of Badr, and he led the people in the Maghrib prayer and recited al-Tur in it.\""],[1488,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding the captives of Badr, \"If al-Mut'im b. 'Adi were alive and spoke to me about these foul ones, I would have left them for him.\""],[1489,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If Mut'im b. 'Adiyy were alive and then spoke to me concerning these foul ones—or concerning these captives—I would have released them,” meaning the captives of Badr."],[1490,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak to him about the captives of Badr, and he said: “If he had come to us regarding them, we would have granted his intercession,” meaning his father al-Mut'im b. 'Adiyy. Hushaym said: “He had a favor owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[1491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If he had come to me concerning these foul ones, I would have granted his intercession,” meaning al-Mut'im b. 'Adiyy. At that, Jubayr accepted Islam."],[1492,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the ransom of the people of Badr. When I spoke to him, he said: “If Mut'im b. 'Adiyy were with me and then spoke to me concerning these, I would have released them for him.” Mut'im b. 'Adiyy had a favor owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1493,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1494,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1495,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.” Sufyan said: “Its explanation is one who severs ties of kinship,” and the wording is that of al-Humaydi."],[1496,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1497,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.” Baqiyyah added in his narration: “ties of kinship.”"],[1499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1501,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ: “The one who severs ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[1502,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who severs ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[1503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no alliance (ḥilf) in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the time of ignorance, Islam only increases it in strength.”"],[1504,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I will surely know you, O Banū 'Abd Manāf, if you prevent any circumambulator who goes around this House at any hour of night or day.\""],[1505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A prayer in my mosque exceeds a prayer in other mosques by a thousand prayers, except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1506,"I was with Quraysh at their encampment below 'Arafah, and I lost a donkey, so I went looking for it among the people who were at 'Arafah, and I found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Arafah."],[1507,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In his naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Jubayr b. Khalid b. Makhlad b. Iyas.\""],[1508,"In the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': \"In the naming of those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ: Jubayr b. Hubab b. al-Mundhir.\""],[1509,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those Muslims killed on the day of al-Yamamah, then from Banu Quraysh: Jubayr b. Malik, who is Ibn Buhaynah, and he is from Banu Nawfal b. 'Abd Manaf.\""],[1510,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The prescribed punishment of the sorcerer is a strike with the sword.”"],[1511,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he sent a group and appointed Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah or Ubaydah as their leader. When he went to depart, Subabah (the wife of Abu Ubaydah) wept and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . She sat down and he sent Abdullah bin Jahsh in his place and wrote a letter to him, instructing him not to read the letter until he reached a certain place. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not force anyone from your companions to travel with you.\" When he read the letter, he reconsidered and said, \"We listen and obey Allah and His Messenger.\" He informed them of the news and read the letter to them. Two men returned and the rest continued on. They met Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him without realizing that it was Rajab or Jumada [lunar months] (the sacred months). The disbelievers then said to the Muslims, \"You killed in the sacred month.\" Allah revealed the verse, \"They ask you about the sacred month - about fighting therein. Say, 'Fighting therein is great [sin], but averting [people] from the way of Allah and disbelief in Him and [preventing access to] al-Masjid al-Haram and the expulsion of its people therefrom are greater [evil] in the sight of Allah. And fitnah is greater than killing.' And they will continue to fight you until they turn you back from your religion if they are able. And whoever of you reverts from his religion [to disbelief] and dies while he is a disbeliever - for those, their deeds have become worthless in this world and the Hereafter. And those are the companions of the Fire, they will abide therein eternally\" (Quran 2:217). Some of them said, \"If they had not encountered us, they would not be burdened with sin.\" Allah revealed, \"Indeed, those who have believed and those who have emigrated and fought in the cause of Allah - those expect the mercy of Allah. And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful\" (Quran 2:218)."],[1512,"I witnessed Safwan and Jundub and his companions while he was advising them, and they said to him: Have you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I heard him say: 'Whoever lets others hear of his deed, God will let others hear of him on the Day of Resurrection.' And I think he said: 'And whoever makes a breach, God will make things hard for him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1513,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of God ﷻ, so let not God demand of you anything from His protection. For whoever He demands of anything from His protection, He will catch him and cast him into the fire of Hell.'"],[1514,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ five [days] before his death saying: 'I had among you brothers and friends, and I declare myself free to God from having any intimate friend among you. If I were to take an intimate friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend. Indeed, my Lord ﷻ has taken me as an intimate friend just as He took Abraham as an intimate friend. Indeed, those before you used to take the graves of their prophets and righteous ones as places of worship, so do not take graves as places of worship, for I forbid you from that.'"],[1515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “After me there will be trials like patches of dark night. A man will wake up a believer and become a disbeliever by evening, and a disbeliever by evening and wake up a believer.” A man among the Muslims said: “What should we do then, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Enter your houses and keep your remembrance.” A man said: “What if someone enters the house of one of us?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let him hold back his hand and be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the servant of Allah who kills. For a man may be in the group of Islam yet devour his brother’s wealth, shed his blood, disobey his Lord, and disbelieve in his Creator, and the Fire becomes due for him.”"],[1516,"A magician was performing before al-Walid b. 'Uqbah; he would take a sword and slaughter himself and do such-and-such, and it would not harm him. Jundub then rose to the sword, took it, and struck his neck. Then he recited: \"Will you then come to magic while you see plainly?\""],[1517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ghalib b. 'Abd Allah al-Kalbi, of the Kalb of 'Awf b. Layth, on a raiding party in which I was among them. He ordered him to attack Banu al-Mulawwih at al-Kadid. He said: We set out, and when we were at Qudayd we met al-Harith b. Barsa' al-Laythi and captured him. He said: I have only come to become Muslim; I set out intending to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: We said: If you are a Muslim, a night's tethering will not harm you, and if you are otherwise, we will secure you. So we tied him up, then left behind one of our small black men who was with us. We said to him: If he struggles with you, cut off his head. Then we came to al-Kadid at sunset, and we were on one side of the valley. My companions sent me as a lookout for them to a hill overlooking the settlement. He said: I climbed it, and when I was on its top and looked at the people, I lay flat. By Allah, I was on it looking when a man came out of his tent and said to his wife: By Allah, I see a black shape that I did not see at the beginning of the day. Look in your vessels, lest the dogs have dragged off some of them. She looked and said: By Allah, I do not miss anything from my vessels. He said: Give me my bow. She gave him a bow and two arrows with it. He said: He shot an arrow, and by Allah, it did not miss my side. He said: I pulled it out and remained still. He said: Then he shot the other and placed it in my shoulder. I pulled it out and remained still. He said to his wife: If it were something that moves, it would have moved by now; my two arrows have struck it. When morning comes, look for them and take them, lest the dogs ruin them. He said: Then he entered. When the people's animals had returned from their camels and sheep, and they had milked them and were at ease and settled, we launched the raid upon them. We killed and captured the sheep. Then we drove them away, and the cry of the people went out among their tribe, and a host came. They came in pursuit of us until we passed by Ibn al-Barsa', and we took him with us along with our companion whom we had left behind. He said: The people caught up with us until we saw them, and between us and them was nothing but the valley, with us facing one side and them on the other side in pursuit of us. Then Allah brought from where He willed what we had never seen before—rain such that no one could cross it. I saw them standing, looking at us while we drove the camels, and no man among them could reach us. When we had gone up with them, I will never forget the words of a poet among the Muslims as he drove them from behind them."],[1518,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The one who severs ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[1519,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I have names: I am Ahmad, I am Muhammad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom God effaces disbelief, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib.” He said: I asked al-Zuhrī, “What is al-ʿĀqib?” He said: “The one after whom there is no prophet ﷺ.”"],[1520,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I have five names: I am Ahmad, I am Muhammad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom God effaces disbelief, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib.”"],[1521,"Al-Qaʿnabī and Ibrāhīm b. Bashshār al-Ramādī narrated to us, and Bishr b. Mūsā narrated to us from al-Ḥumaydī; they said: Sufyān narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to us; Muḥammad b. Jubayr b. Muṭʿim narrated to me from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom disbelief is effaced, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib, after whom there is no prophet.”"],[1522,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom God effaces disbelief, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib, after whom there is no prophet.”"],[1523,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one who effaces disbelief, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one who gathers people at my feet, and I am al-ʿĀqib, after whom there is no prophet.”"],[1524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom disbelief is effaced, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib.” And al-ʿĀqib is the one after whom there is no one, and God has named him Kind and Merciful."],[1525,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, by whom God effaces disbelief, al-Ḥāshir, at whose feet people will be gathered, and al-ʿĀqib.” I asked Sufyān, “What is al-ʿĀqib?” He said: “The last of the prophets.”"],[1526,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I have names: I am Muhammad and Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom God effaces the disbelievers, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib.”"],[1527,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I have names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī, the one by whom God effaces the disbelievers, I am al-Ḥāshir, the one at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib.”"],[1528,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have five names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Māḥī (the eraser) through whom God erases disbelief, I am al-Ḥāshir (the gatherer) after whom people will be gathered, and I am al-ʿĀqib (the final one).”"],[1529,"Abū Yūsuf said: “Al-Ḥārith was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever.”"],[1530,"From Ḥamzah: “O assembly of Quraysh, Muhammad has indeed settled in Yathrib and sent out his scouts. He only wants to inflict something upon you, so beware lest you pass by his route or approach him, for he is like a ferocious lion. He is enraged against you because you expelled him as ticks are removed from a camel’s humps. By God, he has sorcerers: I have never seen him or any of his companions without seeing devils with them. You have known the enmity of the two sons of Qaylah, so he is an enemy who has sought help from an enemy.” Muṭʿim b. ʿAdī said to him: “O Abū al-Ḥakam, by God, I have never seen anyone more truthful in speech or more faithful to his promise than your brother whom you drove out. Since you have done what you did, be the most restrained of people concerning him.” Abū Sufyān b. al-Ḥārith said: “Be firmer than you have ever been, for if the two sons of Qaylah gain victory over you, they will not respect any bond or covenant with you. If you feed me, you will make them swallow the news of Kinānah, or they will expel Muhammad ﷺ from among them, and he will be alone and banished. As for the two sons of Qaylah, by God, they and the people of your lowland are equal in humiliation. I will suffice you against their might.” And he said."],[1531,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to his companions: “Let us go to Banū Wāqif to visit the blind man.” Sufyān said: “A clan of the Anṣār, and the blind man was blind of sight.”"],[1532,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to his companions: “Let us go to Banū Wāqif to visit the blind man.” Sufyān said: “A clan of the Anṣār, and he was veiled of sight.”"],[1533,"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not have the call to prayer given for any of the prayers on a journey except by the iqāmah, except for the dawn prayer, for which the adhān and iqāmah were given."],[1534,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say to ʿUthmān b. Ṭalḥah when he handed him the key of the Kaʿbah: “Here, take it and conceal it.” He said: “That is why the key is kept hidden.”"],[1535,"I went as a merchant to Sham (Syria) during the pre-Islamic period. When I was near Sham, a man from the People of the Book met me and asked, \"Do you have a fortune-teller among you?\" I replied, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Bring him to me.\" So I took him to a house where there were depictions (of various things), for I had not seen a depiction before that. When I came to know what a depiction was, I saw him holding the anklet of the Prophet ﷺ . I said, \"Who is this man holding the anklet?\" He replied, \"He is not a prophet, but there is no prophet after him. He is the successor after him.\" Then he mentioned Abu Bakr's characteristics."],[1536,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has become wicked (khabuthat nafsī),’ but rather, ‘My soul has become avaricious (laqisat nafsī).’”"],[1537,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Juḥfah. He came out to us and said: “Do you not bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God, and that the Qurʾān has come from God?” We said, “Yes.” He said: “Then rejoice, for this Qurʾān has one end in God’s hand and the other in your hands. Hold fast to it, and you will never perish after it, ever.”"],[1538,"I and so-and-so walked to the Prophet ﷺ. I said: “O Messenger of God, you gave to Banū al-Muṭṭalib and left us, although we and they are of the same status in relation to you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Banū Hāshim and Banū al-Muṭṭalib are one and the same.”"],[1539,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say at al-Khayf—the Khayf of Minā: “May God brighten the face of a servant who hears my words, memorizes them, comprehends them, and conveys them to those who have not heard them. Many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more knowledgeable than himself. There are three things upon which the heart of a believer does not harbor resentment: sincerity of action for God, sincere advice to the leaders of the Muslims, and adherence to their community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them.”"],[1540,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ at the Khayf of Minā saying: “May God brighten the face of a servant who hears my words, memorizes them, then conveys them to those who have not heard them. Many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more knowledgeable than himself. There are three things upon which the heart of a believer does not harbor resentment: sincerity of action for God, obedience to those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their supplication will be from behind them.”"],[1541,"The Prophet ﷺ stood at al-Khayf and said: 'May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears my words, retains them, and conveys them to one who has not heard them. For many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things the heart of a believer does not bear malice over: sincerity of action for Allah, obedience to those in authority, and holding fast to the community of the Muslims; for their supplication encompasses those behind them.'"],[1542,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Which land is the worst?' He said: 'I do not know.' When Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah, upon both of them be peace, he said: 'Which land is the worst?' He said: 'I do not know until I ask my Lord.' So Jibril ﷺ went and remained as long as Allah willed, then said: 'O Muhammad, you asked me which land is the worst, and I said, \"I do not know.\" I asked my Lord, saying: \"Which land is the worst?\" He said: \"Its marketplaces.\"'"],[1543,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the souls are exhausted, the dependents are lost, the wealth has perished, and the livestock are emaciated. Ask Allah, may He be exalted, for rain for us, for we seek intercession through you with Allah, and we seek intercession through Allah with you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Woe to you! Do you know what you are saying?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ glorified Allah and kept glorifying Him until that was evident on the faces of his companions. Then he said: 'Woe to you! Intercession is not sought through Allah with anyone of His creation. The matter of Allah is greater than that. Woe to you! Do you know what Allah, may He be exalted, is? His Throne is above His heavens and His earth like this' — and he indicated with his two fingers — 'like a dome, and it creaks under Him as a saddle creaks under its rider.'"],[1544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah, may He be exalted, tests His servant with illness until it expiates every sin from him.'"],[1545,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the road to Makkah. He said: 'The people of Yemen have come to you like clouds, the best of those on earth.' A man from the Ansar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, except us?' He was silent. Then he repeated it and was silent. Then he repeated it, and he said a quiet word: 'Except you.'"],[1546,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head to the sky and said: 'The people of Yemen have come to you like patches of dark night, and they are the best people on earth.' A man who was with him said: 'And from us, O Messenger of Allah?' Then he said a quiet word: 'Except you.'"],[1547,"He informed him that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him were the people, on his return from Hunayn, the bedouins clung to him asking him, and they forced him toward a samurah tree, and it snatched his cloak while he was on his mount. He stopped and said: 'Give me back my cloak. Do you fear stinginess from me? By Allah, if there were as many livestock as these thorn trees, I would distribute them among you, and then you would not find me stingy, nor cowardly, nor a liar.'"],[1548,"While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him were the people, on his return to Hunayn, the bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him until they forced him to a samurah tree, and it snatched his cloak. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped and said: 'Give me my cloak. If I had as many livestock as these thorn trees, I would distribute them among you, and then you would not find me stingy, nor a liar, nor cowardly.'"],[1549,"While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his return from Hunayn, the bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him until they forced him against a sidrah tree, and it snatched the cloak of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stopped and said: 'For Allah, give me my cloak! If there were as many livestock as these thorn trees, I would distribute them among you, and you would not find me stingy, nor cowardly, nor a liar.'"],[1550,"While he was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ, and with the people, on his return from Hunayn, the bedouins clung to the Prophet ﷺ asking him until they forced him to a samurah tree, and it snatched his cloak. The Prophet ﷺ stopped and said: 'Give me my cloak. If I had as many livestock as these thorn trees, I would distribute them, and then you would not find me stingy, nor a liar, nor cowardly.'"],[1551,"While he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him were the people, on his return from Hunayn, the bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him until they forced him to a samurah tree, and it snatched his cloak. The Prophet ﷺ stopped and said: 'Give me my cloak. If there were as many livestock as these thorn trees, I would distribute them among you, and then you would not find me stingy, nor a liar, nor cowardly.'"],[1552,"I lost a camel of mine on the day of 'Arafah, so I went out to look for it at 'Arafah, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the people at 'Arafah. I said: 'This one is from the Hums, so what is his business here?' Sufyan said: 'Al-Ahmas is the one who is strict in his religion.' Quraysh used to be called al-Hums, and Satan had led them astray, saying to them: 'If you venerate other than your sanctuary, people will belittle your sanctuary.' So they would not leave the sanctuary."],[1553,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him about something, so he told her to come back to him. She said, “O Messenger of God, if I come and do not find you” — meaning death — he said, “If you do not find me, then go to Abu Bakr.”"],[1554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque.”"],[1555,"\"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1556,"“The moon split while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[1557,"“The moon split while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[1558,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in anything besides it, except the Sacred Mosque.”"],[1559,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi, and al-Khatam, and al-‘Aqib.”"],[1560,"He heard ﷺ say, “I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-‘Aqib, and al-Hashir, and al-Mahi.”"],[1561,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey of his and said, “Who will keep watch over us tonight so that we do not sleep past the dawn prayer?” Bilal said, “I will.” He faced the direction the sun rises, and sleep overcame them until the heat of the sun woke them. Then they got up, led their mounts, performed ablution, and Bilal gave the call to prayer. Then they prayed the two rak‘ahs of dawn, then they prayed the dawn prayer."],[1562,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God, may He be exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven and says, ‘Is there anyone asking so that I may give him? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness so that I may forgive him?’”"],[1563,"ﷺ said, “O sons of ‘Abd Manaf, if you are ever given authority over this matter, do not prevent anyone performing tawaf around this House at any hour of the hours of the night or the day.”"],[1564,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ enter into prayer and say, “God is most great, greatly,” three times, “and praise be to God, abundantly,” three times, “O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed, from his blowing, his spitting, and his prodding.” ‘Amr said: His blowing is pride, his prodding is madness, and his spitting is poetry."],[1565,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he entered into prayer and said, “God is most great, greatly,” three times, “and praise be to God, abundantly,” three times, “and glory be to God morning and evening,” three times, “O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed, from his prodding, his blowing, and his spitting.”"],[1566,"When the Prophet ﷺ began the prayer, he would say 'Allah is the Greatest, greatly' three times, and 'Praise be to Allah, abundantly' three times, and 'Glory be to Allah, morning and evening' three times. Then he would say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from Satan — from his pricking, his blowing, and his puffing.' And he would say: 'His blowing is poetry, his puffing is arrogance, and his pricking is the one who dies in his affliction.'"],[1567,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying the Duha prayer."],[1568,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his bowing: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,' and in his prostration: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.'"],[1569,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Walking to Friday prayers is an expiation for sins, and performing ablution in a perfect manner is an expiation for sins, and awaiting the next prayer after the previous prayer is an expiation for sins.\""],[1570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed a portion among a group of people, and the people followed him. He passed by a tree and it caught his clothes, so he said: 'Return my clothes to me. Do you fear for me? By Allah, if I had wealth, I would distribute it.'"],[1571,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'While he was at the pass of al-Arakah, distributing after he had finished with Hunayn, he turned to us with a face like a piece of the moon.'"],[1572,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'A people's sister's son is one of them.'"],[1573,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ standing on a camel of his at 'Arafat among his people until he departed after them, by Allah's granting him success."],[1574,"Quraysh used to depart from al-Muzdalifah saying: 'We are the Hums, so we do not leave the sacred precinct.' And they abandoned standing at 'Arafah. But I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the people at 'Arafah on a camel of his, and departing with them until he reached al-Muzdalifah with his people in the morning, and he stayed with them, then departed when they departed."],[1575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have already made the intention to sit, so do not rush me to stand during prayer, and during bowing and prostration.\""],[1576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the pre-Islamic era, Islam only increased it in strength.'"],[1577,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ at al-Marwah during his 'Umrah, shortening his hair, and he was saying: 'The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection; no one should remain without performing Hajj.'"],[1578,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ shorten his hair at al-Marwah with a blade, and he said: 'The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1579,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'All of 'Arafah is a standing place, but keep away from 'Uranah. All of al-Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from the valley of Muhassir. All the days of Tashriq are for slaughtering, and all the roads of Makkah are places of sacrifice.'"],[1580,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visit Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applying a heated cloth to him (as a compress)."],[1581,"I came to Madinah — when I arrived there I was not yet a Muslim at that time — and I entered while I was overcome with severe drowsiness, so I slept in the mosque until I was startled by the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting “By the Mount, and a Book inscribed” (Q 52:1–2). I kept repeating the istirjāʿ (saying “To Allah we belong and to Him we return”) until I left the mosque, and that was the first thing that entered my heart of Islam."],[1582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘Glory be to Allah and with His praise. Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You,’ and says it in a gathering of remembrance, it is like a seal stamped upon it; and whoever says it in a gathering of idle talk, it becomes an expiation for him.”"],[1583,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “The expiation for a gathering is that one should not leave until he says, ‘Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. There is no god but You. Turn to me and forgive me’ — saying it three times. If it was a gathering of idle talk, it becomes an expiation for him; and if it was a gathering of remembrance, it is like a seal upon it.”"],[1584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you prays facing a sutrah (barrier), let him draw near to it, so that Satan does not pass between him and it.”"],[1585,"The Messenger of Allah, may ﷺ , said, \"Do not ask for swords, do not scatter branches in the mosques, do not swear by Allah in the mosque, do not prevent a woman from praying in the mosques, whether she is a resident or a visitor, do not build with images, and do not decorate with glass containers. For indeed, they are only constructed with trustworthiness and honored with dignity.\""],[1586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prescribed legal punishments (ḥudūd) are not to be carried out in the mosques.”"],[1587,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted the share of the near relatives and the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib, I and ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, these are the Banū Hāshim — their excellence is not denied because of the position in which Allah has placed you among them. What do you think? You have given to our brothers from the Banū al-Muṭṭalib and withheld from us, when we and they are in the same standing in relation to you.” He said, “They did not separate from me in the time of ignorance or in Islam. Indeed, the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib are one and the same,” and he interlaced his fingers."],[1588,"He reported to him that he and ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak with him about what he had distributed of the fifth from Khaybar between the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, you distributed to our brothers, the Banū al-Muṭṭalib b. ʿAbd Manāf, and gave us nothing, although our kinship is like their kinship.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “I consider Hāshim and al-Muṭṭalib to be one and the same.” Jubayr b. Muṭʿim said, “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not distribute anything of that fifth to the Banū ʿAbd Shams or the Banū Nawfal, just as he distributed to the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib.”"],[1589,"ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān asked the Prophet ﷺ when he gave the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib from the fifth of Khaybar and did not give the Banū ʿAbd Shams or the Banū ʿAbd Manāf. He said, “Indeed, the Banū Hāshim and the Banū al-Muṭṭalib are one and the same.”"],[1590,"He came to Madinah for the ransom of captives, and at that time he was a polytheist. He entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying Maghrib, and he recited “By the Mount” (Q 52), and it was as if the recitation of the Qur'an split my heart open."],[1591,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying Maghrib, and it was as if my heart was cracked open when I heard the Qur'an."],[1592,"I lost a donkey on the day of 'Arafah, so I went looking for it, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing on his camel, and that was after revelation had come down to him."],[1593,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"O Banū 'Abd Manāf! O Banū 'Abd al-Muṭṭalib! I will surely know if you prevent anyone from praying at this House at any hour he wishes, whether night or day.\""],[1594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banū 'Abd al-Muṭṭalib and O Banū 'Abd Manāf! If you are given authority over any part of this matter, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House from praying at any hour of night or day.\""],[1595,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"O Banū 'Abd Manāf! Do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House at any hour of night or day.\""],[1596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banū 'Abd Manāf! O Banū 'Abd al-Dār! Do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House and prays at any hour of night or day.\""],[1597,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1600,"I disliked Quraysh harming the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I thought they would kill him, I left until I reached one of the monasteries. The people of the monastery went to their leader and told him, and he said: 'Give him the hospitality he deserves' three times. When three days passed and they saw he had not left, they went to their leader and told him. He said: 'Tell him we have fulfilled the duty of hospitality owed to you. If you are a guardian, then your ward has passed; if you are visiting kin, then you should go to those you visit; if you are a merchant, then you should go out to your trade.' He said: 'I am not visiting kin, nor a merchant, and I have no share [of such matters].' They went back and informed him, and he said: 'He must have some concern; ask him what it is.' They came and asked me. I said: 'No, by Allah, except that I am in the town of Abraham, and my cousin claims that he is a prophet, and his people have harmed him, and I feared they would kill him, so I left so as not to witness that.' They went to their leader and told him what I said. He said: 'Bring him.' I went to him and told him my story. He said: 'Do you fear they will kill him?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Would you recognize his likeness if you saw him in a picture?' I said: 'Yes, for I saw him recently.' He showed me covered pictures and began uncovering picture after picture, saying: 'Do you recognize?' and I said: 'No,' until he uncovered a covered picture, and I said: 'I have not seen anything more like this picture to him, as if it were his height, his body, and the distance between his shoulders.' He said: 'So you fear they will kill him?' I said: 'I think they have already finished him off.' He said: 'By Allah, they will not kill him, and he will surely kill whoever intends to kill him. He is indeed a prophet, and Allah will make him prevail. But our duty of hospitality to you is binding, so stay as long as you wish and ask for whatever you want.' He said: 'So I stayed with them for a while, then I said to myself: If I obey them and go to Makkah...' So I went, and I found that they had expelled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Madinah. When I arrived, Quraysh came to me and said: 'Your affair has become clear to us, and we know your situation. Bring the wealth of the orphans which your father entrusted to you.' I said: 'I would not do that until you separate my head from my body, but let me go and deliver it to them.' They said: 'You have a covenant with Allah and His solemn pledge that you will not eat from his food.' He said: 'I came to Madinah, and the news had reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I entered upon him, and he said to me, among other things: \"I see you are hungry. Bring food.\" I said: 'I will not eat until I tell you, and if you see fit for me to eat, then I will eat.' Then I told him what they had made me pledge. He said: \"Fulfill your covenant with Allah, and do not eat from our food or drink from our drink.\""],[1601,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Jubayr b. Iyas b. Khalid b. Makhlad b. Zurayq.\""],[1602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has not permitted a servant anything better than two rak'ahs or more. Righteousness scatters over the servant's head as long as he is in prayer. A servant does not come to Allah ﷻ with anything better than what comes out of him,\" meaning the Qur'an."],[1603,"It is said the name of Abu Dharr is Burayr.\""],[1604,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Dharr, \"How are you, O Burayr?\" in a hadith we have abridged."],[1605,"I was the fourth of Islam. Three people had become Muslim before me, and I was the fourth. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\" I saw joy in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Who are you?\" I said, \"I am Jundub, a man from Banu Ghifar.\" It was as if he ﷺ recoiled and wished that I were from a tribe other than the one I was from, because I was from a tribe who robbed the pilgrims with hooked sticks of theirs."],[1606,"Abu Dharr used to say: \"I saw myself as the fourth of Islam. No one became Muslim before me except the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Bilal ؓ.\""],[1607,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Abu Dharr was Jundub b. Junadah.\""],[1608,"\"Abu Dharr died at al-Rabadhah in the year 32, and his name was Jundub b. Junadah.\""],[1609,"Ibn Mas'ud \"came with a caravan from Ghimar and passed by the funeral bier of Abu Dharr on the side of the road. He and his companions dismounted and buried him. Abu Dharr had entered Egypt and taken a house there.\""],[1610,"And Abu Dharr was among those who witnessed the conquest with Amr b. al-As."],[1611,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari used to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he finished his service, he would retire to the mosque and lie down in it, and it was his home."],[1612,"Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave anything that Jibril and Mika'il (peace be upon them) poured into his chest except that he poured it into my chest, and I have not left anything that he poured into my chest except that I poured it into the chest of Malik b. Damrah."],[1613,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed Abu Dharr rivals Isa son of Maryam in his worship.\""],[1614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at the likeness of Isa son of Maryam in form and character, let him look at Abu Dharr ؓ.\""],[1615,"\"Indeed I am the closest of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Resurrection. He left this world in the state in which I am leaving it, and by Allah, I have not introduced anything after him, and there is not one of you except that he has clung to something of it.\""],[1616,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed the most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me is the one who meets me upon the covenant upon which he parted from me.\""],[1617,"I saw Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah in a black shelter of his, and beneath him was a generous wife of his, and he was sitting on a piece of sackcloth. It was said to him: \"O Abu Dharr, you are a man who has no children remaining.\" He said: \"Praise be to Allah who takes them in the perishable abode and stores them in the abode of permanence.\" They said: \"O Abu Dharr, would you take a wife other than this one?\" He said: \"To marry a wife who lowers me is dearer to me than a wife who raises me.\" They said: \"Would you take a carpet softer than this?\" He said: \"O Allah, forgive. Take what You have granted whenever it pleases You.\""],[1618,"News reached al-Harith, a man of Quraysh who was in Syria, that Abu Dharr was in need, so he sent him three hundred dinars. He said: \"He has not found a servant of Allah who is more insignificant to Him than me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever begs while he has forty is importunate.'\" And the family of Abu Dharr had forty dirhams and forty sheep and two servants. Abu Bakr b. Ayyash said: meaning two servants."],[1619,"A man came to Abu Dharr offering him a gift. Abu Dharr said: \"We have goats we milk, donkeys that carry, a freedwoman who serves us, and a spare cloak beyond our clothing. I fear being held accountable for the surplus.\""],[1620,"I said to Abu Dharr: \"What about the black dog?\" He said: \"Indeed I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: 'It is a devil.'\""],[1621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Abu Dharr, there will be leaders over you who will kill the prayer. If you reach them, then pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them supererogatory.\""],[1622,"Indeed my close friend ﷺ entrusted to me that \"Any gold or silver that is hoarded and not spent in the way of Allah will be a brand on its owner until he spends it in the way of Allah.\""],[1623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The black dog and the woman cut off the prayer.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the black as opposed to the white or the red? He said: \"Indeed the black one is a devil.\""],[1624,"From Abu Dharr: There was a hadith I had been longing to hear, so I met him and said: O Abu Dharr, a hadith from you had been reaching me, and I had been longing to meet you. He said: May your father be for Allah, you have met me, so bring it. I said: A hadith that reached me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told you. He said: \"Allah ﷻ loves three and hates three.\" He said: I do not at all suppose that I would lie upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: Who are these three whom Allah ﷻ loves? He said: \"A man who went on a military expedition in the way of Allah patiently seeking reward and fought until he was killed, and you find him in the Book of Allah ﷻ.\" Then he recited this verse: {Indeed Allah loves those who fight in His way in ranks as though they were a solid structure.} I said: And who? He said: \"A man who had a bad neighbor who harmed him, and he bore his harm patiently until Allah sufficed him against him by life or death.\" I said: And who? He said: \"A man who traveled with a group, and they journeyed until, when it was the last part of the night, drowsiness or slumber fell upon them, so they dismounted and lay down their heads, then he arose, purified himself and prayed out of desire for Allah ﷻ and desire for what is with Him.\" I said: And what are the three whom Allah ﷻ hates? He said: The miserly, boastful one, and it is in the Book of Allah ﷻ: {Indeed Allah does not love every self-conceited boaster.} I said: What is the self-conceited boaster? He said: \"You find him in the Book of Allah ﷻ, the miserly, self-conceited one.\" I said: And who? He said: The trader who swears much, or the seller who swears much. He said: I do not know which of the two Abu Dharr said. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is wealth? He said: A measure of dates for us and a small herd of camels. I said: O Abu Dharr, I am not asking you about this; I am asking you about quietly stored wealth. He said: What comes in the morning does not see the evening, and what comes in the evening does not see the morning. I said: What about you and your brothers of Quraysh? He said: By Allah, I will not ask them for a religious ruling, nor ask them for worldly things, until I meet Allah and His Messenger. He said it three times."],[1625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best thing with which to change this hair is henna and katam.\""],[1626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, mentioning Zamzam: \"It is blessed; it is food of sustenance.\""],[1627,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever hoards gold or silver and does not spend it in the way of Allah, it will be a brand on the Day of Resurrection with which he will be cauterized.\""],[1628,"He heard Abu Zaynab, the freed slave of Hazim al-Ghifari, say: I heard Abu Dharr say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise?\" I said: Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: \"Say: There is no might and no power except with Allah.\""],[1629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, “O Abū Dharr, Do you think that having wealth is being wealthy?” He said, “Yes.” He ansked, “And do you think that not having wealth is poverty?” He said, “Yes.” He then said three things. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In fact, true wealth is in the heart and true poverty is in the heart: Whoever's richness is in his heart; will not be harmed no matter what happens to him in the world; Whoever is poor in his heart, he will not be satisfied no matter how much he has gained in the world. In fact he is only harmed by the greed of his own soul.”"],[1630,"He met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah driving a camel of his with two water skins on it, and on the camel's neck was a water bag. He said: O Abu Dharr, what is with you? He said: My work is with me. He said: Narrate to me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are no two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching the age of accountability except that Allah forgives them by the grace of His mercy toward them.\""],[1631,"He met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah driving a camel of his with two water skins on it, and on the camel's neck was a water bag. He said: O Abu Dharr, what is with you? He said: My work is with me. He said: Narrate to me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are no two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching the age of accountability except that Allah forgives them by the grace of His mercy toward them.\""],[1632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever spends a pair of anything from his wealth in the way of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will vie with one another to admit him: two camels, two horses, two sheep, two dirhams, two leather socks, two sandals.\""],[1633,"I heard Abu Dharr Al-Ghifari while he was on the pulpit saying, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Whoever comes close to Allah by a handspan, Allah will come close to him by a forearm's length. Whoever comes close to Allah by a forearm's length, Allah will come close to him by a distance of two arms. And whoever comes to Allah walking, Allah will come to him running. And Allah is greater and more majestic, and Allah is greater and more majestic, and Allah is greater and more majestic.'\""],[1634,"We left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no bird flapping its wings in the air but that he reminded us of some knowledge from him. He said: \"There remains nothing that brings one near to Paradise and takes one far from the Fire but that it has been made clear to you.\""],[1635,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to maintain ties with my kin even if they turn away, to speak the truth even if it is bitter, to let no blame of any blamer overtake me for the sake of Allah, to love the poor and sit with them, to look to the one below me and not to the one above me, and to say often: There is no might and no power except with Allah.\""],[1636,"My close friend ﷺ enjoined me with seven things: to love the poor and draw near to them, to look at those who are below me and not look at those who are above me, to maintain ties of kinship even if they shun me, to say often “There is no might nor power except with Allah,” to speak the bitter truth, and not to let the blame of any blamer overtake me regarding Allah, and not to ask people for anything."],[1637,"Abu Dharr said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what saves a servant from the Fire?” He said, “Faith in Allah.” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, with faith there is action.” He said, “That he give from what Allah has provided him.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what if he is poor and finds nothing to give?” He said, “He commands good and forbids evil.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what if he is unable to command good and forbid evil?” He said, “He does something for an unskilled person.” I said, “What if he is unskilled and cannot do anything?” He said, “He helps one who is overpowered.” I said, “What if he is weak and cannot help an oppressed person?” He said, “Do you wish to leave any good in your companion? Refrain from harming people.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, if he does that, will he enter Paradise?” He said, “There is no Muslim who does one of these traits except that it takes him by the hand until it enters him into Paradise.”"],[1638,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said, \"I advise you to have taqwa (God consciousness) of Allah, for it is the head of your affairs.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Recite the Quran frequently and remember Allah, for indeed, that will be light for you in the heavens and in the earth.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Do not laugh excessively, for it kills the heart and takes away the light from the face.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Engage in jihad, for it is the monasticism of my nation (Ummah).\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Maintain silence, except for that which is good, for it is a means of repelling Satan from you and an assistance to you in your religious affairs.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Look at those who are below you and do not look at those who are above you, for it is more appropriate that you do not belittle the blessings of Allah upon you.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Maintain relations with your relatives even if they cut you off.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Do not fear the blame of anyone in Allah's cause.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, increase me.\" He said, \"Love for the people what you love for yourself.\" Then he struck my chest with his hand and said, \"O Abu Dharr, there is no astuteness like careful consideration, no piety like withholding, and no reckoning like the remorse of character.\""],[1639,"“We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were strong youths.”"],[1640,"From Jundub b. Abdullah al-Bajali, and he had met the Prophet ﷺ."],[1641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware lest Allah call you to account for anything of His protection.”"],[1642,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, and Allah will never seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1643,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, may He be exalted, so beware lest Allah seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah, beware, son of Adam, lest Allah seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah, so Allah will never seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1646,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware lest Allah seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1647,"“These people have plunged into their blood and allied over this world and competed in building, and I swear by Allah that only a short time will pass before a strong camel, two ropes, and a saddle will be more beloved to one of you than a great palace.” You know that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Let nothing stand between any of you and Paradise while he sees its gate except a handful of blood of a Muslim man that he shed without right. Indeed, whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware lest Allah seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1648,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “O people, let nothing stand between any of you and Paradise except a handful of blood that he shed unjustly. Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah, O son of Adam, so beware lest Allah seek from you anything of His protection.”"],[1649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever can manage that no measure of a palm full of blood he sheds should come between him and Paradise—as if he were slaughtering a chicken—each time he advances to a gate of the gates of Paradise, it comes between him and it. Whoever of you can manage not to admit into his belly anything but what is good, then let him do so, for the first part of a person to putrefy is his belly.”"],[1650,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Adam met Musa, may Allah bless them both. Musa said: ‘Are you Adam whom Allah created with His hand, caused to dwell in His garden, made His angels prostrate to you, then you did what you did and brought your progeny out of the Garden?’ Adam ﷺ said: ‘Are you Musa whom Allah chose with His message, spoke to, and brought near as a confidant?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ Adam said: ‘Am I older, or the Remembrance?’ He said: ‘Rather the Remembrance.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “So Adam confuted Musa, so Adam confuted Musa, so Adam confuted Musa.”"],[1651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A man among those who came before you was wounded, and he became afraid of his wound. So, he took a knife, and he cut his hand with it, and the blood did not stop flowing until he died. Then Allah ﷻ said: 'My servant hastened his death, so I have forbidden Paradise for him.'\""],[1652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prescribed punishment of the sorcerer is a strike with the sword.”"],[1653,"A bedouin came, made his riding camel kneel and hobbled it, then prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, he went to his riding camel, untied its hobble, mounted it, then called out: “O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not associate anyone with us in Your mercy.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What do you say? Is he more astray, or his camel? He has restricted a vast mercy. Allah ﷻ created one hundred mercies, then sent down one mercy by which creatures show compassion to one another—their jinn, their humans, and their beasts—and with Him are ninety-nine. Do you say he is more astray, or his camel?”"],[1654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays the dawn prayer has the protection of Allah.”"],[1655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays the dawn prayer has the protection of Allah.”"],[1656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat—that is the Muslim, who has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger.”"],[1657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed under a banner of blind partisanship, supporting tribalism and becoming angry for tribalism, his killing is a killing of ignorance.”"],[1658,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says (something) about the Qur'an according to his own opinion and he is correct, yet he has committed a mistake.\"(Using translation from Tirmidhī 2952)"],[1659,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Come together over the Quran as long as you agree upon it, and when you differ concerning it, then depart.”"],[1660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Quran as long as your hearts agree upon it, and when they differ, then depart.”"],[1661,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Come together over the Quran as long as you agree upon it, and when you differ, then depart.”"],[1662,"We used to requisition them from one village to another, guiding us on the road, then we would leave them."],[1663,"I said: I do not want that, but I am asking you for a ruling so that you may give me one. He said: Jundub said: I was, in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, a vigorous youth, and so-and-so informed me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The one killed will come on the Day of Resurrection with his killer, clinging to him, and God ﷻ will say: Why did you kill this one? He will say: In [the matter of] the dominion of so-and-so. So beware lest you be that man."],[1664,"We were with our Prophet ﷺ as vigorous youths, and we learned faith before we learned the Quran, then we learned the Quran and increased thereby in faith. But today you learn the Quran before faith."],[1665,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man said: By God, God will not forgive so-and-so. Then God ﷻ said: Who is this who swears by Me that I will not forgive so-and-so? For I have forgiven so-and-so and nullified your deed."],[1666,"That God would not forgive so-and-so, so God ﷻ revealed to His Prophet ﷺ, or to a prophet, that it is equivalent to a sin, so let him begin the work anew."],[1667,"From Jundub b. Abdullah al-Azdi, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I set out with him to Basra until we came to a place called Bayt al-Miskin, which is to Basra like al-Thawiyya is to Kufa. He said: Have you been studying the Quran with anyone? I said: Yes. He said: When we reach Basra, bring them to me. So I brought him Salih b. Musarrih, Abu Bilal, Najda, and Nafi' b. al-Azraq, and they were in my estimation that day among the most virtuous of the people of Basra. He began to narrate to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Jundub said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The example of the scholar who teaches people good and forgets himself is like the example of a lamp that gives light to people and burns itself.'"],[1668,"Narrated Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Azdi: The companion of the Prophet, Peace be upon Him, said: \"I set out with him towards Basra until we reached a place called Bayt al-Miskin, which is to Basra what Sawiya is to Kufa. He asked me, 'Did you used to teach anyone the Quran?' I replied, 'Yes.' He said, 'When we reach Basra, bring them to me.' So, I brought him Salah ibn Musarrih, Abu Bilal, Najdah, and Nafi' ibn al-Azraq, who were among the distinguished people of Basra in my sight that day. Then, he started to speak to me about the Messenger of Allah, Peace be upon Him. Jundub narrated: The Messenger of Allah, Peace be upon Him, said, 'The likeness of the scholar who imparts knowledge to the people but forgets himself is like a lamp that illuminates the people but burns itself.'\""],[1669,"Do not let these people deceive you. They recite the Quran today and will fight one another with swords tomorrow. Then he said: Bring me a group of Quran reciters, and let them be elders. So I brought him Nafi' b. al-Azraq and I brought him Mirdas Abu Bilal and a group with them, six or eight. When we entered upon Jundub, he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The example of one who teaches people good and forgets himself is like the example of a lamp that gives light to people and burns itself. Whoever shows off his knowledge to people, God will expose him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever lets people hear of his deed, God will let others hear of him.'"],[1670,"Do not let these people deceive you. They recite the Quran today and will fight one another with swords tomorrow. Then he said: Bring me a group of Quran reciters, and let them be elders. So I brought him Nafi' b. al-Azraq and I brought him Mirdas Abu Bilal and a group with them, six or eight. When we entered upon Jundub, he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The example of one who teaches people good and forgets himself is like the example of a lamp that gives light to people and burns itself. Whoever shows off his knowledge to people, God will expose him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever lets people hear of his deed, God will let others hear of him.'"],[1671,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'When one of you asks permission three times and is not given permission, let him return.'"],[1672,"ﷺ said: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1673,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1674,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1675,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1676,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1677,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"I will precede you to the Hawd.\""],[1678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, I will be waiting for you by the Pond.\""],[1679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"The best prayer after the obligatory one is prayer in the depths of the night, and the best fasting after Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram.\""],[1680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—and I did not hear anyone else say \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said\"—he said: Then I drew near to him and heard him saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever makes himself heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.'\""],[1681,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever makes himself heard, Allah will make him heard; whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off; and whoever has two tongues in this world, Allah will give him two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1682,"Only Jundub heard from the Prophet ﷺ, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever makes himself heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.\""],[1683,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off; and whoever makes himself heard, Allah will make him heard.\""],[1684,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever makes himself heard, Allah will make him heard; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.\""],[1685,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it."],[1686,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No servant conceals a secret except that Allah clothes him with its garment—if good, then good, and if evil, then evil.\""],[1687,"I heard Jundub say: While the Prophet ﷺ was walking, a stone hit him and he stumbled, and his finger bled. He said, \"Are you anything but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered?\""],[1688,"While the Prophet ﷺ was walking, a stone hit his finger and it bled. He said, \"You are nothing but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered.\""],[1689,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when his finger was injured. He said, \"Are you anything but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered?\""],[1690,"A stone hit the finger of the Prophet ﷺ and it bled, so he said, \"Are you anything but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered?\""],[1691,"A stone hit the leg of the Prophet ﷺ and it bled, so he said, \"Are you anything but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered?\""],[1692,"The finger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bled during one of the battles, so he said, \"You are nothing but a finger that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have encountered.\""],[1693,"I heard Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill and did not get up for a night or two. Then a woman came to him and said, \"O Muhammad, I have not seen your shaytan except that he has left you.\" So Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {By the morning brightness and by the night when it covers with darkness, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He detested you}."],[1694,"From the Prophet ﷺ: One of his paternal cousins' daughters said, \"I do not think your companion has anything but that he has hated you.\" So it was revealed: {By the morning brightness and by the night when it covers with darkness, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He detested you}. The wording is from the hadith of Amr b. Marzuq."],[1695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill and did not get up for two or three nights. A woman said, \"O Muhammad, I hope that your shaytan has left you, for I have not seen him approach you for two or three nights.\" So Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {By the morning brightness and by the night when it covers with darkness, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He detested you}."],[1696,"Jibril was delayed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the polytheists said, \"Muhammad has been forsaken.\" Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed to His Messenger ﷺ: {Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He detested you. And the Hereafter is better for you than the first [life]. And your Lord is going to give you, and you will be satisfied}."],[1697,"I heard Jundub say: I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ, then he delivered a sermon and said: “Whoever slaughtered before praying should slaughter and replace it with another, and whoever has not slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1698,"I witnessed the sacrifice with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He did no more than pray, and when he had finished his prayer, he saw meat of sacrifices that had been slaughtered before he finished his prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before praying should slaughter another in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1699,"I witnessed a sacrifice with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He prayed with the people, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had completed the prayer, he saw sheep that had been slaughtered. He said: “Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should slaughter a sheep in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1700,"I witnessed the sacrifice with the Prophet ﷺ. He saw people who had slaughtered before the prayer and said: “Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should repeat the slaughter, and whoever has not slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1701,"I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He learned that people had slaughtered before the prayer, so he addressed the people and said: “Whoever slaughtered before the prayer should repeat his slaughter, and whoever has not should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and then said: “Whoever slaughtered his sacrifice before the prayer should slaughter another in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered should slaughter in the name of Allah.”"],[1703,"A tree struck the Prophet’s ﷺ finger and it bled. He said: “It is nothing but a finger that bled, and what it suffered is in the path of Allah.” Then he was carried and placed on a bed woven with palm fronds or a strap, and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber was placed under his head. The strap left marks on his side. Then Umar b. al-Khattab came and wept. He said: “What makes you weep?” He replied: “O Messenger of Allah, Kisra and Caesar sit on golden beds and wear silk brocade and heavy silk.” He said: “Are you not pleased that they have this world and you have the Hereafter?”"],[1704,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to enjoy night prayer.”"],[1705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “when he met his companions, did not shake hands with them until he had greeted them.”"],[1706,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Some people came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we forgot the prayer and did not pray until the sun rose.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform ablution and pray.” Then he said: “This is not forgetfulness; this is from Satan. When one of you lies down at night, let him say: In the name of Allah, I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan.”"],[1707,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a bringer of good news from his expedition came to him and informed him of the victory that Allah had granted his expedition and the conquest that Allah had opened for them. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the people, whom Allah Almighty had defeated, I caught up with a man with my sword. When he felt that the sword was about to strike him, he ran and said, ‘I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim.’” He said: “Did you kill him?” He replied: “O Messenger of Allah, he only sought protection.” He said: “Why did you not split open his heart to see whether he was truthful or lying?” He said: “If I had split open his heart, how would I know? Is his heart anything but a piece of flesh?” He said: “Neither do you know what is in his heart, nor did you believe his tongue.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me.” He said: “I will not ask forgiveness for you.” He said: Then that man died and they buried him, but in the morning he was on the surface of the earth. Then they buried him again, and in the morning he was on the surface of the earth, three times. When they saw that, they were ashamed and humiliated by what had happened to him, so they carried him and threw him into one of those mountain passes."],[1708,"When we were at al-Ghamim, news came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Quraysh that they had sent Khalid b. al-Walid with a troop of cavalry to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked meeting him, and he was merciful toward them. He said: \"Who is a man who will turn us away from the road?\" I said: I, may my father be your ransom. So he took them on a road that had rough stony ground, hillocks, and an 'uqab (steep pass). The land leveled out for us until he brought him down at al-Hudaybiyah, which was a dry well. He tilted into it an arrow, or his arrow, from his quiver, then spat into it, then supplicated, and its springs gushed forth until I say, or we say: If we wished, we could scoop water with our hands."],[1709,"From 'Urwah, in \"the naming of those who were martyred among the Muslims on the Day of Ajnadayn: Jundub b. Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams.\""],[1710,"From Ibn Shihab, in \"the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn: Jundub b. 'Amr Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams.\""],[1711,"From 'Urwah, in \"the naming of the participants of the 'Aqabah pledge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar: Jabir b. 'Abd Allah b. Haram b. Ka'b b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salamah.\""],[1712,"From Ibn Shihab, \"in the naming of those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar: Jabir b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr.\""],[1713,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year seventy-eight, and his age was eighty-five, and he was given the kunyah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.\""],[1714,"\"I saw on his bier a striped cloak, and Aban b. 'Uthman, who was governor of Madinah, prayed over him. Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died at the age of ninety-four, and he was given the kunyah Abu 'Abd Allah, and he had lost his sight, may Allah have mercy on him.\""],[1715,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah perished in the year seventy-four.\""],[1716,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year seventy-nine.\""],[1717,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year sixty.\""],[1718,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr saying, 'Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year ninety-eight, having lost his sight.'"],[1719,"The sons of Jabir swore by Allah, and he went out, and al-Hajjaj plunged into the pit until he finished it."],[1720,"We came to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah after his sight had become weak."],[1721,"I saw Jabir b. 'Abd Allah dyeing with yellow, and he attended al-'Aqabah."],[1722,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqabah. Jabir said, 'My maternal uncle brought me out, and I could not throw a stone.'"],[1723,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever unjustly takes the wealth of a Muslim by his right hand, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him.\" They asked, \"Even if it is a small amount, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Even if it is a twig of a miswak tree.\""],[1724,"I sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ more than a hundred times."],[1725,"I went on thirteen military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1726,"People saw a fire in a graveyard, so they came to it, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Hand me your companion,' and he was the man who used to raise his voice in remembrance."],[1727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Part of the completeness of prayer is the straightening of the rows.'"],[1728,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms apart until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[1729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I have been commanded to fight people until they say, \"There is no god but Allah.\" If they say it, they protect their blood and property from me, except for what is due, and their reckoning is with Allah ﷻ.'"],[1730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever gives a life grant, it belongs to him and his descendants.'"],[1731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates, and grapes for raisins, but allowed 'araya. And 'araya is when a Bedouin comes to a cousin of his or a man of his household, and he orders for him one or two palm trees that have not ripened, and he wants to go out, so there is no harm in selling them for dry dates."],[1732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Vinegar is an excellent condiment.\""],[1733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am Ahmad, I am Muhammad, I am al-Hashir before whom people will be gathered, and I am al-Mahi through whom Allah erases disbelief. On the Day of Resurrection the banner of praise will be with me, and I will be the leader of the messengers and the holder of their intercession.\""],[1734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no place in the seven heavens, neither a foot's span, a hand-span, nor a palm, except that there is an angel standing, bowing, or prostrating. On the Day of Resurrection they will all say: 'Glory be to You, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped, but we have not associated anything with You.'\""],[1735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the people under protection are wronged, the state becomes the state of the enemy. When adultery becomes widespread, captivity increases. When sodomy becomes widespread, Allah ﷻ withdraws His hand from creation and does not care in which valley they perish.\""],[1736,"My ears heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah while there was silver in Bilal's garment, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing it to the people. A man said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, be just.\" He said: \"Woe to you! Who will be just if I am not just? You would surely be a loser if I were not just.\" Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"Let me kill this hypocrite, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah forbid that people should say that I kill my companions. This man and his companions recite the Qur'an but it does not pass their throats; they pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its target.\""],[1737,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Mu'adh, I am sending you to a people of the Book. If you are asked about the milky way in the sky, say: It is the saliva of a serpent beneath the Throne.\""],[1738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah wills evil for a servant, He makes him flourish in mud and clay until he builds.\""],[1739,"On the day of the battle of al-Ta'if, the Prophet ﷺ stood with Ali ؓ for a long time during the day. Abu Bakr ؓ said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, your private conversation with Ali has been long today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I did not confide in him; rather Allah confided in him.\""],[1740,"My maternal uncle Jadd b. Qays carried me among seventy riders who came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with his uncle al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib and said: \"O uncle, take the oath from your maternal nephews.\" The seventy said: \"O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish.\" He said: \"As for what I ask you for my Lord, that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. As for what I ask for myself, that you protect me from what you protect yourselves from.\""],[1741,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black."],[1742,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the sea: \"Its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful.\""],[1743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on an expedition, and we had no food except a leather bag of dates. He appointed Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah over us, and he would give each of us a handful of dates, until we ran out, and he would give us one date at a time. Then the sea cast up a creature and we ate from it. Abu Ubaydah ordered its rib and it was bent, then he ordered a man who mounted a camel, and the rider passed on the camel."],[1744,"Dates and unripe dates are wine."],[1745,"From ʿUrwa: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar b. al-Najjar: Jabir b. Khalid b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal b. Haritha b. Dinar."],[1746,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar b. al-Najjar: Jabir b. Khalid b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal, who has no descendants."],[1747,"From ʿUrwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Riʾab b. Nuʿman b. Sinan."],[1748,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then Banu ʿUbayd b. ʿAdi: Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Ziyad b. Nuʿman."],[1749,"Ibn Ishaq: When Allah, exalted is He, wished to make His religion prevail, to honor His Prophet ﷺ, and to fulfill His promise, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went forth in the season in which the group from the Ansar met him. They were, as they claim, six, among them Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Riʾab."],[1750,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Jibril passed by me while I was praying, and he smiled at me, so I smiled back at him."],[1751,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Khadija: Jibril came to me and said, “Give Khadija glad tidings of a house of reeds in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[1752,"And Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Haysha said."],[1753,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Muʿawiya b. Malik b. ʿAwf: Jabr b. ʿAtik b. al-Harith."],[1754,"Jabir b. ʿAtik died in the year sixty-one; his age was seventy-one."],[1755,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say: “Part of jealousy is loved by Allah and part of it is hated by Allah. The jealousy Allah loves is jealousy in suspicion; the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy without suspicion. And part of pride is loved by Allah and part of it is hated by Allah. The pride Allah loves is a man’s pride in himself at the time of charity and fighting; the pride Allah hates is his pride in wrongdoing and immorality.”"],[1756,"And his father was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Of jealousy, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates; and of pride, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates. As for the jealousy that Allah loves, it is jealousy in suspicion; and the jealousy that Allah hates is jealousy without suspicion. And the pride that Allah loves is a man’s showing off of himself for Allah at the time of battle; and the pride that Allah hates is pride in wrongdoing or in wickedness.”"],[1757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Of jealousy, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates. As for what Allah loves of jealousy, it is jealousy in suspicion; and as for the jealousy that Allah hates, it is jealousy without suspicion. And as for the pride that Allah loves, it is a man’s showing off of himself at the time of battle; and as for the pride that Allah hates, it is a man’s showing off in wrongdoing and wickedness.”"],[1758,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever goes out as a fighter in the path of Allah,” then he joined his three fingers, then said: “And where are the fighters? For if he falls from his mount and dies, then his reward has fallen upon Allah; or if he dies a natural death, then his reward has fallen upon Allah; and whoever is killed instantly has certainly deserved the final abode.”"],[1759,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jābir b. ʿAtīk, from ʿAtīk b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAtīk—and he is the grandfather of ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh, the father of his mother—that he informed him that Jābir b. ʿAtīk informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit ʿAbd Allāh b. Thābit and found him overcome. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to him, but he did not answer. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return,” and he said, “We have been overcome for you, O Abū al-Rabīʿ.” The women shouted and wept, and Ibn ʿAtīk began to hush them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave them; for when it becomes due, let no weepers weep.” They said, “And what is the due, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “When he dies.” His daughter said, “By Allah, I had hoped that you would be a martyr, for you had completed your equipment.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah ﷻ has indeed placed his reward upon his intention. And what do you count as martyrdom?” They said, “Being killed in the path of Allah.” He said, “Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the path of Allah: the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one with a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies by fire is a martyr, the one who dies under a collapsed building is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr.”"],[1760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him during his illness, and someone said, “We had certainly hoped that his death would be a killing in the path of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In that case, the martyrs of my nation would indeed be few. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one with a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one who dies by fire is a martyr, and the one with pleurisy is a martyr.”"],[1761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked in the mosque of Banū Muʿāwiya for three things, and he was given two and denied one. He asked Him that He should not destroy his nation by famine, and that He should not give an enemy dominance over them, and he was given these. And he asked Him that He should not put their misfortune among themselves, and he was denied that."],[1762,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him and made the Fire due for him.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something little?” He said, “Even if it is a toothstick.”"],[1763,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Everything that is not part of the remembrance of Allah ﷻ is either frivolity or heedlessness, except four qualities: a man’s walking between the two targets, his training of his horse, his playing with his family, and learning swimming.”"],[1764,"I met the Prophet ﷺ among his Companions in the market, and I asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah where he was heading. They said, “He is marking out a mosque for your people.” So I returned, and there were my people standing. I said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out a mosque for us and fixed a piece of wood in the qiblah, standing it in it.”"],[1765,"I went to the market and met the Prophet ﷺ among his Companions. I asked them where he was heading, and they said, “He is marking out a mosque for your people.” So I returned and found my people standing. I said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out a mosque for us with his foot and fixed a piece of wood in the qiblah, fixing it in it.”"],[1766,"And he is called Abū ʿAbd Allāh, his lineage is such."],[1767,"And he is called Abū ʿAbd Allāh, his lineage is such."],[1768,"Jabir b. Samurah died, and Amr b. Hurayth prayed over him."],[1769,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: This religion will continue to be strong till the time of twelve caliphs. The people then uttered: Allah is more great and uproared. He then silently a word which I could not understand. So I said to my father: What did he say, father ? He said: All of them will belong to Quraish. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4280)"],[1770,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs.”"],[1771,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “This community will have twelve upright leaders; those who abandon them will not harm them.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ whispered a word I did not hear. I said to my father: What was the word the Prophet ﷺ whispered? He said: “All of them from Quraysh.”"],[1772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon one day, and I heard him say, \"This religion will always be strong, preventing anyone who opposes it, until twelve will rule it, all of them from Quraysh.\" Then the people became confused and started discussing, and I did not understand what he meant by \"all of them\". So I asked my father, \"Oh my father, what did he mean by 'all of them'?\" He said, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[1773,"I have heard the Prophet ﷺ saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage, \"This matter will always remain apparent to anyone who seeks it, unaffected by any opposing or deviant individuals, until there have been twelve Caliphs from the Quraysh.\""],[1774,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I heard him say, \"The matter of this nation will remain apparent until there are twelve (caliphs).\" And he said a word that I did not hear, and my father was closer to him in the gathering than me. So I asked, \"What did he say?\" He said, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[1775,"I went to the Prophet with my father, and the Messenger of Allah said, \"This nation will remain upright in its affair until there are twelve caliphs.\" Then he said a whispered word, and I asked my father what he said. He said, \"All of them will be from Quraish.\""],[1776,"I came with my father to the mosque and the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon. I heard him say, \"There will be twelve successors after me.\" Then he lowered his voice and I couldn't catch what he was saying. So, I asked my father, \"What was he saying?\" He replied, \"All of them will be from the Quraysh tribe.\""],[1777,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage, \"The affairs of this Ummah will continue to be stable for those who adhere to it, until there are twelve leaders among you.\" Then he said something I did not hear, so I asked my father, who was closer to him than me, what did he say? He said he said, \"All of them will be from Quraish.\""],[1778,"We heard Jabir b. Samurah say: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said: “This affair will continue standing until twelve amirs have passed.” He said: And he shortened a word I did not hear. He said: When the Prophet ﷺ fell silent, I said to my father Samurah: What was the word he shortened? He said: “All of them from Quraysh.”"],[1779,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When God ﷻ bestows a favor on a servant, let him begin with himself and his household.”"],[1780,"Regarding a hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God gives any of you good, let him begin with himself and his family.”"],[1781,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on a Friday evening, the day he stoned Maiz al-Aslami, say: “A band of Muslims will conquer the White House.” I said: Kisra? He said: “Kisra.”"],[1782,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will extract the treasure of the White One, Kisra and the family of Kisra.”"],[1783,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the one who precedes you to the Pool.”"],[1784,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I am your predecessor at the Lake-Fount, and some of you will be brought in front of me till I will see them and then they will be taken away from me and I will say, 'O Lord, my companions!' It will be said, 'You do not know what they did after you had left.' (Using translation from Bukhārī 6576)"],[1785,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"The religion will continue to be established until there are twelve caliphs from the Quraysh, then there will emerge liars before the Hour.\""],[1786,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The religion will continue to stand until the Day of Judgment, or until there are twelve caliphs, all of them from the Quraysh.'\""],[1787,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows behind me as the angels form rows before their Lord?” They said: How do the angels form rows before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1788,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to us and said: “Will you not form rows as the angels form rows before their Lord?” They said: O Messenger of God, how do the angels form rows before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?” He said: “They complete the foremost rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows as the angels who are in the presence of their Lord form rows?” They said, “And how do the angels who are in the presence of their Lord form rows?” He said: “They establish the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1791,"Why do you stand in rows as the angels do in the presence of their Lord? We asked: how do the angles stand in rows in the presence of their Lord? He replied: they make the first row complete and keep close together in the row. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 661)"],[1792,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gestured to us to sit, so we sat. Then he said: “What prevents you from forming rows as the angels form rows in the presence of the Most Merciful?” They said, “And how do they form rows, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “They complete the first rows and align themselves in the rows in a compact manner.”"],[1793,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them while they were raising their eyes, and he said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1795,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The people who lift their eyes towards the sky in Prayer should avoid it or they would lose their eyesight. (Using translation from Muslim 428)"],[1797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Certain people should stop casting their gazes around during prayer or else their sight will not be returned to them.\""],[1798,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque and saw them raising their hands. He said: “What is the matter with them, raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still during the prayer.”"],[1799,"I entered with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat with him, and he said, \"Islam will continue to be apparent until there are twelve princes or caliphs, all of them from Quraysh.\""],[1800,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in the garment in which I have intercourse?” He said: “Yes, unless you see something on it, in which case wash it.”"],[1801,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “This matter (Islam) will remain prevail, and no one who opposes it will harm it.”"],[1802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It suffices one of you, when he finishes his prayer, to place his hand on his thigh and greet his brother on his right: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' and on his left the like of that.\""],[1803,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ more than a hundred times in the mosque; his companions would sit reciting poetry to one another, and sometimes they would discuss matters of the pre-Islamic era, and the Prophet ﷺ would smile with them."],[1804,"«When the Prophet ﷺ returned from the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah, a horse was brought to him unsaddled, and he mounted it while we walked around him.»"],[1805,"«I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deliver a sermon except standing on Friday. He would deliver a sermon, then sit, then stand and deliver a sermon. He used to deliver two sermons with a sitting between them.»"],[1806,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah, \"Did you mention poetry in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, we used to mention poems in his presence and laugh, and he would smile.\""],[1807,"The Prophet ﷺ would not go out on the day of Fitr until he had eaten seven dates."],[1808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose to pray Fajr and then leaned with his hand."],[1809,"Ma'iz, a short man wearing a waist-wrapper, was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining on a cushion. When he was brought, he turned aside from the cushion and spoke with him. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned red, and he knew that he had angered him. So he gestured with his hand: “Stone him.” Then he sent a man after him and spoke with him briefly. Then he said, “Take him away and stone him.” The people rose, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: “Now then, whenever we set out in the way of Allah, one of them stays behind and bleats like a billy goat, giving one of them something. Indeed, if Allah gives me power over any of them, I will make an example of him.”"],[1810,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come out for the funeral of Thabit b. al-Dahdah while he was on a white-faced horse with white feet, wearing nothing on it, and the people were with him around him. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted, then sat until it was finished, then stood and mounted his horse, then departed riding."],[1811,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver his sermons on the pulpit while sitting and someone denied it, and Jabir said: \"I bear witness that he used to deliver his sermons while standing, then he would sit and then stand again and deliver the sermon of the hereafter.\" He said, \"So I said, 'How were his sermons?' He said, 'He would advise the people and recite verses from the Book of Allah, and it would be concise. His prayer timings were in accordance with the rising and setting of the sun and the sky and the morning prayer and the noon prayer, except for the morning prayer and the noon prayer when Bilal would recite the call to prayer when the sun was declining, and sometimes the call to prayer would be delayed a little and sometimes he would hasten it. As for the call to prayer, it should not be delayed and the Asr prayer should be offered close to the time that you normally offer it, and the Maghrib prayer close to the time that you normally offer it, and the evening prayer should be delayed a little from your prayer timings.'\""],[1812,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray prayers similar to your prayer. He would pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and in the Fajr prayer he would recite Qāf wa-l-Qur'ān al-Majīd, Yā Sīn, and the like."],[1813,"I saw the seal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was by his shoulder like a pigeon's egg."],[1814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling animals for animals on credit."],[1815,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointing with his finger while in prayer. When he said the taslim, I heard him say: “O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know.”"],[1816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This nation will remain upright, and its affairs will be apparent against its enemies until twelve caliphs pass from them, all of them from Quraysh.\" When he returned home, Quraysh came to him and asked, \"And then what will happen?\" He said, \"Then there will be turmoil.\""],[1817,"I entered with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"Indeed, this matter will not pass and it will not come to an end until twelve Caliphs have passed.\" Then he said something that I did not understand. I asked my father, \"What did he say?\" He said, \"All of them are from the Quraysh.\""],[1818,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"There will be twelve leaders after me.\" Then he spoke softly, and I asked the one next to me, and he said, \"All of them are from Quraysh.\""],[1819,"I was in the assembly of the Prophet ﷺ with Samurah and Abu Umamah, and he said: \"Obscenity and indecency have nothing to do with Islam in any way. Indeed, the best people in Islam are those who are best in character.\""],[1820,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: \"Twelve custodians from Quraysh; the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them.\" He said: Then I turned around, and there was 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and my father among the people, and they confirmed the hadith for me just as I had heard it."],[1821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated. May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated. May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated, except during a period of tribulation, for Bedouin life is better than remaining in the midst of tribulation.\""],[1822,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Will you not form rows just as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" He said: \"They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row.\""],[1823,"I went to the market and encountered the Prophet ﷺ among his companions. I asked them where he was heading, and they said: \"He is going to mark out a mosque for your people.\" So I returned and found my people standing. I said: \"What is the matter with you?\" They said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ marked out a mosque for us with his foot, and he set up a piece of wood in the qiblah that he had planted there.\""],[1824,"I saw cut squash before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: What do you do with this? He said: \"We use it to increase our food.\""],[1825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take fresh water for the head.\""],[1826,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks the world through the work of the Hereafter, his face will be blackened, his remembrance will be effaced, and his name will be registered in the Fire.”"],[1827,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a captive who had been among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They had captured him while he was still a polytheist, but then he embraced Islam. They brought that captive to the Prophet ﷺ, who gave him two garments as a gift, one made of fine linen and the other made of coarse wool. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go to Aisha, and she will give you from the fine garments that she has, two garments.\" He entered upon Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and said, \"May Allah bless you, choose for me two garments from these fine garments that you have, as the Prophet ﷺ has given me two garments from them.\" She replied, \"May I extend the garment for you like I see others?\" He said, \"Take this one and take this one.\" At that time, Arab women did not cover their faces."],[1828,"“ʿAbdullah b. Rawaha estimated for the people of Khaybar for one year only, then he was struck down on the Day of Muʾta. Then Jabir b. Sakhr b. Khansaʾ—the Messenger of God ﷺ used to send him after Ibn Rawaha, and he would estimate for them.”"],[1829,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ while food was in front of him, so Jarhad brought his left hand near to eat, and his right hand was injured. He said: “Eat with the right.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is injured. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ blew on it, and he did not complain about it until he died."],[1830,"That he came with a group of his people wanting to accept Islam. They attended the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the salam, he said: “Let every man take the hand of his companion.” None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was big and tall, so no one could be preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I finished it until he had milked seven goats for me, and I finished them. Then I was brought a cooked dish in a pot, and I finished it. Umm Ayman said: May Allah starve whoever starves the Messenger of Allah this night. He said: “Enough, O Umm Ayman. He has eaten his provision, and our provision is with Allah.” When morning came, they went out and gathered with his companions, and each man told what had been brought to him. Jahjah said: Seven goats were milked for me, and I finished them, and a cooked dish in a pot, and I finished it. Then they prayed the Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Let every man take the hand of his companion.” None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was big and tall, so no one could be preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I drank my fill and was satisfied. Umm Ayman said: O Messenger of Allah, is this not our guest? He said: “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tonight he ate in the intestine of a believer, and before that he ate in the intestine of a disbeliever. A disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while a believer eats in one intestine.”"],[1831,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta’if: Julayhah b. ‘Abd Allah b. Muharib b. Nashib b. Sa‘d b. Layth."],[1832,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended the expedition to Tabuk, he said to Jadd b. Qays, \"Would you like (to fight) the fair-skinned women (lit. daughters of the yellow ones)?\" He said, \"Permit me to stay behind and do not tempt me.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: \"And among them is he who says, 'Permit me and do not tempt me'\" (Qur'an 9:49)."],[1833,"We met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Friday, and he asked us who we were. We said, \"We are the Banu 'Abd Manaf.\" He said, \"You are the Banu 'Abd Allah (servants of Allah).\""],[1834,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I asked my Lord for four things, and He gave me three and withheld one. I asked Him that my Ummah not unite upon misguidance, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not destroy them with years of famine as He destroyed the nations before them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not let an enemy from other than themselves overcome them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not make them into factions, nor let them taste one another’s violence, but He withheld it from me.”"],[1835,"That Junadah al-Azdi led a people in prayer. When he stood for the prayer, he turned to his right and said, “Do you approve?” They said, “Yes.” Then he did the same on his left, then said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever leads a people while they dislike him, his prayer does not go beyond his collarbone.’”"],[1836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things are from the deeds of the people of ignorance that the people of Islam will not abandon: seeking rain from the stars, reviling lineage, and wailing over the dead.”"],[1837,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you retire to your bed, recite \"Say, O disbelievers\" until you finish it, for it is a declaration of freedom from polytheism.'"],[1838,"From Jabalah b. al-Azraq, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed beside a wall with many stones, a Zuhr or 'Asr prayer. When he sat in the two rak'ahs, a scorpion came out and stung him, and he fainted. The people treated him with incantations. When he regained consciousness, he said, “Allah healed me, not your incantation.”"],[1839,"And in the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': “In naming those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , Jabalah b. 'Amr, and from Banu Bayadah, a Badri.”"],[1840,"And in the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': “In his naming of those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib: Jabalah from Banu Bayadah, a Badri.”"],[1841,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have a desert area in which I pray. Command me a night to go down to the mosque to pray in it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Go down on the night of the twenty-third.”"],[1842,"I recited aloud behind the Prophet ﷺ. When he finished, he said, “O Jahr, let your Lord hear, but do not let me hear.”"],[1843,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote him a letter, and he patched his bucket with it. His daughter said to him, “You took the letter of the master of the Arabs and patched your bucket with it!” So he fled, taking every little and much that was his, then later came as a Muslim. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Look for whatever of your belongings you find before the division of shares, and take it.”"],[1844,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to consult him about jihad. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do you have parents?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Stay with them, for Paradise is under their feet.”"],[1845,"From Jidar, a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Our enemy met us, and he stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “O people, you have woken up among green, yellow, and red, and in the baggage is what is in them. When you meet your enemy, advance, advance! For there is no one who charges in the path of Allah but two of the wide-eyed houris hasten to him. When he is martyred, the first drop that falls from his blood, Allah ﷻ expiates every sin from him, and the two wipe the dust from his face, saying, ‘We are for you,’ and he says, ‘I am for you both.’”"],[1846,"Jarir, 'Adi b. Hatim, and Hanzalah the scribe left Kufah for Qarqisiya, and they said: \"We will not stay in a city where 'Uthman ؓ is reviled.\""],[1847,"The Prophet ﷺ came while his companions were sitting, and he said: “Why do I see you in separate groups?” Sufyan said, meaning separate circles."],[1848,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a people who had raised their hands during prayer, and he said: “They have raised their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses. Be still during the prayer.”"],[1849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque upon us and saw them raising their hands during prayer, and he said: “What is the matter with me, seeing them raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still during the prayer.”"],[1850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them—I think he said in the mosque—while they were raising their hands, and he said: “What is the matter with me, seeing you raising your hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still during the prayer.”"],[1851,"The Prophet ﷺ came out and entered the mosque, and he saw the people raising their hands. He said: “What is the matter with me, seeing the people raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still during the prayer.”"],[1852,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a group who had raised their hands, and he said: \"They are like the tails of spirited horses. Be still in prayer.\""],[1853,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to the mosque and saw them in separate circles, sitting. He said: \"Why do I see you in scattered groups?\""],[1854,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque while they were sitting, and he said: \"Why do I see you in scattered groups?\""],[1855,"The enemy captured a she-camel belonging to a man from Banu Sulaym. Then a Muslim man bought it, and its owner recognized it. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take it for the price he had paid to the enemy, or else leave it between him and the other man."],[1856,"Two men brought a dispute over a camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Each of them produced evidence that it was his, and he judged between them."],[1857,"Two men brought a dispute over a camel to the Prophet ﷺ. Each of them produced two witnesses that it was his, and the Prophet ﷺ divided it between them."],[1858,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: When we prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, we would say, \"Peace be upon you, peace be upon you\" — and Mis'ar gestured with his hand to his right and left — so he said: \"What is the matter with these people raising their hands as if they were the tails of spirited horses? Is it not enough for one of you — or for one of them — to place his hand on his thigh and then greet his brother on his right and left?\""],[1859,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ and we would say with our hands, \"Peace be upon you, peace be upon you.\" He said: \"What is the matter with people who fling their hands as if they were the tails of spirited horses? Is it not enough for one of you — or rather, it is enough for one of you — to place his hand on his thigh and then greet his brother on his right and left?\""],[1860,"My father and I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he prayed with us. When he said the salam, the people gestured with their hands to the right and left. He saw them and said: \"What is the matter with you, turning your hands as if they were the tails of spirited horses? When one of you says the salam, let him greet the one on his right and the one on his left.\" When they prayed with him again, they did not do that."],[1861,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we said the salam, we gestured with our hands, \"Peace be upon you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at us and said: \"What is the matter with you, gesturing with your hands as if they were the tails of spirited horses? When one of you says the salam, let him turn to his companions and not gesture with his hand.\""],[1862,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ on a moonlit night, wearing a red hulla.\" He said: \"I began to look at him and at the moon, and he was more beautiful in my eyes than the moon.\""],[1863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour have been sent like this from this\" — his two fingers, the middle and index."],[1864,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two.”"],[1865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two.”"],[1866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two.”"],[1867,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “I was sent, I and the Hour, like this one from this one.”"],[1868,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two.”"],[1869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This religion will continue to exist until there are twelve caliphs.\" Isma'il said, \"I think that my father (meaning the Prophet Ibrahim) said that all the ummah (nation/community) will unite upon them.\""],[1870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This religion will not be harmed by those who seek it until twelve successors stand up, all of them from the Quraysh.\""],[1871,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Three things I fear for my Ummah: seeking rain by the stars, oppression of the ruler, and denial of the divine decree.”"],[1872,"“The first to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sa'd.”"],[1873,"“The first to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sa'd.”"],[1874,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition, and we routed them. Sa'd pursued a rider among them. He turned to him and saw his leg protruding from the stirrup, so he shot him with an arrow. I saw the blood flowing as if it were a shoelace, and he dismounted.”"],[1875,"From Jabir b. Samurah or a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Prophet ﷺ used to tend sheep. He advanced in shepherding and came to be among camels, and he had a partner. They hired out the sister of Khadijah. When they completed the journey, something remained owed to them by her. His partner kept coming to them and demanding payment, and he would say to Muhammad ﷺ, “Come along.” But he would say, “You go, for I am too shy.” She said once, when he came to them, “Where is Muhammad? Why does he not come with you?” He said, “I told him, but he claimed he was too shy.” She said, “I have never seen a man more intensely shy, nor more chaste, nor more loyal.” This fell into the heart of her sister Khadijah, so she sent to him, saying, “Come to my father and propose to me.” He said, “Your father is a man of great wealth, and he will not do it.” She said, “Go, meet him, and speak to him; then I will suffice you. Come when he is drunk.” So he did, and he came to him, and he married him to her. When morning came, he sat in the assembly, and it was said to him, “You have done well; you have married Muhammad.” He said, “Did I do that?” They said, “Yes.” He stood up and went in to her and said, “The people say that I have married Muhammad, but I did not do it.” She said, “Do not make a fool of your own judgment, for Muhammad ﷺ is such and such.” She kept at him until he was satisfied. Then she sent to Muhammad ﷺ two measures of silver or gold, and she said, “Buy a garment and gift it to me, and a ram, and such and such.” So he did."],[1876,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, should I purify myself after eating the meat of sheep?” He said, “If you wish, then purify yourself, and if you wish, then leave it.” He said, “May I pray in sheep pens?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Should I purify myself after eating camel meat?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “May I pray in camel resting places?” He said, “No.”"],[1877,"“O Messenger of Allah, should I perform ablution after eating sheep meat?” He said, “If you wish, do it, and if you wish, do not.” He said, “Should I perform ablution after eating camel meat?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in sheep resting places?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “May I pray in camel resting places?” He said, “No.”"],[1878,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: Should one perform wudu' after eating sheep meat? He said, \"If you wish, perform wudu', and if you wish, do not perform wudu'.\" He said: May I pray in a sheep pen? He said, \"Yes.\""],[1879,"A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Should I purify myself after eating camel meat? The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" He said: May I pray in camel resting places? The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No.\" He said: May I purify myself after sheep meat? He said, \"If you wish, purify yourself, and if you wish, do not purify yourself.\" He said: May I pray in sheep pens? He said, \"Yes.\""],[1880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: May one pray in camel watering places? He said, \"No.\" It was said: Should one perform wudu' after eating their meat? He said, \"Yes.\" He said: May one pray in sheep pens? He said, \"Yes.\" It was said: Should one perform wudu' after eating their meat? He said, \"No.\""],[1881,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform wudu' after eating camel meat, not to perform wudu' after sheep meat, to pray in sheep folds, and not to pray in camel watering places.”"],[1882,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform wudu' after eating camel meat, not to perform wudu' after sheep meat, to pray in sheep pens, and not to pray in camel watering places.”"],[1883,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was asked: Should we perform wudu' after eating camel meat? He said, \"Yes, perform wudu' after eating camel meat.\" They said: May we pray in camel resting places? He said, \"No.\" They said: Should we perform wudu' after eating sheep meat? He said, \"If you wish, perform wudu', and if you wish, do not perform wudu'.\" They said: May we pray in sheep pens? He said, \"Yes.\""],[1884,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, should I perform wudu' after eating sheep meat? He said, \"If you wish, perform wudu', and if you wish, do not perform wudu'.\" He said: Should I perform wudu' after eating camel meat? He said, \"Yes.\" He said: May I pray in camel resting places? He said, \"No.\" He said: May I pray in sheep pens? He said, \"Yes.\""],[1885,"From his grandfather Jabir b. Samurah: “We used to pray in sheep pens and not pray in camel resting places, and we used to perform wudu' after eating camel meat and not perform wudu' after eating sheep meat.”"],[1886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to fast on Ashura, urge us to do it, and check on us regarding it. When Ramadan was made obligatory, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and he did not check on us regarding it.”"],[1887,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him.”"],[1888,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him, and when Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will certainly be spent in the path of Allah ﷻ.”"],[1889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him.”"],[1890,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When Kisra perishes, there will be no Kisra after him; and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the cause of Allah ﷻ.”"],[1891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Caesar is gone, there will be no Caesar after him; and when Kisra is gone, there will be no Kisra after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the cause of Allah.”"],[1892,"'There will be twelve Amir after me.\"' He said: \"Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me, who said that he ﷺ had said: 'All of them are from Quraish.\"' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2223)"],[1893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This matter will continue to exist until there are twelve successors.\""],[1894,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the dabb (a lizard)?” He replied: “A nation from the Children of Israel was transformed, and I do not know which of the creatures it was transformed into. I neither command it, nor forbid it.”"],[1895,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A group of Muslims will certainly conquer the white palace of the family of Kisra.”"],[1896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who is consulted is entrusted.”"],[1897,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"The evil ones will leave the city until they enter the wasteland, not fearing anyone except Allah (SWT).\""],[1898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This matter will remain prevail, and no one who opposes it will harm it, until twelve rulers appear, all of them from Quraysh.”"],[1899,"The Prophet ﷺ used to sit between the two sermons on Friday, and he would deliver the sermon standing. His prayer was moderate, and his sermon was moderate, and he would recite verses from the Qur'an on the pulpit."],[1900,"The Prophet ﷺ used to sit in his place of prayer when dawn broke until the sun rose brightly."],[1901,"Regarding the Prophet's ﷺ sermon, he said: “He would deliver the sermon standing, then sit for a short while, then stand.”"],[1902,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver the sermon standing, then sit for a short while, then stand."],[1903,"I asked Jabir b. Samurah what the Prophet ﷺ would do after praying the morning prayer. He said, \"He would remain seated in his place until the sun rose.\""],[1904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of Abu Ayyub. Whenever food was brought to him and he ate from it, he would send its leftovers to Abu Ayyub. Then food containing garlic was brought to him, and he did not eat from it; he sent it to Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub did not eat from it because he did not see the trace of the Prophet ﷺ in it. Then Abu Ayyub came to him and asked him about it, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, is it unlawful?\" He said, \"No, but I disliked it because of the odor.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"Then I dislike what you dislike.\""],[1905,"\"The gray hair of the Prophet ﷺ, when he combed his beard — I think he said and oiled it — did not show; and when he left it, it showed.\""],[1906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This religion will remain standing, a band of Muslims fighting for it until the Hour is established.\""],[1907,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Madinah was named Tabah.\""],[1908,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the noon prayer 'By the night when it covers' and 'By the sun and its brightness' and the like of them; and he would recite longer than that in the morning prayer.\""],[1909,"\"When the sun declined, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer and recited approximately 'By the night when it covers'; and in the afternoon prayer likewise; and in the other prayers likewise, except the morning prayer, for he would prolong it.\""],[1910,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the noon prayer when the sun declined, meaning when it passed the meridian, and he would pray the afternoon prayer around the time of your prayer.\""],[1911,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"There will be twelve leaders.\" Then he said a word that I did not understand, so the people said, \"He said, 'All of them are from Quraysh.'\""],[1912,"That he heard Jabir b. Samurah say: A man with abundant hair, short, and muscular was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he confessed to fornication. He turned him away twice, then he ordered that he be stoned. Then he said, \"Every time we go out in a military expedition in the path of Allah, one of you stays behind and bleats like the bleating of a billy goat, giving one of them a small amount of milk. Indeed, if anyone of you is brought to me having done this, I will make him an exemplary punishment.\" Simak sometimes said, \"I will punish him harshly.\""],[1913,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.\""],[1914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah while we were present. Then a horse was brought, and it was hobbled until he mounted it. It began to prance with him while we ran around him. A man near Jabir b. Samurah said that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"How many clusters of dates for Ibn al-Dahdah are hanging in Paradise!\""],[1915,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah, and he was on a horse, and it was swaying with him.\""],[1916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “How many a date-palm cluster Ibn al-Dahdah will have in Paradise.”"],[1917,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “You shall certainly open the white treasure of the family of Kisra — or he said: that which is in the white — a band of the Muslims.”"],[1918,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had dark-rimmed eyes.” Shuʿbah said: I said to Simāk, “What is ‘dark-rimmed eyes’?” He said, “Wide eyes with reddish rims.”"],[1919,"About the description of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He had dark-rimmed eyes, a wide mouth, and lean ankles.”"],[1920,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the noon prayer “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” and in the dawn prayer something longer than that."],[1921,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan.”"],[1922,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed I recognize a stone that used to greet me before I was sent as a Prophet; indeed I recognize it.”"],[1923,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and between his shoulders was something like a pigeon’s egg — the seal of prophethood.”"],[1924,"Boys used to pass by the Prophet ﷺ, and some of them he would wipe one cheek and some of them he would wipe both cheeks. I passed by him and he wiped my cheek. He said: And the cheek that the Prophet ﷺ wiped became better looking than the other cheek."],[1925,"“The companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to recite poetry to one another while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ listened.”"],[1926,"I heard Jābir b. Samurah say: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit without speaking, then stand and deliver another sermon. So whoever tells you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon sitting has lied.”"],[1927,"“The muʾadhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would give the call to prayer, then wait and not pronounce the iqāmah until he saw the Prophet ﷺ had come out; then he would pronounce the iqāmah when he saw him.”"],[1928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed the morning prayer, would remain seated in his place until the sun rose."],[1929,"He heard Jabir b. Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the prayers similar to the way you pray today, but he would make them light. His prayer was lighter than your prayer. He used to recite in the dawn prayer al-Waqi'ah and surahs like it."],[1930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A group among the Muslims will conquer the treasures of Kisra.\""],[1931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had thick hair and a thick beard."],[1932,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought Ma'iz b. Malik, a short man wearing only a waist-wrapper with no cloak. He spoke to him, and I do not know what he said to him, for I was far from him and people were between me and him. Then he said: \"Take him away.\" Then he said: \"Bring him back.\" He spoke to him, and I could hear, except that people were between me and him. Then he said: \"Take him away and stone him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and delivered a sermon while I heard him say: \"Whenever we go out in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind with a bleating like the bleating of a billy goat, and gives one of the women a small amount of milk. By Allah, if I get hold of any of them, I will make an example of him.\""],[1933,"I saw the seal near his shoulder, like a pigeon's egg, resembling his skin."],[1934,"From Jabir: They entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was leaning on a cushion on his left side."],[1935,"He heard Jabir b. Samurah say: A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died. He said: \"He has not died.\" Then he came to him a second and a third time. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"How did he die?\" He said: He slaughtered himself with a broad-headed arrow he had with him. So he did not pray over him."],[1936,"There was no gray hair on the head of the Prophet ﷺ or his beard except a few hairs at the parting of his head. When he combed his beard and oiled it, they became visible; when he left it, they were not apparent."],[1937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This religion will not cease to be established, with a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes.\""],[1938,"'There will be twelve Amir after me.\"' He said: \"Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me, who said that he ﷺ had said: 'All of them are from Quraish.\"' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2223)"],[1939,"A camel died in al-Harrah, and next to it were needy people. The Prophet ﷺ granted them a concession to eat it."],[1940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer and began rebuking something in front of him. When he finished, we asked him, and he said: \"That was a devil who threw sparks of fire on my foot to distract me from the prayer. Had I seized him, he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of Madinah went around him.\""],[1941,"It was said to Jabir: Was the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like a sword? He said: \"No, rather like the sun and the moon.\""],[1942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he had prayed the dawn prayer, would remain seated in his place until the sun rose."],[1943,"Jabir b. Samurah said: The prayer and sermon of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were moderate."],[1944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the dawn prayer Qāf, and the Glorious Quran, and his prayer after that was light."],[1945,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deliver a Friday sermon except standing. Whoever tells you that he sat, then declare him a liar, for he did not do that. Jabir said: The Prophet ﷺ would deliver the sermon, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon; and he would deliver two sermons, sitting between them."],[1946,"The Prophet ﷺ said: This religion will remain established, with a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."],[1947,"A man fell ill and was mourned over. His neighbor came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: He has died. He said: What makes you know that? He said: I saw him, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: He has not died. The man returned and found him mourned over. His wife said: Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and inform him. The man said: O Allah, curse him. He said: Then the man went and saw that he had stabbed himself with some broad-bladed arrows he had with him. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him that he had died. He said: What makes you know that? He said: I saw him stab himself with broad-bladed arrows he had with him. He said: You saw him? He said: Yes. He said: Then I will not pray over him."],[1948,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah: Did you used to sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, often. He would not leave the place where he had prayed until the sun rose. When it rose, he would get up. He would prolong silence, and they would talk and take up matters of the pre-Islamic era and laugh, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would smile."],[1949,"The Prophet ﷺ would deliver the sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon standing. Whoever tells you that he delivered the sermon sitting or seated has lied. By Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand times."],[1950,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars. I said to Jabir: Did you hear it yourself? He said: I heard it myself."],[1951,"'There will be twelve Amir after me.\"' He said: \"Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me, who said that he ﷺ had said: 'All of them are from Quraish.\"' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2223)"],[1952,"About the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: He would keep it light for them, and he would not pray the prayer of these people."],[1953,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the dawn prayer Qāf, and the Glorious Quran, and the like of it."],[1954,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer and began to rebuke something in front of him. When he finished, we asked him, and he said: That was a devil who threw on my foot sparks of fire to tempt me away from the prayer. He said: I rebuked him, and if I had seized him, he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of the people of Madinah went around him."],[1955,"Bowls would be gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in the house of Abu Ayyub, and he would send back to him the leftover of what he ate. A bowl came to him, and he sent it back as it was, not diminishing anything from it. Abu Ayyub said to his family: Do not eat until I find out why he left it. He said: So he sought permission to enter upon him and entered, and said: Nothing used to come to us from you but that you ate from it, except this bowl; I do not know what is the matter with it. He said: 'It had garlic in it, and I disliked its odor. As for it, there is no harm in it, except that I disliked its odor.' He said: Then I dislike what you dislike. He said: 'Then you know best.'"],[1956,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: 'Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights.'"],[1957,"From the Prophet ﷺ: that he prayed on the day of Eid without an adhan and without an iqamah."],[1958,"When Ibn al-Dahdah died, the Prophet ﷺ followed his funeral procession. When he was buried and he was finished with him, a horse was brought to him and he mounted it, and he returned on it, ﷺ."],[1959,"I prayed along with Messenger of Allah ﷺ the first prayer. He then went to his family and I also went along with him when he met some children (on the way). He began to pat the cheeks of each one of them. He also patted my cheek and I experienced a coolness or a fragrance of his hand as if it had been brought out from the scent bag of a perfumer. (Using translation from Muslim 2329)"],[1960,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and I greeted him, but he did not respond to me. Then he stood up and entered his house, performed ablution, then came out to me and said: 'And upon you be peace, and upon you be peace.'"],[1961,"A she-camel died at al-Harrah, next to which was a household of Banu Sulaym who were in need. The Prophet ﷺ gave them permission to eat it, and they ate from it during their winter, and they melted it (its fat). The wording is from the hadith of Ibn al-Asbahani."],[1962,"Bilal would give the call to prayer for Zuhr when the sun had passed its zenith, and he would sometimes delay the iqamah but would not delay the adhan."],[1963,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ more than a hundred times, and his Companions would recite poetry to one another and mention things from the affairs of the pre-Islamic era, and sometimes he would smile with them."],[1964,"The prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."],[1965,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ a hundred times, and he would not deliver a sermon except standing, and he would sit once (during the sermon)."],[1966,"When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, one of us would sit wherever he ended up."],[1967,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Eid, and no adhan was given for it, nor an iqamah."],[1968,"I said to Jabir: Did you used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ? He said: “Yes; he was long of silence.”"],[1969,"“The Prophet ﷺ stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman.”"],[1970,"“A man killed himself, and the Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him.”"],[1971,"“A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ was wounded and it caused him pain, so he crept to a horn of his on his sword, took a broad-headed arrow, and killed himself; and the Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him.”"],[1972,"“Bilal used to give the call to prayer, then ask permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[1973,"“The Prophet ﷺ led them in the dawn prayer and recited ‘By the sun and its morning brightness’ and ‘By the heaven and the night-comer.’”"],[1974,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to delay the last evening prayer.”"],[1975,"“When the Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he would not rise from the place in which he had prayed until the sun rose.”"],[1976,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I recognize a stone in Makkah that used to greet me during the nights I was sent.”"],[1977,"“I was shown the Night of Decree, then I was made to forget it; so seek it in the last ten.” And he said: “It is a night of wind, rain, and thunder.”"],[1978,"“There was no gray hair on the Prophet’s ﷺ head or in his beard except a few hairs at the parting of his head; when he oiled it, the oil concealed them.”"],[1979,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Islam will continue to be triumphant until there have been twelve Caliphs. Then the Prophet ﷺ said something which I could not understand. I asked my father: What did he say? He said: He has said that all of them (twelve Caliphs) will be from the Quraish. (Using translation from Muslim 1821d)"],[1980,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver speeches standing up."],[1981,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the noon and afternoon prayers ‘By the heaven with constellations’ and ‘By the heaven and the night-comer’ and the like of them.”"],[1982,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned a she-goat but did not mention the skin.\""],[1983,"Bilal used to give the call to prayer for Zuhr when the sun had passed its zenith."],[1984,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.”"],[1985,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God ﷻ named it Tabah.”"],[1986,"A man was in the Harrah with a wife of his, and another man lost a camel of his. The man in the Harrah found it and kept it with him. The camel fell ill, and his wife said to him, “If only you would slaughter it, and we could cut its meat and fat into strips and eat it.” He refused her until it died. Then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. He said, “Do you have anything to sustain you besides that?” or he said, “Do you have anything to sustain you besides that?” He said, “No.” He said, “Cut its fat and meat into strips and eat it.” Later the owner of the camel came and said, “Why did you not slaughter it?” He said, “I felt ashamed before you.”"],[1987,"When food was brought to the Prophet ﷺ and he ate from it, he would send the leftovers to Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub used to seek the traces of the Prophet's ﷺ fingers, placing his fingers where he saw the Prophet's ﷺ fingers. One day a dish was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he found in it the smell of garlic, so he did not eat from it and sent it to Abu Ayyub. Abu Ayyub did not see in it the traces of the Prophet's ﷺ fingers, so he said, “O Messenger of God, I did not see in it the traces of your fingers.” He said, “I found in it the smell of garlic.” He said, “You sent me what you do not eat?” He said, “The angel comes to me.”"],[1988,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering the sermon standing, then he sat for a while without speaking, then he stood and delivered another sermon on his pulpit. Whoever tells you that he saw him delivering the sermon sitting, do not believe him.”"],[1989,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the prayers in a manner similar to your prayers, and he would delay the night prayer a little after your prayer, and he would keep the prayer light.”"],[1990,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A band of the Muslims, or of the believers, will certainly open the treasure of the family of Kisra, which is in the White Palace.”"],[1991,"I heard him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, name Madinah “Taba.”"],[1992,"A mule died in the possession of a man, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his ruling. Jabir claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ said to its owner, “Do you not have what would suffice you from it?” He said, “No.” He said, “Go and eat it.”"],[1993,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.”"],[1994,"I saw Ma'iz when he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ: a short, muscular man. He testified against himself four times that he had committed adultery. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Perhaps you...” He said, “No, by God, he has indeed committed adultery, the other one.” So he stoned him. Then he delivered a sermon and said, “Indeed, whenever we go out in the path of God, one of them leaves behind a bleating like the bleating of a he-goat, giving one of them a small amount of milk. Indeed, if God enables me over any of them, I will make an example of him regarding them.”"],[1995,"The Prophet ﷺ stoned Ma'iz and did not mention flogging."],[1996,"I prayed the Eid prayer with the Prophet ﷺ more than once or twice, without an adhan or an iqamah."],[1997,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed Fajr, he would remain seated in his prayer place until the sun rose."],[1998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the last Isha prayer."],[1999,"I used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, and his prayer was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."],[2000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave two sermons between which he sat, recited the Quran and gave the people an exhortation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1094)"],[2001,"Whenever food was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would eat some of it and then send the remainder to Abu Ayyub. Once, food containing garlic was gifted to him, and he sent it to Abu Ayyub without eating any of it. When Abu Ayyub did not see any trace of the Prophet ﷺ in the food, he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I only left it because of its smell.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"And I dislike what you dislike.\""],[2002,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah, may He be exalted, commanded me to name Madinah Taybah.\" And Abu Bakr said, \"Tabah.\""],[2003,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.\" I said, \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[2004,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver two sermons, sitting between them."],[2005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah. When he returned, a horse was brought to him without a saddle, so he rode it, and we walked."],[2006,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walk alongside a funeral procession, and he rode when a bare horse was brought forward, with nothing on it but its bridle.»"],[2007,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me when I was sent.»"],[2008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This religion will continue to exist, and a group from among the Muslims will fight for it until the Hour is established.\""],[2009,"«It is as if I am looking at the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his locks reaching this place» — and he struck his hand on his chest above his breasts."],[2010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I and the Hour were sent like these two» — and he pointed with his index and middle fingers."],[2011,"«The Prophet ﷺ would remain silent for long periods, so they would speak about matters of the Jahiliyyah and laugh, and he would smile with them.»"],[2012,"Jabir b. Samurah said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite Qaf in the Fajr prayer.»"],[2013,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: «I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and the distance between its two ends is like that between San'a' and Aylah, as if the pitchers in it are stars.»"],[2014,"«The Prophet ﷺ used to stand on the pulpit and deliver a sermon, then sit, then stand and deliver a sermon. He would sit between the two sermons.»"],[2015,"«When the Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon on Friday, he would recite from the Book of Allah and remind the people.»"],[2016,"«I used to pray the prayers with the Prophet ﷺ, and his prayer was moderate, and his sermon was moderate.»"],[2017,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he had prayed the dawn prayer, would remain seated in his place of prayer until the sun rose."],[2018,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Indeed, after me there will be twelve leaders.\" Then he said a word, so I asked my father, and he said, \"All of them will be from the Quraysh tribe.\""],[2019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until he prayed sitting."],[2020,"I saw the seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, like a pigeon's egg."],[2021,"We prayed over Ibn al-Dahdah, a man from the Ansar, and when we had finished with him, a man brought a stallion to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mounted it when he returned from the funeral."],[2022,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"This matter will continue to be established, fought for by a band of Muslims until the Hour comes.\""],[2023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not give a sermon while sitting except when he was standing."],[2024,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah on any day rise from his place where he prayed the dawn prayer until the sun rose, then he would get up."],[2025,"The Prophet ﷺ did not prolong the admonition on Friday; it was only a few brief words."],[2026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Asr slightly before your prayer, and he used to pray Maghrib slightly before your prayer, and he used to delay Isha prayer a bit after your prayer. Bilal used to delay the Dhuhr prayer until the sun's heat disappeared, not exceeding its prescribed time. As for the call to prayer, sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would hurry and sometimes he would delay it."],[2027,"I said to him, \"Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, and he was long in silence.\""],[2028,"I said to him, \"Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, and he was long in silence.\""],[2029,"The Prophet ﷺ returned from the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah on a bareback horse."],[2030,"\"He used to pray Fajr and then remain seated until sunrise.\""],[2031,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The white palace of Kisra will certainly be conquered by a group of the Muslims.\""],[2032,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: \"His sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate.\""],[2033,"The Prophet ﷺ climbed the pulpit and said, \"Ameen, ameen, ameen.\" He ﷺ said, \"Jibreel came to me and said, 'O Muhammad, whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and does not have his sins forgiven and enter Paradise, may Allah distance him.' So I said, 'Ameen.' He ﷺ said, 'O Muhammad, whoever has his parents, either one or both, reaching old age in his life and he does not honor them and receive their compassion, may Allah distance him.' So I said, 'Ameen.' He ﷺ said, 'O Muhammad, whoever has your name mentioned in his presence and he does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him.' So I said, 'Ameen.'\""],[2034,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ wiped over the leather socks.\""],[2035,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had thin shanks, and he would not laugh except smiling, and when I looked at him I said: He has kohl-tinged eyes, but he was not kohl-tinged. The wording is that of the hadith of Abd al-Rahman b. Ubayd Allah."],[2036,"\"The Prophet ﷺ would not break into laughter.\""],[2037,"\"The Prophet ﷺ delivered the sermon standing, then he sat down.\""],[2038,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights.\""],[2039,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"In Makkah there is a stone that greets me; I recognize it when I see it.\""],[2040,"A young man used to serve the Prophet ﷺ and was quick in his errands. He said: \"Ask me for something you need.\" He said: Pray to God Almighty for Paradise for me. He said: He raised his head, drew a deep breath, and said: \"Yes, but help me with much prostration.\""],[2041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever buries three of his children and bears them patiently and seeks reward for them, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\" Umm Ayman said: Or two? He said: \"And whoever buries two and bears them patiently and seeks reward for them, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\" Umm Ayman said: Or one? He fell silent or refrained. Then I heard Umm Ayman say: \"Whoever buries one and bears it patiently and seeks reward, Paradise is for him.\""],[2042,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered all the doors of the mosque to be closed except the door of Ali ؓ. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, let me enter and leave alone. He said: \"I was not commanded regarding any of that.\" So he closed them all except the door of Ali, and sometimes he would pass by while he was in a state of major ritual impurity."],[2043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to discipline his child is better for him than to give charity every day of half a saa' to the poor.\""],[2044,"When the people of Quba asked the Prophet ﷺ to build a mosque for them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let one of you stand up and mount the she-camel.\" Abu Bakr ؓ stood up and mounted her, and he urged her on but she did not move, so he returned and sat down. Then Umar ؓ stood up and mounted her, and he urged her on but she did not move, so he returned and sat down. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Let one of you stand up and mount the she-camel.\" Ali ؓ stood up, and when he placed his foot in the stirrup and steadied himself, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ali, loosen her reins and build around her course, for she is commanded.\""],[2045,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: \"Amin, Amin, Amin.\" Then he said: \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'O Muhammad, whoever reaches one of his parents...'\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[2046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ: \"You are to me of the station of Harun from Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[2047,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who will carry your banner on the Day of Resurrection?\" He said: \"Who else deserves to carry it except the one who carried it in this world, Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ?\""],[2048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ: \"Who was the most wretched of Thamud?\" He said: \"The one who hamstrung the she-camel.\" He said: \"Then who is the most wretched of this nation?\" He said: \"Allah knows best.\" He said: \"Your killer.\""],[2049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ: \"You are a man who will be appointed as a successor, and you will be killed, and this will be dyed from this\" - his beard from his head."],[2050,"No call to prayer was given for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor was the iqamah said, on the two Eids."],[2051,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, before the Hour there will be liars.\""],[2052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen delivering a sermon except standing."],[2053,"A man from Banu Sulaym who was in the harrah, he and his son, used to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah; when evening came he would go to his family. A she-camel of his died, and his wife said to him: \"Feed us its meat, for we are in dire need.\" He said: \"No, by Allah, not until I inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So he came to him and told him the news. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Do you have anything that would make you independent of it?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Go and eat it.\" So they rendered its fat and made use of its meat for the rest of their year."],[2054,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying \"There will be twelve princes\" and then he said something that I didn't hear, so the people assumed that he said \"All of them are from Quraysh.\""],[2055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not leave the place where he had prayed until the sun rose."],[2056,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, “So-and-so has died.” He said, “He has not died,” saying it three times."],[2057,"We prayed an obligatory prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he clasped his hands during the prayer. When he finished the prayer, we said, “O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?” He said, “No, except that Satan wanted to pass in front of me, so I choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue on my hand. By Allah, had it not been for what my brother Sulayman preceded me to, he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque so that the children of Madinah could go around him.”"],[2058,"A man from Jarmaqāniyyā came to the Prophet ﷺ.” And he mentioned the hadith."],[2059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray the obligatory prayer as a medium prayer, neither prolonging it nor making it light, and he would delay the 'Atamah (Isha)."],[2060,"I was with my father while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was giving a sermon. He said, “You will not cease to be in good as long as twelve rulers stand over you.” I said to my father, “Did I hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say just now like that?” My father said, “He said, ‘All of them are from Quraysh.’”"],[2061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My nation will continue to be upon the truth, manifest, until there are twelve leaders among them, all from the Quraysh tribe.\""],[2062,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and I heard him say, \"There will be twelve leaders after me.\" Then he lowered his voice. So I said to my father, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There will be twelve leaders after me.' So what did he lower his voice for?\" He replied, \"All of them will be from the Quraysh.\""],[2063,"'There will be twelve Amir after me.\"' He said: \"Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me, who said that he ﷺ had said: 'All of them are from Quraish.\"' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2223)"],[2064,"From the Prophet ﷺ — Sahl said: and 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Simak b. Harb, from Tamim, from Jabir b. Samurah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \"The enemy seized a man's she-camel from the Muslims, then a man from the Muslims bought it. Its owner recognized it and came to the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take it back for the price he had paid for it to the enemy; otherwise, he was to leave him and it alone.\""],[2065,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them just as a brilliant star is seen on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and 'Umar are among them, and what an excellent pair they are.\""],[2066,"\"...from behind him, so that I could look at the place of the seal. When he saw me, he threw his cloak over his shoulder, and I looked at it.\""],[2067,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"There will be twelve leaders after me.\" Then he spoke something that I did not hear, so I asked the people and I asked my father what he said? And he was closer to him than me, so he said, \"All of them are from Quraysh.\""],[2068,"I was among the delegation that the Messenger of God ﷺ lodged, from 'Abd al-Qays, though I was not one of them; I was only with my father. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking from gourds, glazed jars, hollowed-out palm stumps, and pitch-coated vessels.\""],[2069,"From the Prophet ﷺ — thus said Ibn Numayr: Jabir b. Abi Tariq."],[2070,"\"I saw Hakim b. Jabir dyeing his hair with yellow dye.\""],[2071,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and he had a gourd. I said: \"What are you doing?\" He said: \"We are adding it to our food to increase it.\""],[2072,"I entered upon the Prophet and saw a squash / pumpkin with him, so I asked, \"What is this, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"We increase the meals for our family with it.\""],[2073,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he had this gourd, so I said: What is this? He said: \"This is gourd; this is squash. We use it to increase our food.\""],[2074,"I saw squash with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: What is this? He said: \"We use it to increase our food.\""],[2075,"Jabir b. Tariq said to me: I saw this with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: \"Something with which we increase our food.\""],[2076,"In the book of Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': \"In naming those who witnessed with Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , and Jabr b. Anas, a Badri, from Banu Zurayq.\""],[2077,"A people disputed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over a booth, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Hudhayfah to judge between them, and he ruled in favor of the one whose side faced the cords of the booth. When he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, he said: \"You have judged correctly, or: You have done well.\""],[2078,"Two brothers had a fence in the middle of a house, and they died, each leaving descendants. The descendants of each claimed that the fence belonged to him alone. They disputed before the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman with them, and he ruled that the fence belonged to the one on whose side the knots of the cords were found. Then he returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: \"You have judged correctly, or: You have done well.\""],[2079,"A man struck another with a sword on his forearm, not at a joint. The victim brought a complaint to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ruled for blood money. The injured man wanted retaliation, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah bless it for you,\" but he did not rule for retaliation."],[2080,"A man cut off another man's hand from the middle of the forearm. He brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled for five thousand dirhams, and said: \"Take it, may it be blessed for you.\""],[2081,"The Quran was compiled during the time of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , by six individuals from the Ansar: Zaid ibn Thabit, Abu Zaid, Muadh ibn Jabal, Abu Darda, Saad ibn Ubada, and Ubay ibn Ka'b. In the narration of Zakariyya, it is mentioned that Jarirah ibn Mu'ammar bin Jarirah had memorized the Quran, except for one or two chapters."],[2082,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me something in Islam that I may understand, and be brief. He said: \"Do not get angry.\""],[2083,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Hisham b. Urwah from his father from al-Ahnaf b. Qays from Jariyah b. Qudamah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying that will benefit me, and be brief, perhaps I will retain it. He said: \"Do not get angry.\" He repeated it to him several times, saying: \"Do not get angry.\""],[2084,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Tell me a concise statement, so that perhaps I may comprehend it.” He said: “Do not become angry.” He repeated it to him, and he said: “Do not become angry.”"],[2085,"He said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me a statement that will benefit me, and make it brief, so that perhaps I may comprehend it.” He said: “Do not become angry.” He repeated it to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Do not become angry.”"],[2086,"His paternal uncle came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me a statement and make it brief; perhaps I will retain it.” He said: “Do not become angry.” He repeated it to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Do not become angry.”"],[2087,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, teach me something in Islam that will benefit me.” He said: “Do not become angry.” I repeated it to him, and he did not add anything to that."],[2088,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me a concise statement, so that perhaps I may comprehend it.” He said: “Do not become angry.” I repeated it to him several times, and each time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do not become angry.”"],[2089,"“O Messenger of Allah, tell me a statement that will benefit me, and make it brief, so that perhaps I may comprehend it.” He said: “Do not become angry.” Then he repeated it, and he said: “Do not become angry.”"],[2090,"“When the people of Bahrain arrived, and al-Jarud came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he rejoiced at him, drew him near, and brought him close.”"],[2091,"He informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about stray animals, and he said: “The stray animal of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2092,"From al-Jarud al-Abdi, who traced it back to the Prophet ﷺ: “The stray animal of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not approach it.”"],[2093,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about some wonderful stray camels that were brought back to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The stray animal of a believer is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2094,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The stray animal of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2095,"from the Prophet, ﷺ : \"The lost [property] of a Muslim [leads to] the burning fire.\""],[2096,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The stray animal of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2097,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2099,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.” Sa'id did not mention Yazid b. 'Abd Allah."],[2100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.”"],[2101,"Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, (of) Jadhimah 'Abd al-Qays, narrated to us; al-Jarud narrated to us; he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not approach it.”"],[2102,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and there were few riding camels. The people discussed the riding camels among themselves, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, we pass by a small herd of riding camels at a water-worn bank, so may we make use of their backs?” He said, “No. The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire. The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire. The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire” three times. He said, “And a found item you find: announce it, then do not conceal it or hide it. If you find its owner, return it; otherwise, it is only the wealth of Allah, Mighty and Exalted, which He directs to whomever He wills.”"],[2103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not approach it.” And he said, “A stray animal and a found item you find: announce it, and do not conceal or hide it. If you recognize (its owner), return it; otherwise, it is the wealth of Allah, which He gives to whomever He wills.”"],[2104,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and there were few riding camels. We discussed what riding camels would suffice us, and we said, “A small herd we come upon at a water-worn bank, so we may make use of their backs.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire” three times, “so do not approach it.”"],[2105,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and there were few riding camels. We discussed what riding camels would suffice us, and we said, “A small herd we come upon at a water-worn bank, so we may make use of their backs.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The stray camel of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire” three times, “so do not approach it.”"],[2106,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about drinking while standing? And he forbade him."],[2107,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he forbade a man to drink while standing."],[2108,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have a religion, so if I leave my religion and enter your religion, will Allah not punish me in the Hereafter?” He said, “Yes.”"],[2109,"It is said to him: A part came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my family angers me, so how should I punish them? He said: “Pardon.” Then he said it a second time, until he said it three times. He said: “If you punish, then punish according to the extent of the sin, and avoid the face.”"],[2110,"From Urwah: “In naming those killed on the Day of al-Yamama from the Ansar, then from Banu Jahjaba: Jazʾ b. Malik b. ʿAmir b. Hudayr.”"],[2111,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those martyred on the Day of al-Yamama from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, then from Banu ʿAmr b. ʿAwf: Jazʾ b. Malik.”"],[2112,"From Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Khunas b. Sinan b. ʿUbayd b. ʿAdi b. Ghanm b. ʿAwf b. al-Khazraj: Jubar b. Sakhr b. Umayya b. Khansaʾ b. ʿUbayd b. ʿAdi b. Ghanm.”"],[2113,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who witnessed al-ʿAqaba from the Ansar: Jubar b. Sakhr.”"],[2114,"“Jubar b. Sakhr died in Madinah in the year thirty, and he was sixty-two years old.”"],[2115,"“I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he placed me on his right.”"],[2116,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Cover your thigh, for the thigh is ʿawra.”"],[2117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I had uncovered my thigh, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Cover it, for it is part of the ʿawra.”"],[2118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by him while his thigh was uncovered, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Cover your thigh, O Jarhad, for the thigh is ʿawra.”"],[2119,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he saw him when his thigh had become uncovered, so he said: “Cover it, for the thigh is ‘awrah.”"],[2120,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he had uncovered his thigh, so he said: “Cover it, for it is part of the ‘awrah.”"],[2121,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Zur‘ah b. ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Jarhad, from his father, who said: Jarhad was one of the Ahl al-Suffah. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with us while my thigh was uncovered, so he said: “Do you not know that the thigh is ‘awrah?”"],[2122,"That the Prophet ﷺ sat with him, and he was one of the Ahl al-Suffah, and the Prophet ﷺ saw his thigh uncovered, so he said: “Cover your thigh, for the thigh is ‘awrah.”"],[2123,"That he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with us one day while my thigh was uncovered, so he said: “Cover yourself. Do you not know that the thigh is ‘awrah?”"],[2124,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was in the mosque wearing a burdah, and my thigh had become uncovered, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Cover your thigh, O Jarhad, for the thigh is ‘awrah.”"],[2125,"\"Ibn Jarhad informed me from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ passed by him while his thigh was exposed, so the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Cover your thigh, for indeed it is 'Awrah.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2798)"],[2126,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “A man’s thigh is part of the ‘awrah.”"],[2127,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A Muslim man’s thigh is part of his ‘awrah.”"],[2128,"I heard al-Awza‘i say: “The thigh in the mosque is ‘awrah, but in the bathhouse it is not ‘awrah.”"],[2129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever offers an excuse to his brother and he does not accept it, then upon him is a sin like that of a collector of unjust taxes (maks).\""],[2130,"If you were to come to the Mount, you did not come to it.\" Then he mentioned the hadith."],[2131,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Mounts are not to be ridden except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Mosque of Jerusalem (Bayt al-Maqdis).\""],[2132,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The livers of camels are only to be driven to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No journeys are to be undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of the Messenger, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2134,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No mounts are to be ridden except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"I am riding out to the Jews. Whoever goes with me among you should not initiate the greeting of peace to them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\" So when we came to them, they greeted us, and we said, \"And upon you.\""],[2136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are going tomorrow to the Jews. When you meet them and they greet you, say, 'And upon you.'\" So we met them and they greeted us, and we said, \"And upon you.\""],[2137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am proceeding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of peace with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[2138,"From Abu Basra al-Ghifari ؓ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the 'Asr prayer one day at al-Mukhammas, then departed and said: \"This prayer was presented to those before you, but they neglected it and abandoned it. Whoever of you prays it will have its reward doubled twice, and there is no prayer after it until the witness (the star) rises.\" Al-Layth said: \"I heard it from Khayr b. Nu'aym with this chain.\""],[2139,"That he heard Abu Basrah al-Ghifari say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the ‘Asr prayer at al-Mukhammas, a valley among some of their valleys, then he said, “This prayer was presented to those before you, but they neglected it. Behold, whoever prays it, his reward is doubled, and there is no prayer after it until you see the witness” — and that is the star."],[2140,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ informed me that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Indeed, Allah has added a prayer for you, so pray it between the 'Isha prayer and the Witr prayer. Indeed, it is the Witr prayer.\" And know that he is Abu Basrah al-Ghifari."],[2141,"A man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Indeed, Allah has added a prayer for you, so pray it between the evening prayer and the dawn prayer, the Witr prayer, the Witr.\" And it is Abu Basrah Al-Ghifari."],[2142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has added to you a prayer, so preserve it, and He has made its time from the period between Isha and Fajr, and it is Witr.\""],[2143,"I boarded a ship from al-Fustat with Abu Basrah, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ. Then he brought his lunch near, and said to me, “Come closer.” I said, “Aren’t we in the houses?” Abu Basrah said, “Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”"],[2144,"That he traveled with Abu Basrah al-Ghifari in Ramadan. When they departed from al-Fustat, he called for food while we could still see al-Fustat. I said to him, “Will you eat while, if we wanted to look at al-Fustat, we could see it?” He said, “Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions?” Then he broke his fast."],[2145,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of his expeditions, and I was riding an emaciated, weak mare of mine, so I was at the rear of the people. He caught up with me and said, “Walk on, O owner of the horse.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, she is emaciated and weak.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised a whip he had with him and struck her with it, and said, “O Allah, bless him in her.” He said: I saw myself holding her head back so that she would not outrun the people. He said: And I sold one of her foals for twelve thousand."],[2146,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group from the Azd on Friday, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited us to a meal that was before him. We said, “We are fasting.” He said, “Did you fast yesterday?” We said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” We said, “No.” He said, “Then break your fast.” Then he said, “Do not fast on Friday alone.”"],[2147,"From Junadah al-Azdi, that they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being a group of eight men, he being the eighth of them, on Friday. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food and said to one man, “Eat.” He said, “I am fasting.” He said to another, “Eat.” He said, “I am fasting,” until he had asked them all. Then he said, “Did you fast yesterday?” They said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” They said, “No.” So he ordered them to break their fast."],[2148,"That they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, eight men, he being the eighth of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought food near to them on a Friday, and he said, “Eat.” They said, “We are fasting.” He said, “Did you fast yesterday?” They said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” They said, “No.” He said, “Then break your fast.”"],[2149,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with camels that I had branded on their noses. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Junadah, did you find no limb to brand except on the face? Indeed, ahead of you is retribution.” He said, “I leave the matter to you, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Bring me something that has no brand on it.” So I brought him a two-year-old male camel and a three-year-old female camel. I placed the branding iron on the neck, but he kept saying, “Move it back, move it back,” until it reached the thigh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Brand with the blessing of Allah.” So I branded them on their thighs. Their zakah was two three-year-old females, and they were ninety."],[2150,"From Jurmuz al-Hujaymi, he said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said, “I advise you not to be a curser.”"],[2151,"He heard Jurmuz al-Hujaymi say: I said, 'O Messenger of God, advise me.' He said, 'I advise you not to be a curser.'"],[2152,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'They brought a man to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This man wanted to kill you.\" He said to him, \"Do not be afraid, do not be afraid. If you had intended that, you would not have been given power over me.\"'"],[2153,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had a dream, so he sent for him. He came and narrated it to him. He had a large belly. He said, pointing with his finger at his belly, 'If this were in something other than this, it would be better for you.'"],[2154,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with a large belly. He said, pointing with his finger at his belly, 'If this were in something other than this, it would be better for you.'"],[2155,"It was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that there was a freed slave of the Bani Abd al-Muttalib who prayed all night and did not sleep, fasted continuously without breaking his fast. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"As for me, I pray and sleep, fast and break my fast. For every deed, there is a span (of time), and for every span (of time), there is an interval. Whoever follows the interval according to the Sunnah, is guided, and whoever goes beyond that, is astray.\""],[2156,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the later ones are the worst.'"],[2157,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The best of people are my generation, then the one that follows it, then the later ones are the worst.'"],[2158,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from three things: wearing a gold ring, wearing qassi cloth, and using a saddle cloth."],[2159,"A group from Kindah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'You are from us,' claiming him. He said, 'We do not trace our lineage through our mothers, nor do we disown our fathers. We are the children of al-Nadr b. Kinanah.'"],[2160,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'From whom are you, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'We are the Banu al-Nadr b. Kinanah. We do not trace our lineage through our mothers, nor do we disown our fathers.'"],[2161,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, send my brother Zayd with me.' He said, 'That is up to him. If he goes with you, I will not prevent him.' Zayd said, 'No, by God, O Messenger of God, I will never prefer anyone over you.' He said, 'I saw that my brother's opinion was better than mine.'"],[2162,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he did not go on a military expedition, would give his weapon to Ali or Usamah ؓ."],[2163,"I heard Junayd b. Sab' say, “I fought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of the day as an disbeliever, and I fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim.” And it was revealed about us: {And had it not been for believing men and believing women} [Qur'an 48:25]. He said, “We were nine persons: seven men and two women.”"],[2164,"“Abu 'Abd Allah, meaning Jarir, went early to al-Kunasah to buy a mount from there.”"],[2165,"I said to Jarir, “O Abu 'Amr.”"],[2166,"“I saw Jarir dyeing his beard yellow.”"],[2167,"I saw Jarir dyeing [his hair] with saffron and turmeric."],[2168,"I saw Jarir b. 'Abdullah dyeing his head and beard with black."],[2169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will appear before you the best of a blessed people, upon whom is the touch of an angel.\" Then Jarir b. 'Abdullah appeared."],[2170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Jareer is from us, the people of the household, both in appearance and lineage.” He repeated it three times."],[2171,"Jarir ؓ dueled Mihran and killed him. His belt was valued at thirty thousand, and whoever dueled a man and killed him had the right to his spoils. They wrote to 'Umar ؓ, so 'Umar said: \"This is not among the spoils that are given; it is neither from weapons nor from horses.\" He did not grant it to him as a special reward and made it part of the general booty."],[2172,"When 'Umar ؓ led the people in prayer, something (i.e., wind) came out from a man, so he said: \"I firmly resolve that the one who did this must perform ablution and repeat his prayer.\" Jarir said: \"Would you also firmly resolve that everyone who heard it must perform ablution and repeat the prayer?\" He said: \"What an excellent thing you have said, may Allah reward you with good,\" and he ordered them to do that."],[2173,"I was a doorkeeper at the door of Jarir b. 'Abdullah. He would go out and mount a mule of his, and he would carry his servant behind him."],[2174,"Indeed a man clothes himself while he is naked—meaning thin clothes."],[2175,"Jarir and al-Ash'ath b. Qays met at a funeral, and al-Ash'ath gave precedence to Jarir, so he led the funeral prayer over it."],[2176,"I accompanied Jarir, and he would serve me.\" He was older than Anas. Jarir said: \"I saw the Ansar doing something for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, such that I would not see any one of them except that I honored him."],[2177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled me since I embraced Islam, nor did he ever see me except that he smiled."],[2178,"I heard Jarir b. 'Abdullah say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw me except that he smiled in my face.\""],[2179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled me since I embraced Islam, nor did he ever see me except that he smiled in my face."],[2180,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ never screened me since I became Muslim, and never saw me but that he smiled.”"],[2181,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ never screened me since I became Muslim, and never saw me but that he smiled.”"],[2182,"Jarir said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2183,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see the moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2184,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was looking at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will be presented before your Lord and you will see Him just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting.}"],[2185,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked at the moon on the night of the fourteenth and said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will see your Lord as you see the moon, you will not be harmed by seeing Him.\""],[2187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed you will see your Lord, not being harmed in seeing Him, just as you look at the night of the full moon.”"],[2188,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: “Indeed you will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection clearly (ʿiyānan) just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting.} Abu al-Qasim said: In this hadith there is an additional wording, namely his saying “clearly (ʿiyānan),” which Abu Shihab alone narrated, and he is a careful memorizer of the trustworthy Muslims."],[2189,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the fourteenth of a month, and he said: “Do you see this moon? Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So whoever of you is able, let him never be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset.”"],[2190,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night, and our eyes were raised and we began looking at the moon on the night of the full moon. He said: “Indeed you are looking at your Lord just as you look at this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers, then do so: a prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.”"],[2191,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said to us: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him.”"],[2192,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the moon rose. He said: “You will certainly look at your Lord, not being harmed in seeing Him, just as you look at the moon.”"],[2193,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2194,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2195,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God will not show mercy to one who does not show mercy to people.”"],[2196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2197,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of the idols of Jahiliyyah remains except Dhul-Khalasah.\""],[2199,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man from the best of Dhū Yumn will enter upon you through the door; on his face is the touch of an angel.\" Then Jarir entered."],[2200,"I was in Yemen with Dhū Kalāʿ and Dhū ʿAmr. I came to inform them about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Dhū ʿAmr said: \"O Jarir, if your companion is as you describe, his term has already come three days ago.\" Then a man was raised up for us, and we said: \"What is the news?\" They said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has passed away, and Abu Bakr ؓ has been appointed as his successor, and the people are righteous.\" Then we returned, and they said: \"Convey peace to your companion.\" Then Dhū ʿAmr said: \"O Jarir, you will remain righteous as long as when a leader dies, another leader stands up. But when it becomes swords, you will become kings, pleased with the pleasure of kings and angry with the anger of kings.\""],[2201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a military expedition to Khathʿam. Some of them sought protection by prostrating, but killing was hastened upon them. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he ordered half of the blood money for them and said, “I am free from every Muslim who resides among the polytheists.” They said, “O Messenger of God, why?” He said, “Their fires should not be visible to each other.”"],[2202,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He raised his gaze to the sky and said, “Glory be to God! What trials are being sent down upon them, like the sending of rain?”"],[2203,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The one who transgresses in charity is like the one who withholds it.”"],[2204,"When the ayah, \"Your Lord would never destroy the towns unjustly while their people were reformers,\" was revealed, he said: \"That is, their people treat one another justly.\""],[2205,"\"We used to wipe (over leather socks) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" We said: \"Before the revelation of al-Ma'idah or after its revelation?\" He said: \"I only became Muslim after the revelation of al-Ma'idah.\""],[2206,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2207,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us on the night of the full moon and looked at the moon, then said, “You will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection just as you see this moon, and you will suffer no hardship in seeing Him.”"],[2208,"The Prophet ﷺ said to the owner of a right, “Take your right in a manner that is either full or less than full.”"],[2209,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he urged the people to give charity until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then a man from the Ansar came with a piece of gold and threw it to the Prophet ﷺ, and joy was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “Whoever establishes a good sunnah in Islam that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without any of their rewards being diminished. And whoever establishes an evil sunnah in Islam that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without any of their burdens being diminished.”"],[2210,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, stretch out your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you, and set the conditions upon me, for you know the conditions better than I.\" He said, \"I pledge allegiance to you on the basis that you do not associate anything with God, that you establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.\""],[2211,"I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, and he stipulated for me to worship God, not associating anything with Him, and to give sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[2212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah only has mercy on the merciful among His servants.\""],[2213,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When a slave runs away, no prayer is accepted from him, and if he dies, he dies as a disbeliever.\" Then a slave of Jarir ran away, so he seized him and struck his neck. Abu al-Qasim said: \"Its meaning is that he disbelieved and joined the abode of war.\""],[2214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The charity collector should not return from you except while he is pleased.\""],[2215,"That there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[2216,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, does not show mercy to the one who does not show mercy to people.\""],[2217,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over leather socks. He said: ‘Three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident.’"],[2218,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2219,"I heard Jarir say: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2220,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[2221,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2222,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2223,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2224,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.”"],[2225,"I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ to hear and obey."],[2226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you not relieve me of Dhul-Khalasah?\" It was a house in Khath'am called the Ka'bah of Yemen. So I set out with sixty and one hundred horsemen from Ahmas, and they were people of horses. I was not steady on horses, so he struck my chest until I saw the marks of his fingers on my chest, and said: \"O Allah, make him firm and make him guided and guiding.\" Then he went to it, broke it, and burned it, and sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to inform him. The messenger of Jarir said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I left it as if it were a mangy camel.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ blessed the horses of Ahmas and its men five times."],[2227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you not suffice me against Dhul-Khalasah?\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who is not steady on horses.\" He struck me on my chest and said: \"O Allah, make him guided and guiding.\" He said: So I went out to it with fifty of my people and burned it with fire, then returned to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I left it like a hairless camel.\" So he prayed for Ahmas, its horses and its men, three times."],[2228,"I was not steady on horses, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He struck his hand on my chest until I saw the mark of his hand on my chest, and said: \"O Allah, make him firm and make him guided and guiding.\" After that, I never fell from a horse."],[2229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Jarir, will you not relieve me of Dhul-Khalasah?\" A house belonging to Khath'am called the Ka'bah of Yemen. So I set out with fifty and one hundred horsemen from Ahmas. I was not steady on horses, so I mentioned that to him. He struck me on my chest until I saw the marks of his fingers on my chest, then said: \"O Allah, make him firm and make him guided and guiding.\" So I went and defeated them and burned it with fire. Then Jarir sent a man called Abu Art'ah as a bearer of good news to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I saw it as if it were a mangy camel.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ blessed the horses of Ahmas and the men of Ahmas three times."],[2230,"We pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ on the same terms as the women: \"Whoever dies among us and has not brought any of them is guaranteed Paradise. Whoever dies and has committed something of them and the prescribed punishment has been carried out on him, that is its expiation. Whoever dies among us and committed something of them and it was concealed, his account is with Allah.\""],[2231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever resides with the polytheists, the protection is disowned from him.\""],[2232,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The protection is disowned from whoever resides with the polytheists in their lands.\""],[2233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has his two precious ones taken away, I will compensate him with Paradise for them.\""],[2234,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched an army to Khathʿam. When the cavalry surrounded them, they sought protection through prayer, and a man among them was killed. The Messenger of God ﷺ set half of the blood money for them because of their prayer, and he said, “I am free from every Muslim who lives with a polytheist.”"],[2235,"When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, I came to him to pledge allegiance. He said, “For what purpose have you come, O Jarīr?” I said, “I have come to submit at your hands.” He said, “He called me to bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, to establish the prescribed prayer, to give the obligatory zakāt, and to believe in the divine decree, its good and its evil.” He said, “Then he threw his cloak to me, then turned to his companions and said, ‘When a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.’” The wording is that of the Ḥaḍramī hadith."],[2236,"About the Prophet ﷺ , \"Indeed, Satan has despaired of being worshipped in the land of the Arabs.\""],[2237,"ʿUyaynah b. Ḥiṣn entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while a man was with him. He asked for water, and it was brought, and he screened it and drank. He said, “What is this?” He said, “Modesty and faith: they were given these two, and you were deprived of them.”"],[2238,"ʿUyaynah b. Ḥiṣn entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while ʿĀʾishah was with him. He said, “Who is this woman sitting beside you?” He said, “ʿĀʾishah.” He said, “Shall I not step down for you in favor of one better than her?” meaning his wife. The Prophet ﷺ said, “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Go out and ask permission.” He said, “I have sworn an oath that I will not ask permission of any Muḍarī.” ʿĀʾishah, may God have mercy on her, said, “Who is this?” He said, “This is a fool who is followed.”"],[2239,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: “O God, I seek refuge with You from a supplication that is not heard, a heart that does not humble itself, and a soul that is never satisfied.”"],[2240,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever takes provisions in this world, it will benefit him in the hereafter.”"],[2241,"“Indeed God, exalted be He, grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness.”"],[2242,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Indeed God, exalted be He, grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness. When God loves a servant, He gives him gentleness. There is no household that is deprived of gentleness except that they are truly deprived.”"],[2243,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, ‘There is no god but God.’ When they say it, they protect their blood and property from me except for its right, and their reckoning is with God, exalted be He.”"],[2244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Make the people listen attentively.\" Then he said: \"Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\""],[2245,"Do the family of the deceased visit him after he is buried? I asked Ismail, and he said, \"Yes, we used to count the lamentation for him.\""],[2246,"\"The gathering of the deceased's family and the preparation of food are part of wailing.\""],[2247,"It is said: \"The first glance a man cannot control, but the one who persists in gazing does so deliberately.\""],[2248,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting} he said: \"The rising of the sun is the morning prayer, and before its setting is the afternoon prayer.\""],[2249,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the Tulaqa' of Quraysh and the 'Utaqa' of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[2250,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah and without staining himself with unlawful blood will be admitted through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes.\""],[2251,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, and he never saw me except that he smiled.\""],[2252,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled himself from me since I became Muslim, and he never saw me except that he smiled.\""],[2253,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to us on the night of the full moon and said: \"You will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection just as you see this moon; you will not be harmed in seeing Him.\""],[2254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Will you relieve me of Dhu al-Khalasah?\" He said: \"I went to it with one hundred and fifty horsemen from Ahmas, and I destroyed it and killed those we found there. Then I came to him and informed him, and he supplicated for us and for the Ahmasiyyin.\""],[2255,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he raised his gaze to the sky and said: \"Glory be to Allah! What trials are being sent down upon them, sent down like rain.\""],[2256,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[2257,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it for fear of it is not of me.”"],[2258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Nothing remains of the idols of the pagan era except the House of Dhu al-Khalasah. Who will volunteer for the sake of God and His Messenger?” Jarir said, “I will.” So seven hundred men, all from Ahmas, volunteered with him. The people were taken by surprise only by the forelocks of the horses. They killed and destroyed the house, and wrote to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the good news, informing him that nothing remained of it except like a tarred or mangy camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ then fell in prostration, then said, “O God, bless Ahmas in its horses and its men.”"],[2259,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “Whoever does not show mercy to people will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2260,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not show mercy to people will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2261,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “Whoever does not show mercy to people will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2262,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not show mercy to people will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2263,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever shows mercy to people will be shown mercy by God.”"],[2264,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The Emigrants are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the freed ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[2265,"When the Prophet ﷺ accepted allegiance, he would accept it upon the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, hearing and obeying Allah and His Messenger, and sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[2266,"When the Prophet ﷺ dispatched a raiding party, he would say, “In the name of Allah, in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah: do not embezzle, do not act treacherously, do not mutilate, and do not kill children.”"],[2267,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched his armies, he would say, “In the name of Allah, in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah: do not embezzle, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child.”"],[2268,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, stipulate for me, for you know the conditions better than I.” He said, “I pledge allegiance to you on the condition that you worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.”"],[2269,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, stipulate for me, for you know best.” He said, “Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and disavow the disbeliever.”"],[2270,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, stipulate for me, for you know the conditions better than I; then extend your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you.” He said, “Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.”"],[2271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The Muhajirun are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the released ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[2272,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the released ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another.”"],[2273,"Some people from the desert came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing striped woolen cloaks and asked him. The Prophet ﷺ urged the people to give charity, but they were slow to give it until that was evident in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then a man from the Ansar came with a piece of gold ore and cast it down, and the people followed one another in giving charity until joy was evident in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “Whoever establishes a good sunnah that is acted upon after him will have the like of its reward and the reward of those who act upon it, without any of their rewards being diminished. And whoever establishes an evil sunnah that is acted upon will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it, without any of their burdens being diminished.”"],[2274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The released ones of Quraysh and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[2275,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, accept my allegiance and stipulate for me, for you know best.” He extended his hand and accepted his allegiance, then said, “Do not associate anything with Allah, establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the disbeliever.”"],[2276,"Jarir said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was taking the people's pledge of allegiance, so I said, \"O Messenger of God, stretch out your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you.\" He said, \"How will you pledge allegiance to me?\" He said, \"I pledge allegiance to you on the basis that you worship God, establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.\""],[2277,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2278,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2279,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2280,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2281,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2282,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2283,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2284,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The lahd is for us and the shaqq is for others.\""],[2285,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about Islam, so he said, \"You testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, you establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform pilgrimage to the House, love for people what you love for yourself, and hate for people what you hate for yourself.\""],[2286,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The niche grave (lahd) is for us, and the trench grave (shaqq) is for others.\""],[2287,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on our riding camels from Madinah, and they were eating date stones. A figure appeared to him, so he said: \"This is a man who has not had food for a long time.\" The Prophet ﷺ hastened the pace, and we hastened with him, and behold, there was a young man whose lips had fallen back from eating the bark of trees. He asked him: \"From where have you come?\" He said: \"I want Muhammad ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him.\" He said: \"I am Muhammad, I am the Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Peace be upon you. Guide me to Islam, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"You testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, and you affirm what has come from God.\" He said: \"I affirm.\" He said: \"And you establish the prayer.\" He said: \"I affirm.\" He said: \"And you fast Ramadan.\" He said: \"I affirm.\" He said: \"And you perform the pilgrimage to the House.\" He said: \"I affirm.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned away. Jarir said: We crowded around him as he began to describe Islam to him, watching to see where his description would end. Then he turned away, and we turned away. The foot of his young camel fell into the holes of jerboas, and its neck broke. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned around and said: \"Bring the man to me.\" We found that his neck had snapped and he died. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to him, looked at him, then turned his face away from him and said: \"Carry him to the water.\" We washed him, shrouded him, and perfumed him. Then he said: \"Dig for him and make a niche grave (lahd), for the niche grave is for us and the trench grave (shaqq) is for others.\" He sat by his grave without speaking to us, then said: \"Shall I tell you about this man's story? This is one who did little and was rewarded much—one of those about whom God ﷻ said: {Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrong} (Qur'an 6:82). I turned away from him while two angels were stuffing the fruits of Paradise into his mouth.\""],[2288,"A man entered Islam and was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. The foot of his camel fell into a jerboa's hole, and it broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to him and said: \"He did little and was rewarded much.\" And he said: \"The niche grave is for us, and the trench grave is for others.\""],[2289,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ regarding the runaway slave: \"No prayer is accepted from him until he returns to his masters.\""],[2290,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, but I do not want it to be narrated from me."],[2291,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let the tax collector return while he is pleased with you.\""],[2292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let the tax collector return while he is pleased with you.\""],[2293,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let the tax collector return while he is pleased with you.\""],[2294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When the tax collector comes to you, he should not leave you except while he is pleased with you.\""],[2295,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When the tax collector comes to you, he should not leave except with satisfaction.\""],[2296,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Let the tax collector return, when he returns, while he is pleased.\""],[2297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When the tax collector comes to you, let him leave you while he is pleased with you.\""],[2298,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Let the alms collector depart from you while he is pleased.\""],[2299,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Let the alms collector return from your presence while he is pleased with you.\""],[2300,"I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim. Al-Sha'bi said: Jarir was shrewd, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, in what I am able."],[2301,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no one with a relative who comes to him asking for some of the surplus that Allah has given him, and he withholds it from him, except that on the Day of Resurrection a serpent from Hell is brought out for him, called Shuja', which will slither and be made to encircle him.\""],[2302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a slave reaches the land of the enemy, his blood becomes lawful.\""],[2303,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When a slave flees to the enemy, protection is lifted from him.\""],[2304,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.\""],[2305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your brother the Negus has died, so ask forgiveness for him.\""],[2306,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Ask forgiveness for the Negus.\""],[2307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a slave flees to the land of the enemy, protection is lifted from him.\""],[2308,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Your brother the Negus has died, so ask forgiveness for him.\""],[2309,"\"I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, to listen and obey, to establish prayer, give zakah, and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.\""],[2310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When the charity collector comes to you, he should not leave you except while he is pleased.\""],[2311,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Upon hearing and obedience.\" He prompted me: \"As much as you are able, and sincere counsel to every Muslim.\""],[2312,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The charity collectors should not leave except with satisfaction.\""],[2313,"Jarir said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I pledge allegiance to you upon hearing and obedience in what I like and dislike.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Are you able to do that, O Jarir? Or can you bear that? Say: as much as I am able.\" He said: I said, \"As much as I am able.\" He said: Then he accepted my allegiance, and upon sincere counsel to the Muslim.\""],[2314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.\""],[2315,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When a slave runs away, the protection of Allah and His Messenger is disowned from him.\""],[2316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When a slave runs away, the protection is disowned from him.\""],[2317,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"When the charity collector comes to you, he should not part from you except while he is pleased.\""],[2318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Islam is built upon five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fasting of Ramadan.\""],[2319,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Islam is built upon five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan.”"],[2320,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and he said: “Stretch out your hand, O Jarir.” He said: “Upon what?” He said: “Upon that you submit your face to Allah and give sincere counsel to every Muslim.” Jarir caught this, and he was an intelligent man, so he said: “O Messenger of Allah, as much as I am able.” After him this became a concession for the people."],[2321,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “When a slave runs away and joins the enemy and dies while he is a disbeliever.”"],[2322,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Satisfy your collectors and alms-verifiers.”"],[2323,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me not holding anything, he said, \"O Jarir, it is not necessary for you to hold onto your wealth. Surely, this matter has a duration.\""],[2324,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I have not escaped from the polytheists except with a slave-girl singer; I want to sell her in the market, and I practice coitus interruptus with her.” He said: “Whatever is decreed for her will come to her.”"],[2325,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have not escaped from the polytheists except with a slave-girl singer, and I practice coitus interruptus with her, wanting to sell her in the market.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whatever is decreed for her will come to her.”"],[2326,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of the day, and some bedouins came, barefoot, naked, clad in striped woolen cloaks, with swords and cloaks upon them. I said: “Most of them are from Mudar; rather, all of them are from Mudar.” I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change when he saw their condition. He stood up and entered, then ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer and the iqamah. Then he came out and prayed Zuhr and delivered a sermon: “O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul…” He recited the verse up to His saying: “And let every soul look to what it has sent forth for tomorrow.” He said: “A man should give charity from his dirham, a man should give charity from his dinar, from a sa' of his dates, from a sa' of his barley, from such and such…” until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned even half a date. Then a man came with a purse that his hand could barely hold, or indeed could not hold. He said: And the people followed one after another until I saw two heaps of food and clothing. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brighten as if it were gilded. Then he said: “Whoever introduces a good, righteous practice in Islam has its reward and the reward of those who act upon it after him until the Day of Resurrection, without any decrease in their rewards. And whoever introduces an evil practice in Islam bears its burden and the burden of those who act upon it after him until the Day of Resurrection, without any decrease in their burdens.”"],[2327,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for part of the day when some people came, most of them from Mudar, rather all of them from Mudar, clad in striped woolen cloaks, with swords hanging from their necks. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change when he saw the hardship they were in. Then he said: “O Bilal, hasten the prayer.” When he prayed, he sat for a while, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: “Fear Allah, by whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you.” He said: “May Allah have mercy on a man who gives charity from his dinar and dirham and a sa' of his dates,” until he reduced charity to half a date. Among those who stood was a man from the Ansar with a purse that his hand could barely hold, or indeed could not hold, not knowing whether it was gold or silver. Then the people followed one another until they gathered two huge heaps of food and clothing. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brighten as if it were gilded. When the charity was concluded, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no one among my nation who establishes a good practice that is acted upon after him except that he has its reward and the like of the reward of those who establish his practice, without any decrease in their rewards. And whoever introduces an evil practice in Islam that is acted upon after him except that upon him is its burden and the like of the burdens of those who establish his practice, without any decrease in their burdens.”"],[2328,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a people came to him, clad in striped woolen cloaks, with swords hanging from their necks, wearing nothing but those cloaks. Most of them were from Mudar, rather all of them were from Mudar. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the hardship, nakedness, and hunger they were in, his face changed. He entered his house, then went to the mosque and prayed Zuhr, then climbed a small pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed, Allah Almighty has revealed in His Book: ‘O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul…’ to the end of the verse. ‘O you who believe, fear Allah and let every soul look to what it has sent forth for tomorrow…’ up to His saying: ‘they are the successful.’ Give charity before you are unable to give. A man should give charity from his dinar, a man should give charity from his dirham, a man should give charity from his wheat, a man should give charity from his dates, from his barley. Do not belittle anything of charity, even half a date.” Then a man from the Ansar stood with a purse in his hand and handed it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit. He took it, and joy was seen on his face. Then he said: “Whoever establishes a good practice that is acted upon has its reward and the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without any decrease in their rewards. And whoever establishes an evil practice that is acted upon bears its burden and the burden of those who act upon it after him, without any decrease in their burdens.” Then the people stood and dispersed, some with a dinar and some with a dirham, and he gathered it and distributed it among them."],[2329,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one shelters a stray animal except one who is astray.”"],[2330,"I was with my father at al-Bawarij when the cattle returned in the evening. He saw a cow he did not recognize and said to the herder: “What is this?” They said: “This is a cow that joined the herd; it is not known whose it is.” He ordered that it be driven away until it disappeared from his sight. Then he said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘No one shelters a stray animal except one who is astray.’”"],[2331,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There are no people among whom acts of disobedience are committed while they are more powerful and more protected than the disobedient one, and they do not change it, except that Allah will afflict them all with punishment from it.\""],[2332,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There are no people among whom a man commits acts of disobedience while they are stronger and more powerful than him, and they do not change it, except that Allah will afflict them with punishment.\""],[2333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no group of people who commit sins among themselves, yet they are more honorable and greater in number than those who avoid committing them, except that Allah will surely inflict His punishment upon them.\""],[2334,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no man among a people who commits acts of disobedience among them, and they are able to change it but do not, except that Allah will afflict them with punishment before they die.\""],[2335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are no people among whom a man commits acts of disobedience, and they are able to change it but do not, except that Allah will cover them all with punishment before they die.\""],[2336,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no man who lives next to a people and commits acts of disobedience among them, and they do not seize his hand, except that Allah will soon cover them all with punishment from it.\""],[2337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are no people among whom there is someone who commits acts of disobedience, while they are greater in number and more powerful than him, and they deal gently and remain silent and do not change it, except that punishment will befall them in it.\""],[2338,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at 'Arafah, with his upper garment under his arm, raising his hands not above his head, and his muscles were trembling.\""],[2339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2340,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.\""],[2341,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Indeed, Allah does not show mercy to the one who does not show mercy to people.\""],[2342,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts three days of the month, let him fast the white nights: the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth.\""],[2343,"‘Ali b. Abi Talib sent Ibn ‘Abbas and al-Ash‘ath b. Qays to me while I was at Qirqisiya. They said: ‘The Commander of the Faithful conveys salam to you and says: “What good Allah has shown you in parting from Mu‘awiyah! Indeed I place you in the position that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed you.”’ Jarir said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen to fight them and call them to say “There is no god but Allah.” When they say it, their blood and wealth become inviolable, and I do not fight anyone who says “There is no god but Allah.”’ So we returned on that basis."],[2344,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered a thicket, relieved himself, and Jarir brought him a waterskin. He performed istinja, wiped his hand on the dust, then washed his face and forearms, wiped his head and his leather socks. I said: ‘O Prophet of Allah, your feet?’ He said: ‘I put them in while they were pure.’"],[2345,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wudu and wipe over his leather socks, not removing them, then pray in them."],[2346,"Abu ‘Abd Allah went early to al-Kunasah to buy a riding beast, and a mawla of his went with him. He stood at a side of the market, and beasts began passing by him. A horse passed by and pleased him, so he said to his mawla: ‘Go buy that horse.’ His mawla went and offered its owner three hundred dirhams for it, but the owner refused to sell it. He haggled with him, but the owner refused to sell it. He said: ‘Will you come to a friend of ours at a side of the market?’ He said: ‘I don’t mind.’ So they went to him. His mawla said to him: ‘I offered this man three hundred dirhams for his horse, but he refused and claimed it is worth more than that.’ The owner of the horse said: ‘He spoke the truth, may Allah set you right. Do you think that is a proper price?’ He said: ‘No, your horse is worth more than that. You would sell it for five hundred—’ until it reached seven hundred or eight hundred dirhams. When the man left, he turned to his mawla and said: ‘Woe to you! You went to buy me a beast. A man’s beast pleased me, so I sent you to buy it, and you came back leading a man from the Muslims while he was saying, “What do you think? What do you think?” And I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give sincere counsel to every Muslim.’"],[2347,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ‘Kill all snakes. Whoever leaves them out of fear of retaliation is not of us.’"],[2348,"The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Whoever drinks wine, flog him. If he returns, flog him. If he returns, flog him. If he returns a fourth time, kill him.’"],[2349,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks."],[2350,"Jarir urinated and wiped over his leather socks. A group criticized him for that and said: ‘This was before the Ma’idah.’ He said: ‘I did not embrace Islam until after the Ma’idah was revealed, and I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe except after it was revealed.’"],[2351,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me during the Farewell Pilgrimage: ‘Make the people listen attentively.’ Then he said: ‘Do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another’s necks.’"],[2352,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the glance. He said: ‘Turn it away.’"],[2353,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the unintentional glance, and he commanded me to turn away my gaze."],[2354,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the sudden glance. He commanded me to avert my gaze."],[2355,"Jarir asked the Prophet ﷺ about the sudden glance, and he said, “Avert your gaze.”"],[2356,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twirling the forelock of a horse between his fingers and saying, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: spoils and reward.”"],[2357,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey, and to give sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[2358,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils.”"],[2359,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey, and to give sincere counsel to every Muslim. When he would buy something or sell it, he would say to his companion, “Know that what I take from you is dearer to us than what we give you, so choose.”"],[2360,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “Allah ﷻ revealed to me: Whichever of these three you alight upon, that is the abode of your emigration: Madinah, al-Bahrayn, or Qinnasrin.”"],[2361,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, he said to his companions, “Come with us to the people of Quba’ so we may greet them.” He went to them and greeted them, and they welcomed him. Then he said, “O people of Quba’, bring me stones from this harrah.” Many stones were gathered before him, and he had a short spear with him. He marked out their qiblah, then took a stone and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed it. Then he said, “O Abu Bakr, take a stone and place it next to my stone.” Then he said, “O Umar, take a stone and place it next to the stone of Abu Bakr.” Then he turned and said, “O Uthman, take a stone and place it next to the stone of Umar.” Then he turned to the people at the end and said, “Let a man place his stone wherever he wishes along this line.”"],[2362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever recites ‘Say: He is Allah, the One’ when he enters his home, poverty is repelled from the people of that home and the neighbors.”"],[2363,"Whenever delegations came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would invite them and entertain them with hospitality."],[2364,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do that.” Ibrahim said: They used to think that the wiping was after the revelation of al-Ma’idah, because Jarir was among the last of them to embrace Islam."],[2365,"“What prevents me, when I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it?”"],[2366,"Jareer rushed to perform ablution and wiped over his socks. One of the people criticized him for doing so, to which Jareer replied, \"If I do this, it is because I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.\""],[2367,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ wipe over his leather socks.” Ibrahim said: Our companions used to marvel at the hadith of Jarir, saying, “His Islam was after the revelation of al-Ma’idah.”"],[2368,"Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. He was asked about it, and he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.”"],[2369,"Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, saying, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.”"],[2370,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[2371,"Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said to him, “Do you do this after having urinated?” He said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.”"],[2372,"Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, saying, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.”"],[2373,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his socks."],[2374,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “For the traveler, three days; and for the resident, one day, for wiping over the leather socks.”"],[2375,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[2376,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over them."],[2377,"He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. He was asked about it, so he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe, so I wiped.”"],[2378,"Jarir urinated and performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, saying, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do something like that.”"],[2379,"Jarir urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do something like this.”"],[2380,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The freed ones of Quraysh, the freed ones of Thaqif, the Muhajirun, and the Ansar are allies of one another.\""],[2381,"I heard Jarir b. 'Abd Allah, who was our commander, say: \"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then I returned, and he called me and said: 'I will not accept from you until you pledge allegiance with sincerity to every Muslim.' So I pledged allegiance to him.\""],[2382,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2383,"“The Prophet ﷺ passed by some women and greeted them.”"],[2384,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2385,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heaven will show mercy to you.\""],[2386,"\"I embraced Islam only after the revelation of the Table Spread (Surah al-Ma'idah), and I only saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his feet after I embraced Islam.\""],[2387,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2388,"We witnessed the season during the pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , and it was the Farewell Pilgrimage. We reached a place called Ghadir Khumm, and the call for prayer was made. The immigrants and the supporters gathered and the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , stood in our midst and said, \"O people, what do you bear witness to?\" They said, \"We bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" He said, \"Then what else?\" They said, \"And that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.\" He said, \"Then who is your guardian?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger are our guardians.\" He said, \"Who is your guardian?\" Then he struck Ali on his shoulder, and he stood him up, then he pulled his arm and said, \"Whoever I am his guardian, then Ali is his guardian. O Allah, be a friend to the one who loves him and an enemy to the one who hates him.\" O Allah, I cannot find anyone on earth after the two righteous servants whom I entrust with this matter except for You, so decide in it with the best.\" Bashir said, \"I asked, who are these two righteous servants?\" He said, \"I do not know.\""],[2389,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. The Prophet ﷺ walked away and performed ablution, then he wiped over his socks.\""],[2390,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks.” It was said to him after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed, so he said: “Did I embrace Islam only after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed?”"],[2391,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam, and he held back his hand so that he could stipulate upon me sincerity (nush) toward every Muslim.”"],[2392,"That some people from ‘Uraynah raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “so the Prophet ﷺ ordered that their hands and feet be cut off and that their eyes be branded with heated iron.”"],[2393,"That when he offered a commodity for sale, he would point out its defects and then give the buyer the choice, saying: “If you wish, take it, and if you wish, leave it.” It was said to him: “May Allah have mercy on you; if you do this, your sale will not go through.” He said: “We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon sincerity (nush) toward the people of Islam.”"],[2394,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.”"],[2395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever institutes a good practice in Islam has its reward and the reward of those who act upon it without any decrease in their rewards. And whoever institutes an evil practice in Islam bears its burden and the burden of those who act upon it without any decrease in their burdens.”"],[2396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the Tulaqa’ from Quraysh and the ‘Utaqa’ from Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[2397,"A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ with a bag of gold that filled his fingers and said, “This is for the sake of God.” Then Abu Bakr ؓ stood and gave, then ‘Umar ؓ stood and gave, then the Muhajirun and the Ansar stood and gave. The face of the Messenger of God ﷺ shone until we saw radiance in his cheek. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will have the like of their rewards, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever establishes a bad practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will bear the like of their burdens, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No servant establishes a good practice that is acted upon after him except that he has the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And no servant establishes a bad practice that is acted upon after him except that he bears the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2399,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No servant establishes a good practice that is acted upon after him except that he has the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And no servant establishes a bad practice that is acted upon after him except that he bears the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no one who establishes a good practice in Islam that is acted upon after him except that he has the like of the reward of those who act upon it after him, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever establishes a bad practice in Islam that is acted upon after him bears the like of the burdens of those who act upon it after him, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will have written for him the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without the reward of those who act upon it being diminished in anything. And whoever establishes a bad practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will have written against him the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2402,"A group of Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he saw upon them poverty and hardship. He addressed the people, praised God ﷻ and extolled Him, then commanded them to give charity, urged them toward it, and encouraged them in it. They were slow to respond until that was seen in his face. Then a man came with a handful of silver and gave it to him, then another came, until the people followed one after another in giving charity, until delight was seen in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he said: “Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever establishes a bad practice in Islam that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it, without their burdens being diminished in anything.”"],[2403,"Convey peace to him and ask him how he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever establishes a good practice and is followed in it and it is acted upon.” He said: I went to him and asked him, and he said: “He has the like of the reward of every man who acts upon it, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever establishes a bad practice and is followed in it and it is acted upon bears the like of the sin of every man who acts upon it, without their sins being diminished in anything.”"],[2404,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.”"],[2405,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.”"],[2406,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.”"],[2407,"He who is deprived of tenderly feelings is in fact deprived of good. (Using translation from Muslim 2592b)"],[2408,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.”"],[2409,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of all good.\""],[2410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.\""],[2411,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Gentleness brings increase and blessing, and whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good.\""],[2412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a group of his Companions: \"I am going to recite to you some verses from the end of Surah al-Zumar. Whoever among you weeps, Paradise becomes incumbent for him.\" Then he recited from {And they did not appraise Allah with true appraisal} to the end of the surah. Some of us wept and some of us did not weep. Those who did not weep said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we tried hard to weep but we could not.\" He said: \"I will recite them to you, and whoever does not weep should make himself weep.\""],[2413,"The people said: \"This was only before [the revelation of] al-Ma'idah.\" Jarir said: \"I embraced Islam after al-Ma'idah. And I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over his leather socks.\""],[2414,"\"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam, and he stipulated for me sincerity to every Muslim. Indeed, I am sincere to all of you.\""],[2415,"\"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam and sincerity to every Muslim. Indeed, I am sincere to all of you.\""],[2416,"I heard Jarir b. 'Abd Allah on the minbar saying: \"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stipulated for me sincerity to every Muslim.\""],[2417,"I heard Jarir say: \"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I pledge allegiance to you upon Hijrah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted my pledge and stipulated for me sincerity to every Muslim. So I pledged allegiance to him on that.\""],[2418,"He heard Jarir say: \"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stipulated for me sincerity to every Muslim. By the Lord of the Ka'bah, indeed I am sincere to all of you.\""],[2419,"I heard Jarir say: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with this hand of mine upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincere counsel for every Muslim.” By the Lord of the Kaaba, I am indeed a sincere counselor to all of you."],[2420,"I heard Jarir b. Abd Allah say: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2421,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon establishing prayer, giving zakat, and sincere counsel for every Muslim,” and I am a sincere counselor to you."],[2422,"I heard Jarir say: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon establishing prayer, giving zakat, and sincere counsel for every Muslim,” and I am a sincere counselor to all of you."],[2423,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2424,"“Seek forgiveness for him, may God pardon you, for he used to love well-being.” Then he said: “To proceed, I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he said: ‘And sincere counsel for every Muslim.’”"],[2425,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ took our pledge upon hearing and obedience and sincere counsel for every Muslim, so I pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2426,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon hearing and obedience and sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2427,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[2428,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven.”"],[2429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven, and whoever does not repent will not be granted repentance.”"],[2430,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not repent will not be granted repentance.”"],[2431,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Allah does not forgive one who does not forgive, and Allah does not show mercy to one who does not show mercy.”"],[2432,"Abu Sa'id, the servant of Banu Hashim, narrated to us and Ahmad bin Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us and Bishr bin Adam narrated to us and Ya'qub bin Ishaq al-Hadrami said they both narrated to us and Zaidah narrated to me from Ziyad bin Ilaqa from Jarir who said, \"A scholar told me in Yemen that if your companion was a prophet, then he has died.\" He said, \"So the Prophet ﷺ died on Monday.\""],[2433,"I heard Jarir b. Abdullah say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw me except that he smiled.”"],[2434,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Any slave who runs away has indeed absolved himself of the covenant of protection.”"],[2435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a slave runs away, Allah’s covenant of protection is absolved from him.” He did not mention al-Mughirah b. Shubayl."],[2436,"When I approached Madinah, I made my mount kneel, then I untied my bag and put on my fine clothes and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. I greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and the people stared at me. I said to the one sitting next to me: “O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention anything about me?” He said: “Yes, he mentioned you with the best of mentions. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, he digressed in his sermon and said: ‘There will enter upon you from this mountain pass or from this gate one of the best of those with blessing; indeed, on his face is the mark of an angel.’” He said: “So I praised Allah for what He had bestowed upon me.”"],[2437,"“I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he stipulated sincerity to every Muslim.”"],[2438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[2439,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2440,"“I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wiped over his leather socks after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed.”"],[2441,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.\""],[2442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2444,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah wrote in the Mother of the Book before He created the heavens and the earth: 'I am the Compassionate, the Merciful. I created the womb and derived for it a name from My names. So whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him.'\""],[2447,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to those on the earth will not be shown mercy by the One in the heaven.\""],[2448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon to the people one day and said: \"There has come to you the best of a blessed man, on whose face is the touch of an angel,\" meaning me."],[2449,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Fasting three days of every month is equivalent to fasting for a lifetime: the days of the full moon, the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.\""],[2450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.\""],[2451,"“I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the revelation of al-Ma’idah, and I saw him wiping over the leather socks.”"],[2452,"I heard my grandfather, Abu Qirsafah, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: The beginning of my Islam was that I was an orphan between my mother and my maternal aunt. I inclined more toward my maternal aunt, and I used to tend some little sheep of mine. My maternal aunt would often say to me: “O my son, do not pass by this man”—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—“lest he lead you astray and misguide you.” I would go out until I reached the pasture, leave my little sheep, then go to the Prophet ﷺ and remain with him listening to him. Then I would return with my sheep lean and with dry udders. My maternal aunt said to me: “What is wrong with your sheep? Their udders are dry.” I said: “I do not know.” Then I returned to him on the second day, and he did as he had done the first day, except that I heard him say: “O people, emigrate and hold fast to Islam, for emigration does not cease as long as jihad continues.” Then I returned with my sheep as I had returned the first day. Then I returned to him on the third day, and I remained with the Prophet ﷺ listening to him until I embraced Islam, pledged allegiance to him, and shook his hand. I complained to him about my maternal aunt and about my sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Bring me the sheep.” I brought them to him, and he wiped their backs and their udders and prayed for blessing in them, and they became full of fat and milk. When I entered upon my maternal aunt with them, she said: “O my son, graze them like this.” I said: “O aunt, I did not graze them except where I used to graze every day, but I will tell you my story.” I told her the story and that I had gone to the Prophet ﷺ, and I told her about his conduct and his words. Then my mother and my maternal aunt said: “Take us to him.” So I, my mother, and my maternal aunt went, and they embraced Islam and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but they did not shake hands. This is how Abu Qirsafah’s Islam and his emigration to the Prophet ﷺ came about. Ziyad said: “Abu Qirsafah used to live in the land of Tihamah.”"],[2453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do you have any offspring?” I said: “I have a brother.” He said: “Then bring him.” I was gentle with my brother, and he was a young boy, until he came with me. When he drew near to the Prophet ﷺ, he fled, so I caught him and held his hands and feet together, then brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ accepted his pledge of allegiance. His name was Misam, so the Prophet ﷺ said to me: “What is his name, O Abu Qirsafah?” I said: “His name is Misam.” He said: “Rather, his name is Muslim.” So I said: “Muslim is with you, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[2454,"That he “saw the Prophet ﷺ lying on his back, placing one of his legs over the other.”"],[2455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Narrate from me what you hear, and it is not lawful for a man to lie about me. Whoever lies about me and says about me other than what I said, a house will be built for him in Hell in which he will dwell.”"],[2456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ghifar—may Allah forgive them—and Aslam—may Allah keep them safe.”"],[2457,"I heard Abū Qirṣāfah say: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ — myself, my mother, and my maternal aunt — and we returned from his presence departing, my mother and my maternal aunt said to me, “O my son, we have not seen anyone like this man, more handsome of face, nor cleaner of garment, nor gentler of speech; and we saw as if light were emanating from his mouth.”"],[2458,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever loves a people, God will resurrect him in their group.”"],[2459,"The Messenger of God ﷺ clothed me in a burnoose and said, “Wear it.”"],[2460,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Build mosques and remove rubbish from them, for whoever builds a mosque for God, God builds for him a house in Paradise.” A man said, “O Messenger of God, and these mosques that are built along the road?” He said, “Yes, and removing rubbish from them is the dowry of the wide-eyed houris.”"],[2461,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O God, do not disgrace me on the day of battle, nor disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2462,"The Byzantines took captive a son of Abū Qirṣāfah. Whenever the time of each prayer came, Abū Qirṣāfah would climb the wall of Ascalon and call out, “O so-and-so, the prayer!” and he would hear him while he was in the land of the Byzantines."],[2463,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him say, 'O Allah, do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection, nor on the Day of Judgment.'"],[2464,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: “Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī is given the kunyah Abū Muḥammad.”"],[2465,"Umm al-Faḍl came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I saw a part of your body in me.” He said, “You have seen well. Fāṭimah will give birth to a boy, and you will suckle him with the milk of Qutham.” He said: She came carrying him to the Prophet ﷺ and placed him in his lap, and he urinated, so she slapped him with her hand. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You have hurt my son, may God have mercy on you.” She said, “Give me your waist-wrapper so that we may wash it.” He said, “Only the urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled.”"],[2466,"And he (referring to the Prophet ﷺ) said, \"There is no one like Ali, not even similar to him.\" He (referring to Ali) was present with him, and he started laughing. All agreed."],[2467,"“Indeed he used to resemble the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[2468,"That he “saw al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ, his hair striking his shoulders.”"],[2469,"ʿUbādah, the client of al-Ḥasan, though he is in fact the client of al-Ḥusayn."],[2470,"“I saw al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ dyeing with black.”"],[2471,"«I saw al-Hasan b. Ali dyeing with henna and katam.»"],[2472,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to dye with black.»"],[2473,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to dye with black.»"],[2474,"That he «saw al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ dyed black on a horse with a long tail.»"],[2475,"«I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ as young men, and they did not dye.»"],[2476,"«I saw on al-Hasan's head a tuft of hair, and indeed I saw al-Hasan pulling it until he brought it close.»"],[2477,"That he said: «Al-Hasan used to wear a ring on his left hand.»"],[2478,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to wear a ring on his left hand.»"],[2479,"I said: O Messenger of God, I saw in a dream as if a limb of your limbs was in my house, or she said: in my room. He said: «Fatimah will give birth to a boy, if God wills, and you will nurse him.» She said: So Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and he handed him to her, and she nursed him with the milk of Qutham b. al-Abbas. She said: I brought him one day to the Prophet ﷺ, and he urinated on his chest, so I pushed him on his back. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Gently, may God have mercy on you; you have hurt my son.» I said: Give me your waist-wrapper so I can wash it. He said: «No, pour water on it, for water is poured on the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed.»"],[2480,"I was among those who attended Fatimah ؓ when labor struck her, among some women. The Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: «How is she?» I said: She is exhausted, O Messenger of God. He said: «When she gives birth, do not do anything with the child before me.» She said: So she gave birth, and they anointed him and wrapped him in a yellow cloth. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said: «What has she done?» I said: She has given birth to a boy, and I anointed him and wrapped him in a cloth. He said: «You disobeyed me.» She said: I seek refuge in God from disobeying God and from the anger of His Messenger. He said: «Bring him to me.» I brought him to him, and he threw away the yellow cloth and wrapped him in a white cloth, and he spat in his mouth and fed him with his saliva. Ali ؓ came, and he said: «What have you named him, O Ali?» He said: I named him Jafar, O Messenger of God. He said: «No, but Hasan, and after him Husayn, and you are Abu Hasan al-Khayr.»"],[2481,"«The one who resembled the Messenger of God ﷺ the most was al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ.»"],[2482,"«I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him.»"],[2483,"We discussed the resemblance of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If you want to look at someone resembling the Prophet ﷺ, then look at al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ.\""],[2484,"Abū Juḥayfah said to me: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2485,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2486,"I said to Abū Juḥayfah: \"Did you see the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, and the person who most resembled him was al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ.\""],[2487,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2488,"Al-Haytham b. ʿAdī, and he was contradicted."],[2489,"\"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2490,"\"Saʿd and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2491,"\"Saʿd and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died after ten years had passed of Muʿāwiyah's rule ؓ.\""],[2492,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died when he was forty-seven.\""],[2493,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2494,"\"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died in the year forty-nine, and Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ prayed over him. His death was in Madinah, and his age was forty-six or forty-seven. He was called Abū Muḥammad.\""],[2495,"\"The turmoil lasted for five years for Al-Hasan ibn Ali, and from that, four months. And the group was with Muawiyah for forty years.\""],[2496,"In it died al-Hasan b. Ali and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas in the year fifty-eight."],[2497,"Muʿawiyah said to him: When it is so, stand and speak, and inform the people that you have surrendered this matter to me. Perhaps Sufyan said: Inform the people of this matter which you have left to me. So he stood and delivered a speech from the pulpit. He praised Allah and extolled Him—al-Shaʿbi said: while I was listening—then he said: To proceed: the most prudent prudence is piety, and the most foolish folly is wickedness. This matter over which I and Muʿawiyah differed: either it was a right of mine which I relinquished to Muʿawiyah, desiring the well-being of this community and the sparing of their blood, or it was a right belonging to a man more entitled to it than me, and so I did that. And I do not know; perhaps it is a trial for you and an enjoyment for a time."],[2498,"That Ali ؓ would return before the Day of Resurrection. He laughed and said: Glory be to Allah! If we knew that, we would not have married off his wives nor cast lots for his inheritance."],[2499,"One of them, and I think it was Hanafiyyah: a small provision from a departing beloved."],[2500,"A small provision from a departing beloved."],[2501,"By Allah, I will marry you off, and I know that you are prone to attachment, prone to divorce, and flattering, except that you are the noblest of the Arabs in house and the noblest in lineage."],[2502,"Al-Hasan b. Ali married a woman and sent her one hundred slave girls, with each slave girl a thousand dirhams."],[2503,"I used to play with al-Hasan and al-Husayn using toy horses. When they won against me, they would ride on me, and when I won against them, they would say: Would you ride on a part of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"],[2504,"I asked Ata, \"Should I carry water from Zamzam?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried it, and so did Hasan and Husayn.\""],[2505,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"gave his approval for Hasan and Husain.\""],[2506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2507,"On behalf of al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ."],[2508,"That Hasan and Husayn had ʿaqiqah performed for them."],[2509,"From Abu Saʿid al-Khudri ؓ, he said: Ali ؓ said: As for Hasan, Husayn, and Muhassin, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named them, performed ʿaqiqah for them, shaved their heads, gave charity equal to the weight of it, and ordered that they be circumcised, and they were circumcised."],[2510,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2511,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2512,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2513,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the heads of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, the two sons of ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ, to be shaved on their seventh day, so they were shaved, and he gave its weight in silver as charity, and he did not find an animal to slaughter.»"],[2514,"When Fāṭimah ؓ gave birth to Ḥasan, she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not perform ʿaqīqah on behalf of my son? He said: No, but shave his head and give in charity the weight of his hair in silver — or he said silver — to the poor. Then when she gave birth to Ḥusayn ؓ, she did the same for him. Mūsā b. Dāwūd said in his narration: to the awfāḍ and the poor. Abū al-Qāsim said: “Al-awfāḍ are the poor, and al-awqāṣ are the amounts between the two obligatory shares.”"],[2515,"That she perform ʿaqīqah for him with a great ram. So she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Do not perform ʿaqīqah for him with anything, but shave the hair of his head then give in charity its weight in silver in the way of Allah or to the awfāḍ.” Then she gave birth to al-Ḥusayn ؓ in the following year and did the same for him."],[2516,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ call the iqāmah for prayer in the ear of al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī when Fāṭimah ؓ gave birth to him»"],[2517,"«The Prophet ﷺ called the iqāmah for prayer in the ears of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn when they were born and ordered it.»"],[2518,"«Raise your garment so that I may kiss where I saw the Prophet ﷺ kiss.» So he raised it from his belly and placed his hand on his navel."],[2519,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced Ḥasan, then said: «O Allah, I have loved him, so love him.»"],[2520,"I heard al-Barāʾ b. ʿĀzib say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī on his shoulder, and he was saying: «O Allah, I love him, so love him.»"],[2521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ: «O Allah, I have loved him, so love him and love those who love him.»"],[2522,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ carrying al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ on his shoulder, saying: “O God, I love Hasan, so love him.”"],[2523,"The Prophet ﷺ would take Hasan and embrace him, saying: “O God, this is my son, so love him and love whoever loves him.”"],[2524,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we were invited to a meal, and there was al-Husayn ؓ playing in the road. The Prophet ﷺ hurried ahead of the people, then spread out his hands, and Husayn began running this way and that, making him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one of his hands on his chin and the other between his head and ears, then embraced and kissed him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Husayn is from me and I am from him. May God love whoever loves him. Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are two grandsons among the grandsons.”"],[2525,"Hasan and Husayn came walking towards the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . When one of them arrived, he placed his hand on his neck. Then the other came and placed his other hand on his neck. He kissed this one, then kissed the other one. Then he said, \"O Allah, I love them, so love them, O people. Indeed, children are a source of stinginess and cowardice.\""],[2526,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ climbed up to him, and the Prophet ﷺ embraced him and said: “This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God ﷻ will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2527,"From Ya'la b. Murra al-'Amiri that they went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to a meal to which they had been invited, and there was Husayn ؓ playing with some boys. He came to meet the Messenger of God ﷺ, who spread out his hand, and the boy began to flee this way and that while the Messenger of God ﷺ made him laugh until he caught him. He placed one of his hands on his neck and the other on the crown of his head, then embraced and kissed him. Then he said: “Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May God love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a grandson among the grandsons.”"],[2528,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the pulpit with al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ beside him, looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ once, and the Messenger of God ﷺ looking at him once, saying: “This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2529,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying, and al-Hasan would come, being a small child. Whenever the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he would jump onto his neck and back, and the Prophet ﷺ would raise his head gently so as not to drop him. They said: “O Messenger of God, you do something with this boy that we have not seen you do with anyone.” He said: “He is my sweet basil in this world. This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2530,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ with al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ, saying: “This son of mine is a master, and God will bring about reconciliation at his hands between two great factions of the Muslims.”"],[2531,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said of al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: “This son of mine is a master, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of my community.”"],[2532,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one day with Hasan and Husayn present. When he prostrated, al-Hasan came and jumped onto his back, and whenever he raised his head he would move him aside, fearing he might fall. When he finished, he took him by the hand and seated him in his lap and kissed him, and said: “This son of mine is a master, and he is my sweet basil in this world, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two great factions of the Muslims.”"],[2533,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said of al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: “This son of mine is a master, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of my community.”"],[2534,"And upon you, my master. It was said to him: “Do you say ‘my master’?” He replied: “I bear witness that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘He is a master.’”"],[2535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My son—meaning al-Hasan—is a chief, and through him Allah will surely reconcile two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2536,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: “By Allah, there is no prophet but that the prophets’ children were born to others, not to me. Indeed, your two sons are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, except for the two cousins, Yahya and Isa.”"],[2541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An angel from heaven who had never visited me asked Allah ﷻ permission to visit me, and he gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2542,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2543,"The Messenger ﷺ said: “This is an angel from among the angels who asked his Lord’s permission to greet me and visit me. He had never descended to the earth before. He gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2544,"We saw joy in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, so we said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have seen signs of joy in your face.” He said: “How could I not be joyful when Jibril ﷺ came to me and gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.”"],[2545,"I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I saw a figure with him. He said to me: “O Hudhayfah, did you see?” I said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “This is an angel who has not descended to me since I was sent. He came to me tonight and gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2546,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri ؓ narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, except for the two cousins, Isa son of Maryam and Yahya son of Zakariyya.”"],[2547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2549,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.”"],[2554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. O Allah, I love them, so love them.”"],[2555,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and al-Husayn: “I am at peace with those with whom you are at peace, and at war with those with whom you are at war.”"],[2556,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a house in which were Fatimah, Ali, Hasan, and Husayn ؓ, and said: “I am at war with those with whom you are at war, and at peace with those with whom you are at peace.”"],[2557,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Ali, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and Fatimah ؓ and said: “I am at war with those who fight you, and at peace with those who make peace with you.”"],[2558,"Ali ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and spent the night with us while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up to a water skin of ours and began squeezing it into a cup. Then he came to give him water and handed it to al-Hasan, but al-Husayn reached out to drink, so he stopped him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if he is the more beloved of the two to you. He said: “He asked for water first.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and these two—and I think he said: and this sleeping one, meaning Ali—on the Day of Resurrection will be in one place.”"],[2559,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “I, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn are gathered together—and whoever loves us on the Day of Resurrection—we will eat and drink until the servants are separated.” This reached a man among the people, so he asked about it, and I informed him. He said, “What about the presentation and the reckoning?” I said to him, “How was it for the companion of Ya-Sin in that regard when he was admitted to Paradise immediately?”"],[2560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ: “The first four to enter Paradise will be I, you, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, with our descendants behind our backs, our wives behind our descendants, and our Shi'ah to our right and to our left.”"],[2561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah guarded her chastity, and Allah (Mighty and Sublime) admitted her and her offspring to Paradise because she guarded her chastity.”"],[2562,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit addressing the people. Al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ came out with a rag around his neck dragging it, and he tripped on it and fell on his face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit heading for him. When the people saw him, they took the child and brought him to him, so he carried him and said: “May Allah curse Satan. Verily a child is a trial. By Allah, I did not know that I had descended from the pulpit until he was brought to me.”"],[2563,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying on his back in one of his rooms, al-Hasan came toddling until he sat on the Prophet's ﷺ chest, then urinated on his chest. I came to remove him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke and said: “Woe to you, O Anas! Leave my son and the fruit of my heart, for whoever harms this one has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, pouring it, and said: “Water is poured over a boy's urine, and a girl's urine is washed.”"],[2564,"Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: “This one is from me, and Husayn is from 'Ali.”"],[2565,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prophets will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on mounts so that they may arrive at the gathering place on that day. Salih will be sent on his she-camel, I will be sent on al-Buraq, and my two sons, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, will be sent on two she-camels from the she-camels of Paradise.”"],[2566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah (Mighty and Sublime) placed the progeny of every prophet in his loins, and Allah, Exalted is He, placed my progeny in the loins of 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ.”"],[2567,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every child of a female, their 'asabah (paternal kin) are from their father, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their 'asabah and I am their father.”"],[2568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every child of a mother affiliates with a paternal group, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and I am their 'asabah.”"],[2569,"He said: “O 'Ali, the days, months, and years only increase you in blindness regarding your affair. By Allah, if you do it, there will certainly be—there will certainly be matters whose number is known.” Then he went off dragging his garment. 'Ali said to al-'Abbas: “By Allah, that from him is not sincere advice, but rather 'Umar's whip has brought him out to what you see. By Allah, it is not desire for you, O 'Aqil, but 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Every tie and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.’” So 'Umar ؓ laughed and said: “Woe to 'Aqil, a fool and an idiot.”"],[2570,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every tie and lineage on the Day of Resurrection will be severed except my tie and my lineage.”"],[2571,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"On the Day of Resurrection every bond and lineage will be severed except my bond and my lineage.\""],[2572,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns. Whoever fights against us in the last days is as if he fought alongside the Dajjal.\""],[2573,"I saw Abu Dharr holding the two doorposts of the Ka'bah while saying: \"Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Noah among the people of Noah: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it perishes; and like the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel.'\""],[2574,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns.\""],[2575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Love God for the blessings He bestows upon you, love me for the love of God, and love my household for love of me.\""],[2576,"\"Place the family of Muhammad ﷺ in the position of the head to the body, and of the eyes to the head; for the body is only guided by the head, and the head is only guided by the eyes.\""],[2577,"\"When {Say, I do not ask you for this message any payment except loving kinship} They said, O Messenger of Allah, who are your close relatives that we are obligated to love them? He said, 'Ali, Fatimah, and their children.'\""],[2578,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take me and Al-Hussein, and one of us would sit on his right thigh and the other on his left thigh, and he would say, \"O Allah, I love them, so love them.\""],[2579,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to al-Husayn b. Ali: \"Whoever loves this one has loved me.\""],[2580,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were on his back. People tried to separate them, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave them alone, by my father and mother. Whoever loves me, let him love these two.\""],[2581,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.\""],[2582,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me\" - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2583,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me\" - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2584,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.\""],[2585,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: \"Whoever loves them loves me, and whoever hates them hates me.\""],[2586,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves me has loved them\"—meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2587,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"O God, I love them, so love them and hate whoever hates them.\""],[2588,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at Fatimah's house and greeted, and al-Hasan or al-Husayn came out to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Climb up, may your father be your ransom, you are a little bug's eye.\" He took hold of his two fingers, and he climbed onto his shoulder. Then the other one—al-Hasan or al-Husayn—came out with one of his eyes raised, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Welcome! Climb up, may your father be your ransom, you are the little bug's eye.\" He took hold of his two fingers, and he settled onto his other shoulder. The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of the backs of their necks until he placed their mouths on his mouth, then said: \"O God, I love them, so love them and love whoever loves them.\""],[2589,"These two ears of mine heard and these two eyes of mine saw the Messenger of God ﷺ holding by both his hands al-Hasan or al-Husayn, with his feet on the feet of the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he said: \"Huzuqqah, huzuqqah, climb up, little bug's eye.\" The boy would climb until he placed his feet on the chest of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he said to him: \"Open.\" He said: Then he kissed him. Then he said: \"O God, love him, for I love him.\""],[2590,"“Whoever loves me and loves these two and their father and their mother will be with me at my level on the Day of Resurrection.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 576)"],[2591,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: \"Whoever loves them, I love him; and whoever I love, God loves him; and whoever God loves, He admits him to the Gardens of Bliss. And whoever hates them or transgresses against them, I hate him; and whoever I hate, God hates him; and whoever God hates, He admits him to the punishment of Hell, and for him is an abiding punishment.\""],[2592,"From Ishaq b. Abi Habibah, the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, from Abu Hurayrah, that Marwan b. al-Hakam came to Abu Hurayrah during his final illness and said: \"O Abu Hurayrah, I have not found fault with you in anything since we have been companions except in your love for al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\" Abu Hurayrah stirred and sat up and said: \"I bear witness that we went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when we were on part of the road, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the sound of al-Hasan and al-Husayn crying while they were with their mother. He hastened his pace until he reached them, and I heard him say to her: 'What is the matter with my two sons?' She said: 'Thirst.' The Messenger of God ﷺ turned back to a water skin seeking water in it—water that day was in pools, and the people were seeking water. He called out: 'Does any of you have water with him?' Not one remained but that he turned his hand to his hook, seeking water in a water skin, and not one of them found a drop. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Hand me one of them.' She handed him one from beneath the curtain, and I saw the whiteness of her forearms when she handed him. He took him and pressed him to his chest while he was crying and would not be quiet. He stuck out his tongue for him, and he began to suck it until he calmed down or became still, and I no longer heard him crying. The other one kept crying and would not be quiet. He said: 'Hand me the other one.' She handed him to him, and he did the same with him, so they both became quiet, and I heard no sound from them. Then he said: 'Move on.' We dispersed right and left away from the women's litters until we met him on the main road. So should I not love these two when I have seen this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\""],[2593,"Al-Husayn came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying, and he clung to the neck of the Prophet ﷺ. He stood up with him and took hold of his hand, and he did not cease holding it until he bowed."],[2594,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ parting the thighs of Al-Hussein and kissing his little private area.\""],[2595,"While we were praying the night prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, whenever he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ would jump on his back. When he wanted to bow, he would take them by the hand gently and place them on the ground. When he returned, they returned, until he finished his prayer and turned away, placing them on his thighs. Abu Hurayrah said: I went to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I take them away?\" He said: \"No.\" Then a lightning flash flashed, and he said: \"Go to your mother.\" They kept walking in its light until they entered."],[2596,"Al-Husayn ؓ was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he loved him intensely. He said: \"I am going to my mother.\" I said: \"I will go with him.\" Then a lightning flash came from the sky, and he walked in its light until he arrived."],[2597,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was walking on all fours, with al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ on his back, and he was saying: \"What an excellent camel is your camel, and what excellent riders are you two.\""],[2598,"This verse was revealed in my house: {God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.} She was sitting at the door, and I said: \"O Messenger of God, am I not from the People of the House?\" He said: \"You are towards good.\""],[2599,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , brought together Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and then he brought them under his cloak. Then he said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household.\" Umm Salamah said, \"I said, O Messenger of Allah, include me with them.\" He said, \"Indeed, you are among my family.\""],[2600,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah, “Bring me your husband and his two sons.” So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast a Fadakī cloak over them, then placed his hand upon them and said, “O Allah, these are the family of Muḥammad ﷺ, so make Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muḥammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.” Umm Salamah said, “I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hand and said, ‘You are upon good.’”"],[2601,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah, “Bring me your husband and your two sons.” So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast a cloak over them, then said, “O Allah, these are the family of Muḥammad, so make Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muḥammad as You made them upon Ibrāhīm. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[2602,"I heard Umm Salamah saying, \"Fatimah came, carrying a tray with food in it, and she placed it between his hands. He then asked her, 'Where is your cousin?' She said, 'He is at home.' He said, 'Go and call him, and bring me my two grandsons.' So she came with her two sons, each of them holding the hand of the other, and Ali walking behind them, until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He made them sit in his chamber, with Ali on his right and Fatimah on his left.\" Umm Salamah said, \"I took off my cloak, which was our mattress at home, and in which there was a piece of pig's meat. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Pray to Allah for your husband and your two sons, Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn.' So she called upon Allah for them, and they all ate from that piece of pig's meat.\" Umm Salamah said, \"And I was praying in that chamber when this verse was revealed: 'Allah only desires to keep away the uncleanness from you, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification.' Then the Prophet ﷺ took the edge of the cloak and covered them with it, and then he extended his right hand out from beneath it, pointing it towards the sky, and said, 'O Allah! These are the people of my household and my close ones, so keep away impurity from them and purify them with a thorough purification.' Umm Salamah said, 'I entered my head into the chamber and said, 'O Messenger of Allah! Am I not included with you?' He said, 'You shall have a good outcome twice.'\""],[2603,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced ʿAlī and Fāṭimah with one hand and Ḥasan and Ḥusayn with the other, wrapped over them a black cloak that was upon him, and kissed ʿAlī and kissed Fāṭimah ؓ. Then he said, “O Allah, to You, not to the Fire—I and my household.” Umm Salamah said, “I said, ‘And I?’ He said, ‘And you.’”"],[2604,"Fatimah brought a dish to her father while he was at the house of Umm Salamah. She said, \"Mother, go and call my son and your nephew.\" They came and he covered them with a garment and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household and my protection. Remove impurity from them and cleanse them thoroughly.\" Umm Salamah said, \"And am I included with them, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You are the wife of the Prophet ﷺ , and you have a good status.\""],[2605,"Regarding what they insulted me about, I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a certain day when Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn came. He threw his cloak over them and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household. O Allah, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\" So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about me?\" He said, \"And you.\" He said, \"By Allah, it is indeed the most steadfast action in myself.\""],[2606,"Fāṭimah went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling him until he came. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ḥasan and Ḥusayn and seated each one of them on his thigh, drew Fāṭimah near to his lap, then wrapped his garment over them while I was leaning back. Then he said, {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.} Then he said, “These are my family.” Wāthilah said, “I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, and am I of your family?’ He said, ‘And you are of my family.’” Wāthilah said, “It is indeed the most hope I have.”"],[2607,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months when he went out from the morning prayer, he would say, \"O family of the house, the prayer. Allah desires only to remove from you all impurity, O people of the house, and to purify you with thorough purification.\""],[2608,"I heard Abu Al-Hamra'a saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming to the door of Fatimah for six months, saying, \"Indeed, Allah wants to remove impurity from you, O people of the household, and purify you with a thorough purification.\""],[2609,"This verse was revealed: {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity} O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly—regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn ؓ."],[2610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Exalted is He, divided creation into two divisions and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {And the companions of the right} and {the companions of the left}. I am of the companions of the right and I am of the best of the companions of the right. Then He made the two divisions into houses and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {And the companions of the right—what are the companions of the right? And the companions of the left—what are the companions of the left? And the foremost—the foremost.} I am of the best of the foremost. Then He made the houses into tribes and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {peoples and tribes}. I am the most God-fearing of the children of Ādam and the most honorable of them before Allah, may He be glorified, and no boast. Then He made the tribes into houses and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.}”"],[2611,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his illness in which he was taken, and Fāṭimah ؓ was at his head. She wept until her voice rose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to her and said, “My beloved Fāṭimah, what makes you weep?” She said, “I fear loss after you.” He said, “O my beloved, do you not know that Allah, may He be glorified, looked upon the earth one look and chose your father from it, and sent him with His message? Then He looked another look and chose your husband from it, and revealed to me that I should marry you to him. O Fāṭimah, we are a household to whom Allah has given seven qualities not given to anyone before us, nor given to anyone after us: I am the seal of the prophets and the most honorable of the prophets before Allah and the most beloved of creation to Allah, may He be glorified, and I am your father. My successor is the best of successors and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is your husband. Our martyr is the best of martyrs and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is your paternal uncle Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he is the uncle of your father and the uncle of your husband. Among us is one who has two green wings, flying in Paradise with the angels wherever he wishes, and he is the cousin of your father and the brother of your husband. Among us are the two grandsons of this community, and they are your two sons, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, and they are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. Their father, by the One who sent me with the truth, is better than them. O Fāṭimah, by the One who sent me with the truth, from them is the Mahdī of this community when the world becomes chaos and confusion, tribulations appear, ways are cut off, and they raid one another, no elder shows mercy to a child and no child honors an elder. Then Allah, may He be glorified, will send from them at that time one who conquers the fortresses of misguidance and sealed hearts, who will uphold the religion at the end of time as I upheld it at the beginning of time, and will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with oppression. O Fāṭimah, do not grieve and do not weep, for Allah, may He be glorified, is more merciful and more compassionate to you than I, because of your place with me and your position in my heart. Allah married you to your husband, and he is the noblest of your household in lineage, the most generous of them in standing, the most merciful of them to the people, the most just of them in equity, and the most discerning of them in judgment. I asked my Lord, may He be glorified, that you be the first of my household to join me.” ʿAlī ؓ said, “When the Prophet ﷺ was taken, Fāṭimah ؓ remained after him only seventy-five days until Allah joined her to him ﷺ.”"],[2613,"We were around the Prophet ﷺ when Umm Ayman came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn have gone astray.” He said, “That was at the rising of the day,” meaning the height of the day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Arise and seek my two sons.” He said, “Each man took the direction he faced, and I took the direction of the Prophet ﷺ. He did not stop until he came to the foot of a mountain, and there were al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ, each one clinging to his companion, and a serpent standing on its tail, from its mouth coming something like fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastened to it, and it turned addressing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then slithered and entered among some rocks. Then he came to the two of them, separated them, wiped their faces, and said, ‘May my father and mother be your ransom, how honored you are before Allah.’ Then he carried one of them on his right shoulder and the other on his left shoulder. I said, ‘Blessed are you two, what an excellent mount is your mount.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘And what excellent riders are they, and their father is better than them.’”"],[2614,"\"Narrated by Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'O people, I am leaving behind among you two things, if you hold onto them, you will never go astray after me: the Book of Allah, which is a stretched rope between the heaven and the earth, and my family, the people of my household. Indeed, they will not part ways until they meet me at the Pond of Kawthar.'\""],[2615,"It is as if I have been called and I answered. I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, a rope stretched between heaven and earth, and my progeny, my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool. So consider carefully how you succeed me in them."],[2616,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his pilgrimage on the day of ʿArafah while he was on his she-camel al-Qaṣwāʾ, and he delivered a sermon. I heard him saying, “O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household.”"],[2617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the pool, whose width is between Ṣanʿāʾ and Buṣrā, containing as many golden and silver goblets as the number of stars. So consider carefully how you succeed me in the two weighty things.” A man stood and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two weighty things?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The greater is the Book of Allah, a rope one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end in your hands. Hold fast to it, and you will never cease nor go astray. The lesser is my progeny. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool, and I asked that for them from my Lord. So do not go ahead of them and perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you.”"],[2618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the ʿaṣr prayer, and when he was in the fourth rakʿah, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn came and climbed onto the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said salām, he placed them in front of him, and al-Ḥusayn came forward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried al-Ḥasan on his right shoulder and al-Ḥusayn on his left shoulder, then said, “O people, shall I tell you of the best of people in grandfather and grandmother? Shall I tell you of the best of people in paternal uncle and paternal aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in maternal uncle and maternal aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in father and mother? They are al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn. Their grandfather is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their grandmother is Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid, their mother is Fāṭimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their father is ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ, their paternal uncle is Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib, their paternal aunt is Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib, their maternal uncle is al-Qāsim b. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their maternal aunts are Zaynab, Ruqayyah, and Umm Kulthūm, daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Their grandfather is in Paradise, their father is in Paradise, their paternal uncle is in Paradise, their paternal aunt is in Paradise, their maternal aunts are in Paradise, they are in Paradise, and whoever loves them is in Paradise.”"],[2619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O people, I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the Pond, a pond as wide as the distance between Sana'a and Busra, in which there are as many silver cups as the number of stars. I will ask you when you come to me about the two weighty things, so consider how you will succeed me in them. The greater tie is the Book of God ﷻ, a tie one end of which is in God's hand and the other in your hands, so hold fast to it and do not go astray and do not alter it. And my progeny, the people of my house, for the Gentle, the All-Aware has informed me that they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond.”"],[2620,"“The pen has been lifted and the pages have dried, and matters are decreed in a book that has already passed.”"],[2621,"Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to practice coitus interruptus with her, and she was his concubine."],[2622,"“Put down the knife, say the name of God, and eat.”"],[2623,"“I saw Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn ؓ circumambulate after Asr and pray two rak'ahs.”"],[2624,"He asked his son al-Hasan ibn ʿAlī about certain matters of manly virtue (murū’ah). He said: “My son, what is soundness (sadād)?” He replied: “Father, soundness is repelling wrongdoing with what is right.” He said: “Then what is nobility (sharaf)?” He replied: “Doing good to one’s clan, bearing burdensome liabilities, being in harmony with one’s brothers, and safeguarding the neighbors.” He said: “Then what is murū’ah?” He replied: “Chastity and setting one’s wealth aright.” He said: “Then what is meticulousness (diqqah)?” He replied: “Looking into small matters and preventing what is insignificant.” He said: “Then what is blameworthiness (lawm)?” He replied: “A man’s guarding himself while exposing his wife.” He said: “Then what is generosity (samāḥah)?” He replied: “Giving in hardship and in ease.” He said: “Then what is miserliness (shuḥḥ)?” He replied: “To regard what you have spent as loss.” He said: “Then what is brotherhood (ikhā’)?” He replied: “Sharing and consoling in hardship and in prosperity.” He said: “Then what is cowardice (jubn)?” He replied: “Boldness against a friend and shrinking from an enemy.” He said: “Then what is booty (ghanīmah)?” He replied: “Desiring piety and renouncing the world—this is the cool (easy) gain.” He said: “Then what is forbearance (ḥilm)?” He replied: “Suppressing anger and mastering oneself.” He said: “Then what is wealth (ghinā)?” He replied: “The soul’s contentment with what God Most High has allotted it, even if little; wealth is only the wealth of the soul.” He said: “Then what is poverty (faqr)?” He replied: “The soul’s avid craving in everything.” He said: “Then what is strength (manaʿah)?” He replied: “Great severity in battle and contending with the mighty among people.” He said: “Then what is humiliation (dhull)?” He replied: “Panic when truly tested.” He said: “Then what is ineptness (ʿiyy)?” He replied: “Fidgeting with the beard and much spitting when speaking.” He said: “Then what is audacity (jur’ah)?” He replied: “Keeping pace with one’s peers.” He said: “Then what is affectation/burdening oneself (kulfah)?” He replied: “Your speaking about what does not concern you.” He said: “Then what is glory (majd)?” He replied: “To give despite liability, and to pardon despite offense.” He said: “Then what is intellect (ʿaql)?” He replied: “Preserving in the heart whatever you have taken in.” He said: “Then what is stupidity/rashness (kharq)?” He replied: “Opposing your leader and raising your voice against him.” He said: “Then what is good praise?” He replied: “Doing what is beautiful and leaving what is ugly.” He said: “Then what is prudence/resolve (ḥazm)?” He replied: “Long deliberation and gentleness with those in authority.” He said: “Then what is foolishness (safah)?” He replied: “Following baseness and keeping company with the errant.” He said: “Then what is heedlessness (ghaflah)?” He replied: “Your leaving the mosque and your obeying the corrupter.” He said: “Then what is deprivation (ḥirmān)?” He replied: “Your leaving your share when it has been offered to you.” He said: “Then what is the corrupter (mufsid)?” He replied: “The fool with his wealth, the one who is careless about his honor.” Then ʿAlī said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘No poverty is harsher than ignorance; no wealth is more beneficial than intellect; no loneliness is more desolate than self-admiration; no support is more fitting than consultation; no intellect is like sound planning; no lineage is like good character; no piety is like restraint; no worship is like reflection; and no faith is like modesty and patience. The bane of speech is lying; the bane of knowledge is forgetfulness; the bane of forbearance is foolishness; the bane of worship is slackening; the bane of elegance is insolence; the bane of courage is transgression; the bane of generosity is reminding others of one’s favors; the bane of beauty is arrogance; and the bane of lineage is boastfulness.’ My son, never belittle any man you ever see: if he is better than you, then consider him your father; if he is like you, then he is your brother; and if he is younger than you, then consider him your son.” Abū al-Qāsim said: “No one narrated this ḥadīth from Shuʿbah except Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh Abū Rajā’ al-Ḥabaṭī; it was uniquely reported by ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Zayyāt. And it is not narrated from ʿAlī except with this chain of transmission.”"],[2625,"“They are two sufficing (prayers) beyond which there is nothing else.”"],[2626,"“O God, make his death be solitary, for killing is an expiation.”"],[2627,"I went out with Al-Hassan and a servant who had some henna on her nails. Suddenly, pangs of pain from a toothache struck him. He said, \"Oh servant, bring the powdered medicine,\" so she poured water in it and threw the books in the water. None of them opened or reacted to it, and he did not look at it. So, I asked, \"Oh Abu Muhammad, whose books are these?\" He said, \"They are from the people of Iraq, who do not return to the truth nor abstain from falsehood. I am not afraid of them for myself, but I fear them for that.\" And he pointed towards Al-Hussein.\""],[2628,"Take me out to the open desert so that I may look at the dominion of the heavens, meaning the signs. When he was taken out, he said: “O God, I seek reward from You for my soul, for it is the dearest of souls to me.” And it was part of what God did for him that he sought reward for his soul."],[2629,"I heard Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr say: “Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ died at the age of forty-seven.”"],[2630,"That he poisoned him."],[2631,"I heard Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr say: “Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ died in the year forty-nine, in the month of Rabi al-Awwal.”"],[2632,"“Al-Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ died in the year forty-nine, and Sa'id b. al-As prayed over him. His death was in Madinah, and his age was forty-six or forty-seven.”"],[2633,"to bury him with the Prophet ﷺ, but he feared that Banu Umayyah would prevent him. So when they brought him to the mosque, Banu Umayyah stood up, and 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far stood up and said: \"I heard him say: 'If they prevent you, then bury me with my mother.'\""],[2634,"\"I will not ascend or speak until you grant me that if I speak truth, you will affirm me, and if I speak falsehood, you will refute me.\" So they granted him that, and he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: \"By Allah, O 'Amr, and you, O Mughirah, you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah cursed the driver and the rider' — one of them being so-and-so?\" They said: \"O Allah, yes, indeed.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, O Mu'awiyah, and O Mughirah, do you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed 'Amr with a curse for every rhyme he uttered?\" They said: \"O Allah, indeed.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, O 'Amr, and you, O Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, do you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the people of this one?\" They said: \"Indeed.\" Al-Hasan said: \"I praise Allah that you have fallen among those who dissociated from this one.\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[2635,"Mu'awiyah ؓ: \"Do not say that, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into his mouth, and whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into his mouth is not inarticulate.\" Then al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ said: \"As for you, O 'Amr, two men disputed over you, so consider which of them is your father. And as for you, O Abu al-A'war, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed Ri'l, Dhakwan, and 'Amr b. Sufyan.\""],[2636,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"I was walking with him one day when he passed by a pile of charity dates. I found a date and threw it into my mouth, and he took it out with my saliva. Some of the people said: 'What harm would it have been, O Messenger of Allah, if you had left it?' He said: 'We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us.'\""],[2637,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with her two sons, and he gave her three dates. She gave each of her two sons one date, and they ate their two dates, then they began looking at their mother. She split her date into two halves between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has shown her mercy because of her mercy to her two sons.\""],[2638,"O people, tonight a man has passed away among you whom the earlier ones did not surpass, nor will the later ones overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on expeditions, and Jibril would flank him on his right and Mika'il on his left. He would not turn back until victory was granted to them. He left nothing except seven hundred dirhams with which he intended to buy a servant. He passed away on the night on which Isa b. Maryam was raised—the night of the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."],[2639,"We are a people who do not marry off our women until we consult them, so go to her. So I went to her and mentioned Yazid to her. She said, 'By Allah, that will not happen until your companion behaves among us as Pharaoh behaved among the Children of Israel, slaughtering their sons and sparing their women.' I returned to al-Hasan and said, 'You sent me to a splitting piece of creation who calls the Commander of the Believers Pharaoh.' He said, 'O Muawiya, beware of hating us, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hates us or envies us except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be increased with whips of fire.\"'"],[2640,"A man called Muawiya—meaning Ibn Hudayj—reviled Ali ؓ with a foul insult in Muawiya's presence. Do you know him? He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'When you see him, bring him to me.' He said, 'He saw him at the house of Amr b. Hurayth, and he pointed him out to him.' He said, 'Are you Muawiya b. Hudayj?' He remained silent and did not answer him three times. Then he said, 'You are the one who reviled Ali in the presence of the son of the liver-eater. Indeed, if you reach the Pond—and I do not think you will reach it—you will find him with his sleeves rolled up and his arms bared, driving the disbelievers and hypocrites away from the Pond of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as stray camels are driven away from their owner. This is the saying of the truthful one, the one who was believed, Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[2641,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Among the things that obligate forgiveness is your bringing joy to your Muslim brother.”"],[2642,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, he would leave extra water until he let it flow over the place of his prostration."],[2643,"I was between al-Hasan and al-Husayn while Marwan was exchanging insults with them. Al-Hasan kept trying to silence al-Husayn, but Marwan said, “A cursed household!” Al-Hasan became angry and said, “You said, ‘A cursed household’? By God, God has cursed you on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ while you were still in your father’s loins.”"],[2644,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I climbed with him to the room where charity (dates) was stored. I took a date and chewed it. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Spit it out; charity is not lawful for us.”"],[2645,"If you were to look between Jabars and Jabalq, you would not find a man whose grandfather is a prophet other than me and my brother. I think you should unite behind Mu'awiyah. {And I do not know; perhaps it is a trial for you and enjoyment for a time.} Ma'mar said: Jabars and Jabalq are the east and the west."],[2646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The gift for the fasting person is perfume and incense.\""],[2647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did both: he entered ihram when his mount stood him upright, and he entered ihram while he was at al-Bayda', on the ground, before his mount stood him upright.\""],[2648,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the saying of Allah ﷻ {Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet}?\" He said, \"This is from what is hidden, and had you not asked me about it, I would not have informed you. Indeed, Allah ﷻ appointed two angels over me. I am not mentioned before a Muslim servant who sends blessings upon me except that those two angels say, 'May Allah forgive you,' and Allah and His angels say in response to those two angels, 'Amin.' And no one sends blessings upon me except that those two angels say, 'May Allah forgive you,' and Allah and His angels say in response to those two angels, 'Amin.'\""],[2649,"Do not rebuke me, may God have mercy on you, for the Messenger of God ﷺ was shown the Umayyads mounting his pulpit, one man after another, and that grieved him. Then this verse was revealed: {Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar} — a river in Paradise — and it was revealed: {Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree. And what can make you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months} — the Umayyads will possess it. Al-Qasim said: 'We calculated that, and it was exactly one thousand, neither more nor less.'"],[2650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot and naked.' A woman said, 'O Messenger of God, how will we see one another?' He said, 'The eyes that Day will be staring.' He raised his gaze to the sky, and she said, 'O Messenger of God, ask God to cover my nakedness.' He said, 'O God, cover her nakedness.'"],[2651,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to wear the best of what we find, to perfume ourselves with the best of what we find, and to slaughter as sacrifices the fattest of what we find: a cow on behalf of seven, a camel on behalf of ten, and to proclaim the takbir aloud, with tranquility and dignity upon us."],[2652,"He said to her, 'Do you show gloating over the killing of Ali? Go, for you are divorced thrice.' She veiled herself with a cloak of hers and sat in a corner of the house, saying, 'By God, I did not intend what you thought.' She remained until her waiting period ended, then moved away from him. He sent her the remainder of her dower that he owed and a gift of ten thousand. When the messenger came to her with that, she said, 'A small provision from a departing beloved.' When the messenger returned to al-Hasan and told him what she said, al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ wept and said, 'Were it not that I heard my grandfather the Messenger of God ﷺ — or heard my father narrating from my grandfather — that he said: \"If a man divorces his wife thrice at the times of purity or divorces her thrice without specification, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband,\" I would have taken her back.'"],[2653,"Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan performed Hajj, and with him performed Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj, who was among the people most abusive of Ali. He passed through Madinah in the mosque of the Messenger ﷺ while al-Hasan b. Ali was sitting with a group of his companions. It was said to him, 'This is Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj, the abuser of Ali ؓ.' He said, 'Bring the man to me.' The messenger came to him and said, 'Answer.' He said, 'Who?' He said, 'Al-Hasan b. Ali is calling you.' He came to him and greeted him. Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ said to him, 'Are you Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj?' He said, 'Yes.' He repeated it three times. Then al-Hasan said to him, 'The abuser of Ali?' He seemed ashamed. Al-Hasan ؓ said to him, 'By God, if you reach the pool — and I do not think you will reach it — you will find him with his garment girded up his shin, driving away the hypocrites as a stray camel is driven away. This is the saying of the truthful one, the one who is believed ﷺ, and he who fabricates has failed.'"],[2654,"I heard al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ say: 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream clinging to the Throne. I saw Abu Bakr ؓ holding the waist of the Prophet ﷺ. I saw Umar ؓ holding the waist of Abu Bakr ؓ. I saw Uthman ؓ holding the waist of Umar ؓ. And I saw blood pouring from the sky to the earth.' Al-Hasan narrated this hadith while a group of Shi'ah were with him. They said, 'And what did you see of Ali?' Al-Hasan said, 'There was no one I would have loved more to see holding the waist of the Prophet ﷺ than Ali, but it was a dream I saw.'"],[2655,"Ali ؓ said to him, 'How have you become this morning, O son of the Messenger of God?' He said, 'By God's praise, I have become cured.' Ali said, 'So it is, God willing.' Then al-Hasan ؓ said, 'Support me.' Ali ؓ leaned him against his chest. He said, 'I heard my grandfather the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"In Paradise there is a tree called the Tree of Trial. On the Day of Resurrection the people of trial will be brought, and no record will be raised for them, nor will a scale be set up for them; their reward will be poured upon them in abundance.\"' And he recited: {Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account.}"],[2656,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Feed food and speak good words.'"],[2657,"That 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it from pride that I wear a fine suit? He said, 'No.' He said: Is it from pride that I ride a noble she-camel? He said, 'No.' He said: Is it from pride that I prepare food and invite a people who eat at my place and walk behind my heels? He said, 'No.' He said: Then what is pride? He said, 'To treat the truth as foolish and to despise people.'"],[2658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The bearers of the Qur'an are the nobles of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2659,"Yes, I saw him sitting at the well of Zamzam. I said: Did you see him dye (his hair)? He said, 'No, except that I saw him and his beard was black up to this place, meaning his 'anfaqa (the hair below the lower lip), and below that there was whiteness. And he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ had gray hairs in that place, and he used to imitate him.'"],[2660,"That he asked al-Husayn b. 'Ali ؓ: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrust you with anything regarding this journey of yours? He said, 'No.'"],[2661,"What is the name of this place? They said: Karbala'. He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: it is distress (karb) and affliction (bala').'"],[2662,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'An excellent thing is a gift before the need (arises).'"],[2663,"'I saw the Prophet ﷺ drinking while standing.'"],[2664,"\"He bears witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. I asked, 'Do you bear witness that Abdullah is also a messenger?' He replied, 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah used to like to make things easy for his ummah (followers). I said, 'How should I bear witness that Ali is the messenger?' He said, 'The greetings are for Allah, and the prayers and the good things. The gifts, the fragrances, the pure things are for Allah.'\""],[2665,"That when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hid the word 'smoke' (dukhan) for Ibn Sayyad, he asked him what he had hidden for him. He said, 'Dukh.' He said, 'Be gone! You will never exceed your appointed term.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away, the people said, 'What did he say?' Some said, 'Dukh,' and others said, 'Rather, Zukh.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This while you are with me you differ, so after me you will differ even more.'"],[2666,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I am cowardly and I am weak. He said, 'Come to a jihad in which there is no hardship: the Hajj.'"],[2667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2669,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2671,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me: \"O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed; for You decree and none decrees over You. He whom You befriend is not humiliated, and he whom You oppose is not honored. Blessed and exalted are You.\""],[2672,"“My grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, taught me some words to say in Qunut of Witr: Allahumma ‘afini fiman ‘afait, wa tawallani fiman tawallait, wahdini fiman hadait, wa qini sharra ma qadait, wa barik li fima a’tait. Innaka taqdi wa la yuqda ‘alaik, innahu la yudhillu man walait. Subhanaka rabbana tabarakta wa ta’alait (O Allah, pardon me along with those whom You have pardoned, be an ally to me along with those whom You are an ally to, guide me along with those whom You have guided, protect me from the evil that You have decreed, and bless for me that which You have bestowed. For verily You decree and none can decree over You. He whom You support can never be humiliated. Glory is to You, our Lord, You are Blessed and Exalted).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1178)"],[2673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me some words that I say during the witr. (The version of Ibn Jawwas has: I say them in the supplication of the witr.) They were: \"O Allah, guide me among those Thou hast guided, grant me security among those Thou hast granted security, take me into Thy charge among those Thou hast taken into Thy charge, bless me in what Thou hast given, guard me from the evil of what Thou hast decreed, for Thou dost decree, and nothing is decreed for Thee. He whom Thou befriendest is not humbled. Blessed and Exalted art Thou, our Lord.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1425)"],[2675,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ: \"What were you like during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and what did you retain from him?\" He said: \"I retained from him that I heard him say: 'Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for evil is doubt and good is tranquility.' And I retained from him the five prayers and words that I say at their completion. He said: \"Say: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed; for You decree and none decrees over You. He whom You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You, our Lord.\" Burayd b. Abi Maryam said: \"I entered upon Muhammad b. Ali in the mountain pass and narrated this hadith to him from Abu al-Hawra' from al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ. He said: 'He spoke the truth. These are words that we were taught to say in the qunut.'\""],[2676,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ: \"What did you memorize from the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"The five prayers.\""],[2677,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali: \"What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"I remember from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulled it out with its saliva and put it back among the dates. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what harm would this date have done to this boy?' He said: 'We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us.'\""],[2678,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ: \"What were you like on the day the Prophet ﷺ died, and what do you retain from him?\" He said: \"I retained from him that a man came to him one day and asked him about something, and he said: 'Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for evil is doubt and good is tranquility.' And I retained from him that I passed by him one day while there was in front of him a trough of charity dates, and I took a date and threw it into my mouth. He grabbed me by the back of my neck, then inserted his hand into my mouth and pulled it out with its saliva, then threw it back into the trough. His companions said to him: 'If only you had left the boy to eat it.' He said: 'Charity is not lawful for the family of Muhammad.'\" He said: \"And he taught me words that I supplicate with at the end of the qunut: 'O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and take me as an ally among those You have taken as allies, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed; for You decree and none decrees over You, and he whom You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed and exalted are You.'\""],[2679,"“My grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, taught me some words to say in Qunut of Witr: Allahumma ‘afini fiman ‘afait, wa tawallani fiman tawallait, wahdini fiman hadait, wa qini sharra ma qadait, wa barik li fima a’tait. Innaka taqdi wa la yuqda ‘alaik, innahu la yudhillu man walait. Subhanaka rabbana tabarakta wa ta’alait (O Allah, pardon me along with those whom You have pardoned, be an ally to me along with those whom You are an ally to, guide me along with those whom You have guided, protect me from the evil that You have decreed, and bless for me that which You have bestowed. For verily You decree and none can decree over You. He whom You support can never be humiliated. Glory is to You, our Lord, You are Blessed and Exalted).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1178)"],[2680,"About your father Muhammad ﷺ? He taught me some words to say in Witr. I asked, \"What are they?\" He said, \"O Allah, guide me among those whom You have guided, pardon me among those whom You have pardoned, turn to me in friendship among those on whom You have turned in friendship, and bless me in what You have bestowed, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none can decree over You.\" I said to myself, \"Did you remember anything else from him?\" He said, \"I walked with him in the alley of charity and I took a date and put it in my mouth. He put his hand in my mouth and took it out and said, 'O my son, don't you know that we, the people of the Prophet's house, do not eat charity?'\""],[2681,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while there was a bone in his hand from which he was gnawing. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and bit from it one or two bites, then prayed without performing ablution.\""],[2682,"\"O people, you have lost a man whom the earlier ones did not outstrip and the later ones will not overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him out on a military expedition with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left. By Allah, he left neither white nor yellow except eight hundred dirhams for the price of a servant.\""],[2683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him—meaning Ali ؓ—with a raiding party, and Jibril would fight on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory."],[2684,"O people, yesterday a man departed from you whom the earlier ones did not surpass in knowledge, nor will the later ones overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on expeditions and give him the banner, and he would not return until Allah granted him victory. Indeed, Jibril was on his right and Mika'il on his left. He left no gold or silver except seven hundred dirhams with which he intended to buy a servant."],[2685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never sent Ali on an expedition except that he gave him the banner."],[2686,"The Prophet ﷺ never sent Ali on an expedition except that he gave him the banner."],[2687,"A man has departed from you whom no one among the earlier ones surpassed in knowledge, and no one among the later ones will overtake. He was the one whom the Prophet ﷺ would send, and he would give him the banner, then he would set out and not return until Allah ﷻ granted him victory. Jibril was on his right and Mika'il on his left, fighting with him. He died and left no dinar or dirham except ornaments worth seven hundred dirhams that remained from his stipend."],[2688,"A man has departed from you who left no gold or silver except seven hundred dirhams from his stipend, with which he intended to buy a servant—meaning Ali ؓ."],[2689,"Yesterday a man departed from you whom the earlier ones did not surpass in knowledge, nor will the later ones overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on expeditions and give him the banner; Jibril was on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah ﷻ granted him victory."],[2690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'War is deception.'"],[2691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wherever you are, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me.'"],[2692,"It was said, “O Messenger of God, a group of people come to a house and one of them asks permission—does that suffice for all of them?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “And one man of the group responds—does that suffice for the whole group?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “A group passes by and one of them gives the greeting of peace—does that suffice for all of them?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “And one man of the group returns the greeting—does that suffice for the whole group?” He said, “Yes.”"],[2693,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Among the things that bring about forgiveness is bringing joy to your Muslim brother.”"],[2694,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The one who is cheated is neither praiseworthy nor rewarded.”"],[2695,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites the Verse of the Throne after the prescribed prayer is in the protection of God until the next prayer.”"],[2696,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed while men and women were walking in front of him, with no barrier, on the side facing the Black Stone."],[2697,"A man from the people of Madinah, whose kunya is Abu Abd Allah, narrated to me: Abd Allah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ , who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Palm trees and trees are a blessing upon their owners and upon their descendants after them, if they are thankful to God.”"],[2698,"Ammar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Nakha‘i narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Hasan b. Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever offers a sacrifice, his soul being pleased with it, seeking reward for his sacrificial animal, it will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[2699,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit on the day of the expedition of Tabuk, praised God and extolled Him, then said, “O people, by God, I do not command you except with what God has commanded you, nor do I forbid you except from what God has forbidden you. So be moderate in seeking; for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, one of you is sought by his provision just as he is sought by his appointed term. If any of it becomes difficult for you, then seek it through obedience to God, exalted is He.”"],[2700,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Fatimah's house, and she handed him a cooked shoulder of a sheep. He ate it, then stood to pray. She took hold of his clothes and said, \"Will you not perform ablution, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"From what, my dear daughter?\" She said, \"You have eaten from that which the fire has touched.\" He said, \"The purest of your food is that which the fire has touched.\""],[2701,"One of them said, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not stand?\" The other said, \"Yes, then he sat.\""],[2702,"Al-Hasan said, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ not stand for the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess that passed by him?\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Yes, and he sat.\""],[2703,"The one standing said to the one sitting, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ not stand?\" He said, \"Yes, then he sat.\""],[2704,"That a funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and he stood?\" He said, \"Yes, and he has sat.\""],[2705,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed stood and sat?\""],[2706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Anas, go and summon for me the master of the Arabs,\" meaning Ali. Aisha ؓ said, \"Are you not the master of the Arabs?\" He said, \"I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.\" When Ali ؓ came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for the Ansar, and they came to him. He said to them: \"O assembly of Ansar, shall I not direct you to something which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after it?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"This is Ali, so love him with my love and honor him for my honor, for Jibril ﷺ commanded me with what I have told you from Allah ﷻ.\""],[2707,"I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: \"Whoever regularly goes to the mosque gains a brother obtained for Allah ﷻ, novel knowledge, a word that calls him to guidance, a word that turns him away from ruin, and he abandons sins out of modesty or fear, and a blessing or awaited mercy.\""],[2708,"When Al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) became the leader after Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was killed, while he was leading the people in prayer, a man attacked him and stabbed him in the thigh with a dagger. He was bedridden because of it for months. Then he stood on the pulpit to deliver a sermon and said: \"O people of Iraq, fear Allah concerning us, for we are your leaders and your guests. We are the family of the house about whom Allah Almighty said: {Allah only desires to remove defilement from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly}.\" He continued speaking that day until no one in the mosque was seen except that they were weeping."],[2709,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever receives a gift while a group of people are sitting with him, they are his partners in it.'"],[2710,"'Lift your garment so that I may kiss where I saw the Prophet ﷺ kiss.' He lifted it from his belly and placed his hand on his navel."],[2711,"Between al-Hasan and al-Husayn there was only one purity period."],[2712,"O Abu Abd Allah, I saw you on the hands of the Messenger of God ﷺ with them stained with blood when you were brought to him at birth, and he delighted in you and wrapped you in a cloth. He spat into your mouth and spoke words I do not know. Fatimah ؓ had raced ahead of him in cutting the navel cord of al-Hasan ؓ, and he said, 'Do not race me in that.'"],[2713,"Whoever would like to look at the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his neck to his face, let him look at al-Hasan b. Ali; and whoever would like to look at the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his neck to his ankle in physique and complexion, let him look at al-Husayn b. Ali."],[2714,"Whoever would like to look at the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ from his head to his neck, let him look at al-Hasan; and whoever would like to look at what is below his neck, let him look at al-Husayn. They divided it between themselves."],[2715,"Al-Hasan was the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from the chest upward. Then he mentioned something similar."],[2716,"The person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his head to his chest was al-Hasan."],[2717,"Al-Hasan was the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from the head to the chest."],[2718,"When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Hasan.' When al-Husayn was born, we named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Bring me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Husayn.' When the third was born, I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Muhassin.' Then he said, 'I have named them with the names of the sons of Aaron: Shabar, Shubayr, and Mushabbir.'"],[2719,"When al-Hasan was born, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: “Show me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: I named him Harb [which means ʿwarʿ]. He said: ʿRather he is Hasan.” When al-Husain was born, he said: ʿShow me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: I named him Harb, He said: ʿRather he is Husain.” When the third one was born, the Prophet ﷺ said: ʿShow me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: Harb, He said: “Rather. he is Muhassin.” Then he said: “I have named them after the fashion of the sons of Haroon, Shabbar and Shabeer and Mushabbir.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 953)"],[2720,"I wanted to have the kunya Abu Harb. When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said, 'He is al-Hasan.'"],[2721,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'No, name him Hasan.' Then al-Husayn was born, and I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, name him Husayn.' Then another was born, and I named him Harb. He ﷺ said, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Name him Muhassin.'"],[2722,"Ali ؓ said: I was a man who loved war. When al-Hasan was born, I wanted to name him Harb, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Hasan. When al-Husayn was born, I wanted to name him Harb, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Husayn, and he ﷺ said, 'I have named these two sons of mine after the two sons of Aaron: Shabar and Shubayr.'"],[2723,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I have named them—meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn—after the two sons of Aaron: Shabar and Shubayr.'"],[2724,"Al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye his hair with wasima (a dark dye)."],[2725,"He named his eldest son Hamza and named Husayn Ja'far after his uncle, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named them Hasan and Husayn."],[2726,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ dying [their hair] with henna and katam."],[2727,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ dying [their hair] with black."],[2728,"Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed on the day of Ashura in the year sixty-one, and he was fifty-eight years old, and he used to dye [his hair] with henna and katam."],[2729,"Ali was killed when he was fifty-two, and at that same age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed, and at that same age Ali b. al-Husayn died, and at that same age Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn died."],[2730,"I heard al-Mahdi ask Ja'far, \"How old was Ali when he was killed?\" He said, \"Fifty-eight, and at that same age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed.\""],[2731,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing [his hair] with black."],[2732,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ, the two sons of Fatimah ؓ, dyeing [their hair] with black, and al-Husayn used to leave the tuft under the lip."],[2733,"I entered upon Al-Husayn ibn Ali, and he had dyed himself with black."],[2734,"Al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye [his hair] with black."],[2735,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing [his hair] with black."],[2736,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ used to dye [his hair] with black."],[2737,"From Umar b. Ata b. Abi al-Khuwar and Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid, they said: \"We saw al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ dyeing [his hair] with wasmah.\""],[2738,"\"No.\" I said, \"Then should I let it hang below the two ankles?\" He said, \"What is below the two ankles is in the Fire.\""],[2739,"I saw on al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ upright khazz socks, and I saw them riding trade horses."],[2740,"I saw on al-Husayn b. Ali a red khazz cloak."],[2741,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali with a khazz turban on him, his hair emerging from beneath the turban."],[2742,"I entered upon al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ and he had a khazz garment on."],[2743,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ used to wear a ring on his left hand."],[2744,"I saw on al-Husayn on the day he was killed a sindus yalmaq."],[2745,"A man said: O Abu Firas, who is this? Al-Farazdaq said:"],[2746,"Ali ؓ said: \"Shall I not tell you about my own special self and my household?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"As for Hasan, he is a man of large bowls and a table, a youth among the youths. If the two loops of the girth meet, he will not avail you in war more than a sparrow's snare. As for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of amusement, shade, and falsehood. Let not the two sons of Abbas deceive you. As for me and Husayn, I and Husayn are of you and you are of us. By Allah, I fear that these people will be given power over you because of their uprightness in their land and your corruption in yours, their discharging the trust and your betrayal, their obedience to their leader and your disobedience to him, their unity upon their falsehood and your division over your truth, until their rule lasts long, until they leave no sacred thing of Allah but they make it lawful, and no town dweller or desert dweller remains but their oppression enters upon him, and until one of you becomes a follower of them, and until one of you's support from them is like the slave's support from his master: when he is present he obeys him, and when he is absent he reviles him, and until the wealthiest of you in it is the one with the best opinion of Allah. If Allah brings you well-being, accept it; if you are tested, be patient, for the outcome belongs to the God-fearing.\""],[2747,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ and they mentioned his household. Ali ؓ said: \"As for al-Hasan, he will not avail you in war more than a sparrow's snare. As for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of shade and a table. As for Husayn, he is of you and you are of him.\""],[2748,"Muawiyah died in the month of Rajab, after four nights had passed. Yazid was appointed as his successor for two years. In the year 61, Husayn ibn Ali and his companions were killed, for ten nights, starting from the first day of Muharram, until the day of Ashura. Abbas ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib and his mother Umm al-Banin Amiriyya, Ja'far ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Uthman ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Abu Bakr ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, and his mother Layla bint Mas'ud Nahshalyya, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib (the eldest), and his mother Layla Thaqafiyya, Abdullah ibn al-Husayn and his mother Rabbab bint Imru' al-Qays Kalbiyya, Abu Bakr ibn al-Husayn, Qasim ibn al-Hasan, Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, Ja'far ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, Muslim ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, Sulaiman, a servant of Husayn, and Abdullah, the infant of Husayn, were all killed. Husayn himself was killed at the age of 58."],[2749,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed when he was fifty-eight years old."],[2750,"Indeed, with him were killed seventeen of those who had moved in the womb of Fatimah ؓ."],[2751,"He was to be taken captive, so they fought him and killed him, and killed his two sons and his companions who fought on his side at a place called al-Taff. Ali b. Husayn, Fatimah bt. Husayn, and Sukaynah bt. Husayn were taken to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad. Ali was that day a youth who had reached puberty. He sent them to Yazid b. Muawiyah. He ordered Sukaynah to be placed behind his bed so she would not see the head of her father and her relatives. Ali b. al-Husayn ؓ was in shackles. He placed his head and struck the front teeth of al-Husayn ؓ and said."],[2752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Husayn b. Ali ؓ will be killed at the head of sixty [years] from my emigration.”"],[2753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Husayn will be killed when grey hair overtakes him.” Abu al-Qasim said: al-qatir means white hair."],[2754,"“Ali ؓ was killed while he was fifty-eight years old, al-Husayn ؓ was killed while he was fifty-eight years old, and Ali b. al-Husayn died while he was fifty-eight years old.”"],[2755,"He traveled with Ali ؓ, and when he came parallel to Nineveh, he said: “Patience, Abu Abd Allah, patience by the bank of the Euphrates.” I said: “And what is that?” He said: “I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while his eyes were overflowing [with tears], so I said: ‘Has someone angered you, O Messenger of Allah? Why do I see your eyes overflowing?’ He said: ‘Jibril ﷺ had just left me and informed me that my ummah will kill al-Husayn, my son.’ Then he said: ‘Would you like me to show you some of his soil?’ I said: ‘Yes.’ So he stretched out his hand and grasped [some], and when I saw it, I could not control my eyes from overflowing.”"],[2756,"He said: “What is the name of this land?” It was said: “Karbala.” Then he said: “The Prophet ﷺ spoke the truth: ‘It is the land of distress and affliction.’”"],[2757,"The angel of rain sought permission from his Lord, exalted and glorified, to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and He granted him permission. So he came to him while he was in the house of Umm Salama. He said: “O Umm Salama, guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us.” While they were at the door, al-Husayn came and opened the door, and he began jumping on the Prophet’s ﷺ back while the Prophet ﷺ embraced him and kissed him. The angel said to him: “Do you love him, O Muhammad?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Indeed, your ummah will kill him, and if you wish, I can show you some of the soil of the place where he will be killed.” He said: “So he grasped a handful from the place where he will be killed and brought him red soil, and Umm Salama took it and placed it in her garment.” Thabit said: “We used to say that it is Karbala.”"],[2758,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while revelation was descending upon him, and he climbed onto the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was prostrate and played on his back. Jibril said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Do you love him, O Muhammad?” He said: “O Jibril, why would I not love my son?” He said: “Indeed, your ummah will kill him after you.” Then Jibril ﷺ stretched out his hand and brought him white soil and said: “In this land your son will be killed, O Muhammad, and its name is al-Taff.” When Jibril ﷺ left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with the soil in his hand, weeping, and said: “O A’isha, Jibril ﷺ informed me that al-Husayn, my son, will be killed in the land of al-Taff and that my ummah will be tested after me.” Then he went out to his companions, among them Ali, Abu Bakr, Umar, Hudhayfa, Ammar, and Abu Dharr ؓ, while he was weeping. They said: “What makes you weep, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Jibril informed me that my son al-Husayn will be killed after me in the land of al-Taff, and he brought me this soil and informed me that his resting place is in it.”"],[2759,"that al-Husayn b. Ali entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Aishah, shall I not tell you something astonishing? A moment ago an angel entered upon me who had never entered upon me before, and he said: This son of mine will be killed. He also said: If you wish, I will show you the soil in which he will be killed. The angel then reached out with his hand and showed me red soil.\""],[2760,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ were playing in front of the Prophet ﷺ in my house when Jibril ﷺ descended and said: “O Muhammad, your ummah will kill this son of yours after you,” and he gestured with his hand toward al-Husayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept and clasped him to his chest. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This soil is a trust with you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smelled it and said: “Woe, distress and affliction!” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Umm Salama, when this soil turns into blood, know that my son has been killed.” He said: Umm Salama placed it in a glass bottle, then she began to look at it every day and say: “The day you turn into blood will be a great day.”"],[2761,"She said: “They killed him – may Allah, exalted and glorified, kill them! They deceived and humiliated him – may Allah curse them!”"],[2762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day in my house and said: “Let no one enter upon me.” So I waited, and al-Husayn ؓ entered. I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping, so I looked and saw Husayn in his lap while the Prophet ﷺ was wiping his forehead and weeping. I said: “By Allah, I did not know when he entered.” He said: “Jibril ﷺ was with us in the house and said: ‘Do you love him?’ I said: ‘As for in this world, yes.’ He said: ‘Your ummah will kill this one in a land called Karbala.’ Then Jibril ﷺ took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet ﷺ. When Husayn was surrounded at the time he was killed, he said: ‘What is the name of this land?’ They said: ‘Karbala.’ He said: ‘Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: the land of distress and affliction.’”"],[2763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Sit by the door and no one should enter upon me.\" So I stood by the door when Al-Hussein came, and I went to fetch him, but the young boy went in before me and entered upon his grandfather. I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, may Allah sacrifice me for you, you ordered me that no one should enter upon you, and yet your son has come and I went to fetch him, but the young boy entered before me.\" When a long time passed, I looked out of the door and found you turning something in your hands and tears flowing, with the child on your chest. You said, \"Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my ummah will kill him, and he brought me the soil on which he will be killed. It is this soil that I am turning in my hands.\""],[2764,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down one day and woke up distressed, with red soil in his hand, turning it over. I said: “What is this soil, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Jibril ﷺ informed me that this one – meaning al-Husayn – will be killed in the land of Iraq. I said to Jibril ﷺ : ‘Show me the soil of the land in which he will be killed.’ So this is its soil.”"],[2765,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in what the sleeper sees at midday, disheveled, dusty, with a glass bottle in his hand containing blood. I said: “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is this?” He said: “The blood of al-Husayn and his companions. I have been collecting it since today.” That day was counted, and it was found that he had been killed on that day."],[2766,"I accompanied Ali ؓ until he reached Kufa. He ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled God, then said, “How will you be when the descendants of your Prophet settle among you?” They replied, “In that case, we shall strive for God’s sake concerning them in an excellent manner.” He said, “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they will surely settle among you, and you will surely go out against them and kill them.” Then he turned away saying,"],[2767,"“Al-Husayn will certainly be killed, and I know the very soil in which he will be slain, near the two rivers.”"],[2768,"I was with Ali ؓ at the two rivers of Karbala. He passed by a tree beneath which was gazelle dung. He took a handful of it, smelled it, then said, “From this ridge will be gathered seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[2769,"I was with Ali ؓ when he came to Karbala and said, “Martyrs will be killed in this place, whose like are no martyrs except the martyrs of Badr.” I said, “This is one of his lies,” while there was the leg of a dead donkey. I told my servant, “Take this donkey’s leg and peg it into his seat and conceal it.” Time passed, and when al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, I set out with some companions of mine, and there was the body of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ upon the leg of that donkey, with his companions lying slain around him."],[2770,"We used to hear that a son of a Prophet would be killed at Karbala. Whenever I entered it, I would spur my horse until I passed beyond it. But when al-Husayn was killed, after that I began to travel at my own pace.”"],[2771,"The passage translates to: \"Hajjaj said to him, 'Indeed, the two of you will never meet in one place.'\""],[2772,"that I might pass by the Prophet ﷺ and he would look at my face.”"],[2773,"I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi say: Do not revile Ali or the people of this house, for a neighbor of ours from Balhujaym said, “Do you not see this sinner al-Husayn b. Ali? May God kill him.” So God struck him with two stars in his eyes, and God obliterated his sight."],[2774,"\"To keep that a secret.\""],[2775,"When the head of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad and his companions were brought and placed in the open square, I came to them while they were saying, “It has come, it has come.” And behold, a snake came, weaving through the heads until it entered the nostril of Ubayd Allah. It stayed for a little while, then came out and went away. Then they said again, “It has come,” and it did that two or three times."],[2776,"It was as if men descended from heaven with spears, pursuing the killers of al-Husayn ؓ . It was not long before al-Mukhtar came down and killed them.”"],[2777,"“When al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, no stone was lifted in Jerusalem but that fresh blood was found beneath it.”"],[2778,"from blood ؓ ”"],[2779,"“Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed while I was then a young girl, and the sky remained for days like a clot of blood.”"],[2780,"\"When al-Husayn was killed, the sky turned red.\" I said, \"What is it you are saying?\" He replied, \"Indeed, the liar is a hypocrite. The sky turned red when he was killed.\""],[2781,"It is she."],[2782,"\"When al-Husayn ؓ was killed, we remained for seven days; when we prayed the afternoon prayer we looked at the sun on the edges of the walls as if it were dyed yellow sheets, and we looked at the stars striking one another.\""],[2783,"\"There was no redness in the sky until al-Husayn was killed.\""],[2784,"A man threw (something) at al-Husayn while he was drinking, and his jaw was paralyzed, so he said, \"May Allah not quench your thirst.\" He said, \"So he drank until it overflowed.\""],[2785,"\"What you see of the matter has indeed come down. The world has changed and become disfigured; its goodness has turned away and continued until nothing remains of it except like the dregs in a vessel, except a despicable livelihood like a barren pasture. Do you not see that truth is not acted upon and falsehood is not forbidden? Let the believer long for the meeting with Allah. Indeed, I see death as nothing but happiness and life with the wrongdoers as nothing but weariness.\" And al-Husayn ؓ was killed on the Day of Ashura in the year sixty-one at al-Taff in Karbala. He was wearing a dark green khazz cloak, dyed with black, and he was fifty-six years old."],[2786,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave allegiance to al-Hasan, al-Husayn, 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas, and 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far ؓ while they were young and had not reached puberty.\" He said, \"He did not accept the allegiance of any minor except from among us.\""],[2787,"\"Al-Husayn ؓ performed the pilgrimage twenty-five times on foot.\""],[2788,"\"The body of al-Husayn was similar to the body of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2789,"Husayn had indeed set out toward Kufa, and your time has been tested with him among all times, and your city among all cities, and you have been tested with him among all governors. At that point, he will either be freed or return to being a slave as slaves are enslaved. Then 'Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad killed him and sent his head to him. When it was placed before him, he recited the verse of al-Husayn b. al-Humam."],[2790,"The Prophet ﷺ came out of 'A'ishah's house ؓ and passed by Fatimah's house, and he heard Husayn crying ؓ, so he said, \"Do you not know that his crying hurts me?\""],[2791,"When the family of al-Husayn b. 'Ali ؓ was brought before Yazid b. Mu'awiyah and his head was placed before him, Yazid wept and said..."],[2792,"“O Allah, drive him into the Fire.” The mount bolted with him, and his foot caught in the stirrup. He said: By Allah, nothing of him remained on it except his foot."],[2793,"“No; that is the garment of one upon whom humiliation has been struck.” So he took a garment and tore it and put it beneath his clothes. Then when he was killed, they stripped him."],[2794,"Ali ؓ passed by Ka'b and said, “A man from the children of this man will be killed among a band whose horses’ sweat will not dry before they arrive at Muhammad ﷺ.” Then Hasan ؓ passed by, and they said, “This one, O Abu Ishaq?” He said, “No.” Then Husayn passed by, and they said, “This one?” He said, “Yes.”"],[2795,"Sinan b. Anas."],[2796,"Zaynab the Younger, daughter of Aqil b. Abi Talib, went out to the people at al-Baqi' weeping for her slain at al-Taff, and she said, “"],[2797,"Sufyan: “And who doubts this?”"],[2798,"When we mentioned Husayn and those who were killed with him ؓ, Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya said, “Seventeen youths were killed with him, all of whom had stirred in the womb of Fatima ؓ.”"],[2799,"I said, “No stone was lifted at the Holy House except that fresh blood was found beneath it.” Abd al-Malik said, “You and I are paired in this hadith.”"],[2800,"“As for one of them, his penis grew long until he would wrap it around, and as for the other, he would face the waterskin with his mouth until he came to its end.” Sufyan said, “I saw the child of one of them as if he had a defect and as if he was mad.”"],[2801,"“I saw the wars (dye) that was taken from Husayn’s camp become like ashes.”"],[2802,"“That this should disparage me or you, I would have clasped my hand in your head.” He said: But what he replied to me was: “That I should be killed at such-and-such a place is dearer to me than that the sanctity of Allah and His Messenger should be violated through me.” He said: That is what consoled me about him."],[2803,"“And the people of that house were afflicted with defect, madness, leprosy, illness, and poverty.”"],[2804,"Amr b. Bukayr b. Bakkar al-Qanabi narrated to us, Mujashi b. Amr narrated to us, both said: Abdullah b. Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil: Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As narrated to me that Muadh b. Jabal informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a changed complexion and said: \"I am Muhammad. I was given the openings of speech and its closings, so obey me as long as I am among you. When I am taken away, then hold fast to the Book of Allah, glorified and exalted be He. Make lawful its lawful, and forbid its forbidden. It has come to you with the spirit and the ease, a Book from Allah that has preceded. Tribulations will come to you like patches of the dark night. Whenever messengers go, messengers come. Prophethood was succeeded and became kingship. May Allah have mercy on one who takes it by its right and leaves it as he entered it. Hold back, O Muadh, and count.\" He said: When I reached five, he said: \"Yazid. Allah will not bless Yazid.\" Then the eyes of the Prophet ﷺ shed tears, then he said: \"Husayn was announced to me as killed, and I was brought his soil, and I was informed of his killer. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, he is not killed among a people who do not defend him except that Allah will cause discord between their chests and hearts, give their wicked ones power over them, and clothe them in sects.\" Then he said: \"Alas for the offspring of the family of Muhammad ﷺ from a successor appointed, a luxurious one who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold back, O Muadh.\" When I reached ten, he said: \"Al-Walid is the name of a Pharaoh, a destroyer of the laws of Islam. Before him is a man from a household; Allah will draw his sword and there will be no sheath for it. The people differed and were thus,\" and he interlaced his fingers, then said: \"After one hundred and twenty, there will be swift death and rapid killing. In that will be their destruction. Woe to them from a man of the descendants of al-Abbas.\""],[2805,"\"I heard the jinn mourning over Husayn ibn Ali.\""],[2806,"I was in Khuza'ah when they brought something from the inheritance of al-Husayn. It was said to them: 'Shall we slaughter or sell and divide?' He said: 'Slaughter.' He said: 'He sat on a large bowl, and when it was placed, it boiled with fire.'"],[2807,"When al-Husayn ؓ was killed, a camel from his army was plundered. When it was cooked, it was blood, so they overturned it."],[2808,"Crying of the jinn over al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ was heard."],[2809,"The plasterers narrated to me: They said: 'When we went out at night to the cemetery at the place where al-Husayn ؓ was killed, we heard the jinn wailing over him and saying.'"],[2810,"I heard the jinn wailing over al-Husayn ؓ."],[2811,"I heard the jinn wailing over al-Husayn."],[2812,"I have heard the wailing of the jinn since the Prophet ﷺ passed away, except tonight. I do not think my son except that he has been killed, meaning al-Husayn ؓ. She said to her slave girl: 'Go out and ask.' She was informed that he had been killed, and there was a female jinn wailing."],[2813,"The first humiliation that entered upon the Arabs was the killing of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ and the claim of Ziyad."],[2814,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed while he had a large debt, so Ali b. Husayn sold such-and-such a spring and such-and-such a spring for it."],[2815,"Al-Husayn ordered a caller, and he called out: 'Let no man with a debt accompany us.' A man said: 'My wife guaranteed my debt.' Husayn ؓ said: 'And what is the guarantee of a woman?'"],[2816,"When al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, they cut off his head and sat at the first halt drinking nabidh, greeting each other with the head. Then a pen of iron came out from a wall and wrote in a line of blood."],[2817,"From some of his elders who raided the Romans and stopped in one of their churches, and they read on a stone something written."],[2818,"And he said this poetry to Zaynab bt. Aqil b. Abi Talib."],[2819,"\"The head of al-Husayn ؓ was the first head carried in Islam.\""],[2820,"\"I entered upon Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad and there was the head of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ before him on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon al-Mukhtar, and there was the head of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr, and there was the head of al-Mukhtar on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, and there was the head of Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr on a shield.\""],[2821,"When the head of al-Husayn b. Ali was brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, he began poking it with a stick in his hand and saying, \"Indeed he had beautiful teeth.\" I said, \"By Allah, I will displease you: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing the place where your stick is, from his mouth.\""],[2822,"I was with Ibn Ziyad when the head of al-Husayn was brought, and he began saying, poking with a stick in his nose, \"I have not seen anything as beautiful as this.\" I said, \"Indeed, he was among the most similar of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2823,"\"Whoever loves us for the sake of this world, then the lover of this world is loved by both the righteous and the wicked. Whoever loves us for the sake of Allah, we and he will be on the Day of Resurrection like these two,\" and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."],[2824,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ has three sanctities. Whoever preserves them, Allah will preserve for him the affairs of his religion and his world; and whoever does not preserve them, Allah will not preserve anything for him: the sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kinship.\""],[2825,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"I have been given al-Kawthar.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Kawthar?\" He said, \"A river in Paradise whose width and length are between the east and the west. No one drinks from it and remains thirsty, and no one performs ablution from it and becomes disheveled. No person who violates my protection or kills the people of my household will drink from it.\""],[2826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Six I have cursed, and every prophet is answered: the one who adds to the Book of Allah ﷻ, the one who denies the decree of Allah, the one who makes lawful what Allah has forbidden, the one who makes lawful from my kindred what Allah has made forbidden, and the one who abandons the Sunnah.\""],[2827,"About the blood of a mosquito, while they have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"They are my two fragrant flowers in this world.\""],[2828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The miser is he before whom I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me.\""],[2829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Part of the excellence of a person’s Islam is his leaving alone what does not concern him.”"],[2830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he errs in sending blessings upon me has missed the path of Paradise.”"],[2831,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Observing Iʿtikāf (seclusion for worship) for ten days in Ramadan is like performing two Hajj pilgrimages and two Umrah pilgrimages.\""],[2832,"Love us with the love of Islam, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not raise me above my due, for Allah, Exalted is He, took me as a servant before He took me as a messenger.”"],[2833,"I heard my father say: Three days before the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Gabriel ﷺ descended upon him and said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you as an honor for you, a distinction for you, and specifically for you, to ask you what He knows better than you. He says: How do you find yourself? The Prophet ﷺ said: “I find myself, O Gabriel, distressed, and I find myself, O Gabriel, grieved.” He said: Then on the third day, Gabriel ﷺ descended, and the Angel of Death (peace be upon them) descended, and with them descended an angel in the air called Isma'il, over seventy thousand angels, and there was not an angel among them except that he was over seventy thousand angels, with Gabriel ﷺ accompanying them. Then he said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you as an honor for you, a distinction for you, and specifically for you, to ask you what He knows better than you. He says: How do you find yourself? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I find myself, O Gabriel, distressed, and I find myself, O Gabriel, grieved.” He said: Then the Angel of Death ﷺ asked permission at the door. Gabriel ﷺ said: O Muhammad, this is the Angel of Death asking permission to enter upon you. He has never asked permission from any human before you, nor will he ask permission from any human after you. He said: Give him permission. So Gabriel ﷺ gave him permission, and he came forward until he stood before him. He said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you and commanded me to obey you in whatever you command me. If you command me to take your soul, I will take it, and if you dislike it, I will leave it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Will you do so, O Angel of Death?” He said: Yes, and with that I have been commanded, to obey you in whatever you command me. Then Gabriel ﷺ said to him: Allah, Majestic is He, has longed to meet you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Proceed with what you have been commanded.” Gabriel said to him: This is the last time I will set foot on the earth; my need was only in this world. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and condolences came, someone came whose voice they heard but whose person they did not see. He said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Every soul will taste death. In Allah there is consolation for every affliction, a replacement for every loss, and a compensation for everything missed. So in Allah put your trust, and on Him place your hope, for the truly afflicted is the one deprived of reward. And peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."],[2834,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his death gave three instructions: he instructed that the army of Usama be sent out, and that no one but the people of his religion should live with him in Madinah.” Muhammad said: And I forgot the third."],[2835,"Come to lunch. I said: I have already had lunch, O son of the Messenger of Allah. He said to me: It is endive. I said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, what is in endive? He said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no leaf among the leaves of endive except that upon it is a drop from the water of Paradise.”"],[2836,"Come to lunch. I said: I have already had lunch, O son of the Messenger of Allah. He said to me: It is endive. I said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, what is in endive? He said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no leaf among the leaves of endive except that upon it is a drop from the water of Paradise.”"],[2837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The beggar has a right, even if he comes on a horse.”"],[2838,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Khalid b. Ilyas narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Uthman, from Fatima bt. al-Husayn, from Husayn b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah loves noble matters and their heights, and He dislikes their lowly ones.”"],[2839,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever is afflicted by a calamity and says when he remembers it: “Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return,” Allah will renew for him the reward of it, the like of what it was on the day it afflicted him."],[2840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not disturb birds in their nests, for the night is a protection for them.”"],[2841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prolong looking at lepers.”"],[2842,"I heard al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever wears a garment of fame (to stand out), Allah will turn away from him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2843,"That the Prophet ﷺ hid the word 'smoke' (dukhan) for Ibn Sayyad and asked him what he had hidden for him. He said: 'Dukh.' He said, 'Be gone! You will never exceed your station.' When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'What did he say?' Some of them said, 'Dukh,' and others said, 'Rather he said, Zukh.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You have differed while I am still among you, so you will differ even more after me.'"],[2844,"A woman from the wives of al-Husayn prepared food in some of his land, and he ate. Then the food was cleared away, and a client (mawla) of his came, and he called for the food. He said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, I do not want it. He said: Why? He said: We ate a short while ago at the house of 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abbas. Al-Husayn said: Indeed, his father was the leader of Quraysh. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, feed the food and speak kindly.'"],[2845,"It is the Sunnah. He says: The gray hair—I have not outlived it?” And Sa'id was governor of Madinah at that time."],[2846,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ put Sa'id b. al-'As forward for the funeral prayer of al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ."],[2847,"'Abd al-Muttalib married Halah bt. Uhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah."],[2848,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib."],[2849,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf."],[2850,"'Abd al-Muttalib: I went out to Yemen on one of the two journeys of ilaf, and I stayed with a man from the Jews. A man from the people of the monasteries saw me and asked about my lineage, so I traced my lineage for him. He said, 'Do you permit me to look at some part of you?' I said, 'Yes, as long as it is not private.' He opened one of my nostrils and looked, then looked in the other, and said, 'I bear witness that in one of your hands is kingship and in the other prophethood, and we find that in the Banu Zuhrah. How is that?' I said, 'I do not know.' He said, 'Do you have a sha'ah?' I said, 'What is a sha'ah?' He said, 'A wife.' I said, 'Not today.' He said, 'When you return, marry among the Banu Zuhrah.' 'Abd al-Muttalib returned and married Halah bt. Wuhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah. He married his son 'Abd Allah to Aminah bt. Wahb. The Quraysh said, 'Abd al-Muttalib has outdone his son.' She bore him the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So Hamzah ؓ was the brother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through suckling—Thuwaybah, the freedwoman of Abu Lahab, suckled both of them—and he was older than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2851,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'Shall I point out to you the most beautiful young woman of Quraysh?' He said, 'Who is she?' He said, 'The daughter of Hamzah.' He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2852,"Ali ؓ said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like the daughter of your paternal uncle, the most beautiful young woman in Quraysh? He said, 'Do you not know that Hamzah is my brother through suckling?'"],[2853,"I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he might marry her. He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2854,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you seeking wives among Quraysh and leaving us aside?' He said, 'Do you have someone?' I said, 'Yes, the daughter of Hamzah.' He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2855,"The Prophet ﷺ was offered the daughter of Hamzah, and he said, 'She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and whatever is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling.'"],[2856,"The Prophet ﷺ was offered the daughter of Hamzah, and he said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and Allah ﷻ forbids through suckling what He forbids through lineage.'"],[2857,"I heard Umm Salamah say: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the daughter of Hamzah?' Or it was said, 'Will you not propose to the daughter of Hamzah?' He said, \"Hamzah is my brother through suckling.\""],[2858,"Yes, by Allah, people saw him. He came forward until he reached that gathering at al-Safa and al-Marwah, and there they were sitting with Abu Jahl among them. He leaned on his bow and said, \"I have shot such and such and done such and such.\" Then he gathered his hand with the bow and struck with it between the ears of Abu Jahl, breaking its end. Then he said, \"Take this from the bow, and another from the sword. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and that he has come with the truth from Allah.\" They said, \"O Abu 'Umarah, he has insulted our gods. If it had been you, and you are better than him, we would not have accepted this from you. And you, O Abu 'Umarah, are not one who speaks obscenely.\""],[2859,"Abu Jahl confronted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Safa and harmed him. Hamzah ؓ was a hunter and a man of game, and that day he was out hunting. When he returned, his wife, who had seen what Abu Jahl had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said to him, \"O Abu 'Umarah, if only you had seen what Abu Jahl did to your nephew.\" Hamzah became angry and went off just as he was, before entering his house, with his bow hanging from his neck, until he entered the mosque and found Abu Jahl in one of the gatherings of Quraysh. He did not speak to him until he struck his head with his bow and wounded him. Some men of Quraysh stood up to Hamzah to restrain him from Abu Jahl. Hamzah said, \"My religion is the religion of Muhammad. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I will not turn away from that, so prevent me from it if you are truthful.\" When Hamzah accepted Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims were strengthened by him, and some of their affairs became established. Quraysh feared him, and they knew that Hamzah ؓ would protect him."],[2860,"Abu Jahl confronted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Safa and harmed him. Hamzah ؓ was a hunter and a man of game, and that day he was out hunting. When he returned, his wife, who had seen what Abu Jahl had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said to him, \"O Abu 'Umarah, if only you had seen what Abu Jahl did to your nephew.\" Hamzah became angry and went off just as he was, before entering his house, with his bow hanging from his neck, until he entered the mosque and found Abu Jahl in one of the gatherings of Quraysh. He did not speak to him until he struck his head with his bow and wounded him. Some men of Quraysh stood up to Hamzah to restrain him from Abu Jahl. Hamzah said, \"My religion is the religion of Muhammad. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I will not turn away from that, so prevent me from it if you are truthful.\" When Hamzah accepted Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims were strengthened by him, and some of their affairs became established. Quraysh feared him, and they knew that Hamzah ؓ would protect him."],[2861,"\"O Messenger of Allah, you established brotherhood between me and Hamzah.\""],[2862,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and Zayd b. Harithah, and Hamzah ؓ was martyred on the day of Uhud.\""],[2863,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on Friday after praying the Friday prayer, and by morning he was at the mountain pass of Uhud. They met on Saturday in the middle of Shawwal in the year three.\""],[2864,"\"Uhud was in Shawwal in the year three.\""],[2865,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the emigrants: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib."],[2866,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stripped Hamzah, he wept, and when he saw his mutilated form, he sobbed.\""],[2867,"\"Hamzah was struck down on the day of Uhud.\""],[2868,"\"Hamzah was struck down on the day of Uhud.\""],[2869,"When Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, Safiyyah came looking for him, not knowing what had happened to him. She met Ali and al-Zubayr. Ali said to al-Zubayr, \"Mention it to your mother,\" and al-Zubayr said to Ali, \"You mention it to your paternal aunt.\" She said, \"What has happened to Hamzah?\" They indicated to her that they did not know. Then the Prophet ﷺ came and said, \"I fear for her mind.\" He placed his hand on her chest and supplicated for her. She sought Allah's reward and wept. Then he came and stood over him, and he had been mutilated. He said, \"Were it not for the grief of women, I would have left him until he is gathered from the crops of birds and bellies of beasts.\" Then he ordered the slain, and he began praying over them. He would place nine and Hamzah, and pronounce seven takbirs over them. Then they would be lifted and Hamzah left. Then he would bring nine and pronounce seven takbirs over them, until he finished with them."],[2870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray over the martyrs of Uhud, nine with Hamzah as their tenth, until he finished with them."],[2871,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ looked at Hamzah, who had been killed and mutilated, and saw a sight more painful and more frightening to his heart than any he had ever seen. He said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, for you were one who maintained ties of kinship and did much good. Were it not for the grief of those after you, it would please me to leave you until you come forth from various groups.\" Then, while standing in his place, he swore, \"By Allah, I will mutilate seventy of them in your place.\" Then the Qur'an was revealed while he was still standing in his place, not having moved: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you are patient, it is better for the patient} until the surah was completed. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ atoned for his oath and refrained from what he had intended."],[2872,"On the day of Uhud, sixty-four of the Ansar were killed and six of the Muhajirun, among them Hamzah ؓ. They mutilated their dead. The Ansar said, \"If we ever defeat them one day, we will surpass them.\" When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, a man whose identity is unknown called out, \"No Quraysh after today.\" Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you are patient, it is better for the patient.} The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Refrain from the people.\""],[2873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Hamzah after Uhud, and he had been mutilated. He said, \"Were it not that Safiyyah would feel distress, I would have left him until scavengers ate him, until he is gathered from their bellies.\" Then he called for a striped cloak. When it was extended over his head, his feet showed; and when it was extended over his feet, his head showed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Extend it over his head.\" The cloth was scarce and the slain were many. One, two, or three men would be shrouded in a single cloth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask which of them knew more Qur'an and would place him toward the qiblah. So they buried them, and he did not pray over them."],[2874,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated that Muhammad bin Salih Al-Tammar narrated from Yazid bin Zaid, from Abu Usaid Al-Sa'idi, who said: \"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the grave of Hamza bin Abd al-Muttalib. They began dragging thorns on his face, causing his feet to be exposed. Then they dragged them on his feet, causing his face to be exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Place it on his face and place it on his feet with this tree.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head and saw his companions crying. He said, 'Indeed, a time will come upon people when they will go out to the outskirts and the cities will be better for them if they knew. No one will endure its hardships and difficulties except that I will be his intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[2875,"I saw Hamzah, and we found no cloth to shroud him in except a burdah. When we covered his feet with it, his head was exposed; and when we covered his head with it, his feet were exposed. So we covered his head and placed idhkhir (a fragrant grass) over his feet."],[2876,"Hamzah had a striped cloak. When his head was covered with it, his feet showed; and when his feet were covered, his head showed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that his head be covered, and a tree branch and stones were placed over his feet."],[2877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shrouded Hamzah in a single cloth. Jabir said, \"That cloth was a striped cloak.\""],[2878,"The Prophet ﷺ returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their dead. He said, \"But Hamzah has no weepers.\" So the women of the Ansar came and wept over Hamzah in his presence. He woke up while they were weeping and said, \"Woe to them! They are still here until now. Tell them to go back and not weep over any dead after today.\""],[2879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Last night I entered Paradise and looked around, and there was Hamzah reclining on a couch.\""],[2880,"When Hamzah and his companions were struck down on the day of Uhud, they said, \"Would that those behind us knew what reward Allah has given us, so that it would be a reward for them.\" Allah, exalted is He, said, \"I will inform them.\" So Allah, blessed and exalted is He, revealed: {And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead} – the verse."],[2881,"About his killing of Hamzah, may Allah have mercy on him, how did he kill him? We went toward him, and a man met us as we were asking about him. He said, \"He is a man overcome by this wine. If you find him sober, you will find an Arab man who will tell you whatever you want of his story; but if you find him otherwise, leave him.\" So we came to him and found him in his courtyard. He looked at Ubaydullah b. Adi and said, \"Son of Adi b. al-Khiyar?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I have not seen you since your mother al-Sa'diyyah handed you to me in your swaddling. It was only when your feet glimmered that I recognized you.\" He said, \"I said to him, 'We have come to you to tell us about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him.'\" He said, \"I was a slave of Jubayr b. Mut'im. His uncle Tu'aymah b. Adi was killed on the day of Badr. He said, 'If you kill Muhammad's uncle in return for my uncle, you are free.' So I went out on the day of Uhud among the people with my spear. My only concern was to be freed. I made Hamzah my target. I headed for him, but Sabba' b. Abd al-Uzza got ahead of me toward him.\" He said, \"I withdrew from him while he was cutting down people with his sword like a dark gray camel. When Sabba' got ahead of me toward him, Hamzah said, 'Come here, O son of the cutter of clitorises.'\" He said, \"He approached him and struck him, but it was as if he missed him. I hid behind something and shook my spear until I was satisfied with it, then I thrust it and it struck his groin.\" He said, \"He tried to rise but was overcome. I withdrew and returned to the people, then to Makkah, and I was freed. When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, I went out to al-Ta'if and stayed there. When the people of al-Ta'if agreed to make peace with the Prophet ﷺ, the paths became unclear to me. I began thinking about where to go. While I was in my worry, a man met me and said, 'Why do I see you like this?' I said, 'This man – I have done to his uncle what I did, and I see these people have agreed to make peace with him, so I do not know where to go.' He said, 'By Allah, he does not kill anyone who comes to him and bears witness to his testimony.' So I went out as I was. By Allah, I was not aware until I stood before his head in Madinah. He raised his head and looked at me and said, 'Wahshi?' I said, 'Wahshi,' and I bore witness to his testimony. He said, 'Woe to you, tell me about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him.' So I told him, by Allah, just as I have told you two. He said, 'Woe to you, hide your face from me.' So I avoided him until Allah, exalted is He, took him. When Abu Bakr ؓ sent the army to al-Yamamah, I went out with the people. I made Musaylimah my target. I charged at him along with a man from the Ansar, and with me was my spear with which I had killed Hamzah. He said, 'I hurled the spear at him, and the Ansari charged at him. Your Lord knows best which of us killed him. If I killed him, then I have killed the best of people and the worst of people.'"],[2882,"And there were killed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud among the Muslims, then from Banu Hashim, Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. Wahshi, the freed slave of 'Utbah b. Ghazwan, killed him."],[2883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in a dream the kind of thing a sleeping person sees. He said: \"I saw as if I was riding behind a ram, and as if the blade of my sword broke. I interpreted it that I would kill the ram of the people, and I interpreted the blade of my sword as the killing of a man from my kin.\" Then Hamzah was killed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed Talhah, who was the standard-bearer."],[2884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is written with Allah in the seventh heaven: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger.\""],[2885,"Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib used to fight in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with two swords, saying: \"I am the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger.\""],[2886,"I heard Abu Dharr say: I swear by Allah, this verse was revealed: {These are two adversaries who disputed concerning their Lord} about these six: Hamzah, 'Ubaydah, 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and 'Utbah, Shaybah the two sons of Rabi'ah, and al-Walid b. 'Utbah. They had challenged each other to single combat on the day of Badr."],[2887,"That did not escape the notice of the Prophet ﷺ."],[2888,"Mu'awiyah said to him: \"O Hawdhah, did you witness Badr?\" He said: \"Yes, O Commander of the Faithful, against me, not for me.\" He said: \"How old were you then?\" He said: \"On that day I was a sturdy, compact youth, like a solid boulder. It is as if I am looking at them when they lined up against us in a long row, and it is as if I am looking at the gleam of their swords like the rays of the sun through the gaps in the clouds. I did not regain my senses until the vanguard of the people overwhelmed us, at their head 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, a mighty lion, striking ferociously, saying: 'You will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah; you will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah.' Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib followed him, with a white feather on his chest by which he was marked, as if he were a camel trampling dry grass. I was terrified of the two of them, and the two of them turned upon Hanzalah,\" meaning Mu'awiyah's brother. Mu'awiyah ؓ said: \"Away from you, and no ingratitude to Allah. You have gone on. I wish I knew when you rested, O Hawdhah.\" He said: \"By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not rest until I looked at the hills of Arthad and said: I wish I knew what happened to Hanzalah.\" Mu'awiyah said: \"By your mentioning Hanzalah, you are like the rich man remembering his poor brother, for he hardly mentions him except drowsy or half-asleep.\""],[2889,"That is the one who did to us what he did."],[2890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib one day and did not find him, so he asked his wife 'Inabah, who was from Banu al-Najjar. She said: He went out just now, may my father be your ransom, heading toward you. I think he missed you in one of the alleys of Banu al-Najjar. Will you not enter, O Messenger of Allah? So he entered, and she served him some hais, and he ate from it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, may it be wholesome and pleasant for you. You have come while I intended to come to you to congratulate you and wish you well. Abu 'Umarah told me that you were given a river in Paradise called al-Kawthar. He said: \"Yes, and its expanse is of ruby, coral, chrysolite, and pearl.\" She said: I would love for you to describe your pool to me with a description I can hear from you. He said: \"It is the distance between Aylah and San'a'. In it are pitchers like the number of the stars, and the dearest of those who come to it to me are your people, O daughter of Qahd,\" meaning the Ansar."],[2891,"The Prophet ﷺ would bring near two horned rams and slaughter one of them, saying, 'O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' And he brought the other near and said, 'O Allah, this is on behalf of my Ummah, for whoever bears witness to You of Your Oneness and bears witness to me of conveying the message.'"],[2892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten things before the Hour: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Hijaz of the Arabs, Ya'juj and Ma'juj, a wind that will sweep them and cast them into the sea, the rising of the sun from its west, the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, and the descent of 'Isa son of Maryam.'"],[2893,"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah died in the year thirty. His kunyah was Abu Muhammad. His age was sixty-five. Ibn 'Affan prayed over him in Madinah."],[2894,"I went out to Yemen and bought a hulla of Dhu Yazan, then I gifted it to the Prophet ﷺ during the truce that was between him and Quraysh. He said, 'I do not accept the gift of a polytheist,' and returned it. So I sold it, and he bought it and wore it. Then he came out to his companions wearing it, and I never saw anything on anyone more beautiful than it on him ﷺ. I could not help saying—"],[2895,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ and pressed him, so he said, 'How strange is your request, O Hakim! Indeed this wealth is lush and sweet, and it is, along with that, only the filth of people's hands. Indeed Allah's hand is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the recipient, and the lowest of hands is the hand of the recipient.'"],[2896,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated. If they are truthful and clear, they are blessed, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out.\""],[2897,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best charity is that given from sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.\""],[2898,"A vessel containing milk was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. On his right was a man from the desert dwellers and on his left a man from his companions who was older than him. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his need of drinking, he said, \"O young man, this is for you. Will you permit me to give it to him?\" He said, \"It is for me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I will never give my share of your leftover to anyone.\" The Prophet ﷺ handed it to him and he drank."],[2899,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was among his companions, he said to them, \"Do you hear what I hear?\" They said, \"We do not hear anything.\" He said, \"I hear the creaking of the sky, and it is not blamed for creaking. There is not a handspan in it except that upon it is an angel prostrating or standing.\""],[2900,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting. He said, \"Fast three days of every month.\" I said, \"I am able to do more,\" until he debated with me. Then he said, \"Fast three days of the month.\" I said, \"I am able to do more,\" until he debated with me. Then he said, \"Fast the fast of David: fast one day and break the fast one day.\""],[2901,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him, and he said: \"Whoever asks people and is given will be like one who eats but what he eats does not benefit him. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is what is given from surplus wealth. Begin with those whom you support.\" Hakim said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, by the One who honored you, I will never take anything from anyone ever again.\""],[2902,"Muhammad ﷺ was the most beloved man to me among the people in the pre-Islamic era. When he was made a prophet ﷺ and went out to Madinah, Hakim attended the fair while he was a disbeliever and found a suit belonging to Dhu Yazan being sold. He bought it to give as a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He brought it to him in Madinah and wanted him to accept it as a gift, but he refused, saying: \"We do not accept anything from the polytheists. However, if you wish, I will take it from you for its price.\" So I gave it to him when he refused the gift, and he wore it. I saw him wearing it on the pulpit, and I never saw anything more beautiful than him on that day. Then he gave it to Usama b. Zayd. Hakim saw it on Usama and said: \"O Usama, are you wearing the suit of Dhu Yazan?\" He said: \"Yes, by God, I am better than Dhu Yazan and my father is better than his father.\" Hakim said: \"So I went to the people of Makkah to amaze them with Usama's statement.\""],[2903,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered and took a handful of pebbles, faced us with it, threw it at us, and said: \"May the faces be ugly!\" So we were defeated, and God ﷻ revealed: {You did not throw when you threw, but God threw}."],[2904,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Which charity is best?\" He said: \"Begin with those whom you support, and charity is given from surplus wealth.\""],[2905,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that retaliation be carried out in mosques, that poems be recited in them, or that legal punishments be carried out in them.\""],[2906,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Legal punishments are not carried out in mosques, nor is retaliation carried out in them.\""],[2907,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him to buy a sacrificial animal for him for a dinar. He bought it, then sold it for two dinars. He bought a sheep for a dinar and brought back a dinar. \"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for blessing for him and ordered him to give the dinar as charity.\""],[2908,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no bad omen, and good fortune may be in the house and the woman.”"],[2909,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys.\" He said, 'Al-Hakam b. Amr al-Ghifari used to say among us, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the sea refused that' — meaning Ibn Abbas ؓ — and he recited: {Say, I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden} to the end of the verse."],[2910,"When the Prophet ﷺ died and Abu Bakr was made caliph, it was said to him about al-Hakam b. Abi al-As. He said, 'I would not loosen a knot that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied.'"],[2911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever takes a handspan of the Muslims' path, he will come carrying it from seven earths.'"],[2912,"Al-Hajjaj b. ‘Ilat gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ his sword Dhu al-Fiqar, and Dihya al-Kalbi gifted him his gray mule."],[2913,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banu Sahm: Hajjaj b. al-Harith."],[2914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The master of the martyrs is Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib.\""],[2915,"A recent hadith narrated from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Recite this supplication: O Allah, I ask You by Your Greatest Name and Your Greatest Pleasure.\" Salma repeated it multiple times, as it is one of the names of Allah the Almighty. I have always heard that Jadd bin Amir had a rock that would rise up without sinking into the water. He was the son of Malik, the son of Fatimah, the daughter of Abi Marthad, from the Kinana tribe descended from Husayn bin Nafar bin Yarbu'."],[2916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him the kunyah Abu Salih."],[2917,"He said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: I am a man who fasts continuously. Should I fast while traveling? He said: \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break your fast.\""],[2918,"That he said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"I am a man who fasts; should I fast while traveling?\" He said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2919,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Hisham b. 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah ؓ that Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"Should I fast while traveling?\" He was a man who fasted a great deal. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2920,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2921,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2922,"\"Hamzah asked the Messenger of Allah: 'O Messenger of Allah, should I fast while then fast and if you wish then do not fast.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2307)"],[2923,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"I am a man who travels, so should I fast while traveling?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2924,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Hisham b. 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah that Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"I am a man who fasts; should I fast while traveling?\" He said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2925,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of God, I am a man who fasts continuously; should I fast while traveling?\" He said, \"Fast if you wish, and break the fast if you wish.\""],[2926,"That Hamzah al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2927,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2928,"\"O Messenger of God, I have strength while traveling; should I fast?\" He said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2929,"\"O Messenger of God, I fast continuously and do not break the fast; should I fast while traveling?\" He said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2930,"That Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break the fast.\""],[2931,"O Messenger of God, I used to fast continuously, so should I fast while traveling? He said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2932,"Hamzah b. ʿAmr al-Aslamī asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2933,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2934,"I said, \"O Messenger, I am able to fast.\" He said, \"If you are able, then that is up to you.\""],[2935,"Hamzah b. ʿAmr al-Aslamī asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"Fast if you wish, and break the fast if you wish.\""],[2936,"He said, \"O Messenger of God, I have strength to fast while traveling; is there any sin upon me?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"It is a concession from God, may He be exalted. Whoever takes it, it is good; and whoever loves to fast, there is no sin upon him.\""],[2937,"Hamzah b. ʿAmr al-Aslamī asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2938,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"You have the choice: if you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2939,"Hamzah al-Aslamī asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, you may fast; and if you wish, you may break the fast.\""],[2940,"\"O Messenger of God, I find strength to fast while traveling.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2941,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, \"If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.\""],[2942,"He saw a man at Mina going around on his camel, a dark brown one, saying, \"Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking,\" while the Messenger of God ﷺ was among them."],[2943,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about fasting while traveling, and he said, “Whichever is easier for you, do it.”"],[2944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Aslamis, “Throw, O Banu Isma'il, for your forefather was an archer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ added, “I am with Mihjan b. al-Adra'.” So the people stopped. He said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “Whoever you are with has won.” He said, “Then throw, and I am with all of you.”"],[2945,"From 'Abdullah 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi; and Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Qattan al-Misri narrated to us; Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us; they said: al-Mughirah b. 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad that Muhammad b. Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami informed him that his father informed him that the Prophet ﷺ appointed him over a raiding party. He said: I went out with it, and he said, “If you seize so-and-so, burn him with fire.” When I turned away, he called me back and said, “If you seize him, kill him, for no one punishes with fire except the Lord of the Fire.” The wording is from the hadith of Sa'id b. Mansur."],[2946,"“We set out at night while we were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a dark, slippery night, and my fingers lit up so that they gathered their mounts upon it and nothing of their baggage fell, and indeed my fingers were shining.”"],[2947,"The food of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to rotate among his companions: one night for this one and one night for that one. He said: It was my turn one night, so I prepared food for the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I left the skin of ghee without tying it and I went with the food to him. It moved and its contents spilled. I said: Was the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spilled because of my hand? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring it here.” I said: I cannot, O Messenger of Allah. So I returned to my place, and there was the skin saying, “Qab, qab.” I said: Enough, a little leftover that remained in it has been spilled. I came to look into it and found it filled up to its two udders, so I pulled it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, “Indeed, if you had left it, it would have been filled up to its mouth, then tied.”"],[2948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on the expedition of Tabuk, and I was in charge of serving him on that journey. I noticed that the ghee skin had little left in it, and I prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ. I placed the skin in the sun and slept, then woke up to the gurgling of the skin. I got up and grabbed its mouth with my hand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me and said, “If you had left it, it would have flowed into a valley of ghee.”"],[2949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “On the back of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride them, mention the name of Allah, and do not neglect your needs.”"],[2950,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who owns riding camels; I work them, travel on them, and hire them out. Sometimes this month, meaning Ramadan, comes upon me while I find strength, and I am a young man. I find that fasting, O Messenger of Allah, is easier for me than postponing it so it becomes a debt upon me. Should I fast, O Messenger of Allah, for a greater reward, or break my fast? He said, “Whichever you wish, O Hamzah.”"],[2951,"Hamzah b. 'Amr al-Aslami, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him with a group of men on a raiding party against a man from his enemy. He said, “If you are able to overpower so-and-so, burn him with fire.” They set out until they were out of his sight, then he called them back and sent someone after them, so they returned. Then he said, “If you overpower him, kill him and do not burn him with fire, for no one punishes with fire except the Lord of the Fire.”"],[2952,"“We used to fast and break our fast, and the one breaking his fast did not criticize the one fasting, nor did the one fasting criticize the one breaking his fast.”"],[2953,"I ate food with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Eat with your right hand, eat from what is near you, and mention the name of Allah.” Al-Hadrami said: I heard Minjab b. al-Harith say, “This is a mistake that Sharik made in it. 'Ali b. Mushir informed us of it from Hisham b. 'Urwah from his father from 'Umar b. Abi Salamah from the Prophet ﷺ something similar.” He said, “Hamzah b. 'Amr is not sound; Sharik erred in it.”"],[2954,"I and a companion of mine went to Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman and said, “O Abu 'Abdillah.”"],[2955,"Hudhayfa belonged to the Banu Abs, but his lineage was counted among the Ansar."],[2956,"The polytheists seized Hudhayfa and his father before Badr and wanted to kill them, and they took from them a covenant and pact that they would not aid [the Muslims] against them, so they released them. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We gave them [a pledge] that we would not aid against them. If you wish, we will fight alongside you.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Rather, we will fulfill our pledge to them, and we will seek help from God against them.\""],[2957,"Hudhayfa and his father were coming on the day of Badr when Abu Jahl and his companions met them. They said to them, \"Perhaps you two intend [to join] Muhammad?\" He said: We said, \"No.\" He said: So he took from us [a pledge] that we would not aid against them. When we came to the Prophet ﷺ , we mentioned that to him and said, \"O Prophet of God, the people have taken a pledge from us. If you order us to fight alongside you, we will do it.\" He said, \"Rather, we will seek help from God and fulfill our pledge to them.\""],[2958,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him alone on a military expedition on the day of the Confederates."],[2959,"Hudhayfa used to say: There is no day more pleasing to my eye or more beloved to me than a day when I come to my family and find no food with them, and they say, \"We cannot manage even a little or a lot.\" He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"God is more protective of the believer with regard to this world than a sick person's family is protective of him from food. And God, exalted be He, is more attentive to the believer through trials than a parent is attentive to his child through good.\""],[2960,"By God, if I wished, I could narrate to you a thousand words by which you would love me, or follow me and believe me, out of piety toward God and His Messenger. And if I wished, I could narrate to you a thousand words by which you would hate me, shun me, and call me a liar."],[2961,"Hudhayfa sent someone to buy a shroud for him, so they bought him a shroud for three dirhams. Hudhayfa said, \"This is not what I want. Rather, buy two fine white linen garments.\""],[2962,"He sent me and Abu Mas'ud, and we bought for him a shroud, a striped Yemeni garment, for three hundred dirhams. He said, \"Show me what you bought for me.\" So we showed it to him, and he said, \"This is not a shroud for me. Two white linen garments without a shirt will suffice me. I will not remain except a little while until I attain something better than them or worse than them.\" So we bought for him two white linen garments."],[2963,"I seek refuge in God from a morning that leads to the Fire. Buy for me two white garments and shroud me in them, for they will not remain on me except a short while until I am clothed with something better than them or I am stripped of them quickly."],[2964,"\"The polytheists took a pledge from us...\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[2965,"We said: How did Hudhayfa attain what Abu Bakr and Umar did not attain? Sila b. Zufar said: By God, we asked Hudhayfa about that, and he said: I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey one night, and we traveled in the early part of the night. The Messenger of God ﷺ dozed off on his mount, and some people said, \"If we pushed him now, he would fall and his neck would break, and we would be relieved of him.\" When I heard them, I went ahead of them and walked between him and them, and I began reciting a surah of the Quran. The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up and said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"Hudhayfa, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Come closer.\" So I drew near, and he said, \"Did you hear what those behind you said?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God; that is why I walked between you and them.\" He said, \"Indeed, they are hypocrites: so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so.\""],[2966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me the choice between emigration and supporting [the Prophet in Madinah], and I chose supporting."],[2967,"The polytheists took me and my father captive on the day of Badr, and they made us promise that we would not help the Prophet ﷺ. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Fulfill your pledge to them, and we seek Allah’s help against them.”"],[2968,"“Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman died in the year thirty-six.”"],[2969,"“Hudhayfah died in the year thirty-six.”"],[2970,"We said to Hudhayfah: How did you know the affair of the hypocrites when none of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew it—not Abu Bakr or Umar ؓ? He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he fell asleep on his mount. I heard some people among them saying, “If we threw him off his mount, his neck would break and we would be rid of him.” So I rode between them and him, and I began to recite [Qur’an] and raise my voice. The Prophet ﷺ woke up and said, “Who is this?” I said, “Hudhayfah.” He said, “Who are these?” I said, “So-and-so and so-and-so,” until I had listed them. He said, “Did you hear what they said?” I said, “Yes; that is why I rode between you and them.” He said, “These—so-and-so and so-and-so,” until he listed their names—“are hypocrites. Do not inform anyone.”"],[2971,"We used to say that they were fourteen men. Ammar said, “If you are among them, then they are fifteen.” Wadiah said, “Wait, O Abu al-Yaqzan, I adjure you by Allah not to expose me.” Ammar said, “By Allah, I have not named anyone and I will never name anyone. But I bear witness that of the fifteen men, twelve of them are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the day when the witnesses stand.”"],[2972,"Muhammad promises us the treasures of Chosroes and Caesar, while one of us is not safe even when he goes to relieve himself. He is the one who said, “If we had any say in the matter, we would not have been killed here.” Al-Zubayr said: The one against whom al-Zubayr testified for this statement is Wadiah b. Thabit b. Amr b. Awf. He is the one who said, “We were only conversing and playing.” And he is the one who said, “Why do I see our reciters the greediest of us in appetite and the most cowardly of us at the time of meeting?” And Judd b. Abd Allah b. Nabil b. al-Harith of the Banu Amr b. Awf. He is the one about whom Gabriel ﷺ said, “O Muhammad, who is this black man with abundant hair, whose eyes are like two brass pots, looking with the eyes of a devil and whose liver is the liver of a donkey, informing the hypocrites of your news—the one who chews his own dung?” And al-Harith b. Yazid al-Ta’i, an ally of the Banu Amr b. Awf. He is the one who went first to the water seepage that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade anyone to touch, and drew water from it. And Aws b. Qayzi of the Banu Harithah. He is the one who said, “Indeed, our houses are exposed.” He is the grandfather of Yahya b. Sa’id b. Qays. And al-Jallas b. Suwayd b. al-Samit of the Banu Amr b. Awf. We have heard that he repented after that. And Sa’d b. Zurarah of the Banu Malik b. al-Najjar. He is the one who lit smoke upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was the youngest of them in age and the most malicious. And Qays b. Qahd of the Banu Malik b. al-Najjar. And Suwayd and Da’is, both of the Banu Balhabla; they are among those whom Ibn Ubayy equipped in Tabuk to discourage the people. And Qays b. Amr b. Sahl and Zayd b. al-Lasit. He was among the Jews of Qaynuqa, then he professed Islam, yet he retained the deceit of the Jews and the hypocrisy of the hypocrites. And Salamah b. al-Humam of the Banu Qaynuqa, who professed Islam."],[2973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, mentioning the Dajjal: “Written between his eyes is ‘kafir’; every Muslim reads it.”"],[2974,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Qur’an was revealed in seven modes.”"],[2975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be rulers over you who lie. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him. Whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond tomorrow, if Allah wills.”"],[2976,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “No talebearer will enter Paradise.”"],[2977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By Him in whose hand is my soul, the one who is sinful in his religion yet foolish in his livelihood will surely enter Paradise. By Him in whose hand is my soul, the one whom the Fire has scorched because of his sin will surely enter Paradise. By Him in whose hand is my soul, Allah will surely grant on the Day of Resurrection a forgiveness for which Iblis himself will stretch out in hope that it might reach him.”"],[2978,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Slandering a chaste woman destroys the deeds of a hundred years.”"],[2979,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning the trial? Hudhayfah said, \"I did.\" Umar said, \"You are indeed bold.\" He said, \"Bolder than me is one who conceals knowledge.\" Umar said, \"How did you hear it?\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Indeed in a man's wealth there is a trial, and in his wife there is a trial, and in his child.'\" Umar said, \"I did not ask about his private trial.\" Hudhayfah said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'There will come to you after me trials like the waves of the sea, some pushing others.' He raised his hand and said, 'O Allah, let me not live to see it.'\" Hudhayfah said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, do not fear; indeed between you and it there is a closed door.\" Umar said, \"Will the door be opened by opening or by breaking?\" Hudhayfah said, \"By breaking, then it will never be closed until the Day of Resurrection.\" Umar said, \"That is evil for this nation.\""],[2980,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I was given the closing verses of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne.\""],[2981,"I read in my father's book in his own handwriting, though I did not hear it from him, from Qatadah, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Hammam b. al-Harith, from Hudhayfah ؓ who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be in my nation liars and deceivers, twenty-seven of them, four of whom are women, and I am the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after me.\""],[2982,"From Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman that they were discussing coitus interruptus and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them and said, \"You do it?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Did you not know that Allah ﷻ has not created a soul that He is fashioning except that it will come into existence?\""],[2983,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us from an upper room and said, \"What are you saying? What are you mentioning?\" We said, \"The Hour.\" He said, \"Indeed it will not come until you see ten signs: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the emergence of Gog and Magog, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, and a fire that comes out from the bottom of Aden that will make people depart; it will rest with them when they take their midday nap, and it will set out with them when they set out, and with a wind that will cast them into the sea.\""],[2984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us while we were discussing the Hour, and said: \"The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: the rising of the sun from its west, the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, three sinkings - a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, the opening of Gog and Magog, and a fire that comes out from the bottom of Aden driving people to the gathering place.\""],[2985,"We were sitting talking in the shade of an upper room of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we mentioned the Hour, and our voices rose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us from his upper room and said, \"What are you asking one another about? Or what are you talking about?\" We said, \"We mentioned the Hour and our voices rose.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Hour will not come until before it there are ten signs: the rising of the sun from its west, the emergence of the Beast, the emergence of Gog and Magog, the Dajjal, Jesus son of Mary, the smoke, and three sinkings - a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula. The last of that is a fire that comes out from Yemen, from the bottom of Aden, driving people to the gathering place.\""],[2986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down from an upper room while we were discussing the Hour, and said: \"The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: the Dajjal, the smoke, the rising of the sun from its west, the Beast of the earth, Gog and Magog, three sinkings - a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire that comes out from the bottom of Aden Abyan driving people to the gathering place. It will descend with them when they descend and rest with them when they take their midday nap.\""],[2987,"Hudhayfah b. Asid, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me: We were talking in the shade of an upper room, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us from that upper room and said, \"What are you talking about?\" We said, \"We are talking about the Hour.\" He said, \"The Hour will not come until ten signs appear: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the Beast of the earth, three sinkings - a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, and Gog and Magog emerge, and a fire comes out from the bottom of Aden that surrounds people; no one will be left behind. It will drive them to the land of the gathering place and stay until they finish their needs, then it will move with them and make them depart.\" He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Hour will not come until a fire comes out from Ruman or Rakubah, from which the necks of camels in Busra are illuminated.\""],[2988,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked down upon us from an upper chamber while we were discussing the Hour, and said: \"You will see before it ten signs: the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, Gog and Magog, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, the rising of the sun from its west, and three sinkings: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula. The last of that is a fire that comes out from Yemen, or near Aden, driving people to their gathering place.\""],[2989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour will not come until ten signs appear: the rising of the sun from its west, the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, three sinkings - a sinking in the west, a sinking in the east, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, Gog and Magog, and a fire that comes out from the bottom of Aden that makes people depart to the gathering place. It will not leave anyone behind; it will stay for them, meaning for their needs.\""],[2990,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: \"The Beast will have three emergences over time. It will emerge once in the farthest part of Yemen, so that its mention spreads among the people of the desert, but its mention does not enter the town. Then it will hide for a long time after that. Then it will emerge another time near Makkah, so its mention spreads among the people of the desert and its mention spreads in Makkah. Then it will hide for a long time. Then while people are one day at the greatest mosque in sanctity to Allah, the best and most honored by Allah - the Sacred Mosque - nothing will startle them except a side of the mosque swelling between the Corner and the Station up to the gate of Banu Makhzum, to the right of the one leaving the mosque. The people will scatter from it in all directions, but a group of Muslims will remain firm before it, knowing that they cannot frustrate Allah. It will emerge upon them shaking the dust from its head. It will appear to them and mark their faces until it leaves them like shining stars. Then it will move through the earth; no pursuer can catch it and no fleer can escape it. Even a man will get up to seek refuge from it by prayer, and it will come to him and say, 'O so-and-so, now you pray?' He will turn his face toward it, and it will mark his face. Then it goes away. People will converse in their homes and journeys, share in wealth, and the disbeliever will be distinguished from the believer, until the believer says to the disbeliever, 'O disbeliever, give me my right,' and the disbeliever says, 'O believer, give me my right.'\""],[2991,"That the wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate one is he who is admonished by another. So he said, 'Which of that do you find strange?' I said, 'Can anyone become wretched without a deed?' He moved his hands to his ears and said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ with these two ears saying: The drop (nutfah) falls into the womb for forty nights, then the angel forms it—I think he said the one who creates it—and says: O Lord, male or female? So He makes it male or female. Then he says: O Lord, sound or unsound? So God ﷻ makes it sound or unsound. Then he says: O Lord, what is its term? What is its character? Then he says: O Lord, wretched or fortunate? So God, exalted is He, makes it wretched or fortunate.'"],[2992,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The wind comes in which God takes the soul of every believer, then the rising of the sun from its west—and it is the sign which God mentioned in His Book.\""],[2993,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; and Yaḥyā b. ʿUthmān b. Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us. They both said: Muḥammad b. Muslim al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Abū al-Ṭufayl ʿĀmir b. Wāthilah, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd ؓ saying: 'The wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate one is he who is admonished by another.' So I went to Ḥudhayfah b. Asīd and said: 'Do you not wonder at the saying of Ibn Masʿūd?' He said: 'And what did he say?' He said: 'The wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate one is he who is admonished by another.' Ḥudhayfah said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: When forty-five nights have passed over the drop, the angel says: Male or female? God ﷻ decrees and the angel writes. Then the angel says: Wretched or fortunate? God decrees and the angel writes. He said: Then he says: What is its provision, its term, and its deeds? He said: God decrees and the angel writes. He said: Then the page is folded, and nothing is added to it or subtracted from it.'"],[2994,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angel enters upon the drop after it settles in the womb for forty or forty-five nights and says: O Lord, wretched or fortunate? So God ﷻ says, and they both write. Male or female? So God says, and they both write. Its afflictions, its character, its provision, and its term. Then the page is folded, and nothing is added to it or subtracted from it.\""],[2995,"\"The wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate one is he who was fortunate in his mother's womb.\" He said: So I went to Ḥudhayfah b. Asīd, one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said: 'How strange is the saying of Ibn Umm ʿAbd: The wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb.' He said: Ḥudhayfah said to me: 'And what amazes you about that, O Abū al-Ṭufayl? Shall I not inform you of this from wretchedness?' And he raised the hadith: 'An angel is entrusted with the womb for forty-some nights. When God wants to create what He wills, by God's permission, he says: O Lord, male or female? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, wretched or fortunate? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, what is its term? Your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then it is folded, neither increased nor decreased.'"],[2996,"That the wretched one is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate one is he who is admonished by another. So what is the sin of this child? Ḥudhayfah said: 'And what do you find objectionable in that? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say many times: When the drop settles in the womb and forty days pass—and one of my companions said forty-eight days—the angel of the womb comes and forms its bones, flesh, blood, hair, skin, hearing, and sight. Then he says: O Lord, male or female? O Lord, wretched or fortunate? God ﷻ decrees what He wills and writes. Then he says: O Lord, what is its provision? God decrees what He wills and writes. Then the page is folded and not unfolded until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When God ﷻ wills to create the servant, the angel says: O Lord, male or female? The Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes. Then the angel says: O Lord, wretched or fortunate? The Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, what will it meet? The Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes. Then the angel says: What is its provision? God says what He wills, and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, what is its term? The Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes.\""],[2998,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: \"When forty-two nights pass over the drop, God sends an angel to it, who forms it and creates its hearing, sight, skin, flesh, and bones. And he says: O Lord, male or female? Your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes. Then he says: What is its provision? Your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes. And the page is in his hand, so he does not add to what he was commanded or subtract from it.\""],[3000,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: \"Pray over a brother of yours who died outside your land.\" They said: \"Who is he?\" He said: \"Al-Najāshī.\" So they prayed over him. He had been good to those of the Muslims who fled to him."],[3001,"That when the Messenger of God ﷺ was informed of the death of al-Najāshī, he said: \"Pray over a brother of yours who died outside your land.\""],[3002,"That the Prophet ﷺ was informed of the death of al-Najāshī, so he said to his companions: \"Your brother al-Najāshī has died. Whoever wishes to pray over him, let him pray over him.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned toward Abyssinia and said four takbīrs over him."],[3003,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever's patron I am, ʿAlī is his patron.\""],[3004,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever harms Muslims in their pathways, their curse becomes incumbent upon him.\""],[3005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Prophethood has gone, so there is no prophethood after me except the glad tidings.\" It was said: \"And what are the glad tidings?\" He said: \"The righteous dream that a man sees or is seen for him.\""],[3006,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he forbade his companions from certain closely spaced trees at al-Batḥāʾ from camping beneath them. Then he sent for them, and the thorns beneath them were removed, and he went to them and prayed beneath them. Then he stood and said: \"O people, indeed the Subtle, the All-Aware has informed me that no prophet was granted a lifespan except half the lifespan of the one who preceded him, and I think that I am about to be called and I will answer. I will be questioned, and you will be questioned, so what will you say?\" They said: \"We bear witness that you have conveyed, striven, and counseled, so may Allah reward you well.\""],[3007,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he forbade his companions from certain closely spaced trees at al-Batḥāʾ from camping beneath them. Then he sent for them, and the thorns beneath them were removed, and he went to them and prayed beneath them. Then he stood and said: \"O people, indeed the Subtle, the All-Aware has informed me that no prophet was granted a lifespan except half the lifespan of the one who preceded him, and I think that I am about to be called and I will answer. I will be questioned, and you will be questioned, so what will you say?\" They said: \"We bear witness that you have conveyed, striven, and counseled, so may Allah reward you well.\""],[3008,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he forbade his companions from certain closely spaced trees at al-Batḥāʾ from camping beneath them. Then he sent for them, and the thorns beneath them were removed, and he went to them and prayed beneath them. Then he stood and said: \"O people, indeed the Subtle, the All-Aware has informed me that no prophet was granted a lifespan except half the lifespan of the one who preceded him, and I think that I am about to be called and I will answer. I will be questioned, and you will be questioned, so what will you say?\" They said: \"We bear witness that you have conveyed, striven, and counseled, so may Allah reward you well.\""],[3009,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he forbade his companions from certain closely spaced trees at al-Batḥāʾ from camping beneath them. Then he sent for them, and the thorns beneath them were removed, and he went to them and prayed beneath them. Then he stood and said: \"O people, indeed the Subtle, the All-Aware has informed me that no prophet was granted a lifespan except half the lifespan of the one who preceded him, and I think that I am about to be called and I will answer. I will be questioned, and you will be questioned, so what will you say?\" They said: \"We bear witness that you have conveyed, striven, and counseled, so may Allah reward you well.\""],[3010,"When the Prophet ﷺ looked at the House, he said: \"O Allah, increase this House of Yours in honor, veneration, dignity, righteousness, and awe.\""],[3011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My community was presented to me last night near this chamber, until I am more familiar with a man among them than one of you is with his companion.\" A man among the people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, those who were created were presented to you; what about those who have not yet been created?\" He said: \"They were formed for me, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, I am more familiar with a person among them than a man is with his companion.\""],[3012,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"My community was presented to me last night by this chamber, from its first to its last.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, those who were created were presented to you; how were those not yet created presented to you?\" He said: \"They were formed for me in clay, until I am more familiar with a person among them than one of you is with his companion.\""],[3013,"From Suraihah or Abu Suraihah - 'Abd al-Razzaq was uncertain - he said: \"My family urged me to depart from the Sunnah after I had come to know it. The people of a household used to sacrifice a sheep or two sheep, but now our neighbors make us stingy.\""],[3014,"\"We used to sacrifice a single sacrificial animal, and they claimed that only miserliness prevents us from that, so they made us abandon the Sunnah after we had known it.\""],[3015,"\"I saw Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and they did not sacrifice for fear that it would be made a practice after them. Then my family urged me to depart from the Sunnah after I had come to know it, until I indeed sacrifice on behalf of everyone.\""],[3016,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, about the Hour (i.e., the Day of Judgment). The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, replied, \"What have you prepared for it?\" The man said, \"I have not prepared much except that I love Allah and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said, \"You will be with those whom you love.\""],[3017,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah."],[3018,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, an ally of theirs."],[3019,"A slave of Hatib came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ complaining about Hatib. He said, 'O Prophet of Allah, Hatib will certainly enter the Fire.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You lie. He will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah.'"],[3020,"His father wrote a letter to the disbelievers of Quraysh while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, having witnessed Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called 'Ali and al-Zubayr and said, 'Go until you catch up with a woman who has a letter. Bring it to me.' They went until they met her and said, 'Give us the letter that is with you.' They told her that they would not turn back until they stripped every garment from her. She said, 'Are you not two Muslim men?' They said, 'Yes, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that you have a letter.' When she was certain that she could not escape them, she untied the letter from her head and handed it to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Hatib until he read the letter to him and said, 'Do you recognize this letter?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What made you do that?' He said, 'There I have children and relatives, and I was a stranger among you, O group of Quraysh.' 'Umar said, 'Permit me to kill Hatib.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No, for he witnessed Badr. You do not know, perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said, \"Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.\"'"],[3021,"Huwaytib b. 'Abd al-'Uzza died, and his kunyah was Abu Muhammad, in the year fifty-four. His age was one hundred and twenty years."],[3022,"We were sitting in the courtyard of the Ka'bah in the Jahiliyyah when a woman came to the House seeking refuge from her husband. He extended his hand toward her, and his hand became withered. I saw him in Islam, and he was indeed paralyzed."],[3023,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: 'Hakim b. Hizam is Abu Khalid.'"],[3024,"Hakim b. Hizam died, and his kunyah was Abu Khalid, in the year fifty-four, and one says in the year fifty-eight. His age was one hundred and twenty years. He lived sixty years in the Jahiliyyah and sixty in Islam."],[3025,"That he would be slain on a day when ‘I will not do such and such,’ and he would not do it. His kunyah was Abu Khalid."],[3026,"for one hundred thousand. It was said to him, \"You sold your house for one hundred thousand?\" He said, \"By God, I only acquired it in the pre-Islamic era for a skin of wine. Bear witness that its price is in the way of God.\""],[3027,"that he sold his house to Muʿāwiyah ؓ for sixty thousand. They said, \"By God, Muʿāwiyah has cheated you.\" He said, \"I only acquired it in the pre-Islamic era for a skin of wine. I call you to witness that it is for the cause of God, the poor, and the slaves. So which of us is the cheated one?\""],[3028,"to them both, \"Do not hurry until I come out to you both.\" He said: Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām used to wear clothes brought from Egypt like nets, worth four dirhams, and take a staff in his hand and go out with a servant of his. Whenever he passed by a rubbish heap or sweepings and saw in it a scrap of cloth suitable for the gear of the camels that he loaded for the cause of God, he picked it up with the tip of his staff, shook it, then said to his two servants, \"Take hold of it, you two can use it for your gear.\" The two Bedouins, while he was doing that, one of them said to his companion, \"Woe to you, let us escape. By God, this one has nothing but picking up scraps.\" His companion said to him, \"Woe to you, do not hurry until we see.\" He went out with them until he brought them to the market. He looked at two fine, fat, pregnant she-camels and bought them and bought their gear. Then he said to his two servants, \"Repair with these scraps what needs repair of their gear.\" Then he loaded them with food, wheat, and fat, gave them spending money, then gave them the two she-camels.\" He said: one of them said to his companion, \"By God, I have never seen a better day from a picker of scraps than today.\""],[3029,"\"This is all for God.\" Then he freed the slaves and ordered that it be slaughtered."],[3030,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I freed forty emancipated slaves in the pre-Islamic era.\" He said, \"You have embraced Islam upon the good that preceded from you.\""],[3031,"ʿĀʾishah, Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām, Shaybah b. ʿUthmān, and ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿĀmir entrusted ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr as their executor."],[3032,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām a gift on the day of Ḥunayn, and he considered it small, so He (the Prophet) increased it. He said, \"O Messenger of God, which of your gifts is better?\" He said, \"The first one.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"O Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām, this is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous soul and good consumption will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with eager desire and bad consumption will not be blessed in it, and he will be like one who eats but never becomes full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.\" He said, \"And from you, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And from me.\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never ask anyone for anything after you, ever.\" He said: So he did not accept a register or a gift until he died. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ used to say, \"O God, I call You to witness concerning Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām that I invite him to his right from this wealth, and he refuses.\" He said, \"By God, I will not ask you or anyone else for anything.\" He died when he died, and he was among the wealthiest of Quraysh."],[3033,"ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr and Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib informed me that they heard Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām say: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he gave me. Then I asked him, and he gave me. Then he said, \"This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a good soul will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with eager desire will not be blessed in it, and he will be like one who eats but never becomes full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.\""],[3034,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he gave me. Then I asked him, and he gave me. Then I asked him, and he gave me. Then he said, \"O Ḥakīm, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous soul will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with eager desire will not be blessed in it, like one who eats but never becomes full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not ask anyone for anything after you until I depart this world.\" Abu Bakr ؓ used to invite Ḥakīm to the gift, but he refused to accept it from him. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ invited him to give him, but he refused to accept anything from him. ʿUmar said, \"I call you to witness, O assembly of Muslims, concerning Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām that I offer him his right that has been allotted to him from this fayʾ, and he refuses to take it.\" Ḥakīm did not ask anyone of the people for anything after the Messenger of God ﷺ until he passed away."],[3035,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for wealth and persisted, so he gave me. Then I asked him, and he gave me. He said, \"How persistent your asking is, O Ḥakīm. This wealth is green and sweet, and it is the filth of people's hands. Whoever takes it with generosity will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with eager desire will not be blessed in it, and he will be like one who eats but never becomes full. The hand of God is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the recipient, and the hand of the recipient is the lowest of hands.\""],[3036,"that Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for a hundred camels, and he gave him. Then he asked him for a hundred, and he gave him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous soul will be blessed in it, and whoever takes it with eager desire will not be blessed in it, and he will be like one who eats but never becomes full. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.\""],[3037,"that he heard Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām say: I said, \"O Messenger of God, I freed forty emancipated slaves in the pre-Islamic era.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have embraced Islam upon the good that preceded from you.\""],[3038,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that the things I used to do in the Jahiliyyah, seeking righteousness by them—will I be rewarded for them?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You have embraced Islam upon the good that has preceded.' Hisham said, 'He had manumitted slaves in the Jahiliyyah.'"],[3039,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that the matters in which I used to devote myself in the Jahiliyyah—of manumission and maintaining family ties—is there any reward for me in them?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You have embraced Islam upon the good that has preceded for you.'"],[3040,"He informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Do you think that the matters in which I used to devote myself in the Jahiliyyah—is there anything for me from them?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'You have embraced Islam upon the good you have sent ahead.'"],[3041,"He informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , \"I have done certain acts during the time of ignorance like maintaining ties of kinship, freeing slaves, and giving charity. Will I be rewarded for them?\" Al-Hakim ibn Hizam replied that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"You have embraced Islam for the good deeds you have done before.\""],[3042,"He informed him that he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you think that the matters in which I used to devote myself in the Jahiliyyah—of charity, manumission, or maintaining family ties—is there any reward in them?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You have embraced Islam upon the good you have sent ahead.'"],[3043,"That he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, incantations with which we used to seek cure, and medicines with which we used to treat ourselves—do they repel anything from Allah's decree?' He said, 'They are part of Allah's decree, may He be exalted.'"],[3044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and let one of you begin with those he supports. The best charity is that given from surplus means. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient, may He be exalted.'"],[3045,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and let one of you begin with those he supports. The best charity is that given from surplus means. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will make him self-sufficient, may He be exalted.'"],[3046,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and let one of you begin with those he supports. The best charity is that given from surplus means. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will keep him chaste; and whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will enrich him.'"],[3047,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Have I not been informed, or have I not been told, or has it not reached me—or as Allah willed—that you sell food?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'When you buy food, do not sell it until you have taken full possession of it.'"],[3048,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a man asks me to sell him something that I do not have; should I buy it for him?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not sell what you do not have.'"],[3049,"I said: O Messenger of God, a man comes to me and wants to buy from me, and I do not have it. Should I buy it for him from the market? He said: \"Do not sell what you do not have.\""],[3050,"I said: O Messenger of God, a man comes to me asking me to sell what I do not have; may I sell it to him and then obtain it for him from the market? He said: \"Do not sell what you do not have.\""],[3051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3053,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Hakim b. Hizam: \"Do not sell what you do not have.\""],[3054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not sell what you do not have.\""],[3055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3057,"I gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ that I would not fall down [in prostration] except while standing."],[3058,"O Messenger of God, I engage in many sales. What is lawful for me from them and what is forbidden to me? He said: \"Do not sell anything until you take possession of it.\""],[3059,"I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who buys these goods and sells them. What is lawful for me from them and what is forbidden to me from them? He said: \"Do not sell anything until you take possession of it.\""],[3060,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed the women one day, admonishing them and commanding them to have taqwa (consciousness) of Allah and obedience to their husbands, and to give in charity. He said, \"Indeed, among you are those who will enter Paradise while gathering firewood, and among you are those whose scalp is like the skin of Hell.\" So he separated between his fingers and said, \"Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" A woman asked. He said, \"Because you curse frequently and show ingratitude to your spouses and you are ungrateful for the good done to you.\""],[3061,"I bought some food from the charity food from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I made a profit on it before taking full possession of it. I said: I will not sell it until I ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about it. He said: \"Do not sell it until you take possession of it.\""],[3062,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"You have entered a time of many jurists, few orators, many givers, few askers; action in it is better than knowledge. A time will come of few jurists, many orators, many askers, few givers; knowledge in it is better than action.\""],[3063,"He provided two horses on the day of Hunayn, and they were both injured. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, my two horses have been injured, so compensate me.\" He gave him, and he asked for more, so he gave him more. Then he asked for more, and he gave him more. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever asks people, they give him, and the asker is like one who eats without ever being full.\""],[3064,"He provided two horses on the day of Hunayn, and they were both injured. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My two horses have been injured, so compensate me.\" He gave him, then he asked for more, so he gave him more. Then he asked for more. Then he said, \"O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever asks people, they give him, and the asker in it is like one who eats without ever being full.\""],[3065,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever asks people, they give him, and the asker from it is like one who eats without ever being full.\""],[3066,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated. If they are truthful and clear, they are blessed in their sale, and if they conceal and lie, the blessing of their sale is wiped out.\""],[3067,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.\" Hammam said, \"I found in my book: 'he may choose three times.' If they are truthful and clear, they are blessed in their sale, and if they lie and conceal, they may gain a profit but the blessing of their sale is wiped out.\""],[3068,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.\""],[3069,"It was said: \"O Messenger of God, which charity is best?\" He said: \"Charity given to a hostile relative.\""],[3070,"\"We heard a sound from the sky falling to the earth like the sound of a pebble in a basin. The Messenger of God ﷺ threw that pebble at us, and we were defeated.\""],[3071,"\"I used to buy food and sell it, and the Prophet ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have.\""],[3072,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him to buy a sacrificial animal for him for a dinar. He bought it, then sold it for two dinars. He bought a sheep for a dinar and brought back a dinar. \"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for blessing for him and ordered him to give the dinar as charity.\""],[3073,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen, he said: \"Do not touch the Quran unless you are in a state of purity.\""],[3074,"Wealth came from al-Bahrayn. The Prophet ﷺ called al-ʿAbbas and scooped for him, then said, “Shall I give you more?” He said, “Yes.” So he scooped for him again. Then he said, “Shall I give you more?” He said, “Yes.” So he scooped for him again. Then he said, “Shall I give you more?” He said, “Yes.” So he scooped for him again. Then he said, “Shall I give you more?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Leave some for those after you.” Then he called me and scooped for me. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, is this good for me or bad for me?” He said, “No, rather it is bad for you.” So I returned to him what he had given me. Then I said, “No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I will never accept a gift from anyone after you.” Muhammad said: Hakim said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to bless me.” He said, “O Allah, bless the work of his hands.”"],[3075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3080,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, “I have been blessed in trade, so I sell an item and then buy it back?” He said, “No.”"],[3081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not ever sell what you do not have.”"],[3082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from selling what I did not have."],[3084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from four things in trade: a loan with a sale, two conditions in one sale, selling what you do not have, and profiting from what you have not taken liability for."],[3085,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, with what did our Lord send you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim. O Hakim b. Muʿawiya, this is your religion; wherever you are, it will suffice you.”"],[3086,"From ʿUrwah concerning the naming of those Muslims who were killed on the Day of al-Yamāmah, then from Quraysh, then from Banū Makhzūm: Ḥakīm b. Ḥazn b. Abī Wahb b. ʿAmr b. ʿĀʾidh."],[3087,"“Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah’?” Al-Ḥakam said: “Yes.”"],[3088,"\"Shall I increase you?\" Then I caught up with al-Ḥukm and mentioned that to him, so he stopped until the people caught up, then he said: \"I repeated the prayer with you because of the donkeys that passed in front of you, and you struck me as an example for Ibn Abī Muʿayṭ. I ask Allah to make your conduct good, to make your conveyance good, to grant you victory over your enemy, and to separate me from you.\" They went on and saw in their faces nothing but what pleased them, and when they finished, he died."],[3089,"From al-Ḥakam al-Ghifārī, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-dubbāʾ (gourds), al-ḥantam (green jars), al-muzaffat (pitched vessels), and al-naqīr (hollowed palm trunks).”"],[3090,"\"Do you remember the day when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade (us) from offering nahr, muqayyir, dubbaa, and hantam?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The other person said, \"And I bear witness to that.\""],[3091,"\"A man from the Banu Ghifar, from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , narrated that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the offering of sacrificial animals to an idol, selling an animal by estimating its weight, and the practice of Dubba' (a type of divination). He also prohibited a man from purifying himself with the water used for ablution by a woman.\""],[3092,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leftover water of a woman.”"],[3093,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade performing ablution with the leftover water of a woman.”"],[3094,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: “The Prophet ﷺ forbade performing ablution with the leftover water of a woman.”"],[3095,"I was with al-Ḥakam b. ʿAmr al-Ghifārī when the messenger of ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ came to him and said: “ʿAlī ؓ says: ‘You are the most deserving of those who help us in this matter.’” He replied: “I heard my close friend, your cousin ﷺ, say: ‘When the matter is like this, or like this, I will take a sword of wood.’ So I have taken a sword of wood.”"],[3096,"“Do you know why I came to you? Do you not remember that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was told what his commander had said to him—‘Stand and fall into the fire’—the man rose to fall into it, but he was caught and restrained, and the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Had he fallen into it, he would have entered the Fire. There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah’?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I only wanted to remind you of this hadith.”"],[3097,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah.” He said: And he wished to meet the other because of the hadith, and indeed he met him and said: “Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: ‘There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah’?” The other said: “Yes.” He said: “Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar,” or as he said."],[3098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The dog, the donkey, and the woman interrupt the prayer.”"],[3099,"Al-Hakam al-Ghifari said, 'O plague, take me to You.' A man from the people said to him, 'Why do you say this when I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Let none of you wish for death\"?' He said, 'I heard what you heard, but I am hastening toward six things: the selling of judgment, the abundance of stipulations, the rule of boys, the shedding of blood, the severing of kinship, and a generation at the end of time who take the Quran as flutes.'"],[3100,"Al-Nu'man, I think he is al-Ghifari, said: I was eating, while I was a boy, from here and from there. He said, 'O my son, do not eat like this; this is how Satan eats. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand in the bowl or vessel, his fingers did not go beyond the place of his palm.'"],[3101,"I sat with a man who had been a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, called al-Hakam b. Hazn al-Kulfi, and he began to narrate. He said: I came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the seventh of seven or the ninth of nine. Permission was sought for us, and we entered upon him. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we have come to you so that you may supplicate for good for us.' He supplicated for good for us, ordered that we be lodged, and ordered for us some dates. At that time the situation was humble. We stayed there for some days, and we attended the Friday prayer with the Prophet ﷺ. He stood leaning on a bow or a staff, praised Allah Almighty, and extolled Him with light, good, blessed words, then said: 'O people, you will never be able to do all that you have been commanded, but aim for what is right and rejoice.'"],[3102,"The daughter of al-Hakam said: I said to my grandfather al-Hakam, 'I have not seen a people more incapable or worse in the affair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you, O Banu Umayyah.' He said, 'Do not blame us, my daughter. I will only tell you what I saw with these two eyes. We said, \"By Allah, we keep hearing Quraysh elevating this Sabian in our mosque.\" They agreed to confront him until we seize him. So we set an appointment. When we saw him, we heard a sound so that we thought no mountain remained in Tihamah but had crumbled upon us. We did not recover until he finished his prayer and returned to his family. Then we set another appointment for another night. When he came, we rose against him, but I saw al-Safa and al-Marwah meet each other and come between us and him. By Allah, that did not avail us.'"],[3103,"Al-Hakam b. Abi al-As used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ spoke, he would twitch at first. The Prophet ﷺ noticed him and said, 'You are like that.' He did not cease to twitch until he died."],[3104,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give him allegiance. He said, 'What is your name?' I said, 'Al-Hakam.' He said, 'Rather, you are Abdullah.'"],[3105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me among the spoils. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while my she-camel had been let loose and I was beating her. He said, 'Do not beat her,' and he said ﷺ, 'Untie her.' She stood up and went along with the people."],[3106,"He went on three military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He said to us, 'When you have buried me and sprinkled water on my grave, stand at my grave, face the qiblah, and supplicate for me.'"],[3107,"From Urwah, in naming those who were killed on the Day of Bi'r Ma'unah among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: al-Hakam b. Kaysan al-Makhzumi."],[3108,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he performed ablution, would take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his private part."],[3109,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his private part."],[3110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he performed ablution, would sprinkle water in front of his private part."],[3111,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution, then take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his clothes."],[3112,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entering and performing ablution, then he took some water and sprinkled it.\""],[3113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated, then performed ablution and sprinkled water on his private part."],[3114,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and took a handful of water and sprinkled it on his private part."],[3115,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and sprinkled water on his private part."],[3116,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and sprinkle water on his private part."],[3117,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, and he sprinkled water on the private parts of his body. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 167)"],[3118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you performs ghusl and then something appears from his penis, let him perform ablution.\""],[3119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Patience and seeking reward are the emancipation of slaves, and Allah will admit their possessor to Paradise without reckoning.\""],[3120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The most beloved of deeds to Allah ﷻ is feeding a needy person out of hunger, or repaying a debt on his behalf, or relieving him of distress.\""],[3121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not mutilate any of Allah's ﷻ creation in which there is a soul.\""],[3122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever brings you a favor, repay him; if you cannot find anything, then supplicate for him.”"],[3123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us: “When you stand for prayer, raise your hands level with your ears and do not let them deviate from your ears. Then say: Allahu Akbar, glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You. If you do not add anything to the takbir, it will suffice you.”"],[3124,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a meal. A man from the people took the household servant’s napkin, but the servant took hold of his garment and wiped himself with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not wipe yourself with the garment of someone you have not clothed.”"],[3125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be truly modest before Allah: guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it holds, and remember death and decay. Whoever does that, his reward will be the Garden of Refuge.”"],[3126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Qur’an descends, and it is the speech of Allah, mighty and majestic.”"],[3127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The calamitous matter, the burdensome load, and the evil that never ceases is the open proclamation of innovations.”"],[3128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Trim the mustache down to the lips.”"],[3129,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj b. ‘Ilat said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah and family there, and I want to go to them. Am I absolved if I disparage you or say something?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him permission to say whatever he wished. He said: So when he arrived, he went to his wife and said: “Collect whatever you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his companions. They have been plundered and their wealth taken.” That spread through Makkah: the Muslims withdrew in dismay, while the polytheists showed joy and delight. The news reached al-‘Abbas b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib, who was stricken and could not stand. Then he sent a servant to al-Hajjaj b. ‘Ilat, saying: “Woe to you! What have you brought? What are you saying? What Allah, mighty and majestic, promised is better than what you have brought.” Al-Hajjaj said: “Convey peace to Abu al-Fadl and tell him to clear a place for me in one of his houses so I may come to him, for the news is what will please him.” His servant came, and when he reached the door he said: “Rejoice, O Abu al-Fadl!” Al-‘Abbas leapt up in joy and kissed him between the eyes. The servant told him what al-Hajjaj had said, and he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came to him and informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had conquered Khaybar, taken their wealth as spoils, and the shares Allah allotted fell upon their wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ chose Safiyya bt. Huyayy for himself and gave her the choice between his freeing her and being his wife or returning to her people, and she chose to be freed and become his wife. “But I came for what I have here; I wanted to collect it and take it away. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he permitted me to say whatever I wished. So conceal it for me for three days, then mention whatever you like.” He said: His wife collected all the jewelry and goods she had and gave it to him, and he departed with it. After three days, al-‘Abbas went to al-Hajjaj’s wife and said: “What has your husband done?” She told him that he had left on such-and-such a day, and said: “May Allah not grieve you, O Abu al-Fadl; what reached you distressed us.” He said: “Indeed, Allah will not grieve me, and by Allah’s praise it was only what we loved. Allah opened Khaybar to His Messenger ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ chose Safiyya for himself. If you have any need of your husband, go join him.” She said: “I think, by Allah, you are truthful.” He said: “Indeed, by Allah, I am truthful, and the matter is as I told you.” Then he went to the gatherings of Quraysh, and as he passed them they said: “Nothing befalls you but good, O Abu al-Fadl.” He said: “Nothing befalls me but good, by Allah’s praise. Al-Hajjaj b. ‘Ilat informed me that Allah opened Khaybar to His Messenger ﷺ, the shares of Allah took effect, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ chose Safiyya for himself. He asked me to conceal it for him for three days, and he came only to take his wealth and whatever he had here, then depart.” So Allah turned back upon the polytheists the grief that had been on the Muslims, and the Muslims who had entered their homes in despair came out until they reached al-‘Abbas, and he told them the news. The Muslims rejoiced, and Allah returned upon the polytheists whatever grief, anger, or sorrow had been there."],[3130,"The extra share (nafal) is a right which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted."],[3131,"\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how can I pay back the dues of the one who breast-fed me?' He said: 'By giving a male or female slave.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3329)"],[3132,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “What removes from me the reproach of suckling?” He said: “A slave, male or female.”"],[3133,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the reproach of suckling?” He said: “A slave, male or female.”"],[3134,"I said: O Messenger of God, what removes from me the reproach of suckling? He said: “A slave or a slave girl at weaning.”"],[3135,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: What removes from me the reproach of suckling? The Prophet ﷺ said: “A ghurra: a slave or a slave girl.”"],[3136,"I said: O Messenger of God, what removes from me the reproach of suckling? He said: “The ghurra: the slave or the slave girl.”"],[3137,"I said: O Messenger of God, what removes from me the reproach of suckling? He said: “A ghurra: a slave or a slave girl.”"],[3138,"He said: O Messenger of God, what removes from me the reproach of suckling? He said: “The ghurra: the slave or the slave girl.”"],[3139,"He said to the Messenger of God ﷺ: What removes from me the reproach of suckling, O Messenger of God? He said: “A slave or a slave girl.”"],[3140,"That we say to our Lord when we meet Him: {Our Lord, indeed we obeyed our masters and our great ones, and they led us astray from the way}."],[3141,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever breaks [a bone] or becomes lame has exited [ihram] and owes another hajj.” He said: I related it to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, and they said: He spoke the truth."],[3142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever breaks [a bone] or becomes lame has exited [ihram] and owes a hajj.” So I asked Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas, and they said: He spoke the truth."],[3143,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever breaks [a bone] or becomes lame or falls ill has exited [ihram] and owes the hajj from the next year.” Ikrimah said: I asked Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas about it, and they said: Al-Hajjaj spoke the truth."],[3144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever becomes lame or breaks [a bone] or falls ill or is detained, let him perform the like of it and he has exited [ihram].” Ikrimah said: I related it to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, and they said: He spoke the truth."],[3145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform tahajjud after sleeping, and he used to use the miswak before performing tahajjud."],[3146,"On the authority of al-Hajjaj b. 'Amr b. Ghaziyyah, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: It is enough for one of you, when he gets up at night to pray until morning, that he has performed tahajjud. \"Indeed, tahajjud is that a man prays a prayer after a sleep, then prays a prayer after a sleep. And that was the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[3147,"On the authority of 'Abd Allah b. 'Amir al-Thumali, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and on the authority of al-Hajjaj b. 'Amir al-Thumali, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that they both prayed the morning prayer with 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and he recited, \"When the sky is split asunder,\" and prostrated in it."],[3148,"I saw five of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ trimming their moustaches, letting their beards grow, and tying them up: Abu Umamah al-Bahili, al-Hajjaj b. 'Amir al-Thumali, al-Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib, 'Abd Allah b. Busr al-Mazini, and 'Utbah b. 'Abd al-Sulami. They used to trim along the edge of the lip."],[3149,"On the authority of 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those Muslims who were killed on the day of Ajnadayn, then from Quraysh, then from Banu Sahm: Hajjaj b. al-Harith b. Qays."],[3150,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banu Sahm: Hajjaj b. al-Harith b. Qays."],[3151,"On the authority of a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, I think he is 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud: \"The Prophet ﷺ commanded them to delay the noon prayer until it cools down, because the heat is from the scorching heat of Hell.\""],[3152,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr: Harithah b. al-Nu'man b. Zayd b. 'Ubayd b. Tha'labah b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[3153,"About Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr from the Ansar and then from the Banu Najjar, Harithah bin Al-Nu'man is mentioned. He was the one who passed by the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ while being accompanied by Jibril (Gabriel) ﷺ near the meeting places."],[3154,"Harithah b. al-Nu'man passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while Gabriel ﷺ was with him, conversing privately, and he did not greet. Gabriel ﷺ said, \"What prevented him from greeting? If he had greeted, I would have returned the greeting to him.\" Then he said, \"Indeed, he is one of the eighty.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"And what are the eighty?\" He said, \"People will flee from you except eighty, and they will remain with you; their provision and the provision of their children will be with God in Paradise.\" When Harithah returned, he greeted, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Why did you not greet when you passed by?\" He said, \"I saw a person with you, and I disliked interrupting your conversation.\" He said, \"Did you see him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That was Gabriel ﷺ, and he said...\" Then he informed him of what Gabriel ﷺ had said."],[3155,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while Gabriel ﷺ was sitting with him in the sitting places, and I greeted him and then went on. When I finished and the Prophet ﷺ returned, he said to me, \"Did you see the one who was with me?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, he was Gabriel ﷺ , and he returned the greeting to you.\""],[3156,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Three things are inseparable from my nation: belief in omens, envy, and bad thoughts. A man said, \"What removes them, O Messenger of God, from the one who has them?\" He said, \"If you envy, seek forgiveness from God; if you think badly, do not act on it; and if you foresee an evil omen, proceed.\""],[3157,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Handing over food to a poor person protects against an evil death.\""],[3158,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man goes out with his small flock to the outskirts of the village, attends the prayers, and returns to his family. Then when he has grazed what is around him and the land becomes difficult for him, he says, 'If only I moved up to a hollow that has more abundant pasture than this.' So he moves up until he does not attend any of the prayers except Friday. Then when he has grazed what is around him and the land becomes difficult for him, he says, 'If only I moved up to a hollow that has more abundant pasture than this.' So he moves up until he does not attend Friday and does not know what the day of Friday is, until a seal is placed on his heart."],[3159,"That he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man goes out with his sheep and is on the outskirts of the village, and he attends the prayers and returns to his family. Then when he has grazed what is around him and the land becomes difficult for him, he says, 'If only I moved to a hollow that has more abundant pasture than this.' So he moves until he does not attend any of the prayers except Friday. Then when he has grazed what is around him and the land becomes difficult for him, he says, 'If only I moved to a hollow that has more abundant pasture than this.' So he moves until he does not attend Friday and does not know what Friday is, and a seal is placed on his heart."],[3160,"Harithah perished on the day of Uhud; an arrow struck him. His mother came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, if he is in Paradise I will not weep over him, and if he is in the Fire, God will see what I do. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"They are Paradises, and he is in the highest Firdaws.\""],[3161,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Harithah b. Zayd b. Abi Zuhayr b. Imri' al-Qays."],[3162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If I were to take an intimate friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah as an intimate friend, but your companion is the intimate friend of Allah, Exalted is He.'"],[3163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer on the day of Fitr and Adha. He said the takbir seven times in the first rak'ah and recited, 'Qaf. By the Glorious Quran,' and in the second rak'ah five times and recited, 'The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split.'"],[3164,"Umar ؓ asked me about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited on the day of Eid, and I said: “Qāf and Iqtarabat al-sāʿah.”"],[3165,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where we are afflicted by hunger. What is suitable for us from dead meat?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you have not had a morning drink or an evening drink, and you have not gathered wild greens, then you may make use of it.” This is how al-Walīd b. Muslim reported it from al-Awzāʿī, from Ḥassān, from Marthad or Abū Marthad, and it is a mistake. The correct version is what ʿAbd Allāh b. Kathīr al-Qārī reported from al-Awzāʿī."],[3166,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever regularly attends this prayer will have his past sins forgiven.”"],[3167,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “This, then the backs of the mats.”"],[3168,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of the Bridge from the Anṣār, then from Banū Muʿāwiya: al-Ḥārith b. Masʿūd b. ʿAbd b. Muẓāhir."],[3169,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Nabīt, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: al-Ḥārith b. Anas b. Mālik b. ʿUbayd b. Kaʿb."],[3170,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among my community is one whose intercession will cause to enter Paradise more than Mudar.”"],[3171,"He passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to him: “How have you entered upon morning, O Harith?” He said, “I have entered upon morning as a true believer.” He said, “Look at what you say, for everything has a reality. What is the reality of your faith?” He said, “My soul has turned away from the world, and for that I have stayed awake at night and made my day thirsty. It is as if I am looking at the Throne of my Lord appearing, and as if I am looking at the people of Paradise visiting one another in it, and as if I am looking at the people of the Fire howling in it.” He said, “O Harith, you have known, so hold fast” — three times."],[3172,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and all his companions were routed except al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw a handful of earth at our faces, and we were routed. It did not seem to me that there was any tree or stone except that it was in our tracks."],[3173,"From Ibn Shihāb, regarding the names of those who witnessed the ʿAqabah pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: al-Ḥārith b. Qays b. Khālid b. Makhlad; he witnessed Badr."],[3174,"Al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimma said: The Messenger of God ﷺ asked me on the day of Uḥud while he was in the mountain pass, “Have you seen ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God, I saw him at the foot of the mountain with a band of polytheists upon him, so I rushed to him to defend him, but then I saw you and turned to you.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Indeed, the angels are fighting alongside him.” Al-Ḥārith said: I returned to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and found him among seven slain men. I said to him, “May your right hand prosper! Did you kill all of these?” He said, “As for this one—Arṭāh b. Shuraḥbīl—and this one, I killed them. As for those others, someone I did not see killed them.” I said, “God and His Messenger have spoken the truth.”"],[3175,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those among the Anṣār who were martyred on the day of Uḥud from the Banū al-Nabīt: al-Ḥārith b. Aws b. Rāfiʿ."],[3176,"From his father regarding the naming of those who attended [battles] with ʿAlī ؓ: al-Ḥārith b. al-Nuʿmān, a Badrī."],[3177,"He heard Al-Harith bin Dirar Al-Khuzai say: \"I visited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he invited me to Islam, so I embraced it and affirmed it. He then invited me to pay Zakat, so I affirmed it too. I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : 'Shall I return to my people and invite them to Islam and paying Zakat? Whoever responds to me, I will collect his Zakat, and you can send a messenger to me to collect what I have gathered. So, when Al-Harith collected Zakat from those who responded to him, and the messenger to whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intended to send to him was delayed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ detained him. When he did not come, Al-Harith assumed that Allah and His Messenger ﷺ were angry with him, so he called the people of his tribe and said to them: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had set a time for me; he would send his messenger to me to collect the Zakat I had. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never keeps the things of this world, and I do not see him detaining his messenger without a justified reason. So, go, and we will meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then sent Al-Walid bin 'Uqbah to Al-Harith to collect the Zakat he had gathered. So, when Al-Walid had ridden for some distance, he returned. When he met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Al-Harith prevented me from collecting the Zakat, and he wanted to kill me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then sent a group of Sahaba to Al-Harith. When they approached him, they said: 'This is Al-Harith.' But when they came closer, he said: 'Whom have you been sent to?' They replied: 'To you.' He asked them: 'Why?' They said: 'Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent Al-Walid bin 'Uqbah but he returned, claiming that you prevented him from collecting the Zakat and wanted to kill him.' Al-Harith said: 'By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I have not done what he claims, nor has he come to me. I did not come until I received a message from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ due to my detention of his messenger, fearing that there may be anger from Allah and His Messenger ﷺ against me.' Then Allah revealed the verses from Surah Al-Hujurat (49:6-7) to this point: 'O you who have believed, if there comes to you a disobedient one with information, investigate, lest you harm a people out of ignorance and become, over what you have done, regretful.' 'And know that among you is the Messenger of Allah.'"],[3178,"How often he was eager for command. We said, 'And what is that?' He said, 'A thief was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered his execution. It was said to him, \"He only stole.\" He said, \"Cut off his hand.\" Then later he was brought to Abu Bakr, after he had stolen and his limbs had been cut off. Abu Bakr ؓ said, \"I find nothing for you except what the Messenger of God ﷺ decreed concerning you on the day he ordered your execution, for he was more knowledgeable about you.\" Then he ordered his execution by a group of young boys from the sons of the Muhajirun, among whom I was. Ibn al-Zubayr said, \"Put me in command over us.\" Then we set off with him.' And he mentioned the hadith."],[3179,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not command you with five words that God ﷻ commanded me with? The community, hearing, obedience, emigration, and jihad in the path of God. Whoever leaves the community by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his head, unless he returns. And whoever calls with the call of Jahiliyyah, he is among the rubble of Hell.\" A man said: O Messenger of God, even if he fasts and prays? He said: \"Even if he fasts and prays. Call with the call of God, who named you Muslims, believers, servants of God.\""],[3180,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You are a nation shown mercy and given immunity. So be upright and take on the capacity of the matter.”"],[3181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage in the middle of the days of sacrifice: “Is this not the sacred day?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The sanctity between you until the Day of Resurrection is like the sanctity of this day.” Then he said: “Shall I tell you who the Muslim is? The one from whose tongue the Muslims are safe. And shall I tell you who the believer is? The one whom the believers trust with their lives and their blood. And shall I tell you who the emigrant is? The one who abandons evil deeds and abandons what God has forbidden. The believer is sacred to the believer like the sanctity of this day. His flesh is sacred to him – it is forbidden for him to eat it or to backbite him in his absence. His honor is sacred to him – it is forbidden to tear it. His face is sacred to him – it is forbidden to slap it. And it is forbidden for him to push him with a push that harms him.”"],[3182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there are chambers whose outside is seen from their inside and their inside is seen from their outside. Allah, may He be glorified, has prepared them for whoever feeds food, persists in fasting, and prays at night while people are sleeping.”"],[3183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, may He be glorified, commanded me to enjoin upon you five words: upon you is jihad, hearing and obedience, and emigration. So whoever separates from the community by the length of a bow, neither prayer nor fasting will be accepted from him. Those are the fuel of the Fire.”"],[3184,"I went out seeking companionship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I set out early to Hurayth b. Ghanim and asked him for companionship, and he agreed. I accompanied him, and we arrived upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying the dawn prayer and the stars were still entangled in the sky."],[3185,"He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Arafah while my uncle was riding behind me. I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was placing his two fingers, one over the other.” He said: “I said: ‘What is he saying?’ He said: ‘He is saying: “Throw with stones like those used in khazf.”’”"],[3186,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Harmala b. Zayd came to him and sat down in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, faith is here,” and he pointed with his hand to his tongue, “and hypocrisy is here,” and he pointed with his hand to his chest, “and I do not mention Allah except a little.” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent about him. He repeated that to him, and Harmala fell silent. The Prophet ﷺ took hold of the tip of Harmala's tongue and said: “O Allah, grant him a truthful tongue and a grateful heart, and provide him with love of me and love of those who love me, and turn his affair to good.” Harmala said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have brothers who are hypocrites, among whom I was a leader. Shall I not point them out to you?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “No. Whoever comes to us as you came to us, we will seek forgiveness for him as we sought forgiveness for you. And whoever persists in his sin, Allah is more entitled to him. Do not tear the veil of anyone.”"],[3187,"I set out with the delegation of the tribe to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he led us in the morning prayer. When he had said the salam, I began looking at the face of the man beside me, and I could barely recognize him because of the darkness before dawn. I said, “O Messenger of God, give me a parting instruction.” He said, “Fear God, and if you are among people and hear them saying to you what pleases you, do it; and if you hear them saying to you what you dislike, leave it.”"],[3188,"His father was Hidhyam. “O Messenger of God, I have sons, and this is the youngest of my sons, so bless him.” He said, “Come here, boy.” He took me by the hands and wiped my head and said, “May God bless you in him.” He said, “I saw Hanzala: a man with a tumor would be brought to him, and he would wipe his hand over it and say, ‘In the name of God,’ and the tumor would go away.”"],[3189,"From Habba and Sawa’, the two sons of Khalid, they said: We entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Do not despair of provision as long as your heads shake, for a person is born from his mother red, with no shell upon him, then God ﷻ provides for him.”"],[3190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no orphanhood after puberty, and no orphanhood applies to a girl once she has menstruated.”"],[3191,"I fought the Prophet ﷺ at the beginning of the day as an unbeliever, and I fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim. We were three men and nine women, and concerning us was revealed {Were it not for believing men and believing women}."],[3192,"Ibn Numayr—and people say Nusayba—and her sister, the two daughters of Kaʿb b. ʿAmr; her husband Zayd b. ʿĀṣim; and her two sons, ʿAbdallāh b. Zayd and Ḥabīb b. Zayd, the one whom Musaylima seized."],[3193,"And it is said, “Rather, it was revealed about Khārija b. Zayd b. Abī Zuhayr, the brother of the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj.”"],[3194,"His father brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ while his eyes were whitened and he could not see anything with them. He asked him, “What happened to him?” He said, “I was driving a camel of mine and my leg fell on snake eggs, so my sight was afflicted.” The Messenger of God ﷺ blew into his eye, and he regained his sight. I saw him passing thread through a needle while he was eighty years old and his eyes were still whitened."],[3195,"Ḥuṣayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “What do you think of a man who maintained family ties and hosted guests and died before you?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “My father and your father are in the Fire.” Not twenty nights passed before he died as an idolater."],[3196,"When Ṭalḥa b. al-Barāʾ met the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “O Messenger of God, command me to do whatever you love, and I will not disobey any command of yours.” The Prophet ﷺ marveled at that, for he was a youth, and said to him at that point, “Go and kill your father.” He turned and went out to do it, but the Prophet called him back and said, “Come back, for I was not sent to sever family ties.” After that Ṭalḥa fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him in winter during cold and clouds. When he departed, he said to his family, “I think Ṭalḥa is about to die, so inform me when it happens so that I may be present and pray over him; and hasten him.” But the Prophet ﷺ had not yet reached the Banū Sālim b. ʿAwf when he died, and night fell over him. Among what Ṭalḥa had said was: “Bury me and join me to my Lord ﷻ, and do not call the Messenger of God ﷺ, for I fear for him from the Jews lest he be harmed because of me.” The Prophet ﷺ was informed when morning came, and he came and stood at his grave. The people lined up with him, then he raised his hands and said, “O God, meet Ṭalḥa while You smile at him.”"],[3197,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is nothing in the hāmah, and the evil eye is real, and the truest of birds is the fa'l.\""],[3198,"Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by on the day of Siffin, leaning on Al-Ashtar. Then, Habis, who was known to be a devout worshiper, also passed by. Al-Ashtar said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, Habis is with them. By Allah, my last account of him was that he was a believer.\" Ali replied, \"Today, he is indeed a believer.\""],[3199,"Habis b. Sa'd al-Ta'i entered the mosque in the pre-dawn while he had met the Prophet ﷺ, and some people were praying in the front of the mosque. He said, \"The ostentatious ones, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, frighten them! Whoever frightens them has obeyed God and His Messenger.\" Then he said, \"The angels pray in the pre-dawn in the front of the mosque.\""],[3200,"I passed by one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ called me, so I came to him, and he said: \"Say often: 'There is no power and no strength except with God,' for it is one of the treasures of Paradise.\""],[3201,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit on Friday saying: \"We have ordered for the women wars and needles. As for the wars, it came to them from Yemen; and as for the needles, they were taken from some of the people of the covenant from the jizyah that they owe.\" I said to al-Rabi', or it was said to him, or al-Rabi' b. Harb heard him: Yes."],[3202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed during his Hajj, while we were with him, by a man who had finished his Hajj, and said to him: \"Has your Hajj been accepted for you?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Start the work anew.\""],[3203,"I came to Madinah with merchandise to sell, and I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “I will give you twenty sāʿs of dates if you guide these companions of mine to the road to Khaybar.” I did so. When the Messenger of God ﷺ reached Khaybar and conquered it, I came and he gave me the twenty. Then I embraced Islam."],[3204,"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ proposed to Fāṭimah ؓ. The Prophet ﷺ said, “She is yours, O ʿAlī.”"],[3205,"The Prophet of God ﷺ delivered a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, “O people, what land is this?” They said, “A sacred land.” He said, “What month is this?” They said, “A sacred month.” He said, “What day is this?” They said, “A sacred day.” He said, “Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, like this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours. Let those present convey to those absent. Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[3206,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon on the day of Khaybar. “He forbade them to sell a share of the spoils before it was divided, to have intercourse with pregnant captives until they gave birth, and to sell fruit until its ripeness was evident and it was safe from blight.” Duḥaym added in his report: “And he permitted them three things that he had forbidden them: he permitted them the meat of sacrificial animals, visiting graves, and leather containers.”"],[3207,"A man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, should I make one-third of my prayers for you?\" He said, \"Yes, if you wish.\" The man asked, \"What if I make two-thirds of my prayers for you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The man then asked, \"And if I dedicate all of my prayers to you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In that case, Allah will suffice you in all matters of your worldly life and the Hereafter that concern you.\""],[3208,"From the belly of a woman, her clothes, until he treated her.”"],[3209,"We, the Ansar, had a need to present to the governor, and what we sought from him was a difficult matter. We went to him with men from Quraysh and others, and they spoke to him and mentioned the bequest of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning us. He mentioned the difficulty of the matter, so the people excused him and left, while Ibn Abbas kept pressing him, and by God, he found no alternative but to fulfill our need. We went out until we entered the mosque, and there the people were in circles. Hassan said: I laughed as I listened to them. For by God, he was the most deserving of it; it is the remnant of prophethood and the inheritance of Ahmad ﷺ, the refinement of his roots and the extraction of the likeness of his character. The people said: “Speak well, O Hassan.” Ibn Abbas said: “They are right.” Then Hassan began to praise Ibn Abbas ؓ and said:"],[3210,"His mother went as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to you as a delegate so that you may supplicate for this son of mine, that God may place blessing for him in it and make him abundant and good. So he performed ablution, and from the leftover water of his ablution he wiped his face, and said: “O God, bless her in him and make him abundant and good.”"],[3211,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Ta’if, and he saw men among his companions who had dyed their beards red and dyed their beards yellow, so he said: “Welcome to those who dyed yellow and those who dyed red.”"],[3212,"His wife said: Now you will be sold on account of his debt. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Who is the one responsible for the estate of al-Hubab?” His brother Abu al-Yasar Ka‘b b. ‘Amr said: I am. The Prophet ﷺ called him and said: “Do not sell her; set her free. When you hear of slaves that have come to me, come to me and I will compensate you.” They did so. Then they differed among themselves after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some said: An umm walad is owned as a slave; were it not for that, the Prophet ﷺ would not have compensated them. Others said: She is free; the Prophet ﷺ had set her free."],[3213,"“I am its little trimmed stump and its propped-up little palm—Hubab b. al-Mundhir.”"],[3214,"He spent the night dragging a rope on his back for two saa‘s of dates. He turned back with one of them to his family, who benefited from it, and he brought the other to draw near to God Almighty. He brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Scatter it among the charity.” The hypocrites said about him and mocked him: “This man had no need to draw near to God with a saa‘ of dates.” Then God Almighty sent down: {Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities, and those who find nothing but their effort} to the end of the two verses."],[3215,"He was called Humam, and that was in the pre-Islamic era. My uncle came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and spoke to him about his son. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Receive back your son as much as you are able.” So he went and took his son and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The boy’s master also came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ offered him two slave boys and said: “Take one of them and leave the man his son.” So he took a slave boy and left him his son."],[3216,"His grandfather came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: “What is your name?” He said: Hazn. He wanted to change his name, but he said: “I would not change a name my father gave me.” Sa‘id said: That ruggedness has remained among us until now."],[3217,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed a man over a military expedition. When he set out and then returned to him, he said to him: “How did you find command?” He said: I was like one of the people; when I rode, they rode, and when I dismounted, they dismounted. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The holder of authority stands at the gate of hardship, except for the one whom God Almighty protects.” The man said: By God, I will never work for you or for anyone else again. The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars showed."],[3218,"Some people from the tribe of Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him to send with them people who can teach them the Quran. So he sent with them seventy men from the Ansar, among them Harām ibn Milhān, the uncle of Anas. However, they betrayed them and killed them.Harām was the first to be stabbed with a spear, and blood was flowing from him. He grabbed it, raised it towards the sky, and said, \"I have won by the Lord of the Kāʿbah.\" Then the Quran was revealed regarding them, \"Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.\""],[3219,"“I saw Hashraj, a man whom the Prophet ﷺ took and placed in his lap, wiped his head, and supplicated for him.”"],[3220,"\"I was holding the halter of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel during the middle of the days of Tashriq in the Farewell Pilgrimage.\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[3221,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Giving to the poor protects against a bad death.\""],[3222,"O Messenger of God, you know Harithah's place with me. If he is among the people of Paradise, I will be patient; otherwise, you will see what I do. He said: \"O Umm Harithah, it is not one Paradise, but many Paradises, and he is in the highest Firdaws.\" She said: Then I will be patient."],[3223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Umm Harithah, it is a Paradise among Paradises, and Harithah is in the highest Firdaws. When you ask God ﷻ, ask Him for Firdaws.\""],[3224,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of the companions of al-'Aqabah from the Ansar from the Banu Bayadah: Harithah b. Malik b. Ghadib b. Jusham."],[3225,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu 'Ubayd b. 'Adi b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salamah: Harithah b. al-Humayyir, an ally of theirs from Ashja' from the Banu Dahman."],[3226,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu 'Ubayd b. 'Adi: Harithah b. al-Humayyir al-Ashja'i, an ally of theirs."],[3227,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer in Mina, two rak'ahs, when the people were greater in number and more secure.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1446)"],[3228,"That he prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ when the people were at their most secure and most numerous, at Mina, two rak'ahs. He said: And I prayed with him at al-Abtah two rak'ahs. Abu Ishaq said: It was said to him: Like whom were you that day? He said: I that day was trimming arrows and fletching them."],[3229,"\"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ at Mina while the people were at their most numerous: two rak'ahs during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\""],[3230,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina when the people were most secure and most numerous: two rak'ahs."],[3231,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he led us in prayer at Mina while we were at our fullest number: two rak'ahs."],[3232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer at Mina: two rak'ahs, when the people were most secure and most numerous."],[3233,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina when the people were most numerous and most secure, and he prayed two rak'ahs."],[3234,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina: two rak'ahs, when the people were most secure."],[3235,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman four rak'ahs."],[3236,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina when the people were most numerous and most secure: two rak'ahs."],[3237,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah and at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman at the beginning of his caliphate two rak'ahs."],[3238,"That he prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina: two rak'ahs."],[3239,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina: two rak'ahs, when the people were most numerous and most secure."],[3240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the noon prayer at Mina when the people were most secure and most numerous: two rak'ahs."],[3241,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise? Every weak and oppressed person who, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Shall I inform you of the people of Hell? Every cruel, greedy, and arrogant person.'"],[3242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"A weak man who is considered weak; were he to swear by God, He would fulfill his oath. Shall I inform you of the people of the Fire?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Every rude, arrogant miser.\""],[3243,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise? Every weak person who is considered weak; were he to swear by God, He would fulfill his oath. And the people of the Fire are every rude, haughty miser.\""],[3244,"\"Shall I inform you of the people of Paradise? Every weak person who is considered weak; were he to swear by God, He would fulfill his oath. Shall I inform you of the people of the Fire? Every rude, arrogant miser.\""],[3245,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Give charity, for a time will come upon you when a man will go about with his charity and a man will say, 'If you had brought it yesterday I would have accepted it, but today I have no need of it.'\""],[3246,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Give charity, for a time will come upon you when a man will go about with his charity and find no one to accept it.\""],[3247,"ﷺ \"Give charity, for a day will come when charity will not be accepted.\""],[3248,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"My basin is between Madinah and San'ā'.\" Al-Mustawrid said to him, \"Did you not hear him?\" He said, \"The vessels.\" Al-Mustawrid said, \"In it are vessels like the stars.\" The wording is from the hadith of Zakariyyā al-Sājī."],[3249,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"My community will continue to hold firmly to part of their religion as long as they do not entrust funerals to their families.\""],[3250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"My community will continue to be upon Islam as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars appear in imitation of the Jews, and as long as they do not hasten the Fajr prayer in imitation of the Christians, and as long as they do not entrust funerals to their families.\""],[3251,"The Prophet ﷺ taught them the prayer over the deceased: \"O God, forgive our living and our dead, set right our mutual relations, and bring our hearts together. O God, this is Your servant so-and-so son of so-and-so; we know nothing but good of him, and You know him best, so forgive us and him.\" He said: I said to him—and I was the youngest of the people—\"What if I do not know any good of him?\" He said, \"Then say only what you know.\""],[3252,"When the Prophet ﷺ heard the muezzin, he would say as he said, and when he said, \"Come to prayer; come to success,\" he would say, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\""],[3253,"I came to the gathering of the Bani Abdul-Muttalib and asked their elders how many shrouds the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was buried in. They said, \"In two red garments without a shirt.\""],[3254,"I asked the family of Muhammad ﷺ, among whom was Ibn Nawfal, in what the Messenger of God ﷺ was shrouded. They said, \"In a red garment without a shirt, and a worn velvet cloth that belonged to them was placed in his grave niche.\""],[3255,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Abu Qatadah, al-Harith b. Rib'i, and Abu Qatadah was one of the horsemen of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatadah,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him on the day of al-Mida'ah."],[3257,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys when he swayed on his mount, so I supported him with my hand until he awoke. Then he swayed again, so I supported him with my hand until he awoke. He said: \"O Allah, preserve Abu Qatadah as he preserved me since tonight. I think we have only caused you hardship.\" Abu Qatadah used to dye his hair with yellow."],[3258,"\"I saw Abu Qatadah, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn 'Umar, and Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi pass by us while we were in the Qur'anic school, and we detected from them the scent of perfume, and they dyed their beards yellow.\""],[3259,"\"I saw Zayd b. Thabit, Ibn 'Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, and Abu Qatadah wearing silk-blend mantles.\""],[3260,"\"Abu Qatadah, whose name was al-Harith b. Rib'i, died in the year fifty-four, and he was seventy years old.\""],[3261,"\"Abu Qatadah Al-Harith ibn Rib'i died in the year forty-five.\""],[3262,"That he \"saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinating facing the qiblah.\""],[3263,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever would like to be secure from the distress of the Day of Resurrection, let him give respite to a debtor in difficulty or waive the debt.\""],[3264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever sits on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent, a serpent will be appointed for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[3265,"Al-Bara' b. Ma'rur bequeathed to the Prophet ﷺ a third of his wealth to dispose of as he wished. The Prophet ﷺ returned it to his son."],[3266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit down until he prays two rak'ahs.\""],[3267,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: While he was on the pulpit speaking to the people, a man came and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended his hand and said: \"O so-and-so, did you pray two rak'ahs before sitting?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"What prevented you?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I disliked standing up while you were standing.\" Then he turned to us and said: \"When one of you enters the mosque, let him begin by praying two rak'ahs before sitting down.\""],[3268,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the Hour. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'So what have you prepared for it?' He replied, 'Love of Allah ﷻ and His Messenger ﷺ.' He said, 'Then you will be with the one you love.'"],[3269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer?' He said, 'He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.'"],[3270,"'Abu Waqid al-Laythi, whose name was al-Harith b. Malik, died in the year sixty-eight at the age of seventy.'"],[3271,"'And it is said: 'Awf b. Malik.'"],[3272,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. Numayr say, 'Abu Waqid died in the year sixty-eight.'"],[3273,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say, 'Abu Waqid al-Laythi, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was 'Awf b. al-Harith.'"],[3274,"Hisham al-Kalbi said, 'Al-Harith b. 'Awf.' Others say, ''Awf b. al-Harith b. Usayd b. Jabir b. Gharīra b. 'Abd Manāf b. Shuja' b. 'Āmir b. Layth.'"],[3275,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. Numayr say, 'Abu Waqid, and his name was al-Harith b. Malik.'"],[3276,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ toward Hunayn, and we passed by a lote tree. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as the disbelievers have a Dhat Anwat.' The disbelievers used to hang their weapons on a lote tree and devote themselves around it. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Allah is most great! This is as the Children of Israel said to Moses: {Make for us a god as they have gods.} You will surely follow the ways of those before you.'"],[3277,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sinan b. Abi Sinan al-Du'ali, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Hunayn while we were new converts from disbelief. The polytheists had a lote tree at which they would devote themselves and hang their weapons, called Dhat Anwat. He said: We passed by the lote tree and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah is most great! These are the ways. You have said, by the One in whose hand is my soul, as the Children of Israel said: {Make for us a god as they have gods. He said: You are a people who are ignorant.} You will surely follow the ways of those before you.'"],[3278,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Hunayn, he passed by a tree called Dhat Anwat on which the polytheists used to hang their weapons. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Allah is most great! This is as the Children of Israel said to Moses: {Make for us a god as they have gods.} You will surely follow the ways of those before you.'"],[3279,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were new converts from the pre-Islamic era. The disbelievers of Quraysh and other Arabs had a great tree called Dhat Anwat. They would come to it every year, hang their weapons on it, rest beneath it, and devote themselves to it for a day. While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we saw a great green lote tree. We called out from the sides of the road, 'O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat.' He said, 'Allah is most great! You have said, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, as the people of Moses said: {Make for us a god as they have gods}—the verse—'You will surely follow the ways of those before you.'"],[3280,"We set out with the Prophet ﷺ while we were recent in disbelief, having accepted Islam on the day of the conquest. We came to a tree on which the polytheists used to hang their weapons, staying by it for a year. It was called Dhat Anwat. We said, 'Make for us a Dhat Anwat.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Allah is greatest. You have said as the people of Musa said: \"Make for us a god as they have gods.\"' Then he said, 'You will surely follow the ways of those before you.'"],[3281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A servant among Allah's servants was given the choice between this world with its dominion and bliss and the Hereafter, and he chose the Hereafter.' Abu Bakr said, 'Rather we ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, with our wealth and our lives.'"],[3282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.'"],[3283,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my knee touching his knee, when a man came and clung to his ear. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed and blood rushed to his veins. Then he said, 'This is the messenger of Amir b. al-Tufayl, threatening me and threatening those near me. But Allah sufficed me against him through the sons of Isma'il, through the two sons of Qaylah.' Hisham said, 'Meaning the Ansar.'"],[3284,"We used to come to the Prophet ﷺ when revelation descended upon him, and he would speak to us. One day he said to us, 'If the son of Adam had a valley, he would love to have a second. If he had two valleys, he would love to have a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. Then Allah turns to whoever repents.'"],[3285,"When revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would come to him and he would teach us what was revealed to him. I came to him one day and he said, 'Allah, the Exalted, says: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam had a valley, he would love to have a second. If he had two, he would love to have a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents.'"],[3286,"We used to be with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when something descended upon him he would inform us of it. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A verse descended upon me: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam had a valley, he would seek a second. If he had a second, he would seek a third. Nothing fills the soul of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents.' Rabi'ah b. Uthman disagreed with Hisham b. Sa'd and Ibn Muhabbar concerning the chain of this hadith."],[3287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, Exalted is He, said, 'We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam had a valley, he would love to have two valleys. If he had two valleys, he would love to have a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents.'"],[3288,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while the people were cutting off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whatever is cut from a living animal is carrion.'"],[3289,"I heard Ubayd Allah b. Abdullah b. Utbah say: Umar ؓ went out on a day of Eid and asked Abu Waqid al-Laythi, 'With what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in the prayer on the day of Eid?' He said, 'With Qaf and Iqtarabat.'"],[3290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while we were sitting on a carpet: “There will be a fitnah.” They said: “And what should we do, O Messenger of Allah?” He withdrew his hand to the carpet and grasped it, then said: “Do like this.”"],[3291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while we were sitting on a carpet: “There will be a fitnah.” They said: “And what should we do, O Messenger of Allah?” He withdrew his hand to the carpet and grasped it, then said: “Do like this.”"],[3292,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Isḥāq b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Ṭalḥa, that Abū Murrah, the freed slave of ʿAqīl, informed him from Abū Wāqid al-Laythī that while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque with the people around him, three persons came. Two of them came toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one went away. He said: The two stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them saw a gap in the circle and sat in it; the other sat behind them; and the third turned away and left. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished, he said: “Shall I inform you about the three persons? As for one of them, he sought refuge with Allah ﷻ, so Allah gave him refuge. As for the other, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him. As for the last, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him.”"],[3293,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a circle, three persons came. One man found a gap in the circle and sat in it. Another sat behind the circle. Another man went away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you about the three? As for the one who sat in the circle, he is a man who sought refuge, so Allah gave him refuge. As for the one who sat behind the circle, he is a man who was shy, so Allah was shy of him. As for the one who turned away, Allah turned away from him.”"],[3294,"We visited Abū Wāqid al-Laythī during the illness in which he died, and I heard him say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer when leading the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself.”"],[3295,"He entered upon Abū Wāqid al-Laythī in the illness in which he died, and he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer when leading the people, and the most constant of it for himself.”"],[3296,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the lightest of people in prayer for the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself.”"],[3297,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer for the people, and the longest of people in prayer for himself.”"],[3298,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer when leading the people, and the most constant of it for himself.”"],[3299,"From Abū Wāqid al-Laythī that they said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land where we are afflicted by hunger. What is permitted for us from dead meat?” He said: “If you have not had a morning drink or an evening drink, and you have not gathered wild greens, then you may make use of it.”"],[3300,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of the Bridge in the year 15 [AH] from the Anṣār, then from Banū Muʿāwiya: al-Ḥārith b. ʿAdī b. Mālik."],[3301,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of the Bridge in the year 15 [AH]: al-Ḥārith b. Masʿūd b. ʿAbd b. Muẓāhir."],[3302,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, from Banū al-Nabīt, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: al-Ḥārith b. Aws."],[3303,"“By Allah, a woman who prevents me from the dawn prayer in congregation is indeed an evil woman.”"],[3304,"I passed by an old woman at al-Rabadha who had been left behind among Banū Tamīm. She said: “Where are you heading?” We said: “We are heading to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: “Then carry me with you, for I have a need to bring to him.” He said: I entered the mosque while it was packed with people, and there was a black banner fluttering, and Bilāl was girt with a sword standing before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I sat in the mosque. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in, he gave me permission, so I entered. He said: “Was there anything between you and Tamīm?” I said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah. We had the upper hand over them, and I passed by an old woman of theirs at al-Rabadha who had been left behind. She said: ‘I have a need to bring to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,’ so I carried her, and there she is at the door.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her permission, and she entered. When she sat down, I said: “O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to place al-Dahnāʾ between us and Tamīm, then do so, for it was ours once.” He said: The old woman started up, seized by zeal, and said: “O Messenger of Allah, then where will your Muḍar be forced to go?” He said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I am as the first one said: a young camel carried its own destruction. I carried this one without realizing that she would be an adversary against me. I seek refuge in Allah and in the Messenger of Allah from being like the envoy of ʿĀd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And what is the envoy of ʿĀd?” He said: I said: “You have come upon one who knows.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is coaxing the story out of me.” And ʿAffān said: “I seek refuge in Allah from being as the first one said.” He said: “And what did the first one say?” He said: “You have come upon one who knows.” He said: “Go on, he is coaxing the story out of him.” So he said: “ʿĀd suffered drought, and they sent their envoy Qayl. He stayed with Muʿāwiya b. Bakr for a month, who gave him wine to drink and the two jarādāt sang to him.” Sallām said: meaning the two singing-girls. He said: “Then he went on until he reached the mountains of Mahra and said: ‘O Allah, You know that I have not come to ransom a captive or to treat a sick person, so give Your servant what You are to give him to drink, and give with him Muʿāwiya b. Bakr a month of drink in gratitude for the wine he drank with him.’ He said: Then black clouds passed by, and from them it was called: ‘Choose the cloud.’ And he said: ‘This is a black cloud.’ He said: Then from it was called: ‘Take it as dust, destructive, leaving not one of ʿĀd.’” He said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that no wind was sent upon them except the amount that can be seen in a ring.” Abū Wāʾil said: “And thus it has reached us.”"],[3305,"“I arrived in Madinah and saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon while Bilāl was girt with a sword and black banners were planted. The Prophet ﷺ had sent ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ.”"],[3306,"I arrived in Madinah and saw the Prophet ﷺ standing on the pulpit, and Bilāl was standing before him girt with a sword, and there were black banners. I said: “What are these?” They said: “ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ has come back from a military expedition.”"],[3307,"We arrived in Madinah, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit, and Bilāl was standing before him girt with a sword before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there were black banners. I said: “What are these banners?” They said: “ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ has come back from a military expedition.”"],[3308,"We arrived in Madinah, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the minbar, with Bilal standing before him, girded with a sword before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there were black banners. I asked, “What are these banners?” ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ said, “He has returned from a military expedition.”"],[3309,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was walking between two of the jamrah pillars saying, “Whoever takes something of a Muslim man’s property by a false oath, let him take a seat in the Fire.”"],[3310,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “No one swears a false oath to deprive a Muslim man of his right but that he will meet Allah, may He be exalted, while He is angry with him.”"],[3311,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah, “It will not be invaded after it until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[3312,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying, \"No fighting or battles will take place after this day until the Day of Judgment.\""],[3313,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah, “It will not be invaded after this day until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[3314,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah, “It will never be invaded after this day.” Sufyān said: Its meaning is “on account of disbelief.”"],[3315,"“Al-Ḥārith b. Hishām died in Syria in the year eighteen.”"],[3316,"And Nawfal b. Maymūn narrated to me: Abū Mālik Muḥammad b. Mālik b. ʿAlī b. Harmah recited to me for his paternal uncle Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Harmah: “"],[3317,"Ibn al-Kawsaj, the client of the family of Abū Farwah, for a man"],[3318,"ʿIkrimah: Give it to ʿAyyāsh, but it did not reach any of them until they all died without tasting it."],[3319,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ, “How does the revelation come down to you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Like the ringing of a bell, and then it departs from me after I have understood what it said.” He said, “It is more intense for me, and sometimes the angel comes to me in the form of a man and speaks to me what he says.”"],[3320,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “How does the revelation come to you?” He said, “It comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and sometimes it comes to me in the form of a man who speaks to me, and that is easier for me, and then it departs from me after I have understood.”"],[3321,"Al-Harith b. Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ how the revelation came to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and that is the hardest on me; then it leaves me and I have retained what it said. And sometimes the angel appears to me as a man and speaks to me, and I retain what he says.\" 'A'ishah said: \"I saw it descending upon him on a severely cold day, and when it left him, his forehead was dripping with sweat.\""],[3322,"Al-Harith b. Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ how the revelation came to him. He said: \"Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, then it leaves me and I have retained it, and that is hardest on me. Sometimes the angel comes to me in the form of a man, and I retain what he says.\""],[3323,"The Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with her in Shawwal."],[3324,"He informed him that he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Tell me of something I can hold fast to.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Control this,\" and he pointed to his tongue."],[3325,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me of something I can hold fast to.\" He said, \"Control this for yourself,\" and he pointed to his tongue."],[3326,"He met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on his she-camel al-'Adba'. He said: I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"May Allah forgive you all.\" Then I came around from the other side hoping he would single me out, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"May Allah forgive you all.\""],[3327,"He met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on his she-camel al-'Adba'. He said: I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"May Allah forgive you all.\" Then I came around from the other side hoping he would single me out, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"May Allah forgive you all.\""],[3328,"He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Mina or at 'Arafat, and the Bedouins were coming. When they saw his face, they said, \"This is a blessed face.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"O Allah, forgive us.\" He said: Then I went around and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.\" He said, \"O Allah, forgive us.\" Then he went to spit, and he gestured with his hand, caught his spittle with it, and wiped it on his sandal, disliking that it should hit anyone around him. Then he said, \"O people, what day is this? Indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. O Allah, have I conveyed? Let the one present convey to the one absent.\" He said: And he commanded about charity, saying, \"Give charity, for I do not know—perhaps you will not see me after this day of mine.\" He set Yalamlam as the miqat for the people of Yemen to enter ihram from there, and Dhat 'Irq for the people of Iraq—or he said, \"for the people of the East.\" A man asked him about the 'atirah. He said, \"Whoever wishes may offer an 'atirah, and whoever wishes may not; and whoever wishes may offer a fara', and whoever wishes may not.\" And he said about sheep, \"Its sacrifice,\" with the fingers of his right hand, and he placed them on the joint of the middle finger and his index finger, bending the tip slightly."],[3329,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on his she-camel al-'Adba'. Al-Harith was a large man, so he dismounted and approached him until his face was level with the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ reached out to wipe the face of al-Harith, and a freshness remained on al-Harith's face until he died. Al-Harith said to him, \"O Prophet of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me.\" He said, \"O Allah, forgive us.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of 'Abd al-Warith."],[3330,"Al-Harith said: \"Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give me a legal ruling.\" So 'Umar said, \"You have gained advantage over me. You asked me about something about which you had already asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so that I might contradict him.\""],[3331,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever performs Hajj or 'Umrah, let his last act be to circumambulate the House.\" 'Umar said, \"You should have informed me sooner. You heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and did not tell me?\""],[3332,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of the Trench while he was accepting the people's pledge for emigration. We thought they were being called to the pledge, so he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, accept the pledge of this one.\" He said, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"This is my cousin, Hawt b. Yazid—or Yazid b. Hawt.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I will not accept your pledge. People emigrate to you, but you do not emigrate to them.\" Then he said, \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, no man loves the Ansar until he meets Allah except that he will meet Allah loving them, and no man hates the Ansar until he meets Allah except that he will meet Allah hating them.\""],[3333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah will love him until he meets Him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah will hate him until he meets Him.”"],[3334,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah will love him when he meets Him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah will hate him when he meets Him.”"],[3335,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There are no two Muslims who have four [children] die and they seek reward for them, except that they enter Paradise.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, and three?” He said, “And three.” It was said, “And two?” He said, “And two.”"],[3336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who has four of his children die, except that Allah will admit him to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, and three?” He said, “And three.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, and two?” He said, “And two.” He said: “And indeed among my community is one who will grow great until he becomes one of its corners, and indeed among my community is one whose intercession will bring into Paradise more than Mudar.”"],[3337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed a man from my community will enter Paradise and intercede for more than Mudar, and indeed a man from my community will become great for the Fire until he is one of its corners. And there are no two Muslims who send ahead four of their children except that Allah admits them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy.” They said, “Or three?” He said, “Or three.” They said, “Or two?” He said, “Or two.”"],[3338,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no Muslim man or Muslim woman who has four of their children die before reaching the age of accountability, except that Allah admits them to Paradise.” Then he mentioned the like of it."],[3339,"From Urwah, in naming those who attended Badr: al-Harith b. Sawwad."],[3340,"From Urwah, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar, then from Banu Adi b. al-Najjar: al-Harith b. Suraqah b. al-Harith."],[3341,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Harithah b. Suraqah."],[3342,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, when he had finished his food: “O Allah, to You belongs praise. You have fed, given drink, satisfied, and quenched thirst. To You belongs praise, unceasingly, without abandonment, and without being dispensed with, O our Lord.”"],[3343,"These people have gathered around one of their apostates. He said: So we dismounted, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling the people to the oneness of Allah, exalted is He, and to faith in Him, while they were rejecting him and harming him. When the day had reached its midpoint and the people had dispersed from him, a woman came forward, her throat exposed, carrying a cup and a towel. He took it from her, drank, and performed ablution. Then he raised his head and said, “O my little daughter, cover your throat, and do not fear for your father.” We said, “Who is this?” They said, “His daughter Zaynab.”"],[3344,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the names of those Muslims who were killed on the Day of Ajnadayn, then from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays."],[3345,"From Ibn Shihāb, regarding the names of those who were martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: al-Ḥārith b. Abī Qārib."],[3346,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq, regarding the names of those who were martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ḥārith."],[3347,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the names of the participants of the ʿAqabah pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: al-Ḥārith b. Qays b. Makhlad, and he witnessed Badr, and he is Abū Khālid."],[3348,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the names of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from al-Aws, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: al-Ḥārith b. Muʿādh b. al-Nuʿmān."],[3349,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the names of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿĀmir b. Mālik b. al-Najjār, then from Banū ʿĀmir b. Mabdhūl: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah b. ʿUbayd b. ʿĀmir."],[3350,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq, regarding the names of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, from Banū ʿĀmir b. Mālik: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah b. ʿAmr b. ʿUbayd b. ʿAmr b. Mabdhūl. He was injured at al-Rawḥāʾ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned him a share by his arrow."],[3351,"From Ibn Shihāb, regarding the names of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿĀmir b. Mālik b. al-Najjār, then from Banū Mabdhūl: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah b. ʿAmr b. ʿAtīk. He was injured at al-Rawḥāʾ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned him a share by his arrow."],[3352,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the names of those Muslims who were killed on the Day of Biʾr Maʿūnah: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah."],[3353,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'ūna: al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimma."],[3354,"That Saʿd b. Muʿādh sent al-Ḥārith b. Aws b. al-Nuʿmān, a brother of the Banū Ḥāritha, with Muḥammad b. Maslama to Ibn al-Ashraf. When they struck Ibn al-Ashraf, the point of the sword wounded al-Ḥārith’s foot, so his companions carried him."],[3355,"\"Regarding the identification of one who was martyred on the day of Uhud, first among the Ansar (the helpers of Medina), then from the tribe of Banu Amr ibn Awf, Harith ibn Aws ibn Rafi.\""],[3356,"From ʿUrwa regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Aws, then from the Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: al-Ḥārith b. Ashyam b. Rāfiʿ b. Imriʾ al-Qays b. Zayd b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal."],[3357,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “There is no emigration after the conquest; it is only faith and intention.”"],[3358,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “The mutʿa of women is forbidden,” three times."],[3359,"From ʿUrwa regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Banū Thaʿlaba b. ʿAmr b. ʿAwf: al-Ḥārith b. al-Nuʿmān."],[3360,"About Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr among the Ansar, then among the Bani Aws, then among the Bani Tha'labah ibn Amr ibn Awf, Harith ibn al-Nu'man."],[3361,"From ʿUrwa regarding the naming of those from the Anṣār who were killed on the day of Muʾta: al-Ḥārith b. al-Nuʿmān b. Yasāf b. Naḍla b. ʿAbd ʿAwf b. Ghanm."],[3362,"From ʿUrwa regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār: al-Ḥārith b. Khazma b. Abī Ghanm b. Sālim b. ʿAwf b. al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj."],[3363,"About Ibn Shihab's statement about the naming of those who participated in the Battle of Badr from the Ansar and then from the Banu Nabit, and then from the Banu Abdul-Ashhal, Harith bin Khazmah bin Adi, an ally from the Banu Salim."],[3364,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ used to place his right hand over his left hand in prayer. Abū Rāshid was not mentioned."],[3365,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ placing his right hand upon his left in prayer."],[3366,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws, then from Banu Amr b. Awf, then from Banu Umayya b. Zayd: al-Harith b. Hatib."],[3367,"From his father, regarding the naming of those who attended with Ali ؓ: al-Harith b. Hatib al-Ansari, of Banu Haritha; he returned from al-Rawha'."],[3368,"The Messenger of God ﷺ allotted to a group of the Muhajirun and Ansar their full shares on the day of Badr, although they were absent from it due to an excuse they had. Among them from the Ansar were Abu Lubaba b. Abd al-Mundhir and al-Harith b. Hatib."],[3369,"I met my paternal uncle, and he had a banner. I said, 'Where are you heading?' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and he commanded me to kill him.'"],[3370,"Al-Harith b. Amr passed by me, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had tied a banner for him. I said, 'Where has the Messenger of God ﷺ sent you?' He said, 'He sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck.'"],[3371,"I met my paternal uncle, and he had fastened a banner. I said, 'Where are you heading?' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, to strike his neck and take his property.' Thus it was narrated by Ashath b. Sawwar and Zayd b. Abi Unaysa, from Adi b. Thabit, from Yazid b. al-Bara', from his father, who said: I met my paternal uncle. Al-Suddi disagreed with them and narrated it from Adi b. Thabit, from al-Bara', who said: I met my maternal uncle—his maternal uncle was Abu Burda b. Niyar—and he did not include Yazid between Adi and al-Bara'."],[3372,"I met my maternal uncle, and he had a banner. I said, 'Where are you going?' He said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck and kill him.'"],[3373,"A thief was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, 'Kill him.' They said, 'O Messenger of God, he only stole.' He said, 'Kill him.' They said, 'O Messenger of God, he only stole.' He said, 'Cut off his hand.' Then he stole, and his foot was cut off. Then he stole during the caliphate of Abu Bakr ؓ until all his limbs were cut off. Then he stole a fifth time, and Abu Bakr ؓ said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ was more knowledgeable about this when he said, \"Kill him.\"'"],[3374,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'There will be in my community sinking, transformation, and pelting.' We said, 'For what, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'For their taking singing-girls and their drinking wine.'"],[3375,"He said to his people, 'Gather so that I may lead you in prayer like the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ.' When he gathered them, he said, 'Is there anyone among you who is not of you?' They said, 'No, except a nephew of ours.' He said, 'A people's nephew is one of them.' Then he called for a large bowl containing water and washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet. Then he led them in the noon prayer, in which he said twenty-two takbirs, saying takbir when he prostrated and when he raised his head from prostration, and he recited in the first two rak'ahs the Opening of the Book, and he made those next to him hear it."],[3376,"“Shall I lead you in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He was a man of the Ash'arites. “He called for a wide bowl of water, washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and snuffed water three times, washed his face three times and his arms, wiped his head and his ears, and wiped his feet. Then he prayed Zuhr, reciting in it the Opening of the Book and saying the takbīr twenty-two times.”"],[3377,"He said to his people, “Gather so that I may lead you in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” They gathered, and he said, “Is there anyone among you [who is not of you]?” They said, “No, except a nephew of ours.” He said, “One's sister's son is of the people.” “He called for a wide bowl containing water and performed ablution while they watched: he rinsed his mouth and snuffed water three times, washed his face three times and his arms three times, wiped his head and the top of his feet. Then he led them in Zuhr, saying the takbīr in it twenty-two times — saying takbīr when he prostrated and when he raised his head — and he recited to them in the first two rak'ahs and made those nearest to him hear.”"],[3378,"He said, “Gather so that I may lead you in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” They gathered, and he said, “Is there anyone among you besides yourselves?” They said, “No, except a nephew of ours.” He said, “The nephew of a people is one of them.” “He called for a wide bowl, performed ablution from it — rinsing his mouth and snuffing water, washing his face three times and his hands three times, and wiping his head and the top of his feet — then advanced and led them in Zuhr, reciting the Opening of the Book and making those nearest to him hear.”"],[3379,"He said, “Come, that I may show you how the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed. He stood and said the takbīr when he bowed and when he prostrated, and when he rose after the first two rak'ahs he said the takbīr.”"],[3380,"Abū Mālik al-Ash'arī said, “I shall certainly lead you in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He called for ablution water and performed ablution, then stood for prayer, arranged the men in rows and the boys behind them. He said the takbīr when he prostrated and when he raised his head, and when he stood up after the two rak'ahs. Then he said the salām to his right and to his left.” 'Abd al-Raḥmān b. Ghanm was not mentioned."],[3381,"Abu 'Amir or Abu Malik Al-Ash'ari told me: \"By Allah, he did not lie to me when he said that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There will be people in my Ummah who will make permissible silk, alcohol, and musical instruments. And there will be people who will descend next to a flag where they will travel with ease. Then a man will come to them with a need, and they will say to him, 'Come back to us tomorrow.' Allah will leave them overnight and turn others into monkeys and pigs until the Day of Judgment.\""],[3382,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God ﷻ said, “Whoever goes forth in My path as a warrior, seeking My countenance, confirming My promise, and believing in My messengers, is guaranteed by God ﷻ: either He takes his soul in the army by whatever death He wills and admits him to Paradise, or he roams in the guarantee of God ﷻ — however long his absence — until He returns him to his family with whatever reward and spoil he has obtained.” And he said, “Whoever sets out in the path of God and dies or is killed, or his horse or camel throws him and breaks his neck, or a venomous creature stings him, or he dies on his bed by whatever death God wills — he is a martyr.”"],[3383,"I heard Abū Mālik al-Ash'arī, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrate from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Some people of my community will certainly drink wine, calling it by other than its name, while stringed instruments and singing girls are played over their heads. God will cause the earth to swallow them up and will turn some of them into apes and pigs.”"],[3384,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the perfection of piety?” He said, “That you perform in secret the deed you perform openly.”"],[3385,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he turned his face toward the people.”"],[3386,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed. When he bowed, he said, “Glory be to God and with His praise,” three times, then he raised his head."],[3387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale. Subhan Allah and Alhamdulillah fill what is between the heavens and the earth. Salat is a light, and charity is proof (of one's faith), and patience is illumination, and the Quran is a proof for you or against you. Every person goes out in the morning to sell his soul, so he either frees it or destroys it.\" And this wording is from the hadith of Musa ibn Ismail, and Muslim said in his hadith: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, filling what is between the sky and the earth."],[3388,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Purity is half of faith; ‘Praise be to God’ fills the scale; ‘Glory be to God’ and ‘God is greater’ fill what is between heaven and earth; prayer is light; charity is a proof; and patience is a radiance.”"],[3389,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Four things remain in my community from the affair of the Age of Ignorance; they will not abandon them: boasting of noble lineages, slandering genealogies, seeking rain from the stars, and wailing. The wailing woman, if she does not repent before she dies, will come on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of tar and a coat of flame.” 'Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ said, “We abandoned wailing when we abandoned al-Lāt and al-'Uzzā.”"],[3390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God ﷻ commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them. He almost delayed, so 'Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them; either you command them or I command them. He said: Do not, my brother, for I fear if you precede me to them that I will be punished or swallowed by the earth. So he gathered the people in Bayt al-Maqdis until it was full, and he sat on the elevated place. He praised God and extolled Him, then he admonished them and said: God ﷻ commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them is that you worship God and associate nothing with Him. The likeness of that is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and this is my work, so work and render to me your work. But he began working and rendering his work to other than his master. Which of you would be pleased for his slave to be like that, working and rendering his work to other than him? God created you and provided for you, so worship Him and associate nothing with Him. He commanded you with prayer, so when you pray, do not turn away, for God ﷻ sets His face toward the face of His servant as long as he does not turn away. He commanded you with fasting, and the likeness of that is like a man with a band containing a pouch of musk, and everyone loves to find its scent. The mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you with charity, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy captured, tied his hand to his neck, and brought him near to strike his neck. He said: I ransom myself from you, and he began giving the little and the much until he redeemed himself from them. He commanded you with much remembrance of God, and the likeness of the remembrance of God ﷻ is like a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks, and he came to a strong fortress and secured himself in it. The most secure a servant is from Satan is when he is in the remembrance of God, the Exalted."],[3391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God ﷻ commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them. He almost delayed, so 'Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them; either you command them or I command them. He said: Do not, my brother, for I fear if you precede me to them that I will be punished or swallowed by the earth. So he gathered the people in Bayt al-Maqdis until it was full, and he sat on the elevated place. He praised God and extolled Him, then he admonished them and said: God ﷻ commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them is that you worship God and associate nothing with Him. The likeness of that is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and this is my work, so work and render to me your work. But he began working and rendering his work to other than his master. Which of you would be pleased for his slave to be like that, working and rendering his work to other than him? God created you and provided for you, so worship Him and associate nothing with Him. He commanded you with prayer, so when you pray, do not turn away, for God ﷻ sets His face toward the face of His servant as long as he does not turn away. He commanded you with fasting, and the likeness of that is like a man with a band containing a pouch of musk, and everyone loves to find its scent. The mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you with charity, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy captured, tied his hand to his neck, and brought him near to strike his neck. He said: I ransom myself from you, and he began giving the little and the much until he redeemed himself from them. He commanded you with much remembrance of God, and the likeness of the remembrance of God ﷻ is like a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks, and he came to a strong fortress and secured himself in it. The most secure a servant is from Satan is when he is in the remembrance of God, the Exalted."],[3392,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God ﷻ commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them. He was delaying, so 'Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to know them; either you command them with them, or I stand up and command them with them. Yahya said: If you precede me with them, I fear that I will be punished or swallowed by the earth. So he gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was full and people sat on the balconies. He admonished the people, then said: God commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them is that you associate nothing with God, for whoever associates anything with God, his likeness is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and my work, so render your work. But he began working and rendering his work to other than his master. Which of you would love to have a slave like that, rendering his work to other than his master? God ﷻ created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with God. God commanded you with prayer, so when you set your faces, do not turn away, for God ﷻ sets His face toward the face of His servant when he stands praying, and He does not turn His face away from him until the servant himself turns away. He commanded you with fasting, for the likeness of the fasting person is like a man with a pouch of musk among a band, none of whom has musk besides him, and all of them desire to find its scent. The scent of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you with charity, for its likeness is like a man whom the enemy seized and captured, tied his hand to his neck, and brought him forward to strike his neck. He said: Do not kill me, for I ransom myself from you with such and such wealth. So they released him, and he began collecting for them until he ransomed himself. Thus is charity: the servant ransoms himself from God's punishment. He commanded you with much remembrance of God, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy wronged, and they went swiftly in pursuit of him. He fled until he came to a strong fortress and secured himself in it. Likewise is the likeness of Satan: servants do not secure themselves from him except by the remembrance of God."],[3393,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God ﷻ commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them. He was delaying, so 'Isa said to him: You have been commanded with five words, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to know them; either you command them with them, or I stand up and command them with them. Yahya said: If you precede me with them, I fear that I will be punished or swallowed by the earth. So he gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was full and people sat on the balconies. He admonished the people, then said: God commanded me with five words, to act upon them and to command you to act upon them. The first of them is that you associate nothing with God, for whoever associates anything with God, his likeness is like a man who bought a slave from his pure wealth with gold or silver, and said: This is my house and my work, so render your work. But he began working and rendering his work to other than his master. Which of you would love to have a slave like that, rendering his work to other than his master? God ﷻ created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with God. God commanded you with prayer, so when you set your faces, do not turn away, for God ﷻ sets His face toward the face of His servant when he stands praying, and He does not turn His face away from him until the servant himself turns away. He commanded you with fasting, for the likeness of the fasting person is like a man with a pouch of musk among a band, none of whom has musk besides him, and all of them desire to find its scent. The scent of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you with charity, for its likeness is like a man whom the enemy seized and captured, tied his hand to his neck, and brought him forward to strike his neck. He said: Do not kill me, for I ransom myself from you with such and such wealth. So they released him, and he began collecting for them until he ransomed himself. Thus is charity: the servant ransoms himself from God's punishment. He commanded you with much remembrance of God, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy wronged, and they went swiftly in pursuit of him. He fled until he came to a strong fortress and secured himself in it. Likewise is the likeness of Satan: servants do not secure themselves from him except by the remembrance of God."],[3394,"He and his companions arrived in a ship, and with him was a piebald horse. When they were sent out, they found many camels belonging to the polytheists and took them. Abu Malik ordered them to slaughter a camel from them and make use of it. Then he went on foot until he came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him about his journey, his companions, and the camels they had captured. Then he returned to his companions. Those who were with the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Give us, O Messenger of God, from these camels. He said: \"Go to Abu Malik.\" When they came to him, he divided them into fifths; he sent one fifth to the Messenger of God ﷺ and took one third of the remainder after the fifth and divided it among his companions, and the remaining two thirds among the Muslims, and it was divided among them. They came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: We have not seen the like of what Abu Malik did with this booty. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If it were I, I would have done only as he did.\""],[3395,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when this verse was revealed: {Do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you}. He said: We were asking him when he said: \"God has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs; the prophets and martyrs envy them for their nearness and their seat with God ﷻ on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: In a corner of the people was a bedouin. He stood up, knelt on his knees, gestured with his hands, and said: Tell us, O Messenger of God, about them; who are they? He said: I saw the face of the Prophet ﷺ brighten. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Servants from among God's servants, from various lands and tribes of the peoples of the tribes, between whom there are no ties of kinship by which they connect for God; not for worldly gain that they exchange. They love one another by the spirit of God ﷻ. God will make their faces light, and He will make for them pulpits of pearl before the Most Merciful, the Exalted. People will be terrified, and they will not be terrified; people will fear, and they will not fear.\""],[3396,"On the authority of Abu Malik al-Ash'ari ؓ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Servants of God for whom pulpits of light will be placed on the Day of Resurrection; they are neither prophets nor martyrs, and the prophets and martyrs will envy them.\" They said: Who are they? He said: \"Those who love one another for the sake of God ﷻ.\""],[3397,"There was a man among us who had accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ, called Malik or Abu Malik. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"I have known peoples who are neither prophets nor martyrs, whom the prophets and martyrs envy, as if they are from God ﷻ—peoples from various tribes who love one another for the sake of God.\""],[3398,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prayed and placed the men nearest to him, placed the boys behind that, and placed the women behind that.\""],[3399,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in all of them,\" meaning the four [rak'ahs] of Zuhr and 'Asr."],[3400,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The sweetness of this world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of the Hereafter is the sweetness of this world.\""],[3401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Three persons: one of them had ten dinars and gave one dinar of them in charity; another had ten uqiyyas and gave one uqiyya of them in charity; and another had a hundred uqiyyas and gave ten uqiyyas in charity.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “They are equal in reward; each of them gave a tenth of his wealth.” God ﷻ said: {Let a man of wealth spend out of his wealth}."],[3402,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ has protected you from three afflictions: that your Prophet does not invoke against you so that you all perish, and that the people of falsehood do not prevail over the people of truth, and that you do not gather upon misguidance. So these are the protections from Allah for you, and your Lord has warned you of three things: the Smoke which takes the believer from it like the cold, and takes the disbeliever and he swells and comes out from every opening, and the second is the beast, and the third is the False Messiah.\""],[3403,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When a man sneezes, let him say, “Praise be to God in every situation,” and let those around him say, “May God have mercy on you,” and let him say to those around him, “May God guide you and set your affairs aright.”"],[3404,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: I do not fear for my community except three traits: that wealth becomes abundant for them and they envy one another and fight; that the Book is opened to them and the believer takes it seeking its interpretation, but none knows its interpretation except God and those firmly rooted in knowledge, who say, “We believe in it; all is from our Lord,” and none take heed except people of understanding; and that they see their man of knowledge and waste him and do not care about him."],[3405,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not associate anything with God after having believed in Him, establishes the prescribed prayer, pays the obligatory zakat, fasts Ramadan, and hears and obeys, and then dies upon that, Paradise becomes binding for him.”"],[3406,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage on the days of sacrifice to the people: “Is this not the sacred day?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “The sanctity of what is between you until the Day of Resurrection is like the sanctity of this day. I shall tell you who the Muslim is: the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. I shall tell you who the believer is: one whom the Muslims trust with their lives and their wealth. I shall tell you who the emigrant is: one who abandons evil deeds. And the believer is inviolable to the believer, like the sanctity of this day: his flesh is inviolable to him, that he should consume it by backbiting—he backbites him; his honor is inviolable to him, that he should violate it; his face is inviolable to him, that he should slap it; his blood is inviolable to him, that he should shed it; and his wealth is inviolable to him, that he should wrong him; and harming him is inviolable to him; and he is inviolable to him, that he should push him away forcefully.”"],[3407,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Your enemy is not the one whom, if you kill, it will be light for you, and if he kills you, you will enter Paradise. But your most hostile enemy is your child who came out of your own loins, then the most hostile enemy to you is your wealth that your right hand possesses.”"],[3408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Tribulation is sent, and with it are sent desire and patience. Whoever follows desire, his death will be black; and whoever follows patience, his death will be white.”"],[3409,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Three traits I have hidden from My servants; if they saw them, they would never do evil at all: if I removed My veil and they saw Me, so that they would be certain and know how I deal with My creation when I cause them to die, and I grasp the heavens with My hand, then I grasp the earth and the earths, then I say, ‘I am the King; who is there that has dominion besides Me?’ Then I show them Paradise and what I have prepared for them in it of every good, and they would be certain of it. And I show them the Fire and what I have prepared for them of every evil, and they would be certain of it. But deliberately I have hidden that from them, so that I may know how they act, and I have made it clear to them.”"],[3410,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no man who wakes up during the night and wakes his wife; if sleep overcomes her, he sprinkles water on her face; then they both stand in their house and remember God ﷻ for an hour of the night, except that they are forgiven.”"],[3411,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The most complete word with God is that a servant says: O God, You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I have wronged myself and I confess my sin, and none forgives sins except You. O Lord, forgive me.”"],[3412,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to say when we enter the morning, when we enter the evening, and when we lie down on our beds: “O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You are the Lord of everything, and the angels bear witness that there is no god but You. We seek refuge in You from the evil of our souls, from the evil of the accursed Satan and his trap, and from committing a wrong against ourselves or bringing it upon a Muslim.”"],[3413,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When the son of Adam sleeps, the angel says to Satan, “Give me your scroll,” and he gives it to him. Whatever good he finds in his scroll, he erases with it ten evil deeds from Satan’s scroll and writes them as good deeds. So when one of you wants to sleep, let him say Allahu akbar thirty-three times, praise God thirty-four times, and glorify God thirty-three times: that is one hundred."],[3414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: When a man enters his house, let him say: “O God, I ask You for the best of entering and the best of exiting. In the name of God we enter, and in the name of God we exit, and upon God our Lord we rely.” Then he should greet himself."],[3415,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: When one of you rises in the morning, let him say: “We have risen in the morning, and the dominion has risen in the morning belonging to God, Lord of the worlds. O God, I ask You for the good of this day: its opening, its victory, its light, its blessing, and its guidance. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what is in it and from the evil of what was before it and the evil of what comes after it.” Then when evening comes, let him say the like of that."],[3416,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Let one of you say when he wants to sleep: “I believe in God and disbelieve in false gods. God’s promise is true, and the messengers have told the truth. O God, I seek refuge in You from the night visitors of this night, except for a visitor who comes with good.”"],[3417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, some of you will surely be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection to Paradise like the black night – a single group surrounding the earth. The angels will say: Those who came with Muhammad are more numerous than those who came with the prophets."],[3418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God ﷻ does not look at your bodies, nor at your lineages, nor at your wealth, but He looks at your hearts. Whoever has a righteous heart, God is compassionate toward him. You are only the children of Adam, and the most beloved of you to Me is the most God-fearing of you.”"],[3419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, make death beloved to the one who knows that I am Your messenger.”"],[3420,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The promised day is the Day of Resurrection; the witness is the day of Friday; and the witnessed is the day of ʿArafah. Friday is a day God has stored up for us, and the middle prayer is the afternoon (ʿaṣr) prayer.”"],[3421,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Friday is an expiation for what is between it and the previous Friday, plus three additional days. That is because God ﷻ said: {Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times its like}.”"],[3422,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The prayers are expiations for what occurs between them, because God ﷻ said: {Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds}.”"],[3423,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “The greatest treachery in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection is a cubit of land” – or he said “a span” – “which a man steals, and the neighbor: when there is land between two people and one of them steals it from his companion, he will be made to wear it as a collar from the seven earths.”"],[3424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, and dies worshiping Allah without associating anything with Him, then it is a right upon Allah, may He be glorified, to admit him to Paradise, whether he migrated or stayed in his birthplace.” A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, if I tell this to the people they will become complacent about it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has prepared for the mujahidin in His path one hundred ranks, between each two ranks is like what is between heaven and earth. If I had the means to strengthen myself and to strengthen the Muslims, or if they had in their hands what to spend, no military expedition would set out except that I would be its companion. But that is not in my hand nor in their hands. If I went out, no one with any good in him would remain except that he would go with me, and that would be difficult for me. I would love to go on a campaign, be killed, then brought to life, then go on a campaign, be killed, then brought to life, then be killed.”"],[3425,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Whoever asks Allah for death in His path, sincerely from his own soul, then dies or is killed, he will have the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah, or is afflicted with an injury, it will come on the Day of Resurrection in the most abundant form it ever had, its color like saffron and its scent like musk. Whoever departs with wounds in the path of Allah, upon him is the seal of the martyrs.”"],[3426,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and its inside is seen from its outside. Allah has prepared it for whoever feeds food, softens speech, follows up the prayer, and stands at night while people are sleeping.”"],[3427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[3428,"From Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Jusham b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Hurayth b. Zayd b. Tha'laba."],[3429,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Hurayth b. Zayd b. Tha'laba b. Abd al-Rabb."],[3430,"I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Prophet ﷺ while I was a boy riding behind my uncle. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placing one of his two fingers over the other. I said to my uncle: “What is he saying?” He said: “He is saying: ‘Throw the pebbles with stones like those used in khazf (small pebbles).’”"],[3431,"That he witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said, “Indeed your blood and your property are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours. Indeed, have I conveyed?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness.” And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Rabiʿ."],[3432,"From Habba and Sawa’, the two sons of Khalid, they said: We entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was working on something, so we helped him. He said, “Do not despair of provision as long as your heads shake, for a person is born from his mother red, with no shell upon him, then God provides for him.”"],[3433,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, “O ʿAli, I enjoin you to do good to the Arabs; I enjoin you to do good to the Arabs.”"],[3434,"ʿUmar ؓ stood on the pulpit and said, “I adjure by God any man who heard the Messenger of God ﷺ give a judgment concerning the fetus to stand up.” Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabigha al-Hudhali stood up and said, “O Commander of the Faithful, I was between two neighbors—that is, two co-wives—and one of them struck or hit the other with the tent pole of her shelter and killed her and killed what was in her belly.” So the Prophet ﷺ judged for the fetus a ghurra, a male or female slave. ʿUmar said, “God is greatest. If we had not heard this, we would not have judged otherwise.”"],[3435,"That he had a wife, and he married another in addition to her, and the two became jealous. So the Hilali woman struck the ʿAmiri woman with the pole of my tent, and she miscarried a dead child. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, “Pay the blood money for it.” Her guardian came and said, “Should we pay blood money for one who did not eat or drink or cry out? Such a one should be disregarded.” He said, “The rhymed speech of the Bedouins? Yes, pay for it; in it is a ghurra, a male slave or a female slave.”"],[3436,"Hamal b. Malik said to ʿImran b. ʿUwaymir, “Pay me the blood money for my wife.” They brought the dispute to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “The blood money is on the ʿasaba, and for the miscarried fetus there is a ghurra, a male or female slave.”"],[3437,"That Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabigha had two co-wives, Mulayka and Umm ʿAfif. One of them threw a stone at her companion and struck her private part, and she cast a dead fetus and died. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he made her blood money the responsibility of the clan of the killer, and for her fetus he made a ghurra: a male or female slave, or twenty camels, or one hundred sheep. Her guardian said, “By God, O Prophet of God, it did not eat or drink or cry out, so such a one should be disregarded.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “We have nothing to do with the rhymed prose of the Age of Ignorance.”"],[3438,"From ʿUrwa, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of God ﷺ: Hanzala b. Abi ʿAmir b. Sayfi b. Nuʿman, the one washed by the angels."],[3439,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Hanzala b. Abi ʿAmir, and he is the one whom the angels washed."],[3440,"The Aws and Khazraj tribes boasted, and Aws said, \"We have four individuals.\" Khazraj said, \"We have four individuals as well.\" Aws said, \"Among us is Sa'd bin Mu'adh, whose shaking caused the Throne of the Most Merciful to tremble. Among us is also Khuzaimah bin Thabit, whose testimony is equivalent to that of two men. Among us is Hanzala bin Al-Rabi', who was washed by the angels. Among us is also Asim bin Thabit bin Al-Aflah, who protected his backside.\" Khazraj said, \"Among us are four individuals who gathered the Quran during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and no one else did so. They are Ubay bin Ka'b, Mu'adh bin Jabal, Zaid bin Thabit, and Abu Zaid.\" I asked Anas, \"Who is Abu Zaid?\" He replied, \"One of my uncles.\""],[3441,"We went on a raid with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we passed by a woman who had been killed. The people had gathered around her, and they made way for the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “This woman was not one to have fought.” Then he said: Go and catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and tell him: Do not kill children or a hired laborer (ʿasīf)."],[3442,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he mentioned Paradise and Hell. We were overwhelmed with joy and I went back to my family and laughed with them. Something then occurred to me and I met Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, \"Indeed, I have become a hypocrite.\" He asked, \"And what is that?\" So I said, \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he mentioned Paradise and Hell, and it was as if we saw them with our own eyes. But when I came back to my family, I laughed with them.\" Abu Bakr said, \"We also do the same.\" So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him about it. He said, \"O Hanthalah, if you were to remain in the state you are in while you are with your family, angels would shake hands with you on your beds and on your paths, O Hanthalah, for an hour and an hour.\""],[3443,"“We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we spoke of Paradise and Hell until it was as if we could see them. Then I got up and went to my family and children, and I laughed and played (with them). Then I remembered how we had been, and I went out and met Abu Bakr, and said: ‘I have become a hypocrite!’ Abu Bakr said: ‘We all do that.’” So Hanzalah went and mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “O Hanzalah, if you were (always) as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you in your beds and in your streets. O Hanzalah, there is a time for this and a time for that.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4239)"],[3444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you were to remain as you are when you are with me, the angels would shade you with their wings.”"],[3445,"It is said of him: the scribe of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever guards the five prayers – or the prescribed prayer – with its ablution, its times, its bowing, and its prostration, seeing it as a duty owed by him, Allah will make the Fire forbidden to him.”"],[3446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ali ibn Abi Talib and Khalid ibn al-Walid to Yemen and said, \"When you are together, I am the leader, and when you separate, each of you is responsible for his own work.\" Khalid ibn al-Walid wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and started with himself, and the Prophet ﷺ did not object to that. Ali also wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and he was pleased with him, so he started with the Prophet ﷺ ."],[3447,"“Al-Muqawqas, the ruler of the Copts, sent a gift to the Prophet ﷺ, together with a gray mule, and he ﷺ accepted it.”"],[3448,"“I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw him sitting cross-legged.”"],[3449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “used to like a man to be called by the most beloved of his names to him and the most beloved of his kunyahs.”"],[3450,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have an orphan under my care, and I gave one hundred camels in charity on his behalf.” I saw anger in his face, and he said, “No. Charity is five, or ten, or fifteen, up to forty.”"],[3451,"His father is Hidhyam. “O Messenger of Allah, I have sons, and this is the youngest of my sons, so invoke blessing upon him.” He said, “Come here, O boy.” He took me by the hand and wiped my head and said, “May Allah bless him.” He said: I saw Hanzala when a person with a swelling was brought to him; he would wipe his hand over it and say, “In the name of Allah,” and the swelling would go away."],[3452,"On the authority of his father, in the naming of those who were present with Ali among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hanzala b. al-Nuʿman."],[3453,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing at Arafah during the Farewell Pilgrimage. A bedouin came and took hold of the edge of his cloak and asked him for it, so he gave it to him and he went off with it. At that point, begging was prohibited. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied, except in cases of crushing poverty or overwhelming debt.” And he said, “Whoever asks people in order to increase his wealth, it will be scratches on his face and hot stones that he eats from Hellfire. So let him who wishes ask little, and let him who wishes ask much.”"],[3454,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever asks people without being in need, it is as though he is taking live coals into his mouth.”"],[3455,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever asks without being poor, it is as if he is eating live coals.”"],[3456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks without being poor, it is as if he is eating from live coals.”"],[3457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks without being poor, it is as if he is eating live coals.” Al-Hadrami said: Ghusn b. Hammad is Ghusn b. Muhammad b. Yunus b. Ishaq."],[3458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten?” He said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” He said in the third and fourth time: “And those who shorten.”"],[3459,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” It was said, “And those who shorten?” He said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” It was said, “And those who shorten?” He said: “O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.” He said in the fourth time: “And those who shorten.”"],[3460,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ali is from me and I am from him, and no one fulfills on my behalf except me or Ali.” Abu b. Abi Shaybah added in his hadith: Sharik said: I said, “O Abu Ishaq, did you see him?” He said: “He stood over us in our gathering and narrated this to us.”"],[3461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one will settle my debt other than me or Ali.”"],[3462,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ali is from me and I am from him, and no one fulfills on my behalf except me or Ali ؓ.”"],[3463,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: “O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him, and support whoever supports him, and help whoever helps him.”"],[3464,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said to Ali: “You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.”"],[3465,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Al-ma‘k is a part of injustice.”"],[3466,"Habib b. Maslama died in the year forty-two, and his age was fifty years."],[3467,"The Prophet ﷺ gave as extra share the third after the fourth."],[3468,"The Prophet ﷺ gave as extra share the third after the fifth."],[3469,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving as extra share the third in his initial expedition."],[3470,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving as extra share the third."],[3471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give as extra share in the initial expedition the fourth, and in the return the third."],[3472,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave as extra share the fourth and the third."],[3473,"The Prophet ﷺ gave as extra share the fourth of what the people brought in the initial expedition, and in the return the third after the fifth."],[3474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give as extra share, when he set out in a military expedition, the fourth after the fifth, and give as extra share, when he returned, the third after the fifth."],[3475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave as extra share the third."],[3476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave as extra share in the initial expedition the fourth, and in the return the third."],[3477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give us as extra share in our initial expedition the fourth, and in the return the third."],[3478,"'Amr said, 'No extra share after the Prophet ﷺ.' Sulayman said to him, 'The people of raisins distracted you at al-Ta'if. Makhul narrated to us from Ziyad b. Jariya from Habib b. Maslama that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave as extra share in the initial expedition the fourth, and in the return the third.'"],[3479,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ 'give as spoil a quarter in the first expedition and a third in the return.'"],[3480,"The Messenger of God ﷺ 'gave as spoil a quarter in the first expedition and a third in the return.'"],[3481,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ 'give as spoil a quarter in his first expedition and a third in his return, in a military campaign.'"],[3482,"We camped at Dabiq, with Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah over us, and Habib b. Maslama learned that the leader of Cyprus had set out toward the road of Adhribijan with emeralds, rubies, pearls, gold, and silk brocade among horsemen, so he killed him and brought what was with him. Abu Ubayda wanted to take one-fifth of it, but Habib said: 'Do not deprive me of provision God has granted me, for the Messenger of God ﷺ assigned the spoils to the killer.' Muadh said: 'O Habib, I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A person only has what his leader's soul is pleased with.\"'"],[3483,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The owner of the riding beast is more entitled to its front.' Habib said: 'I am not ignorant of what the Messenger of God ﷺ said, but I fear for you.'"],[3484,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Visit occasionally, and you will increase in love.'"],[3485,"He was appointed commander over an army and he entered the mountain passes. When he met the enemy, he said to the people: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"No group gathers and some of them supplicate while the rest say ameen except that God answers them.\"' Then he praised God and extolled Him, and said: 'O God, preserve our blood and make our rewards the rewards of martyrs.' While they were in that state, the hinbat, the commander of the enemy, came down and entered Habib's tent. Abu al-Qasim said: 'Al-hinbat in Byzantine means the leader of the army.'"],[3486,"We ate lunch with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us was Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah. He said: 'O Messenger of God, is anyone better than us? We embraced Islam with you.' He said: 'Yes, a people who will come after you, who believe in me without having seen me.'"],[3487,"He said: 'Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: 'Yes, I will tell you a good hadith. We ate lunch with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us was Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah. He said: \"O Messenger of God, is anyone better than us? We believed in you and strove with you.\" He said: \"A people who will come after you, who believe in me without having seen me.\"'"],[3488,"We went on a military campaign with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us was Abu Ubayda b. al-Jarrah. He said: 'Is anyone better than us, O Messenger of God? We embraced Islam, migrated, and strove with you.' He said: 'Yes, a people who will come after me, who believe in me without having seen me.'"],[3489,"Abu Jumua al-Ansari, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, came to us in Jerusalem to pray there, and Raja b. Haywa was with us that day. When he finished, we went out with him to see him off. When we wanted to depart, he said: 'You have a right and a reward upon me, that I tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.' We said: 'Give it, may God have mercy on you.' He said: 'We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us was Muadh b. Jabal, ten of us. We said: \"O Messenger of God, are there any people with greater reward than us? We believed in you and followed you.\" He said: \"What prevents you from that, while the Messenger of God ﷺ is among you and revelation comes to you from heaven? Rather, a people to whom a book between two covers comes, and they believe in it and act according to what is in it. Those have greater reward than you. Those have greater reward than you. Those have greater reward than you.\"'"],[3490,"We said: 'O Messenger of God, is anyone better than us?' He said: 'A people who will come after you, who will find a book between two covers, believe in it, and accept it as true. They are better than you.'"],[3491,"From Abu Jumʿa Ḥabīb b. Sibāʿ—he was one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ—that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed Maghrib and forgot ʿAṣr. He said to his Companions, “Did you see me pray ʿAṣr?” They said, “No, O Messenger of God.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the muezzin, who called the adhān, then the iqāma, and he prayed ʿAṣr, and the first one was shortened, then he prayed Maghrib."],[3492,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The Muslims are brothers; none has virtue over another except through God-consciousness.”"],[3493,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, “My father is an old man who owes the ḥajj of Islam, but he cannot travel except lying crosswise. Should I perform ḥajj on his behalf?” He remained silent, then said, “Perform ḥajj on behalf of your father.”"],[3494,"I said, “O Messenger of God, my father has lived to see the ḥajj but cannot perform it except lying crosswise.” He remained silent for a while, then said, “Perform ḥajj on behalf of your father.”"],[3495,"I said, “O Messenger of God, my father is an old, weak man. He has performed all the rites of Islam except the ḥajj, and he cannot stay upright on a camel. Should I perform ḥajj on behalf of my father?” He said, “Tell me, if your father owed a debt, would you pay it?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then God’s debt is more worthy of being paid.”"],[3496,"Al-Ḥuṣayn, the father of ʿImrān b. al-Ḥuṣayn al-Khuzāʿī, came to the Prophet ﷺ as an idolater and said, “O Muḥammad, ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib was better for his people than you.” He then mentioned a similar tradition to that of Shaybān."],[3497,"That he came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him with the pledge of Islam, and gave him the charity of his wealth; and the Prophet ﷺ granted him the waters of several places at al-Maruth, and the ascription of Jarad, among them Usayhib, and among them al-Maghira, and among them Ahwa', and among them al-Thimad, and among them al-Sudayra. And the Prophet ﷺ stipulated upon Husayn b. Mushmit, regarding what he granted, that its pasture should not be uprooted and its water should not be sold. And the Prophet ﷺ stipulated upon Husayn b. Mushmit that \"he should not sell its water and should not withhold its surplus.\" Then Zuhayr b. 'Asim b. Husayn recited some poetry."],[3498,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in \"Naming Those Who Witnessed Badr: Husayn b. al-Harith b. 'Abd Manaf.\""],[3499,"From his father, in \"Naming Those Who Witnessed with 'Ali: Husayn b. al-Harith, a Badri; he witnessed with him all his battles, from the Banu al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf.\""],[3500,"\"O Messenger of God, command the people of the valley to help me and to treat me well in their dealings with me.\" So he commanded them, and they stood with him and treated him well in their dealings. Then he called him, passed his hand over his face, and supplicated for him."],[3501,"That he carried food to Madinah and met the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said, \"What are you carrying, O Bedouin?\" He said, \"Wheat.\" He said, \"What did you intend with it, or what do you intend with it?\" He said, \"I intended to sell it.\" Then he wiped my head and said, \"Be good in trading with the Bedouin.\""],[3502,"We came to Madinah while the Prophet ﷺ was there, and with me were some camels of mine. I said, \"O Messenger of God, command the people of the lowland to treat me well in their dealings with me and to help me.\" He said, \"So they stood with me.\" When I had sold my camels, I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, \"Come closer.\" Then he passed his hand over my forelock and supplicated for me three times."],[3503,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is nothing in the hāmah, and the evil eye is real, and the truest of birds is the fa'l.\""],[3504,"I saw Hujr b. ʿAdī when Muʿāwiyah seized him, and he was saying, “This is my pledge of allegiance: I will not retract it, nor will I ask to be released from it, with God and the people as witnesses.”"],[3505,"ʿAlī ؓ proposed to the Messenger of God ﷺ for Fāṭimah ؓ. He said, “She is yours, on condition that you treat her well as a companion.”"],[3506,"From Ḥayyān b. Buḥḥ al-Ṣudāʾī, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: He said, “My people disbelieved. I was told that the Prophet ﷺ was preparing an army against them, so I went to him and said, ‘My people are upon Islam.’ He said, ‘Is that so?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘So I followed him that night until morning, and I announced the prayer. When morning came, he gave me a vessel and I performed ablution from it. The Prophet ﷺ placed his fingers in the vessel, and springs gushed forth. He said, ‘Whoever among you wishes to perform ablution, let him do so.’ So I performed ablution and prayed, and he appointed me over them and gave me their charity.”"],[3507,"From Ḥayyān b. Buḥḥ al-Ṣudāʾī, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: He said, “My people disbelieved. I was told that the Prophet ﷺ was preparing an army against them, so I went to him and said, ‘My people are upon Islam.’ He said, ‘Is that so?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘So I followed him that night until morning, and I announced the prayer. When morning came, he gave me a vessel and I performed ablution from it. The Prophet ﷺ placed his fingers in the vessel, and springs gushed forth. He said, ‘Whoever among you wishes to perform ablution, let him do so.’ So I performed ablution and prayed, and he appointed me over them and gave me their charity.”"],[3508,"From Ḥayyān b. Buḥḥ al-Ṣudāʾī, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: He said, “My people disbelieved. I was told that the Prophet ﷺ was preparing an army against them, so I went to him and said, ‘My people are upon Islam.’ He said, ‘Is that so?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘So I followed him that night until morning, and I announced the prayer. When morning came, he gave me a vessel and I performed ablution from it. The Prophet ﷺ placed his fingers in the vessel, and springs gushed forth. He said, ‘Whoever among you wishes to perform ablution, let him do so.’ So I performed ablution and prayed, and he appointed me over them and gave me their charity.”"],[3509,"I heard Ḥayyān, the grandfather of Ibn Abjar al-Akbar, say, “Leave off medicine as long as your body can bear the illness.”"],[3510,"The owner of this house, Ḥarīz or Abū Ḥarīz, told me: “When I reached the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, I placed my hands on the cushion of his saddle and found it to be from the skin of a wool-bearing sheep.”"],[3511,"Hassan b. Thabit died in the year fifty-four."],[3512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to place a pulpit for Hassan b. Thabit in the mosque, upon which he would recite poetry. She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, support him with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends Your Prophet.”"],[3513,"The Prophet ﷺ placed a pulpit for Hassan, upon which he recited satire against the polytheists."],[3514,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Satirize Quraysh, for it is harder on them than a volley of arrows.” He sent for Ibn Rawaha and said, “Satirize them,” so he satirized them, but he was not satisfied. Then he sent for Ka'b b. Malik, then he sent for Hassan b. Thabit. When Hassan entered, he said: “It is time for you to send for this lion who strikes with his tail.” Then he stuck out his tongue and began wagging it. He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall flay them as leather is flayed.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not be hasty, for Abu Bakr knows Quraysh's genealogies better than anyone, and I have kinship among them, so that my lineage may be made clear to you.” Hassan went to him and then returned, saying: “O Messenger of God, your lineage has been made clear to me. By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough.” A'isha said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Hassan: “The Holy Spirit will never cease to support you as long as you defend God and His Messenger.” She said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Hassan satirized them, and he healed and was satisfied.” Hassan said:"],[3515,"Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ passed by a gathering of the Prophet's ﷺ Companions while Hassan b. Thabit was reciting his poetry to them, and they were not attentive to what they heard from him. Al-Zubayr sat with them and said: “Why do I see you not listening to the poetry of Ibn al-Furay'a? He used to present it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would listen well, generously reward him, and not be distracted from him by anything.” Hassan said:"],[3516,"He said to him: “I adjure you by God, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Respond on my behalf, may God support you with the Holy Spirit?’” He said: “O God, yes.”"],[3517,"Hassan recited poetry in the mosque, and Umar ؓ passed by him and glanced at him, saying: “In the mosque? In the mosque?” Hassan said: “By God, I recited in it to one better than you.” Umar feared that he meant the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he let him be and left him."],[3518,"I used to recite in it to one better than you. Umar ؓ turned away, fearing that he would say the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: “I adjure you by God, do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘O Hassan, respond on behalf of the Messenger of God. O God, support him with the Holy Spirit’?” He said: “Yes.”"],[3519,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Hassan, \"Lampoon them (i.e. the pagans) and Gabriel is with you.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3213)"],[3520,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Satirize them—or ‘satirize them’—meaning the polytheists, for Gabriel is with you.”"],[3521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Hassan, \"Verily, the Holy Spirit is with you as long as you befriend them.\" He means the polytheists."],[3522,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves."],[3523,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves."],[3524,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Trench while he was taking the people’s pledge for emigration. He said: O Messenger of God, accept the pledge of this one for emigration. He said: “And who is this?” He said: My cousin Hawt b. Yazid, or Yazid b. Hawt. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I will not accept your pledge. The people emigrate to you, but you do not emigrate to them.”"],[3525,"When he accepted Islam, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and recited poetry to him."],[3526,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Mecca, migrating to Madinah, he was accompanied by Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr's servant Amir b. Fuhayrah, and their guide Abdullah b. Urayqit. They passed by the two tents of Umm Mabad al-Khuzaiyyah. She was a strong woman who would sit in front of her tent and provide water and food to travelers. They asked her for some meat and dates to purchase, but found nothing with her as the people were facing a severe famine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed a sheep in the corner of the tent and asked, \"What is this sheep, O Umm Mabad?\" She replied, \"This sheep has been left behind by weakness.\" He asked, \"Does it have any milk?\" She replied, \"It is too weak for that.\" He ﷺ asked, “Would you allow me to milk it?” She replied, \"Yes, may my parents be sacrificed for you, if you see any milk in it, then milk it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the sheep, put his hand on its udder, and invoked the name of Allah. Suddenly, milk started flowing abundantly. He ﷺ called for a large container which could satisfy the thirst of many people. He milked it until it filled the container, then gave her to drink until she was satisfied, and then he gave to his companions to drink until they were satisfied. Finally, he ﷺ drank. Then he repeated the milking to fill the container again, leaving it with her. Shortly after they left, Umm Mabad's husband, Abu Mabad, returned driving some lean goats whose udders were dry. When he saw the milk, he was astonished and asked, \"From where did you get this milk, O Umm Mabad, as the sheep is dry and there's no milking goat in the house?\" She replied, \"No, by Allah, a blessed man passed by us.\" He asked, \"Describe him to me, O Umm Mabad.\" She replied, \"I saw a man of radiant appearance, with a bright face, beautiful in form. Neither too thin nor deficient in physique. He was handsome and well-proportioned, with large dark eyes, long eyelashes, and a deep, slightly hoarse voice. His neck was well-defined, and his beard was thick. His eyebrows were long and arched, and if he remained silent, he was enveloped in dignity, but when he spoke, he was adorned with grace and majesty. From a distance, he was the most beautiful of people, and up close, he was the most pleasant and delightful. His speech was sweet, distinct, neither too brief nor excessive, as if his words were strung pearls flowing down. He was neither too tall to intimidate nor too short to be disregarded, but perfectly proportioned, like a branch between two other branches, the most striking and noble of the three. He was surrounded by companions who were attentive to him. When he spoke, they listened intently, and when he commanded, they hastened to fulfill his command. He was well-attended, always surrounded by people, yet never frowning nor disregarded.” Abu Mabad said, \"By Allah, he is the companion of Quraysh whom we were informed about. I have decided to accompany him, and if I find a way to do so, I will surely do it.\" Later, there was a loud voice in Mecca heard from the sky, saying..."],[3527,"He mentioned seventy of the Ansar. When night fell upon them, they would retire to a teacher in Madinah and spend the night studying the Quran. When morning came, those who had strength would gather firewood and fetch fresh water, and those who had means would get a sheep and prepare it. It would be hanging by a stone of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the morning. When Khubayb was killed, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent them out, and among them was my maternal uncle Haram. They came to a clan of Banu Sulaym. Haram said to their commander: Shall I tell these people that we are not after them, so that they leave us alone? He said: So he went to them and told them that. A man among them met him with a spear and thrust it through him. When Haram felt the touch of the spear in his belly, he said: God is greatest! I have won, by the Lord of the Ka‘bah. They were delayed against them, and no one survived to bring news. I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ grieve over an expedition as he grieved over them. Anas said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ every time he prayed the dawn prayer raise his hands supplicating against them.” After that, Abu Talhah came to me and said: Would you like to confront the killer of Haram? I said: What is the matter with him? May God do to him and do. Abu Talhah said: Do not do that, for he has accepted Islam."],[3528,"He is called Humamah, one of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. He went out as a warrior to Isfahan during the caliphate of Umar ؓ, and Isfahan was conquered. Humamah said, \"O Allah, Humamah claims that he loves to meet You. If he is truthful, then decree for him upon it with sincerity, and if he is lying, then decree for him upon it even if he dislikes it.\" Then he was seized by a stomach illness and died in Isfahan. Abu Musa said, \"O people, by Allah, we have not heard in what we have heard from your Prophet ﷺ and what our knowledge has reached except that Humamah is a martyr.\""],[3529,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr: \"Among those who witnessed Badr was Khabbab b. al-Aratt b. Khuwaylid b. Sa'd b. Jadhima b. Ka'b b. Sa'd.\""],[3530,"\"Khabbab b. al-Aratt was a freed slave of Banu Zuhrah. He witnessed Badr and was given the kunya Abu Abdullah. He died in the year thirty-seven, when Ali ؓ returned from Siffin to Kufa, and he was the first of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to be buried in Kufa. Khabbab's Islam was in Makkah.\""],[3531,"I heard Kurdus say: \"Khabbab embraced Islam as the sixth of six; he was one-sixth of Islam.\""],[3532,"\"It is not with me, but upon you is the one who took it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Upon you is Abu Abdullah Khabbab b. al-Aratt.\""],[3533,"\"In this chest there are eighty thousand, for which no purse-string was tied and no beggar was turned away. I wish it were such-and-such\" — either he said, \"dung\" or something else."],[3534,"Khabbab returned with remnants of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . They said, \"Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, your brothers will come before you tomorrow.\" So he cried and then said, \"Indeed, those [companion] have already gone with their rewards, and I fear that my recompense for those actions will be what we have been given after them.\""],[3535,"\"...that he be buried among the people of Kufa.\""],[3536,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Kaaba, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists and they had exhausted us. I said, 'Won't you supplicate for us?' He said, 'Among those before you, a man would be seized and combed with iron down to his flesh and bones, and that would not turn him away from his religion.'"],[3537,"He said, \"I will not repay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad ﷺ.\" I said, \"No, by Allah, I will not disbelieve in him until you die and are resurrected.\" He said, \"When I am resurrected, I will have wealth and children, and I will repay you your due.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses} the verse."],[3538,"We said to Khabbab: How did you know the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Ashura: \"O people, whoever of you has eaten, let him not eat for the rest of his day, and whoever of you intended to fast, let him fast it.\""],[3540,"He was brought his shroud, and white fine Egyptian linen was spread over him. He wept. They said, \"What makes you weep, O Abu Abdullah, when you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"I remembered Mus'ab b. Umayr, who did not hasten to enjoy any of its good things. He was shrouded in a burdah, and nothing was found to shroud him in it. When we covered his head with it, his feet stuck out, and when we covered his feet, his head stuck out, until we placed idhkhir and plants of the earth over him.\""],[3541,"Some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Khabbab. They said, \"Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, you will come to Muhammad ﷺ at the Hawd.\" He said, \"How can I, with this?\" and he pointed to the upper part of his house and its lower part. The Prophet ﷺ had said: \"What suffices any of you in this world is like the provision of a rider.\""],[3542,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When you fast, use the tooth-stick in the morning, but do not use it in the evening; for there is no fasting person whose lips become dry in the evening except that it becomes light between his eyes on the Day of Resurrection.\" 'Ali did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[3543,"Who among us complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat of the hot season, but he did not complain and said, \"When the sun sets, then pray\"?"],[3544,"I entered upon Khabbab and saw in his house uncovered dirhams. I said, “What is this?” He said, “I sold my such-and-such estate, and I have spent it. I do not see anyone more entitled to it than myself.”"],[3545,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Horses are of three kinds: a horse for the Most Merciful, a horse for man, and a horse for Satan. The horse of the Most Merciful is that which is kept for the cause of God and upon which the enemies of God, may He be exalted, are fought. The horse of man is that which is used for breeding and for carrying loads. The horse of Satan is that which is staked for gambling and wagered upon.”"],[3546,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ that he never went to his bed without reciting “Say: O disbelievers” until he completed it."],[3547,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me on an errand. I said, “O Messenger of God, you are sending me far away while I am anxious about you.” He said, “What has your anxiety about me reached?” I said, “I wake in the morning and do not think you will reach the evening, and I reach the evening and do not think you will reach the morning.” He said, “O Khabbab, [there are] five things: if you do them, you will see me, and if you do not do them, you will not see me.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what are they?” He said, “Worship God, associating nothing with Him, even if you are cut up and burned, and believe in divine decree.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what is belief in divine decree?” He said, “Know that what befalls you could not have missed you, and that what misses you could not have befallen you. Do not drink wine, for its sin knocks against other sins just as its tree clings to trees. Be dutiful to your parents, even if they command you to leave this world. And hold fast to the rope of the community, for God’s hand is upon the community. O Khabbab, if you see me on the Day of Resurrection, you will not be separated from me.”"],[3548,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O God, cover my faults, calm my fears, and settle my debt.”"],[3549,"We traveled with him, that is ʿAlī, when he came back from Ṣiffīn until he was at the door or Kūfah and we were at the graves of seven [people] toward our right and ʿAlī then said, \"Whose graves are these?\" They said, \"O Leader of the Believers, Khabbāb b. al-Aratt passed away after you left to go to Ṣiffīn. His wished to be buried behind Kūfah. The people buried their dead in their yards and at the doorsteps of their houses. But when they [heard from] Khabbāb wishing to be buried behind [Kūfah], the people then buried [him there.]\"ʿAlī then said, \"May Allah have Mercy on Khabbāb. He accepted Islam with zeal, emigrated in obedience, lived as a mujāhid (fighter in the cause of Allah), and was heavily tested [by Allah] with his body in various ways. Allah will never overlook the reward of the one who did iḥsān (excelled) in deeds.\"Then he drew closer to the graves and said, \"Peace be upon you all, O people of the abodes, from the believers and the Muslims, you are our forerunners and predecessors and we are your followers and soon [shall] be meeting you. O Allah, forgive us and them and be increasingly pardoning of us and them. Glad tidings to the one who remembered the place of return, worked for [an easy] accounting, was content with little provision, and was pleased with Allah ﷻ.\""],[3550,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they do not practice ruqya, nor seek ruqya, nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[3551,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A believer does not spend any expenditure except that he is rewarded for it, except the expenditure on this dust.\""],[3552,"He watched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he prayed until it was near dawn. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you tonight pray a prayer the like of which I have not seen you pray?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed, it was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord ﷻ for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us with what He destroyed the nations, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set an enemy over us who would destroy us, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make my ummah into factions, and He withheld it.\""],[3553,"I watched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a prayer he performed until it was near dawn. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, Khabbab stood and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, tonight you prayed a prayer the like of which I have not seen you pray?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed, it was a prayer of hope and fear. In it I asked my Lord ﷻ for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us with what He destroyed the nations before us, and He granted them to me. I asked Him not to let an enemy from other than them prevail over us, and He granted them to me. I asked Him not to make us into factions, and He withheld it from me.\""],[3554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed a prayer and lengthened it. They said, “O Messenger of God, you prayed a prayer that you had not been praying.” He said, “Yes, indeed. It is a prayer of desire and fear. I asked my Lord three things in it; He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my community through a widespread famine, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set over them an enemy from other than themselves, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make some of them taste the violence of others, and He withheld that from me.”"],[3555,"I observed the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I will certainly watch how the Messenger of God ﷺ prays.” He prayed, and when he finished, I came to him from in front of him and said, “O Messenger of God, tonight you prayed a prayer the like of which I have not seen you pray.” He said, “It is a prayer of fear and hope. I asked my Lord three things in it; He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us with what He destroyed the nations before us, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set an enemy over us, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make us into conflicting factions, and He withheld that from me.”"],[3556,"We were sitting at the door of the Prophet ﷺ when he came out to us and said, “Do you hear?” We said, “We have heard—twice or thrice.” He said, “There will be rulers over you. Do not affirm their lies and do not help them in their wrongdoing. Whoever affirms their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing will not come to me at the pool.”"],[3557,"A man from ʿAbd al-Qays who used to sit with us in the congregational mosque related to us: He said, “I accompanied the people of the canal and was among them. Then I came to dislike their affair, fearing lest they kill me. While I was with a group of them, we came upon a village, and between us and the village was a canal. A man came out of the village, terrified. They said to him, ‘It is as if we frightened you.’ He said, ‘Yes.’ They said, ‘No fear for you.’ I said, ‘By God, they know him, but I did not know him.’ They said, ‘Are you the son of Khabbab, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ They said, ‘Have you heard a hadith from your father that you would narrate to us about the Messenger of God ﷺ?’ He said, ‘Yes. I heard my father narrate from the Prophet ﷺ that he mentioned a trial and said, “The one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it is better than the one running. If it reaches you, then be the servant of God who is killed.”’” He said, “They brought him to the bank of the canal and slaughtered him. I saw his blood flowing in the water like a strap, not dispersing. He said, “They took the mother of his child and killed her; she was pregnant, and they ripped open her belly. I never accompanied a people whose company was more hateful to me than theirs, until I found an opportunity to slip away and escaped.”"],[3558,"I was with the Kharijites when we came upon a man. They said, “Are you ʿAbd Allah b. Khabbab, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Yes.” They said, “Will you narrate to us from your father, from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Yes. I heard my father narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘There will be a trial in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running. When that occurs, be the servant of God who is killed.’” They said to him, “Then be the servant of God who is killed.” He said, “They brought him to the bank of the canal and struck his neck, and his blood flowed as if it were a sandal strap, not dispersing. Then they brought the mother of his child and ripped open what was in her belly. When I saw that, I left them.”"],[3559,"When the people dispersed, I accompanied a people whose company was not more beloved to me than theirs. We traveled along the bank of a canal, and a mosque was visible to us. In it there was a man. When he saw the forelocks of the horses, he came out in alarm, dragging his garment. Our commander said to him, “Why are you alarmed?” He said, “You have frightened me.” He said, “It is ʿAbd Allah b. Khabbab.” Our commander said to him, “Narrate to us a hadith you heard from your father, narrating from the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He narrated from his father that the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned a trial: “The one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it is better than the one running. If it reaches you, then be the servant of God who is killed.” He said, “They brought him to the bank of the canal and slaughtered him. I saw his blood flowing in the water like a strap, not dispersing.” He said, “Then they took the mother of his child and killed her; she was pregnant, and they ripped open her belly. I never accompanied a people more hateful to me than them, until I found an opportunity to slip away and escaped.”"],[3560,"I entered upon Khabbab to visit him, and he had cauterized himself seven times in his belly. Khabbab said, “Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it. Indeed, our companions passed on and did not attain anything of this world. But we have attained after them, until we find no place for it except in the dust. A person is rewarded for all his spending, except for something he puts into this dust.” He said, “And at that time he was building a wall for himself.”"],[3561,"We came to Khabbab to visit him, and he had cauterized himself seven times in his belly. He said, “Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it.” Then he mentioned those of his companions who had passed on: they passed on and had not consumed anything of their rewards, while we remained after them until we attained from this world such that one of us does not know what to do with it except to spend it on the dust. And a Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends, except what he spends on the dust.”"],[3562,"I came to Khabbab, and he had cauterized himself seven times in his belly. He said, “Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it.”"],[3563,"We entered upon Khabbab to visit him, and he had cauterized himself with seven cauterizations. He said, “Our companions who preceded passed on and departed, and this world did not diminish them in anything. But we attained after them such that we find no place for it except the dust.” He said, “Then we came after that to visit him, and he was building a wall for himself. He said, “A Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends, except for something he puts into the dust. And were it not that the Prophet ﷺ forbade—or forbade us—to pray for death, I would have prayed for it.”"],[3564,"We entered upon Khabbab, and he had cauterized himself with seven cauterizations in his belly. He said, “Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it.”"],[3565,"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ while he was using a cloak of his as a pillow in the shade of the Kaʿbah. We said, “Will you not seek victory for us? Will you not supplicate for us?” He said, “Among those before you, a man would be taken and combed with iron combs through what was beneath his flesh and bone, and that did not turn him away from his religion. By God, this matter will be completed until a rider travels from Sanʿaʾ to Hadramawt fearing none but God—or the wolf for his sheep. But you are in haste.”"],[3566,"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kaaba. We said, 'Won't you seek victory for us? Won't you supplicate for us?' He said, 'Among those before you, a man would be seized and combed with iron combs down to his flesh and bones, and that would not turn him away from his religion. By Allah, this affair will surely be completed until a rider travels from Sana'a to Hadramawt fearing nothing but Allah, or the wolf for his sheep. But you are hasty.'"],[3567,"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kaaba. We said, 'Won't you seek victory for us? Won't you supplicate for us?' He said, 'Among those before you, a man would be seized and combed with iron combs down to his flesh and bones, and that would not turn him away from his religion. By Allah, this affair will surely be completed until a rider travels from Sana'a to Hadramawt fearing nothing but Allah, or the wolf for his sheep. But you are hasty.'"],[3568,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kaaba. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, won't you supplicate to Allah? Won't you seek victory?' He sat up, his face red with anger, then said, 'Among those before you, a pit would be dug for a man, then he would be placed in it, then a saw would be placed on his head, then he would be combed with iron combs down to his bones, and that would not turn him away from his religion. But you are hasty. By Allah, this affair will surely be completed until a rider travels from Sana'a to Hadramawt fearing nothing but Allah and the wolf for his sheep.'"],[3569,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Every expenditure that a servant spends, he is rewarded for it, except building.'"],[3570,"Khabbab used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3571,"I used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3572,"I used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3573,"I used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3574,"We entered upon Khabbab to visit him while he was ill, and he had cauterized himself. He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from invoking death. Were it not for that, I would have invoked it.' And he was repairing a wall of his."],[3575,"We entered upon Khabbab to visit him while he was ill, and he had cauterized himself. He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from invoking death. Were it not for that, I would have invoked it.' And he was repairing a wall of his."],[3576,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Kaaba, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, won't you supplicate to Allah for us?' He sat up angry, his face red, and said, 'Indeed, those before you would be asked for the word, and he would not give it, so a saw would be placed on him and he would be split into two, and that would not turn him away from his religion. And indeed, one of them would be combed from his bones with flesh or sinews with iron combs, and that would not turn him away from his religion. But you are hasty. And Allah will surely complete this affair until a rider travels from Sana'a to Hadramawt fearing nothing but Allah.' And Bayan added in it: 'or the wolf for his sheep.'"],[3577,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was lying under a tree with his hand placed under his head. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah against these people whom we fear will turn us away from our religion?\" He turned his face away from me. I moved to face him, and he turned his face away from me three times, each time I spoke to him and he turned his face away. Then he sat up on the third time and said, \"O people, fear Allah. By Allah, a man among the believers before you would have a saw placed on his head and be split in two, yet he would not turn back from his religion. Fear Allah, for Allah ﷻ will open for you and will provide.\""],[3578,"He said, \"I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad.\" I said, \"I will not disbelieve in Muhammad until Allah causes you to die.\" Then I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, \"I will surely be given wealth and children\"? Has he looked into the unseen or taken a covenant with the Most Merciful?} He said, \"A binding covenant.\""],[3579,"He said, \"Leave me until I die, then I am resurrected, and I will have wealth and children, and I will repay you.\" Then this verse was revealed: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, \"I will surely be given wealth and children\"?} to the end of the verse."],[3580,"He said, \"You claim that you will return to wealth and children, and I will return to wealth and children. When I return to you, then I will give you.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses} the verse."],[3581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cover his head with it and place something of idhkhir (sweet rush) on his feet.\""],[3582,"We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking the face of Allah, so our reward became incumbent upon Allah. Among us were those who passed away without eating any of their reward. Among them was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud, and he had nothing but a striped cloak. When we covered his head with it, his feet were exposed, and when we covered his feet, his head was exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cover his head with it and place idhkhir on his feet.\" And among us are those whose fruit has ripened for them, and they are picking it."],[3583,"I heard Khabbab b. al-Aratt say: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking the face of Allah ﷻ, so our reward became incumbent upon Allah. Among us were those who passed away without eating any of their good deeds. Among them was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud and left behind a striped cloak. When we placed it over his feet, his head was exposed, and when we placed it over his head, his feet were exposed. The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to place it over his head and to place something of idhkhir on his feet. And among us are those whose fruit has ripened for them, and they are picking it, meaning eating it."],[3584,"We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking the face of Allah ﷻ, and our reward became incumbent upon Allah. Among us were those who passed away without eating any of their reward. Among them was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud, and we found nothing to shroud him in except a striped cloak. When we covered his head with it, his feet were exposed, and when we covered his feet, his head was exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to cover his head and to place idhkhir on his feet. And among us are those whose fruit has ripened for them, and they are picking it."],[3585,"We are a people who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so our reward became incumbent upon Allah. Among us were those who passed away without eating any of their reward. Among them was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud, and nothing was found for him except a striped cloak. When his head was covered with it, his feet were exposed, and when his feet were covered with it, his head was exposed. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Cover his head with it and place idhkhir on him.\" And among us are those whose fruit has ripened for them, and they are picking it."],[3586,"He said, \"I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad.\" I said, \"I will not disbelieve in Muhammad ﷺ until you die, then you are resurrected.\" He said, \"Will I be resurrected after death?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then I will have wealth and children.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses} until {alone}. Abu al-Qasim said: \"This is how Hammad b. Shu'ayb narrated it from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il.\" The people narrated it as we mentioned first from al-A'mash from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from Khabbab. If Hammad b. Shu'ayb accurately preserved it from al-A'mash, then it is rare from the hadith of Abu Wa'il."],[3587,"He said, \"In this chest there are eighty thousand dirhams. By Allah, I did not tie a thread for it, nor did I withhold it from any beggar.\" Then he wept. It was said, \"What makes you weep?\" He said, \"I weep because my companions passed away and the world did not diminish them in anything, and we remained after them until we cannot find a place for it.\""],[3588,"He said concerning this chest, \"Seventy thousand — no cover was tied over it and no beggar was refused from it. I wish it were such-and-such\" — either he said \"camel dung\" or he said \"something else.\""],[3589,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Let none of you wish for death; (if not for the prohibition,) I would have wished for it.\""],[3590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to wish for death; (if not for the prohibition,) I would have wished for it."],[3591,"We entered upon Khabbab to visit him, and he had cauterized his stomach seven times. He said, \"Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Do not wish for death,' I would have wished for it.\""],[3592,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Let none of you wish for death; (if not for the prohibition,) I would have wished for it.\""],[3593,"We entered upon Khabbab, and he had cauterized his stomach seven times. He said, \"Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Let none of you wish for death,' I would have wished for it.\""],[3594,"\"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I did not own a dirham, and now here are forty thousand (dirhams) set aside.\""],[3595,"\"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I did not own a dirham, and today in one corner of my house there are forty thousand dirhams.\""],[3596,"We entered upon Khabbab while a wall was being built in his house. He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A believer is rewarded for his spending, except for what he puts into the dust (i.e., building on earth).'\""],[3597,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunger, but he did not show any signs of discontent.\""],[3598,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying on the scorching hot ground, but he did not relieve us (of that hardship).\""],[3599,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying on the scorching hot ground, but he did not relieve us (of that hardship).\""],[3600,"\"That our rewards go (to us) along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and whatever worldly things we obtained after him.\""],[3601,"Hamzah was shrouded in a burdah (striped cloak) such that when his head was covered, his feet would show, and when his feet were covered, his head would show."],[3602,"I saw Hamzah and we could not find any cloth to shroud him in except a burdah. When we covered his feet with it, his head showed, and when we covered his head with it, his feet showed. So we covered his head and placed idhkhir (a kind of grass) over his feet."],[3603,"We entered upon Khabbab, then his shroud was brought. When he saw it, he wept and said: 'But Hamzah had no shroud found for him except a burdah. When it was put over his head, it shrank away from his feet, and when it was put over his feet, it shrank away from his head, until it was stretched over his head and idhkhir was placed over his feet.'"],[3604,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3605,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3606,"I said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3607,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the sun-baked ground, but he did not respond to our complaint."],[3608,"We said to Khabbab: How did you know the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3609,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3610,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Let none of you wish for death; for had it not been so, I would have wished for it.'"],[3611,"On the day of 'Ashura', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O people, whoever among you wants to fast this day, let him fast it. Whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast. And whoever has eaten, let him fast the rest of his day.'"],[3612,"In His saying, \"And do not turn away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon, seeking His countenance\". It was narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to sit with Bilal, 'Ammaar bin Yaasir, Sohayb, and Khabbaab ibn Al-Aratt (may Allah be pleased with them), in the company of some weak believers. When they saw those around the Prophet ﷺ , they demeaned them, so they went to him and spoke in this manner, \"We would like for you to establish a separate gathering for us, where the Arabs can recognize our importance. When Arab delegations come to visit you, we feel ashamed to be seen sitting with these slaves. Or when we come to you, have them leave, and when we leave, let them sit if you wish.\" He said, \"Yes.\" They said, \"Then write for us a treaty.\" He called for a parchment in order to write for them, and he called 'Ali to write. While we were sitting in a corner, with him, Angel Gabriel descended upon him, and he recited the verse, \"And do not turn away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon\". Then, he mentioned Al-Aqra' Ibn Habis and his companion and said, \"And thus We made some of them as a trial for others to say, “Are these the ones upon whom Allahhas bestowed favor among us?” Is not Allah most knowing of the grateful?\" Then, he mentioned him and said, \"And when those come to you who believe in Our verses, say, 'Peace be upon you; your Lord has decreed upon Himself mercy'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the parchment, called us, and approached us while saying, \"Peace be upon you,\" until we sat down with our knees touching his knees."],[3613,"In His saying ﷻ{And do not send away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon, continuing in devotion to Him.} It is narrated that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was sitting with Bilal, Ammar ibn Yasir, Suhaib, and Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, amongst a group of weak believers. When the Prophet saw them gathered around him, he honored them and allowed them to approach him. They said, \"We would like you to reserve a position for us that the Arabs recognize as a mark of distinction. When the delegations of the Arabs come to you, we feel ashamed to be seen sitting with these slaves. Or at least, when we come to you, allow us to have them move aside, and once we have finished, allow them to sit if you wish.\" He said, \"Yes.\" They then said, \"Write a document for us.\" So he called for a paper to be written for them, and he called upon Ali to write it. While we were sitting in one corner, Gabriel descended upon him revealing the verse ﷻ{And do not send away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon.} Then he mentioned 'Aqra ibn Habis and his companion, stating ﷻ{And thus We have tried some of them through others that they might say, \"Are these the ones Allah has favored among us?\" Is not Allah most knowing of the grateful?\"} He then mentioned him and said ﷻ{And when those come to you who believe in Our verses, say, \"Peace be upon you. Your Lord has decreed upon Himself mercy.} Upon mentioning this, the Prophet threw the document and called us to approach him, saying \"Peace be upon you.\" We approached him until we put our knees against his knees."],[3614,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. We were afflicted with thirst, and we had no water with us. A she-camel belonging to one of us knelt down, and between her legs there was something like a water-skin, so we drank from her milk.\""],[3615,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint,\" meaning regarding the midday prayer."],[3616,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3617,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not grant us relief.\""],[3618,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the severity of the ground's heat, and he did not heed our complaint. He said, \"When the sun declines, then pray.\""],[3619,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3620,"\"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the intense heat on our foreheads and palms, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3621,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the Children of Israel were destroyed, they told stories.\""],[3622,"“Khuzaymah b. Thabit fought on the Day of Siffin until he was killed.”"],[3623,"Zayd b. Thabit said: When we wrote the mushafs, I missed a verse that I used to hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I found it with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to God; among them are those who have fulfilled their vow, and among them are those who await, and they have not changed in the least.” He said, “Khuzaymah used to be called Dhu al-Shahadatayn.”"],[3624,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not come to women in their rears.”"],[3625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah forbids you to come to women in their rears.”"],[3626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this plague is a defilement and a remnant of a punishment with which some people were punished. If it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it.”"],[3627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this ailment is a defilement and a remnant of a punishment with which people before you were punished. If it is in a land, do not enter it; and if it is in a land while you are in it, do not approach it” — meaning the plague."],[3628,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3629,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night, wiping over his leather socks when he put them on while his feet were pure.”"],[3630,"There were men among us who, when they came from defecation, would wash away the traces of feces. Then this verse was revealed concerning them: {In it are men who love to purify themselves}."],[3631,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping: “For the traveler, three days; and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3632,"“I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Jam’ (Muzdalifah) with one iqamah.”"],[3633,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed at Jam’ (Muzdalifah) three [rak’ahs] and two [rak’ahs].” Abu al-Qasim said: This hadith was narrated by Yahya b. Sa’id al-Ansari, Shu’bah, Zuhayr and others from ‘Adi b. Thabit, from ‘Abd Allah b. Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Ghaylan and Jabir al-Ju’fi disagreed with them and said, from Khuzaymah b. Thabit. The correct version is the hadith of Abu Ayyub. Al-Thawri also narrated it from ‘Adi b. Thabit, from ‘Abd Allah b. Yazid, from Abu Ayyub."],[3634,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God is not shy of the truth. Do not approach women in their anuses.”"],[3635,"It was as if he was prostrating on the forehead of the Prophet ﷺ. So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Sit, prostrate, and do as you saw.”"],[3636,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Beware of the supplication of the wronged, for it is carried upon the clouds. God, may His majesty be exalted, says: By My might and My majesty, I will surely help you, even if after a time."],[3637,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Satan comes to a person and says, 'Who created the heavens?' He says, 'God.' Then he says, 'Who created the earth?' He says, 'God.' Until he says, 'Who created God?' So if any of you finds that, let him say, 'I believe in God and His messengers.'"],[3638,"My father withheld his weapon on the Day of the Camel and at Siffin. When 'Ammar was killed, he drew his sword and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.'"],[3639,"When the Prophet ﷺ finished his talbiyah, he asked God, may He be glorified, for His forgiveness and His good pleasure, and sought His deliverance from the Fire."],[3640,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar."],[3641,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about cleansing after relieving oneself. He said: 'Three stones, with no dung among them.'"],[3642,"Cleansing after relieving oneself was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Is not one of you sufficed by three stones, with no dung among them?' Hisham said: And Abu Wajzah informed me from 'Umarah b. Khuzaymah b. Thabit. It was said to Sufyan: 'They say Abu Khuzaymah.' He said: 'No, it is only Abu Wajzah the poet.'"],[3643,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Regarding cleansing after relieving oneself, three stones, with no dung among them.'"],[3644,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about cleansing after relieving oneself, and he said: 'Three stones, with no dung among them.'"],[3645,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Cleansing after relieving oneself is with three stones, with no dung among them.'"],[3646,"Whoever commits something for which the prescribed punishment for that sin is carried out upon him, it is an expiation for him."],[3647,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever cleanses himself with three stones, with no dung among them, they will be a purification for him.'"],[3648,"The Prophet ﷺ bought a horse from Sawa' b. al-Harith, who then denied it, so Khuzaymah b. Thabit testified for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"What made you testify when you were not present with him?\" He said, \"I believed you when you brought it, and I knew that you say nothing but the truth.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever Khuzaymah testifies for or against, it is sufficient for him.\""],[3649,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Any servant who commits something that God has forbidden, and then the prescribed punishment for it is carried out on him, that sin is expiated.\""],[3650,"The Messenger of God said, \"Whoever commits a sin and the prescribed punishment for that sin is carried out on him, it is an expiation for him.\""],[3651,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Be ashamed, for God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their anuses.\""],[3652,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their anuses.\""],[3653,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their posteriors.\""],[3654,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. It is not lawful for anyone to go to women in their anuses.\""],[3655,"I testify that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their anuses.\""],[3656,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their anuses.\""],[3657,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their anuses.\""],[3658,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not go to women in their posteriors.\""],[3659,"He heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say, \"Do not go to women in their posteriors.\""],[3660,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not come to women in their back passages.”"],[3661,"The Prophet ﷺ said: He who eats from this plant should not come near the mosques. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3825)"],[3662,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set three days for the traveler and one day for the resident.” And by Allah, if the questioner had pressed his question, he would have made it five."],[3663,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks. He said: “For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night.” And if the questioner had pressed his question, he would have increased it."],[3664,"From Khuzaymah b. Thabit: A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks. He said: “For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night.” And if we had asked for more, he would have made it five."],[3665,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Wiping over the leather socks is for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3666,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted us a concession regarding wiping over the leather socks: “Three days and their nights for travelers, and for the resident a day and a night.” And if we had asked for more, he would have increased it."],[3668,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Wipe over the leather socks for three days.\" And if we had asked for more, he would have increased for us."],[3669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set a time limit for the traveler to wipe three days, and for the resident a day and a night. And if we had asked for more, he would have increased for us. Abu al-Qasim said: \"Abu al-Ahwas omitted 'Amr b. Maymun from the chain.\""],[3670,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ directed us to wipe three times; and if we had asked for more, he would have granted us more.\""],[3671,"An Arab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about ablution. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Three for the traveler and one for the resident.\" If the Arab had insisted, the Prophet ﷺ would have allowed him to wipe over his socks."],[3672,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The traveler wipes for three days.\" Shu'bah said: \"I think he said: 'and their nights.'\""],[3673,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks, he said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights.\""],[3674,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Regarding wiping over the leather socks, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set three days for the traveler and one day for the resident."],[3676,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3677,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The traveler wipes over the leather socks for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.\""],[3678,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3679,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3680,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3681,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights.\""],[3682,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding wiping: “For the traveler, three days, and one day for the resident.”"],[3683,"I asked ʿAʿishah ؓ about wiping over the khuff (leather slippers) and she said: Ask ʿAli ؓ . I asked him and he said: Three days and nights - i.e., for the traveller - and one day and night for one who is not travelling (Using translation from Aḥmad 780)"],[3684,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks, he said: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3685,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler wipes for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3686,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “For the traveler, three days, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3687,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to wipe: for the resident, a day and a night, and for the traveler, three.”"],[3688,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3689,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3690,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3691,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night, without removing them.”"],[3692,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3693,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wiping over the leather socks is for three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.”"],[3694,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also said: “The traveler [may wipe over his leather socks] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3696,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3697,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three [days], and the resident for one day, wiping over the leather socks.”"],[3698,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler wipes over his leather socks for three days, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3699,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “A day and a night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler.”"],[3700,"From the Prophet ﷺ [regarding] wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.” ʿAbd Allāh said: My father said this is a mistake. Abū al-Qāsim said: Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal meant that he considered the ḥadīth of Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, to be a mistake, and the correct [version] from the ḥadīth of Manṣūr is the ḥadīth of ʿAmr b. Maymūn."],[3701,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3702,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3703,"A woman was stoned during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and the people said, “Her deeds have been nullified.” That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “It is an expiation for her sins, and she will be resurrected [in a state] besides that.”"],[3704,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, [what about] the rabbit?” He said: “I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.” I said, “But I will not leave it unless you forbid it.” He said: “It menstruates,” or he said, “It bleeds.” I said, “Then what about the hyena?” He said: “And who would eat the hyena?”"],[3705,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to ask you about some things, about the creeping creatures of the earth. What do you say about the dabb (spiny-tailed lizard)? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it.” I said: Then I will eat what you have not forbidden. And why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “An ummah (nation) among the nations was lost, and I saw a creation that disturbed me.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the rabbit? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it.” He said: Then I will eat what you have not forbidden. And why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “I was informed that it menstruates.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the hyena? He said: “And who would eat the hyena?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the fox? He said: “And who would eat the fox?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the wolf? He said: “And would anyone with any good in him eat the wolf?”"],[3706,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the creeping creatures of the earth, and he said: “Ask about whatever you wish.” So I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about the dabb (spiny-tailed lizard)? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it. I was told that an ummah (nation) from the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth.” I said: I will not leave anything that you have not forbidden without eating it. He said: I said: And the rabbit? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it. I was informed that it menstruates.” I said: I will not leave anything that you have not forbidden without eating it. I said: And the fox? He said: “Does anyone eat the fox?” I said: And the hyena? He said: “Does anyone eat the hyena?” I said: And the wolf? He said: “Does anyone with any good in him eat the wolf?”"],[3707,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, and he mentioned Khalid b. al-Walid: An excellent servant of Allah and brother of the clan, and a sword among the swords of Allah."],[3708,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he announced the death of the people of Mu'tah, said: “Then a sword among the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah granted victory through him.”"],[3709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the people of Mu'tah from the pulpit, then said: “Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the standard, and he is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Glorified.”"],[3710,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Glorified, which Allah has poured upon the disbelievers.”"],[3711,"“And a Yemeni plate of mine held firm in my hand.”"],[3712,"Khuraym b. Aws: “No one was more hostile to the Arabs than Hurmuz. When we had finished with Musaylimah and his companions, we proceeded toward the area of Basrah, and Hurmuz met us at Kazimah with a huge gathering. Khalid went out to meet him and called for single combat. Hurmuz came out against him, and Khalid killed him, and he wrote about that to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ, who granted him his spoils. The qalansuwah (cap) of Hurmuz was worth one hundred thousand dirhams. The Persians, when a man was honored among them, would make a cap worth one hundred thousand dirhams.”"],[3713,"“Look for it,” so they found it, and it was an old worn cap. Khalid said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ‘umrah and shaved his head, and the people rushed to get the sides of his hair. I beat them to his forelock hair, and I placed it in this cap. I have never witnessed a battle with it with me except that I was granted victory.”"],[3714,"“O assembly of Quraysh, Allah, Exalted, has not given your faces any superiority over our faces except what Allah favored His Prophet ﷺ with.” Then Khalid said: “Let him retaliate.” The man said to his nephew: “Slap him.” But when he raised his hand, he said: “Leave it for Allah, Mighty and Glorified.”"],[3715,"“...from our hands while you are humiliated, for with me are people who love killing in the path of Allah as a Persian loves wine. And peace be upon those who follow guidance.”"],[3716,"I heard Qays b. Abi Hazim say: “Khalid b. al-Walid led the people in prayer wearing a garment wrapped around him.”"],[3717,"When Khalid b. al-Walid came to al-Hirah, he said, \"Bring me the poison.\" So it was brought to him, and he placed it in his palm and then said, \"In the name of Allah,\" and swallowed it, and it did not harm him."],[3718,"\"In the name of Allah,\" and he swallowed it down."],[3719,"\"Enough, for what is between us has not reached the level of our religion.\""],[3720,"\"Your disbelief, not your glorification: indeed I have seen that Allah has humiliated you.\""],[3721,"\"I sought death but it was not decreed for me except to die on my bed. There is no deed I hope in more than 'there is no god but Allah,' and I am shielded by it.\" Then he said, \"When I die, look at my weapons and my horse and make them provisions in the path of Allah.\""],[3722,"\"Yes, by Allah, He is sought for help in that.\""],[3723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Maymunah, and she brought him a cooked dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) with dates. Maymunah said, “Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he eats.” When he was informed of it, he held back his hand from it. They said, “Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “No, but I find it distasteful.” Khalid b. al-Walid pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ watched him."],[3724,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: 'Amr b. Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu Najih narrated to me from Khalid b. Hakim b. Hizam, who said: Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah took hold of a man from the people of the earth over something, and Khalid b. al-Walid spoke to him about it. It was said to him, “Did you anger the commander?” He said, “I did not intend to anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were most severe in punishing people in this world.’”"],[3725,"'Ammar insulted me during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, were it not for you, the son of Sumayyah would not have insulted me.” He said, “Gently, O Khalid. Whoever insults 'Ammar, Allah insults him, and whoever belittles 'Ammar, Allah belittles him.”"],[3726,"“...that we teach our children archery and the Qurʾān.”"],[3727,"He complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: “I feel terror at night.” He said: “Shall I not teach you words that Jibrīl ﷺ taught me? He claimed that an ʿifrīt of the jinn was scheming against me.” He said: “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither a righteous nor a wicked person can surpass, from the evil of what descends from heaven and what ascends in it, from the evil of what He has scattered in the earth and what emerges from it, from the evil of the trials of the night and the trials of the day, and from the evil of the night visitors and day visitors, except a visitor who comes with good, O Merciful.”"],[3728,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Shall I not teach you words that, if you say them, you will sleep? Say: O God, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they lead astray, be for me a neighbour against the evil of all jinn and humans, that any of them may assault me or harm me. Mighty is Your protection, exalted is Your praise, and there is no god but You.”"],[3729,"From Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ashʿarī ؓ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man who did not complete his bowing, pecking in his prostration while he was praying. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If this man died in this state of his, he would die on other than the religion of Muḥammad ﷺ.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The example of one who does not complete his bowing and pecks in his prostration is like a hungry person who eats one or two dates, which do not avail him anything.” Abū Ṣāliḥ said: I said to Abū ʿAbd Allāh: “Who told you this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “The commanders of the armies: ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, Khālid b. al-Walīd, and Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasana heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[3730,"“...and al-Hind, in our hearts at that time, was al-Baṣra, while I disliked that.” He said: A man stood and said: “O Abū Sulaymān, fear God ﷻ, for tribulations have appeared.” He said: “Is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb alive? It will only be after him, and the people at Dhī Billiyān—and Dhī Billiyān is at such-and-such a place. A man will look and reflect whether he can find a place that has not been struck by the like of what struck his own place, of tribulation and evil, and he will not find it.” He said: “And those are the days that the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned: ‘Before the Hour there will be days of harj.’ We seek refuge with God that those days should overtake us and you.”"],[3731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If anyone were to escape the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped it.\""],[3732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Measure your food, and you will be blessed in it.\""],[3733,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[3734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse.\""],[3735,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought food, he would eat some of it and then send it to us. We were brought food that he had not eaten from at all. I said to the woman, \"Do not be hasty.\" I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"This herb—I dislike its smell.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"I dislike what you dislike, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[3736,"I never prayed behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him when he finished his prayer saying: \"O Allah, forgive me all my errors and sins. O Allah, revive me, restore me, provide for me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness and none turns away any of their evil except You.\""],[3737,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Ibrahim ﷺ . He said: 'O Jibril, who is this with you?' He said: 'Muhammad.' He greeted me and welcomed me, and said: 'Command your ummah to plant abundantly in Paradise, for its soil is good and vast.' I said: 'What is the planting of Paradise?' He said: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah).'\""],[3738,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to me: 'Shall I not teach you a word that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me?' I said: 'Yes, uncle.' He said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, he said: \"Shall I not teach you, Abu Ayyub, a word from the treasure of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\" He said: \"Increase in saying: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah).\"'"],[3739,"He said to me: 'Shall I not command you with what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me? To increase in saying: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah), for it is among the treasures of Paradise.'"],[3740,"I asked Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, “How were sacrifices among you in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “In the time of the Prophet ﷺ, a man would sacrifice a sheep on behalf of himself and his household, and they would eat from it and feed others from it; then people began to vie with one another, and it became as you see.”"],[3741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to face the qiblah while defecating or urinating. When we came to Syria, we found their latrines were built facing the qiblah, so we would turn aside and seek Allah’s forgiveness, exalted be He."],[3742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Abū Ayyūb, shall I not guide you to a charity that Allah and His Messenger love? You reconcile between people when they hate one another and become corrupt.”"],[3743,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “Do not sever relations, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of God, brothers. The separation of believers is three [days]; if the two do not speak, God turns away from them until they speak.”"],[3744,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ washing his head while in iḥrām.”"],[3745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lodged on the lower floor, and Abu Ayyub went up to the upper floor. When evening came and night fell, Abu Ayyub kept thinking that he was above the roof of the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Prophet was below him, and that he was between him and the revelation. So Abu Ayyub could not sleep, fearing that dust might fall on him or that he might move and disturb him. When morning came, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not sleep a wink last night, neither I nor Umm Ayyub.' He said, 'Why is that, O Abu Ayyub?' He said, 'I remembered that I am above the roof of a house while you are below me, and I move and dust falls on you and my movement disturbs you, and I am between you and the revelation.' He said, 'Do not do that, O Abu Ayyub. Shall I not teach you some words? If you say them in the morning ten times and in the evening ten times, you will be given ten good deeds for them, ten evil deeds will be wiped away from you, you will be raised ten degrees, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be for you like the reward of ten freed slaves. You say: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise, and He has no partner.'\""],[3746,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me and be brief.' He said, 'When you stand for your prayer, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell. Do not speak a word for which you will have to apologize. And renounce hope for what people possess.'"],[3747,"The Prophet said: \"The five daily prayers, from one Friday to the next, and fulfilling the trust are all expiation for whatever (sins) come between them.\" I said: \"What is fulfilling the trust?\" He said: Having a bath to cleanse oneself from sexual impurity, for under every hair there is the state of sexual impurity.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 598)"],[3748,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ were playing in front of him and in his lap. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you love them?' He said, 'How could I not love them? They are my two fragrant flowers of this world whom I smell.'"],[3749,"A man may have from his wife anything except intercourse, meaning while she is menstruating. He said, 'They may spend the night under one cover,' meaning the menstruating woman, if there is a cloth over the private part."],[3750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not weep over the religion when its people are put in charge of it, but weep over it when other than its people are put in charge of it.\""],[3751,"“Will you not listen to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought of good?” They said, “And how much good has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought?” He said: “Who can recite a third of the Qur’an in a night?” We feared it, so we remained silent. He repeated it to us three times, then said: “Whoever recites Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad, it is as if it equals a third of the Qur’an.”"],[3752,"I saw Abū Ayyūb remove his leather socks, and people looked at him. He said: “Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over them, but ablution has been made beloved to me.”"],[3753,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise.”"],[3754,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, \"Did you not know that Allah looked at the people of the earth and chose your father, so He sent him as a prophet? Then He looked again and chose your husband, so I received revelation and married him, and took him as my successor?\""],[3755,"The Prophet ﷺ was going between Safa and Marwa when a feather fell onto his beard. Abu Ayyub hastened to him and removed it from his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “May God keep away from you what you dislike.”"],[3756,"We came to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari while he was feeding horses of his in Sa'naba. We asked him: O Abu Ayyub, you fought the polytheists with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and now you have come to fight the Muslims? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to fight three groups: the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the renegades. I have fought the oath-breakers and fought the deviators, and I shall fight, if God wills, the renegades at the passes, the paths, and the Nahrawan areas. And I do not know who they are."],[3757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The angel has a station with me that none of you has, and I dislike that he should find any odor from me.”"],[3758,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ when a group of riders from the Ansar came wearing turbans and said: Peace be upon you, O our master. Ali ؓ said: I am your master, and are you Arab people? They said: Yes, we heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever has me as his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.” And this is Abu Ayyub among us. Abu Ayyub uncovered his face from the turban and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever has me as his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.”"],[3759,"He brought the Messenger of God ﷺ a beef broth containing garlic, and the Messenger of God ﷺ detected the smell of garlic and said: “Take it away.” He said: Why, O Messenger of God? Is it forbidden? He said: “No, but Gabriel is conversing with me.”"],[3760,"An Arab came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I love horses. Are there horses in Paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"When you enter Paradise, you will be brought a horse made of ruby with wings. You will be carried on it and you will fly in Paradise wherever you wish.\""],[3761,"Whenever our food was ready, we would send for Abu Ayyub and the people of his ship. Abu Ayyub came and said, \"You invited me while I was fasting, but it was my duty to answer you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'A Muslim has six obligatory rights over his fellow Muslim. Whoever abandons one of them has abandoned an obligatory right owed to his brother: to answer him when he calls him, to greet him when he meets him, to respond to his sneeze, to visit him when he falls ill, to follow his funeral procession when he dies, and to give him sincere counsel when he seeks his advice.'\" My father said: There was among us a man who was a joker, and a man was in charge of our expenses. The joker would say to the one in charge of the food, \"May God reward you with good and righteousness.\" When he repeated that many times, the man began to get angry and insult him. The joker said, \"O Abu Ayyub, what do you think of a man who, when I say to him, 'May God reward you with good and righteousness,' gets angry and insults me?\" Abu Ayyub said, \"We used to say: Whoever good does not reform, evil will reform.\" So it was turned around for him. When the man came, the joker said to him, \"May God reward you with evil and hardship.\" The man laughed and was pleased, and he said, \"You never abandon your nonsense in any state.\" The joker said, \"May God reward Abu Ayyub with good and righteousness, for he told me.\""],[3762,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate or drank, he said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has given food and drink and made it easy to swallow, and provided an exit for it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3851)"],[3763,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"My community will remain in good—or upon the natural disposition—as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars become dense.\""],[3764,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed this prayer—meaning the 'Asr—was made obligatory upon those before you, but they neglected it. So whoever among you today guards it will be given its reward twice, and there is no prayer after it until the witness appears, meaning the star.\""],[3765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Four are from the practices of the Messengers: modesty, applying perfume, marriage, and the tooth-stick.\""],[3766,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the news of the sky. He said, 'You ask me about the news of the sky while you leave your nails like the claws of birds, in which filth and dirt accumulate.'"],[3767,"I prepared for the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr enough food for the two of them, and I brought it to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Go and invite thirty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' That was hard for me. I said, 'I have nothing to add.' It was as if I pretended not to hear. He said, 'Go and invite thirty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' So I invited them and they came. He said, 'Eat.' They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said, 'Go and invite sixty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' Abu Ayyub said, 'By Allah, I am more generous with sixty than with thirty.' He said, 'So I invited them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stay.\" They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said, \"Go and invite ninety of the Ansar for me.\" He said, 'I am more generous with ninety and sixty than with thirty.' He said, 'So I invited them. They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. One hundred and eighty men, all of them from the Ansar, ate from that food of mine.'"],[3768,"The Ansar cast lots for their dwellings to see which of them would host the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The lot fell to Abu Ayyub, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed at his house. When food was given as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would eat some of it, then send it to us."],[3769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten things: whoever says them at the end of his prayers, when he has prayed, \"There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things,\" Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, raises him ten degrees, and they are equivalent to ten slaves, and they are a protection for him from Satan until evening. And whoever says them in the evening, the same applies until morning.'"],[3770,"He said, while he was in the land of the Romans: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever says in the morning: \"There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things,\" ten times, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and they are equivalent to ten slaves, and Allah protects him from Satan. And whoever says it in the evening, the same applies.'"],[3771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever meets the enemy and remains patient until he is killed or prevails will not be tried in his grave.'"],[3772,"Khālid—then he perished."],[3773,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, the people most severe in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those most severe in punishment in this world.” Then he said, “Go and let them go.”"],[3774,"I saw Khalid b. al-Hawari, a man from Abyssinia among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He came to his family, and when he finished, death came upon him, so he said: “Wash me with two washings: one washing for janāba and one washing for death.”"],[3775,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever receives good from his brother without asking or expecting it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only provision that Allah has driven to him.”"],[3776,"That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the eastern part of Thaqīf while he was standing on a bow or a staff when he came to them seeking victory. He said: “I heard him reciting ‘By the sky and the night comer’ until he completed it.” He said: “I memorized it in the Jāhiliyya while I was a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam. They said, ‘What did you hear from this man?’ So I recited it to them, and those of Quraysh who were with them said, ‘We know our companion better. If we knew that what he says is true, we would have followed him.’”"],[3777,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has given you at your death one-third of your wealth as an increase in your deeds.”"],[3778,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Saḥbal b. Muḥammad b. Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us (ḥ), and al-Ḥusayn al-Tustarī narrated to us, ʿAmr b. Hishām Abū Umayya al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from Saḥbal b. Muḥammad al-Madanī from Khālid b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥarmala al-Mudlijī who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at ʿUsfān, and a man said, “Would you like some of the noblest women and the best camels of Banū Mudlij?” Among the people was a man from Banū Mudlij, and that was recognized on his face. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of people is the one who defends his people as long as he does not sin.”"],[3779,"From his father, “regarding the naming” of those who witnessed with ʿAlī from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Khālid b. Abī Dujāna ؓ."],[3780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sows a crop and a bird or a passerby eats from it, it will be charity for him.”"],[3781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: Allah the Exalted has given you an extra prayer which is better for you then the red camels (i.e. high breed camels). This is the witr which Allah has appointed for you between the night prayer and the daybreak. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1418)"],[3782,"And it is said: Rather, it was revealed about Kharija b. Zayd Abu Zuhayr, the brother of Balharith b. al-Khazraj."],[3783,"I heard a clamor, and I turned away, and there he was moving. He said: \"The most excellent of the people is their middle one: 'Abd Allah 'Umar, Commander of the Faithful, strong in body, strong in the command of God ﷻ. 'Uthman b. 'Affan, Commander of the Faithful, the chaste, the self-restrained, who pardons many sins. Two nights came and four remained. The people differed and had no order. O people, turn to your leader, listen to him, and obey. This is the Messenger of God ﷺ and Ibn Rawaha.\" Then he said: \"What happened to Zayd b. Kharija?\"—meaning his father—then he said: \"I took concubines wrongfully.\" Then the voice became faint."],[3784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he sat at the end of his prayer, would point with his index finger. The polytheists used to say that he was casting a spell with it—they lied—but it is tawḥīd."],[3785,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with my son, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not commit a crime against him, and he will not commit a crime against you.”"],[3786,"On the authority of his father: “In naming those who witnessed with ‘Ali ؓ from the Ansar: Khalifa b. ‘Adi from Banu Bayada, a Badri.”"],[3787,"On the authority of ‘Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi‘, the two sons of Yazid b. Jariya, they said: “Khidam married off his daughter, while she was unwilling, to a man, and she was a thayyib. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he annulled her marriage.”"],[3788,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be trials in which the one sleeping is better than the one awake, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening. Lo, whoever it comes upon, let him strike his sword against the rock until it breaks, then lie down until it clears from what it cleared.”"],[3789,"On the authority of Kharasha b. al-Haritha, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Let none of you witness a person killed in retaliation, for perhaps he may be killed unjustly, and wrath will descend upon them and afflict him along with them.”"],[3790,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if there may be harm in it that hurts him.”"],[3791,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: \"Khalid b. al-Walid died in Homs in the year twenty-one.\""],[3792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought two roasted lizards, and Khalid ibn al-Walid was with him. The Prophet ﷺ desired to eat them, so it was said to him that they were lizards. He then grabbed them with his hand and Khalid ibn al-Walid said to him, \"Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"No, but they are not found in my people's land, so I find them delicious.\" Khalid then ate, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching him."],[3793,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the house of Maymunah bt. al-Harith. A roasted dabb lizard was brought. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached his hand toward it. Some of the women who were in Maymunah's house said, \"Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he intends to eat from.\" They said, \"It is a dabb.\" So he raised his hand. I said, \"Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and I find myself averse to it.\" Khalid said, \"So I pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching.\""],[3794,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she was his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. He found with her a roasted dabb lizard that her sister Hufaydah bt. al-Harith had brought from Najd. She offered the dabb to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was rare for him to extend his hand to food until he was told about it and it was named for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached his hand toward the dabb. A woman among the women present said, \"Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what you have offered him.\" They said, \"It is a dabb, O Messenger of Allah.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hand. Khalid b. al-Walid said, \"Do you forbid the dabb, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and I find myself averse to it.\" Khalid said, \"So I pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching, and he did not forbid me.\""],[3795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a roasted dabb. He reached his hand toward it to eat from it. Some of those present said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dabb meat.\" So he raised his hand. Khalid said to him, \"Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and I find myself averse to it.\""],[3796,"Umm Hufayd gifted Maymunah dabb meat. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered and it was offered to him. He would not eat any food until he knew what it was. A woman said, \"Inform the Prophet ﷺ what this is.\" They said, \"It is dabb meat that Umm Hufayd gifted to Maymunah.\" He said, and he had intended to eat from it but refrained, \"Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but I find myself averse to it, and it is not from the food of my people.\" Khalid said, \"So I ate it while he was sitting, and he did not fault me for that.\""],[3797,"He entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she was his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. He found with her a roasted dabb lizard that her sister Hufaydah bt. al-Harith had brought from Najd. She offered the dabb to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was rare for him to extend his hand to food until he was told about it and it was named for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached his hand toward the dabb. A woman among the women present said, \"Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what you have offered him.\" They said, \"It is a dabb, O Messenger of Allah.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hand. Khalid b. al-Walid said, \"Is the dabb forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and I find myself averse to it.\" Khalid said, \"So I pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching, and he did not forbid me.\""],[3798,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah.”"],[3799,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “It is not lawful to eat the flesh of horses, mules, and donkeys.”"],[3800,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him that the people had rushed into their enclosures. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and I called out among the people, “Indeed the prayer is to be gathered, and none will enter Paradise except a Muslim.” When the people gathered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said, “What is the matter with the Jews complaining that you rushed into their enclosures? Indeed, the wealth of those with whom we have a treaty is not lawful except by right. Forbidden to you are domestic donkeys and their horses, and every beast of prey with fangs, and every bird with talons.”"],[3801,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it: “Indeed, let no man reclining on his couch say, ‘Whatever we find lawful in the Book of Allah, we declare lawful, and whatever we find unlawful in the Book of Allah, we declare unlawful.’ Indeed, I forbid to you the wealth of those with whom we have a treaty,” and the rest of the hadith."],[3802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Khalid, announce among the people that prayer is to be gathered; none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul.” Then he went out and prayed at the time of midday heat."],[3803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Khalid, announce among the people that prayer is to be gathered; none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul.” Then he went out and prayed at the time of midday heat."],[3804,"Khalid b. al-Walid said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me in a military detachment, and we captured a household who had declared the oneness of Allah. 'Ammar said, “These people have protected themselves from us by their declaration of tawhid,” but I did not pay attention to 'Ammar's words. He said, “Indeed I will inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” When we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he complained about me to him. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that he was not exacting retribution from me, 'Ammar turned away with his eyes flowing with tears, and the Prophet ﷺ called him back and said, “O Khalid, do not insult 'Ammar, for whoever insults 'Ammar, Allah insults him; whoever hates 'Ammar, Allah hates him; and whoever treats 'Ammar as foolish, Allah treats him as foolish.” Khalid said, “O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.” By Allah, nothing prevented me from loving him except my treating him as foolish. Khalid said, “There is no sin of mine I fear more than my treating 'Ammar as foolish.”"],[3805,"There was some speech between 'Ammar and Khalid b. al-Walid, and Khalid b. al-Walid complained about him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is hostile to 'Ammar, Allah is hostile to him, and whoever treats 'Ammar as foolish, Allah treats him as foolish.” Shu'bah said: Salamah said something like this."],[3806,"Khalid b. al-Walid said: I have not done any deed that I fear more will cause me to enter the Fire than the matter of 'Ammar. We said, “O Abu Sulayman, what was it?” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with some of his companions to a tribe among the Arab tribes, and I attacked them, and among them was a Muslim household. 'Ammar spoke to me regarding some of his companions and said, “Release them,” but I said, “No, not until I bring them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; if he wishes he will release them, and if he wishes he will do with them whatever he wants.” I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and 'Ammar asked permission and entered, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, did you not see what Khalid did, and did?” Khalid said, “By Allah, were it not for your presence, the son of Sumayyah would not have insulted me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave, O 'Ammar,” so he left weeping and said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not support me against Khalid.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Will you not answer the man?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from him except that I considered him lowly.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever considers 'Ammar lowly, Allah considers him lowly; whoever insults 'Ammar, Allah insults him; and whoever disparages 'Ammar, Allah disparages him.” Then I went out and followed him and spoke to him until he sought forgiveness for me."],[3807,"There was between me and ʿAmmār b. Yāsir some of what occurs between people. I approached him and rebuked him. He went to the Prophet ﷺ to complain about me. When I saw that he was complaining about me, I approached as well and he said: “O Messenger of God, do you not see what he says while you are present?” He said: “Gently, Khālid! Say nothing but good. Whoever hates ʿAmmār, God hates him, and whoever is hostile to him, God is hostile to him.” When I heard that, I began seeking out ʿAmmār until I met him, apologised to him, and asked what he held against me."],[3808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Khālid b. al-Walīd to some people of Khathʿam. They sought protection by prostrating, but he killed them. The Messenger of God ﷺ paid their bloodwite at half the diyah. Then he said: “I am free from every Muslim who stays with the idolaters; their two fires should not be visible to one another.”"],[3809,"He complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the narrowness of his dwelling. He said: “Raise your eyes to heaven and ask God for spaciousness.”"],[3810,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: “Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī is Khālid b. Zayd.”"],[3811,"From Abū Isḥāq concerning the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr, then from Banū Thaʿlaba b. ʿAbd ʿAwf b. Ghanm: Abū Ayyūb, whose name is Khālid b. Zayd b. Kulayb b. Thaʿlaba."],[3812,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed with me, and I was the first with whom he stayed.”"],[3813,"Abū Ayyūb raided the Byzantines and fell ill. When death approached, he said: “When I die, carry me, and when you meet the enemy in battle lines, place me beneath your feet.”"],[3814,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: \"Abu al-Ansari died in the land of the Romans during the time of Muawiyah.\""],[3815,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those of the Ansar who attended Badr: Abu Ayyub Khalid b. Zayd b. Kulayb, of the Banu al-Najjar.\""],[3816,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those of the Ansar who attended Badr, then of the Banu al-Khazraj, then of the Banu al-Najjar: Abu Ayyub Khalid b. Zayd b. Kulayb b. Tha'labah b. Abd Awf b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar. He died at Constantinople with Yazid b. Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan in the year fifty-one.\""],[3817,"\"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari perished in the year fifty in the land of the Romans while he was raiding with Yazid.\""],[3818,"\"Abu Ayyub came to Muawiyah, may God have mercy on them both, and complained to him that he had a debt.\" Then he mentioned the hadith."],[3819,"I got married during my father’s lifetime, and my father gave people permission (invited them), and Abu Ayyub was among those we invited. They had screened my house with a green cloth. Abu Ayyub came, entered, and saw me standing. He looked and saw the house covered with a green cloth, and he said, “O ‘Abdullah, do you cover the walls?” My father spoke, feeling ashamed: “The women have overpowered us, O Abu Ayyub.” He said, “As for one who fears that women will overpower him—then I did not think that they would overpower you.” Then he said, “I will not eat your food, and I will not enter your house.” Then he left—may Allah have mercy on him."],[3820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed with me for a month. I saw that when the sun declined or had passed its zenith - or as he said - if he was engaged in some worldly work he abandoned it, and if he was sleeping it was as if he was awakened. He would stand, perform ghusl or wudu, then pray four rak'ahs, completing them, perfecting them, and taking his time in them. When he wanted to leave, I said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, I noticed that when the sun declined or passed its zenith, if you had some worldly work in hand you abandoned it, or if you were sleeping it was as if you were awakened, then you would perform ghusl or wudu and pray four rak'ahs, completing them, taking your time in them, and perfecting them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The gates of heaven - or the gates of Paradise - are opened at that hour, and no one coincides with this prayer except that I loved that something good from me should ascend to my Lord at that hour.\""],[3821,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stayed with me, I said: By my father and mother, I dislike being above you while you are below me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is more gentle for us to be on the lower floor because of those who visit us from the people.\" I saw a water jar of ours break and its water spill. I and Umm Ayyub stood up with a velvet cloth of ours - we had no blanket other than it - drying the water with it, out of fear that some of it might reach the Messenger of God ﷺ and harm him. We used to prepare food, and when he returned what remained of it, we would seek out the places where his fingers had been and eat from them, seeking blessing thereby. One night he returned his dinner to us, and we had put garlic or onion in it, so we did not see any trace of his fingers in it. I mentioned to him what we used to do and what we saw of his returning the food without eating it. He said: \"I detected in it the smell of this plant, and I am a man who converses intimately, so I did not like that its smell be found on me. As for you, eat it.\""],[3822,"The Messenger of God ﷺ heard a sound at sunset, or near sunset, and said: \"These are the Jews being tormented in their graves.\""],[3823,"I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ when the sun had set or turned yellow for setting, and I had a small jug of water with me. The Messenger of God went off for his need, and I sat waiting for him until he came, and I helped him perform wudu. He said: \"O Abu Ayyub, do you hear what I hear?\" I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: \"I hear the voices of the Jews being tormented in their graves.\""],[3824,"Mu'awiyah ؓ arrived, and the Ansar were slow to meet him, so he did not show them any favor. Abu Ayyub said, \"Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You will experience selfishness (favoritism), so be patient until you meet me.\" Mu'awiyah said, \"Then be patient.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"We will be patient as we were commanded. By Allah, we will not abandon it.\""],[3825,"The Prophet ﷺ \"prayed both of them at Jam' (Muzdalifah): Maghrib and 'Isha combined.\""],[3826,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from 'Adi b. Thabit, from 'Abd Allah b. Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, he informed him \"that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and 'Isha at Muzdalifah combined.\" \"The wording is from the hadith of Mutarrif.\""],[3827,"“I prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha’ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, at Muzdalifah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3020)"],[3828,"He informed him \"that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and the later 'Isha at Muzdalifah.\""],[3829,"\"I was with the Prophet ﷺ at Jam' (Muzdalifah), and he combined Maghrib and 'Isha.\""],[3830,"That the Prophet ﷺ combined Maghrib and Isha prayers by combining them."],[3831,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at Jam' (Muzdalifah) Maghrib as three rak'ahs and 'Isha as two rak'ahs with one iqamah.\""],[3832,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib and 'Isha at Muzdalifah with one iqamah.\""],[3833,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plundering and mutilation.\""],[3834,"Abu Ayyub b. Zayd al-Ansari, with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed when he migrated to Madinah, raided the land of the Romans. He passed by Mu'awiyah ؓ, who treated him coldly. He went on, then returned from his raid and passed by him again, and he treated him coldly and did not raise his head to him. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that we will see selfishness (favoritism) after him.\" Mu'awiyah said, \"What did he command you?\" He said, \"He commanded us to be patient.\" He said, \"Then be patient.\" Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas came to Basra, and 'Ali ؓ had appointed him over it. He said, \"O Abu Ayyub, I want to move out of my dwelling for you as I moved out for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He ordered his family and they moved out, and he gave him everything that the house enclosed. When he was leaving, he said, \"What is your need?\" He said, \"My need is my stipend and eight slaves to work in my land.\" His stipend was four thousand, so he multiplied it for him five times and gave him twenty thousand and forty slaves."],[3835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in the lower part of his house while I was in the upper room. Some water was spilled in the upper room, so I and Umm Ayyub got up with a velvet cloth of ours to soak up the water, fearing it might reach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I went down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, feeling concerned, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is not appropriate that we be above you. Move to the upper room.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his belongings to be moved, and they were moved; his belongings were few. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, you used to send us food, and I would look at it. When I saw the traces of your fingers, I would place my hands in it. Then came this food that you sent me, and I looked at it but did not see the traces of your fingers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Yes, indeed it contained onion, and I disliked eating it because of the angel who comes to me. As for you, eat it.”"],[3836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “Every prayer removes the sin that came before it.”"],[3837,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every prayer removes the sin that came before it.”"],[3838,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every prayer removes the sin that came before it.”"],[3839,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , went out to them and said, \"Indeed, my Lord has chosen me between seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being held to account, and between the 'hathiya' with Him.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what does 'hathiya' mean for you?\" So the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , entered and then came out to them while he was saying the takbir (Allahu Akbar). He said, \"Indeed, my Lord has increased for me with every thousand seventy thousand and the 'hathiya' is with Him.\" Abu Ru'hum said, \"O Abu Ayyub, what do you think the 'hathiya' of Allah is?\" So the people began to consume it with their mouths. Abu Ayyub said, \"Leave your companion to inform you about the 'hathiya' of the Prophet, ﷺ , as I think it is, rather I am certain that the 'hathiya' of the Prophet, ﷺ , is to say, 'O Lord, whoever testifies that there is no deity except You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your slave and Messenger, and his heart verifies what his tongue utters, Paradise will be incumbent upon him.'\""],[3840,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever says in the morning: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things’ ten times, ten good deeds are recorded for him for each time he says it, ten evil deeds are erased from him, Allah raises him ten degrees by it, they are for him like freeing ten slaves, and they are for him a protection from the beginning of the day to its end. On that day he will not perform any deed that overpowers them. If he says them in the evening, the same applies.”"],[3841,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says in the morning: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things’ ten times, Allah records for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, they are for him equal to freeing ten slaves, and he is protected from Satan. Whoever says them in the evening will have the like of that.”"],[3842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who does not associate anything with Allah, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids major sins, except that Paradise is guaranteed for him.” They asked him, “What are the major sins?” He said, “Associating partners with Allah, killing a Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle.”"],[3843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever comes to Allah worshiping Him and not associating anything with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids major sins, then Paradise is for him.” They asked him, “What are the major sins?” He said, “Associating partners with Allah, killing a Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle.”"],[3844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the soul of a believer is taken, the people of mercy among Allah’s servants meet it as you meet a bringer of good news in this world. They say, ‘Look at your companion to rest, for he was in severe distress.’ Then they ask him, ‘What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? Has she married?’ When they ask him about a man who died before him, he says, ‘Alas, that one died before me.’ They say, ‘Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. He was taken to his mother, the abyss. What an evil mother and what an evil nurturer!’ He said, ‘Your deeds are shown to your relatives and kinsfolk among the people of the Hereafter. If it is good, they rejoice and receive good tidings and say, “O Allah, this is Your bounty and Your mercy, so complete Your favor upon him and cause him to die upon it.” The deeds of the evildoer are shown to them, and they say, “O Allah, inspire him with a righteous deed that You are pleased with and that draws him near to You.”’”"],[3845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the soul of a believer dies, the people of mercy among Allah’s servants meet it as they meet a bringer of good news in this world. They say, ‘Look at your companion to rest, for he was in severe distress.’ Then they ask him, ‘What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? Has she married?’ When they ask him about someone who died before him, he says, ‘Alas, that one died before me.’ They say, ‘Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. He was taken to his mother, the abyss. What an evil mother and what an evil nurturer!’”"],[3846,"He said something from the Prophet ﷺ: “May no evil befall you, Abu Ayyub.”"],[3847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Maghrib and Isha prayers at Muzdalifah with one adhan and one iqamah."],[3848,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs of Maghrib Surat al-Anfal."],[3849,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in Maghrib al-A'raf."],[3850,"He told him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Water is from water.\""],[3851,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say: \"No prophet was ever sent, nor was there ever a caliph after him, but he had two confidants: a confidant who enjoined him to do good and forbade him from evil, and a confidant who spared no effort to corrupt him. So whoever is protected from the evil confidant is protected.\""],[3852,"It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, here are people who recite aloud in the daytime prayer.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"Why don't you pelt them with dung?\""],[3853,"'Uthman said: 'Woe to you! Where are the witnesses? Has he consummated the marriage?' They said: 'He married a woman but has not yet consummated with her.' 'Ali said to 'Uthman ؓ: 'If he had consummated with her, stoning would be lawful upon him. But since he has not consummated with his wife, flog him with the hadd punishment.' Abu Ayyub said: 'I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say what Abu al-Hasan mentioned.' So 'Uthman ؓ ordered it, and he was flogged with one hundred lashes."],[3854,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"Conceal the engagement, then perform wudu and perfect your wudu, then pray what Allah has decreed for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: 'O Allah, You have power and I have no power, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see in [name her by name] good for me in my worldly life and my hereafter, then decree her for me'—or he said: 'then destine her for me.'\""],[3855,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, that is fasting for the whole year.\" He said: I said to him: 'Every day counts as ten?' He said: \"Yes.\""],[3856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, that is fasting for the whole year.\""],[3857,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal has fasted the entire year.”"],[3858,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal is like one who has fasted all time.”"],[3859,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal has fasted all time.”"],[3860,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal has fasted all time.”"],[3861,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan, then follows it with six from Shawwal, it is like fasting all time.”"],[3862,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan, then follows it with from Shawwal, has fasted all time.”"],[3863,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal, it is as though he fasted the year.”"],[3864,"From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ: he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is as though he fasted all time.”"],[3865,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is as though he fasted all time.” Hafs said: Then I met Sa'd and he narrated to me."],[3866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six, it is as though he fasted the entire year.”"],[3867,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is like fasting all time.”"],[3868,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is like fasting all time.”"],[3869,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal, it is as if he has fasted a whole year.\""],[3870,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not face the qiblah or turn your backs to it while defecating or urinating; rather, turn east or west.”"],[3871,"He found some boys who had cornered a fox into an angle, so he drove them away, and I do not think he said anything except: “Is this done in the sanctuary of Allah?”"],[3872,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from ʿUmārah b. Ṣayyād, that ʿAṭāʾ b. Yasār informed him that Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī informed him, saying: “We used to sacrifice a single sheep that a man would slaughter on behalf of himself and his household; then later people began to vie with one another, and it became a matter of ostentation.”"],[3873,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The best charity is charity given to a relative who harbors hidden enmity.”"],[3874,"A bedouin intercepted the Prophet ﷺ during his journey and said, “Tell me what will bring me near Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.” He said, “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakāh, and maintain ties of kinship.”"],[3875,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.” The people said, “What is with him? What is with him?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “He is in need. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakāh, and maintain ties of kinship. Leave it.”"],[3876,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Guide me to a deed that will bring me near Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.” He said, “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakāh, and maintain ties of kinship.” When the man turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If he holds fast to what he has been commanded, he will enter Paradise.”"],[3877,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Ashjaʿ, Aslam, Ghifār, and whoever is from Banū Kaʿb are allies apart from other people; Allah and His Messenger are their allies.”"],[3878,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Perform ablution from touching the penis,” and sometimes he said, “Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.”"],[3879,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he ate something that had been changed by fire, would perform wudu."],[3880,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform wudu from what fire has touched.'"],[3881,"I heard Abu Ayyub in Egypt saying: 'By Allah, I do not know what to do with these karabees (latrines), for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you goes to defecate or urinate, he should not face the qiblah with his private parts.\"'"],[3882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not face the qiblah with your private parts, nor turn your backs to it.'"],[3883,"He heard Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from facing or turning away from the Qiblah (direction of prayer) when one of us goes to urinate or defecate.\""],[3884,"I heard Abu Ayyub, upon whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you urinates or defecates, he should not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it with his private parts.'"],[3885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you goes to defecate, he should not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but let him turn east or west.'"],[3886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it when defecating or urinating; turn east or west.'"],[3887,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us; and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; they said: Sufyan b. Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata' b. Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it when urinating or defecating, but turn east or west.'"],[3888,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever among you goes to defecate should not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it; turn east or west.'"],[3889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not face the qiblah when defecating or urinating, but turn east or west.'"],[3890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the one who goes to defecate from facing the qiblah, and he said: 'Turn east or west.'"],[3891,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'When one of you goes out to defecate, he should not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but let him turn east or west.'"],[3892,"By Allah, \"Whoever among you goes to defecate, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it. Turn eastward or westward.\""],[3893,"He heard Abu Ayyub say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the one who wants to defecate from facing the qiblah, and he said: \"Turn eastward or westward.\""],[3894,"He heard Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, forbidding the one who goes to defecate from facing the qiblah, and he said: \"Turn eastward or westward.\" He did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[3895,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When one of you goes to defecate, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back toward it, but turn eastward or westward.\""],[3896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs toward it, but turn eastward or westward.\""],[3897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not face the qiblah while urinating or defecating, but turn eastward or westward.\""],[3898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the one who goes to defecate from facing the qiblah, and he said: \"Turn eastward or westward.\""],[3899,"From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari: I do not think he did anything but trace it back to the Prophet, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. They meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away. The better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3900,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ata' b. Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days.\""],[3901,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. They meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away. The better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3902,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. They meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away. The better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3903,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Mu'adh b. al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us; and 'Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; they all said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' b. Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. They meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away. The better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to forsake his brother for more than three nights, so that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3905,"Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights, so that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights, so that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not turn your backs on one another, do not sever relations, and be servants of Allah as brothers. The abandonment of the believers is for three days; if they speak, then fine, otherwise Allah ﷻ turns away from them until they speak.\""],[3908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights, so that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3909,"Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim man to forsake his brother for more than three nights, so that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days, so that this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of them is the one who initiates the greeting of peace.\""],[3911,"\" Ibn Shihab informed me, saying: 'Ata bin Yazid narrated to me from Abu Ayyub: That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Witr is a duty, and whoever wants to pray witr with seven (rak'ahs), let him do so; whoever wants to pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever wants to pray witr with three, let him do so; and whoever wants to pray witr with one, let him do so.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1710)"],[3912,"The Prophet said, \"Witr (Odd) prayer is a duty, so whoever likes to pray with five units, let them do so, and whoever likes to pray with three units, let them do so, and whoever likes to pray with one unit, let them do so.\""],[3913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Witr prayer is five or three or one. If you are unable to do so, then make a gesture.\" \"This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Sulayman.\""],[3914,"\"Witr is obligatory upon every Muslim, so whoever is able to perform Witr with five (units), then let him perform Witr. And whoever is not able to perform Witr with five (units), then let him perform Witr with three (units). And whoever is not able to perform Witr with three (units), then let him perform Witr with one (unit). And whoever is not able to perform Witr with one (unit), then let him make a gesture (as a substitute).\""],[3915,"\" Ibn Shihab informed me, saying: 'Ata bin Yazid narrated to me from Abu Ayyub: That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Witr is a duty, and whoever wants to pray witr with seven (rak'ahs), let him do so; whoever wants to pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever wants to pray witr with three, let him do so; and whoever wants to pray witr with one, let him do so.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1710)"],[3916,"\" Ibn Shihab informed me, saying: 'Ata bin Yazid narrated to me from Abu Ayyub: That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Witr is a duty, and whoever wants to pray witr with seven (rak'ahs), let him do so; whoever wants to pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever wants to pray witr with three, let him do so; and whoever wants to pray witr with one, let him do so.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1710)"],[3917,"\"Az-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: 'Ata bin Yazid, from Abu Ayyub: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Witr is a duty, and whoever wants to pray witr with seven (rak'ahs), let him do so; whoever wants to pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever wants to pray witr with three, let him do so; and whoever wants to pray witr with one, let him do so.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1711)"],[3918,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever plants a tree, Allah records for him reward equal to what comes out of the fruit of that tree.\""],[3919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first to dispute on the Day of Resurrection will be a man and his wife. By Allah, her tongue will not speak, but her hands and feet will testify against her for what she used to conceal from her husband, and his hands and feet will testify for what he used to give her. Then the man and his household will be called, and the like of that. Then the people of the markets will be called, and whatever is found—then there will be no daniq or qirat, but the good deeds of this one will be given to that one whom he wronged, and the evil deeds of that one whom he wronged will be placed upon him. Then the tyrants will be brought in iron hammers, and it will be said: 'Drive them to the Fire.' By Allah, I do not know whether they will enter it or as Allah, the Exalted, said: {There is none of you but will come to it; this is upon your Lord an inevitability decreed. Then We will save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers in it, on their knees}.\""],[3920,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Two men may head to the mosque, and one of them leaves while his prayer is more virtuous than the other's, if he is the one with more intellect; and the other leaves while his prayer does not equal the weight of an atom.\""],[3921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O assembly of Muslims, whoever of you comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform the ritual bath; and if he finds perfume, there is no harm in applying some of it; and I urge you to use this toothstick.\" Ata' b. Yazid said: \"Then Ibn Abbas, who narrated to me from Abu Ayyub, told me, and Abdullah said: 'As for the bath, yes; as for the perfume, I do not know.'\""],[3922,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no Monday or Thursday except that the deeds are raised in them, except the deeds of two who are forsaking one another.\""],[3923,"The Prophet said, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be seated on thrones made of ruby around the Throne.\""],[3924,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you goes to relieve himself, he should not face the qiblah.”"],[3925,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥunayn, from his father, that Ibn ʿAbbās and al-Miswar b. Makhrama disagreed at al-Abwāʾ. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “The pilgrim in iḥrām washes his head,” while al-Miswar said: “The pilgrim in iḥrām does not wash his head.” So Ibn ʿAbbās sent him to Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī. He found him bathing between the two posts, screening himself with a garment. He said: I greeted him, and he said: “Who is this?” I said: “I am ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥunayn. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās sent me to ask you how the Messenger of God ﷺ used to wash his head while in iḥrām.” He said: Abū Ayyūb placed his hand on the garment and lowered it for me, then said to a man pouring water on him: “Pour.” So he poured on his head, then moved his head with his hands, bringing them forward and back. Then he said: “This is how I saw him do it.”"],[3926,"Ibn ʿAbbās and al-Miswar b. Makhrama debated about the pilgrim in iḥrām washing his head, so they sent me to Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī. I came to him while he was bathing between the two posts of a well. When he saw me, he pulled the garment to himself. I said: “Your nephew Ibn ʿAbbās sent me to ask you how you saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pour water over his head while in iḥrām.” He poured water over his head, then said: “Like this,” and he gestured with his hand over his head, bringing them forward and back three times."],[3927,"So I came to him and found Abū Ayyūb between the two posts washing his head, having screened himself with a garment. I asked him, and he lowered the garment with his hand until his head appeared, then moved his head and hair with his hands, bringing his hands forward through his hair and back. Then he said: “This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ bathe while in iḥrām.” Ibrāhīm said: I returned to them and informed them."],[3928,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Yes.” So Ibn ʿAbbās sent me to Abū Ayyūb: “Your nephew ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās sends you greetings and asks you how the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe and wash his head when in iḥrām.” I found him bathing between the two posts of a well, having screened himself with a garment. When I identified myself and asked him, he pulled the garment to himself until his face and head became visible to me, while a man stood at the well pouring water on him. Abū Ayyūb passed his hands over his head, bringing them forward and back. Then al-Miswar said to Ibn ʿAbbās: “I will never dispute with you again.” Ibn Jurayj did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[3929,"“We lived with our Prophet ﷺ and the people of the household used to sacrifice a sheep. Then a man sacrificed two sheep, and that was after [a spirit of] boasting.”"],[3930,"He used to command wiping over the leather socks and would wash his feet. It was said to him about that, and he said: “Wretched is my wealth if its benefit is for you and its sin is upon me. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and command it, but ablution has been made beloved to me.”"],[3931,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the turban.”"],[3932,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed with him, and the Prophet ﷺ settled on the lower floor while Abū Ayyūb was on the upper floor. Abū Ayyūb woke up one night and said: “Shall we walk above the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” So he went down to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “The lower floor is more comfortable for us.” He said: When Abū Ayyūb sent food to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would ask about the places where the Prophet’s fingers had left traces. Abū Ayyūb sent him food containing garlic, and he did not see in it the trace of the place of the Prophet’s fingers. He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Is it forbidden?” He said: “No, but I dislike it.” He said: “I dislike what you dislike, or what you dislike.” And the Prophet ﷺ used to be brought [food]."],[3933,"“Our ḥadīth? The Messenger of God ﷺ narrated it to us in this very gathering we are in?” He said: “Yes, about Madinah. I heard him while he was claiming that a time will come upon people when conquests of the earth will be opened, and men will go out to them and attain ease, livelihood, and food. They will pass by their brothers who are pilgrims or performing ʿumrah and say: ‘What keeps you in the hardship of living and severe hunger?’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘So one goes and another stays,’ until he said it several times, ‘and Madinah is better for them. No one remains in it and patiently endures its hardship and severity until he dies except that I will be for him on the Day of Resurrection a witness or an intercessor.’”"],[3934,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Were it not that you commit sins, Allah would create a people who sin, and He would forgive them.'"],[3935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and He would forgive them.'"],[3936,"Marwan said to him, 'What makes you do this?' He said, 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying a prayer: if I agreed with him, I agreed with you; and if I differed from him, I prayed and then returned to my family.'"],[3937,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever performs ablution as he was commanded and prays as he was commanded, his past deeds will be forgiven.' Is that so, O 'Uqbah b. 'Amir? He said, 'Yes.'"],[3938,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever performs ablution as he was commanded and prays as he was commanded, his past sins will be forgiven.' Is that so, O 'Uqbah b. 'Amir? He said, 'Yes.'"],[3939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him food with vegetables, containing onion or leek, and he did not see any trace of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it, so he refused to eat it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'What prevented you from eating?' He said, 'I did not see your trace in it, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I feel shy before the angels of Allah, and it is not forbidden.'"],[3940,"He asked Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ؓ , about a man who prays in his house, then comes to the mosque and catches that prayer: should he repeat it with the people or not? We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, 'Yes, he should repeat it; that gives him a share of the gathering.'"],[3941,"He asked Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ؓ , about a man who prays in his house, then comes to the mosque and catches that prayer: should he repeat it with the people or not? We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said, 'Yes, he should repeat it; that gives him a share of the gathering.'"],[3942,"They mentioned one day what nabidh is made in, and they disagreed about the gourd. Abu Ayyub al-Ansari passed by them, so they sent a man to him. Abu Ayyub said: \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ forbid every pitch-coated vessel in which nabidh is made,\" and he did not add anything to it."],[3943,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that an animal be made to stand and be shot (as a target)."],[3944,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the killing of animals by confinement (i.e., tying them up and using them as targets)."],[3945,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the confining of a beast (to be shot)."],[3946,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the confining of a beast (to be shot)."],[3947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the confining of an animal; if it were a chicken, I would not confine it."],[3948,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on Friday: \"Whoever performs ghusl, touches some perfume if he has any, wears his best clothes, then goes out until he reaches the mosque and does not step over people's necks, and remains silent when the imam comes out and does not speak, will be forgiven what is between that Friday and the next.\""],[3949,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, touches perfume if he has any, wears his best clothes, then goes out until he reaches the mosque and prays as much as he wishes without harming anyone, then remains silent when the imam comes out, it will be an expiation for what is between that Friday and the next Friday.\""],[3950,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Al-hamdu lillahi 'ala kulli hal' (Praise be to Allah in every situation), and let the one who hears him say: 'Yarhamuka Allah' (May Allah have mercy on you), and he should reply to him: 'Yahdikumu Allah wa yuslihu balakum' (May Allah guide you and set your affairs right).\""],[3951,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.\""],[3952,"He had a loft, and a ghoul used to come and enter it. He complained about it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"When you see it, say: 'Bismillah, answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\" So it came and he said that to it, and he seized it. It said: \"I will not return,\" so he released it. Then he went to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to him: \"What did your captive do?\" He said: \"I seized it, and it said: 'I will not return,' so I released it.\" He said: \"It will return.\" He seized it two or three times, each time it said: \"I will not return,\" and the Prophet ﷺ would say: \"What did your captive do?\" and he would say: \"I seized it, and it said: 'I will not return,'\" and he would say: \"It will return.\" Then I seized it and it said: \"Release me and I will teach you something you can say so that nothing will come near you: the Verse of the Throne (Ayat al-Kursi).\" So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: \"She spoke the truth, though she is a liar.\""],[3953,"I had date palms in my enclosure, and I noticed them diminishing. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Tomorrow you will find a cat in it. Say: Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The next day I found a cat in it, so I said, “Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” It turned into an old woman and said, “I adjure you by Allah to leave me, for I will not return.” So I left her. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “What did the man and his captive do?” I told him her story, and he said, “She lied. She will return. Say to her: Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So [I did], and she turned into an old woman and said, “I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Ayyub, to leave me this time, for I will not return.” So I left her. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me as he had said before. I did that three times, and on the third she said to me, “I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Ayyub, to leave me until I teach you something that no devil hears without leaving that house.” I said, “What is it?” She said, “The Verse of the Throne. No devil hears it but he departs.” I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “She spoke the truth, though she is a liar.”"],[3954,"“…that I teach you something which, if you say it, none of us will harm you.” He said: I said, “What is it?” She said, “The Verse of the Throne: {Allah – there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence}.” I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “She spoke the truth, but she is a liar.”"],[3955,"I was disturbed by the night visitor of the house, so I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said—and there was a small window in a house of ours—“Lie in wait for it. When you see something, say: ‘Begone! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ calls you.’” He said: So I lay in wait, and something dangled down from the small window. I leaped at it and said, “Begone! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ calls you.” And I seized it. It pleaded with me and said, “I will not return.” He said: So I released it. In the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “What did your captive do?” I told him what had happened, and he said, “Indeed, he will return.” He said: I did that three times, each time seizing him and telling the Prophet ﷺ what had happened. On the third time, I seized him and said, “You will not part from me until I bring you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He adjured me and pleaded with me, saying, “I will teach you something which, if you say it at night, no jinn or thief will come near you.” He said: “Recite the Verse of the Throne.” He said: So I released him, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “What did your captive do?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, he adjured me and pleaded with me until I had mercy on him, and he taught me something which, if I say it, no jinn or thief will come near me.” He said, “He spoke the truth, though he is a liar.”"],[3956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says after the dawn prayer ten times: ‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,’ it will be for him the equivalent of freeing four slaves from the descendants of Isma‘il.”"],[3957,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says: ‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent’ ten times, it will be for him the equivalent of ten freed slaves—or a freed slave.” [The wording is that of the hadith of ‘Abd al-Wahhab.]"],[3958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says: ‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,’ it will be for him like the equivalent of a freed slave—or freed slaves.”"],[3959,"…‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things competent’ once or ten times, that will equal a slave or ten slaves for him.” I said, “From whom did you hear it?” He said, “From ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla.” So I went to him, and he narrated it. I said, “From whom did you hear it?” He said, “From Abu Ayyub, narrating from the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[3960,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Whoever says: ‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,’ it will be for him as the equivalent of ten slaves from the descendants of Isma‘il ﷺ .”"],[3961,"…‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things competent’ is like one who frees four persons from the descendants of Isma‘il.” He said: I said to al-Rabi‘ b. Khuthaym, “From whom did you hear it?” He said, “From ‘Amr b. Maymun.” So I went to ‘Amr b. Maymun and said, “From whom did you hear it?” He said, “From Ibn Abi Layla.” So I went to Ibn Abi Layla and said, “From whom did you hear it?” He said, “From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, narrating it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[3962,"“He is right. I told them to him.” I said, “From whom do you narrate it?” He said, “From Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[3963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says: ‘There is no deity but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things competent,’ it is like freeing four persons from the descendants of Isma‘il.”"],[3964,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Say: ‘He is Allah, the One’ equals one third of the Qur’an.”"],[3965,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad (Say: He is Allah, the One) is a third of the Qur’an.”"],[3966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qur’an in a night?” We feared that he would command us with something we could not do, so we remained silent. Then he said: “Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qur’an in a night?” We feared that he would command us with something we could not do, so we remained silent. Then he said: “Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qur’an in a night? For whoever recites in a night ‘Allāhu al-Wāḥid al-Ṣamad’ (Allah, the One, the Eternal Refuge) has recited in his night a third of the Qur’an.”"],[3967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Can any of you not recite one-third of the Quran in one night?\" We remained silent, so he repeated it three times and then said, \"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Surah Al-Ikhlas) in one night, has indeed recited one-third of the Quran.\""],[3968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The transgressing party will kill ʿAmmār.”"],[3969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray four rakʿahs before Ẓuhr when the sun began to decline. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer?” He said: “The gates of heaven are opened at the sun’s decline until Ẓuhr is prayed, and I love that righteous deeds be raised for me during them.”"],[3970,"From Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī regarding the four [rakʿahs] before Ẓuhr: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer that you keep performing when the sun declines?” He said: “O Abū Ayyūb, the gates of heaven are opened at the sun’s decline, and the gates of the heavens do not close until Ẓuhr is prayed.” He said: “Does he recite in them?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Does he separate them with salām?” He said: “No.”"],[3971,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, I saw him persistently praying four [rakʿahs] before Ẓuhr, and he said: “When the sun declines, the gates of heaven are opened, and none of them is closed until Ẓuhr is prayed, so I love that good be raised for me at that hour.”"],[3972,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are these four rakʿahs?” He said: “This is the hour in which the gates of heaven are opened and they do not close until Ẓuhr is prayed, so I love to offer them beforehand.”"],[3973,"He used to pray four units before Dhuhr prayer, so he was asked, and he said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying it, so I asked him, and he said, 'Indeed, it is a time when the gates of the heavens are opened, and I love to have a righteous deed raised for me in it.'\""],[3974,"He used to pray four [rakʿahs] before Ẓuhr, and it was said to him, “What is this prayer?” He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying them, so I asked him and he said: ‘It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, so I love that righteous deeds be raised for me during it.’”"],[3975,"I saw Abū Ayyūb removing his leather socks, and people looked at him. He said: “Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over them, but ablution has been made beloved to me.”"],[3976,"Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī campaigned in the land of the Romans. When he became gravely ill, he said: “When I die, carry me with you, and when you line up against the enemy, bury me beneath your feet. I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; were it not for my present condition, I would not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise.’”"],[3977,"From their elders, they said: We were with Abu Ayyub in the land of the Romans, and he fell ill and instructed us: Carry me, and when you line up against the enemy, bury me beneath your feet. Then he said: I shall relate to you a hadith that, were I not in this state, I would not relate to you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise.”"],[3978,"From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best charity is charity to a hostile relative.”"],[3979,"While Ali ؓ was sitting in the courtyard, a man came showing signs of travel and said: Peace be upon you, O my master. It was asked: Who is this? He said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Abu Ayyub said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever has me as his master, Ali is his master.”"],[3980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you defecates, let him wipe with three stones, for that suffices him.”"],[3981,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while we were in Madinah: “I have been informed of the caravan of Abu Sufyan, that it is approaching. Would you like us to go out against this caravan? Perhaps God will grant it to us as booty.” We said: Yes. So he went out and we went out with him. When we had traveled for a day or two, he said to us: “What do you think about the people, for they have been informed of your departure?” We said: No, by God, we have no strength to fight the enemy, but we wanted the caravan. Then he said: “What do you think about fighting the people?” We said the same. Al-Miqdad b. Amr said: Then we will not say to you, O Messenger of God, as the people of Moses said to Moses: “So go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are sitting right here.” He said: Then we, the Ansar, wished that we had said as al-Miqdad said, more beloved to us than having great wealth. Then God ﷻ sent down to His Messenger: “Just as your Lord brought you out of your home in truth, while a party of the believers were unwilling, disputing with you about the truth after it had become clear, as if they were being driven to death while looking on.” Then God ﷻ sent down: “I am with you, so strengthen those who believe. I will cast terror into the hearts of those who disbelieve, so strike above the necks and strike every fingertip of theirs.” And He said: “And when God promised you one of the two groups that it would be yours, and you wished that the one without power would be yours.” The one with power was the people, and the one without power was the caravan. When He promised us one of the two groups, either the people or the caravan, our souls were at ease. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a man to see what was before the people. He said: I saw a black mass, and I do not know. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is they, it is they. Come, let us count ourselves.” We did so, and we were three hundred and thirteen men. The Messenger of God told us our number, and that pleased him, and he praised God and said: “The number of the companions of Talut.” Then we met the people and formed ranks. Some of us advanced in front of the row, and the Messenger of God ﷺ looked at them and said: “With me, with me.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, I implore You to fulfill Your promise.” Ibn Rawaha said: O Messenger of God, I wish to advise you, and the Messenger of God ﷺ is the best one to be advised. God ﷻ is too great for you to implore His promise. He said: “O Ibn Rawaha, I will certainly implore God to fulfill His promise, for God does not break His appointment.” Then he took a handful of dust and the Messenger of God ﷺ threw it in the faces of the people, and they were defeated. Then God ﷻ sent down: “You did not throw when you threw, but God threw.” We killed and took captives. Umar ؓ said: O Messenger of God, I do not think you should have captives, for we are only callers and reconcilers. We, the Ansar, said: Umar only urges this out of envy toward us. The Messenger of God ﷺ slept, then woke and said: “Summon Umar for me.” He was summoned, and he said: God ﷻ has sent down to me: “It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made much slaughter in the land. You desire the goods of this world, but God desires the Hereafter. And God is Mighty, Wise.”"],[3982,"“We used to pray Maghrib when the sun had set.”"],[3983,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Pray the Maghrib prayer as the sun sets; hasten to it before the star appears.”"],[3984,"We said among ourselves, secretly from the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Our wealth has been lost, so if only we could devote ourselves to it.” Then God ﷻ revealed in His Book, refuting what we had intended: “And spend in the way of God and do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction” (2:195), concerning staying with wealth and improving it, and abandoning jihad and spending in the way of God ﷻ."],[3985,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: “How excellent are those who use the toothpick!” They said: “And what are those who use the toothpick, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Those who use the toothpick for ablution and those who use it for food. As for the toothpick of ablution, it is rinsing the mouth, sniffing water, and between the fingers. And as for the toothpick of food, it is after food. For nothing is harder on the two angels than to see something between the teeth of their companion while he stands praying.”"],[3986,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: “How excellent are those who use the toothpick for food and ablution!”"],[3987,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I have a nephew who does not refrain from what is forbidden.” He said: “What is his religion?” He said: “He prays and affirms God’s oneness.” He said: “Ask him to give you his religion as a gift; if he refuses, then buy it from him.” So that man sought it from him, but he refused. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: “I found him stingy with his religion.” Then God ﷻ revealed: “God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills” (4:48)."],[3988,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seeking permission is that you call the servant so that the household you are seeking permission from may become aware.”"],[3989,"We said: “O Messenger of God, this is the greeting (salām), so what is seeking permission (isti’nās)?” He said: “A man speaks a glorification, an akbīr, a praise, and clears his throat, thereby alerting the household.”"],[3990,"The Messenger of God ﷺ “used to use the toothstick at night two or three times.”"],[3991,"The Messenger of God ﷺ “when he stood for night prayer, would pray four rakʿahs, neither speaking nor commanding anything, and he would say the salām between every two rakʿahs.”"],[3992,"“When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, he sniffed water three times, rinsed his mouth, inserted his two fingers into his mouth, and his palms would reach, when washing his face, the front parts of his ears. When he wiped his head, he wiped with his two fingers the back parts of his ears along with his head, and he ran his fingers through his beard.”"],[3993,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will visit one another on white she-camels as if they were rubies. There is no beast in Paradise except camels and birds.”"],[3994,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Who are those whom God ﷻ meant by ‘men who love to purify themselves, and God loves those who purify themselves’ (9:108)?” He said: “They used to cleanse themselves with water, and they would not sleep the whole night.”"],[3995,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, the polytheists went to one another saying, \"Indeed, this Sābi' has been cut off tonight.\" So God, the Exalted, revealed: {Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar} to the end of the surah."],[3996,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about tas'īr (distorting the mouth), and he said: \"It is twisting the corner of the mouth.\""],[3997,"And about the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked about Shafa' and Witr (prayers). So he said, \"Two days and one night - the day of Arafah and the day of sacrifice. And Witr is the night of sacrifice, the night of gathering.\""],[3998,"And from the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked about His saying, Exalted is He: {mudhāmmatān} (two dark green gardens), and he said: \"Two intensely green ones.\""],[3999,"From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ that food was sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ with some green vegetables containing onion or leek. He did not see the trace of the Messenger of God ﷺ in it, so he refused to eat it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"What prevented you from eating?\" He said, \"I did not see your trace in it, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I feel shy before the angels of God, though it is not forbidden.\""],[4000,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A morning or evening journey in the path of God is better than what the sun rises and sets upon.\""],[4001,"I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari ؓ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A morning or evening journey in the path of God is better than what the sun rises and sets upon.\""],[4002,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever separates a mother from her child, God will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4003,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he supplicated, would begin with himself."],[4004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali, 'You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.'"],[4005,"A man was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Praise be to Allah, much, good, and blessed therein.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Who is the owner of this word?' The man fell silent, thinking that he had been caught by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for something he disliked. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Who is he? For he has said nothing but what is correct.' The man said, 'I said it, O Messenger of Allah, hoping for good thereby.' He said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw thirteen angels hastening to your word, each of them vying to raise it to Allah, Blessed and Exalted.'"],[4006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Shall I not teach you, O Abu Ayyub?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Say in the morning: \"There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; no partner with Him,\" ten times. No Muslim servant says it ten times except that Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and they will be better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than freeing ten slaves. And no one says it in the evening except that Allah writes for him the like of that.'"],[4007,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at al-Ji'ranah at his place and made a sacrifice for him, and spent the day with him, and Khalid spent the evening with him. Then the Prophet ﷺ called for the 'Umrah, and the Prophet ﷺ descended with Muharrish to the valley until they reached a place called Ashqab. He said, 'O Muharrish, the water of this place is up to the kurr, and whatever is for Khalid and the rest of the valley is for you, O Muharrish.' Then the Prophet ﷺ scraped the kurr with his hand, and water gushed out, and he drank. Then the Prophet ﷺ called for the 'Umrah and sent Khalid to a man from his companions called Muharrish b. 'Abd Allah. The Prophet ﷺ was at that time afraid of entering Makkah, so he took him by a route that turned him away from those he feared, which he knew, until he completed his rites, and they returned at dawn to Khalid, and Muharrish shaved him, meaning he shaved his head."],[4008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He is free from miserliness who pays the zakat, shows hospitality to the guest, and gives in times of calamity.'"],[4009,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Three things: whoever has them is protected from the miserliness of his soul: paying the zakat, showing hospitality to the guest, and giving in times of calamity.'"],[4010,"From Khalid, ‘and Sa‘d had appointed him as his deputy over Kufa.’"],[4011,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘O Khalid, there will be tribulation, new occurrences, disagreement, and division. When that happens, if you are able to be the one killed rather than the killer, then do so.’"],[4012,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.’"],[4013,"One of them said to the other, \"Did you not receive the message? Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, 'Whoever kills himself will not be punished in his grave'?\" He replied, \"Yes.\""],[4014,"‘You heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave”?’ Khalid said, ‘Yes.’"],[4015,"‘That you inform us of the funeral of a righteous man so that we may attend it?’ We said, ‘It was hot and the man had a stomach illness.’ One of them said to his companion, ‘Did you not hear the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave”?’ He said, ‘Indeed, yes.’"],[4016,"‘You hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave”?’ He said, ‘Indeed, yes.’"],[4017,"‘You heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave”?’ He said, ‘Yes.’"],[4018,"‘You heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave.”’"],[4019,"‘That you inform us about your companion?’ I said, ‘He had a stomach illness, so we buried him early.’ Sulayman b. Surad said, ‘I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The one with a stomach illness will not be punished in the grave.” Do you bear witness, O Khalid?’ He said, ‘Indeed, yes.’"],[4020,"‘We heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The one with a stomach illness will not be punished in his grave.”’"],[4021,"‘You heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed by his stomach will not be punished in his grave”?’ One of them said to his companion, ‘Yes.’"],[4022,"I saw the Messenger of God raising his hands, saying: ‘O God, bless the horses of Ahmas and its men.’"],[4023,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “You will surely be tested concerning my family after me.”"],[4024,"My father narrated to me, and he was one of the companions of the Tree [who gave the pledge under the tree]. Ḥ; and Abū Muslim al-Kashshī narrated to us; ʿAlī b. al-Madīnī narrated to us; Marwān b. Muʿāwiya narrated to us. Ḥ; and Muḥammad b. al-ʿAbbās al-Muʾaddib narrated to us; Saʿīd b. Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; ʿAbbād b. al-ʿAwwām narrated to us—all from Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī; Nāfiʿ b. Khālid al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us from his father, and he was one of the companions of the Tree. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer one day, and he made it light, then sat and prolonged the sitting. When he finished, we said, “O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the sitting in your prayer.” He said, “It was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked Allah in it for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy you with a punishment that afflicted those before you, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to give an enemy power over your community to annihilate it, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make you into factions and make some of you taste the violence of others, but He withheld it from me.”"],[4025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed while people were watching, prayed a light prayer but complete in bowing and prostration."],[4026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed while people were around him, prayed a light prayer but complete in bowing and prostration. Then one day he sat and prolonged the sitting until some of us gestured to others, “Be quiet, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is receiving revelation.” When he finished, some of the people said, “O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the sitting until some of us gestured to others that revelation was coming down to you.” He said, “No, but it was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked Allah in it for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to punish you with a punishment with which those before you were punished, and I asked Him not to give an enemy power over your common people to violate them, and He granted these to me. And I asked Him not to make you into factions and make some of you taste the violence of others, but He withheld it from me.” I said to him, “Did your father hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “Yes, I heard him say that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the number of my fingers—these ten fingers.”"],[4027,"After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr sent commanders to Syria and appointed Khālid b. Saʿīd over an army."],[4028,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Yemen and said, “Whoever of the Arabs you pass by and you hear the call to prayer among them, do not confront them. Whoever you do not hear the call to prayer among, invite them to Islam, and if they do not respond, then fight them.”"],[4029,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ when he arrived from the Abyssinian migration, and with him was his daughter, Umm Khālid. He brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was wearing a yellow shirt that pleased the girl. She had understood some of the speech of Abyssinia, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to her in the language of Abyssinia and said, “Sanah, sanah,” which means “beautiful” in Abyssinian. Then he said to her, “Wear it out and wear it ragged, then wear it out and wear it ragged.” He said, By Allah, she wore it out, then wore it ragged, then wore it out, then wore it ragged. Then she leaned toward the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed her hand on the spot of the seal of prophethood, and her father pushed her away, but the Prophet ﷺ said, “Leave her.”"],[4030,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a ring on his hand, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “O Khālid, what is this ring?” He said, “A ring I have acquired.” He said, “Throw it to me.” So I threw it to him, and it turned out to be a ring of iron coated with silver. The Prophet ﷺ said, “What is its inscription?” I said, “Muḥammad, Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ took it and wore it, and it was the ring that was on his hand."],[4031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When a plague occurs in a land and you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it. And when it occurs in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it.”"],[4032,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, the people most severe in punishing people in this world will be the most severe in punishment with Allah on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4033,"From his father, “regarding the naming of those who witnessed with ʿAlī ؓ from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Khālid b. Abī Khālid.”"],[4034,"That he “saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing on a bow or a staff in the eastern part of Thaqīf while reciting ‘By the sky and the night comer’ until he completed it. I memorized it in the Jāhiliyya while I was a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam.”"],[4035,"From his father, “regarding the naming” of those who witnessed with ʿAlī ؓ from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: Khuwaylid b. ʿAmr al-Anṣārī, a Badrī from Banū Salama."],[4036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nothing befalls any of your crops or fruits from a bird or a beast except that there is reward for him in it.”"],[4037,"“My brother Khallād and I went out to Badr on a lean camel of ours.”"],[4038,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: \"God, may He be exalted, has granted you a prayer that is better for you than red camels. It has been appointed for you between the evening prayer and the rising of dawn.\""],[4039,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest, while I was at his camel's side: \"No bequest to an heir. God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right. For the fornicator is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father or takes as patrons other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. God will accept from him neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4040,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Khawwat b. Jubayr is given the kunya Abu Salih.\""],[4041,"From his father: \"In the naming of those who were present with 'Ali ؓ: Khawwat b. Jubayr, a Badri from Banu Haritha. He turned back from the road, so the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted him a share.\""],[4042,"Khawwat b. Jubayr b. al-Nu'man b. Umayya b. al-Bark—and the name of al-Bark is Imru' al-Qays b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. 'Awf—the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted him on the Day of Badr his share and his reward."],[4043,"Khawwat b. Jubayr died in the year forty, and his age was seventy-four."],[4044,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Khawwat b. Jubayr died in the year forty.\""],[4045,"We encamped with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Marr al-Zahran. He said: I came out of my tent, and there I saw some women conversing. They pleased me, so I returned, took out my bag, and from it took out a fine garment and put it on. Then I came and sat with them. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out of his dome and said: \"Abu 'Abd Allah, what makes you sit with them?\" When I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, I was awed and confused. I said: \"O Messenger of God, a camel of mine has strayed, and I am looking for a hobble for it.\" He went on, and I followed him. He threw his cloak to me and entered the arak trees. It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his back against the greenness of the arak. He relieved himself, performed ablution, and came back while water was flowing from his beard onto his chest—or he said dripping from his beard onto his chest. He said: \"Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of your camel?\" Then we set off, and he would not catch up with me on the journey except to say: \"Peace be upon you, Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of that camel?\" When I saw that, I hurried to Madinah and avoided the mosque and sitting with the Prophet ﷺ. When that went on for a long time, I looked for a time when the mosque was empty, so I went to the mosque and stood praying. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out suddenly from one of his rooms and prayed two brief rak'as. I prolonged my prayer hoping he would leave and let me be. He said: \"Prolong as much as you wish, Abu 'Abd Allah, for I will not stand until you finish.\" I said to myself: By God, I will apologize to the Messenger of God ﷺ and clear his heart. When he said: \"Peace be upon you, Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of that camel?\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, that camel has not strayed since I became a Muslim.\" He said: \"May God have mercy on you\" three times. Then he did not return to any of what had been."],[4046,"A man died and left a bequest to me. Among what he bequeathed were the mother of his child and a free woman. There occurred between the mother of the child and the woman some talk, and the woman said to her: \"You wretched one, tomorrow you will be taken by your ear and sold in the market.\" I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"She will not be sold.\""],[4047,"I fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ visited me. When I recovered, he said: \"There is no sick person who falls ill except that he vows something and intends something good. So fulfill for God what you promised Him.\""],[4048,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is unlawful.\""],[4049,"I was praying when a man behind me said: \"Make it light, for we have a need for you.\" I turned and there was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4050,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are of six kinds. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies as a Muslim, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and whoever dies as a disbeliever, the Fire becomes obligatory for him. Like for like: a servant intends a good deed, so a good deed is recorded for him; and he intends an evil deed but is not requited except with the like of it. The servant does a good deed, so ten are recorded for him. And the servant spends an expenditure in the path of God, so it is multiplied for him seven hundred times. And people are of four kinds: one given abundance in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; one given scarcity in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and scarcity in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[4051,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are of six kinds. Among them is one given abundance in this world and in the Hereafter; among them is one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; among them is one given restriction in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; and among them is one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies not associating anything with God enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating something with God enters the Fire. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him; and whoever does it, an evil deed is recorded against him. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him; and if he does it, ten times are recorded for him. And an expenditure in the path of God, exalted is He, is seven hundred times.\""],[4052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are six. The people are: one given abundance in this world and the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; one given restriction in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies as a Muslim or a believer not associating anything with God, Paradise becomes obligatory for him; and whoever dies as a disbeliever, the Fire becomes obligatory for him. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, but God knows that he has made his heart aware of it and was eager for it, a good deed is recorded for him and nothing is multiplied. Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not recorded against him; and whoever does it, one is recorded against him and nothing is multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, it is for him ten times the like of it; and whoever spends an expenditure in the path of God, it is for him seven hundred times.\""],[4053,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are six. [Among people are:] one given abundance in this world and the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; one given restriction in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; and one given abundance in the Hereafter and restriction in this world. The deeds are six: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times its like, and seven hundred times. Whoever dies as a Muslim or a believer not associating anything with God enters Paradise; and whoever dies as a disbeliever enters the Fire. Whoever intends a good deed until his heart is aware of it, a good deed is recorded for him and it is not multiplied. Whoever does an evil deed, one evil deed is recorded against him and it is not multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, ten times its like are recorded for him; and whoever spends an expenditure in the path of God, seven hundred times are recorded for him.\""],[4054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What a man you would be were it not for two traits in you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, what are they?\" He said: \"You let your lower garment hang low and you let your hair grow long.\" I said: \"No doubt I will not go back.\" He said: \"So he cut his hair and raised his lower garment.\""],[4055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man: letting the lower garment hang low and letting the hair grow long.\""],[4056,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Excellent is the young man Khuraym, if only he would take from his hair and shorten his lower garment.\""],[4057,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"O Khuraym b. Fātik, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man.\" He said: \"What are they, may my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God? Is one enough for me?\" He said: \"Letting your hair grow long and letting your lower garment hang low.\" So Khuraym went off and cut his hair and shortened his lower garment."],[4058,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Excellent is the young man Khuraym, if only he would shorten from his hair and raise from his lower garment.\" Khuraym said: \"My hair will not pass my ears and my lower garment will not pass my ankles.\""],[4059,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the morning prayer, and when he finished, he said while standing: \"False testimony has equated with associating partners with God\" three times, then he recited this verse: {And avoid the word of falsehood, being upright for God, not associating partners with Him}."],[4060,"From Khuraym b. Fātik al-Asadī, a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The people of Syria are God's whip on His earth; He takes vengeance through them upon whomever He wills of His servants. It is forbidden for their hypocrites to prevail over their believers, and they will die only in grief and sorrow.”"],[4061,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There will be a tribulation in which the one sleeping is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one striving, and the one striving is better than the one riding.”"],[4062,"While I was going about seeking some cattle of mine, I suddenly came upon their tracks when night overtook me at Abraq al-ʿAzzāf. I cried out at the top of my voice: “I seek refuge in the mighty one of this valley from the fools of his people,” and suddenly a caller called out."],[4063,"I set out in search of camels and found them at al-Abraq al-ʿAzzāf. I hobbled them and used the foreleg of one of them as a pillow—this was around the time of the Prophet's ﷺ emergence. Then I said: “I seek refuge in the great one of this valley.” He said: That is what they used to do in the pre-Islamic era. Then suddenly a caller called out to me and said."],[4064,"Khuraym b. Aws b. Ḥāritha b. Lām: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, may God have mercy on him, said to him: “O Messenger of God, I wish to praise you.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Go ahead; may God not break your mouth.” So al-ʿAbbās began to say."],[4065,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “This white al-Ḥīra has been shown to me, and this al-Shaymāʾ bt. Buqayla al-Azdiyya on a dappled gray mule, veiled with a black khimār.” I said: “O Messenger of God, if we enter al-Ḥīra and I find her in this description, is she mine?” He said: “She is yours.” Then the Arabs apostatized, but no one from Ṭayyiʾ apostatized. We fought Banū Asad, among whom was Ṭulayḥa b. Khuwaylid al-Faqʿasī. Khālid b. al-Walīd praised us, and among what he said about us was."],[4066,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood in one of the prayers, and when he raised his head from bowing he said: “O God, curse Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God and His Messenger. Ghifār—may God forgive them—and Aslam—may God grant them peace.”"],[4067,"He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said during a prayer: “O God, curse Banū Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God. Ghifār—may God forgive them—and Aslam—may God grant them peace.”"],[4068,"The Prophet ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer. When he raised his head from the last rakʿa he said: “God curse Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God and His Messenger. Aslam—may God grant them peace—and Ghifār—may God forgive them.” Then he fell down in prostration. When he finished the prayer he turned his face to the people and said: “O people, it was not I who said this; rather God, exalted be He, said it.”"],[4069,"Khafāf b. Īmāʾ: The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, then raised his head and said: “Ghifār—may God forgive them—Aslam—may God grant them peace—and ʿUṣayya disobeyed God and His Messenger. O God, curse Banū Liḥyān, Riʿl, and Dhakwān.” Then he went down into prostration. Khafāf said: On account of that, the curse of the disbelievers was made to fall."],[4070,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed—ḥ—and ʿUbayd b. Ghannām narrated to us: Abū Bakr b. Abī Shayba narrated to us—ḥ—and al-Ḥusayn b. Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUthmān b. Abī Shayba narrated to us: They both said: Muḥammad b. Bishr narrated to us: Muḥammad b. ʿAmr narrated to us: Khālid b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥarmala narrated to us, from al-Ḥārith b. Khafāf b. Īmāʾ, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, then raised his head and said: “Ghifār—may God forgive them—Aslam—may God grant them peace—and ʿUṣayya disobeyed God and His Messenger. O God, curse Banū Liḥyān. O God, curse Riʿl and Dhakwān. God is greatest.” Then he fell down in prostration."],[4071,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said the salam after three rak‘ahs in the ‘Asr prayer, then entered. A man called al-Khirbaq, who had long arms, stood up to him and said, “Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of God?” He came out angry, dragging his cloak, and said, “He spoke the truth?” They said, “Yes.” So he stood and prayed that rak‘ah."],[4072,"“Abu Salama al-Sulami stayed with us, and we hosted him for two months.”"],[4073,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if he has harm that hurts him.”"],[4074,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if he may suffer harm from him that hurts him.”"],[4075,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, while the Prophet ﷺ looked at the Angel of Death ﷺ at the head of a man from the Ansar: “O Angel of Death, be gentle with my companion, for he is a believer.” The Angel of Death ﷺ said: “Be of good heart and cool of eye, and know that I am gentle with every believer. And know, O Muhammad, that I seize the soul of the son of Adam, and when a crier from his family cries out, I stand in the house with his soul and say, ‘What is this crier? By God, we have not wronged him, nor have we preceded his term, nor have we hastened his decree. We have no sin in seizing him. If you are content with what God has done, you will be rewarded; but if you grieve and are displeased, you will sin and be burdened. You have no claim against us, and we still have a return to you, and then another return, so beware. There is no household, O Muhammad, of hair or clay, land or sea, plain or mountain, but I examine them every day and night, until I know their young and old better than they know themselves. By God, O Muhammad, if I wanted to seize the soul of a mosquito, I could not do so until God Himself permits its seizure.’” Ja‘far said: “It has reached me that he examines them only at the times of prayer. When he looks at the time of death, whoever was diligent in the prayers, the angel draws near to him, drives away Satan from him, and prompts him with ‘There is no god but God; Muhammad is the Messenger of God.’ And that is the tremendous state.”"],[4076,"“The Prophet ﷺ commanded the cutting of bells.”"],[4077,"He narrated to me that a traveling group from Mudar passed by and in it was a bell, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “The angels do not approach a traveling group in which there is a bell.”"],[4078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a detachment as spies for him and appointed over them 'Asim b. Thabit, who was the grandfather of 'Asim b. 'Umar. They set out until when they were in part of the way between 'Usfan and Makkah and stopped at a place, they were reported to a tribe of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. They pursued them with nearly a hundred archers, tracking their traces until they reached a stopping place where they found a date-stone from dates they had taken as provision from the dates of Madinah. They said, 'This is from the dates of Yathrib,' and followed their traces until they caught up with them. When 'Asim b. Thabit and his companions sensed them, they took refuge on a hillock. The people came and surrounded them and said, 'You have a covenant and a pledge that if you come down to us, we will not kill any man of you.' 'Asim b. Thabit said, 'As for me, I will not descend under the protection of an unbeliever. O Allah, inform Your Messenger about us.' So they fought them, and they shot them until they killed 'Asim among seven men. Khubayb b. 'Adi and Zayd b. Dathina remained until they sold them in Makkah. Banu al-Harith b. 'Amir b. Nawfal bought Khubayb, and al-Harith had been killed on the day of Badr. He remained with them as a prisoner until they resolved to kill him. He borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Harith, and she lent it to him to shave his pubic hair. She said: 'I became heedless of a little child of mine, who crawled to him until he reached him. He took him and placed him on his thigh. When she saw him, she became terrified with a fright that he recognized in her, while the razor was in his hand. He said, \"Do you fear that I will kill him? I would not do that, if Allah wills.\"' She used to say, 'I have not seen a prisoner better than Khubayb. I saw him eating from a bunch of grapes, and there was no fruit in Makkah that day, while he was bound in iron. It was nothing but provision that Allah provided him.' Then they took him out of the sanctuary to kill him. He said, 'Let me pray two rak'ahs.' So he prayed two rak'ahs, then said, 'Were it not that you would think that what is in me is fear of death, I would have increased.' He was the first to institute the two rak'ahs at the time of killing. Then he said, 'O Allah, count them by number,' then he said..."],[4079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me alone as a spy to Quraysh. He said: I came to the wood of Khubayb while I was wary of being seen, and I climbed up it and untied Khubayb. He fell to the ground, and I withdrew not far. Then Khubayb seemed as if the earth had swallowed him, and Khubayb has not been seen until now. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba said: Ja'far b. 'Awn had narrated from Ja'far b. 'Amr b. Umayya, from his father, from his grandfather."],[4080,"The Prophet ﷺ went out seeking a face, so I and another man from my people went with him. We said, \"We dislike that our people witness something that we do not witness with them.\" He asked, \"Have you both embraced Islam?\" We replied, \"No.\" He said, \"Then we do not seek assistance from pagans.\" We both embraced Islam and witnessed with him. Afterward, a man from the pagans struck me on my shoulder, so I killed him. Then I married his daughter, and she used to say, \"May you never be deprived of a man who wears this turban!\", and I used to reply, \"May you never be deprived of a man who made your father hasten towards Hell.\""],[4081,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and a man from my people, before we had embraced Islam, and we said: 'We feel ashamed that our people should witness a scene that we do not witness with them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Have you embraced Islam?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'I do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists.' So we embraced Islam and witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4082,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I do not seek help from a polytheist.”"],[4083,"“By Allah, today I have seen a matter that I did not think I would see: a people who turned away from the guidance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions.” He said that about those who fasted, then he said at that: “O Allah, take me to You.”"],[4084,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Caesar, the ruler of the Romans, with a letter. I said, 'Ask permission for the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' It was told to Caesar, 'There is a man at the door who claims that he is the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They were alarmed at that. He said, 'Let him enter.' So he admitted me to him, and with him were his patricians. I gave him the letter, and it was read to him. In it was: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Caesar, the ruler of the Romans.' A nephew of his, ruddy, blue-eyed, and lank-haired, snorted and said, 'Do not read the letter today. He began with himself and wrote \"ruler of the Romans\" and did not write \"king of the Romans.\"' He said: The letter was read until they finished, then he ordered them and they left his presence. Then he sent for me, so I entered upon him. He asked me and I informed him. He sent for the bishop, and he entered upon him; he was the one in charge of their affairs, and they acted according to his opinion and his word. When he read the letter, the bishop said, 'By Allah, he is the one whom Moses and Jesus gave us glad tidings of, the one we have been waiting for.' Caesar said, 'What do you command me?' He said, 'As for me, I believe in him and follow him.' Caesar said, 'I know that it is so, but I cannot do it. If I do, my kingdom will be gone and the Romans will kill me.'"],[4085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took some fine Egyptian linen (qibati) and gave me a qibtiyyah garment, saying: \"Tear it into two pieces and cut one of them into a shirt, and give the other to your wife to cover her head with.\" When I turned away, he said: \"Tell your wife to put under that torn piece another cloth so that it does not describe her.\""],[4086,"“A woolen jubba and two leather socks were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wore them until they were worn out, and he did not ask about them whether they had been properly slaughtered or not.”"],[4087,"Mu'awiya ؓ sent to Daghfal and asked him about Arabic, about the genealogies of people, and about the stars, and he found him a scholar. He said, 'O Daghfal, from where did you memorize this?' He said, 'I memorized this with an inquiring tongue and a comprehending heart, and the bane of knowledge is forgetfulness.' He said, 'Then go with Yazid and teach him Arabic, the genealogies of Quraysh, and the stars.'"],[4088,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five years.”"],[4089,"The Christians were required to fast the month of Ramadan. A king ruled over them and fell ill, so he said, 'If Allah heals him, he will increase by ten.' Then another king ruled after him and ate meat, and it caused him pain, so he said, 'If Allah heals him, he will increase by eight days.' Then another king ruled after him and said, 'We will not leave any of these days but we will complete them and make our fasting in the spring.' So he did, and it became fifty days."],[4090,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land and we drink a beverage to gain strength from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Does it intoxicate?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then do not approach it.\" Then he repeated the question to him, and he ﷺ said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Do not approach it.\" He said: They will not be able to abstain from it. He said: \"Whoever does not abstain from it, then kill him.\""],[4091,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, a drink made from this wheat that we use to gain strength for our work and against the cold of our land. He said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then avoid it.\" Then I came to him from in front of him and said the same thing to him. He said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then avoid it.\" I said: The people will not leave it. He said: \"If they do not leave it, then kill them.\""],[4092,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land, intensely cold, where we make a drink from wheat. Is drinking it lawful? He said: \"Does it intoxicate you?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then it is khamr.\""],[4093,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as four hundred riders asking him for food. He said: \"O Umar, go and feed them and give them.\" Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only a few measures of dates, which my family subsists on. Abu Bakr ؓ said: Hear and obey. Umar ؓ said: Hearing and obedience. Umar went until he came to an upper room, took out a key from his waistband, opened it, and said to the people: Enter. They entered, and I was the last of the people to enter, so I delayed. Then I turned and found the like of a weaned camel of dates."],[4094,"That a dirham came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have come to ask you for a ruling about going on military expeditions. He said: \"Do you have a mother?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then stay with her.\""],[4095,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a sacrificial camel with him and said: \"If any of it becomes defective and you fear it will die, then slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it. Do not eat from it yourself, nor anyone of your traveling companions, and distribute it.\""],[4096,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send sacrificial camels with him and then say: \"If any of it becomes defective and you fear it will die, then slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it. Do not eat from it yourself, nor anyone of your traveling companions, and distribute it.\" The wording is from the hadith of Yazid b. Zuray', and Khalid b. al-Harith said: Dhu'ayb b. Qabisa."],[4097,"That when the Prophet ﷺ was dying, Safiyya said: O Messenger of Allah, every woman among your wives has family to whom she can turn, and you have expelled my family. If something happens, to whom should I turn? He said: \"To Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ.\""],[4098,"That the delegation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Umm Zubayb and took her carpet. Zubayb caught up with the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, the delegation took my mother's carpet. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Return his mother's carpet to him.\" So he took from the one who took his mother's carpet a measure of barley, his sword, and his belt. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and wiped Zubayb's head with it, then said: \"May Allah bless you, O boy, and bless your mother.\" Musa b. Harun said: The carpet (zirbiyya) is a covering heavier than a ziliyya. Allah ﷻ said: {And rich carpets spread out} (Q 88:16), meaning spread out."],[4099,"O Prophet of Allah, I want a freed slave from the descendants of Ishmael ﷺ, deliberately. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Wait until the spoil from al-Anbar comes tomorrow.\" The spoil from al-Anbar came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take from among them four young boys, fair and handsome, whose heads are not hidden.\" Ata' b. Khalid said: I took my grandfather Rudayh, I took my paternal cousin Samura, I took my paternal cousin Rakhya, and I took my maternal uncle Zabib. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and wiped their heads with it and blessed them, then said: \"These, O Aisha, are from the descendants of Ishmael, deliberately.\""],[4100,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud, from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays.\""],[4101,"Something was entrusted to me for the Banu Hashim, so I came to Abu Ja'far in Madinah. He sent me to a woman among them, a daughter of Ali, a very old woman. He said: The mawla of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Tahman or Dhakwan narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sadaqah is not lawful for me nor for my household. The mawla of a people is one of them.\""],[4102,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended the Second pledge at al-Aqaba from the Ansar, then from the Banu Zurayq: Dhakwan b. Abd Qays b. Khalda.\""],[4103,"From Urwa: \"In the naming of those who attended al-ʿAqaba from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays b. Khalada. He had left Madinah for Makkah as an emigrant to Allah, and he witnessed Badr.\""],[4104,"From Urwa: \"In the naming of those who were martyred with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uḥud, from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays.\""],[4105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be four armies, so upon you is Syria, for Allah, Exalted is He, has guaranteed Syria for me.\""],[4106,"ʿAmmār: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three of us, all of us were aḍbaṭ.\" It was said to Abū Shayba: \"What is al-aḍbaṭ?\" He said: \"The one who works with both his hands: Dhū al-Shimālayn, ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, and Abū Laylā.\""],[4107,"From his father Muṭīr, and Muṭayr was present, confirming his statement. He said: \"How did I inform you?\" He said: \"O father, you informed me that Dhū al-Yadayn met you at Dhū Khashab and told you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in one of the two evening prayers, which was ʿAṣr, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then gave the salutation. The swift among the people left, saying, 'The prayer has been shortened.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, may Allah have mercy on them both, followed him. Then Dhū al-Yadayn caught up with him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said, 'The prayer has not been shortened, nor did I forget.' Then he turned to Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ and said, 'What is Dhū al-Yadayn saying?' They said, 'He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and the people came back, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then gave the salutation, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[4108,"I was with al-Ḥasan when a man passed by him and spoke to him. He said: Dhū al-Yadayn said: \"O assembly of the Anṣār, did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you to be patient until you meet him?\""],[4109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This affair was in Ḥimyar, then Allah took it from them and put it in Quraysh.\""],[4110,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a raid. They traveled at night for a while, then they stopped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said: \"O Dhū Makhmar.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.\" He took hold of the head of my she-camel and said: \"Sit here and do not be a lukaʿ tonight.\" So I took hold of the she-camel's head, but my eyes overcame me and I slept. The she-camel slipped away and went off, and I did not wake up except with the heat of the sun. The Prophet ﷺ came to me and said: \"O Dhū Makhmar.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.\" He said: \"By Allah, last night you were a lukaʿ as I said.\" So we moved away from that place, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us. When he finished the prayer, he supplicated that the she-camel be brought back, and a whirlwind came driving her. The next day, when dawn broke, he ordered Bilāl, so he gave the call to prayer, then he ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah, then he prayed with us. When he finished the prayer, he said: \"This is our prayer from yesterday.\" Then he started the prayer of that day afresh.\""],[4111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will make peace with the Byzantines, a secure peace, until you and they raid a common enemy, and you will be victorious. Then you will encamp in a meadow with hills.\""],[4112,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will soon make peace with the Byzantines, a secure peace. Then you and they will raid a common enemy, and you will be victorious, take spoils, and be safe. Then you will depart until you encamp in a meadow with hills. A man from among the Christians will raise a cross and say, 'The cross has prevailed.' A Muslim man will become angry, rise to it, and smash it. At that point, the Byzantines will act treacherously and gather for the great battle.\""],[4113,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will make peace with the Byzantines for ten years, a secure peace. They will fulfill two years and break the treaty in the third, or fulfill four and break it in the fifth. Then an army of you will encamp in their city, and you and they will raid an enemy behind you and behind them. You will fight that enemy and Allah will grant you victory, and you will depart with the reward and spoils you have gained. Then you will encamp in a meadow with hills. One of your men will say, 'Allah has prevailed,' and one of their men will say, 'The cross has prevailed,' and they will go back and forth over it. The Muslims will become angry, and their cross will be not far from them. That Muslim will rise to their cross and smash it, and they will come out against the breaker of their cross and strike his neck. Then that band of Muslims will rise to their weapons, and the Byzantines will rise to their weapons, and they will kill that band of Muslims, who will be martyred. Then they will go to their king and say, 'We have spared you the might and strength of the Arabs, so what are we waiting for?' He will gather for you an army the size of a woman's pregnancy, and then they will come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.\""],[4114,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ looked upon the people of Madinah when it was a wide, gravelly plain before it was built up, with no clod of earth or soft grassy place in it, and He said: 'O people of Yathrib, I lay upon you three conditions and will drive to you fruits of every kind: do not disobey, do not become exorbitant in prices, and do not wax arrogant. If you do any of that, I will leave you like a slaughtered camel that no one prevents from being eaten.'\""],[4115,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Do we act in a matter newly begun or in a matter already decreed?\" He said: \"Rather in a matter already decreed.\" He said: \"Then what is the point of action?\" He said: \"Act, for each is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[4116,"That he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do we act in a matter newly begun or in a matter already decreed?\" He said: \"No, rather in a matter already decreed.\" He said: \"Then what is the point of action?\" He said: \"Act, for each is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[4117,"That he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if we are tested with remaining after you, what do you command us?\" He said: \"You must keep to the House of the Holy, perhaps Allah will provide you with offspring who go there in the morning and return in the evening.\""],[4118,"We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if we are tested after you with remaining, where do you command us?\" He said: \"You must keep to the House of the Holy, for perhaps offspring will arise for you who go to that mosque in the morning and return in the evening.\""],[4119,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, commanding the people and forbidding them, then he said: \"Have I conveyed?\" They said: \"O Allah, yes.\" He said: \"O Allah, bear witness.\" Then he said: \"Take the stipend as long as it is fresh. But when Quraysh violently wrest the kingship among themselves and the stipend becomes bribery for your religion, then leave it.\""],[4120,"I saw Rafi' b. Khadij dyeing with yellow."],[4121,"He went out on the day of Uhud, and the Prophet ﷺ intended to send him back, but he insisted on going. His uncle said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, my nephew insists on going, and he is young.\" So he allowed him to go. He was then struck by an arrow in his chest or neck. He came to his uncle, the Prophet ﷺ , and said, \"My son has been struck by an arrow.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you leave it in him, he will die as a martyr.\" Abdullah bin Hussein said, \"His wife told me that she used to see him showering and moving in his chest.\""],[4122,"\"That Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj was hit by an arrow alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud or the day of Khaybar. ʿUmar doubted it, so he went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, remove the arrow.' He ﷺ replied, 'O Rāfiʿ, if you want, I will remove the arrow along with its barbs. And if you want, I will remove the arrow and leave the barbs, and I will testify for you on the Day of Judgment that you are a martyr.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed the arrow and left the barbs, and Rāfiʿ lived with them until the time of the Caliphate of Muʿāwiyah. Then the wound burst open, and he died after ʿAṣr prayer. Ibn ʿUmar came, and it was said to him, 'O Abā ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj has died.' He showed mercy and said, 'A person like Rāfiʿ should not be buried without informing the villages around Madīnah.' So when we carried his funeral, Ibn ʿUmar came and sat by the head of the grave. A woman from our party shouted, 'What does this crazy woman want, harming the old man?' Ibn ʿUmar replied, 'Surely, she should not harm the sheikh, for he does not deserve Allah's punishment.'\""],[4123,"I came with my paternal uncle to the Prophet ﷺ when he was heading to Badr. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I wish to go out with you.\" He began to take hold of my hand and say: \"I consider you too young, and I do not know what you will do when you meet the enemy.\" I said: \"Do I know how to shoot whoever shoots?\" So he sent me back."],[4124,"Indeed Rafi' b. Khadij is an old man who has no strength to endure the punishment of Allah."],[4125,"Rafi' b. Khadij died in the year seventy-three in Madinah."],[4126,"And in it Rafi' b. Khadij died at the beginning of this year, and Ibn Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, attended his funeral, meaning the year seventy-three, and Rafi' was eighty-six on the day he died."],[4127,"Rafi' b. Khadij died in the year seventy-four, at its beginning."],[4128,"I heard Rafi' b. Khadeej say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping (muzara'ah).\""],[4129,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prohibited it, and we abandoned it because of his statement.\""],[4130,"\"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ prohibited it.\""],[4131,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited it.\""],[4132,"Rafi' b. Khadeej: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us.\""],[4133,"Ibn 'Umar: \"Rafi' b. Khadeej certainly deprived us of the benefit of our land.\""],[4134,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prohibited leasing land.\""],[4135,"We did not see any harm in leasing land until Rafi' b. Khadeej narrated to us: \"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited leasing land.\""],[4136,"“The Prophet forbade the hire and purchase of non-Arabs.”"],[4137,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a matter that was lenient for us, but in the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ there is blessing and right guidance.” They said: What is that? He said: “Ḥaql.” I said to Usayd: What is ḥaql? He said: “Leasing land.” I said: How did they lease it? He said: “For quarters and for a portion of the harvest.”"],[4138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muḥāqalah, muzābanah, and munābadhah; he forbade a man saying to another man, \"Buy this for cash and buy it on credit,\" until he buys it and takes possession of it; and he forbade a deferred [payment] for a deferred [payment] and a debt for a debt."],[4139,"On the Day of the Trench, there was no fortress more fortified than the fortress of Banū Ḥārith, so the Prophet ﷺ placed the women, the boys, and the children in it and said, \"If anyone comes near you, flash your swords at them.\" Then a man from Banū Thaʿlabah b. Saʿd, called Bujdān, one of Banū Jaḥḥāsh, came to them on a horse until he reached the base of the fortress, then he began saying to the women, \"Come down to me; it is better for you.\" So they brandished the swords, and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw him. A group of people rushed to the fortress, among them a man from Banū Ḥārithah called Ẓuhayr b. Rāfiʿ, and he said, \"O Bujdān, come out!\" So he came out to him, and his horse charged at him and killed him, and he took his head and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[4140,"I came with al-Khatmi to the Prophet ﷺ when he was intending to go to Badr and said: 'O Messenger of God, I want to go out with you.' He began to clench his hand and said: 'I consider you too young, and I do not know what you will do when you meet the people.' I said: 'Do you know that I can shoot whoever shoots?' So he sent me back, and I did not witness Badr."],[4141,"He said to him: O my father, we have rented our land to so-and-so for two hundred dirhams. He said: My son, leave that aside, for Allah will provide you with a crop other than it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade renting out land."],[4142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The love that is inherited among the people of Islam.\""],[4143,"and from Rafi bin Khadij, the two of them said - :\"Abdullah bin Sahl bin Zaid and Muhayysah bin Mas'ud went out until when they reached Khaibar, they went their separate ways. Then Muhayysah found 'Abdullah bin Sahl slain, so he buried him. Then he came to the Mesenger of Allah, along with Huwayysah bin Mas'ud and 'Abdur-Rahman bin Sahl, who was the youngest of them, 'Abdur-Rahman started to speak before his two companions, but the Messenger of Allah said to him: \"Let the clear speak first.\" So he fell silent and his two companions spoke, then he spoke with them. They told the Messenger of Allah about the killing of 'Abdullah bin Sahl, and he said to them: \"Will you swear fifty oaths, then you will receive compensation, or be entitled to retaliate?\" They said: \"How can we swear an oath when we did not witness what happened?\" he said: \"Then can the Jews swear fifty oaths declaring their innocence?\" They said: \"How can we accept the oath of a disbelieving people?\" When the Messenger of Allah saw that, he paid the blood money (himself). (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4712)"],[4144,"Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Banu Tamim, narrated to me from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Rafi' b. Khadij: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tie a thread on his ring to remind himself.\""],[4145,"Rijal b. Ghanmawayh had such an astonishing amount of humility, constancy in reciting the Quran, and goodness in what the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that it was a wonder. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while Rijal was sitting with us among a group. He said, «One of this group is in the Fire.» Rafiʿ said: I looked at the people, and there were Abu Hurayra al-Dawsi, Abu Arwa al-Dawsi, al-Tufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsi, and Rijal b. Ghanmawayh. I began to look and wonder, saying, \"Who is this wretched one?\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, Banu Hanifa apostatized and asked what Rijal b. Ghanmawayh had done. They said, \"He was tried. He is the one who testified to Musaylima against the Messenger of God ﷺ that he made him a partner in his affair after him.\" I said, \"What the Messenger of God ﷺ said is true.\" And Rijal was heard saying, \"Two rams butted heads; the more beloved of them to us is our ram.\""],[4146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Badr, «By Him in whose hand is my soul, if a newborn were born in the understanding of the people of religion for forty years, acting in complete obedience to God and avoiding all sins until he is returned to the most abject age or returned to knowing nothing after having knowledge, none of you would reach what they have reached this night.» And he said, «The angels who witnessed Badr have excellence over those who stayed behind among them.»"],[4147,"He cultivated a piece of land, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was watering it. He asked, «Whose is the crop and whose is the land?» He replied, \"My crop by my own hand and labor is from one half, and the land of Banu So-and-so is the other half.\" He said, «You have dealt in usury; return the land to its people and take your expenses.»"],[4148,"The Prophet ﷺ said: «People are a faction, and my Companions are a faction.» Zayd b. Thabit and Rafiʿ b. Khadij said: \"He has spoken the truth,\" while they were with Marwan b. al-Hakam."],[4149,"The Prophet ﷺ would not rise from a gathering until he said: «Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.» Then he would say: «It is an expiation for whatever occurred in the gathering.»"],[4150,"Rafi‘ b. Khadij said, “Our Prophet ﷺ forbade us—or the Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade—leasing land.”"],[4151,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on our mounts cloths with red threads, wide. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do I not see that red has overcome you?” He said, so we rose quickly at the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until some of our camels bolted. We took the cloths and pulled them off them."],[4152,"O you who are speaking, I see that you have spoken at length in Makkah and mentioned some of its virtue. What you omitted of its virtue is greater. But you did not mention Madinah, and I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Madinah is better than Makkah.”"],[4153,"And it is said: Rafi' b. Zayd."],[4154,"A slave belonged to Banu Sa'id, and they freed him except one of them. He came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his intercession with the man, and he spoke to him about him, so the man gave his share to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ freed him. He used to say: I am the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his name was Rafi' Abu al-Bahi."],[4155,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr — then from Banū al-Najjār: Rāfiʿ b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād.”"],[4156,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr — then from Banū al-Aws, then from Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf, then from Banū Umayyah b. Zayd: Rāfiʿ b. ʿUnjudah.”"],[4157,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar: Rifa'ah b. Aws b. Za'ur b. 'Abd al-Ashhal.\""],[4158,"\"This verse was revealed concerning ten people, I being one of them.\" {And We have conveyed to them the Word} to the end of the verse."],[4159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “Ask me about whatever you wish.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He said, “Your father is so-and-so, the one to whom you are attributed.” Another man asked him, “Am I in Paradise?” He said, “In Paradise.” Another said, “Am I in Paradise?” He said, “In the Fire.” Umar ؓ stood up and said, “We are content with Allah as Lord.”"],[4160,"A man from Banu Layth came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I implore you\"—he said it three times—then on the fourth he implored him with a eulogy for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If any poet excels, you have excelled.\""],[4161,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Persist in invoking 'O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.'\""],[4162,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uhud, then from Quraysh: Rabi'ah b. Aktham, ally of Banu 'Abd Shams from Banu Asad.\""],[4163,"Rabi'ah b. Ruwa' al-'Ansi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him having supper, so he invited him to supper and he ate. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" Rabi'ah said, \"I testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said, \"Out of desire or fear?\" Rabi'ah said, \"As for desire, by God, it is not in your hand; as for fear, by God, I am in a land that your armies and cavalry do not reach us, but I was made to fear and so I feared, and I was told to believe and so I believed.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What an orator from 'Ans!\" He stayed, coming and going to the Prophet ﷺ, then came to bid him farewell. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"If you sense any danger, flee to the people of the town.\" He left, sensed danger, and fled to a town where he died."],[4164,"Rabi'ah b. Umayyah b. Khalaf al-Jumahi was the one who called out on the day of 'Arafah beneath the chest of the Messenger of God's ﷺ she-camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Call out\"—and he had a loud voice—\"O people, do you know which month this is?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, the sacred month.\" He said, \"Indeed God has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this month of yours.\" Then he said, \"Call out: Do you know which land this is?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, the sacred land.\" He said, \"Indeed your blood and your wealth are sacred to you until the day you meet Him, like the sanctity of this land of yours.\" Then he said, \"Call out: Which day is this?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, this is a sacred day, and this is the day of the greater pilgrimage.\" He said, \"Indeed God, exalted be He, has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you until the day you meet Him, like the sanctity of this day of yours.\""],[4165,"From Ibn Shihab: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Bilhubla: Rabi' b. Iyas.”"],[4166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited the son of Jabar al-Ansari's brother, and his family began weeping over him. Jabar said to them, “Do not annoy the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave them; let them weep as long as he is alive, and when death occurs, let them be silent.” Some of them said, “We never thought that your death would be on your bed until you were killed in the path of Allah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is martyrdom only in being killed in the path of Allah? The martyrs of my community would then be few. Indeed, plague and pestilence are martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, the woman who dies in childbirth with a child in her womb is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, demolition is martyrdom, and pleurisy is martyrdom.”"],[4167,"He heard Rabi' b. Ziyad say: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, he saw a young man from Quraysh traveling apart. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is that not so-and-so?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Call him.” He came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “What is the matter with you that you have turned aside from the road?” He said, “I disliked the dust.” He said, “Do not turn aside from it, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is the perfume of Paradise.”"],[4168,"From his father: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed with 'Ali ؓ from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Rib'i b. 'Amr, a Badri.”"],[4169,"From his father: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed with 'Ali ؓ: Rib'i b. Rafi', from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, a Badri.”"],[4170,"From Ibn Shihab in naming \"those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamama from the Ansar, then from the Aws, then from Banu Amr b. Awf: Rabah, the freedman of Banu Jahjaba.\""],[4171,"When Islam appeared, and we had a well at al-Danina, we feared that those around us would overpower us over it. He said: So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: He wrote for me a document: \"From Muhammad the Messenger of God ﷺ. To proceed: they have their well, if he was truthful.\" He said: We never brought a case regarding it to any of the judges of Madinah except that they judged in our favor. He said: In the Prophet's ﷺ document it was such-and-such, and he claimed that it was such-and-such, this was the Prophet's ﷺ document."],[4172,"I met a number of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, among those who were truthful was Ruqad b. Rabi'a. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ took from us from sheep: from a hundred, one ewe; and if they increased, then two ewes.\""],[4173,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came to him with a plate on which were dates. He said to him: \"What is this? A gift or charity?\" The man said: Charity. He said: \"Present it to the people.\" He said: Hasan was in front of him, playing in the dirt. The boy took a date and put it in his mouth. The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed him, inserted his finger into the boy's mouth, extracted the date, then threw it away, and said: \"We, the family of Muhammad, do not eat charity.\""],[4174,"That he was with his grandfather when he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a boy, and found him with his buttons undone."],[4175,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: 'In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from the Aws: Ruqaym b. Thabit b. Tha'laba b. Zayd b. Lawdhan b. Mu'awiya.'"],[4176,"From Ibn Shihab: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Bayada: Rukhayla b. Tha'laba b. Khalda.'"],[4177,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited muhaqalah and said: \"Whoever has land and has no need of it should grant it to his brother.\""],[4178,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited muhaqalah and said: \"Whoever has land and has no need of it should grant it to his brother.\""],[4179,"Allah: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.\""],[4180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The earnings of a cupper are vile, the dowry of a prostitute is vile, and the price of a dog is vile.\""],[4181,"The Prophet ﷺ said: The earnings of a cupper are impure, the price paid for a dog is impure, and the hire paid to a prostitute is impure. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3421)"],[4182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The earnings of a cupper are vile, the hire of a fornicatress is vile, and the price of a dog is vile.”"],[4183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Evil is the earning of a cupper, the hire of a fornicatress, and the price of a dog.”"],[4184,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Evil is the earning of a cupper, the hire of a fornicatress, and the price of a dog.”"],[4185,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The worst of earnings is the earning of a cupper, the price of a dog, and the hire of a fornicatress.”"],[4186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leasing of farmlands. So Abdullah b. Umar abandoned leasing them, although he had been leasing them before that. Al-Zuhri said: I said to Salim, “Do you lease them?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Then what about the hadith of Rafi' b. Khadij?” Salim said, “Rafi' made it too hard upon himself.”"],[4187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leasing of farmlands."],[4188,"His father used to do that until it reached him that Rafi' b. Khadij said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leasing of land.”"],[4189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Banu Harithah and saw a crop in the land of Zuhayr. He said, “How fine is the crop of Zuhayr.” They said, “It is not Zuhayr's.” He said, “Is it not Zuhayr's land?” They said, “Yes, but it is the crop of so-and-so.” He said, “Then return to him his expenses and take your crop.” Rafi' said: So we returned his expenses to him and took our crop."],[4190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah."],[4191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah."],[4192,"Some people say: “Allah has decreed everything except deeds.” He (the narrator) said: By Allah, I never saw Sa'id b. al-Musayyab become so intensely angry that he was about to stand up; then he calmed down and said: They have uttered it. By Allah, I heard a hadith about them that suffices them as evil. Woe to them! Do they not know? I said, “May Allah have mercy on you, Abu Muhammad, what is it?” He looked at me after some of his anger had subsided and said: Rafi' b. Khadij narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will be a people among my community who disbelieve in Allah and the Quran while they are unaware, just as the Jews and Christians disbelieved.” I said, “May I be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, how is that?” He said, “They affirm part of the decree and disbelieve in part of it.” I said, “Then what do they say?” He said, “They say good is from Allah and evil is from Iblis, thus affirming the Book of Allah upon that and disbelieving in the Quran after faith and recognition. What enmity, hatred, and disputation my community will encounter from them! Those are the heretics of this community in their time. There will be oppression from the ruler, and they will suffer oppression, injustice, and favouritism. Then Allah ﷻ will send a plague that destroys most of them. Then there will be a sinking [of the earth], and how few of them will escape! The believer on that day will have little joy and intense grief. Then there will be transformation, and Allah ﷻ will transform most of those into apes and pigs. Then the Dajjal will come forth soon after that.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept until we wept because of his weeping. We said, “What makes you weep?” He said, “Out of mercy for the distress of the wretched, for among them is the devoted worshipper and among them is the one who strives hard, even though they are not the first to have preceded to this saying and found its burden too heavy. Indeed most of those who perished among the Children of Israel did so by denying the decree.” I said, “May I be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, tell me how is faith in the decree?” He said, “You believe in Allah alone, and that no one alongside Him possesses any harm or benefit; you believe in Paradise and Hell; and you know that Allah ﷻ created them both before the creation of creatures. Then He created His creatures and made of them whomever He willed for Paradise and whomever He willed for Hell as justice from Him. Each one works for what has been determined for him and is heading to what has been determined for him.” I said, “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.”"],[4193,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a foreleg. When he finished, he wiped his fingers on the wall, then prayed Asr and Maghrib without performing ablution."],[4194,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, “He forbade muḥāqalah and muzābanah.”"],[4195,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade leasing land.”"],[4196,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There is no amputation for fruit or for palm hearts.”"],[4197,"“We used to practice muḥāqalah with land, leasing it for a third, a quarter, and a specified amount of food. Then he commanded us concerning the land that we should cultivate it or have it cultivated, and he disliked leasing it for anything other than that.”"],[4198,"We used to practice muḥāqalah with land, leasing it for a third, a quarter, and a specified amount of food. Then one of my paternal uncles came to me and said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us today from a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to God and His Messenger is more beneficial. We used to practice muḥāqalah with land, leasing it for a third, a quarter, and a specified amount of food, and he forbade us to lease it for a quarter, a third, and a specified amount of food. He commanded the owner of the land to cultivate it or have it cultivated.”"],[4199,"We used to practice muḥāqalah with land at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, leasing it for a third, a quarter, and a specified amount of food. Then one day a man from among my paternal uncles came to us and said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to God and His Messenger is more beneficial for us. He forbade us to practice muḥāqalah with land, to lease it for a third, a quarter, and a specified amount of food. He commanded the owner of the land to cultivate it or have it cultivated, and he disliked leasing it for anything other than that.”"],[4200,"We used to practice muḥāqalah at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and muḥāqalah is when a man gives his land for a third or a quarter or for a specified amount of food. Then one of my paternal uncles came to us and said, “The Prophet ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to God and obedience to His Messenger is more beneficial for us.” We said, “And what is that?” He said, “The Prophet of God ﷺ said, ‘Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or have his brother cultivate it, and not lease it for a third or a quarter or for a specified amount of food.’”"],[4201,"We used to practice muḥāqalah at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and muḥāqalah is when a man leases his land for a third or a quarter or for a specified amount of food. Then one of his paternal uncles came and said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us; obedience to God and His Messenger is more beneficial for us. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or have his brother cultivate it, and not lease it for a third and a quarter and not for a specified amount of food.’”"],[4202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Delay the dawn prayer until it is light, for that is greater for your reward.”"],[4203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Delay the morning prayer until it is light, for that is greater for the reward.”"],[4204,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Perform the morning prayer at the break of light, for that is greater for the reward.”"],[4205,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Perform the Subh prayer when it becomes light, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform the Subh prayer when it becomes light, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The collector of zakah who acts justly is like one who fights in the path of Allah until he returns.\""],[4208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform the Subh prayer when it becomes light, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform the Subh prayer when it becomes light, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Make the Fajr prayer luminous, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4211,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \"Perform the Fajr prayer when it becomes light, for that yields a greater reward.\""],[4212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whatever you delay of the Fajr prayer until it becomes light, that yields a greater reward.\""],[4213,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us among Banu Abd al-Ashhal and prayed Maghrib with us in our mosque, then said: \"Pray these two rak'ahs in your homes.\""],[4214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah ﷻ loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you protects his sick one from water.\""],[4215,"Nu'ayman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a severe burning fever. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Where are you, O Nu'ayman, in relation to Mahya'ah? And it was a land of pestilence.\""],[4216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The collector of zakah who acts justly is like one who fights in the path of Allah until he returns to his home.\""],[4217,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The one who works on the sadaqah is like the one who goes out fighting in Allah’s cause until he returns to his house.”"],[4218,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “The one who works on the sadaqah with honesty is like the one who fights in the path of Allah.”"],[4219,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the thing I fear most for you is minor polytheism.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is minor polytheism?\" He said, \"Showing off. It is said to someone who does it when people praise their actions, 'Go to those whom you sought to impress and seek their praise from them.'\""],[4220,"Ibn Umar used to lease out his farms during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and the early part of Mu’awiyah’s rule ؓ. Then a man came to him and said: “Rafi’ b. Khadij claims that the Prophet ﷺ forbade leasing farms.” Nafi’ said: “So Ibn Umar went to Rafi’, and I went with him. Ibn Umar said: ‘What is this that has reached me from you, that you mention from the Prophet ﷺ about leasing farms?’ He said: ‘Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.’ After that, when Abdullah was asked about leasing farms, he would say: ‘Rafi’ b. Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it.’”"],[4221,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to forbid leasing farms.” So Ibn Umar abandoned it, and when he was asked about it he would say: “Rafi’ claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it.”"],[4222,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a hadith. So he went out to him at al-Balat and asked him, and Rafi’ informed him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.” So Abdullah stopped leasing them."],[4223,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.” So Ibn Umar abandoned it."],[4224,"\"He went out to him (and met him) in Al-Balat, and I was with him. He asked him (about that) and he said: 'Yes, the Messenger of Allah forbade leasing arable land.' So 'Abdullah stopped leasing it.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3912)"],[4225,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he forbade that. Nafi’ said: “So Abdullah went out to him at al-Balat and I was with him. He asked him, and Rafi’ said: ‘Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.’ So Abdullah stopped leasing them.”"],[4226,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.”"],[4227,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4228,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sharecropping.”"],[4229,"And he said: “The Prophet ﷺ forbade leasing farms.”"],[4230,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing farms.”"],[4231,"He heard the hadith of Rafi' b. Khadij: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land.” Ibn 'Umar said: “We used to lease it for the spring crop of the irrigated land and for some of what came out of it of straw.”"],[4232,"“That the Prophet ﷺ forbade leasing land,” so he abandoned that."],[4233,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade leasing land.”"],[4234,"And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. And he said: We had been leasing land before we came to know the hadith of Rafi' b. Khadij. Then he felt uneasy about it, so he placed his hand on my shoulder until we reached Rafi' b. Khadij. 'Abdullah b. 'Umar said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding leasing land? Rafi' said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — otherwise may Allah blind these two [eyes] — saying: “Do not lease land for anything.”"],[4235,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade leasing land.”"],[4236,"That his paternal uncles came to the Prophet ﷺ, then they returned to Rafi' after they had narrated that the Prophet ﷺ “forbade leasing farms.”"],[4237,"That he used to lease his land until Rafi' met him and informed him “of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ prohibition of that.” Nafi' said: And I was with Ibn 'Umar when he asked Rafi'."],[4238,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land,” so Ibn 'Umar abandoned it."],[4239,"\"We used to divide the land between us, half and one third, based on what was in spring and what was in Ba'al. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. After he left, Tawus hit my hands and said, 'If you have land, then mention the hadith.'\""],[4240,"To lease it.”"],[4241,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared sacred what is between the two lava fields of Madinah.”"],[4242,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from 'Utbah b. Muslim, from Nafi' b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from Rafi' b. Khadij: “That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared sacred what is between the two lava fields of Madinah.”"],[4243,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning Makkah and he said, \"Indeed, Ibrahim has declared Makkah as sacred, and I declare sacred what is between its two mountains.\" He meant Madinah."],[4244,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned Makkah, and said: “Indeed Ibrahim ﷺ declared Makkah sacred, and I declare sacred what is between its two lava fields,” meaning Madinah."],[4245,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned Makkah, saying: \"Indeed, Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred, and I declare sacred what lies between its two lava tracts for Madinah.\""],[4246,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf; and ʿAlī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl b. Abī Uways, all of them from Mālik, from Rabīʿa, from Ḥanẓala b. Qays, that he asked Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj about leasing land. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land.\" I said, \"For gold and silver?\" He said, \"As for gold and silver, there is no harm.\""],[4247,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from leasing land in return for what it produces.\""],[4248,"From the armāth"],[4249,"\"We used to lease our land for the mādhiyānāt and the heads of the streams, and this would be safe while that would perish. So we were forbidden from that. There is no harm in a specified payment.\""],[4250,"\"We used to lease land at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the mādhiyānāt and the heads of the streams, and this would perish while that would be safe. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that.\""],[4251,"\"We used to lease land, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that.\""],[4252,"\"We used to lease land at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the spring of the waterer, the mādhiyānāt, and a portion of straw, and the Prophet disliked that.\""],[4253,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from leasing our land.\" At that time there was no gold or silver, and we used to lease our land for a quarter and the unknown amount, and sometimes this would perish while that would be safe."],[4254,"\"We, the Banū Ḥārith, were the largest field owners among the people of Madinah, and we used to lease land and stipulate with the tenants that whatever the mādhiyānāt and the spring irrigated would be ours, and whatever the streams irrigated would be yours. Sometimes this would perish while that would be safe, and sometimes this would be safe while that would perish. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that. At that time we had no gold or silver, so we knew that.\""],[4255,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid leasing it—meaning land—for gold and silver. But we used to lease it, then we would cultivate it, and this side would be for us and that side for them. Whatever Allah ﷻ brought forth from this would be for this one, and whatever Allah ﷻ brought forth from that would be for that one. So he forbade us from that.\""],[4256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no amputation for fruit or for dates still on the palm.\""],[4257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4258,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; (Ḥ) and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyāṭī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us, all of them from Mālik, from Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd, from Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Ḥabbān: A slave stole a small palm shoot from the walled garden of a man and put it in the walled garden of his master. The owner of the shoot went out looking for his shoot and seized it, then he sought help against the slave from Marwān b. al-Ḥakam. Marwān imprisoned the slave and wanted to amputate his hand. The slave’s master went to Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj and asked him about that, and he informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4260,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4262,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4263,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4264,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4265,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4267,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4268,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no amputation for fruit, nor for palm pith.”"],[4269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No amputation (for theft) in fruit or in palm hearts.\""],[4270,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, yet the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ is upon the head and the eye. He forbade us from working the land for a portion of its produce and for minted silver, and he forbade us from the earnings of a cupper."],[4271,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he passed by a walled garden and it pleased him, so he said: \"Whose is this?\" I said: \"It is mine.\" He said: \"How did you obtain this?\" I said: \"I rented it.\" He said: \"Do not rent it for anything.\""],[4272,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, yet the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ is upon the head and the two eyes. He forbade us from leasing our land for a portion of what it produces and for minted silver, and he said: \"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother.\""],[4273,"The Messenger of God forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us. When any of us had land, he forbade him from giving it for a portion of its produce, for a third or a half, and he said: \"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother.\""],[4274,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade leasing white (uncultivated) land."],[4275,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he forbade leasing land."],[4276,"My two maternal uncles came to us and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to God and obedience to His Messenger are more beneficial for us. He said: \"Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother.\""],[4277,"Rafi' came to us from the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was convenient for us, but obedience to the Messenger of God ﷺ is more convenient for us. He forbade us from cultivating any land except land whose neck one of us owns, or a grant that a man bestows.\""],[4278,"Regarding his land, he gave it for a third, a fourth, and a half, and he stipulated that a third of it was for irrigation channels, the butchers, and what the spring watered. He said: We used to work with iron and whatever God willed, and we obtained benefit from it until Rafi' b. Khadij came to us and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbids you from a matter that was beneficial to you, yet obedience to the Messenger of God ﷺ is more beneficial for you: \"When one of you has no need of his land, let him grant it to his brother or leave it. And he forbids you from muzabanah.\" Muzabanah is when there is a large amount of palm trees and one says: I have taken it for such-and-such a measure of dates."],[4279,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade muzabanah."],[4280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When one of you has no need of his land, let him grant it to his brother or leave it.\""],[4281,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you is in no need of his land, let him grant it to his brother or leave it.”"],[4282,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from muḥāqalah and muzābanah."],[4283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from ḥaql.” And ḥaql is [sharecropping for] a third and a quarter."],[4284,"The Messenger of God came out to us and forbade us from a matter that was beneficial to us, but the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ is better. He said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, grant it, or leave it.” This was mentioned to Ṭāwūs, and he said: Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ knew better. He said: Ibn ʿAbbās said: “For a man to grant his land to his brother is better for him.”"],[4285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man of the Anṣār cultivating his land, and he knew that he was in need. He said: “Whose is this?” He said: “It belongs to so-and-so; he gave it to me for a wage.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If only he had granted it to his brother.”"],[4286,"I heard Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj say: My paternal uncles went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then returned to us and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ has forbidden you from a matter that was beneficial to us, but obedience to the Messenger of God ﷺ is more beneficial for you. He said: “Let one of you cultivate his land, or grant it, or leave it fallow.”"],[4287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ has forbidden you from a matter that was lenient for you, but obedience to the Messenger of God ﷺ in what is hard for you is better than disobeying him in what is lenient for you. He forbade you from giving your land for a third and a quarter, “but let him cultivate it, or let his brother cultivate it.” They said: Then it will be fallow. He said: “Leave it; it will be fallow.”"],[4288,"He said: “You report to me from Rāfiʿ, while Muʿādh b. Jabal acted upon it during the time of the Messenger of God, giving land for half and a third?”"],[4289,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade us from leasing land in return for some of what it produces."],[4290,"I said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, I am the most land-rich of the Anṣār. He said: “Cultivate.” I said: It is more than that. He said: “Then leave it fallow.”"],[4291,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by him and called him. He went out to him and walked with him until he reached the mosque, then he left, performed ghusl, and returned. The Prophet ﷺ saw the trace of ghusl on him and asked him about his ghusl. He said: I heard your call while I was having intercourse with my wife, so I got up before finishing and performed ghusl. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Water is only from water.” Then after that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory.”"],[4292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command delaying the ʿaṣr."],[4293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not lie upon me, for lying upon me is not like lying upon anyone else.\""],[4294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seek the neighbor before the house, and the companion before the road.\""],[4295,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhū al-Khalīfah in Tihāmah. The people got camels and sheep, and they hurried and brought the cooking pots to a boil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he distributed and equated ten sheep with one camel. He said: A camel from among them bolted, and a man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These animals have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts. Whatever of them overpowers you, do with it like this.\" Then Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we fear, or we hope, to meet the enemy, but we have no knives with us. May we slaughter with reeds?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah is mentioned, then eat, except tooth and nail. I will tell you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\" Rāfiʿ said: Then a camel that carries water fell into a well in Madinah, and it was slaughtered from the side of its shākilah, meaning its flank, and ʿUmar took a tenth of it for a dirham."],[4296,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we hope to meet our enemy, and perhaps some of the equipment that would prepare us will not be with us. May we eat every animal slaughtered by a reed?\" He said, \"Yes, whatever makes the blood flow is a means of slaughter, except tooth and nail.\""],[4297,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives with us.\" He said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah is mentioned, then eat, except tooth and nail. I will tell you: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ obtained camels, and a camel among them bolted. A man from the people shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These camels have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts. If any of them overcomes you, do with it like this.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ used to set ten sheep for one camel in the division of spoils. He said: Sufyān narrated to me from him. Muḥammad said: I heard this wording from Sufyān."],[4298,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah in Tihāmah, and the people were hungry, they obtained sheep and camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the last of the people, so they hurried and slaughtered and prepared cooking pots. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he distributed and equated ten sheep with one camel. There was a camel among the people that bolted, and they pursued it but could not catch it. A man shot at it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These animals have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts. Whatever of them bolts away from you, do with it like this.\" We said, \"We fear, or we hope, to meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives with us. May we slaughter with reeds?\" He said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah is mentioned, then eat, except tooth and nail. I will inform you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4299,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah. Camels and sheep were captured, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the last of the people. They hurried and slaughtered and prepared cooking pots. The Prophet ﷺ came to them and ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he distributed and equated ten sheep with one camel. There was a camel among the people that bolted, and they pursued it but could not catch it. A man shot at it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These animals have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts. Whatever of them bolts away from you, do with it like this.\" My grandfather said, \"We hope, or we fear, to meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives with us. May we slaughter with reeds?\" He said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah Most High is mentioned, then eat, except tooth and nail. I will inform you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4300,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives with us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah is mentioned, then eat, as long as it is not a tooth or a nail. I will tell you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4301,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah. We captured camels and sheep, and some people went ahead among the vanguard of the people and slaughtered and set up their cooking pots before the spoils were distributed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by, and he was among the last of the people, and he saw the pots had been set up. He said, \"What is this?\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, they slaughtered and cooked.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he ordered the spoils to be distributed, and he set ten sheep for every camel. He said: While we were in that state, a camel among them bolted, and a man from the people pursued it. Then a man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"These camels have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts. Whatever of them overcomes you, do with it like this.\" Then my grandfather said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we fear meeting the polytheists tomorrow, and we have no knives with us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever makes the blood flow and upon which the name of Allah is mentioned, then eat, except a tooth or a nail. I will tell you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4302,"From the Prophet ﷺ: A camel from the charity camels bolted, so they sought it. When they were unable to catch it, a man shot it with an arrow and hit its vital spot. They asked him about eating it, and he ordered them to eat it, saying: \"These camels have wild streaks like the wild streaks of wild animals. So if you fear anything of them, do to it the like of what you did to this one, then eat it.\""],[4303,"We were on an expedition with the Prophet ﷺ. A man of the people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we will raid the enemy tomorrow, and we have no knives. May we slaughter with reeds and flint?\" He said: \"Yes. Mention Allah's name over it and eat, except the tooth and the nail. As for the tooth, it is bone; and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4304,"\"We encountered some camels, and we slaughtered a she-camel among them and we threw at it the noble parts. Then we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said: 'Indeed, this camel has reproductive organs similar to the reproductive organs of wild animals, so whatever you throw at it, use it and eat it.'\""],[4305,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a battle, and we said: \"Tomorrow we will attack the enemy, but we do not have sufficient provisions.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Anything that is slaughtered and the name of Allah is mentioned upon it, then it is permissible for you to eat it, except for what is considered a bone or a claw, for the tooth is a bone and the claw is the horn of the Abyssinians.\""],[4306,"We acquired some sheep and divided them at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Then a camel from them bolted, and a man pursued it on his horse and stabbed it with a spear or struck it with a sword. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"These camels have wild streaks like the wild streaks of wild animals. So if any of them bolts, do to it like this.\" A man said: \"We used to slaughter with flint and split sticks.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, as long as it is not a tooth or a nail. For the tooth is bone, and the nail is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[4307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave to Abu Sufyan, Safwan b. Umayyah, 'Uyaynah b. Hisn, and al-Aqra' b. Habis — the hadith."],[4308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.\""],[4309,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Fever is from the blaze of Hell, so cool it with water.\""],[4310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so extinguish it with cold water.\""],[4311,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.\""],[4312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ibn Nu'ayman and began to say: \"Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people, O God of the people.\""],[4313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Charity blocks seventy gates of evil.\""],[4314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The upper hand of the giver, and the lower hand of the taker, until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Muslims abide by their conditions in what is permissible.\""],[4316,"He left when he died a slave girl, a water-carrying camel, a cupper slave, and land. The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the slave girl: 'He forbade her earnings.' And he said concerning the cupper: 'Whatever he earns, feed it to the water-carrying camel.' And he said concerning the land: 'Cultivate it.'"],[4317,"Rifa'ah died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and left a cupper slave, a water-carrying camel, and land. He said: 'As for the cupper, do not eat from his earnings, but feed them to the water-carrying camel.' They said: 'The slave girl earns.' He said: 'Do not eat from the earnings of a slave girl, for I fear that she may earn with her private parts.'"],[4318,"\"My father died and left behind land, a slave girl, a servant boy, and a payment. So they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said to them regarding the land: 'Cultivate it or gift it.' And he forbade them from the earnings of the slave girl and said: 'Combine the earnings of the servant boy.'\""],[4319,"His grandfather died and left a slave girl who earned. They mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he disliked the earnings of a slave girl and said: 'Perhaps she finds nothing and then earns with herself.' Ibn Abi Shaybah said in its chain: Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Balj from 'Abayah b. Rifa'ah b. Rafi' al-Ansari."],[4320,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw the new moon, he would say: 'A crescent of good and guidance.' Then he would say three times: 'O God, I ask You for the good of this — O God, I ask You for the good of this month and the good of destiny, and I seek refuge in You from its evil.'"],[4321,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: 'Speak, and let the one who lies about me take his seat in Hellfire.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, we hear things from you and we write them down.' He said: 'Write, and there is no harm.'"],[4322,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked: 'Which earning is best?' He said: 'A man's work with his own hand and every righteous sale.'"],[4323,"Gabriel ﷺ or an angel came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'How do you count the people of Badr among you?' He said: 'They are the most virtuous of people.' Gabriel ﷺ said: 'And likewise those of the angels who witnessed Badr.'"],[4324,"A man of the Ansar was found killed at Khaybar, so his heirs went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Do you have two witnesses who testify against the killer of your companion?' They said: 'O Messenger of God, there was no Muslim there; they are only Jews, and they dare to do what is greater than this.' He said: 'Then choose fifty of them and make them swear.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ paid his blood money from his own resources."],[4325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Bilal: 'Make the dawn prayer bright enough that the people can see the places where their arrows fall.'"],[4326,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Brighten the dawn prayer enough that the people can see the places where their arrows fall.'"],[4327,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was a farmer and asked him about it. He informed him that the land belonged to the family of Usayd and that he had leased it from them. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him 'to take his lease payment from them and pay them the value of their land.' The wording is that of Ahmad b. Salih. Ahmad b. Salih said: The 'ita' is the value, the value of what it produces."],[4328,"The Prophet ﷺ said: When one of you lies down on his right side and then says: O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, and I have turned my back to You, and I have entrusted my affair to You; there is no refuge from You except in You. I believe in You, our Lord, and in Your messengers. If he dies that night, he will enter Paradise."],[4329,"\"We used to pray the Asr prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then slaughter a camel, distribute it, then cook it, and eat cooked meat before the sun set.\""],[4330,"\"We used to pray Maghrib during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one of us would leave while he could still see the places where his arrows fell.\""],[4331,"He said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us something that was beneficial to us. Rafi' said: I said: Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said is the truth. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you think about your muhaqalah? What do you do with it?\" We said: We lease it for a quarter and for measures of dates and barley. He said: \"Do not do that. Cultivate it yourselves, or let others cultivate it, or keep it.\""],[4332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while they were pollinating date-palms, meaning fertilizing them. He said: \"What are you doing?\" They said: We used to do it. He said: \"If you did not do it, it would be better.\" So they left it, and the dates became unripe and inferior. That was mentioned to him, and he said: \"I am only a human. If I command you regarding something of your religion, then follow it; but if I command you regarding something of your worldly affairs, then I am only a human.\""],[4333,"Rafi bin Khadij and Sahl Bi Abi Hathamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah forbade Muzabanah, which means selling fresh dates still on the tree for dried dates, except in cases of 'Araya, for which he gave permission. (Sahih (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4543)"],[4334,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates, but allowed the 'ariyyah, that its owners could buy it by estimating its amount with dry dates that they eat.\""],[4335,"One day I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was a pot boiling with meat. A piece of fat appealed to me, so I took it and swallowed it, and I suffered from it for a year. Then I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"It contained the soul of seven people.\" Then he wiped my stomach, and I vomited it out green. By the One who sent him with the truth, I have not suffered from my stomach until this hour."],[4336,"I saw a thread in the hand of the Prophet ﷺ, so I asked: What is this? He said: \"I use it to remind myself.\""],[4337,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a limb and then prayed without performing ablution.\""],[4338,"«Arab delegations came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and no delegation came to us with harder hearts or more deserving that Islam had not settled in their hearts than Banu Hanifa.»"],[4339,"Rafi'ah bin Khadeej used to say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us from plowing the mahaqil.\" And mahaqil is excess land coming from the earth."],[4340,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: «Whoever sows in a people's land without their permission has no right to any of the crop, and his expenses are returned to him.»"],[4341,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ «forbidding leasing land and forbidding muhaqala and muzabana.»"],[4342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and forbade us something that had been beneficial to us, and the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ is better for us than what he forbade us from. He said: «Whoever has land should either let his brother cultivate it or grant it (as a gift).» Shuʿba said: ʿAbd al-Malik used to combine the statements of Tawus, ʿAtaʾ, and Mujahid. Shuʿba said: It is as if the one Mujahid narrates from said—Shuʿba said—the companion of the hadith."],[4343,"Ali ؓ told ʿAmmar to ask the Prophet ﷺ about madhy (pre-ejaculatory fluid), so he said: «He should wash his private parts and perform ablution.»"],[4344,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about madhy, and he said: «Wash your penis and perform ablution as you do for prayer.»"],[4345,"From the Prophet ﷺ: «He forbade sharecropping (muzaraʿa).»"],[4346,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by a crop and said, “Whose crop is this?” They said, “It belongs to so-and-so, and the land belongs to so-and-so.” He forbade that and said, “Whoever has land should cultivate it or give it to his brother.”"],[4347,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land.”"],[4348,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Good management is increase, bad character is ill omen, righteousness increases lifespan, and charity prevents an evil death.”"],[4349,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended the ‘Aqabah: Rafi‘ b. Malik al-Zuraqi.”"],[4350,"“We set out in the Hajj in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-‘Aqabah, and the leader of Banu Zurayq was Rafi‘ b. Malik b. al-‘Ajlan.”"],[4351,"Mu‘adh b. Rifa‘ah b. Rafi‘ narrated to me: “Rifa‘ah was a Badri, and Rafi‘ b. Malik was one of the people of al-‘Aqabah, but he did not witness Badr.”"],[4352,"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “How are the people of Badr regarded among you?” He said, “They are the best of us.” Jibril said, “And those of the angels who witnessed Badr, they are the best of us.”"],[4353,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The tree and the ‘ajwah are from Paradise.” Abu al-Qasim said: “He is al-Mushma‘ill b. ‘Amr b. Iyas.”"],[4354,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when I was a young servant, say: “The tree and the ‘ajwah are from Paradise.”"],[4355,"And Ya'la said: it is fivefold or sixfold in the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Then the Messenger of God ﷺ was addressing the people on a gray mule, while Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ was interpreting for him, and the people were either sitting or standing. My father sat down and I made my way through the riding camels until I reached the mule, then I took hold of its stirrup and placed my hand on his knee, wiping down to the shin until I reached the foot. Then I put my palm between the sandal and the foot, and it seems to me even now that I feel the coolness of his feet on my palm.” The wording is that of the Umawi hadith."],[4356,"I was a boy. I used to throw stones at the palm-trees of the Ansar. So I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ who said: O boy, why do you throw stones at the palm-trees? I said: eat (dates). He said: Do not throw stones at the palm trees, but eat what falls beneath them. He then wiped his head and said: O Allah, fill his belly. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2622)"],[4357,"\"I was throwing stones at a date-palm belonging to some of the Ansar. They took me along with them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"O Rafi'! Why were you throwing stones at their date-palm?'\" He said: \"I said: 'Out of hunger, O Messenger of Allah! He said: 'Do not throw stones at them, eat what falls. May Allah fill you and quench your thirst.'\" This Hadith is Hasan Gharib Sahih. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1288)"],[4358,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be after me a people of my community who recite the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They depart from the religion as the arrow departs from the game, then they do not return to it. They are the worst of creation and creatures.” Sulayman said: Most of my thought is that he said: “Their mark is shaving.” Ibn al-Samit said: Then I met Rafi' b. Amr, the brother of al-Hakam b. Amr al-Ghifari, and said to him: What is a hadith I heard from Abu Dharr saying such and such? And I mentioned this hadith to him. He said: “What surprises you about this, for I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[4359,"A man from his descendants, whose name is Rafi' b. al-Mu'alla al-Ansari of the Banu Khubayb b. Abd Haritha b. Malik, narrated to me.”"],[4360,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: “Among those martyred on the day of Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Muslims from the Ansar, then from Banu Khubayb b. Abd Haritha: Rafi' b. al-Mu'alla.”"],[4361,"From Urwa: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar: Rafi' b. al-Mu'alla b. Lawdhan b. Haritha b. Adi b. Zayd b. Tha'laba b. Zayd b. Manat b. Khubayb b. Haritha b. Ghadib b. Jusham b. al-Khazraj. He was martyred on the day of Badr.”"],[4362,"From Ibn Shihab: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Rafi' b. al-Mu'alla b. Lawdhan. He was martyred on the day of Badr.”"],[4363,"“Rafi' b. Umayra al-Sanbasi used to provide morning food for the people of three mosques and give them qurtuma, meaning al-hays, while he had nothing but a shirt, and it was for the house and for Friday.”"],[4364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Amr b. al-As over the army of Dhat al-Salasil, and sent with him in that army Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ and the noble leaders of his companions. They set out until they encamped at the mountain of Tayyi'. Amr said: Look for a man who is a guide to the way. They said: We know none but Rafi' b. Amr, for he was a rabil in the Jahiliyya. I asked Tariq: What is al-rabil? He said: The thief who raids a people alone and steals. Rafi' said: When we finished our expedition and I reached the place from which we had set out, I took note of Abu Bakr ؓ and went to him and said: O companion of al-khallal, I have taken note of you from among your companions, so bring me something by which, if I memorize it, I will be like you. He said: “Do you memorize your five fingers?” I said: Yes. He said: “You bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and you establish the five prayers, and you give zakah if you have wealth, and you perform the pilgrimage to the House, and you fast Ramadan. Have you memorized it?” I said: Yes. He said: “And another thing: do not accept leadership over two people.” I said: Is leadership anything but among you, the people of Badr? He said: “It is about to spread until it reaches you and those lesser than you. Verily God ﷻ, when He sent His Prophet ﷺ, people entered Islam. Among them were those who entered and God guided them, and among them were those whom the sword compelled. He is one who returns to God and a neighbor of God under God's protection. Verily when a man is a leader and people wrong each other, and he does not take from some for others, God will take vengeance on him. Verily a man's neighbor's sheep is taken, and he remains with his muscle protruding in anger for his neighbor, for God is behind his neighbor.” Rafi' said: I stayed for a year, then Abu Bakr was appointed caliph, so I rode to him and said: I am Rafi'; I met you on such and such a day in such and such a place. He said: “I recognized you.” I said: You forbade me from leadership, then you took on something greater than that: the community of Muhammad ﷺ. He said: “Yes, for whoever does not uphold the Book of God among them, upon him is the curse of God,” meaning the curse of God."],[4365,"“The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me on an expedition or pilgrimage, and I looked at them and saw no one among them better in appearance than Abu Bakr ؓ, who had wrapped a cloak over himself against heat and cold.” And he mentioned the hadith."],[4366,"During the Battle of Dhat al-Salasil, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Amr ibn al-Aas to lead an army that included Abu Bakr."],[4367,"From Urwa: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then from Za'ur b. Abd al-Ashhal: Rafi' b. Yazid.”"],[4368,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr: Rāfiʿ b. Jaʿdabah.”"],[4369,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr: Rāfiʿ b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād b. Zayd b. Thaʿlabah.”"],[4370,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah ﷻ said to Dāwūd ﷺ , “Build for Me a house on the earth.” So Dāwūd built a house for himself before the house he had been commanded to build. Then Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “O Dāwūd, you erected your house before My house.” He said: “O Lord, thus You decreed: whoever possesses something keeps it exclusively for himself.” Then he began building the mosque. When the wall was completed, two-thirds of it collapsed. He complained of that to Allah ﷻ, and Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “It is not fitting that you build a house for Me.” He said: “O Lord, why?” He said: “Because of the bloodshed committed by your hands.” He said: “O Lord, was it not in Your love and for Your sake?” He said: “Yes, but they are My servants, and I am more merciful to them.” That distressed him, so Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “Do not grieve, for I shall complete its construction through the hands of your son Sulaymān.” When Dāwūd died, Sulaymān began building it. When it was completed, he offered sacrifices, slaughtered offerings, and gathered the Children of Isrā’īl. Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “I see joy at the building of My house, so ask Me and I shall give you.” He said: “I ask You for three qualities: a judgment that coincides with Your judgment, a kingdom that no one after me should have, and that whoever comes to this house desiring nothing but prayer in it should come out of his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for two, they have been granted to him, and I hope that he has been granted the third.”"],[4371,"In the year forty-six, Ruwayfiʿ was appointed commander over Aṭrābulus."],[4372,"From Ruwayfiʿ b. Thābit, regarding the expedition of some people before sunset, saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the expedition of Khaybar: “It has reached me that you are exchanging a mithqāl for half or two-thirds; that is not right except mithqāl for mithqāl and weight for weight.”"],[4373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says: O Allah, bless Muḥammad and grant him the near station with You on the Day of Resurrection, my intercession becomes incumbent for him.”"],[4374,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever says: O Allah, bless Muḥammad and grant him the near station with You on the Day of Resurrection, I shall intercede for him.”"],[4375,"It is called Jarbah. Ruwayfiʿ stood among us delivering a speech and said: “I do not stand among you except with what I heard the Messenger of Allah say when he stood among us on the day of Ḥunayn after we had conquered it. He said: ‘Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not water his own crop with another’s water. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not approach a previously married woman from the captives until he has ascertained that she is not pregnant. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sell spoils of war until they have been distributed. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not ride a beast from the fayʾ of the Muslims until, when he has made it lean, he returns it to it. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear a garment from the fayʾ of the Muslims until, when he has worn it out, he returns it to it.’”"],[4376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not ride a beast from the spoils of war until, when he has exhausted it, he returns it to the spoils; nor a garment he wears until, when it is worn out, he returns it to the spoils.”"],[4377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not ride a beast from the spoils of war until, when he has exhausted it, he returns it to the spoils; nor a garment he wears until, when it is worn out, he returns it to the spoils.”"],[4378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us on the day of Hunayn: \"It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to sell spoils until they are divided, and it is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to ride a beast from the spoils of the Muslims until, when he has made it lean, he returns it, and not to wear a garment until, when he has worn it out, he returns it in it.\""],[4379,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Beware of embezzlement, and of a man who marries a woman before the spoils are divided, then returns her to the spoils, and who wears a garment until it becomes worn out, then returns it to the spoils.\""],[4380,"He said to us: \"Whoever of you obtains any of these captives should not have intercourse with her until she has menstruated, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for a man to pour his water into the child of another.'\""],[4381,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: \"It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day — or for one who believes in Allah and the Last Day — to pour his water into the child of another.\""],[4382,"I heard the Messenger of Allah forbidding that a pregnant woman be had intercourse with until she gives birth, and he said: \"Indeed one of you adds to his hearing and to his sight,\" and forbidding that captive women be had intercourse with until they have become pure."],[4383,"I heard the Messenger of Allah forbidding that a pregnant woman be had intercourse with until she gives birth, and he said: \"Indeed one of you adds to his hearing and to his sight,\" and forbidding that captive women be had intercourse with until they have become pure."],[4384,"One of us in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take the lean camel of his brother on the condition that he would give him half of what he gained, and he would have the other half, to the extent that one of us would get the arrowhead and the feather, and the other the arrow shaft. Then Ruwayfi' said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Ruwayfi', perhaps life will be prolonged for you after me, so tell the people that whoever ties his beard, or hangs a bowstring around his neck, or cleans himself with the dung of his riding beast or with a bone, then Muhammad ﷺ is free of him.\""],[4385,"Fresh and dried dates were brought near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they ate from them until they left nothing except pits and what had no good in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know what this is?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"You will take away the best, then the best, until there remains of you nothing like this.\""],[4386,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"The owner of the dice will be in the fire,\" meaning the tenth."],[4387,"That Bashir b. 'Abd al-Mundhir b. al-Zinbir and al-Harith b. Hatib went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Badr, but he sent them back and appointed Abu Lubabah over Madinah, and allotted for them two shares with the people of Badr."],[4388,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Umayyah b. Zayd: Abu Lubabah Bashir b. 'Abd al-Mundhir.\""],[4389,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Abu Lubabah is Rifa'ah b. 'Abd al-Mundhir.\""],[4390,"Abu Lubabah b. 'Abd al-Mundhir b. Zinbir b. Umayyah b. Zayd b. Malik b. 'Awf b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Malik b. al-Aws had gone out with the Prophet ﷺ to Badr, but he sent him back and appointed him over Madinah, and allotted for him his share, and included him among the people of Badr."],[4391,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Kill snakes. Kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause miscarriage and blind the sight.”"],[4392,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Kill snakes. Kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause miscarriage and blind the sight.”"],[4393,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ḥātim b. Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm b. Mujammiʿ narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill snakes.”"],[4394,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ḥātim b. Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm b. Mujammiʿ narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill snakes.”"],[4395,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Abū Lubābah: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses, unless it is the one with two stripes or the short-tailed one, for they snatch away sight and cause women to miscarry what is in their wombs.”"],[4396,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4397,"He informed him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4398,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4399,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4400,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes.”"],[4401,"He informed him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4402,"He informed him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses.”"],[4403,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, according to what he told him, when he saw him he threatened and advanced toward him, and sometimes he ordered us together to carry him until we cast him away."],[4404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing the small snakes that are in houses, so he left them after that, and he used to kill whatever was other than that."],[4405,"When Allah accepted the repentance of Abu Lubabah, Abu Lubabah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am abandoning the dwelling of my people in which I committed the sin, and I am divesting myself of my wealth as charity for Allah and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Abu Lubabah, a third will suffice you.\" He said, \"So I gave a third in charity.\""],[4406,"That he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, part of my repentance is that I abandon the dwelling of my people in which I committed the sin, and divest myself of my wealth as charity to Allah and His Messenger.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A third of your wealth will suffice you.\""],[4407,"“The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Friday is the chief of days, the greatest day before Allah. It is greater before Allah then the Day of Adha and the Day of Fitr. It has five characteristics: On it Allah created Adam; on it Allah sent down Adam to this earth; on it there is a time during which a person does not ask Allah for anything but He will give it to him, so long as he does not ask for anything that is forbidden; on it the Hour will begin. There is no angel who is close to Allah, no heaven, no earth, no wind, no mountain, and no sea that does not fear Friday.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1084)"],[4408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr, \"How will you fight the people when you meet them?\" Asim b. Thabit stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when the people are from us at the range where arrows reach them, it will be archery with arrows; when they draw near until stones reach us and them, it will be stoning with stones.\" He took three stones in his hand and two in his belt. \"When they draw near until spears reach us and them, it will be thrusting with spears; when the spears are exhausted, it will be striking with swords.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For this war was sent down. Whoever fights, let him fight the fighting of Asim.\""],[4409,"\"Welcome and greetings, traders and earners.\" I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not of us who does not chant the Quran melodiously.\" Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: I said, \"O Muhammad, what if he does not have a good voice?\" He said, \"He should beautify it as much as he can.\""],[4410,"I heard Anas b. Malik ؓ say: \"The farthest people in dwelling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were two men of the Ansar: Abu Lubabah b. 'Abdul-Mundhir, whose dwelling was in Quba', and Abu Yahya, who was among the Banu Harithah. They used to pray 'Asr with him, then they would come to their people and they had not prayed, because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ early performance of 'Asr.\""],[4411,"On the authority of 'Urwah: \"In naming the companions of al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Rifa'ah b. Rafi' b. Malik b. 'Ajlan b. 'Amr b. Zurayq. He was a naqib and had witnessed Badr.\""],[4412,"About Ibn Shihab: \"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr from the Ansar and then from the Banu Zurayq tribe, it is Rifaa'ah bin Rafi' bin Malik bin Ajlan.\""],[4413,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from al-Khazraj, then from Banu Zurayq: Rifa'ah b. Rafi' b. Malik b. al-'Ajlan b. 'Amr b. 'Asim b. Zurayq b. 'Abd Harithah b. Malik b. Ghadab b. Jusham b. al-Khazraj.\""],[4414,"On the authority of his father: \"In naming those who witnessed with 'Ali ؓ from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: Rifa'ah b. Rafi', a Badri from Banu Zurayq.\""],[4415,"While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, a man entered and prayed two rak'ahs, and the Prophet ﷺ was watching him. Then he came and greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and he returned the greeting. Then he said, \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He said: So he went back and prayed, then came and greeted, and he returned the greeting. Then he said, \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He repeated it to him a third or fourth time, and the Prophet ﷺ said the same as his first statement. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, and by the One who sent down the Book to you, I have striven and tried hard. Show me and teach me.\" He said, \"When you intend to pray, perform wudu' and perfect your wudu', then face the qiblah, say takbir, and recite. Then bow until you are at rest in bowing. Then rise until you are upright in rising. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then rise until you are at rest in sitting. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then rise. If you complete your prayer on this basis, then you have completed it, and whatever you diminish from this, you only diminish from yourself.\""],[4416,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, and there was a man praying in a corner of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was watching him, and he did not notice. When he finished praying, he came forward until he stood before the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. The Prophet ﷺ returned the greeting, then said, \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He went back and prayed, then came forward and greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and he returned the greeting, then said, \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He did that twice or three times. The man said, \"By the One who sent down the Book to you in truth, I have striven and tried hard. Show me, O Messenger of Allah, and teach me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you intend to pray, perform wudu' and perfect your wudu' as Allah commanded, then recite. Then bow until you are at rest in bowing. Then rise until you are upright in standing. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then rise until you are level in sitting. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then stand. If you complete your prayer on this basis, then it is complete, and if you detract from that, then you only detract from your prayer.\""],[4417,"A man entered the mosque and prayed while the Messenger of God ﷺ was watching him without him realizing. When he finished, he came and greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said to him: \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" So he went back and prayed, then came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said to him: \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" So he went back and prayed two or three times. The man said: \"By the One who honored you, O Messenger of God, I have exerted myself, so teach me.\" He said to him: \"When you stand intending to pray, perform ablution and do it well, then face the qiblah, then recite, then bow and be at ease, then prostrate and be at ease while prostrating, then rise until you are at ease sitting, then prostrate until you are at ease while prostrating, then rise, and do that until you finish your prayer.\""],[4418,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, he looked around and saw a man. The man faced the qiblah and prayed two rak'ahs. Hajjaj said in his narration: I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and entered the mosque. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He said: So he went back and prayed, and he began to observe his prayer, not knowing what fault there was in it. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He said: And he mentioned either two or three times. The man said: \"I do not know what you have found faulty in me.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The prayer of any of you is not complete until he performs ablution thoroughly as God commanded him: he washes his face and his hands to the elbows, wipes his head and his feet to the ankles. Then he magnifies God, praises Him, and recites from the Qur'an what God has permitted and made easy for him. Then he magnifies God and bows, placing his palms on his knees until his joints are at ease and relaxed. Then he says, 'God hears the one who praises Him,' and stands upright until every bone takes its proper place and his back is straight. Then he magnifies God and prostrates, enabling his forehead—Hammam said: and perhaps he said: enabling his face—to the ground until his joints are at ease and relaxed. Then he magnifies God and raises his head, sitting upright on his sitting place and straightening his back.\" He described the prayer like this until he finished, then said: \"The prayer of any of you is not complete until he does that.\" The wording is from the narration of Hajjaj."],[4419,"A man entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, and he prayed. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him to repeat it two or three times. He said: \"O Messenger of God, after two or three times I have not fallen short in completing my prayer.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The prayer of anyone among the people is not complete until he performs ablution and puts the ablution in its places, then says 'God is greatest,' then praises God Almighty and extols Him, and recites what is easy from the Qur'an. Then he magnifies God until his joints are at ease, then says 'God hears the one who praises Him' until he stands upright, then magnifies God and prostrates until his joints are at ease, then raises his head until he sits upright, then prostrates until his joints are at ease. If he does not do that, his prayer is not complete.\""],[4420,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying in the mosque and said: \"Go back and pray.\" He said it two or three times. Then the man said: \"O Messenger of God, teach me.\" He said: \"When you stand for prayer, perform ablution as God commanded you, then stand and face the qiblah and say 'God is greatest.' If you have Qur'an with you, recite it; otherwise, glorify God and magnify Him. Then bow and place your palms on your knees, then rise until your back is straight, then prostrate and place your forehead on the ground, then do that. If you do that, your prayer is complete; whatever you omit from that, you have omitted from your prayer.\""],[4421,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a man from the Ansar came after the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished the prayer, and he prayed. Then he came and greeted him. He said: \"And upon you be peace. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have exerted myself, so make it clear to me.\" He said: \"When you stand in your prayer, magnify God, then recite what is easy for you from the Qur'an. Then when you bow, place your hands firmly on your knees until every bone of yours is at ease. Then when you raise your head, stand upright until every bone of yours returns to its place. Then when you prostrate, be at ease until every bone of yours is upright. Then when you raise your head, hold still until every bone returns to its place. Then likewise. When you sit in the middle of your prayer, be at ease and spread out your left thigh, then recite the tashahhud. Then when you stand, do likewise until you finish your prayer.\""],[4422,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting in the mosque and prayed near him. Then he finished, stood, and greeted him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Repeat your prayer, for you have not prayed.\" He prayed similarly to what he had prayed, then finished and stood before the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Repeat your prayer, for you have not prayed.\" He said: \"O Prophet of God, teach me.\" He said: \"When you face the qiblah, magnify God, then recite what God wills you to recite. When you bow, place your palms on your knees, extend your back, and settle into your bowing. When you rise, straighten your back until the bones return to their joints. When you prostrate, settle into your prostration. When you rise, sit on your left thigh, and do likewise in every rak'ah and prostration.\""],[4423,"Rifa'ah b. Rafi' said: One day we were praying behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he raised his head from the rak'ah and said, \"God hears the one who praises Him,\" a man behind him said: \"Our Lord, and to You be praise, abundant, good, blessed praise.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: \"Who spoke just now?\" The man said: \"I, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I saw thirty-some angels racing to see which of them would write it down first.\""],[4424,"He prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Rifa'ah sneezed and said: \"Praise be to God, abundant, good, blessed praise, blessed upon it, as our Lord loves and is pleased with.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: \"Where is the one who spoke during the prayer?\" Rifa'ah said: \"I wished I had lost a portion of my wealth and had not attended that prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he said, 'Where is the one who spoke?'\" I said: \"I, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"How did you say?\" I said: \"I said: Praise be to God, abundant, good, blessed praise, blessed upon it, as our Lord loves and is pleased with.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, thirty-some angels raced to see which of them would ascend with it.\""],[4425,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the children of the children of the Ansar, their descendants, and their neighbors.\""],[4426,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, their descendants, and their neighbors.\""],[4427,"So I stabbed him with a sword thrust and killed him. I was shot with an arrow on the day of Badr, and my eye was put out. The Messenger of God ﷺ spat in it and prayed for me, and nothing has harmed me from it since.\""],[4428,"Umar ؓ said: \"Bring him to me so that I may be a witness against him.\" When he came to him, he said to him: \"O enemy of yourself, you mislead people without knowledge.\" He said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, by God, I did not originate it; rather, I heard that from my paternal uncles.\" He said: \"Which of your paternal uncles?\" He said: \"Ubayy b. Ka'b, Rifa'ah b. Rafi', and Abu Ayyub.\" Rifa'ah, who was present, said: \"Do not rebuke him, O Commander of the Faithful, for by God, we used to do this during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said: \"Did you know whether the Messenger of God ﷺ was aware of any of that?\" He said: \"No.\" Ali b. Abi Talib said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, this matter is not right.\" He said: \"Whom should I ask after you, O best people of Badr?\" Ali ؓ said: \"Send to the Mothers of the Believers.\" He sent to Hafsah ؓ, and she said: \"I have no knowledge.\" He sent to A'ishah ؓ, and she said: \"When the two circumcised parts meet, bathing becomes obligatory.\" Then they delved into the mention of coitus interruptus and said: \"There is no harm in it.\" A man whispered to his companion, and he said: \"What is this private conversation? One of them claims that it is the minor buried alive.\" Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ said: \"It cannot be a buried alive until it passes through seven stages. God Almighty said: {And certainly did We create man from an extract of clay. Then We placed him as a sperm-drop in a firm lodging. Then We made the sperm-drop into a clinging clot, and We made the clot into a lump, and We made the lump into bones, and We covered the bones with flesh; then We developed him into another creation. So blessed is God, the best of creators.}\" They dispersed upon the statement of Ali b. Abi Talib that there is no harm in it."],[4429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No less than twenty verses are to be recited in the morning prayer, and no less than ten verses are to be recited in the night prayer.”"],[4430,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ to the market. He said: “O company of merchants!” The merchants raised their eyes toward him and responded to him. He said: “Indeed, merchants will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as wicked people, except for those who fear Allah, act righteously, and are truthful.”"],[4431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to al-Baqiʿ and said: “O company of merchants!” until they craned their necks. He said: “Indeed, merchants will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection as wicked people, except for those who fear Allah, act righteously, and are truthful.”"],[4432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in Madinah and found the people buying and selling. He called out: “O company of merchants!” They responded to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and raised their eyes toward him. He said: “Indeed, merchants will be resurrected as wicked people, except for those who fear Allah, act righteously, and are truthful.”"],[4433,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the prayer area in Madinah and found the people buying and selling. He said: “O company of merchants!” They responded and raised their necks and eyes toward him. He said: “Indeed, merchants will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as wicked people, except for those who fear Allah, are truthful, and act righteously.”"],[4434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ: “Gather your people for me, O ʿUmar.” So he gathered them. When they had arrived at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿUmar entered upon him and said: “I have gathered my people for you.” The Anṣār heard of that and said: “Revelation has descended concerning Quraysh.” So the listeners and onlookers came to see what he would say to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and stood among them and said: “Is there anyone among you who is not one of you?” They said: “Yes, among us are our allies, the sons of our sisters, and our freedmen.” The Messenger of Allah said: “Our ally is one of us, the son of our sister is one of us, and our freedman is one of us. You hear: my allies on the Day of Resurrection are the God-fearing. If you are those, then that is so; otherwise, beware lest people come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds while you come with heavy burdens, and He turns away from you.” Then he called out and said: “O people, Quraysh are people of trustworthiness. Whoever seeks for them the pitfalls or the stumbles—Zuhayr said: I think it is the stumbles—Allah will cast him down on his nostrils.” He said that three times."],[4435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar ؓ: “Gather your people.” So he gathered them at the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he entered upon him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall I bring them in to you or will you go out to them?” He said: “No, rather I will go out to them.” He came to them and stood over them and said: “Is there anyone among you other than you?” They said: “Yes, among us are our allies, the sons of our brothers, and our freedmen.” He said: “Our ally is one of us and the son of our brother is one of us.” He said: “You hear: my allies among you are the God-fearing. If you are those, then that is so; otherwise, beware lest people come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds while you come with heavy burdens, and I turn away from you.” Then he raised his hands while standing and they were sitting, and said: “O people, Quraysh are people of trustworthiness. Whoever seeks for them the stumbles, Allah will cast him down on his nostrils.” He said it three times."],[4436,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿUmar: “Gather your people for me.” So he gathered them, and they were at the door. He said: “Is there anyone among you from other than you?” They said: “No, except the son of our sister and our freedman.” He said: “The son of your sister and your freedman are from you.” Then he said: “Indeed, my allies among you are the God-fearing. Beware lest people come to me with good deeds and you come to me with heavy burdens that you carry on your backs.” Then he said: “Indeed, Quraysh are people of endurance and trustworthiness. Whoever seeks for them the stumbles, Allah will cast him down on his face on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4437,"We set out on the day of Badr and missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The traveling groups called out to one another: “Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among you?” They stopped until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, with him ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we missed you.” He said: “Abū Ḥasan had a stomach cramp, so I stayed behind with him.”"],[4438,"On the day of Uḥud, when the polytheists turned back, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Stand in rows so that I may praise my Lord.” He said: So they formed rows behind him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, to You belongs all praise. There is no withholder for what You extend, no extender for what You withhold, no guide for whom You lead astray, no misleader for whom You guide, no bringer near for what You put far, no putter far for what You bring near, no giver for what You prevent, and no preventer for what You give. O Allah, spread over us from Your blessings, Your mercy, Your bounty, and Your provision. O Allah, I ask You for enduring bliss on the day of need and security on the day of fear. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld from us. O Allah, cause us to die as Muslims and join us with the righteous, without disgrace or trial. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who block Your path and deny Your messengers. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who were given the Scripture, O God of truth.”"],[4439,"When Iblīs saw what the angels were doing to the polytheists on the day of Badr, he feared that the killing would reach him. Al-Ḥārith b. Hishām clung to him, thinking he was Surāqah b. Mālik, so he struck al-Ḥārith in the chest and threw him down. Then he fled until he threw himself into the sea and raised his hands, saying: “I ask You for Your respite for me.” He feared that the killing would reach him. Then Abū Jahl b. Hishām came and said: “O people, do not let Surāqah’s desertion of you defeat you, for he had an appointment with Muḥammad ﷺ. Do not let the killing of ʿUtbah, Shaybah, and al-Walīd terrify you, for they acted hastily. By al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā, we will not return until we bind them with ropes. Let no man among you kill one of them, but take them captive so that you may make them know the evil of their deed in separating from you and turning away from al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā.” Then Abū Jahl said, quoting poetry:"],[4440,"From ʿUrwah: “In naming the people of al-ʿAqabah: Rifāʿah b. ʿAmr b. Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Qays b. Thaʿlabah b. Mālik b. Sālim b. Ghānim b. ʿAwf b. al-Khazraj. He witnessed Badr and was one of those who went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as an emigrant.”"],[4441,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Hubla: Rifa'ah b. 'Amr, and he attended Badr.\""],[4442,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu Sawa': Rifa'ah b. 'Amr.\""],[4443,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who attended the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Zufur—and the name of Zufur is Ka'b al-Khazraj—: Rifa'ah b. al-Mundhir b. Rifa'ah b. Dinar b. Zayd b. Umayyah b. Malik b. 'Awf b. 'Amr b. 'Awf, and he attended Badr.\""],[4444,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Aws, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Umayyah b. Zayd: Rifa'ah b. 'Abd al-Mundhir.\""],[4445,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began giving them permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: Then you would see none of the people but weeping. He said: Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"The one who asks your permission for himself after this is indeed foolish.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: \"I bear witness before Allah\"—and when he swore, he would say: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad—there is none among you who believes in Allah and then remains upright except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord ﷻ has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that they will not enter it until you, and the righteous among your spouses and offspring, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4446,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began giving them permission. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: Then you would see none of the people but weeping. He said: Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"The one who asks your permission for himself after this is indeed foolish.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: \"I bear witness before Allah\"—and when he swore, he would say: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad—there is none among you who believes in Allah and then remains upright except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord ﷻ has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that they will not enter it until you, and the righteous among your spouses and offspring, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4447,"He said: We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would give them permission. He said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: Then you would see none among the people but weeping. Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"The one who asks your permission for himself after this is indeed foolish.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: \"I bear witness before Allah\"—and when he swore, he would say: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul—there is none among you who believes in Allah and then remains upright except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that they will not enter it until you, and the righteous among your spouses and your children, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4448,"He said: We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would give them permission. He said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" He said: Then you would see none among the people but weeping. Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"The one who asks your permission for himself after this is indeed foolish.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: \"I bear witness before Allah\"—and when he swore, he would say: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul—there is none among you who believes in Allah and then remains upright except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that they will not enter it until you, and the righteous among your spouses and your children, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4449,"He said: We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when we were at al-Kadid, they began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to go to their families, and he would give them permission. He said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" After that, none of the people were seen except weeping. Then a man from the people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the one who asks your permission after this is indeed foolish.\" Then he praised Allah and extolled Him with good, then said: \"I bear witness before Allah: no servant who bears witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart, and then remains upright, will die except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that you will not enter until you, and the righteous among your spouses and your children, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4450,"He said: We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when we were at al-Kadid, they began asking permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to go to their families, and he would give them permission. He said: \"What is the matter with the side of the tree that is next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being more hateful to you than the other side?\" After that, none of the people were seen except weeping. Then a man from the people said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the one who asks your permission after this is indeed foolish.\" Then he praised Allah and extolled Him with good, then said: \"I bear witness before Allah: no servant who bears witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart, and then remains upright, will die except that he will be led thereby into Paradise. And my Lord has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community, with no reckoning upon them and no punishment. And I hope that you will not enter until you, and the righteous among your spouses and your children, have taken up dwellings in Paradise.\""],[4451,"Rifa'ah b. Zayd al-Judhami came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the truce of al-Hudaybiyyah, and he gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a servant boy as a gift, and he embraced Islam, and his Islam was good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for him to his people a letter, in which was: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a letter from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah to Rifa'ah b. Zayd. I have sent him to his people generally, and to those who enter among them, calling them to Allah and to His Messenger. Whoever accepts is in the party of Allah and His Messenger, and whoever turns away has a guarantee of safety for two months.\" When Rifa'ah came to his people, they responded and embraced Islam."],[4452,"\"This verse was revealed concerning ten people, I being one of them.\" {And We have conveyed to them the Word so that they might remember}"],[4453,"He informed him that his father Rabi'ah b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and 'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib said to 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Rabi'ah and al-Fadl b. 'Abbas: \"Go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and say: 'O Messenger of God, you see that we have reached marriageable age. We would like to marry. You, O Messenger of God, are the most dutiful and most gracious of people, but our fathers have nothing with which to pay our bridal dowers. So appoint us, O Messenger of God, over the sadaqat (charitable revenues), and we shall deliver to you what the collectors deliver, and we shall take whatever benefit there is in them.'\" He said: 'Ali b. Abi Talib came to us while we were in that situation and said to us: \"No, by God, he will not appoint any of you over the sadaqah.\" Rabi'ah b. al-Harith said to him: \"This is from your envy and your wrongdoing. You have attained the Prophet's ﷺ kinship by marriage, and we did not envy you for it.\" So 'Ali threw down his cloak and lay upon it, then said: \"I am Abu al-Hasan today. By God, I will not leave this place of mine until your two sons return to you with the answer to what you sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" 'Abd al-Muttalib said: So al-Fadl and I went off until we arrived just as the noon prayer was being established. We prayed with the people, then al-Fadl and I hurried to the door of the Messenger of God's ﷺ chamber. That day he was with Zaynab bt. Jahsh. We stood at the door until the Messenger of God ﷺ came. He took hold of my ear and al-Fadl's ear and said: \"Go out, you two are muttering.\" Then he entered and gave permission for me and al-Fadl. We entered and left the talking to each other for a while. Then I spoke to him, or al-Fadl spoke to him - 'Abd Allah was uncertain about that - and we spoke to him about what our fathers had instructed us. The Messenger of God ﷺ fell silent. Then he raised his gaze toward the ceiling of the house until it seemed to us that he would not return to us with anything, and until we saw Zaynab gesturing from behind the curtain with her hand, meaning that we should not be hasty and that the Messenger of God ﷺ was considering our matter. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ lowered his head and said to us: \"This sadaqah is but the filth of people, and it is not lawful for Muhammad or for the family of Muhammad. Call Nawfal b. al-Harith for me.\" So Nawfal b. al-Harith was called for him. He said: \"O Nawfal, marry 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said: So Nawfal married me. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Call Mahmiyah b. Jaz' for me.\" He was a man from Banu Zubayd whom the Messenger of God ﷺ had appointed over the khums (fifths). The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Mahmiyah: \"Marry al-Fadl.\" So he married him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Stand and give their bridal dower from the khums, such and such.\" 'Abd Allah b. al-Harith did not hear it."],[4454,"I used to sleep in the Prophet's ﷺ chamber, and I would hear him when he got up at night to pray, saying \"Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds\" for the hawi, then he would say \"Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent and praise be to Him\" for the hawi. I said: What is the hawi? He said: \"He supplicates for a while.\""],[4455,"I used to spend the night with the Messenger of God ﷺ, bringing him his ablution water and his needs. He would get up at night and say: \"Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him, glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him\" for the hawi, \"Glory be to the Lord of the worlds, glory be to the Lord of the worlds\" for the hawi. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you have a need?\" I said: O Messenger of God, your companionship in Paradise. He said: \"Then help me against your own self by abundant prostration.\""],[4456,"I used to spend the night at the Messenger of God's ﷺ door, and I would hear him for the hawi of the night saying: \"Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,\" and I would hear him for the hawi of the night saying: \"Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him.\""],[4457,"He informed him that he used to spend the night at the Messenger of God's ﷺ door, and he would hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say during the night: \"Glory be to God, Lord of the worlds\" for the hawi, then he would say: \"Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him,\" something like that."],[4458,"I used to spend the night with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I would hear him for the hawi of the night saying: \"Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,\" then he would say: \"Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him\" for the hawi."],[4459,"He informed him that he heard Rabi'ah b. Ka'b say: I spent the night at the Messenger of God's ﷺ door, and I heard him say when he got up at night: \"Glory be to the Lord of the worlds\" for the hawi, then he would say: \"Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him\" for the hawi."],[4460,"I used to serve the Messenger of God ﷺ during my day. When night came, I would retire to the Messenger of God's ﷺ door and spend the night there. I would keep hearing him say: \"Glory be to God, glory be to my Lord,\" until I would grow weary or sleep would overcome me and I would fall asleep. One day he said: \"O Rabi'ah, ask me and I will give you.\" I said: Let me think, so I considered and remembered that this world is transient and fleeting. I said: O Messenger of God, I ask you to supplicate God to keep me away from the Fire and admit me to Paradise. The Messenger of God ﷺ was silent, then said: \"Who commanded you this?\" I said: No one commanded me, but I knew that this world is fleeting and transient, and you have the standing with God that you have, so I wanted you to supplicate God. He said: \"I shall do it, so help me against your own self by abundant prostration.\""],[4461,"I used to serve the Messenger of God ﷺ. He gave me a piece of land, and he gave Abu Bakr a piece of land. Then worldly affairs came and we disagreed over a bunch of dates from a palm tree. Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"It is within the boundary of my land,\" and I said: \"It is within my boundary.\" There were words between me and Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said a word to me that I disliked, and he regretted it. He said to me: \"O Rabi'ah, say the like of it back to me so that it may be retaliation.\" I said: I will not do that. Abu Bakr said: \"You will say it, or I will complain to the Messenger of God ﷺ against you.\" I said: I am not going to do it. He said: And he abandoned the land. Abu Bakr ؓ went off to the Prophet ﷺ, and I went off following him. Some people from Aslam came and said: \"May God have mercy on Abu Bakr. Why would he complain to the Messenger of God against you when he is the one who said to you what he said?\" I said: Do you know who this is? This is Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the second of the two, the one with the gray hair of the Muslims. Beware lest he turn and see you supporting me against him, for he will become angry and go to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God will become angry for his anger, and God will become angry for the anger of both of them, and Rabi'ah will perish. They said: What do you command us? He said: Go back. So Abu Bakr ؓ went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I followed him alone. I kept following until he reached the Prophet ﷺ and told him the story as it had happened. He raised his head to me and said: \"O Rabi'ah, what is the matter between you and al-Siddiq?\" I said: O Messenger of God, it was such and such, and he said a word to me that I disliked. He said to me: Say as I said to you so that it may be retaliation. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Yes, do not retaliate against him, but say: May God forgive you, O Abu Bakr. May God forgive you, O Abu Bakr.\" He said: Abu Bakr, may God have mercy on him, turned away weeping."],[4462,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. One day he said: \"O Rabi'ah, will you not marry?\" I said: By God, O Messenger of God, serving you is dearer to me. He said: Then he repeated it to me another time, and I said the like of that. He said: I said: By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ knows better what is good for me than I do. If he says it to me another time, I will say: Yes, O Messenger of God. Then he said to me: \"O Rabi'ah, will you not marry?\" I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said to me: \"Go to so-and-so, a man of the Ansar, and let them marry you to their daughter so-and-so.\" He said: So I went to them and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to marry me to her. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ does not go except for his need. He said: So they married me without asking me for any proof. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was distressed. He said to me: \"What is the matter with you, O Rabi'ah?\" I said: O Messenger of God, I came to a noble people and they married me without asking me for proof, and I have nothing to give as a bridal dower. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Collect for him the weight of a date stone of gold.\" They collected for me the weight of two date stones of gold. I brought it to them, and they accepted it and said: \"It is much and good.\" I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was distressed. He said: \"What is the matter with you, O Rabi'ah?\" I said: O Messenger of God, I came to a noble people and they accepted it and said: \"It is much and good,\" but I have nothing with which to hold a wedding feast. He said: \"Collect for him the price of a ram.\" They collected for me the price of a ram. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent to his family, and a basket containing barley was brought. I took it to them, and they said: As for the ram, you may take care of it, and as for the barley, we will take care of it for you. He said: So they did that, and in the morning I invited the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions."],[4463,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his leather socks.”"],[4464,"From his father, “In naming those who witnessed with Ali ؓ among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Rabi'ah b. Qays, and he is from 'Udwan.”"],[4465,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period at the market of Dhu al-Majaz saying, “O people, say there is no god but Allah and you will prosper.” He kept repeating it many times while people were lined up around him following him, and behind him was a cross-eyed man with two long locks of hair and a bright face, saying, “He is a renegade, a liar,” twice. I asked, “Who is this?” They said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4466,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going around among the people at Mina in their encampments before he emigrated to Madinah, saying, “O people, Allah ﷻ commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a man saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I asked, “Who is this man?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4467,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhu al-Majaz following the people, calling them to Allah in their encampments.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man saying, “Do not let this one tempt you away from the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4468,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhu al-Majaz following the people in their encampments, calling them to Allah ﷻ.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man saying, “O people, do not let this one deceive you away from your religion and the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4469,"He heard Rabi'ah b. 'Abbad al-Dili say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going around among the people at Mina in their encampments before he emigrated to Madinah, saying, “O people, Allah has commanded you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man with a bright face and two long locks of hair, saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I asked about him and it was said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4470,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the market of Dhu al-Majaz before he emigrated, going around among the people saying, “O people, Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a man saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4471,"I saw Abu Lahab at 'Ukaz following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was saying, “O people, this one has gone astray, so do not let him lead you astray from the noble deeds of your forefathers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fleeing from him while he followed him."],[4472,"I was with my father, a young man, looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ following the tribes, and behind him was a cross-eyed man with a bright face and a full head of hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stop at a tribe and say, “O Banu So-and-so, I am the Messenger of Allah to you, commanding you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and to believe me and protect me until I convey what Allah has sent me with.” When he finished his speech, the other man behind him would say, “O Banu So-and-so, this one wants you to cast off al-Lat and al-'Uzza and your allies from the tribe of Banu Malik b. Uqaysh, in favor of the innovation and misguidance he has brought. Do not listen to him and do not follow him.” I said to my father, “Who is this?” He said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4473,"I saw Abu Lahab at 'Ukaz following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was saying, “O people, this one has gone astray, so do not let him lead you astray from the noble deeds of your forefathers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was hastening away with Abu Lahab on his tracks, and we were following them. It is as if I am looking at him: cross-eyed, with two long locks of hair, the fairest and most handsome of people."],[4474,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing in a place before he was sent as a Prophet, then I saw him after he was sent standing in that same place at 'Arafat.\""],[4475,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing with the polytheists at 'Arafat, then I saw him after he was sent standing at his station there, so I knew that God had guided him to that.\""],[4476,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, then from Banu Mu'awiyah b. 'Awf: Rabi'ah b. al-Fadl b. Habib b. Zayd b. Tamim.\""],[4477,"He heard Rabi'ah al-Jurashi say that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Remain upright, and excellent it is if you remain upright; maintain ablution, for the best of your deeds is prayer; and be wary of the earth, for it is your mother, and there is no one who acts upon it with good or evil but that it will report it.\""],[4478,"He heard Rabi'ah al-Jurashi say that the Prophet of God ﷺ was approached and it was said to him, \"Let your eye sleep, let your ear hear, and let your heart comprehend.\" He said, \"So my eye slept, my ear heard, and my heart comprehended.\" He said, it was said to him: \"A master built a house and prepared a banquet and sent an inviter. Whoever answers the inviter enters the house and eats from the banquet and the master is pleased with him. Whoever does not answer the inviter does not enter the house, does not attain the banquet, and the master is angry with him. The master is God, the inviter is Muhammad ﷺ, and the banquet is Paradise.\""],[4479,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the allies of Banu 'Abd Shams b. 'Abd Manaf: Rabi'ah b. Aktham from Banu Asad b. Khuzaymah.\""],[4480,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Banu 'Abd Shams: Rabi'ah b. Aktham, an ally of theirs from Banu Asad.\""],[4481,"I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered for us two small flocks of camels and said, “Command your household to trim their nails so that they do not injure the udders of their livestock with them when they milk.”"],[4482,"From 'Urwah: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Lawdhan b. Ghanm b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj: Rabi' b. Iyas b. Ghanm b. Umayyah b. Lawdhan b. Ghanm.”"],[4483,"From Ibn Shihab: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from Banu al-'Ajlan: Rib'i b. Abi Rib'i.”"],[4484,"He divorced his wife irrevocably, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him. He said to him, “What did you intend?” He said, “One.” He said, “By Allah?” He said, “By Allah.” He said, “It is what you intended.”"],[4485,"He divorced his wife irrevocably, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned it to him. He said to him, “What did you intend by it?” He said, “One.” He said, “By Allah, did you intend by it only one?” He said, “By Allah, I intended by it only one.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “It is one.”"],[4486,"I met a man in Makkah from the people of 'Asqalan called Abu al-Hasan, and he narrated to me from Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. 'Ali, from Ibn Rukanah, from his father, that Rukanah wrestled with the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ threw him. Rukanah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The difference between us and the polytheists is the turbans over the caps.”"],[4487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Blessed is one who is humble without deficiency, humbles himself without poverty, spends wealth he has gathered without disobedience, shows mercy to the poor and needy, and associates with people of understanding and wisdom. Blessed is one who humbles himself, makes his earning good, improves his inner self, and keeps his evil away from people. Blessed is one who acts upon his knowledge, spends the surplus of his wealth, and withholds the surplus of his speech.”"],[4488,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Blessed is he who humbles himself without deficiency and lowers himself in his own soul without destitution, and spends wealth he gathered without disobedience, and shows mercy to the people of humility and poverty, and mixes with the people of understanding and wisdom. Blessed is he whose earnings are pure, whose inner self is sound, whose outward conduct is honorable, and who keeps his evil away from people. Blessed is he who acts upon knowledge, spends the surplus of his wealth, and withholds the surplus of his speech.\""],[4489,"He informed him that he went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition he undertook, in which Khalid b. al-Walid was in command of the vanguard. Rabah and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a woman who had been killed, one of those the vanguard had struck. They stopped at her, looking at her and marveling at her form, until the Messenger of God ﷺ caught up with them on a she-camel of his. They parted to make way for the woman. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he looked into the faces of the people and said to one of them: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid. He must not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4490,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, with Khalid b. al-Walid in command of the people's vanguard. There was a woman killed on the road, and they were marveling at her form; the vanguard had struck her. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and stood over her, then said to a man: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and say: He must not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4491,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition when the people were gathered around a woman who had been killed. He said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he said: \"Who is in command of the vanguard?\" They said: \"Khalid b. al-Walid.\" He sent a man to him and said: \"Command Khalid not to kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4492,"He informed him that he went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, and the vanguard was under Khalid b. al-Walid. Rabah and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ passed by a slain woman whom the vanguard had killed. They gathered around her, looking at her and at her form, and marveling at her, until the Messenger of God ﷺ came and they parted. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at her and said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he looked into the faces of the people and said to one of them: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and say: Do not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4493,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he had given every three of us a camel, with two riding it and one driving it in the deserts, while we led it in the mountains. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was walking, and said to me: \"I see you, O Rabah, walking.\" I said: \"I have just dismounted, and these two companions of mine have ridden.\" He went on and passed by my two companions, and they made their camel kneel and dismounted from it. When I caught up, they said: \"Ride the front of this camel, and remain on it until we return, and my companion and I will take turns.\" I said: \"Why?\" They said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You have a righteous companion, so be good to him.'\""],[4494,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"What has been born to you?\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, what could be born to me? Either a boy or a girl.\" He said: \"Whom will he resemble?\" He said: \"What could he resemble? Either his mother or his father.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Hush! Do not say that. When the drop settles in the womb, God ﷻ brings before it every lineage between it and Adam. Have you not read this verse in the Book of God ﷻ: 'In whatever form He willed, He assembled you'?\""],[4495,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Egypt will be conquered, so seek the best of its pasture, but do not make it a dwelling, for the people with the shortest lifespans will be driven to it.\""],[4496,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a servant boy named Rabah.\""],[4497,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a servant boy named Rabah.\""],[4498,"From Urwa: \"In naming those killed on the day of al-Yamama from the Ansar: Rabah, the freedman of Banu Jahjaba.\""],[4499,"From his father, who was from the people of Hajar and was a jurist, that he set out to the Messenger of God ﷺ in a delegation with some alms, and brought them to him. He forbade them from nabidh in these vessels, so they returned to their land, which is the land of Tihama, a hot land. They found it unhealthy, so they returned to him the second year with their alms. They said: O Messenger of God, you forbade us from these vessels, so we left them, and that was hard on us. He said: \"Go and drink whatever you wish, but do not drink what is tied in a skin that leads to sin.\""],[4500,"That the Prophet ﷺ wrote him a document on red leather, and he patched his bucket with it. The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a raiding party. They did not leave him any grazing livestock, nor any going out to pasture, nor family, nor property, except that they took it. He escaped naked on a horse and came to his daughter, who was married among Banu Hilal. The people's sitting place was in the courtyard of her door. He entered upon her from behind the houses. She said: What is wrong with you? He said: Every evil has befallen your father; no grazing livestock, nor any going out to pasture, nor family, nor property was left to him except that it was taken. I said: She had been called to Islam, and she had already become Muslim. He said: So she threw a garment over him, and he went out. He said: Where is your husband? She said: In the camp. He came to him wearing a garment that, if his head was covered with it, his buttocks were exposed; and if his buttocks were covered, his head was exposed. He said: What do I see with you? He said: Every evil has befallen me. He repeated to him the same words he had said to his daughter. He said: I want Muhammad before he divides my property. He said: Take my riding camel. He said: I have no need of it, but give me the young camel. So he took it and went to the Prophet ﷺ. He came to him at the dawn prayer while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, he said: Stretch out your hands, I will pledge allegiance to you. The Messenger of God ﷺ stretched out his hand, but when he wanted to strike it, the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew it. He did that several times, then he turned to him and said: \"Who are you?\" He said: Ri'ya al-Suhaymi. The Prophet ﷺ took him by his upper arm and lifted him off the ground, then said: \"Here is Ri'ya al-Suhaymi; I wrote him a document and he patched his bucket with it.\" Ri'ya said: My property and my son? He said: \"As for your property, it is too late; it has already been divided. As for your son and your family, whoever you find among them.\" He said: He went away, then returned, and there was his son, who had been recognized. He came back to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: This is my son. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Bilal, go out with him; if he claims that he is his son, then hand him over to him.\" So he went out with him, and he said: This is my son, so he handed him over to him. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: He claimed that he was his son, and I did not see either of them shed a tear for the other. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is the harshness of the Bedouins.\""],[4501,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote him a document, and he patched his bucket with it. A raiding party of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by him and drove away some camels of his, so he became Muslim. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"As for what you find of your property intact before it is divided, you have the most right to it.\""],[4502,"From 'Urwa: 'In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Mu'awiya b. al-Harith: Ruqaym b. Thabit b. Tha'laba.'"],[4503,"Some of them said to others: 'Kingship was among us, the people of Syria, and it is being transferred to the Hijaz; we are not pleased with that.'"],[4504,"From 'Urwa: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraysh, from Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b: Zayd b. al-Khattab.'"],[4505,"From ʿUrwa: “Concerning the naming of those from Quraysh from Banū ʿAdī b. Kaʿb who witnessed Badr: Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[4506,"From ʿUrwa: “Concerning the naming of those from Quraysh from Banū ʿAdī b. Kaʿb who witnessed Badr: Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[4507,"It is said: Abū Thawr.”"],[4508,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause miscarriage and take away sight.”"],[4509,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause miscarriage and take away sight.”"],[4510,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ḥātim b. Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Mujammiʿ narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Kill snakes.”"],[4511,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ḥātim b. Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Mujammiʿ narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Kill snakes.”"],[4512,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade the killing of jinn.\""],[4513,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Kill snakes: the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they seek out sight and cause miscarriage.”"],[4514,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Kill snakes: the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they seek out sight and cause miscarriage.”"],[4515,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah toward the graveyards. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down by a grave, and we saw him as if he were conversing privately. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up wiping tears from his eyes. ʿUmar, may God have mercy on him, met him—he was the first of us—and said: “With my father and mother as ransom for you, what makes you weep?” He said: “I asked my Lord, exalted be He, for permission to visit my mother’s grave. She was a mother, and she had a right over me that I ask forgiveness for her, but He forbade me.” Then he gestured to us to sit, so we sat. He said: “I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so whoever of you wishes to visit, let him visit. I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so eat and store whatever you wish. I had forbidden you from certain vessels, and I have commanded you concerning vessels, so soak [in them], for vessels do not make anything lawful or unlawful, and avoid every intoxicant.”"],[4516,"From ʿUrwa: “Concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Zayd b. Ḥāritha b. Sharāḥīl b. Kaʿb b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā b. Yazīd b. Imriʾ al-Qays al-Kalbī, upon whom God and His Messenger bestowed favor.”"],[4517,"From Ibn Shihāb: “Concerning the naming of those from Quraysh who witnessed Badr, then from Banū Hāshim: Zayd b. Ḥāritha.”"],[4518,"It is said that the mother of Zayd was Suʿād bt. Zayd, from Ṭayyiʾ."],[4519,"It is said that the mother of Zayd was Suʿād bt. Zayd, from Ṭayyiʾ."],[4520,"Zayd b. Ḥāritha embraced Islam after ʿAlī ؓ and was the first to embrace Islam after him."],[4521,"The first to embrace Islam was Zayd b. Ḥāritha."],[4522,"From ʿUrwa: regarding the naming of those killed on the day of Muʾta, Zayd b. Ḥāritha."],[4523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Muʾta in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year eight. He appointed Zayd b. Ḥāritha as commander and said to them: \"If Zayd is struck down, then Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib is over the people; and if Jaʿfar is struck down, then ʿAbdullāh b. Rawāḥa is over the people.\""],[4524,"Then the people went on until, when they were at the borders of al-Balqāʾ, the hosts of Heraclius met them. The Muslims withdrew to a village called Muʾta, and the people met there. The Muslims arrayed themselves and placed on their right wing a man from Banū ʿUdhra called Quṭba b. Qatāda, and on their left wing a man from the Anṣār called ʿAbāya b. Mālik. Then the people met, and Zayd b. Ḥāritha fought with the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he was pierced by the spears of the people."],[4525,"Jibrīl ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ at the first of what was revealed to him and taught him the ablution and the prayer. When he finished, the Prophet ﷺ took some water in his hand and sprinkled his private part with it."],[4526,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you made a bond of brotherhood between me and Ḥamza b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.\""],[4527,"O Messenger of Allah, you made a bond of brotherhood between me and Ḥamza."],[4528,"Ḥamza, the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was the brother of Zayd b. Ḥāritha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a bond of brotherhood between them."],[4529,"Zayd b. Ḥāritha said regarding the daughter of Ḥamza: \"She is the daughter of my brother; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a bond of brotherhood between me and her father.\""],[4530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give glad tidings to those who walk in the darkness to the mosques of a radiant light on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, with me riding behind him, to one of the stone altars. We slaughtered a sheep for him, then we cooked it in a fire pit. When it was done, we took it out into our traveling provision bag. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted his she-camel, with me riding behind him. When we reached the upper part of Makkah, he met Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl. One of them greeted the other with the greeting of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Why do I see that your people have come to dislike and hate you?\" He said: \"By Allah, that from them is not because of any wrong I did to them, except that I see them in error. So I went out seeking this religion until I came to the Jewish scholars of Khaybar. I found them worshiping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said: By Allah, this is not the religion I am seeking. So I went out until I came to the Jewish scholars of Syria. I found them worshiping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said: By Allah, this is not the religion I went out seeking. A rabbi among the Jewish scholars of Syria said: You are asking about a religion we know of no one who worships Allah by it except a certain person in the Peninsula. So I went out until I came to him and told him what I had gone out for. He said to me: Everyone you have seen is in error. You are asking about the religion of Allah and His angels. A prophet has appeared in your land, or is about to appear. Return, believe in him, and follow him. So I returned, and I have not tested any prophet since.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his she-camel kneel and placed the provision bag before him. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"A sheep we slaughtered for such-and-such a stone altar.\" Zayd b. ʿAmr said: \"We do not eat anything slaughtered for other than Allah.\" Then we parted. He said: Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl died before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent as a prophet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation unto himself.\""],[4532,"I circumambulated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and I touched one of the idols. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do not touch it.\" I said: I will go back until I see what he says. Then I touched it. He said: \"Were you not forbidden from this?\" He said: By the One who honored him with the Book, he did not touch any idol among them until Allah honored him and sent down the Book upon him."],[4533,"I was a young boy during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let us go to a person whose situation we have seen.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went walking, and his companions with him, until they entered between two walls in a long alley. They stopped at a small door at the far end of the alley and entered a house. They saw no one in the house except a single woman, and there was a large water skin full of water. They said: We see a water skin but we do not see its carrier. Speak to the woman. She pointed to a velvet cloth in a corner of the house and said: Look under the velvet cloth. They uncovered it, and under it was a man. He raised his head, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Ugly is the face.\" He said: O Muhammad, why do you use obscene language against me? The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"I have hidden something for you. Tell me what it is?\" And he said to his companions: Indeed I have hidden for him Surat al-Dukhan. He said: \"Dukh.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Be off! What Allah wills happens.\" Then he left."],[4534,"\"I gave a horse of mine in charity. Then I saw its filly being sold in the market, and I wanted to buy it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about it.\""],[4535,"He had given a horse in the way of Allah. Then later he found it being sold in the market, tied up and emaciated. He bargained for it, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: I had given a horse in the way of Allah, and I found it being sold in the market for a small price, emaciated and tied up, and I recognized its sweat. Should I buy it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade him to buy it."],[4536,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the time of the dawn prayer. He said: \"Pray it with us today and tomorrow.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at Qāʿ Nimrah from al-Juhfah, he prayed it when the first light of dawn appeared. Then when he was at Dhū Ṭuwā, he delayed it until the people said: \"Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away? If only we had prayed.\" He then prayed just before sunrise. Then he turned to the people and said: \"What did you say?\" They said: \"If only we had prayed.\" He said: \"If you had done so, punishment would have befallen you.\" Then he called the questioner and said: \"Its time is between my two prayers.\""],[4537,"I entered the mosque and I recognized in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hunger, so I asked Umm Sulaym, “Do you have anything?” She gestured with her two hands and said, “I have something.” I said, “Prepare it, knead it,” and I sent Anas and said, “Go to him, whisper in his ear, and invite him.” When Anas returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This is a man who has brought you good. With what thing did your father send you to invite us?” Anas said, “Yes.” So I met him, and he said, “Get up, in the name of Allah.” Anas turned and ran quickly until he came to Abu Talhah and said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he has come to you among the people.” Abu Talhah said, “So I met him at the door, at the rest of the step, and I said, ‘What have you done to us, O Messenger of Allah? I only recognized hunger in your face, so I prepared something for you to eat.’ He said, ‘Enter and rejoice.’ He entered, and their dish was brought, and he began to smooth it with his hand, then he said, ‘Is there any—’ as if he meant condiment. They brought him their small butter-skin, containing something or not containing it, and he gestured with his hand, and ghee poured from it. Then he said, ‘Admit to me ten at a time, ten at a time.’” He said, “And they were about a hundred. They entered and ate until they were full. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the leftover that remained, ‘Eat, you and your dependents.’ So they ate and were full.”"],[4538,"From Abū Ṭalḥah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he entered upon Sahl while he was ill, and beneath Sahl was a coverlet containing figures. Sahl said, “Remove from beneath me this coverlet.” Abū Ṭalḥah said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding images: ‘The angels do not enter it, except what is embroidery in a cloth, for there is no harm in it.’” Sahl said, “Even so, remove it.”"],[4539,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate pieces of dried curd, then performed ablution because of it.”"],[4540,"Yaḥyā b. Sulaym b. Zayd, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me that he heard Ismāʿīl b. Bashīr, the freed slave of Banū Maghālah, saying: I heard Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Ṭalḥah b. Sahl al-Anṣārī, the two Anṣārīs, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no person who forsakes a Muslim in a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated, except that Allah forsakes him in a place where he loves His help. And there is no one who helps a Muslim in a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated, except that Allah helps him in a place where he loves His help.”"],[4541,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'My Companions are a group, and the people are a group.' Zayd b. Thābit and Rāfi' b. Khadīj said: He has spoken the truth."],[4542,"I heard Zayd b. Thābit say: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he became heavy because of it, and his forehead poured sweat like pearls, even in the cold. The wording is that of 'Uqba b. Mukram."],[4543,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah remains in the servant’s need as long as he remains in his brother’s need.”"],[4544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Zayd, give the zakah of your head along with the people, even if you find nothing but a saʿ of wheat.”"],[4545,"He said in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ: \"Authority is an evil thing.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Authority is a good thing for the one who takes it by its right and fulfills it, and authority is an evil thing for the one who takes it without its right, and it will be a regret for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4546,"A man from the Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a piece of land between two mountains, so he wrote it for him. Then he embraced Islam, and then went to his people and said to them: Embrace Islam, for I have come to you from a man who gives like one who does not fear poverty."],[4547,"Zayd b. Thabit said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge except in three cases: for the head wound reaching the brain, the bone-breaking wound, and the flesh-exposing wound. For the head wound reaching the brain, thirty-three; for the bone-breaking wound, fifteen; and for the flesh-exposing wound, five. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged concerning the eye of an animal at a quarter of its price.”"],[4548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There was no emigrant between Uthman and Ruqayya and Lot\" — meaning that they were the first to emigrate to the land of Abyssinia."],[4549,"Someone related to us a hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"And what shall I tell you? I was his neighbor. When revelation descended, he would send for me, and I would write down the revelation. When we mentioned the Hereafter, he would mention it with us; when we mentioned this world, he would mention it with us; and when we mentioned food, he would mention it with us.\" So all of this I relate to you from him."],[4550,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? [It is] 'There is no might nor power except with God.'\" Abu Nu'aym did not mention Kharijah."],[4551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ partitioned off a room and used to pray in it. His companions noticed him and would pray following his prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best prayer is a man's prayer in his house, except the prescribed prayer.”"],[4552,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If you hear of a plague in a land, do not enter it. If it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave it.”"],[4553,"“The verse intensifying the killing of a soul, which is in Surat al-Nisa’, came down after the one in al-Furqan by six months.” His saying: {And whoever does that will meet a penalty}."],[4554,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi’b narrated to us, from ‘Uqbah b. ‘Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad b. ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Thawban, from Zayd b. Thabit, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[4555,"“That ‘Ali consummated marriage with Fatimah ؓ before he allotted her anything.”"],[4556,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lengthen the recitation and move his lips.”"],[4557,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not dispute about the Qur’an, for disputing about it is disbelief.”"],[4558,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If this is your affair, then do not compel her.”"],[4559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am leaving among you after me the two weighty things: the Book of God, exalted be He, and my kindred, the people of my house. They will never separate until they come to me at the pool.”"],[4560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God have mercy on a person who hears my statement and conveys it, for many a bearer of understanding is not a jurist, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more learned than himself.”"],[4561,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Things come to me that I dislike being read. Can you learn Syriac?\" I said, \"Yes.\" \"So I learned it in seventeen [days].\" Abu al-Qasim said: \"This is how Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated it from Adi b. Thabit, thus differing from the companions of al-A'mash in the chain. If he preserved it, it is strange from the hadith of Adi b. Thabit; otherwise, the hadith is as the people narrated from al-A'mash, from Thabit b. Ubayd.\""],[4562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Every weak, humble person; if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Shall I not tell you about the people of the Fire?\" He said: \"Every harsh, coarse, arrogant person.\""],[4563,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while we were with him: \"Blessed is Syria (al-Sham).\" We said, \"What about it, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The Most Merciful spreads His mercy over it.\""],[4564,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-four portions, up to his prayer [being] twenty-five.\""],[4565,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever makes a claim against his brother without evidence, the defendant is more entitled to take the oath.\" The wording is that of Ali b. Bahr."],[4566,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping (mukhabarah).\" I said, \"What is mukhabarah?\" He said: \"That you take land in return for a half, a third, or a quarter [of its produce].\""],[4567,"\"Do you not feel shy before one from whom the angels feel shy?\" We said, \"What is that?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Uthman passed by me while an angel from among the angels was with me, and he said: \"A martyr whom his people will kill; we feel shy before him.\" Badr said: \"So a band of people turned away from him.\"\""],[4568,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the ruqbā for the one to whom he granted ruqbā and the ‘umrā for the one to whom he granted ‘umrā.”"],[4569,"From ‘Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Jusham b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Zayd b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.”"],[4570,"From ‘Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Jazrah b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and they are Banu al-Hubullayy: Zayd b. al-Marsi.”"],[4571,"A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Convey peace to him and say: Were we not in a state of consecration, we would not have returned it.\""],[4572,"The Prophet ﷺ stopped at al-Juhfa, then turned to the people, praised and extolled Allah, and said: \"I find that no prophet lives beyond half the age of the one before him, and I am about to be summoned and will answer. So what will you say?\" They said: \"You have counseled well.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Paradise is true, and the Fire is true, and that resurrection after death is true?\" They said: \"We testify.\" He said, raising his hands and placing them on his chest: \"And I testify with you.\" Then he said: \"Do you not hear?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I will go ahead of you to the Pond, and you will come to me at the Pond. Its width is as far as the distance between San'a' and Busra; in it are goblets of silver numbering the stars. So watch how you succeed me in the two weighty things!\" A caller asked: \"What are the two weighty things, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The Book of Allah, one end in the hand of Allah, Mighty and Exalted, and one end in your hands, so hold fast to it and you will not go astray; and the other is my offspring. The Subtle, the Aware has informed me that they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond. I asked that for them from my Lord. So do not precede them or you will perish, and do not fall short of them or you will perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you.\" Then he took 'Ali ؓ by the hand and said: \"He whose affairs I have more right to than his own self, 'Ali is his guardian. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[4573,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicate and raise his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits."],[4574,"Ali adjured the people in the Rahbah: 'Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say what he said to him?' Sixteen men stood up and testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.' Zayd b. Arqam said: 'I was among those who concealed it, so my sight was taken away, and Ali ؓ had supplicated against those who concealed it.'"],[4575,"Ali ؓ was in Yemen when three men came to him disputing about a child, each claiming it was his son. He was alone with two of them and said, 'Would you be content to give the child to this one?' They said, 'No.' Then he was alone with two of them and said to them the like of that, and they said, 'No.' He said, 'I see you are obstinate partners, so I will draw lots among you.' He drew lots among them and made the child belong to the one whom the lot struck, and he charged him two-thirds of the blood money for the remaining two."],[4576,"On the authority of al-Bara’ and Zayd b. Arqam, they said: The Prophet ﷺ came while we were exchanging money. He said: “There is no harm in it hand to hand, but deferred payment is disliked.”"],[4577,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of God and my family (ʿitrah)?” He said: Yes."],[4578,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication that, if you call upon with it, even if you had sins as numerous as the number of atoms, they would be forgiven for you, although you are forgiven? Say: O God, there is no god but You, the Wise, the Generous. Blessed are You, glory be to You, Lord of the Mighty Throne.”"],[4579,"We were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , when we were in prayer, if one of us wanted something, he would speak to him and continue walking until this verse was revealed, \"And stand before Allah, devoutly obedient\" (Quran 2:238), so we were commanded to remain silent."],[4580,"I was sitting in the gathering of the Banu al-Arqam when a man from Murad came riding on his mount until he stopped at the gathering and greeted. He said: Is Zayd among the people? They said: Yes, this is Zayd. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god, O Zayd, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Ali: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy”? He said: Yes. Then the man turned away from him."],[4581,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon on the day of Ghadir and said: “Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves?” They said: Yes. Then he took hold of Ali’s ؓ hand and said: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy.”"],[4582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever wants to live my life, die my death, and reside in the eternal paradise that my Lord has promised me, should take 'Ali ibn Abi Talib as their leader. For he will not lead you astray and will not admit you into misguidance.\""],[4583,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How can I be at ease while the companion of the horn has placed the horn in his mouth, waiting for when he is commanded, and then he will blow into it?” They said: What should we say? He said: “Say: Sufficient for us is God, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.”"],[4584,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah ﷻ is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately deviate; He guides him toward good as long as he intends nothing else.”"],[4585,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “‘Abd Allah b. Mas’ud taught me a surah, Zayd taught it to me, and my father taught it to me, and their recitations differed. Whose recitation should I adopt?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, while ‘Ali ؓ was beside him. ‘Ali ؓ said: “Let each person recite as he was taught; each is good and beautiful.”"],[4586,"“It is the night of the seventeenth, the night of the Quran’s revelation, and the day the two armies met.”"],[4587,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “If a man promises his brother, intending to keep it, but does not come to the appointment, there is no sin upon him.”"],[4588,"“I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said the takbir five times.” I will not abandon them for anyone after him."],[4589,"I heard ‘Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul say: {Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse.} I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. Ibn Ubayy came to him and swore that he had not said it. Then the companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to me and blamed me. I went to my home and slept in a dejected state. The Prophet ﷺ sent for me, and I came to him—or he said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ—and he said: “Allah has confirmed you and excused you.” And he recited these two verses: {They are the ones who say, ‘Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah’} until he completed the two verses."],[4590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his father or mother, it suffices him and them.”"],[4591,"He said: “Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, senility, the torment of the grave, and the trial of the Dajjal. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best to purify it, You are its guardian and master. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not heard.” Or he said: “a call that is not answered.”"],[4592,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali on the day of Ghadir Khumm: \"O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[4593,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, the sons of the sons of the Ansar, the women of the Ansar, the women of the sons of the Ansar, and the women of the sons of the sons of the Ansar.”"],[4594,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What an excellent man Bilal is, and the muezzins will be the longest of people in necks.\""],[4595,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What an excellent person Bilal is, and none follows him except a believer, and he is the master of the muezzins, and the muezzins will be the longest of people in necks on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4596,"Ilyas ibn AbuRamlah ash-Shami said: I witnessed Mu'awiyah ibn AbuSufyan asking Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you offer along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Friday and 'Id prayers synchronised on the same day? He said: Yes. He asked: How did he do? He replied: He offered the 'Id prayer, then granted concession to offer the Friday prayer, and said: If anyone wants to offer it, he may offer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1070)"],[4597,"Some people from the Arabs came and said: \"Let us go to this man. If he is a prophet, then we will be the happiest of people with him, and if he is a king, we will live under his protection.\" So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him what they had said. Then they came to the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ and began calling out, \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad!\" He said: Then God, may He be exalted, sent down: {Indeed, those who call you from behind the rooms, most of them do not understand}. The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of my ear and said: \"God has confirmed your words, O Zayd.\""],[4598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to plant trees, so we stood up what was under them and sprinkled them with water. Then he addressed us and said, \"By Allah, there is nothing that will happen until the Hour comes, but we have been informed about it on that day.\" Then he said, \"O people, who is more worthy of you than yourselves?\" We said, \"Allah and His Messenger are more worthy of us than ourselves.\" He said, \"So whoever I am his guardian, 'Ali is his guardian.\" Then he took his hand and said, \"O Allah, be a protector to those who protect him and be an enemy to those who show enmity to him.\""],[4599,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade gourds, pitch-covered vessels, and hollowed-out stumps.\""],[4600,"And I said while I was in prayer: 'Glory be to God, glory be to God.' Then he said: 'Be silent, be silent.' (He said): 'Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' This was in the first book. 'Abu Bakr al-Siddiq has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth — weak in his body, strong in the cause of God.' This was in the first book. 'Umar b. al-Khattab has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth — strong in his body, strong in the cause of God.' This was in the first book. 'Uthman b. Affan has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth.' 'Two have passed and four remain, and the protected zones have been permitted — the well of Aris. And what is the well of Aris? Peace be upon you, 'Abd Allah b. Rawaha. Have you sensed Kharija and Sa'd with me?' Sharik said: 'They are his father and his brother.'"],[4601,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque of Madinah, and he began to say: 'Where is so-and-so, son of so-and-so?' He did not cease to notice their absence and send for them until they had gathered before him. Then he said: 'I am going to tell you a hadith, so memorize it, understand it, and relate it to those after you: God has chosen a creation from His creation.' Then he recited this verse: {God chooses from the angels messengers and from the people} 'a creation whom He will admit to Paradise. I am chosen from among you; whoever I wish to choose, I choose, and I make brotherhood among you just as God made brotherhood among the angels. Rise, O Abu Bakr.' He rose and knelt before him. He said: 'You have a hand with me that God will reward you for. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken you as a close friend. You are to me like my shirt to my body.' And he moved his shirt with his hand. Then he said: 'Come close, O 'Umar.' He came close. He said: 'You were harsh in your opposition to us, Abu Hafs. I called upon God to strengthen the religion through you or through Abu Jahl, and God did that through you. You are the more beloved of the two to me, and you will be with me in Paradise, the third of three of this ummah.' Then he stepped aside and made him a brother with Abu Bakr. Then he called 'Uthman and said: 'Come close, O 'Uthman. Come close, O 'Uthman.' He kept drawing near until he touched his knee to the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he looked at him, then looked at the sky and said: 'Glory be to God, the Magnificent' three times. Then he looked at 'Uthman, and his buttons were undone, so the Messenger of God ﷺ buttoned them with his hand. Then he said: 'Gather the two ends of your cloak over your chest, for you will have an affair among the people of heaven. You are among those who will come to me at the cistern with his jugular veins gushing blood, and I will say: Who did this to you? You will say: So-and-so and so-and-so. That is the speech of Gabriel ﷺ , when he called from heaven: Verily 'Uthman is trustworthy over every one who is forsaken.' Then he called 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and said: 'Come close, O trusted one of God, the trusted one in heaven. God will give you power over your wealth with truth. Verily you have a supplication with me, and I have delayed it.' He said: 'Choose for me, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'You have burdened me, O 'Abd al-Rahman, with a trust. May God increase your wealth.' He said: And he began to move his hand. Then he stepped aside and made him a brother with 'Uthman. Then Talha and al-Zubayr entered, and he said: 'Come close to me.' They came close. He said: 'You two are my disciples, like the disciples of Jesus son of Mary ﷺ .' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he called Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas and 'Ammar b. Yasir and said: 'O 'Ammar, you will be killed by the rebellious faction.' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he called 'Uwaymir Abu al-Darda' and Salman al-Farisi and said: 'O Salman, you are from us, the People of the House. God has given you the first knowledge and the last knowledge, the first book and the last book.' Then he said: 'Shall I direct you, O Abu al-Darda'?' He said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'That you rescue them, they would rescue you; if you leave them, they will not leave you; if you flee from them, they will catch you. So lend them your honor for the day of your poverty.' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he looked at the faces of his companions and said: 'Rejoice and be comforted, for you are the first to come to me at the cistern, and you will be in the highest chambers.' Then he looked at 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar and said: 'Praise be to God who guides from misguidance.' Then 'Ali said: 'O Messenger of God, my spirit has departed and my back has broken when I saw you do what you did with your companions other than me. If it is from displeasure with me, then to you belongs the right to be pleased and honor.' He said: 'By the One who sent me with the truth, I did not delay you except for myself. You are to me in the position of Aaron to Moses, and you are my heir.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, what do I inherit from you?' He said: 'What the prophets inherited.' He said: 'And what did the prophets inherit before you?' He said: 'The Book of God and the sunnah of their prophet. And you will be with me in my palace in Paradise, with Fatimah my daughter, and my companion.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited the verse: {Brothers on couches, facing one another} 'the beloved friends in God, looking at each other.'"],[4602,"“The Prophet ﷺ deemed some people too young on the day of Uhud: among them Zayd b. Jariya — meaning himself — al-Bara' b. 'Azib, Sa'd b. Khaythama, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, and Jabir b. 'Abd Allah.”"],[4603,"From his father: “In naming those who witnessed with 'Ali: Zayd b. Aslam, from the Ansar, a Badri.”"],[4604,"“And among those killed on the day of Hunayn from the Muslims, from Quraysh, then from Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Zayd b. Rabi'a.”"],[4605,"From 'Urwa: “In naming those killed on the day of al-Yamama from the Muslims: Zayd b. Ruqaysh, an ally of Banu Umayya.”"],[4606,"From ʿUrwa: “In the naming of those who were killed on the Day of the Bridge, the Bridge of al-Madāʾin, with Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Najjār: Zayd b. Surāqa b. Kaʿb.”"],[4607,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Zayd b. al-Muzayyan.”"],[4608,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAwf b. al-Khazraj, from Balḥublā: Zayd b. Wadīʿa b. ʿAmr b. Qays.”"],[4609,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of al-Yamāma from Quraysh, then from Banū Zuhra: Zayd b. Usayd b. Jāriya.”"],[4610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[4611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not leave anything for another thing among the prayers until he used the toothstick."],[4612,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade plundering and mutilation."],[4613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not make your houses graves, and pray in them.\""],[4614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever shelters a stray, he remains a stray as long as he doesn't identify it.\""],[4615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out intending Makkah until when he was in part of Wadi al-Rawha, the people found a wounded wild donkey. They mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Leave it until its owner comes.\" Al-Bahzi, who was its owner, came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this donkey is yours to deal with.\" He ordered Abu Bakr to distribute it among the traveling groups, and they were in ihram. Then we passed on until when we were at al-Uthaya, there was a gazelle standing in the shade with an arrow in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to stand by it until he informed the people about it."],[4616,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge be taken away while we recite the Qur’an, teach it to our sons, our women, and our slaves?” He said: “By Allah, I used to consider you, O Ziyad, among the jurists of the Muslims. Do you not know that the Torah and the Gospel were sent down to the Jews and the Christians, so what did it benefit them when they did not act upon it?”"],[4617,"He came to Madinah with a camel of his loaded with food, and the Prophet ﷺ met him and said: “O Bedouin, what are you carrying?” I said: “I am preparing wheat.” He said to me: “What do you want?” I said: “I want to sell it.” Then he wiped my head and said: “Be fair in trading with the Bedouin.”"],[4618,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Saʿida b. Kaʿb b. al-Khazraj: Ziyad b. ʿAmr al-Juhani, an ally of theirs.”"],[4619,"From Abu al-Yasar b. ʿAmr and Ziyad b. al-Fard that they both heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to ʿAmmar: “The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[4620,"That when the delegation of Hawazin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah, having already embraced Islam, they said: 'We are a root and a clan, and affliction has befallen us that is not hidden from you. So bestow upon us as Allah has bestowed upon you.' A man from Hawazin stood up, then one of Banu Sa'd b. Bakr called Zuhayr, whose kunya was Abu Surad, and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, our women are your paternal aunts, your maternal aunts, and your wet-nurses who took care of you. If we had joined al-Harith b. Abi Shimr and al-Nu'man b. al-Mundhir, and then there befell us from him what you have brought upon us, we would have hoped for his sympathy and kindness toward us. And you are the best of those who were taken care of.' Then he recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poetry he had composed, mentioning their kinship and what they had done in caring for him. He said:"],[4621,"From Qabisah b. Mukhariq al-Hilali and Zuhayr b. Amr, they said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: {And warn your closest kindred}, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ went to a pile of rocks on a mountain and climbed to the top of it, on a rock, then said: 'O Banu Abd Manaf, I am a warner to you. My likeness and yours is like a man who saw the enemy and went to alert his family, fearing that they would reach his family before him, so he began shouting: \"O morning! O morning! You have been attacked! You have been attacked!\"'"],[4622,"He was called Ma'ruf; if his name was not Zuhayr b. Uthman, I do not know what it was. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The walimah on the first day is a right, the second is a kindness, and the third is showing off and ostentation.'"],[4623,"A woman from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a son of hers who had died, and it was as if the people had rebuked her. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, two of my children have died since I entered Islam, besides this one.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah, you have shielded yourself from the Fire with a strong shielding.'"],[4624,"A man of shabby appearance came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Do you have wealth?' He said: 'Yes, of all kinds of wealth.' He said: 'Then let it be seen on you, for Allah ﷻ loves to see the traces of His blessing on His servant in a good way, and He does not love misery or feigning misery.' Zuhayr b. Mu'awiyah al-Jushami: he is not included in the authentic collections."],[4625,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ and Zuhayr b. Umayyah came and asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and they praised me in his presence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I know him better than you two; he was my partner in the Jahiliyyah.'"],[4626,"Her grandfather al-Zari' set out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and took with him a son of his, or a son of his sister, who was insane. My grandfather said: When we arrived in Madinah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have with me a son of mine, or a son of my sister, who is insane; I have brought him to you so that you may supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for him. He said: 'Bring him to me.' So I went with him to the Prophet while he was still on the riding camel, and I untied him, removed his travel clothes, and dressed him in two fine garments. I took him by the hand until I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Bring him close to me, and place his back facing me.' He then took hold of the gathers of his garment from its top and bottom and began striking his back until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, while saying: 'Come out, enemy of Allah! Come out, enemy of Allah!' Then he began looking with the gaze of a healthy person, not his previous gaze. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then seated him in front of him, called for water, wiped his face, and supplicated for him. After the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, there was none in the delegation who surpassed him."],[4627,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ: 'The Prophet ﷺ wrote to al-Dahhak b. Sufyan instructing him to give inheritance to the wife of Ashaym al-Dibabi from the blood-money of her husband.'"],[4628,"From the Prophet ﷺ: {Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, all things We created with predestination.} He said: 'It was revealed concerning some people of my community in the last days who deny the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[4629,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone says: \"I ask pardon of Allah than Whom there is no deity, the Living, the eternal, and I turn to Him in repentance,\" he will be pardoned, even if he has fled in time of battle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1517)"],[4630,"Ibn Lahīʿah said: Sahl b. Zayd is the correct name in the list of those who attended al-ʿAqabah, and he said so correctly in the list of those who attended Badr."],[4631,"From Ibn Shihāb in the list of those who attended al-ʿAqabah from the Ansar: Abū Ṭalḥah Zayd b. Sahl from Banū al-Najjār, and he attended Badr."],[4632,"From ʿUrwah in the list of those who attended al-ʿAqabah from the Ansar, then from Banū ʿAdiyy b. ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Najjār b. Aws: Abū Ṭalḥah, whose name is Zayd b. Sahl b. al-Aswad b. Ḥarām b. ʿAmr b. Zayd Manāt b. ʿAdiyy b. ʿAmr b. Mālik."],[4633,"\"Abū Ṭalḥah Zayd b. Sahl b. al-Aswad b. Ḥarām b. ʿAmr b. Zayd Manāt b. ʿAdiyy b. ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Najjār.\""],[4634,"Some of his children told me."],[4635,"Abu Talha proposed to Umm Sulaym before he embraced Islam. She said, \"Indeed I desire you, and the like of you is not rejected, but you are a disbelieving man and I am a Muslim woman. If you embrace Islam, that will be my dowry; I will not ask you for anything else.\" So Abu Talha embraced Islam and married her."],[4636,"Abu Talha married Umm Sulaym, and the dowry between them was Islam. Umm Sulaym embraced Islam before Abu Talha, so he proposed to her. She said, \"I have embraced Islam; if you embrace Islam, I will marry you.\" So he embraced Islam, and the dowry between them was Islam."],[4637,"\"Umm Sulaym married Abu Talha on the basis of his Islam.\""],[4638,"Abu Talha al-Ansari set up a mosque in his house and sent for the Prophet ﷺ. \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with me and Abu Talha, while Umm Sulaym was behind us.\""],[4639,"\"Abu Talha did not fast during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because of military expeditions. When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, I did not see him break his fast except on the Day of Sacrifice or the Day of Breaking the Fast.\""],[4640,"\"Abu Talha fasted continuously after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he died.\""],[4641,"Anas reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ established fraternity between Abu Ubaida b. Jarrah and Abu Talha. (Using translation from Muslim 2528)"],[4642,"\"Abu Talha went out on a military expedition by sea and died on the ship. They could not find a place on land to bury him, so they waited with him for six days, until after seven they found a place to bury him, and he had not changed from how he was.\" As for those who said he died in Madinah…"],[4643,"\"Abu Talha died in the year 34, and Uthman b. Affan ﷺ ؓ prayed over him, in the year 70. His name was Zayd b. Sahl.\""],[4644,"Abu Talha Zayd b. Sahl died in the year 34, and Uthman b. Affan prayed over him. He died at the age of seventy. It has also been said that Abu Talha died in the year 32."],[4645,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images of statues.\""],[4646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4647,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4648,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And 'Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us. They said: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4649,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4650,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4651,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4652,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[4653,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and 'Umrah.\""],[4654,"Abu Khalid al-Ahmar and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us. And al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: 'Uthman b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hasan b. Sa'd, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Abu Talhah narrated to me: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and 'Umrah.\""],[4655,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a statue.\""],[4656,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.\""],[4657,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a statue.\""],[4658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.\""],[4659,"\"I was among those upon whom drowsiness was poured on the day of Uhud.\""],[4660,"\"And the sword would fall from his hand, so he would grab it and it would fall from my hand, then I would grab it from sleepiness.\""],[4661,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered some thirty-some men of the leading figures of Quraysh, and they were thrown into a well from the wells of Badr, where they had stank. When he gained victory over a people, he would stay at the open area for three days. When it was the third day, he ordered his riding camel, saddled it, then walked and his companions followed him. They said, \"We only see him going for some need of his.\" Then he came to the edge of the well and said, \"O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so son of so-and-so! You wished that you had obeyed God and His Messenger. Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For we have found what our Lord promised us to be true.\" Umar said, \"O Messenger of God, do you speak to bodies in which there are no souls?\" He said, \"By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, you are not more hearing of what I say than they are.\" Sa'id said: Qatadah said, \"God, by God, brought them to life so that they heard his words.\""],[4662,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ defeated a people, he loved to stay at their open area for three days or three nights."],[4663,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came upon Khaybar in the morning, he recited this verse: \"Indeed, when we descend upon the open area of a people, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.\""],[4664,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came upon Khaybar in the morning, they had taken their hoes and baskets and gone out to their fields. When they saw the Prophet of God ﷺ with the army, they retreated, turning back. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is greatest! God is greatest! God is greatest! Khaybar is ruined! Indeed, when we descend upon the open area of a people, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.\""],[4665,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ. If I said that my knee touched his knee, he remained silent about them until when it was near dawn, and the owner of the milch animal had gone to his milch animal and the owner of the farm to his farm, he raided them and said, \"Indeed, when we descend upon the open area of a people, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.\""],[4666,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say in his talbiyah, \"Labbayk for a Hajj and an Umrah together.\""],[4667,"I observed the Prophet ﷺ and his companions on the day of Uhud, and I did not see anyone except that he was nodding off under his shield from drowsiness."],[4668,"\"I was among those overwhelmed by drowsiness on the day of Sunday.\""],[4669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"May God reward you well, O company of the Ansar, for you are, as far as I know, chaste and patient.\""],[4670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Convey peace to your people, for they are, as far as I know, chaste and patient.\""],[4671,"It was said to Matar while I was with him, from whom did al-Hasan take [the ruling] \"Ablution is required from what the fire has touched\"? He said, \"He took it from Anas, and Anas took it from Abu Talhah, and Abu Talhah took it from the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4672,"He bought wine for orphans. When wine was forbidden, he said, \"O Messenger of God, should I make it into vinegar?\" He said, \"No.\""],[4673,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I bought wine for orphans under my care.\" He said, \"Spill the wine and break the jars.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, it belongs to orphans.\" He said, \"Spill the wine and break the jars.\""],[4674,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the two mixtures."],[4675,"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade al-aqrān."],[4676,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever sends one blessing upon me, God sends ten blessings upon him.”"],[4677,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him pleasant in spirit and cheerful of countenance. I said: O Messenger of God, I have never seen you more pleasant in spirit than today. He said: “And what would prevent me, when the angel has informed me that whoever sends blessings upon you, I and My angels send ten blessings upon him, and whoever greets you with peace, I and My angels greet him with peace ten times.”"],[4678,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw from his cheerfulness and openness something I had never seen in such a state before. I said: O Messenger of God, I have never seen you in such a state before. He said: “And what would prevent me, O Abu Talhah, when Jibril ﷺ just left me, bringing me good news from my Lord. He said: God sent me to you to give you good news that there is no one among your community who sends a blessing upon you except that God and His angels send ten blessings upon him for it.”"],[4679,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and the features of his face were shining. I said: O Messenger of God, I have never seen you more pleasant in spirit or more cheerful of countenance than on this day of yours. He said: “And why should my spirit not be pleasant and my countenance not be cheerful when Jibril ﷺ has just left me this hour? He said: O Muhammad, whoever sends a blessing upon you from your community, God records for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and raises him by it ten degrees, and the angel says to him the like of what he said to you. I said: O Jibril, and what angel is that? He said: God ﷻ has appointed an angel over you from the time He created you until He resurrects you; no one from your community sends a blessing upon you except that he says: And may God send blessings upon you.”"],[4680,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while his face was radiant and he was rejoicing. I said: O Messenger of God, you are in a state the like of which I have never seen you. He said: “And what would prevent me? Jibril ﷺ came to me just now and said: Give good news to your community that whoever sends a blessing upon you, ten good deeds are recorded for him, ten evil deeds are erased for him, he is raised ten degrees, God returns to him the like of what he said, and it is presented to him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[4681,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and a man was offering prayer. He then made supplication: O Allah, I ask Thee by virtue of the fact that praise is due to Thee, there is no deity but Thou, Who showest favour and beneficence, the Originator of the Heavens and the earth, O Lord of Majesty and Splendour, O Living One, O Eternal One. The Prophet ﷺ then said: He has supplicated Allah using His Greatest Name, when supplicated by this name, He answers, and when asked by this name He gives. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1495)"],[4682,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Charity to the poor is charity, and to a relative it is charity and maintaining kinship ties.”"],[4683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came one day with joy visible on his face. It was said: O Messenger of God, we see on your face a joy we have not seen before. He said: “An angel came to me and said: Your Lord says to you: Are you not pleased, or does it not please you, that no one from your community sends a blessing upon you except that I send ten blessings upon him, and no one greets you with peace except that I greet him with peace ten times? I said: Yes.”"],[4684,"We were sitting in the courtyards, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by us and said: “What is with you and sitting on the elevated paths?” We said: O Messenger of God, we sat to converse and remember God. He said: “Then give the gatherings their due.” We said: O Messenger of God, and what is their due? He said: “Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, guiding to the path, and good speech.”"],[4685,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ghusl and washes himself, goes early and arrives early, draws near to the imam, listens attentively, and does not engage in idle talk on Friday, God records for him for every step he takes to the mosque the reward of fasting a year and standing in prayer for it.”"],[4686,"That Abu Talhah invited the Messenger of God ﷺ for Umayr b. Talhah when he died. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and prayed over him in his house. The Messenger of God ﷺ advanced, Abu Talhah was behind him, and Umm Sulaym—there was no one else with them."],[4687,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Perform ablution from that which the fire has touched.”"],[4688,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Perform ablution from that which the fire has touched.”"],[4689,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Abū al-Naḍr, the freed slave of ʿUmar b. ʿUbayd Allāh, from ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd, that he entered upon Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī to visit him. He said: We found Sahl b. Ḥunayf with him. He said: Abū Ṭalḥah called a person, and he removed a coverlet that was beneath him. Sahl b. Ḥunayf said to him, “Why do you remove it?” He said, “Because it contains images, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about them what you know.” Sahl said, “Did he not say, ‘Except what is embroidery in a cloth’?” He said, “Yes, but it is more pleasing to myself.”"],[4690,"“You heard the Prophet ﷺ forbidding images except embroidery in a cloth, or a cloth in which there is embroidery?” He said, “Yes, but I dislike it,” so he removed it."],[4691,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed two horned rams with white and black markings. He said over the first, “On behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,” and he said over the second, “On behalf of those of my ummah who believe in me and affirm me.”"],[4692,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr saying: “Zayd b. Thābit b. al-Ḍaḥḥāk.”"],[4693,"“I have been seeking this evil creature whose killing Allah records as a good deed and by which He erases a bad deed, and it is the gecko.”"],[4694,"to Zayd b. Thābit: “O Abū Saʿīd.”"],[4695,"They said to Zayd b. Thabit, “O Abu Sa’id.”"],[4696,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. Numayr say, “Zayd b. Thabit is given the kunya Abu Sa'id.”"],[4697,"“The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah when I was eleven years old.”"],[4698,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed me to take part on the Day of the Trench and clothed me in a qibtiyyah garment.”"],[4699,"'Uthman: “Which of the people should I have write?” They said, “Zayd b. Thabit.”"],[4700,"'Uthman, may Allah have mercy on him: “Summon Zayd b. Thabit for me, the scribe of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[4701,"Ibn 'Abbas: “Thus we do with the senior scholars.”"],[4702,"“The scholars after Mu'adh b. Jabal were 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, Abu al-Darda', Salman, and 'Abdullah b. Salam. And the scholars after these were Zayd b. Thabit. Then after Zayd were Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas.”"],[4703,"“The Prophet ﷺ employed 'Abdullah b. al-Arqam as a scribe, and he used to write to the kings. Such was his trustworthiness with him that he would write to one of the kings, then he would order him to fold it and seal it without reading it, due to his trustworthiness with him. He also employed Zayd b. Thabit as a scribe, and he used to write down the revelation and also write to the kings. When 'Abdullah b. al-Arqam and Zayd b. Thabit were absent and he needed to write to one of the commanders of the armies and the kings, or to write a document for a person granting him a share, he would order whoever was present to write. Those who wrote for him included 'Umar b. al-Khattab, 'Uthman b. 'Affan, 'Ali b. Abi Talib, Zayd b. Thabit, al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, Khalid b. Sa'id b. al-'As ؓ, and others among the Arabs who have been named.”"],[4704,"“A great deal of knowledge was buried today.”"],[4705,"“That he appoint someone from Ibn 'Abbas as his successor.”"],[4706,"“That he knows how knowledge departs; for thus does knowledge depart. By Allah, a great deal of knowledge departed today.” Sa'id b. al-Musayyib said, “The one who said, ‘A great deal of knowledge departed with him,’ meaning Ibn 'Abbas.”"],[4707,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: “Zayd b. Thabit died in the year forty-five, and Kharijah b. Zayd b. Thabit died in the year ninety-nine.”"],[4708,"Because the Messenger of God ﷺ deemed him fit for service on the Day of the Trench when he was fifteen years old, and the Trench was in Shawwal of the year four; and there is disagreement about his death."],[4709,"Zayd b. Thabit died in the year fifty-one.”"],[4710,"“Zayd b. Thabit died in the year fifty-five.”"],[4711,"“The Prophet ﷺ prohibited muzabanah.”"],[4712,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us; and Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us; and Ubayd b. Ghannam narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah narrated to us. They said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd b. Thabit: “The Prophet ﷺ allowed the sale of araya.”"],[4713,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed the sale of araya to be sold for their estimated amount of dry dates, and he did not allow anything other than that.”"],[4714,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed the sale of araya for dry dates and fresh dates, and he did not allow anything other than that.”"],[4715,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed the sale of araya by measure according to their estimated amount of dry dates.”"],[4716,"“The Prophet of God ﷺ allowed the sale of araya for fresh dates or dry dates, and he did not allow anything other than that.”"],[4717,"He informed him that “the Messenger of God ﷺ allowed the sale of araya for fresh dates and dry dates, and he did not allow anything other than that.”"],[4718,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed araya to be sold for their estimated amount of dry dates.”"],[4719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding 'arāyā: that they may be sold by estimating their quantity in dates."],[4720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā by estimating their quantity in dates."],[4721,"The Prophet ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of al-'ariyya: the household may take it by its estimated quantity and eat it as fresh dates."],[4722,"Al-Qa'nabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Nāfi', from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd b. Thābit: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to the owner of al-'ariyya to sell it by its estimated quantity, measured out."],[4723,"And Abū Muslim al-Kashshī and Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān b. Ḥarb narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfi', from Ibn ʿUmar: Zayd b. Thābit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā by estimating their quantity."],[4724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā."],[4725,"Zayd b. Thābit: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā: the palm tree or two palm trees that are given to a man, so he sells them by their estimated quantity in dates."],[4726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā by their measured quantity."],[4727,"Al-Qa'nabī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿUmar narrated to us, from Nāfi', from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd b. Thābit: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā by their estimated quantity, measured out."],[4728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā: that they may be sold by their estimated quantity, measured out."],[4729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā: that they may be sold by their estimated quantity, measured out."],[4730,"From Zaid bin Thabit that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted selling in Al-'Araya by estimating it. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1302)"],[4731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of 'arāyā by estimating their quantity."],[4732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted the sale of 'arāyā [unpicked dates] by estimating their amount as dry dates."],[4733,"The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted the owner of an 'ariyya to sell it by estimating its amount."],[4734,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade muḥāqala and muzābana."],[4735,"Do not sell it until you have taken possession of it in your house, for the Prophet of God ﷺ forbade the sale of that."],[4736,"I bought oil from the market, and when I had received it in full, a man met me and offered me a good profit for it. I wanted to strike my hand on his hand [to conclude the sale], but a man behind me took hold of my arm. I turned and it was Zayd b. Thābit. He said: Do not sell it where you bought it until you have taken possession of it at your camel saddle, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling goods where they are bought until the merchants have taken possession of them at their saddles."],[4737,"Do not sell it until you have moved it to your camel saddle, for the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that."],[4738,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in a garden belonging to the Banū al-Najjār, mounted on a mule of his and we were with him, he said: 'Seek refuge with God from the punishment of the grave. Seek refuge with God from the punishment of the Fire.' We said: We seek refuge with God from the punishment of the grave; we seek refuge with God from the punishment of the Fire. He said: 'Seek refuge with God from trials, both apparent and hidden.' We said: We seek refuge with God from trials, both apparent and hidden. He said: 'Seek refuge with God from the trial of the Dajjāl.' They said: We seek refuge with God from the trial of the Dajjāl."],[4739,"Abū Sa'īd al-Khudrī ؓ said: When the Prophet ﷺ died, the orators of the Anṣār stood up and said: O assembly of the Muhājirūn, the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he sent one of you, he paired him with one of us. So we think that this matter should be undertaken by two men: one from you and one from us. Then Zayd b. Thābit stood and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was from the Muhājirūn, and we were the supporters of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so we will be the supporters of whoever takes his place. Abū Bakr ؓ said: May God reward you with good, O assembly of the Anṣār, and may He make firm the one who spoke among you. By God, if you had said otherwise, we would not have made peace with you."],[4740,"They would wait until it ripened, then they would dispute before the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'If you do this, do not trade until its ripeness becomes apparent.'"],[4741,"The Prophet ﷺ looked toward Yemen and said: 'O God, turn their hearts [to You] and bless us in our ṣā' and our mudd.'"],[4742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked toward Yemen and said, “O Allah, turn their hearts.” He looked toward Iraq and said, “O Allah, turn their hearts.” He looked toward Syria and said, “O Allah, turn their hearts and bless us in our ṣāʿ and our mudd.”"],[4743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for his ummah and said, “O Allah, turn their hearts to Your religion, and remove what is behind them by Your mercy.” He did not mention Zayd b. Thābit."],[4744,"“We took suḥūr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we went out to the prayer.” I said, “How much time was there between the adhān, the iqāmah, and the suḥūr?” He said, “The amount of fifty verses.”"],[4745,"“We took suḥūr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we went out to the prayer.” I said, “How much time was there between the adhān and the iqāmah?” He said, “The amount of fifty verses.”"],[4746,"“We took suḥūr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we went out and prayed.”"],[4747,"“We took suḥūr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we did not get up until he had prayed the morning prayer.” I said, “What was the extent of that?” He said, “The amount that a person recites fifty verses.”"],[4748,"“Do you know why I walked with you in this manner?” I said, “No.” He said, “So that our steps increase in walking to the prayer.” Al-Sariyy b. Yaḥyā did not raise it to the Prophet."],[4749,"When he was on level ground, he walked with me, then he shortened his steps until I entered the mosque. He said, “Do you know, O Thābit, why I walked with you in this manner until I entered the mosque? The Prophet ﷺ walked with me in this manner and said, ‘Do you know why I walked with you in this manner?’ I said, ‘Allah and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘So that the number of steps increases in seeking the prayer.’”"],[4750,"The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, and I was with him. He shortened his steps and said, “I did this only so that the number of my steps increases in seeking the prayer.”"],[4751,"I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were heading to the prayer, and he was shortening his steps. He said, “Do you know why I shorten my steps?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The servant remains in prayer as long as he is seeking the prayer.”"],[4752,"“Do you know why I walked with you in this manner?” I said, “No.” He said, “I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he shortened his steps, then he said, ‘Do you know why I walked with you in this manner?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘So that our steps increase in walking to the prayer.’”"],[4753,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Allah remains in the servant’s need as long as the servant is in his brother’s need.”"],[4754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him this supplication and commanded him to learn it and recite it daily, saying in the morning: \"Labbaik Allahumma labbaik wa sa'daik wa al-khayr fi yadayk, wa minka wa bika wa ilaik Allahumma ma qultu min qawl aw halaf tu min halaf aw nadartu min nadar, fa ma shi'ta bayna yadayhi ma shi'ta kana wa ma lam tashaa lam yakun, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa bika innaka 'ala kulli shay'in qadeer. Allahumma ma sallaytu min salatin fa 'ala man sallayta, wa ma la'antu min lanatan fa 'ala man la'anta, innaka waliyyun fi al-dunya wa al-akhirah, tawaffani musliman wa alhiqni bi al-saliheen. Allahumma inni as'aluka al-rida ba'da al-qada', wa bard al-'aysh ba'da al-mawt, wa ladhat al-nathar fi wajhik al-karim, wa shawqan ila liqa'ik min ghayr zarra'a mudhira, wa la fitnah mudillah. A'oodhu bika Allahumma an adhlima aw udhlama aw a'tadiya aw yu'tada 'alayya aw uksiba khati'atan mukhti'atan aw dhamban la yughfar. Allahumma Fatir al-samawat wa al-ardh, 'alim al-ghayb wa al-shahadah, dha al-jalal wa al-ikram. Fa inni ahdhu ilayka fi hadhihi al-hayat al-dunya, wa ushkuduka wa kafa bika shahidan, inni ashhadu anna la ilaha illa Allah, wahdahu la sharika lah, lahu al-mulk wa lahu al-hamd, wa anta 'ala kulli shay'in qadeer. Wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduka wa rasuluh, wa ashhadu anna wa'adaka haqqun wa liqa'aka haqqun, wa al-sa'ah atiya la rayba fiha, wa innaka tab'athu man fi al-qubur. Wa ashhadu annaka in takilni ila nafsi, takilni ila da'f wa 'awrata wa dhanb wa khalal wa khati'ah, wa inni la athiqu illa bi rahmatika wa ighfir li dhambiy kullahu, innahu la yaghfir al-dhunub illa anta, wa tub 'alayya innaka anta al-tawwab al-rahim.\""],[4755,"I heard Zayd b. Thabit say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Uhud, some people turned back from the road. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ split into two groups concerning them: one group said, “Accept them,” and another group said, “Do not accept them.” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {So what is the matter with you that you are two factions concerning the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned}."],[4756,"The hypocrites and the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ were in a house. One group said, “We wish they would come out to us so we could fight them,” and another group disliked that, until their voices rose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said to Zayd, “Write it down”: {So what is the matter with you that you are two factions concerning the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned}."],[4757,"“O Commander of the Faithful, my son was born on my bed, then he rejected me and claimed affiliation to his master and my master.” ʿUmar said to Zayd b. Thabit: “Do you not know that we used to recite, ‘Do not reject your fathers, for that is disbelief on your part’?” Zayd said, “Yes.” ʿUmar said to him: “Go and tie your son to your camel, then set off and strike your camel with a whip and your son with a whip until you bring him to your family.”"],[4758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the Dhuhr prayer in Al-Hajirah while people were in their houses and markets. They did not pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except in rows. Then Allah ﷻ revealed, \"Guard strictly the (five obligatory) prayers, especially the middle prayer and stand before Allah with obedience.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let those who neglect their prayers or delay them (beyond their appointed times) beware, lest I burn their houses.\""],[4759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? Increase in saying: There is no might and no power except with Allah.”"],[4760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fruits until they are free from blight."],[4761,"He informed him, saying: Zayd b. Thabit said to me, “Why do you recite in the Maghrib prayer from the short mufassal surahs, when the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Maghrib prayer the longer of the two long ones?” I said to ʿUrwah, “And what are the two long ones?” He said, “Al-Aʿraf.”"],[4762,"Zayd b. Thabit said to me, “Why do I see you reciting in the prayer from the short mufassal surahs? I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the two long ones.” I said, “And what are the two long ones?” He said, “Al-Aʿraf and Yunus.”"],[4763,"Zayd b. Thabit said: “I swear that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the longest of the two long ones.”"],[4764,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated to him: {Not equal are those who sit} {and the mujahidin}. Ibn Umm Maktum said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, if I were able to go on jihad, I would.” Then Allah ﷻ revealed upon him, while his thigh was on my thigh, and his thigh became heavy on me until my thigh was about to be crushed. Then it was relieved from him, and he said: {except the disabled}."],[4765,"From Sahl b. Saʿd al-Saʿidi, the Companion of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, from Marwan b. al-Hakam, from Zayd b. Thabit, who said: I was sitting next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my thigh under his thigh, while he was dictating to me: {Not equal are those who sit among the believers} {and the mujahidin in the way of Allah with their wealth and their lives}. Ibn Umm Maktum was sitting and listening, and he said, “By Allah, if I were able to go on jihad, I would, O Prophet of Allah.” Then Allah revealed Quran to His Messenger ﷺ concerning him, and his thigh became heavy on my thigh until I thought it would crush it. Then it was relieved from him, and he said: {Not equal are those who sit among the believers, except the disabled}."],[4766,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated to him: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]} {and those who strive in the cause of Allah}. Then Ibn Umm Maktum came to him while he was dictating it to me, and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, if I were able to go forth in jihad, I would.\" He was a blind man. Then Allah ﷻ revealed to His Messenger, while his thigh was on my thigh, and it became so heavy upon me that I thought it would crush my thigh. Then it was relieved from him, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {other than those who have a disability}."],[4767,"I suffered from insomnia at night, so I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Say: O Allah, the stars have set, the eyes have become still, and You are Ever-Living, Self-Sustaining. O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining, grant rest to my eye and calm my night.\" I said it, and it went away from me."],[4768,"\"Bilal calls the Adhan during the night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls (the Adhan)\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 637)"],[4769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer.\""],[4770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not sell fruit until its ripeness is evident.\""],[4771,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray at the midday heat, or he said at the hottest time of day, and it was the most difficult prayer for his companions. Then it was revealed: {Guard strictly the prayers, especially the middle prayer, and stand before Allah devoutly obedient.} He said: \"Because before it are two prayers and after it are two prayers.\""],[4772,"May Allah forgive Rafi' b. Khadij. By Allah, I knew the hadith better than he did. Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ who had fought each other, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If this is your affair, then do not lease farmland.\" Rafi' heard his saying \"do not lease farmland.\" The wording is from the hadith of Musaddad."],[4773,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prayed two units of prayer at Al-Maghrib (sunset) in Al-A'raf.\""],[4774,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs of Maghrib Surat al-Anfal."],[4775,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lead us in Maghrib prayer with al-Ma'idah until he reached its end."],[4776,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"None of the fruit may be sold until its ripeness is evident, which is when the red or yellow color becomes distinct.\""],[4777,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Maghrib the longer of the two long surahs."],[4778,"Zayd b. Thabit said: \"The mosque founded on piety is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" 'Urwah said: \"The mosque of the Prophet ﷺ is better than it. It was only revealed concerning the mosque of Quba'.\""],[4779,"I recited Surat al-Najm to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not prostrate."],[4780,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Yunus b. Yusuf, from 'Ata' b. Yasar, from Zayd b. Thabit al-Ansari, \"that he found some boys who had cornered a fox, so he drove them away from it.\" And Malik said: \"I do not know but that he said: 'In the sanctuary of the Messenger of God ﷺ this is done.'\""],[4781,"\"A wolf bit into a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sharp stone (marwah), and the Prophet ﷺ permitted eating it.\""],[4782,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has changed.\""],[4783,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4784,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4785,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4786,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4787,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4788,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4789,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4790,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\" Abu al-Qasim said: \"Ma'mar did not mention 'Abd al-Malik b. Abi Bakr.\""],[4791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[4792,"Zayd said: When we were writing the mushafs, I missed a verse that I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I found it with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari: {Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah. Some of them have fulfilled their vow, and some are still waiting, and they have not changed in the least.} He said, \"Khuzaymah was called Dhu al-Shahadatayn (the one of two testimonies).\""],[4793,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting it, so I searched for it and found it with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari: {Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah.} I then appended it in its surah in the mushaf."],[4794,"On the day of the Battle of Yamamah, many people who used to recite the Quran were killed. It was mentioned that about four hundred people were killed. So, I went to Abu Bakr and said to him, \"If there is another calamity where the Quran might be lost, what do you think we should do?\" Abu Bakr said, \"I am not going to change anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.\" So, he sent a message to Umar ibn Al-Khattab and he said the same thing, \"We will not change anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did.\" Zaid ibn Thabit said, \"Then what should we do?\" They both agreed that I was right, and Abu Bakr wrote it down on parchments and pieces of bones."],[4795,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Do not sell fruit until the Pleiades rises and its goodness becomes apparent.\""],[4796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not sell fruits until the Pleiades rises.\""],[4797,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not sell fruit until its goodness becomes apparent.\""],[4798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of araya for dates and ripe dates."],[4799,"He used to say when lying down, \"O Allah, I ask You for the sufficiency of family and kinsfolk, and I seek refuge with You from a womb (kinship) that I have severed calling against me.\""],[4800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of araya for dates and ripe dates."],[4801,"The sakinah (tranquility) overwhelmed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Zayd said, \"I was beside him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell upon my thigh. I did not find anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then it was lifted from him, and he said, 'Write.' So I wrote: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]} and {the mujahidun in the cause of Allah with their wealth and their lives} — all of the verses. He said, 'I wrote that on a shoulder blade.' Then Ibn Umm Maktum stood up — and he was a blind man — when he heard the virtue of the mujahidun over those who sit, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the believers who cannot fight?' He had hardly finished his words — or he said, except that he was counting his words — when the sakinah overwhelmed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his thigh fell upon my thigh. I felt the same heaviness from it the second time as I had felt the first time. Then it was lifted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Read.' So I read: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]}. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: {except those who are disabled}. Zayd said, 'I appended it, and it is as if I am looking at its insertion at a crack in the shoulder blade.'"],[4802,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when the sakinah overwhelmed him — or it descended — and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell upon my thigh. I did not see anything that pressed down heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was taken from him — or lifted from him — he said, 'Read.' I read. He said, 'Write: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]} and {the mujahidun in the cause of Allah}.' Then Amr b. Umm Maktum, the blind man, said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my eyes have a disability.' Then the sakinah overwhelmed him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell upon my thigh. I never found anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was taken from him — or lifted from him — he said, 'Read.' I read. He said, 'Write: {except those who are disabled}.' I never forgot its insertion at a crack in the shoulder blade."],[4803,"The mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the mosque founded on piety: \"It is this mosque of mine.\""],[4805,"\"Recitation is a Sunnah.\" Ibn Abi Maryam added: \"Do not oppose the people with your opinion.\""],[4806,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to learn the script of the Jews.\" He said: \"I would write for him, write to them, and read for him when they wrote.\""],[4807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to learn the script of the Jews, and not half a month passed before I became skilled at it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I do not trust the Jews with my letters.\" When I learned it, I would write for him."],[4808,"\"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah when I was eleven years old.\""],[4809,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession in the sale of 'araya: that they may be sold by measure according to their estimated quantity.\""],[4810,"About the inheritance of the grandfather and brothers, and that kalalah and much of what is adjudicated in these inheritances—none knows its full extent except Allah. We used to attend matters of that sort before the caliphs after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we retained of them as much as we wished to retain, and with it we still give rulings to whoever asks us about inheritances."],[4811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in the city while they were trading fruits before they ripened. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard noise and loud voices from the people, so he asked, \"What is this?\" They replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, these are people who are trading fruits in the palm trees and then they mention that they have encountered corruption afterward.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"So do not conduct transactions until they ripen.\""],[4812,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed a ritual bath for his ihram when he entered ihram.\""],[4813,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, the Banu al-Najjar came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, among us is a boy who has recited from what has been revealed to you over ten surahs.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me, and I recited to him."],[4814,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the boundaries are fixed, there is no preemption.\""],[4815,"He used to keep vigil on the twenty-third night of Ramadan and the twenty-seventh night, but not like his vigil on the seventeenth night. It was said to him: \"How do you single out the seventeenth night?\" He said: \"In it the Quran was sent down, on its morning the truth was distinguished from falsehood, and in it one rises with a radiant face.\""],[4816,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"War is deception.\""],[4817,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted two shares for a horse and one share for a man."],[4818,"This verse, which is in Surah An-Nisa' (Chapter 4) {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell to abide therein, and the wrath and the curse of Allah are upon him, and a great punishment is prepared for him}, was revealed after the verses in Surah Al-Furqan (Chapter 25) {And those who do not invoke with Allah another deity or kill the soul which Allah has forbidden [to be killed], except by right, and do not commit unlawful sexual intercourse. And whoever should do that will meet a penalty}. Six months apart."],[4819,"When this verse in al-Furqan was revealed: “And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right,” we marveled at its leniency. We waited seven months, then the verse in al-Nisa’ was revealed: “And whoever kills a believer deliberately, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah’s wrath is upon him and He has cursed him,” until the end."],[4820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade blowing during prostration and blowing into a drink."],[4821,"Zayd refused, so Marwan seated a scribe for him behind the canopy, and he began questioning Zayd while the scribe wrote down what Zayd narrated. He said: O Abu Sa‘id, I think we have succeeded in what you refused. He said: By Allah, I will not throw it away until it is brought to me. So he brought the writing and tore it up, and said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from writing down his hadith.”"],[4822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this wealth is sweet and green.”"],[4823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this wealth is sweet and green.”"],[4824,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed this wealth is sweet and green.”"],[4825,"About a man who raids, sells, buys, and trades during his campaign? My father said to him: “We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Tabuk, buying and selling while he saw us, and he did not forbid us.”"],[4826,"“The day of Ashura’ is not the day that people speak of. It was only the day on which the Kaaba used to be covered and the Abyssinians used to play in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it used to rotate through the year. People used to go to such-and-such a Jew and ask him. When the Jew died, they came to Zayd b. Thabit and asked him.”"],[4827,"Umm al-‘Ala’ said: Be at ease, Abu al-Sa’ib, for you are in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard her and said: “Who is this?” She said: I, O Prophet of Allah. He said: “And how do you know?” She said: O Messenger of Allah, ‘Uthman b. Maz‘un. He said: “Yes, we have seen nothing but good. I am the Messenger of Allah, and by Allah I do not know what will be done with me.”"],[4828,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is forbidden.\""],[4829,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? [It is] 'There is no might nor power except with God.'\""],[4830,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\" They said: \"Yes, indeed.\" He said: \"'There is no might nor power except with God.'\""],[4831,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would lengthen the recitation in the Zuhr and Asr prayers and move his lips, and I knew that he only moved his lips for recitation."],[4832,"Zayd b. Thabit said: One morning we went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ until we were at a crossroads in Madinah. We saw a Bedouin who had taken hold of the halter of his camel until he stopped before the Prophet ﷺ while we were around him. He said: \"Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings.\" The Prophet ﷺ returned the greeting, then said: \"How have you entered the morning?\" The camel then grumbled, and a man who looked like a guard came. The guard said: \"O Messenger of God, this Bedouin has stolen the camel.\" The camel grumbled for a while and moaned. The Messenger of God ﷺ listened to its grumbling and moaning. When the camel quieted down, the Prophet ﷺ turned to the guard and said: \"Leave him, for the camel has testified against you that you are lying.\" The guard left, and the Prophet ﷺ turned to the Bedouin and said: \"What did you say when you came to me?\" He said: \"I said, may my father and mother be your ransom: O God, bless Muhammad so that no blessing remains; O God, grant blessings to Muhammad so that no blessing remains; O God, grant peace to Muhammad so that no peace remains; O God, have mercy on Muhammad so that no mercy remains.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, made them manifest to me, and the camel spoke in his defense, and the angels filled the horizon.\""],[4833,"I used to write down the revelation in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ. His breathing would become heavy and he would sweat profusely like pearls. Then it would be lifted from him, and I would write while he dictated to me. I would not finish until it became heavy [again]. When I finished, he would say: \"Recite it.\" I would recite it, and if there was an omission, he would correct it."],[4834,"I found in the book of my maternal uncle Abd al-Hamid: Aqil narrated to me; Sa'id b. Sulayman narrated to me; he informed him from his father Sulayman b. Zayd, from Zayd b. Thabit, who said: I used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of God ﷺ. When it descended upon him, intense distress would seize him and he would sweat profusely like pearls. Then it was relieved from him. I would enter upon him with a piece of saddle-wood or a potsherd and write while he dictated to me. I would not finish until my legs almost broke from the weight of the Qur'an, until I would say: I will never walk on my legs again. When I finished, he would say: \"Recite it.\" If there was an omission, he would correct it. Then I would take it out to the people."],[4835,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"May God brighten [the face of] a person who hears a hadith from us, memorizes it, and conveys it. For many a bearer of understanding is not himself a faqih.\""],[4836,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"May God brighten [the face of] a person who hears a hadith from us, memorizes it, and conveys it. For many a bearer of understanding is not himself a faqih.\""],[4837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever's intention is the Hereafter, Allah will gather his affairs together for him, place richness in his heart, and the world will come to him submissively. And whoever's intention is the world, Allah will scatter his affairs, place poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world will come to him except what Allah has decreed for him.”"],[4838,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever makes the Hereafter his intention, Allah will gather his affairs for him, place richness in his heart, and the world will come to him, humbled. And whoever makes the world his intention, Allah will disperse his affairs, place poverty before his eyes, and he will get nothing of the world except what has been decreed for him.\""],[4839,"The Prophet ﷺ partitioned off a room—I think he used a mat—and prayed in it. Some people heard about that, and some of them began clearing their throats. He came out to them and said: “What you have been doing—as I observed—continued until I feared it would be made obligatory upon you. If it were made obligatory upon you, you would not be able to keep it up. So pray, O people, in your houses, for the best prayer of a man is in his house, except the prescribed prayer.”"],[4840,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “A man's prayer in his house is better than his prayer in this mosque of mine, except the prescribed prayer.”"],[4841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ partitioned off a room in the mosque and used to pray in it. A man saw him and they prayed following his prayer. One night they came while he did not come out to them, so they cleared their throats, threw pebbles at the door, and raised their voices. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them angry and said: “O people, your persistent action made me think that it would be prescribed. So adhere to praying in your houses, for the best prayer of a man is in his house, except the prescribed prayer.”"],[4842,"We were commanded to glorify Allah thirty-three times at the end of every prayer, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times. A man of the Ansar saw in a dream—as one who sleeps sees—and said: “Your Prophet ﷺ commanded you to glorify so many times, praise so many times, and magnify so many times?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Make them twenty-five and add the tahleel (saying ‘La ilaha illa Allah’) to them.” The Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him of his dream. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Make them as he said.”"],[4843,"I was writing for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me: “Write: ‘Not equal are those believers who sit [at home] and the mujahideen in the cause of Allah.’” Then Abdullah b. Umm Maktum came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I love jihad in the cause of Allah, but I have the disability you see—my eyesight has gone.” Zayd b. Thabit said: “The thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pressed heavily on my thigh until I feared it would crush it. Then he said: ‘Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]—other than the disabled—and the mujahideen in the cause of Allah.’”"],[4844,"Abu Huraira is reported to have said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited to observe prayer after the 'Asr prayer till the sun is set, and after the dawn till the sun rises. (Using translation from Muslim 825)"],[4845,"He said to me: “Killing has intensified among the people of al-Yamama from among the Quran reciters of the Muslims, and I fear that killing will intensify among the reciters in other places, and much of the Quran will be lost, not preserved. I think you should order the collection of the Quran.” I said to Umar: “How can I do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” Umar said: “By Allah, it is good.” He kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to it, and I saw in it what Umar saw. He said to Zayd b. Thabit, while Umar was sitting with him, not speaking: “You are a young man, and I do not accuse you. You used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So pursue the Quran and compile it.” Zayd said: “By Allah, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me to do of compiling the Quran.” I said: “How can you do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” He said: “By Allah, it is good.” Abu Bakr kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to that to which He had opened the chest of Abu Bakr and Umar. So I got up and pursued the Quran, compiling it from palm stalks, thin white stones, pieces of leather, date-palm branches, and the memories of men, until I found the last part of Surah al-Tawbah with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari, not finding it with anyone else: “There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves.” The sheets remained with Abu Bakr ؓ during his life until Allah took him, then with Umar ؓ until Allah took him, then with Hafsah bt. Umar until Uthman compiled the Quran from them into the codices."],[4846,"He said to me: “Killing has intensified among the people of al-Yamama from among the Quran reciters of the Muslims, and I fear that killing will intensify among the reciters in the places, and much of the Quran will be lost, not preserved. I think you should order the collection of the Quran.” I said to Umar: “How can I do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” Umar said: “By Allah, it is good.” He kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to it, and I saw in it what Umar saw, while Umar was sitting with him, not speaking. Abu Bakr said: “You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not accuse you. You used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So pursue the Quran and compile it.” Zayd said: “By Allah, if he had tasked me with moving a mountain, it would not have been heavier upon me than what he ordered me to do of compiling the Quran.” He said: I said: “How can you do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” He said: “By Allah, it is good.” Abu Bakr kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to that to which He had opened the chest of Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: So I got up and pursued the Quran, compiling it from palm stalks, thin white stones, pieces of leather, date-palm branches, and the memories of men, until I found the last part of Surah al-Tawbah, two verses, with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari, not finding them with anyone else: “There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves.” The sheets in which I compiled the Quran remained with Abu Bakr during his life until Allah took him, then with Umar until Allah took him, then with Hafsah bt. Umar."],[4847,"Abu Bakr sent for me after the killing of the people of al-Yamama. I found Umar sitting with him. Abu Bakr said: “Umar came to me and said: ‘Killing has intensified among the people of al-Yamama among the Quran reciters.’” I said: “How can I do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” Umar said: “By Allah, it is good.” He kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to that to which He had opened Umar's chest, and I saw in that what Umar saw. Abu Bakr said to Zayd: “You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not accuse you. You used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So pursue the Quran and compile it.” Zayd said: “By Allah, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain, it would not have been heavier than what he ordered me to do of compiling the Quran.” He said: I said: “How can you do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?” He said: “By Allah, it is good.” Abu Bakr kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to that to which He had opened Abu Bakr's chest. He said: So I pursued the Quran, compiling it from palm stalks, date-palm branches, and the memories of men, until I found the last part of Surah al-Tawbah with Khuzaymah or Abu Khuzaymah al-Ansari, not finding it with anyone else: “There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves,” until the end of Bara'ah. The sheets remained with Abu Bakr until Allah took him, then with Umar during his life until Allah took him, then with Hafsah bt. Umar."],[4848,"I heard a verse from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sought it but did not find it, until I found it with a man from the Ansar: “There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves”—the verse."],[4849,"Zayd b. Thabit said: “This severe [verse] came after this lenient [verse] by six months, so the severe abrogated the lenient.”"],[4850,"“That the Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath along with a witness.”"],[4851,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made haram what is between its two lava tracts.”"],[4852,"That he entered the markets and hunted in them a nahs, meaning a bird. Zayd b. Thabit said: “Let it go, may you have no mother! Do you not know that the Prophet ﷺ made haram hunting the birds of what is between its two lava tracts?”"],[4853,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made haram what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah,” meaning what is between its two harrahs."],[4854,"“That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made haram its game,” meaning Madinah."],[4855,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril ﷺ kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[4856,"I drink until, when the breath is cut off, I lift the vessel from my mouth; and when I eat, I lick my fingers, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies.”"],[4857,"“The Messenger of God stood and led them in prayer. A row stood behind him and a row faced the enemy. He led them in one rakʿah, then those went to the position of those, and those came, and he led them in one rakʿah, then he concluded.”"],[4858,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the prayer of fear once; he did not lead us in it before or after that.”"],[4859,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “I have left among you two successors: the Book of God and my household. They will not separate until they come to me at the pool.”"],[4860,"“I have left among you the two successors: the Book of God and my kindred. They will never separate until they come to me at the pool.”"],[4861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God brighten a servant who hears my statement and carries it to someone else, for many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more learned than himself, and many a bearer of understanding is not a jurist.”"],[4862,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God brighten a servant who hears my statement and carries it to someone else, for many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more learned than himself, and many a bearer of understanding is not a jurist.”"],[4863,"I was writing for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I had placed the pen on my ear when fighting was ordered, when a blind man came and said, “What about me, when I am losing my sight?” Then it was revealed: {There is no blame upon the blind}."],[4864,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Letters come to me from people, and I do not like anyone to read them. Can you learn the Syriac script?” I said, “Yes.” “So I learned it in seventeen days.”"],[4865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Letters come to me from people that I would not like everyone to read. Can you learn the Syriac script?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So I learned it in seventeen [days].\""],[4866,"The Prophet ﷺ taught him and commanded him to commit himself to it every morning for his family: \"Here I am, O Allah, here I am; at Your service, and all good is in Your hands. From You, through You, and to You. O Allah, whatever word I have spoken, vow I have made, or oath I have sworn, Your will precedes it. What You will comes to pass, and what You do not will does not occur. There is no might nor power except with Allah, and Allah is over all things competent. O Allah, whatever prayer I have prayed, let it be upon the one I prayed for; whatever curse I have uttered, let it be upon the one I cursed. You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter. Make me die a Muslim and join me with the righteous. O Allah, I ask You for contentment with Your decree, a pleasant life after death, the delight of looking at Your face, and longing to meet You, without harmful adversity or misleading trial. I seek refuge with You lest I wrong or be wronged, transgress or be transgressed against, or earn a sin that leads astray, or commit an offense. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Possessor of majesty and honor, I make a covenant with You in this worldly life, and I call You as witness—and sufficient is You as witness—that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, with no partner. Yours is the dominion and Yours is the praise, and You are over all things competent. And I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. I bear witness that Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, and the Hour is coming—there is no doubt about it—and that You will resurrect those in the graves. I bear witness that if You entrust me to myself, You entrust me to weakness, vulnerability, sin, and error, for I trust only in Your mercy. So forgive me my sin, for none forgives sins but You, and turn to me in mercy—You are the Ever-Relenting, the Merciful.\""],[4867,"While we were around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ compiling the Qur'an from parchments, he suddenly said: \"Blessed is Syria (al-Sham).\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why is that?\" He said: \"Because the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over them.\""],[4868,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ writing down the revelation when he said: \"Blessed is Syria (al-Sham)\" three times. We said, \"What is that, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said: \"The angels spread their wings over Syria.\""],[4869,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"If Allah were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and His earth, He would punish them while not being unjust to them; and if He had mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If Mount Uhud, and the like of Uhud, were gold that you spent in the cause of Allah, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in the divine decree entirely, and you know that what befalls you could not have missed you, and what misses you could not have befallen you; and that if you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire.\""],[4870,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The ʿumrā belongs to the heir.”"],[4871,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled concerning the ʿumrā that it belongs to the one to whom it is given for his lifetime and after his death.”"],[4872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever grants an ʿumrā in something, it belongs to the recipient during his life and after his death. Do not grant ruqbā in anything; for whoever grants a ruqbā in something, it follows the same course.”"],[4873,"“The Prophet ﷺ made the ʿumrā belong to the heir.”"],[4874,"“The Prophet ﷺ ruled concerning the ʿumrā that it is permissible.”"],[4875,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The ʿumrā is permissible.”"],[4876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever grants an ʿumrā, it belongs to him during his lifetime and after his death. Do not grant ruqbā in anything; for whoever grants a ruqbā in something, it follows the course of inheritance.”"],[4877,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not grant ruqbā; for whoever grants a ruqbā in something, it follows the course of inheritance.”"],[4878,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The ʿumrā follows the course of inheritance.”"],[4879,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The ʿumrā and the ruqbā follow the course of inheritance.”"],[4880,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The ʿumrā follows the course of inheritance.”"],[4881,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The ʿumrā is an inheritance.”"],[4882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The ‘umrā belongs to the heir,” or he said: “Its course is the course of inheritance.”"],[4883,"“The ‘umrā is permissible.”"],[4884,"Abu al-Qasim said: “The two Hammads stopped it.”"],[4885,"From ‘Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim b. Ghanim b. ‘Awf b. al-Khazraj, and they are Banu al-Hubullayy: Zayd b. Wadi‘ah b. ‘Amr b. Qays b. Jaz’ b. ‘Adiyy b. Malik b. Salim b. Ghanim b. ‘Awf b. al-Khazraj.”"],[4886,"I said to Zayd b. Arqam: O Abu ‘Amir."],[4887,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ considered some people too young on the day of Uhud, among them Zayd b. Arqam.”"],[4888,"About meat that was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ [while he was] in a state of ihram. He said: Yes, a limb of game meat was gifted to him, and he returned it to him and said: “We do not eat it; we are in a state of ihram.”"],[4889,"About game meat that was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a state of ihram, and he returned it and said: “We are in a state of ihram.”"],[4890,"Was a limb of game gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in a state of ihram, and he returned it? He said: Yes. Hajjaj said: He did not accept it and said: “We are in a state of ihram.” He said: Yes."],[4891,"I heard Mu'awiya giving a sermon, saying: \"O people of Syria, the Ansari narrated to me\"—Shu'ba said, meaning Zayd b. Arqam—\"that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'A group of people from my community will continue fighting for the truth until the decree comes to them.' And I think you, O people of Syria, are they.\""],[4892,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He whose guardian I am, 'Ali is his guardian.\""],[4893,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage and stopped at Ghadir Khumm, he ordered that the large trees be cleared. Then he arose and said: \"It is as if I have been summoned and I will answer. I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of Allah and my offspring, the people of my house. So watch how you succeed me in them, for they will never separate until they return to me at the Pond.\" Then he said: \"Allah is my Master, and I am the guardian of every believer.\" Then he took 'Ali by the hand and said: \"He whose master I am, this is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\" I said to Zayd: \"Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"There was no one among the trees who did not see him with his own eyes and hear him with his own ears.\""],[4894,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar.\" Ibn al-Fadl was uncertain regarding the sons of the sons of the Ansar."],[4895,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cursing the dead.\" So why do you curse 'Ali when he has died?"],[4896,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid cursing the dead? So why do you curse 'Ali when he has died?"],[4897,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid cursing the dead.\""],[4898,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbir for it.\""],[4899,"I heard Zayd b. Arqam say: We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, every people has followers, and we have followed you, so supplicate Allah to make our followers from us.\" He supplicated. 'Amr b. Murra said: I conveyed that to Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: \"Zayd b. Arqam claimed that.\""],[4900,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: severe."],[4901,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, so he came and swore that he had not said it. People started saying, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has brought a lie,' until I sat in the house for fear that when they saw me they would say, 'This is the one who lies,' until Allah ﷻ sent down: {They are the ones who say}."],[4902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool.'"],[4903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool.'"],[4904,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: 'Whoever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.'"],[4905,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached Ghadir Khumm. He ordered a tree branch and it was swept on a day when no hotter day had come upon us. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, no prophet was ever sent except that he lived half as long as the one before him, and I am about to be called and I will answer. I am leaving among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray after it: the Book of Allah.' Then he stood and took the hand of Ali ؓ and said: 'O people, who is more entitled to you than your own selves?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Whoever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla.'"],[4906,"Ali ؓ was in Yemen when a woman was brought to him who had been had intercourse with by three men during a single purity period. He asked two of them, 'Do you acknowledge this child for this one?' They did not acknowledge. Then he asked two, 'Do you acknowledge this child for this one?' Then he asked two until he finished. Then he asked two about one, and they did not acknowledge. So he drew lots among them and made the child belong to the one upon whom the lot fell, and he imposed on him two-thirds of the blood money. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he laughed until his molars appeared."],[4907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ali to Yemen. He was brought a case of three men who had had intercourse with a woman during a single purity period, and she gave birth to a child. He kept saying to each one: 'Would you accept that the child be for this one? You are obstinate partners.' So he drew lots among them and made the child belong to the one whom the lot struck, and he imposed on him two-thirds of the blood money for the other two. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he laughed until his molars appeared."],[4908,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a letter came to him from Ali ؓ in which he said: 'Three men came to me disputing about a boy whose mother they had had intercourse with during pre-Islamic times in a single purity period, each claiming he was his son. I judged among them by drawing lots among them and made the boy belong to the one who drew the lot, on condition that he pay two-thirds of the blood money to the other two.' The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars appeared, then said: 'I know nothing in this matter except what Ali ؓ judged.'"],[4909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ali as governor over Yemen. A rikaz (buried treasure) was brought to him, so he took the khums from it and gave the rest to its owner. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he was pleased with it."],[4910,"Rather, deliberately. Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ used to pray it."],[4911,"And he said, \"Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray.\""],[4912,"Ali adjured the people: \"I adjure by God any man who heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Whoever's mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.'\" Twelve Badris stood and testified to that. Zayd said, \"I was among those who concealed it, and my sight went away.\""],[4913,"I heard Zayd b. Arqam say: We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"You are one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond.\" I said, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Seven hundred men or eight hundred men.\""],[4914,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You are one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond.\" I said, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Six hundred or seven hundred.\""],[4915,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey during a military expedition, and he said, \"You are not one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond on the Day of Resurrection.\" They said to Zayd, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Between eight hundred and seven hundred.\""],[4916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us, \"You are not one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond.\" We said to Zayd, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Between six hundred and seven hundred.\""],[4917,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Today you are not one part out of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond.\" I said, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Seven hundred or eight hundred.\""],[4918,"I heard Zayd b. Arqam say, \"The first to pray with the Prophet ﷺ was Ali.\" I related that to Ibrahim, and he rejected it and said, \"The first to pray was Abu Bakr.\""],[4919,"I heard Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul say, 'Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God until they disperse.' So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. Ubayy's son came to him and swore to him that he had not said that. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to me and blamed me. I went to my home and slept—as if he was dejected. Then the Prophet ﷺ sent for me, and I came to him—or he said, I came to the Prophet ﷺ—and he said, \"God has confirmed you and excused you,\" and he recited these two verses: 'They are the ones who say, \"Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God\"' until he completed the two verses."],[4920,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink. But one who eats and drinks has a need.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The need of one of them is sweat that flows from his skin, and then his belly becomes lean.\""],[4921,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"You claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink.\" He said, \"Yes, by Him in whose hand is my soul, a man among them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire.\" The man said, \"One who eats and drinks has a need.\" He said, \"Sweat. When that is so, his belly becomes lean for him.\""],[4922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, a man from the people of Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, desire, and sexual intercourse.” A man from the Jews said: “But the one who eats and drinks will need to relieve himself.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The need of one of them is sweat that flows from his skin, and then his belly becomes lean.”"],[4923,"A man from the People of the Book said: “O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink.” He said: “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed one of them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, sexual intercourse, and desire.” He said: “But the one who eats will need to relieve himself.” He said: “The need of one of them is sweat like the fragrance of musk, which makes his belly shrink.”"],[4924,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink.” He said: “Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed a man will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, sexual intercourse, and desire.”"],[4925,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a Jewish man said to him, \"Do you believe that there is food, drink, and spouses in paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" The Jewish man said, \"We find it delicious and pleasant.\" The Prophet ﷺ then asked him, \"Do you believe in the musk tree and find it in your scripture?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If urine and seminal fluid are a bad odor that flows from their private parts to their feet, it is like musk.\""],[4926,"There was a man who used to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and he tied knots for him and placed them in a well belonging to a man from the Ansar. Then two angels came to visit him. One of them sat at his head and the other at his feet. One of them said: “Do you know what his ailment is?” He said: “So-and-so, the one who visits him, tied knots for him and threw them into the well of so-and-so the Ansari. If a man were sent to take the knots, he would find the water had turned yellow.” He said: “So he sent a man who took the knots and untied them, and he recovered. After that, the man used to visit the Prophet ﷺ, but he never mentioned anything about it to him, nor did he rebuke him ﷺ .”"],[4927,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ, a man from the Jews came, called Tha‘labah b. al-Harith, and said: “Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.” He said: “And upon you.”"],[4928,"When the Prophet ﷺ greeted us after the prayer, we would say: “And upon you be peace, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.”"],[4929,"A man from the Jews bewitched the Prophet ﷺ, and he suffered from that for some days. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: “A man from the Jews has bewitched you; he has tied knots for you.” So the Messenger of Allah sent ‘Ali ؓ to him, and he extracted them and brought them. Every time he untied a knot, he felt relief, and the Prophet ﷺ stood up as if he had been released from a tether. The Prophet ﷺ never mentioned that Jew, nor did he ever show it in his face.”"],[4930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[4931,"My ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[4932,"My ears heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[4933,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[4934,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Do we not find it in the Book of Allah? Do you narrate that Muhammad ﷺ has a pool (Hawd)?” He said: “I said: ‘He has told us that and promised it to us.’ He said: ‘You have lied, but you are an old man who has become senile.’ He said: ‘I said: Indeed, my ears heard it and my heart retained it, saying: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in Hell.” So I have not lied about him.’”"],[4935,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? You claim that he has a cistern in Paradise? I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us this and promised it to us. He said: You have lied; rather you are an old man who has become senile."],[4936,"“Who is forbidden from receiving charity?” It was said: Who are they? He said: “The family of Ali, the family of Aqil, the family of Ja'far, and the family of al-Abbas.”"],[4937,"“They are the family of Ali, the family of al-Abbas, the family of Ja'far, and the family of Aqil.”"],[4938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am leaving among you two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my family. So watch how you treat them after me.” We said: Who are the people of his house? He said: “The family of Ali, the family of Ja'far, the family of Aqil, and the family of al-Abbas.”"],[4939,"We entered upon him and said: You have seen much good; you accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed behind him. He said: I have seen good, but I fear that I have been delayed only for evil. Whatever I narrate to you, accept it; and whatever I remain silent about, leave it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in a valley between Makkah and Madinah and delivered a sermon to us, then said: “I am a human being; I am about to be called and I will answer. I am leaving among you two things: one of them is the Book of Allah, in which is the rope of Allah. Whoever follows it is upon guidance, and whoever abandons it is upon misguidance. And my household—I remind you of Allah concerning my household,” three times. We said: Who are the people of his house? Are his wives among them? He said: “No. A man may marry a woman for a period of time, then divorce her and she returns to her father and mother. The people of his house are his family and his close relatives who are forbidden from charity after him: the family of Ali, the family of al-Abbas, the family of Ja'far, and the family of Aqil.”"],[4940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I adjure you by Allah concerning my household.” We said to Zayd: Who are the people of his house? He said: “Those who are forbidden from charity: the family of Ali, the family of al-Abbas, the family of Aqil, and the family of Ja'far.”"],[4941,"Husayn b. Sabrah said to him: O Zayd, you saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, heard his words, and campaigned with him. You have indeed attained much good, O Zayd. Narrate to us what you witnessed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what you heard. He said: O son of my brother, by Allah, my age has advanced, my time has passed, and I have forgotten some of what I used to memorize from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whatever I narrate to you, accept it; and whatever I do not narrate, do not compel me. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood one day among us as a preacher at a watering place called Khumm, between Makkah and Madinah. He praised Allah, exalted be He, extolled Him, admonished, and reminded. Then he said: “To proceed, O people, I am only a human being; the messenger of my Lord is about to come to me and I will answer him. I am leaving among you two weighty things: one of them is the Book of Allah, in which is guidance and light. So take hold of the Book of Allah and cling to it.” He urged adherence to the Book of Allah and encouraged it. Then he said: “My household—I remind you of Allah concerning my household,” saying it three times. Husayn said to him: Who are the people of his house, O Zayd? Are not his wives among the people of his house? He said: “His wives are among the people of his house, but the people of his house are those who are forbidden from charity after him.” He said: Who are they? He said: “They are the family of Ali, the family of Ja'far, the family of al-Abbas, and the family of Aqil.” It was said: Are all of these forbidden from charity? He said: “Yes.”"],[4942,"“The family of Ali, the family of al-Abbas, the family of Aqil, and the family of Ja'far.”"],[4943,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn: “I am at peace with those with whom you are at peace, and at war with those with whom you are at war.”"],[4944,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a house in which were Fatimah, Ali, Hasan, and Husayn, and said: “I am at war with those who make war on them, and at peace with those who make peace with them.”"],[4945,"We used to recite at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold or silver, he would desire a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah relents to whoever repents.”"],[4946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not trim his moustache is not one of us.”"],[4947,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not trim his mustache is not from us.”"],[4948,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not trim his mustache is not from us.”"],[4949,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He is not from us who does not trim his mustache.”"],[4950,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"O Allah, I entrust them both to You and the righteously believing people.\" It was said to Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, \"Indeed, Zaid ibn Arqam said such and such.\" He said, \"That is an old man whose sanity has gone.\""],[4951,"About exchanging (money). One would say, “Ask this one,” and the other would say, “Ask that one, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable.” Both of them said that. So I asked them both, and they said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling silver for gold on credit.”"],[4952,"We went on a military campaign with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us were some Bedouins who would go ahead of us. A Bedouin went ahead of his companions, filled the watering trough, placed stones around it, and laid a leather mat over it until his companions arrived. An Ansari man came to the Bedouin and let loose the halter of his she-camel so she could drink, but the Bedouin refused to let him do so. So the Ansari pulled out a stone, and the water drained away. The Bedouin had a piece of wood, and he struck the Ansari’s head with it, wounding him. The Ansari went to ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy, the head of the hypocrites, and told him—and the Bedouin was one of his companions. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy became angry and said: {Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God until they disperse from around him}, meaning the Bedouins, for they used to attend the Messenger of God ﷺ at meal times. ʿAbd Allāh said to his companions: When they disperse from Muhammad, bring food to Muhammad so that he and those with him may eat. Then he said to his companions: When you return to Madinah, the more honored among you will expel the more lowly. Zayd said: I was riding behind my uncle ؓ. He said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy—and we were his maternal uncles—so I informed my uncle, who went and told the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for him, and he swore and denied it. The Messenger of God ﷺ believed him and disbelieved me. My uncle came to me and said: You intended nothing but that the Messenger of God ﷺ should hate you and the Muslims disbelieve you. Then there fell upon me such distress as has never fallen upon anyone. While I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, my head was drooping from distress, and suddenly the Messenger of God ﷺ came to me, tweaked my ear, and smiled in my face. Nothing would have pleased me more than to have in return for that the eternal life of this world. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you? I said: He said nothing to me except that he tweaked my ear and smiled in my face. He said: Rejoice. Then ʿUmar caught up with me, and I said to him something similar to what I had said to Abu Bakr. When morning came, the Messenger of God ﷺ recited Surah al-Munafiqun."],[4953,"The people went out to pray for rain, and Zayd b. Arqam went out among them. I approached him and said: How many campaigns did the Messenger of God ﷺ undertake? He said: “Nineteen campaigns.” I said: How many did you go on with him? He said: “Seventeen campaigns.” He said: “And he led the people in two rakʿahs.” Abu al-Walid added in his narration: I said: What was the first campaign of the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: “Dhu al-ʿAshirah or Dhu al-ʿUsayrah.”"],[4954,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ undertook nineteen campaigns.”"],[4955,"“I went on seventeen campaigns with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[4956,"“I went on seventeen campaigns with the Messenger of God ﷺ; I missed two.”"],[4957,"“I went on seventeen campaigns with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I said: How many campaigns did the Messenger of God ﷺ undertake? He said: “Nineteen campaigns.”"],[4958,"I went on seventeen military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ; he preceded me in two expeditions."],[4959,"I went on seventeen military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ; he preceded me in two expeditions."],[4960,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed one Hajj after he emigrated, and he did not perform any Hajj after it except the Farewell Hajj."],[4961,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey in which the people suffered hardship. 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy said to his companions, {Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God until they disperse} from around him. And he said, {If we return to Madinah, the more honored will surely expel the more humble from it}. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him. He sent for 'Abd Allah and questioned him, and he swore emphatically, saying, 'He lied, O Messenger of God.' Then what they said weighed heavily on me, until God sent down my vindication in {When the hypocrites come to you}. 'The Prophet ﷺ called them to seek forgiveness for them, but they turned their heads away.' And His saying, {As if they were propped-up timbers}. He said, 'They were the most handsome of men.'"],[4962,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy say, {Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of God until they disperse} from around him. {If we return to Madinah, the more honored will surely expel the more humble from it}. I mentioned that to my uncle, and he mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ called me, and the Prophet ﷺ sent for 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul and his companions. They swore that they had not said it. The Messenger of God ﷺ disbelieved me and believed him. I was afflicted with distress the like of which had never afflicted me. I sat in the house, and my uncle said to me, 'You only wanted the Prophet ﷺ to disbelieve you and hate you.' Then God ﷻ sent down {When the hypocrites come to you}. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for me and recited it, then said, 'Indeed God ﷻ has vindicated you.'"],[4963,"I heard Zayd b. Arqam say: My eyes became inflamed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ visited me during the inflammation. He said, 'O Zayd, if your eyes were to suffer what is afflicting them, what would you do?' I said, 'I would be patient and seek reward.' He said, 'O Zayd, if your eyes were to suffer what is afflicting them and you were patient and sought reward, your reward would be nothing less than Paradise.'"],[4964,"O Messenger of God, is there no concession for me? He said, 'No.' Ibn Umm Maktum said, 'O God, I am blind,' so a concession was granted to me, and God sent down {other than those who are disabled}. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered it to be written down."],[4965,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am the Prophet, there is no lying in me. I am the son of Abdul-Muttalib.\""],[4966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[4967,"We heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours.'"],[4968,"On the authority of al-Bara' and Zayd b. Arqam, they said: We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Ghadir Khumm, while we were lifting the branch of a tree from over his head. He said, 'Charity is not lawful for me or for my household. God has cursed whoever claims descent from other than his father, and God has cursed whoever takes as allies other than his patrons. The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone. There is no bequest for an heir.'"],[4969,"'Ali ؓ adjured the people: Whoever heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever I am his ally, 'Ali is his ally,' then more than ten stood up and testified that they heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever I am his ally, 'Ali is his ally.'"],[4970,"On the authority of 'Amr b. Dhi Marr and Zayd b. Arqam, they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon on the day of Ghadir Khumm and said, 'Whoever I am his mawla, 'Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him, and support whoever supports him, and help whoever helps him.'"],[4971,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Abu Bakr ؓ , and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then he sent me to Umar ؓ , and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then he sent me to Uthman, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise along with a trial that would befall him. Uthman took hold of my hand and set off, or took me, until he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, what is this trial that will befall me? For by God, I have not sung, I have not wished [for forbidden things], I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I became Muslim, or since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I have not committed fornication, whether in the time of ignorance or in Islam. He said to him: “God will clothe you with a shirt, and if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off.”"],[4972,"We used to speak during the prayer; one of us would speak to his brother about his need until the verse was revealed: {Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before God devoutly obedient}. Then we were commanded to be silent."],[4973,"In the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to speak during the prayer; one of us would speak to his companion about a need between him and him until it was revealed: {Guard strictly the prayers, and the middle prayer, and stand before God devoutly obedient}. Then we were commanded at that point to be silent."],[4974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said: “Am I not more entitled to you than your own selves?” They said: Yes. He said: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla.”"],[4975,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy.” I began to ask him for more, and he said: “I will only stop where I have been stopped.”"],[4976,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out at al-Juhfah on the day of Ghadir Khumm, holding Ali by the upper arm, and said: “O people, do you not know that I am more entitled to the believers than their own selves?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Whoever’s mawla I am, this is his mawla.”"],[4977,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla.”"],[4978,"I was sitting with Abdullah b. Ubayy when the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by with some of his companions. Abdullah b. Ubayy said: {If we return to Madinah, the more honored will surely expel from it the more humble}. I went to Saʿd b. ʿUbadah and informed him, and he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Abdullah b. Ubayy, and Abdullah b. Ubayy swore to him by God that he had not said this. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at Saʿd b. ʿUbadah, who said: O Messenger of God, only the boy Zayd b. Arqam informed me of it. Saʿd came and took me by the hand and brought me, and said: This one told me. He said: Abdullah b. Ubayy scolded me, and I went to the Messenger of God and wept and said: Yes, by the One who sent down upon you the light and prophethood, he did say it. He said: The Prophet of God ﷺ turned away from him, and God ﷻ sent down {When the hypocrites come to you} until the end of the surah."],[4979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah’ sincerely will enter Paradise.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Its sincerity is that it restrains him from what Allah has forbidden him.”"],[4980,"“The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what are these sacrifices?’ He said: ‘The Sunnah of your father Ibrahim.’ They said: ‘What is there for us in them, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said: ‘For every hair, one merit.’ They said: ‘What about wool, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said: ‘For every hair of wool, one merit.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3127)"],[4981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not assign My servants, the knowing monotheists among the sinners, to Paradise or to Hell until I am the One who assigns them, based on My knowledge of them. And do not burden yourselves with what you have not been burdened, and do not judge the servants apart from their Lord.”"],[4982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman does not fulfill Allah’s right upon her until she fulfills her husband’s right, even if he were to ask her while she is on the back of a camel saddle, she should not withhold herself from him.”"],[4983,"I am not going to say anything but only that which Messenger of Allah (may peace be upgn him) used to say. He used to supplicate:\" O Allah, I seek refuge in Thee from incapacity, from sloth, from cowardice, from miserliness, decrepitude and from torment of the grave. O Allah, grant to my soul the sense of righteousness and purify it, for Thou art the Best Purifier thereof. Thou art the Protecting Friend thereof, and Guardian thereof. O Allah, I seek refuge in Thee from the knowledge which does not benefit, from the heart that does not entertain the fear (of Allah), from the soul that does not feel contented and the supplication that is not responded.\" (Using translation from Muslim 2722)"],[4984,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, senility, and the torment of the grave. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best to purify it, You are its guardian and master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, a prayer that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered.”"],[4985,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he was asked about fasting on the Day of Arafah. He said: \"It expiates the year you are in and the year after it.\""],[4986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Treat pleurisy with Indian costus and olive oil.\""],[4987,"He said: We halted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a valley called Wadi Khumm. He commanded the prayer and prayed it at midday. Then he addressed us, while a cloth was spread over a tree to shade the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the sun. He said: \"Do you not know that I am closer to every believing man and believing woman than their own selves?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[4988,"I asked Zayd b. Arqam: \"What was the name of the mother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Aminah bt. Wahb.\""],[4989,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali when he wanted to go on a military expedition: \"It is necessary that either you stay or I stay.\" So he left him behind. Some people said: \"He only left him behind because of something he disliked.\" That reached Ali, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He laughed, then said: \"O Ali, are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?\""],[4990,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali: \"Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Harun to Musa?\""],[4991,"That the Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Ghadir Khumm: \"Whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla.\""],[4992,"My eye became diseased, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me. He said: \"O Zayd, if your eyes were to remain with what afflicts them, how would you act?\" I said: \"Then I would seek reward and be patient.\" He said: \"Then you would meet Allah without any sin.\""],[4993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"These latrines are attended by devils. When one of you enters the toilet, let him say: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the foul, the unclean, the accursed devil.'\""],[4994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"These latrines are attended by devils. When one of you wants to enter, let him say: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils.'\""],[4995,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar.\""],[4996,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar.”"],[4997,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the descendants of the Ansar, and the descendants of their descendants.”"],[4998,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, the sons of the sons of the Ansar, the women of the Ansar, the women of the sons of the Ansar, and the women of the sons of the sons of the Ansar.”"],[4999,"Zayd said to him: “Raise the stick, for I saw the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in its place.”"],[5000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prayer of the penitent is when the young weaned camels feel the heat of the sun.”"],[5001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the mosque of Quba while they were praying two rak'ahs. He said: “What is this prayer?” They said: “Glorification.” He said: “The prayer of the penitent is when the young weaned camels feel the heat of the sun.”"],[5002,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by them while they were praying the Duha prayer when the sun had risen brightly, and he said: “The prayer of the penitent is when the young weaned camels feel the heat of the sun.”"],[5003,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Quba while they were praying when the sun had risen brightly, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “The prayer of the penitent is when they used to pray it when the young weaned camels felt the heat of the sun.”"],[5004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Quba and saw them praying the Duha prayer, so he said: “This is the prayer of the penitent.”"],[5005,"He went out to the people of Quba while they were praying the Duha prayer, and he said: “The prayer of the penitent is when the young weaned camels feel the heat of the sun,” without attributing it to the Prophet."],[5006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: These privies are frequented by the jinns and devils. So when anyone amongst you goes there, he should say: \"I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils.\" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 6)"],[5007,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “These places of relieving oneself are attended by devils. When one of you wants to enter, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils.”"],[5008,"I said: O Messenger of God, do you see the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and their patricians? Should we not prostrate to you? He said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband. And the woman does not fulfill her husband's right, even if he asked her for herself while on a camel saddle, she would give it to him.\""],[5009,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Syria. When he arrived, he said: O Messenger of God, I saw the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and their patricians. Should we not prostrate to you? He said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband. And the woman does not fulfill her husband's right, even if he asked her for herself on the back of a camel saddle, she would give it to him.\""],[5010,"\"I saw the mouth of the Messenger of God ﷺ in its place.\""],[5011,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say after the prayer: \"O God, You are our Lord and the Lord of everything. I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Your messenger. O God, You are our Lord and the Lord of everything. I bear witness that all the servants are brothers. O God, You are our Lord and the Lord of everything. Make me sincere to You and my family in this world and the Hereafter, O Possessor of majesty and honor. Hear and respond. God is the Greatest, the Greatest. O God, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth. God is the Greatest, the Greatest. God suffices me, and He is the best disposer of affairs. God is the Greatest, the Greatest.\""],[5012,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever says after every prayer: 'Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,' three times, has taken the fullest measure of reward.\""],[5013,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my community and forbidden for its males.\""],[5014,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Zayd b. Arqam to visit him during an illness he had. He said: \"There is no harm upon you from this illness of yours, but how will you be when you live long after me and then become blind?\" He said: \"Then I will seek reward and be patient.\" He said: \"Then you will enter Paradise without reckoning.\" He said: He became blind after the Prophet ﷺ died, then God restored his sight, then he died, may God have mercy on him."],[5015,"O Abu 'Amir, if you had gone ahead you would have seen Gabriel and Michael. He said: \"You have dug and pecked. You are more insignificant to God than I am. That one is a liar, fabricating against God and His Messenger.\""],[5016,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Verily Allah ﷻ loves silence at three times: when reciting the Qur'an, when advancing in battle, and at a funeral procession.\""],[5017,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Abu 'Ayyash al-Zuraqi is Zayd b. al-Nu'man.\""],[5018,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan when the polytheists, led by Khalid b. al-Walid, confronted us, and they were between us and the qiblah. The Prophet ﷺ led us in Zuhr prayer. They said: \"They were in a situation where, if we had caught them off guard...\" They also said: \"Now a prayer is coming upon them that is dearer to them than their children and their own selves.\" He said: Then Jibril ﷺ descended with these verses between Zuhr and 'Asr: {And when you are among them and lead them in prayer...} He said: \"When the prayer was due, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to take up their weapons. We formed two rows behind him. Then he bowed, and we all bowed. Then he raised his head, and we all raised our heads. Then the Prophet ﷺ prostrated with the row nearest to him, while the others remained standing, guarding them. When they had prostrated and stood up, the others sat down and prostrated in their place. Then these moved forward to the position of those, and those came to the position of these. They all bowed, then he raised his head and they all raised their heads. Then the Prophet ﷺ prostrated with the row nearest to him, while the others remained standing, guarding them. When they sat down, the others sat down and prostrated. Then he concluded with the salam. Then he departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed it twice: once at 'Usfan and once in the land of Banu Sulaym.\""],[5019,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan when the polytheists, led by Khalid b. al-Walid, confronted us, and they were between us and the qiblah. The Prophet ﷺ led us in Zuhr prayer. They said: \"They were in a situation where, if we had caught them off guard...\" They also said: \"Now a prayer is coming upon them that is dearer to them than their children and their own selves.\" He said: Then Jibril descended with these verses between Zuhr and 'Asr: {And when you are among them and lead them in prayer...} He said: \"When the prayer was due, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to take up their weapons. We formed two rows behind him. Then he bowed, and we all bowed. Then he raised his head, and we all raised our heads. Then the Prophet ﷺ prostrated with the row nearest to him, while the others remained standing, guarding them. When they had prostrated and stood up, the others sat down and prostrated. Then he concluded with the salam. Then he departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed it twice: once at 'Usfan and once in the land of Banu Sulaym.\""],[5020,"The Prophet ﷺ was in the ranks facing the enemy at 'Usfan, and the polytheists were led by Khalid b. al-Walid. The Prophet ﷺ led them in Zuhr prayer. Then the polytheists said: \"They have a prayer that is dearer to them than their wealth and their children.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer, arranging them in two rows behind him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed with them all together. When they raised their heads, the row nearest to him prostrated, while the others remained standing. When they raised their heads from prostration, the rear row prostrated because of their bowing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the front row moved back and the rear row moved forward, and each of them stood in the position of the other. Then he bowed, and the others stood. When they finished their prostration, the others prostrated. Then the Prophet ﷺ concluded with the salam upon them."],[5021,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the polytheists met us at 'Usfan, with their cavalry that day led by Khalid b. al-Walid. When the time for Zuhr prayer came upon us, the mu'adhdhin called the adhan and then the iqamah. The polytheists intended to attack us, but some of them said: \"A prayer will come upon them that is dearer to them than their children\"—meaning the 'Asr prayer. Jibril ﷺ brought him the verses containing the prayer of fear. \"When the prayer was due, the mu'adhdhin called the adhan and the iqamah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward and we formed two rows behind him, while the polytheists that day were on the side of the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed and we bowed. Then he prostrated and the row nearest to him prostrated, while the rear row remained standing. When they finished their prostration, the rear row prostrated. The polytheists blamed one another.\" Abu 'Ayyash said: \"He also led us in a similar prayer in the land of Banu Sulaym.\""],[5022,"About the Prophet ﷺ in the prayer of fear: He prayed with the people, and they all bowed, then they all raised their heads. Then some of them prostrated with him while the others remained standing. When they raised their heads, they moved back, and the others came forward and some of them prostrated with him while others remained standing. When they raised their heads, they moved back, and the others came and prostrated in their place. Then he prayed the second rak'ah the same as the first. Then he sat down, and those nearest to him sat down, while the others remained standing. Then he concluded with the salam, and those nearest to him concluded with the salam. Then they stood up, and those others came and prostrated in their place, then concluded with the salam."],[5023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in Zuhr prayer at 'Usfan, while the polytheists were led by Khalid b. al-Walid. The polytheists said: \"They were in a situation where, if we had caught them off guard...\" They also said: \"Now a prayer is coming upon them that is dearer to them than their children and their own selves.\" Jibril ﷺ descended with the verses containing the prayer of fear. \"He arranged his companions in two rows behind him. He said the takbir and we all said the takbir. He bowed and we all bowed. He prostrated and the row nearest to him prostrated. When he stood up, the row nearest to him moved back and took the position of the rear row, and the rear row moved forward and took their position. He bowed and we all bowed. He raised his head and we all raised our heads. The row nearest to him prostrated. When he sat down, the rear row prostrated.\""],[5024,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan when the time for prayer—the Zuhr prayer—arrived, and the polytheists' cavalry was led by Khalid b. al-Walid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led his companions in Zuhr prayer. The polytheists said: \"They have a prayer after this one that is dearer to them than their children, their wealth, and their own selves\"—meaning the 'Asr prayer. Jibril ﷺ descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between Zuhr and 'Asr and informed him, and this verse was revealed: {And when you are among them and lead them in prayer...} to the end. \"When the prayer was due, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arranged his companions in two rows, carrying their weapons, with the enemy in front of the Prophet ﷺ. They all said the takbir and all bowed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, and the row nearest to him prostrated, while the others remained standing, guarding them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he stood for the second rak'ah, and the others prostrated. Then these moved forward to the position of those, and those moved back to the position of these. He led them in the other rak'ah, and they all bowed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated, and the row nearest to him prostrated, while the others remained standing, guarding them. When they finished, these prostrated. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concluded with the salam.\" Abu 'Ayyash said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed this prayer twice: once at 'Usfan and once in the land of Banu Sulaym.\""],[5025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things,' it will be for him like freeing a slave from the descendants of Isma'il, ten good deeds will be written for him, ten evil deeds will be erased from him, ten ranks will be raised for him, and he will be safeguarded from Satan until evening. If he says it in the evening, he will have the like of that.\" He said: Then a man saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a dream and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu 'Ayyash al-Zuraqi told us such-and-such from you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Abu 'Ayyash spoke the truth.\""],[5026,"When the news of the Negus's death reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Your brother has died.\" He went out, and we formed rows behind him and prayed, though we could not see anything."],[5027,"\"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we know how to send salams upon you, but how should we send salah upon you?' He said: 'Say: \"Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin 'abdika wa rasulika kama salaita 'ala Ibrahim wa barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta 'ala Ibrahim (O Allah, send salah upon Muhammad, Your slave and Messenger , as You sent Salah upon Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim).\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1293)"],[5028,"Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the unlettered Prophet, the seal of the prophets—this was in the first Book. Then it was said on his tongue: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq spoke the truth—the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the strong, the trustworthy. He was weak in body but strong in the command of Allah—this was in the first Book. Then it was said on his tongue: He spoke the truth; he spoke the truth—three times. And the middle one, 'Abd Allah 'Umar, Commander of the Faithful, who did not fear in Allah the blame of any blamer, and who prevented people from the strong among them devouring the weak—this was in the first Book. Then it was said on his tongue: He spoke the truth; he spoke the truth; he spoke the truth. Then he said: 'Uthman, Commander of the Faithful, merciful to the believers. Two have passed, and four remain. Then the people will differ, and there will be no order for them. The protected domains will be violated—meaning the sacred ordinances will be transgressed. The Hour will draw near, and people will devour one another."],[5029,"Zayd b. Sa'na said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out one day from his apartments with 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ with him. A man came to him on his mount like a Bedouin and said: 'O Messenger of God, the village of the Banu so-and-so in Busra has embraced Islam and entered into Islam. I had told them that if they embraced Islam, provision would come to them abundantly. A year of drought, hardship, and lack of rain has befallen them, so I fear, O Messenger of God, that they may leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed. If you see fit to send them something to help them, do so.' He looked at a man beside him, whom I think was 'Ali ؓ, and said: 'O Messenger of God, nothing of it remains.' Zayd b. Sa'na said: I approached him and said: 'O Muhammad, would you like to sell me a specified amount of dates from the orchard of Banu so-and-so to a certain term?' He said: 'No, O Jew. But I will sell you a specified amount of dates to a certain term, and do not name the orchard of Banu so-and-so.' I said: 'Yes.' So he made a transaction with me. I untied my money belt and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for a specified amount of dates to a certain term. He gave it to the man and said: 'Go early to them and help them with it.' Zayd b. Sa'na said: When it was two or three days before the term was due, I came to him, grabbed the collar of his shirt and cloak, and looked at him with a harsh face. I said to him: 'Will you not repay me my due, O Muhammad? By God, I do not know you Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib except as ones who delay payment. I have knowledge of your mixing with people.' I looked at 'Umar, whose eyes were rolling in his face like a revolving celestial sphere. Then he cast his gaze at me and said: 'O enemy of God, do you say to the Messenger of God ﷺ what I hear and do to him what I see? By the One who sent him with truth, if I did not fear missing his command, I would strike your head with my sword.' The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at 'Umar with calmness and deliberation, then said: 'O 'Umar, I and he were in greater need of other than this: that you command me to pay well and command him to demand well. Take him, O 'Umar, give him his due, and add twenty sa's of dates for what you frightened him.' Zayd said: 'Umar ؓ took me and gave me my due and added twenty sa's of dates. I said: 'What is this addition, O 'Umar?' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to add it for you for what I frightened you.' I said: 'Do you know me, O 'Umar?' He said: 'No. Who are you?' I said: 'I am Zayd b. Sa'na.' He said: 'The rabbi?' I said: 'The rabbi.' He said: 'What made you do to the Messenger of God ﷺ what you did and say to him what you said?' I said: 'O 'Umar, there was none of the signs of prophethood but I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ when I looked at him, except for two that I had not tested in him: his forbearance preceded his ignorance, and ignorance did not increase him except in forbearance. I have now tested them. I call you to witness, O 'Umar, that I am pleased with God as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet. And I call you to witness that half of my wealth — and I am the wealthiest of them — is charity for the ummah of Muhammad.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Or upon some of them, for you cannot encompass them all.' I said: 'Or upon some of them.' 'Umar and Zayd returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Zayd said: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger ﷺ.' He believed in him, confirmed him, pledged allegiance to him, and witnessed with him many expeditions. Then Zayd died in the Battle of Tabuk, advancing and not retreating. May God have mercy on Zayd."],[5030,"“I saw five of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing gold rings: among them Zayd b. Jariya, Zayd b. Arqam, al-Bara' b. 'Azib, Anas b. Malik, and 'Abd Allah b. Yazid.”"],[5031,"“May God have mercy on him.” It was said: “O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, he left a hundred thousand.” He said: “But it did not leave him.”"],[5032,"The Prophet of God ﷺ caught up with me at the gate of the mosque and said: “Shall I not direct you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?” I said: “Yes, O Prophet of God.” He said: “There is no might nor power except with God.”"],[5033,"From 'Urwa: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Zayd b. Aslam b. Tha'laba b. 'Adi b. al-'Ajlan.”"],[5034,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Zayd b. Aslam b. Tha'laba.”"],[5035,"From ʿUrwa: “In the naming of those who witnessed al-ʿAqaba from the Anṣār, then from Banū Bayāḍa: Zayd b. Labīd.”"],[5036,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: “Zayd b. Khālid is given the kunya Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.”"],[5037,"“Zayd b. Khālid al-Juhanī died in the year seventy-eight. He is given the kunya Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and his age was eighty-five.”"],[5038,"“Zayd b. Khālid al-Juhanī died, and he is given the kunya Abū Muḥammad, in the year seventy-eight.”"],[5039,"It is said: “The kunya of Zayd b. Khālid is Abū Ṭalḥa.”"],[5040,"“By Allah, O Commander of the Believers, I will not abandon them after I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying them.”"],[5041,"That he said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb regarding the two rakʿas after ʿAṣr: “I will not abandon them after I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying them.”"],[5042,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Jibrīl came to me and said to me: ‘O Muḥammad, command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiya, for it is among the emblems of the ḥajj.’”"],[5043,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Jibril came to me and said: 'Command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is one of the rites of Hajj.'\""],[5044,"On the authority of Zaid bin Khalid al-Juhani, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , that the Messenger of Allah said: \"Gabriel came to me and said, 'Raise the crescent, for it is a symbol of Hajj.'\""],[5045,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'Allah commands you to order your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is one of the rites of Hajj.'\""],[5046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'Command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is one of the rites of Hajj.'\" [The narrator] did not mention Zaid b. Khalid."],[5047,"The Prophet ﷺ was invited to a funeral to pray over it, and he said: \"Your companion has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\""],[5048,"He informed him that he heard Zaid b. Khalid al-Juhani say: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Khaybar when a man from Ashjaʿ died. The Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him. They went to inspect his belongings and found in them beads from the beads of the Jews worth two dirhams.\""],[5049,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. al-Hakam narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; they said: Malik reported to us, from Yahya b. Saʿid, from Muhammad b. Yahya b. Habban, from Abu ʿAmrah al-Ansari, that Zaid b. Khalid al-Juhani informed him that a man died on the day of Khaybar, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Zaid claimed that he said: \"Pray over your companion.\" He said: The faces of the people changed because of that. Zaid claimed that he said: \"Your companion has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\" He said: We opened his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews worth two dirhams."],[5050,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ from Ashjaʿ died, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Pray over your companion.\" The faces of the people changed because of that. When he saw what had befallen them, he said: \"Your companion has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\" We searched his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews worth two dirhams."],[5051,"A man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Ashjaʿ died, and they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Pray over your companion, for he has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\" They searched his belongings and found in them beads from the beads of the Jews worth two dirhams."],[5052,"A Muslim man died at Khaybar, and it was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Pray over your companion.\" The faces of the people changed because of that. When he saw what had befallen them, he said: \"Your companion has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\" We searched his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews worth two dirhams."],[5053,"A man died on the day of Khaybar, and that was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"Pray over your companion.\" That weighed heavily on the people and their faces changed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your companion has stolen from the spoils in the cause of Allah.\" He looked into his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews that he had stolen. By Allah, I do not think they were worth two dirhams."],[5054,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Hakam narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; they both said: Malik reported to us, from ʿAbd Allah b. Abi Bakr, from his father, from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr b. ʿUthman, from Ibn Abi ʿAmrah al-Ansari, from Zaid b. Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses? The one who brings his testimony before he is asked for it, or who gives his testimony before he is asked for it.\""],[5055,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The best of witnesses is the one who fulfills his testimony before he is asked about it.\""],[5056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best testimony is that which its bearer gives before he is asked for it.”"],[5057,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I not inform you of the best witnesses? They are those who come forward with their testimony before they are asked for it.”"],[5058,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Hospitality is three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity.”"],[5059,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent; whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Hospitality is three nights, and whatever is beyond that is charity.”"],[5060,"That a man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I adjure you by God to judge for me according to the Book of God.” The other disputant, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: “Yes, so judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission [to speak].” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Speak.” He said: “My son was a hired worker for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. They told me that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told us that my son was only subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was upon his wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: the sheep and the slave girl are to be returned, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for one year. O Unays, go to the wife of this man, and if she confesses, stone her.” So he went to her in the morning, and she confessed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered her stoned, and she was stoned."],[5061,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, my son was a hired worker for this man and he committed adultery with his wife. They told us that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a slave girl and a hundred sheep. Then the people of knowledge told me that my son was subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was upon this man's wife.” He said, I think: “So judge between us according to the Book of God.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: as for the sheep and the slave girl, they are to be returned to you; as for your son, he is subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year.” And he said to a man from Aslam called Unays: “Rise, O Unays, and ask this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her.”"],[5062,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, that they informed him that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of God ﷺ. One of them said: “O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God,” and the other, who was the more knowledgeable of the two, said: “Yes, O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission to speak.” Or he said: “Permit me to speak.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Speak.” He said: “My son was a hired worker for this man—and al-'asif means the hired worker—and he committed adultery with his wife. They told me that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son was subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was only upon his wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: as for your sheep and your slave girl, they are to be returned to you.” So he had his son flogged with a hundred lashes and exiled for a year, and he ordered Unays al-Aslami to go to the other man's wife, and if she confessed, to stone her. She confessed, and he stoned her."],[5063,"Sufyan and Shibl: that two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of God ﷺ. One of them said: “O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God,” and the other, who was the more knowledgeable of them, said: “Yes, O Messenger of God, so judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission to speak.” He said: “Speak.” He said: “My son was a hired worker for this man”—he said: “and al-'asif is the hired worker”—“and he committed adultery with his wife. They told me that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and I was informed that my son was only subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was upon his wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: as for your slave girl and your sheep, they are to be returned to you.” So he had his son flogged with a hundred lashes and exiled for a year, and he ordered Unays al-Aslami to go to the other man's wife, and if she confessed, to stone her. She confessed, and he stoned her."],[5064,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say regarding someone who has not been muhsan (previously married): “When he commits adultery, he is flogged with a hundred lashes and exiled for a year.”"],[5065,"That two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ disputing before him. One of them said: “O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God,” and the other, who was the more knowledgeable of them, said: “Yes, so judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission to speak.” He said: “Speak.” He said: “My son was a hired worker for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl of mine. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son was only subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was only upon his wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: as for your sheep and your slave girl, they are to be returned to you.” So he had his son flogged with a hundred lashes and exiled for a year, and he ordered Unays al-Aslami to stone the other man's wife if she confessed. She confessed, and he stoned her."],[5066,"That two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ disputing before him. One of them said: “O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission to speak.” He said: “Speak.” He said: “O Messenger of God, my son was a hired worker for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son was subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that stoning was upon his wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will certainly judge between you according to the Book of God: as for your sheep and your slave girl, they are to be returned to you.” He said: So he had his son flogged with a hundred lashes and exiled for a year, and he ordered Unays al-Aslami to stone the other man's wife, and he stoned her."],[5067,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ “commanding, regarding someone who committed adultery and was not muhsan, a flogging of a hundred lashes and exile for a year.”"],[5068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning one who committed fornication and had not been previously married: one hundred lashes and banishment for a year."],[5069,"Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them said, \"I adjure you by Allah to judge between us according to the Book of Allah.\" His opponent stood and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired worker for this man—meaning his employee—and he committed adultery with his wife. I ransomed him with one hundred sheep and a servant. When I asked the people of knowledge, they informed me that my son is due one hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that this man's wife is due stoning.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you according to the Book of Allah. As for the hundred sheep and the servant, they are to be returned to you. Your son is due one hundred lashes and banishment for a year. Go, O Unays, to this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her.\" He asked her, she confessed, and he stoned her."],[5070,"Two men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them said, \"I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah, to judge between me and this man according to the Book of Allah, and permit me.\" He said, \"My son was a hired worker for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was due stoning, so I ransomed him with one hundred sheep and a slave girl. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that my son is due one hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that stoning is due upon this man's wife.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will surely judge between you according to the Book of Allah. As for the slave girl and the sheep, they are to be returned to you. Your son is due one hundred lashes and banishment for a year.\" He said, \"Go, O Unays, to this man's wife, and if she confesses, stone her.\" So he went to her, she confessed, and he stoned her."],[5071,"From Abu Hurayrah and Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave woman who had not been previously married. He said, \"If she commits fornication, flog her. Then if she commits fornication a third or fourth time—al-Zuhri was uncertain—sell her, even for a rope of hair.\""],[5072,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us. They both said: Malik reported to us from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Utbah b. Mas'ud, from Abu Hurayrah and from Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave woman if she commits fornication and has not been previously married. He said, \"If she commits fornication, flog her. Then if she commits fornication, flog her. Then if she commits fornication, flog her. Then sell her, even for a rope of hair.\" Ibn Shihab said, \"I do not know whether after the third or the fourth time. Al-dafir is a rope.\""],[5073,"From Abu Hurayrah, Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, and Shibl, who said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man asked him about a slave woman who fornicates before being previously married. He said, \"Flog her.\" He said, \"Then if she fornicates?\" He said, \"Flog her.\" Then he said, regarding the third or fourth time, \"Sell her, even for a rope of hair.\" And al-dafir is a rope made of hair."],[5074,"He heard Abu Hurayrah and Zayd b. Khalid, who testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave woman if she fornicates. He said, \"Flog her three times, then sell her, even for a hobble-cord.\""],[5075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the slave woman of one of you fornicates, let him flog her. If she repeats, let him flog her. If she repeats, let him flog her. Then if she repeats a fourth time, let him sell her, even for a rope of hair.\""],[5076,"He informed him that Abu Hurayrah and Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani informed him that they heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about a slave woman who fornicates and has not been previously married. He said, \"Flog her if she fornicates. Then if she fornicates, flog her. Then sell her, even for a rope of hair,\" at the third or fourth time."],[5077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the slave woman of one of you fornicates, let him flog her. Then if she fornicates, let him flog her. Then if she fornicates, let him flog her. Then if she fornicates, let him sell her, even for a rope of hair.\""],[5078,"A man cursed a rooster that crowed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Do not curse it, for it calls to prayer.\""],[5079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cursing the rooster and said, \"Indeed it calls the adhan for prayer.\""],[5080,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not curse the rooster, for it wakes [people] for prayer.”"],[5081,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not curse the rooster, for it calls the adhan at the [proper] time.”"],[5082,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Do not curse the cock, for it awakens for prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5101)"],[5083,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer at al-Hudaybiyyah after rainfall. When he finished, he said: “Did you not hear what your Lord said tonight? He said: ‘I have not bestowed any blessing upon My servants except that a group of them became disbelievers in it. As for the one who praises Me for My rain and extols Me, that one has believed in Me and disbelieved in the star. And as for the one who says, “We were given rain by such-and-such a star,” that is the one who has believed in the star and disbelieved in My blessing.’”"],[5084,"We were given rain with the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Hudaybiyyah. The Prophet ﷺ said when morning came: “Do you know what your Lord said?” We said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said it twice, then said: “Some of My servants this morning are believers and some are disbelievers. As for the one who says, ‘We were given rain by such-and-such a star,’ that one is a disbeliever in Me and a believer in the star. And as for the one who says, ‘This is a mercy and provision from God,’ that one is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the star.”"],[5085,"We were given rain during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When morning came, he said: “Do you know what your Lord said tonight? He said: ‘I have not bestowed any blessing upon My servants except that a group of them became disbelievers in it, saying, “We were given rain by such-and-such a star.” As for the one who believes in Me and praises Me for My rain, that is the one who has believed in Me and disbelieved in the star. And as for the one who says, “We were given rain by such-and-such a star,” that is the one who has believed in the star and disbelieved in Me.’”"],[5086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sheep among his companions and gave me a young goat. I said: “O Messenger of God, may I offer it as a sacrifice? It is a jadha‘ah from the goats.” He said: “Yes.” So I sacrificed it."],[5087,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions and gave me a young goat. I found it to be a jadha‘, so I went back to him and said: “O Messenger of God, it is a jadha‘.” He said: “Sacrifice it.”"],[5088,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sheep among his companions for sacrifices and gave me a jadha‘ young goat. I went back to him and said: “O Messenger of God, it is a jadha‘.” He said: “Sacrifice it.” So I sacrificed it."],[5089,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions and gave me a jadha‘ young goat from the goats. I brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “It is a jadha‘.” He said: “Sacrifice it.”"],[5090,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution.”"],[5091,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution.”"],[5092,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to use the toothstick at every prayer.”"],[5093,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Were I not afraid that it would be hard on my followers, I would order them to use the siwak (as obligatory, for cleaning the teeth). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7240)"],[5094,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence with goodness has indeed fought.”"],[5095,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of his affairs with goodness has indeed fought.”"],[5096,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence has indeed fought.”"],[5097,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence has indeed fought.”"],[5098,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence with goodness has indeed fought.”"],[5099,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence with goodness has indeed fought.”"],[5100,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God has indeed fought, and whoever takes care of his family in his absence with goodness has indeed fought.”"],[5101,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever equips a warrior or takes care of his family in his absence has indeed fought.”"],[5102,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior will have the like of his reward, and whoever takes care of a warrior's family in his absence will have the like of his reward.” Ibn Shihab said: Then Busr b. Sa'id informed me of it."],[5103,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God will have the like of his reward, and whoever takes care of a warrior in the path of God in his family with goodness and spends will have the like of his reward.”"],[5104,"Did you hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a man passing in front of a person praying? He said: I heard him say: “For one to stand in his place for forty is better than to pass in front of a person praying.” He said: I do not know whether he said forty years, or forty months, or forty days."],[5105,"Did the Prophet ﷺ hear about the one who passes in front of a person praying? I asked him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “For one of you to stand for forty is better for him than to pass in front of the one praying.” He does not know whether forty years, or forty months, or forty days."],[5106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a found item (luqatah). He said, \"Announce it for a year. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, note its container and its tie and its number, then consume it. If its owner comes, return it to him.\""],[5107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a found item. He said, \"Announce it for a year. If it is recognized, hand it over; otherwise, note its container and its number. If its owner comes, hand it over to him.\""],[5108,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from [going to] the mosques, and let them go out without perfume.\""],[5109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from [going to] the mosques, and let them go out without perfume.\""],[5110,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever is offered a good deed by his brother without asking for it or supervising it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only a provision that Allah has sent to him.\""],[5111,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said, \"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[5112,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from 'Abdullah b. Abi Bakr from his father that 'Abdullah b. Qays b. Makhramah informed him from Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani that he said: \"I will certainly watch the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tonight.\" So I rested my head on his doorstep or his tent. \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two light rak'ahs, then prayed two long rak'ahs, then prayed two rak'ahs that were shorter than the two before them, then prayed two rak'ahs shorter than the two before them, then prayed two rak'ahs shorter than the two before them, then performed witr. That is thirteen.\""],[5113,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and those of Juhaynah and Ashja' are allies; they have no patron (mawla) other than Allah and His Messenger.\""],[5114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, and those of Ashja' and Juhaynah are allies and clients; they have no patron (mawla) other than Allah and His Messenger.\""],[5115,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a found item. He said, \"Announce it for a year, then note its container and its tie—or he said its vessel. If its owner comes, hand it over to him; otherwise, spend it or benefit from it.\""],[5116,"An Arab came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a found object. The Prophet ﷺ told him to announce it for one year, and if its owner comes, then return it to him. If not, then use it for oneself or enjoy it."],[5117,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a found item. He said, \"Announce it for a year, then note its container and its tie—or he said its vessel. If its owner comes, hand it over to him; otherwise, spend it or benefit from it.\""],[5118,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Rabi'ah b. Abi 'Abd al-Rahman from Yazid, the mawla of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about a found item. He said, \"Note its container and its tie, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, it is your concern.\""],[5119,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Rabi'a b. Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, the freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about lost property. He said: “Note its purse and its tying cord, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, it is your business.”"],[5120,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Rabi'a b. Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, the freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about lost property. He said: “Note its purse and its tying cord, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, [return it]; otherwise, it is your business.”"],[5121,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about stray camels. He said: “What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and their own shoes; they eat trees and drink water until their owner finds them.”"],[5122,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about stray camels. He said: “What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and their own shoes; they eat trees and drink water until their owner finds them.”"],[5123,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about stray camels. He said: “What do you have to do with them? They have their own water-skins and their own shoes; they eat trees and drink water until their owner finds them.”"],[5124,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about lost property. He said: “Note its purse and its tying cord, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, return it to him; otherwise, spend it.”"],[5125,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about lost property. He said: “Note its purse and its tying cord, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, return it to him; otherwise, spend it.”"],[5126,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about lost property. He said: “Note its purse and its tying cord, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, return it to him; otherwise, spend it.”"],[5127,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about stray sheep. He said: “It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.”"],[5128,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about stray sheep. He said: “It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.”"],[5129,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, [what about] lost property? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Announce it for a year; if no one comes to claim it, then spend it.”"],[5130,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, [what about] lost property? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Announce it for a year; if no one comes to claim it, then spend it.”"],[5131,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was with him and said, \"O Messenger of God, [what about] a found property?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Announce it for a year, and if no claimant comes for it, then spend it.\""],[5132,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found property. He said, \"Announce it for a year, then recognize its container and its tying cord, then spend it. If its owner comes, then return it to him.\""],[5133,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found property. He said, \"Announce it for a year, then recognize its container and its tying cord, then spend it. If its owner comes, then return it to him.\""],[5134,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about a found property. He said, \"Announce it for a year, then recognize its container and its tying cord, then spend it. If its owner comes, then return it to him.\""],[5135,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you say about a stray camel?\" He became angry and his cheeks reddened. He said, \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own shoes and its own water-skin; it eats from trees and drinks from water until its owner finds it.\""],[5136,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you say about a stray camel?\" He became angry and his cheeks reddened. He said, \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own shoes and its own water-skin; it eats from trees and drinks from water until its owner finds it.\""],[5137,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you say about a stray camel?\" He became angry and his cheeks reddened. He said, \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own shoes and its own water-skin; it eats from trees and drinks from water until its owner finds it.\""],[5138,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a stray sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\""],[5139,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a stray sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\""],[5140,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a stray sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\""],[5141,"\"We used to pray the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we would leave until we reached the market, and the place where his arrow would fall could still be seen.\""],[5142,"I heard Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani say, \"I used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then go out to the market, and if I were to shoot, I would see the places where my arrows fell.\""],[5143,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to give glad tidings to the people that whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, will have Paradise."],[5144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade snatching and plundering."],[5145,"I and a companion of mine were engaged in temporary marriage on the day of Khaybar, bargaining with a woman over the term, and we haggled. Then someone came to us and informed us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had forbidden temporary marriage and forbidden eating every fanged beast of prey and domestic donkeys."],[5146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person will have the like of his reward, without that diminishing anything from his reward. And whoever equips a pilgrim or equips a warrior or looks after his family in his absence will have the like of his reward, without that diminishing anything from his reward.\""],[5147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, or equips a warrior, or equips a pilgrim, will have the like of their rewards, without that diminishing anything from their rewards.\""],[5148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, feeding him and giving him drink, will have the like of his reward, without that diminishing anything from his reward.\""],[5149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, or performs Hajj on behalf of a man, or equips a warrior, or looks after his family in his absence, will have the like of his reward.\""],[5150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever equips a warrior or a pilgrim, or looks after his family in his absence, or provides iftar to a fasting person, will have the like of his reward, without that diminishing anything for him.\""],[5151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person will have the like of the fasting person's reward, and it will not diminish anything from the fasting person's reward. And whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or looks after his family in his absence will have the like of the warrior's reward, and it will not diminish anything from the warrior.\""],[5152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, the like of his reward will be written for him, and it will not diminish anything from the fasting person's reward. And whoever equips a warrior or looks after his family in his absence will have the like of his reward, and it will not diminish anything from the warrior's reward.\""],[5153,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, the like of his reward is written for him, without diminishing anything from the fasting person's reward. And whoever equips a warrior or takes care of his family in his absence, he will have the like of his reward, without diminishing anything from the warrior's reward.\""],[5154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, he will have the like of his reward, and nothing will be diminished from his reward. And whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, he will have the like of his reward, and nothing will be diminished from his reward.\""],[5155,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or takes care of his family with good, he will have the like of the warrior's reward without diminishing anything from his reward. And whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, he will have the like of his reward.\""],[5156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person or equips a pilgrim or a warrior, he will have the like of their rewards without diminishing anything from their rewards.\""],[5157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Pray in your houses and do not make them graves.\""],[5158,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \"Pray in your houses and do not make them graves.\""],[5159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent them as scouts to Makkah to inform him of the news of Quraysh. They took the Najdiyya route until when they were at al-Raji' in Najd, Banu Lihyan from Hudhayl intercepted them. As for 'Asim b. Thabit, he fought with his sword until he was killed. As for Khubayb and Zayd b. al-Dathina, they were taken up into the mountain, and the people could not overcome them until they made covenants and pledges to them. So they came down to them, and they bound them tightly, then they took them to Makkah and sold them to Quraysh. As for Khubayb, 'Uqba b. al-Harith b. Nawfal, the brother of Husayn b. al-Harith, bought him, and he shared in his purchase with him Abu Ihab b. 'Aziz b. Qays b. Suwayd b. Rabi'a b. 'Adas b. 'Abd Allah b. Darim. And Qays b. Suwayd b. Rabi'a was the maternal brother of 'Amir b. Nawfal; their mother was the daughter of Nahshal al-Tamimi. And 'Ikrima b. Abi Jahl, al-Akhnas b. Shurnun b. 'Ilaj b. Ghubra al-Thaqafi, 'Ubayda b. Hakim al-Sulami then al-Dhakwani, Umayya b. 'Utba b. Hammam b. Hanzala from Banu Darim and Banu al-Hadrami, Sa'ya b. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Qays from Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, and Safwan b. Umayya b. Khalaf b. Wahb al-Jumahi. They handed him over to 'Uqba b. al-Harith, and he imprisoned him in a house. He stayed with him as long as Allah willed him to stay. A woman from the family of 'Uqba b. al-Harith b. 'Amir used to open the door for him and feed him. He said to her: \"When the people intend to kill me, notify me before that.\" When they intended to kill him, she informed him. He said to her: \"Get me a piece of iron with which I can shave my pubic hair.\" The son of the woman who used to help him entered with a razor in his hand. He took the boy's hand and said: \"Has Allah given you power over us?\" She said: \"This is not what I expected of you.\" Then he handed her the razor and said: \"I was only joking.\" The people who shared in his purchase took him out, and the people of Makkah went out with them, and they brought out a wooden stake with them until when they were at al-Tan'im, they set up that stake and crucified him on it. The one who was in charge of killing him was 'Uqba b. al-Harith. Abu Husayn was young and was with the people. They killed him in retaliation for al-Harith b. 'Amir, who had been killed on the Day of Badr as a disbeliever. Khubayb said to them at the time of his killing: \"Release me from the bonds so that I may pray two rak'ahs.\" They released him, and he prayed two light rak'ahs, then he turned away and said: \"Were it not that you would think I am afraid of death, I would have lengthened them. That is why I made them light.\" He said: \"O Allah, I see no face but the face of an enemy. O Allah, I find no messenger to Your Messenger, so convey my greetings to him.\" Jibril ﷺ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of that. Khubayb said while they were raising him onto the stake: \"O Allah, count them by number, kill them one by one, and leave none of them.\" Khubayb b. 'Adi was killed by the sons of the polytheists who had been killed on the Day of Badr. When they put the weapons in him while he was crucified, they called out to him and adjured him: \"Would you like Muhammad to be in your place?\" He said: \"No, by Allah the Almighty, I would not love to be ransomed by a thorn that pricks him in his foot.\" They laughed. And Khubayb said when they raised him onto the stake:"],[5160,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him. It reached me that he intended to send an army to my people. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, turn back the army, for I will guarantee their submission and obedience to you.\" He said: \"Do it.\" So he wrote to them. A delegation from them came to the Prophet ﷺ with their submission and obedience. He said: \"O brother of Suda', you are indeed obeyed among your people.\" I said: \"Rather Allah guided them and was good to them.\" He said: \"Should I appoint you as commander over them?\" I said: \"Yes.\" So he appointed me over them and wrote a document for me to that effect. I asked him for some of their sadaqat, and he did so. The Prophet ﷺ was then on one of his journeys. He stopped at a place, and we camped at the beginning of the night. I stayed close to him, and his companions kept falling behind until no man among them remained with him except me. When dawn approached, he ordered me, and I gave the call to prayer. Then he said to me: \"O brother of Suda', do you have water?\" I said: \"Yes, a little, not enough for you.\" He said: \"Pour it into the vessel, then bring it to me.\" I brought it to him, and he put his hand into it. I saw between every two of his fingers a spring gushing forth. He said: \"O brother of Suda', were it not that I feel shy before my Lord, we would have drunk and given drink. Call out to the people: whoever wants to perform ablution.\" So those who wanted scooped water. Bilal came to give the iqama, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"The brother of Suda' gave the adhan, and whoever gives the adhan should give the iqama.\" When he prayed the dawn prayer, the people of the place came complaining about their governor and saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell us about what was between us and our people in the Jahiliyya.\" He turned to his companions, and I was among them, and said: \"There is no good in leadership for a believing man.\" That fell into my heart. A beggar came to him and asked him. He said: \"Whoever asks people while having enough, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly.\" The man said: \"Give me from the sadaqat.\" He said: \"Allah did not approve in the sadaqat the judgment of a prophet or anyone else until He made them eight portions. If you are one of those, I will give you your right.\" When morning came, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, take back your appointment, for I have no need of it.\" He said: \"Why?\" I said: \"I heard you say: 'There is no good in leadership for a believing man,' and I have believed. And I heard you say: 'Whoever asks people while having enough, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly,' and I asked you while I am wealthy.\" He said: \"It is that. If you wish, take it, and if you wish, leave it.\" I said: \"Rather I leave it.\" He said: \"Guide me to a man I can appoint.\" I guided him to a man from the delegation, and he appointed him."],[5161,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him. It reached me that he intended to send an army to my people. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, turn back the army, for I will guarantee their submission and obedience to you.\" He said: \"Do it.\" So he wrote to them. A delegation from them came to the Prophet ﷺ with their submission and obedience. He said: \"O brother of Suda', you are indeed obeyed among your people.\" I said: \"Rather Allah guided them and was good to them.\" He said: \"Should I appoint you as commander over them?\" I said: \"Yes.\" So he appointed me over them and wrote a document for me to that effect. I asked him for some of their sadaqat, and he did so. The Prophet ﷺ was then on one of his journeys. He stopped at a place, and we camped at the beginning of the night. I stayed close to him, and his companions kept falling behind until no man among them remained with him except me. When dawn approached, he ordered me, and I gave the call to prayer. Then he said to me: \"O brother of Suda', do you have water?\" I said: \"Yes, a little, not enough for you.\" He said: \"Pour it into the vessel, then bring it to me.\" I brought it to him, and he put his hand into it. I saw between every two of his fingers a spring gushing forth. He said: \"O brother of Suda', were it not that I feel shy before my Lord, we would have drunk and given drink. Call out to the people: whoever wants to perform ablution.\" So those who wanted scooped water. Bilal came to give the iqama, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"The brother of Suda' gave the adhan, and whoever gives the adhan should give the iqama.\" When he prayed the dawn prayer, the people of the place came complaining about their governor and saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell us about what was between us and our people in the Jahiliyya.\" He turned to his companions, and I was among them, and said: \"There is no good in leadership for a believing man.\" That fell into my heart. A beggar came to him and asked him. He said: \"Whoever asks people while having enough, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly.\" The man said: \"Give me from the sadaqat.\" He said: \"Allah did not approve in the sadaqat the judgment of a prophet or anyone else until He made them eight portions. If you are one of those, I will give you your right.\" When morning came, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, take back your appointment, for I have no need of it.\" He said: \"Why?\" I said: \"I heard you say: 'There is no good in leadership for a believing man,' and I have believed. And I heard you say: 'Whoever asks people while having enough, it is a headache in the head and a disease in the belly,' and I asked you while I am wealthy.\" He said: \"It is that. If you wish, take it, and if you wish, leave it.\" I said: \"Rather I leave it.\" He said: \"Guide me to a man I can appoint.\" I guided him to a man from the delegation, and he appointed him."],[5162,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered me, and I gave the call for the dawn prayer. Bilal came to give the iqama, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Bilal, the brother of Suda' gave the adhan, and whoever gives the adhan should give the iqama.\""],[5163,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the time for the morning prayer came, so he said to me: “Call the adhan, O brother of Suda’.” So I called the adhan while I was on my mount."],[5164,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Bayada b. ʿAmir b. Zurayq b. ʿAbd b. Haritha: Ziyad b. Labid b. Thaʿlaba b. Sinan b. ʿAmir b. ʿAdi b. Umayya.”"],[5165,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who witnessed the ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Bayada: Ziyad b. Labid, and he witnessed Badr.”"],[5166,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was speaking to his companions, saying: “How will it be when the time of knowledge has departed?” I said: “May my father and mother be your ransom, how will the time of knowledge depart while we recite the Qur’an, teach it to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons until the Hour arises?” He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Labid! I used to consider you among the most understanding of the people of Madinah. Do not the Jews and Christians recite the Torah and the Gospel, yet they do not benefit from them in anything?”"],[5167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned something and said: “That is at the time of the departure of knowledge.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge depart while we recite the Qur’an, teach it to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons until the Day of Resurrection?” He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, Ziyad! I used to consider you among the most knowledgeable men in Madinah. Are not these Jews and Christians reciting the Torah and the Gospel, yet they do not act upon anything from them?”"],[5168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This is the time of the departure of knowledge.” I said: “How, while among us is the Book of Allah, which we teach to our sons, and our sons will teach it to their sons?” He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, Ibn Labid! I did not think of you except as among the most intelligent of the people of Madinah. Do not the Jews and Christians have the Book of Allah, the Torah and the Gospel, yet they did not benefit from it in anything?”"],[5169,"A letter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, in it was: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Ziyad b. Jahwar. Peace be upon you, for I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no deity. To proceed: I remind you of Allah and the Last Day. To proceed: every religion practiced by the people will be removed except Islam, so know that.”"],[5170,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever has an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Ishmael, let him free one from Balʿanbar.”"],[5171,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent his companions, and they took captives from Banu al-Anbar, who were mukhaddramun and had already embraced Islam. Zubayb rode a she-camel of his, then went ahead of the people and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom! Your companions have taken captives from Banu al-Anbar, who are mukhaddramun and have already embraced Islam.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Do you have proof, O Zubayb?' He said: 'Yes.' Samura b. Amr testified, and Zubayb swore. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Return to Banu al-Anbar everything that belongs to them.' So everything was returned to them except my mother's zurbiyya. Sa'd said: 'The zurbiyya is a velvet cloth.' Zubayb came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom! Everything belonging to Banu al-Anbar has been returned to them except my mother's zurbiyya.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Do you know who took it?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'When the people attend the prayer, sit at the door of the mosque, and when you see the one who has it, hold on to him until he finishes the prayer, then settle between you and him.' He did so. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he turned to him and said: 'O Zubayb, O brother of Banu al-Anbar, what do you want with your captive?' Zubayb burst into tears and let the man go. He said: 'Good; we want Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the man: 'Do you have the zurbiyya of Zubayb's mother?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it left my possession.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Take off your sword for him and add some measures of food.' He did so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew near to Zubayb and passed his hand over his head until he brought it down to his navel. Zubayb said: 'I felt the coolness of the Prophet's ﷺ palm on my navel.' Then he said: 'O Allah, grant him pardon and well-being.' Then Zubayb departed with the sword and sold it for two young she-camels from the Prophet's ﷺ sadaqah. They bred with Zubayb until they reached a hundred and more."],[5172,"That Zinba' Abu Rawh found a slave of his with his slave-girl, so he cut off his penis and mutilated his nose. The slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'What made you do what you did?' He said: 'He did such and such.' The Prophet ﷺ said to the slave: 'Go, for you are free.'"],[5173,"That his grandfather 'chose a slave of his, then came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he freed him because of the mutilation.'"],[5174,"I heard Abu Jarwal Zuhayr b. Surad al-Jushami say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took us captive on the day of Hunayn, the day of Hawazin, and went to distribute the young men and the captives, I recited to him this poetry."],[5175,"He was a Bedouin man who, whenever he came to the Prophet ﷺ, brought only a gift or a present. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him in the market selling some goods, and he had not come to him, so he embraced him from behind with his palms. He turned and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and kissed his palms. He said: 'Who will buy the slave?' He said: 'Then you will find me, O Messenger of Allah, unsellable.' He said: 'But you are profitable with Allah.'"],[5176,"\"From his father, and his father was one of those who witnessed the tree. He said, 'I used to roast the red meat under the pots, or he said, 'about the pots,' when a caller called the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Verily, Allah prohibits you from eating the meat of donkeys.'\""],[5177,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the fasting of Ashura and said: \"Whoever is fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever is not fasting, let him complete the rest of his day.\""],[5178,"From her grandfather al-Zari', who was among the delegation of Abd al-Qays, he said: When we arrived in Madinah, we began to leap down from our mounts and kiss the hands and feet of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Mundhir al-Ashajj waited until he came to his saddlebag, put on his garment, then came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'You have two traits that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do I cultivate them, or has Allah created me with them?' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Rather, Allah has created you with them.' Al-Mundhir said: 'Praise be to Allah Who has created me with two traits that Allah and His Messenger love.' It is said that the name of al-Ashajj is A'idh b. Amr. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi mentioned it from Matar b. Abd al-Rahman with this chain. Al-Hadrami narrated to us from Mahmud b. Abdah from Abu Dawud."],[5179,"That he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned something. Al-Zibriqan said: O Messenger of Allah, should we proclaim it publicly? He said: 'No, O Zibriqan. Listen to Allah and His Messenger, and obey.' He said: Hearing and obedience are due to Allah and His Messenger."],[5180,"From Urwah: 'In the naming of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Sa'd b. Mu'adh b. al-Nu'man b. Imri' al-Qays b. Zayd b. Abd al-Ashhal.'"],[5181,"From Ibn Shihab: 'In the naming of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr, from al-Nabit, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Sa'd b. Mu'adh b. al-Nu'man b. Imri' al-Qays.'"],[5182,"About Muhammad ibn Ishaq,\"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr among the Ansar, then among the Banu Abdul Ashhal, Sa'd bin Mu'adh bin Nu'man bin Amr bin Quraysh bin Zaid bin Abdul Ashhal bin Jusham bin Harith bin Khazraj bin Amr bin Awf bin Malik bin Aws.\""],[5183,"I never heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that I knew it was true, and I never performed a prayer without talking to myself about other things until I finished it, and I never followed a funeral procession without talking to myself about other than what the deceased was saying and what was being said to him."],[5184,"Three qualities are in me: I never heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relate a hadith except that I believed him and knew it was true; I never attended a dying person except that I made myself attentive to what he was saying and what was being said to him; and I never performed a prayer without talking to myself about other things until I completed my prayer."],[5185,"The Prophet ﷺ sent for Sa'd b. Mu'adh regarding the affair of Banu Qurayzah. Sa'd came on a donkey whose legs almost touched the ground. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he said to his Companions: 'Stand up for your chief.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'These people have agreed to your judgment, so judge between them.' He said: I judge that their fighting men be killed and their women and children be taken captive. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'You have judged with the judgment of Allah and the judgment of the King.'"],[5186,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Sa'd b. Mu'adh came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is your chief.'"],[5187,"Sa'd b. Mu'adh ؓ was struck in his median vein on the day of the Trench. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set up a tent for him in the mosque so that he could visit him closely. He recovered until his wound began to heal. He said: O Allah, You know that the people whose fighting I loved most were those who denied Your Prophet, expelled him, fought him, and did what they did. I think You have put an end to the war between us and them. O Allah, if You have kept any fighting between us and them, then keep me alive to fight them. While he was one night, his wound burst open and blood flowed from it until it reached the tent next to him. He called out: O people of the tent, what is this coming to us from your direction? They looked and found Sa'd's wound had burst open, with blood gushing from it, and he died."],[5188,"Sa'd b. Mu'adh ؓ was struck on the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir, and his median vein was cut. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized it, but it became dusty and trembled, so he cauterized it a second time. Sa'd ؓ said: O Allah, do not take my soul until You cool my eyes from Qurayzah and al-Nadir."],[5189,"And he ﷺ remained with Banu Qurayzah until they asked him to appoint an arbiter between him and them, upon whose ruling they would submit. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Choose whomever you wish from my Companions, so that we may listen to his word.' They chose Sa'd b. Mu'adh, and the Messenger of God ﷺ approved of him, and they surrendered. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that their weapons be placed in a house, and he commanded that they be bound and fettered, so they were placed in the house of Usamah b. Zayd. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Sa'd b. Mu'adh, and he came on a Bedouin's donkey, whose saddle pad they claim was of palm fiber. A man from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal followed him, walking with him, exalting the rights of Banu Qurayzah, mentioning their alliance and what they had endured on the day of Bu'ath, and that they had chosen him over anyone else hoping for his compassion and tenderness toward them: 'So spare them, for they are an adornment and a number for you.' He said: That man spoke at length, but Sa'd did not respond to him at all until they drew near. Then the man said to him, 'Will you not reply to me with anything?' Sa'd said, 'By God, in God's cause I do not care about the blame of any blamer.' So the man left him and went to his people, having despaired of their being spared, and informed them of what he had said to him and what he had replied. Sa'd went on until he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said, 'O Sa'd, judge between us and them.' Sa'd ؓ said, 'I judge concerning them that their fighting men be killed, their captives be taken as spoils, their wealth be seized, and their women and children be taken captive.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Sa'd b. Mu'adh has judged among them with the judgment of God.' Some people claim that they submitted to the judgment of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ referred the judgment concerning them to Sa'd b. Mu'adh. They were brought out group by group, and their necks were struck. Huyayy b. Akhtab was brought out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'Has God disgraced you?' He said, 'You have prevailed over me, and I do not blame myself regarding you.' The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded, and he was taken out to the stones of the oil market, and his neck was struck—all of that before the eyes of Sa'd b. Mu'adh. They claim that Sa'd's wound had healed and closed with scar tissue over the healing. Then he supplicated, saying, 'O God, Lord of the heavens and the earth: there was no people on earth more hateful to me than a people who denied Your Messenger and expelled him. I think that You have ended the war between us and them. If there remains between us and them any fighting, then keep me alive to fight them for Your sake; and if You have ended the war between us and them, then open this place and make my death therein.' God, Blessed and Exalted, opened it, and indeed he lay down in the middle of the night, and they did not realize it until he died. And the wound did not cease flowing until he died, may God have mercy on him."],[5190,"Sa'd's mother began to say"],[5191,"Sa'd's mother, when his bier was carried while she wept for him"],[5192,"When Sa'd b. Mu'adh died, Abu Bakr wept and 'Umar ؓ wept, until Abu Bakr's weeping could be distinguished from 'Umar's weeping, and 'Umar's weeping from Abu Bakr's. I said to 'A'ishah, 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ weep?' She said, 'No, but he would clutch his beard ﷺ.'"],[5193,"The Messenger of God ﷺ departed from the funeral of Sa'd b. Mu'adh with his tears rolling down onto his beard and his hand on his beard."],[5194,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived at Dhu al-Hulayfah, the youths of the Ansar would meet him and inform him about their families. It was said to Usayd b. Hudayr, 'Your wife has died,' so he wept, and I was between him and the Prophet ﷺ. I said, 'Do you weep while you are a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ and have such precedence as you have attained?' He said, 'Is it not right for me to weep, when I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The pillars of the Throne shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh ؓ\"?'"],[5195,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'This is the one for whom the Throne moved, for whom the gates of heaven were opened, and whom seventy thousand angels attended. He was squeezed once, then it was relieved from him.'"],[5196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, the Throne has trembled for the death of Saad.\""],[5197,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The Throne of the Most Merciful shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh ؓ.'"],[5198,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ, while the bier of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was before them, say, 'The Throne of the Most Merciful, Exalted, shook for it.'"],[5199,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ, while the bier of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was before him, say, 'The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it.'"],[5200,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ, while the bier of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was before them, say, 'The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it.'"],[5201,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ, while the bier of Sa'd was before him, say, 'The Throne of the Most Merciful, Exalted is He, shook for it.'"],[5202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about Sa'd b. Mu'adh on the day he died, as he was being buried: “This is the righteous servant for whom the Throne of the Most Merciful shook, and for whom the gates of heaven were opened. He was squeezed, then Allah relieved him.”"],[5203,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.”"],[5204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while the funeral bier of Sa'd was placed down: “The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd.”"],[5205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sa'd.”"],[5206,"When they brought out the funeral bier of Sa'd, his mother cried out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Will your tears not cease and your grief depart? For your son is the first at whom Allah smiled and for whom the Throne shook.”"],[5207,"The hypocrites said concerning his light funeral, on account of his judgment regarding the Qurayza: that reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “No, but the angels are carrying it.”"],[5208,"When Sa'd b. Mu'adh was buried and we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he glorified Allah, and the people glorified Allah with him for a long time. Then he said “Allahu akbar,” and the people said “Allahu akbar” with him. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, why did you glorify Allah?” He said, “The grave squeezed this righteous man severely, until Allah relieved him by His mercy.”"],[5209,"A garment of fine brocade was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. People began touching it with their hands and marveling at it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Does this impress you? By Allah, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd in Paradise are finer than this.”"],[5210,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a silk garment. They began marveling at its softness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A handkerchief—or some of the handkerchiefs—of Sa'd in Paradise is softer than it, or better than it.”"],[5211,"“The Battle of the Trench was in Shawwal of the year five, and in it Sa'd b. Mu'adh ؓ died.”"],[5212,"Umayyah said to Sa'd: “Wait until midday when the people are heedless, then go and circumambulate.” While Sa'd was circumambulating the Ka'bah safely, Abu Jahl came to him and said, “Who is this circumambulating the Ka'bah safely?” Sa'd said, “I am Sa'd.” Abu Jahl said, “You circumambulate the House safely while you have sheltered Muhammad and his companions?” There was an exchange between them until Umayyah said to Sa'd, “Do not raise your voice over Abu al-Hakam, for he is the chief of the people of the valley.” Sa'd said to him, “By Allah, if you prevent me from circumambulating the House, I will cut off your trade route to Syria.” Umayyah kept saying to Sa'd, “Do not raise your voice over Abu al-Hakam,” trying to restrain him. Sa'd became angry and said, “Leave us alone. For I heard Muhammad ﷺ claim that he will kill you.” He said, “Me?” Sa'd said, “Yes.” He said, “By Allah, Muhammad does not lie.” When they went out, he returned to his wife and said, “Do you know what my Yathribi brother said?” He informed her, and Umayyah’s wife said, “Muhammad will not leave us alone.” When the call to arms came and they went out to Badr, she said to him, “Do you not remember what your Yathribi brother said to you?” He wanted not to go out, but Abu Jahl said, “You are one of the nobles of the people of the valley, so march with us for a day or two.” He marched with them, and Allah killed him."],[5213,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: “Sa'd b. 'Ubadah is given the kunya Abu Thabit.”"],[5214,"About Urwa Ibn Mas'ud Al-Thaqafi, he said, \"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Al-Aqaba, they were from the Ansar and then from the Banu Sa'idah bin Ka'b bin Al-Khazraj. Sa'd bin 'Ubadah bin Dulaym bin Harithah bin Khuzaymah, who was a captain and also witnessed the Battle of Badr.\""],[5215,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Sa'idah b. Ka'b: Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, and he was a captain."],[5216,"We went out to the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Aqabah, and the captain of Banu Sa'idah was Sa'd b. 'Ubadah and al-Mundhir b. 'Amr."],[5217,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr was with 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and the banner of the Ansar was with Sa'd b. 'Ubadah."],[5218,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in all the battles was the banner of the Muhajirun with 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and the banner of the Ansar was with Sa'd b. 'Ubadah."],[5219,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah died in Hawran in the land of Damascus in the year sixteen."],[5220,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah died two and a half years into the caliphate of 'Umar ؓ in Hawran in the land of Syria, and he was given the kunya Abu Thabit."],[5221,"While Sa'd was urinating standing, he leaned and died. The jinn killed him, and they said..."],[5222,"\"I feel something in my back.\" He did not remain long before he died, and the jinn lamented him, and they said..."],[5223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled by the oath with a single witness in rights (cases)."],[5224,"that they found in the book of Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled by swearing an oath with a single witness. The wording is from the hadith of Ibn Abi Uwais."],[5225,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Take charge of the zakat of Banu so-and-so, and be careful not to come on the Day of Resurrection with a young camel carrying it on your neck or shoulder, while it bleats.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, excuse me from it, so he excused him."],[5226,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a vow that his mother had made, so he ordered him to fulfill it."],[5227,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother has passed away and she had made a vow but did not fulfill it.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5228,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a vow his mother had made, then she died before fulfilling it. He said: \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5229,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah al-Anṣārī sought a ruling from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\" So let the Muslims follow this precedent in everything that was due from a person who died before fulfilling it."],[5230,"\"O Messenger of God, my mother died while she had a vow owed; will it suffice for her if I free a slave on her behalf?\" He said, \"Free a slave on behalf of your mother.\""],[5231,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah sought a ruling from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a debt upon his mother: a slave [was owed]. \"Should I free one on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[5232,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"My mother died while I was absent from her. Will anything benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then I call you to witness that my walled garden of Mikhraf is a charity on her behalf.\""],[5233,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"My mother died while she had a vow she had not fulfilled.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5234,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah sought a ruling from the Prophet ﷺ concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5235,"He informed him that Sa'd b. 'Ubādah sought a ruling from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a vow that was upon his mother, that he should fulfill it. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him \"to fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5236,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah sought a ruling from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a vow that had been upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that \"he should fulfill it.\""],[5237,"Sa'd b. 'Ubādah sought a ruling from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning a debt that had been upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fulfill it on her behalf.\""],[5238,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"On Friday there are five distinctive matters: on it God created Adam, on it Adam passed away, on it there is an hour in which no servant asks God for anything but He gives it to him, as long as he does not ask for a sin or severing of kinship, on it the Hour will be established, and there is no angel brought near, nor heaven, nor wind, nor mountain but that it is anxious about Friday.\""],[5239,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"This tribe of the Anṣār is a touchstone: love for them is faith, and hatred for them is hypocrisy.\""],[5240,"\"O Messenger of God, I would like you to pray over my mother.\" The Prophet ﷺ came to her grave, \"and prayed over her, though a month had already passed since her death.\""],[5241,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my mother has died; shall I give charity on her behalf?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Which charity is best?” He said, “Providing water.”"],[5242,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “My mother died without leaving a will and without giving charity. Will it be accepted if I give charity on her behalf?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Will it benefit her?” He said, “Yes, even with a burnt sheep’s shank.”"],[5243,"His mother died while he was absent, and he asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?” He said, “Yes.”"],[5244,"I said, “O Messenger of God, Umm Saʿd has died without leaving a will; shall I give charity on her behalf?” He said, “Yes.”"],[5245,"I said, “O Messenger of God, my mother used to give charity and spend from my wealth during her lifetime, and she has now died. If I give charity on her behalf or free a slave on her behalf, can we hope for something for her?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “O Messenger of God, guide me to a charity.” He said, “Provide water.” Al-Hasan said, “Saʿd’s water jars remained in Madinah after that.”"],[5246,"I said, “O Messenger of God, guide me to a charity.” He said, “Provide water.”"],[5247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “O Saʿd, shall I not guide you to a charity that is easy to maintain but has a great reward?” He said, “Of course.” He said, “Provide water.” So Saʿd provided water."],[5248,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a house, and I stood facing the door and asked permission to enter. He gestured to me to move back. Then I came and asked permission, and he said, “Is permission not sought except because of looking?”"],[5249,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “There is no one in charge of ten people but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, and nothing will release him except justice.”"],[5250,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “There is no commander of ten but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, and nothing will release him from his bonds except justice.”"],[5251,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There is no commander of ten but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in chains, and nothing will release him from the chain except justice.”"],[5252,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “There is no one who learns the Qurʾan and then forgets it except that he will meet God, Mighty and Exalted, as a leper.”"],[5253,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no one who reads the Qur’an and then forgets it except that he will meet Allah ﷻ while he is mutilated.”"],[5254,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Do not ask permission while facing the door.”"],[5255,"Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah when a man came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I found a man on the belly of my wife. Should I strike him with the sword?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What evidence is clearer than the sword?” Then he returned and said: “This, the Book of our Lord.” Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: “O Messenger of Allah, what evidence is clearer than the sword?” He said: “The Book of Allah and a witness there.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O company of the Anṣār, this is your chief. Jealousy has provoked him until he contradicted the Book of Allah.” A man from the Anṣār said: “O Messenger of Allah, Saʿd is a jealous man. He has never married a woman who was previously married because of his jealousy, and none of us is able to marry a woman he has divorced because of his jealousy.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Saʿd is jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah ﷻ is more jealous than me.” A man from the Anṣār said: “For what does Allah, Exalted is He, feel jealousy?” He said: “He feels jealousy for a man striving in the path of Allah whose family is approached unlawfully.”"],[5256,"On the authority of ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of the Muslims who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-ʿAqabah from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ b. ʿAmr, who was a captain, and he witnessed Badr.”"],[5257,"On the authority of ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ b. Abī Zuhayr b. Mālik b. Imriʾ al-Qays b. Thaʿlabah b. Kaʿb b. al-Khazraj b. al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj.”"],[5258,"On the authority of Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ, and he was a captain.”"],[5259,"On the authority of Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ.”"],[5260,"On the authority of ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred at Uḥud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Anṣār: Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ.”"],[5261,"About Ibn Shihab, \"Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar and then from the Banu Harith bin Al-Khazraj, Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi'.\""],[5262,"“O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, who is this?” He said: “This is the daughter of one who is better than me and you.” He said: “And who is better than me and you except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” Abū Bakr said: “A man who died during the Prophet’s ﷺ lifetime and took his seat in Paradise, while I and you remain.”"],[5263,"“We set out for the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, and the captain of Banū al-Khazraj was ʿAbd Allāh b. Rawāḥah and Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ.”"],[5264,"I heard Anas b. Mālik say: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf came to Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ al-Anṣārī. Saʿd offered to share half of his family and wealth with him, and he had two wives. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to him: “May Allah bless you in your family and wealth. Show me the market.” He went to the market and earned some profit from aqit (dried curd) and ghee. The Prophet ﷺ saw him after some days with a trace of yellow perfume on him and said: “Mahyam, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said: “I married a woman from the Anṣār.” He said: “What did you give her as a dowry?” He said: “The weight of a date stone of gold.” He said: “Hold a wedding feast, even if with one sheep.”"],[5265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between the Quraysh and the Anṣār, and he established brotherhood between Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf. Saʿd said to him: “I have wealth, so it is between me and you in two halves. I have two wives, so look at which of them you prefer, and I will divorce her, and when she becomes lawful, marry her.” He said: “May Allah bless you in your family and wealth. Show me the market.” He did not return until he came back with dates and aqit, then he increased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on him a trace of yellow perfume and said: “Mahyam?” He said: “I married a woman from the Anṣār.” He said: “What did you give her as a dowry?” He said: “The weight of a date stone of gold.” He said: “Hold a wedding feast, even if with one sheep.”"],[5266,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received Ibn Awf, he handed him over to Sa'd b. al-Rabi' and said, “This is your brother.” So he took him away, gave him supper, and spread bedding for him. When morning came, Sa'd went to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and greeted him. He said, “I am the best of the Ansar in wives and the best of the Ansar in gardens. Look at my two wives: whichever of them pleases you, I will divorce her for you, for her family will not disobey me. And look at whichever of my two gardens you wish, and take it.” But he accepted nothing from him."],[5267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Sa'd and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. He took him home to his family and said, “Choose whichever of my two wives you wish, and I will divorce her for you; and my wealth is yours, half and half.” 'Abd al-Rahman said, “May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth. Show me the market.” So they showed it to him, and he did not return until he had gained something. Then he married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him while he had traces of yellow perfume on him and said, “Mahyam?” He replied, “I married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date stone of gold.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.”"],[5268,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, may Allah have mercy on him, emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd. Sa'd had two gardens and two wives. Sa'd said to 'Abd al-Rahman, “Choose whichever of my wives you wish, and I will give her up for you; and choose whichever of my two gardens you wish.” He said, “I have no need of your wife or your garden. I did not become Muslim for this. Rather, show me the market.” So he showed him, while he had nothing. He would buy ghee, dried curd, hides, and things, then sell them, until he gathered something. Then he married and came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces of yellow perfume on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “'Abd al-Rahman, mahyam?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I married for a date stone of gold.” He said, “Then hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.” He prospered and his wealth increased."],[5269,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, may Allah have mercy on him, emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd. Sa'd had two gardens and two wives. Sa'd said to 'Abd al-Rahman, “Choose whichever of my wives you wish, and I will give her up for you; and choose whichever of my two gardens you wish.” He said, “I have no need of your wife or your garden. I did not become Muslim for this. Rather, show me the market.” So he showed him, while he had nothing. He would buy ghee, dried curd, hides, and things, then sell them, until he gathered something. Then he married and came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces of yellow perfume on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “'Abd al-Rahman, mahyam?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I married for a date stone of gold.” He said, “Then hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep.” He prospered and his wealth increased."],[5270,"“I do not know what they say, but would that what is in this chest of mine were coals.” When he died, they looked, and found in it a thousand or two thousand."],[5271,"Al-Harith al-Ghatafani came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, share with us the dates of Madinah.” He said, “Until I consult the Sa'ds.” So he sent for Sa'd b. Mu'adh, Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, Sa'd b. al-Rabi', Sa'd b. Khaythamah, and Sa'd b. Mas'ud, may Allah have mercy on them. He said, “I know that the Arabs have shot at you from a single bow, and al-Harith is asking you to share with him the dates of Madinah. If you wish to give him this year of yours until you consider your affairs afterward…” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it revelation from heaven, so submission is to Allah's command, or is it your own opinion or desire? Our opinion follows your desire and opinion. If you only intend to preserve us, by Allah, we have seen ourselves and them on equal footing: they do not get a single date from us except by purchase or hospitality.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There, you hear what they say.” They said, “You have acted treacherously, O Muhammad.” Hassan b. Thabit, may Allah have mercy on him, said…"],[5272,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab: “Among those who attended the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf: Sa'd b. Khaythamah, and he was a naqib.”"],[5273,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws: Sa'd b. Khaythamah.”"],[5274,"On the authority of 'Urwah: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf: Sa'd b. Khaythamah.”"],[5275,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq: “Among those who were martyred on the day of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar: Sa'd b. Khaythamah.”"],[5276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed at Quba' with Kulthum b. Hidm, the brother of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf; and it is also said that he stayed with Sa'd b. Khaythamah. He stayed among Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf on Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, and laid the foundation of their mosque. He left Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf and reached Friday among Banu Salim b. 'Awf, so he prayed Jumu'ah in the mosque in the valley floor. Ibn Ishaq said: “Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with Abu Ayyub and commanded the building of his mosque in that year.”"],[5277,"On the authority of 'Urwah: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws b. Jariyah: Sa'd b. Khaythamah.”"],[5278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I saw as if a mercy fell between Banū Sālim and Banū Bayāḍa.” They said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, should we move to its place? He said: “No, but bury in it.” So they buried their dead in it."],[5279,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Aws: Saʿd b. Khaythama b. al-Ḥārith b. Mālik b. Kaʿb b. al-Naḥḥāṭ b. Kaʿb b. Ḥāritha b. Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Imriʾ al-Qays b. Mālik b. al-Aws.”"],[5280,"“We set out in the pilgrimage in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the naqīb of Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf was Saʿd b. Khaythama.”"],[5281,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the expedition of Tabūk: “...until the Messenger of God ﷺ went on. I entered a walled garden and saw a trellis that had been sprinkled with water, and I saw my wife. I said: This is not fair—the Messenger of God ﷺ is in the scorching heat and hot wind while I am in shade and comfort. So I got up to a camel I used for irrigation, mounted it, and took some dried dates as provisions. My wife called out: Where to, O Abū Khaythama? I set out seeking the Messenger of God ﷺ until, when I was partway, ʿUmayr b. Wahb al-Jumaḥī caught up with me. I said: You are a bold man, and I know where the Prophet ﷺ is. I am a sinful man, so keep back from me until I am alone with the Messenger of God ﷺ. So ʿUmayr stayed back from me. When I came in sight of the army and the people saw me, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Be Abū Khaythama.” I came and said: I almost perished, O Messenger of God. I told him my story, and the Messenger of God ﷺ spoke well to me and prayed for me.”"],[5282,"\"He was named Noah, a grateful servant, because whenever he ate or drank, he praised Allah.\""],[5283,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and embraced Islam and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, grant my people what they have embraced Islam upon.\" \"So he did, and appointed me over them.\" Abu Bakr appointed me after the Prophet ﷺ, and 'Umar appointed me after Abu Bakr. I said to my people: \"There is no good in wealth whose zakat is not paid, so pay the zakat of honey.\" They said: \"How much do you think?\" I said: \"A tenth.\" So I took a tenth from them and brought it to 'Umar ؓ, and he sold it and placed it in the charities of the Muslims."],[5284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, when visiting Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ during the Farewell Pilgrimage, “O God, complete for my Companions their emigration, and do not turn them back on their heels.” But the unfortunate one, Saʿd b. Khawla — the Messenger of God ﷺ mourned for him because he died in Makkah."],[5285,"I heard my father say: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from residing in the land of the enemy (th-th-nāwah). Whoever stays in the lands of the kharāj has indeed committed thanāwah, and I dislike to stay."],[5286,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ about the earnings of a cupper, and he forbade him from it. He complained to him of need, so he said, “Feed it to your water-carrying camels.”"],[5287,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Saʿd b. ʿUthmān b. Khalda b. Makhad.”"],[5288,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Dīnār b. al-Najjār: Saʿd b. Suhayl b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal b. Ḥāritha b. Dīnār b. al-Najjār.”"],[5289,"Saʿd b. Abī Rāfiʿ: The Prophet ﷺ entered to visit me, and he placed his hand between my chest and my navel until I felt its coolness on my heart. Then he said: “You are a man with a heart ailment. Go to al-Ḥārith b. Kalada, for he is a man who practices medicine. Let him take five dates of ʿajwa of al-Madīna and crush them with their pits, then rub them on your chest.”"],[5290,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade cauterization and said: “I dislike hot water (or feverish heat).”"],[5291,"Six of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ collected the Qur'an, all of them from the Ansar: Ubayy b. Kaʿb, Muʿādh b. Jabal, Zayd b. Thābit, Abū Zayd, and Saʿd b. ʿUbayd."],[5292,"I presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ dates, and they were eating in front of him, pairing them up. The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade pairing dates."],[5293,"From Ibn Shihāb: In naming those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāma among the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿida, Saʿd b. Ḥimār, an ally of theirs."],[5294,"From ʿUrwa: In naming those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāma among the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿida, Saʿd b. Ḥāritha b. Lūdhān b. ʿAbd Wudd."],[5295,"From ʿUrwa: In naming those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāma among the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿida, Saʿd b. Ḥibbān, an ally of theirs from Balī."],[5296,"Saʿd b. Khawlī, mawlā of Ḥāṭib b. Abī Baltaʿa, and he is a man from Madhḥij."],[5297,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said one day: 'O Abu Bakr, come; O 'Umar, come. I have been commanded to make you two brothers by revelation sent down upon me from heaven. You are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise. Let each of you greet his companion and shake his hand.' Abu Bakr took 'Umar by the hand, and the Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said, 'He will be before him; he will die before him.' Then he said: 'O Zubayr, O Talhah, come. I have been commanded to make you two brothers. You are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise. Let each of you greet his companion.' They did so. Then he said: 'O 'Ali, come; O 'Ammar, come. I have been commanded to make you two brothers. You are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise. Let each of you greet his companion.' They did so. Then he said to Ubayy b. Ka'b and Ibn Mas'ud the like of that, and they did so. Then he said to Abu al-Darda' and Salman the like of that, and they did so. Then he said to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas and Suhayb the like of that, and they did so. Then to Abu Dharr and Bilal, the freedman of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, the like of that, and they did so. Then he said: 'O Usamah and O Abu Hind, come.' He was a cupper who used to cup the Prophet ﷺ and drink his blood. 'Come,' and he said to them the like of that. And to Abu Ayyub and 'Abdullah b. Salam the like of that, and they did so. Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[5298,"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his military expeditions. His mother was on her deathbed in Madinah. She was told, “Make a bequest.” She said, “Concerning what should I make a bequest? The wealth is Sa'd's wealth.” She died before Sa'd arrived. When Sa'd arrived, that was mentioned to him, and Sa'd said, “O Messenger of God, will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Yes.” Sa'd said, “The garden of such-and-such is a charity on her behalf,” for a garden he named."],[5299,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those of the Ansar who were martyred on the Day of Yamamah, then of the Aws, then of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf: Sa'id b. Rabi' b. 'Adi b. Malik.”"],[5300,"I heard Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani say: “I remember that I heard of the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was tending camels for my family at Kazimah.”"],[5301,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who were killed on the day of Ajnādayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays.”"],[5302,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq: “In the naming of those who were martyred among the Muslims on the day of al-Ṭāʾif, then from Quraysh, from Banū Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams: Saʿīd b. Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ.”"],[5303,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “There will be in my Ummah sinking, metamorphosis, and pelting.”"],[5304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rajab is a great month in which Allah multiplies the rewards. So whoever fasts for a day in Rajab, it is as if he has fasted for a whole year. And whoever fasts for seven days, the seven gates of Hell will be closed to him. And whoever fasts for eight days, the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him. And whoever fasts for ten days, Allah will grant him whatever he asks for. And whoever fasts for fifteen days, a caller will announce in the heavens: 'May Allah forgive what has passed for you, so start anew.' And whoever does more, Allah will increase it. And in Rajab, Allah carried Noah in the ark, so he fasted in Rajab and commanded his companions to fast. The ark set sail with them for six months, until they landed on Mount Judi. And Noah and those with him expressed gratitude to Allah. And on the day of Ashura, Allah split the sea for the children of Israel. And on the day of Ashura, Allah accepted the repentance of Adam and the city of Yunus. And in Rajab, Ibrahim ﷺ was born.\""],[5305,"that he asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"Give me [some] advise.\" He said, \"I advise you to be modest in front of Allah ﷻ just as you show modesty in front of a righteous man among your people.\""],[5306,"From Saʿīd b. ʿUbayd, who was called ‘the reciter’ in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. He had encountered an enemy and fled from them. Then ʿUmar said to him, “Would you like to go to Syria? Perhaps Allah will bless you.” He said, “No, except [to fight] the enemy from whom you fled.” He said: So he addressed them at al-Qādisiyyah and said, “Indeed, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, if Allah wills, and we will be martyred. So do not wash any blood from us, and do not shroud us except in the garment that was upon us.”"],[5307,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: He said: \"Whoever helps a warrior in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a slave in his contract of emancipation, Allah ﷻ will shade him in His shade on the day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[5308,"I used to suffer greatly from madhi (pre-seminal fluid) and I would often perform ghusl because of it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Wudu' is sufficient for you for that.\" Yazid added: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about what touches my garment from it?\" He said: \"A handful of water is sufficient for you; you sprinkle your garment with it where you see it touched.\""],[5309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among the rights of Friday are the siwak and the ghusl, and whoever finds perfume should apply some of it.\""],[5310,"Sahl b. Hunayf: \"O people, be suspicious of your own opinion, for by God, we never took hold of their legs for any matter that cut us off except that it led us smoothly to a matter we recognized, except this matter of yours, for it only increases in hardship and confusion. If only you had seen me on the day of Abu Jandal — had I found helpers against the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would have objected.\""],[5311,"Sahl b. Hunayf used to say, \"I have never seen anyone like the one who did not question his own judgment: We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ as pilgrims, and when we arrived in Makkah, he ordered us to turn it into an Umrah.\""],[5312,"From his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathmah, they both said: Habibah bt. Sahl was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, and he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I see him, and were it not for fear of God ﷻ, I would spit in his face.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Will you return to him his garden that he gave you as a dowry?' She said: 'Yes.' So he sent for him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated them. That was the first khul' in Islam."],[5313,"Turn to what you have turned to, O Abu Hazim. Shall I not tell you from my father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'That I pray the morning prayer and then sit in a gathering remembering God ﷻ until the sun rises is dearer to me than racing fine horses in the path of God ﷻ.'"],[5314,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sawwād: Sahl b. Qays b. Abī Kaʿb b. al-Qayn.\""],[5315,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Biʾr Maʿūnah from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Najjār: Sahl b. ʿĀmir b. Saʿd.\""],[5316,"From ʿUrwah: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāmah from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Sahl b. ʿAdī from Banū Tamīm, an ally of theirs.\""],[5317,"\"About Urwah, in regards to the identification of the person who witnessed the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , at Al-Aqaba, from the Ansar, and then from the Banu Najjar, Sahl ibn Atik.\" (Note: The translation may not be exact as the passage provided does not have context)"],[5318,"That he married seventy women, who either died or he divorced, and he saw nothing wrong with that."],[5319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should brandish a sword at his brother, for Satan may seize his hand and cause him to fall into a pit of the pits of Hell.”"],[5320,"He was in a gathering in which were his father, Abu Hurayrah, Abu Usayd, and Abu Humayd, and they discussed the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they mentioned that he gave the greeting of peace to his right and to his left."],[5321,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There is no one reciting the talbiyah except that what is to his right and left of stones and trees recites the talbiyah.”"],[5322,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Every people has a forerunner, and I am your forerunner at the Pond. Whoever comes to me at the Pond and drinks will never thirst, and whoever never thirsts will enter Paradise.\""],[5323,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the people of the chambers above them just as you see the brilliant star passing across the horizon, east and west, because of the superiority that exists among them.”"],[5324,"“I saw someone better than me wipe over them.”"],[5325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I will precede you to the Basin. Whoever comes to me will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst. Indeed, some people will come to me whom I will recognize, but then they will be prevented from reaching me.\""],[5326,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Dhū al-Ḥulayfah and there was a dead sheep with its leg raised. He said: “Do you consider this sheep insignificant to its owners?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this sheep is to its owners. If the world weighed as much as a mosquito’s wing in the sight of Allah, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it.”"],[5327,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to eat watermelon with fresh dates.”"],[5328,"And with his chain: I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when his front tooth was broken, his face was wounded, and his helmet was crushed on his head. I surely know who washed the blood from his face, who carried water to him, and what was placed on his wound until the blood stopped. Fatimah bt. Muhammad, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, was washing the blood from his face, and ʿAlī ؓ was carrying water to her in a shield. When she had washed the blood from her father’s face, she burned a mat until it became ash, then took some of that ash and placed it on his face until the blood stopped. Then he said that day: “God’s anger has intensified against a people who wounded the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then he paused for a while, then said: “O God, forgive my people, for they do not know.”"],[5329,"“Abū Usayd married and invited the Prophet ﷺ to his wedding feast. His wife served us and gave us nabīdh to drink that she had soaked overnight, and she served it to him.”"],[5330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Everything has a summit, and the summit of the Qurʾān is Sūrat al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it in his house at night, no devil will enter it for three nights, and whoever recites it in his house by day, no devil will enter it for three days.”"],[5331,"“The midday nap during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ was after the Friday prayer.”"],[5332,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour were sent like these two.\""],[5333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it.”"],[5334,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “If the world weighed as much as a mosquito’s wing in God’s sight, He would not give a disbeliever any of it.”"],[5335,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A man came to him and confessed in his presence that he had committed adultery with a woman whom he named. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for the woman and asked her about that, but she denied having committed adultery, so he flogged him the prescribed punishment and left her.'"],[5336,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The intention of a believer is better than his action, and the action of a hypocrite is better than his intention, and each acts according to his intention. When a believer performs an action, a light is kindled in his heart.”"],[5337,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will certainly follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until even if they entered a lizard’s hole you would follow them.” We said: O Messenger of God, the Jews and the Christians? He said: “Who else but the Jews and the Christians?”"],[5338,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There has been no heresy except that it was preceded by denial of destiny.”"],[5339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed heartily, so they said, “O Messenger of God, we have seen you laugh a laugh the like of which we have not seen you laugh.” He said, “Because of a people who will be brought to Paradise in iron chains.”"],[5340,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Some people open the door to good and close the door to evil, and some people open the door to evil and close the door to good. Glad tidings to those in whose hands Allah places they keys to good, and woe to those in whose hands Allah places the keys to evil.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 237)"],[5341,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Clapping is only for women, and glorification (tasbih) is for men.\""],[5342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they hasten to break the fast.\""],[5343,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The station of one of you in the path of God is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[5344,"There was a conflict among the Ansar, and the Prophet ﷺ came to them to make peace between them. The Prophet ﷺ came while Abu Bakr ؓ was leading the people in prayer, and he prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ."],[5345,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and he was describing Paradise until he reached it, then he said, \"In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.\" Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds to call upon their Lord in fear and hope, and they spend out of what We have provided them} up to His saying {as a reward for what they used to do}."],[5346,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"A morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5347,"He said: There was an old woman who used to cook on Friday the roots of chard and throw on it grains of barley. When we finished the Friday prayer, we would enter and eat."],[5348,"\"Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever is in the mosque waiting for the prayer is in prayer.'\""],[5349,"“We used to take a midday nap after Friday prayer.”"],[5350,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while some of us were teaching others. He said: “Praise be to God. The Book is one, and among you are the red and the black. Recite the Qur'an, recite the Qur'an, recite it before there come people who will pronounce it perfectly, as an arrow is made straight, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They seek its reward in haste and do not defer it.”"],[5351,"“I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his hands at all in supplication, whether on the pulpit or elsewhere. But I saw him do this” – and he pointed with his index finger and bent the middle finger against the thumb."],[5352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were reciting. He said, “Praise be to God. The Book of God is one, and among you are the white and among you are the black. Recite it before people recite it who will straighten it as an arrow is straightened. One of them will hasten his reward and not delay it.”"],[5353,"Two men differed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ about the mosque founded on piety. One said it was the mosque of Madinah, and the other said it was the mosque of Quba. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “It is this mosque of mine.”"],[5354,"“If I were to give you water from the well of Buda‘ah, you would dislike it, but by God, I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ water from it with my own hand.”"],[5355,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever has roots in Madinah, let him hold fast to them, and whoever does not have roots there, let him establish roots there. There will come upon people a time when one who has no roots there will be like one leaving it, passing through to elsewhere.”"],[5356,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, Suhayl ibn Bayda’ was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Suhayl ibn Bayda’,” and raised his voice twice or three times. Each time Suhayl answered him, so that the people heard the voice of the Messenger of God ﷺ and knew that he meant them. Those in front sat down, and those behind caught up, until when they had gathered, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, God forbids him from the Fire and makes Paradise obligatory for him.”"],[5357,"From Ibn Shihab, “In the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Suhayl ibn Rafi‘ ibn Abi ‘Amr. He and his brother had the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ as a date-drying ground.”"],[5358,"I heard al-Hasan say: The nobles of Quraysh gathered at the door of Umar ؓ, among them al-Harith b. Hisham, Abu Sufyan b. Harb, and Suhail b. Amr. Meanwhile, those slaves and freedmen from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ [were also present]. His permission came out, and he gave permission to Bilal, Suhaib, and their like, and left the others. Abu Sufyan said: 'I have never seen [anything] like today; he gave permission to these slaves and left us sitting at his door without granting us permission.' Suhail b. Amr, who was a wise man, said: 'O people, by God, I see what is in your faces. If you are angry, then be angry with yourselves. The people were called and you were called; they hastened and you delayed. By God, what they preceded you to of virtue is more severely missed by you than this door of yours over which you competed.' Al-Hasan said: 'God does not make a servant who hastens to Him like a servant who delays from Him.'"],[5359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever says: 'O Allah, I call You to witness, and I call to witness Your angels and the bearers of Your Throne, and I call to witness whoever is in the heavens and the earth that You are Allah; there is no god but You, alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger' — whoever says it once, Allah frees one-third of him from the Fire; whoever says it twice, Allah frees two-thirds of him from the Fire; and whoever says it three times, Allah frees all of him from the Fire."],[5360,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, every prophet has a wasi (legatee/trustee); who is your wasi? He was silent. Later he saw me and said: \"O Salman.\" I hastened to him and said: At your service. He said: \"Do you know who Musa's wasi was?\" I said: Yes, Yusha' b. Nun. He said: \"Why?\" I said: Because he was the most knowledgeable of them. He said: \"My wasi, the keeper of my secret, the best of those I leave after me, who fulfills my promise and pays my debt, is 'Ali b. Abi Talib.\" Abu al-Qasim said: His saying \"my wasi\" means he entrusted him with his family, not with the caliphate; and his saying \"the best of those I leave after me\" means from his household ﷺ."],[5361,"I entered upon Salman and saw his house was worn and shabby. Someone remarked to him about that, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me that your provision in this world should be like the provision of a rider.\""],[5362,"He said: I was a man from the people of Jayy, the city of Isfahan. While I was thus, Allah cast into my heart concern about the truth of the heavens and the earth. I went to a man who would not speak to people out of scrupulousness and asked him, 'Which religion is best?' He said, 'What do you have to do with this talk? Do you want a religion other than your father's religion?' I said, 'No, but I would like to know who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, and which religion is best.' He said, 'I do not know anyone upon this except a monk in Mosul.' So I went to him and stayed with him. He was straitened in worldly provisions; he would fast by day and stand in prayer by night. I worshipped as he worshipped, and I remained with him for three years. Then he died. I said, 'To whom do you entrust me?' He said, 'I do not know anyone among the people of the east upon what I am upon. You should go to a monk beyond the Jazirah, and convey my greetings to him.' So I went to him, conveyed his greetings, and told him that he had died. I remained with him for another three years. Then he died. I said, 'Where do you command me to go?' He said, 'I do not know anyone on earth upon what I am upon except a monk in Amorium, an old man. I do not know whether you will reach him or not.' So I went to him and stayed with him. He was a man with ample provision. When death came to him, I said, 'Where do you command me to go?' He said, 'I do not know anyone on earth upon what I am upon. But if you live to see a time when a man is heard of who comes forth from the house of Ibrahim ﷺ — and I do not think you will live to see him, though I had hoped to — then if you can be with him, do so, for he is upon the religion. Its signs are that his people will say he is a sorcerer, a madman, a soothsayer; that he eats gifts but does not eat charity; and that at the cartilage of his shoulders there is the seal of prophethood.' While I was thus, a caravan came from the direction of Madinah. I said, 'Who are you?' They said, 'We are from the people of Madinah. We are merchants who live by our trade. But a man has come forth from the house of Ibrahim ﷺ and came to us. His people fight him, and we fear that he may come between us and our trade. But he has taken possession of Madinah.' I said, 'What do they say about him?' They said, 'They say he is a sorcerer, a madman, a soothsayer.' I said, 'This is the sign. Direct me to your companion.' I went to him and said, 'Will you carry me to Madinah?' He said, 'What will you give me?' I said, 'I have nothing to give you except that I will be your slave.' So he carried me. When I arrived, he put me among his palm trees. I would water them as a camel waters, until my back and chest became calloused from that. I found no one who understood my speech until an old Persian woman came to water. I spoke to her, and she understood my speech. I said to her, 'Where is the man who has come forth? Direct me to him.' She said, 'He will pass by you in the morning when he prays the dawn prayer at the beginning of the day.' I went out and gathered dates. When morning came, I approached and brought the dates near to him. He said, 'What is this? Is it charity or a gift?' I gestured that it was charity. He said, 'Take it to these,' and his companions were with him. They ate, but he did not eat. I said, 'This is one sign.' The next day, I came with dates. He said, 'What is this?' I said, 'This is a gift.' He ate and called his companions, and they ate. Then he saw me trying to look at the seal. He recognized that, so he threw off his cloak. I began to turn him around and embrace him. He said, 'What is the matter with you?' He asked me, so I told him my story. He said, 'You stipulated to them that you are a slave. Purchase your freedom from them.' So the Prophet ﷺ purchased him on the condition that he bring them one hundred palm trees and forty uqiyahs of gold; then he would be free. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Plant.' So he planted. Then he said, 'Go and throw the bucket into the well. Then do not raise it until it rises, for when it is full, it will rise. Then sprinkle [the water] at their roots.' He did so, and the palms grew the fastest of growth. He said, 'Glory be to Allah! We have never seen the like of this slave. This slave has great importance.' People gathered around him. The Prophet ﷺ gave him gold nuggets, and in it were forty uqiyahs."],[5363,"He said to him: 'Shall I not urge you toward what you are upon?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Ribat (guarding the frontier) for one day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever dies as a murabit in the path of Allah, his deeds continue to be recorded for him, and he is protected from the trial of the grave.'"],[5364,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"When the heart of a believer trembles in the path of God, his sins fall away as the branches of a date-palm tree fall away.\""],[5365,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn, I love him; whoever I love, God loves him; and whoever hates them, I hate him; and whoever I hate, God hates him.\""],[5366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange.”"],[5367,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ is too shy, when a servant raises his hands to Him, to return them empty, with nothing in them.”"],[5368,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about locusts, so he said: “That is the most numerous of God's armies; I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.”"],[5369,"Salman led us in a prayer, then he went to a branch of a dry tree and shook it, and its leaves fell. Then he said, “Do you know why I did this?” They said, “No.” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in a prayer, then he went to a branch of a dry tree and shook it, and its leaves fell. Then he said, ‘When a servant performs ablution and does it well, then prays and does it well, his sins fall away just as the leaves of this tree fall away.’” The wording is that of the hadith of Abdan."],[5370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “On the Day of Resurrection, a man will come with so many good deeds that he thinks they will save him. Then another man will keep coming—someone he had wronged with an injustice—and it will be taken from his good deeds and given to the wronged one, until no good deed remains for him. Then someone else will come seeking recompense from him while he has no good deed left, so it will be taken from the sins of the wronged one and placed upon his own sins.”"],[5371,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You must observe the night prayer, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, a means of drawing near to God, the Exalted, an atonement for evil deeds, a deterrent from sin, and a repeller of disease from the body.”"],[5372,"Salman ؓ said: Hudhayfa used to narrate things that the Messenger of God ﷺ said in his anger to certain people. I said, “O Hudhayfa, either you stop, or I will write to Umar about you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am one of the children of Adam; any servant of my community whom I have cursed or insulted without just cause, I will make it a blessing upon him.”"],[5373,"“Your superiority over the rest of the Messenger of God ﷺ—meaning the Arabs—is that we do not marry your women.”"],[5374,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the head-covering."],[5375,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When speech proliferates, action is stowed away, tongues come together, hearts come to hate one another, and every relative severs his ties of kinship—then God curses them, makes them deaf, and blinds their sight.”"],[5376,"I asked Salmān al-Fārisī about the tashahhud. He said: “I will teach you as the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me. The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me the tashahhud word by word: ‘Greetings are for God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon God's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His messenger.’”"],[5377,"I set out when I came to al-Madāʾin, and there was a man wearing worn-out clothes, holding a red hide and rubbing it. I turned, and he looked at me and gestured with his hand: “Stay where you are, servant of God.” I stood still and asked those who were with me: “Who is this man?” They said: “This is Salmān.” He entered his house, put on white clothes, then came back, took my hand, shook it, and asked me about myself. I said: “Abū ʿAbd Allah, you have not seen me before, nor have I seen you, nor did you know me.” He said: “Indeed, by the One in whose hand is my soul, my spirit recognized your spirit when I saw you. Are you not al-Ḥārith b. ʿAmīra?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Spirits are assembled troops. Those among them that recognize one another in God become close, and those that do not recognize one another in God differ.’”"],[5378,"I was walking with Salmān along the bank of the Tigris. He said: “Brother of Banū ʿAbs, go down and drink.” I drank. Then he said: “Drink.” I drank. He said: “Has your drinking decreased the Tigris?” I said: “How could it possibly decrease?” He said: “Knowledge is like that: it is taken from, and it does not decrease.” Then he said: “Mount.” We passed by piles of wheat and barley, and he said: “Do you see this? It was opened for us and withheld from the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ. Was that good for us and bad for them, or bad for us and good for them?” I said: “I do not know.” He said: “But I know: it was bad for us and good for them. The Messenger of God ﷺ never ate his fill for three consecutive days until he joined God, Exalted is He.”"],[5379,"The first of this Ummah to embrace Islam was Ali ibn Abi Talib."],[5380,"Salman: “It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ: {That is because among them are priests and monks}.”"],[5381,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Four things are from the deeds of the living that continue for the dead: a man who leaves behind righteous offspring who supplicate for him, and their supplication follows him; a man who gives a perpetual charity after him, and he has its reward as long as it continues after him; and a man who teaches knowledge that is acted upon after him, and he has the like of the reward of those who act upon it without any decrease in the reward of those who act upon it.”"],[5382,"When death came to him, they noticed some anxiety in him, so they said: “What makes you anxious, O Abu ʿAbd Allah, when you have a precedence in good? You witnessed great conquests with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: “It grieves me that our beloved Muhammad ﷺ, when he parted from us, made a covenant with us, saying: ‘Let the provision of one of you be like that of a rider.’ That is what has grieved me.” So Salman's wealth was gathered and its value was fifteen dirhams."],[5383,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The most hungry of people on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were most full in this world. O Salman, this world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.”"],[5384,"And from Salman, they both said: The Messenger of God ﷺ took ʿAli ؓ by the hand and said: “This is the first to believe in me, and he is the first to shake my hand on the Day of Resurrection. This is the greatest ṣiddīq, and this is the Fārūq of this community, by whom truth is distinguished from falsehood. This is the leader of the believers, and wealth is the leader of the wrongdoer.”"],[5385,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to visit a man from the Ansar. When he entered upon him, he placed his hand on his forehead and said: “How do you find yourself?” But he gave no reply. It was said: “O Messenger of God, he is too distracted by pain to answer you.” He said: “Leave me alone with him.” So the women left his presence and left the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hand, and the sick man gestured: put your hand back where it was. Then he called out: “O so-and-so, what do you feel?” He said: “I feel good. Two persons have come to me, one black and one white.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Which of them is closer to you?” He said: “The black one.” He said: “Good is little and evil is much.” He said: “Then give me the benefit of a supplication from you, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, forgive the much and increase the little.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What do you see?” He said: “Good, may my father and mother be your ransom. The good is growing, and I see the evil fading away. The black one has withdrawn from me.” He said: “Which of your deeds was most in control of you?” He said: “I used to give water to drink.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Listen, O Salman, do you find anything objectionable in me?” He said: “Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. I have seen you in many situations, but I have never seen you in a state like today.” He said: “I know well what he is meeting: there is no vein in him but it is experiencing death on its own.”"],[5386,"Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays.” They left the Messenger of God ﷺ feeling heavy-hearted. I met them and said: “Why do I see you two heavy-hearted?” They said: “Because of a hadith we heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: ‘Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays.’” He said: “Did you not ask him about it?” They said: “We were in awe of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I said: “But I will ask him.” So I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Abu Bakr and ʿUmar met me, and they were heavy-hearted.” Then I mentioned what they had said. He said: “I did tell them that, but I did not place it where they placed it. Rather, a hypocrite is one who speaks while telling himself that he is lying, promises while telling himself that he will break it, and is entrusted while telling himself that he will betray.”"],[5387,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from putting ourselves to hardship for a guest by providing what we do not have."],[5388,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"No man performs the major ablution on Friday, purifies himself with whatever purification he can, anoints himself with some of his oil, or touches some perfume from his house, then goes out, and does not separate between two people, then prays what is decreed for him, then remains silent when the imam speaks, except that he is forgiven what is between that Friday and the next.\""],[5389,"When it was the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ, but his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said about that and had doubts about his affair: 'A man who died by his own weapon,' and they had doubts about some aspect of his affair. Salamah said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Khaybar, I said: 'O Messenger of God, permit me to recite war poetry for you?' The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted him. Then Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: 'Be mindful of what you say.' So I said:"],[5390,"On the authority of Jabir b. Abdullah and Salamah b. al-Akwa', a man from Aslam among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that they both said: We were on a military expedition when the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ says: \"Enjoy yourselves.\"'"],[5391,"We visited with the Messenger of God ﷺ a man who was feverish. I said, “O Messenger of God, I have never seen anything hotter than him.” He said, “Shall I not tell you of something hotter on the Day of Resurrection? Those two men, the two riders coming forward,” referring to two men from his companions at that time."],[5392,"“I gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ among those who gave allegiance under the tree.”"],[5393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered among the sacrificial camels in the year of Hudaybiyyah a camel that had belonged to Abu Jahl at the Battle of Badr, with a silver ring in its nose.\" Abdullah said: \"My father narrated it from him long ago, then later abandoned it.\""],[5394,"God forbid that I would do so without the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Go out to the desert, O Aslam, and smell the winds and dwell in the mountain passes.\" They said: \"We fear that this will change our status as emigrants.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You are emigrants wherever you are.\""],[5395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Amir b. al-Akwa: \"Dismount, O Amir, and let us hear some of your verses.\" So he dismounted while reciting rajaz poetry."],[5396,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and entered the mosque. He said: \"Catch him, for he is a spy.\" I caught him, being swift, and killed him, and the Prophet ﷺ gave me his belongings as a reward."],[5397,"Amir b. al-Akwa fought a duel with a man, struck him and killed him, but the sword struck Amir's leg. He began to say: \"I have killed myself,\" and he died. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"He will have two rewards.\""],[5398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not leave camels untethered; tie them securely, for the devils suckle them.\""],[5399,"In Ramadan during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whoever wished fasted and whoever wished broke his fast and fed a poor person as ransom, until this verse was revealed: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it}."],[5400,"A young man came and stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said at the top of his voice: O Messenger of God, what do you think of someone who did not leave any evil deed except that he did it, nor any sin except that he committed it, nor any arrow that was raised for him except that he seized it with his right hand, and someone whose sins, if distributed among the people of Madinah, would overwhelm them? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Have you become a Muslim?\" Or \"Are you a Muslim?\" He said: As for me, I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: \"Go, for God has replaced your evil deeds with good deeds.\" He said: O Messenger of God, and my treacheries and my immoralities? He said: \"And your treacheries and your immoralities,\" three times. Then the young man turned away saying: God is greater. I kept hearing him say takbir until he disappeared from me or was hidden from me."],[5401,"ʿAyyāsh b. Abī Rabīʿa, Salama b. Hishām, and al-Walīd b. al-Walīd b. al-Mughīra fled from the polytheists to the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAyyāsh and Salama were riding together on a camel, and al-Walīd was driving them. Al-Walīd's finger was injured, and he said:"],[5402,"From his two paternal uncles Yaʿlā and Salama, the two sons of Umayya, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabūk, and with us was a companion of ours from the people of Makkah. He fought a man, and the man bit his forearm, so he pulled it out of his mouth, and his two front teeth fell out. He went to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him for compensation. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"One of you goes to his brother and bites him like a stallion bites, or as a stallion bites, then comes to ask for compensation? There is no right for it.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ nullified it."],[5403,"He came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he and a group from his household and his children. They asked permission to enter upon him, and they entered. He said: \"Who are these?\" It was said to him: This is the delegation of ʿAnaza. He said: \"Excellent, excellent, excellent! What a good tribe ʿAnaza is: wronged but helped. Welcome to the people of Shuʿayb and the in-laws of Moses. Ask, O Salama, about your need.\" He said: I have come to ask you about what you have made obligatory upon me regarding camels, sheep, and goats. So he informed him. Then he sat near him. Then he asked his permission to leave, and he said to him: \"Leave.\" No sooner had he stood up than he said: \"O God, provide ʿAnaza with sufficiency, not bare sustenance and not extravagance.\""],[5404,"He was called Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfa. Just as the Prophet ﷺ adopted Zayd, Abu Hudhayfa married Salim — while considering him his son — to his niece, Fatima bt. al-Walid b. Utba. She was among the first Muhajirat and was then one of the most virtuous unmarried women of Quraysh. When God ﷻ revealed what He revealed concerning that — 'Call them by their fathers' — each of those adopted persons was called to his father; if his father was unknown, he was returned to his patron. Then Sahla bt. Suhayl, the wife of Abu Hudhayfa, who was from Banu Amir b. Luayy, came and said, 'O Messenger of God, we used to consider Salim a son. He used to enter upon me while I was in a loose garment, and we had only one house. What do you think?' He said to her, 'Suckle him, and you will become forbidden to him.'"],[5405,"He was with Abu Bakr ؓ on a rooftop in Ramadan while he was praying. He came to him and said, 'Will you not eat, O Caliph of the Messenger of God?' He gestured with his hand, and he did that twice. When it was the third time, he said, 'Bring me your food.' He ate, prayed two rak'ahs, then entered the mosque and the prayer was established."],[5406,"His father Salim came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a young boy. 'The Messenger ﷺ invoked blessing upon him and prayed for him, and he performed ablution from the leftover water of his ablution.' That day he had a forelock, and he had reached or nearly reached puberty."],[5407,"I sought the Prophet ﷺ but did not find him. I sat down and saw a group of five or six men, and a man was reconciling between them regarding wounds that had occurred. He made peace between them on the basis of sheep. When the people stood up, a man said: O Messenger of Allah. When I heard that, I said: Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah, three times. He said to me three times: \"Upon you be peace is the greeting of the dead.\""],[5408,"We were among the delegation that came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He pitched two tents for us near the house of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. Bilal used to come to us with our iftar, so we would say, 'O Bilal, has the Messenger of God ﷺ broken his fast?' He would say, 'Yes, I did not come to you until the Messenger of God ﷺ had broken his fast.' Then he would put it down and eat, and we would eat. And Bilal used to come to us with our suhur."],[5409,"Our delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they accepted Islam in the middle of Ramadan. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them, and they fasted with him for what they faced, but he did not order them to make up what they had missed."],[5410,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'It is enough of a betrayal that you tell your brother something he believes from you while you are lying to him.'"],[5411,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition, and we were afflicted with severe thirst. We complained of that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Is there any leftover water in a waterskin?\" A man brought him leftover water in a waterskin. The Prophet ﷺ dug a pit in the ground, placed a leather mat over it, put his palm on the ground, then said to the owner of the waterskin, \"Pour the water onto my palm and mention the name of God.\" He did so. Abu Layla said, \"I saw water springing from between the fingers of the Messenger of God ﷺ until the people drank and all were given water.\""],[5412,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I shall give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger love.\" Then he called Ali and gave it to him."],[5413,"From his brother Isa or al-Hakam or both of them, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it for fear of its retaliation is not one of us.\""],[5414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing house snakes. He said, \"When you see any of them in your dwellings, say: We adjure you by the covenant which Noah took upon you, and we adjure you by the covenant which Sulayman b. Dawud took upon you. If they return, then kill them.\""],[5415,"He passed by the Prophet ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ was praying a voluntary prayer, and he came across a verse mentioning the Fire, so he said, \"Woe to the people of the Fire! I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire.\""],[5416,"When the Prophet ﷺ came seeking support at al-Ta'if and entered upon her, she ordered a drink of sawiq for him and he drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O Ruqayqa, do not worship their taghut and do not pray to it.\" I said, \"Then they will kill me.\" He said, \"When they say that to you, say: My Lord is the Lord of this taghut. And when you pray, turn your back to it.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left them. The daughter of Ruqayqa said: My two brothers Sufyan and Wahb, the sons of Qays b. Aban, informed me. They said: When Thaqif embraced Islam, we went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"What happened to your mother?\" We said, \"She died in the state in which you left her.\" He said, \"Then your mother has indeed embraced Islam.\""],[5417,"\"I ate hubara meat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5418,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Ali came and sought permission. He lightly knocked on the door and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Safinah, open the door for him.\""],[5419,"From Safinah, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a bird, and he said, \"O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird.\" Then Ali ؓ came, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, be his ally.\""],[5420,"We set out intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ, and Wa'il b. Hujr was with us. An enemy of his seized him. The people were reluctant to take an oath, so I swore that he was my brother, and they released him. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and I informed him. He said, \"You have spoken the truth. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim.\""],[5421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best property of a man is a well-trained mare or a productive palm grove.\""],[5422,"\"I came to the Prophet, ﷺ , and he ordered me to give them an instruction. He said, 'When you return to your home, tell them to beautify their actions and order them to trim their nails. And they should not harm the udders of their livestock when milking them.'\""],[5423,"The Prophet ﷺ heard two men while they were exchanging insults, one of them getting angry, and his anger intensified. The Prophet ﷺ said, “I know a word which, if he said it, Satan would leave him.” So the man came to him and he said, “Say: I seek refuge in God from Satan.”"],[5424,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to him, “By our fathers and mothers, O Messenger of God, we hear a hadith from you but we are unable to transmit it exactly as we heard it.” He said, “If you do not make lawful what is unlawful and do not make unlawful what is lawful, and you get the meaning right, then there is no harm.”"],[5425,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon a dead young she-camel and said, “What harm would it have been to the owners of this if they had benefited from its hide?”"],[5426,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, the expedition of al-Muraysiʿ, and our battle cry was: “O Victorious One, kill, kill!”"],[5427,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on the migration, he was accompanied by Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), Amir ibn Fuhayrah, the servant of Abu Bakr, and 'Abdullah bin Uraiqit, who was guiding them on the way. When they passed by the tent of Umm Ma'bad al-Khuza'iyyah, she did not recognize him. He said to her, \"O Umm Ma'bad, do you have any milk?\" She replied, \"No, by Allah, the sheep are too weak.\" He then said, \"What about this sheep I see in the corner of the tent?\" She replied, \"It is a sheep that has been left behind by the flock because it is too weak.\" He asked, \"Will you allow me to milk her?\" She said, \"By Allah, no male has touched her; still, go ahead and try.\" He then stroked her back and her udder, prayed, and asked for a large bowl. He milked it until it was full and then gave his companions a drink, all drinking until satisfied. Then he milked her again, filling another bowl, which he left with her, and set off. When Umm Ma'bad's husband came home in the evening, he asked her, \"O Umm Ma'bad, what is this milk? There is no milking sheep in the house, and the flock is too weak.\" She replied, \"By Allah, a man who appeared to be blessed, with a handsome face, bright eyes, and a lovely voice passed by. His presence was calm when he spoke and dignified when silent. His words were well-arranged, and he was the best-looking and most handsome of his companions, surrounded by men who listened to his commands and followed his instructions promptly. When he forbade something, they adhered to his prohibition.\" The husband said, \"This is the description of the companion of Quraysh. If I saw him, I would follow him and strive to do so.\" They did not know in Mecca where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had headed until they heard someone calling out on Mount Abu Qubais."],[5428,"From ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Nabt: Salīṭ b. Thābit b. Waqsh.”"],[5429,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ saw a cloud and said: “O Messenger of God, we hoped that this cloud would rain on us.” He said: “It has been commanded to rain on Balīl”—meaning a valley called Balīl."],[5430,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The balance is in God’s hand: He raises some peoples and lowers others. And the heart of the son of Adam is between two of the fingers of the Most Merciful: if He wills, He causes it to deviate; and if He wills, He keeps it upright.”"],[5431,"From Sabrah b. Abī Fākih, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Satan sits in wait for the son of Adam on all his paths. He sits for him on the path of Islam and says: ‘Will you submit and leave your religion and the religion of your forefathers?’ Then he sits for him on the path of emigration and says: ‘Will you emigrate and leave your birthplace, so that you will be like a horse on a long tether?’ Then he sits for him on the path of jihad and says: ‘Will you fight, so that you will be killed, your wife will be remarried, and your wealth will be divided?’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Whoever does that, God has guaranteed him Paradise.’”"],[5432,"That his father came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked: “What are your children’s names?” He said: “ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā, Sabrah, and al-Ḥārith.” He said: “Do not name him ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā,” and he named him ʿAbd God. Then he said: “The best of names are ʿAbd God and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” And he supplicated for him and for his children, and they have remained in honor to this day. Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥajjāj b. al-Minhāl said: Khaythamah b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is one of them."],[5433,"Is our ʿUmrah for this year of ours or for ever and ever? The Messenger of God ﷺ interlaced his fingers, one over the other, and said, 'The ʿUmrah has been merged into the Hajj—twice. No, rather, for ever and ever.'"],[5434,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ during his illness and said, 'What do you think about a stray animal that comes to the watering trough of my camels—is there any reward for me if I give it water?' He said, 'Yes, in every warm liver there is a reward.'"],[5435,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us at al-Batha' and said: \"The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5436,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram for both Hajj and 'Umrah together, and I heard him say: \"The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5437,"He informed him that when the Messenger of God ﷺ left Makkah as an emigrant to Madinah, Quraysh offered a hundred she-camels to whoever brought him back. While I was sitting in the assembly of my people, a man came and said: By God, I have just seen three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad ﷺ. He said: I gestured to him to be quiet: they are only the sons of so-and-so seeking a stray animal of theirs. I stayed for a little while, then I got up, entered, and ordered that my horse be led to the bottom of the valley. I took out my weapons from behind my room, then took the divining arrows with which I sought omens and put on my armor. Then I brought out my divining arrows and drew omens, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. He said: I had been hoping to bring him back and take the hundred she-camels. So I mounted and followed his tracks. While my horse was galloping with me, it stumbled and I fell off. I took out my divining arrows and drew omens with them, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. But I refused anything except to follow him. I mounted my horse, and when the group appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me and its forelegs sank into the ground, and I fell off. It pulled out its forelegs and there followed them smoke like a staff. Then I knew that he had been protected from me and that he would prevail. So I called out to them: Wait for me, for by God I will not harm you, and nothing you dislike will come from me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What do you want? I said: Write for me a document that will be a sign between me and you. He said: Write for him, O Abu Bakr. He said: So he wrote a document for me, then threw it to me. He said: I returned and kept silent, and did not mention anything of what had happened until God ﷻ granted His Messenger ﷺ victory over Makkah and he had finished with Hunayn. Then I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ to meet him, with the document he had written for me. While I was making for him, I entered among a battalion of the Ansar's battalions, and they began prodding me with their spears, saying: Away with you, away with you, until I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was on his she-camel. I looked at his shin in the stirrup as if it were a palm pith. I raised my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of God, this is your document. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A day of fulfillment and kindness. So I became a Muslim, and I brought him the sadaqah of my wealth."],[5438,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed tamattu', and we performed tamattu' with him. It was said: O Messenger of God, is it for us or for ever? He said: For ever."],[5439,"I heard my father say: Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum came from the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us such-and-such. A man said, as if mocking: Did he not teach you how to defecate? He said: Indeed, by the One who sent him with the truth, he commanded us to lean on the left foot and set up the right."],[5440,"From Ibn Shihab: In naming those who were martyred with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Khaybar among the Ansar, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Murrah b. Suraqah b. Hubab. Thus said Ibn Shihab."],[5441,"Two men passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting and reminding. He said: Sit, for you are upon good. When the Messenger of God ﷺ got up and his companions dispersed from him, the two stood and said: O Messenger of God, you said to us: Sit, for you are upon good. Is that for us specifically or for the people generally? He said: No servant seeks knowledge except that it is an expiation for what came before."],[5442,"He used to say, \"Drink from the water dispenser of al-Abbas, for it is from the Sunnah.\""],[5443,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There is no ablution except from wind or sound.\""],[5444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever afflicts the crop of any of you from straying animals or birds, Allah records for him a reward for it.”"],[5445,"It is also said that he died in the year eighty-two."],[5446,"A woman entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “O ʿĀʾishah, do you know this one?” She said, “Yes.” Then she sang to her, and he said, “Satan has blown into her nostrils.”"],[5447,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bring out Abdullah b. Hanzalah from beneath the curtains of the Kaaba and kill him. Then he said, “No Qurayshi will be executed patiently after this.”"],[5448,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man behind him turning pebbles while he was in prayer and said, “Who turned the pebbles?” A man said, “I did.” He said, “That is your share of your prayer.”"],[5449,"I heard al-Sa'ib b. Yazid say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited a protective charm over me with the Opening of the Book, with a light spitting.”"],[5450,"The middle of al-Sa'ib's head was black while the rest of his head and his beard were white. I said to him, “O my master, by Allah I have never seen the like of this head of yours: this is white and this is black.” He said, “Shall I not inform you, O my son?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “I was with some boys playing when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me. I presented myself to him and greeted him. He said, ‘And upon you. Who are you?’ I said, ‘I am al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, the brother of al-Namir b. Qasit.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped my head and said, ‘May Allah bless you.’ He said, ‘By Allah, it will never turn white,’ or he said, ‘it will remain like this forever.’”"],[5451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed Hasan. Al-Aqra' b. Habis said to him, “I have ten children and have never kissed any of them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah will not have mercy on one who does not have mercy on people.”"],[5452,"Go to that old man and say to him: My uncle Isa b. Talhah says to you: Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? So I went to him and he said, “Yes, I saw him ﷺ, and I entered upon him with some boys who were with me. We found him eating dates from a basket, and with him were some people from his companions. He took a handful of those dates for us and wiped our heads.”"],[5453,"He came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon on the pulpit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Have you prayed?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Pray two rak'ahs and keep them brief.\""],[5454,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Perform ablution from the meat of camels, but do not perform ablution from the meat of sheep. Pray in the sheep pens, but do not pray in the camels' resting places.\""],[5455,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ at the stones of oil, and he was muffled with his hands, supplicating.\""],[5456,"\"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by a witness and an oath.\""],[5457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while my father was dying, and he spat on him from his head to his feet, and it was as if I were looking at the specks of saliva on his body."],[5458,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am the son of the 'Awatik.\""],[5459,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and I heard from his mouth to my ear. We carried wheat from al-Balqa' to Madinah and sold it, and we wanted to buy dates of Madinah, but they prevented us. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said to those who prevented us: \"Does it not suffice you that this food is cheap while these dates they are carrying are expensive? Leave them so they may carry it.\" Simuwayh was from al-Balqa', a Christian deacon who embraced Islam, and his Islam became good. He lived one hundred and twenty years."],[5460,"He was with al-Zinba' b. Salama al-Judhami, who became angry with him, so he castrated him and mutilated him. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke harshly to al-Zinba' and freed him from him. He said, \"Enjoin me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"I enjoin [you to be good to] every Muslim.\""],[5461,"When I came to Abu Mahdhura, he would ask me about a certain man, and when I came to that man, he would ask me about Abu Mahdhura. So I said to Abu Mahdhura: When I come to you, you ask me about so-and-so, and when I come to him, he asks me about you. He said: I, Abu Hurayrah, and so-and-so were in a house, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'The last of you to die will be in the Fire.' Then Abu Hurayrah died, then Abu Mahdhura died, then the man died."],[5462,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral. When he finished, he said, “Is there anyone here from the family of so-and-so?” He said, “No one stood up until he said it three times. Then a man stood up and said, ‘I, O Messenger of Allah.’ The Prophet ﷺ said to him, ‘What prevented you from standing up on the first two times? Indeed, I did not call you by name except for good. Indeed, so-and-so died as a man held captive by his debt.’ He said, ‘I saw his family and those who were grieving over his affair.’ He said, ‘They paid off what he owed until nothing remained against him.’”"],[5463,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever narrates a hadith from me while he thinks it is false is one of the liars.”"],[5464,"A man from Ashjaʿ asked the Prophet ﷺ: “My wife is breastfeeding and I dislike her becoming pregnant; should I practice coitus interruptus with her?” He said: “What is decreed in the womb will come to be.”"],[5465,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAbd b. Kaʿb b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Saʿd b. Zayd b. Mālik b. ʿAbd b. Kaʿb.”"],[5466,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Saʿd b. Zayd.”"],[5467,"He gifted to the Prophet ﷺ a sword from Najrān—or a sword from Najrān was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. When he came to him, he gave it to Muḥammad b. Maslama and said: “Strive with this in the path of God. When the necks of people differ, strike the stone with it, then enter your house and be a cast-off saddlecloth until a stray hand kills you or a decreed death comes to you.”"],[5468,"When the Prophet ﷺ was informed of his own death, he went out wrapped in worn garments until he sat on the pulpit. The people heard of it, and the people of the market attended the mosque. He praised God and extolled Him, then said: “O people, guard me concerning this quarter of the Anṣār, for they are my inner circle that I rely on and my trusted companions. Accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.”"],[5469,"“Salama b. al-Akwaʿ, whose kunya was Abū Iyās, and Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī died in the year seventy-four.”"],[5470,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: “Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī died in the year seventy-four.”"],[5471,"“I saw the beard of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī white in tufts.”"],[5472,"I saw Abu Sa'id al-Khudri dyeing with yellow."],[5473,"That she heard Umm 'Abd al-Rahman bt. Abi Sa'id narrate from her father that he said: The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wounded on the day of Uhud. Malik b. Sinan faced him and sucked the wound of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. \"Whoever would like to look at the one whose blood mixed with my blood, let him look at Malik b. Sinan.\""],[5474,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri is Sa'd b. Malik b. Sinan.\""],[5475,"I saw Abu Sa'id al-Khudri with his beard plucked out. I said: You are messing with your beard. He said: \"No. This is what I suffered from the wrongdoers of the people of Syria. They entered upon me at the time of al-Harrah and took whatever was in the house of goods or chattel. Then another group entered upon me and found nothing in the house, and they disliked to leave without anything.\" He said: \"Lay the old man down.\" So they laid me down, and each one of them took a tuft of my beard."],[5476,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will emerge from this nation people who pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game.\""],[5477,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ informed me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies.\""],[5478,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand and then is afflicted with leprosy, let him blame no one but himself.\""],[5479,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is praying, let him not raise his gaze to the sky lest his sight be snatched away.\""],[5480,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the Prophet, no lie. I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib. I am the most eloquent of the Arabs. Quraysh gave birth to me, and I grew up among Banu Sa'd b. Bakr. So how could solecism come to me?\""],[5481,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man should not look at the private part of a man, and a woman should not look at the private part of a woman. A man should not lie with a man, and a woman should not lie with a woman.\""],[5482,"He informed him that the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us your ransom, which drinks are lawful for us? He said: \"Do not drink from a naqir.\" They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us your ransom, do you know what a naqir is? He said: \"Yes, a trunk whose middle is hollowed out. And not from a dubba', and not from a hantama. Use a vessel with a tied mouth.\""],[5483,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \"When a man is uncertain in his prayer and does not know whether he has added or subtracted, let him prostrate twice while sitting.\""],[5484,"and to put his mouth to the mouth of the waterskin and drink from it.\""],[5485,"We were sitting at the door of the Messenger of God ﷺ, reminding one another, one citing a verse and another citing a verse, when the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us, his face looking as if pomegranate seeds had burst upon it. He said, \"O you people, is it with this that you were sent? Or is it this that you were commanded? Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\""],[5486,"that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Gabriel led me in prayer. He prayed Zuhr when the sun began to decline, prayed Asr when a thing's shadow was equal to its height, prayed Maghrib when the sun set, prayed Isha when the twilight disappeared, and prayed Subh when dawn broke. Then he led me on the second day: he prayed Zuhr when the shadow of everything was equal to it, prayed Asr when the shadow was twice its height, prayed Maghrib at the moment the sun set, prayed Isha until the first third of the night, and prayed Subh when the sun was about to rise.\" Then he said, \"Prayer is between these two times.\""],[5487,"that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The five prayers are expiations for what is between them.\""],[5488,"that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The five prayers are expiations for what is between them.\""],[5489,"On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The fast of Ramadan to Ramadan is an expiation for what is between them.\""],[5490,"that a crippled man—whose chronic illness was mentioned—was by the wall of Umm Sa'd. A woman became visibly pregnant. She was asked about it and said, \"It is from him.\" He was asked, and he confessed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be lashed with the stalks of a palm branch."],[5491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, like for like. Whoever increases or asks for an increase has committed usury.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, the owner of your dates buys one sa' for two sa's.\" So he sent for him, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, my dates are such and such, and they will not take them unless I give them more.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not do that.\""],[5492,"The Messenger of Allah commanded Bilal to put his fingers in his ears when calling the Adhan, and he said: \"It makes the voice louder.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 710)"],[5493,"Abd al-Rahman b. Ammar b. Sa'd al-Qaraz, the muezzin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal to insert his two fingers into his ears and said, \"It makes your voice higher.\""],[5494,"Abd al-Rahman b. Ammar b. Sa'd al-Qaraz, the muezzin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal to insert his two fingers into his ears and said, \"It makes your voice higher.\""],[5495,"Abd al-Rahman b. Ammar b. Sa'd al-Qaraz, the muezzin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal to insert his two fingers into his ears and said, \"It makes your voice higher.\""],[5496,"Abd al-Rahman b. Ammar b. Sa'd al-Qaraz, the muezzin of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded Bilal to insert his two fingers into his ears and said, \"It makes your voice higher.\""],[5497,"That the imam should pronounce the takbir seven times in the first [rak'ah] before the recitation, and pronounce the takbir five times in the second rak'ah before the recitation."],[5498,"So the Prophet ﷺ was informed, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded Bilal to give the call to prayer. The Ansari man cast it upon him: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah. Then he repeated: ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-salah; hayya 'ala al-falah, hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; la ilaha illa Allah."],[5499,"On the authority of his grandfather: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed a call to prayer for him.\""],[5500,"That the Prophet ﷺ, at whatever time he came to Quba', Bilal would give the call to prayer so that the people would know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had come and would gather to him. One day he came without Bilal being with him. The blacks of counsel looked at one another, so Sa'd climbed a palm branch of the call to prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"What prompted you to give the call to prayer, O Sa'd?\" He said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom. I saw you with few people and did not see Bilal with you, and I saw these blacks looking at one another and looking at you, so I feared for you from them, and so I gave the call to prayer.\" He said: \"You have done right, O Sa'd. If you do not see Bilal with me, then give the call to prayer.\" So Sa'd gave the call to prayer three times during the life of the Prophet ﷺ."],[5501,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to combine the two prayers, between Maghrib and 'Isha', in rain."],[5502,"That the Negus sent the Prophet ﷺ three short spears. The Prophet ﷺ kept one for himself, gave 'Ali ؓ one, and 'Umar one. Bilal used to walk with it in front of him and plant it in front of him on the two 'Ids, and he would pray toward it."],[5503,"That Muhallim b. Jaththamah al-Laythi killed a man from Ashja' after embracing Islam, and that was the first blood-money case that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adjudicated. He said: 'Uyaynah b. Badr spoke concerning the killing of the Ashja'i because he was a man from Ghatafan, and al-Aqra' b. Habis spoke on behalf of Muhallim b. Jaththamah because he was a man from Khindif. He said: The voices rose, and dispute and clamor increased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you not accept blood-money, O 'Uyaynah?\" He said: \"No, by Allah, until I bring upon his women the same war and grief that he brought upon my women.\" He said that twice or thrice. Then a man from Banu Layth called Mukaytil stood up with a shield in his hand and said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I find for what this one did at the dawn of Islam nothing but sheep that came to water: the first of them was shot and the last took flight. So establish a precedent today and change it tomorrow.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fifty in this our immediate time, and fifty when we arrive.\" That was during one of his journeys. And Muhallim was a tall, dark, robust man at the edge of the people. He said: They kept at him until he stood and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his eyes shedding tears and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the matter that has reached you has occurred, and I repent to Allah ﷻ, so ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in a loud voice: \"You killed him with your weapon at the dawn of Islam. O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim.\" He said that three times, each time saying: \"You killed him with your weapon at the dawn of Islam. O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim.\""],[5504,"When he died, his people buried him, but the earth cast him out three times, so they threw him among the outskirts of a mountain and heaped stones over him, and wild beasts ate him. Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: It reached me that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned that the earth had cast him out, he said: \"Verily the earth accepts one who is worse than him, but Allah wanted to show you the enormity of bloodshed in His sight.\""],[5505,"My father and grandfather narrated to me, and they had both witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said: The Messenger of Allah led us in Zuhr prayer, then sat in the shade of a tree. Al-Aqra' b. Habis and 'Uyaynah b. Badr stood up. 'Uyaynah b. Hisn demanded the blood of the Ashja'i, 'Amir b. al-Ahbat, who was that day the chief of Qays, while al-Aqra' b. Habis defended Muhallim b. Jaththamah for Khindif. They disputed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will take the blood-money: fifty in this journey of ours and fifty when we return.\" Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad. Sa'd b. Abi Dhubab al-Dawsi."],[5506,"He said to him: \"Admonish me concerning myself, may Allah have mercy on you.\" He said: \"When you stand for prayer, perform ablution thoroughly, for there is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and no faith for one who has no prayer.\" Then he said: \"When you pray, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, and abandon seeking many needs, for that is present poverty. And gather despair of what is in people's hands, for that is true wealth. And look at what you would apologize for in word and deed, and avoid it.\""],[5507,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of your community is best?\" He said: \"I and my contemporaries.\" We said: \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Then the second generation.\" I said: \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Then the third generation.\" I said: \"Then who, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Then there will come a people who swear but are not asked to swear, who testify but are not asked to testify, and who are entrusted but do not fulfill.\""],[5508,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what is due to the caliph after you?” He said, “To me? What is due to him is that he shows mercy to kinsfolk, acts equitably in fairness, and is just in apportionment.”"],[5509,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Where are your sons?” I said, “Here they are.” He said, “Bring them to me.” So I instructed my family and I dressed them in white shirts, then I brought them to him, and he said, “O God, I seek refuge in You for them from disbelief and misguidance, and from the poverty that befalls the children of Adam.”"],[5510,"On the authority of Ibn Shihāb, in naming those who attended Badr from Banū ʿĀmir b. Luʾayy, then from Banū Mālik b. Ḥasal: Saʿd b. Khawla."],[5511,"“Saʿd b. al-Aṭwal b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Khālid b. Wāhib b. ʿAttāb b. Mālik b. Saʿd b. Ṣaʿba b. ʿAdī b. ʿAwf b. Ghaṭafān b. Qays b. Juhayna b. Zayd, one of the inhabitants of Basra.”"],[5512,"That his brother died, leaving three hundred dirhams and dependents. I wanted to spend it on his dependents, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Your brother is detained by his debt, so settle it on his behalf.” I settled it on his behalf, then I said, “O Messenger of God, I have paid on his behalf except for two dinars which a woman claimed without any proof.” He said, “Give them to her, for she is truthful.”"],[5513,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what do you think of incantations we use for healing and medicines we use for treatment — do they avert God’s decree?” He said, “They are part of God’s decree.” This is how ʿUthmān b. ʿUmar narrated it from Yūnus, but the people disagreed with him, narrating it from Yūnus as the people narrated it from al-Zuhrī from Abū Khuzāma."],[5514,"“A she-camel belonging to al-Barāʾ b. ʿĀzib entered a man’s walled garden and caused damage in it, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that the owners of property are responsible for guarding it by day, and the owners of livestock are responsible for guarding them by night.”"],[5515,"“A she-camel belonging to al-Barāʾ b. ʿĀzib entered the people’s walled garden and damaged their crops, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that livestock owners are responsible for guarding their livestock by night, and crop owners are responsible for guarding their crops by day.”"],[5516,"On the authority of Ibn Shihāb: “In naming those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Saʿd b. Suwayd.”"],[5517,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who were killed on the day of the bridge of al-Madāʾin with Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal b. Zaʿūrāʾ: Saʿd b. Salāma.”"],[5518,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq: “In naming those who were killed on the day of the bridge from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then from Banū Zaʿūrāʾ: Saʿd b. Salāma.”"],[5519,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Saʿd b. Yazīd b. Khalda b. ʿĀmir b. Zurayq.”"],[5520,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of God, show me a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire. He was silent for a while, then he raised his head to the sky and looked, then said: “Worship God and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakāt, fast Ramaḍān, and love for people what you love to be brought to you, and whatever you dislike to be brought to you, leave people alone from it.”"],[5521,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of God, show me a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire. He was silent for a while, then he raised his head to the sky and looked, then said: “Worship God and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakāt, fast Ramaḍān, and love for people what you love to be brought to you, and whatever you dislike to be brought to you, leave people alone from it.”"],[5522,"He said: O Messenger of God, shall I recite the Qurʾān in three days? He said: “Yes, if you are able.” And he used to recite it thus until he died."],[5523,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he taught me: “When the earth is shaken,” “Say: O disbelievers,” and “Say: He is God, One,” and he taught me: “Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest.” And he said: “These are the enduring good deeds.”"],[5524,"I was among the first from the people of al-Ṭāʾif who came to the Prophet ﷺ. I left my family from al-Surāt in the morning, and I arrived at Minā at the time of ʿaṣr. I climbed the mountain, then descended, and came to the Prophet ﷺ and embraced Islam. He taught me “Say: He is God, One” and “When the earth is shaken with its quaking,” and he taught me these words: “Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest.” And he said: “These are the enduring good deeds.”"],[5525,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn, and I heard him say: 'Whoever rises at night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, then says \"Glory be to God\" one hundred times, \"Praise be to God\" one hundred times, \"There is no god but God\" one hundred times, and \"God is greatest\" one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven—except for bloodshed and [unlawful taking of] wealth, for that is not nullified.'"],[5526,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn, and I heard him say: 'Whoever rises at night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, then says \"Glory be to God\" one hundred times, \"Praise be to God\" one hundred times, \"There is no god but God\" one hundred times, and \"God is greatest\" one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven—except for bloodshed and [unlawful taking of] wealth, for that is not nullified.'"],[5527,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn, and I heard him say: 'Whoever rises at night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, then says \"Glory be to God\" one hundred times, \"Praise be to God\" one hundred times, \"There is no god but God\" one hundred times, and \"God is greatest\" one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven—except for bloodshed and [unlawful taking of] wealth, for that is not nullified.'"],[5528,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn, and I heard him say: 'Whoever rises at night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, then says \"Glory be to God\" one hundred times, \"Praise be to God\" one hundred times, \"There is no god but God\" one hundred times, and \"God is greatest\" one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven—except for bloodshed and [unlawful taking of] wealth, for that is not nullified.'"],[5529,"I witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ the Battle of Hunayn, and I heard him say, \"Whoever stands to pray at night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, and then says, 'SubhanAllah' (Glory be to Allah) one hundred times, 'Alhamdulillah' (Praise be to Allah) one hundred times, 'La ilaha illa Allah' (There is no god but Allah) one hundred times, and 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) one hundred times, his sins will be forgiven except for bloodshed and wealth, for they cannot be pardoned.\""],[5530,"From ʿUrwa, concerning the naming of those from the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from Banū Sawaad b. Kaʿb—and the name of Kaʿb is Zufar—Saʿd b. ʿUbayd b. al-Nuʿmān."],[5531,"From Ibn Shihāb: 'Concerning the naming of those from the Ansar who were present at Badr, then from al-Aws, then from Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf, then from Banū Umayya b. Zayd: Saʿd b. ʿUbayd b. al-Nuʿmān.'"],[5532,"I heard Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: 'Saʿd b. ʿUbayd is Abū Zayd, and he is the one who collected the Qur'an. His son ʿUmayr b. Saʿd was the governor of ʿUmar. He is Saʿd b. ʿUbayd b. al-Nuʿmān.'"],[5533,"I heard Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: 'Saʿd b. ʿUbayd was killed at al-Qādisiyya in the year sixteen.'"],[5534,"Saʿd b. ʿUbayd was called 'the reciter' during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5535,"From ʿUrwa: 'Concerning the naming of those from the Ansar who were present at Badr: Saʿd b. al-Nuʿmān b. Qays b. ʿAmr b. Zayd b. Umayya.'"],[5536,"A man complained to the Prophet ﷺ about Safwān b. al-Muʿattal, who used to recite this poetry. He said, 'O Messenger of God, Safwān has satirized me.' He ﷺ said: 'Leave Safwān alone, for Safwān has a foul tongue but a pure heart.'"],[5537,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ—I think he said on a journey—and we stopped at a place. He said to me, “O Saʿd, go to that she-goat and milk it.” I knew that place and that there was no she-goat there. I went to it and found a she-goat with full udders, and I milked it. He said, I do not know how many times. Then I entrusted it to someone and became busy with the departure, and the she-goat disappeared. The Messenger of God ﷺ thought I was slow and said, “Saʿd?” I said, O Messenger of God, the departure kept us busy and the she-goat disappeared. He said, “The she-goat was taken back by its Lord.”"],[5538,"Saʿd said: We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a march, and we had some dates with us. Ṣafwān said to me, “Feed me these dates.” I said, “They are few dates, and I do not feel safe that he will call for them. When they halt, you can eat with them.” He said, “Feed me, for hunger has nearly destroyed me,” and he mentioned what he had reached. I refused him that, so he hamstrung the camel that carried the dates. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “Tell Ṣafwān to leave.” He did not stay that night; he went around among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then came to ʿAlī ؓ and said, “Where should I go? Should I go to unbelief?” ʿAlī went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that, and he said, “Tell Ṣafwān to rejoin.”"],[5539,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever knows something, let him not conceal it. Whoever's eyes shed tears from fear of God, it is not lawful for him to enter the Fire ever, except as the fulfillment of the Most Merciful's oath. And whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in Hell.”"],[5540,"From ʿUrwa: In naming those who witnessed Badr, Saʿd, mawlā of Ḥāṭib b. Abī Baltaʿa."],[5541,"From Ibn Shihāb: In naming those who witnessed Badr, Saʿd, mawlā of Ḥāṭib b. Abī Baltaʿa."],[5542,"From Ibn Shihāb: In naming those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uḥud, Saʿd, mawlā of Ḥāṭib b. Abī Baltaʿa."],[5543,"From ʿUrwa: In naming those who witnessed Badr, Saʿd, mawlā of Khawlī, from Banū ʿĀmir b. Luʾayy."],[5544,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say about the poor Muslims: 'They will be led in procession as doves are led. It will be said to them, \"Stop for the reckoning.\" They will say, \"By God, we left nothing for which we could be held to account.\" God, exalted be He, will say, \"My servants have spoken truly.\" Then they will enter Paradise seventy years before the rest of mankind.'"],[5545,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The poor Muslims will come on the Day of Resurrection on their saddle frames. It will be said to them, \"Stop for the reckoning.\" They will say, \"You gave us nothing for which You could call us to account.\" Then they will enter Paradise forty years before the rest of mankind.'"],[5546,"He (Sa'd) did not store up in his house anything of need. So [the Prophet] sent him ten thousand [dirhams], and he took it and began dividing it into portions. His wife said to him, 'Where are you going with this?' He said, 'I am taking it to one who will trade for us with it.' He left nothing of it except a little. When what they had was gone, his wife said to him, 'Go to some of your companions whom you gave it to so they may trade for you, and take from their profits.' He kept putting her off and delaying her until that went on for a long time. Then he said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"If a houri were to look out with one of her fingers, every living being would find its scent.\" So I am leaving them for her. By God, you women are more deserving that I leave you for them than they are for you.'"],[5547,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'If a woman of the people of Paradise were to look down upon the people of the earth, she would fill the earth with the scent of musk and would extinguish the light of the sun and the moon.' By God, I would never choose you over them—and he pushed her in the chest, meaning his wife."],[5548,"'Uthman [asked]: \"Which of the people is most eloquent?\" They said, \"Sa'id b. al-'As.\""],[5549,"Abu Bakr ؓ asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was lying down on his bed wearing 'A'ishah's cloak—she was the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. He granted Abu Bakr permission while he was in that state. Then [Abu Bakr] brought his need to him, then departed. Then 'Umar asked permission, and he granted him permission while he was in that state. Then he brought his need to him, then departed. 'Uthman said: Then I asked permission to enter upon him, and he sat up and gathered his garments about him. I brought my need to him, then departed. 'A'ishah said, 'O Messenger of God, why did you not sit up for Abu Bakr and 'Umar as you sat up for 'Uthman?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Uthman is a bashful man, and I feared that if I granted him permission while I was in that state, he would not fully present his need.'"],[5550,"He informed him that Abu Bakr asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was lying down on his bed wearing 'A'ishah's cloak. He granted Abu Bakr permission while he was in that state. Abu Bakr brought his need, then departed. Then 'Umar asked permission while he was in that state, and he brought his need, then departed. 'Uthman said: Then I asked permission, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sat up and gathered his garments about him. Then I brought my need to him, then departed. 'A'ishah said, 'O Messenger of God, why did you not sit up for Abu Bakr and 'Umar as you sat up for 'Uthman?' He said, 'Uthman is a bashful man, and I feared that if I granted him permission while he was in that state, he would not present his need to me.'"],[5551,"He was called Dhakwan or Tahman. He had a slave, and he set half of him free. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'He becomes free in the portion you freed, and enslaved in the portion you kept.'"],[5552,"Abu Uhayhah, his grandfather, was ill when the Prophet ﷺ was sent. During his illness he said: 'Do not raise me from my bed; the son of Abu Kabshah will not turn toward me in Makkah.' His son, who was at his head, said: 'O God, do not raise him.'"],[5553,"O Messenger of God, permit me to castrate myself. He said to him: 'O 'Uthman, God has replaced monasticism for us with the easy, tolerant Hanifiyyah and with saying \"God is great\" on every hill. If you are one of us, then do as we do.'"],[5554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Go to them and present me to them.' Abu Bakr came to them and said, 'Who are the people?' They said, 'Banu Dhuhl b. Tha'labah.' He said, 'It is not you I want. You are the tails.' Then Daghfal stood up to him and said, 'And who are you?' He said, 'A man of Quraysh.' He said, 'Are you from Banu Hashim?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then from Banu Umayyah?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then you are one of the tails.' Then Abu Bakr returned to them a second time and said, 'Who are the people?' They said, 'Banu Dhuhl b. Shayban.' He said, 'It is you I want.' So he presented [the message] to them. They said, 'Wait until our elder so-and-so comes.' Khallad said: I think he said al-Muthanna b. Harithah. When their elder came, Abu Bakr ؓ presented [the message] to them. He said, 'There is war between us and the Persians. When we finish what is between us and them, we will return and consider what you say.' Abu Bakr said, 'Do you think that if you defeat them, you will follow us in our affair?' He said, 'We do not stipulate that for you upon ourselves, but when we finish what is between us and them, we will return and consider what you say.' When they met the Persians on the day of Dhu Qar, their elder said, 'What is the name of the man who called you to what he called you to?' They said, 'Muhammad.' He said, 'Then let it be your battle cry.' So they were granted victory over the people. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Through me they were aided.'"],[5555,"There used to be among our households a little weak, sickly, epileptic man. The neighborhood was startled only to find him upon a slave woman of their slaves, committing adultery with her. Sa'd mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Give him his prescribed punishment.” He said, “O Messenger of God, if we give him the prescribed punishment, we will kill him; he is weak.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Take for him a palm branch with a hundred twigs and strike him with it once.”"],[5556,"There used to be among our households an epileptic, weak man. The neighborhood was startled only to find him upon a slave woman of the slaves of the household, committing adultery with her. Sa'd raised his matter to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “Flog him with a hundred lashes.” He said, “O Messenger of God, he is weaker than that; if he were struck a hundred times he would die.” He said, “Then take for him a palm branch with a hundred twigs and strike him with it once.”"],[5557,"I performed the Hajj in the pre-Islamic era, and there I saw a man circumambulating the House while reciting rajaz, saying:"],[5558,"“My brother Sa'id was older than me.”"],[5559,"My brother Sa'id b. Hurayth told me—and he was a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ and an excellent brother—and I desired Kufa, so I asked his permission to sell the house, and he permitted selling it. He said to me, “O my brother, hold back your hand from the price of this house and do not reduce it by anything while you can, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whoever among you sells a house or real estate, it is not blessed for him unless he puts it into something like it.’” I believed my brother's words and sought blessing through the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I bought part of this house of ours from that, and God granted us through it something better."],[5560,"“Sa'id b. Yarbu' died in the year fifty-four, and he died at the age of one hundred twenty.”"],[5561,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Which of us is older?” He said, “You are greater and better than I, but I am older in years.” So he named him Sa'id and said, “The toothless one has gone.”"],[5562,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Four I will not grant protection to, whether in the sacred precinct or outside it: al-Huwayrith b. Nufayl, Maqis b. Dababah, Hilal b. Khatal, and 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh.” As for Huwayrith, 'Ali ؓ killed him. As for Maqis b. Dababah, a cousin of his killed him openly. As for Hilal b. Khatal, al-Zubayr killed him. As for 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh, 'Uthman b. 'Affan sought protection for him, and he was his foster brother. And there were two singing slave girls belonging to Miqyas who used to sing satires against the Messenger of God ﷺ; one of them was killed and the other fled and later accepted Islam."],[5563,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those of the Ansar who were killed on the Day of Yamamah, then of Banu Jahjabi: Sa'id b. Rabi' b. 'Adi b. Malik.”"],[5564,"He used to hunt sparrows at the well of Ihab, which belonged to them. Then ʿUbādah saw me after I had caught a sparrow, so he snatched it from me and said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade [hunting] what is between its two lava tracts.”"],[5565,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those who were killed on the day of Ajnādayn among the Muslims, then from Quraysh, from Banū Sahm: Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays.”"],[5566,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār: Saʿīd b. Qays b. Ṣakhr b. Ḥarām b. Rabīʿah b. ʿAdī b. Ghanm b. Kaʿb b. Salamah.”"],[5567,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, from Banū Ṣabīghah b. Zayd b. Mālik b. ʿAwf: Sahl b. Ḥunayf b. Wāhib b. Ḥakīm b. Thaʿlabah b. Majdaʿah b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAmr.”"],[5568,"He is called Bukhruj b. Ḥanash b. ʿAwf b. ʿAmr b. ʿAwf."],[5569,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Ṣabīghah b. Zayd: Sahl b. Ḥunayf.”"],[5570,"“ʿAlī ؓ prayed over Sahl b. Ḥunayf and said the takbīr over him six times.”"],[5571,"“He was a Badrī.”"],[5572,"Ali performed the funeral prayer for Sahl b. Hunayf and said the takbir six times."],[5573,"Ali ؓ performed the funeral prayer for Sahl b. Hunayf and said the takbir six times."],[5574,"Sahl b. Hunayf died in Kufa in the year thirty-eight."],[5575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever asks God for martyrdom sincerely from his heart, God will bring him to the stations of the martyrs even if he dies on his bed.”"],[5576,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not be harsh on yourselves, for those before you were destroyed only by their harshness on themselves. You will find their remnants in monasteries and hermitages.”"],[5577,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “With the first blood shed of a martyr, all his sins are forgiven except debt.”"],[5578,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever witnesses a believer being humiliated and does not help him, though able to do so, God will humiliate him before all witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5579,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed 'umrah, he said while on the road: “If we looked at every fat camel and slaughtered it and ate it, so that they would see our strength.” 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: “O Messenger of God, rather call for the people's provisions and then invoke blessing in them, for God ﷻ will bless them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ did that, and then said: “When you arrive, perform ramal in the first three circuits so that they see your strength.”"],[5580,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed 'umrah, he said while on the road: “If we looked at every fat camel and slaughtered it and ate it, so that they would see our strength.” 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: “O Messenger of God, rather call for the people's provisions and then invoke blessing in them, for God ﷻ will bless them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ did that, and then said: “When you arrive, perform ramal in the first three circuits so that they see your strength.”"],[5581,"My father said: “My son, I saw us on the day of Badr: one of us would point his sword at the head of a polytheist, and his head would fall from his body before the sword reached it.”"],[5582,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man's freed slave is his brother and his paternal cousin.”"],[5583,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque and prays in it—meaning the mosque of Quba—it is equal to an 'umrah.”"],[5584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever comes to the mosque of Quba and prays in it, it is as if he performed an 'umrah.\""],[5585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs ablution properly and then enters Masjid Quba and prays four units of prayer in it, then that is equivalent to freeing a slave.\""],[5586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then prays two rak'ahs in the mosque of Quba, it is as if he performed an 'umrah.\""],[5587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum' ten good deeds are written for him; whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu llāh' twenty good deeds are written for him; and whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu llāhi wa barakātuh' thirty good deeds are written for him.\""],[5588,"ʿAlī came to Fāṭimah ؓ on the day of Uḥud and said, \"Hold this sword of mine, for I have done well in striking with it today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you did well in fighting with it, then ʿĀṣim b. Thābit, Sahl b. Ḥunayf, and al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah did well too.\""],[5589,"\"They brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a crippled man who had committed adultery, so they struck him with a palm branch bearing leaves or with a bunch of palm leaves.\""],[5590,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade two kinds of dates: al-Juʿrūr and the kind called al-Ḥubayq.\" He said: People used to select the worst of their dates and give them as charity, so the verse was revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]} (2:267)."],[5591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the collection of charity, and a man brought clusters of this sakhil (inferior dates) and put them down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, \"Who brought this?\" For whenever anyone came, he would pour out what he had brought. Then the verse was revealed: {O you who have believed, spend from the good things which you have earned and from that which We have produced for you from the earth. And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]} (2:267). On that day he also forbade taking al-Juʿrūr and the kind called Ibn al-Ḥubayq in charity. Al-Zuhrī said: \"They are two kinds of dates of Madinah.\" ʿAbbād said: Sufyān said: \"Al-sakhil is al-shīṣ (worthless dates).\""],[5592,"A man fell ill until he became skin and bones. A slave girl entered to visit him, and he had intercourse with her. He became distressed about his sin. The people came to visit him, and he said, \"Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me, for I have committed adultery with a woman unlawfully, so let him carry out the prescribed punishment on me and purify me.\" They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, \"If he is carried to you, his bones would disintegrate, and if he is flogged, he would die.\" He said: \"Take a hundred palm branches and strike him with them once.\""],[5593,"Allah, glorified be He, said: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]} (2:267). He said: \"It is al-Juʿrūr and the kind called Ibn Ḥubayq.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade taking these two in charity."],[5594,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"None of you should say 'My soul has become wicked (khabuthat nafsī),' but let him say 'My soul has become disinclined (laqisat nafsī).'\""],[5595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of you should say 'My soul has become wicked (khabuthat nafsī),' but let him say 'My soul has become disinclined (laqisat nafsī).'\""],[5596,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"None of you should say 'My soul has become wicked (khabuthat nafsī),' but let him say 'My soul has become disinclined (laqisat nafsī).'\""],[5597,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until when he was at al-Kharrār, he entered some water to wash, and he was a fair-skinned man. ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah passed by him and said, \"Never have I seen, as on this day, the beauty of anything, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.\" Sahl did not remain but that he was struck down. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him and said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? Whom do you suspect in this?\" They said, \"ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah.\" So he summoned ʿĀmir and called for a vessel containing water. He ordered ʿĀmir to wash his face in the water, the extremities of his hands, his knees, and the extremities of his feet. Then the Prophet ﷺ took the upper portions of ʿĀmir's waist-wrapper and its inner side and immersed them in the water. Then he poured the vessel over Sahl's head and tilted the vessel from behind him. Sahl was released, with no harm upon him."],[5598,"By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, a secluded maiden in her chamber — or he said, a young woman in her chamber. He said: He was struck down until he could not raise his head. He said: That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Do you suspect anyone?\" They said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah, except that ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah said to him such-and-such.\" He said: So he summoned him and summoned ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah, and said, \"Glory be to Allah! For what reason does one of you kill his brother? When he sees something from him that pleases him, let him supplicate for blessing for him.\" He said: Then he ordered him, and he washed for him. He washed his face, the outer part of his palms, his elbows, his chest, the inner side of his waist-wrapper, his knees, and the extremities of his feet in the vessel, their outer sides. Then he ordered it to be poured over his head, and he tilted the vessel from behind him. I think he said: And he ordered him, and he sipped from it several sips. Then he ordered him, and he stood up and departed with the riding party."],[5599,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyāṭī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Umāmah b. Sahl b. Ḥunayf, that he said: ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah saw Sahl b. Ḥunayf washing himself and said, \"By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.\" So Sahl b. Ḥunayf was struck down, by Allah, unable to raise his head. He said, \"Do you suspect anyone for him?\" They said, \"We suspect ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah, became angry with him, and said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? Wash for him.\" So ʿĀmir washed for him his face, his hands, his elbows, his knees, the extremities of his feet, and the inner side of his waist-wrapper in a bowl. Then he poured it over him, and Sahl departed with no harm upon him."],[5600,"That ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah, the brother of the Banū ʿAdī b. Kaʿb, saw Sahl b. Ḥunayf while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Kharrār washing himself, and said, \"By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.\" So Sahl was struck down. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you attend to Sahl b. Ḥunayf? He cannot raise his head.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you suspect anyone in this?\" They said, \"Yes, ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah passed by him while he was washing himself and said, 'By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah, became angry with him, and said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? Wash for him.\" So ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah washed for him, and Sahl departed with the riding party with no harm upon him."],[5601,"By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. So Sahl was struck down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought, and it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you attend to Sahl b. Ḥunayf? By Allah, he cannot raise his head.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you suspect anyone in this?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah passed by him while he was washing himself and said, 'By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, ever, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah, became angry with him, and said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? If you do not invoke blessing, wash for him.\" So ʿĀmir washed for him, and Sahl departed with the riding party. Ibn Shihāb said: The washing that we found our scholars practicing is that a man is brought to the one who helps his companion, with a bowl containing water, and he holds it raised from the ground. The one who helps inserts his right hand into the water and pours it over his face, one pour into the bowl. Then he inserts his left hand into the water and washes his right hand, one pour into the bowl. Then he inserts his right hand and washes his left hand, one pour up to the elbows. Then he inserts both hands into the water and washes his chest, one pour into the bowl. Then he inserts his left hand, scoops water, and pours it over the back of his right palm, one pour into the bowl. Then he inserts his left hand and pours it over the elbow of his right hand, one pour into the bowl, while it is in his hand up to his neck. Then he does the like of that with the elbow of his left hand. Then he does the like of that with the back of his right foot, from the bases of the toes, and the left similarly. Then he inserts his left hand and pours it over the back of his right knee. Then he does with the left the like of that. Then he immerses the inner side of his right waist-wrapper. Then the one in whose hand is the bowl stands up with the bowl and pours it over the back of his right knee. Then the one in whose hand is the bowl stands up with the bowl and pours it over the head of the afflicted one from behind him. Then he turns the bowl over onto the face of the ground from behind him."],[5602,"Never have I seen, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. So he was struck down until he could not pray from the severity of the pain. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, so the Prophet ﷺ summoned him, became angry with him, and said, \"You have killed him. For what reason does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing?\" The Prophet ﷺ ordered a bucket of water and said, \"Wash him with it.\" So he washed, and he went out with the riding party."],[5603,"By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, ever, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. So Sahl was struck down with it. The Messenger of Allah was approached, and it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you attend to Sahl b. Ḥunayf? By Allah, he cannot raise his head.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you suspect anyone in this?\" They said, \"Yes, ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah passed by him while he was washing himself and said, 'By Allah, never have I seen, as on this day, ever, nor the skin of a secluded maiden.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned ʿĀmir, became angry with him, and said to him, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother and not invoke blessing? Wash for him.\" So ʿĀmir washed, and Sahl departed with the riding party."],[5604,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Muḥammad b. Abī Umāmah b. Sahl b. Ḥunayf, that he heard his father say: Sahl b. Ḥunayf washed himself at al-Kharrār, and he took off a cloak that was upon him while ʿĀmir b. Rabīʿah was looking. He said: He was a fair-skinned man with beautiful skin. So ʿĀmir said to him, \"Never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a virgin.\" Sahl fell ill on the spot, and his illness became severe. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was approached and informed that Sahl had fallen ill and that he would not be departing with you. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him, and Sahl informed him of what had happened with ʿĀmir. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? Indeed, the evil eye is real. Perform ablution for him.\" So ʿĀmir performed ablution for him, and Sahl departed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with no harm upon him."],[5605,"That he was with the Prophet ﷺ in one of his military expeditions. He passed by a pool and washed himself in it, and he was a man of good physique. A man from the Anṣār passed by him and said, \"Never have I seen, as on this day, nor the skin of a secluded maiden,\" out of admiration for his form. So he was struck down and carried as a stretcher-bearer's burden to the Prophet ﷺ. He asked him, and he informed him of what the Anṣārī had said. He said, \"So-and-so passed by me and said such-and-such.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What prevents one of you, when he sees from his brother something that pleases him, regarding himself or his property, from invoking blessing upon him? For indeed, the evil eye is real.\""],[5606,"It was as if the creation of a secluded maiden. So I was struck down and became feverish. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"For what reason does one of you kill his brother? When something of his brother pleases him, let him supplicate for blessing.\" And the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to wash his face, his hands, the edge of his waist-wrapper, and his knees, then he drank from it and poured it over him. So he departed with the people."],[5607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Asʿad b. Zurārah to visit him during an illness that afflicted him from the thorn, and he cauterized him on his shoulder, then he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"An evil dead man for the Jews! They will say, 'His companion treated him, but it did not benefit him.'\""],[5608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Asʿad b. Zurārah, who had an illness called the thorn, and he cauterized him on his shoulder. Then he died. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"An evil dead man for the Jews! They will say, 'His companion treated him; did it not benefit him?'\""],[5609,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his room, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared from a private part of the house and looked, and he had a comb with him. He said: \"If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would have come so that I could insert this into your eyes. Permission is only to restrain the gaze.\""],[5610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the poor of the people of Madinah and attend their funerals when they died. A woman from the people of al-'Awali died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When she is present, inform me.\" They came to inform him but found him sleeping, and part of the night had passed, so they disliked waking him and feared for him the darkness of the night and the creatures of the earth. They took her away. When morning came, he asked about her. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we came to inform you but found you sleeping, so we disliked waking you and feared for you the darkness of the night and the creatures of the earth.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked to her grave and prayed over her, saying four takbirs. The wording is that of the hadith of 'Uthman."],[5611,"A man among us fell ill until he became skin over bone. A slave girl entered upon him to visit him, and he fell upon her. He said to the people who were visiting him: \"Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for I have fallen upon a woman unlawfully, so let him carry out the punishment on me to purify me.\" They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then they said: \"By Allah, if he were carried to you, his bones would crumble, and if he were struck, he would die.\" He said: \"Take for him a hundred branches of a date-palm stalk and strike him with one blow.\""],[5612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid in Makkah; before him she had been married to 'Atiq b. 'A'idh al-Makhzumi. Then he married 'A'ishah in Makkah; he did not marry any virgin besides her. Then he married in Madinah Hafsah bt. 'Umar; before him she had been married to Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi. Then he married Sawdah bt. Zam'ah; before him she had been married to al-Sakan b. 'Amr, the brother of Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy. Then he married Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan; before him she had been married to 'Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh al-Asadi, of Asad Khuzaymah. Then he married Umm Salamah bt. Abi Umayyah, whose name was Hind; before him she had been married to Abu Salamah b. 'Abd al-Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza. Then he married Zaynab bt. Jahsh; before him she had been married to Zayd b. Harithah. Then he married Maymunah bt. al-Harith. He took Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith b. Abi Dirar of Banu al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah as a captive during his expedition in which he destroyed Manat, the expedition of al-Muraysi'. He also took Safiyyah bt. Huyayy b. Akhtab of Banu al-Nadir as a captive. They were both among what Allah granted him as spoils, and he allotted shares to them. He took Rayhanah of Banu Qurayzah as a concubine, then freed her, and she joined her family and veiled herself while she was with her family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced al-'Aliyah bt. Zabyan, and he separated from the sister of Banu 'Amr b. Kilab, and he separated from the sister of Banu al-Jawn al-Kindiyyah because of a whiteness that was in her. Zaynab bt. Khuzaymah al-Hilaliyyah died while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive. It reached us that al-'Aliyah bt. Zabyan married after Allah made his wives unlawful to remarry, and she married a cousin of hers from her people and bore children among them."],[5613,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who approaches his wife and emits madhi (pre-seminal fluid). He said: \"He should wash his private part and perform wudu'.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about what touches the garment from it?\" He said: \"He should locate the spot and wash it.\""],[5614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever helps a warrior in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a slave in his contract of emancipation, Allah will shade him in His shade on the day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[5615,"The people of al-'Aliyah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we must have gatherings.\" He said: \"Then fulfill the right of gatherings.\" They said: \"And what is the right of gatherings?\" He said: \"Remembering Allah often, guiding the way, and lowering the gaze.\""],[5616,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about madhi (pre-seminal fluid). He said: \"Wudu' is sufficient for you for it.\" He said: \"What should I do about what touches my garment?\" He said: \"Take a handful of water and sprinkle it on your garment where you see that it touched.\""],[5617,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was coming out of one of his houses, dragging his cloak, saying: \"The people will reach Sal'; then a time will come upon Madinah when a traveler will pass by some of its outskirts and say: 'This was once inhabited,' because of the length of time and the obliteration of traces.\""],[5618,"Sahl b. Hunayf said on the day of Siffin: \"O people, be suspicious of personal opinion in religion, for I have seen us when we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ — and had we been able to oppose him, we would have — yet we never placed our swords on our shoulders for any matter except that it became easy for us, leading to a matter we recognized, other than this matter of ours. And I have seen us on the day of Abu Jandal; had we been able to reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we would have rejected it.\""],[5619,"From Sahl b. Hunayf: \"Be suspicious of personal opinion in religion, for I have seen us when we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ...\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[5620,"From Sahl b. Hunayf: \"O people, be suspicious of personal opinion in religion, for I have seen us when we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ...\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[5621,"\"...that I would reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would reject it. By God, we have never placed our swords on our shoulders for any matter except that it led us smoothly to a matter we recognized, except this matter of yours.\""],[5622,"\"Be suspicious of personal opinion in religion. I have seen myself on the day of Abu Jandal; had we been able to reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ, we would have rejected it.\" And God and His Messenger know best."],[5623,"\"...that I would reject the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would reject it, and he was better than me and nobler.\" He said: \"Abu Jandal came to the Messenger of God ﷺ as a Muslim, while his father was a disbeliever, so the Messenger of God ﷺ returned him to his father, who bound him; then he came again and he returned him.\""],[5624,"That he said on the day of Siffin: \"O people, be suspicious of yourselves, for I have seen us on the day of Hudaybiyyah — had we seen any fighting, we would have fought them.\" So Umar said: \"O Messenger of God, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in the Fire?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then why should we accept humiliation in our religion and return when God has not yet judged between us and them?\" He said: \"O Ibn al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of God, and He will never abandon me.\" So he turned away in anger and did not remain patient until he went to Abu Bakr and said: \"Are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in the Fire?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then why should we accept humiliation in our religion and return when God has not yet judged between us and them?\" He said: \"O Ibn al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of God, and God will never abandon him.\" Then Surah al-Fath was revealed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sent for Umar and recited it to him. He said: \"O Messenger of God, is it indeed a victory?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[5625,"Sahl b. Hunayf and Qays b. Sa'd were at al-Qadisiyyah when a funeral procession passed by them and they stood up. It was said to them, \"It is only one of the local people.\" They said, \"A funeral procession passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ and he stood up. It was said, 'It is the funeral of a Jew.' He said, 'Is it not a soul?'\""],[5626,"\"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything about the Haruriyyah?\" He said: \"I will tell you what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I will not add anything to it. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he struck with his hand and said: 'From here — and he gestured with his hand — a people will emerge who recite the Quran but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will pass through Islam as an arrow passes through its target.'\""],[5627,"\"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything about the Khawarij?\" He said: \"I heard him say, and he gestured with his hand toward Iraq: 'From among them a people will emerge who recite the Quran but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will pass through religion as an arrow passes through its target.'\""],[5628,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said with his hand: \"A people will emerge from the direction of the east with shaved heads.\""],[5629,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything about Madinah? He said: I heard him say, \"It is a sacred sanctuary, secure; it is a sacred sanctuary, secure.\""],[5630,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, while gesturing with his hand toward Madinah, \"It is a sacred sanctuary, secure.\""],[5631,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about Madinah, and he said, \"A secure sanctuary, a secure sanctuary.\""],[5632,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ as pilgrims, so we entered the state of ihram for Hajj. When we arrived in Makkah, he ordered us to turn it into an Umrah."],[5633,"We passed by a stream and I entered it and bathed, and I came out with a fever. News of that reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"Tell Abu Thabit to seek refuge in God.\" I said to him, \"O my master, are incantations effective?\" He said, \"No, except from three things: the evil eye, fever, and a bite.\""],[5634,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' in Damascus. He told me that there was a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He was a solitary man who rarely sat with people; he was always praying, and when he finished, he engaged in glorifying God, declaring His oneness, and magnifying Him until he returned to his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda', and he greeted us. Abu al-Darda' said to him, \"A word that benefits us, by God, and does not harm you.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military detachment, and I was among them. A man came and sat in the gathering where the Messenger of God ﷺ was, and he said to a man beside him, 'If only you had seen us when we met the enemy! So-and-so thrust at so-and-so, and he said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth!\" What do you think?'\" He said, \"I think he has nullified his reward.\" Another man said, \"I see no harm.\" They argued about that until the Messenger of God ﷺ heard it, and he said, \"Glorified be Allah! There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\" Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that and kept saying, \"You heard this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He kept saying, \"Yes,\" until I said—while he was lifting his head to him—\"He will surely mount his knees [out of eagerness].\""],[5635,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' in Damascus. He told me that there was a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He was a solitary man who rarely sat with people; he was always praying, and when he finished, he engaged in glorifying God, declaring His oneness, and magnifying Him until he returned to his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda', and he greeted us. Abu al-Darda' said to him, \"A word that benefits us, by God, and does not harm you.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military detachment, and I was among them. A man came and sat in the gathering where the Messenger of God ﷺ was, and he said to a man beside him, 'If only you had seen us when we met the enemy! So-and-so thrust at so-and-so, and he said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth!\" What do you think?'\" He said, \"I think he has nullified his reward.\" Another man said, \"I see no harm.\" They argued about that until the Messenger of God ﷺ heard it, and he said, \"Glorified be Allah! There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\" Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that and kept saying, \"You heard this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He kept saying, \"Yes,\" until I said—while he was lifting his head to him—\"He will surely mount his knees [out of eagerness].\""],[5636,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' in Damascus. He told me that there was a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He was a solitary man who rarely sat with people; he was always praying, and when he finished, he engaged in glorifying God, declaring His oneness, and magnifying Him until he returned to his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda', and he greeted us. Abu al-Darda' said to him, \"A word that benefits us, by God, and does not harm you.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military detachment, and I was among them. A man came and sat in the gathering where the Messenger of God ﷺ was, and he said to a man beside him, 'If only you had seen us when we met the enemy! So-and-so thrust at so-and-so, and he said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth!\" What do you think?'\" He said, \"I think he has nullified his reward.\" Another man said, \"I see no harm.\" They argued about that until the Messenger of God ﷺ heard it, and he said, \"Glorified be Allah! There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\" Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that and kept saying, \"You heard this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He kept saying, \"Yes,\" until I said—while he was lifting his head to him—\"He will surely mount his knees [out of eagerness].\""],[5637,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' in Damascus. He told me that there was a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He was a solitary man who rarely sat with people; he was always praying, and when he finished, he engaged in glorifying God, declaring His oneness, and magnifying Him until he returned to his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda', and he greeted us. Abu al-Darda' said to him, \"A word that benefits us, by God, and does not harm you.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military detachment, and I was among them. A man came and sat in the gathering where the Messenger of God ﷺ was, and he said to a man beside him, 'If only you had seen us when we met the enemy! So-and-so thrust at so-and-so, and he said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari youth!\" What do you think?'\" He said, \"I think he has nullified his reward.\" Another man said, \"I see no harm.\" They argued about that until the Messenger of God ﷺ heard it, and he said, \"Glorified be Allah! There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\" Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that and kept saying, \"You heard this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He kept saying, \"Yes,\" until I said—while he was lifting his head to him—\"He will surely mount his knees [out of eagerness].\""],[5638,"My father was one of the companions of Abu al-Darda'. He told me that there was a man there from the Ansar, a devoted worshipper who kept to himself and hardly ever finished his worship, called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He would pass by Abu al-Darda' and stop by him, and Abu al-Darda' would say, 'Tell us a hadith that benefits us and does not harm you.' So he told him, and one day he said to him, 'A military detachment went out, and in it a man from Banu Ghifar fought. He struck a man from the polytheists, then said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari!\" They returned and told about the words of the Ghifari. Some of the Muslims said, \"His reward is nullified,\" while others said, \"Not at all,\" until that reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\"' He said, 'Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that.'"],[5639,"My father was one of the companions of Abu al-Darda'. He told me that there was a man there from the Ansar, a devoted worshipper who kept to himself and hardly ever finished his worship, called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He would pass by Abu al-Darda' and stop by him, and Abu al-Darda' would say, 'Tell us a hadith that benefits us and does not harm you.' So he told him, and one day he said to him, 'A military detachment went out, and in it a man from Banu Ghifar fought. He struck a man from the polytheists, then said, \"Take it, and I am the Ghifari!\" They returned and told about the words of the Ghifari. Some of the Muslims said, \"His reward is nullified,\" while others said, \"Not at all,\" until that reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"There is no harm in being rewarded and praised.\"' He said, 'Abu al-Darda' was delighted by that.'"],[5640,"My father was one of the companions of Abu Darda, and he told me that there was a man from the Ansar who was devout and ascetic. He was constantly engaged in worship and was known as Ibn Hanzaliyya. He used to pass by Abu Darda and stop to speak to him, saying, \"Abu Darda, narrate to us a beneficial Hadith that will not harm you.\" So he narrated to him that one day they went on a secret mission and a man from the Banu Ghifar tribe fought alongside them. He struck one of the polytheists and then said, \"Take it, I am from the Ghifar tribe.\" They reported this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by attributing it to the Ghifari. Some Muslims said that his reward was nullified, while others disagreed until this matter reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He said, \"There is no harm in him receiving a reward and being praised.\" Abu Darda was pleased with this."],[5641,"I heard Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party, and they met the enemy. A man from Banu Ghifar attacked and said, 'Take it, and I am the young Ghifari brave!' A man said, 'His reward has become void.' This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'There is no harm that he be rewarded and praised.'"],[5642,"From Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah: They marched with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and they prolonged the march until evening, and the time of prayer came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A horseman came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I went ahead of you until I ascended such-and-such a mountain, and there I found Hawazin with all their people, their women, their livestock, and their sheep, gathered at Hunayn.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, 'That is the spoil of the Muslims tomorrow, if Allah wills.' Then he said, 'Who will guard us tonight?' Anas b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said, 'I will, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Ride,' so he mounted a horse of his and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Face this mountain pass until you are at its top, and do not be taken by surprise from your direction tonight.' When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to his place of prayer and prayed two rak'ahs, then said, 'Have you sensed your horseman?' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we have not sensed him.' He called for the prayer, and while praying, the Messenger of Allah kept turning toward the mountain pass until he finished his prayer and said the salam. Then he said, 'Rejoice, for your horseman has come.' We began looking through the gaps in the trees in the pass, and there he was, coming until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'I went until I was at the top of this pass, where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me. When morning came, I looked out over both passes and saw no one.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Did you dismount last night?' He said, 'No, except to pray or to relieve myself.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'You have made it obligatory, so no matter what you do after this, it will not harm you.'"],[5643,"No, by Allah, I will not ask anyone for anything after what Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah told me. He said: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when 'Uyaynah b. Badr al-Fazari and al-Aqra' b. Habis al-Tamimi came to him and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for something. He called Mu'awiyah, may Allah have mercy on him, and ordered him with something I do not know what it was. Mu'awiyah came carrying two sheets. He threw one of the sheets to 'Uyaynah—and he was the more forbearing of the two men—so he took it and tied it to his turban. He threw the other to al-Aqra' b. Habis, who said, 'What is in it?' He said, 'In it is what you commanded.' He said, 'What a bad envoy of a people I am if I come to them with a sheet I carry, not knowing what is in it, like the sheet of al-Mutalammis!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was facing a man, talking to him, and when he heard his words, he took the sheet and opened it, and it contained a hobbled camel. He said, 'Where is the owner of this camel?' They searched but did not find him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fear Allah regarding these beasts: eat them fat and ride them sound.' Then he went on until he entered his house, and I was with him. He began saying, as if displeased, 'Whoever asks people despite having enough is only increasing the embers of Hell.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the meaning of having enough?' He said, 'That you know that his family has what suffices them for their morning or evening meal.'"],[5644,"Sahl said: 'Advance to your place of prayer so that Satan does not cut off your prayer.' And I do not tell you except what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5645,"I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw people gathered with an old man narrating to them. I said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah.' I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever eats meat should perform ablution.'"],[5646,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are assisted because of them. Whoever ties a horse in the way of Allah, his spending on it is like one who extends his hand with charity without withholding it.'"],[5647,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When one of you prays toward a sutrah, let him draw near to it so that Satan does not cut off his prayer.'"],[5648,"He heard Sahl b. Abi Hathmah say: 'Abd Allah b. Sahl was found slain in a well or pit of the wells or pits of Khaybar. His brother 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl and his paternal uncles Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah, the two sons of Mas'ud, came to the Prophet ﷺ. 'Abd al-Rahman went to speak, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The eldest, the eldest.' So Muhayyisah spoke and mentioned the killing of 'Abd Allah b. Sahl. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we found 'Abd Allah b. Sahl slain, and the Jews are a people of disbelief and treachery, and they are the ones who killed him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Will you swear fifty oaths and thus be entitled to your companion or the blood of your companion?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how can we swear about what we did not witness or see?' He said, 'Then the Jews will absolve themselves to you with fifty oaths.' They said, 'How can we accept the oaths of a polytheist people?' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid the blood money from his own resources. Sahl said, 'A young she-camel from it kicked me.'"],[5649,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to the kharras (estimators): 'Take and leave a third; if you do not leave—or he said, find—then leave a fourth.'"],[5650,"That Abdullah bin Sahl and Muḥayṣah bin Masʿūd came to Khaybar with a need, and they separated among its palm trees. Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, so his brother, the Prophet's ﷺ cousin, Abdullah bin Sahl, and the sons of his uncle, Muḥayṣah and Ḥuwayṣah bin Masʿūd, came to the Prophet ﷺ. Abdullah bin Sahl started to speak and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Start with the most important matters,\" meaning to make the major issue the first one. And Abdullah bin Sahl was older than his companions, so they spoke about the killing of their companion. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You deserve your killer or your companion by fifty oaths among them.\" They said, \"They are a disbelieving people.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By Allah, I wish I had your killing.\" Sahl said, \"I encountered a she-camel of theirs and it ran away with me in their marsh.\""],[5651,"Some people of the Ansar went out, and a man among them was killed. This was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Your proof?' They said, 'We have no proof.' He said, 'Their oaths?' They said, 'In that case the Jews will kill us and then swear.' He said, 'Then your oaths?' They said, 'We did not witness it.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid his blood money."],[5652,"He informed him that a group of his people went to Khaybar and dispersed there, and they found one of them slain. They said to those with whom they found him, 'You killed our companion?' They said, 'We did not kill him, and we did not know.' They went to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, we went to Khaybar and found one of us slain.' The youngest of the people spoke, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The eldest, the eldest.' Then he said to them, 'Do you bring proof against the one who killed him?' They said, 'We have no proof.' He said, 'Then they will swear to you.' They said, 'We will not accept the oaths of the Jews.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ disliked that his blood be wasted, so he paid his blood money with one hundred camels from the zakah camels."],[5653,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us; Malik informed us from Abu Layla b. 'Abd Allah b. Sahl from Sahl b. Abi Hathmah that he informed him from men among the elders of his people that 'Abd Allah b. Sahl and Muhayyisah went out to Khaybar because of hardship that befell them. Muhayyisah came and was informed that 'Abd Allah b. Sahl had been killed and thrown into a well or a spring. He went to the Jews and said, 'By Allah, you killed him.' They said, 'By Allah, we did not kill him.' Then he returned until he came to his people and mentioned that to them. He, his brother Huwayyisah—who was older than him—and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl came. Huwayyisah went to speak, as he was the one who had been at Khaybar, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Muhayyisah, 'Let the elder speak, the elder,' meaning age. So Huwayyisah spoke, then Muhayyisah spoke. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Either they pay the blood money for your companion, or they declare war.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to them about that, and they wrote back, 'By Allah, we did not kill him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Huwayyisah, Muhayyisah, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Sahl, 'Will you swear and thus be entitled to the blood of your companion?' They said, 'No.' He said, 'Then will the Jews swear for you?' They said, 'They are not Muslims.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid the blood money from his own resources and sent them one hundred she-camels, which were brought into the house. Sahl said, 'A red she-camel from them kicked me.'"],[5654,"The imam stands facing the qiblah, and a group of them stands facing the enemy, with their faces toward the enemy. He leads those with him in one rak'ah, then he stands and they perform one rak'ah for themselves and prostrate twice in their place. Then these go to the position of those, and those come, and he leads them in one rak'ah, so it is two for him and one for them. Then they perform a rak'ah for themselves and prostrate twice."],[5655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fruits for dried dates, but gave license regarding the 'araya for its sale on the basis of a calculation of their amount. But those who buy them can eat them when fresh. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3363)"],[5656,"The Messenger of God ﷺ divided Khaybar into two halves: one half for his needs and his special share, and one half among the Muslims. He divided it among them into eighteen shares."],[5657,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade muzabanah, and muzabanah is dates for dates, except for the owners of 'araya, for he permitted them."],[5658,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit saying: 'Avoid the seven major sins.' The people fell silent, and no one spoke. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Will you not ask me about them? Associating partners with God, killing a soul, fleeing from the battlefield, consuming the orphan's wealth, consuming riba, slandering chaste women, and becoming a bedouin after emigration.'"],[5659,"A people complained to the Prophet ﷺ that they had dwelt in a house, and they were numerous, and they perished. He said: 'Why did you not leave it, for it is blameworthy?'"],[5660,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, Abu Bakr has never harmed me, so acknowledge that for him. O people, I am pleased with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and the first Muhajirun—I am pleased with them, so acknowledge that for them.' O people, honor me concerning my companions, my in-laws, and my sons-in-law. Let not God seek you for the grievance of any one of them. O people, remove the disapproved from the Muslims, and when one of them dies, speak well of him."],[5661,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, Abu Bakr has never harmed me, so acknowledge that for him. O people, I am pleased with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and the first Muhajirun—I am pleased with them, so acknowledge that for them.' O people, honor me concerning my companions, my in-laws, and my sons-in-law. Let not God seek you for the grievance of any one of them. O people, remove the disapproved from the Muslims, and when one of them dies, speak well of him."],[5662,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah from the Farewell Pilgrimage, he ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, Abu Bakr has never harmed me, so acknowledge that for him. O people, I am pleased with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and the first Muhajirun—I am pleased with them, so acknowledge that for them.' O people, honor me concerning my companions, my in-laws, and my sons-in-law. Let not God seek you for the grievance of any one of them. O people, remove the disapproved from the Muslims, and when one of them dies, speak well of him."],[5663,"It is also said Suhayl, but the correct is Sahl: 'He used to reside in Basrah.'"],[5664,"Suhayl b. Sakhr, who had companionship, said to me: 'If I own the price of a slave and buy a slave with it, then fortunes are in the forelocks of men.'"],[5665,"Suhayl b. Sakhr said, and he had companionship (with the Prophet): \"Indeed, when I possess the price of a slave and buy a slave with it, for the forelocks of men are (a place of) fortunes.\""],[5666,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, from Banū Sawwād b. Ghanm: Sahl b. Qays b. Abī Kaʿb b. al-Qayn.\""],[5667,"From ʿUrwah: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Muʿāwiyah b. ʿAwf b. al-Khazraj: Sahl b. ʿAdī.\""],[5668,"From ʿUrwah: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Biʾr Maʿūnah from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Najjār: Sahl b. ʿĀmir b. Saʿd b. ʿAmr b. Thaqīf.\""],[5669,"Her mother ʿAmīrah bt. Sahl, the owner of the two ṣāʿs whom the hypocrites defamed, narrated to her that he went out with his zakāt with a ṣāʿ of dates and with his daughter ʿAmīrah until he came to the Prophet ﷺ and poured it out, then said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a need to you.\" He said: \"And what is it?\" He said: \"Supplicate Allah for blessing for me and for her, and wipe her head, for I have no child other than her.\" She said: \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on me, and I swear by Allah, it was as if the coolness of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on my liver.\""],[5670,"Sahl b. Saʿd died, and he was given the kunyah Abū al-ʿAbbās, in Madinah in the year ninety-one, and his age was ninety-six years."],[5671,"Sahl b. Saʿd al-Sāʿidī died in the year ninety-one."],[5672,"Sahl b. Saʿd: \"He had seen the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him, and he mentioned that he was fifteen years old on the day the Prophet ﷺ died.\""],[5673,"Sahl b. Saʿd: \"He had seen the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him, and that he was fifteen years old on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died.\""],[5674,"Sahl b. Saʿd al-Ansari, who reached the Prophet ﷺ at the age of fifteen during his lifetime."],[5675,"He was in the gathering of his people, relating to them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while some of them were facing one another, conversing. He became angry and said: “Look at them! I am relating to them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what my eyes saw and my ears heard, while some of them are facing one another. By Allah, I will surely depart from among you and never return to you again.” I said to him: “Where will you go?” He said: “I will go and fight in the path of Allah.” I said: “You are not able to fight; you cannot keep steady on a horse, you cannot strike with a sword, and you cannot thrust with a spear.” He said: “O Abu Hazim, I will go and stand in the battle line, and a passerby or a stone will come to me among them, and Allah will grant me martyrdom.” He said: So he went, by my life, and he did not return except as one struck by a spear."],[5676,"That he was present when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a man to a woman for two surahs of the Quran that he would teach her."],[5677,"A man looked at the Prophet ﷺ from behind the curtain of the room, while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb in his hand. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If I knew that this man was waiting for me to come to him, I would poke the comb into his eye. Was permission to enter made except for the sake of sight?”"],[5678,"He informed him that a man looked at the Prophet ﷺ from the room, while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb in his hand. He said: “If I knew that this man was waiting for me to come to him, I would poke the comb into his eyes. Was permission to enter made except for the sake of sight?”"],[5679,"Sahl b. Saʿd, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, informed him that a man looked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: “If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would poke it into your eye. Permission to enter was only established because of sight.”"],[5680,"I heard Sahl b. Saʿd say: A man looked from the room of the Prophet ﷺ, while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. He said: “If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would poke it into your eye. Permission to enter was only made for the sake of sight.”"],[5681,"A man looked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was scratching his head with a comb. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would poke it into your eye. Permission to enter was only made for the sake of sight.”"],[5682,"He informed him that a man looked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a comb with which he was combing or scratching his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would poke it into your eye. Permission was only made for the sake of sight.”"],[5683,"He informed him that a man looked through a hole in the door of the Prophet ﷺ, while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would poke it into your eye. The curtain was only made for permission,” or he said, “for the sake of looking.”"],[5684,"While the Prophet ﷺ was in his room and had with him an iron comb with which he was combing his beard, a man came and looked in through a hole in his room. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said, \"If I knew that you were waiting for me, I would have poked your eye out with this iron comb. Permission is only required because of seeing.\" This Abu Salama, from whom Sufyan narrated, is Muhammad b. Abi Hafsa."],[5685,"A man looked through a hole at the Prophet ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. He said, \"If I knew that you were looking, I would have stood up and stabbed you in the eye with it. Permission is only required because of seeing.\""],[5686,"A man looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while in the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a stick or an iron comb. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If I knew that you were looking at me, I would have poked your eye out.\""],[5687,"He informed him that a man looked through a hole in the door of the Prophet ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said, \"If I knew that you could see me, I would have stabbed you in the eye with it. Asking permission is only required because of seeing.\""],[5688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man looking into his house while in the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was an iron comb with which he was combing his hair. He said, \"If I knew that you could see me, I would have stabbed you in the eye with it.\""],[5689,"A man looked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had an iron comb with which he was combing his hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"If I knew that you were looking at me, I would have stabbed you in the eye with it. Permission is only required because of looking.\""],[5690,"A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do?\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed concerning his affair what is mentioned in the Quran about the matter of the two who invoke curses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Allah has decreed concerning you and your wife.\" He said, \"Then they invoked curses on each other in the mosque while I was present. When they finished, he said, 'I have lied against her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her.' So he divorced her three times before the Prophet ﷺ commanded him, when they had finished the mutual cursing, and he parted from her in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'That is the separation between every pair who invoke curses.' And the Prophet ﷺ said, 'If she gives birth to a reddish, short child, as if he were a small lizard, then I think she has told the truth and he has lied against her; but if she gives birth to a black, large-eyed child with large buttocks, then I think he has told the truth against her.' She gave birth to the disliked description of that.\""],[5691,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us from Ibn Shihab that Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed him that 'Uwaymir b. Ashqar al-'Ajlani came to 'Asim b. 'Adi al-Ansari and said to him, \"O 'Asim, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that for me, O 'Asim.\" So 'Asim asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he disliked such questions and criticized them, until 'Asim felt distressed about what he had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When 'Asim returned to his family, 'Uwaymir came to him and said, \"O 'Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?\" 'Asim said to 'Uwaymir, \"You have never brought me any good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked the question I asked him.\" 'Uwaymir said, \"By Allah, I will not stop until I ask him about it myself.\" So 'Uwaymir went until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the midst of the people and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It has been revealed concerning you and your companion. Go and bring her.\" Sahl said, \"Then they invoked curses on each other while I was with the people in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they finished, 'Uwaymir said, 'I have lied against her if I keep her.' So 'Uwaymir divorced her three times before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him.\" Ibn Shihab said, \"That became the sunna for the two who invoke curses.\""],[5692,"\"What do you say about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do?\" And he said, \"Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that for me.\" So 'Asim went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man finds another man with his wife. Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked such questions.\" Then 'Uwaymir asked him, and he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them.\" 'Uwaymir said, \"By Allah, I will not stop until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.\" He said, \"So 'Uwaymir came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a man finds another man with his wife. Should he kill him, and then you would kill him, or what should he do?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Quran has been revealed concerning you and your companion.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to invoke curses on each other according to what Allah clarified in His Book. So they invoked curses on each other. Then he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her, then I have wronged her.'\" He said, \"Then he divorced her, and that became a sunna for those who came after them among those who invoke curses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Look, if she gives birth to a child who is black, with dark eyes, large buttocks, and thick legs, then I think 'Uwaymir has told the truth against her; but if she gives birth to a reddish child, as if he were a small lizard, then I think 'Uwaymir has lied against her.'\" He said, \"She gave birth to the child with the description that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned, confirming 'Uwaymir, and this child's lineage was attributed to his mother.\""],[5693,"\"What do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him, and then you would kill him for it? Ask the Prophet ﷺ, O 'Asim.\" So 'Asim went and asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he disliked such questions and criticized them. He returned and told him that the Prophet ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them. 'Uwaymir said, \"By Allah, I will definitely go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He went, and Quran had been revealed after 'Asim's visit. He asked the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Quran has been revealed concerning you.\" So he called them both, and they came forward and invoked curses on each other. Then he said, \"I have lied against her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her.\" So he parted from her, and the Prophet ﷺ did not command him to part from her. Thus the sunna of the two who invoke curses was established. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Look, if she gives birth to a red, short child like a small lizard, then I think he has lied against her; but if she gives birth to a black, large-eyed child with large buttocks, then I think he has told the truth against her.\" She gave birth to the disliked description.\""],[5694,"He said that a man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife? Should he kill him?\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed concerning his affair what is mentioned in the Quran about invoking curses. He said, \"It has been decreed concerning you and your wife.\" He said, \"Then they invoked curses on each other while I was present. Then he parted from her in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. After that, the sunna was that separation should be made between the two who invoke curses. She was pregnant, and he denied her pregnancy. Her son was called after his mother. Then the sunna in inheritance was that her son would inherit her, and she would inherit from him what was prescribed for her.\""],[5695,"He said to his cousin 'Asim b. 'Adi, \"Come with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"What do you think if I found a man with my wife? Should I kill him?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked his words. So he returned, and 'Uwaymir said, \"I will definitely mention that to him even if he dislikes it.\" So 'Uwaymir came to him and said, \"What do you think if I found a man with my wife?\" He said, \"Bring your wife, for it has been revealed concerning you two.\" So he brought her, and they invoked curses on each other. Then he said, \"I have fabricated a lie against her.\" So he separated them. Ibn Shihab said, \"His separation from her became a sunna among the Muslims.\""],[5696,"O ‘Āṣim, ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for me about a man who finds another man with his wife and kills him—is he to be killed in retribution, or what should he do? So ‘Āṣim asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that, and he disapproved of such questions and disliked it. Then ‘Uwaymir came and said, “O ‘Āṣim, what did you do?” He replied, “What did I do? You brought nothing good. I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and he disapproved of such questions.” ‘Uwaymir said, “By God, I will go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him myself.” So he came to him and found that revelation had already been sent down concerning them. The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned them both and conducted the mutual cursing (li‘ān) between them. ‘Uwaymir said, “If I keep her, I will have lied against her.” So he separated from her before the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to. Ibn Shihāb said, “Thus it became the sunnah for the two parties of li‘ān.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Observe her: if she gives birth to a dark-complexioned child with deep black eyes and large buttocks, I think he spoke the truth against her; but if she gives birth to a small reddish child like a gecko (waghara), then I think he is a liar.” She gave birth to a child matching the disliked description. The wording is from al-Ḥumaydī’s ḥadīth."],[5697,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, what do you think about a man who sees another man with his wife—should he kill him, and then you would kill him in retribution, or what should he do?” Then God, exalted is He, revealed concerning them what is mentioned in the Qur’an about mutual cursing. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Judgment has been passed regarding you and your wife.” He said, “So they performed li‘ān while I was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then he said, “O Messenger of God, if I keep her, I will have lied against her.” So he separated from her. Thus the sunnah was established thereafter that the two who perform li‘ān are to be separated. She was pregnant, and he denied the pregnancy, though the child was attributed to her. The sunnah was also established thereafter concerning inheritance: that she inherits from him and he inherits from her whatever God has ordained for her."],[5698,"The one who performed li‘ān divorced her with three divorces in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ enforced it. What was done in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ became sunnah.” Sahl said, “I witnessed this in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the sunnah was thereafter established concerning the two parties of li‘ān: that they be separated and never be reunited.” Ibn Shihāb said, “The man said at that time, ‘What a bad servant of God I am if I lied in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ and bore a false accusation.’”"],[5699,"I attended their li‘ān in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ when I was fifteen years old. When they finished their mutual cursing, ‘Uwaymir said, “O Messenger of God, I have lied against her if I keep her.” He said, “So he divorced her three times.” And he said, “By God, if I lied, I have borne a false accusation.” Then she passed by pregnant, and the child was attached to its mother."],[5700,"Ask the Prophet ﷺ: What do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife and kills him—will you kill him in retribution, or what should he do? The man waited a while, then came and said, “O ‘Āṣim, what did you do about what I told you?” ‘Āṣim replied, “You never brought me anything good. I asked the Prophet ﷺ and he disapproved of such questions.” ‘Uwaymir was not satisfied until he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him the same as he had asked ‘Āṣim. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Come forward, for God, exalted is He, has revealed something concerning you and your wife.” The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned them both and conducted the li‘ān between them. Then ‘Uwaymir said, “O Prophet of God, I have lied against her if I keep her after having performed li‘ān.” Thus the sunnah was established between the two parties of li‘ān that they be separated."],[5701,"And that the Messenger of God ﷺ separated them."],[5702,"‘Uwaymir said to ‘Āṣim, “A man finds another man with his wife—should he kill him and then you would kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for me about that.” So ‘Āṣim asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that, and he disliked such questions and criticized them. This weighed heavily on ‘Āṣim and troubled him deeply. Then ‘Uwaymir came to him and said, “Did you ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about what I told you?” He replied, “You brought me no good. I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and he disliked such questions and criticized them, until I wished I had given up my wealth and never asked him. It is your affair with your wife.” So ‘Uwaymir went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, a man finds another man with his wife—should he kill him and then you would kill him, or what should he do?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “God has revealed something concerning you and your wife, so bring her quickly.” The Messenger of God ﷺ brought them to the mosque after ‘asr while I was among the people watching, and they performed li‘ān. When they finished, ‘Uwaymir stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have wronged her if I keep her—she is divorced irrevocably.”"],[5703,"He performed li‘ān against his wife in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ. ‘Uwaymir stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have wronged her if I keep her—she is divorced irrevocably.”"],[5704,"He witnessed the two parties of li‘ān during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ when they were separated. The man said, “O Messenger of God, I have lied against her if I keep her.”"],[5705,"O ‘Āṣim, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife—should he kill him and then you would kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for me. The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them, until what ‘Āṣim heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ weighed heavily on him. When ‘Āṣim returned to his family, ‘Uwaymir came and said, “O ‘Āṣim, what did the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you?” ‘Āṣim replied, “The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked the question you asked about.” So ‘Uwaymir went and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ in the midst of the people, saying, “O Messenger of God, what do you think about a man who finds another man with his wife—should he kill him and then you would kill him, or what should he do?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Something has been revealed concerning you and your wife, so go and bring her.” Sahl said, “So they performed li‘ān while I was among the people with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When they finished their mutual cursing, ‘Uwaymir said, ‘O Messenger of God, I have lied against her if I keep her.’ So he divorced her before the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to divorce her, and his separation from her became the sunnah between the two who perform li‘ān.”"],[5706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to Banū ‘Amr b. ‘Awf to reconcile between them. The time for prayer came, so the muezzin went to Abū Bakr ؓ and said, “Will you lead the people in prayer?” He said, “Yes.” So Abū Bakr ؓ led the prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came while the people were in prayer, and he made his way through until he stood in the row with the people. Abū Bakr ؓ did not turn around during his prayer, but when the people clapped repeatedly, he turned and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to him to remain in his place. Abū Bakr ؓ raised his hands and praised God, exalted is He, for what the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him. Then he stepped back until he stood in the row, and the Prophet ﷺ came forward and led the prayer. When he finished, he said, “O Abū Bakr, what prevented you from staying when I commanded you?” Abū Bakr ؓ replied, “It was not appropriate for the son of Abū Quḥāfah to lead the prayer while the Messenger of God ﷺ was present.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Why did I see you clapping so much? Whoever notices something during prayer should glorify God, for when he glorifies, attention is turned to him. Clapping is only for women.”"],[5707,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Uḥud, “O God, forgive my people, for they do not know.”"],[5708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only granted us a concession for mut'ah because of a severe need among the people; then he forbade it afterwards."],[5709,"The saying of the Ansar was 'water from water' in the beginning of Islam; then the full bath came after that."],[5710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about cleansing oneself after relieving oneself, and he said, 'Does not one of you find three stones: two for the sides and one for the orifice?'"],[5711,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'There is no ablution for one who does not send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[5712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no prayer for one who does not have ablution, and there is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it, and there is no prayer for one who does not send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ , and there is no prayer for one who does not love the Ansar.\""],[5713,"The Prophet ﷺ had a horse in a garden called al-Luhayf."],[5714,"The Prophet ﷺ used to have a bowl from Sa'd b. 'Ubadah every night, and the Prophet ﷺ would address the women, saying, 'You shall have such and such, and Sa'd's bowl will come with me to you whenever I come.'"],[5715,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Deliberateness is from Allah and haste is from Satan.'"],[5716,"The Prophet ﷺ would give one salam, to his right."],[5717,"The Prophet ﷺ blessed the well of Buda'ah and spat into it."],[5718,"His name was Hazn, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Sahl."],[5719,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Indeed in Paradise there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of anyone.'"],[5720,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'There is no ill omen; if there is any ill omen, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling.'"],[5721,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouths of waterskins."],[5722,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Love Quraysh, for whoever loves them, God ﷻ loves him.”"],[5723,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Renew your Islam by loving the Ansar, for none loves them except a believer and none hates them except a hypocrite.”"],[5724,"“I was present on the day of Uhud, and I was looking when the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ was struck and wounded. I recognize who was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ and who was carrying water in the leather shield. The wound refused to stop bleeding until Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, burned a worn-out mat and placed its ashes on it, and it stopped. The one carrying water in the leather shield was Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and Fatimah was the one washing the blood and treating him.”"],[5725,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed over Dhubab.” Abu al-Qasim said, “It reached me that Dhubab is a mountain in the Hijaz, and his saying ‘prayed over him’ means he invoked blessing upon him.”"],[5726,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over Dhubab."],[5727,"“We used to rejoice on Friday. One of our old women would send to Quda'ah and take stalks of chard, then scatter over it a handful of barley and cook it, then bring it to us and we would lick it, and we rejoiced on Friday because of that.”"],[5728,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ would go to al-'Aliyah and be overtaken by sunset at the camel enclosure, so they would perform tayammum."],[5729,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A whip's length in Paradise is better than this world and all that it contains.”"],[5730,"He was present with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud."],[5731,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted a share to Sa'd b. Sa'd on the day of Badr, and he is the brother of Sahl b. Sa'd."],[5732,"The Prophet ﷺ enjoined that good be done to our doer of good and that our wrongdoer be pardoned."],[5733,"That when the Prophet ﷺ was returning from Tabuk and was on the mountain pass, he said, \"Allah is Greatest.\" Then when he looked at Uhud, he said, \"This is a mountain that loves us and we love it.\" Then he turned and said, \"Would you like me to tell you about the dwellings of the Ansar?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The best dwellings of the Ansar are those of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then the dwellings of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then the dwellings of Banu Sa'idah.\" Sa'd said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have placed us last among the tribes?\" He said, \"If you are among the best, that is sufficient for you.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Mus'ab."],[5734,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Rinse your mouths from milk, for it has fat.\""],[5735,"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade blowing into a drink and drinking from a cracked spot in a cup or from its handle."],[5736,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command wiping over the leather socks."],[5737,"That 'Amir b. al-Tufayl came to the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah, and he argued with the Prophet ﷺ and raised his voice, while Thabit b. Qays was standing with his sword over the Prophet ﷺ. Thabit said, \"O 'Amir, lower your voice before the Prophet ﷺ.\" 'Amir said, \"What does that matter to you?\" Thabit said, \"By the One who honored him, were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked it, I would strike your head with this sword.\" 'Amir looked at him while he was sitting and Thabit was standing, and said, \"By Allah, O Thabit, if you were exposed to me in battle, you would turn away from me.\" Thabit said, \"By Allah, O 'Amir, if you were exposed to my tongue, you would hate my life.\" Then a nephew of 'Amir sneezed and praised Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ responded to him, saying, 'May Allah have mercy on you.' Then 'Amir sneezed and did not praise Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ did not respond to him. 'Amir said, \"You responded to this boy and left me out?\" He said, \"This one praised Allah.\" 'Amir said, \"Then I swear that I will fill it against you with cavalry and infantry.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah will suffice me against you, along with the two sons of Qaylah.\" Then 'Amir left and gathered forces against the Prophet ﷺ, and three clans of Banu Sulaym joined him, the ones against whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: 'Usayyah, Dhakwan, and Ri'l. The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate against them in the dawn prayer: \"O Allah, curse Lihyan, Ri'l, Dhakwan, and 'Usayyah who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. Allah is Greatest.\" He supplicated for seventeen nights. When he heard that 'Amir had gathered forces against him, the Prophet ﷺ sent against them 'Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri and others from the Ansar, with their commander al-Mundhir b. 'Amr. They went until they halted at the well of Ma'unah. Then 'Amir came and attacked them, and he killed them all. None of them escaped except 'Amr b. Umayyah, who was with the pack animals. Allah revealed to His Prophet ﷺ on the day they were killed the news of his companions, and he said, \"Your companions have been killed, so consider your situation.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ supplicated against 'Amir, saying, \"O Allah, suffice me against 'Amir.\" And Allah sufficed him against him. 'Amir went until he stopped at his courtyard, and Allah struck him with a gland in his throat in the house of a woman of Sulul. He began jumping and saying, \"Woe to 'Amir from a gland like the gland of a camel in the house of a Sululite woman; he desires to die in her house.\" He remained like that until he died in her house. And Arbad b. Qays was struck by a thunderbolt and burned, and died. And those who were with them returned."],[5738,"That he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he and Abu Dharr, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Muhammad b. Maslamah, and another man, that the blame of a blamer would not deter them in [the cause of] Allah."],[5739,"Before he built the mosque, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray facing a piece of wood. When he built the mosque, he built a mihrab for him, and he moved forward to it. Then the piece of wood moaned like the moaning of a camel, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on it, and it became still."],[5740,"That he carried one of the steps of the pulpit from the forest until he placed it in the mosque, and that the wood of the pulpit was from tamarisk trees."],[5741,"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade killing the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, the shrike, and the frog."],[5742,"The Prophet ﷺ had with my father three horses that he fed. He said: And I heard my father naming them al-Ladan, al-Lahif, and al-Tarab."],[5743,"On the day of Khaybar, while we were with the Prophet ﷺ, he took the banner and said, \"I will give this banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger.\" The people stretched their necks to see who would be given it. He called 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and 'Ali had sore eyes. The Prophet ﷺ spat in his eyes, then gave it to him, and Allah granted victory through him."],[5744,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"O people, fear Allah, for if you fear Allah, Allah will soon satisfy you with the olive oil of Syria and the wheat of Syria.\""],[5745,"The Prophet ﷺ used to lean against a palm trunk. When the people became numerous, he said, “The people have become numerous, so if only there were a pulpit on which I could sit.” Abbas said: My father went and cut the wood for the pulpit from the forest. I do not know whether he made it himself or had it made."],[5746,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ at the Trench. He took a pickaxe and dug with it, and he came upon a stone, and he laughed. It was said, “What makes you laugh, O Messenger of God?” He said, “I laughed at people who will come to you from the direction of the east and will be driven to Paradise while they are unwilling.”"],[5747,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Take her to yourself until she gives birth. If she bears him red like a small lizard, then he belongs to his father, Uwaymir, the one who disowned him. But if she bears him black of tongue and hair, then he belongs to Ibn al-Sahma’, the man with whom she is accused.” Uwaymir said: When she gave birth, I brought him, and he met me like a black hide. Then I took hold of his jaws and his tongue met me like a date. I said, “God and His Messenger have spoken truly.”"],[5748,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it.”"],[5749,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said, “The best of the clans of the Ansar are the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith, then Banu Sa’idah, and in all the Ansar there is good.”"],[5750,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “That I pray the dawn prayer, then sit in my place remembering God until the sun rises, is dearer to me than charging upon swift horses in the path of God.” This is how al-Dabari said: Ayyash, but he is only Abbas."],[5751,"Abu Bakr ؓ: It was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer. Then he said, “If something happens to you during the prayer, the men should say subhan Allah and the women should clap.”"],[5752,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There is no believer who recites the talbiyah except that whatever is to his right and to his left of trees or stones recites the talbiyah with him, until the earth is cut off from here and from here. Indeed, the people of the highest degrees see those below them as a star is seen in the sky.”"],[5753,"The Prophet ﷺ was summoned urgently on behalf of Banu Amr b. Awf for something that was between them to reconcile it. The prayer was commenced, and they waited. When he was delayed, Abu Bakr ؓ advanced. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and the people clapped for Abu Bakr to step back. Abu Bakr stepped back and the Messenger of God ﷺ advanced. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished his prayer, he faced the people and said, “What is this clapping? Subhan Allah is for men and clapping is for women.”"],[5754,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The believer among the people of faith is in the position of the head to the body. The believer suffers for the people of faith just as the body suffers for what is in the head.”"],[5755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A believer is friendly and there is no good in one who is not friendly and does not seek friendship.\""],[5756,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I entered Paradise and heard a sound, so I looked, and there was Bilal.\""],[5757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but God.' When they say, 'There is no god but God,' they protect from me their blood and their property except for its due, and their reckoning is with God.\""],[5758,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse.\""],[5759,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The place of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and all that is in it.\""],[5760,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf to reconcile between them concerning something they had differed about. The Messenger of God ﷺ did not return until the noon prayer was called. Abu Bakr stepped forward to lead the people in prayer and said the takbir. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered, and the people saw him and began clapping to alert Abu Bakr to the entrance of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Abu Bakr ؓ did not turn around during his prayer. When he heard the parting of the rows behind him, he knew that the Messenger of God ﷺ had come, so he stepped back toward the row. The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand between Abu Bakr's shoulders and pushed him forward to his place, and Abu Bakr remained still for a moment, then he moved back a single pace and entered the row. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he stepped forward and led the prayer until he finished. Then he said the salam and turned to Abu Bakr and said: \"What made you do what you did? Why did you not remain when I placed you forward?\" He said: \"I wanted to, but I did not think it was proper for the son of Abu Quhafah to stand in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Then he turned to the people and said: \"When something occurs during prayer, you should say subhan Allah, for saying subhan Allah is for men and clapping is for women.\""],[5761,"He said: While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a woman came to him and said: \"I have come, O Messenger of God, to give myself to you.\" He raised his gaze upon her and lowered it, then he was silent. A man who had nothing on but a single garment, tying its two ends around his neck, stood up and said: \"If you have no need of her, marry her to me.\" He said to him: \"Do you have anything?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then she must have something. Go and seek.\" He went and sought but found nothing and returned, saying: \"I found nothing.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Go and seek, even if it is an iron ring.\" He went and returned, saying: \"Not even an iron ring; I did not find one.\" Then he sat down. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"What do you have of the Qur'an?\" He said: \"Surah so-and-so and Surah so-and-so.\" He said: \"I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an.\""],[5762,"He said: A woman came to the Messenger of God with a striped cloak and said: \"I made this for you with my own hands.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ accepted it from her, and he needed it, so he wrapped it around himself as a waist wrapper. Then he went out, and a man among his companions said: \"Give it to me to wear?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he gave it to him. Sahl said: I said to the man: \"You saw the Messenger of God's need for it, yet you asked for it?\" He said: \"I saw what you saw, but I wanted to keep it so that I might be shrouded in it.\" And he was shrouded in it."],[5763,"A group of people came to him disputing about the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ, of what wood it was made. He said: \"I know of which wood it is, who made it, and the day on which the Messenger of God ﷺ stood upon it.\" He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a woman of the Ansar to instruct a servant boy of hers who was a carpenter to make wooden planks for him upon which he could address the people. He made it for him from the tamarisk of al-Ghabah. When he finished, the woman informed the Messenger of God ﷺ about it, so he sent for it and it was brought. He addressed the people upon it. Then the prayer was established, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said the takbir while on the pulpit, then he bowed upon it, then he descended for the prostration and prostrated, then he mounted the pulpit again and did the same until he completed his prayer.\""],[5764,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The place of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and all that is in it.\""],[5765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan, through which the fasting will be called. Whoever was among those who fasted will enter it and never thirst again.\""],[5766,"Fatimah ؓ, on the day the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ was wounded, burned a reed mat and treated his wound with it, applying it to the wound."],[5767,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Two (prayers) are not rejected, or seldom rejected: Prayer at the time of the call to prayer, and (the prayer) at the time of fighting, when the people grapple with each other. Musa said: Rizq ibn Sa'id ibn AbdurRahman reported from AbuHazim on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa'd from the Prophet ﷺ as saying: And while it is raining. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2540)"],[5768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The people will console one another after me for the consolation of me.\" The people said: \"What is this?\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away, the people met one another, each consoling the other for the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5769,"The wooden staff that was in the maqsura was made for the Messenger of God ﷺ when he became old, and he would lean on it when he stood. When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, it was stolen. It was searched for and found in the mosque of the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, and termites had damaged it."],[5770,"'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ entered upon Fatimah ؓ, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, while Hasan and Husayn were crying. He said, \"What is making them cry?\" She said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"Send a message to your father.\" So she sent a messenger. The messenger came to him while he had before him leftover dates. He said, \"Your daughter says: O Messenger of God, if you have anything, then give it to us, for Hasan and Husayn are crying.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the messenger, and he carried it to them. He brought it to Fatimah, and 'Ali entered upon her while it was before her. 'Ali said, \"Did he find nothing other than this?\" Fatimah ؓ said, \"No.\" 'Ali said, \"There is nothing in this that will calm them.\" So 'Ali ؓ went out and found a dinar in the market. He brought it to Fatimah ؓ and told her, and said, \"This is the dinar.\" Fatimah ؓ said, \"Take it to so-and-so the Jew and get us some flour with it.\" So 'Ali ؓ went out and came to the Jew and bought flour with it. When he finished, the Jew said, \"Are you the son-in-law of this man who claims that he is the Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Jew said, \"Take your dinar, and the flour is yours.\" So 'Ali went out until he brought it to Fatimah and told her, and said, \"This is the dinar.\" Fatimah said, \"Take it to so-and-so the butcher and get us a dirham's worth of meat. We will send word to the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he may eat with us.\" So he went and pawned the dinar for a dirham. He brought it, and she kneaded, set up the oven, and baked. She sent for her father, and he came to her. There was a large bowl containing bread, the meat was boiling, and there was flour. She said, \"O Messenger of God, I will mention something to you. If you consider it lawful for us, we will eat and you will eat, concerning its matter, such and such.\" He said, \"Eat, in the name of God.\" So they ate. While they were in their place, there came a boy calling out for the dinar, by God and by Islam. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that he be brought, and he questioned him. He said, \"My family sent me with a dinar to buy something with it, and it fell from me in the market.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Go to the butcher and tell him that the Messenger of God ﷺ says: Send me the dinar, and your dirham is on me.\" So he sent it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave it to him."],[5771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"To perform the morning prayer, then sit remembering God until the sun rises, is more beloved to me than to carry out raids on excellent horses in the path of God until the sun rises.\""],[5772,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will see a room among the rooms of Paradise just as you see the brilliant morning star in the east or the west.\""],[5773,"In the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , women were commanded during prayer not to lift their heads until men took their seats on the ground from the opening of their garments."],[5774,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan. On the Day of Resurrection it will be said: Where are those who fasted? When they enter, it will be closed, and no one other than them will enter through it.\""],[5775,"From Sahl b. Sa'd, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"Clapping is for women, and glorification (tasbih) is for men.\""],[5776,"That men from the Muslims used to witness the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tying their garments and none of them had more than one garment."],[5777,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I have committed adultery with so-and-so,\" naming her. The Prophet ﷺ sent for the woman and questioned her, but she denied it. So he stoned the man and left her."],[5778,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Abu Hazim from Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they hasten to break the fast.\""],[5779,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Abu Hazim from Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi that the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drink and drank from it. On his right was a young boy and on his left were the elders. He said to the boy: \"Do you permit me to give these?\" The boy said: \"By God, O Messenger of God, I will not prefer anyone to my share from you.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ placed it in his hand."],[5780,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Abu Hazim from Sahl b. Sa'd that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If there is ill omen, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling.\""],[5781,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik (h), and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us (h), and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me from Abu Hazim from Sahl b. Sa'd that the Messenger of God ﷺ went to the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf to reconcile between them. The time for prayer came, so the mu'adhdhin came to Abu Bakr ؓ and said: \"Will you lead the people in prayer so that I may give the iqamah?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So Abu Bakr ؓ led the prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ came while the people were in prayer. He made his way through until he stood in the row. The people clapped, and Abu Bakr did not turn around during his prayer. When the people clapped a lot, Abu Bakr turned and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to him: \"Stay in your place.\" Abu Bakr ؓ raised his hands and praised God ﷻ for what the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him of that. Then he stepped back until he stood in the row, and the Prophet ﷺ came forward and led the prayer. When he finished, he said: \"O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from staying in place when I commanded you?\" He said: \"It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to pray before the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Why did I see you clapping a lot? Whoever is disturbed by something in his prayer should glorify God, for if he glorifies God, attention will be turned to him. Clapping is only for women.\""],[5782,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl b. Saʿd, who said: “The people used to be commanded that a man place his right hand upon his left forearm.”"],[5783,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Indeed Bilāl calls the adhān at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm calls.”"],[5784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There are two moments in which the supplication of a supplicant is not rejected: when the night prayer is established, and when in the ranks fighting in the path of God.”"],[5785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by some children who were playing with dirt, and some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ wanted to forbid them, so he said: “Leave them, for dirt is the springtime of children.”"],[5786,"Have you considered a man who finds another man with his wife? If he kills him, will you kill him? Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for me. So ʿĀṣim asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ disliked such questions and criticized them. ʿĀṣim informed ʿUwaymir, and ʿUwaymir said: By God, I will go to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came, and the Qurʾān had already been revealed. He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Qurʾān has been revealed concerning you two.” So they came forward and invoked curses upon each other. Then he said: I would have lied about her if I keep her. So he separated from her, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not command him to divorce her. Thus a precedent was set for the two who invoke curses. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Look at her. If she gives birth to a child who is reddish and short, as if he were a lizard (waraʿa), then I think he has lied about her. But if she gives birth to a dark-complexioned child with wide eyes and large buttocks, then I think he has spoken the truth about her.” She gave birth to the disliked description."],[5787,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A place the size of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and all that is in it.”"],[5788,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “My pulpit is upon one of the channels of Paradise.”"],[5789,"A cup was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he drank from it. On his right was a boy, the youngest of the people, and the elders were on his left. He said: “O boy, will you permit me to give it to the elders?” He replied: I would not prefer anyone over the remnant of your lips, O Messenger of God. So he gave it to him."],[5790,"A woman offered herself in marriage to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from the people said: Marry her to me. He said: “What do you have?” He replied: I have nothing. He said: “Go and seek something, even an iron ring.” He went and then returned, saying: No, by God, I found nothing, not even an iron ring, but this is my lower garment, and she may have half of it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What would you do with your lower garment? If you wear it, she would have nothing from it, and if she wears it, you would have nothing from it.” The man sat until his sitting became long. The Messenger of God ﷺ saw him and called him, or he was brought to him, and said: “What do you have with you from the Qurʾān?” He said: I have Sūrah so-and-so and so-and-so. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have married her to you for what you have from the Qurʾān.”"],[5791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand or seven hundred thousand from my nation will enter Paradise together, their hands holding each other, until the first and the last of them enter Paradise, and their faces will be like the full moon on a clear night.\""],[5792,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am your predecessor at the Ḥawḍ. Whoever passes by me will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst again. There will come to me peoples whom I recognize and who recognize me, but then a barrier will be placed between me and them.”"],[5793,"A man was among the greatest of the Muslims in benefit to the Muslims in an expedition he undertook with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at him and said: “Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this man.” A man from the people followed him while he was in that state, one of the harshest of people against the polytheists, until he was wounded. Then he sought to hasten death. He took the tip of his sword, placed it between his chest and thrust it until it came out between his shoulders. The man came rushing to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “And what is that?” He said: You said: “Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this man,” and he was among the greatest of us in benefit to the Muslims. I knew that he would not die upon that state. When he was wounded, he hastened death and killed himself. The Messenger of God ﷺ said at that: “A servant may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise while he is from the people of the Fire, and he may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire while he is from the people of Paradise. Indeed, deeds are judged by their endings.”"],[5794,"Sahl bin Saʿd said that a woman brought a Burda (sheet) to the Prophet. Sahl asked the people, \"Do you know what is a Burda?\" The people replied, \"It is a 'Shamla', a sheet with a fringe.\" That woman said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I have brought it so that you may wear it.\" So the Prophet ﷺ took it because he was in need of it and wore it. A man among his companions, seeing him wearing it, said, \"O Allah's Apostle! Please give it to me to wear.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" (and gave him that sheet). When the Prophet left, the man was blamed by his companions who said, \"It was not nice on your part to ask the Prophet for it while you know that he took it because he was in need of it, and you also know that he (the Prophet) never turns down anybody's request that he might be asked for.\" That man said, \"I just wanted to have its blessings as the Prophet ﷺ had put it on, so l hoped that I might be shrouded in it.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6036)"],[5795,"Between the mosque—on the side facing the qiblah—and the qiblah there was a passageway for a sheep."],[5796,"We used to pray Jumuʿah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then the midday rest would follow."],[5797,"There was a woman among us who used to plant chard in a field of hers. On Fridays she would pull up the chard roots, put them in a pot, then add a handful of barley and cook it; the chard roots became a stew. Sahl said: We would go to her after the Friday prayer, greet her, and she would bring that food to us. We used to look forward to Friday because of that food of hers."],[5798,"The helmet was shattered on the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, his front tooth was broken, and his face was wounded. Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was washing the blood from him while Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ brought her water. When the water reached the wound, his bleeding increased and did not stop until she took a piece of a mat, burned it until it became ashes, and then placed it on the wound, and the bleeding stopped."],[5799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for a woman among the Emigrants who had a carpenter slave. He said to her: “Order your slave to make me some wooden planks like a minbar.” So she ordered her slave. He went to the forest, cut some tamarisk, and made a minbar for him. When he had finished it, she sent word to the Prophet ﷺ that it was ready. He said: So it was sent to me. They brought it to him, and the Prophet ﷺ carried it and placed it where you now see it."],[5800,"When the verse was revealed: “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread” — the phrase “of dawn” had not yet been revealed. Some men, when they intended to fast, would tie a black thread and a white thread to their legs and would keep eating and drinking until they could distinguish between them. Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed after that: “of dawn,” and they knew that by it He meant night and day."],[5801,"A woman of the Arabs was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered Abu Usayd al-Saʿidi to send for her. He sent for her, and she arrived and stayed with the Banu Saʿidah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until he came to her. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to her, she said: “I seek refuge in Allah from you.” He said: “He has granted you refuge from me.” They said to her: “Do you know who this is? This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he came to propose to you.” She said: “Then I am most unfortunate in that.” Sahl said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then came and sat with his companions in the portico of the Banu Saʿidah. Then he said: “Give us something to drink, Abu Saʿd.” He said: So I brought out this drinking bowl and served them from it. Abu Hazim said: Sahl brought out that bowl for us and we drank from it. Later ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAziz, may Allah have mercy on him, asked for it as a gift, and he gave it to him."],[5802,"Al-Mundhir b. Abi Usayd was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was born. He placed him on his thigh while Abu Usayd was sitting. The Prophet ﷺ became distracted by something in front of him, so Abu Usayd ordered his son to be taken away from the Prophet ﷺ. They removed him, and the Prophet ﷺ asked: “Where is the child?” Abu Usayd said: “We removed him, O Messenger of Allah.” He asked: “What is his name?” He said: “So-and-so.” He said: “No, rather his name is al-Mundhir.” So that day he named him al-Mundhir."],[5803,"When Abu Sahl Usayd al-Saʿidi got married, he invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. He prepared food for them, and no one served it to them except his wife, Umm Usayd. She had soaked some dates overnight in a stone vessel. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished eating, she brought it to him and served him the drink."],[5804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there are eight gates. One of them is called al-Rayyan; none will enter it except those who fast.”"],[5805,"I asked Sahl b. Saʿd: Did you ever see in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fine white flour? He said: “No.” Abu Hazim said: I said: How did you sift barley? He said: “We did not sift it; rather we blew on it.”"],[5806,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A morning or evening journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5807,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man may perform, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Paradise, while he is among the people of the Fire; and a man may perform, in what people see, the deeds of the people of the Fire, while he is among the people of Paradise. Indeed, deeds are judged by their endings.”"],[5808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man may perform, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Paradise, while he is among the people of the Fire; and a man may perform, in what people see, the deeds of the people of the Fire, while he is among the people of Paradise. Indeed, deeds are judged by their endings.”"],[5809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed God, Exalted is He, has seventy thousand veils of light and darkness; if any soul were to hear anything of the sound of those veils, it would perish.”"],[5811,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If ill luck exists in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the dwelling.”"],[5812,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Hud and its sisters have made me grey: al-Waqi‘ah, al-Haqqah, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat.”"],[5813,"The Prophet ﷺ would fast until it was said he would not break his fast, and he would break his fast until it was said he would not fast; and most of his fasting was in Sha‘ban."],[5814,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise as appears to people, while he is among the people of the Fire; and a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire as appears to people, while he is among the people of Paradise.”"],[5815,"When ill luck was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If it exists in anything, it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse.”"],[5816,"I heard him say: The dearest of ‘Ali’s names to him was Abu Turab, and he would rejoice to be called by it. None named him Abu Turab except the Messenger of God ﷺ. One day he became angry with Fatimah ؓ and went out and lay down against a wall. The Messenger of God ﷺ came looking for him and did not find him in the house, so he said to Fatimah, “Where is your cousin?” She said, “He went out a short while ago in anger.” The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered someone with him to look for him, and he said, “He is lying against the wall, and his cloak has slipped from his back and become covered in dust.” The Messenger of God ﷺ began wiping the dust from his back and saying, “Sit up, Abu Turab.”"],[5817,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The minbar is upon one of the channels of Paradise.”"],[5818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In the last days there will be earthquakes, peltings, and disfigurements.\" It was said, \"And when is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"When musical instruments and singing girls appear and wine is deemed lawful.\""],[5819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves to bracelet his child with two bracelets of fire, let him bracelet him with a bracelet of gold; but as for silver and white metal, play with them as you wish.\""],[5820,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"At Allah, there are treasuries of good and evil, and the keys to these treasuries are men. So, blessed is he who makes himself a key to good and a lock to evil, and woe to him who makes himself a key to evil and a lock to good.\""],[5821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Uhud is a pillar from the pillars of Paradise.\""],[5822,"I heard Sahl b. Sa'd say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand on his pulpit and pray for the people while he was on the pulpit. He said the takbir on it, then bowed, then moved backwards and prostrated at the bottom of the pulpit, then went back and did the same until he completed his prayer. Then he turned to the people and said: \"O people, I only did this so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.\""],[5823,"I heard Sahl b. Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a cup and he drank. The elders were on his left, and a boy who was the youngest of the people was on his right. When he had drunk, he said: \"O boy, do you permit me to give it to the elders?\" The boy said: I would not prefer anyone over you for my share of your leftover, O Messenger of Allah. So he gave it to him."],[5824,"There was a dispute among the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them to reconcile between them. He then returned, and the prayer had been established, with Abu Bakr ؓ leading the people in prayer. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ."],[5825,"I saw Sahl b. Sa'd, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, urinate while standing, the urination of an old man such that it almost raced from him. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said to him: \"Will you not take them off?\" He said: \"No, for I have seen one better than me wipe over them.\""],[5826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: \"I shall certainly give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory.\" The people spent that night wondering which of them would be given it. When morning came, they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Where is 'Ali?\" They said: \"He is here, O Messenger of Allah, suffering from sore eyes.\" So he sent for him, spat into his eyes, and supplicated as Allah willed, and he was healed until there was no pain in him. Then he gave him the banner and said: \"Advance steadily.\" 'Ali said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they become like us?\" He said: \"Proceed at your leisure until you descend upon their courtyard, then call them to Islam and inform them of what is due to Allah from them in it. For Allah to guide one man through you is better for you than red camels.\""],[5827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan. On the Day of Resurrection it will be said: 'Where are those who fasted? Will you not come to al-Rayyan?' Whoever enters through it will never thirst again. They will enter through it, and when the last of them has entered it will be closed, and no one besides them will enter through it.\""],[5828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought an old man with dropsy, pale, whose veins had become prominent, who had committed adultery with a woman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him once with a palm branch containing a hundred twigs."],[5829,"I witnessed Ma'iz when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his stoning. He ran, and the people followed him stoning him until 'Umar met him in the graveyard and struck him with a camel's jawbone and killed him."],[5830,"He had grown so old that he could hardly control that from himself. He said: Then he called for water, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks. I said: \"Will you not take off your leather socks?\" He said: \"I saw one better than me do that.\""],[5831,"He said: \"On the day of Uhud, when the polytheists withdrew from the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions, the women went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions to help them. Fatimah bint the Messenger of God ﷺ was among those who went out. When she met the Messenger of God ﷺ, she embraced him and began washing his wounds with water, but the blood increased. When she saw that, she took a piece of a mat, burned it with fire, and applied it to the wound until it stuck to the wound and the blood stopped.\""],[5832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever encounters something during his prayer, let him glorify God, saying: 'Glory be to God,' for glorification is for men and clapping is for women.\""],[5833,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise as they appear to people, yet he is among the people of Hell; and a man may perform the deeds of the people of Hell as they appear to people, yet he is among the people of Paradise.\""],[5834,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan. None will enter through it except those who fast. When they have entered through it, it will be closed.\""],[5835,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, mentioning Paradise: \"In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.\""],[5836,"Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib asked the Prophet ﷺ permission to emigrate. He said to him: \"O uncle, remain in your place where you are, for God will seal emigration with you as He sealed prophethood with me.\""],[5837,"The Prophet ﷺ returned from one of his expeditions on a hot day. Water was placed for him to cool himself with it. Al-Abbas, may God have mercy on him, came and turned his back to him and covered him with a cloak he was wearing. He said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"Your uncle al-Abbas, O Messenger of God.\" When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he raised his hands until they appeared from the cloak and said: \"May God cover you and your offspring from the Fire, O uncle.\""],[5838,"We went on an expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we met the polytheists, we fought them until we separated from them at evening. Both parties were exhausted and tired. A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ did not tire or weary; he did not leave any isolated or separated one of the people except that he killed him. The people marveled at his endurance. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Hell, let him look at this one.\" A man from the people said: \"By God, I will be his companion until I see what becomes of him.\" He was wounded and became distressed at death. He took his sword, placed it on his liver, then leaned on it until it came out of his back. The man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and informed him of that. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A servant may perform deeds of obedience to God, exalted is He, as they appear to people, yet he is recorded with God among the people of Hell; and a servant may perform deeds of disobedience to God as they appear to people, yet he is recorded with God among the people of Paradise.\""],[5839,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on a white earth like a pure white loaf of bread.\""],[5840,"I heard Sahl b. Sa'd say: Bad omens were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"If there is bad omen in anything, it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse.\""],[5841,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one day with the people behind him. He began to pray and then moved backwards.\""],[5842,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “A morning spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains, and an evening spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains, and the space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what it contains.”"],[5843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a man to a woman for an iron ring whose stone was of silver."],[5844,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: “What do you think of the worthlessness of this to its owners?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is a dead sheep.” He said: “By Allah, the world is more worthless to Allah than this is to its owners.”"],[5845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever frees a slave for Allah, Allah will free for every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire.”"],[5846,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “People follow Quraysh in good and evil.”"],[5847,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A morning or an evening spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains.”"],[5848,"There occurred a dispute among the Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf until they threw stones at each other. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he went out to reconcile them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delayed until Bilāl called the adhān for prayer. Then he came to Abū Bakr and said to him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been delayed; will you lead the prayer?” Abū Bakr said: “Yes.” So he made the iqāmah and Abū Bakr ؓ stepped forward and said the takbīr. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared, and the people clapped for Abū Bakr, but he would not turn around during his prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved through the people until Abū Bakr heard his footsteps behind him, so he began to step back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Stay where you are, O Abū Bakr, and lead us in prayer.” Abū Bakr raised his hands to the sky to step back, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished, he said: “O Abū Bakr, what prevented you, when I commanded you to lead the people in prayer, from leading them?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, it was not appropriate for the son of Abū Quḥāfah to lead the prayer in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “You raise your hands to the sky?” He said: “I praised Allah when you commanded me to lead you in prayer.” Then he turned to the people and said: “O people, what is the matter with you that when something occurred during your prayer you resorted to clapping? Clapping is only for women. If something occurs to someone during his prayer, let him say subḥān Allāh, and the one next to him should turn to him.”"],[5849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If something occurs to you, you resort to clapping. If something occurs to you during your prayer, then glorification (tasbīḥ) is for men and clapping is for women.”"],[5850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a rolling place of musk like the rolling places of your riding animals in this world.”"],[5851,"I said to Sahl b. Saʿd: “Were there sieves at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “I did not see a sieve in that time, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not eat sifted barley until he departed from this world.” I said: “How did you prepare it?” He said: “We would grind it, then blow on it, so whatever flew away flew away, and whatever remained we used.”"],[5852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two times when supplication is not rejected: at the time of prayer and at the time of fighting.”"],[5853,"The Messenger of God ﷺ never had his fill twice in a single day until he departed this world."],[5854,"“We used to rejoice on Friday.” I said to him, “And what was that?” He said, “A woman of the tribe would take chard and pour it over barley with vinegar, and when Friday came she would pull it up by its roots and gather onto it some barley, then put it in a pot of hers, then insert it into her oven, and serve it to us. We used to call it ‘drowned chard’ and lick it, and we used to rejoice on Friday because of her pot; and the midday nap used to be for the midday meal on Friday, after the Friday prayer, in the time of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[5855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not enter the houses of the dhimmis except with permission.”"],[5856,"The Messenger of God ﷺ held a wedding feast when Safiyyah entered upon him. I said, “What was in his wedding feast?” He said, “There was nothing but dates and sawiq.”"],[5857,"Ill omens were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the dwelling, the horse, and the woman.”"],[5858,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ walking behind the funeral procession.”"],[5859,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ while his companions were with him. She went around them and found no place. A man noticed her and stood up, so she sat down and fulfilled her need. Then she stood up, and the Prophet ﷺ said to the man, \"Do you know her?\" He replied, \"No.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Did you not show kindness to her? May Allah have mercy on you.\" This happened three times."],[5860,"“The Prophet ﷺ married a woman from the desert people and saw whiteness on her, so he separated from her before consummating the marriage.”"],[5861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5862,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If something occurs to one of you during his prayer, let him glorify God, for glorification is for men and clapping is for women.”"],[5863,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5864,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray toward Jerusalem, and when the qiblah was changed, a man went to the people of Quba and found them praying the dawn prayer. He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ has been commanded to pray toward the Kaaba,” so their imam turned around until he faced the qiblah with them."],[5865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A whip from Paradise is better than this world and all it contains, and a morning expedition in the path of God or an evening expedition is better than this world and all it contains.”"],[5866,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “And you are amusing yourselves? By God, I shall part from you.” So he said: “Where to?” He said: “I shall go on a military expedition.” I said: “And is that in you?” He said: “I increase the ranks of the Muslims.”"],[5867,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange, so blessed are the strangers.” They said: “O Messenger of God, who are the strangers?” He said: “Those who set things right when people are corrupt.”"],[5868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were in a gathering that included ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ and his son. He said: “How do you think it will be when you are left behind in a time of the dregs of people, their covenants and vows have become mixed, and they have become intertwined, and they become like this?” And he interlaced his fingers. They said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “You take what you recognize and leave what you disapprove of, and each of you should attend to his own private affairs and leave the affairs of the general public.”"],[5869,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib brought water in a leather shield — meaning a buckler — on the day of Uḥud, and the Messenger of God ﷺ washed his face and said: “This water has become brackish,” meaning it had changed. He said: And Fāṭimah took a piece of a mat, burned it, and placed it on his wound."],[5870,"Words passed between ʿAlī and Fāṭimah ؓ, and ʿAlī went out angry and threw himself on the dust. The Messenger of God ﷺ asked her, and she said: “There were words between me and him, and he went out angry.” The Messenger of God ﷺ went out and found him sleeping on the dust. He woke him and began wiping the dust from his back, saying: “You are only Abū Turāb.” Sahl b. Saʿd said: “We used to praise him with it, but some people criticize him with it.”"],[5871,"“I used to take the pre-dawn meal with my family, and then my haste was such that I would catch the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[5872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of the small sins that are belittled, for the likeness of belittled sins is like a people who camped in the bottom of a valley, and one brought a stick and another brought a stick until they had gathered enough to cook their bread with. When belittled sins are taken by their doer, they destroy him.”"],[5873,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Allah, forgive the Companions and those who saw the one who saw me.\" He (the narrator) said: I said: \"What about his saying 'and those who saw'?\" He said: \"Those who saw the one who saw them.\""],[5874,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl b. Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were digging the trench and carrying the dirt on our shoulders. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Muhajirun and the Ansar.\""],[5875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.\""],[5876,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Khaybar: \"I will surely give the banner to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory.\" The people spent the night wondering who would be given it. When morning came, all the people went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, each hoping to be given it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Where is 'Ali b. Abi Talib?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he is suffering from an eye ailment.\" He sent for him, then spat in his eyes and prayed for him, and he was cured on the spot as if he had had no ailment. He gave him the banner. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall we fight them until they become like us?\" He said: \"Proceed gently until you reach their courtyard, then call them to Islam and inform them of the rights that are obligatory upon them therein. By Allah, for Allah to guide one man through your guidance is better for you than red camels.\""],[5877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will see the rooms in Paradise just as you see the stars in the sky.\""],[5878,"This is Fulan, a prince from the city, inviting you tomorrow to meet at the pulpit. He said, \"What should I say?\" He said, \"You should say, 'Abu Turab.'\" Sahel laughed and then said, \"By Allah, no one called him by this name except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and by Allah, there was no name dearer to him than this.\" Abdul Aziz said, \"My father, O Abu Abbas, how did that happen?\" He said, \"Ali entered upon Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , then he came out and lay down in the mosque. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered upon Fatima and said, 'Where is your cousin?' She said, 'He is over there in the mosque.' So the Prophet ﷺ went out and found his cloak had fallen from his back and dust had settled on it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped the dust off his back and said, 'Sit, O Abu Turab, sit, O Abu Turab.' By Allah, there was no name dearer to him than the name that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him.\""],[5879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast and do not delay it as the people of the east delay it.\""],[5880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a certain woman, whom he named, saying: \"Tell your carpenter slave to make for me some wooden planks from which I can address the people.\" He made for him these three steps from tamarisk wood of al-Ghabah. The Prophet ﷺ ordered them, meaning the steps, and they were placed in this spot. Sahl said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ on the first day he sat on them. He said the takbir, and the people behind him said the takbir. Then he bowed while on the pulpit, then raised his head, then descended backward and prostrated at the base of the pulpit. Then he returned until he finished the end of his prayer, doing in it as he had done in the first rak'ah. When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he faced the people and said: \"O people, I did this only so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.\""],[5881,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If something occurs to someone during his prayer, let him say 'Subhan Allah' (glory be to Allah), and clapping is for women.\""],[5882,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked at him, then said: \"What is your opinion of this man?\" I said: \"This is a man of the nobles of the people. This man, if he proposes marriage, he is worthy to be married; if he intercedes, he is worthy to be allowed intercession; and if he speaks, he is worthy to be listened to.\" Then another man passed by, and he said: \"What is your opinion of this man?\" I said: \"This is a man of the poor Muslims. This man, if he speaks, he is worthy not to be listened to; if he proposes, he is worthy not to be married; and if he intercedes, he is worthy not to be allowed intercession.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This one is better than an earth full of the likes of that one.\""],[5883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The lowest in station among the people of Paradise—and there is no lowly one in it—is the one who will wish and say with an eloquent, fluent tongue and a collected mind: 'Give me, give me such and such,' until when he finds nothing, he will be prompted, and it will be said to him: 'Say such and such, say such and such.' Then it will be said to him: 'It is yours, and the like of it with it.'\""],[5884,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl b. Sa'd, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour were sent like these two,\" and he gestured with his two fingers."],[5885,"Narrated Sa'd bin Sa`d: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"The space occupied in Paradise by a whip is better than everything upon which the sun rises or sets.\""],[5886,"A woman brought the Prophet ﷺ a woven cloak with a border, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I wove this with my own hands and came to clothe you with it.” A man—he named him—felt it and said, “O Messenger of Allah, how fine this cloak is! Clothe me with it?” He said, “Yes.” When he entered, he folded it and sent it to him. The people said, “By Allah, you have not done well. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was clothed with it while he needed it, then you asked him for it, knowing that he does not turn away a beggar?” He said, “By Allah, I did not ask him for it to wear it, but I asked him for it so that it might be my shroud on the day I die.” Sahl said, “And it was his shroud on the day he died.”"],[5887,"We used to say, “The pulpit is at one of the gates of Paradise.” Sahl said, “Do you know what a tur‘ah is? It is the gate.”"],[5888,"“I never saw marrow until Allah took the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He was asked, “Did you have sieves in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “I never saw a sieve until Allah took His Messenger.” He was asked, “How did you eat unsieved barley?” He said, “Yes, we blew on it, and whatever flew off, flew off.”"],[5889,"A cup containing water was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he drank from it. On his right was a boy, the youngest of the people, and the elders were on his left. When he finished, he said, “O boy, do you permit me to give it to the elders?” The boy said, “I would not prefer anyone over what is left from you.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed it in the boy’s hand."],[5890,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise, as you see, yet he is among the people of the Fire; and a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire, as you see, yet he is among the people of Paradise.”"],[5891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A morning or an evening spent in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5892,"“Abu Usayd al-Sa‘idi stopped for the night, and his wife steeped dates from the night. When morning came, she strained it and gave it to the Prophet ﷺ to drink.”"],[5893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I will precede you to the Pool. Whoever comes to me will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst again. Beware that there should not come to me people whom I know and who know me, then a barrier shall be placed between me and them.”"],[5894,"“I saw one better than me and you doing this.”"],[5895,"“Between the prayer place of the Prophet ﷺ and the wall there was the space of a sheep’s passage.”"],[5896,"About the wound of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, he said: “His face was wounded, his front tooth was broken, and the helmet was crushed on his head. Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was washing the blood while Ali ؓ poured water for her with a shield. When Fatimah saw that the water only increased the blood, she took a piece of a mat and burned it until it became ash, then pressed it onto the wound, and the blood stopped.”"],[5897,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand and seven hundred thousand from my nation will enter paradise, clinging to one another like the stars on a moonlit night.\""],[5898,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of uncertainty.”"],[5899,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A servant does not believe until he believes in divine decree.”"],[5900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the Quran were in a hide, the Fire would not touch it.”"],[5901,"“We did not take a midday nap nor eat lunch except after the Friday prayer.”"],[5902,"“I used to eat the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then my only haste was to catch the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[5903,"“We used to rejoice on Friday.” I said: “And why?” He said: “There was an old woman of ours who would send and take from the roots of chard, then throw them into a pot and grind some grains of barley and put them in it. When we had prayed the Friday prayer, we would go to her, and we rejoiced on Friday because of that, and we did not take a midday nap except after the Friday prayer.”"],[5904,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I and the guardian of an orphan will be in Paradise like this,” and he gestured with his two fingers and separated them."],[5905,"We used to say: “If there is any ill omen in anything, it is in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse.”"],[5906,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have come to give myself to you.” She stood for a long time while the Prophet ﷺ did not look at her. He raised his gaze to her and lowered it. When her standing became prolonged, she withdrew and sat down. A man from the people stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you have anything to give her as a dowry?” He said: “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Go and look.” He went and then returned and said: “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing.” He said: “Go and search, even for an iron ring.” He went and then returned and said: “No, by Allah, I found nothing, not even an iron ring.” He said, while he was wearing a lower garment and had no upper garment: “O Messenger of Allah, my lower garment.” He said: “If you wear your lower garment, she will have nothing of it, and if she wears it, you will have nothing of it.” The man withdrew, then stood up. The Prophet ﷺ saw him turning away, so he ordered that he be called. He said: “What do you have of the Quran?” He said: “Surah so-and-so and Surah so-and-so,” for surahs he counted. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Go, for I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Quran.”"],[5907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on a white earth like a loaf of pure bread, with no landmark for anyone.”"],[5908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. The prayer became due, so Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said: “O Abu Bakr, the prayer time has come and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is delayed. Will you lead the people?” He said: “If you wish.” Bilal called the iqamah, and Abu Bakr stepped forward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and the people began clapping. Abu Bakr ؓ would not turn around during his prayer. When the people did it repeatedly, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the row. The Prophet ﷺ gestured, so Abu Bakr raised his hand and praised Allah, then retreated backward until he returned to the row. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished, he faced the people and said: “O people, why is it that when something occurred to you in prayer you resorted to clapping? Clapping is only for women. Whoever has something occur to him in prayer should say ‘Glory be to Allah,’ for no one hears it except that he turns to him. O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from praying when I gestured to you?” He said: “It was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafah to pray in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[5909,"“The people did not use the era from the sending of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor from his death; they only counted from his arrival in Madinah.”"],[5910,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever enters this mosque of mine to learn good or to teach it is like a warrior in the path of Allah, and whoever enters it for other than that, such as people’s talk, is like one who sees what pleases him while it belongs to someone else.”"],[5911,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I and the Hour have been sent like this from this,” and Sufyān indicated with his index and middle fingers."],[5912,"They asked Sahl b. Saʿd, “From what wood was the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ made?” He said, “There is no one left among the people who knows more about it than I. It was made from the tamarisk of al-Ghābah. So-and-so, the freedman of so-and-so, made it for him. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he climbed onto it: he faced the qiblah and said the takbīr, then recited, then bowed, then descended backwards and prostrated, then climbed up, recited, bowed, descended backwards, then prostrated.”"],[5913,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to reconcile between the Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf in a matter that had occurred among them, until they threw stones at one another. When the prayer time came, Bilāl gave the call to prayer, but the Messenger of God ﷺ was delayed, so Abū Bakr ؓ stepped forward to lead the people in prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and began making his way through the rows. When he reached the row next to Abū Bakr, the people began clapping. Abū Bakr was a man who never turned around during the prayer, but when he heard that, he turned and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to him to remain in place. Abū Bakr ؓ raised his head to the sky in thanks to God, stepped back backwards, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came forward. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he turned to us and said, “O Abū Bakr, what prevented you from remaining when I gestured to you?” He replied, “God would never see the son of Abū Quḥāfah standing before the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to the people and said, “O people, why, when something happened to you in your prayer, did you start clapping? Clapping is only for women, and glorification (tasbīḥ) is for men. Whoever experiences something in his prayer should say: subḥāna Allāh.”"],[5914,"He heard Sahl b. Saʿd say: I was among the people with the Prophet ﷺ when a woman came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, I have given myself to you, so consider me as you see fit.” A man stood up and said, “Marry her to me, O Messenger of God, if you have no need of her.” The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. Then she stood again and said the same thing, and the man said, “Marry her to me, O Messenger of God, if you have no need of her.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the man, “Do you have anything to give her?” He said, “No.” He said, “Go and look for something.” He went, then came back and said, “O Messenger of God, I did not find anything.” He said, “Go and look, even for an iron ring.” He went, then came back and said, “O Messenger of God, I did not find anything, not even an iron ring.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do you have any of the Qurʾān with you?” He said, “Yes, Sūrah so-and-so and Sūrah so-and-so.” He said, “Go, for I have married her to you for what you have of the Qurʾān.”"],[5915,"The people disagreed about what the wound of the Messenger of God ﷺ was treated with on the day of Uḥud, so they asked Sahl, who was among the last of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ remaining in Madinah. He said, “No Muslim remains who knows more about it than I. Fāṭimah ؓ was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and ʿAlī ؓ was bringing water in his shield. A mat was taken and burned, and his wound was stuffed with it.”"],[5916,"I asked Sahl b. Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, “With what was the wound of the Messenger of God ﷺ treated on the day of Uḥud?” He said, “No one on the face of the earth knows more about it than I. ʿAlī ؓ was carrying water in his shield, Fāṭimah was washing the blood, and a mat was burned and stuffed into it.”"],[5917,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ died while a woolen cloak of his was still in the loom being woven.”"],[5918,"A suit of black wool with white wool tassels was woven for the Messenger of God ﷺ. He went out to the gathering wearing it and struck his thigh, saying, “Do you not see how fine this suit is?” A bedouin said, “O Messenger of God, give me this suit to wear.” Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ was asked for something, he never said “no” to anything he was asked for. He said, “Yes.” He called for two tied garments, put them on, and gave the suit to the bedouin. He ordered a similar one to be woven for him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ died while it was still in the loom."],[5919,"There was a conflict among the Anṣār, so the Prophet ﷺ went out to reconcile them. He said to Bilāl, “If I am delayed, call the prayer and tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” Then the Prophet ﷺ came while Abū Bakr ؓ was leading the people in prayer, and he prayed behind him."],[5920,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever fasts the day of ʿArafah, his sins of two consecutive years will be forgiven.”"],[5921,"'The Prophet ﷺ was invited to the wedding feast of a man from the Anṣār. We stood up with the Prophet ﷺ when he was invited, and he fed us barley bread. Then the servant who was serving us food and giving us drink was verily the bride herself.'"],[5922,"It is an old matter; that had already happened. We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he was approached and told that something had occurred among the people of Qubāʾ. The Prophet ﷺ went to them to reconcile between them, and he was delayed from the people. Bilāl said to Abū Bakr ؓ, 'Shall I call the iqāmah for the prayer?' He said, 'Whatever you wish.' So he called the iqāmah, and the people put Abū Bakr forward. While he was praying, the Prophet ﷺ came and began making his way through the rows until he stood behind Abū Bakr ؓ. The people began clapping, but Abū Bakr did not turn around during the prayer. When they did it a lot, he turned around and saw the Prophet ﷺ standing behind him. The Prophet ﷺ gestured to him to continue praying as he was, so Abū Bakr stepped back, and the Prophet ﷺ came forward. When he finished, he said to Abū Bakr ؓ, 'What prevented you, when I commanded you, from continuing to pray?' He said, 'It is not fitting for the son of Abū Quḥāfah to lead the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What is this clapping in prayer? Glorification is for men and clapping is for women.'"],[5923,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and offered herself to him, but he remained silent. A man stood up and said, 'O Messenger of God, if you have no need of her, marry her to me.' He said, 'Do you have anything?' He said, 'No, by God, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Do you know anything of the Qurʾān?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What?' He said, 'Sūrah so-and-so and Sūrah so-and-so.' He said, 'I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Qurʾān.' I saw him going off and she was following him."],[5924,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God ﷻ is noble and loves nobility; He loves lofty character and dislikes its lowly aspects.'"],[5925,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand or seven hundred thousand of my Ummah (nation) will enter Paradise without being held accountable.\""],[5926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf concerning a dispute that was between them. The time for the ʿAṣr prayer came, so Bilāl said, 'Shall I call the iqāmah, O Abū Bakr, and you lead the people in prayer?' Bilāl called the iqāmah, and Abū Bakr ؓ stepped forward and led the people in prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ came, making his way through the rows, and the people clapped. Abū Bakr would hardly turn around in his prayer, but the people clapped a lot, so Abū Bakr turned around and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ making his way through the rows. Abū Bakr stepped back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, 'Stay where you are.' He stepped back, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said, 'O Abū Bakr, what was the matter with you that when I gestured to you to stay in your place, you did not stay?' He said, 'It was not for the son of Abū Quḥāfah to lead the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer.' Then he said to the people, 'What is the matter with you that when something happens you clap? Glorify; clapping is only for women.'"],[5927,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Give them compensation, even if it is a whip,' meaning in marriage."],[5928,"There was fighting between Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf b. ʿAwf, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ. He prayed Ẓuhr and then went to them to reconcile between them. He said, 'O Bilāl, if the time for ʿAṣr comes and I have not come to you, tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' When the time for the ʿAṣr prayer came, he called the adhān and the iqāmah, then he ordered Abū Bakr, who stepped forward. The Messenger of God ﷺ came while Abū Bakr was in prayer and made his way through the people until he stood behind Abū Bakr in the row next to him. The people clapped, but Abū Bakr, when he entered prayer, would not turn around until he finished. When he saw that the clapping did not stop, he turned around and saw the Prophet ﷺ behind him. The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to him to go ahead, and he said with his hand like this. Abū Bakr remained for a little while, praised God for what the Prophet ﷺ said, then he stepped backward. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he came forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said, 'O Abū Bakr, what prevented you, when I gestured to you, from continuing?' He said, 'It was not for the son of Abū Quḥāfah to lead the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer.' He said, and he said to the people, 'If something alarms you, let the men glorify and the women clap.' The wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿĀrim."],[5929,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When God brings a servant to sixty, He has excused him and given him full span of life.'"],[5930,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and offered herself to him. He said, 'I have no need for women today.' A man said, 'O Messenger of God, marry her to me.' He said, 'What do you have?' He said, 'I have nothing.' He said, 'Give her something, even an iron ring.' He said, 'I have nothing.' He said, 'What do you have of the Qurʾān?' He said, 'Such-and-such.' He said, 'I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Qurʾān.' The wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿĀrim."],[5931,"A young man from the Anṣār had recently married. He went out with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition, but he returned from the road to look at his family. He found a woman standing in the chamber, so he aimed his spear at her. She said, 'Enter and see what is in the house.' He entered and found a snake coiled on his bed, so he pierced it with his spear. Then he planted the spear in the courtyard. The snake convulsed and the man convulsed, so the snake died and the man died. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Muslim jinn have settled in Madinah,' or he said, 'These houses have inhabitants. When you see any of them, seek refuge from it, and if it returns, then kill it.'"],[5932,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyān. The fasting people will be called to it; it will be said to them, \"Come.\" When they enter, they will close that gate, and no one else will enter with them.'"],[5933,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while their clothes were tightly tied around their necks due to the tightness of their clothes."],[5934,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and offered herself to him. He remained silent and did not respond, so she stood there for a long time until we pitied her because of how long she had been standing. Then a man stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you have anything to give as mahr (dowry)?\" The man replied, \"I have nothing except my waistbelt (shamlah), which I am wearing.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you agree to marry her with what you have from the Quran?\" The man said, \"Yes, by Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ then told him, \"Go and search even if it is just an iron ring.\" So the man went and stayed for as long as Allah willed. Then he returned and said, \"I could not find anything, not even an iron ring.\" The Prophet ﷺ then asked him, \"What do you have from the Quran?\" The man mentioned certain verses. The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"I have married you to her based on what you have from the Quran.\""],[5935,"The Messenger of God said: “In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it.”"],[5936,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the people of the upper chambers as you see a star in the horizon of the sky.”"],[5937,"A man from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ began praising him and mentioning his worship while the Messenger of God ﷺ was silent. When they fell silent, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Did he remember death often?” They said: No. He said: “Did he give up much of what he desired?” They said: No. He said: “Your companion did not attain much of what you are attributing to him.”"],[5938,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who points to good is like the one who does it.”"],[5939,"“We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then return and take a midday nap.”"],[5940,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “People will remain in good as long as they hasten to break the fast.”"],[5941,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drink, with a boy on his right and elders on his left. He drank and then passed it to the boy.”"],[5942,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at the Trench while we were digging and he was carrying away the dirt. He said: “O God, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun.”"],[5943,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tomorrow I will certainly give the banner to a man through whose hands God will grant victory.” The people went early to the Messenger of God ﷺ, all of them hoping to be given the banner. He said: “Where is Ali?” They said: He is suffering from an eye ailment, O Messenger of God. He said: “Send for him.” He was brought, and the Messenger of God ﷺ spat in his eyes and prayed, and he was healed. Then he handed him the banner and said: “Advance and do not turn aside until you reach the people and call them to me.” Ali advanced, then turned and said: O Messenger of God, should we fight them until they say “There is no god but God”? He said: “Take it easy. When you come to them, call them to say ‘There is no god but God.’ If one man becomes a Muslim through your hands, that is better for you than having red camels.”"],[5944,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a woman came to him offering herself to him. He lowered his gaze at her and raised it, but he did not respond to her. A man among his companions said, “O Messenger of God, marry her to me.” He said, “Do you have anything?” He said, “No, by God, O Messenger of God, I have nothing.” He said, “Not even a ring of iron?” He said, “Not even a ring of iron, but I will split this cloak of mine and give her half, and take the other half.” He said, “No, but do you have anything of the Quran with you?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Go, for I have married her to you for what you have of the Quran.”"],[5945,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of the Fire. And a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Paradise.”"],[5946,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ say, holding his middle finger and the one next to the thumb, “I and the Hour have been sent like this.”"],[5947,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “A morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5948,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a drink and drank from it, then handed it to a boy on his right, while the elders were on his left."],[5949,"There was a dispute between two clans of the Ansar, from Banu Amr b. Awf, until they threw stones at each other. The news reached the Prophet ﷺ while Bilal had already called the adhan for Zuhr prayer. The Prophet ﷺ went to reconcile between them, and was delayed. Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said, “Will you lead the prayer so I may announce the iqamah?” He said, “Yes.” Bilal announced the iqamah and Abu Bakr stepped forward. Then the Prophet ﷺ came, making his way through the rows until he stood behind Abu Bakr. The people began to clap, but Abu Bakr would not turn around during his prayer. When they did it excessively, he turned around and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ. He stepped back walking backwards, so the Prophet ﷺ pushed him forward and prayed. When he finished the prayer, he turned to Abu Bakr and said, “What prevented you from remaining in front when I ordered you?” He said, “It is not for God to see the son of Abu Quhafah lead the Messenger of God ﷺ in prayer.” Then he turned to the people and said, “O people, what is the matter with you that when something happens to you during your prayer, you turn to clapping? Clapping is only for women, and glorification (tasbih) is for men.”"],[5950,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “A morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that it contains. And the space of one of your whips in Paradise is better than the world and all that it contains.”"],[5951,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his thighs will enter Paradise.”"],[5952,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and offered herself to him, but he remained silent. She then presented herself to him again, and he remained silent. He said, \"I saw her standing or leaning, offering herself to him while he remained silent.\" A man from the Ansar (helpers) stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need for her, then marry her to me.\" He said, \"Do you have anything to offer?\" The man said, \"No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Then go and find something, even if it is just a ring made of iron.\" So the man went and then returned, saying, \"By Allah, I did not find anything except for this garment of mine, which is the most precious thing I have between me and her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no favor for you in your garment, so have you memorized anything from the Quran?\" The man said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"What?\" The man mentioned a specific chapter. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have indeed given her away with what you have from the Quran.\" Then, I saw him walking while she was following him."],[5953,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “People will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast.”"],[5954,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “People will continue to be upon good as long as they hasten the iftar.”"],[5955,"They used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ while they had tied their waist-wrappers from their smallness onto their necks. It was said to the women, “Do not raise your heads until the men are seated upright.”"],[5956,"We used to pray Jumu'ah, then we would return and take a midday nap."],[5957,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Tasbih (saying subhan Allah) is for men, and clapping is for women.\""],[5958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A morning's or an evening's journey in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5959,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A morning's journey in the path of Allah, or an evening's journey, is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5960,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A morning's journey in the path of Allah, or an evening's journey, is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5961,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A morning's journey in the path of Allah, or an evening's journey, is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5962,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"My pulpit is upon one of the streams of Paradise.\""],[5963,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed which, if I do it, will make people love me.\" He said: \"Be abstinent in this world, and Allah will love you; and be abstinent in what people possess, and people will love you.\""],[5964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Everything has a zakat, and the zakat of the body is fasting.\""],[5965,"It never happened that Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked for anything and he said: No. (Using translation from Muslim 2311a)"],[5966,"We used to have lunch and then pray Jumu'ah."],[5967,"There was a dispute between two men of the Ansar, so the Prophet ﷺ went to reconcile between them at the time of prayer. When the prayer became due, Bilal came to Abu Bakr ؓ and said: \"O Abu Bakr, the prayer has become due and the Prophet ﷺ is not here. Shall I give the adhan and iqamah and you lead the prayer?\" He said: \"Whatever you wish.\" So he gave the adhan and iqamah, and Abu Bakr began the prayer. Then the Prophet ﷺ came during the remainder of that prayer, so the people clapped. Abu Bakr started to move back, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured to him to remain in his place. When Abu Bakr moved aside, the Prophet ﷺ came forward and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he said: \"O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from remaining as I ordered you?\" He said: \"It is not for the son of Abu Quhafah to stand ahead of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand by a tree trunk. When the number of people increased, they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the people have increased. Why not have a pulpit made for you to stand on? For the one who comes will find it difficult to go back without hearing anything from you.\" So he ordered a young servant of the Ansar, who took some tamarisk wood from al-Ghabah and made this pulpit for him. When he sat upon it, the tree trunk that he used to stand by lamented, so he came and placed his hand on it until it became silent."],[5969,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came and said: \"O Messenger of God, among the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf words were exchanged until they threw stones at one another.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That has long been the case among them. Let us go to them.\" Ubayy b. Ka'b and Suhayl b. Bayda' stood up with him, and he made peace between them. Then the prayer time arrived, and Bilal gave the call to prayer, but the Messenger of God ﷺ was delayed in returning to them, meaning he was slow. The people said to Abu Bakr: \"Go forward (and lead the prayer).\" He said: \"Do you think that is right?\" They said: \"Yes.\" So he went forward. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came, and the people began clapping. Abu Bakr ؓ would not turn around during the prayer, but when he heard them clapping, he turned and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ. He stepped back on his heels, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: \"Stay in your place.\" So he moved back, and the Messenger of God ﷺ stepped forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished, he said: \"O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from remaining in your place when I gestured to you?\" He replied: \"It was not for the son of Abu Quhafa to stand in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Why did I see you clapping? If something occurs to someone during the prayer, then glorification (tasbih) is for men and clapping is for women.\""],[5970,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have given myself to you as a gift.\" He remained silent. A man from the Ansar said: \"O Messenger of God, if you have no need of her, then marry her to me.\" He said: \"Do you have anything (as a dowry)?\" He said: \"No, by God.\" He said: \"Can you recite anything from the Qur'an?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Qur'an.\""],[5971,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr: \"How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people, whose covenants and trusts have been mixed up, and they have differed and become like this?\" and he interlaced his fingers. He said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Act according to what you know and leave what you disapprove of. Beware of wavering in the religion of God. Keep to your own self and leave the common people.\""],[5972,"About the matter while he and she were in a single garment, fearing that something of the Qur'an might be revealed concerning it."],[5973,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Uhud when his face was wounded, his front tooth was broken, and his helmet was smashed. 'Ali ؓ brought him water in a leather shield, and Fatimah ؓ came and washed the blood from him, burned a piece of a palm-leaf mat, and placed it on his wound."],[5974,"'Adi b. Hatim came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my father used to maintain ties of kinship, bear the burden of the needy, and feed people.\" He said: \"Did he live to see Islam?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Your father loved to be remembered, and so he is remembered.\""],[5975,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour have been sent like these two,\" and he gestured with his two fingers."],[5976,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drink while the elders were on his left and a young boy, the youngest of the people, was on his right. He said to the boy: \"Will you permit me to give it to the elders?\" He said: \"I would not prefer anyone over you for my share from you.\" So he gave it to him."],[5977,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had seven dinars which he had placed with ʿĀʾishah. When he was in his illness, he said: “O ʿĀʾishah, take the gold to ʿAlī.” Then he fell unconscious, and ʿĀʾishah was distracted by his condition. He said that several times, each time the Messenger of God ﷺ fell unconscious and ʿĀʾishah was distracted by his condition. Then she sent it to ʿAlī ؓ , and he gave it as charity. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered Monday night in the throes of death, so ʿĀʾishah sent a lamp of hers to one of her women and said: “Give us some of the skins of clarified butter for our lamp, for the Messenger of God ﷺ has entered the throes of death.”"],[5978,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I will give the banner tomorrow to a man through whom God will grant victory.” The people were wondering which of them would receive it. He said: “Where is ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib?” They said: “O Messenger of God, he is complaining of his eyes.” So they sent for him, and he was brought. The Messenger of God ﷺ spat into his eye and prayed for him, and he recovered as if he had had no pain. Then he gave him the banner. ʿAlī said: “O Messenger of God, shall I fight them until they become like us?” He said: “Go at your ease until you enter their courtyard, then call them to Islam and inform them of what is obligatory upon them of the rights of God. For God to guide one man through you is better than for you to have red camels.”"],[5979,"By God, I know what it is, and I saw it the first day it was placed and the first day the Messenger of God ﷺ sat on it. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent to a certain woman, whom Sahl named, saying: “Tell your carpenter slave to make me a wooden structure on which I can sit when I speak to the people.” She ordered him, and he made it from the tamarisk of al-Ghābah. Then he brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so she sent it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered it to be placed here. Then I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said the takbir while on it, then bowed while on it, then descended backwards and prostrated at the base of the minbar, then climbed again. When he finished, he turned to the people and said: “O people, I did this so that you may follow me and learn my prayer.”"],[5980,"A woman came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I have come to give myself to you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at her, raising his gaze and lowering it, then bowed his head. When the woman saw that he had not decided anything about her, she sat down. Then a man from among his companions stood up and said: “O Messenger of God, if you have no need of her, marry her to me.” He said: “Do you have anything?” He said: “No.” He said: “What do you have of the Quran?” He said: “Surah so-and-so and Surah so-and-so.” He said: “I have married her to you for what you have of the Quran.”"],[5981,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed that there was some dispute among Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf. He mentioned the hadith, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tasbīḥ is for men, and clapping is for women.”"],[5982,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed that there was some dispute among Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf. He mentioned the hadith, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tasbīḥ is for men, and clapping is for women.”"],[5983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed that there was some dispute among Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf. He mentioned the hadith, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tasbīḥ is for men, and clapping is for women.”"],[5984,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I am your predecessor at the Pond. Whoever comes to it will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst again. Some people will come to me whom I recognize and who recognize me, but then a barrier will be placed between me and them.”"],[5985,"O Messenger of God, I wove this with my own hands to clothe you. The Messenger of God ﷺ took it, though he needed it, and came out to us wearing it as his waist-wrapper. A man from the group felt it and said: “O Messenger of God, give it to me to wear?” He said: “Yes.” The man sat for as long as God willed in the gathering, then he returned, folded it, and sent it back to him. The people said to him: “You did not do well. You asked it of him when you knew that he does not refuse anyone who asks.” The man said: “By God, I asked for it only so that it might be my shroud on the day I die.” Sahl said: “And it was his shroud.” Qutaybah said: “He was Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ.”"],[5986,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the upper chambers in Paradise as you see the star on the horizon of the sky.”"],[5987,"I asked Sahl b. Saʿd: “Did the Messenger of God ﷺ eat marrow?” Sahl said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not see marrow from the time God sent him until God took him.”"],[5988,"Abū Usayd al-Sāʿidī came and invited the Messenger of God ﷺ to his wedding feast. His wife was serving them that day, and she was the bride. Abū Usayd said: “Do you know what I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ to drink? I had soaked dates for him overnight.”"],[5989,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ met the polytheists and they fought. When the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew to his camp, the others withdrew to their camp. Among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ there was a man who would not leave any isolated one or straggler of theirs but he followed it with a strike of his sword. Then he mentioned the hadith."],[5990,"The Messenger of God ﷺ described Paradise and said, \"In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.\""],[5991,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Indeed, in the loins of the loins of the loins of men among my Companions are men and women who will enter Paradise without reckoning.\" Then he recited {And others of them who have not yet joined them, and He is the Mighty, the Wise}."],[5992,"\"We used to take a midday nap after the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[5993,"A drink was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, with a boy on his right and the elders on his left. The Prophet ﷺ drank, then said to the boy, \"Shall I give it to the elders?\" The boy said, \"I would not prefer anyone over you for your leftover, or for the blessing I get from you.\" So the Prophet ﷺ gave it to him, and he drank, and he left the elders."],[5994,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Clapping is only for women, and saying subhan Allah is for men.\""],[5995,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Fatimah, \"Where is your husband?\" She said, \"There was some talk between me and him, and he went out angry.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, \"Look for Ali for me.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, there he is in the mosque.\" The Prophet ﷺ came to him while the wind was blowing dust over him. He said, \"Get up, O Abu Turab.\" Sahl said, \"By God, it was the most beloved of his names to him.\""],[5996,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever sits in the mosque waiting for the prayer is in prayer.\""],[5997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not revile Tubba', for he had embraced Islam.”"],[5998,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ, he said: “When one of you prays toward a sutrah, let him draw near to it, so that Satan may not pass between him and his prayer.” This is how Ibn Lahi'ah narrated it, from 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Ja'far, from Safwan b. Sulaym, from Nafi' b. Jubayr, from Sahl b. Sa'd. And Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from Safwan b. Sulaym, from Nafi' b. Jubayr, from Sahl b. Abi Hathmah."],[5999,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you prays toward a sutrah, let him draw near to it, so that Satan may not cut off his prayer upon him.”"],[6000,"“There was a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ whose name was Aswad, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Abyad.”"],[6001,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you will certainly follow the ways of those before you, just as one sandal matches another.”"],[6002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you will certainly follow the ways of those before you, just as one sandal matches another.”"],[6003,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you will certainly follow the ways of those before you, just as one sandal matches another.”"],[6004,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to his uncle al-'Abbas, may God have mercy on him: “I am the Seal of the Prophets.” Then he raised his hand and said: “O God, forgive al-'Abbas, the sons of al-'Abbas, and the sons of the sons of al-'Abbas.”"],[6005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were reciting the Qur'an, and some of us were teaching it to others. He said: “Praise be to God. The Book of God is one, and among you are the black and the red. Recite the Qur'an, recite the Qur'an, recite the Qur'an before there come people who recite the Qur'an and pronounce its letters perfectly, as an arrow is made straight, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They seek its reward in haste and do not defer it.”"],[6006,"I attended al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf beating Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa‘d al-Sa‘idi concerning the affair of Ibn al-Zubayr. His father Sahl appeared in his waist-wrapper and cloak, and shouted at al-Hajjaj, “Do you not remember the injunction of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning us?” He said, “What did the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoin concerning you?” He said, “He enjoined that good be done to the good-doer of the Ansar, and that pardon be granted to their wrongdoer.” So he released him."],[6007,"I swear by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over Suhail b. al-Baida' in the mosque. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3189)"],[6008,"From ‘Urwah, “In the naming of those who attended Badr from Quraysh, then from Banu al-Harith ibn Fihr: Suhayl ibn Bayda’.”"],[6009,"From Ibn Shihab, “In the naming of those who attended Badr from Quraysh, then from Banu al-Harith ibn Fihr: Suhayl ibn Bayda’.”"],[6010,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, Suhayl was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on his camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Suhayl ibn Bayda’,” and raised his voice. Suhayl said, “At your service,” and raised his voice. He did that twice or three times. Suhayl said, “The people knew that he wanted to say something for them to hear.” So those behind us caught up, and those in front held back for us until they gathered. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, God makes Paradise obligatory for him, and forbids him from the Fire thereby.”"],[6011,"From Ibn Shihab, “In the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Suhayl ibn ‘Ubayd ibn al-Nu‘man. No descendants.”"],[6012,"“Suhayl ibn ‘Amr died in Syria in the year eighteen.”"],[6013,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No people sit in a gathering remembering God ﷻ therein and then rise except that it is said to them: Rise, for God has forgiven you your sins and your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.'"],[6014,"The Messenger of God ﷺ marked out the trench from Ahmar al-Baskhatayn, the edge of Banu Harithah, in the year of the confederates, until it reached al-Madhabih. He allotted forty cubits for every ten men. The Muhajirun and the Ansar disputed over Salman al-Farisi, may God have mercy on him, and he was a strong man. The Muhajirun said: Salman is from us. The Ansar said: Salman is from us. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Salman is from us, the people of the house.'"],[6015,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6016,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6017,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6018,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6019,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6020,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6021,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6022,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6023,"He recited the Qur'an and paused at its ambiguous [verses], made lawful its lawful, and made unlawful its unlawful."],[6024,"He read the Quran and stopped at its ambiguous parts, then he clarified its lawful and unlawful."],[6025,"He recited the Quran and paused at its ambiguous verses, so he made lawful what is lawful in it and forbid what is forbidden in it."],[6026,"When death came to Salmān, he called me while he was in an upper room with four doors. He said, “Open these doors, O Buqayra, for I have visitors today, and I do not know from which of these doors they will enter upon me.” Then he called for some musk of his and said, “Soak it in a basin.” I did so. Then he said, “Sprinkle it around my bed, then go down and wait; you will soon see me carried on my bed.” I looked, and behold, his soul had been taken, and it was as if he were asleep on his bed or something like that."],[6027,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, “Three men will have the houris with large lovely eyes brought to them: ʿAlī, ʿAmmār, and Salmān ؓ.”"],[6028,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed Paradise longs for four: ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, ʿAmmār b. Yāsir, Salmān al-Fārisī, and al-Miqdād b. al-Aswad ؓ.”"],[6029,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his gaze toward the sky. I said, “O Messenger of God, what is this?” He said, “I saw an angel ascending with the deeds of Salmān.”"],[6030,"\"Ali said, 'Verily, every prophet is given seven intimate advisers, and we have been given fourteen. We asked Ali, 'Who are they?' He replied, 'Me, my two sons, Ja'far and Hamza, Abu Bakr, Umar, Mus'ab ibn Umair, Bilal, Salman, Ammar, and Abdullah ibn Mas'ood.' The number fourteen was not completed in this narrative.\""],[6031,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “Every prophet was given nine companions, and I have been given fourteen.” It was said to ʿAlī, “Who are they?” He said, “I, my two sons al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, Ḥamza, Jaʿfar, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, al-Miqdād, Salmān, Ṭalḥa, and al-Zubayr ؓ.” Fiṭr b. Khalīfa disagreed with Ibn ʿUyayna in the chain of this hadith."],[6032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “No prophet has been given seven companions who were noble, viziers, but I have been given fourteen: Ḥamza, Jaʿfar, ʿAlī, Ḥasan, Ḥusayn, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd, Abū Dharr, al-Miqdād, Ḥudhayfa, ʿAmmār, Salmān, and Bilāl, may God have mercy on them.”"],[6033,"Abū al-Dardāʾ went with Salmān al-Fārisī to ask for a woman of the Banū Layth in marriage for him. He entered and mentioned Salmān’s virtue, his precedence, and his Islam, and said that he was asking for their daughter so-and-so in marriage. They said, “As for Salmān, we will not marry him off, but we will marry you.” So he married her. Then he came out and said, “Something happened, and I am too shy to mention it.” Salmān said, “What is it?” Abū al-Dardāʾ told him the news, and Salmān said, “I am more entitled to feel shy than you, for I asked for her hand, but God had decreed her for you.”"],[6034,"He spent the night at Salmān’s to observe his exertion in worship. He said: He got up to pray at the end of the night, but it seemed he did not see what he had expected. He mentioned that to him, and Salmān, may God have mercy on him, said, “Guard these five prayers, for they are expiations for these wounds as long as the fatal blow is not struck. When people pray ʿIshāʾ, they disperse into three ranks: among them are those against whom it counts and not for them, those for whom it counts and not against them, and those for whom it neither counts for nor against. A man who seizes the darkness of the night during people’s heedlessness and rides headlong into sins—that is against him and not for him. A man who seizes the darkness of the night and people’s heedlessness and stands to pray—that is for him and not against him. A man who prays then sleeps—that is neither for him nor against him. Beware of excessive striving, and keep to moderation and steadfastness.”"],[6035,"There was a dispute between Salmān al-Fārisī and a man, so Salmān said, “O God, if he is lying, then do not cause him to die until one of three things befalls him.” When his anger had subsided, I said, “O Abū ʿAbd Allāh, what was the supplication you made against this man?” He said, “I will tell you: the tribulation of the Dajjāl, the tribulation of a ruler like the tribulation of the Dajjāl, and a severe greed that comes upon people—when a man acquires wealth, he does not care from where he got it.”"],[6036,"Salmān ؓ came with twelve riders or thirteen riders from the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ. When the prayer time arrived, they said, “Lead us, O Abū ʿAbd Allāh.” He said, “We will not lead you in prayer nor marry your women. God, exalted is He, guided us through you.” So a man from the group stepped forward and prayed four rakʿahs. When he said the salutation, Salmān said, “What do we have to do with the four? Half of the four would have sufficed us, and we are more in need of the concession.” ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: meaning while traveling."],[6037,"Salmān ؓ captured a slave girl. He said to her in Persian, “Pray.” She said, “No.” He said, “Prostrate once.” She said, “No.” It was said, “O Abū ʿAbd Allāh, what does a single prostration avail her?” He said, “If she had prayed, she would have prayed, and one who has a share in Islam is not like one who has no share.”"],[6038,"Salman al-Farisi used to say when he finished his food: Praise be to Allah who spared us the burden and granted us ample provision."],[6039,"Ibn Sireen reported that Abu Darda used to revive the night of Jumu'ah (Friday) and fast during its day. Salman came to him and the Prophet ﷺ had established a brotherly relationship between them, so Salman slept with him. Abu Darda intended to stay awake for the night, but Salman stood up to him and did not leave him until he fell asleep and broke his fast. Abu Darda then went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Salman knows better than you. Do not single out the night of Jumu'ah with prayer or its day with fasting.\""],[6040,"Zayd said to him: O Abu Abdullah, do you do this when you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"When the soul secures its provision, it becomes at ease and free for worship, and waswasah (whisperings) despairs of it.\""],[6041,"They said: Yes. They said: Are you the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I do not know. They doubted and said: Perhaps he is not the one we want. He said to them: I am your companion whom you seek; I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat with him. But his companion is only the one who enters Paradise with him. What do you need? They said: We came to you from a brother of yours in Syria. He said: Who is he? They said: Abu al-Darda'. He said: Where is the gift he sent with you? They said: He did not send any gift with us. He said: Fear Allah and deliver the trust; no one comes from him except with a gift. They said: Do not hold this against us; we have wealth, so exact from it whatever you want. He said: I do not want your wealth, but I want the gift he sent with you. They said: By Allah, he did not send anything with us except that he said: \"Among you is a man whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was alone with him, no one else sought besides him. When you reach him, convey to him my salam.\" He said: A gift I wanted from you other than this? What gift is better than salam? A greeting from Allah, blessed and good."],[6042,"Salman al-Farisi was looking for a place to pray. A non-Arab woman said to him: Seek a pure heart and pray wherever you wish. He said: \"You have understood.\""],[6043,"I heard Salman al-Farsi in Isfahan say, \"A servant does not believe until he knows that what befalls him could not have missed him, and what misses him could not have befallen him.\""],[6044,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever says: 'O Allah, I call You to witness, and I call to witness Your angels, the bearers of the Throne, the heavens and whoever is in them, the earths and whoever is in them, and I call all Your creation to witness that You are Allah; there is no god but You; and I disavow whoever rejects that among the earlier and later people; and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger' — whoever says it once, one-third of him is freed from the Fire; whoever says it twice, two-thirds of him are freed from the Fire; and whoever says it three times, he is freed from the Fire."],[6045,"Salman passed by Ka'b b. Ujrah while he was stationed at a frontier post in the land of Fars and said: Shall I tell you something that will help you in your ribat (frontier duty)? He said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Ribat for one day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it.\""],[6047,"He brought the Prophet ﷺ a gift, and he ate from it along with his companions; and he brought him sadaqah (charity), and he did not eat from it."],[6048,"Salman returned from an absence, and 'Umar ؓ met him and said: May Allah keep you a righteous servant. He married into Kindah. On the night he was to enter upon his wife, the house was adorned and there were women in it. He said: Has the Ka'bah moved to Kindah, or is it redness? My friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ commanded us not to keep furnishings except simple belongings like those of a traveler, and not to keep women except those we marry. The women left, and he entered upon his wife and said: O you, will you obey me or disobey me? She said: Rather I will obey you in whatever you wish. He said: My friend ﷺ commanded us that when one of us enters upon his wife, he should stand and pray, and order her to pray behind him, and he should supplicate and she should say amin. He did so and she did. When he sat in the gathering of Kindah, a man said to him: How did you wake, O Abu Abdullah? How did you find your wife last night? He remained silent. He repeated it a second time, and he said to him: Why does one of you ask about what walls and doors conceal? It is enough for one of you to ask about something, whether it is answered or kept silent."],[6049,"Salman entered upon 'Umar ؓ while he was reclining on a cushion, and he tossed it to him. Salman said: Allah is greatest; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. 'Umar said: Tell us, O Abu Abdullah. He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on a cushion, and he tossed it to me, then said: \"O Salman, no Muslim enters upon his Muslim brother and he tosses him a cushion in honor of him except that Allah forgives him.\""],[6050,"He brought a table with fresh dates to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'What is this?' He replied, 'This is charity for you and your companions.' He said, 'O Salman, we do not eat charity.' So Salman took it away. The next day, Salman came to him with a table bearing fresh dates. He said, 'What is this table?' He replied, 'This is a gift.' He said to his companions, 'Come near and eat,' and he ate."],[6051,"I brought charity to the Prophet ﷺ, and he returned it. I brought him a gift, and he accepted it."],[6052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the like of this of gold. If one [of the two amounts] were placed on one pan of a scale and the other on the other pan, it would outweigh him as the ransom for my neck."],[6054,"I am from Jayy."],[6055,"I am from the people of Ramahurmuz."],[6056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Salman, frequently say: My Lord, settle my debt and make me free of want from poverty.'"],[6057,"The polytheists said: 'We see that your companion teaches you even how to defecate.' He said: 'Indeed, he forbids us to face the qiblah, to cleanse oneself with the right hand, and he forbade us from using dung and bones. And he said: None of you should be content with fewer than three stones.'"],[6058,"A man from the polytheists said to me: 'By Allah, I see that your companion teaches you everything, even how to defecate.' He said: 'Yes. He forbade us to face the qiblah, to cleanse ourselves with our right hands, to cleanse ourselves with fewer than three stones, and to cleanse ourselves with dung or bone.'"],[6059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to face the qiblah when relieving ourselves, to cleanse ourselves with fewer than three stones, and to cleanse ourselves with bone or dung."],[6060,"They said to Salman: 'Your Prophet ﷺ has taught you everything.' He said: 'Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to face the qiblah with feces or urine, to cleanse oneself with the right hand, to cleanse oneself with fewer than three stones, and to cleanse oneself with dung or bone.'"],[6061,"We entered upon Salman, and he brought to us whatever was in the house and said, \"Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us—or were we not forbidden—that a man should put himself to trouble for his brother, I would have put myself to trouble for you.\""],[6062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to put ourselves to trouble for a guest."],[6063,"A companion of mine and I went to Salman al-Farisi, and Salman said, \"Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from putting ourselves to trouble, I would have put myself to trouble for you.\" Then he brought bread and meat. My companion said, \"Would that there were thyme in our salt.\" So Salman sent his water-skin and pawned it, then he brought thyme. When we had eaten it, my companion said, \"Praise be to God who has given us enjoyment of what He provided us.\" Salman ؓ said, \"If you had been content with what God provided you, my water-skin would not have been pawned.\""],[6064,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Those who are fullest of food in this world will be the hungriest on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6065,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Those who are fullest of food in this world will be the hungriest on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6066,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"When a believing servant stands in prayer, his sins are placed upon his head and then scatter from him to the right and left, just as the clusters of a date-palm scatter.\""],[6067,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Salman, do you know what the day of Friday is?\" I said, \"It is the day on which your father—or your forefather—was assembled.\" He said, \"No, but I shall tell you about the day of Friday: there is no Muslim who purifies himself, puts on his best clothes, and applies some of his family's perfume if they have any—otherwise water—and then comes to the mosque and remains silent until the imam comes out, and then prays, except that it will be an expiation for him between that Friday and the next, so long as major sins are avoided, and that is for all time.\""],[6068,"From al-Qartha' al-Dabbi, who was one of the early reciters, from Salman ؓ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"O Salman, the day of Friday is the day on which your father—or your forefather—was assembled. There is no man who purifies himself on Friday as he has been commanded, then leaves his house until he comes to the Friday prayer and sits and remains silent until he completes his prayer, except that it is an expiation for what came before it from the previous Friday.\""],[6069,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Salman, do you know what Friday is? On it your father Adam was assembled.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs the ritual bath on Friday and then comes to the mosque, he will be forgiven, or it will be expiated for him.\""],[6070,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"O Salman, do not hate me, for then you would depart from your religion.\" I said, \"How could I hate you when through you God has guided me?\" He said, \"Do not hate the Arabs, for then you would hate me.\""],[6071,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is nothing better than a thousand like it except a human being.\""],[6072,"I said: O Messenger of God, I read in the Torah that the blessing of food is in ablution before it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The blessing of food is in ablution before it and after it.'"],[6073,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ: 'Your lover is my lover, and your hater is my hater.'"],[6074,"I had a nosebleed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he commanded me to perform ablution."],[6075,"Blood flowed from my nose, so I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Perform ablution for what has occurred.'"],[6076,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ, he said: 'Three things are from the pre-Islamic ignorance: boasting about lineages, defaming genealogies, and wailing.'"],[6077,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'There is no servant who desires to rise in this world a degree and rises, except that God Most High will lower him in the Hereafter by a greater degree.' Then he recited: 'And the Hereafter is greater in degrees and greater in distinction.'"],[6078,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever would like Satan not to find food or a resting place with him, let him greet with salam when he enters his house and mention God's name over his food.'"],[6079,"The Prophet of God ﷺ commanded us to ransom the captives of the Muslims and to give to their beggar. Then he said: 'Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs; and whoever leaves debt, it is upon me and upon the rulers after me from the treasury of the Muslims.'"],[6080,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever dies in one of the two sanctuaries, he has warranted my intercession and will be on the Day of Resurrection among the secure.'"],[6081,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Indeed, in Paradise there are open plains, so increase their planting.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what is their planting?' He said: 'Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest.'"],[6082,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me to visit me when I was ill. When he was about to leave, he said: 'O Salman, may God remove your harm, forgive your sin, and grant you well-being in your religion and your body until your appointed term.'"],[6083,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever feeds a sick person what he craves, God Most High will feed him from the fruits of Paradise.'"],[6084,"No one had greater sanctity than the Messenger of God ﷺ. When his Companions wrote to him, they wrote: \"From So-and-so to Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[6087,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Three persons God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: an old adulterer, a poor person who is arrogant, and a man who made God a commodity—he does not buy except by swearing by God, and he does not sell except by swearing by God.\""],[6088,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the people of good in this world are the people of good in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter.\""],[6089,"Fever sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he asked it, \"Who are you?\" It said, \"I am fever; I consume the flesh and suck the blood.\" He said, \"Go to the people of Quba'.\" So it came upon them, and they came to the Prophet ﷺ with their faces having turned yellow. They complained of fever to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"Whatever you wish: if you wish, I will supplicate God and He will remove it from you; and if you wish, you may leave it so that it may erase the remainder of your sins.\" They said, \"Rather leave it, O Messenger of God.\""],[6090,"A man came and greeted the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God.\" He replied, \"And upon you be peace and the mercy of God.\" Then another came and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, and the mercy of God.\" He replied, \"And upon you be peace and the mercy of God and His blessings.\" Then another came and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, and the mercy of God and His blessings.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"And upon you.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of God, so-and-so and so-and-so came to you, and you greeted them with something better than you greeted me?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ replied, \"Indeed, you did not leave anything. God ﷻ said: {And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with one better than it or return it.} So I returned your greeting.\""],[6091,"I brought the zakat to the Messenger of God ﷺ three times, and he said, \"Whom do you count as a martyr among you?\" They said, \"The one who is killed in the cause of God.\" He said, \"Then the martyrs of my Ummah would be few. Being killed in the cause of God is martyrdom; the plague is martyrdom; a woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom; burning is martyrdom; drowning is martyrdom; tuberculosis is martyrdom; and a stomach ailment is martyrdom.\""],[6092,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whom do you count as a martyr among you?\" They said, \"The one who is killed in the cause of God.\" He said, \"Then the martyrs of my Ummah would be few. Being killed is martyrdom; the plague is martyrdom; a stomach ailment is martyrdom; and a woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom.\""],[6093,"On the Day of Judgment, the sun will be given intense heat for ten years, then it will come close to the heads of people. It is mentioned in the narration that they will come to the Prophet ﷺ and say, \"O Prophet of Allah, you are the one through whom Allah opened (the gates of mercy) and forgave you for your past and future sins. You see what we are going through, so intercede for us with our Lord.\" He ﷺ will say, \"I am the one who will intercede for you.\" He will then come out, herding the people until he reaches the gate of Paradise. He will take hold of a golden ring on the gate and knock. It will be said, \"Who is this?\" They will answer, \"Muhammad.\" The gate will be opened for him and he will enter, going to stand before Allah, prostrating. It will be called out, \"Raise your head and ask, you will be given and intercede, your intercession will be accepted.\" That is the praiseworthy station."],[6094,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not be the first to enter the market, nor the last to leave it; for in it Satan lays his eggs and hatches them.\""],[6095,"Some people came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to them, \"Do you have food?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do you have drink?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He asked, \"Do you strain it?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He asked, \"Do you cool it?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then the final state of both is like the final state of the world: one of you will go behind his house and hold his nose because of its stench.\""],[6096,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When a man is in a barren land and the time for prayer comes, let him perform ablution; if he finds no water, let him perform tayammum. If he gives the iqamah, his two angels pray with him; and if he gives the adhan and the iqamah, behind him pray soldiers of God whose two ends are not visible.\""],[6097,"From Salman ؓ about his embracing Islam. He said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, I prepared some food and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'What is this, O Salman?' I said, 'Charity.' He said to his Companions, 'Eat,' but he did not eat. Then I returned and gathered some food and brought it to him. He said, 'What is this, O Salman?' I said, 'A gift.' He reached out with his hand and ate, and said to his Companions, 'Eat.'\""],[6098,"From Salman ؓ regarding his embracing of Islam, he said: When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, I prepared some food and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"What is this, O Salman?\" I said, \"Charity.\" So he said to his companions, \"Eat,\" but he did not eat. Then I returned until I had gathered some food and brought it to him. He said, \"What is this, O Salman?\" I said, \"A gift.\" So he reached out with his hand and ate, and said to his companions, \"Eat.\""],[6099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: A man among those before you was given abundant wealth and children by Allah. He said to his family: When I die, burn me until I become charcoal, then crush me, and then scatter me [in the wind]. For if my Lord gets hold of me, He will punish me with a punishment such as He has not punished anyone in all the worlds. So they did that. Then Allah, Exalted is He, commanded concerning him, and he was gathered together. There he was, standing before Allah, Exalted is He. He said, \"What made you do what you did?\" He said, \"Fear of You, O Lord.\" So He forgave him."],[6100,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about [the meat of] wild asses, ghee, and cheese. He said, \"The lawful is what Allah has made lawful in His Book, and the unlawful is what Allah has made unlawful in His Book. Whatever He has remained silent about is among that which He has pardoned.\""],[6101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a Muslim prays while his sins are suspended above his head. Every time he prostrates, they fall away. So by the time he finishes his prayer, his sins have fallen away.\""],[6102,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, Allah created one hundred mercies. One mercy among them is that by which this creation shows mercy to one another, and ninety-nine are for the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Blessing is in three things: the congregation, tharid [bread soaked in broth], and the pre-dawn meal.\""],[6104,"\"Nothing turns back the Decree except supplication, and nothing increases the life-span except righteousness.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2139)"],[6105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about locusts. He said, \"They are the most numerous of Allah's soldiers on earth.\""],[6106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah is not shy to return the hands of His servant empty-handed when they are raised towards Him.\""],[6107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not be the first to enter the market, nor the last to leave it, for it is the battlefield,\" or he said, \"the resting place of Satan, and therein is his banner.\""],[6108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus until it ruins him is better than for it to be filled with poetry.\""],[6109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is a sin that is not forgiven, a sin that is not left alone, and a sin that is forgiven. As for the one that is not forgiven, it is associating partners with Allah. As for the one that is forgiven, it is a sin between [a person] and Allah, Exalted is He. As for the one that is not left alone, it is the oppression of servants against one another.\""],[6110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ribat [guarding the frontier] for one day in the path of Allah is better than the world and all that is in it. And the space of one of your bows in Paradise is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[6111,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Let not the call of Bilal prevent any of you from his pre-dawn meal, for Bilal only gives the call to prayer in order to return the one of you who is standing in prayer and to awaken the one of you who is asleep.\""],[6112,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not say Amin before me.”"],[6113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O son of Adam, there are three: one is Mine, one is yours, and one is between Me and you. As for the one that is Mine: you worship Me and do not associate anything with Me. As for the one that is yours: whatever deed you do, I will reward you for it; if I forgive, then I am the Forgiving, the Merciful. As for the one between Me and you: from you is supplication and asking, and upon Me is answering and giving.”"],[6114,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever eats clay has assisted in killing himself.”"],[6115,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs ablution (wudu) in his house and performs it well, then goes to the mosque, is the guest of Allah, and it is obligatory upon the host to honor the guest.\""],[6116,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed, so he said: “Will not a man give charity to this one and pray with him?”"],[6117,"Allah ﷻ said: “When My servant draws near to Me a span, I draw near to him a cubit; when he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him running.”"],[6118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No people raise their hands to Allah ﷻ asking Him for something except that it is incumbent upon Allah to place in their hands what they asked for.”"],[6119,"Salman wrote to Abu al-Dardaʾ: “O my brother, let the mosque be your home, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The mosque is the home of every pious person, and Allah ﷻ has guaranteed for those whose homes are the mosques comfort, mercy, and passage over the Sirat.’”"],[6120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ created, on the day He created the heavens and the earth, one hundred mercies, each mercy equal to what is between heaven and earth. Of them, one mercy is in the earth; by it a mother shows compassion to her child, and wild animals show compassion to one another. He has deferred ninety-nine mercies until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No Muslim performs ablution and performs it well except that he becomes a visitor of Allah ﷻ, and it is incumbent upon the visited one to honor His visitor.”"],[6122,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever goes out early to the morning prayer is given a quarter of faith, and whoever goes out early to the market is given the banner of Iblis, and he is with the first to go and the last to return.”"],[6123,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When a Muslim meets his Muslim brother and takes his hand, their sins fall away from them just as leaves fall from a dry tree on a day of violent wind. Otherwise, they are both forgiven, even if their sins were like the foam of the sea.”"],[6124,"I was with Salman al-Farsi under a tree, and he took a dry branch from its branches and shook it until its leaves fell. Then he said, \"Ask me why I did this, O Salman.\" So I said, \"Why did you do it?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did the same. I was with him under a tree, and he took a dry branch from its branches and shook it until its leaves fell. Then he said, 'Don't you ask me why I did this, O Salman?' So I said, 'Why did you do it?' He said, 'Indeed, when a Muslim performs ablution and perfects it, then prays the five daily prayers, his sins are shaken off just as these leaves are shaken off.' Then he recited this verse, 'Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.'\""],[6125,"I gathered firewood and prepared some food, then brought it to the Prophet ﷺ, and it was small in amount. I placed it before him, and he said, “What is this?” I said, “Charity.” He said to his companions, “Eat,” but he did not eat. I said, “This is one of his signs.” Then I remained as long as God willed, then I said to my mistress, “Grant me a day off.” She said, “Yes.” So I went out, gathered firewood, sold it for more than that, prepared some food, and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ while he was among his companions. I placed it before him, and he said, “What is this?” I said, “A gift.” He placed his hand and said to his companions, “Take it, in the name of God.” Then I said, “I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.” He said, “And why is that?” I told him about the man, then I said, “Will he enter Paradise, O Messenger of God, for he told me that you are a Prophet?” He said, “Only a Muslim soul will enter Paradise.”"],[6126,"Hudhayfa was in al-Mada'in, and he used to mention things that the Messenger of God ﷺ had said to some of his companions in anger. So some people who heard that from Hudhayfa would go to Salman and mention to him Hudhayfa's statement, and Salman would say, “Hudhayfa knows best what he says.” They would return to Hudhayfa and say, “We mentioned that to Salman, and he neither confirmed you nor denied you.” So Hudhayfa came to Salman while he was in a tent of his and said, “O Salman, what prevents you from confirming me in what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” Salman said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ would get angry and say in anger to some of his companions, and he would fall ill and say in illness to some of his companions. Will you not stop until you cause some men to inherit love for other men, and other men to inherit hatred for other men, until you bring about discord and division? You know that the Messenger of God ﷺ gave a sermon and said, ‘Any man of my community whom I have insulted or cursed in my anger—I am but one of the children of Adam; I get angry as they get angry. God sent me as a mercy to the worlds, so I will make it a blessing upon him on the Day of Resurrection.’ By God, either you stop, or I will write to Umar ؓ about you.”"],[6127,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about cheese, clarified butter, and furs. The Prophet ﷺ said: “The lawful is what God has made lawful in the Quran, the unlawful is what God has made unlawful in the Quran, and whatever He remained silent about, He has pardoned.”"],[6128,"A covenant that the Messenger of God ﷺ made with us, which none of us preserved. He said: “Let the provision of one of you be like the provision of a rider.” Muwarriq said: “So they looked in his house, and there was a saddle of such and such.”"],[6129,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever provides iftar for a fasting person during Ramadan from lawful earnings, the angels will pray for him.”"],[6130,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever provides an ifṭār to a fasting person with lawful food and drink, the angels send blessings upon him during the hours of the month of Ramadan, and Gabriel ﷺ sends blessings upon him on the Night of Decree.”"],[6131,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever rejects a hadith that reaches him from me, let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever rejects a hadith that reaches him from me, I will be his adversary on the Day of Resurrection. And when a hadith reaches you from me that you do not recognize, say: God knows best.”"],[6132,"I was with Salmān when he saw a man who had broken his ablution and wanted to remove his leather socks to perform ablution. Salmān said: “Wipe over them and over your turban.” And Salmān said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wiping over his head-covering and his leather socks.”"],[6133,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the turban and the leather socks."],[6134,"He saw Salmān come out from relieving himself and wipe over his leather socks. It was said: “Do you really do this?” He said: “Yes, I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and the turban.”"],[6135,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I named them—meaning al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn—after the names of Hārūn's two sons, Shabar and Shubayr.”"],[6136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Spirits are assembled troops. Those among them that recognize one another become close, and those that do not recognize one another differ.”"],[6137,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever glorifies God ﷻ once, or praises Him once, or declares His oneness once, or magnifies Him once, God plants for him a tree in Paradise because of it, whose root is red ruby, crowned with pearls, whose fruit is like the breasts of virgins, sweeter than honey and softer than butter.”"],[6138,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Ribat for a day and a night is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it, and whoever dies as a murābiṭ in the path of God, the same reward continues for him, his provision is made to flow to him, and he is safeguarded from the two tempters.”"],[6139,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Ribat for a day and a night in the path of God is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it, and whoever dies as a murābiṭ, his deeds that he used to do continue for him, and he is safeguarded from the two tempters.”"],[6140,"He saw Salman al-Farisi while he was a murābiṭ on the coast of Hims, and said: “What brings you to this?” He said: “I am a murābiṭ.” Salman said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Ribat for a day in the path of God is like fasting a month and standing in prayer during it, and whoever dies as a murābiṭ, his deeds that he used to do continue for him, he is safeguarded from the two tempters, and he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a martyr.”"],[6141,"I went out seeking the religion and I came upon remnants of the People of the Book among the monks. God ﷻ said: {They recognize him as they recognize their own sons}, and they used to say: “This is the time of a prophet who has drawn near, who will emerge from the land of the Arabs. He has signs, among them a round mole between his shoulders, the seal of prophethood.” So I reached the land of the Arabs, and the Prophet ﷺ emerged, and I saw all that they had said, and I saw the seal. So I bore witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and I heard him say: “Ribat for a day and a night is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it, standing without flagging and fasting without breaking the fast. If he dies as a murābiṭ, his righteous deeds continue for him until he is raised, and he is protected from the punishment of the grave.”"],[6142,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"If one of you visits his brother and he places something for him that protects him from the dust, God will protect him from the punishment of the Fire.\""],[6143,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs the major ablution on Friday and perfects his ablution, then applies some perfume and puts on some of his clothes, then does not separate between two people, then prays what is decreed for him; and when the imam comes out, remains silent and then listens, he will be forgiven what is between that Friday and the next.\""],[6144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No one will enter Paradise except with a pass: 'In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a writ from God for so-and-so son of so-and-so: admit him into a lofty Paradise, whose clusters of fruit are near at hand.'\""],[6145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates; if he does not find any, then with water, for water is purifying.\""],[6146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates; if he does not find any, let him drink water, for it is purifying.\""],[6147,"From ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal: Ḥafṣa bt. Sīrīn narrated to me, from al-Rabāb, from Salmān b. ʿĀmir al-Ḍabbī, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates if he finds them; if he does not find any, then with water, for water is purifying.\""],[6148,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates; if he does not find any, then with water, for it is purifying.\""],[6149,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast on them; and whoever does not find dates, let him break his fast on water, for water is purifying.\" Shuʿba did not mention al-Rabāb."],[6150,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"With the boy is his ʿaqīqa, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him.\""],[6151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"With the boy is his ʿaqīqa, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him.\""],[6152,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Concerning the boy, his 'aqiqah [sacrifice]; so shed blood for him and remove harm from him.\""],[6153,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Concerning the boy, his 'aqiqah [sacrifice]; so shed blood for him and remove harm from him.\""],[6154,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Concerning the boy, his 'aqiqah [sacrifice]; so shed blood for him and remove harm from him.\""],[6155,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Concerning the boy, his 'aqiqah [sacrifice]; so shed blood for him and remove harm from him.\""],[6156,"Abu Na'amah al-'Adawi narrated to us: My maternal aunt Sumaytah narrated to me, saying: I heard my grandfather Salman b. 'Amir al-Dabbi say: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Every newborn is held in pledge by his 'aqiqah, so shed blood for him and remove harm from him.\""],[6157,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Charity given to relatives is both charity and maintaining kinship ties.\""],[6158,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Charity to the poor is charity, and to a relative it is two: charity and maintaining a tender bond of kinship.\""],[6159,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Your charity to a Muslim is charity, and to a relative it is two: charity and maintaining kinship ties.\""],[6160,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Your charity to the poor is charity, and your charity to a relative is two charities: charity and maintaining kinship ties.\""],[6161,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Charity to a close relative, or he said to one with kinship ties, is two charities, and to the poor it is one charity.\""],[6162,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Charity to the poor is charity, and to one with kinship ties it is two: charity and maintaining kinship ties.\""],[6163,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, charity to the poor is charity, and indeed, to one with kinship ties it is two: charity and maintaining kinship ties.\""],[6164,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Charity to a poor person is charity, but to a relative it is two things: charity and maintaining kinship ties."],[6165,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my father used to maintain kinship ties, host guests, and fulfill covenants. He said: \"Did he live to see Islam?\" I said: No. When I turned away, he said: \"Bring the old man to me.\" He said: \"That will be in your descendants, so they will never be humiliated nor ever become poor.\""],[6166,"Salim ibn AbulJa'dah said: A man said: (Mis'ar said: I think he was from the tribe of Khuza'ah): would that I had prayed, and got comfort. The people objected to him for it. Thereupon he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: O Bilal, call iqamah for prayer: give us comfort by it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4985)"],[6167,"I went with my father to visit a relative of ours who had recently embraced Islam. I overheard him saying, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Grant us relief through it, O Bilal, with the prayer.'\" I asked him, \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?\" He became angry and turned to the people, informing them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent a man to a tribe of the Arabs. When he arrived, he said: 'Verily, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded me to judge in your affairs as I wish.' They replied: 'We hear and obey the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' They then sent a man to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , informing him: 'So-and-so came to us and said: 'Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ has commanded me to judge in your affairs as I wish. If it is your command, we hear and obey, and if it is other than that, then we prefer to inform you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and sent a man from the Ansar (Helpers) saying, 'Go to so-and-so and kill him and burn him with fire.' He was brought and burned with fire after being dug out of his grave. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever intentionally lies about me, let him find his seat in the Fire.'\" He then turned to me and said, \"Do you think that I would lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after this?\""],[6168,"It is said: Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ died at the age of eighty."],[6169,"He saw ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah, Abu Usayd al-Saʿidi, Anas b. Malik, Rafiʿ b. Khadij, and Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ shaving their mustaches closely, plucking their armpits, and trimming their nails."],[6170,"He used to pray in a single garment."],[6171,"Water was heated for him and he performed ablution with it."],[6172,"When Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ performed ablution, he would take musk, mix it in his hand, then wipe it on his beard."],[6173,"Salamah used to pray the Duha prayer."],[6174,"I used to shoot wild game, hunt it, and gift its meat to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ missed me and said: \"Salamah, where do you go?\" I said: We go far for hunting, O Messenger of God; I hunt with the tips of a spear from the direction of Bayt. He said: \"If only you hunted at al-ʿAqiq, I would go out with you when you left and meet you when you returned, for I love al-ʿAqiq.\""],[6175,"The Prophet ﷺ had a servant called Yasar. He noticed that he prayed well, so he freed him and sent him to his milch camels at al-Harrah, where they were. Some people from ʿUraynah in Yemen professed Islam and came while they were ill with fever and their bellies were swollen. The Prophet ﷺ sent them to Yasar. They drank from the camels' milk until their bellies subsided. Then they attacked Yasar, slaughtered him, put thorns in his eyes, and drove off the camels. The Prophet ﷺ sent Muslim horsemen after them, led by Kurz b. Jabir al-Fihri. He caught up with them and brought them back. He cut off their hands and feet and put out their eyes."],[6176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You, O Talhah, are the generous one.\""],[6177,"On the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely, but his sword recoiled on him and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ spoke about that and doubted him: a man who died by his own weapon; they doubted some of his affair. Salamah said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Khaybar, I said: O Messenger of God, permit me to recite rajaz poetry to you. The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted him. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: Be mindful of what you say. So I said:"],[6178,"When it was the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ, but his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said about that: 'This is a man who died by his own weapon,' and they had doubts about some aspect of his affair. Salamah said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Khaybar, I said to him: 'Permit me, O Messenger of God, to recite war poetry for you?' The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted me. Then Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: 'Be mindful of what you say.' So I said:"],[6179,"His brother, when it was the day of Khaybar, fought fiercely alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ, but his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said about that: 'He died by his own weapon,' and they had doubts about some aspect of his affair. Salamah said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from Khaybar, I said to him: 'Permit me, O Messenger of God, to recite war poetry for you?' The Messenger of God ﷺ permitted me. Then Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'Be mindful of what you say.' So I said:"],[6180,"When it was the day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ, but his sword recoiled upon him and killed him. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said about that and expressed doubt concerning it: 'A man who died by his own weapon.' Salamah said: 'O Messenger of God, permit me to recite war poetry.' Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: 'What will you say?' So I said:"],[6181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ kept us away from our wives for three months. I would go out with the army, and I would be present when they were present and stay when they stayed. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever wishes may enjoy these women.'"],[6182,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Khaybar: 'I will certainly give the banner today to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger love.' He said: Then he sent me to Ali while he was suffering from ophthalmia. I brought him, leading him. He spat into his eye and he was cured, and he gave him the banner."],[6183,"A man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'May God have mercy on you.' Then he sneezed again, and he said: 'May God have mercy on you.' Then he sneezed another time, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The man has a cold.' The wording is from the hadith of Asim b. Ali."],[6184,"The Prophet ﷺ saw Busr b. Ra'i al-'Anz eating with his left hand and said: 'Eat with your right hand.' He said: 'I cannot.' He said: 'May you never be able.' His right hand never reached his mouth after that."],[6185,"A man was eating in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ with his left hand. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'Eat with your right hand.' He said: 'I cannot.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'May you never be able.' He said: He never raised it to his mouth after that."],[6186,"We went out with Abu Bakr and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to lead us, so we engaged in battle until we reached a water source. Abu Bakr commanded us to give water to our animals. After performing the Fajr prayer, Abu Bakr commanded us to launch a surprise attack. We killed those we fought against near the water. Salamah said, \"I looked and saw some people with their offspring and women. I was afraid they would escape to the mountains before me, so I shot an arrow that landed between them and the mountain. They got up and I brought them to Abu Bakr to see what to do with them. We continued driving them until we reached the water. Among them was a woman from Fazara, wearing a red leather necklace, and with her was a beautiful Arab girl. Abu Bakr's daughter fell in love with her and requested me to give her the girl as a servant. I did not uncover her until we reached Madinah. I left without uncovering her and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me and said, 'O Salamah, give me the woman.' I replied, 'O Messenger of Allah, I swear by Allah, she has amazed me and I have not uncovered her.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and left me. The next day, he met me in the market and said, 'O Salamah, give me the woman for the sake of Allah, not your father.' I replied, 'O Messenger of Allah, I swear by Allah, I have not uncovered her and she is yours.' After that day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent her to the people of Makkah who were holding Muslim captives. He ransomed them with that woman and they were freed. This is according to the narration of Abu al-Walid."],[6187,"I captured a slave girl from Banu Fazara. The Prophet ﷺ met me and said: 'May your father be devoted to God; give her to me.' I gave her to him, and he ransomed with her some people among the Muslims."],[6188,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Abu Bakr ؓ as our commander. We raided some of the polytheists and killed them. Our battle cry was 'Amit!' Salamah said: I killed with my own hand that night nine people of households."],[6189,"We returned from Al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we pledged allegiance to him at the base of a tree. He said: I pledged allegiance among the first of the people. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, “O Salamah, pledge allegiance to me.” I said, “O Prophet of God, by God, I have already pledged allegiance to you among the first of the people.” He said, “And again.” He said: So I pledged allegiance to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ saw me without a shield. And he mentioned the hadith."],[6190,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ the Hawazin. While we were seated taking our mid-morning meal, a man came on a red camel. He pulled out a strap from the camel’s hind girth and hobbled his camel with it. Then he came walking until he sat with us to eat. He looked at the faces of the people and saw that their condition was weak and most of them were on foot. When he looked at the faces of the people, he went out running until he reached his camel, sat on it, and rode off as a scout for the disbelievers. A man from us of Aslam followed him on a gray she-camel of his. I followed him running on foot and caught up with him, being at the side of the she-camel’s haunch. Then I moved forward until I took hold of the camel’s halter. I drew my sword and struck his head. Then I came leading his she-camel, on which was his spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ met me with the people and said, “Who killed the man?” They said, “Ibn al-Akwa‘.” He said, “You shall have all his spoils.” The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."],[6191,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ the Hawazin. While we were seated taking our mid-morning meal, a man came on a red camel. He pulled out a strap from the camel’s hind girth and hobbled his camel with it. Then he came walking until he sat with us to eat. He looked at the faces of the people and saw that their condition was weak and most of them were on foot. When he looked at the faces of the people, he went out running until he reached his camel, sat on it, and rode off as a scout for the disbelievers. A man from us of Aslam followed him on a gray she-camel of his. I followed him running on foot and caught up with him, being at the side of the she-camel’s haunch. Then I moved forward until I took hold of the camel’s halter. I drew my sword and struck his head. Then I came leading his she-camel, on which was his spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ met me with the people and said, “Who killed the man?” They said, “Ibn al-Akwa‘.” He said, “You shall have all his spoils.” The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."],[6192,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ the Hawazin. While we were seated taking our mid-morning meal, a man came on a red camel. He pulled out a strap from the camel’s hind girth and hobbled his camel with it. Then he came walking until he sat with us to eat. He looked at the faces of the people and saw that their condition was weak and most of them were on foot. When he looked at the faces of the people, he went out running until he reached his camel, sat on it, and rode off as a scout for the disbelievers. A man from us of Aslam followed him on a gray she-camel of his. I followed him running on foot and caught up with him, being at the side of the she-camel’s haunch. Then I moved forward until I took hold of the camel’s halter. I drew my sword and struck his head. Then I came leading his she-camel, on which was his spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ met me with the people and said, “Who killed the man?” They said, “Ibn al-Akwa‘.” He said, “You shall have all his spoils.” The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."],[6193,"We went out to Khaybar, and ‘Amir was reciting rajaz poetry while he said:"],[6194,"We went out to Khaybar, and ‘Amir was reciting rajaz poetry while he said:"],[6195,"We raided with the Prophet ﷺ the Hawazin, and severe hardship befell us until we considered slaughtering some of our riding animals. The Prophet of God ﷺ said, “Gather some of your provisions.” The Prophet of God ﷺ ordered a leather mat to be spread out. The people came with dates and scattered them. I stretched myself toward it to estimate how much it was, and it was like the resting place of a sheep. We all ate until we were full, and we were fourteen hundred. Then we filled our provision bags from it. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ called for a little water in a small skin, ordered it to be poured into a cup, and we began to perform ablution with it until we all had performed ablution."],[6196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in a red leather tent when a man came to him on a mare with a foal following her. He said, “Who are you?” He said, “I am the Messenger of God.” He said, “When is the Hour?” He said, “It is unseen, and none knows the unseen except God.” He said, “When will we be given rain?” He said, “It is unseen, and none knows the unseen except God.” He said, “What is in the belly of my mare?” He said, “It is unseen, and none knows the unseen except God.” He said, “Give me your sword.” He said, “Here.” He took it, drew it, then shook it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “You will never be able to do what you intended.” Then he said, “This man came forward and said, ‘I will go to him and question him, then take my sword and kill him.’” Then he sheathed the sword."],[6197,"My paternal uncle came with a man from ‘Ajlan, leading him and his horse, among seventy of the polytheists, until he stood them before the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Leave them.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ paid blood money on their behalf. Then God ﷻ revealed, {And He it is who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah after He had given you victory over them} to the end of the verse."],[6198,"“The Prophet of God ﷺ came with al-Hasan and al-Husayn on his gray mule until he brought them into the chamber of the Prophet ﷺ, this one in front of him and this one behind him.”"],[6199,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Whoever draws a sword against us is not of us.”"],[6200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When dinner is served and the prayer is present, then begin with dinner.”"],[6201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever carries a weapon against us is not from us.”"],[6202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best of our knights is Abu Qatadah, and the best of our women is Salamah.\""],[6203,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ beginning with a supplication and only heard him beginning with: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Bestower.”"],[6204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man persists in being arrogant and full of self-conceit until he is recorded among the tyrants, and then what befell them befalls him.”"],[6205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Aslam—may Allah grant it peace—and Ghifar—may Allah forgive it. I did not say it, but Allah said it.”"],[6206,"We used to pray Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the walls had no shade to seek shelter in."],[6207,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral of a man from the Ansar was brought. He said: “Did he leave behind a debt?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, two dinars. He said: “Pray over your companion.” Abu Qatadah said: They are on me, O Messenger of Allah. Then he prayed over him. Then another funeral was brought. He said: “Does he have a debt?” They said: No. He said: “Did he leave behind any treasure?” They said: Two dinars. He said: “Two cauterizations.” And he prayed over him."],[6208,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral was brought, and the people said: If you were, and if you were. Then another was brought, and the people said: If you were, and if you were. They praised one with good and the other with evil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You are Allah’s witnesses on earth, and the angels are Allah’s witnesses in heaven.”"],[6209,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The stars were made as a safeguard for the inhabitants of the heaven, and the people of my house are a safeguard for my community.”"],[6210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Then Allah will see your work, and His Messenger, and the believers}."],[6211,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a funeral, and the people praised him with good praise. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It has become incumbent.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, what has become incumbent? He said: “The angels are Allah’s witnesses in heaven, and you are Allah’s witnesses on earth. When you bear witness, it becomes incumbent.”"],[6212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pledged allegiance on behalf of Uthman b. Affan ؓ with one of his hands over the other, and said: \"O Allah, Uthman is engaged in Your service and the service of Your Messenger.\""],[6213,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Any man and unmarried woman who mutually agree, their marriage is for three nights. If they wish to extend, they may extend; and if they wish to separate, they may separate.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Muhammad b. Ali."],[6214,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted me behind him many times, wiped my head, and sought forgiveness for me and my descendants as many times as the number of fingers on my hand."],[6215,"The milch-camels of the Prophet ﷺ were raided, and I began to shoot at them until the cavalry came from the direction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Remain steadfast, though you will never fully do so, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and no one maintains prayer except a believer.\""],[6217,"The battle cry of the Prophet ﷺ was \"Amit, amit.\" Ali b. Hakim added: \"in one of his campaigns.\""],[6218,"A spy from the polytheists came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on a journey. He sat conversing with his companions, then slipped away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek him and kill him.\" I got to him before them, killed him, and took his belongings, and he gave them to me as a reward."],[6219,"On the authority of the Prophet of God ﷺ that he said: \"Excellent are thirty camels: one is given from them in their zakah, one is saddled from them in the path of God, and one is granted as a gift from them. They are better than forty, fifty, sixty, seventy, eighty, ninety, and one hundred. And woe to the owner of one hundred, from the one hundred.\""],[6220,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about praying while carrying a bow and a quiver? He said: \"Pray while carrying the bow, but put down the quiver,\" meaning the arrow-holster."],[6221,"'Uyaynah b. Hisn raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of God ﷺ and drove them away. Salamah b. al-Akwa' al-Aslami said: I went out with my bow and arrows, and I used to hunt game. Then when I was at Thaniyyat al-Wada', I looked and saw them driving the camels. So I ran onto the mountain at Sal' and then cried out, \"O morning raid!\" My cry reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the call went out among the people: \"Alarm! Alarm!\" I went out shooting at them and saying: \"Take it! I am the son of al-Akwa'.\" It was not long before I saw the cavalry of the Messenger of God ﷺ threading through the trees. Eight horsemen caught up with them. The first to catch them was Abu Qatadah b. Rib'i. He stabbed a man from Banu Fazarah called Mas'adah, took off his own cloak and covered him with it, then went on in pursuit of the enemy with the horsemen. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by while the people were alarmed, and they were saying: \"Abu Qatadah is killed.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not Abu Qatadah; rather it is a man killed by Abu Qatadah. Leave him and his spoils.\" Then he said: \"Press on in pursuit of the people.\" So they pressed on and recovered what they recovered of the milch-camels, while the enemy went off with what remained. Muhammad b. Talhah said: And in the hadith: \"He named those who went out in pursuit of the milch-camels: 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan, al-Miqdad b. 'Amr—who is the one called Ibn al-Aswad, the ally of Banu Zuhrah—and Muhriz b. Nadlah al-Asadi, the ally of Banu 'Abd Shams. It is said no one of the enemy was killed except him. And of the Ansar: Sa'd b. Zayd al-Ash-hali, who was the commander of the group, 'Abbad b. Bishr al-Ash-hali, Zuhayr b. Rafi' al-Harithi, Abu Qatadah b. Rib'i al-Sulami, and Mu'adh b. Ma'is al-Zuraqi. Abu 'Ayyash al-Zuraqi was one of the five-man band.\""],[6222,"'Uyaynah b. Hisn raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of God ﷺ and drove them away. Salamah b. al-Akwa' al-Aslami said: I went out with my bow and arrows, and I used to hunt game. Then when I was at Thaniyyat al-Wada', I looked and saw them driving the camels. So I ran onto the mountain at Sal' and then cried out, \"O morning raid!\" My cry reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the call went out among the people: \"Alarm! Alarm!\" I went out shooting at them and saying: \"Take it! I am the son of al-Akwa'.\" It was not long before I saw the cavalry of the Messenger of God ﷺ threading through the trees. Eight horsemen caught up with them. The first to catch them was Abu Qatadah b. Rib'i. He stabbed a man from Banu Fazarah called Mas'adah, took off his own cloak and covered him with it, then went on in pursuit of the enemy with the horsemen. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by while the people were alarmed, and they were saying: \"Abu Qatadah is killed.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not Abu Qatadah; rather it is a man killed by Abu Qatadah. Leave him and his spoils.\" Then he said: \"Press on in pursuit of the people.\" So they pressed on and recovered what they recovered of the milch-camels, while the enemy went off with what remained. Muhammad b. Talhah said: And in the hadith: \"He named those who went out in pursuit of the milch-camels: 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan, al-Miqdad b. 'Amr—who is the one called Ibn al-Aswad, the ally of Banu Zuhrah—and Muhriz b. Nadlah al-Asadi, the ally of Banu 'Abd Shams. It is said no one of the enemy was killed except him. And of the Ansar: Sa'd b. Zayd al-Ash-hali, who was the commander of the group, 'Abbad b. Bishr al-Ash-hali, Zuhayr b. Rafi' al-Harithi, Abu Qatadah b. Rib'i al-Sulami, and Mu'adh b. Ma'is al-Zuraqi. Abu 'Ayyash al-Zuraqi was one of the five-man band.\""],[6223,"He heard Ibn al-Akwa' say: I said: O Messenger of God ﷺ, I am out hunting and I pray while wearing only a single shirt? He said: \"Button it, even if you find nothing but a thorn.\""],[6224,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever attributes to me something that I have not said, let him take his place in Hell.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 34)"],[6225,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, then I withdrew. He said: \"O Salamah, will you not pledge allegiance?\" I said: I have already pledged allegiance. He said: \"Come forward and pledge allegiance.\" So I drew near and pledged allegiance to him. I said: On what did I pledge allegiance, O Abu Muslim? He said: \"On death.\""],[6226,"\"I went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and seven military expeditions with Zayd b. Harithah, whom he appointed as commander over us.\""],[6227,"I participated in seven battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : Uhud, Hunayn, Khaybar, Al-Hudaybiyah, and the Battle of the Day of the Trench. He said, \"And I forgot the rest of them.\""],[6228,"Then I heard a slave-boy of 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf saying: \"The milch-camels of the Messenger of God ﷺ have been taken.\" I said: \"Who took them?\" He said: \"Ghatafan and Fazarah.\" So I climbed the mountain pass and cried: \"O morning raid! O morning raid!\" Then I went off running in their tracks until I recovered the camels from them. The Messenger of God ﷺ came with a group of his companions, and I said: \"O Messenger of God, the people are thirsty; we made them hurry so that they could not water their camels.\" He said: \"O Ibn al-Akwa', you have gained mastery, so be gracious. The people of Ghatafan are being entertained as guests in their land.\""],[6229,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution once, wipe his head once, and give the greeting of peace once.\""],[6230,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd, from Salamah b. al-Akwa', who said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ seated me behind him on his she-camel until we entered Madinah.\""],[6231,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us, from Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd, from Salamah b. al-Akwa': The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the night before the morning of Khaybar: \"I will surely give the banner tomorrow to a man whom God and His Messenger love, and through whom God will grant victory.\" Then there was 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave him the banner, and God granted victory through him."],[6232,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us from Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd from Salamah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a crier on the day of 'Ashura' announcing: \"Whoever has not yet fasted should complete the rest of his day, and whoever has fasted should complete his fast.\""],[6233,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated from Hatim, from Yazid ibn Abi 'Ubayd, from Salamah who said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the Maghrib prayer when the sun set and disappeared behind the veil.\""],[6234,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us from Yazid from Salamah, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral was brought. It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray over this one?\" He said, \"Did he leave anything?\" It was said, \"No.\" He said, \"Does he owe any debt?\" They said, \"No.\" So he prayed over him. While I was standing, another funeral was brought. He said, \"Does he owe any debt?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Did he leave anything?\" They said, \"Yes, three dinars.\" He said, \"Three scorch marks.\" Then we waited as long as Allah willed, and another funeral was brought. He said, \"Did he leave anything?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Does he owe any debt?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Pray over your companion.\" Abu Qatadah said, \"I will take responsibility for his debt, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he prayed over him."],[6235,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us from Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd from Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of men from Aslam who were shooting arrows. He said, \"Shoot, O sons of Isma'il, for your forefather was an archer. Shoot, and I am with the sons of so-and-so.\" One of the two teams withheld their hands. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with you that you do not shoot?\" They said, \"Should we shoot, O Messenger of Allah, while you are with them?\" He said, \"Shoot, and I am with all of you.\""],[6236,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us from Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd from Salamah b. al-Akwa', who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khaybar and traveled by night. A man of the group said to 'Amir, \"O 'Amir, will you not let us hear some of your little songs?\" 'Amir was a poet, so he dismounted and began chanting to the people, saying..."],[6237,"Whenever the wind blew strongly, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: \"O Allah, make it a fertilizing wind, not a barren one.\""],[6238,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one swears a false oath on the minbar except that he will take his seat in the Fire.\""],[6239,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim narrated to us: Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd narrated to us from Salamah b. al-Akwa' that he entered upon al-Hajjaj, who said, \"O Ibn al-Akwa', have you turned back on your heels and become a Bedouin?\" He said, \"No, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me to live in the desert.\""],[6240,"He used to prostrate at the place of the mushaf, glorifying Allah there, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek out that spot."],[6241,"\"Give me your weapon,\" so I gave it to him. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Provide me with a weapon.\" He said, \"Where is your weapon?\" I said, \"I gave it to 'Amir, my paternal uncle.\" He said, \"I find no one who resembles you except the one who said: 'Grant me a brother dearer to me than myself.'\" Then he gave me his bow, his shield, and three arrows from his quiver."],[6242,"We were struck by severe hunger on the day of Khaybar, and the people lit fires. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What are these fires?\" They said, \"Domestic donkeys.\" He said, \"Spill out what is in them and break the pots.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we spill out what is in them and wash them?\" He said, \"Or that.\""],[6243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the banner to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and sent him to one of the fortresses of Khaybar. He fought and then returned without any conquest, and he had exerted himself. He said, \"Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and through whose hands Allah will grant victory—not one who flees.\" Then he called 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ while he was suffering from ophthalmia, spat into his eyes, and said, \"Take this banner until Allah grants you victory.\" Salamah said: By Allah, he went out at a brisk pace, and I followed his footsteps behind him until he planted the banner in a heap of stones. A Jew looked down on him from the top of the fortress and said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am 'Ali b. Abi Talib.\" The Jew said, \"You have overcome them, and by what was revealed to Musa.\" He did not return until Allah granted him victory."],[6244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the banner to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and sent him against one of the fortresses of Khaybar. He fought, then returned without any conquest, and he had exerted himself. He said: “I will give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, through whose hands Allah will grant victory; he is not one who flees.” He called 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, who had sore eyes. He spat into his eyes, then said: “Take this banner until Allah grants you victory.” Salamah said: “By Allah, he went out at a brisk pace, and I was behind him, following his tracks, until he planted the banner in a pile of stones. A Jew looked down at him from the top of the fortress and said: ‘Who are you?’ He said: ‘I am 'Ali b. Abi Talib.’ The Jew said: ‘You have overcome them, and what was revealed to Musa.’ He did not return until Allah granted him victory.”"],[6245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the banner to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and sent him against one of the fortresses of Khaybar. He fought, then returned without any conquest, and he had exerted himself. He said: “I will give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, through whose hands Allah will grant victory; he is not one who flees.” He called 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, who had sore eyes. He spat into his eyes, then said: “Take this banner until Allah grants you victory.” Salamah said: “By Allah, he went out at a brisk pace, and I was behind him, following his tracks, until he planted the banner in a pile of stones. A Jew looked down at him from the top of the fortress and said: ‘Who are you?’ He said: ‘I am 'Ali b. Abi Talib.’ The Jew said: ‘You have overcome them, and what was revealed to Musa.’ He did not return until Allah granted him victory.”"],[6246,"I came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the direction of al-'Aqiq until when we were at the mountain pass called Thaniyyat al-Hawd, which is at al-'Aqiq, he pointed with his hand towards the east and said: “Indeed, I am looking at the landing places of the enemy of Allah, the Dajjal. He will come until he descends at such-and-such a place, until the rabble of the people go out to him. There is no opening among the openings of al-Madinah except that upon it there is an angel or two angels guarding it. With him are two images: an image of Paradise and an image of Hell, a red one. With him are devils who take the form of the dead. They say to the living person: ‘Do you recognize me? I am your brother; I am your father; I am your relative. Did I not die? This is our Lord, so follow him.’ Then Allah decrees what He wills concerning him, and Allah sends to him a man from the Muslims who silences him and refutes him. He says: ‘This is a liar. O people, do not let him deceive you, for he is a liar. He speaks falsehood, and your Lord is not one-eyed.’ He says: ‘Will you follow me?’ He refuses, so he splits him into two halves. Then he is given that, and he says: ‘I will bring him back to you.’ Then Allah resurrects him, and he is more intense in denying him and more severe in reviling him. He says: ‘O people, what you have seen is a trial with which you have been tested and a tribulation with which you have been tempted. If he is truthful, let him bring me back another time. Indeed, he is a liar.’ So he orders him to be cast into this fire, and it is the image of Paradise. He goes out towards al-Sham.”"],[6247,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When you inhale water into the nose, then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6249,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When you inhale water into the nose, then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you inhale water into the nose, then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6253,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution, snuff water and then expel it; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6256,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you perform ablution, sniff water into the nose and expel it, and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number.”"],[6257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Four matters” — I am not more protective of them today than the day I heard them. He said: “Do not associate anything with God, and do not kill the soul which God has made inviolable except with right, and do not commit adultery, and do not steal.”"],[6258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Indeed they are only four.” And I am not more protective of them today than the day I heard them from the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Do not associate anything with God, and do not kill the soul which God has made inviolable except with right, and do not commit adultery, and do not steal.”"],[6259,"That the Prophet ﷺ passed by Abū Mūsā while he was reciting, and he said: “This one has been given one of the flutes of the family of David.”"],[6260,"My brother and I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, our mother in the pre-Islamic era used to honor the guest and maintain ties of kinship. Will any of that action benefit her? He said: “No.” We said: She buried alive a sister of ours who had not reached the age of sin. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The buried girl and the one who buried her are in the Fire, unless the one who buried her reaches Islam and submits.”"],[6261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who buries alive and the one buried alive are in the Fire.”"],[6262,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “{Indeed We have produced them in a [new] creation, and made them virgins, loving, equal in age} (Qur’an 56:35-37).” He said: “From the previously married and the non-previously married.”"],[6263,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “{Indeed We have produced them in a [new] creation, and made them virgins, loving, equal in age} (Qur’an 56:35-37).” He said: “From the previously married and the non-previously married.”"],[6264,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, We have created them (the camels) with creation and made them young, prime, Arab companions.\" He said, \"From the male and female (camels), both intact and not intact.\""],[6265,"From ʿUrwa: “In the naming of those who attended al-ʿAqaba from the Anṣār, then the Aws, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Salama b. Salāma b. Waqsh, and he attended Badr.”"],[6266,"About Ibn Shihab, \"Regarding the identification of those who witnessed the Battle of al-'Aqabah from the Ansar and then from the tribe of Bani 'Abd al-Ashhal, Salamah bin Salamah bin Waqsh.\""],[6267,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq: “In the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Aws, then from Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Salama b. Salāma b. Waqsh b. Zughba b. Zaʿūrāʾ b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal b. Jusham b. al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj b. ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Aws.”"],[6268,"From Salama b. Salāma b. Waqsh, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that they entered a wedding feast while Salama had ablution, and they ate, then they left, and Salama performed ablution. Jubayra said to him: Were you not in a state of ablution? He said: Yes, but I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ (and we left a banquet to which we had been invited while the Messenger of God ﷺ had ablution, he ate, then performed ablution). I said to him: Were you not in a state of ablution, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes, but matters occur, and this is one that has occurred.”"],[6269,"That he declared his wife to be like his mother’s back until Ramadan passed. Then she became plump and well-rounded, and he had intercourse with her in the middle of Ramadan. He came to the Prophet ﷺ as if magnifying that, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Can you free a slave?” He said: No. He said: “Can you fast two consecutive months?” He said: No. He said: “Can you feed sixty poor people?” He said: No. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Farwa b. ʿAmr, give him that basket” — it was a container holding fifteen ṣāʿs — “so let him give it to sixty poor people.” He said: To one poorer than me? By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava tracts more in need of it than us. The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed, then said: “Take it to your family.”"],[6270,"And that he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: \"I cannot find one.\" He said: \"Can you fast two consecutive months?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then feed sixty poor people.\" He said: \"I cannot find (the means).\" So he said to Farwah b. ʿAmr, who used to estimate the dates in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Give him that basket\" — in it were fifteen ṣāʿs of dates. He said: \"Go and feed sixty poor people.\""],[6271,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him a basket containing fifteen ṣāʿs and said: \"Feed it to sixty poor people, one mudd for each poor person.\""],[6272,"That Salmān b. Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī made his wife like his mother's back to him if he had intercourse with her until Ramaḍān passed. When half of Ramaḍān had passed, she became plump and well-rounded, and she pleased him, so he had intercourse with her at night. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: \"Free a slave.\" He said: \"I cannot find one.\" He said: \"Fast two consecutive months.\" He said: \"I am not able.\" He said: \"Feed sixty poor people.\" He said: \"I cannot find (the means).\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a faraq containing fifteen ṣāʿs of dates, or sixteen ṣāʿs of dates, and he said: \"Take it and give it as charity to sixty poor people.\""],[6273,"That he \"made ẓihār from his wife and then had intercourse with her before making expiation, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to make a single expiation.\""],[6274,"I was a man who desired many women. I did not think that any man got more of that than I did. When Ramaḍān entered, I made ẓihār from my wife until Ramaḍān ended. While she was talking one night, something of her was revealed to me, so I jumped on her and had intercourse with her. When morning came, I went to my people and told them my story, and I said to them: \"Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me.\" They said: \"We would not do that; then a book from Allah would descend concerning us, or there would be a matter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning us, and a disgrace would remain upon us. But we will hand you over with your offense, so go yourself and mention your affair to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: So I went out until I came to him and told him the news. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And you did that?\" I said: \"I did that, and here I am, O Messenger of Allah, patiently accepting Allah's ruling upon me.\" He said: \"Then free a slave.\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I woke this morning owning nothing but my own neck.\" He said: \"Then fast two consecutive months.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the affliction only came upon me because of fasting.\" He said: \"Then give charity and feed sixty poor people.\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, we spent this night of ours without any supper.\" He said: \"Then go to the keeper of the charity of Banū Zurayq and tell him to give it to you, and feed sixty poor people, and benefit from what remains.\""],[6275,"\"I made ẓihār during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then I had intercourse before making expiation. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he gave me a ruling of one expiation.\""],[6276,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave woman: \"If he forced her, then she is free, and he owes her mistress a similar one; and if she consented, then she is his, and he owes her mistress a similar one.\""],[6277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife's slave woman: \"If he forced her, then she is free, and he owes her mistress a similar one; and if she consented, then she is his slave woman, and he owes her mistress a similar one.\""],[6278,"And that was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she consented, then she is a slave woman, and her mistress is owed a similar one; and if he forced her, then she is free, and her mistress is owed a similar one.\" ʿAlī said: I said to Sufyān: \"Qatādah says, on the authority of al-Ḥasan, from Qabīṣah b. Ḥurayth, from Salamah b. al-Muḥabbiq.\" Sufyān said: \"ʿAmr said: Between the two of them there is a person, or a man.\" Al-Hudhalī — meaning Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī — said to him: \"Between the two of them is Qabīṣah b. Ḥurayth.\" Sufyān said: \"I only know that this al-Hudhalī is from Salamah's people.\""],[6279,"I heard a woman ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a slave-girl she owned: her husband had taken her with him on a journey and had intercourse with her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If he compelled her, then she is free, and he owes one like her; but if she consented to him, then she is his slave-girl, and he owes one like her.”"],[6280,"That a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ used to travel and go on military expeditions constantly, and his wife sent her slave woman with him. She said: \"She will wash your head, serve you, and guard your baggage,\" and she did not give her to him. His journey on that occasion became prolonged, and he had intercourse with the slave woman. When he returned, the slave woman informed her mistress of that, and she became intensely jealous and angry. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what he had done. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"If he forced her, then she is freed, and he owes a similar one; and if he came to her with her willing consent, then she is his, and he owes the like of her value.\" And he did not impose any punishment on him."],[6281,"That the Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and came upon a hanging waterskin and asked for water. It was said: \"It is from a dead animal.\" He said: \"The purification of the hide is its tanning.\""],[6282,"That the Prophet ﷺ came to a woman and asked for water. A waterskin was brought, and he drank. It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is from a dead animal.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tanning the hide is its purification.\""],[6283,"The Prophet of God ﷺ, during the expedition of Tabuk, asked a woman for water. She said, 'I only have water in a waterskin from an animal that died.' He said, 'Did you not tan it?' She replied, 'Yes.' He said, 'Its purification is its tanning.'"],[6284,"A man from Quraysh traveled, and his wife sent her slave-girl with him. He had intercourse with her. When he came to the Prophet ﷺ, she informed him of that. He said, 'If she consented, she belongs to him and he owes a similar one; and if he forced her, she is free and he owes a similar one.'"],[6285,"From his father, who had been a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ sent two camels for sacrifice with a man and said, 'Mark them on their humps, then dip the sandal in their blood and strike their sides with it so that they are known as sacrificial camels.'"],[6286,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he passed on the day of Khaybar by pots containing meat from the people's domestic donkeys, and he ordered that they be overturned."],[6287,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise.'"],[6288,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever says, \"There is no god but God,\" will enter Paradise.'"],[6289,"We were at a watering place where people passed by. We would ask them, 'What is this matter?' They would say, 'A man claims that he is a prophet, that God sent him, and that God revealed to him such and such.' I began to not hear anything of that without memorizing it, as if it were glued into my chest, until I had gathered from it a great deal of Qur'an. The Arabs used to delay their conversion until the conquest, saying, 'Wait and see; if he prevails over them, then he is truthful and a prophet.' When the news of the conquest came to us, every people hastened to embrace Islam, and my father went with the conversion of the people of our neighborhood. He stayed with the Prophet ﷺ as long as God willed, then returned. When he drew near, we met him. When we saw him, he said, 'I have come to you, by God, from the Messenger of God ﷺ in truth.' Then he said, 'He commands you with such and such and forbids you from such and such, and to pray the prayer of such and such at the time of such and such. When the prayer is due, let one of you call the adhan, and let the one among you with the most Qur'an lead you.' They looked at the people of our neighborhood and found no one with more Qur'an than I, because of what I had memorized from the riders. So they put me forward, and I led them in prayer while I was a boy of six years. I had a burdah that, when I prostrated, rode up and exposed me. A woman of the tribe said, 'Will you not cover from us the backside of your reciter?' So they clothed me in a shirt from the weaving of Bahrain, and I never rejoiced at anything as much as I rejoiced at that shirt."],[6290,"We were at a settlement where those coming from the Prophet ﷺ would pass by us. They would say, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said such and such,' and 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said such and such,' and I memorized from that a great deal of Qur'an. My father went as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a group of his people, and he taught them the prayer. He said, 'Let the one among you who recites best lead you.' I was the best reciter among them because of what I had memorized, so I led them. I had a burdah that, when I prostrated, exposed me. A woman of the people said, 'Conceal from us the private parts of your reciter.' So they bought me an Omani shirt, and I never rejoiced at anything after Islam as much as I rejoiced at it. I led them while I was a boy of seven or eight years."],[6291,"We were at a large watering place on the main road. Riders would come to us, and we would ask them, 'What does this man say?'—meaning the Prophet ﷺ. They would say, 'He says such and such and commands them with such and such and forbids you from such and such.' I was a boy of six years; I would not hear anything except that it was as if it were written on my heart. The people used to say, 'Wait and see what the people of this man do.' When Makkah was conquered, people sent their delegations to the Messenger of God ﷺ. My father was the delegate of his people, and he came to them and said, 'I have come to you from the Messenger of God. He commands you with such and such and forbids you from such and such. When the prayer is due, let the one among you with the most Qur'an lead you.' They looked and found no one with more Qur'an than I, so they put me forward and I prayed with them. I had a burdah or a shroud-like garment, and an old woman said, 'Will you not cover from us the backside of your reciter?' So a garment was bought from the weaving of Bahrain, and a woman of the tribe cut it into a shirt for me. I never rejoiced at anything after Islam as much as I rejoiced at that shirt."],[6292,"A group of people from the tribe came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and heard him say, 'Let the one among you with the most Qur'an lead you.' So they put me forward, while I was a boy, and I led them in a patched burdah that had a tear. When I prostrated, my backside would show. They said to my father, 'Will you not cover his backside from us?' I encouraged them in teaching the Qur'an. Zuhayr said, 'He continued to be the imam of his people in prayer and over their funerals.'"],[6293,"His father and some people of his tribe came to the Messenger of God ﷺ when the people had embraced Islam, and they learned the Qur'an and fulfilled their needs. Then they asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Who should lead us in prayer?' or 'Who should pray for us?' He said, 'The one among you who has taken the most of the Qur'an should lead you,' or he said, 'The one among you who has gathered the most Qur'an.' They returned to their people and asked them, and they found no one who had gathered more than I had, while I was a boy wearing a shroud-like garment. So they put me forward, and I prayed with them—or he said, I prayed for them—and I have remained the imam of Jarm to this day. He led them in their mosque and prayed over their funerals."],[6294,"I was a boy, and I would meet the riders coming from the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask them to recite to me. They told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Let the one among you with the most Qur'an lead you,' and so I led them."],[6295,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, a questioner asked him: Has food been brought to you from the sky? He said: \"Yes, food was brought to me in a covered dish.\" He said: O Prophet of God, was there any of it left over from you? He said: \"Yes.\" He said: What was done with it? He said: \"It was raised up to the sky, and it is being revealed to me that I will not remain among you except for a little while. Then you will not remain after me except for a little while. You will say: When? When? Then you will come in scattered groups. Before the Hour there will be a severe death, and after it years of earthquakes.\""],[6296,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"It is revealed to me that I will be taken in death without delay, and that you will follow me in scattered groups, striking one another's necks. A group of people from my community will continue fighting for the truth, and God will cause the hearts of some people to deviate by means of them, and God will provide for them from them, until the Hour stands and until God's promise comes.\""],[6297,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"It is revealed to me that I will be taken in death without delay, and that you will follow me in scattered groups, striking one another's necks. A group of people from my community will continue fighting for the truth, and God will cause the hearts of some people to deviate by means of them, and God will provide for them from them, until the Hour stands and until God's promise comes.\""],[6298,"I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ until my knees almost touched his thigh. I said: O Messenger of God, horses have been abandoned, weapons have been laid down, and some people claim that there is no fighting. He said: \"They have lied. Now fighting has come. A community from my community will continue standing upon the truth, prevailing over the people. God will cause the hearts of a people who fight them to deviate so that they may obtain something from them.\" He said, while turning his back toward Yemen: \"I find the breath of the Most Merciful from here. It has been revealed to me that I will be taken in death without delay, and you will follow me in scattered groups.\""],[6299,"I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ until my knees almost touched his thigh. I said: O Messenger of God, horses have been abandoned, weapons have been laid down, and some people claim that there is no fighting. He said: \"They have lied. Now fighting has come. A community from my community will continue standing upon the truth, prevailing over the people. God will cause the hearts of a people who fight them to deviate so that they may obtain something from them.\" He said, while turning his back toward Yemen: \"I find the breath of the Most Merciful from here. It has been revealed to me that I will be taken in death without delay, and you will follow me in scattered groups.\""],[6300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The heartland of Islam is being attacked in Syria.\""],[6301,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , a man came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the horses have been stolen and weapons have been put down, and some people claim that there is no fighting and that war has laid down its burdens. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"They have lied. Fighting has now come, and a group from my Ummah will continue to fight for the sake of Allah. They are not harmed by those who oppose them, causing Allah to turn the hearts of a people against themselves. They will continue to fight until the Hour is established, and horses will continue to be harnessed. Goodness will remain in the foreheads of horses until the Hour is established, and war will not lay down its burdens until Ya'juj and Ma'juj [Gog and Magog] are released.\""],[6302,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever fasts one day seeking the face of God, God will distance him from Hell the distance a crow flies, from when it is a fledgling until it dies of old age.\""],[6303,"\"From Sālim b. ʿUbayd, who was one of the people of the Ṣuffa.\""],[6304,"Salama b. Nubayṭ narrated to us, from Nuʿaym b. Abī Hind, from Nubayṭ b. Shurayṭ, from Sālim b. ʿUbayd, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ fell unconscious during his illness, then regained consciousness and said: \"Has the prayer come?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Tell Bilāl to call the adhan and tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" ʿĀʾisha ؓ said: My father is a tender-hearted man. If only you would order someone else to lead the people in prayer. Then he fell unconscious, then regained consciousness and said: \"Has the prayer come?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Tell Bilāl to call the adhan and tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\" ʿĀʾisha said: My father is a tender-hearted man. If only you would order someone else to lead the people in prayer. Then he fell unconscious, then regained consciousness and said: \"Has the prayer been established?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Bring me a person to lean on.\" Burayda and another man came, and he leaned on them. He came to the mosque and entered while Abū Bakr ؓ was standing leading the people in prayer. Abū Bakr started to step back, but the Messenger of God ﷺ prevented him. He was seated beside Abū Bakr ؓ until he finished his prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away. ʿUmar ؓ said: I will not hear any man say that the Messenger of God ﷺ has died except that I will strike him with the sword. He took my arm and leaned on me, and he walked until we came. He said: Make room. They made room for him. He leaned over him and touched him and said: {Indeed, you are to die, and indeed they are to die.} They said: O companion of the Messenger of God, has the Messenger of God died? He said: Yes. So they knew it was as he said. They said: O companion of the Messenger of God, shall we pray over the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: Yes. They said: How shall we pray over him? He said: A group enters and says takbir and supplicates and prays, then leaves, and others come, until they finish. They said: O companion of the Messenger of God, shall the Messenger of God ﷺ be buried? He said: Yes. They said: And where shall he be buried? He said: Where he passed away, for God Almighty did not take him except in a good spot. So they knew it was as he said. Then he stood and said: Your companion is with you. He ordered them to wash him. Then he went out, and the Muhājirūn gathered to consult. They said: Go to our brothers from the Anṣār, for they have a share in this matter. They went, and a man from the Anṣār said: From us an emir and from you an emir. ʿUmar took the hand of Abū Bakr ؓ and said: Tell me, who has these three: {Second of two when they were in the cave} – who are the two? {When he said to his companion: Do not grieve} – who is his companion? {Indeed, God is with us.} He took the hand of Abū Bakr ؓ and struck it, and said to the people: Pledge allegiance to him. So they pledged allegiance to him with a good and beautiful pledge."],[6305,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ and a man sneezed, so he said, \"Peace be upon you.\" Abu Hurairah said, \"May the peace and blessings of Allah be upon you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And upon your mother.\" Then he said, \"When one of you sneezes, let him say, 'Alhamdulillah, Rabbil 'Alamin (Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds) ' abundantly or 'Alhamdulillah 'ala kulli hal (Praise be to Allah in every circumstance).' Let whoever is with him say, 'Yarhamuk Allah (May Allah have mercy on you),' and let him reply, 'Yaghfirullah (May Allah forgive us) and you.'\""],[6306,"I wish you had not mentioned my mother in a good or bad way in front of people. He said to him, 'I only said to you what the Messenger of God ﷺ said.' A man sneezed and said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Upon you and upon your mother.' And the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When one of you sneezes, let him say, \"Praise be to God in every situation,\" and let his brother or companion say to him, \"May God have mercy on you,\" and he should say, \"May God forgive us and you.\"'"],[6307,"I wish you had not mentioned my mother in a good or bad way in front of people. He said to him, 'I only said to you what the Messenger of God ﷺ said.' A man sneezed and said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Upon you and upon your mother.' And the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When one of you sneezes, let him say, \"Praise be to God in every situation,\" and let his brother or companion say to him, \"May God have mercy on you,\" and he should say, \"May God forgive us and you.\"'"],[6308,"I wish you had not mentioned my mother in a good or bad way in front of people. He said to him, 'I only said to you what the Messenger of God ﷺ said.' A man sneezed and said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Upon you and upon your mother.' And the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When one of you sneezes, let him say, \"Praise be to God in every situation,\" and let his brother or companion say to him, \"May God have mercy on you,\" and he should say, \"May God forgive us and you.\"'"],[6309,"He heard Ibn Umar, may God have mercy on him, say: 'Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfa, used to lead the first Muhajirun, the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Ansar in prayer in the mosque of Quba, among them Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, Abu Salama, Zayd, and Amir b. Rabi'a.'"],[6310,"Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfa, used to lead the Muhajirun who had emigrated to Madinah in prayer, among them Umar and others of the Muhajirun, because he was the most learned of them in the Quran."],[6311,"Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Sahla bt. Suhayl b. Amr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, Salim — the client of Hudhayfa — is with us in our house, and he has reached what men reach and has learned what men learn.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Suckle him, and you will become forbidden to him.'"],[6312,"The wife of Abu Hudhayfa came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfa, enters upon me while I have put down my garment, and I find something in myself?' He said, 'Suckle him, and what you find will go away from you.'"],[6313,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Sahla bt. Suhayl to suckle Salim so that what was in Abu Hudhayfa's mind would go away."],[6314,"Sahla bt. Suhayl came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, I see in Abu Hudhayfa's face something concerning Salim.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Suckle him.' She said, 'He is an adult.' The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said, 'Do I not know that he is a man?' Then she came and said, 'By the One who honored you with what He honored you, I have not seen anything in Abu Hudhayfa's face after that.'"],[6315,"From Salim, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to make their heads into four braids, and when they performed ghusl they gathered them together on the middle of their heads."],[6316,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people from the desert, and we would like you to teach us a deed through which Allah may benefit us. He said: \"Do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and even speaking to your brother with a cheerful face.\""],[6317,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people from the desert, and we would like you to teach us a deed through which Allah may benefit us. He said: \"Do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and even speaking to your brother with a cheerful face.\""],[6318,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people from the desert, and we would like you to teach us a deed through which Allah may benefit us. He said: \"Do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and even speaking to your brother with a cheerful face.\""],[6319,"Abu Jurayy Jabir: I mounted my young camel and came to Makkah seeking him. I found him sitting ﷺ, so I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"And upon you.\" I said: We are a group of desert people, and among us is harshness, so teach me words by which Allah may benefit me. He said: \"Fear Allah and do not consider any act of kindness or goodness insignificant. Beware of letting your lower garment hang down, for that is from pride, and Allah, Mighty and Exalted, does not love the arrogant.\" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, you mentioned letting the lower garment hang down, but a man may have sores on his leg or something he is ashamed of. He said: \"There is no harm up to the middle of the shin or to the ankles. A man from those before you wore a fine cloak and strutted in it, so Allah looked at him from above His Throne and detested him, and He commanded the earth and it seized him, and he is sinking between the earth. So beware of the detestation of Allah, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[6320,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting wrapped in a cloak whose fringe had fallen onto his feet. I said: Which of you is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah? He pointed with his hand to himself. I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I am from the desert people and I have their roughness, so advise me. He said: \"Do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, even meeting your brother with a cheerful face, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water. If a man reviles you for something he knows about you, do not revile him for something you know about him, for the reward will be yours and the sin will be his.\" And beware of letting your garment hang down, for letting the garment hang down is from pride, and Allah does not love pride. Do not curse anyone.\" After that I never cursed anyone, nor a sheep, nor a camel."],[6321,"I said: Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Do not say 'Upon you be peace'; 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead. Say 'Peace be upon you.'\" I said: Are you the Messenger of Allah? He said: \"I am the Messenger of Allah who, when harm afflicts you, you call upon him and he removes it from you, and when a year of drought afflicts you and you call upon him, he makes it easy for you.\" I said: Make a covenant with me. He said: \"Do not curse anyone, and do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, and speak to your brother with a cheerful face. Raise your garment to the middle of the shin, and if you refuse then to the ankles. Beware of letting the garment hang down, for it is from pride, and Allah does not love pride. If a man reviles you for something he knows about you, do not revile him for something you know about him, for the burden of that falls upon him.\""],[6322,"I ended up at a man whom the people would not depart except by his word. I said: By Allah, who is this man? They said: This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Do not say 'Upon you be peace,' for it is the greeting of the dead, but say 'Peace be upon you.'\" Then he mentioned something similar."],[6323,"I heard about the Prophet ﷺ, so I called for my riding camel and said: I will surely go to this man and hear from him. I came to him and found him sitting wrapped in a cloak. I heard him responding to a questioner: \"Do not consider any act of kindness insignificant, even pouring the surplus from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water. Beware of letting the garment hang down, for it is from pride, and Allah does not love pride. If a man reviles you or says what is not in you, do not revile him and do not say to him what is not in him, so the reward will be yours and the burden will be upon him. Do not curse anyone.\" After that I never cursed anything, not a camel, not a sheep, not a human, since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid cursing."],[6324,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Yahya, from Mu'adh b. Rifa'ah al-Zuraqi, that a man from Banu Salimah called Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we spend our days in our work, and when evening comes, Mu'adh b. Jabal comes and calls to prayer, and we go to him, and he lengthens it for us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Mu'adh, do not be a troublemaker. Either pray with me, or lighten it for your people.\""],[6325,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Yahya, from Mu'adh b. Rifa'ah al-Zuraqi, that a man from Banu Salimah called Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we spend our days in our work, and when evening comes, Mu'adh b. Jabal comes and calls to prayer, and we go to him, and he lengthens it for us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Mu'adh, do not be a troublemaker. Either pray with me, or lighten it for your people.\""],[6326,"He saw the Messenger of Allah perform ablution then take a handful of water and sprinkle it over his private area to remove any doubts about urine drippings. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 461)"],[6327,"The Banu Shababa tribe had a valley full of intelligence. They used to deliver to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , honey from a bee colony they owned, with ten portions from every ten portions. They also had two valleys which they protected. When Umar became the caliph, he appointed Sufyan ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi to manage their affairs. They refused to deliver anything to him and said that they only used to deliver it to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ . So, Sufyan wrote a letter to Umar informing him of this and Umar wrote back to him saying, \"Indeed, bees are flies of sustenance that Allah sends to whom He wills. If they deliver to you what they used to deliver to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , then give them their valleys. If not, then create a separation between them and the people. They should deliver to him what they used to deliver to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , and protect their valleys.\""],[6328,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik from Thawr b. Zayd al-Dili from a son of 'Abd Allah b. Sufyan from his grandfather Sufyan b. 'Abd Allah that 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent him as a zakat collector. He used to count kids on the people, so they said, 'You count kids on us but do not take anything from them?' When he came to 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and mentioned that to him, 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said to him: 'Yes, count on them the kid that the shepherd carries, but do not take it, and do not take the one that is eaten, nor the one that has recently given birth and is kept for its young, nor the pregnant one, nor the ram of the flock. Take the jadha'ah and the thaniyyah, and that is a just balance between the young of the property and its best.'"],[6329,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and 'Umar b. Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim b. 'Ali narrated to us; and Yahya b. 'Uthman b. Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym b. Hammad narrated to us; and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl b. al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; they said: Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ma'iz al-'Amiri from Sufyan b. 'Abd Allah al-Thaqafi who said: I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me something I can hold fast to.' He said, 'Say: My Lord is God, then be steadfast.' I said, 'What do you fear most for me?' He took hold of his own tongue and then said, 'This.'"],[6330,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me something I can hold fast to.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Say: My Lord is God, and be steadfast.' I said, 'O Messenger of God, what do you fear most for me?' He took hold of his own tongue and then said, 'This.'"],[6331,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, tell me something about Islam such that I will not ask anyone after you.' He said, 'Say: I believe in God, then be steadfast.' I said, 'What should I guard against, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'And he gestured to his tongue.'"],[6332,"I said to the Prophet of God ﷺ, 'O Prophet of God, tell me something I can benefit from, and be brief, so that perhaps I can comprehend it.' The Prophet of God ﷺ said, 'Do not get angry.' He repeated it to him several times asking about that, and the Prophet of God ﷺ kept saying, 'Do not get angry.'"],[6333,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Forbid your people from the nabidh of earthen jars, for it is forbidden from God and His Messenger.'"],[6334,"That he was in the shade of the riding camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage, or that a man narrated that to him from the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: 'A journey in the morning or evening in the path of God ﷻ is better than the world and all that is in it.'"],[6335,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The year one hundred will not come while anyone on its face remains.'"],[6336,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The year one hundred will not come while anyone on its face remains.'"],[6337,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Syria will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6338,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik b. Anas reported to us, from Hisham b. ‘Urwa, from his father, from ‘Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from Sufyan b. Abi Zuhayr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6339,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Iraq will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Syria will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6340,"‘Abd Allah b. Maslama al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from Hisham b. ‘Urwa, from his father, from ‘Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, from Sufyan b. Abi Zuhayr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Iraq will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Syria will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6341,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yemen will be conquered, and men will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them, but Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Iraq will be conquered, and men will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them, but Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. Then Syria will be conquered, and men will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them, but Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.” Ahmad b. Dawud al-Makki added in his hadith: ‘Urwa said: Then I met Sufyan b. Abi Zuhayr at the time of his death, and he reported this hadith to me."],[6342,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6343,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Yemen will be conquered, and people will come driving their camels, taking their families and those who obey them. Madinah is better for them, if only they knew.”"],[6344,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik reported to us, from Yazid b. Khusayfa, that al-Sa’ib b. Yazid informed him that he heard Sufyan b. Abi Zuhayr, a man from Azd Shanu’a and one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrating to people at the gate of the mosque, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever keeps a dog that does not benefit him in guarding crops or livestock, one qirat is deducted from his deeds every day.” He said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba."],[6345,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yazid b. Khusayfa, from al-Sa’ib b. Yazid, that Sufyan b. Abi Zuhayr informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever keeps a dog that does not benefit him in guarding crops or livestock, one qirat is deducted from his deeds every day.” Al-Sa’ib said: O Sufyan, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba."],[6346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No servant truly believes until I am dearer to him than his own self, and my family is dearer to him than his own family, and my very being is dearer to him than his own being.”"],[6347,"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever buys a camel that has been kept with its milk tied back, and then dislikes it, may return it along with a sa‘ of dates.”"],[6348,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the house of charity, and Hasan ؓ was with him. He took a date and put it in his mouth. The Prophet ﷺ inserted his finger and took it out of his mouth, then said: “We are a household for whom charity is not permissible.”"],[6349,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest. He said, \"Abu Sufyan is in the arak trees.\" So we entered and seized him. The Muslims kept coming to him, concealing their swords, until they brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said to him, \"Woe to you, O Abu Sufyan! I have brought you the world and the Hereafter, so submit and you will be safe.\" Al-Abbas was his friend, so al-Abbas said, \"O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves renown.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a caller to announce in Makkah: \"Whoever closes his door is safe, whoever lays down his weapon is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe.\" Then he sent al-Abbas with him until they sat on the mountain pass. Banu Sulaym approached, and he said, \"O Abbas, who are these?\" He said, \"These are Banu Sulaym.\" He said, \"What do I have to do with Sulaym?\" Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ and the Muhajirun approached, and he said, \"O Abbas, who are these?\" He said, \"This is Ali b. Abi Talib among the Muhajirun.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ approached among the Ansar, and he said, \"O Abbas, who are these?\" He said, \"These are the red death. This is the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Ansar.\" Abu Sufyan said, \"I have seen the kingdom of Kisra and Caesar, but I have not seen the like of your nephew's kingdom.\" Al-Abbas said to him, \"It is only prophethood.\""],[6350,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ observed i'tikaf in the last ten days of Ramadan in a dome made of palm leaves.\""],[6351,"Al-Hasan or al-Husayn ؓ was in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. He urinated, and I saw his urine flowing in streams. I rushed toward him, but he said, \"Leave my son until he finishes his urination, and do not startle him until he finishes his urination.\" Then he poured water over it."],[6352,"Al-Hasan or al-Husayn ؓ was in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. He urinated, and I saw his urine flowing in streams. I rushed toward him, but he said, \"Leave my son until he finishes his urination, and do not startle him until he finishes his urination.\" Then he poured water over it."],[6353,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when al-Hasan came crawling until he climbed onto his chest and urinated on him. We rushed to take him, but the Prophet ﷺ said, \"My son, my son.\" Then he called for water and poured it over the spot."],[6354,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ distributed sheep, giving one sheep for every ten of his companions, and that they were spoils. He said, \"On that day, the Prophet ﷺ ordered the cooking pots to be overturned, and that was the day of Khaybar.\""],[6355,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ in a prayer that was not obligatory. He came to the mention of the Fire and said, \"I seek refuge in God from the Fire. Woe to the people of the Fire.\" The wording is from the hadith of Uthman b. Abi Shaybah."],[6356,"Abu Layla: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about snakes in houses. He said, \"When you see them in your dwellings, say: We adjure you by the covenant of God which Noah took upon you, and we adjure you by the covenant which Sulayman took upon you, that you not harm us. If they return, then kill them.\""],[6357,"Safinah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: I sailed on the sea and the ship I was in broke apart, so I rode on one of its planks. The plank threw me into a thicket where there was a lion. It came toward me, and I said, \"O Abu al-Harith, I am the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" It lowered its head and came to me, then pushed me with its shoulder until it brought me out of the thicket and placed me on the road, and it made a low sound, so I thought it was bidding me farewell. That was the last I saw of it."],[6358,"From Burayh b. Umar b. Safinah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: He had cupping done and said, \"Take this blood and bury it away from animals, birds, and people.\" I hid myself and drank it. Then I mentioned that to him and he laughed. The wording is that of Ahmad b. Salih."],[6359,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution with one mudd and bathe with one sa'.\""],[6360,"I will tell you my name. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Safinah. I said, \"Why did he name you Safinah?\" He said: He went out with his companions, and their baggage became heavy for them, so he said, \"Spread your cloak.\" I spread it, and he placed their baggage in it, then loaded it on me and said, \"Carry it, for you are nothing but a ship (safinah).\" He said: If I had carried that day the load of a camel, or two camels, or five wasqs, it would not have been heavy on me."],[6361,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Whenever a person became tired, he would throw his sword and shield on me until I was carrying a great deal. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You are a ship (safinah).\""],[6362,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Everyone among his companions whose baggage became heavy for him loaded it on me, until I carried a great deal of it. The Prophet ﷺ passed by me and said, \"You are nothing but a ship (safinah).\""],[6363,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"The caliphate will be among my nation for thirty years, then there will be kingship after that.\" Then he said to me, \"Hold on to the ship.\" So I held on to the caliphate of Abu Bakr, the caliphate of Umar, the caliphate of Uthman, and the caliphate of Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. And I found it to be thirty years."],[6364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The caliphate after me in my community will be thirty years, then kingship.\""],[6365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The caliphate of prophethood will be thirty years, then Allah will give authority to whomever He wills,\" or he said, \"His kingdom to whomever He wills.\" Sa'id said: \"Abu Bakr held it for two years, Umar for ten, Uthman for twelve, and Ali for six.\""],[6366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “There was no prophet before me except that he warned his nation against the Dajjal. He is one-eyed, his left eye; on his right eye is a thick, protruding white membrane. Between his eyes is written ‘kāfir.’ He will emerge with two valleys; one of them is a garden and the other is a fire. His garden is really a fire, and his fire is really a garden. With him are two angels from among the angels who resemble two prophets from among the prophets, one on his right and the other on his left. That is a trial for the people. He will say: ‘Am I not your Lord? I give life and I cause death.’ Then one of the two angels will say: ‘You have lied,’ but no one among the people will hear it except his companion. His companion will say to him: ‘You have spoken the truth,’ and the people will hear him, so they will think that the Dajjal has spoken the truth. That is a trial. Then he will travel until he reaches Madinah, but he will not be granted entry into it. He will say: ‘This is the village of that man.’ Then he will travel until he reaches Syria, and Allah ﷻ will destroy him at the pass of Afiq.”"],[6367,"A man invited Ali and he prepared food for him. Fatimah ؓ said: ‘If only we could invite the Prophet ﷺ and he could eat with us.’ So Ali sent a man to him, and he came. He took hold of the doorposts and saw a decorated curtain in the corners of the house, so he turned back. Fatimah ؓ said to Ali ؓ: ‘Follow him and see what made him turn back.’ So he followed him and said: ‘What made you turn back, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said: “It is not proper for me to enter an adorned house.”"],[6368,"Safina said: Umm Salamah said to me: “I will set you free on the condition that you serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as you live.” I said: “Even if you had not stipulated this condition upon me, I would not have parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as I live.” So she set me free and stipulated that upon me."],[6369,"Safina reported: We, the sons of Muqarrin, were seven during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had a servant, and we had no other servant besides her. One of us slapped her, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Set her free.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have no servant besides her.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let her serve you until you are self-sufficient, then release her.”"],[6370,"Safina reported: We, the sons of Muqarrin, were seven during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had a servant, and we had no other servant besides her. One of us slapped her, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Set her free.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have no servant besides her?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let her serve you until you are self-sufficient, then release her.”"],[6371,"Safina reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Were you unable to do anything but strike her face? I saw myself as the seventh of seven of the children of Muqarrin, and we had no servant except one servant. The youngest of us slapped her face, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to set her free.”"],[6372,"Safina reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “You slapped her face? I saw myself as the seventh of seven, and we had no servant except one servant. A man slapped him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to set him free.”"],[6373,"Safina reported: The image was forbidden. I saw myself as the seventh of seven brothers during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no servant except one servant. One of us slapped him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to set him free.”"],[6374,"Suwayd b. Muqarrin al-Muzani reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed defending against an injustice, he is a martyr.”"],[6375,"Suwayd b. Muqarrin al-Muzani reported: “We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khaybar until we reached al-Sahba’, and between it and Khaybar there is a distance of a morning’s journey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the people for their provisions, and nothing was brought except sawiq (a coarse mixture of ground barley or wheat). He ate and we ate. Then he stood, rinsed his mouth with water, and then prayed Zuhr and Asr.”"],[6376,"It was narrated from Yahya b. Sa‘id, from Bashir b. Yasar, that Suwayd b. al-Nu‘man informed him that he “went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Khaybar, until when we were at al-Sahba’, which is part of the nearest area of Khaybar, he dismounted and prayed Asr. Then he called for the provisions, and nothing was brought except sawiq, so he ordered it and it was moistened. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate and we ate. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for Maghrib, rinsed his mouth with water, and we rinsed our mouths, then he prayed, and he did not perform wudu.” The wording is that of al-Qa‘nabi’s report."],[6377,"Suwayd b. Muqarrin al-Muzani reported: “We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Khaybar. When we were at al-Sahba’ and had prayed Asr, the Prophet ﷺ called for the people’s provisions. They brought sawiq, and they ate and drank. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for Maghrib prayer, rinsed his mouth with water, and the people rinsed their mouths, then they prayed, and they did not add anything beyond that.”"],[6378,"Suwayd b. al-Nu'man, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that they set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khaybar. He said: When we were at al-Sahba', which is a short distance from Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food, but nothing was found except sawiq. So we ate, then we drank water with it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rinsed his mouth, stood up, and prayed."],[6379,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to Khaybar and encamped at a place near it called al-Sahba'. He asked his companions for what remained of their provisions, and they brought him nothing but sawiq. He mixed it and ate, then he rinsed his mouth, stood up and prayed Maghrib without performing wudu'."],[6380,"We set out intending to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Wa'il b. Hujr was with us. An enemy of his seized him. The people were reluctant to take an oath, but I swore that he was my brother, so he was released. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"The people were reluctant to take an oath, so I swore that he was my brother.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim.\""],[6381,"Makhramah al-'Abdi and I brought cloth from Hajar, and we came with it to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us at Mina and bought a pair of trousers from us. There was a weigher who weighed for a fee. He said, \"O weigher, weigh and give full measure.\""],[6382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it.\""],[6383,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a lost sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He said: And I asked him about a lost camel. When he became angry, it was recognizable by the redness of his cheeks. He said, \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own water-skin and its own shoes. It will come to water and eat from the trees. Leave it alone until it meets its Lord.\""],[6384,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a lost sheep. He said, \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He said: And I asked him about a lost camel. When he became angry, it was recognizable by the redness of his cheeks. He said, \"What do you have to do with it? It has its own water-skin and its own shoes. It will come to water and eat from the trees. Leave it alone until it meets its Lord.\""],[6385,"He heard his father, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, say: We were returning with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a military expedition. When Uhud appeared to us, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah is the Greatest. Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it.\""],[6386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best property of a man is a productive palm grove or a well-trained mare.\""],[6387,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or someone who heard him told me, say: \"Allah has made this tribe of Lakhm and Judham a source of relief in Syria through their camels and livestock, just as He made Joseph a source of relief for the people of Egypt.\""],[6388,"He informed me who traveled with the collector of the zakah of the messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there was in the covenant of the messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Do not take from a suckling animal, and do not combine what is separate, and do not separate what is combined.\""],[6389,"Suwaid bin Ghafalah said: ”The Zakah collector of the Prophet came to us, and I took him by the hand and read in his order: 'Do not gather separate herds and do not separate herd for fear of Sadaqah'. A man brought him a huge, fat she-camel, but he refused to accept it. So he brought him another of lower quality and he accepted it. He said: 'What land would shelter me, if I came to the Messenger of Allah having taken the nest of a Muslim man's camels?' ” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1801)"],[6390,"A man said, \"O commander of the believers, do you know this passing man?\" He said, \"No. Who is he?\" He said, \"This is Sawad b. Qarib, a man from the people of Yemen who has honor and status among them, and he is the one whose companion from the jinn came to him with the appearance of the messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Umar ؓ said, \"Call him to me.\" He was called to him. He said, \"Are you Sawad b. Qarib?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So you are the one whose jinn companion came to you with the appearance of the messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So you are still upon what you were upon of your soothsaying?\" He became extremely angry and said, \"O commander of the believers, no one has confronted me with this since I became Muslim.\" Umar said, \"Glory be to Allah! By Allah, what we were upon of idolatry is greater than your soothsaying. Tell me about your jinn companion coming to you with the appearance of the messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Yes, O commander of the believers. While I was one night between sleeping and waking, my companion from the jinn came to me, struck me with his foot, and said: 'Rise, O Sawad b. Qarib, understand and comprehend, if you can comprehend, that a messenger has been sent from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib, calling to Allah, may He be exalted, and to His worship.' Then he began to recite.\""],[6391,"I was sleeping on a mountain among the mountains of al-Sarah, when a visitor came, struck me with his foot, and said: 'Rise, O Sawad b. Qarib, a messenger from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib has come to you.' I sat up straight, and he turned away while reciting."],[6392,"I said, \"O messenger of Allah, I am a man to whom beauty has been made beloved, and I was given of it what you see, so I do not love for anyone to surpass me in the strap of my sandal\" or he said \"the lace of my sandal. Is that from arrogance?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Then what is arrogance, O messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Whoever rejects the truth and despises people.\""],[6393,"A man asked the messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"O messenger of Allah, I am a man to whom handsomeness and beauty have been made beloved, to the point that I do not love for anyone to surpass me in a sandal strap. Is that from arrogance?\" He said, \"No, but arrogance is from despising people and rejecting the truth.\""],[6394,"O messenger of Allah, I have been given handsomeness and beauty, and it has been made beloved to me, so I do not love for anyone to excel me in the strap of my sandal. Is that from arrogance? He said, \"No, but arrogance is whoever rejects the truth and despises people.\""],[6395,"I came to the messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered for me some livestock, and he said to me, \"You should have horses, for the horses have goodness tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6396,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing a ring."],[6397,"Sulayman b. Surad al-Khuza'i and al-Musayyib b. Najabah al-Fazari went out with four thousand, and they camped at al-Nukhaylah seeking the blood of al-Husayn ؓ, and Sulayman b. Surad was over them. That was at the beginning of Rabi' al-Akhir in the year sixty-five. Then they marched toward Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad and met his vanguard, and they fought. Sulayman b. Surad and Ibn Najabah were killed in the month of Rabi' al-Akhir."],[6398,"The messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the confederates, \"Now we fight them and they do not fight us.\""],[6399,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of the confederates, \"Today we fight them and they do not fight us.\""],[6400,"\"Sulaiman bin Surad said to Khalid bin Urfutah - or, Khalid said to Sulaiman - 'Did you hear the Messenger of Allah saying: \"Whoever is killed by his stomach then he will not be punished in the grave\"?' One of them said to the other: \"Yes.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1064)"],[6401,"A bedouin prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and had with him a horn. Some of the people took it. When the Prophet ﷺ had finished, the bedouin said, \"Where is the horn?\" Some of the people seemed to laugh, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not frighten a Muslim.\""],[6402,"Two men reviled each other in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became intensely angry. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I know a word which, if he said it, what he feels would leave him: if he said, ‘I seek refuge in God from Satan,’ what he feels would leave him.”"],[6403,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The grateful eater is like the patient faster.”"],[6404,"A man from the Emigrants gave as charity a large piece of land of his to his mother, then she died and had no heir other than him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My mother, so-and-so, was one of the dearest and most beloved people to me, and I gave her a large piece of land of mine as charity, then she died and has no heir other than me. How do you command me to deal with it?” He said, “God has made your reward obligatory and has returned to you your land. Do with it whatever you wish.”"],[6405,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I gave my mother something as charity, and she has died. What should I do?” He said, “God has returned to you your land and accepted your charity.”"],[6406,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a man who dies among women and a woman who dies among men, neither of them having a mahram: He said, “They should perform tayammum and not be washed.”"],[6407,"A man came to his family after he had picked up an abandoned infant, then he went to ʿUmar ؓ and mentioned it to him. ʿUmar said, “Perhaps the little cave brings misfortune.” The man said, “It was only picked up while I was absent.” ʿUmar asked about him and he was praised with good. So ʿUmar said to him, “Its walaʾ belongs to you, and its maintenance is on us from the public treasury.”"],[6408,"He found an abandoned infant during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ and brought it to him, and ʿUmar suspected him regarding it, but he was praised with good, so ʿUmar said, “He is free, his walaʾ belongs to you, and his maintenance is from the public treasury.”"],[6409,"He met the Prophet ﷺ and was with him in the year of the conquest."],[6410,"He informed him that he picked up an illegitimate child and brought him to ʿUmar ؓ, who said, “Go and have him suckled with the wealth of Allah, and you shall have his clientage.” Ibn Shihāb said, “The man who picked him up and brought him to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb—he himself reported that to me.”"],[6411,"From Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿidah: Abū Dujānah Simāk b. Kharashah, and he is the one who took the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uḥud.”"],[6412,"From ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāmah from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿidah: Simāk b. Kharashah, and he is Abū Dujānah.”"],[6413,"From Muḥammad b. Isḥāq: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāmah from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿidah: Simāk b. Kharashah, and he is Abū Dujānah.”"],[6414,"From Ibn Shihāb: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāmah from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿidah: Simāk b. Kharashah, and he is Abū Dujānah.”"],[6415,"ʿAlī entered upon Fāṭimah on the day of Uḥud and said, “Take this sword, not blameworthy.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “If you fought well, then Sahl b. Ḥunayf and Abū Dujānah Simāk b. Kharashah also fought well.”"],[6416,"On the day of Uḥud, Abū Dujānah marked himself with a red headband. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him while he was swaggering in his walk between the two ranks, and said, “Indeed, it is a walk that Allah hates, except in this place.”"],[6417,"From ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAdī b. al-Najjār: Salīṭ b. Qays b. ʿAmr b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. Mālik b. ʿAdī b. ʿĀmir.”"],[6418,"From ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Rabīʿ b. Sabrah b. Maʿbad b. ʿAmr b. Ṣuḥārah b. Jurayj b. Dhuhl b. Zayd b. Juhaynah b. Quḍāʿah."],[6419,"He informed him that they set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the Farewell Pilgrimage until they stopped at ʿUsfān, entering consecration for ḥajj. A man from Banū Mudlij called Surāqah b. Mālik b. Juʿshum stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, decide for us as you would for a people as if they were born today.” He said, “Allah ﷻ has included an ʿumrah for you in this ḥajj of yours. So when you arrive, whoever circumambulates the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah has exited consecration, except whoever has a sacrificial animal with him.” Then when we exited consecration, he said, “Enjoy these women.” Enjoyment among us meant marriage. We proposed that to the women, but they refused unless they set a term between us and them. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Do it.” So I went out with a cousin of mine; I had a cloak and he had a cloak, and his cloak was better than mine while I was more youthful than him. We came to a woman, and she liked his cloak and she liked my appearance. Then the matter came to her saying, “Give me your cloak.” The term between me and her was ten days. I spent the night with her, then in the morning I went out to the mosque. There was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing between the corner and the door, saying, “O people, I had permitted you enjoyment of these women. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has forbidden that until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever has any of them with him, let him let her go, and do not take back anything of what you have given them.”"],[6420,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-Madīnah for the Farewell Pilgrimage until, when we were at ʿUsfān, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, ʿumrah has entered into ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.” Surāqah b. Mālik said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, teach us as you would teach a people as if they were born today. Is this ʿumrah of ours for this year of ours or forever?” He said, “No, rather forever.” Then when we reached Makkah, we circumambulated the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Then he commanded us with the enjoyment of women. We went back to him and said, “They refuse unless there is a specified term.” He said, “Do it.” So I went out with a companion of mine. I had a cloak and he had a cloak. We entered upon a woman and presented ourselves to her. She began to look at my companion’s cloak and saw it was better than my cloak, and she looked at me and saw I was more youthful than him. She said, “A cloak for a cloak,” and she chose me. So I married her with my cloak and spent that night with her. When morning came, I went to the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the minbar delivering a sermon. I heard him say, “Whoever has married a woman for a term, let him give her what he specified for her and not take back anything of what he gave her, and let him separate from her, for Allah ﷻ has made it forbidden for you until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6421,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade temporary marriage (mut'ah) during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[6422,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted temporary marriage, then after three days I came to him while he was prohibiting it and forbidding it with the strongest prohibition."],[6423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had permitted us temporary marriage. When we arrived in Makkah, my cousin and I went to a young woman. I had a burdah (cloak) and my cousin had a burdah; my cousin's burdah was better than mine, but I was more handsome than my cousin. She began looking at me and said, 'A burdah is like a burdah,' so she chose me. I gave her my burdah, then I stayed with her as long as Allah willed. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him standing between the door and Zamzam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We had permitted you this mut'ah (temporary marriage). Whoever has any of these women, let him release her, for Allah, Exalted be He, has made it forbidden until the Day of Resurrection. And do not take back anything of what you have given them.'"],[6424,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted us to do mut'ah. So I and another man went to a woman from Banu Amir, as if she were a long-necked young she-camel. We offered ourselves to her. She said, 'What will you give me?' I said, 'My cloak,' and my companion said, 'My cloak.' My companion's cloak was better than mine, but I was more handsome than him. When she looked at my companion's cloak, she liked it, and when she looked at me, she liked me. Then she said, 'You and your cloak will suffice me.' I stayed with her for three days. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever has any of these women whom he is enjoying in temporary marriage, let him release her.' The wording is that of the hadith of Yahya b. Bukayr."],[6425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of the Conquest, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted them mut'ah with women. So I and a cousin of mine went out. I had a worn burd, and my cousin had a new, fresh burd. I was handsome, surpassing my cousin in beauty, while my cousin was below me in beauty. We went out until when we were in the upper part of Makkah or the lower part of it, a young woman from Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah met us, like a young she-camel. We said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded us, or permitted us, to do mut'ah with women. Would you accept one of us?' She said, 'Did he really do that?' We said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Yes.' We spread out our two burds. She began looking at the two burds, then looking at me and my cousin. When my cousin saw her looking at me, he turned her attention away, saying, 'My burd is new and fresh, while my cousin's burd is old and worn.' The girl said, 'The burd of this one is not bad.' He repeated that statement once or twice, then she chose me. Then we did not leave Makkah until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made it forbidden."],[6426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted us mut'ah in the year of the Conquest. So I and another man went to a young woman, as if she were a long-necked young she-camel, to do mut'ah with her. We sat before her. I had a burd and he had a burd. We spoke to her and gave her our two burds as her dower. I was more handsome than him, but his burd was better than mine. She began looking at me sometimes and at his burd sometimes. Then she accepted me, and I married her. I stayed with her for three days. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it, so I separated from her, or something like that."],[6427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah. He said, 'It is forbidden from this day of ours until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever gave anything, let him not take it back.'"],[6428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah."],[6429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah on the Day of the Conquest."],[6430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made mut'ah with women forbidden."],[6431,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mut'ah with women on the Day of the Conquest."],[6432,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade temporary marriage (nikah al-mut'ah)."],[6433,"He informed him. He said: 'I engaged in mut'ah marriage with a woman from Banu Amir during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for two red cloaks. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us from mut'ah with women.'"],[6434,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited it during the Farewell Pilgrimage.'"],[6435,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited mut'ah with women on the day of the conquest of Makkah.'"],[6436,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, when the people entered it, there was a man from Qays who had arranged with a woman and given her two garments. I was better looking than him, and I had a garment with me. I said to her, 'I will give you this garment and enjoy mut'ah with you.' She left the Qaysi man and said, 'Yes.' I made an appointment with her to return to her. Then I entered the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it, prohibiting it. So I returned and took my garment back from her."],[6437,"I heard al-Zuhri say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited mut'ah with women at the time of the conquest.' I said, 'Who narrated this to you?' He said, 'A man narrated to me from his father.'"],[6438,"'The Prophet ﷺ prohibited mut'ah with women on the day of the conquest of Makkah.'"],[6439,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to engage in mut'ah during the conquest of Makkah, so we enjoyed mut'ah with women. Then he prohibited us from it.'"],[6440,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited mut'ah with women.'"],[6441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Let one of you use a sutrah in his prayer, even if it is only an arrow.'"],[6442,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Let one of you use a sutrah in his prayer, even if it is only an arrow.'"],[6443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pray in sheep enclosures, but do not pray in camel enclosures.'"],[6444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Teach the child to pray when he is seven years old, and strike him for it when he is ten.'"],[6445,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The child is commanded to pray when he reaches seven years of age; and when he reaches ten, beat him for it.”"],[6446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When a boy reaches seven years, command him to pray; and when he reaches ten, beat him for it.”"],[6447,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ encamped at al-Hijr, he said: “Do not drink any of their water.” So some of them had kneaded dough and mixed hais, and they threw it away."],[6448,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to his companions when they encamped at al-Hijr: “Whoever has kneaded anything from this—meaning their well—let him throw it away.” So the one with dough threw away his dough, and the one with hais threw away his hais."],[6449,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not pray in the resting places of camels, but pray in the sheepfolds.”"],[6450,"I attended the Prophet ﷺ one day when he said: “Whoever here is from Maʿadd, let him stand.” ʿAmr b. Murrah al-Juhani stood up, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Sit down,” until he had done that three times. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Quḍāʿah is the son of Mālik b. Ḥimyar.”"],[6451,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ [said]: “We hoped that this cloud would rain on us.” He said: “This cloud has been commanded to rain—meaning on the valley.”"],[6452,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The ʿumrah has entered into the ḥajj.”"],[6453,"O Messenger of God, tell us about this umrah of ours: is it for this year of ours, or forever? He said, \"No, rather forever. The umrah has entered into the hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\" I said, O Messenger of God, tell us about our religion as though we are looking at it: is it according to what the pens have written and the decrees have fixed, or is it something we initiate anew? He said, \"Rather, it is according to what the pens have written and the decrees have fixed.\" He said, Then what is the point of deeds, O Messenger of God? He said, \"Act, for everyone is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[6454,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, proclaiming the talbiyah, even the women and children. When we arrived in Makkah, we circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to us, \"Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram.\" We said, What kind of exiting? He said, \"Complete exiting.\" So we went to our wives, wore our clothes, and applied perfume. Then on the day of al-Tarwiyah, we entered ihram for hajj, and the first circumambulation between al-Safa and al-Marwah sufficed us. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us to share in camels and cattle: every seven of us in one budanah. Then Suraqah b. Malik came and said, O Messenger of God, explain to us our religion as though we were created just now. Do you think this umrah of ours is for this year of ours or forever? He said, \"Rather, forever.\""],[6455,"\"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ and entered ihram for hajj from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and we entered ihram on behalf of the children, and we circumambulated on their behalf and performed sa'y on their behalf. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us, and we exited ihram completely. Then on the eve of al-Tarwiyah, we entered ihram for hajj from al-Batha'.\" He did not mention the story of Suraqah b. Malik."],[6456,"O Messenger of God, tell us about this religion of ours, as though we were created for it just now. In what thing do we act? Is it concerning something in which the decrees are fixed and the pens have run, or concerning a newly initiated matter? He said, \"Rather, concerning what the pens have fixed.\" Suraqah said, Then what is the point of deeds, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Act, for every worker is facilitated toward what he was created for.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: {As for him who gives and fears, and confirms the best} with \"there is no god but God\" {We will ease him toward ease. But as for him who is miserly and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best} he said, \"there is no god but God\" {We will ease him toward hardship}."],[6457,"Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, O Messenger of God, tell us about this umrah of ours: is it for this year of ours or forever? He said, \"Rather, forever.\" He said, O Messenger of God, tell us about our deeds, as though we were created just now: is it something for which the book is fixed and the decrees have run, or something we initiate anew? He said, \"No, rather it is something for which the book is fixed and the decrees have run.\" He said, O Messenger of God, then what is the point of deeds? He said, \"Act, for everyone is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[6458,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, proclaiming the talbiyah for hajj. When we arrived in Makkah, we circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us and said, \"Whoever among you has not driven a sacrificial animal should exit ihram and make it an umrah.\" We said, Exit from what, O Messenger of God? He said, \"Complete exiting.\" So we had relations with women, wore clothes, and applied perfume. Then some people said, He makes us exit ihram while there are only four days between us and Arafah. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he stood among us, as if angry, and said, \"By God, you know that I am the most God-fearing of you. Had I known you would say such a thing, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal. So comply with what you are commanded.\" Then Suraqah b. Malik stood up and said, O Messenger of God, is this umrah of ours, which you commanded us, for this year or forever? The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Rather, forever.\" Suraqah said, Tell us, O Messenger of God, about our religion, as though we were created just now: is it concerning something for which the pens have dried and the decrees have run, or concerning something newly initiated? He said, \"Rather, concerning what the pens have dried upon and the decrees have run with.\" Suraqah said, Then what is the point of deeds, O Messenger of God? He said, \"Act, for every worker is facilitated.\" Then he recited: {As for him who gives and fears, and confirms the best, We will ease him toward ease. But as for him who is miserly and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best, We will ease him toward hardship}."],[6459,"O Messenger of God, do we act for a matter that has already been decreed, or for a matter we initiate anew? He said, \"For a matter that has already been decreed.\" Suraqah said, Then what is the point of deeds? The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Every worker is facilitated.\""],[6460,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ as pilgrims, intending nothing but hajj and resolving on nothing else. When he was at Sarif, Aishah menstruated. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her while she was weeping and said, \"What makes you weep?\" She said, I have been afflicted with the ailment. He said, \"You are only one of the daughters of Adam; what afflicts them afflicts you.\" Then we arrived in Makkah with four nights having passed of Dhu al-Hijjah, and we circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah as the Messenger of God ﷺ had commanded us. We discussed among ourselves and said, We set out as pilgrims, intending nothing but hajj and resolving on nothing else, until when there remained between us and Arafat only four nights, while our private parts were dripping semen from women. That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he stood up as a preacher and said, \"Indeed, the umrah has entered into the hajj. Had I known earlier what I came to know later, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal. Were it not for the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. So whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram.\" Then Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum al-Mudliji said, O Messenger of God, tell us the story of a people as though they were born today: is this umrah of ours for this year of ours or forever? He said, \"Forever.\" Then we went to Arafah. When it was time to depart, Aishah said, O Messenger of God, you have circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, but I have not circumambulated. He said, \"You have the like of what the people have.\" She said, But I feel something within myself. So the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped for her at the highest part of the valley of Makkah, and Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr seated her behind him until she reached al-Tan'im."],[6461,"We arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the morning of the fourth of Dhu al-Hijjah, all of us proclaiming the talbiyah for hajj. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us, so we circumambulated the House, prayed, and performed sa'y between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he ordered us, and we shortened our hair. Then he said, \"Exit ihram.\" We said, O Messenger of God, from what? He said, \"From what the one who is halal is permitted: women and perfume.\" So women were approached and incense burners sent forth their fragrance. He was informed that some of them were saying, Would one of us go to Mina while his private part drips semen? He preached to them, praised God Almighty, and extolled Him. Then he said, \"Had I known earlier what I came to know later, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal. Had I not driven the sacrificial animal, I would have shaved. Now, take your rituals from me.\" So all the people remained until the day of al-Tarwiyah. When they wanted to head to Mina, they entered ihram for hajj. The sacrificial animal was upon whoever could afford it, and fasting upon whoever could not. He made them share in their sacrificial animals: a camel among seven and a cow among seven. Their circumambulation of the House and their sa'y between al-Safa and al-Marwah was a single circumambulation and a single sa'y for their hajj and their umrah. He did not mention the story of Suraqah b. Malik."],[6462,"I arrived in Makkah performing tamattu' with an umrah. We arrived three days before al-Tarwiyah. The people of Makkah said to me, Your hajj will now become a Makkan one. So I went to Ata' b. Abi Rabah to seek his legal opinion. He said, Jabir b. Abd Allah narrated to me that he performed hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day he drove the budn, and they had entered ihram for hajj as individuals. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them, \"Exit your ihram by circumambulating the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and remain halal until the day of al-Tarwiyah, then enter ihram for hajj. Make what you came with a mut'ah.\" They said, How can we make it a mut'ah when we have already named it hajj? He said, \"Do what I commanded you. Had I not driven the sacrificial animal, I would have done the same as what I commanded you. But no forbidden thing becomes lawful for me until the sacrificial animal reaches its place of sacrifice.\" So they did it. He did not mention the story of Suraqah b. Malik."],[6463,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived with four nights having passed of Dhu al-Hijjah. When they had circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Make it an umrah.\" On the day of al-Tarwiyah, they proclaimed the talbiyah for hajj. On the day of sacrifice, they circumambulated the House but did not perform sa'y between al-Safa and al-Marwah. He did not mention the story of Suraqah b. Malik."],[6464,"The Prophet (along with his companions) reached Mecca in the morning of the fourth of Dhul-Hijja assuming Ihram for Hajj only. So when we arrived at Mecca, the Prophet ﷺ ordered us to change our intentions of the Ihram for ʿUmra and that we could finish our Ihram after performing the ʿUmra and could go to our wives (for sexual intercourse). The people began talking about that. Jabir said surprisingly, \"Shall we go to Mina while semen is dribbling from our male organs?\" Jabir moved his hand while saying so. When this news reached the Prophet ﷺ he delivered a sermon and said, \"I have been informed that some peoples were saying so and so; By Allah I fear Allah more than you do, and am more obedient to Him than you. If I had known what I know now, I would not have brought the Hadi (sacrifice) with me and had the Hadi not been with me, I would have finished the Ihram.\" At that Suraqa bin Malik stood up and asked \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Is this permission for us only or is it forever?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It is forever.\" In the meantime ʿAli bin Abu Talib came from Yemen and was saying Labbaik for what the Prophet ﷺ has intended. (According to another man, ʿAli was saying Labbaik for Hajj similar to Messenger of Allah ﷺ's). The Prophet ﷺ told him to keep on the Ihram and let him share the Hadi with him. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2505)"],[6465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram, and we entered ihram with him for hajj exclusively, until we arrived in Makkah on the morning of the fourth of Dhu al-Hijjah. We circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered whoever among us had not driven a sacrificial animal to exit ihram. He did not firmly command concerning the matter of women. Jabir said, We said, He left us until when there remained between us and Arafah only five nights, he ordered us to exit ihram, so that we would go to Arafat while pre-seminal fluid dripped from our private parts, but he himself did not exit ihram. The Messenger of God ﷺ had driven the sacrificial animal. Our words reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he stood up to preach to the people, praised God and extolled Him, then mentioned what had reached him of their words, and said, \"You know that I am the most God-fearing of you toward God Almighty, the most truthful, and the most righteous. Had I not driven the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. Had I known earlier what I came to know later, I would not have offered the sacrificial animal.\" Jabir b. Abd Allah said, We heard and obeyed, so we exited ihram. Al-Layth said, He means the mut'ah. Al-Layth did not mention the story of Suraqah b. Malik."],[6466,"We arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Makkah on the morning of the fourth day, and he ordered us to exit the state of consecration. We said, 'Which kind of exiting, O Prophet of God?' He said, 'Exit the state completely.' We said, 'We shall go to Mina in the morning while our private parts are dripping semen.' He said, 'Exit the state completely, for if I had known at the beginning of my affair what I came to know at its end, I would have done the same as you are doing.' So we exited the state and went to our women. Ibn ʿUyaynah did not mention the story of Surāqah b. Mālik."],[6467,"The Prophet ﷺ announced the Hajj among us. He departed, and when we reached the mosque near the tree, he dismounted and we dismounted. Then he mounted, and we waited until he mounted. When we arrived in Makkah, he circumambulated the Kaʿbah and we circumambulated with him, and he prayed two units in which he recited: 'Say, O disbelievers' and 'Say, He is God, the One.' Then we performed the going between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. When we were at al-Marwah, he said, 'Whoever has not brought a sacrificial animal should exit the state of consecration.' We said, 'O Messenger of God, we intended Hajj.' He said, 'Hajj has been merged into ʿUmrah.' So we had relations with women and applied perfume. When we arrived, we were four days away from going to Mina, and we said, 'We will go to Mina with our private parts dripping from contact with our women?' Surāqah b. Mālik stood up and said, 'Inform us, O Messenger of God—are we like a people who were only born today?' He said, 'Hajj has been merged into ʿUmrah.' He said, 'For us or forever?' He said, 'No, rather forever.'"],[6468,"We arrived declaring the intention for Hajj, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us to make it an ʿUmrah and exit the state of consecration. He had a sacrificial animal with him, so he could not make it an ʿUmrah. Abū Bishr did not mention in his hadith the story of Surāqah b. Mālik."],[6469,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Makkah during the Farewell Pilgrimage, he said to his Companions, 'With what did you declare your intention?' Among them were those who said 'with Hajj,' those who said 'with ʿUmrah,' and those who said 'with what you declared, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Then all of you exit the state of consecration except those who have brought a sacrificial animal. If I had known at the beginning of my affair what I came to know at its end, I would not have brought a sacrificial animal, so that I might be in the state of having exited consecration along with you.' He had brought one hundred camels to garland them. Muḥammad b. Salamah did not mention the story of Surāqah."],[6470,"When I arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ on his Pilgrimage, he asked the people, 'With what have you declared your intention?' Some people said, 'We have declared intention for Hajj.' Others said, 'We have arrived as those performing tamattuʿ.' Others said, 'We have declared intention with your declaration, O Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever has arrived and has not brought a sacrificial animal should exit the state of consecration. For if I had known at the beginning of my affair what I came to know at its end, I would not have brought a sacrificial animal, so that I might be in the state of having exited consecration.' Surāqah b. Mālik said to him, 'O Messenger of God ﷺ, is this ʿUmrah of ours for this year of ours or forever?' He said, 'No, rather forever.'"],[6471,"O Messenger of God, is our ʿUmrah for us specifically or forever? He said, 'No, rather forever.'"],[6472,"We arrived with the Messenger of God ﷺ intending nothing but Hajj. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered anyone who did not have a sacrificial animal to make it an ʿUmrah. That was hard on the people. Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allah had a sacrificial animal with him, and ʿAlī ؓ arrived from Yemen. The Messenger of God ﷺ asked him, 'With what did you declare your intention?' He said, 'With what you declared.' The Prophet ﷺ had a sacrificial animal with him, one hundred sacrificial animals. Surāqah said, 'O Messenger of God, is this Hajj of ours for this year of ours or forever?' He said, 'No, rather forever.'"],[6473,"We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ when five days remained of Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and we entered Makkah when four days had passed of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. Surāqah b. Mālik b. Juʿshum said, 'O Messenger of God, is this tamattuʿ for us specifically or forever?' He said, 'No, rather forever. ʿUmrah has been merged into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[6474,"We declared intention for pilgrimage with the Prophet ﷺ and arrived in Makkah when four days had passed of Dhū al-Ḥijjah. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered us to exit the state of consecration and make it an ʿUmrah. We exited the state completely and circumambulated the House and went between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah. Then on the Day of Tarwiyah he ordered us, and we declared intention for Hajj. Some of us said to others, 'We left our land, and when there were only four days between us and Mina, we are going out while our private parts are dripping semen?' That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, 'Do you suspect me, while I am the trusted one of the people of heaven and the people of earth? If I had known at the beginning of my affair what I came to know at its end, the sacrificial animals would have come only from Makkah.' He did not mention the story of Surāqah."],[6475,"O Messenger of God, is the ʿUmrah for this year of ours or forever? He said, 'No, rather forever.'"],[6476,"I said: O Messenger of God, shall we act upon what the pen has already dried with and the decrees have already unfolded, or upon some future matter? He said: \"O Suraqah, act upon what the pen has dried with and the decrees have unfolded, for each is facilitated.\""],[6477,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Suraqah, shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire?\" He said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"As for the people of the Fire, they are every rough, arrogant, boastful, and haughty person. As for the people of Paradise, they are the weak and the oppressed.\""],[6478,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[6479,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not guide you to the best charity? Your daughter who is returned to you, and she has no provider other than you.\""],[6480,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Shall I not inform you of the greatest charity? Indeed, among the greatest charity in reward is your daughter who is returned to you, and she has no provider other than you.\""],[6481,"He said: O Messenger of God, shall we act upon something that has already been decreed, or shall we begin the action anew? He said: \"Rather, upon an action that has already been decreed.\" So he said: O Messenger of God, then what is the point of action? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Each is facilitated for what he was created for.\" He said: O Messenger of God, now I strive, now I strive."],[6482,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed the Hajj, Suraqah b. Malik stood up to him and said: O Messenger of God, do for us what you would do for people as if they were born today. When they came to the House, he commanded them, and they circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he stood in the upper part of the valley and addressed them, saying: \"The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6483,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to deliver a speech in this valley, and said: ‘Lo! ‘Umrah has been included in Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2977)"],[6484,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ during the illness in which God took his soul, and I asked him, and I did not ask him about anything except that he informed me of it, until I remembered something that night, among what I remembered. He said: Among what I asked him about was that I said to him: What do you think of a man who fills his water trough, and stray camels and lost animals come to it - does he have reward in giving them water? He said: \"For every thirsty liver there is reward.\""],[6485,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a lost animal that comes to his water trough - does he have reward in it if he satisfies its thirst? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Yes, in every living creature with a thirsty liver there is reward.\""],[6486,"He informed him that he heard a thief saying, \"The disbelieving messengers of the Quraysh came to us, demanding that we pay a ransom for killing or capturing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr. While I was sitting in a gathering of my people from the tribe of Banu Mudlij, a man from among them came and stood in front of us. He said, 'O Surahqa, I have seen a group of black camels on the coast, and I believe it is Muhammad and his companions.' Surahqa said, 'I knew that it was them, so I said that it wasn't them, but it was so-and-so and so-and-so, a gang of bandits who had fled.' Then, I didn't stay in the gathering for more than an hour before I got up, entered my house, and told my slave girl to bring out my horse, which was being kept behind a hill. I took my spear and went out of the house, planting the spear in the ground. I lowered the spear until I reached my horse, mounted it, and approached them slowly. When I got closer to them, I heard the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , who was not turning back, while Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) kept looking back. My horse stumbled, and I got off it. I went towards my camel to take out my arrows, and I swore by them, 'Will they harm me or not?' The one I hated the most not to harm me came out, so I mounted my horse again, raised my arrows, and approached them until, when I approached them, I heard the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He did not turn back, but Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) moved his hands and my horse sank into the ground until its knees were visible. I got off it, scolded it, and it got up, but its hands were still stuck. When it finally stood up, I saw two shining spots from its tracks in the sky like smoke. Ma'mar said, 'I asked Abu 'Amr ibn al-'Ala', 'What are the shining spots?' He remained silent for a while and then said, 'That is smoke without fire.' Ma'mar said that az-Zuhri said about his statement, 'So I swore by my arrows, and the one I hated the most not to harm me came out. I called them with the guarantee, so they stood still. I mounted my horse until I reached them, and I had it in my mind, when I met them, what I had in mind when I met them after they escaped from me.' I said to him, 'Your people have put a ransom on you, and I informed them about their journey and what people want from them, and I offered them supplies and provisions, but they did not agree to anything and only asked me to keep their presence a secret.' So, I asked him to write me a security document that I could trust. He ordered 'Amir bin Fuhayra to write the document for me on a piece of leather, and then he left.\""],[6487,"He informed him that when the Messenger of God ﷺ left Makkah as an emigrant to Madinah, Quraysh set a reward of one hundred camels for whoever brought him back to them. He said: While I was sitting in the gathering of my people, a man from among us came and said: By God, I have just seen a group of three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad. He said: I signaled to him to be quiet and said: They are only the sons of so-and-so, looking for a lost camel of theirs. He said: Perhaps; then he fell silent. I remained for a little while, then I got up and ordered my horse to be brought to the bottom of the valley. I took out my weapons from behind my room, then I took my divination arrows which I used for seeking omens. Then I put on my armor, then I took out my arrows and cast them, and the one I disliked came out - it does not harm him. I had been hoping to capture him and take the hundred camels. So I rode in pursuit of them. While my horse was galloping with me, it stumbled and I fell off. I took out my arrows and cast them, and the arrow I disliked came out - it does not harm him. But I refused to do anything but continue following him, so I mounted again. When the group appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me, and its forelegs sank into the ground, and I fell off. Then it pulled out its leg, and smoke followed it like thick dust. I knew that he had been protected from me and that he would prevail. So I called out to them: \"Wait for me, for by God, I will not trouble you, and nothing you dislike will come from me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Tell him: What does he seek?\" I said: \"Write for me a document between me and you as a sign.\" He said: \"Write, O Abu Bakr.\" He said: So he wrote for me, then he threw it to me, and I returned. I kept silent and did not mention anything of what had happened, until God granted His Messenger victory over Makkah and he finished with the people of Hunayn. Then I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the document he had written for me. He said: While I was heading toward him, I entered amidst a battalion of the Ansar, and they began to strike me with their spears and say: \"Get away, get away.\" When I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon his she-camel, I looked at his shins in the stirrup as if they were the trunk of a palm tree. I reached out my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of God, this is your document. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A day of fulfillment and kindness, come closer.\" Then I embraced Islam."],[6488,"He informed him that when the Messenger of God ﷺ left Makkah as an emigrant to Madinah, Quraysh offered a hundred she-camels to whoever brought him back. He said: While I was sitting in the assembly of my people, a man from among us came and said: By God, I have just seen three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad. He said: I gestured to him to be quiet and said: They are only the sons of so-and-so following a stray animal of theirs. He said: Perhaps. Then he fell silent. I remained for a little while, then I got up and ordered that my horse be led to the bottom of the valley. I took out my weapons from behind my room, then took my divining arrows with which I sought omens, then put on my armor. Then I brought out my divining arrows and drew omens with them, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. I had been hoping to bring him back and take the hundred she-camels. So I mounted and followed their tracks. While my horse was galloping with me, it stumbled and I fell off. I took out my divining arrows and drew omens, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. But I refused anything except to follow him. I mounted, and when the group appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me and its forelegs sank into the ground, and I fell. It pulled out its foreleg, and there followed it smoke like dust. Then I knew that he had been protected from me and that he would prevail. So I called out to them: Wait for me, for by God I will not cause you any harm, and nothing you dislike will come from me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Ask him what he wants. I said: Write for me a document between me and you as a sign. He said: Write, O Abu Bakr. He said: So he wrote for me, then threw it to me. I returned and kept silent, and did not mention anything of what had happened until God granted His Messenger victory over Makkah and he had finished with the people of Hunayn. Then I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the document he had written for me. While I was making for him, I entered among a battalion of the Ansar's battalions, and they began prodding me with their spears, saying: Away with you, away with you, until I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ on his she-camel. I looked at his shins in the stirrup as if they were a palm pith. I stretched out my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of God, this is your document. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A day of fulfillment and kindness; come near. So I became a Muslim."],[6489,"From 'Urwah: In naming those who were martyred on the day of Mu'tah among the Muslims, then among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Najjar, then among Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar: Suraqah b. 'Amr b. 'Atiyyah b. Khansa'."],[6490,"From 'Urwah: In naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Ansar, from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Suraqah b. al-Hubab."],[6491,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: In naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Ansar: Suraqah b. al-Hubab b. 'Adi b. al-'Ajlan."],[6492,"From Habbah and Sawa', the two sons of Khalid, who said: We entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was working on something and it tired him. He said: Do not despair of provision as long as your heads shake, for a person is born of his mother red, with no shell upon him, then God provides for him."],[6493,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever is given and is thankful, is tried and is patient, wrongs and seeks forgiveness, and is wronged and forgives. Then he fell silent. They said: O Messenger of God, what is for him? He said: Those will have security, and they are guided."],[6494,"My family sent with me a bowl of milk and butter to their gods. I went with it, but I was afraid to eat any of it. I set it down when a dog came, drank the milk, ate the butter, and urinated on the idol."],[6495,"He used to be a partner of the Messenger of God ﷺ before Islam in trade. When the day of the conquest came, he came to him and he said, \"Welcome to my brother and my partner. He does not contend nor dispute. O Sa'ib, you used to do deeds in the pre-Islamic times that were not accepted from you, and today they are accepted from you.\" He had a past and connections."],[6496,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"You were my partner in the pre-Islamic period, and you were the best partner: you did not contend nor dispute.\""],[6497,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they began to praise me and mention me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I know him best among you.\" He said, \"You have spoken truly, by my father and mother. You were my partner, and what an excellent partner you were: you did not contend nor dispute.\""],[6498,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When one of you enters the lavatory, let him wipe with three stones.\""],[6499,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated, he raised his palms toward his face."],[6500,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr b. Hazm, from 'Abd al-Malik b. Abi Bakr b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith, from Khallad b. al-Sa'ib al-Ansari, from his father, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Gabriel ﷺ came to me and commanded me to command my companions—or those with me—to raise their voices with the talbiyah or with the ihlaal. And he said: It is among the rites of Hajj."],[6501,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Gabriel ﷺ came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with the ihlaal, for it is among the rites of Hajj. Sufyan said: Ibn Jurayj had concealed a hadith from me, and when 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr came to us, I did not inform him. When he departed to Madinah, I narrated it to him, and he said to me, \"O one-eyed one, you hide hadiths from us; when their people have gone away, you inform us of them. I will not narrate it from you.\" So he wrote to 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr, and 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr wrote back to him with it. Ibn Jurayj used to narrate it in his books: 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr wrote to me."],[6502,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Gabriel ﷺ came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with the ihlaal—or he said with the talbiyah."],[6503,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Gabriel ﷺ came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah or the ihlaal—I do not know which of us, I or 'Abd al-Malik, was uncertain about ihlaal and talbiyah."],[6504,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, God will frighten him, and upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor voluntary acts will be accepted from him.\""],[6505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[6506,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “O Allah, whoever wrongs the people of Madinah and frightens them, frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory deed.”"],[6507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah will frighten him on the Day of Resurrection, curse him, and be angry with him, and He will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory deed.”"],[6508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Jibril ﷺ came and said: “O Muhammad, be one who raises his voice with the talbiyah and who sheds sacrificial blood,” meaning by al-ʿajj the talbiyah and by al-thajj the blood."],[6509,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “None of you should take his companion's belongings in jest or in earnest, and if any of you takes his companion's staff, he should return it to him.”"],[6510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only one muezzin; no one else called the adhan for him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the pulpit on Friday, he called the adhan at the door of the mosque, and when he descended, he made the iqamah. Then Abu Bakr ؓ did likewise, then ʿUmar ؓ did likewise, until the time of ʿUthman. When the people became numerous, he ordered the first call to be made in the market on a house of his called al-Zawra'. The adhan was called for him on it, and when ʿUthman ؓ sat on the pulpit, his muezzin called the first adhan, and when he descended, he made the iqamah."],[6511,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he had a muezzin, and when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the pulpit, he called the adhan, and when he descended, he made the iqamah. That was the practice in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and the time of Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ. But when it was the time of ʿUthman ؓ, the people had spread out and become numerous, so he ordered a muezzin to call the adhan at al-Zawra' before he came out, informing the people that Friday prayer had arrived."],[6512,"The first adhan on Friday during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the pulpit: he would call the adhan, and when he descended, he would make the iqamah. That was the practice in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and the time of Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ. But when it was the time of ʿUthman ؓ, the people had spread out and become numerous, so he ordered a muezzin to call the adhan at al-Zawra' before he came out."],[6513,"The call to prayer in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar ؓ was at the pulpit, and the first one to introduce the second call was ʿUthman ؓ."],[6514,"The call to prayer on Friday originally began when the imam sat down and when the prayer was about to begin, in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar ؓ. But when it was the time of ʿUthman ؓ and the people became numerous, he added the third call at al-Zawra'."],[6515,"The first call to prayer used to be when the imam sat on the pulpit on the day of Jumu'ah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar. When Uthman became caliph and the people became numerous, Uthman b. Affan commanded on the day of Jumu'ah a third call to prayer, and it was given at al-Zawra'."],[6516,"It was Uthman who commanded the third call to prayer on the day of Jumu'ah when the people of Madinah became numerous, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only one mu'adhdhin. The call to prayer on the day of Jumu'ah was indeed when the imam sat down."],[6517,"The first call to prayer used to be when the imam sat on the pulpit on the day of Jumu'ah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ."],[6518,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only one mu'adhdhin. The call to prayer on the day of Jumu'ah used to be when the imam sat down."],[6519,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us. And Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me. They said: Sufyan b. Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, who said: \"I was among the boys who went out to Thaniyyat al-Wada' to meet the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[6520,"He informed him that Shurayh al-Hadrami was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"That is a man who does not use the Qur'an as a pillow.\""],[6521,"The Prophet ﷺ, when Makhramah b. Shurayh al-Hadrami was mentioned in his presence, said: \"That is a man who does not use the Qur'an as a pillow.\""],[6522,"No one narrated religious stories during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar, until the first one to narrate was Tamim al-Dari. He sought permission from Umar ؓ, and he permitted him, so he narrated while standing."],[6523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hamah.\""],[6524,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Ham.\""],[6525,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Ham.\""],[6526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the jizyah from the Magians of Hajar, and Umar b. al-Khattab took it from the Magians of Persia, and Uthman ؓ took it from the Berbers."],[6527,"The Prophet ﷺ used to deliver two sermons on Friday, sitting between them."],[6528,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ did not appoint a judge, and the first to appoint a judge was Umar ؓ. He said to him: \"Return the people to me [even] in the matter of a dirham or two dirhams.\""],[6529,"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the hand of Abu Bakr ؓ until he died, then in the hand of Umar until he died, then in the hand of Uthman until it fell into the well of Aris."],[6530,"The blood money at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one hundred camels, of four ages: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadha'ah, twenty-five bint labun, and twenty-five bint makhad. Then when Umar ؓ came and established the garrison towns, Umar said: \"Not all people can find camels, so appraise the camels at an uqiyyah each.\" Thus it became four thousand dirhams. Then camels became expensive, and Umar ؓ said: \"Appraise the camels.\" So the camels were appraised at an uqiyyah and a half, and it became six thousand dirhams. Then camels became expensive, and Umar ؓ said: \"Appraise the camels.\" So they were appraised at two uqiyyahs, and it became eight thousand dirhams. Then camels became expensive, and Umar ؓ said: \"Appraise the camels.\" So they were appraised at three awaq, and it became twelve thousand. He then made it incumbent upon the people of silver [to pay] twelve thousand, upon the people of camels one hundred camels, upon the people of gold one thousand dinars, upon the people of fine garments two hundred hullas, each hulla worth five dinars, upon the people of sheep one thousand ewes, upon the people of goats one thousand she-goats, and upon cattle two hundred cows."],[6531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed the fay' which Allah granted at Hunayn from the spoils of Hawazin, and he spread the distribution among the people of Makkah, both Quraysh and others. The Ansar became angry. When the Prophet ﷺ heard of that, he came to them in their dwellings and said: \"Whoever is here but is not of the Ansar, let him go out to his mount.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the tashahhud and praised Allah ﷻ, then said: \"O company of the Ansar, word of your talk concerning these spoils has reached me, which I favored to certain people to win their hearts to Islam, that perhaps they may bear witness after today, for Allah has entered Islam into their hearts.\" He then said: \"O company of the Ansar, did Allah not bestow upon you faith and single you out for honor and name you with the best of names: Ansar Allah and Ansar of His Messenger? Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar. If the people were to take one valley and you another, I would take your valley. Are you not pleased that the people go with these spoils—sheep, cattle, and camels—while you go with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" When the Ansar heard the words of the Prophet ﷺ, they said: \"We are pleased.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Answer me regarding what I have said.\" The Ansar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you found us in darkness and Allah brought us out through you to light; you found us on the brink of a pit of fire and Allah saved us through you; you found us astray and Allah guided us through you. We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet. So do, O Messenger of Allah, whatever you will in the broadest of permission.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By Allah, had you answered me with other than this statement, I would have said you spoke truthfully. Had you said: 'Did you not come to us as a fugitive and we sheltered you, as one denied and we believed you, as one forsaken and we supported you, and we accepted what the people rejected?' Had you said this, you would have spoken truthfully.\" The Ansar said: \"Rather to Allah and His Messenger belong the favor and grace upon us and upon others.\" Then they wept, and their weeping grew intense, and the Prophet ﷺ wept with them and was pleased with them. And they were by what he said to them more delighted and more excellent in their sight than all wealth."],[6532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encountered some slave girls singing, saying: \"You greet us, we greet you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped, then called them and said: \"Do not say that, but say: 'May He give us life and you.'\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you permit people to do this?\" He said: \"Yes, for it is marriage, not fornication. Proclaim the marriage.\""],[6533,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed away, his son Tahir began to shed tears. It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you cry?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Indeed, the eye sheds tears, and indeed, tears overcome, and indeed, the heart feels sadness, but we do not disobey Allah.\""],[6534,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined. How can we know what is in our hearts of that arrogance, and where is it?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears wool, or milks a sheep, or eats with what his right hand possesses, then there is not in his heart, if Allah wills, arrogance.\""],[6535,"The Prophet ﷺ doubled two coats of mail on the day of Uhud."],[6536,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: It is sufficient for a person to supplicate, saying: \"O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and admit me to Paradise.\""],[6537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My community will remain upon the fitrah as long as they pray Maghrib before the stars appear.\""],[6538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever drinks an intoxicant, his prayer will not be accepted by Allah for forty days.\""],[6539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no person who sits in a gathering and says when he wants to rise: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You' except that he is forgiven for what occurred in that gathering.\" So I narrated this hadith to Yazid b. Khusayfah, and he said: \"Thus did al-Sa'ib b. Yazid narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6540,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I was favored over the prophets with five: I was sent to all people, my intercession was stored up for my community, I was granted victory by awe for a month ahead of me and a month behind me, the earth was made a place of prostration and a means of purification for me, and spoils of war were made lawful for me, and they were not lawful for anyone before me.”"],[6541,"“I fell ill during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I was carried to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I saw him treating me with the Qurʾān and blowing on me with it.” The wording is that of Hishām b. ʿAmmār."],[6542,"I heard al-Sāʾib b. Yazīd al-Kindī, the nephew of al-Namir, say: “The prayer was prescribed as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs; then it was increased in the prayer of settled residence, while the prayer of travel was left as it was.”"],[6543,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from Saʿd b. Saʿīd al-Anṣārī, from al-Sāʾib b. Yazīd, who said: “The prayer was prescribed as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs; then it was increased in the prayer of settled residence, while the prayer of travel was left as it was.”"],[6544,"“I performed the Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage when I was seven years old.”"],[6545,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[6546,"My maternal aunt took me to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my sister’s son is in pain.” The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, and I drank his leftover ablution water. Then I stood behind his back and saw the seal between his shoulder blades, like the button of a bridal canopy."],[6547,"\"He (Saib ibn Yazid) was the measurement during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , equaling one and a third of your measurement today. It increased during the time of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz. Saib said, 'I performed Hajj during the time of the Prophet ﷺ while I was still a young boy.'\""],[6548,"My maternal aunt took me to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my sister’s son is unwell.” He wiped my head and supplicated for blessing for me. Then he performed ablution, and I drank from his leftover ablution water. Then I stood behind his back and looked at the seal between his shoulder blades, like the button of a bridal canopy."],[6549,"“We were in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and Abū Bakr, and part of the time of ʿUmar ؓ, we did not flog for wine,” until they became audacious with it, and ʿUmar ؓ flogged eighty. They did not stop, so ʿUmar ؓ made it eighty and said, “When he gets drunk, he slanders and speaks falsehood.”"],[6550,"A man was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ. They said, “O Messenger of God, this man stole a camel’s saddlecloth, or a riding animal’s saddlecloth.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I do not think he did it.” Then they said, “O Messenger of God, this man stole.” He said, “I do not think he did it,” until he testified against himself several times. Then he said, “Take him and cut off his hand, then bring him to me.” So they cut off his hand, then brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said, “Woe to you, repent to God.” He said, “I repent to God.” He said, “O God, turn to him in mercy.”"],[6551,"“This man has spoiled his face. By God, that is not the mark that God has named. I have prostrated on my face for eighty years, and prostration has not left a trace between my eyes.”"],[6552,"I heard al-Sa'ib b. Yazid say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah from the expedition of Tabuk, the people went out to meet him, and the women and children went out. Al-Sa'ib said: I was among those who met him with the children until we met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Thaniyyat al-Wada'."],[6553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Excellent suhur is dates.”"],[6554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Excellent suhur is dates.”"],[6555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Excellent condiment is vinegar.”"],[6556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among illicit earnings are the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper.”"],[6557,"He is called Sulayk, from Ghatafan, while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon standing. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “O Sulayk, stand and pray two brief rak'ahs.”"],[6558,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Pray two rak'ahs, and make them brief.”"],[6559,"Sulayk came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and he sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, making them brief."],[6560,"He heard Jabir b. 'Abd Allah say: A man came while the Prophet ﷺ was on the minbar on Friday delivering the sermon. He said to him, “Have you prayed two rak'ahs?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then pray them.”"],[6561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while he was delivering the sermon: “When one of you comes on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon or has already come out, let him pray two rak'ahs.”"],[6562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon when a man entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Have you prayed?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then pray.” He said, so he prayed two rak'ahs."],[6563,"A man from Ghatafan came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Have you prayed?” He said, “No.” He said, “Prostrate two prostrations and make them light.”"],[6564,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was on the minbar delivering the Friday sermon, standing. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Have you prayed?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then pray two rak'ahs.”"],[6565,"A man entered while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to pray two rak'ahs."],[6566,"A man came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He said, “Have you prayed?” He said, “No.” He said, “Stand and pray.”"],[6567,"A man came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was addressing the people. He said, “Have you prayed, O so-and-so?” He said, “No.” He said, “Stand and pray.”"],[6568,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs."],[6569,"He heard Jabir b. 'Abd Allah say: Sulayk b. 'Amr al-Ghatafani entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was on the minbar delivering the Friday sermon, standing. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Have you prayed?” He said, “No.” He said, “Then pray two rak'ahs.”"],[6570,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon on the pulpit, and he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, keeping them brief."],[6571,"Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, keeping them brief, and he said: \"When one of you comes while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rak'ahs and keep them brief.\""],[6572,"The Prophet ﷺ looked over the people of the well and said: \"O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised to be true?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do they hear?\" He said: \"They hear as you hear, but they do not respond.\""],[6573,"A man said to me: \"Shall I direct you to a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He pointed to a man beside him. I said: \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said: \"I am Surraq.\" I said: \"Glory be to Allah! It is not fitting that you be called by this name while you are a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Surraq, and I will never abandon that.\" I said: \"Why did he name you Surraq?\" He said: \"A man from the desert came with two camels of his to sell them. I bought them from him and said to him: 'Go, so that I can pay you.' I entered my house and spent the price of the two camels on my needs, and I hid myself until I thought that the Bedouin had left. Then I went out, and there was the Bedouin still waiting. He seized me and brought me before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he told him the story. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What made you do what you did?' I said: 'I spent their price on my needs, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Then pay him.' I said: 'I do not have it.' He said: 'You are Surraq. Take him, O Bedouin, and sell him until you recover your right.' The people began to bargain for me, and he would turn to them and say: 'What do you want?' They said: 'We want to ransom him from you.' He said: 'By Allah, none of you is more in need of Allah than I am. Go, for I have freed you.'\""],[6574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him remember his calamity in me, for it is the greatest of calamities to him.\""],[6575,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat or the hollow of the neck?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6576,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat or the hollow of the neck?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6577,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6578,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the 'atirah and he deemed it good."],[6579,"I was in a district of Makkah, and a Muslim man came while I was among my sheep. I said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah.\" I said, \"Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah and greetings. What do you want?\" He said, \"I want the zakat of your sheep.\" He said, \"So I brought him a ewe that had just given birth. When he looked at it, he said, 'Our due is not in this.' I said, 'Then in what is your due?' He said, 'In the thaniyyah and the jadha'ah that is fleshy.'\""],[6580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases. The adhan is: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah. And the iqamah is in pairs."],[6581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhan and said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah. Then he would go back and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah."],[6582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases."],[6583,"He was an orphan in the care of Abu Mahdhurah, who equipped him for Syria. He said: I said to Abu Mahdhurah, \"I am going to Syria, and I fear that I will be asked about your adhan.\" So he informed me that Abu Mahdhurah told him: He said: I went out with a group, and we were on part of the road when the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called to prayer in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We heard the voice of the mu'adhdhin while we were near him, and we shouted, imitating him, so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might hear the voice. He sent for us, and we stood before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Which of you is the one whose voice I heard raised?\" The people all pointed to me, and they were truthful. He sent them all away and detained me. He said, \"Get up and call the adhan for prayer.\" I got up, and nothing was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what he commanded me. I stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he himself dictated the adhan to me. He said: Say: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah.\" Then he said to me, \"Go back and extend your voice, and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah.\" Then he called me when I had finished the adhan and gave me a purse containing some silver. Then he placed his hand on the forelock of Abu Mahdhurah, then passed it over his face from the front, then over his liver, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the purse of Abu Mahdhurah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah bless you and bless upon you.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, command me to call the adhan in Makkah.\" He said, \"I have already done so.\" Every feeling of dislike in my heart toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ vanished, and all of it turned into love for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to 'Attab b. Asid, the governor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and called the adhan for prayer with him by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated the adhan to me word by word: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah.\""],[6585,"Abu Mahdhurah said: I went out with ten youths with the Prophet ﷺ to Hunayn, and they were the most hateful people to us. They called the adhan, and we stood mocking them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Bring me these youths.\" Then he said, \"Call the adhan.\" They called the adhan, and I was the last of them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes, this is the one whose voice I heard. Go and call the adhan for the people of Makkah, and tell 'Attab b. Asid that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the adhan for the people of Makkah.\" He wiped his forelock and said: Say: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah twice; then go back and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah twice; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah twice; Hayya 'ala al-salah twice; Hayya 'ala al-falah twice; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah. And when you call the adhan for the first prayer of the morning, say: Al-salahu khayrun mina al-nawm, al-salahu khayrun mina al-nawm. And when you pronounce the iqamah, say twice: Qad qamat al-salah. Did you hear?\" Abu Mahdhurah did not cut his forelock or comb it because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had wiped over it. Abu al-Qasim 'Uthman, from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith, is 'Uthman b. al-Sa'ib, the mawla of Banu Jumah."],[6586,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the Sunnah of the call to prayer. He wiped the front of his head and said: You say: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, raising your voice with it. Then you say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, lowering your voice with it. Then you raise your voice with the testimony, then you say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to success, Hasten to success. If it is the dawn prayer, you say: Prayer is better than sleep, Prayer is better than sleep. Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is no deity except Allah."],[6587,"Tell me about your father's call to prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He would begin and say the takbir, then say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to the prayer, once each. Then he would return, saying: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, until he came to the end of the call to prayer: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is no deity except Allah."],[6588,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the water supply to the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib and the custody of the Ka'bah to the Banu 'Abd al-Dar, and made the call to prayer for us and our clients.\""],[6589,"I used to give the call to prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the dawn prayer, and when I said in the first call to prayer, 'Hasten to success,' I would say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep."],[6590,"I heard Abu Mahdhura saying: I was a young boy, and I gave the call to prayer before the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. When I reached 'Hasten to the prayer, hasten to success,' the Prophet ﷺ said to me: Add to it: Prayer is better than sleep."],[6591,"I asked Abu Mahdhura: How did you give the call to prayer for the Prophet ﷺ? What did you make the end of your call to prayer? He said: I used to say the phrases of the call to prayer twice and the phrases of the iqamah twice, and I made the end of my call to prayer: there is no deity except Allah."],[6592,"\"The final words of the Adhan are: 'Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illallah (Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is none worthy of worship except Allah.)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 649)"],[6593,"\"There is no deity except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\""],[6594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The muezzins are the trustees of the Muslims over their breaking the fast and their pre-dawn meal.\""],[6595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"When you give the call to prayer for Maghrib, let it descend with the sun, descending quickly.\""],[6596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"At sunset, watch for it with the sun.\""],[6597,"Abu Mahdhura had a forelock at the front of his head; when he sat, he would let it down and it would reach the ground. They said to him: Why don't you shave it? He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped it with his hand, and I will not shave it until I die.\" So he did not shave it until he died."],[6598,"I saw Abu Mahdhura and he had hair, so I said to him: Why don't you cut your hair? He said: \"I would not cut hair that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed his hand over.\""],[6599,"That Umm Samurah bint Jundub died and her husband died and left behind her son Samurah, and she was a beautiful woman. She came to the city and she was proposed to. She said, \"I will not marry a man except a man who will take care of the expenses of her son Samurah until he comes of age.\" So a man from the Ansar married her on that condition, and she lived with him among the Ansar."],[6600,"That the wife of Samurah b. Jundub lost her husband, and he left his son Samurah. She was a beautiful woman, so she came to Madinah and was sought in marriage. She began to say, “I will not marry any man except a man who will guarantee her the maintenance of her son Samurah until he reaches maturity.” So a man from the Ansar married her on that condition, and she was with him among the Ansar."],[6601,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so? Indeed, your companion is being held at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owes.”"],[6602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the prayers, then said, “Who is here from the clan of so-and-so? Indeed, your companion has been detained from Paradise because of a debt he owed. So either ransom him from the punishment of Allah or surrender him [to it].”"],[6603,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is there anyone here from Banu al-Najjar?” He called out three times and no one answered him. Then a man answered him, so he said, “Did you hear my call?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, so-and-so who died among you has been detained from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, ransom him, and if you wish, surrender him to the punishment of Allah.”"],[6604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and when he finished, he said, “Is there anyone here from Banu al-Najjar?” He called out three times, and a man answered him on the third. He said, “Did you hear my call?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, your companion so-and-so has been detained from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, ransom him from the punishment of Allah, and if you wish, surrender him.”"],[6605,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the people and said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so?” The people remained silent, and whenever he began something with them they would remain silent. Then he said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so?” A man from the people said, “This is so-and-so.” He said, “Indeed, your companion is being held short of Paradise because of his debt.” A man from the people said, “His debt is upon me.”"],[6606,"“From the Prophet ﷺ that he addressed the people and forbade [drinking from] gourds and vessels smeared with pitch.”"],[6607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wear these white garments and shroud your dead in them, for they are purer and better.”"],[6608,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wear white, for indeed it is very pure and cleaner, and shroud your dead in it.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2810)"],[6609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wear white garments, for they are better and purer, and shroud your dead in them.”"],[6610,"“The best of your garments are those which are white, so shroud your dead in them, and wear them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1472)"],[6611,"“A woman died in her postpartum bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed over her and stood at her middle.”"],[6612,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a woman and stood at her middle.”"],[6613,"“A woman died in childbirth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over her and stood at her middle.”"],[6614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Asking is like a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it.”"],[6615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Asking is only scratches with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that he asks a man of authority or in a matter from which he finds no alternative.”"],[6616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “These askings are like a scratching with which one of you scrapes his face, except that a man asks a man of authority or a matter from which he has no alternative.”"],[6617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “These askings are like a scratching with which a man scrapes his face, except that he asks a man of authority or in a matter from which he finds no alternative.”"],[6618,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks a man of authority or in a matter from which there is no alternative.”"],[6619,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks a man of authority or in a matter from which there is no alternative.”"],[6620,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face.”"],[6621,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ‘ids: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6622,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ‘ids: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to “recite in the Friday prayer: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6625,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” in the first, and in the second “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6626,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” in the first, and in the second “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6627,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the Friday prayer: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6628,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from splitting a leather strap between his fingers."],[6629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loses an item and finds it in the possession of a particular man, he has more right to it, and the buyer returns to the seller for the price.”"],[6630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two months do not complete sixty days.”"],[6631,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Two months do not complete sixty days.”"],[6632,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best thing by which you treat yourselves is cupping.\""],[6633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a barber and had him shaved with a razor and a blade. An Arab man from the tribe of Banu Fazara saw this and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why do you let him cut your flesh?\" He ﷺ said, \"Do you not know the benefit and the best thing you can use for treatment?\""],[6634,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he called a cupper and ordered him to cup him. He brought out his cupping horns and applied them to him, then made an incision with the tip of a blade and let the blood flow into a vessel he had. A man from Banu Fazara entered upon him and said, “What is this, O Messenger of Allah? Why do you allow this one to cut your skin?” He said, “This is cupping.” He said, “It is the best treatment people use.”"],[6635,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, interrupting his sermon. He turned to him, and he was to his right, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about lizards?” He said, “A community of the Children of Israel was transformed. Allah knows best into which animals it was transformed.”"],[6636,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “What do you say about lizards?” He said, “A community of the Children of Israel was transformed. Allah knows best which animals were transformed.”"],[6637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved speech to Allah, Exalted is He, is four: ‘There is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, Glory be to Allah, and Praise be to Allah.’ It does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[6638,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The most beloved speech to Allah ﷻ is: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. It does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[6639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not name your boy Yasar, nor Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, for you will say, 'Is he there?' and he will not be, so it will be said, 'No.' They are only four, so do not add to them.”"],[6640,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not name your slave Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, nor Yasar.”"],[6641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from naming our slaves with four names: Nafi', Aflah, Rabah, and Yasar."],[6642,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer during a solar eclipse, and no voice was heard from him.”"],[6643,"One of us said to his companion: “Come with us, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will surely speak to us today about the solar eclipse, concerning his Ummah.” We reached the mosque and found it filled to capacity. That coincided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming out. He came forward and prayed with the people while we were behind him. He stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed with us for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated with us for the longest prostration, and we heard no voice from him. Then in the second rak'ah he did the same, and the clearing of the sun coincided with the sitting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He then finished, praised Allah, extolled Him, bore witness that there is no god but Allah, and bore witness that he is His servant and Messenger. Then he said: “O people, I am only a human messenger. I remind you by Allah: if you know that I have fallen short in conveying any of the messages of my Lord, then tell me, for I have conveyed the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed. And if I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then why do you not tell me?” They said: “We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.” Then he said: “To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and this moon, or the disappearance of stars from their rising places, is due to the death of great men of the earth. They have lied. But they are signs among the signs of Allah by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. I was shown while standing in prayer what you will encounter in this world and the Hereafter. The Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Tahya, an old man of the Ansar who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him and affirms him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and denies him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. The believers will be besieged in Bayt al-Maqdis with a severe siege and pressed with severe pressure.” Al-Aswad b. Qays said: “And I think he said: 'Isa b. Maryam ﷺ will appear among them, and Allah will defeat him and his armies, until the base of a wall and the branch of a tree will call out to the believer, saying: 'Here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him.' That will not happen until you see matters of your own affair growing grave in your souls, until you ask among yourselves: 'Did your Prophet mention anything of this?' And until mountains move from their places. Then upon that comes the seizing, the seizing.'” Ibn al-Mubarak said: “i.e., death.”"],[6644,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “While I and a boy from the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the sun rose and was in the eye of the beholder about a spear or two spears from the horizon, then darkened until it became like a colocynth. One of us said to his companion: 'Come with us to the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ, for by Allah, he will surely speak to us today about the matter of this sun regarding his Ummah.' We went to the mosque and met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he came out to the people. He came forward and prayed. He stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed with us for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated with us for the longest prostration he ever prostrated with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he stood and led us in another rak'ah like it. Then he sat, and his sitting coincided with the clearing of the sun. He said the taslim and turned around, praised Allah and extolled Him. Then he said: 'O people, I remind you by Allah: if you know that I have conveyed the message of my Lord, then tell me. And if you know that I have fallen short in conveying anything of the message of my Lord, then tell me.' They said: 'We bear witness that you have conveyed the message of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.' Then he said: 'To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon and the disappearance of stars from their rising places is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth. They have lied. But they are only signs of Allah by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. By Allah, I saw what you will encounter in the affairs of your world and your Hereafter from the time I stood to pray. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Yahya, an old man of the Ansar who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him and affirms him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and fights him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. He will drive the people to Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be besieged with a severe siege.'” He said: “And I think he said: 'Isa b. Maryam will appear among them and kill him and his armies, until the stone or the base of a wall will call out: O Muslim, or O believer, here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him. That will not happen until you see great matters whose gravity grows in your souls, and you ask among yourselves: Did your Prophet ﷺ mention anything of them to you?' Then he said: 'Immediately after that comes the seizing.'”"],[6645,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “While I and a boy from the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the sun was about two or three spears' length in the eye of the beholders from the horizon, it darkened until it became like a colocynth. One of us said to his companion: 'Come with us to the mosque, for by Allah, the matter of this sun will surely cause the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak to his Ummah.' We went to the mosque and found it packed, that is, full. We met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he came out to the people. He came forward and stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated for the longest prostration he ever prostrated with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then in the second rak'ah he did the same, and the clearing of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak'ah. He said the taslim, then praised Allah and extolled Him, and bore witness that there is no god but He and that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: 'O people, I am only a human messenger. I adjure you by Allah: if you know that I have fallen short in conveying any of the messages of my Lord, then tell me—so that I may convey the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed. And if you know that I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then why do you not tell me?' The people stood and said: 'We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.' Then they fell silent. Then he said: 'To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon and the disappearance of these stars from their rising places is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth. They have lied. But they are only signs among the signs of Allah ﷻ by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. By Allah, I saw from the time I stood to pray what you will encounter in the affairs of your world and your Hereafter. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Tahya, an old man of the Ansar at that time who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him, affirms him, and follows him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and denies him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. He will besiege the Muslims in Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be pressed with severe pressure. Then Allah will destroy him and his armies, until the base of a wall and the root of a tree will say: O believer, or O Muslim, here is a disbeliever, come and kill him. That will not happen until you see great matters whose gravity grows in your souls, then you ask among yourselves: Did your Prophet ﷺ mention anything of them to you? And until mountains move from their places. Then immediately after that comes the seizing.' He closed his fingers and gestured right and left. Then I attended a sermon of Samura in which he mentioned this hadith, and he did not advance a word or delay it from its place.”"],[6646,"“The Prophet ﷺ ruled in favor of the neighbor.”"],[6647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house and the land than anyone else.”"],[6648,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house than anyone else.”"],[6649,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the right of preemption of the house.”"],[6650,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6651,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of the neighbor.”"],[6652,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6653,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6657,"“Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates (his slave) we will mutilate him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2663)"],[6658,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6660,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him; and whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him.”"],[6662,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Dajjal will appear. His left eye is blind, with a thick growth over it. He will heal the born-blind and the leper, bring the dead to life, and say to people: ‘I am your lord.’ Whoever says, ‘You are my lord’ has been tried; and whoever says, ‘My Lord is God’ and remains on that until he dies will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal, and there will be no trial upon him. He will remain on earth as long as God wills, then Jesus son of Mary will come from the west, affirming Muhammad ﷺ, and will kill the Dajjal. Indeed, it is the coming of the Hour.”"],[6663,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from cutting a leather strap between his two fingers."],[6664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every boy is held in pledge for his aqiqah, to be slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, his head shaved, and he is named.”"],[6665,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The neighbor of a house has the greater right to its preemption.”"],[6666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pause twice: when he entered the prayer, and when he finished the recitation. Imran b. Husayn rejected that, so they wrote about it to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and he wrote back to them that Samurah spoke the truth."],[6667,"A man manumitted six slaves of his at the time of death while he had no property other than them, so the Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them and freed two and kept four enslaved."],[6668,"The Prophet ﷺ used to forbid mutilation and urge giving charity."],[6669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that an animal be tied up and shot, and that its flesh be eaten if it was tied up and shot."],[6670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People have not given charity anything like knowledge that is spread.\""],[6671,"\"O Messenger of God, I saw as if a bucket was lowered from the sky. Abu Bakr ؓ came and took hold of its rope, and drank a weak drink. Then Umar ؓ came and took hold of its rope until he was filled. Then Uthman ؓ came and took hold of its rope and drank until he was filled. Then Ali ؓ came and took hold of its rope, but it slipped from him and spilled on him.\""],[6672,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid mutilation and urge charity.\""],[6673,"\"A bowl of tharid was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and placed before the people, and they took turns with it from early morning until noon; people would get up and others would sit down.\" A man said to Samurah, \"Was it replenished?\" Samurah said, \"From what thing are you amazed? It was not replenished except from here,\" and he gestured with his hand toward the sky."],[6674,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among them are those whom the Fire will take up to their ankles, and among them are those whom it will take up to their waist, and among them are those whom it will take up to their collarbone.\""],[6675,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[6676,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Adhere to these white garments; let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them.\" Ibn 'Ulayyah did not mention Abu al-Muhallab."],[6677,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it the next day at its time.\""],[6678,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the children of the polytheists, and he said: \"They are the servants of the people of Paradise.\""],[6679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"I would enter this room, only fearing that there may be wealth in it that I have not spent before I die.\""],[6680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him; and whoever cuts off his nose, we will cut off his nose.”"],[6681,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it suffices him and is good, but whoever performs a full bath, the bath is more virtuous.\""],[6682,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it suffices him and is good, but whoever performs a full bath, the bath is more virtuous.\""],[6683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution, it suffices him and is good, but whoever performs a full bath, the bath is more virtuous.\""],[6684,"That the Prophet ﷺ ordered his caller on a cold night to announce \"Prayer in the camp.\""],[6685,"Rain fell upon us while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he called out: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[6686,"\"The Prophet of God ﷺ commanded us to maintain the prayers and the middle prayer, and he informed us that it is the 'Asr prayer.\""],[6687,"From Samura regarding His word, Exalted is He: {Maintain the prayers and the middle prayer} — he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is the 'Asr prayer.\""],[6688,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"The middle prayer is the 'Asr prayer.\""],[6689,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The middle prayer is the 'Asr prayer.\""],[6690,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah.\""],[6691,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Every boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah; an animal is slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day and his head is shaved.\""],[6692,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Every boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah; an animal is slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named.\""],[6693,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Every boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah; an animal is slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, he is named, and his head is shaved.\""],[6694,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every boy is held in pledge for his ʿaqīqah; it is slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, his head is smeared, and he is named.”"],[6695,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The boy is held in pledge for his ʿaqīqah; it is offered on his behalf on his seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named.”"],[6696,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated, unless their sale is with an option.”"],[6697,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[6698,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated, and each of them may take what he is satisfied with from the sale.”"],[6699,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[6700,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[6701,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated.”"],[6702,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whichever woman is given in marriage by two guardians, she belongs to the first of them; and whichever man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them.”"],[6703,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When two men give a woman in marriage, the first has the greater right; and when two men purchase a sale, the first has the greater right.”"],[6704,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When a woman is married to two husbands, she belongs to the first of them; and when a sale is sold to two men, it belongs to the first of them.”"],[6705,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “Whichever woman two guardians give in marriage together, she belongs to the first of them; and whichever man sells a sale to two men together, it belongs to the first of them.”"],[6706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When two guardians marry [a woman] off, she belongs to the first of the two, and when two parties authorize a sale, it belongs to the first of the two.\""],[6707,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A lifetime gift ('umra) is permissible.\""],[6708,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A lifetime gift ('umra) is permissible.\""],[6709,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A lifetime gift ('umra) is permissible for its recipients.\""],[6710,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6711,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6712,"Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi related to us, saying: Muhammad b. al-Minhal related to us, saying: Yazid b. Zuray' related to us; and Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Azdi related to us, saying: Shihab b. 'Abbad related to us, saying: Muhammad b. Bishr related to us, saying: Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah related to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6713,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6714,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6715,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever owns a relative within the prohibited degrees of marriage, that [relative] is free.\""],[6716,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The Quran was revealed in seven dialects.\""],[6717,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Attend the Friday prayer and draw near to the imam, for a man may have a station in Paradise but then he lags behind from the Friday prayer, so he is delayed from it.\""],[6718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Shayṭān has kohl and a lick. When he applies kohl to a person from his kohl, his eyes sleep away from remembrance; and when he makes him lick from his lick, his tongue becomes sharp with evil.”"],[6719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A group of those who were with me will come to me, and when they raise their heads toward me they will be taken away before me. I will say: My Lord, my companions, my companions? It will be said: You do not know what they introduced after you.”"],[6720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not come until mountains vanish from their places and you see the great matters that you used not to see.”"],[6721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire.”"],[6722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire.”"],[6723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever finds the very property of his wealth is more entitled to it, and the seller follows the sale to the one who sold it.”"],[6724,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever recognizes his property, let him take it, and the seller seeks his sale wherever it was.”"],[6725,"“The hand that takes is responsible for what it has taken until it returns it.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2400)"],[6726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever encloses something, it belongs to him.”"],[6727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever builds a wall around land, it belongs to him.”"],[6728,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever encloses it with a wall, it belongs to him.”"],[6729,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever encloses land with a wall, it belongs to him.”"],[6730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever builds a wall around land, it belongs to him.”"],[6731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gains control over water, it belongs to him.\" And Wahb b. Baqiyya said: \"He has the most right to it.\""],[6732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a Muhājir from selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[6733,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of fruits for years [in advance]."],[6734,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sām is the father of the Arabs, Ḥām is the father of the Abyssinians, and Yāfith is the father of the Byzantines.\""],[6735,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"The sons of Nūḥ were Sām, Yāfith, and Ḥām.\""],[6736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nūḥ had three sons: Sām, Yāfith, and Ḥām.\""],[6737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The warranty period for slaves is three days.\""],[6738,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: [Samura said] \"a pause when he said the takbīr, and a pause when he finished reciting the sūrah.\" ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn objected to that, so they wrote to Ubayy b. Kaʿb about it, and Ubayy wrote back: \"Samura spoke the truth,\" and he said: \"Samura memorized the ḥadīth from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to make two pauses."],[6740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you comes upon livestock, if he sees its owner there, let him ask his permission. If he gives him permission, let him milk and drink. If the owner is not there, let him call out three times. If someone comes, let him ask his permission; otherwise, let him milk and drink, but not carry [any away].\""],[6741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you passes by livestock, let him call out three times. If anyone answers him, [he should ask permission]; otherwise, he may milk and drink.\""],[6742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The greatest regrets of the children of Ādam are over three things: a man who had a beautiful, lovely wife who bore him a son, then she died and he had nothing with which to hire a wet-nurse for his son; a man who was on a horse in a military expedition and saw the spoils, so he raced his companions to them until, when he drew near, the horse fell and died, while his companions reached the spoils and divided them; and a man who had a crop and a watering camel, and when his crop ripened and was ready for harvest, his camel died and he had nothing with which to buy another camel.\""],[6743,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who goes early to Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a chicken.”"],[6744,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Every prophet has a basin at which they vie with one another as to which of them has the greatest number of comers, and I hope that I will have the greatest number of comers.”"],[6745,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār to stand close to him in prayer so that they could learn from him.”"],[6746,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to be balanced in prostration and not to crouch hastily.”"],[6747,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to be balanced in prostration and not to crouch hastily.”"],[6748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Garden of Firdaws is the elevated part of the highest Garden, which is its middle and its best.”"],[6749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Firdaws is the elevated part of the Garden, its highest and its middle, and from it the rivers of the Garden gush forth.”"],[6750,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let the Bedouins stand behind the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār so that they may follow their lead in prayer.”"],[6751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The son of Adam grows old, but two things in him grow young: desire for wealth and desire for a long life.”"],[6752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the people of the Fire are those whom the Fire will take up to their ankles, up to their knees, up to their waists, and up to their collarbones.”"],[6753,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us that when the imam gives the salutation, we should respond to him.”"],[6754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the imam says, {not of those who earned wrath nor of those who went astray}, say ‘Āmīn,’ and Allah will answer you.”"],[6755,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Begging is a scratching and a deficiency in a man's face, unless a man asks his father or the ruler in charge of him.\""],[6756,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade celibacy.\" Then Qatadah recited: {And We have certainly sent messengers before you and made for them wives and descendants}."],[6757,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Day of the Greater Pilgrimage is the day Abu Bakr ؓ led the people in Hajj.\""],[6758,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Eve had no child that lived for her, so Satan said to her: 'Name him Abd al-Harith, for he will live.' So they named him that, and that was from Satan's inspiration and his command. Then she conceived a light pregnancy which was not apparent, and when her pregnancy became apparent she passed by him.\""],[6759,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The dead is punished by the weeping of the living.\""],[6760,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Establish the prayer, give the zakat, perform Hajj and Umrah, and be upright; you will be treated uprightly.\""],[6761,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A man shall not propose to a woman when his brother has already proposed.\""],[6762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When the imam says the salam, then respond to him.\""],[6763,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Kill the elderly of the polytheists and spare their young.\""],[6764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Kill the elderly of the polytheists and spare their young.\""],[6765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Kill the elderly of the polytheists and spare their young.\""],[6766,"\"The battle cry of the Emigrants was 'Abd Allah', and the battle cry of the Helpers was 'Abd al-Rahman'.\""],[6767,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he prayed for rain, used to say: “O Allah, send down upon our land its adornment and its tranquility.”"],[6768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not dwell with the polytheists nor intermix with them, for whoever dwells with them or intermixes with them is one of them.”"],[6769,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to greet those on our right and that some of us should greet one another.”"],[6770,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to greet our women and that some of us should respond to one another.”"],[6771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman may not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt.”"],[6772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.”"],[6773,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from cutting a leather strip between two fingers.”"],[6774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever misses the Friday prayer should give a dinar in charity; if he cannot find it, then half a dinar.”"],[6775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nobility is wealth and honor is piety.”"],[6776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nobility is wealth and honor is piety.”"],[6777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one consulted is entrusted.”"],[6778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The place of the lower garment is the shin, and the lower garment has no right over the ankles.”"],[6779,"“Today I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you and have approved for you Islam as religion” was revealed on the Day of Arafah, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was standing at Arafah on a Friday."],[6780,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever prays Fajr is under God’s protection, so let not God demand anything of you concerning His protection.”"],[6781,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Dajjal will appear. His left eye is blind, with a thick growth over it. He will heal the born-blind and the leper, bring the dead to life, and say to people: ‘I am your lord.’ Whoever says, ‘You are my lord’ has fabricated a lie; and whoever says, ‘My Lord is God’ and remains on that until he dies will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal.” The wording is that of al-Khalil b. Murrah."],[6782,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The neighbor of a dwelling has more right to the dwelling.”"],[6783,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Soon God will fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then He will make them lions who do not flee; they will kill your fighters and consume your spoils.”"],[6784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The likeness of one who flees from death is like a fox pursued by the earth for a debt. He kept running until, when he became exhausted and distressed, he entered his burrow. The earth said to him, ‘O fox, my debt?’ So he came out with a scurrying motion, and he remained like that until his neck was severed and he died.”"],[6785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The neighbor of a dwelling has more right to the dwelling.”"],[6786,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If two guardians give a woman in marriage, the first has more right; and if two sellers sell, the first has more right.”"],[6787,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to pray at night, a little or a lot, and to make that an odd number."],[6788,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution on Friday, it suffices and is good; and whoever performs the full bath, the bath is better.”"],[6789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him.”"],[6790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate when he prayed for rain: “O Allah, place in our land its blessing, its beauty, and its tranquility.”"],[6791,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade going out to meet caravans until they reach the market."],[6792,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A resident may not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[6793,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Every newborn is held in pledge for its aqiqah, to be slaughtered on its behalf on its seventh day, and he is to be named and his head shaved.”"],[6794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the disbelievers: “Kill their old men and spare their young men.”"],[6795,"The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his hands when delivering the sermon until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[6796,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah’s protection.”"],[6797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him.”"],[6798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give one salutation facing straight ahead."],[6799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is invited to a ruler and does not answer, he is a wrongdoer and has no right.”"],[6800,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."],[6801,"The Prophet ﷺ used to urge giving charity and forbid mutilation."],[6802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not purposely time your prayers with the rising of the sun or its setting, for it rises between the two horns of a devil and sets between the two horns of a devil.”"],[6803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fever is a piece of the Fire, so cool it away from yourselves with cold water.”"],[6804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fever is a piece of the Fire, so cool it away from yourselves with cold water.”"],[6805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cursing one another with the curse of Allah, or with His wrath, or with the Fire."],[6806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade any of us to cut something or a strap between two of his fingers at the threshold of cutting, and it is pierced with his hand."],[6807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “O Allah, distance me from my sins as You have distanced between the east and the west, and purify me from my errors as the white garment is purified from dirt.”"],[6808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us, when we are three, to put forward one of us to be the imam, and when we are two, to form one row."],[6809,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain, he would say: “O God, send down upon our land its adornment and send down upon our land its tranquility, and provide for us, for You are the best of providers.”"],[6810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to join Ramadan with a fast."],[6811,"We used to travel with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when the sky rained we heard the caller of the Messenger of God ﷺ announce: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[6812,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The boy is pledged by his ʿaqīqah; it is slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, and he is named and his head is shaved.”"],[6813,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you becomes drowsy on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him get up from his seat and let him seat his brother in his place.”"],[6814,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade squatting on the heels in prayer."],[6815,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four.”"],[6816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The believer eats in one intestine, while the hypocrite eats in seven intestines.”"],[6817,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my father has consumed my wealth. He said: “You and your wealth belong to your father.”"],[6818,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best charity is the tongue.” It was said: O Messenger of God, what is the charity of the tongue? He said: “Intercession by which a captive is freed, blood is spared, you bring kindness and goodness to your brother, and you ward off harm from him.”"],[6819,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The food of two is sufficient for four, and the food of four is sufficient for eight.\""],[6820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ struck the example of the one who comes early on Friday as being like the one who sacrifices a camel, and like the one who sacrifices a cow, and like the one who sacrifices a sheep, and like the one who sacrifices a bird, until he reached the sparrow."],[6821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among the people of the Fire are those whom it will take up to their ankles, and among them are those whom it will take up to their knees, and among them are those whom it will take up to their waist, and among them are those whom it will take up to their collarbones.\""],[6822,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It does not harm any of you whatever he uses to stave off hunger if he obtains it lawfully.\""],[6823,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not pray when the sun rises and do not pray when it sets, for it sets between the two horns of a devil and disappears between the two horns of the devil.\""],[6824,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade praying after the morning prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil."],[6825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Adhere to this white clothing; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments.\""],[6826,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Adhere to white clothing; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments.\""],[6827,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever misses a Friday prayer without an excuse, let him give charity of a dinar; if he cannot find it, then half a dinar.\""],[6828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let not Bilal's call or the whiteness seen at the height of the pre-dawn deceive you.\""],[6829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let not Bilal's call to prayer or this darkness deceive you until it breaks like this,\" and he gestured with his hand horizontally."],[6830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let not Bilal's call to prayer prevent you from your pre-dawn meal, nor the elongated dawn, but rather the elongated dawn on the horizon.\" The wording is that of Hajjaj b. Nusayr."],[6831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let not Bilal's call to prayer or the whiteness of dawn deceive you from your pre-dawn meal, like this,\" and he raised his hands until it spread across the horizon, and he gestured with his hand horizontally."],[6832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say to his companions: \"Has any of you seen a dream?\" We would narrate to him whatever Allah willed we narrate. One morning he said: \"Two came to me last night, or two came to me, and they sent me forth and told me: 'Go.' So I went with them. We came upon a man lying down, and another standing over him with a rock. He was bringing the rock down upon his head, smashing it. The rock rolled away, he followed it and took it, and did not return to him until his head was restored as it was. Then he returned to him and did the same as the first time. I said to them: 'Glory be to Allah, what is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' So we went on and came upon a man lying on his back, and another standing over him with an iron hook. He would come to one side of his face and tear his cheek to the back of his neck, then turn to the other side and do the same. He would not finish until that side was restored as it was, then he would return to it and do as he had done the first time. I said to them: 'Glory be to Allah, what are these two?' They said to me: 'Go.' So we went on and came upon a structure like a clay oven. I think he said we heard noise and voices. We looked into it and saw men and women naked, and flames came at them from below. When the flames came at them, they cried out. I said to them: 'Glory be to Allah, who are these?' They said to me: 'Go.' So we went on and came upon a river—I think he said red like blood—and in the river a man was swimming, and on the bank a man had gathered stones. The swimmer would swim as he swam, then come to the one with the stones, open his mouth, and the man would put a stone in it. Then he would go and swim, then return, and each time he returned he opened his mouth and received a stone. I said to them: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' So we went on and came upon a man of ugly appearance, the ugliest man you could see, with a fire that he was stoking and walking around. I said to them: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So we went on and came to a lush meadow in which was every kind of spring herb, and in the middle of the meadow was a tall man whose head I could hardly see in the sky, and around him were the most numerous and most beautiful children I had ever seen. I said to them: 'Glory be to Allah, what is this and who are these?' They said to me: 'Go.' We reached a great tree, the greatest and most beautiful tree I had ever seen. They said to me: 'Climb it.' So we climbed and reached a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver. We came to the gate of the city and asked for it to be opened. It was opened and we entered. There we were met by men, half of whose form was the most beautiful you could see, and half the ugliest you could see. They said: 'Go and plunge into that river.' There was a river flowing across, its water like pure milk in whiteness. They went and plunged into it, then returned to us with the ugliness gone, and they were in the most beautiful form. They said to me: 'This is the Garden of Eden, and this is your abode.' My sight rose upward, and I saw a palace like a white cloud. They said: 'That is your abode.' I said to them: 'May Allah bless you both, let me enter it.' They said: 'Not now, but you will enter it.' I said: 'I have seen wonders since last night. What is this that I have seen?' They said: 'We will tell you. The first man whose head was smashed with the rock is a man who takes the Qur'an and sleeps through the prescribed prayers. The man whose cheek, eye, and nostril were torn to the back of his neck is a man who leaves his house and tells a lie that reaches the horizons. The naked men and women in the structure like an oven are the fornicators and adulteresses. The man swimming in the river and being fed stones is the eater of usury. The man of ugly appearance at the fire is Malik, the keeper of Hell. The man in the meadow is Ibrahim ﷺ . The children around him are every child born upon the natural disposition.' Some of the Muslims said: 'O Messenger of Allah, and the children of the polytheists?' He said: 'And the children of the polytheists. As for the people who were half beautiful and half ugly, they are people who mixed a righteous deed with an evil one, and Allah overlooked them.'\""],[6833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever he woke up in the morning, would say to his companions: \"Has any of you seen a dream?\" One day he woke up and said: \"I saw as if two came to me and said: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to an old man with white hair and beard, gloomy and sad, with a fire that he was stoking and tending. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, who is this old man and what is this fire?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to a man, and another man standing at his head with an iron hook in his hand. He was tearing his mouth to the back of his neck, his nostril to the back of his neck, and his eye to the back of his neck, then he did the same to the other side. He would not finish until that side returned to the healthiest it had been. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, what are these two men?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to a man lying on his back, and another standing at his head with a rock in his hand, smashing his head with it. The rock rolled away, he went and took it, and did not return to his companion until his head returned to the healthiest it had been, then he did the same again. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, what are these two?' They said: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to something like a pool, and in it a man was swimming, and a man standing on the edge of the pool with a rock in his hand. The swimmer would come, open his mouth, and the man would put that rock in it. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, what are these two?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to something like an oven, and in it were men and women. Flames came at them from below and they cried out. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, who are these?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to a white land like silver, in which was every spring flower, and a man with white hair and beard, the most beautiful man you could see, with children around him, gathering them and tending to them. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, who is this old man and who are these children?' They said to me: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to a white land like silver, in which a river flowed. People came, half of whose bodies were the most beautiful you could see and half the ugliest you could see. They entered that river as if commanded, and came out of it as if anointed with oil. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, who are these?' They said: 'Go, go.' So I went with them until they brought me to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and it is the Garden of Eden, and that is your abode. I said: 'May Allah bless you both, let me enter it.' They said: 'No, but you will enter it.' I said: 'May Allah bless you both, I have seen wonders since last night.' They said: 'We will tell you. The one with white hair and beard is Malik, the keeper of Hell. The one you saw whose mouth, nostril, and eye were torn to the back of his neck is a man who leaves his house and tells a lie that spreads across the horizons. The one you saw whose head was smashed and left like a loaf of bread is the slanderer. The one you saw in the pool being fed a stone is the man who consumes the orphan's wealth. The ones you saw in the thing like an oven are the adulteresses and fornicators. The one with white hair and beard is Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah, and the children you saw are the children of the Muslims, and every child is born upon the natural disposition. As for those you saw with half their bodies the most beautiful and half the ugliest, they are people who did a righteous deed and another evil one, and Allah will forgive them.'\""],[6834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he woke up in the morning, would say: \"Has any of you seen a dream?\" and he would interpret it for him, until one day he woke up and said: \"Has anyone of you seen a dream?\" The people were silent, so he said: \"But I myself saw in sleep: two men came to me and said: 'Go.' I passed by a man with a rock in his hand, striking the head of another man with it and scattering his brains. The rock returned to his hand and the head returned as it was. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Go.' Then I passed by a man with an iron hook in his hand, tearing the cheek of another man until it reached the back, then he started on the other side, and this one returned as it was. I said: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' Then I passed by a man in a river of blood, and he was bridled, and on the bank of the river was a man kindling a fire with stones in it. Whenever he wanted to come out, he took a stone and threw it into his mouth, and he returned. I said: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' Then they took me past a house whose lower part was narrower than its upper part, in which were naked people, with fire kindled beneath them. Whenever it was kindled, they cried out, and when it was extinguished, they became quiet. I said: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' Then they took me past a tree under which a man was kindling a fire and tending it; when it scattered, he gathered it together. I said: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go,' until they brought me to the middle of a tree, and there were beautiful dwellings. I said: 'What is this?' They said to me: 'Go.' So they took me until they brought me to the top of the tree, and there were dwellings more beautiful than those, and three chambers. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Take your time. As for the one with the rock striking the man's head, those are those who sleep through the prayer.' Ibn 'Abbas said: 'This is the one who was given knowledge but it awakens him.' 'As for the man you saw with a hook tearing the cheek of a man, those are those who go about with malicious gossip. As for the one you saw in a river of blood, those are the consumers of usury. As for those you saw in a house whose lower part is narrower than its upper part, naked people, those are the fornicators of the nation, and so they will be until the Day of Resurrection. As for the man you saw under the tree kindling a fire and tending it, that is Malik, the keeper of the Fire. As for the dwellings you saw in the middle of the tree, those are the dwellings of the believers in general, and these are the dwellings of the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs, and this chamber is for you. I am Jibril, and this is Mika'il.'\""],[6835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us one day, and whenever he prayed, he would turn to face us and say: \"Did any of you see a dream last night?\" If any of us had seen a dream, he would relate it to him, and he would say about it whatever Allah willed. One day he asked us: \"Did any of you see a dream?\" We said: \"No.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I saw two men who came to me, took me by the hand, and brought me out to a level land, or an open space. I passed by a man while another man was standing at his head with an iron hook in his hand, which he inserted into one side of his mouth and tore it until it reached the back of his neck, then he did the same with the other side of his mouth. Meanwhile the first side of his mouth healed, and he returned and did the same thing again. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Move on.' So we moved on until we came to a man lying on his back, with another man standing at his head holding a boulder or a large stone, with which he crushed his head. When he struck him, the stone rolled away, and he went to retrieve it, but by the time he returned to him, his head had healed and become as it was before. He went back and struck him again, and he continued doing that to him. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Move on.' So we moved on until we came to a structure built like a tannur (oven), narrow at the top and wide at the bottom, with a fire burning beneath it. Inside were naked men and women. When the fire was kindled beneath it, they rose up until they almost came out of it, and when it was extinguished, they went back down into it. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Move on.' So we moved on until we came to a river of blood, with a man standing in the middle of the river and another man in front of him with stones. Whenever the man in the river tried to come out, the man threw a stone into his mouth and forced him back to where he had been. I said: 'What is this?' They said: 'Move on.' So we moved on until we came to a green meadow, in which there was a great tree, and at its base was an old man surrounded by children and women, and a man near the tree with a fire in front of him which he was kindling and stoking. I asked the two of them about it, and they said: 'Move on.' So we moved on until we came to the tree, and they brought me into a dwelling, and I had never seen a dwelling more beautiful than it. In it were old men, young men, children, and women. Then they climbed the tree and brought me into another dwelling which was even more beautiful and better than the first, containing old men and young men. I said to them: 'You have taken me around since last night and have been kind to me, so tell me about what I have seen.' They said: 'Yes. As for the first man you saw, he was a liar who used to tell a lie, and it would be carried from him until it reached the horizons, so what you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection. As for the man whose head was being crushed, he was a man whom Allah had taught the Qur'an, but he slept through it at night and did not act upon it during the day, so what you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection. As for those you saw in the structure, they are the adulterers of this community. As for the one you saw in the river of blood, he is the one who consumes usury. As for the old man you saw at the base of the tree, that is Ibrahim ﷺ . As for the children you saw, they are the offspring of mankind. As for the fire you saw and the man kindling it, that is the Fire and its keeper. As for the first dwelling you entered, it is the dwelling of 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers. As for this one, it is the dwelling of the martyrs. I am Jibril, and this is Mika'il.' I said to them: 'Tell me, where is my dwelling?' They said: 'Raise your head.' So I raised my head, and there above me was something like a cloud. They said: 'That is your dwelling.' I said: 'Let me enter my dwelling.' They said: 'You still have some work remaining that you have not yet completed. When you have completed it, you will enter your dwelling.'\""],[6836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of what people treat themselves with is cupping.\""],[6837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A woman is like a rib, if you try to straighten it, you will break it; so, leave her as she is and live with her.\""],[6838,"I asked Matar al-Warraq: \"Does a man recite 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' and seek refuge from the accursed Satan in every rak'ah and in every surah that he begins?\" He said: \"Qatadah informed me from Muhammad b. Sirin from 'Imran b. Husayn and Samurah b. Jundub from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'There are two pauses: he does that within himself when he begins the prayer and when he rises from sitting after the two rak'ahs.'\""],[6839,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever kills an enemy combatant, the spoils belong to him.\""],[6840,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever kills an enemy combatant, the spoils belong to him.\""],[6841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Whoever kills an enemy combatant, the spoils belong to him.\""],[6842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: \"Whoever kills a man, his spoils are his from the booty, if he overcame him.\""],[6843,"When it was a rainy day—I think he said during travel—the Prophet ﷺ would have his caller announce: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[6844,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever kills an enemy combatant, the spoils belong to him.\""],[6845,"To proceed: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us that one of us should pray every night after the prescribed prayer, whether little or much, and make it odd-numbered (witr).\""],[6846,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us that a man should pray every night after the prescribed prayer, whether much or little, and make it odd-numbered (witr).\""],[6847,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you becomes drowsy during the Friday prayer, let him change his seat.”"],[6848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us: “When one of you becomes drowsy during a Friday prayer, let him change his seat to another place.”"],[6849,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you knew that which I know, you would laugh little and weep much.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6486)"],[6850,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to us: “If one of you had a valley full [of gold] from its top to its bottom, he would love to have another valley filled for him.” He said: “Indeed, by Allah, if I could, I would fill it for you. A man's soul will never be filled with wealth until it is filled with dust.”"],[6851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to pray at any hour we wished of the night or day, except that he commanded us to avoid the rising of the sun and its setting. He said: “Indeed, Satan sets with it and rises with it when it rises.”"],[6852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to pray at any hour we wished of the night or day, except that he commanded us to avoid the rising of the sun and its setting. He said: “Indeed, Satan sets with it when it sets and rises with it when it rises.”"],[6853,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to maintain all the prayers, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ especially enjoined the middle prayer, and he informed us that it is the 'Asr prayer."],[6854,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to maintain all the prayers, and he especially enjoined the middle prayer, and he informed us that it is the 'Asr prayer."],[6855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from continuous fasting in the month of fasting, and he disliked it, but it is not an emphatic command."],[6856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from continuous fasting in the month of fasting, disliking it, but it is not an emphatic command."],[6857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to curse with the curse of Allah and His wrath."],[6858,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from cursing one another with the curse of Allah or with His wrath, and he forbade us from cursing one another with the Fire."],[6859,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us that when the prayer overtakes us and we are three or more, one of us should stand as our imam, and if we are two, we should stand in a row together."],[6860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us that when prayer overtook us while we were three or more, we should put forward one of us to lead, and if we were two, that we should stand in one row together."],[6861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to love one another and to greet one another with salam when we meet."],[6862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us: when we are in the middle of the prayer or at the time of its ending, begin before the taslim by saying: 'Greetings, good words, prayers, peace, and sovereignty belong to Allah. Then send peace upon the prophets, then send peace upon your relatives and upon yourselves.'"],[6863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When the time of taslim comes in the middle of the prayer or at the time of its ending, begin before the taslim and say: 'Greetings, good words, prayers, peace, and sovereignty belong to Allah. Then send peace upon the Prophet ﷺ, then send peace upon your relatives and upon yourselves.'"],[6864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were in prayer and raised our heads from prostration, to settle on the ground sitting, and not to perch on the tips of our feet."],[6865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid a man from celibacy and forbade entering the houses of the believers."],[6866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid a man from celibacy and forbade entering the houses of the believers."],[6867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'Whoever conceals stolen war booty is like him, and whoever associates with a polytheist and lives with him is like him.'"],[6868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever conceals stolen war booty is like him, and whoever gathers with a polytheist and lives with him is like him.'"],[6869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: When two men from among us trade with one another, one of them sells to the other with an option until he settles with his companion, and each of them gives his companion the choice, and each of them chooses what he desires from the sale."],[6870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us concerning mosques: that we should build them in our dwellings, improve their construction, and purify them."],[6871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us concerning the mosque: that we should build them in our dwellings, beautify their construction, and purify them."],[6872,"A man from the Bedouins came to him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—seeking his ruling about a man: what is lawful for him and what is forbidden for him regarding his property, his sacrificial rites, his livestock, his firstborn offerings, and the offspring of his camels and barren ones. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “I make lawful for you the good things and forbid you the foul things, except that if you become poor and in need of food, you may eat of it until you are self-sufficient.” Then the man asked him: “What is my poverty that permits me to eat that when I reach it, or my self-sufficiency that makes me dispense with it?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you hope for offspring and can reach your offspring with the meat of your livestock, or you hope for rain and it comes in time so that you can reach your offspring with the meat of your livestock, or you hope for profit from its wealth and reach it with the meat of your livestock. But when you hope for none of that, then feed your family what seems good to you until you are self-sufficient from it.” The Bedouin said: “What is my self-sufficiency that I should leave when I find it?” He said: “When you have given your family an evening drink of milk, then avoid what is forbidden to you of food. As for your property, it is all permitted and none of it is forbidden, except that you owe a firstborn from the offspring of your camels and a firstborn from the offspring of your sheep; your livestock may graze until you are self-sufficient, then if you wish feed its meat to your family, or if you wish give its meat in charity.” And he commanded him to offer a tenth from every hundred sheep."],[6873,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to instruct us to give charity to the young and elderly individuals who are unable to work, without intending to sell them. He would also command us not to take anything from them in charity. He would order us to give charity from what is prepared for sale.\""],[6874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from reviling, and he said: “If one of you must inevitably revile his companion, let him not slander him, nor revile his parents, nor revile his people. But if he knows that, let him say: ‘You are miserly,’ or ‘You are cowardly,’ or ‘You are a liar,’ or ‘You are base.’”"],[6875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “Do not swear by idols, and do not swear by your fathers. Swear by God, for it is more beloved to Him that you swear by Him, and do not swear by anything besides Him.”"],[6876,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to recite the Noble Quran as he taught us to recite it, and he said: “It was revealed in three modes; do not differ about it and do not dispute about it, for it is blessed. Recite it as you have been taught to recite it.”"],[6877,"The messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, the Arabs are descendants of Sam ibn Noah, and the Romans are descendants of Japheth ibn Noah, and the Abyssinians are descendants of Ham ibn Noah.\""],[6878,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us that if one of us was distracted from the prayer or forgot it until its time in which it is prayed had passed, that we should pray it with the next prescribed prayer."],[6879,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The month does not always complete thirty nights.” Musa b. Harun said: Its meaning is that not every month completes thirty; sometimes it is twenty-nine."],[6880,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you stand for prayer, do not race your reciter in bowing, prostrating, and standing. Rather, let him precede you so that you may catch up with what he has preceded you in, if he raises his head in bowing, prostration, and standing before you, then you may make up what you missed thereby.”"],[6881,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “When you fight the polytheists, kill their elders, for the softest of hearts among them are their youth.”"],[6882,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you spits while he is praying, let him not spit in front of his face or to his right, but let him spit under his foot and rub it into the ground.”"],[6883,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us: “Whoever loses property or has it stolen, then recognizes it, and a year passes over it, his property is to be returned to him, and the one who bought it may reclaim its price from the one who sold it to him.”"],[6884,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said at the time of the conquest: “This is the year of the greater pilgrimage.” He said: “The pilgrimage of the Muslims and the pilgrimage of the polytheists coincided in three consecutive days, and the pilgrimage of the Muslims, the polytheists, the Christians, and the Jews coincided this year in six consecutive days. They have not coincided like this since the heavens and the earth were created before this year, and they will not coincide after this year until the Hour begins.”"],[6885,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid women from lying down together unless there were clothes between them, and he forbade a man from lying down with his companion unless there was a garment between them."],[6886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid women from lying with one another unless there were garments between them, and a man from lying with his companion unless there was a garment between them."],[6887,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.”"],[6888,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “Whichever of you prepares food enough for two men, it is sufficient for three; or prepares for three, it is sufficient for four; or for four, it is sufficient for five—and so on with such numbers.”"],[6889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us to attend the Friday prayer and not to be absent from it; and when the believers are summoned with a call on Friday and they stand, each of them is more entitled to his seat when he returns to it."],[6890,"A man from the Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his ruling on what is forbidden to him and what is lawful for him, regarding his ritual offerings, his livestock, his goats, and the firstborn offspring from the produce of his camels and sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Lawful for you are the good things, and forbidden to you are the foul things—unless you are in need of food that is not lawful for you, in which case you may eat from it until you are free of need of it.” At that time a man asked: “What is my state of need, and what is that from which I may eat when I reach it, and what is the sufficiency that will make me free of need of it?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “When you hope for offspring and you can sustain yourself on the meat of your livestock until your offspring come, or you hope for rain that you think will reach you and you can sustain yourself on the meat of your livestock, or you hope for supplies that you will obtain and you can sustain yourself on the meat of your livestock until you reach them. But if you hope for none of that, then feed your family from what appears to you until you are free of need of it.” The Bedouin said: “What is the sufficiency that I may leave when I find it?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “When you satisfy your family with an evening drink of milk, then avoid the food that has been forbidden to you. As for your wealth, it is all made easy for you; there is nothing forbidden in it, except that in the offspring of your camels there is a firstborn, and in the offspring of your sheep there is a firstborn—you nourish them with your livestock until they are of sufficient age, then if you wish you feed their meat to your family, and if you wish you give their meat in charity.” And he commanded him to sacrifice from every pasturing flock of sheep an ‘atirah."],[6891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command regarding a man’s or woman’s slaves who are their inherited property and their workers, whom they do not intend to sell: he would command us not to give any zakat on their behalf; and he would command us to give zakat on the slaves who are prepared for sale."],[6892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, when one of you prays, let him say: “O Allah, distance me from my sin as You distanced between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from turning Your face away from me on the Day of Resurrection. O Allah, purify me from my sin as the white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, grant me life as a Muslim and cause me to die as a Muslim.”"],[6893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us one day: “It has been said to me: ‘Recite to Ibn al-Khattab.’” So he called him and commanded that he attend the Qur’an when it was revealed so that he could recite it to him."],[6894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid plunder, so much so that he would command a traveling party regarding the meat of a sheep while they were cooking, saying: “Do not eat it.”"],[6895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “The woman is like a rib; if you try to straighten her you will break her, and if you leave her she remains crooked.”"],[6896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “On the Day of Resurrection, every two of the prophets will be intimate friends, apart from the rest of them.” He said: “My intimate friend among them that day will be the Close Friend of Allah, Ibrahim ﷺ .”"],[6897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prophets will vie with one another in boastfulness over which of them has the most companions from his nation, and I hope that on that day I will have the most of them all coming to the water. Each man among them that day will stand at a full watering-place with a staff in his hand, calling those of his nation whom he recognizes, and every nation will have a mark by which its prophet will know them.”"],[6898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Among the nations there was a community for whom a parable was struck like the parable of hired workers whom a man hired to work for him for a whole day, and he set for them a qirat. They worked until when half the day had passed, they became weary and said to the man, 'Settle our account.' So he settled with them, and they had half a qirat. Then he said, 'Who will complete my work until nightfall for a qirat, a qirat?' Another group contracted with him. They worked until when it was close to the afternoon prayer, they became weary and said, 'Settle our account.' So he settled with them, and they had half a qirat. The man wanted his work to be completed before nightfall, so he hired a group to complete what remained of his work until nightfall for two qirats. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: 'I hope, if God wills, that you will be the companions of the two qirats.'"],[6899,"A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking his ruling on kalalah. He said, 'Tell me, O Messenger of God: is kalalah a man who leaves behind brothers from his mother and his father?' The Prophet ﷺ said nothing to him except that he recited to him the verse of kalalah which is in Surah al-Nisa'. Then the man returned asking him, and each time he asked, he recited it to him, until the man became persistent and raised his voice, and his clamor intensified out of eagerness for the Prophet ﷺ to make it clear to him. So he recited the verse to him, then the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'By God, I will not increase you beyond what I have been given; by God, I will not increase you beyond what I have been given,' so much so that he repeated it to him. Then the man sat down and fell silent."],[6900,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid the owner of palm trees from incurring debt against the fruit of his palms until some of its fruit could be eaten, for fear that he would incur a large debt and the fruit would spoil and not fulfill it for him. He used to forbid the owner of crops from incurring debt against his crops until they reached harvest. And he used to forbid the owner of gold, when he sold it for food in exchange for fruit, from selling the food for gold until the food was measured and he took possession of it, for fear of riba."],[6901,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us, \"Abu Bakr interprets the dreams, and indeed, righteous dreams are a portion of Prophethood.\""],[6902,"When the Prophet ﷺ cursed the polytheists in prayer, he would begin with Quraysh, then he would follow them with many tribes of the Arabs. It was said to him once, 'Curse the disbelievers of Quraysh.' So the Prophet ﷺ, when he wanted to curse a tribe, would say: 'O God, curse the disbelievers of Quraysh, Banu so-and-so.'"],[6903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: 'It is not lawful for a Muslim man to cut off the nose of his slave or to castrate him. And whoever we know has done any of that, we will do the same to him.'"],[6904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'A road is not to be blocked, and surplus water is not to be withheld. The wayfarer is entitled to the loan of the bucket, the rope, and the trough; if he does not return it in kind, he is left between it and the well to water, and he is not prevented from digging when the digger reaches twenty-five cubits as a watering place for livestock.'"],[6905,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to entertain guests."],[6906,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid milking a man's livestock except with his permission, and he would say: 'Its milk is like what is in your private stores; neither of them is more lawful than the other.'"],[6907,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone among you nor for anything you cause, but that is among the signs of God by which He makes His servants take heed, so that whoever fears Him may be grateful and remember Him. So when you see any of the signs of God ﷻ, hasten to the remembrance of God, so remember Him and fear Him.' He prayed with us on the day the sun eclipsed, then he admonished us and reminded us, then he said: 'I have not seen anything in this world that has a color, nor have I been told of anything in Paradise or in Hell, except that it was pictured for me facing this wall since I prayed this prayer of mine with you, and I looked at it, visible on the wall of the mosque.'"],[6908,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to us: There is no envy in this world except in two cases: a man who envies another man because God has given him abundant wealth, and he spends from it and increases his spending, so the other says, 'If I had the like of this, I would spend the like of what he spends and do better,' so he envies him. And a man who recites the Quran and stands with it at night, while beside him is a man who does not know the Quran, so he envies him for his standing and for what God ﷻ has taught him of the Quran, and he says, 'If God had taught me the like of this, I would stand the like of what he stands.'"],[6909,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: 'Do not go out to meet the caravans before they reach their market.'"],[6910,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'Do not sell on behalf of the Bedouins, even if one of you is his brother or his father or his mother.'"],[6911,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Whoever sells land or a house, the neighbor of the land or the neighbor of the house has more right to buy it if he meets its price.”"],[6912,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “If a woman is married off and two different men wish to marry her, both of them guardians, the one with the most right among the two suitors is the first of them. And in a sale, if two men purchase the same item, the one with the most right to it is the first of them.”"],[6913,"The Prophet ﷺ used to forbid shighar (exchange marriage) with women."],[6914,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid three people from two of them whispering privately to the exclusion of the third."],[6915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid three people from two of them whispering privately to the exclusion of the third."],[6916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid three people from two of them whispering privately to the exclusion of the third."],[6917,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking his ruling about eating lizard. He said: “I neither command nor forbid anyone regarding it, except that we, the family of Muhammad, do not eat it.”"],[6918,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us one night, while we were encamped at a pit, from eating the meat of domestic donkeys, and he ordered us to use the meat we had with us, so we threw it away."],[6919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “By God, it would not please me to have Mount Uhud all in gold and then bequeath it.”"],[6920,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “One of you on the day he dies has three companions: among them one who withholds from him what he asks—that is his wealth; among them a companion who goes with him until he enters the grave but gives him nothing and does not accompany him after that—those are his relatives; and among them a companion who says, ‘By God, I am going with you wherever you go, and I will never part from you’—that is his deeds, whether they be good or evil.”"],[6921,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “You will be gathered to Jerusalem, then you will assemble on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[6922,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid any of us from cutting a leather strap between two fingers,” saying: “In that there are two eyes.”"],[6923,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “When a man disputes with another and one of them calls his companion to the Messenger to judge between them, whoever refuses to come has no right.”"],[6924,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the believing men and believing women, and for the Muslim men and Muslim women, every Friday.”"],[6925,"When we were caught by rain while traveling and the call to prayer was made, the Messenger of God ﷺ, out of dislike that he should cause us hardship, would order the muezzin to say: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[6926,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: \"Indeed, I get angry with you and excuse you, then I supplicate to Allah between me and Him, 'O Allah, do not punish them, curse them, or be angry with them. Rather, make them a source of blessing, mercy, forgiveness, and prayer for them, for they are my people and I am their well-wisher.\""],[6927,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “The false messiah (al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl) is blind in the left eye, upon which there is a thick white film. He will heal the blind from birth and the leper, bring the dead to life, and say: ‘I am your Lord.’ Whoever takes refuge in God and says: ‘My Lord is God,’ then refuses that until he dies, no punishment or trial will be upon him. But whoever says: ‘You are my Lord,’ has been tried.” And the Prophet ﷺ said: “The false messiah will remain on earth for as long as God wills, then Jesus son of Mary ﷺ will come from the east, confirming Muhammad ﷺ and following his religion, then he will kill the false messiah.”"],[6928,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Before the Hour comes, you will see things you will find gravely objectionable, and you will say: ‘We are destroyed. Were we told of this?’ When you see that, remember God Almighty and know that they are the beginnings of the Hour.” He even said: “You will see mountains move before the time of the Cry.” And he used to tell us: “The Hour will not come until the stone points out a Jew who is hiding: a Muslim man will be chasing him, and he will look ahead and hide, then the stone will say: ‘O servant of God, this is the one you seek.’”"],[6929,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “In this world there is no regret except in three cases: a man who had irrigation and a water-drawing camel with which he watered his land. When his land’s thirst became severe and its fruits emerged, his camel died, and he feels regret for the camel that he had trained to draw water, since he will not find its like, and he feels regret for the fruit of his land, lest it spoil before he can contrive a plan for it. And a man who had a swift horse and met a gathering of disbelievers. When they drew near to one another, the enemies of God fled, and the man raced ahead on his horse. But when he was about to catch up, his horse broke down and left him standing beside it, so he feels regret for his horse, since he will not find its like, and he feels regret for the victory that had been within his reach. And a man who has a wife whose appearance and religion please him, and she gives birth to a boy but dies in childbirth. He feels regret for his wife, thinking he will never find her like, and he feels regret for her child, fearing that he will perish neglected before he can find a wet-nurse for him.” He said: “And this last is the greatest of those regrets.”"],[6930,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to order the Emigrants and the Helpers to be in the front rows, and he would say: “They are more knowledgeable about the prayer than the Bedouins and the foolish. Those behind them follow them, and I do not like the Bedouins to be in front of them, not knowing how to pray.”"],[6931,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a tree standing on a single trunk; the width of its trunk is a journey of seventy years.”"],[6932,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to tell us: “The name of the believing man in the [earlier] books is al-karm (generosity), because of what God has honored him with over creation. But you call the wall of grapevines al-karm, whereas its name is al-ḥafr (the trench), and it is the man who is al-karm.”"],[6933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Al-Firdaws is the middle hill of Paradise, the highest and most beautiful of it.”"],[6934,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “I do not find any kind of beast of which a single one is better than a hundred of its fellows, except the man who finds [another] man: he is better than a hundred men.”"],[6935,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Whoever mortgages land for a debt he owes, he shall repay from its produce what remains after its expenses, and he shall repay that from that time what he owes, after accounting for the owner’s work and expenses with justice.”"],[6936,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us on the day he arrived at the Hijr of Thamud, at a well near the side of the city, from drinking from it or watering with it, and he forbade us from entering their dwellings. And he informed us that the young of the she-camel ascended a mountain that I heard people call Kinanah, and that its track is clearly visible on its slope."],[6937,"When the Prophet ﷺ went on a military expedition or a journey and then returned to Madinah, he would say: “Returning to our Lord, praising our Lord, worshipping our Lord.”"],[6938,"A man once said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: When the confederates come, forbid the people of Madinah from irrigating the palm trees. He replied: “If I were to make things forbidden for you, you would be ruined. Indeed, the prohibitions of the prophets are things mountains cannot bear.”"],[6939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of extremism and haughtiness, for many of the Children of Israel went to extremes, to the point that a short woman would make two wooden clogs, stuff them, then put her feet into them. Then she would go with a tall woman, and when they walked together, she would be equal to her or even taller.”"],[6940,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, he would say: “O Allah, send down upon our land its adornment. O Allah, send down upon our land its tranquility.”"],[6941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: Banu Ghifar and Aslam were a great trial for many people, who said, ‘If there were any good in them, Allah would not have made them the first to accept it.’ But Ghifar—may Allah forgive it—and Aslam—may Allah grant it peace."],[6942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “One of you will soon wish to look at me even once, giving all his family and wealth for it.”"],[6943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “Soon you will be among the people like salt in food; food is only good with salt.”"],[6944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should kill a captive of his companion once he has taken him.”"],[6945,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “There is none among you but that I am holding onto his waist-wrapper to keep him from falling into the Fire.”"],[6946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “Whoever of you is killed while steadfast, advancing, and being killed in the cause of Allah—he is in Paradise.”"],[6947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the battle cry of the Emigrants ‘O Banu Abd al-Rahman,’ the battle cry of the Khazraj ‘O Banu Abd Allah,’ and the battle cry of the Aws ‘O Banu Ubayd Allah.’ And he named our horses ‘the horses of Allah’ when we were alarmed.”"],[6948,"When we were alarmed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command us to come together, remain steadfast, and be calm, and when we fought."],[6949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “Indeed my Ummah is a community, seventy thousand of them will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[6950,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “We are people of the desert and livestock. Do we need to perform ablution after eating camel meat and drinking its milk?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “Do we need to perform ablution after eating sheep meat and drinking its milk?” He said: “No.”"],[6951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us for one of the two daytime prayers, Zuhr or Asr, carrying al-Hasan or al-Husayn. He came forward and placed him by his right foot, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated and lengthened the prostration. I raised my head from among the people and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating while the boy was riding on his back. I returned to prostration. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, people said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you prostrated in this prayer a prostration you never used to do. Was it something you were commanded to do, or was revelation coming to you?” He said: “None of that. But my son climbed on me, and I disliked to rush him until he finished his need.”"],[6952,"A man from the Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ, believed in him and followed him, and said: “I will emigrate with you.” The Prophet ﷺ instructed his Companions to look after him. When it was the battle of Khaybar – or he said Hunayn – the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired some spoils and distributed them, and allotted a share for him. He gave his Companions what he had allotted for him, and the man was tending their riding animals. When he came, they handed it to him. He said: “What is this?” They said: “A share the Prophet ﷺ allotted for you.” He took it and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muhammad, what is this?” He said: “A share I allotted for you.” He said: “It is not for this that I followed you. I followed you so that I may be shot here,” and he pointed to his throat with an arrow, “and die and enter Paradise.” He ﷺ said: “If you are truthful to Allah, He will be truthful to you.” They waited a little, then they went out to fight the enemy. He was brought back carried, having been struck by an arrow where he had pointed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Is it he?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “He was truthful to Allah, so He was truthful to him.” Then the Prophet ﷺ shrouded him in the Prophet’s own jubbah, then brought him forward and prayed over him. Among what was heard of his prayer over him was: “O Allah, this is Your servant who went out as an emigrant in Your path and was killed as a martyr, and I am a witness for him.”"],[6953,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him for emigration, then fell ill. He ﷺ said: “What is the matter with you, O Shaddad?” I said: “I am ill, O Messenger of Allah. If I could drink from the water of Batha, I would recover.” He said: “What prevents you?” I said: “My emigration.” He said: “Go, for you are an emigrant wherever you are.”"],[6954,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took his hand, and it was softer than silk and cooler than snow."],[6955,"“The wise man is the one who takes account of himself and strives for that which is after death. And the helpless man is the one who follows his own whims then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4260)"],[6956,"I said, “O Messenger of God, how were you taken on the Night Journey?” He said, “I prayed the evening prayer with my companions in Makkah, delaying it. Then Jibrīl ﷺ came to me with a white riding beast, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule. He said, ‘Mount.’ It was difficult for me, so he turned it by its ear, then mounted me upon it. It set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. We came to a land with palm trees. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. Then we mounted. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God knows best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Yathrib; you prayed in Ṭībah.’ Then it set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. We came to a white land. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. Then we mounted. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God knows best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Madyan; you prayed at the tree of Mūsā.’ Then it set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. Then we reached a land whose palaces appeared to us. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Bayt Laḥm, where ʿĪsā the Messiah, son of Maryam ﷺ , was born.’ Then he took me until we entered the city from its Yemeni gate. He came to the qiblah of the mosque and tied his mount. We entered the mosque through a gate where the sun inclines. I prayed in the mosque as much as God willed. I was overcome by the most intense thirst I had ever experienced. Then two vessels were brought to me, in one of them milk and in the other honey. They were both sent to me. I balanced between them, then God ﷻ guided me, and I took the milk and drank until it struck my forehead. Before me was an old man leaning on a cushion of his. He said, ‘Your companion has taken the natural disposition; indeed he is guided.’ Then he took me until we came to the valley that is in the city, and behold, Hell was uncovered like carpets. We said, ‘O Messenger of God, how did you find it?’ He said, ‘Like hot bathwater.’ Then he returned with me, and we passed by a caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such a place. They had lost a camel of theirs, and so-and-so had gathered them. I greeted them, and some of them said, ‘This is the voice of Muhammad ﷺ.’ Then I came to my companions before dawn in Makkah. Abu Bakr ؓ came to me and said, ‘O Messenger of God, where were you tonight? I looked for you in your place.’ He said, ‘Do you know that I went to the Aqsa Mosque tonight?’ He said, ‘O Messenger of God, it is a month’s journey; describe it to me.’ Then its image was opened for me, as if I were looking at it. They did not ask me about anything except that I informed them of it. Abu Bakr ؓ said, ‘I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.’ The polytheists said, ‘Look at Ibn Abī Kabshah, claiming that he came to the Aqsa Mosque tonight.’ He said, ‘Among the signs of what I tell you is that I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such a place, led by a gray camel with a black saddlecloth and two black sacks.’ When that day came, the people looked out, and around midday the caravan came led by that same camel described by the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[6957,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “There will come upon you leaders who will delay the prayer beyond its proper times, so pray the prayer at its proper time and make your prayer with them a voluntary one.”"],[6958,"More than one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, among them Shaddad b. Aws and Thawban, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The pen is lifted from the minor until he grows up, from the sleeping person until he wakes, from the insane until he regains his senses, and from the feeble-minded imbecile.”"],[6959,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When people hoard dinars and dirhams, hoard these words: O God, I ask You for steadfastness in the affair and determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.”"],[6960,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O people, indeed this world is a passing enjoyment, from which the righteous and the wicked both eat, and indeed the Hereafter is a true promise, in which a Mighty King will judge, by which He will establish the truth and nullify falsehood. O people, be people of the Hereafter, and do not be people of this world, for every child follows its mother.”"],[6961,"He would hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a matter involving hardship, then he would go out to his desert land, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would later grant a concession in it, and the concession would be preserved from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in that matter. Abu Dharr would not hear it, so Abu Dharr would adhere to the first command that he had heard before that.”"],[6962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will not spend any expense seeking the Face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even what you place in your wife’s mouth.”"],[6963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.'"],[6964,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: There is no servant who, when he enters upon morning and when he enters upon evening, says: O Allah, You are my Lord. There is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive my sins, for none forgives them but You - if he dies that day, he will enter Paradise, and if he dies that night, he will enter Paradise."],[6965,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning leadership and he said: The first part of leadership is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment from Allah on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who shows mercy and acts justly. And he said, moving his hand like this and like this regarding wealth, then he fell silent for as long as Allah willed, then he said: 'How can there be justice when it comes to relatives?'"],[6966,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not inform you of the chief of seeking forgiveness?' They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'O Allah, there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge to You Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge to You my sins, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. No one says it when evening falls and then dies that night except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and no one says it when morning comes and then death comes to him except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"],[6967,"‘The cupper and the one for whom cupping is done both break their fast.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1679)"],[6968,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up after two rakʿahs of prayer and did not sit until he finished his prayer; then he prostrated twice, then he said the salām.”"],[6969,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a wen on my palm and said: O Prophet of God, this wen has harmed me; it comes between me and the grip of the sword when I wish to grasp it, and between me and the rein of the mount. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Come close to me.” So I came close to him. He said: “Open your hand.” So I opened it. Then he said: “Close it.” So I closed it. He said: “Come close to me.” So I came close to him. He said: “Open it.” So I opened it. He then blew on my palm, placed his hand on the wen, and kept rubbing it with his palm until he lifted his hand, and I could see no trace of it."],[6970,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had finished with the people of Badr, bringing a colt of my mare called al-Qarḥāʾ. I said: O Muhammad, I have brought you the colt of al-Qarḥāʾ so that you may take it. He said: “I have no need for it, but if you wish, I can give you in exchange for it the select coats of mail from Badr.” I said: I would not exchange it today for anything else. He said: “I have no need for it.” Then he said: “O Dhū al-Jawshan, will you not become a Muslim, so that you may be among the first of this affair?” I said: No. He said: “Why?” I said: I have seen your people making light of you. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said in his narration: making a game of you. He said: “How did the news of their defeats at Badr reach you?” I said: It has reached me. He said: “Would it surprise you?” I said: Yes — only if you gain mastery over the Kaʿbah and settle in it. He said: “Perhaps, if you live, you will see that.” Then he said: “O Bilāl, take the man's saddlebag and provision him with some ʿajwah dates.” When I turned to leave, he said: “Indeed, he is among the best horsemen of Banū ʿĀmir.” By God, I was still with my family at al-Fawr when a rider approached. I said: From where? He said: From Makkah. I said: What have the people done? He said: By God, Muhammad ﷺ has gained mastery over it and settled in it. I said: May my mother be bereft of me! By God, if I had become a Muslim on that day and then asked him for al-Ḥīrah, he would have granted it to me as a fief. Abu Muslim said: Musaddad said: It has reached me from Ibn al-Mubārak that he said: His name was Shuraḥbīl, and he was called Dhū al-Jawshan only because he was prominent in the chest."],[6971,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no one but has a devil.” They said: And you? He said: “And me, except that God helped me against it.”"],[6972,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever commits adultery, faith departs from him; whoever drinks wine without being forced or compelled, faith departs from him; and whoever plunders a spoil that people keep looking at, faith departs from him — but if he repents, God will turn to him.”"],[6973,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication for protection with which I may seek refuge. He took my hand and said: Say: I seek refuge in You from the evil of my self, from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my tongue, from the evil of my heart, and from my manī. Then he said to me: “Memorize it.” Saʿd said: Manī is his semen."],[6974,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: Four people will torment the inhabitants of the Fire on top of the torment they already have; they run between the ḥamīm and the jaḥīm, calling out with woe and destruction. The inhabitants of the Fire say to one another: What is the matter with these ones? They have tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He said: One is a man with a chest of embers locked upon him; one is a man dragging his intestines; one is a man whose mouth flows with pus and blood; and one is a man eating his own flesh. It will be said to the one with the chest: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He will say: The distant one died while people's wealth was on his neck, and we find no settlement or repayment for it. Then it will be said to the one dragging his intestines: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. It will be said: The distant one did not care if urine got on him and did not wash it. Then it will be said to the one whose mouth flows with pus and blood: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He will say: The distant one used to eat the flesh of people."],[6975,"Umar (said): “A man came who would testify only to truth.” He said: “I saw an ugly sight and a dazzling display.” He said: “So Umar flogged them the prescribed punishment.”"],[6976,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir on the days of tashriq until he left Mina, saying the takbir after every prayer.”"],[6977,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Salm b. Abi al-Dhayyal, from Abu Sinan, a man from the people of Madinah who heard Jabir b. Abd Allah narrate from Shihab, a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who used to reside in Egypt, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever conceals the private shame of a believer, it is as if he has brought a dead person back to life.”"],[6978,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had placed his hand on his thigh, pointing with his index finger and saying: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.”"],[6979,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Umm Mildam (fever) eats the flesh and drinks the blood; its cold and its heat are from Hell.”"],[6980,"He heard Anas b. Malik, Shu'ayb b. Amr, and Najiyah b. Amr say: “We saw the Prophet ﷺ dye (his hair).”"],[6981,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Tell me about a man who committed all sins, leaving none of them, and along with that he did not leave any need or desire but that he fulfilled it. Is there any repentance for him?” He said: “Have you embraced Islam?” He said: “As for me, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that you are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Yes, do good deeds and abandon evil deeds, and Allah will turn them all into good deeds for you.” He said: “And my treacheries and my immoralities?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Allah is greatest,” and he kept saying the takbir until he disappeared."],[6982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him, as long as he is in greater need of it.'"],[6983,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my mother bequeathed that a slave be freed on her behalf, and I have a black female servant.' He said, 'Call her.' She came, and he said, 'Who is your Lord?' She said, 'Allah.' He said, 'Who am I?' She said, 'The Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Then free her, for she is a believer.'"],[6984,"Al-Sharid came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah granted you victory over Makkah, I would pray in Jerusalem.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Pray here,' three times."],[6985,"\"However much I forget, I have never forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing in prayer, his right hand over his left, holding them together.\""],[6986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Circumcision is a sunnah for men and a noble act for women.”"],[6987,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Circumcision is a sunnah for men and a noble act for women.”"],[6988,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, two things: he said: “Allah ﷻ has prescribed excellence in all things. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.”"],[6989,"Two things I heard from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “Allah has prescribed excellence in all things. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.”"],[6990,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ has prescribed excellence in all things. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.”"],[6991,"“Allah has prescribed Al-Ihsan (proficiency) in all things. So if you kill, then kill well, and if you slaughter, then slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and spare suffering to the animal he slaughters.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3170)"],[6992,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his slaughtered animal.”"],[6993,"I memorized two things from the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: “God, exalted is He, is excellent and loves excellence. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade, then give rest to his slaughtered animal.”"],[6994,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “God, exalted is He, has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his slaughtered animal.”"],[6995,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, has prescribed excellence in everything. So when you kill, kill well; and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let one of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his slaughtered animal.”"],[6996,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[6997,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man being cupped on the eighteenth of Ramadan while I was with him, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[6998,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[6999,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon a man while he was being cupped at al-Baqi‘ on the eighteenth day of Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7000,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man being cupped at the time of the conquest, on the eighteenth day of Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7001,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the year of the conquest, and he passed by a man being cupped on the eighteenth or seventeenth of Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7002,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Ma‘qil b. Yasar in the month of Ramadan while he was being cupped, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7003,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man being cupped in Ramadan, and he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7004,"He said, \"I used to walk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in some streets of Medina while he held my hand, when he saw a man shaving in Ramadan, he said, 'The one who shaves and the one who is being shaved have both broken their fast.'\""],[7005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites a line of poetry after the evening prayer, God will not accept any prayer from him that night.”"],[7006,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever performs the full bath and bathes on Friday, then goes early and arrives before the imam, then sits close to the imam and listens attentively, for every step he takes he will have the reward of a year’s fasting and night prayer.”"],[7007,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O Shaddād b. Aws, when you see people hoarding gold and silver, then hoard these words: O God, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and resolve upon right guidance. I ask You for the means that entail Your mercy and the firm resolutions for Your forgiveness. I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing and excellence in worshipping You. I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue. I ask You for the good that You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil that You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. Indeed, You are the Knower of the unseen.”"],[7008,"Shaddād said to him, “Rejoice, for these are expiations for evil deeds and removers of sins. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘God ﷻ says: When I test one of My believing servants and he praises Me for what I have tested him with, then he rises from his bed as free of sins as the day his mother bore him.’ And the Lord ﷻ says, ‘I have restrained this servant of Mine and tested him, so record for him what you used to record for him when he was healthy.’”"],[7009,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, he should not walk in a single sandal.”"],[7010,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The woman, if she kills intentionally, is not to be killed until she gives birth to what is in her womb if she is pregnant, and until she has weaned her child. And if she commits adultery, she is not to be stoned until she gives birth to what is in her womb and until she has weaned her child.”"],[7011,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever prays in order to show off has committed shirk; whoever fasts in order to show off has committed shirk; whoever gives charity in order to show off has committed shirk.”"],[7012,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The worst of this community will indeed follow the ways of those who came before them from the People of the Book, just as one arrow matches another.”"],[7013,"“The wise man is the one who takes account of himself and strives for that which is after death. And the helpless man is the one who follows his own whims then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4260)"],[7014,"“Two hadiths I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said, “I said, ‘What are they?’ He said, ‘I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and saw something in his face that displeased me. I said, “O Messenger of God, what is this that I see in your face?” He said, “Two matters I fear for my community after me: shirk and hidden desire. Indeed, they will not worship the sun, the moon, a stone, or an idol, but they will show off with their deeds.” I said, “O Messenger of God, is that shirk?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “And what is hidden desire?” He said, “A servant begins the day fasting, then a desire from his desires presents itself to him, and he indulges in it and abandons his fast.”’”"],[7015,"From a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioning it: “Among the things I fear most for my community are shirk with God and hidden desire. A man begins the day fasting, then he sees something he desires and indulges in it. And shirk is a people who do not worship a stone or an idol, but they do deeds in order to show off.”"],[7016,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God ﷻ wrote a book two thousand years before creating the heavens and the earth, and sent down in it two verses with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights except that no devil comes near it.”"],[7017,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7018,"While I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ on one of the roads of Madinah, with the Messenger of God ﷺ holding my hand, on the eighteenth of Ramadan, he came upon a man being cupped and said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7019,"While the Prophet ﷺ was holding my hand on the eighteenth of Ramadan, he turned and saw a man being cupped and said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7020,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by on the eighteenth of Ramadan and saw a man being cupped and said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7021,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon a man while he was being cupped on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7022,"I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was holding my hand on the morning of the eighteenth, and he happened to turn and saw a man being cupped, so he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7023,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the eighteenth of Ramadan and he saw a man being cupped, so he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7024,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the eighteenth of Ramadan and he saw a man being cupped, so he said: “The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.”"],[7025,"I sat with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, among them Shaddad b. Aws and Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while they were reminding one another. They said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man may perform such-and-such good deeds while he is a hypocrite.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, how can he be a hypocrite while he believes in you?” He said: “He curses the leaders and slanders them.”"],[7026,"“We used to consider showing off in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as minor shirk (associating partners with Allah).”"],[7027,"And he said: “Do you two know what makes me sit between you? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When you see the two of them together, separate them, for by Allah, they never come together except for treachery.’ So I wanted to separate you two.”"],[7028,"That he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was dying. He said: “What is the matter with you, O Shaddad?” He said: “The world has become constricted for me.” So he said: “It will not be upon you. Syria will be conquered and Jerusalem will be conquered, and you and your children will be leaders among them, if Allah wills.”"],[7029,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of a man from his Companions. He said: “Check whether there is any stranger among you.” They said: “No.” He said: “Close the door.” So he closed the door, then said: “Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands and we raised our hands. Then he said: “Put down your hands and rejoice, for you have been forgiven. I was sent with it, and with it I was commanded, and upon it I will enter Paradise.”"],[7030,"From his father or another Companion of the Prophet ﷺ – Hilal was uncertain – he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pray in your sandals and do not imitate the Jews.”"],[7031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pray in your sandals; differ from the Jews.”"],[7032,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When Allah gathers the first and the last in one open plain, sight will pierce them and the caller will make them hear.” He said: “I am the best partner. Every deed that was done for Me in the world in which someone else was associated with Me, I abandon it today and accept only what is purely for Me.” Then he recited: {Except the sincere servants of Allah} and {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteous deeds and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord}."],[7033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you attend your dying ones, close their eyes, for the sight follows the soul, and say good, for it is affirmed upon what the family says.”"],[7034,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “He is not a liar who says something good or reports something good.”"],[7035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever wrongs even a handspan's worth of land, a collar of it will be put around his neck from seven earths, and whoever is killed unjustly, then he is a martyr.\""],[7036,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The chief of seeking forgiveness is that you say: O Allah, You are my Lord. There is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. If he says it after evening falls and then dies that night, he will enter Paradise; and if he says it after morning comes and then dies that day, he will enter Paradise."],[7037,"Shall I not teach you what the Prophet ﷺ used to teach us: 'O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your favor and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.' He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'There is no Muslim servant who recites a surah from the Book of Allah when he goes to sleep but that Allah appoints an angel for him, so that nothing harmful comes near him until he wakes up, whenever he wakes up.'"],[7038,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever recites a surah from the Qur'an when he takes to his bed, an angel is appointed for him to guard him until he wakes up, whenever he wakes up.' And I heard him say: 'I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, and I ask You for determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your favor, and I ask You for excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know.'"],[7039,"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say in his prayer: 'O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your favor and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.'"],[7040,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his prayer: 'O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your favor and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.'"],[7041,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Poverty is more becoming upon the believer than a fine blaze upon the cheek of a horse.'"],[7042,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing you will lose from your religion is trustworthiness.'"],[7043,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The first thing to be lifted from people is humility.\""],[7044,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Shall I not guide you to the chief of seeking forgiveness? It is that you say: 'O Allah, You are my God. You created me, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and I acknowledge to You Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge to You my sins. For none forgives sins but You. There is no servant who says it and then his appointed time comes to him during his day before evening falls, or during his evening before morning comes, except that he will be among the people of Paradise, if Allah wills.'"],[7045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Kaaba and did not pray in it. He said: 'They lied. He ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars, then pressed his belly and back against them.'"],[7046,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Hunayn. By Allah, it was not Islam that brought me out, nor any knowledge of it, but I disdained that Hawazin should prevail over Quraysh. I said while standing with him: 'O Messenger of Allah, I see piebald horses?' He said: 'O Shaybah, none sees them but a disbeliever.' Then he struck my chest with his hand and said: 'O Allah, guide Shaybah.' Then he struck it a second time and said: 'O Allah, guide Shaybah.' Then he struck it a third time and said: 'O Allah, guide Shaybah.' By Allah, he had not lifted his hand from my chest after the third time before there was no one among Allah's creation more beloved to me than him. He said: Then the people met, and the Prophet ﷺ was on a she-camel or a mule, with 'Umar holding its bridle and al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib driving his mount. The Muslims were routed, so al-'Abbas called out with his loud voice: 'Where are the first Muhajirun? Where are the companions of Surat al-Baqarah?' while the Prophet ﷺ was saying: 'Forward! I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.' The Muslims turned back and clashed with swords, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Now the battle has grown hot.' He said: And Allah defeated the polytheists."],[7047,"Shaybah b. 'Uthman said: When the Prophet ﷺ raided Hunayn, I remembered my father and my uncle, whom 'Ali and Hamzah had killed, and I said: 'Today I will avenge my blood on Muhammad.' I came to him and found al-'Abbas on his right, wearing a white coat of mail that looked like silver, and the dust had settled on it. I said: 'His uncle will not forsake him.' Then I came to his left and found Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith. I said: 'His cousin, and he will not forsake him.' Then I came from behind him and drew closer and closer until there was nothing left but for me to strike him with the sword. Then a flame of fire rose up before me like lightning, and I feared it would burn me, so I retreated backwards. The Prophet ﷺ turned to me and said: 'Come, O Shayb.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on my chest, and Allah extracted the devil from my heart. I raised my eyes to him, and he was dearer to me than my hearing, my sight, and such-and-such. Then he said to me: 'O Shayb, fight the disbelievers.' Then he said: 'O 'Abbas, call out to the Muhajirun who pledged allegiance under the tree and to the Ansar who gave shelter and helped.' I never likened the turning of the Ansar to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except to cows turning to their calves, until they gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like a thicket. He said: The spears of the Ansar were more frightening to me for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the spears of the disbelievers. Then he said: 'O 'Ayyash, hand me some pebbles from the valley.' He said: Allah made the mule understand his words, and it lowered itself until its belly almost touched the ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took some pebbles and blew into their faces, saying: 'May the faces be ugly! Ha Mim, they will not be helped.'"],[7048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Kaaba and prayed two rak'ahs. He saw images in it and said: 'O Shaybah, rid me of these.' Shaybah found that hard. A man from Persia said to him: 'If you wish, I will coat and smear them with saffron,' and he did."],[7049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf and said: 'Three things, the heart of a believer never harbors treachery regarding them: sincere devotion in action, good counsel to the leaders of the Muslims, and keeping to their community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them.'"],[7050,"A man sent with me some dirhams as a gift to the House. I entered the House while Shaybah was sitting on a chair, and I handed them to him. He said: 'Are these for you?' I said: 'No, and if they were mine, I would not have brought them to you.' He said: 'Since you have said that, 'Umar b. al-Khattab sat in your seat where you are sitting and said: \"I will not leave until I distribute what is in the Kaaba among the poor Muslims.\" I said: \"You will not do that.\" He said: \"I will certainly do it. And why is that?\" I said: \"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw its place, and so did Abu Bakr ؓ, and they were more in need of this wealth than you, yet they did not move it.\" So he got up as he was and left.'"],[7051,"'Umar sat with me in this seat of yours and said: 'I have resolved not to leave in it any gold or silver except that I distribute it, meaning the Kaaba.' Shaybah said: I said to him: 'You had two companions who did not do so: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ.' 'Umar ؓ said: 'Those are the two men I follow.'"],[7052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you comes to a gathering, if room is made for him, let him sit; otherwise, let him look for the widest place he sees and sit there.'"],[7053,"He came and stayed with Abu Kulthum al-Dawsi. They discussed the middle prayer, and he said: 'We differed about it just as you have differed, while we were in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ house. Among us was the righteous man Abu Hashim b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah b. 'Abd Shams. He said: \"I know that for you.\" So he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being bold with him, asked permission, entered, then came out to us and told us that it is the 'Asr prayer.'"],[7054,"Mu'awiyah ؓ said to him: 'What makes you weep? Is it pain that troubles you, or is it for the world, whose clear part has gone?' He said: 'For neither. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with me, and I wish I had followed it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perhaps you will live to see wealth distributed among peoples. But enough for you from gathering wealth is a servant and a mount.\" But I found and gathered.'"],[7055,"O uncle, what makes you weep? Is it pain that troubles you, or greed for the world? He said: 'Neither. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with me that I did not keep. He said: \"O Abu Hashim, you will see wealth given to peoples. Enough for you from all the world is a servant and a mount in the way of Allah.\" And today I see that I have gathered.'"],[7056,"Muawiyah entered upon his uncle, and when he saw him, he said, \"Why do you look anxious and eager for the world?\" His uncle replied, \"No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'You may come across people who value wealth, but it is enough for one of you to have a house and a means of transportation in the way of Allah.'\""],[7057,"About what has come from the Prophet ﷺ regarding trimming the mustache? He said: 'I had trimmed my mustache and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He passed his hand over it and said: \"When did you trim your mustache?\" I said: \"Just now.\" He said: \"Do not trim it until you meet me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died before I met him, so I will never cut it until I meet him.'"],[7058,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Numbness of the face from nabīdh causes good deeds to fall away.”"],[7059,"I was playing with my wife, and I struck her on my hand, and she died — that was during the campaign of the Messenger of God ﷺ to Tabūk. I came to him and told him about my wife whom I had struck by mistake, and he said: “You do not inherit from her.”"],[7060,"It is also said that he was from Kindah."],[7061,"From Mūsā b. ʿUqbah: “Regarding the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia and remained there until arriving after Badr: Shuraḥbīl b. ʿAbd Allāh, and his mother was Ḥasanah.”"],[7062,"“Shuraḥbīl ibn Ḥasanah died — his kunyah was Abū ʿAbd Allāh — in the year 17 or 18, aged sixty-seven, and he was a governor for ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[7063,"“Abū ʿUbaydah, Shuraḥbīl ibn Ḥasanah, and Abū Mālik were all struck by the plague on a single day.”"],[7064,"ʿAmr lied. I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ, while ʿAmr is more astray than the donkey of his family. “Rather, it is a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.”"],[7065,"This defilement has fallen; disperse from it. Ibn Ḥasanah said: “I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he is more astray than the donkey of his family. It is only a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you, so gather around him and do not disperse from him.” That reached ʿAmr, and he said: “He spoke the truth.”"],[7066,"From Shuraḥbīl b. Aws al-Kindī, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If he drinks wine, flog him; if he drinks it a second time, flog him; if he drinks it a third time, flog him; if he drinks it a fourth time, kill him.”"],[7067,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a tall, fair-complexioned bedouin came to him and said: “O Messenger of God, an old man with a boiling fever that will bring him to the graves.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “An old man with a boiling fever — it is an expiation and purification for him.” He repeated it, and the Prophet ﷺ repeated his response; he repeated it three or four times. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Since you insist, it is as you say, and what God has decreed will come to pass.” He said: By the next evening he was dead."],[7068,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever finds livelihood difficult, let him go to ʿUmān.”"],[7069,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say to ʿAlī ؓ: “Rejoice, O ʿAlī — your life and your death are with me.”"],[7070,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy and grace from Him.”"],[7071,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter Paradise by his deeds.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy and grace from Him.”"],[7072,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy.”"],[7073,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is not one among you whom his deeds will cause to enter Paradise.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy from Him.”"],[7074,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is none of you but has a devil.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, except that God helped me against it, so it submitted.”"],[7075,"He went early to the mosque and sat by one of the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ. He heard his voice, and he said: “Abu Yahya?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Enter.” He entered, and the Prophet ﷺ was having lunch. He said: “Come to lunch.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I intend to fast.” He said: “And I intend to fast. Our muezzin has weak eyesight; he called the adhan before dawn.”"],[7076,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir on the days of tashriq from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until he left Mina.”"],[7077,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is not ashamed of what he said or what was said to him, then he is not of sound maturity; his mother bore him without purity.”"],[7078,"The Prophet ﷺ seated me behind him and said: “Do you not recite to me something of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Go on.” So I recited to him one hundred verses, or one hundred rhyming lines; every time I came to a verse or a rhyming line, he said: “Go on.”"],[7079,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Do you have with you anything of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Go on.” So I recited a verse to him, and he kept saying: “Go on.” I recited a verse to him, and he kept saying: “Go on,” and I kept reciting to him until I had recited one hundred verses."],[7080,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Do you have any poetry with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then recite something to me.\" So I recited one verse, then I stopped. He said, \"Go on.\" So I recited one verse, then I stopped. He said, \"Go on.\" So I recited one verse, until I had recited one hundred verses, then I stopped and he was silent."],[7081,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had let his lower garment hang down, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Raise your lower garment.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of God, I am bow-legged; my knees knock together.\" He said, \"Raise your lower garment, for all of God's creation is beautiful.\" After that, the man was not seen except with his lower garment reaching halfway down his shins."],[7082,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man letting his lower garment hang down, so he hurried towards him or hastened towards him and said, \"Raise your lower garment and fear God.\" The man said, \"I have bow legs; my knees knock together.\" He said, \"All of God's creation is beautiful.\" He said, \"After that, the man was not seen except with his lower garment reaching halfway down his shins or hitting the middle of his shins.\" Asad b. Musa did not mention in his hadith the uncertainty about 'Amr b. al-Sharid and Ya'qub b. 'Asim."],[7083,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was sitting like this, leaning on the back of his hand behind his back, and said, \"This is the sitting posture of those upon whom is [God's] wrath.\""],[7084,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had sat down and leaned on his left hand, and he said, \"This is the sitting posture of those upon whom is [God's] wrath.\""],[7085,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"If one of you drinks [intoxicants], flog him. If he repeats, flog him. Then if he repeats, flog him. Then if he repeats a fourth time, kill him.\""],[7086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever kills a sparrow in vain, it will cry out to God on the Day of Resurrection, saying, 'O Lord, this servant of Yours killed me in vain and did not kill me for any benefit.'\""],[7087,"A leper came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, so I went to him and mentioned him. He said, \"Go to him and inform him that I have accepted his pledge, so let him return.\""],[7088,"\"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks.\""],[7089,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Delay by a wealthy person makes his honor and punishment permissible.\""],[7090,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Delay by a wealthy person makes his honor and punishment permissible.\" Sufyan said, \"Makes his honor permissible means that one may complain about him, and his punishment means his imprisonment. The correct reading is Wabar b. Abi Dulaylah, with a damma on the dal. Al-Nu'man b. 'Abd al-Salam narrated it from Sufyan and said, \"'Amr, from Wabar b. Abi Dalilah,\" with a fatha on the dal."],[7091,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking about something concerning camels. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Slaughter the fat one, ride the thin one, milk on the day of watering, and enter Paradise in peace.\""],[7092,"A woman was stoned during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we finished with her, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'We have stoned this wicked woman.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The stoning is an expiation for what she did.'"],[7093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him.'"],[7094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him.' I said to 'Umar, 'What is al-saqab?' He said, 'Neighborliness.'"],[7095,"The Prophet ﷺ would grant preemption in a well, a house, and a walled garden before it was divided."],[7096,"While al-Sharid was walking between Mina and the mountain pass during the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he performed, he said: I heard the sound of a camel behind me, so I turned and it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He recognized me and said, 'Al-Sharid?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Shall I carry you behind me, O Sharid?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, though I am not tired or exhausted, but I seek blessing in riding with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'O Sharid, do you have any of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?' I said, 'I am the best of people in narrating it.' He said, 'Recite.' So I recited, and whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was silent, I stopped, and whenever he said, 'Continue,' I recited until it went on for a long time. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has knowledge of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt.'"],[7097,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb died, may Allah have mercy on him, nine years into the rule of 'Uthman ؓ, and Abu Sufyan b. Harb had lost his sight."],[7098,"In that year Abu Sufyan Sakhr b. Harb died, and he was eighty-eight years old, meaning in the year thirty-one."],[7099,"Umayyah said to me, 'O Abu Sufyan, shall we go ahead of the caravan and talk?' I said, 'Yes.' So we did, and he said to me, 'O Abu Sufyan, what about 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah?' I said, 'What about 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah?' He said, 'Noble on both sides, who avoids injustices and forbidden things?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And an elder of high rank?' I said, 'And an elder of high rank.' He said, 'Age and rank have diminished him.' I said to him, 'You lie; he only increases in honor as he increases in age.' He said, 'O Abu Sufyan, this is a word I have not heard anyone say to me since I became a Christian. Do not be hasty with me until I tell you.' I said, 'Proceed.' He said, 'I used to find in my books a prophet who would be sent from this region of ours, and I thought—rather I did not doubt—that I was him. But when I studied with the people of knowledge, he was from Banu 'Abd Manaf. I looked among Banu 'Abd Manaf and found no one suitable for this matter except 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah. When you told me his age, I knew it was not him, since he had passed forty and had not received revelation.' Abu Sufyan said: Time passed, and revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I set out with a group of Quraysh to Yemen for trade and passed by Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt. I said to him, as if mocking, 'O Umayyah, the prophet you were waiting for has emerged.' He said, 'Indeed, it is true, so follow him.' I said, 'What prevents you from following him?' He said, 'Nothing prevents me from following him except shyness before the women of Thaqif. I used to tell them that I was him, and then they would see me following a young man from Banu 'Abd Manaf.' Then Umayyah said, 'And it is as if, O Abu Sufyan, if I oppose him, I will be tied up as a kid is tied until you are brought to him and he judges in your case as he wishes.'"],[7100,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with twelve thousand, comprising the Muhajirun, the Ansar, Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, and Banu Sulaym, and they led the horses until they encamped at Marr al-Zahran, and Quraysh did not know about them. They sent Abu Sufyan and Hakim b. Hizam to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Secure for us a guarantee of protection from him, or give him notice of war.' Abu Sufyan b. Harb and Hakim b. Hizam went out and met Budayl b. Warqa', so they took him as a companion. When they were at al-Arak, near Makkah, and that was at nightfall, they saw the tents and the army and heard the neighing of the horses, and that alarmed and frightened them. They said, 'These are Banu Ka'b whom war has stirred up.' Budayl said, 'These are more than Banu Ka'b; their gathering has not reached this extent. Would Hawazin seek pasture in our land? By Allah, we do not recognize this either; this is like the pilgrimage of the people.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent cavalry ahead to seize scouts, and Khuza'ah was on the road, not letting anyone pass. When Abu Sufyan and his companions entered the Muslim camp, the cavalry seized them under cover of night and brought them fearing execution. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ went to Abu Sufyan and struck his neck, and the people grabbed him and took him out to bring him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The guards prevented him from reaching the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he feared being killed. Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ had been his close friend in the pre-Islamic era, so Abu Sufyan called at the top of his voice, 'Will you take me to 'Abbas?' He came to him and defended him, and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hand him over to him. He went among the people in his place, and 'Abbas rode with him under cover of night and moved through the army camp until they all saw him. 'Umar ؓ had said to Abu Sufyan when he struck his neck, 'By Allah, you will not approach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until you die.' So he sought help from 'Abbas and said, 'I am going to be killed.' 'Abbas protected him from the people so they would not seize him. When he saw the size of the army and their obedience, he said, 'I have never seen a gathering of people like tonight.' 'Abbas saved him from their hands and said, 'You will be killed if you do not submit and bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' He kept trying to say what 'Abbas commanded him, but his tongue would not obey. So he spent the night with 'Abbas. As for Hakim b. Hizam and Budayl b. Warqa', they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accepted Islam, and he began asking them about the people of Makkah. When the call to the dawn prayer was made, the people stirred, and Abu Sufyan was startled and said, 'O 'Abbas, what do they want?' He said, 'They are the Muslims preparing to attend the Prophet ﷺ.' 'Abbas took him out, and when Abu Sufyan saw them passing to the prayer, bowing and prostrating in their prayer, whenever they prostrated he said, 'O 'Abbas, does he not command them to do anything but they do it?' 'Abbas said, 'If he forbade them food and drink, they would obey him.' He said, 'O 'Abbas, then speak to him about your people; does he have any pardon for them?' So 'Abbas took Abu Sufyan and brought him before the Prophet ﷺ. 'Abbas said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Sufyan.' Abu Sufyan said, 'O Muhammad, I sought help from my god and sought help from your God. By Allah, I have never met you but you prevailed over me. If my god had been right and your God false, I would have prevailed over you.' Then he bore witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. 'Abbas said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I would like you to permit me to go to your people and warn them of what has come and call them to Allah and His Messenger.' He permitted him. 'Abbas said, 'How should I speak to them, O Messenger of Allah? Make clear to me a guarantee of safety that they can rely on.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Say to them: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and bears witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and withholds his hand, he is safe. Whoever sits at the Ka'bah and lays down his weapon, he is safe. Whoever locks his door upon himself, he is safe.'"],[7101,"Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went out with twelve thousand of the Muhājirūn, the Anṣār, Ghifār, Aslam, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, and Banū Sulaym. They led the horses until they camped at Marr al-Ẓahrān, and Quraysh did not know of them. So they sent Abū Sufyān and Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “Obtain for us from him a guarantee of protection, or warn him of war.” Abū Sufyān b. Ḥarb and Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām set out and met Budayl b. Warqāʾ and took him as a companion. When they reached al-Arāk near Makkah, at night, they saw the tents and the army and heard the neighing of horses. This alarmed and frightened them, and they said, “These are Banū Kaʿb, stirred up by war.” Budayl said, “These are more than Banū Kaʿb; their mobilization has never reached this extent. Would Hawāzin raid our land? By God, we do not recognize this either. This is like the pilgrimage of the people.” The Messenger of God ﷺ had sent ahead cavalry to seize scouts, and Khuzāʿah were on the road, not letting anyone pass. When Abū Sufyān and his companions entered the Muslim camp, the cavalry seized them under cover of night and brought them in fear of execution. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ rose to Abū Sufyān and struck his neck, and the people seized him and took him to bring him before the Messenger of God ﷺ. The guards prevented him from reaching the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he feared for his life. Al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib ؓ had been his close friend in the Jāhiliyyah, so he cried out at the top of his voice, “Will you not direct me to ʿAbbās?” He came to him, defended him, and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to hand him over to him, and he walked among the people in his place. ʿAbbās mounted him under cover of night and rode with him through the camp until they all saw him. ʿUmar ؓ had said to Abū Sufyān when he struck his neck, “By God, you will not come near the Messenger of God ﷺ until you die.” So he sought ʿAbbās’s help and said, “I am a dead man.” He prevented the people from plundering him. When he saw the size of the army and their obedience, he said, “I have never seen such a gathering for a people as tonight.” ʿAbbās rescued him from their hands and said, “You will be killed if you do not submit and testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God.” He kept trying to say what ʿAbbās commanded, but his tongue would not utter it. He spent the night with ʿAbbās. As for Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām and Budayl b. Warqāʾ, they entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and embraced Islam, and he asked them about the people of Makkah. When the call to the morning prayer was made, the people stirred, and Abū Sufyān was alarmed and said, “O ʿAbbās, what do they intend?” He said, “They are the Muslims preparing to attend upon the Prophet ﷺ.” ʿAbbās brought him out, and when Abū Sufyān saw them passing to prayer, bowing and prostrating in their prayer whenever he prostrated, he said, “O ʿAbbās, does he not command them to do anything but that they do it?” ʿAbbās said, “If he forbade them food and drink, they would obey him.” He said, “O ʿAbbās, speak to him about your people. Does he have any pardon for them?” ʿAbbās then took Abū Sufyān and brought him before the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAbbās said, “O Messenger of God, this is Abū Sufyān.” Abū Sufyān said, “O Muḥammad, I have sought the aid of my god and sought the aid of your God. By God, I have never met you in battle but that you prevailed over me. If my god had been right and your God false, I would have prevailed over you.” Then he testified that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God. ʿAbbās said, “O Messenger of God, I would like you to permit me to go to your people, warn them of what has befallen, and call them to God and His Messenger.” He granted him permission. ʿAbbās said, “How shall I speak to them, O Messenger of God? Explain to me a guarantee of safety they can rely on.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Say to them: Whoever testifies that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and testifies that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God, and withholds his hand, he is safe. Whoever sits by the Kaʿbah and lays down his weapon, he is safe. Whoever locks his door, he is safe.”"],[7102,"Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went out with twelve thousand of the Muhājirūn, the Anṣār, Ghifār, Aslam, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, and Banū Sulaym. They led the horses until they camped at Marr al-Ẓahrān, and Quraysh did not know of them. So they sent Abū Sufyān and Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “Obtain for us from him a guarantee of protection, or warn him of war.” Abū Sufyān b. Ḥarb and Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām set out and met Budayl b. Warqāʾ and took him as a companion. When they reached al-Arāk near Makkah, at night, they saw the tents and the army and heard the neighing of horses. This alarmed and frightened them, and they said, “These are Banū Kaʿb, stirred up by war.” Budayl said, “These are more than Banū Kaʿb; their mobilization has never reached this extent. Would Hawāzin raid our land? By God, we do not recognize this either. This is like the pilgrimage of the people.” The Messenger of God ﷺ had sent ahead cavalry to seize scouts, and Khuzāʿah were on the road, not letting anyone pass. When Abū Sufyān and his companions entered the Muslim camp, the cavalry seized them under cover of night and brought them in fear of execution. ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ rose to Abū Sufyān and struck his neck, and the people seized him and took him to bring him before the Messenger of God ﷺ. The guards prevented him from reaching the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he feared for his life. Al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib ؓ had been his close friend in the Jāhiliyyah, so he cried out at the top of his voice, “Will you not direct me to ʿAbbās?” He came to him, defended him, and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to hand him over to him, and he walked among the people in his place. ʿAbbās mounted him under cover of night and rode with him through the camp until they all saw him. ʿUmar ؓ had said to Abū Sufyān when he struck his neck, “By God, you will not come near the Messenger of God ﷺ until you die.” So he sought ʿAbbās’s help and said, “I am a dead man.” He prevented the people from plundering him. When he saw the size of the army and their obedience, he said, “I have never seen such a gathering for a people as tonight.” ʿAbbās rescued him from their hands and said, “You will be killed if you do not submit and testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God.” He kept trying to say what ʿAbbās commanded, but his tongue would not utter it. He spent the night with ʿAbbās. As for Ḥakīm b. Ḥizām and Budayl b. Warqāʾ, they entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and embraced Islam, and he asked them about the people of Makkah. When the call to the morning prayer was made, the people stirred, and Abū Sufyān was alarmed and said, “O ʿAbbās, what do they intend?” He said, “They are the Muslims preparing to attend upon the Prophet ﷺ.” ʿAbbās brought him out, and when Abū Sufyān saw them passing to prayer, bowing and prostrating in their prayer whenever he prostrated, he said, “O ʿAbbās, does he not command them to do anything but that they do it?” ʿAbbās said, “If he forbade them food and drink, they would obey him.” He said, “O ʿAbbās, speak to him about your people. Does he have any pardon for them?” ʿAbbās then took Abū Sufyān and brought him before the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAbbās said, “O Messenger of God, this is Abū Sufyān.” Abū Sufyān said, “O Muḥammad, I have sought the aid of my god and sought the aid of your God. By God, I have never met you in battle but that you prevailed over me. If my god had been right and your God false, I would have prevailed over you.” Then he testified that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God. ʿAbbās said, “O Messenger of God, I would like you to permit me to go to your people, warn them of what has befallen, and call them to God and His Messenger.” He granted him permission. ʿAbbās said, “How shall I speak to them, O Messenger of God? Explain to me a guarantee of safety they can rely on.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Say to them: Whoever testifies that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and testifies that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God, and withholds his hand, he is safe. Whoever sits by the Kaʿbah and lays down his weapon, he is safe. Whoever locks his door, he is safe.”"],[7104,"We came as a delegation to Muʿāwiyah ؓ, and among us was Abū Hurayrah ؓ. One of us would prepare food one day and invite the other, and the other would prepare food another day and invite this one. I said, “O Abū Hurayrah, today is my day.” He came before the food was ready, so I said, “O Abū Hurayrah, tell us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ until our food is ready.” He said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest, and he said, ‘O Abū Hurayrah, call the Anṣār for me.’ I called them, and they came hurrying. He said, ‘Do you see the riffraff of the people?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘When you meet them tomorrow, mow them down completely, then your appointment is at al-Ṣafā.’” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Khālid b. al-Walīd over one of the two flanks and al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām over the other flank ؓ, and he appointed Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ over the infantry in the middle of the valley. When the people came, we met them, and no one advanced but that they struck him down. Victory was granted to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came and climbed al-Ṣafā, and the Anṣār came and surrounded al-Ṣafā. Abū Sufyān came and said, ‘O Messenger of God, the green of Quraysh has been made lawful. There is no Quraysh after today.’ He said, ‘Whoever locks his door is safe, and whoever throws down his weapon is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.’”"],[7105,"That when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest, Abū Sufyān came and said, “O Messenger of God, Quraysh has been made lawful. There is no Quraysh after today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever locks his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.” Then he mentioned something similar to the ḥadīth of Ḥammād b. Salamah."],[7106,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Abū Sufyān is close to you, so beware of him.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Submit, O Abū Sufyān.” He said, “O Messenger of God, my people, my people.” He said, “As for your people, whoever locks his door is safe.” He said, “Grant me something.” He said, “Whoever enters your house is safe.”"],[7107,"I set out during the truce that was between us and the Messenger of God ﷺ. While I was in Syria, a letter from the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought to Heraclius. Diḥyah al-Kalbī had brought it and handed it to the governor of Buṣrā, who handed it to Heraclius. Heraclius said, “Is there here a man from the people of this man who claims to be a prophet?” They said, “Yes.” So I was summoned along with a group of Quraysh, and we entered upon Heraclius. He seated us before him and said, “Which of you is closest in kinship to this man who claims to be a prophet?” Abū Sufyān said, “I said, ‘I am.’” So they seated me before him and seated my companions behind me. Then he called for his interpreter and said, “Tell them that I am going to ask about this man who claims to be a prophet. If he lies to me, then call him a liar.” Abū Sufyān said, “By God, were it not that lying would be reported of me, I would have lied.” Then he said to his interpreter, “Ask him how is his lineage among you?” I said, “He is among us of noble lineage.” He said, “Was any of his fathers a king?” I said, “No.” He said, “Did you ever accuse him of lying before he said what he said?” I said, “No.” He said, “Who follows him, the nobles of the people or their weak ones?” I said, “Rather their weak ones.” He said, “Are they increasing or decreasing?” I said, “Rather they are increasing.” He said, “Does anyone of them apostatize from his religion after entering it out of displeasure with it?” I said, “No.” He said, “Have you fought him?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “How was your fighting against him?” I said, “War between us and him alternates; he strikes us and we strike him.” He said, “Does he betray?” I said, “No, and we are with him in a truce, not knowing what he will do during it.” He said, “By God, I was not able to insert anything else into a word besides this.” He said, “Has anyone said this saying before him?” I said, “No.” He said to his interpreter, “Tell him: I asked you about his lineage, and you claimed that he is among you of noble lineage, and so are messengers sent among the noblest of their people. I asked you whether any of his fathers was a king, and you claimed not, so I said, had any of his fathers been a king, I would have said he is a man seeking the kingdom of his fathers. I asked you about his followers, whether they are their weak ones or their nobles, and you said rather their weak ones, and they are the followers of the messengers. I asked you whether you accused him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed not, so I knew that he would not refrain from lying against people and then go and lie against God. I asked you whether anyone of them apostatizes from his religion after entering it out of displeasure with it, and you claimed not, and so is faith when it mingles with the joy of hearts. I asked you whether they increase or decrease, and you claimed that they increase, and so is faith until it is complete. I asked you whether you fought him, and you claimed that you fought him, and war between you and him alternates; he gains from you and you gain from him, and so are messengers tested, then the outcome is theirs. I asked you whether he betrays, and you claimed that he does not betray, and so messengers do not betray. I asked you whether anyone said this saying before him, and you claimed not, so I said, had anyone said this saying before him, I would have said a man following a saying said before him.” Then he said, “What does he command you?” I said, “He commands us to prayer, zakāh, maintaining ties, and chastity.” He said, “If what you say about him is true, he is a prophet. I knew that he was to emerge, but I did not think he would be from among you. If I knew I could reach him, I would love to meet him, and if I were with him, I would wash his feet. His dominion will surely reach what is beneath my feet.” Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and read it. In it was: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Arīsiyyīn. And {O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you} until His saying {that we are Muslims}.” When he finished reading the letter, voices rose around him and clamor increased, and we were ordered to leave. When we left, I said to my companions, “The affair of Ibn Abī Kabshah has become great. The king of the Banū al-Aṣfar fears him.” I remained convinced that the affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ would prevail until God brought Islam to me. Al-Zuhrī said: Heraclius summoned the nobles of the Romans and gathered them in a hall of his. He said, “O assembly of Romans, will you accept success and right guidance forever and that your kingdom remain firm?” They bolted like wild asses to the doors, but found them locked. Then he called them back: “I only tested your steadfastness in your religion. I have seen from you what pleases me.” So they prostrated to him and were pleased with him."],[7108,"Abu Sufyan bin Harb informed me that Heraclius had sent a messenger to him while he had been accompanying a caravan from Quraish. They were merchants doing business in Sham (Syria, Palestine, Lebanon and Jordan), at the time when Messenger of Allah ﷺ had truce with Abu Sufyan and Quraish infidels. So Abu Sufyan and his companions went to Heraclius at Ilya (Jerusalem). Heraclius called them in the court and he had all the senior Roman dignitaries around him. He called for his translator who, translating Heraclius's question said to them, \"Who amongst you is closely related to that man who claims to be a Prophet?\" Abu Sufyan replied, \"I am the nearest relative to him (amongst the group).\" Heraclius said, \"Bring him (Abu Sufyan) close to me and make his companions stand behind him.\" Abu Sufyan added, Heraclius told his translator to tell my companions that he wanted to put some questions to me regarding that man (The Prophet) and that if I told a lie they (my companions) should contradict me.\" Abu Sufyan added, \"By Allah! Had I not been afraid of my companions labeling me a liar, I would not have spoken the truth about the Prophet. The first question he asked me about him was: 'What is his family status amongst you?' I replied, 'He belongs to a good (noble) family amongst us.' Heraclius further asked, 'Has anybody amongst you ever claimed the same (i.e. to be a Prophet) before him?' I replied, 'No.' He said, 'Was anybody amongst his ancestors a king?' I replied, 'No.' Heraclius asked, 'Do the nobles or the poor follow him?' I replied, 'It is the poor who follow him.' He said, 'Are his followers increasing decreasing (day by day)?' I replied, 'They are increasing.' He then asked, 'Does anybody amongst those who embrace his religion become displeased and renounce the religion afterwards?' I replied, 'No.' Heraclius said, 'Have you ever accused him of telling lies before his claim (to be a Prophet)?' I replied, 'No. ' Heraclius said, 'Does he break his promises?' I replied, 'No. We are at truce with him but we do not know what he will do in it.' I could not find opportunity to say anything against him except that. Heraclius asked, 'Have you ever had a war with him?' I replied, 'Yes.' Then he said, 'What was the outcome of the battles?' I replied, 'Sometimes he was victorious and sometimes we.' Heraclius said, 'What does he order you to do?' I said, 'He tells us to worship Allah and Allah alone and not to worship anything along with Him, and to renounce all that our ancestors had said. He orders us to pray, to speak the truth, to be chaste and to keep good relations with our Kith and kin.' Heraclius asked the translator to convey to me the following, I asked you about his family and your reply was that he belonged to a very noble family. In fact all the Apostles come from noble families amongst their respective peoples. I questioned you whether anybody else amongst you claimed such a thing, your reply was in the negative. If the answer had been in the affirmative, I would have thought that this man was following the previous man's statement. Then I asked you whether anyone of his ancestors was a king. Your reply was in the negative, and if it had been in the affirmative, I would have thought that this man wanted to take back his ancestral kingdom. I further asked whether he was ever accused of telling lies before he said what he said, and your reply was in the negative. So I wondered how a person who does not tell a lie about others could ever tell a lie about Allah. I, then asked you whether the rich people followed him or the poor. You replied that it was the poor who followed him. And in fact all the Apostle have been followed by this very class of people. Then I asked you whether his followers were increasing or decreasing. You replied that they were increasing, and in fact this is the way of true faith, till it is complete in all respects. I further asked you whether there was anybody, who, after embracing his religion, became displeased and discarded his religion. Your reply was in the negative, and in fact this is (the sign of) true faith, when its delight enters the hearts and mixes with them completely. I asked you whether he had ever betrayed. You replied in the negative and likewise the Apostles never betray. Then I asked you what he ordered you to do. You replied that he ordered you to worship Allah and Allah alone and not to worship any thing along with Him and forbade you to worship idols and ordered you to pray, to speak the truth and to be chaste. If what you have said is true, he will very soon occupy this place underneath my feet and I knew it (from the scriptures) that he was going to appear but I did not know that he would be from you, and if I could reach him definitely, I would go immediately to meet him and if I were with him, I would certainly wash his feet.' Heraclius then asked for the letter addressed by Allah's Apostle which was delivered by Dihya to the Governor of Busra, who forwarded it to Heraclius to read. The contents of the letter were as follows: \"In the name of Allah the Beneficent, the Merciful (This letter is) from Muhammad the slave of Allah and His Apostle to Heraclius the ruler of Byzantine. Peace be upon him, who follows the right path. Furthermore I invite you to Islam, and if you become a Muslim you will be safe, and Allah will double your reward, and if you reject this invitation of Islam you will be committing a sin of Arisiyin (tillers, farmers i.e. your people). And (Allah's Statement:) 'O people of the scripture! Come to a word common to you and us that we worship none but Allah and that we associate nothing in worship with Him, and that none of us shall take others as Lords beside Allah. Then, if they turn away, say: Bear witness that we are Muslims (those who have surrendered to Allah).' (3:64). Abu Sufyan then added, \"When Heraclius had finished his speech and had read the letter, there was a great hue and cry in the Royal Court. So we were turned out of the court. I told my companions that the question of Ibn-Abi-Kabsha) (the Prophet ﷺ Muhammad) has become so prominent that even the King of Bani Al-Asfar (Byzantine) is afraid of him. Then I started to become sure that he (the Prophet) would be the conqueror in the near future till I embraced Islam (i.e. Allah guided me to it).\" The sub narrator adds, \"Ibn An-Natur was the Governor of llya' (Jerusalem) and Heraclius was the head of the Christians of Sham. Ibn An-Natur narrates that once while Heraclius was visiting ilya' (Jerusalem), he got up in the morning with a sad mood. Some of his priests asked him why he was in that mood? Heraclius was a foreteller and an astrologer. He replied, 'At night when I looked at the stars, I saw that the leader of those who practice circumcision had appeared (become the conqueror). Who are they who practice circumcision?' The people replied, 'Except the Jews nobody practices circumcision, so you should not be afraid of them (Jews). 'Just Issue orders to kill every Jew present in the country.' While they were discussing it, a messenger sent by the king of Ghassan to convey the news of Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Heraclius was brought in. Having heard the news, he (Heraclius) ordered the people to go and see whether the messenger of Ghassan was circumcised. The people, after seeing him, told Heraclius that he was circumcised. Heraclius then asked him about the Arabs. The messenger replied, 'Arabs also practice circumcision.' (After hearing that) Heraclius remarked that sovereignty of the 'Arabs had appeared. Heraclius then wrote a letter to his friend in Rome who was as good as Heraclius in knowledge. Heraclius then left for Homs. (a town in Syrian and stayed there till he received the reply of his letter from his friend who agreed with him in his opinion about the emergence of the Prophet ﷺ and the fact that he was a Prophet. On that Heraclius invited all the heads of the Byzantines to assemble in his palace at Homs. When they assembled, he ordered that all the doors of his palace be closed. Then he came out and said, 'O Byzantines! If success is your desire and if you seek right guidance and want your empire to remain then give a pledge of allegiance to this Prophet (i.e. embrace Islam).' (On hearing the views of Heraclius) the people ran towards the gates of the palace like onagers but found the doors closed. Heraclius realized their hatred towards Islam and when he lost the hope of their embracing Islam, he ordered that they should be brought back in audience. (When they returned) he said, 'What already said was just to test the strength of your conviction and I have seen it.' The people prostrated before him and became pleased with him, and this was the end of Heraclius's story (in connection with his faith). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7)"],[7109,"We were a trading people, and the war between us and the Messenger of God had confined us until our wealth was destroyed. When the truce was made between us and the Messenger of God ﷺ, we felt secure in our wealth. I set out with a group of Quraysh heading to Syria, where our trade was. I arrived there when Heraclius had defeated those Persians who had opposed him and expelled them from it, and his great cross was recovered for him, which they had seized. When he learned of that and that his cross had been retrieved, and Ḥimṣ was his residence, he left it on foot, thanking God for what had been restored to him, to pray in Jerusalem. Carpets were spread for him on the road and aromatic plants were thrown on them. When he reached Īliyāʾ and completed his prayer there, with his patricians and bishops of the Romans, the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought to him with Diḥyah b. Khalīfah al-Kalbī: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the Messenger of God, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the peasants.” Muḥammad b. Isḥāq said: Ibn Shihāb said: The bishop of the Christians narrated to me, saying, “I lived to see him in the time of ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān, and he claimed that he witnessed that affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the affair of Heraclius and understood it.” He said: When the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived with Diḥyah, he took it and placed it between his thighs and his side. Then he wrote to a man in Rome who read Hebrew, mentioning his affair, describing his situation, and the news of what he brought. The man of Rome wrote back to him that he is the prophet we have been awaiting, no doubt about it, so follow him and believe him. Heraclius ordered the patricians of the Romans to be gathered in the hall of his kingdom, and he ordered the hall to be locked upon them. Then he looked down upon them from an upper room, fearing them for himself, and said, “O assembly of Romans, I have gathered you for a matter. A letter from this man has come to me calling me to his religion. By God, he is the man we have been awaiting and whom we find in our book. Come, let us follow him and believe him, and our world and our hereafter will be safe for us.” They snorted with one snort, then rushed to the doors of the hall to leave, but found them locked against them. He said, “Bring them back to me,” fearing them for himself. They were brought back, and he said, “O assembly of Romans, I only said this statement to you to see how firm you are in your religion in this matter that has occurred. I have seen from you what pleases me.” So they prostrated to him and were pleased with him. He ordered the doors of the hall to be opened for them, and they departed."],[7110,"That he was in Syria with men of Quraysh who had come as merchants, during the truce between the Messenger of God ﷺ and the disbelievers of Quraysh. Abū Sufyān said: The messenger of Caesar came and took me and my companions until we arrived at Īliyāʾ. We entered upon him, and he was seated in his royal court wearing the crown, with the nobles of the Romans around him. He said to his interpreter, “Ask them which of them is closest in kinship to this man who claims to be a prophet.” Abū Sufyān said, “I said, ‘I am the closest of them to him in kinship.’” He said, “What is the relationship between you and him?” I said, “He is my cousin.” Abū Sufyān said, “There was no one from Banū ʿAbd Manāf in the caravan that day except me.” Caesar said, “Bring him near me.” Then he ordered my companions, and they were placed behind my back at my shoulders. Then Caesar said to his interpreter, “Tell his companions: I am going to ask this man about the man who claims to be a prophet. If he lies, then call him a liar.” Abū Sufyān said, “Were it not for the shame that my companions would report lying about me, I would have lied about him when he asked me. But I was ashamed that they would report lying, so I told the truth.” Then Caesar said to his interpreter, “Ask him how is this man’s lineage among you?” I said, “He is among us of noble lineage.” He said, “Has anyone among you ever said this saying?” I said, “No.” He said, “Did you accuse him of lying before he said what he said?” I said, “No.” He said, “Was any of his fathers a king?” I said, “No.” He said, “Do the nobles of the people follow him or their weak ones?” I said, “Rather their weak ones.” He said, “Are they increasing or decreasing?” I said, “Rather increasing.” He said, “Does anyone of them apostatize out of displeasure with his religion after entering it?” I said, “No.” He said, “Does he betray?” I said, “We are with him in a truce now, and we fear that.” Abū Sufyān said, “I was not able to insert into any word anything by which I could disparage him, except that I feared it would be reported of me.” He said, “Have you fought him and has he fought you?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “How is his war and your war?” I said, “It has been alternating, sometimes favoring us and sometimes favoring him.” He said, “What does he command you?” I said, “He commands us to worship God alone and not associate anything with Him, and he forbids us to worship what our fathers worshipped. He commands us to prayer, charity, chastity, fulfilling covenants, and returning trusts.” He said to his interpreter when I said that, “Tell him: I asked you about his lineage among you, and you claimed that he is among you of noble lineage, and so messengers are sent among the nobility of their people. I asked you whether anyone said this saying before him, and you said no, so I said, had anyone of you said this saying, I would have said he is a man following the saying of one who said it before him. I asked you whether you accused him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed not, so I knew that he would not refrain from lying against people and then lie against God. I asked you whether any of his fathers was a king, and you claimed not, so I said, had any of his fathers been a king, I would have said he is a man seeking the kingdom of his fathers. I asked you whether the nobles of the people follow him or their weak ones, and you claimed that their weak ones are his followers, and so are the followers of messengers. I asked you whether they increase or decrease, and you claimed that they increase, and so is faith. I asked you whether anyone of them apostatizes out of displeasure with his religion after entering it, and you claimed not, and so is faith when it mingles with the joy of hearts; no one dislikes it. I asked you whether he betrays, and you claimed not, and so messengers do not betray. I asked you whether you fought him and he fought you, and you claimed that he has done that and that your war and his war alternates, sometimes favoring you and sometimes favoring him, and so are messengers, then the outcome is theirs. I asked you what he commands you, and you claimed that he commands you to worship God alone and not associate anything with Him, and he forbids you from what your fathers worshipped, and he commands you to prayer, charity, chastity, and returning trusts. He is a prophet. I knew that he was to emerge, but I did not think he would be from among you. If what I said is true, he will soon possess the place of these two feet of mine. By God, if I hoped to reach him, I would endure meeting him and wash his feet.” Abū Sufyān said: Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and ordered it to be read. In it was: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the servant of God and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Arīsiyyīn. And {O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you: that we worship none but God and associate nothing with Him, and that none of us takes others as lords besides God. If they turn away, then say: Bear witness that we are Muslims}.” Abū Sufyān said: When he finished his speech, the voices of those around him from the nobles of the Romans rose, and their clamor increased. I do not know what they were saying. He ordered us to leave. When I left with my companions and was alone, I said, “The affair of Ibn Abī Kabshah has become great. This king of the Banū al-Aṣfar fears him.” Abū Sufyān said: By God, I remained humbled and convinced that his affair would prevail until God brought Islam to me, though I was reluctant."],[7111,"I met the Prophet ﷺ between Arafah and Muzdalifah, so I took hold of the halter of his she-camel and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what will bring me near Paradise and keep me far from the Fire?\" He said, \"By Allah, if you have been brief in asking, you have indeed made it great and lengthy. Establish the prescribed prayers, pay the obligatory zakat, perform Hajj to the House, and whatever you would love people to do to you, do it to them; and whatever you would hate people to do to you, leave people alone from it. Let go of the halter of the she-camel.\" Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj said: \"And Sakhr b. al-Qa'qa' al-Bahili said it.\""],[7112,"Caesar, in his kingdom, his power, and his presence, what did he say? It means that his saying was \"If I had known that he was him, I would have walked to him, kissed his head, and washed his feet.\" Abu Sufyan and his presence, his forehead was sweating with the anxiety of the letter that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to him. Abu Sufyan said, \"So, I remained desired by Muhammad ﷺ until I embraced Islam and in his message, he said: 'O people of the Book, come to a word that is just between us and you, that we worship none but Allah, and that we do not associate anything with Him, and that none of us shall take others as lords besides Allah. But if they turn away, then say: 'Bear witness that we are Muslims'.\" \"It is He who has sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, that He may make it prevail over all religions, even if the disbelievers hate it.\" \"Fight against those who do not believe in Allah, nor in the Last Day, nor forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, and do not adhere to the religion of truth from among those who were given the Scripture, until they give the jizyah willingly while they are humbled.\""],[7113,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “O God, bless my community in its early morning.” And when he sent out a raiding party, he would send it at the beginning of the day. Ṣakhr was a merchant, and he would send his servants at the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased."],[7114,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O God, bless my community in its early morning.”"],[7115,"From Ṣakhr, who lived to see the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not revile the dead, for you will hurt the living.”"],[7116,"I took the paternal aunt of al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and al-Mughīrah came and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for his aunt. He said, “O Ṣakhr, when people embrace Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so return her to them.” So I returned her to him. He said: And the Prophet ﷺ had given me wealth for Banū Sulaym, and they embraced Islam and came to the Prophet ﷺ asking for the wealth. The Prophet of God ﷺ called me and said, “O Ṣakhr, when people embrace Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so return it to them.” So I returned it to them."],[7117,"The Prophet ﷺ saw his father standing in the sun while he was delivering a sermon, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to move, or ordered that he be moved, and he was moved."],[7118,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby appearance, so he said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth. Allah has given me camels, cattle, and sheep.\" He said, \"Whoever has wealth, let it be seen on him.\""],[7119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"After one hundred years, no child will be born for whom Allah has any need.\""],[7120,"Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to your people, Banu Sa'd, and I began presenting Islam to them and calling them to it? I said, 'Indeed, he calls to good and commands it. Indeed, he calls to good and commands it.' So I conveyed that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Allah, bind [good] for al-Ahnaf.' And al-Ahnaf used to say: 'There is nothing among my deeds that I hope for more than this.'\""],[7121,"Suhayb b. Sinan, whose kunya was Abu Yahya, died in Madinah in Shawwal of the year thirty-eight. He was among the captives of Mosul, taken captive by the Byzantines."],[7122,"When Umar ؓ was stabbed, he ordered Suhayb, the freedman of Banu Jud'an, to lead the people in prayer."],[7123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The forerunners are four: I am the forerunner of the Arabs, Suhayb is the forerunner of the Byzantines, Salman is the forerunner of Persia, and Bilal is the forerunner of Abyssinia.\""],[7124,"In his saying {And among the people is he who sells himself} it was revealed about Suhaib ibn Sinan and Abu Dharr, and that the one who met Suhaib on the way to the city was Qunfudh ibn Umayr ibn Jud'an."],[7125,"Suhayb ransomed himself from his people with his wealth, then he set out as an emigrant, and they caught up with him on the road, so he brought out for them what remained of his wealth."],[7126,"Ibn Umar [said]: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Banu Amr b. Awf to pray in it, and Suhayb entered with him. Then some men from the Ansar entered upon him greeting him. Abdullah said: So I asked Suhayb, \"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond when someone greeted him during prayer?\" He said, \"He would gesture with his hand.\""],[7127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the mosque of Quba and was praying, and people began entering and greeting him. When Suhayb came out, I asked him, \"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond to them?\" He said, \"With his hand, like this,\" and he gestured with it."],[7128,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he responded to me with a gesture."],[7129,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal came to Syria, he saw the Jews prostrating to their rabbis and scholars, and he saw the Christians prostrating to their bishops. When he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he prostrated to him. He said, \"What is this, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"I came to Syria and saw the Jews prostrating to their scholars and rabbis, and I saw the Christians prostrating to their priests and monks. I asked, 'What is this?' They said, 'The greeting of the prophets.'\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"They lied about their prophets, just as they distorted their book. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[7130,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"He who declares lawful its forbidden things has not believed in the Qur'an.\""],[7131,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I was shown the abode of your emigration, a land of salt marshes between two lava tracts; either it is Hajar or it is Yathrib.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ departed for Madinah, and Abu Bakr ؓ departed with him. I had intended to go out with him, but some young men of Quraysh prevented me. That night I kept standing and did not sit. They said, \"God has distracted him from you with his stomach,\" but I was not ill. They slept, so I went out. Some people from them caught up with me after I had traveled, wanting to bring me back. I said to them, \"Would you like me to give you some ounces of gold and two bracelets of mine in Makkah, and you let me go and give me your word?\" They did so. I followed them to Makkah and said, \"Dig under the threshold of the door, for beneath it are the ounces. Go to such-and-such a woman with such-and-such a sign and take the two ornaments.\" I left until I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ at Quba before he moved from it. When he saw me, he said, \"O Abu Yahya, did the bargain profit?\" three times. I said, \"O Messenger of God, no one has preceded me to you, and nothing informed you except Gabriel ﷺ.\""],[7132,"Umar ؓ said, \"What is wrong with him—may he have no father—he calls the people against me?\" He said, \"He is only calling a servant of his named Yahnas.\" He said, \"O Suhayb, there is nothing in you that I find fault with except three traits; were it not for them, I would not place anyone ahead of you.\" He said, \"What are they?\" He replied, \"You are a fault-finder.\" He said, \"Will he tell me about them?\" He said, \"You will not ask me about anything but I will inform you of it.\" He said, \"And you will not inform me of anything but I will believe you.\" He said, \"I see you squander your wealth, you take a kunya with the name of a prophet—Abu Yahya—and you claim Arab lineage while your tongue is non-Arab.\" He said, \"As for my squandering my wealth, I spend it only in its proper right. As for my kunya, the Messenger of God ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya; shall I abandon it because of your words? And as for my claiming Arab lineage, the Byzantines captured me when I was young, and I do not remember my family. Even if I had emerged from a piece of dung, I would trace my lineage to it.\""],[7133,"David, the prophet of God ﷺ, when he finished his prayer, would say, \"O God, set right for me my religion, which You have made the protection of my affair; and set right for me my worldly life, in which You have placed my livelihood. O God, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. None can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can avail against You his fortune.\" Ka'b al-Ahbar said: Suhayb informed me that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to conclude his prayer with this supplication."],[7134,"Ka'b swore by God who parted the sea for Moses that Suhayb narrated to him that the Messenger of God ﷺ never saw a town he intended to enter but that he said when he saw it, \"O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people.\""],[7135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to supplicate, saying, \"O God, You are not a god whom we have newly invented, nor a Lord whom we have originated, nor was there for us before You any god to whom we could flee and abandon You, nor did anyone help You in creating us so that we would associate him with You. Blessed are You, and exalted.\" Ka'b said, \"Thus did David, the prophet of God ﷺ, use to supplicate.\""],[7136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever gives a woman a dowry while resolving not to fulfill it to her will meet God ﷻ as an adulterer, and whoever takes on a debt while resolving not to repay it will meet God as a thief.\""],[7137,"The sons of Suhayb said to Suhayb, \"O our father, the sons of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrate from their fathers.\" He said, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[7138,"The sons of Suhayb said to Suhayb, \"O our father, the sons of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrate from their fathers.\" He said, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[7139,"\"I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ before revelation came to him.\""],[7140,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while there were dates and bread in front of him. He said, \"Draw near and eat.\" I began eating from the dates. He said, \"Do you eat dates while you have an eye inflammation?\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, I suck them from the other side.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled."],[7141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man’s prayer in congregation equals twenty-five times his prayer alone.”"],[7142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You should use cupping on the jugular area of the back of the head, for it is a cure for seventy-two diseases and five ailments: insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, and toothache.”"],[7143,"Abu Bakr ؓ passed by a captive of his to seek protection for him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Suhayb was sitting in the mosque. He said to Abu Bakr, “Who is this with you?” He said, “A captive of mine from the polytheists; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has granted him protection.” Suhayb said, “There was a place for the sword on this one’s neck.” Abu Bakr ؓ became angry. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said, “Why do I see you angry?” He said, “I passed by this captive of mine in front of Suhayb, and he said, ‘There was a place for the sword on this one’s neck.’” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Perhaps you harmed him.” He said, “No, by Allah.” He said, “If you had harmed him, you would have harmed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[7144,"That the polytheists, when they circled around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and approached the cave and retreated, Wahshi said: Neither Suhayb (was wounded), nor Suhayb should (stay) by me. So when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to leave, he sent Abu Bakr twice or three times to Suhayb, and he found him praying. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I found him praying, so I disliked interrupting his prayer. Abu Bakr said: You were right. So they both left during the night. And when it was morning, he continued until he came to Umm Rumân, the wife of Abu Bakr, and she said: Shouldn't I see you here (with your brother)? They have left (and they) have left something for you from their provisions. Suhayb said: So I left until I entered upon my wife, Umm 'Umar, and I took my sword, my provisions, and my bow, until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Al-Madinah, and I found him (with) Abu Bakr sitting. So when Abu Bakr saw me, he stood up and gave me the glad tidings of the verse that was revealed about me, and he held my hand. So I mentioned some complaints to him, and he apologized and granted me a blessing. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Abu Yahya has made a profit.\""],[7145,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never witnessed any scene except that I was present; he never pledged allegiance except that I was present; he never dispatched a raiding party except that I was present; he never went on any expedition, from the first of the time to its last, except that I was in it on his right or his left. Whenever they feared what was before them, I was in front of them; whenever they feared what was behind them, I was behind them. I never placed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between me and the enemy until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away.”"],[7146,"He said to him, “O Suhayb, you have adopted a kunya though you have no son, and you claim Arab lineage though you are a man from the Byzantines.” He said, “O Commander of the Faithful, as for your saying that I have adopted a kunya though I have no son, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya. As for your saying that I claim Arab lineage though I am a man from the Byzantines, I am a man from the tribe of al-Namir b. Qasit; I was taken captive from Mosul after I had been a boy who knew my family and lineage.”"],[7147,"From the Prophet ﷺ that one day he said to Ali ؓ, “Who is the most wretched of the early peoples?” He said, “The one who hamstrung the she-camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “You have spoken the truth. Then who is the most wretched of the later peoples?” He said, “I have no knowledge, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The one who will strike you on this,” and the Prophet ﷺ pointed with his hand to the crown of his head. Ali ؓ used to say to the people of Iraq, “By Allah, I wish that the most wretched of you would be sent and would dye this,” meaning his beard, “from this,” and he placed his hand on the front of his head. The wording is that of the hadith of Suwayd b. Sa’id; al-Hadrami said in his version, “and he pointed with his hand to the crown of his head.”"],[7148,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a donkey brays, seek refuge in Allah from Satan the accursed.”"],[7149,"When water, then wine, then milk were presented to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , he took the milk and said to him, Jibril, \"You have chosen the fitrah (natural disposition). With it, every living creature is punished. If you had taken the wine, you would have gone astray and your nation would have also gone astray. And he pointed to the valley known as Hellfire. So I looked into it and saw that it was blazing."],[7150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out: ‘O people of Paradise, you have a promise with Allah that He intends to fulfill for you.’ They will say, ‘What is it? Has He not made our scales heavy, whitened our faces, admitted us to Paradise, and saved us from the Fire?’ He said: ‘Then the veil will be lifted, and they will look at Him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, He has not given them anything dearer to them than looking at Him.’”"],[7151,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I am amazed at Allah’s decree for the Muslim; it is all good. If ease befalls him and he is grateful, Allah ﷻ rewards him; and if hardship befalls him and he is patient, Allah ﷻ rewards him.” Hammad added in it: “And every decree that Allah ﷻ decrees for the Muslim is good.”"],[7152,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one of the night prayers. When he finished, he turned to us with a smiling face and said, “Will you not ask me why I laughed?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “I am amazed at Allah’s decree for the Muslim servant. Indeed, everything Allah decrees for him is good, and no one has all of Allah’s decrees be good for him except the Muslim servant.”"],[7153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to move his lips with something during the days of Hunayn when he prayed the dawn prayer. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, you keep moving your lips with something after the dawn prayer, and you did not used to do that.” He said, “A prophet before us was impressed by the large number of his community and said, ‘These will not last,’ I think he said something, so Allah ﷻ revealed to him: ‘The best of your community is between one of three: either I send death upon them, or the enemy, or famine.’ He presented that to them, and they said, ‘As for famine, we have no strength for it, and we have no strength for the enemy, but death.’ So seventy thousand of them died in three days. Today I say: O Allah, by You I strive, by You I attack, by You I fight.”"],[7154,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed the afternoon prayer, he murmured. Murmuring, according to some of their statements, is moving his lips as if speaking something. It was said to him, “O Prophet of Allah, when you pray the afternoon prayer, you murmur.” He said, “A prophet among the prophets was impressed by his community and said, ‘Who can stand against these?’ So Allah ﷻ revealed to him: ‘Give them a choice between My taking vengeance on them and My setting their enemy upon them.’ They chose vengeance, so He set death upon them, and seventy thousand of them died in one day.”"],[7155,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed the afternoon prayer, he would murmur. The murmuring, according to some of them, meant that he moved his lips as if speaking something. It was said to him, 'O Prophet of God, when you pray the afternoon prayer, you murmur?' He replied, 'A prophet among the prophets was impressed with his nation and said, \"Who will stand up for these?\" So God ﷻ revealed to him to give them a choice between His taking revenge on them and His unleashing their enemy upon them. They chose the punishment, so death was unleashed upon them, and seventy thousand of them died in a single day.'"],[7156,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Among those before you there was a king who had a sorcerer. When the sorcerer grew old, he said to the king, \"I have become old, so send me a boy whom I can teach sorcery.\" He sent him a boy, and he taught him sorcery. Between the king and the sorcerer there was a monk. The boy heard his words, and he was impressed by his manner and speech. Whenever he went to the sorcerer, he sat with the monk, and when he went to the sorcerer, he beat him, saying, \"What kept you?\" When he returned to his family, he sat with the monk, and when he went to his family, they said, \"What is keeping you?\" and they beat him. He complained about that to the monk, who said, \"When the sorcerer wants to beat you, say, 'My family kept me,' and when your family wants to beat you, say, 'The sorcerer kept me.'\" He said, \"While that was the case, one day he came upon a great beast that had blocked the people from passing. He said, 'Today I will know whether the affair of the sorcerer is dearer to God or the affair of the monk.' He took a stone and said, 'In the name of God. O God, if the affair of the monk is dearer to You and more excellent, then kill this beast.' He threw it and killed it, and the people went on. This reached the monk, who said, 'My son, you are more excellent than I, and you will be tested. If you are tested, do not point to me.' The boy used to heal the blind from birth and the leper and these diseases. The king had a close companion who went blind. He heard about the boy and came to him with many gifts, saying, 'Heal me, and you shall have all that is here.' The boy said, 'I do not heal anyone; only God ﷻ heals. If you believe in God, He will heal you.' So he believed in Him, and the boy called upon God ﷻ, and he was cured. The blind man was seized and continually tortured until he pointed to the boy. The king said to him, 'Do you have a lord other than me?' He said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is God.' He kept at him until he pointed to the monk. He seized him with torture and said, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He ordered a saw, and it was placed on the top of his head, and they split him. He said to the blind man, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He placed the saw on the top of his head until its two halves fell to the ground. It was said to the boy, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He sent him with a group to a mountain and said, 'Climb such-and-such mountain with him, and when you reach its summit, if he recants his religion, then fine; otherwise, push him down.' He said, 'They took him to the mountain, and when he reached its summit, he said, \"O God, suffice me against them however You will.\" The mountain shook them, and they all perished. The boy came and entered upon the king, who said, 'What happened to your companions?' He said, 'God ﷻ sufficed me against them.' He sent them with a group in a ship, saying, 'Take him to the sea, and when you are in the middle of the sea, if he recants, then fine; otherwise, drown him.' They took him, and when they were in deep water, he said, \"O God, suffice me against them however You will.\" They all drowned. The boy came, and the king said, 'What happened to your companions?' He said, 'God ﷻ sufficed me against them.' Then the boy said to the king, 'You will not kill me until you do what I command you. If you do it, you will kill me.' He said, 'What is it?' He said, 'Gather the people on a single open plain, then take an arrow from your quiver and say, \"In the name of God, the Lord of the boy,\" then shoot me. If you do that, you will kill me.' He did so, placed the arrow, and said, 'In the name of God, the Lord of the boy.' The arrow struck his temple. The boy placed his hand on the spot of the arrow and died. The people said, 'We believe in the Lord of the boy' three times. It was said to the king, 'Do you see what you were wary of? By God, it has befallen you; all the people have believed.' He ordered the mouths of the streets to be dug, and trenches were dug in them. He said, 'Whoever recants his religion, then fine; otherwise, throw him into them.'"],[7157,"I prepared food for the Messenger of God ﷺ and came to him while he was sitting among a group of people. I stood facing him and gestured to him, and he gestured to me, 'And these?' I said, 'No.' So I remained silent and stood in my place. When he looked at me, I gestured to him, and he said, 'And these?' I said, 'No.' He did that twice or three times. Then I said, 'Yes, and these,' though it was only a little food I had prepared for him. He came, and they came with him, and they ate. I think he said, 'And some of it remained.'"],[7158,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The superiority of a man's prayer in his home over his prayer where people can see him is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary prayer.'"],[7159,"'By God, I do not know which of the two calamities is greater: the death of my father or the killing of Uthman.'"],[7160,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'With whom did you stay, Abu Wahb?' He said, 'I stayed with Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib.' He said, 'You stayed with the Qurayshite who has the greatest love for Quraysh.'"],[7161,"It was said to Safwan, 'Whoever does not emigrate has perished.' So he called for his mount, rode it, and came to Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'What has brought you, Abu Wahb?' He said, 'I have heard that there is no religion for one who has no emigration.' He said, 'Return to the valleys of Makkah.' So he returned and entered the mosque, and he placed his cloak under his head as a pillow. A man came and stole it, and he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'O Messenger of God, this man stole my cloak.' The Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be punished by cutting. He said, 'O Messenger of God, my cloak did not reach the value for which a man's hand is cut; I have given it to him as charity.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Why not before you brought him to me?'"],[7162,"Safwan b. Umayyah came to Madinah and slept in the mosque, placing a khamisah of his under his head. A thief came and stole it. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that his hand be cut. He said, 'O Messenger of God, it is his.' He said, 'Why not before you brought him to me?'"],[7163,"Safwan ibn Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and there was a garment under his head. A man came and took it from under his head while he was sleeping. Safwan woke up and followed him, and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned the matter to him. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the man be punished. Safwan said to the Prophet ﷺ , \"I had not reached the point of wanting it to be severed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Why didn't you come to me before bringing him?\""],[7164,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague is martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, and a woman who dies in childbirth is martyrdom.'"],[7165,"From Safwan b. Umayyah, raised to the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague, the woman who dies in childbirth, and drowning are martyrdom.'"],[7166,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague, drowning, burning, and the woman who dies in childbirth are martyrdom for my nation.'"],[7167,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Eat meat by tearing it with your teeth, for it is tastier, more wholesome, and more agreeable.'"],[7168,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “It is more appetizing, more wholesome, more pleasant, and more wholesome.”"],[7169,"Safwan b. Umayyah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was cutting meat off the bone, so he said, “O Safwan.” I said, “At your service.” He said, “Bring the meat close to your mouth, for it is more pleasant and more wholesome.”"],[7170,"A thief came to him while he was sleeping and stole his waist-wrapper from beneath him. He woke up, seized him, and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have made it lawful for him.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me? When a case reaches the ruler concerning any of the prescribed punishments, he must carry it out.”"],[7171,"I was sleeping in the mosque on a cloak of mine worth thirty dirhams. A man came to me and snatched it from me. The man was caught and brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that his hand be cut off. I went to him and said, “Will you cut off his hand for thirty dirhams? It is his.” He said, “Why was this not before you brought him to me?”"],[7172,"A thief came to his father while he was sleeping and stole his waist-wrapper from under his head. He woke up, seized him, and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have made it lawful for him.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me? When a case reaches the ruler concerning any of Allah’s prescribed punishments, he must carry it out.”"],[7173,"A man stole a cloak, and he brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have pardoned him.” He said, “If only this had been before you brought him to me, O Abu Wahb.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had his hand cut off."],[7174,"I slept in the mosque, and my waist-wrapper was stolen from beneath me. I caught the thief and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is his.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me?”"],[7175,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed some iron armor from me on the day of Hunayn. I said, “Is it guaranteed, O Muhammad?” He said, “Guaranteed.” He said: Then some of it was lost. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “If you wish, we will compensate you for it.” He said, “No, I desire Islam more than that.”"],[7176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me gifts on the day of Hunayn, while he was the most hated of people to me, and he kept giving to me until he became the most beloved of people to me."],[7177,"When it was said to me, “Whoever does not emigrate is destroyed,” I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, “Return, Abu Wahb, to the valleys of Makkah.”"],[7178,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Amr b. Qurrah came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, misery has been decreed for me, and I see that I have no provision except from my tambourine with my hand. Will you permit me to sing without obscenity?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I do not permit you, nor honor. You have lied, O enemy of Allah! Allah has provided you with lawful, good sustenance, but you chose what Allah has forbidden of His provision over what He has made lawful of His lawful sustenance. If I had warned you before, I would have done so. Get away from me and repent to Allah. Indeed, if you obtain anything after this warning, I will strike you a painful blow, shave your head as a disgrace, banish you from your family, and make your spoils lawful plunder for the youths of Madinah.” Amr got up, bearing evil and disgrace that only Allah knows. When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, “These are the disobedient ones. Whoever among them dies without repentance, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection as he was, effeminate, naked, not covering himself from the people even with a thread; whenever he stands, he falls down.”"],[7179,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Amr b. Qurrah came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, misery has been decreed for me, and I see that I have no provision except from my tambourine with my hand. Will you permit me to sing without obscenity?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I do not permit you, nor honor. You have lied, O enemy of Allah! Allah has provided you with lawful, good sustenance, but you chose what Allah has forbidden of His provision over what He has made lawful of His lawful sustenance. If I had warned you before, I would have done so. Get away from me and repent to Allah. Indeed, if you obtain anything after this warning, I will strike you a painful blow, shave your head as a disgrace, banish you from your family, and make your spoils lawful plunder for the youths of Madinah.” Amr got up, bearing evil and disgrace that only Allah knows. When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, “These are the disobedient ones. Whoever among them dies without repentance, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection as he was, effeminate, naked, not covering himself from the people even with a thread; whenever he stands, he falls down.”"],[7180,"«I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on one of his journeys. He prayed Isha, then slept until, when it was around the middle of the night, he rose and recited these verses from the end of Surah Al Imran until he completed the surah. Then he performed ablution, used the siwak, and prayed two rak'ahs—I do not know whether his standing, bowing, or prostration was longer.» Then he said: «Then he woke and recited the verses again, then used the siwak, performed ablution, and did the same as before. Then he prayed the same as the first time. Then he continued praying two rak'ahs at a time, sleeping and then waking as he did the first time, until he had prayed eleven rak'ahs.»"],[7181,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: «Verily, when the sun rises, Satan accompanies it; when it becomes high, he leaves it; when it nears its zenith, he accompanies it; when it declines, he leaves it; when it nears its setting, he accompanies it; and when it sets, he leaves it.» So he prohibited prayer at those times."],[7182,"We set out as pilgrims. When we were at al-Arj, we came upon a snake writhing, and before long it died. A man among us took out a cloth from his 'ubayyah and wrapped it, and dug a trench for it in the ground. Then we arrived in Makkah, and while we were in the Sacred Mosque, a person stood before us and said: 'Which of you is the companion of Amr b. Jabir?' We said: 'We do not know him.' He said: 'Which of you is the companion of the jinni?' They said: 'This one.' He said: 'Indeed he was the last of the nine believers who came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to listen to the Quran.'"],[7183,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to announce: «Do not make nabidh in earthenware jars.»"],[7184,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was reclining in the mosque on a cloak of his, and I said to him: 'O Messenger of God, I have come seeking knowledge.' He said: «Welcome to the seeker of knowledge. The seeker of knowledge—the angels cover him and shade him with their wings, then they climb one upon another until they reach the lowest heaven, out of love for what he seeks. What have you come to seek?» He said: Safwan said: 'O Messenger of God, we do not cease traveling between Makkah and Madinah, so give us a ruling about wiping over the leather socks.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: «Three days for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.»"],[7185,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey, a man came and said: 'O Muhammad.' They said: 'Lower your voice.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, a man loves a people but has not seen them.' He said: «A person is with those whom he loves.» Then he asked him about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: «Three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident. He does not remove them for urine, sleep, or defecation, only for major impurity.» Then he asked him about repentance, and he said: «For repentance there is a gate in the west, a journey of seventy years—or forty years—that remains open until some of the signs of your Lord come: the sun's rising from its west.»"],[7186,"Indeed, no one does what you have done except that the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does. I said: 'I came early to ask you about wiping over the leather socks.' He said: 'I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Should I wipe over the leather socks, O Messenger of God?' He said: «Yes, three for the traveler—he does not remove them due to defecation, urine, or sleep—and a day for the resident.»"],[7187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has opened a gate from the west, its extent being seventy years, for repentance; He will not close it until the sun rises from its west. And no man goes out seeking knowledge except that the angels lay down their wings for him, pleased with what he does.” At that the Arabs said, “O Prophet of Allah, has not Allah given a servant a single trait that is better?” He said, “Good character.” Then they said to him, “Shall we seek medical treatment?” He said, “Do you not know that the One who sent down the disease sent down the cure – or no disease has been sent down except that He sent down a cure for it, except one disease.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, what is it?” He said, “Old age.” Then he said, “For the traveler, three days to wipe over his leather socks; and for the resident, one day and one night.”"],[7188,"\"A Jew said to his companion: 'Let us go to this Prophet.' His companion said to him: 'Do not say Prophet; if he hears you, he will become big-headed.' So they came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and asked him about nine clear signs. He said to them: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill any soul whom Allah has forbidden you to kill, except by right, do not speak falsely about an innocent man before a ruler, do not engage in magic, do not consume Riba (usury), do not slander chaste women, and do not flee on the day of the march (to battle). And for you Jews especially, do not break the Sabbath.' They kissed his hands and feet and said: 'We bear witness that you are a Prophet.' He said: 'What is keeping you from following me?' They said: 'Dawud prayed that there would always be a Prophet among his descendants, and we are afraid that if we follow you, the Jews will kill us.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4078)"],[7189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military expedition and said: “Raid in the name of Allah, in the path of Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, and do not kill a child. And for the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night to wipe over the leather socks.”"],[7190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged the seeking of knowledge before its disappearance. A man said, “How will it disappear when we have learned it and taught it to our children?” He became angry and said, “Are not the Torah and the Gospel in the hands of the People of the Book? Does that avail them anything?”"],[7191,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Delay the midday prayer until it cools down, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell.”"],[7192,"My father Safwan migrated to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. The Prophet ﷺ extended his hand to him and wiped over it. Safwan said to him, “I love you, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “A person is with the one he loves.”"],[7193,"He went to his sheep and hunted two rabbits, then slaughtered them with a piece of white flint. He brought them to the Prophet ﷺ and presented them. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered them with a piece of white flint.” He said, “Eat both of them.”"],[7194,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “O Suhar b. Abbas, make your drink good and give your neighbor to drink.”"],[7195,"He had a connection, Sila b. al-Harith al-Ghifari, and he is one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"By Allah, we did not abandon the covenant of our Prophet, nor did we sever our ties of kinship until you and your companions stood among us.\""],[7196,"From Shuqran, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"I saw him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, heading on the day of Khaybar on a donkey, praying while gesturing.\""],[7197,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever introduces satire against Islam, cut off his tongue.” Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal said, meaning that he satirized Islam."],[7198,"A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and no shroud was found for him. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Look inside his waist wrapper.\" A dinar or two dinars were found. He said: \"Two cauterizations. Pray over your companion.\" A man said: \"I will pay it, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he prayed over him."],[7199,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks after he had urinated."],[7200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Love is from Allah and reputation is in the heaven. When Allah loves a servant, He says: ‘O Gabriel, your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him.’ Then Gabriel calls out in the heaven: ‘Your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him.’ Then love is sent down for him upon the people of the earth.”"],[7201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called for his leather socks to put them on. He put on one of them, then a crow came and carried off the other, then dropped it, and a snake came out of it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not put on his leather socks until he shakes them out.\""],[7202,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Gabriel kept instructing me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[7203,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: Mary asked her Lord for meat without blood, and He fed her locusts. She said, “O God, give him life without nursing and make him grow without satiation.”"],[7204,"The Prophet ﷺ came during the Farewell Pilgrimage on a she-camel until he stopped in the middle of the people on the Day of 'Arafah and said: \"Which day is this?\" They said: The Day of 'Arafah, the sacred day. He said: \"Then which month?\" They said: In the sacred month. He said: \"Then which land is this?\" They said: The sacred land. He said: \"Indeed your wealth, your honors, and your blood are sacred to you as this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Indeed every prophet's supplication has passed except my supplication, for I have stored it with my Lord until the Day of Resurrection. Now then, the prophets are vying in numbers, so do not disgrace me, for I will be waiting for you at the Basin.\""],[7205,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no servant who dies and leaves behind gold and silver but he will be branded with it.\""],[7206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The borrowed item is to be returned, the gift is to be given back, and whoever finds a she-camel whose udder has been tied up, it is not lawful for him to untie it until he returns it.\""],[7207,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By the intercession of a single man who is not a prophet, the like of the two tribes, or one of the two tribes, Rabi'ah and Mudar, will certainly enter Paradise.\""],[7208,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among the best of people are the kings, the kings of Himyar, Sufyan, al-Sakun, and al-Ash'ariyyin.\""],[7209,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a commander, he said: \"Shorten the sermon and reduce the speech.\""],[7210,"From the hadith of 'Amr al-Hadrami from the people of Homs, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon one day, and most of his sermon was mention of the Dajjal, warning us against him, telling us about him until he finished his sermon. Among what he said to us that day: \"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not sent a prophet except that he warned his nation, and I am the last of the prophets and you are the last of the nations, and he will certainly come out among you. If he comes out while I am among you, then I am the advocate for every Muslim, and if he comes out among you after me, then each person is the advocate for himself, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is my successor over every Muslim. He will come out from a gap between Iraq and the Levant, spreading corruption right and left. O servants of Allah, remain steadfast, for he will begin by saying: I am a prophet, and there is no prophet after me. Indeed, written between his eyes is 'disbeliever', which every believer will read. Whoever of you meets him should spit in his face and recite the opening verses of Surah of the Companions of the Cave. He will be given power over one soul from the children of Adam, so he will kill it and then bring it back to life, and he will not go beyond that, nor will he be given power over any soul other than it. Among his trials is that with him are a Paradise and a Fire, but his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire. Whoever is tested with his fire should close his eyes and seek help from Allah, and it will be coolness and peace, just as the fire was coolness and peace for Ibrahim. His days are forty days: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and the rest of the days like ordinary days. The last of his days is like a mirage: a man reaches the gate of the city in the morning, and he walks before he reaches its other gate.\" They said: How should we pray, O Messenger of Allah, in those short days? He said: \"Estimate them as you estimate the long days.\""],[7211,"The Prophet ﷺ would say to his companions: \"If one of you has performed ablution, then he eats food, he should perform ablution again, unless it is camel milk. When you drink it, rinse your mouths with water.\""],[7212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A borrowed item is to be returned.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about a covenant with Allah?\" He said, \"A covenant with Allah is most worthy of being fulfilled.\""],[7213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Whoever prays Fajr in a mosque in congregation, then remains until he performs the Duha glorification, will have the reward of a complete Hajj and Umrah, with his Hajj and Umrah accepted.\""],[7214,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A person gets what he intends, and bears what he earns, and a person is with the one he loves. Whoever dies at the end of the road is from its people.\""],[7215,"I heard an elderly man called Abu Abdullah Marih narrate that he heard Abu Umamah narrate that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I do not fear for my Ummah hunger that kills them, nor an enemy that destroys them, but I fear for my Ummah misleading leaders. If they obey them, they will tempt them, and if they disobey them, they will kill them.\""],[7216,"I heard Abu Umamah say: A man died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and they could not find a shroud for him. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we could not find a shroud for him.\" He said, \"Look in his waist-wrapper.\" They found two dinars. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Two brands. Pray over your companion.\""],[7217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah loves that His concessions be accepted, just as the servant loves the forgiveness of his Lord.\""],[7218,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out a commander, he would say: \"Shorten the sermon and reduce the speech, for some speech is sorcery.\""],[7219,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The gates of heaven are opened and the supplication of the Muslim is answered at the establishment of prayer, at the descent of rain, at the advance of the ranks, and at the sight of the Kaʿbah.”"],[7220,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no Muslim who is in charge of ten or more people but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck; his righteousness will release it or his sin will bind it. Its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is the punishment of the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7221,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when he was asked: “Will the people of Paradise have marital relations?” He said: “Yes, with a male organ that does not tire and desire that does not cease, thrust after thrust.”"],[7222,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not fast on Saturday except for an obligatory fast, and if you find nothing but the bark of a tree, then break your fast with it.”"],[7223,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Good character is part of faith, and the best of you in faith are the best of you in character.”"],[7224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.”"],[7225,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, did not make permissible anything in tribulation that He had forbidden before that. What is the matter with one of you that he comes to his brother and greets him, then later comes and kills him?”"],[7226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, a group of people will stand up, filling the horizon, their light like the sun. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it (i.e., wonder if it refers to him). Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then another group will stand up, filling what is between the horizons, their light like the moon on the night of the full moon. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it. Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then another group will stand up, filling what is between the horizons, their light like a star in the sky. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it. Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then he will take two scoops and say: 'This is for you, O Muhammad, and this is from me for you, O Muhammad.' Then the Balance will be set up and the reckoning will begin.\""],[7227,"I witnessed the Prophet's ﷺ sermon in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said many good and beautiful things, and among what he said was: \"Whoever from the People of the two Books (Jews and Christians) becomes Muslim, he will have his reward twice, and he will have the same as what is due to us, and upon him the same as what is due from us. And whoever from the polytheists becomes Muslim, he will have his reward, and he will have the same as what is due to us, and upon him the same as what is due from us.\""],[7228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he praises Allah for it, except that that praise is better than that blessing, even if it were great.”"],[7229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever is terrified by the night to endure it, is stingy with wealth to spend it, and is cowardly before the enemy to fight him, let him frequently say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise. For it is more beloved to Allah than a mountain of gold and silver spent in the path of Allah, Exalted and Glorified."],[7230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah’s chosen land is al-Sham, and in it are His chosen ones from His creation and His servants. A throng from my nation will certainly enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.”"],[7231,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is overwhelmed by the night such that he struggles through it, or is miserly with wealth such that he withholds spending it, or is cowardly before the enemy such that he fears fighting him, let him say abundantly: ‘Glory be to God and with His praise,’ for it is more beloved to God than a mountain of gold that he spends in the path of God ﷻ.”"],[7232,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no hāmah, no ṣafar, no contagion, and two months do not complete thirty days.”"],[7233,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever says in the morning three times: ‘O God, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I have entered upon the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from my evil deeds and seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,’ then if he dies on that day he will enter Paradise. And if he says in the evening three times: ‘O God, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I have entered upon the evening upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from my evil deeds and seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,’ then if he dies on that night he will enter Paradise. He said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ used to swear an oath that he would not swear about anything else, saying: “By God, no servant says it in the morning three times and then dies on that day but that he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening three times then dies on that night but that he will enter Paradise.”"],[7234,"from the Prophet ﷺ that he said, \"Indeed, Allah has forbidden the teaching of female singers, the buying and selling of them, and the consumption of their earnings.\""],[7235,"A foul-tongued woman, known for that, came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ while he had some dried meat before him that he was eating. He took a piece of dried meat with sinew and put it in his mouth, chewing it sometimes on one side and sometimes on the other. The woman said, \"O Prophet of Allah, will you not feed me?\" He said, \"Of course.\" He handed her some of what was before him, but she said, \"No, only the piece in your mouth.\" So he took it out and gave it to her. She took it, put it in her mouth, and kept chewing it until she swallowed it. After that, the foulness and sharpness of tongue that she had were no longer known of her."],[7236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever invites you, respond to him.\""],[7237,"The greatest name of God, when invoked, answers in three Surahs from the Quran: Al-Baqarah, Al-Imran, and Taha."],[7238,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever supplicates with these supplications after every prescribed prayer, my intercession will be permitted for him on the Day of Resurrection: ‘O God, grant Muhammad the wasilah, and place his love among the chosen, his rank among the worlds, and the remembrance of his abode among those brought near.’”"],[7239,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, for every hair he will have a good deed.”"],[7240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Pray.” Then he said: “Will not anyone give charity to this man by praying with him?” A man stood and prayed with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And this is a congregation.”"],[7241,"She was called Umm Hashim. She seated him behind the curtain with an inkpot and a pen, and sent to Abu Umamah asking him about a hadith he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about ablution. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever rises to perform ablution and washes his hands, sins depart from his hands. When he rinses his mouth, sins depart from his mouth. When he sniffs water into his nose and blows it out, they depart from his nose. Thus it continues until he washes his feet. If he goes out to an obligatory prayer, it is like an accepted Hajj. If he goes out to a voluntary prayer, it is like an accepted Umrah.”"],[7242,"A slave lowered himself from the fortress of al-Ta’if and came. His master came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, return my slave to me.” He said: “If a slave accepts Islam before his master, he is not returned to him. If the master accepts Islam, then the slave accepts Islam, the slave is handed over to him.”"],[7243,"I witnessed Abu Umaymah while he was in the throes of death. He said, \"If I die, then treat me as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to treat our deceased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When one of your brethren dies, and you have leveled the earth over his grave, let one of you stand at the head of his grave, and say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So.' For verily, he hears him but does not respond. Then let him say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So.' For verily, he sits up straight. Then let him say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So,' for verily, he says, 'Guide us, may Allah have mercy on you, but you do not perceive.' Then let him say, 'Remember what you used to say in the world: testimony that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that you were pleased with Allah as your Lord, with Islam as your religion, with Muhammad as your Prophet, and with the Quran as your Imam. For verily, Munkar and Nakir will come to him, and one of them will take his hand and say, 'Come with us, where we shall seat ourselves with one who has been taught his argument.' Then Allah shall be his advocate against them.' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if his mother doesn't know him?' He said, 'Then he will be attributed to Hawwa, O son of Hawwa.'\""],[7244,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When a servant stands in prayer, the gates of Paradise are opened for him, the veils between him and his Lord are lifted, and the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise face him, as long as he does not blow his nose or spit.”"],[7245,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fasts on Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside.”"],[7246,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “Praise be to God as many as what God has created; praise be to God as many as what His Book has enumerated; praise be to God as many as every thing; praise be to God for every thing; glory be to God for every thing; and glory be to God as many as every thing.”"],[7247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it.”"],[7248,"While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting, a woman came with her children, carrying some of them while others walked. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she did not ask him for anything that day except that he gave it to her. Then she departed walking. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They are bearers, mothers, and merciful to their children. Were it not for what they do with their husbands, their praying women would enter Paradise.”"],[7249,"I entered the mosque of Hims, and there was Abu Umama delousing himself in it and burying the lice in it. I sat with him, and he glorified God three times, said God is greater three times, and praised God three times. Then he said: “They are light on the tongue, heavy in the balance, and they ascend to the Most Merciful.” I said: “O Abu Umama, I am from the desert people, and the alms collectors used to transgress against us.” He said: “Alms are a right, and its collectors are in the Fire. The saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘Whether he falls short or transgresses, bring the wealth as a delegation and do not hide any of it, lest you corrupt what you hide. When you see them, do not revile them, but seek refuge in God from their evil.’”"],[7250,"Abu Umamah narrated to me in a hadith he raised to the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “No Muslim performs ablution, washing his hands, rinsing his mouth, and performing ablution as he has been commanded, except that Allah removes from him the sins he committed that day — what his mouth uttered, what his hand touched, and what he walked toward — so that the sins trickle down from his extremities. Then when he walks to the mosque, one foot records a good deed and the other erases a bad deed.”"],[7251,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The bath on Friday pulls out sins from the roots of the hair, a thorough pulling out.”"],[7252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Some people from my Ummah will spend their nights indulging in food, amusement, and play, and then they will wake up in the morning transformed into monkeys and pigs.\""],[7253,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. His prayer every day was ten rak'ahs: two rak'ahs of Fajr, two before Zuhr, two after Maghrib, and two after Isha."],[7254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ favored me over the prophets — or he said: my ummah over the nations — with four things: He sent me to all people; He made the whole earth a means of purification and a mosque for me and my ummah, so wherever a man of my ummah is overtaken by the prayer, his mosque and his purification are right there; I was aided with terror (cast into the hearts of the enemy) for a month’s journey; and the spoils of war were made lawful for me.”"],[7255,"From the Prophet ﷺ: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the husband over the wife?” He said: “If a woman were to go out of her house and then return to find her husband afflicted with severe leprosy, his nose constantly dripping, and she were to lick it with her tongue, she would not have fulfilled his right. A woman may not go out of her husband’s house except with his permission, nor may she give from his house except with his permission.”"],[7256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter, and the first of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise will be the people of goodness.\""],[7257,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the morning or the evening, he would supplicate with these words: “O God, You are more worthy of being remembered and more worthy of giving. You are the King, no partner is with You. You are the One, nothing perishes except Your face. You are not obeyed except by Your permission, and You are not disobeyed except by Your knowledge. When You are obeyed You give thanks, and when You are disobeyed You forgive. You are the nearest witness and the closest guardian. You intervened before the frontiers, You seized the forelocks, You recorded the traces, and You copied the appointed times. The hearts are disclosed to You, and the secret with You is open. The lawful is what You have made lawful, the unlawful is what You have made unlawful, the religion is what You have legislated, the command is what You have decreed, the creation is Your creation, and the servant is Your servant. You are God, the Clement, the Merciful. I ask You by the light of Your face, by which the heavens and the earth shine, by every right that is Yours, and by the right of those who ask You, that You accept me in this morning or in this evening and that You protect me from the Fire by Your power.”"],[7258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever peeps at a people through a qatarah (small hole), and his eye is gouged out, it is wasted.” Hafs said, “The qatarah is the small window.”"],[7259,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “No Muslim attends a prescribed prayer, performs ablution well, then prays well, except that God forgives by it the sins between it and the prayer that was before it.”"],[7260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to learn the Qur’an and urged us to it, saying: “The Qur’an will come to its people on the Day of Resurrection when they are most in need of it. It will say to the Muslim: ‘Do you recognize me?’ He will say: ‘Who are you?’ It will say: ‘I am the one whom you used to love and hate to part with, the one who would draw you near and bring you close.’ He will say: ‘Perhaps you are the Qur’an.’ Then he will be brought before his Lord, may He be exalted, and he will be given sovereignty in his right hand and eternity in his left, tranquility will be placed on his head, and upon his parents will be spread two robes the likes of which the world cannot weigh. They will say: ‘For what have we been clothed with this when our deeds did not merit it?’ It will be said: ‘This is because your child took up the Qur’an.’”"],[7261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and the sponsor of an orphan will be in Paradise like these two.”"],[7262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"],[7263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Give glad tidings to those who walk in the dark to the mosques of pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection, when people will be terrified but they will not be terrified.”"],[7264,"That he came to Safwan b. 'Assal al-Muradi, who was among those of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who were asked, and he said: 'Your need?' They said: 'We set out today in pursuit of knowledge.' He said: 'Indeed, whoever leaves his house in pursuit of knowledge, the angels lower their wings for the learner and the scholar.' And I asked him about wiping, and he said: 'Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ was asked and he set three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident, except due to major impurity, but due to defecation, urine, and sleep.'"],[7265,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us during travel not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except due to major impurity—but due to sleep, defecation, and urine, no.»"],[7266,"What brought you? I said: 'I came seeking knowledge.' He said: 'Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: «There is no one who goes out from his house in pursuit of knowledge except that the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does.» I said: 'I came to ask you about wiping over the leather socks.' He said: 'Yes. I was in the army that the Messenger of God ﷺ sent, and he commanded us to wipe over the leather socks when we had put them on in a state of purity—three when we travel and one night when we reside, and we do not remove them due to defecation, urine, or sleep, and we do not remove them except due to major impurity.' He said: 'And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: «There is a gate in the west open for repentance, a journey of seventy years, that will not be closed until the sun rises from its west.»'"],[7267,"What brought you? I said: 'Seeking knowledge.' He said: 'Indeed the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.' He said: I said: 'It has been troubling my mind: wiping over the leather socks after defecation and urine. I was a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I came to you to ask about that. Did you hear from him anything about it?' He said: 'Yes. He used to command us when we were traveling—or when we were travelers—not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except due to major impurity, but not due to defecation, urine, or sleep.' I said: 'Did you hear him mention desire (passionate love)?' He said: 'Yes. While we were with him on a journey, a bedouin called out to him with a loud voice—or he said with a resonant voice; Ibn 'Uyaynah was unsure—saying: \"O Muhammad!\" He answered him in a similar manner to his speech, then said: «Stop!» The man said: \"What do you think of a man who loves a people but has not joined them?\" He said: «On the Day of Resurrection he will be with those whom he loves.»' He said: 'Then he continued narrating to us until he said: «There is a gate toward the west, the width of whose passage is a journey of seventy years. God opened it for repentance on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He will not close it until the sun rises from that direction.»'"],[7268,"«When we traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he commanded us not to remove our leather socks for three nights and their days, except due to major impurity; but due to defecation or urine, no.»"],[7269,"The Prophet ﷺ set for wiping over the leather socks three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night."],[7270,"The Prophet ﷺ used to instruct us, when we traveled or were on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except from major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from urine, sleep, and defecation."],[7271,"Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us when we were on a journey or traveling not to remove or take off our leather socks for three days and their nights on account of defecation, urine, or sleep, except [in the case of] major ritual impurity. A man from the desert came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began calling him in a loud voice, 'O Muhammad, O Muhammad.' We said to him, 'Woe to you, lower or soften your voice, for you have been forbidden from this.' He said, 'No, by Allah, not until I make him hear.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Here I am.' He said, 'What do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them?' He said, 'That is with the one he loves; a person is with the one he loves.'"],[7272,"What brought you? I said, 'Seeking knowledge.' He said, 'Shall I give you glad tidings?' I said, 'Yes.' He raised the hadith and said, 'The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.' Then he asked him about wiping over the leather socks, and he said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The traveler wipes over the leather socks for three days and their nights on account of urine, defecation, or sleep, but not on account of major ritual impurity.' Then he began to narrate to us, saying, 'While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, a Bedouin called him in a loud voice, \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad, O Muhammad.\" I said, \"Lower your voice, for you have been forbidden to raise your voice.\" The Prophet ﷺ answered him in a manner similar to what he heard from him and said, \"Here I am.\" Then he asked him about love: a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A person is with the one he loves.\" Then he began to narrate to us and said, \"The gate of repentance is open from the direction of the west, and its width is a journey of seventy years; it will not be closed until the sun rises from its direction.\" Then he recited this verse: {Do they wait except that the angels should come to them...} to the end of the verse.'"],[7273,"What brought you, O bald one? I said, 'Seeking knowledge.' He said, 'It has reached me that the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does.' I said, 'Something about wiping over the leather socks has troubled me: have you memorized anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding it?' He said, 'Yes, when we were on a journey or traveling, he commanded us not to remove our leather socks for three days except on account of major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from defecation, urine, and sleep.' I said, 'Have you memorized anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about love?' He said, 'Yes, we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on such-and-such a journey when a man from the rear of the people called him in a loud voice—a coarse, rough Bedouin—and said, \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad.\" The people said to him, \"Stop, for you have been forbidden from this.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ answered him in a manner similar to his voice and said, \"Here I am.\" He said, \"A man who loves a people but has not yet joined them.\" He said, \"A person is with the one he loves.\" He continued narrating to me until he told me that Allah ﷻ made a gate in the west whose width is a journey of seventy years for repentance; it will not be closed until the sun rises from its direction. That is the saying of Allah ﷻ: {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith.}"],[7274,"I came as a delegate during the caliphate of Uthman ؓ, and what prompted me to come was to meet the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. I met Safwan b. Assal al-Muradi and said, 'Did you meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes, and I went on twelve military expeditions with him.' I said, 'Tell me about wiping over the leather socks.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were on a journey or traveling, to wipe over our leather socks for three nights and their days on account of urine, defecation, or sleep, but not on account of major ritual impurity. One night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a gate from the direction of the setting sun whose width is a journey of seventy years, open for repentance; it will not be closed until the sun rises from its direction. A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling him in a loud voice and said, \"O Muhammad, what do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them?\" The Prophet ﷺ answered him in a manner similar to his voice: \"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[7275,"When we were on a journey, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to remove our leather socks for three days except on account of major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from defecation, urine, or sleep."],[7276,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: 'For the traveler, three days and their nights; for the resident, one day and one night.'"],[7277,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'For the traveler, when he puts on his leather socks while his feet are pure, he may wipe over them for three days and their nights and not remove them on account of defecation or urine, except [in the case of] major ritual impurity.'"],[7278,"What brought you? I said, 'Seeking knowledge.' He said, 'There is no Muslim person who seeks knowledge except the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does.' I said to him, 'You are a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and something about wiping over the leather socks after defecation and urination has troubled my heart. Tell me something if you heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were on a journey or traveling, to wipe over our leather socks for three nights and their days and not to remove them except on account of major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from defecation, urine, or sleep.' I said to him, 'Have you heard him say anything about love?' He said, 'Yes, we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition or an umrah when a Bedouin came on his mount until he reached the rear of the people and began calling in a loud voice, \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad.\" It was said, \"Woe to you, lower your voice, for you have been commanded to do so.\" He said, \"By Allah, I will not do so until I make him hear.\" He was a coarse, rough Bedouin. When the Prophet ﷺ heard his voice, he said, \"Here I am.\" He said, \"What do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them?\" He said, \"That one is with the one he loves.\" He continued narrating to us until he told me that in the direction of the west there is a gate open for repentance, whose width is a journey of seventy years; it will remain open until the sun rises from its direction, and when it rises from its direction, that is when {no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith.}"],[7279,"No man goes out of his house seeking knowledge except the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does. I said to him, 'You were a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but something about wiping over the leather socks has occurred in my mind.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were on a journey or traveling, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except on account of major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from sleep, defecation, or urine.'"],[7280,"No man goes out of his house seeking knowledge except the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does. I said to him, 'You were a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but something about wiping over the leather socks has occurred in my mind.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us, when we were on a journey or traveling, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except on account of major ritual impurity, but [we could wipe] from sleep, defecation, or urine.'"],[7281,"What has brought you? I said: I have come seeking knowledge. He said: We used to say that the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. Then I asked him about wiping over the leather socks. He said: \"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, and we used to wipe for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.\""],[7282,"What has brought you? I said: You are a man who accompanied the Prophet of God ﷺ, and the matter of wiping over the leather socks after defecation and urination has troubled my heart. Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ mention anything about that? He said: Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us, when we were traveling, not to remove our leather socks for three days, but only for defecation, urination, or sleep."],[7283,"I went early to a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Safwan b. 'Assal. He said: What has brought you? I said: I have come to seek knowledge. He said: Shall I inform you that the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does? And I have seen us while we were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and a bedouin called out to him with a loud voice, saying: O Muhammad. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Here I am.\" The man said: A person loves a people but has not done their deeds. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[7284,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to instruct us, when we traveled or were on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except from major impurity, but only from sleep, urination, and defecation.\""],[7285,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him about wiping over the leather socks. I said: O Messenger of God, I have come to ask you about knowledge. He said: \"The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.\" \"And about which knowledge do you ask?\" I said: O Prophet of God, about wiping over the leather socks. He said: \"Yes, a day and a night for the resident, and three for the traveler, from defecation or urination; then he performs a new ablution.\""],[7286,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us, when we were on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights due to urination, sleep, or defecation, except from major impurity.\""],[7287,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us, when we traveled, not to remove the leather socks for three days and their nights except from major impurity, and he would command us to wipe over them from defecation, urination, and sleep.\""],[7288,"\"When we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to wipe over them for three days while traveling, except from major impurity, but only from defecation, urination, and sleep.\""],[7289,"You heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"He used to command us, when we were traveling or on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three nights and their days, except from major impurity, but only from urination, defecation, or sleep.\""],[7290,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"Three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident.\""],[7291,"What has brought you? I said: I seek knowledge. He said: The angels spread their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. And I asked him about wiping over the leather socks. He said: \"We used to wipe during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ for three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.\""],[7292,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[7293,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning wiping: “For the traveler, over the leather socks, three days and their nights; and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[7294,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to command us to wipe for three days and their nights while traveling, and for a day and a night for the resident.” And I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever sets out early seeking knowledge, the angels lower their wings for him.”"],[7295,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and began to tell us: “Indeed, repentance has a gate whose width between its two doorposts is the distance between east and west; it will not be closed until the sun rises from its west.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: {On the day when some of your Lord’s signs come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith.}"],[7296,"“Did you hear anything about it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Yes; he used to command us, when we were traveling, not to remove the leather socks for three days, except on account of major ritual impurity—but not on account of sleep, defecation, or urination.”"],[7297,"“When we were traveling, or when we were travelers, we would not remove our leather socks for three days.”"],[7298,"“The Prophet ﷺ set wiping over the leather socks for the traveler as three days and their nights, and for the resident as a day and a night.”"],[7299,"“What made you set out early?” I said: “Seeking knowledge.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Whoever sets out early seeking knowledge is in the way of God until he returns, and the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge.’” He said: “And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘God ﷻ has opened a gate for repentance from the direction of the west; the distance between its two doorposts is seventy years, and it will not be closed until the sun rises from that direction.’” He said: I said: “Give me more, may God have mercy on you.” He said: “We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey when a Bedouin with a loud voice called out to him: ‘O Muhammad, stop so that we may ask you three things.’ The Prophet ﷺ answered him with something like his words: ‘Come on.’ The Bedouin came and said: ‘A man loves a people but has not yet done their deeds.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘A person will be with those whom he loves.’ The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ had not rejoiced at any statement as much as they rejoiced at this one.” I said: “Tell me about wiping over the leather socks.” He said: “When we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey, we would wipe for three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night.” The wording is that of Ali b. al-Madini."],[7300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever visits his believing brother wades through the gardens of Paradise until he returns, and whoever visits his believing brother when he is ill wades through the gardens of Paradise until he returns.”"],[7301,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon a Jewish boy who was ill and said: “Do you testify that there is no god but God?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Do you testify that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger?” He said: “Yes.” Then he died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ and the Muslims took charge of him, washed him, and buried him."],[7302,"“Indeed, God has a rooster whose head is beneath the Throne, whose wing is in the air, and whose claws are in the earth. When it is the pre-dawn hours and the ends of the prayers, it flaps its wing and claps in glorification, and the roosters crow, answering it with glorification.”"],[7303,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he heard a man giving the call to prayer. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Upon the natural disposition.” Then he said: “I testify that there is no god but God,” and the Prophet said: “He has testified to the truth.” He said: “I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of God,” and the Prophet said: “He has come out of the Fire.”"],[7304,"From Idris al-Awdi and Ibn Abi Layla, both from Asim b. Abi al-Najud, from Zirr b. Hubaysh, from Safwan b. Assal: “The Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated in ‘When the sky is split apart.’”"],[7305,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night.”"],[7306,"“I sold to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a pair of trousers. He weighed out the payment for me and gave me more.”"],[7307,"He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a man frequently ill, so permit me to make nabidh in a small jar like these,” meaning small ones. So he gave him permission."],[7308,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Hour will not come until entire tribes are swallowed up, until it is said, ‘Who remains of the Banu So-and-so?’” I knew that he meant the Arabs, because the non-Arabs do not have tribes."],[7309,"He said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “We are in a land with many breads and vegetables, and we drink nabidh with that.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Drink of it what does not take away the intellect or the wealth.”"],[7310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Banu al-Mustaliq, and we captured the noblewomen of the Arabs. We desired mut'a, and celibacy had become hard on us, so we wanted to practice mut'a and practice coitus interruptus. Some of us said to others: It is not appropriate for us to do this while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us until we ask him. So we asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Practice coitus interruptus or do not; whatever soul Allah has decreed to exist until the Day of Resurrection will surely exist.\""],[7311,"I heard Shuqran, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: \"By Allah, I am the one who placed the velvet cloth under the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[7312,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and heard him recite this verse: {So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it}. I said: By Allah, I do not care if I hear nothing other than it; it is enough for me, enough for me."],[7313,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he presented Islam to me, so I embraced Islam, and he taught me verses of the Quran. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did deeds in the pre-Islamic era; do I have any reward for them? He said: \"What did you do?\" I said: I lost two ten-month pregnant she-camels of mine, so I went out seeking them on a camel of mine. Two tents in an open area of land appeared to me, and I headed towards them. In one of them I found an old man, and I said: Have you taken in two ten-month pregnant she-camels? He said: What are their brands? I said: The brand of Ibn Darim. He said: We found your two she-camels, and we delivered their young and let them mate, and Allah has revived through them a household of your people from the Arabs of Mudar. While he was speaking to me, a woman from the other tent called out: She gave birth, to whom she gave birth, he said: What did she give birth to? If it is a boy, he has shared in our people; if it is a girl, we bury her. She said: A girl. I said: What is this buried alive one? He said: A daughter of mine. I said: I will buy her from you. He said: O brother of Banu Tamim, do you say, will you sell your daughter, when I have told you that I am a man from the Arabs of Mudar? I said: I am not buying her neck from you; I am buying her soul so that you will not kill her. He said: With what will you buy her? I said: These two she-camels of mine and their young. He said: Will you add this camel of yours? I said: Yes, on condition that you send a messenger with me, and when I reach my family, I will return the camel to you. So he did. When I reached my family, I returned the camel to him. Later that night, I thought to myself: This is a noble act that no one among the Arabs preceded me to, and Islam has appeared, and I have revived three hundred and sixty buried alive girls, buying each one of them with two ten-month pregnant she-camels and a camel. Do I have any reward for that? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have its reward, since Allah has blessed you with Islam.\" Ubada said: The confirmation of Sa'sa'ah's statement is the saying of al-Farazdaq."],[7314,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, sometimes I have surplus food that I set aside for calamity and for the wayfarer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest.\""],[7315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am your forerunner at the Pond, and I will vie with other nations through you, so do not revert after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\""],[7316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am your forerunner at the Pond, and I will vie with other nations through you, so do not fight one another after me.\""],[7317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am your forerunner at the Pond, vying with other nations through you; do not fight one another after me.\""],[7318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a fine she-camel among the zakat camels and said: \"May Allah curse the owner of this she-camel.\" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought it back with a camel from the fringes of the herd. He said: \"Then how excellent.\""],[7319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My nation will remain in a firm hold of its religion as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars become intertwined, imitating the Jews, and as long as they do not delay the Fajr prayer, imitating the Christians.\""],[7320,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7321,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7322,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7323,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7324,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7325,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7326,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about protected grazing land, and he said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7327,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7328,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7329,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no protected grazing land except for God and His Messenger.”"],[7330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Abwā', and I gifted him a wild donkey, but he returned it to me. When he saw the displeasure on my face, he said: “It is not that we are rejecting your gift, but we are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[7331,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; Ḥ; and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyāṭī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us, Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtba, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from al-Ṣaʿb b. Jaththāma, that he gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was at al-Abwā' or at Waddān, a wild donkey, and the Prophet ﷺ returned it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw what was on my face, he said: “We did not reject it except because we are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[7332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him at al-Abwāʾ or at Waddān, and I gave him a wild donkey as a gift, and he returned it to me. When he saw displeasure in my face, he said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7333,"A wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwāʾ, and he returned it to its owner, then said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7334,"He gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned it to him. When he saw what was in my face from his returning my gift, he said: \"Indeed, it is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7335,"I gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a wild donkey that I had hunted at Waddān, and I presented it to him at al-Abwāʾ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to me, and he saw what was in my face from the severity of that upon me, so he said: \"We did not return it to you out of dislike for it, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7336,"A man gifted the meat of a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned it to him and said: \"We are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7337,"He gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned it, and he saw that in his face, so he said: \"We did not return it to you except that we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7338,"I gifted a wild donkey to the Prophet ﷺ, and he returned it to me. When he saw [what was] in my face, he said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7339,"I gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the state of iḥrām, and he returned it to me. When he saw what was in my face, he said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7340,"I heard al-Ṣaʿb b. Jaththāmah say: I gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Abwāʾ, and he returned it to me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognized in my face the dislike of his returning it, he said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7341,"He informed him that he gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Waddān, and he returned it."],[7342,"He informed him that he gifted a wild donkey to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwāʾ or at Waddān. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to me, and when he recognized in my face [the effect of] his returning it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not that we reject it against you, but we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7343,"I gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the leg of a wild donkey while he was at Waddān, and he returned it to me. When he saw what was in my face, he said: \"We did not return it to you except that we are in the state of iḥrām.\""],[7344,"That he gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a wild donkey while he was at Waddan or al-Abwa, and he returned it to him. Then he recognized in my face the sadness of his returning it to me, so he said, “It is not that we reject it for you, but we are in the state of ihram.”"],[7345,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was at al-Abwa, so I gifted him a wild donkey, and he returned it to me. When he saw dislike in my face, he said, “It is not that we reject it for you, but we are in the state of ihram.”"],[7346,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, we strike during a night raid among the children of the polytheists.” He said, “They are from them.”"],[7347,"That he said, “O Messenger of Allah, we raid a settlement at night from the polytheists, and with them are their women and children, and we kill them.” He said, “They are from them.”"],[7348,"That it was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Horses raided at night and struck some of the children of the polytheists.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “They are from their fathers.”"],[7349,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about horses trampling the children of the polytheists at night. He said, “They are from their fathers.”"],[7350,"They said, “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, our horses trampled children among the children of the polytheists.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “They are from their fathers.” And he did not mention al-Zuhri, nor Ubayd Allah, nor al-Sa'b."],[7351,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ about a raiding party that strikes the offspring during the violence of a raid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Their children are from them.”"],[7352,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ about a raiding party that strikes the offspring during the violence of a raid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Their children are from them.”"],[7353,"That he said to the Prophet ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, we raid a settlement at night from the polytheists, and with them are their children and women, and we kill them.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “They are with their fathers.”"],[7354,"“O Messenger of Allah, horses in the violence of a raid strike some of the children of the polytheists.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “They are from them, or with the fathers.”"],[7355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the enemy being raided at night, and some of their women and children being struck during the raid. He said, “They are from them.”"],[7356,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about children in the dwellings of the polytheists—we raid them at night, so what about the children who are under the raid? He said, “They are from them.”"],[7357,"He said: “O Messenger of Allah, the children of the polytheists—we strike them in a night raid.” He said, “Do not do that again, but there is no blame, for their children are from them.” And he forbade killing women and children."],[7358,"We said: “O Messenger of Allah, a dwelling among the dwellings of the polytheists—we attack it at dawn and we may strike the children under the bellies of the horses without realizing it?” He said, “They are from them.”"],[7359,"They are called Banū Sahm b. ʿAmr, a clan from Banū Qutayba.”"],[7360,"“Abū Umāma al-Bāhilī, may Allah have mercy on him, died—his name was Ṣudayy b. ʿAjlān—in the year eighty-six, at the age of ninety-one.”"],[7361,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the words of Allah, may He be exalted, {He will be given to drink of purulent water, which he will gulp} (Q 14:16): He said, “It is brought near to him and he finds it repulsive, but when it is brought close to him, it roasts his face and the scalp of his head falls off, and when he drinks it, it severs his intestines until it comes out of his backside.” Allah, may He be exalted, says, {And they will be given boiling water to drink so that it cuts their intestines} (Q 47:15); Allah, may He be exalted, says, {If they call for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten brass, which scalds the faces—wretched is the drink} (Q 18:29)."],[7362,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Make Allah beloved to His servants, and Allah will love you.”"],[7363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Make Allah beloved to His servants, and Allah will love you.”"],[7364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a military expedition, so I came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared another expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a third expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I came to you twice asking you to pray for martyrdom for me, and you said, ‘O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils,’ so we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils.”"],[7365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a military expedition, so I came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared another expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a third expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I came to you twice asking you to pray for martyrdom for me, and you said, ‘O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils,’ so we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils.”"],[7366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a military expedition, so I came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared another expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for martyrdom for me.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prepared a third expedition, and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I came to you twice asking you to pray for martyrdom for me, and you said, ‘O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils,’ so we went on the expedition and remained safe and obtained spoils.”"],[7367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military detachment, and I went out among them. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to grant me martyrdom.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” So we remained safe and obtained spoils. Then he sent another army, and I went out among them. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to grant me martyrdom.” He said, “O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils.” Then the third time was the same, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I came to you three times asking you to pray for martyrdom for me, and you said, ‘O Allah, grant them safety and grant them spoils,’ so we remained safe and obtained spoils. O Messenger of Allah, command me with a deed.” He said, “You must observe fasting, for it has no like and no equal.” Abū Umāma said, “He was granted much good because of that.”"],[7368,"“The Prophet ﷺ initiated a military expedition,” so Abu Idris al-Khawlani mentioned it from Abu Umamah."],[7369,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Perform the night prayer, for it is the habit of the righteous before you, and it is a means of nearness to your Lord, an expiation for sins, and a deterrent from wrongdoing.”"],[7370,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Fever is a bellows from Hellfire; whatever a believer is afflicted by from it will be his share of the Fire.”"],[7371,"When the dinner was removed from before the Prophet ﷺ, he would say, “Praise be to God, abundant, pure, and blessed, not sufficient, nor abandoned, nor dispensable, our Lord.”"],[7372,"When the Prophet ﷺ removed his dining table, he would say, “Praise be to God, abundant, pure, and blessed, not sufficient, nor abandoned, nor dispensable, our Lord.”"],[7373,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say upon finishing food, “Praise be to God, abundant, pure, and blessed, not sufficient, nor abandoned, nor dispensable.”"],[7374,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that upon finishing his food he would say, “Praise be to God, abundant, pure, and blessed, not sufficient, nor abandoned, nor dispensable, our Lord.”"],[7375,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever goes to the mosque intending only to learn good or to teach it, will have the reward of a pilgrim whose pilgrimage is complete.”"],[7376,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The days will not pass until a group of my ummah drinks wine, calling it by another name.”"],[7377,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “God ﷻ blames for helplessness, so exert yourself; if you are overcome, say: ‘I have put my trust in God’ or ‘God is sufficient for me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.’”"],[7378,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “What a man spends on his household, his family, his children, and his servants is charity for him.”"],[7379,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God, glorified and exalted be He, loves gentleness, is pleased with it, and grants help upon it what He does not grant upon harshness.”"],[7380,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “There is no servant who enters Paradise except that at his head and at his feet sit women of the wide-eyed houris, singing to him with the most beautiful voice heard by jinn and humans — and it is not with the flutes of Satan, but with the glorification of God and His sanctification.”"],[7381,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, “Do the people of Paradise have intercourse?” He said, “Vigorously, vigorously, but there is no semen and no death.”"],[7382,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever dies as a frontier guard in the path of God, God will protect him from the trial of the grave.”"],[7383,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Modesty and ineloquence are from faith, and they draw near to Paradise and distance from the Fire; obscenity and vulgarity are from Satan, and they draw near to the Fire and distance from Paradise.” A Bedouin said to Abu Umamah, “We say in poetry that ineloquence is from stupidity.” He said, “Do you think I say, ‘The Messenger of God ﷺ said’ while you beautify with your poetry something foul?”"],[7384,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “There is no man whose face becomes dusty in the path of God except that God will protect him from the smoke of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, and there is no man whose feet become dusty in the path of God except that God will protect his feet from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7385,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “How excellent a man am I for the wicked of my community.” A man among those seated with him said, “How are you, O Messenger of God, for the best of them?” He said, “As for the wicked of my community, God will admit them to Paradise through my intercession; and as for the best of them, God will admit them to Paradise through their deeds.”"],[7386,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever prays the Friday prayer, fasts his day, visits a sick person, attends a funeral, and witnesses a marriage, Paradise is assured for him.”"],[7387,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ, he said, “There is no servant who is afflicted with a bout of illness except that God raises him from it purified.”"],[7388,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “The bonds of Islam will certainly be undone one by one; and whenever a bond is undone, people cling to the one that follows it. The first of them to be undone is governance, and the last of them is prayer.”"],[7389,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The people of the garrison towns who remain stationed in the path of God are a support for the Muslims and their frontier. So do not charge them excessive prices, do not hoard, let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, let no man outbid his brother, let no man propose over his brother’s proposal, and let no woman seek to overturn her sister’s vessel. For everyone’s provision is upon God, glorified and exalted be He.”"],[7390,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise for one who abandons disputation even if he is in the right; and of a house in the middle of Paradise for one who abandons lying even if he is jesting; and of a house in the highest part of Paradise for one who makes his character excellent.”"],[7391,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Four are cursed by Allah above His Throne, and His angels affirm it against them: the one who withholds himself from women and does not marry or take a concubine in order that no child be born to him; a man who imitates women though Allah created him male; a woman who imitates men though Allah ﷻ created her female; and the one who misleads the poor.\" Khalid b. al-Zibriqan said: \"That is, he mocks them. He says to a poor person, 'Come, I will give you,' but when the man comes, he says, 'I have nothing with me.' And he says to a blind person, 'Beware of the well, beware of the animal,' while there is nothing in front of him. And the man who asks about the people's home and directs him to another.\""],[7392,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"O Allah, I ask You for a soul at peace with You, that believes in meeting You, is content with Your decree, and is satisfied with Your giving.\""],[7393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Three things: whoever has one of them is guaranteed by Allah ﷻ. Whoever goes out in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah: if He takes his life, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family, then with whatever reward or spoils he has obtained. A man who is in the mosque is guaranteed by Allah: if He takes his life, He will admit him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family, then with whatever reward or spoils he has obtained. And a man who enters his house with peace is guaranteed by Allah ﷻ.\""],[7394,"He narrated to us that he said: \"Indeed, this gathering of yours is part of Allah's conveying to you and His proof against you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conveyed what he was sent with, and his companions conveyed what they heard, so convey what you hear. Three are all guaranteed by Allah ﷻ: a man who goes out in the path of Allah, he is guaranteed by Allah until He admits him to Paradise or with whatever reward or spoils he obtains; and a man who enters his house with peace.\" Then he said: \"Indeed, in Hell there is a bridge with seven arches, upon the middle of which is judgment. The servant will be brought until when he reaches the middle arch, it will be said to him: 'What debt do you owe?' And he recited this verse: {And they will not conceal from Allah any account} (4:42). He said: Then he will say: 'O Lord, I owe such-and-such.' It will be said to him: 'Pay your debt.' He will say: 'I have nothing, and I do not know how to pay.' It will be said: 'Take from his good deeds.' So it will continue to be taken from his good deeds until no good deed remains for him. When his good deeds are exhausted, it will be said: 'His good deeds are exhausted.' It will be said: 'Take from the evil deeds of those who have claims against him and load them upon him.' Indeed, I have been informed that men will come with good deeds like mountains, and it will continue to be taken for those who have claims against them until no good deed remains for them.\""],[7395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, banners will emerge from the east for the Banu al-Abbas, the first of them is cursed and the last of them is cursed. Do not help them; may Allah not help them. Whoever walks under any of their banners, Allah will admit him to Hell on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, they are the worst of Allah's creation, and their followers are the worst of Allah's creation. They claim that they are from me; indeed, I am innocent of them and they are innocent of me. Their mark is that they grow their hair long and wear black. Do not sit with them in gatherings, do not trade with them in the markets, do not guide them on the road, and do not give them water to drink. The people of heaven are disturbed by their takbir.\""],[7396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be four truces between you and the Romans. The fourth will be established by the hand of a man from the family of Heraclius and will last seven years.\" A man from Abd al-Qays called al-Mustawrid b. Khaylan said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, who will be the imam of the people on that day?\" He said: \"One of my descendants, forty years old, as if his face is a shining star, with a black mole on his right cheek, wearing two Qahwani cloaks, as if he is from the men of the Children of Israel. He will rule for twenty years, extract treasures, and conquer the cities of polytheism.\""],[7397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the prayer is established, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered. When the one departing from the prayer leaves and has not said: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire, admit me to Paradise, and marry me to the wide-eyed maidens,' the Fire says: 'Woe to this one! Was he unable to seek Allah's protection from Hell?' And Paradise says: 'Woe to this one! Was he unable to ask Allah for Paradise?' And the wide-eyed maidens say: 'Woe to this one! Was he unable to ask Allah to marry him to the wide-eyed maidens?'\""],[7398,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Beware of the believer's insight, for he sees with the light of Allah.\""],[7399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother.\""],[7400,"Abu Umamah met me and took my hand, then he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met me and took my hand, then he said: 'O Abu Umamah, indeed among the believers are those whose hearts soften for me.'\""],[7401,"From Rashid b. Sa'd and Damrah b. Habib that they both heard Abu Umamah say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me what to say upon finishing food. He said: 'O Allah, You have fed us, given us drink, and quenched our thirst. To You be praise, not denied, not forsaken, and not dispensed with.'\""],[7402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Under the shade of the sky, there is no god worshipped besides Allah greater than a followed desire in the sight of Allah.\""],[7403,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Water is not made impure by anything except what overcomes its smell or taste.\""],[7404,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Your Lord, Exalted is He, said: When I seize the dearest part of My servant while he is attached to it, and he praises Me for that, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[7405,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever testifies that I am the Messenger of Allah should not attend the prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7406,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever testifies that I am the Messenger of Allah should not attend the prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7407,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever testifies that I am the Messenger of Allah should not attend the prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of you should come to prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of you should come to prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of you should come to prayer while restraining the urge to urinate until he relieves himself.\""],[7411,"He heard Abu Umamah saying that a man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and left behind two dinars as debt, and he did not have the means to pay it back. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused to offer the funeral prayer for him and said, \"Pray for your companion.\" So Abu Qatadah stood up and said, \"I will settle the debt on his behalf.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and offered the funeral prayer for him."],[7412,"He heard Abu Umamah say: A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and left two dinars as a debt upon him, and he had no means to repay it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused to pray over him and said: \"Pray over your companion.\" Abu Qatadah stood up to him and said: \"I will pay it on his behalf.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed over him."],[7413,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you recognize your nation on the Day of Resurrection? He said: \"Yes.\" I said: Those you have seen and those you have not seen? He said: \"Those I have seen? And those I have not seen?\" I said: By what means? He said: \"They will be radiant, with white marks on their faces and limbs from the traces of ablution.\""],[7414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one who hopes for the days of Allah should enjoy the use of silk.\""],[7415,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one who hopes for the Days of Allah will enjoy wearing silk.\""],[7416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be men from my nation who eat varieties of food, drink varieties of drink, wear varieties of clothing, and are eloquent in speech. Those are the worst of my nation.\""],[7417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be men from my nation who eat varieties of food, drink varieties of drink, wear varieties of clothing, and are eloquent in speech. Those are the worst of my nation.\""],[7418,"From Rashid b. Sa'd and Habib b. Ubayd that they heard Abu Umamah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me what to say upon finishing food. He said: Say: \"O Allah, You fed us and gave us drink, so to You be praise, without being rejected or dispensed with, O our Lord.\""],[7419,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is this matter (leadership) only among your people?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then enjoin them to us.\" So he said to Quraysh: \"I warn you of Allah, lest you be harsh with my nation after me.\""],[7420,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is this matter (leadership) only among your people?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then enjoin them to us.\" So he said to Quraysh: \"I warn you of Allah, lest you be harsh with my nation after me.\""],[7421,"About the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , he said, \"Indeed, when a leader seeks personal gain from the people, he corrupts them.\""],[7422,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The best leaders of Quraysh are the best leaders of people.\""],[7423,"He used to greet everyone he met with salam. He said: I do not know of anyone who preceded him in greeting except a Jew who once hid behind a pillar for him, then came out and greeted him. Abu Umamah said to him: \"Woe to you, O Jew, what led you to do what you did?\" He said: \"I saw that you are a man who greets often, so I knew it was a virtue and I wanted to attain it.\" Abu Umamah said: \"Woe to you, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah has made salam a greeting for our nation and a protection for the people of our covenant.'\""],[7424,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a plowshare and said: \"It does not enter a people's home except that Allah humiliates them.\""],[7425,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"My Lord, may He be exalted, has promised me to admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my nation without reckoning or punishment, and three handfuls from the handfuls of my Lord, may He be exalted.\""],[7426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what does 'sweeten him' mean?\" He said: \"He opens for him a righteous deed then takes him while upon it.\""],[7427,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on his she-camel al-Jad'a during the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: \"I enjoin you to be good to the neighbor,\" until he repeated it a lot, so I said: \"He will surely make him an heir.\""],[7428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to spread salam."],[7429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to spread salam."],[7430,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I am the first of the Arabs to enter Paradise, Suhayb is the first of the Romans to enter Paradise, Bilal is the first of the Abyssinians to enter Paradise, and Salman is the first of the Persians to enter Paradise.\""],[7431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has servants whom He will seat on the Day of Resurrection upon pulpits of light, and their faces will be covered with light until He finishes reckoning the creatures.\""],[7432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever teaches a servant a verse from the Book of Allah, he is his patron; it is not fitting for him to forsake him or to prefer himself over him.\""],[7433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Reprimand (or admonish) the horses, for they are reprimanded.\""],[7434,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Shall I tell you about al-Khidr?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"While he was walking one day in the market of the Children of Israel, a man who was a mukatab (a slave with a contract of manumission) saw him and said, 'Give me charity, may Allah bless you.' Al-Khidr said, 'I believe in Allah; whatever Allah wills of a matter will happen. I have nothing to give you.' The poor man said, 'I ask you by the face of Allah, why did you not give me charity? For I saw the mark of goodness in your face and hoped for blessing from you.' Al-Khidr said, 'I believe in Allah; I have nothing to give you except that you take me and sell me.' The poor man said, 'Is this possible?' He said, 'Yes, I speak the truth. You have asked me by a great matter. I will not disappoint you by the face of my Lord; sell me.' So he took him to the market and sold him for four hundred dirhams. He stayed with the buyer for a time, not using him for anything. Then he said to him, 'You bought me seeking good from me; so advise me of some work.' He said, 'I dislike to burden you, for you are an old, weak man.' He said, 'It does not burden me.' He said, 'Then get up and move these stones,' which would not be moved by fewer than six men in a day. The man went out for some need, then returned and found that he had moved the stones in an hour. He said, 'You have done well and excelled, and you were able to do what I did not think you could do.' Then a journey presented itself to the man, and he said, 'I consider you trustworthy, so be my deputy over my family with good deputation.' He said, 'Advise me of some work.' He said, 'I dislike to burden you.' He said, 'It does not burden me.' He said, 'Then make bricks for my house until I return to you.' The man went on his journey, and when he returned, he found that the building had been raised. He said, 'I ask you by the face of Allah, what is your way and what is your affair?' He said, 'You asked me by the face of Allah, and the face of Allah caused me to fall into servitude.' Al-Khidr said, 'I will tell you who I am. I am al-Khidr, of whom you have heard. A poor man asked me for charity, and I had nothing to give him. He asked me by the face of Allah, so I gave him possession of my neck, and he sold me. And I tell you that whoever is asked by the face of Allah and refuses the asker while able, he will stand on the Day of Resurrection with his skin but no flesh and no bone, rattling.' The man said, 'I believe in Allah; I have burdened you, O Prophet of Allah, and I did not know.' He said, 'No harm; you did well and kept me.' The man said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Prophet of Allah; judge in my family and property as Allah shows you, or I give you the choice and free you.' He said, 'I would love for you to free me so that I may worship my Lord.' So he freed him. Al-Khidr said, 'Praise be to Allah who caused me to fall into servitude and then saved me from it.'\""],[7435,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O people, Allah has given every possessor of a right his right; there is no bequest to an heir.\""],[7436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after every prescribed prayer, nothing prevents him from entering Paradise except death.\" Muhammad b. Ibrahim added in his hadith: \"And 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'\""],[7437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable,' no deed will outstrip it and no sin will remain with it.\""],[7438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' will have the like of a hundred slaves set free if he says it a hundred times.\""],[7439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' will have the like of a hundred slaves set free if he says it a hundred times.\""],[7440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' will have the like of a hundred slaves set free if he says it a hundred times.\""],[7441,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O people, verily there is no prophet after me and no community after you. So worship your Lord, perform your five prayers, fast your month, give the zakah of your wealth with your souls being content with it, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.”"],[7442,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever lashes the back of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[7443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Tabuk and Jibril ﷺ said, \"O Muhammad, bear witness to the funeral of Mu'awiya bin Mu'awiya Al-Muzani.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and Jibril ﷺ descended with seventy thousand angels. He placed his right wing on the mountains, and it became humbled. And he placed his left wing on the earth, and it became humbled until he looked at Makkah and Madinah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ , Jibril, and the angels prayed upon him. When they finished, he said, \"O Jibril, did Mu'awiya bin Mu'awiya Al-Muzani attain this station?\" Jibril replied, \"With the recitation of 'He is Allah, the One' while standing, sitting, riding, and walking.\""],[7444,"A man said: “This is a foolish old man whose mind has gone.” Abu Umamah said: “Indeed, I have not narrated to you except what I heard.”"],[7445,"A man said: “What is sin, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “What pricks in your chest, so leave it.”"],[7446,"A man said: “What is sin, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “What pricks in your chest, so leave it.”"],[7447,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?” He said: “When your good deed pleases you and your evil deed displeases you, then you are a believer.”"],[7448,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Will the people of Paradise marry?” He said: “Yes, and they will eat and drink.”"],[7449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Quran, for it will come as an intercessor for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. And upon you are the two bright ones, al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, arguing on behalf of their companion on the Day of Resurrection. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it.”"],[7450,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Recite the Quran, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection to defend its companions. Recite the two bright ones, al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, arguing on behalf of their companions. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it.”"],[7451,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “How many (years) were between him and Nuh and Ibrahim?” He said: “Ten centuries.” He said: “How many (years) were between Nuh and Ibrahim?” He said: “Ten centuries.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, how many messengers were there?” He said: “Three hundred and thirteen.”"],[7452,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “My cistern is as wide as the distance between Aden and Oman. In it are pitchers as numerous as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst again. Among those who will come to it from my community are those with disheveled heads and dirty clothes, who do not marry the soft-living women and do not attend the gates, meaning the gates of the authorities – those who give everything that is due from them but are not given everything that is due to them.”"],[7453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three people from whom neither ransom nor compensation will be accepted on the Day of Resurrection: an undutiful person, a person who reminds others of his favors, and a person who denies divine decree.”"],[7454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform ablution from what the fire had touched."],[7455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform ablution from trodden ground."],[7456,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “No one wears silk in this world except one who has no share in the Hereafter.”"],[7457,"I was in Damascus when they brought heads and placed them on the steps of the Damascus mosque. I saw Abu Umamah crying, so I asked him, \"What makes you cry, O Abu Umamah?\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There will be people in my Ummah who recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will abandon the religion as an arrow passes through a target. They will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch.' A calamity awaits those who kill them, and they will kill him.\""],[7458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and washed his hands three times each, purified his face three times each, and his forearms three times each, and wiped his head and his ears, and said: “The ears are part of the head,” and he washed what was in it. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu Umar."],[7459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of Quba: “What is this purification with which you have been singled out in this verse: ‘In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves’?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, none of us comes out from defecation except that he washes his posterior.”"],[7460,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever grows a gray hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, whether he misses or hits, it will be for him like freeing a neck from the descendants of Ishmael.”"],[7461,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever deliberately relates a false hadith from me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[7462,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban for three days during travel, and for a day and a night while resident."],[7463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the worst of people in standing with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a servant who destroyed his Hereafter for the worldly gain of another.”"],[7464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a Muslim man performs ablution, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands and his feet. If he sits, he sits forgiven.”"],[7465,"The supererogatory prayer was only for the Prophet ﷺ."],[7466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and does it thoroughly, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”"],[7467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then stands for prayer, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”"],[7468,"He said: ‘Yes. Indeed, had I not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except once, twice, thrice, four times, or five times, I would not have narrated it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a Muslim man performs ablution then sets out for prayer, his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”’ Abu Zabyah then said: ‘Amr b. Abasah narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the like of this hadith, and he added in it: “When a man goes to his bed in a state of purity, then wakes during the night, he does not ask Allah, Exalted is He, for anything of the good of this world or the Hereafter except that He gives it to him.”’"],[7469,"Had I not heard it from the Prophet ﷺ except seven times, I would not have narrated it. He said: “When a man performs ablution as he has been commanded, sin departs from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”"],[7470,"Had I not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except seven times, I would not have narrated it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man performs ablution as he has been commanded, sin departs from his hearing, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”"],[7471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, his sins depart from his ears, his sight, his hands, and his feet.”"],[7472,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever goes to his bed in a state of purity, remembering Allah until drowsiness overtakes him, he does not overcome any hour of the night asking Allah for something of the good of this world or the Hereafter except that Allah gives it to him.”"],[7473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purity expiates, and prayer is a supererogatory act.”"],[7474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ablution expiates what came before it, then prayer becomes a supererogatory act.”"],[7475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ablution expiates what came before it.”"],[7476,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ablution expiates what came before it.”"],[7477,"A man from the People of the Ṣuffah died, and a dinar was found in his waist-wrapper. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A brand-mark.\" Then another died, and two dinars were found in his waist-wrapper. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Two brand-marks.\""],[7478,"A man from the People of the Ṣuffah died, and a dinar was found in his waist-wrapper. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"A brand-mark.\" Then another died, and two dinars were found in his waist-wrapper. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Two brand-marks.\""],[7479,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"People are a tree bearing fruit; soon they will become a tree bearing thorns. If you deal strictly with them, they will deal strictly with you; if you leave them, they will not leave you; and if you flee from them, they will seek you.\" He said: \"Then what is the way out of that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"You lend them from your honor for the day of your need.\""],[7480,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Cheating an unsuspecting person is forbidden.\""],[7481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood among the people, and established brotherhood between himself and 'Alī ؓ."],[7482,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever walks to an obligatory prayer in congregation, it is like a ḥajj; and whoever walks to a voluntary prayer, it is like a complete 'umrah.\""],[7483,"Makḥūl narrated to me that they entered upon Abū Umāmah ؓ, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever goes out in the path of Allah, Allah is a guarantor for him: if Allah causes him to die, He will admit him to Paradise; and if He returns him, He returns him with whatever reward and spoils he has obtained.\" The full hadith."],[7484,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Fulfill the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you.\""],[7485,"I heard Abū Umāmah say: The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite poetry and laugh while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting,\" smiling with them.\""],[7486,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"One prayer following another prayer, with no idle talk between them, is a record in 'Illiyyīn.\""],[7487,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Sunnah prayer on his camel."],[7488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The ablution for sleep is that you touch water, then wipe your face, hands, and feet with that touch, like the wipe of tayammum.\""],[7489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgives when he is able to punish, Allah will forgive him on the Day of Distress.\""],[7490,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The minimum duration of menstruation is three days and its maximum is ten.\""],[7491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer wrapped in a velvet cloak, having crossed its two ends."],[7492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever learns a verse from the Book of Allah ﷻ, it will meet him on the Day of Resurrection smiling in his face.\""],[7493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Any young person who grows up in the worship of Allah until he dies, Allah will grant him the reward of ninety-nine veracious ones (siddiqun).\""],[7494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Any young person who grows up in seeking knowledge and worship until he becomes old, Allah will grant him on the Day of Resurrection the reward of seventy-two veracious ones (siddiqun).\""],[7495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who scratch their faces and tear their garments at the neck in mourning."],[7496,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not sell fruit until its ripeness is apparent.\""],[7497,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be approached until they give birth."],[7498,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that arrows (or shares) be sold until they are divided."],[7499,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches false hair and the one who has it done, and the tattooer and the one tattooed."],[7500,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ cursed the one who severs family ties, the one who maintains severed family ties, the female tattoo artist, and the one who gets tattooed.\""],[7501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was struck by 'Abdullah b. Qami'ah with a stone on the day of Uhud, wounding his face and breaking his front tooth, and he said, \"Take that, and I am Ibn Qami'ah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him while wiping the blood from his face, \"What is the matter with you? May Allah diminish you.\" Then Allah set upon him a mountain goat, not any ordinary goat, and it kept butting him until it cut him into pieces."],[7502,"From the Prophet ﷺ: When Ibn Qami'ah struck him on the day of Uhud, \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he performed ablution, untie a bandage and wipe over it with the water of ablution.\""],[7503,"\"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dislike yawning during prayer.\""],[7504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat between the two eyes of Hell.\" This distressed his companions, so they said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we narrate hadith from you, adding and subtracting.\" He said: \"That is not what I mean by you. I mean only the one who lies about me while speaking, seeking thereby to defame Islam.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you said 'between the two eyes of Hell'—does Hell have an eye?\" He said: \"Yes. Have you not heard Him say: 'When it sees them from a distant place, they will hear its raging and roaring' (Q 25:12)? Does it see them except with two eyes?\""],[7505,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the strap of the Prophet's ﷺ sandal broke. He said: \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return.\" A man said to him: \"This is just a sandal strap.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is a calamity.\""],[7506,"From Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, and Wathilah, they said: We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Keep your children, your insane, your disputes, your voices, the drawing of your swords, and the execution of your legal punishments away from your mosques. Perfume them on Fridays, and place places of purification at the doors of your mosques.\""],[7507,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from sudden death, and he liked to fall ill before dying."],[7508,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from sudden death, and he liked to fall ill before dying."],[7509,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ riding, and we passed by a large herd of camels. He said: \"To whom does this belong?\" They said: \"To the Banu al-Anbar.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Those are our people.\""],[7510,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Beware of urine, for it is the first thing about which a servant is called to account in the grave.\""],[7511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The complete period of ribat (frontier guarding) is forty days. Whoever performs ribat for forty days without buying or selling and without committing any sin will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[7512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of urine, for it is the first thing about which a servant is called to account in the grave.\""],[7513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting is a shield and a fortress among the fortresses of the believer. Every deed belongs to its doer, but fasting is Mine, and I reward for it.\""],[7514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not revile the rulers, but supplicate to Allah for them, for their righteousness is righteousness for you.\""],[7515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, whether it falls short or reaches its target, the reward of freeing a slave is written for him.\""],[7516,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever sends blessings upon me, God sends blessings upon him tenfold, and an angel is entrusted with it until he conveys it to me.\""],[7517,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Dust in the nostrils of a servant in the path of God and the smoke of Hell will never combine.\""],[7518,"From Abu Umamah ؓ that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves for God, hates for God, gives for God, and withholds for God has completed faith.\""],[7519,"\"Indeed, this council of yours is a communication from Allah to you, and His argument against you. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace, has conveyed the message, so convey it.\""],[7520,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest to an heir.\""],[7521,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest to an heir.\""],[7522,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest to an heir.\""],[7523,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right, and there is no bequest to an heir.\""],[7524,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"In the latter times there will be officials who go out in the wrath of God and return in the displeasure of God. Beware lest you be among their intimates.\""],[7525,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in his sermon in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O people, there is no prophet after me, and no community after you. Worship your Lord, perform your five prayers, fast your month, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.\""],[7526,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The devils go out with their banners to the markets, entering with the first to enter and leaving with the last to leave.\""],[7527,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Do not revert to disbelief after me, striking the necks of one another.\""],[7528,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A loan must be returned, a gift of a milking animal must be returned, and a guarantor is liable.\""],[7529,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The borrowed item is to be returned, the gift given temporarily for milking or benefit is to be given back, and the guarantor is responsible for the debt.”"],[7530,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The borrowed item is to be returned, the gift given temporarily for milking or benefit is to be given back, and the guarantor is responsible for the debt.”"],[7531,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There is no prophet after me, and no community after you. Worship your Lord, fast your month, pray your five prayers, and pay the zakat of your wealth willingly, with your souls content, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.”"],[7532,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He turned away from him. Then he said, “I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He turned away from him. Then he said, “O Messenger of God, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He turned away from him. Then the prayer was called, and when he had said the salutation, he said, “O Messenger of God, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He said, “Did you perform ablution?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Did you pray when we prayed?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Go, for God has forgiven you.”"],[7533,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came and said, “O Messenger of God, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. He repeated, “I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.” He said, “The prayer was called, so the Messenger of God ﷺ entered and then left.” Shaddad said: Abu Umamah told me: “I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ while the man followed him, saying, ‘O Messenger of God, I have committed a punishable offense, so carry out the punishment on me.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said, ‘When you left your house, did you perform ablution and do it well?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘And did you attend the prayer with us?’ He said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘God ﷻ has forgiven you your offense’ or he said, ‘your debt.’”"],[7534,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “If you give away surplus wealth, it is better for you; if you withhold it, it is bad for you. You will not be blamed for keeping what is sufficient. Begin with those you support. The upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[7535,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[7536,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “No one wears silk in this world except one who has no share in the Hereafter.”"],[7537,"I heard Abu Umamah say: A man came to the Messenger of God and said, “O Messenger of God, what do you think of a man who seeks good and reputation—what is for him?” He said, “Nothing for him,” saying that three times. “God ﷻ does not accept any deed except what is sincere for Him and by which His face is sought.”"],[7538,"From Abu Umamah al-Bahili ؓ, who said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When the descendants of Maʿd b. ʿAdnan reached forty men, they stood before the camp of Moses ﷺ and plundered it. Moses b. ʿImran ﷺ supplicated against them, saying, “O Lord, these descendants of Maʿd have raided my camp.” God revealed to him: “O Moses b. ʿImran, do not supplicate against them, for among them is the unlettered Prophet, the warner, the bearer of glad tidings of My Paradise. And among them is the community shown mercy, the community of Muhammad, those who are content with God for little provision, and God is content with them for few deeds. God will admit them to Paradise by the word ‘There is no god but God,’ because their Prophet is Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, humble in his appearance, gathered in understanding in his silence, speaking with wisdom, and practicing forbearance. I brought him out from the best generation of his community, Quraysh; then I brought him out from Hashim, the elite of Quraysh. They are the best of the best, moving to the best, and his community moves to the best.”"],[7539,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection, when people are terrified and they will not be terrified.\""],[7540,"I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to say when he ate food, \"Praise be to Allah, much praise, pure and blessed in it, not diminished, not temporary, and not in need of it.\""],[7541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not appoint a governor until he turbaned him and let loose for it a tail from the right side near the ear."],[7542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, turned me toward the Levant and turned my back to Yemen, and said to me: O Muhammad, I have made what is in front of you as spoils and provision, and what is behind your back as support. Islam will continue to increase and polytheism and its people will decrease until two women travel without fearing any injustice.\""],[7543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, turned me toward the Levant and turned my back to Yemen, and said to me: O Muhammad, I have made what is in front of you as spoils and provision, and what is behind your back as support. Islam will continue to increase and polytheism and its people will decrease until two women travel without fearing any injustice.\""],[7544,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"A group from my Ummah will always remain steadfast on the truth, prevailing over those who oppose them, until the command of Allah comes to them while they are in that state.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, where are they?\" He replied, \"In Jerusalem.\""],[7545,"He witnessed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing he uttered was: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ enjoins you to care for your mothers.\""],[7546,"He witnessed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing he uttered was: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ enjoins you to care for your mothers.\""],[7547,"He witnessed the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing he uttered was: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ enjoins you to care for your mothers.\""],[7548,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Two rak'ahs atone for every dispute.\""],[7549,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Kindness is only suitable for one of noble lineage or religion or one of forbearance.\""],[7550,"The Prophet ﷺ took me by the hand and said: \"O Abu Umamah, among the believers are those for whom my heart softens.\""],[7551,"Abu Umamah al-Bahili ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A servant is not given anything better in this world than permission to pray two rak'ahs.\""],[7552,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No permission is granted to a servant for anything more excellent than two rak'ahs he prays. Indeed, righteousness is scattered upon the servant's head as long as he is in his prayer. And the servants draw near to God, Mighty and Majestic, with nothing like what has come forth from him.\" Abu al-Nadr said: \"That is, the Qur'an.\""],[7553,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: \"Who are those firmly grounded in knowledge?\" He said: \"It is the one whose right hand is faithful, whose tongue is truthful, whose belly and private parts are chaste; that is the one firmly grounded.\""],[7554,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7555,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7556,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7557,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7558,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7559,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7560,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7561,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7562,"Abu al-Darda', Abu Umamah, Wathila b. al-Asqa', and Anas b. Malik narrated to me; they said: The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were disputing about something in a matter of religion. He became angry with a severe anger the like of which he had not shown, then he rebuked us and said: \"Gently, O community of Muhammad! Those before you were destroyed only by this; they took up disputation because of the scarcity of good among them.\""],[7563,"Abu Ad-Darda, Abu Umamah, Wathilah bin Al-Asqa', and Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day while we were discussing a matter related to the religion. He became extremely angry in a way we had never seen before. Then we stopped and he said, \"Hold on, O Ummah of Muhammad, those who came before you were destroyed because of their excessive disputes and lack of good manners.\""],[7564,"From Abu al-Darda', Wathila b. al-Asqa', Abu Umamah, and Anas b. Malik; they said: We were in a gathering in which there were some of the Jews while we were discussing divine decree. The Prophet ﷺ came out to us angry; he frowned, scowled, and rebuked, then said: \"Stop, stop! Fear God, O community of Muhammad! Two deep, bottomless, dark valleys—do not stir up against yourselves the blaze of the Fire.\" Then he ordered the Jews to leave. Then he said, and he spread his right hand and spread his left finger."],[7565,"From Abu al-Darda', Wathilah b. al-Asqa', Abu Umamah, and Anas b. Malik, they said: We were in a gathering with some people from the Jews, and we were discussing divine decree, when the Prophet ﷺ came out to us angry. He frowned, scowled, and rebuked us, then said: \"Enough, enough! Fear Allah, O community of Muhammad! There are two deep valleys, dark and bottomless. Do not stir up against yourselves the blaze of the Fire.\" Then he ordered the Jews to stand up. Then he spoke, spreading his right hand and spreading his left finger."],[7566,"From Abu al-Darda', Wathilah b. al-Asqa', Abu Umamah, and Anas b. Malik, they said: We were in a gathering with some people from the Jews, and we were discussing divine decree, when the Prophet ﷺ came out to us angry. He frowned, scowled, and rebuked us, then said: \"Enough, enough! Fear Allah, O community of Muhammad! There are two deep valleys, dark and bottomless. Do not stir up against yourselves the blaze of the Fire.\" Then he ordered the Jews to stand up. Then he spoke, spreading his right hand and spreading his left finger."],[7567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays the dawn prayer in a congregational mosque and remains there until he prays the forenoon voluntary prayer will have the reward of a pilgrim or one performing 'umrah, his Hajj and 'umrah complete.\""],[7568,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage on al-Jad'a', having placed his feet in the stirrup, stretching up to make the people hear him. He said: \"Do you not hear?\" He prolonged his voice, and a man from one of the groups of people said: \"What do you enjoin upon us?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Worship your Lord, pray your five prayers, fast your month, pay the zakah of your wealth, and obey those in authority among you, and you will enter the Garden of your Lord.\" Abu Yahya said: I asked, \"O Abu Umamah, how old were you that day?\" He said, \"Thirty years old, jostling the caravan until I jostled it foot by foot toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[7569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah admits into Paradise seventy thousand from my Ummah without being held accountable.\" Yazid bin Al-Akhnas Al-Sulami asked: \"What is this in comparison to your Ummah? It is like a blue fly in a herd of camels.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without being held accountable, and with every thousand, there will be seventy thousand and three handfuls.\""],[7570,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah will admit into Paradise from my Ummah seventy thousand people without being held to account.\" Yazeed bin Al-Akhnas As-Sulami said, \"What about your Ummah other than that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It will be the equivalent of a blue fly on a white bull.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seventy thousand more will enter Paradise for each of those thousand, with seventy thousand three-handled swords.\""],[7571,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us after the dawn prayer and said: \"I saw a vision that is true, so understand it. A man came to me, took me by the hand and made me follow him until he brought me to a rugged, tall mountain. He said to me: 'Climb it.' I said: 'I cannot.' He said: 'I will make it easy for you.' So whenever I lifted a foot, I placed it on a step until we stood on the level ground of the mountain. Then we went on, and behold, there were men and women whose cheeks were split open. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are those who say what they do not know.' Then we went on, and behold, there were men and women whose eyes and ears were nailed. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are those who made their eyes see what they did not see and made their ears hear what they did not hear.' Then we went on, and behold, there were women hanging by their heels, their heads lowered, snakes biting their breasts. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are those who prevent their children from their milk.' Then we went on, and behold, there were men and women hanging by their heels, their heads lowered, licking from a little water and mud. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are those who fast and break their fast before the time of their fast ends.' Then we went on, and behold, there were men and women, the ugliest of appearance, the ugliest of clothing, and the most foul of odor, as if their odor were that of latrines. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are the fornicators and adulteresses.' Then we went on, and behold, there were dead people, the most swollen of anything and the most foul of odor. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are the dead of the disbelievers.' Then we went on, and behold, we saw smoke and heard howling. I said: 'What is this?' He said: 'This is Hell, so leave it.' Then we went on, and behold, there were men sleeping under the shade of trees. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'The dead of the Muslims.' Then we went on, and behold, there were boys and girls playing between two rivers. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'The offspring of the believers.' Then we went on, and behold, there were men, the most beautiful of face, the most beautiful of clothing, and the most pleasant of odor, as if their faces were paper. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'These are the truthful ones, the martyrs, and the righteous.' Then we went on, and behold, there were three people drinking wine and singing. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'That is Zayd b. Harithah, Ja'far, and Ibn Rawahah.' I turned toward them, and they said: 'You have attained, you have attained.' Then I raised my head, and behold, there were three people under the Throne. I said: 'What are these?' He said: 'That is your father Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa, and they are waiting for you, may Allah bless them all.'\""],[7572,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"While I was sleeping, someone came to me, and I was taken to a rugged mountain. It was said: 'Climb.' I said: 'I am not able to climb.' He said: 'I will make it easy for you.' So I climbed until when I was on the level ground of the mountain, behold, there were sounds. I said: 'What are these sounds?' It was said: 'These are the sounds of Hell.' Then he took me until I passed by a people, the most swollen of anything, the worst in appearance, and the most foul of odor, their odor like that of latrines. I said: 'Who are these?' It was said: 'These are the fornicators and adulteresses.' Then he took me until he brought me to women hanging by their breasts, snakes biting them. I said: 'Who are these?' They said: 'These are the ones who prevent their children from their milk.' Then he took me until I passed by a people hanging by their heels, their cheeks split open, their cheeks flowing with blood. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are those who break their fast before the time of their fast.' Then he took me until I looked upon three people drinking wine. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'This is Zayd, Ja'far, and Ibn Rawahah.' Then he took me until I looked upon boys playing between two rivers. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'The children of the believers, whom Ibrahim cherishes.' Then he took me until I looked upon three people. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon them, waiting for you.'\""],[7573,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would deliver the sermon on the Day of Sacrifice while mounted on his camel.\""],[7574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The last man to enter the Garden is a man who flips over on the bridge, back to belly, like a boy whom his father beats while he flees from him, his deeds unable to make him proceed. He says: 'O Lord, let me reach the Garden and save me from the Fire.' Allah, exalted is He, reveals to him: 'My servant, if I save you from the Fire and admit you to the Garden, will you confess to Me your sins and your errors?' The servant says: 'Yes, O Lord, by Your might and majesty, if You save me from the Fire, I will confess to You my sins and my errors.' He crosses the bridge, and the servant says within himself, between himself and himself: 'If I confess my sins and my errors to Him, He will send me back to the Fire.' Then Allah reveals to him: 'My servant, confess to Me your sins and your errors, and I will forgive them for you and admit you to the Garden.' The servant says: 'No, by Your might, I have never committed a sin and never made an error.' So Allah reveals to him: 'My servant, I have a witness against you.' The servant turns right and left and sees no one, and he says: 'O Lord, show me Your witness.' So Allah makes his skin speak about the small sins. When the servant sees that, he says: 'O Lord, by Your might, I have the great hidden sins.' So Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, reveals to him: 'My servant, I know them better than you. Confess them to Me, and I will forgive them for you and admit you to the Garden.' So the servant confesses his sins and enters the Garden.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, saying: \"This is the lowest of the people of the Garden in rank, so how about the one above him?\""],[7575,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I know the last man of my community to cross the bridge. He will writhe on the bridge like a boy when his father beats him.\" Then he mentioned something similar."],[7576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people and said: \"Allah has prescribed the Hajj upon you.\" A man from the Bedouins stood up and said: \"Every year?\" The speech of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became difficult, and he became angry and remained silent for a long time. Then he spoke and said: \"Who is this questioner?\" The Bedouin said: \"I am here, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Woe to you! What makes you feel safe that I should say yes? By Allah, if I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory, you would abandon it, and if you abandoned it, you would disbelieve. Indeed, it was only the leaders of hardship who destroyed those before you. By Allah, if I made lawful for you everything on earth and forbade for you the like of a camel's hoof, you would fall into it.\" Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {Do not ask about things} [Qur'an 5:101], the verse."],[7577,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Allah ﷻ promised me that He would admit seventy thousand of my ummah into Paradise without reckoning, and He increased me by three handfuls.”"],[7578,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Allah ﷻ promised me that He would admit seventy thousand of my ummah into Paradise without reckoning, and He increased me by three handfuls.”"],[7579,"We used to sit with Abu Umamah al-Bahili and he would narrate to us many hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he fell silent, he would say: “Have you understood? Convey as it was conveyed to you.”"],[7580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “Do the people of Paradise marry each other?” He said: “Yes, with a penis that does not tire and desire that does not cease, thrusting, thrusting.”"],[7581,"He heard Abu Umamah say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, enforce the legal punishment of Allah on me once or twice.” He turned away from him. Then the prayer was established. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: “Where is the one who said: enforce the legal punishment of Allah on me?” He said: “Here I am.” He said: “Did you complete the ablution and pray the evening prayer with us?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then you are free of your sin as on the day your mother gave birth to you, so do not repeat it.” And Allah ﷻ revealed: {Establish the prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaches of the night}."],[7582,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage while he was on his she-camel al-Jadʿaʾ, having placed his feet in the stirrup and put one hand on the front of the saddle and the other on its back, stretching himself up. He said: “O people, listen carefully, for perhaps you will not see me after this year of yours.” Then Allah ﷻ sent a man from the people who said: “What should we do?” He said: “Worship your Lord, establish your five prayers, give the zakat of your wealth, fast your month, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Garden of your Lord.”"],[7583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his companions at the time of the night prayer: “Gather for prayer tomorrow, for I have a need for you.” A group of them said: “O so-and-so, record the first word the Messenger of Allah ﷺ utters, and you follow it, so that nothing of the speech of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ escapes them.” When he finished the dawn prayer, he said: “Did you gather as I commanded you?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him. Do you understand this? Do you understand this? Do you understand this?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “Establish the prayer and give the zakat. Establish the prayer and give the zakat. Establish the prayer and give the zakat. Do you understand this? Do you understand this? Do you understand this?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “Hear and obey. Hear and obey. Do you understand this? Do you understand this? Do you understand this?” They said: “Yes.” We thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would speak many words, but when we examined his speech, he had summarized the entire matter for him."],[7584,"A young boy came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, give me permission to commit adultery.” The people shouted at him. He said: “Enough.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let him be. Come close.” He came close until he sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Would you like it for your mother?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise people do not like it for their mothers. Would you like it for your daughter?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise people do not like it for their daughters. Would you like it for your sister?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise people do not like it for their sisters. Would you like it for your paternal aunt?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise people do not like it for their paternal aunts. Would you like it for your maternal aunt?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise people do not like it for their maternal aunts.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on his chest and said: “O Allah, expiate his sin, purify his heart, and guard his chastity.”"],[7585,"The barley bread was not preferred over the people of the household of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[7586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best sacrifice is the horned ram.\""],[7587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best of sacrifices is a horned ram.\""],[7588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best of sacrifices is a horned ram.\""],[7589,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"The best sacrifice is a horned ram.\""],[7590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you comes to his family, he should cover himself and his family.\" He said, \"And they should not expose themselves like the exposure of donkeys.\""],[7591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The example of the five daily prayers is like that of a fresh river flowing near the door of one of you, in which he washes himself five times a day. So, what remains of dirt on him?\""],[7592,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When you see a matter that you are unable to change, be patient until Allah is the one who changes it.”"],[7593,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is nothing in the hāmah; the evil eye is real; and the truest bird omen is the faʾl.”"],[7594,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “When the imam says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he raises his head from bowing, raise yours; and if he prays sitting, then all of you pray sitting.”"],[7595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nothing interrupts the prayer.”"],[7596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever washes on Friday, performs the major ablution, goes early, arrives at the beginning of the sermon, draws near, listens, and remains silent, will have two portions of reward.\""],[7597,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The one who hastens to the Friday prayer is like one who offers a camel, the next like one who offers a cow, the next like one who offers a sheep, and the next like one who offers a chicken.\""],[7598,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"On Friday, angels are dispatched to the doors of the mosque and they record the first, then the next. When the imam ascends the pulpit, the scrolls are rolled up.\""],[7599,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best rows for men are the first ones, and the worst are the last ones; the best rows for women are the last ones, and the worst are the first ones.\""],[7600,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A man may stand in prayer and make a supplication, and he will be forgiven along with those behind him among the people.\""],[7601,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Holy Spirit breathed into my mind that no soul will depart this world until it completes its appointed term and receives its provision in full. So be moderate in seeking provision, and do not let the delay of provision drive you to seek it by disobeying God, for what is with God is only attained through obedience to Him.\""],[7602,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God, Mighty and Exalted, dislikes for you all excessive eloquence.\""],[7603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The bombastic speakers will be in the Fire.\""],[7604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah SWT says to the angels: \"Go to My servant and pour trials upon him abundantly.\" They thus go to him and pour trials upon him, and he remains praising Allah. They return to Allah and say: Our Lord, we poured trials on him abundantly as You commanded us. He says, \"Return to him, for I love to hear his voice.\""],[7605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God, Mighty and Exalted, tests one of you with affliction as one of you tests his gold with fire. Some of it comes out like pure gold—that is the one whom God, Mighty and Exalted, protected from uncertainties. Some of it comes out like gold of a lesser quality—that is the one who had some doubt. And some of them comes out like black gold—that is the one who was put to trial.\""],[7606,"Al-Husayn was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he began to kiss him while he was in his lap. Then he urinated, so they went to take him aside. He said: \"Do not interrupt his flow.\" He left him until he finished urinating."],[7607,"A man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing a ring of brass. He said: \"What is this ring?\" The man said: \"It is for the wahinah (a type of joint pain).\" He said: \"Indeed, it will only increase weakness.\""],[7608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Verily, when the Muslim falls ill, Allah Almighty inspires the angels, saying: O angels, I have detained My servant with My confinement. If I take his soul, he will be forgiven. If I heal his body, he will be forgiven as if he had no sins.\""],[7609,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"What becomes forbidden by breastfeeding is what becomes forbidden by lineage.\""],[7610,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He is not one of us who does not honor our elders and show mercy to our young.”"],[7611,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “One hundred and ninety angels are entrusted with the believer, defending him from what he cannot fend off. Of that number, nine angels ward off [harm] from him just as flies are warded off a bowl of honey on a hot day. If they were to appear to you, you would see them on every mountain and plain, each with outstretched arms, so know them. Were the servant left to his own devices for the blink of an eye, the devils would snatch him away.”"],[7612,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Nine angels are entrusted with the sun, hurling snow at it every day. Were it not for that, it would not pass over anything without burning it.”"],[7613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day and bears witness that I am the Messenger of God ﷺ, let his house suffice him and let him weep over his sin.”"],[7614,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day and bears witness that I am the Messenger of God ﷺ, let his house suffice him and let him weep over his sin.”"],[7615,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How pious he is, how pious he is, how pious is a shepherd of sheep on a mountaintop who performs the prayer among them.”"],[7616,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every nation has a form of devotion, and the devotion of my nation is striving in the path of God.”"],[7617,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every nation has a form of devotion, and the devotion of my nation is striving in the path of God.”"],[7618,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man may attain, by his good character, the rank of one who stands in prayer at night and thirsts in the midday heat.”"],[7619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban during the campaign of Tabuk."],[7620,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out on one of his campaigns and passed by some Arab households. He sent to them asking, “Is there any water for the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” They replied, “We have no water except in the skin of a dead animal, which we tanned with milk.” He sent back to them, “Its tanning is its purification.” So some of it was brought to him, and he performed ablution and then prayed."],[7621,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that her husband was away on one of the campaigns. She asked his permission to have an image of a palm tree made in her house, so he forbade her and prohibited her from doing so."],[7622,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered in four places: at the meeting of the ranks in the path of God, at the descent of rain, at the establishment of prayer, and at the sight of the Kaʿbah.”"],[7623,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I saw the pillar of the Book being pulled from beneath my pillow, and my gaze followed it, and behold it was a bright light, until I thought that it had been taken away with it, and it was taken with it to Syria (al-Shām). And I interpreted that when trials occur, faith will be in Syria.”"],[7624,"A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, among them ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, ʿAbd Allāh b. Rawāḥah, and ʿUthmān b. Maẓʿūn, had secluded themselves for worship, abstaining from women and eating meat, fasting the day and standing in prayer at night. I disliked that he should see from my state what would call him to what I had, because he would leave it to him. When the Prophet ﷺ entered, ʿĀʾishah informed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ took his sandal and carried it with the index finger of his left hand, then went quickly until he entered upon them and asked them about their condition. They said, “We desired good.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was sent with the lenient ḥanīfiyyah, and I was not sent with the innovated monasticism. Verily, some people innovated monasticism, and it was prescribed for them, but they did not observe it as it should be observed. So eat meat, come to women, fast and break your fast, pray and sleep, for I have been commanded with that.”"],[7625,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The martyr of the sea is like two martyrs of the land. The one who vomits in the sea is like the one who wallows in his blood on land. And between two waves in the sea is like cutting off the world in obedience to God. Indeed, God has entrusted the Angel of Death to take the souls, except for the martyrs of the sea, for He Himself takes charge of taking their souls. And He forgives the martyrs of the land all sins except debt, and He seeks forgiveness for the martyrs of the sea for all sins and the debt.”"],[7626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Qurʾān was sent down in three places: Makkah, Madinah, and Syria (al-Shām).”"],[7627,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Syria (al-Shām) is the choice of God from His lands; He chooses His choice from His servants. Whoever leaves Syria for other than it, it is with displeasure, and whoever enters it, it is with mercy.”"],[7628,"He heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say: \"On the Day of Resurrection, a group will emerge, brightly shining and with long hair, their light filling the horizon like the sun. A caller will call out to them, 'O Prophet of the Unlettered!'. Then every unlettered Prophet will feel honored. It will be said, 'Muhammad and his Ummah (nation/community)!'. They will enter Paradise without any reckoning or punishment. Then another group will come out, brightly shining and with hair as bright as the full moon. Their light will fill the horizon. A caller will call out to them, 'O Prophet of the Unlettered!'. Then every unlettered Prophet will feel honored. It will be said, 'Muhammad and his Ummah!'. They will enter Paradise without any reckoning or punishment. Then another group will come out, brightly shining and with light as bright as the greatest star in the sky. Their light will fill the horizon. A caller will call out to them, 'O Prophet of the Unlettered!'. Then every unlettered Prophet will feel honored. It will be said, 'Muhammad and his Ummah!'. They will enter Paradise without any reckoning or punishment. Then your Lord will come, and the balance and the account will be established.\""],[7629,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no man who is in charge of ten or more people but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck; his righteousness will release it or his sin will bind it. Its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is disgrace on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7630,"“When God ﷻ desires good for a servant, He sweetens him before his death.” It was said: “What is sweetening him?” He said: “He provides him with righteous deeds before his death.”"],[7631,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade killing the house-dwelling snakes, except for the one with two white stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause miscarriage and blind the eyes."],[7632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. Straighten your rows, align your shoulders, be gentle with the hands of your brothers, and fill the gaps, for Satan enters between you like a small lamb.” And al-hadhaf is the small young of sheep."],[7633,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He addressed the people and said in his sermon: “Indeed, perhaps you will not see me after this year of yours,” three times. A tall, disheveled man stood up, as if he were from the men of Shanū’ah, and said: “What then should we do, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Worship your Lord, perform your five prayers, fast your month, and pay the zakah of your wealth willingly, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.”"],[7634,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how did your affair begin? He said: “The supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of ‘Isa son of Maryam, and my mother saw that a light came out of her that illuminated the palaces of Syria.”"],[7635,"No one remains from this nation except that they enter Paradise, except for those who have turned away from Allah like a lost camel from its owner. So whoever believes in me, then indeed Allah says, \"Only the wretched ones will not believe in it and will turn away.\" He has denied what Muhammad ﷺ brought and turned away from it."],[7636,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a rock weighing ten pregnant camels were thrown from the edge of Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns, until it ends at Ghayy and Athām.” It was said: “What are Ghayy and Athām?” He said: “Two wells in the depths of Hell, from which flow the pus of the people of the Fire. They are the two that Allah mentioned in His Book: ‘They neglected the prayer and followed lusts, so they will meet Ghayy’ and ‘Whoever does that will meet Athām.’”"],[7637,"The Messenger of Allah said: “Every grazing animal going out in the morning and returning in the evening belongs to a people and is forbidden to others.”"],[7638,"“I met one hundred of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[7639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever walks to an obligatory prayer while in a state of purification, his reward is like the reward of a pilgrim in ihram. And whoever walks to perform the Duha prayer, his reward is like the reward of one performing ‘umrah.”"],[7640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever walks to perform a prescribed prayer while he is in a state of purification, his reward is like that of the one who performs Hajj, and whoever walks to offer the Dhuha prayer, his reward is like that of the one who performs Umrah.\""],[7641,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked to see a man loud and high-voiced, and he loved to see him low-voiced.”"],[7642,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever loves for the sake of Allah, hates for the sake of Allah, gives for the sake of Allah, and withholds for the sake of Allah has completed faith. And indeed the closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the best of you in character.”"],[7643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Going early and returning to the mosques is part of jihad in the path of Allah.”"],[7644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bathe on Friday, for whoever bathes on Friday has expiation for what is between that Friday and the next Friday, plus three more days.”"],[7645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays the dawn prayer in congregation, then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, then stands and prays two rakʿahs, returns with the reward of a ḥajj and an ʿumrah.”"],[7646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who recites the Qurʾan aloud is like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who recites the Qurʾan quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly.”"],[7647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever initiates the greeting of peace is more deserving of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[7648,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The siwāk is a purifier for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord, Exalted is He.”"],[7649,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays the ʿishāʾ prayer in congregation has taken his share from the Night of Decree.”"],[7650,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Sublime, says: ‘O son of Adam, pray four rakʿahs at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice you for the rest of it.’”"],[7651,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not go on a military expedition, equip a warrior, or take care of a warrior’s family in his absence, Allah will strike him with a calamity on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever recites ten verses in a night is not recorded among the heedless. Whoever recites one hundred verses is recorded for him a qunūt of a night. Whoever recites two hundred verses is recorded among the devoutly obedient. Whoever recites four hundred verses is recorded among the worshipers. Whoever recites five hundred verses is recorded among the memorizers. Whoever recites six hundred verses is recorded among the humble. Whoever recites eight hundred verses is recorded among the reverent. Whoever recites one thousand verses has a qinṭār recorded for him—and a qinṭār is one thousand two hundred ūqiyyahs; an ūqiyyah is better than what is between heaven and earth, or he said, than what the sun rises upon. Whoever recites two thousand verses is among those who make [reward] binding.”"],[7653,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sale of singing slave-girls is not lawful, nor purchasing them, nor trading in them, and their price is forbidden.” He also said: “This verse was revealed only concerning that: ‘And of the people is he who purchases idle talk’ until he finished the verse.”"],[7654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sale of singing slave-girls is not lawful, nor purchasing them, nor trading in them, and their price is forbidden.” He also said: “This verse was revealed only concerning that: ‘And of the people is he who purchases idle talk’ until he finished the verse.”"],[7655,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to connect Shaʿbān with Ramaḍān [by fasting].”"],[7656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No people sit in a gathering and then leave it without remembering Allah and without sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ except that that gathering will be a regret for them.”"],[7657,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A prayer following a prayer with no idle talk between them is a record in ʿIlliyyūn.”"],[7658,"\"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said, 'Whoever leaves his house in a state of purification, he will have the reward of a Hajj pilgrim in a state of Ihram. And whoever walks to the Eid prayer, he will not fix his eyes onto anything but that, he will have the reward of a person performing Umrah.'\""],[7659,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The affair only increases in severity, wealth only increases in abundance, and people only increase in greed.”"],[7660,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The affair only increases in severity, wealth only increases in abundance, and people only increase in greed.”"],[7661,"From the Prophet ﷺ : \"The greatest name of Allah is mentioned in three Surahs of the Quran: Al-Baqarah, Ale-Imran, and Taha.\""],[7662,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, permit me to commit adultery.” The people shouted at him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let him be.” He drew near until he sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Would you like it for your mother?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise, people do not like it for their mothers.” He said: “Would you like it for your daughter?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise, people do not like it for their daughters.” He said: “Would you like it for your sister?” He said: “No.” He said: “Likewise, people do not like it for their sisters.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on his chest and said: “O Allah, expiate his sin, purify his heart, and guard his private parts.”"],[7663,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to travel as a wandering ascetic. He said: “The wandering of my community is striving in the path of Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[7664,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no contagion, no Ṣafar, no hāmah, and two months do not complete; whoever violates a covenant will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[7665,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no Ṣafar, no hāmah, and no contagion.”"],[7666,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “A prayer following a prayer with no idle talk between them is a record in ʿIlliyyūn.”"],[7667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever walks to an obligatory prayer, it is equivalent to a Hajj, and whoever walks to a voluntary prayer, it is equivalent to an ʿUmrah.”"],[7668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever walks to an obligatory prayer, it is equivalent to a Hajj, and whoever walks to a voluntary prayer, it is equivalent to an ʿUmrah.”"],[7669,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The angel on the left withholds the pen for six hours from a Muslim servant who errs or sins. If he regrets it and seeks Allah’s forgiveness, he casts it aside; otherwise, it is recorded as one.”"],[7670,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever performs ablution, then comes to the mosque and prays two rak'ahs before Fajr, then sits until he prays Fajr, his prayer that day will be recorded among the prayers of the righteous, and he will be recorded among the delegation of the Most Merciful.”"],[7671,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever commits acts of disobedience among a people while he is one of them, and they do not prevent him from that until they change the evil, then Allah's protection is absolved from them.”"],[7672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Adhere to humility, for humility is in the heart. Let no Muslim harm another Muslim, for perhaps one dressed in worn-out clothes, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath.”"],[7673,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I am a guarantor for the one who abandons argumentation even though he is in the right, of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise.”"],[7674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not sell fruit until its goodness is apparent.”"],[7675,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be approached until they give birth.”"],[7676,"That the Prophet ﷺ “cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for them, and the woman who tattoos and the one who asks for tattoos.”"],[7677,"“That the Prophet ﷺ forbade selling shares until they are distributed.”"],[7678,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed those who scratch their faces and tear their collars.”"],[7679,"“That the Prophet ﷺ forbade hoarding food.”"],[7680,"From Abu Umamah, who traced it back (to the Prophet): \"The ungrateful is the one who beats his slave, withholds his assistance, and eats alone.\""],[7681,"On the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Judgment, the sun will approach to within a mile of the people, and its heat will increase. People will sweat according to their sins. There will be those whose sweat reaches up to their ankles, and those whose sweat reaches up to their knees, and those whose sweat reaches up to their waist, and there will be those whom the sweat will cover completely.\""],[7682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever becomes Muslim at the hands of a man, that man is his patron.\""],[7683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.\""],[7684,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.\""],[7685,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.\""],[7686,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a funeral with seven people. He placed three in one row, two in a row, and two in a row."],[7687,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The companion of the right is trustworthy over the companion of the left. When a good deed is done, he records it. When an evil deed is done, the companion of the right says to him: 'Wait six hours.' If he seeks forgiveness, he does not write it against him; otherwise he records one evil deed against him.\""],[7688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah, may He be exalted, says: 'Son of Adam, if I take from you your two precious things (i.e., eyes) and you remain patient and seek reward at the first shock, I will not be satisfied with any reward for you less than Paradise.'\""],[7689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah, may He be exalted, said: 'Whoever I deprive of his two precious things (i.e., eyes), I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.'\""],[7690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the sun rises from its rising place as it appears at the time of the afternoon prayer when it sets from its setting place, and a man prays two rak'ahs with four prostrations, the reward of that day will be written for him.\" I think he said: \"And his sin and his error will be expiated.\" And I think he said: \"And if he dies on that day, he will enter Paradise.\""],[7691,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he made many supplications that we did not memorize. Then he said: I will inform you of something that gathers all of that. You say: O Allah, we ask You by what Your Prophet Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, asked You, and we seek refuge in You from what Your Prophet Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, sought refuge in You. You are the one whose help is sought, and upon You is the conveyance of the message, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah."],[7692,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition. He ordered the caller, who announced, “Whoever is weakened should return.” People began returning until they reached a narrow pass in the road, where a man's she-camel stumbled and killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him and called the Muslims. People came to him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with you and what delayed you?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so came to the narrow pass in the road and his mount stumbled and killed him.” He said, “Leave him to pray over him,” but he refused. Then he ordered a caller, who announced, “Paradise is not permissible for a disobedient person.”"],[7693,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition. He ordered the caller, who announced, “Whoever is weakened should return.” People began returning until they reached a narrow pass in the road, where a man's she-camel stumbled and killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him and called the Muslims. People came to him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with you and what delayed you?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so came to the narrow pass in the road and his mount stumbled and killed him.” He said, “Leave him to pray over him,” but he refused. Then he ordered a caller, who announced, “Paradise is not permissible for a disobedient person.”"],[7694,"I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military campaign. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is weakened should return.” People began returning, and the road became narrow. A man's camel stopped with him, and he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. When my father reported about him, he refused to pray over him and called Bilal, who said, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Announce it: Paradise is not permissible for a disobedient person.”"],[7695,"I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military campaign. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is weakened should return.” People began returning, and the road became narrow. A man's camel stopped with him, and he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. When my father reported about him, he refused to pray over him and called Bilal, who said, “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Announce it: Paradise is not permissible for a disobedient person.”"],[7696,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and they mentioned al-Sham and the Romans in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will conquer al-Sham and will obtain on its sea a fortress called Anafa, from which twelve thousand martyrs will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe.”"],[7698,"It was announced among us in the year of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Every fanged beast of prey is forbidden, and domestic donkeys are forbidden.”"],[7699,"It was announced among us in the year of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Every fanged beast of prey is forbidden, and domestic donkeys are forbidden.”"],[7700,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “God ﷻ sent me as a mercy to the worlds and as guidance to the worlds. My Lord commanded me to obliterate musical instruments, reed pipes, idols, crosses, and the affairs of the pre-Islamic era. And my Lord swore by His might that no servant among His servants drinks a gulp of wine deliberately but that I will give him to drink the like of it from the pus of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection, whether he is forgiven or punished. And no one deliberately gives it to a small Muslim child but that I will give him the like of it to drink from the pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether he is forgiven or punished. And no one leaves it out of fear of Me but that I will give him to drink from the cisterns of the Holy Precinct on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7701,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “God ﷻ sent me as a mercy to the worlds and as guidance to the worlds. My Lord commanded me to obliterate musical instruments, reed pipes, idols, crosses, and the affairs of the pre-Islamic era. And my Lord swore by His might that no servant among His servants drinks a gulp of wine deliberately but that I will give him to drink the like of it from the pus of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection, whether he is forgiven or punished. And no one deliberately gives it to a small Muslim child but that I will give him the like of it to drink from the pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether he is forgiven or punished. And no one leaves it out of fear of Me but that I will give him to drink from the cisterns of the Holy Precinct on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7702,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God sent me as guidance and mercy to the worlds, and my Lord commanded me to destroy reed pipes, musical instruments, and the idols that were worshipped besides God. And my Lord swore by His might: no servant among my servants drinks wine but that I will give him to drink it from the boiling water, then either I forgive him or I punish him. And my Lord swore by His might: no servant among my servants gives wine to a child who does not understand but that I will give him to drink the like of what he gave from the boiling water, either I forgive him or I punish him. And my Lord swore by His might: no servant among my servants leaves it out of fear of Me but that I will give him to drink it in the presence of the Holy Precinct.”"],[7703,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “It is not lawful to sell singing slave women, nor to buy them, nor to trade in them. Their prices are unlawful, as is listening to them for enjoyment.”"],[7704,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever fasts one day in the path of God, God will distance his face from the Fire by a distance of one hundred years of riding a swift, well-trained horse.”"],[7705,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Indeed this religion will have times of advance and times of retreat. Verily, among the times of advance of this religion is that the entire tribe will gain understanding of the religion until none remains in it except one or two transgressors, who are humiliated therein; if they speak, they are suppressed and oppressed. And verily, among the times of retreat of this religion is that the entire tribe will become coarse until none remains in it except one or two jurists, who are humiliated; if they speak, they are suppressed and oppressed. And the last of this nation will curse its first. Verily, upon them the curse will descend until they drink wine openly, until a woman passes by a group and one of them stands up to her and lifts her garment as the tail of a ewe is lifted. On that day a person will say: ‘If only he would hide her behind a wall.’ On that day he will be among them like Abu Bakr and Umar are among you. Whoever on that day enjoins good and forbids evil will have the reward of fifty of those who saw me, believed in me, obeyed me, and followed me.”"],[7706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood one day and began the prayer, then he saw phlegm in the direction of the qiblah. He removed his sandal, walked to it, and scraped it off. He did that three times. When he finished his prayer, he faced the people, praised God and extolled Him, then said: “O people, when one of you stands in prayer, he is in a great station before a great Lord, asking for a great matter: success in Paradise and salvation from the Fire. And when one of you stands in prayer, he stands before God facing his Lord, with his angel on his right and his companion on his left. Let none of you spit in front of him or to his right, but rather to his left under his left foot. Then let him rub it, and let him rub it hard, for he is only rubbing the ear of Satan. By the One who sent me with the truth, if the veils between you and him were removed or permission were given to speak, he would complain of what he encounters from that.”"],[7707,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: I was admitted into Paradise and heard a soft sound, so I said, “Who is this?” They said, “Bilal.”"],[7708,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Luqman said to his son: “O my son, keep to the gatherings of the scholars and listen to the words of the wise, for God revives the dead heart with the light of wisdom just as He revives the dead earth with abundant rain.”"],[7709,"I never drew near to your Prophet ﷺ in a prescribed prayer or a voluntary one except that I heard him supplicating with these words and supplications, not adding to them nor subtracting from them: “O Allah, forgive me my sins and my errors. O Allah, revive me, mend me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to what is righteous among them and none turns away what is evil among them except You.”"],[7710,"There was a woman who used to speak obscenely to men and was foul-mouthed. She passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating tharīd on a leather mat. She said: “Look at him sitting as a slave sits and eating as a slave eats.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “And which slave is more enslaved than me?” She said: “He eats and does not feed me.” He said: “Then eat.” She said: “Hand me your hand.” He handed it to her. She said: “Feed me from what is in your mouth.” He gave her some, and she ate. Then modesty overcame her, and she no longer spoke obscenely to anyone until she died."],[7711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created the ḥūr al-ʿīn from saffron.”"],[7712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever initiates the greeting of peace is more entitled to Allah and His Messenger.”"],[7713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, took me as an intimate friend just as He took Ibrahim as an intimate friend, and my intimate friend is Abu Bakr ؓ.”"],[7714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The likeness of a righteous woman among women is like that of the crow with a white leg (al-ghurāb al-aʿṣam).” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is al-ghurāb al-aʿṣam?” He said: “The one whose one leg is white.”"],[7715,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “On the Day of Resurrection, the professional mourner will be on a path between Paradise and Hell, her garments of tar, and fire will cover her face if she does not repent.”"],[7716,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Three whose rights none belittles except a hypocrite: a person of old age in Islam, a person of knowledge, and a just ruler.”"],[7717,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with ʿĀʾishah when a servant girl of hers, or a freedwoman, came to her with some tharīd and said: “Eat this, O my mistress, for I am pleased with its goodness.” She said: “Keep it away from me.” The girl swore insistently, and she said: “Keep it away from me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you make her break her oath, the sin of it will be upon you.”"],[7718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, not wiping it except for the sake of Allah, will have for every hair that his hand passes over good deeds. And whoever treats an orphan well in his care, I and he will be in Paradise like these two,” and he joined his two fingers."],[7719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the mosque in the forenoon and said “Allāhu akbar” three times, then said: “O Allah, give us rain three times. O Allah, grant us ghee, milk, fat, and meat.” There was not a cloud to be seen in the sky, but a wind and dust arose, then clouds gathered, the sky poured down, the people of the markets cried out and fled to the porticoes of the mosque and their houses while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing. The streets flowed with water, and we saw that rain on the ends of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, on his shoulders and upper arms, like pearls. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, and I departed walking with his gait while he was saying: “This — I tell you of its Lord.” Abū Umāmah said: “I have not seen a year with more ghee, milk, fat, and meat. These things in the streets — hardly anyone buys them.”"],[7720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the mosque in the forenoon and said “Allāhu akbar” three times, then said: “O Allah, give us rain three times. O Allah, grant us ghee, milk, fat, and meat.” There was not a cloud to be seen in the sky, but a wind and dust arose, then clouds gathered, the sky poured down, the people of the markets cried out and fled to the porticoes of the mosque and their houses while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing. The streets flowed with water, and we saw that rain on the ends of the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, on his shoulders and upper arms, like pearls. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, and I departed walking with his gait while he was saying: “This — I tell you of its Lord.” Abū Umāmah said: “I have not seen a year with more ghee, milk, fat, and meat. These things in the streets — hardly anyone buys them.”"],[7721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things are from sorcery: incantations, amulets, and charms.”"],[7722,"The sandal strap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ broke, so he said, “Indeed we belong to Allah.” They said, “Is it a calamity, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Whatever afflicts the believer that he dislikes is a calamity.”"],[7723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man raises his voice with a melodious song except that Allah sends two devils to sit on his shoulders, striking their heels upon his chest until he stops; whenever he stops, they stop.”"],[7724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to his companions: “Has any of you begun this day fasting?” They remained silent. Abu Bakr ؓ said, “I have, O Messenger of Allah.” Then he said, “Has anyone among you visited a sick person today?” They remained silent. Abu Bakr ؓ said, “I have, O Messenger of Allah.” Then he said, “Has anyone among you given charity today?” They remained silent. Abu Bakr ؓ said, “I have, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until laughter overtook him, then said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, none combines them in a single day except a believer, and none enters Paradise by them except him.”"],[7725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and the angels affirm it: a man whom Allah made male but who effeminizes himself and imitates women; a woman whom Allah made female but who masculinizes herself and imitates men; the one who leads a blind man astray; and a man who is effeminate—and Allah did not make anyone effeminate except Yahya b. Zakariyya ﷺ .”"],[7726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ: “O Mu'adh, a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife who helps you in the affairs of your worldly life and your religion are the best of what people acquire.”"],[7727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people I most envy are a believer of light circumstances—or clever—with a share of prayer, who worships his Lord well and obeys Him in secret, who is obscure among people, not pointed at with fingers, having just enough and patient over that.” Then he flicked his hand and said, “His death comes quickly, his mourners are few, and his inheritance is little.”"],[7728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of being alone with women. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man and woman are alone except that Satan enters between them. For a man to jostle a pig smeared with mud or mire is better for him than to jostle his shoulder against the shoulder of a woman not lawful to him.”"],[7729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four have their rewards continuing after death: one who dies stationed in the path of Allah; one who teaches knowledge—his reward continues as long as it is acted upon; one who gives charity—its reward continues as long as it remains; and a man who leaves a righteous child who supplicates for him.”"],[7730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “Who will pledge allegiance?” Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said, “Upon what shall we pledge? Have we not already pledged allegiance to you once, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Upon not asking anyone for anything.” Thawban said, “And what is for him in that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Paradise.” So Thawban pledged allegiance to him. Abu Umamah said, “I saw him in Makkah at the time when people were most crowded: his whip would fall while he was riding, and perhaps it would fall on a man’s shoulder; the man would pick it up and hand it to him, but he would not take it until he himself dismounted and picked it up.”"],[7731,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: \"Indeed, Allah says: 'My servant continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts of worship until I love him. When I love him, I become his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his tongue with which he speaks, and his heart with which he thinks. When he calls upon Me, I answer him, and when he asks of Me, I grant him. And when he seeks My help, I help him. And the most beloved of actions to Me are those that are done regularly.\""],[7732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Charity given to a relative has its reward doubled twice.”"],[7733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Lord offered to turn the pebbles of Makkah into gold for me, but I said, ‘No, my Lord; rather I eat my fill one day and go hungry for three. When I am hungry I humble myself to You and remember You, and when I am full I praise You and thank You.’”"],[7734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What am I and a woman with darkened cheeks? When she is tender to her child, obeys her Lord, and guards her chastity, she will be in Paradise like these two,” and he joined his two fingers together."],[7735,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “When Iblis was sent down to the earth, he said: ‘O Lord, You have sent me down to the earth and made me accursed,’ or as he mentioned, ‘so appoint for me a house.’ He said: ‘The bathhouse.’ He said: ‘So appoint for me a gathering place.’ He said: ‘The markets and the meeting places of roads.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me food.’ He said: ‘That over which the name of Allah is not mentioned.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me drink.’ He said: ‘Every intoxicant.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me a caller to prayer.’ He said: ‘Wind instruments.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me a Qur’an.’ He said: ‘Poetry.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me a book.’ He said: ‘Tattooing.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me a discourse.’ He said: ‘Lies.’ He said: ‘Appoint for me traps.’ He said: ‘Women.’”"],[7736,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one of the most cheerful of people and the most pleasant in disposition.”"],[7737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let none of you fail, when he comes to his wife, to say: ‘In the name of Allah. O Allah, keep me away from the accursed Shaytan and keep away from what You grant me.’ For if it is decreed that there be a child between them, no shaytan will ever harm him.”"],[7738,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “You will certainly lower your gazes, guard your private parts, and set your faces aright, or your faces will certainly be darkened.”"],[7739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let none of you fail, when he comes to his wife, to say: ‘In the name of Allah. O Allah, keep me away from the accursed Shaytan and keep away from what You grant me.’ For if it is decreed that there be a child between them, no shaytan will ever harm him.”"],[7740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who looks at a woman with a first glance and then lowers his gaze except that Allah creates for him an act of worship whose sweetness he finds.”"],[7741,"A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ were with him and said: “So-and-so planted a crop and it multiplied,” or as he said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And what is that? Two light rak’ahs are better for you than all of that from this world and what is upon it. If you were to do what you have been commanded, you would eat as vigorous ones, a crop, and not as wretched ones.”"],[7742,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with a woman present, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “I think that you women tell others what your husbands do with you.” She said: “Yes, by Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, we certainly boast about that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then do not do so, for Allah abhors the one who does that.”"],[7743,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with a woman present, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “I think that you women tell others what your husbands do with you.” She said: “Yes, by Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, we certainly boast about that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then do not do so, for Allah abhors the one who does that.”"],[7744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three stones purify the believer, and water is a purifier.”"],[7745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The siwak is a means of purifying the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord, exalted is He ﷻ.”"],[7746,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Gabriel never came to me except that he commanded me to use the tooth-stick, until I feared that I would wear away the front of my mouth.”"],[7747,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Safiyya bt. Abd al-Muttalib, and she offered him a bone with meat on it, or brought one near him, and placed it before him. Then she offered another, or brought it near, and placed it before him. He ate, then the muezzin came and said, “Ablution, ablution.” He said: “Ablution is required of us only for what comes out, not for what goes in.”"],[7748,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Let none of you be unable, when he enters his privy, to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the foul, impure, wicked, and accursed devil.”"],[7749,"When a man entered the mosque and found the people praying, he would ask the person beside him, who would tell him what he had missed so that he could make it up, then he would stand and pray with them. Then one day Mu‘adh came, and they signaled to him that he had missed such-and-such, but he refused to pray [the remainder with them] and prayed [it] first, then prayed what he had missed after that. This was mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Mu‘adh did well, and you, do as he did.”"],[7750,"Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as you are. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Have you trimmed your nails?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Anything that trims the nails, as long as it is not a tooth or a fingernail clipper.”"],[7751,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was sent as a mercy and guidance for the worlds, to obliterate idols, musical instruments, reed pipes, and the affairs of the Age of Ignorance.”"],[7752,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was sent as a mercy and guidance for the worlds, to obliterate idols, musical instruments, reed pipes, and the affairs of the Age of Ignorance.”"],[7753,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever intercedes for his brother with an intercession and then receives a gift for it and accepts it has come to a great door among the doors of usury.”"],[7754,"The Messenger of God said: “The visitor of a sick person plunges into mercy.” And the Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hands on his knees, then said: “When he sits with him, mercy overwhelms him. Part of perfecting the visit to a sick person is that one of you place his hand on his face or on his hand and ask him how he is. And the perfection of love among you is shaking hands.”"],[7755,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is not lawful to buy singing women, nor to sell them, nor to trade in them, and their price is forbidden.” Then he recited this verse: {And among people is he who purchases idle talk to lead astray from the way of God without knowledge} [Q 31:6]."],[7756,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Four are given their rewards twice: the wives of the Messenger of God ﷺ, a person from the People of the Book who embraces Islam, a man who had a slave woman whom he liked and then set her free and married her, and a slave who fulfills the right of God and the right of his masters.”"],[7757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will not a man give charity to this one [by praying with him]?” So a man stood up and prayed with him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “These two are a congregation.”"],[7758,"“Whoever begins with the greeting of peace is closer to God and His Messenger.”"],[7759,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “You will straighten the rows, or faces will be effaced and your eyes will be effaced, or your eyes will be snatched away.”"],[7760,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Indeed, among the most enviable of my friends in my sight is a believer of light means, who has a share of prayer and fasting, who worships his Lord well and obeys Him in secret, who is obscure among people, not pointed to with fingers, whose livelihood is barely sufficient, and who is patient with that. His death comes quickly, his mourners are few, and his inheritance is small.”"],[7761,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The sale of female singers is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor trade in them, and consuming their price is forbidden.” And concerning this, God, Exalted is He, revealed this verse: {And of the people is he who buys idle talk}."],[7762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed, this religion has a time of advance and a time of retreat,” and he mentioned the hadith."],[7763,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Last night I saw in a dream that I was admitted into Paradise and came out of one of its eight gates, and there was my community standing. They were shown to me one by one, and there was a balance set up. My community was placed in one pan of the balance and I was placed in the other pan, and I outweighed them. Then my entire community was placed together in one pan, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ was placed in the other pan, and he outweighed them. Then my entire community was placed in one pan, and Ibn al-Khattab was placed in the other pan, and he outweighed them. Then the balance was raised.”"],[7764,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was walking in intense heat, his sandal strap broke. A man came with a strap and put it on his sandal. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If you knew what you have carried for the Messenger of God ﷺ, if you knew what you have carried for the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[7765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man while he was reciting “Say: He is God, the One,” and said, “This one has made it obligatory; Paradise is assured for him.”"],[7766,"During the Farewell Pilgrimage, the Prophet ﷺ stood, that day riding behind him al-Fadl b. Abbas on a camel, and said, “O people, take knowledge before knowledge is taken away and before knowledge is raised.” God, Exalted is He, had already revealed {O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if shown to you, would distress you} — the verse. We used to recall it often, and it kept us from asking him. So we went to a bedouin and bribed him with a cloak; he wrapped it around his head until I saw the edge of the cloak on his right eyebrow. Then we said, “Ask the Prophet ﷺ.” He said, “O Prophet of God, how will knowledge be raised from us while the scriptures are among us? We have learned from them and taught them to our women, our children, and our servants.” The Prophet ﷺ raised his head, his face flushed with anger, and said, “May your mother be bereft of you! These Jews and Christians have scriptures among them, yet they do not adhere to a single letter of what their prophets brought them. Verily, one way knowledge departs is that its people depart,” three times."],[7767,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his expeditions. A man passed by a cave containing some water, and his soul tempted him to stay in that cave, to live on the water in it, to gather the wild greens around it, and to withdraw from the world. Then he said, “If I go to God’s Prophet ﷺ and mention that to him, then if he permits me I will do it, otherwise I will not.” So he came to him and said, “O Prophet of God, I passed by a cave containing what would sustain me of water and greens, and my soul told me to stay there and withdraw from the world.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I was not sent with Judaism or Christianity, but I was sent with the tolerant pure monotheism. By Him in whose hand is my soul, a morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that is in it, and the standing of any of you in the row is better than his praying for sixty years.”"],[7768,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by on a very hot day toward Baqi al-Gharqad. The people were walking behind him. When he heard the sound of sandals, that settled in his soul, so he stopped until he made them go ahead of him, lest any pride enter his heart. When he passed by Baqi al-Gharqad, there were two graves in which two men had been buried. The Prophet ﷺ stopped and said, “Whom did you bury here today?” They said, “O Prophet of God, so-and-so.” He said, “They are being punished now and being tested in their graves.” They said, “O Messenger of God, why?” He said, “As for one of them, he used to spread malicious gossip; as for the other, he did not guard himself from urine.” He took a fresh palm stalk, split it, and placed it on the two graves. They said, “O Prophet of God, why did you do that?” He said, “That it may be lightened for them.” They said, “O Prophet of God, until when will they be punished?” He said, “A matter of the unseen known only to God.” He said, “Were it not that you would harbor doubt in your hearts or exaggerate in the report, you would hear what I hear.”"],[7769,"We sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he reminded us and made us tremble, and Sa‘d b. Abi Waqqas wept greatly and said, “Would that I had died.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Sa‘d, do you wish for death in my presence?” repeating that three times. Then he said, “O Sa‘d, if you were created for Paradise, then however long your life and however good your deeds, that is better for you; and if you were created for the Fire, then what an evil thing it is to hasten to.”"],[7770,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting, and they thought revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and forced his way in, approached him, and sat by him. He turned to him and said, “O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?” He said, “No.” He said, “Rise and pray.” When he had prayed four rak‘ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, “O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of jinn and humans?” He said, “O Prophet of God, are there devils among humans?” He said, “Yes, devils of humans and jinn, some of them inspire others with adorned speech in deception.”"],[7771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, and they thought that revelation was descending upon him, so they kept away from him until Abu Dharr came and burst in. He came to him and sat with him. He turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Get up and pray.\" When he had prayed four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said, \"O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind?\" He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do mankind have devils?\" He said, \"Yes, the devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as a delusion.\""],[7779,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hellfire by a distance of one hundred years' journey.\""],[7780,"Tha'labah b. Hatib al-Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to provide for me.\" He said, \"Woe to you, O Tha'labah! A little for which you fulfill its gratitude is better than much that you cannot bear.\""],[7781,"Tha'labah b. Hatib al-Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to provide for me.\" He said, \"Woe to you, O Tha'labah! A little for which you fulfill its gratitude is better than much that you cannot bear.\""],[7782,"Tha'labah b. Hatib al-Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to provide for me.\" He said, \"Woe to you, O Tha'labah! A little for which you fulfill its gratitude is better than much that you cannot bear.\""],[7783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Verily, the Fire was created for the foolish, and it is for women except the one who obeys her guardian.”"],[7784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people, upon you is knowledge before the scholar is taken away. The scholar and the learner are partners in reward, and there is no good in the rest of the people.”"],[7785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Use the tooth-stick, for the tooth-stick is a purifier for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.”"],[7786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Use the tooth-stick, for the tooth-stick is a purifier for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord.”"],[7787,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whosoever misses the night to strive in it, and is miserly with his wealth to spend it, and is cowardly against the enemy to fight him, let him increase in saying: ‘Glory be to Allah and with His praise,’ for they are dearer to Allah than a mountain of gold and silver spent in the way of Allah.”"],[7788,"“Mu‘adh b. Jabal had a drinking bowl plated with brass, from which he gave the Prophet ﷺ to drink when he drank, and with which he performed ablution for him when he performed ablution.”"],[7789,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ that he used to swear by Allah three times without exception: “There is no Muslim on the face of the earth who says when he enters the morning: ‘O Allah, to You belongs praise. There is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I enter the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from the evil of my deeds and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins, which none forgives but You,’ and then dies on that day of his, but he will enter Paradise.”"],[7790,"Narrated by the Prophet Muhammad, ﷺ : \"Whoever humiliates a friend of mine, he has declared war against me. You will not comprehend what I possess except by fulfilling what I have obligated upon you. My servant continues to approach me with voluntary acts of worship until I love him, and when I love him, I become the hearing with which he hears, the sight with which he sees, and the hand with which he grasps. If he calls upon Me, I answer him, and if he seeks My help, I assist him. And the most beloved type of worship to me is providing sincere advice to My servant.\""],[7791,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ that he used to say: “A Muslim has not acquired any benefit after the fear of Allah Almighty better for him than a righteous wife: if he commands her she obeys him, if he looks at her she pleases him, if he adjures her she fulfills it for him, and if he is absent from her she is faithful to him in her own self.”"],[7792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ‘Amr b. al-Tufayl to Khaybar to seek reinforcements for him from his people, and said: “O ‘Amr, go and seek reinforcements for us from your people.” ‘Amr said: “O Messenger of Allah, you have sent me while the fighting has broken out.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Are you not pleased to be the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”"],[7793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and passed by the house of ‘Uthman b. Maz‘un. He stood at the door of the house and said: “What is the matter with you, O Kuhaylah, that you are so unkempt? Is ‘Uthman not present?” She said: “Yes, but he has not lain on my bed since such-and-such a time, and he fasts all the time and does not break his fast.” He said: “Tell him to come to me.” When he came, she told him, so he went to him and found him in the mosque. He sat with him, but he turned away from him, so he wept. Then he said: “I knew that something about me had reached you.” He said: “Are you the one who fasts all the time and stands in prayer at night, not placing your side on a bed?” ‘Uthman said: “I have done that seeking good.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Your eye has a right, your body has a right, and your wife has a right. So fast and break your fast, sleep and pray, and go to your wife. For I fast and break my fast, I sleep and pray, and I go to women. Whoever takes my Sunnah has been guided, and whoever leaves it has gone astray. For every action has a period of eagerness, and for every period of eagerness there is a period of slackening. If the slackening leads to heedlessness, then it is destruction, and if the heedlessness leads back to the obligation, then it does not harm its doer at all. So take from deeds what you are able to bear. Verily, I have only been sent with the tolerant Hanifiyyah, so do not make the worship of your Lord burdensome upon yourself. You do not know how long your life will be.”"],[7794,"The Prophet ﷺ went out one day, and with him were Abu Bakr, ‘Umar, Zayd b. Thabit, ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud, Ubayy b. Ka‘b, and ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abbas. The Prophet ﷺ was on his she-camel al-Jad‘a’. When they emerged, the Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying: “Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest.” He stopped to listen. When he said: “Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest,” the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This one has testified, by the One in whose hand is my soul, with the testimony of truth.” When he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,” he said: “This one is free, by the One in whose hand is my soul, from the Fire,” three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This is a dog-owner.” Ibn Mas‘ud and Ibn ‘Abbas went and found him to be so."],[7795,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ he said: “The peak of the hump of Islam is jihad in the way of Allah; none attains it except the best of them.”"],[7796,"That the blind man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and he was a man from Quraysh — and said to him, ‘O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, I am as you see me: my age has grown old, my bones have become weak, and my sight has gone, and I have a guide who does not suit me in guiding me. Is there any concession for me to pray the prayers in my house?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Do you hear the caller to prayer from the house in which you are?’ He said, ‘Yes, O Messenger of Allah.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘I do not find any concession for you. If this one who stays back from the prayer in congregation knew what is [in store] for this one who walks to it, he would come to it even if he had to crawl on his hands and feet.’"],[7797,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘A prayer following another prayer is a written record in ʿIlliyyīn.’"],[7798,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Minā to Makkah on the Day of Tarwiyah, and he arrived with Bilāl beside him carrying a cloth on a stick to shade him from the heat of the sun."],[7799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise more spacious than it.’"],[7800,"When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Banū Hāshim and seated them at the door, and he gathered his women and his family and seated them in the house. Then he looked upon them and said, ‘O Banū Hāshim, ransom yourselves from the Fire, and strive to free your necks, and redeem yourselves from Allah, for I do not possess anything for you from Allah.’"],[7801,"When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Banū Hāshim and seated them at the door, and he gathered his women and his family and seated them in the house. Then he looked upon them and said, ‘O Banū Hāshim, ransom yourselves from the Fire, and strive to free your necks, and redeem yourselves from Allah, for I do not possess anything for you from Allah.’"],[7802,"When {And warn your nearest kindred} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Banū Hāshim and seated them at the door, and he gathered his women and his family and seated them in the house. Then he looked upon them and said, ‘O Banū Hāshim, ransom yourselves from the Fire, and strive to free your necks, and redeem yourselves from Allah, for I do not possess anything for you from Allah.’"],[7803,"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is charity? He said, ‘Multiplied manifold, and with Allah is more.’ Then he recited, {Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, so that He may multiply it for him many times over?}"],[7804,"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is charity? He said, ‘Multiplied manifold, and with Allah is more.’ Then he recited, {Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, so that He may multiply it for him many times over?}"],[7805,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ sat one day among a group of his companions, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ raised his hand and said, ‘Who will pledge allegiance to me?’ three times. No one stood up to him except Thawbān. He said, ‘May my father and mother be your ransom, we have already pledged allegiance to you once, and I will pledge allegiance to you a second time. Upon what shall I pledge allegiance to you, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said, ‘Upon that you do not ask people for anything, and for you is Paradise.’ He said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, if I pledge allegiance to you and do not ask people for anything, will I have Paradise?’ He said, ‘Yes, if Allah wills.’ He said, ‘No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not ask for anything as long as I remain in this world.’"],[7806,"I never prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was close to him except that I heard him say after every prayer, ‘O Allah, forgive me all my errors and sins. O Allah, revive me, protect me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness and none turns away from me their evil except You.’"],[7807,"Words that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ‘Wealth only increases in abundance, people only increase in miserliness, the affair only increases in severity, and the Hour will not rise except upon the worst of people.’"],[7808,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Abu Bakr, Umar, and Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah ؓ among a group of his companions, a cup containing a drink was brought. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed it to Abu Ubaydah. Abu Ubaydah said, \"You are more entitled to it, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said, \"Take it.\" So Abu Ubaydah took the cup. Then, before drinking, he said, \"Take it, O Prophet of Allah.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Drink, for blessing is with our elders. Whoever does not show mercy to our young or honor our elders is not one of us.\""],[7809,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Gabriel came to me and placed his hands, one on my chest and the other between my shoulders, until I felt the coolness of the one on my chest between my shoulders, and the coolness of the one between my shoulders in my chest. Then he said, 'O Muhammad, honor the elder, declare the oneness of Allah with certainty, and say: Glory be to the Lord of the first and the last.'\""],[7810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Prepare to set out against this town whose people are wrongdoers\" — meaning Khaybar — \"for Allah will surely open it for you, if Allah wills. Let no weak person or one deemed weak go out with me.\" Abu Hurayrah went to his mother and said, \"Equip me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has ordered us to equip for the expedition.\" She said, \"Will you go and leave me, though you know that I only enter the privy when you are with me?\" He said, \"I would never stay behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She exposed her breast and adjured him by the milk he had suckled from her. So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ secretly and told him. He said, \"Go, you have been spared worry.\" Abu Hurayrah came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that you are turning away from me, and I think this is only because of something that has reached you.\" He said, \"Are you the one whose mother adjured you, and she exposed her breast to adjure you by the milk you suckled from her, and you did not comply? Does any of you think that if he is with his parents or one of them, he is not in the path of Allah? Indeed, he is in the path of Allah if he treats them kindly and fulfills their right.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"After that I remained for two years without going on a military expedition until she died.\""],[7811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Prepare to set out against this town whose people are wrongdoers\" — meaning Khaybar — \"for Allah will surely open it for you, if Allah wills. Let no weak person or one deemed weak go out with me.\" Abu Hurayrah went to his mother and said, \"Equip me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has ordered us to equip for the expedition.\" She said, \"Will you go and leave me, though you know that I only enter the privy when you are with me?\" He said, \"I would never stay behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She exposed her breast and adjured him by the milk he had suckled from her. So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ secretly and told him. He said, \"Go, you have been spared worry.\" Abu Hurayrah came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that you are turning away from me, and I think this is only because of something that has reached you.\" He said, \"Are you the one whose mother adjured you, and she exposed her breast to adjure you by the milk you suckled from her, and you did not comply? Does any of you think that if he is with his parents or one of them, he is not in the path of Allah? Indeed, he is in the path of Allah if he treats them kindly and fulfills their right.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"After that I remained for two years without going on a military expedition until she died.\""],[7812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Prepare to set out against this town whose people are wrongdoers\" — meaning Khaybar — \"for Allah will surely open it for you, if Allah wills. Let no weak person or one deemed weak go out with me.\" Abu Hurayrah went to his mother and said, \"Equip me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has ordered us to equip for the expedition.\" She said, \"Will you go and leave me, though you know that I only enter the privy when you are with me?\" He said, \"I would never stay behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She exposed her breast and adjured him by the milk he had suckled from her. So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ secretly and told him. He said, \"Go, you have been spared worry.\" Abu Hurayrah came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that you are turning away from me, and I think this is only because of something that has reached you.\" He said, \"Are you the one whose mother adjured you, and she exposed her breast to adjure you by the milk you suckled from her, and you did not comply? Does any of you think that if he is with his parents or one of them, he is not in the path of Allah? Indeed, he is in the path of Allah if he treats them kindly and fulfills their right.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"After that I remained for two years without going on a military expedition until she died.\""],[7813,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was riding al-Jad'a' with al-Fadl b. Abbas behind him, saying: \"Do not swear oaths against Allah; do not swear oaths against Allah, for whoever swears an oath against Allah, Allah will prove him false.\""],[7814,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Ibrahim passed away, and his eyes were shedding tears. He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, do you cry for this child?\" The one whom Allah has sent with the truth, I have buried twelve children in pre-Islamic ignorance. All of them I have laid to rest in the earth while they were alive.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter that the heart becomes sad and the eyes shed tears? We only say what pleases our Lord. Verily, we are sad due to the passing of Ibrahim.\""],[7815,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When Allah wills good for a servant, He purifies him before his death.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and what is the purification of the servant?\" He said, \"A righteous deed that He inspires him to do until He takes him while upon it.\""],[7816,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A prayer following a prayer with no vain talk between them is a record in Illiyyin.\""],[7817,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hell by a hundred years, at the gallop of a swift, trained horse.\""],[7818,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A prayer following a prayer with no vain talk between them is a record in Illiyyin.\""],[7819,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Take hold of knowledge before it vanishes,” three times. They said, “O Messenger of God, how can it vanish while the Book of God is among us?” He became angry in a way God would not cause him to be angry, then said, “May your mothers be bereaved of you! Were not the Torah and the Gospel among the Children of Israel, and then they availed them nothing? The departure of knowledge is the departure of its bearers,” three times."],[7820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Muslims should offer protection and security to each other.\""],[7821,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A man from among them grants protection on behalf of the Muslims.”"],[7822,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, ʿAmr b. Zurārah al-Anṣārī caught up with us wearing a fine garment, an izār and a ridāʾ, which he had let hang low. The Prophet ﷺ began taking hold of the edge of his garment and humbling himself before God, saying, “O God, Your servant, and the son of Your servant, and the son of Your maidservant,” until ʿAmr b. Zurārah heard it. He turned to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have thin shins.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O ʿAmr b. Zurārah, God ﷻ has made all of His creation well. O ʿAmr b. Zurārah, God does not love those who let their garments hang low.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand below his own knee and said, “O ʿAmr b. Zurārah, this is the place of the izār.” Then he raised it, then placed it below that and said, “O ʿAmr b. Zurārah, this is the place of the izār.” Then he raised it, then placed it below that and said, “O ʿAmr b. Zurārah, this is the place of the izār.”"],[7823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There will be a tribulation in which a man will wake up a believer and become an unbeliever by evening, except for one whom God keeps alive through knowledge.”"],[7824,"“There will be tribulation in which a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, except the one to whom Allah grants knowledge.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3954)"],[7825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, Allah and His angels, even the ant in its hole and the fish in the sea, send blessings upon the teacher of goodness among the people.\""],[7826,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever has mercy on a slaughtered animal, God will have mercy on him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7827,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man lying flat on his face and struck him with his foot, saying, “Get up, for it is a hellish sleep.”"],[7828,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever has mercy, even on a slaughtered sparrow, God will have mercy on him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7829,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The best charity is the shade of a tent in the path of God, or the stud service of a stallion in the path of God.”"],[7830,"The Messenger of God ﷺ “forbade two prayers, two fasts, two marriages, two manners of dress, and two sales.”"],[7831,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Nothing is more beloved to God than two drops and two traces: a drop of tears from fear of God, and a drop of blood shed in the path of God. As for the two traces, a trace in the path of God, and a trace in an obligation from the obligations of God.”"],[7832,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Among the believers are those whose intercession will admit into Paradise a number like Rabīʿah and Muḍar.”"],[7833,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Four verses were sent down from a treasure beneath the Throne, from which nothing else was sent down: the Mother of the Book, for He says, ‘And indeed it is in the Mother of the Book with Us, exalted and wise’; the Verse of the Throne; the Sūrah of the Cow; and al-Kawthar.”"],[7834,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever fasts one day in the path of God, God will place between him and the Fire a trench as wide as the distance between the heaven and the earth.”"],[7835,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not honor our elders and show mercy to our young is not one of us.”"],[7836,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I entered Paradise, and suddenly there was a rustling sound before me. I said, ‘Who is this, O Jibril?’ He said, ‘This is Bilal, the muezzin.’ I looked, and the majority of the people of Paradise were the weak and the poor, and the fewest of the people of Paradise were the rich and women. I said to him, ‘What is this, O Jibril?’ He said, ‘The rich are detained at the gate of Paradise, being called to account and purified. As for the women, the two red things distracted them: gold and silk.’ Then I went out to the eight gates of Paradise, and there was the Balance. He took one pan and placed my entire community in it, and I was placed in the other pan, and it outweighed them. Then my community was presented to me man by man, and I thought ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf was slow. When he came, I said, ‘What held you back?’ He wept to me, and I wept to him. He said, ‘O Messenger of God, I was there behind the gate, being called to account and purified, until I thought I would never see you and you would never see me.’”"],[7837,"I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to some elderly men of the Ansar whose beards were white and said, “O assembly of the Ansar, dye your beards red and yellow, and differ from the People of the Book.”"],[7838,"I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to some elderly men of the Ansar whose beards were white and said, “O assembly of the Ansar, dye your beards red and yellow, and differ from the People of the Book.”"],[7839,"I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once went out to a group of Ansar elders, their hair was white and fair. He said, \"O Ansar! Dye your hair with henna and whiten it with kohl, and be different from the people of the Scripture.\""],[7840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever has the ability to seize some worldly greed but gives it up—though if he had wished he could have taken it—God ﷻ will marry him to the wide-eyed houris wherever he wishes.”"],[7841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever intercedes for his brother, and then accepts a gift given to him in return, has entered a great door of riba.”"],[7842,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me moving my lips and said, “What are you saying, O Abu Umamah?” I said, “I am remembering God.” He said, “Shall I not direct you to what is more than your remembering God night and day? Say: ‘Praise be to God as many times as the number of what He has created; praise be to God as much as fills what He has created; praise be to God as many times as the number of what is in the heavens and the earth; praise be to God as many times as the number of what His Book has enumerated; praise be to God as much as fills what His Book has enumerated; praise be to God as many times as the number of all things; praise be to God as much as fills all things’—and glorify God with the like of them.” Then he said, “Teach them to your offspring after you.”"],[7843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I have been given four things that no prophet before me was given: I have been aided by terror from a month’s journey away; I have been sent to every white and black person; spoils of war have been made lawful for me; and the earth has been made for me a place of purification.”"],[7844,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever spends on himself, it is charity; and on his wife and his child.”"],[7845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The one who recites the Qur’an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who recites the Qur’an quietly is like the one who gives charity secretly.”"],[7846,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “We will attack them in the morning, so force them and be strong.”"],[7847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Three are in the shade of God on the day when there is no shade but His: a man who wherever he turns knows that God is with him; a man whom a woman calls to herself and he leaves her out of fear of God; and a man who loves for the majesty of God, Mighty and Exalted.”"],[7848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The people of Paradise will visit each other on camels with padded saddles. The people of ‘Illiyyūn will visit those below them, but those below them will not visit the people of ‘Illiyyūn except those who love one another for God’s sake; they will visit each other from Paradise wherever they wish.”"],[7849,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever takes on a debt while intending to repay it and then dies, God will overlook it and satisfy his creditor as He wills. Whoever takes on a debt without intending to repay it and then dies, God will exact it from him on behalf of his creditor on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7850,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There are four to whom God will not look on the Day of Resurrection: one who is undutiful to his parents, one who reminds others of his gifts, one addicted to wine, and one who denies divine decree.”"],[7851,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Take on of worship what you are able to bear, for God does not tire until you tire.”"],[7852,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God created the creation and decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets, and His Throne was upon the water. The people of Paradise are its people, and the people of the Fire are its people.” They said, “O Prophet of God, then what about deeds?” He said, “Every people acts according to their station.” Then ‘Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said, “Then we should strive, O Messenger of God!”"],[7853,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The first drop of a martyr’s blood that falls expiates his sins, the second clothes him in the robes of faith, and the third marries him to the wide-eyed houris.”"],[7854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The muezzin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and his reward is like the reward of those who pray with him.”"],[7855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When God, Mighty and Exalted, created the creation and decreed the decree, He took the people of the right with His right hand and the people of the left with His left hand. He said, ‘O people of the right.’ They said, ‘At your service and with pleasure.’ He said, ‘Am I not your Lord?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘O people of the left.’ They said, ‘At your service and with pleasure.’ He said, ‘Am I not your Lord?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ Then He mixed them together. Someone said, ‘O Lord, why did You mix them together?’ He said, ‘They have deeds besides that which they will do, so that on the Day of Resurrection they cannot say, “We were heedless of this.”’ Then He returned them to the loins of Adam.”"],[7856,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “No Muslim performs ablution well and then prays the obligatory prayer except that it is like a Hajj for him, and if he prays a voluntary prayer, it is like an ‘Umrah for him.”"],[7857,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"I touched my penis while I was praying.\" He replied: \"No harm; it is only a piece of you.\""],[7858,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A man may rise from his seat for his brother, except the Banu Hashim — they do not rise for anyone.\""],[7859,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the raised beds (in Paradise). He replied: \"If a bed were thrown from its highest point, it would fall to its lowest depth for a hundred autumns.\""],[7860,"The Prophet ﷺ slept until he snored, then said: \"Ablution is required for the one who lies down.\""],[7861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever incurs a debt intending to repay it, God will settle it for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever incurs a debt not intending to repay it and then dies, God ﷻ will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'I thought I would not take the right of My servant.' Then it will be taken from his good deeds and placed among the good deeds of the other. If he has no good deeds, sins will be taken from the other and placed upon him.\""],[7862,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever owes a debt intending to pay it, then dies without leaving enough to cover it, God will overlook his shortfall and satisfy the creditor as He wills; and with God is his satisfaction.\""],[7863,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting for a servant to go to his brother asking for a loan when he has the means, and then refuse him.\""],[7864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Jumu'ah (Friday prayer) is obligatory upon fifty men, and it is not obligatory for less than fifty men.\""],[7865,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wear a ring on his right hand."],[7866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one fasting voluntarily has the choice until midday.\""],[7867,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When the two circumcised parts meet, the full bath becomes obligatory.\""],[7868,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \"Do the people of Paradise visit one another?\" He replied: \"The higher visit the lower, but the lower do not visit the higher, except those who love one another for the sake of God ﷻ; they may come from wherever they wish on she-camels, carrying cushions.\""],[7869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"{They will remain therein for ages} — one age is thirty thousand years.\""],[7870,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Al-kanūd was mentioned in his presence. He said: \"Al-kanūd is the one who eats alone, withholds his support, and strikes his slave.\""],[7871,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Tayammum is one strike for the face and one strike for the two hands.\""],[7872,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever spits in the direction of his qiblah and does not cover it, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as a blister, and it will remain until it falls between his eyes.\""],[7873,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever relates a hadith as he heard it, then if it is true and correct, it is for you, and if it is a lie, then it is upon the one who originated it.\""],[7874,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Allah ﷻ is beautiful and loves beauty.\""],[7875,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever steps over the circle of a people without their permission is a sinner.\""],[7876,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The Hour will not come until you return to being Harrabin, and until a man goes to a Nabatean woman and marries her for her livelihood, and he abandons his paternal cousin, not looking at her.\""],[7877,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There are those among my Ummah who come to the market and buy a shirt for half a dinar or a third of a dinar, then praise Allah when he wears it, and it does not reach his knees before he is forgiven.\""],[7878,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Ask Allah for al-Firdaws, for it is the center of Paradise, and indeed the people of al-Firdaws hear the creaking of the Throne.\""],[7879,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Were it not that the poor lie, the one who turns them away would not prosper.\""],[7880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were the poor truthful, the one who turns them away would not prosper.\""],[7881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A day will surely come upon Hell when it will be like a crop that has dried and turned red, its gates flapping.\""],[7882,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If the son of Adam had two valleys, he would wish for a third. Wealth was only made for establishing prayer and giving zakah, and nothing fills the son of Adam except dust. Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.”"],[7883,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The companion of the right is a trustee over the companion of the left. When a servant does a good deed, he writes it as ten times its like. When he does an evil deed and the companion of the left wants to write it, the companion of the right says to him: ‘Withhold it.’ So he withholds it. If he seeks Allah’s forgiveness, it is not written; if he remains silent, it is written against him.”"],[7884,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no religion for one who has no trustworthiness.”"],[7885,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not wake until the heat of the sun troubled him between his shoulders. When he woke, they stayed. He called the iqamah for prayer, went forward, and led them in prayer. When he had prayed with them, he said: “If one of you sleeps and his eyes overcome him, let him do like this, for Allah takes the souls at the time of their death, and the one that has not died, in its sleep.”"],[7886,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “A man entered Paradise and saw written on its gate: ‘Charity is ten times its like, and a loan is eighteen times its like.’”"],[7887,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Eating in the marketplace is lowliness.”"],[7888,"I was never near the Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him supplicate with this supplication: “O Allah, guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness except You, and none turns away their evil except You.”"],[7889,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you rinses his mouth, whatever his mouth has incurred is removed; when he washes his face, whatever his face has incurred is removed; when he washes his hands, whatever his hands have incurred is removed; and when he washes his feet, whatever his feet have incurred is removed.” A man then said: “Look at what you are narrating, O Abu Umama. We accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ and we did not hear him say what you are saying.” Abu Umama said: “Had I not heard it from him except once or twice, I would not have narrated it.”"],[7890,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no servant who performs ablution except that his sins depart from his hands; then when he washes his face, his sins depart from his face; then when he washes his forearms, his sins depart from his forearms; then when he wipes his head, his sins depart from his head; then when he washes his feet, his sins depart from his feet.”"],[7891,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with her children. The Prophet ﷺ asked his family [for something to give her], but he found only three dates, and he gave them to her. She gave each child a date and kept one for herself. Her children cried, so she took that date, split it in two, and gave half to this one and half to that one. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They are bearers, mothers, and nursers, merciful to their children. Were it not for what they do with their husbands, their praying women would enter Paradise.”"],[7892,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with her children, one of whom she was nursing. She asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he searched but found nothing to give her until he obtained three dates from one of his wives. She gave this one one and this one one, and kept one date for herself. One of the two children cried, so she split the date in two and gave half to this one and half to that one. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They are bearers, mothers, and nursers, merciful to their children. Were it not for what they do with their husbands, their praying women would enter Paradise.”"],[7893,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution and washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, and his forearms three times each.” The wording is that of Abu ‘Umar’s hadith."],[7894,"I asked Abu Umama, and the deeds of the alms collectors were mentioned to him, so he said: “Alms are a right, and its workers are in the Fire,” according to the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[7895,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Six things: whoever comes with one of them on the Day of Resurrection will come with a covenant. Each one of them says: He used to act in prayer, alms, pilgrimage, fasting, fulfilling the trust, and maintaining family ties.”"],[7896,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a horse, and he gave it to a man from the Ansar. He used to hear its neighing. Then he missed it, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What happened to your horse?” He said: “O Messenger of God, I gelded it.” He said: “In the forelocks of horses there is good and booty until the Day of Resurrection; their forelocks are their warmth and their tails are their fly-whisks.”"],[7897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Ayyub b. Zayd: “O Abu Ayyub, shall I not direct you to a deed that pleases Allah and His Messenger?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Reconcile between people when they become corrupt with each other, and bring them close together when they distance themselves.”"],[7898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will emerge from this ummah a people with whips like the tails of cattle, going out in the displeasure of Allah, and returning in His wrath.”"],[7899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My Lord gave me the seven long surahs in place of the Torah, the surahs with about a hundred verses in place of the Gospel, and I was favored with the Mufassal.”"],[7900,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his gaze to the sky. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is this?” He said: “I saw an angel ascending with the deeds of Salman.”"],[7901,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Aisha: “Do you know that Allah ﷻ married me in Paradise to Maryam bt. Imran, Kulthum the sister of Musa, and the wife of Pharaoh?”"],[7902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “One cauterization, or two cauterizations.”"],[7903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Blessed is the one who saw me and believed in me, and blessed is the one who did not see me and believed in me,” seven times."],[7904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Glad tidings to the one who saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings seven times to the one who believed in me and did not see me.\""],[7905,"I heard Abu al-Ja'd, the freed slave of Banu Dubay'ah, narrating from Abu Umamah that a man from the people of al-Suffah died and left a dinar, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A brand.\" Then another died and left two dinars, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Two brands.\""],[7906,"A man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I bought the share of so-and-so and made such and such profit on it.\" He said: \"Shall I not tell you of something with greater profit?\" The man asked: \"Does such a thing exist?\" He said: \"A man who learns verses.\" So he went and learned ten verses, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him."],[7907,"The Messenger of Allah came out to us while a man was recounting stories, so the man fell silent. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Continue your story. For me to sit in this seat from the time you pray the morning prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves, and for me to sit from the time you pray until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves.\""],[7908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Acts of kindness protect against evil deaths, secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, and maintaining family ties increases one's lifespan.\""],[7909,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The prescribed prayer expiates what came before it until the next prayer, the Friday prayer expiates what came before it until the next Friday, the month of Ramadan expiates what came before it until the next Ramadan, and the Hajj expiates what came before it until the next Hajj.\""],[7910,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The prescribed prayer expiates what came before it until the next prayer, the Friday prayer expiates what came before it until the next Friday, the month of Ramadan expiates what came before it until the next Ramadan, and the Hajj expiates what came before it until the next Hajj.\""],[7911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people, protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date.\""],[7912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: when one of you speaks, he does not lie; when he promises, he does not break it; when he is entrusted, he does not betray; lower your gazes, guard your private parts, and restrain your hands.\""],[7913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Three things, whoever has them in his heart will find the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that he would hate to return to disbelief after Allah saved him from it just as he would hate to be thrown into the Fire.\""],[7914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people, come to your Lord. What is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and distracting. O people, there are only two paths: a path of good and a path of evil, so do not make the path of evil more beloved to you than the path of good.\""],[7915,"A man asked, “O Messenger of God, who is a Muslim?” He said, “One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[7916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The first of the signs is the rising of the sun from its west.”"],[7917,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There are three things that if I were to swear by them I would be truthful, and a fourth that if I were to swear by it I hope I would not be sinning: that God will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; that no servant is appointed over a people in this world but God will appoint him over them and among them in the Hereafter; and that God does not conceal a servant in this world but He will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7918,"Umm Hani' asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “O Messenger of God, I am a heavy woman, so teach me supplications by which God may benefit me.” He said, “Say: Glory be to God one hundred times, which equals one hundred slaves set free for God ﷻ. And praise God one hundred times, which equals one hundred bridled horses ridden in the path of God. And magnify God one hundred times, which equals one hundred garlanded camels offered to the House of God. And declare God's oneness one hundred times—no sin will overtake you after shirk.”"],[7919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not be impressed by the action of a doer until you see how it ends for him.”"],[7920,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites Ḥā Mīm al-Dukhān on the night of Friday or the day of Friday, God will build for him a house in Paradise.”"],[7921,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “To remember God from the break of dawn until sunrise—saying ‘God is greatest,’ ‘there is no god but God,’ and ‘glory be to God’—is more beloved to me than setting free four slaves from the descendants of Ishmael. And to remember God after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than setting free such and such a number from the descendants of Ishmael.”"],[7922,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever peeps through a screen at a people, and his eye is gouged out, it is wasted (no compensation).”"],[7923,"I entered upon Abu Umamah while he was delousing himself in the mosque and burying the lice in the pebbles. I said, “O Abu Umamah, a man told me on your authority that you heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whoever performs ablution and completes it, washing his hands and face and wiping his head and ears, then rises to an obligatory prayer, God will forgive him on that day whatever evil his feet walked toward, his hands grasped, his ears heard, his eyes looked upon, and his self whispered.’” He said, “By God, I heard from the Prophet ﷺ what I cannot count.”"],[7924,"When the heads of the Azāriqa were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus, Abu Umamah came. When he saw them, his eyes welled up, then he said: “Dogs of the Fire! Dogs of the Fire! These are the worst of those slain under the canopy of the sky, and the best of those slain under the canopy of the sky are those whom these killed.” I said: “What is the matter with you that your eyes have welled up?” He said: “Out of mercy for them, for they were from the people of Islam.” He said: I said: “Did you say ‘dogs of the Fire’ based on your own opinion, or is it something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Then I would be very bold. Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once, nor twice, nor three times,” and he counted many times. Then he recited: {On the day when faces will turn white and faces will turn black} until he reached {they will abide therein forever}, and he recited: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses that are precise} until he reached {those of understanding}. Then he took my hand and said: “Indeed, they are many in your land, so may God protect you from them.”"],[7925,"I was walking with Abu Umamah while he was on his donkey until we reached the steps of Damascus, and there were heads set up. He said: “What are these heads?” It was said: “Heads of the Khawarij brought from Iraq.” He said: “Dogs of the Fire! Dogs of the Fire! Dogs of the Fire! The worst of those slain under the sky, the worst of those slain under the sky, the worst of those slain under the sky,” he said it three times. “The best of those slain are those whom these killed,” he said it three times. “Blessed is the one who killed them and whom they killed,” he said it three times. Then he wept. I said: “What makes you weep, O Abu Umamah?” He said: “Out of mercy for them, for they were from the people of Islam, then they departed from Islam.” Then he recited: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses that are precise; they are the mother of the Book} until he finished the verses. Then he recited: {And do not be like those who became divided and differed after clear proofs came to them} until he reached {then in God’s mercy; they will abide therein forever}. I said: “O Abu Umamah, is it these?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “Is it something you say by your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Then I would be very bold, very bold, very bold. I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once nor twice,” until he counted seven. Then he put his finger in his ears and said: “Otherwise, may they be deafened.”"],[7926,"I was in Syria when al-Muhallab sent seventy heads of the Khawarij, and they were set up at the gate of the mosque. I was on the roof of my house when Abu Umamah passed by, heading to the mosque. When he stopped at them, his eyes welled up and he said: “Glory be to God! What Satan does to the children of Adam,” three times. He said: “Dogs of Jahannam! The worst of those slain under the shade of the sky,” three times. Then he said: “The best of those slain under the shade of the sky are those whom they killed,” three times. Then he turned to me and said: “O Abu Ghalib, you are in a land where these are many, so may God protect you from them. Do you recite the surah that contains Āl ʿImrān?” I said: “Yes, and I saw your eyes well up.” He said: “I wept out of mercy for them; they were from the people of Islam.” Then he recited: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses that are precise} until he reached {seeking discord and seeking its interpretation}. “Indeed, these had deviation in their hearts, so they were led astray.” Then he recited: {And do not be like those who became divided} until he reached {Have you disbelieved after your faith?}. I said: “These, O Abu Umamah?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “O Abu Umamah, do you say this by your own opinion, or is it something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “I would be very bold, very bold, very bold. Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once nor twice,” until he reached six."],[7927,"I was in Syria when al-Muhallab sent seventy heads of the Khawarij, and they were set up at the gate of the mosque. I was on the roof of my house when Abu Umamah passed by, heading to the mosque. When he stopped at them, his eyes welled up and he said: “Glory be to God! What Satan does to the children of Adam,” three times. He said: “Dogs of Jahannam! The worst of those slain under the shade of the sky,” three times. Then he said: “The best of those slain under the shade of the sky are those whom they killed,” three times. Then he turned to me and said: “O Abu Ghalib, you are in a land where these are many, so may God protect you from them. Do you recite the surah that contains Āl ʿImrān?” I said: “Yes, and I saw your eyes well up.” He said: “I wept out of mercy for them; they were from the people of Islam.” Then he recited: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses that are precise} until he reached {seeking discord and seeking its interpretation}. “Indeed, these had deviation in their hearts, so they were led astray.” Then he recited: {And do not be like those who became divided} until he reached {Have you disbelieved after your faith?}. I said: “These, O Abu Umamah?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “O Abu Umamah, do you say this by your own opinion, or is it something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “I would be very bold, very bold, very bold. Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once nor twice,” until he reached six."],[7928,"I saw Abu Umamah al-Bāhilī when he saw the heads of the Khawarij on the steps of Damascus and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Dogs of the people of the Fire, dogs of the people of the Fire, dogs of the people of the Fire.” Then he wept and said: “The worst of those slain under the canopy of the sky, and the best of those slain are those whom they killed.” Abu Ghalib said: I said to him: “Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Then I would be very bold. I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once, nor twice, nor three times.”"],[7929,"While I was in Damascus, seventy heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. Abu Umamah, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, came, entered the mosque, and prayed as much as he wished. When he came out, he wept, then said: “Dogs of the people of the Fire.” God, exalted be He, says: {It is He who sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses that are precise; they are the mother of the Book, and others ambiguous. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is ambiguous from it}. Then he recited: {On the day when faces will turn white and faces will turn black. As for those whose faces turn black: Have you disbelieved after your faith? Then taste the punishment for what you used to disbelieve}. “They are these.” I said: “O Abu Umamah, is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ or something you say by your own opinion?” He said: “Then I would be very bold. I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ not once, nor twice, nor three times,” until he reached seven."],[7930,"Some Ḥarūriyyah heads were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. Abu Umamah looked at them while they were set up and said: “The worst of those slain under the sky are these—three times. Blessed is the one who killed them, and blessed is the one whom they killed.” I said: “O Abu Umamah, is it something you say by your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Then I would be very bold—three times. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say that.”"],[7931,"I was in Damascus on the roof of a house when Abu Umamah passed by me, so I followed him. Then we came upon the heads of the Khawarij set up on the steps of the mosque. He said: “The worst of those slain under the shade of the sky, and the best of those slain are those whom they killed.” I said: “Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “Yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah, yes, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah,” several times. Then he wept. I said: “Do you weep after what you said?” He said: “I have mercy on them. They are a people who wanted something but did not attain it. Indeed, you are in a land where they are many, so may God protect you from them.”"],[7932,"Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: “Then I would be very bold if I said what I did not hear.”"],[7933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Khawarij are the dogs of the people of the Fire.”"],[7934,"“We used to call the people of whims ‘dogs of the Fire.’”"],[7935,"“The worst of those slain under the shade of the sky.” I said: “Is it something you say by your own opinion, or did you hear it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “If I had not heard it from the Prophet ﷺ except once, or twice, or three times—until he reached seven—I would not have narrated it.”"],[7936,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"You will exit from Islam as an arrow exits from its quarry; you will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch—dogs of the Fire.\""],[7937,"Regarding this verse: {He it is Who has sent down to you the Book; in it are verses that are precise—they are the foundation of the Book—and others unspecific.} up to {seeking its interpretation}. He said: Abu Umamah narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"They are the Khawarij.\" And I asked him about this verse: {As for those whose faces turn black—did you disbelieve after your belief? Then taste the punishment for what you used to deny.} He said: Abu Umamah narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that \"they are the Khawarij.\""],[7938,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {O you who believe! Do not take as intimates those other than yourselves, for they will not spare you any ruin. They wish you would suffer. Hatred has already appeared from their mouths, and what their breasts conceal is greater. We have made clear to you the signs, if you use reason.} He said: \"They are the Khawarij.\""],[7939,"Regarding the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims.} He said: Abu Umamah narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"It was revealed concerning the Khawarij when they saw Allah's pardon for the Muslims and for the Ummah and the community; they said: Would that we had been Muslims.\""],[7940,"I went out with Abu Umamah al-Bahili to the mosque of Damascus. When he was at the gate, there were heads—some of the heads of the Khawarij. When he looked at them, he wept and said: \"What has Satan done?\" three times. \"Dogs of the Fire,\" three times. Then he said: \"The worst of those killed under the shade of the sky,\" three times. \"Whoever they killed was the best of those killed under the shade of the sky.\" I said: O Abu Umamah, do you say this yourself, or is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"Then I would indeed be bold. Do you not recite the verses at the beginning of Al 'Imran? {As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific from it.} It was revealed concerning these people, until you recite the verse in the middle of Al 'Imran: {On the Day when some faces will turn white and some faces will turn black.} It was revealed concerning these people.\" I said: What makes you weep, O Abu Umamah? He said: \"They were believers,\" or he said, \"Muslims.\""],[7941,"I was in Damascus in the time of 'Abd al-Malik. The heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on wooden stakes. I came to see if I recognized anyone among them, and there was Abu Umamah near them. I approached him and looked at the stakes. He said: \"Dogs of the Fire,\" three times. \"The worst of those killed under the canopy of the sky, and those whom they killed are the best of those killed under the canopy of the sky.\" He said it three times. Then he wept. I said: O Abu Umamah, what makes you weep? They were upon our religion, then I remembered what they are heading to tomorrow. I said to him: Is this something you say by your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except once, or twice, or three times—up to seven—I would not have narrated it to you. Do you not recite this verse in Al 'Imran: {On the Day when some faces will turn white and some faces will turn black} to the end of the verse: {As for those whose faces turn white, they will be in the mercy of Allah, abiding eternally therein.}\""],[7942,"I was in Damascus in the time of 'Abd al-Malik. The heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on wooden stakes. I came to see if I recognized anyone among them, and there was Abu Umamah near them. I approached him and looked at the stakes. He said: \"Dogs of the Fire,\" three times. \"The worst of those killed under the canopy of the sky, and those whom they killed are the best of those killed under the canopy of the sky.\" He said it three times. Then he wept. I said: O Abu Umamah, what makes you weep? They were upon our religion, then I remembered what they are heading to tomorrow. I said to him: Is this something you say by your own opinion, or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except once, or twice, or three times—up to seven—I would not have narrated it to you. Do you not recite this verse in Al 'Imran: {On the Day when some faces will turn white and some faces will turn black} to the end of the verse: {As for those whose faces turn white, they will be in the mercy of Allah, abiding eternally therein.}\""],[7943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, and this Ummah will split into what the Children of Israel split into, with one additional sect. All of them will be in the Fire except the main body.\" We said: O Abu Umamah, is there not in the main body what suffices it? He said: \"By Allah, we certainly disapprove of what you do.\""],[7944,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my Ummah will exceed them by one sect. All of them will be in the Fire except the main body.\""],[7945,"The heads of the Azariqa—seventy heads—were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus for seven days. Three days of the seven passed, and on the fourth day Abu Umamah came, prayed two rak'ahs beside a pillar, and said: \"Dogs of the Fire,\" three times. \"The worst of those killed under the shade of the sky; the best of those killed under the shade of the sky are those whom they killed.\" I said: O Abu Umamah, is this something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or something you say of your own accord? He said: \"Then I would indeed be bold. No, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not once, nor twice—until it reached seven.\""],[7946,"The heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. People began looking at them, and I went out to look at them. Abu Umamah came on a donkey wearing a sunbulani shirt. He looked at them and said: \"What has Satan done to this Ummah?\" saying it three times. \"The worst of those killed under the shade of the sky are these; the best of those killed under the shade of the sky are those whom these killed. Dogs of the Fire,\" saying it three times. Then he wept, then departed. Abu Ghalib said: I followed him and said: I heard you say something before—was it your own saying? He said: \"Glory be to Allah! Then I would indeed be bold. Rather, I heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ many times.\" I said to him: I saw you weeping. He said: \"Out of mercy for them—they were once among the people of Islam.\" Then he said to me: \"Do you not recite?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then recite from Al 'Imran.\" I recited, and he said: Do you not hear Allah saying: {As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific from it.} In the hearts of these there was deviation, so they were led astray by it. Recite at the head of the hundred; I recited until I reached: {On the Day when some faces will turn white and some faces will turn black. As for those whose faces turn black—did you disbelieve after your belief?} I said: O Abu Umamah, are they these? He said: Yes, they are these. \"This hadith was not narrated from Khulayd b. Da'laj except by al-Walid.\""],[7947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Khaybar with two servant boys. He gave one of them to 'Ali b. Abi Talib and said: \"Do not strike him, for I have been forbidden from striking the people of prayer, and I have seen him praying.\" He gave Abu Dharr a servant boy and said: \"Treat him with kindness.\" So Abu Dharr freed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What happened to the servant boy I gave you?\" He said: You commanded me to treat him kindly, so I freed him."],[7948,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “More people than Rabīʿah and Muḍar will come out of the Fire through the intercession of one man of my community.”"],[7949,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Through the intercession of one man of my community, more than the number of Muḍar will enter Paradise. A man will intercede for his household, and he will intercede according to the measure of his deeds.”"],[7950,"“It was a supererogatory prayer for the Prophet ﷺ and a virtue for you.”"],[7951,"I heard Abū Umāmah say: “There is no Muslim who hears the call to prayer and then rises to perform his ablution except that he is forgiven at the first drop his palm pours of that water. After that drop, God forgives him his past sins, so he rises to his prayer, and it is supererogatory.” I said: “Did you hear this from the Messenger of God ﷺ, O Abū Umāmah?” He said: “By the One who sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner—not once, not twice, not three times, not four times, not ten times,” and he clasped his hands together."],[7952,"I heard Abū Umāmah say: “When you put the purification water in its proper places, you sit down already forgiven. If you pray, you have a virtue and a reward, and if you sit, you sit forgiven.” A man said to him: “O Abū Umāmah, do you think that if he stands and prays, it is supererogatory for him while he is toiling in sins and errors?” He said: “You have a virtue and a reward.”"],[7953,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who performs ablution and puts the water of his ablution in its proper places except that his sins depart from his hearing, his sight, his body, and his feet, and his prayer is a supererogatory merit for him.”"],[7954,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer consisting of nine units. But when he grew old or his physical condition became difficult, he would perform Witr prayer consisting of seven units. He would pray two units, then prostrate twice while sitting, reciting in them when the verses were revealed, 'When the earth is shaken up its final quake,' and 'Say: O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship, nor are you worshippers of what I worship, nor will I be a worshiper of what you worship, nor will you be worshipers of what I worship. For you is your religion, and for me is my religion.'\""],[7955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two units of prayer after Witr while sitting and reciting in them \"Say: O disbelievers!\""],[7956,"The translation of the passage from Arabic to English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with nine units, but when it became difficult for him, he would perform Witr with seven units.\""],[7957,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “No people go astray after guidance they had except that they are given disputation.” Then he recited: “They did not strike it for you except to dispute; rather, they are a contentious people.”"],[7958,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When you pass by a land whose people have been destroyed, hasten your pace.”"],[7959,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you pass by a land whose people God has destroyed, quicken your pace.”"],[7960,"“When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, he ran his fingers through his beard.”"],[7961,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution with half a mudd.”"],[7962,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us leaning on a staff. When we saw him, we stood up for him, so he said: “Do not do as the non-Arabs do, standing up for one another.”"],[7963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, leaning on a staff. When we saw him, we stood up for him. He said, \"Do not do as the non-Arabs do, standing up for one another.\""],[7964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people. I reached them while I was hungry, and found them eating blood. I said, \"I have only come to forbid you from this.\" Then I laid my head down and got up overcome. Then someone came to me in my sleep with a vessel containing a drink and said, \"Take this and drink.\" Then he filled my stomach, and I was satiated and quenched. I then heard them saying, \"A man from the nobles of your people has come to you; you will not succeed with him by offering the thin milk.\" So they brought me their thin milk, and I said, \"I have no need of it. Allah has fed me and given me drink.\" I showed them my stomach, and they all embraced Islam to the last one."],[7965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people to call them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to present to them the laws of Islam. I came to them after they had watered their camels, milked them, and drunk. When they saw me, they said, \"Welcome to al-Sudayy b. Ajlan.\" They said, \"We have heard that you have inclined to this man.\" I said, \"No, but I have believed in Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to you to present Islam and its laws to you.\" While we were thus, they brought a large bowl of blood and placed it, and they gathered around it eating. They said, \"Come, O Sudayy.\" I said, \"Woe to you! I have only come to you from the one who forbids this to you through what Allah revealed to him.\" They said, \"And what did he say?\" I said, \"This verse was revealed: 'Forbidden to you are carrion, blood, and the flesh of swine' up to His saying 'and that you seek division by divining arrows.'\" I continued calling them to Islam, but they refused. I said to them, \"Woe to you! Bring me some water, for I am extremely thirsty.\" He said, \"And I was wearing my turban.\" They said, \"No, but we will leave you to die of thirst.\" He said, \"So I wrapped my head in my turban and slept in the intense heat on the pebbles. Then someone came to me in my sleep with a glass goblet, the like of which people had never seen more beautiful, containing a drink the like of which people had never seen more delicious. He made it possible for me, and I drank it. When I finished my drink, I woke up, and by Allah, I was not thirsty, nor did I know thirst after that drink.\""],[7966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says after the dawn prayer, before bending his legs: 'There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is all good; and He has power over all things' one hundred times, will on that day be the most excellent of the people of the earth, except one who says the like of what he said or adds to what he said.\""],[7967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When two Muslims shake hands, their hands do not part until they are both forgiven.\""],[7968,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever washes a deceased person and conceals his faults, Allah will conceal his sins; and whoever shrouds him, Allah will clothe him from fine silk.\""],[7969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever washes a deceased person and conceals what he sees, Allah will purify him from his sins; and if he shrouds him, Allah will clothe him from fine silk.\""],[7970,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two categories of my community will never receive my intercession: a tyrannical ruler and every extreme deviant.\""],[7971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The most beloved jihad to Allah is a word of truth spoken to an unjust ruler.\""],[7972,"At the Jamrah: \"O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is most excellent?\" He said, \"The most excellent jihad is a word of truth in the presence of an unjust ruler.\""],[7973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guarantee me six traits and I will guarantee you Paradise.\" They said, \"And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Do not act unjustly when dividing your inheritances, be fair to people from yourselves, do not be cowardly when fighting your enemy, do not steal from your spoils, and restrain your wrongdoer from your wronged.\""],[7974,"From Abu Umamah, I do not know it except as raised to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Garlic, onions, and leeks are among the intoxicants of Iblis.\""],[7975,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu al-Darda' and Salman."],[7976,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The angels stand on Friday at the doors of the mosque, with them scrolls, writing down the people, until when the imam comes out, the scrolls are rolled up.\" I said, \"There is no Friday for one who comes out after the imam?\" He said, \"Indeed, but he is not in what is in the scrolls.\""],[7977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When Allah created the intellect, He said to it, 'Come forward,' and it came forward. Then He said to it, 'Turn back,' and it turned back. He said, 'By My might, I have not created a creation more wondrous to Me than you. By you I give, and by you is reward, and upon you is punishment.'\""],[7978,"The Prophet ﷺ laughed and then said, \"I wonder about people who are being dragged to Paradise in chains while they dislike it.\""],[7979,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Allah has those freed from the Fire at every breaking of the fast.\""],[7980,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Allah has, at every breaking of the fast, those freed from the Fire.\""],[7981,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Three people's prayer does not go beyond their heads: a runaway slave, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and an imam who leads a people while they dislike him.\""],[7982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Spitting in the mosque is a bad deed, and burying it is a good deed.\""],[7983,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever spits in the mosque and does not bury it, it is a bad deed, and if he buries it, it is a good deed.\""],[7984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it.\""],[7985,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he spoke, would speak three times so that he could be understood."],[7986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives, \"Do not make this boy cry,\" meaning Husayn. He said, \"It was the day of Umm Salamah, so Jibril ﷺ descended and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the inner chamber and said to Umm Salamah, 'Do not let anyone enter upon me.' Husayn ؓ came, and when he saw the Prophet ﷺ in the house, he wanted to enter, so Umm Salamah took him and held him in her lap, and began to soothe him and calm him. When he intensified in crying, she let him go, so he entered until he sat in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. Jibril ﷺ said, 'Your nation will kill this son of yours.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'They will kill him while they are believers in me?' He said, 'Yes, they will kill him.' Then Jibril took some soil and said, 'At such and such a place.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, embracing Husayn, distressed and troubled, so Umm Salamah thought that he was angry at the boy's entering upon him. She said, 'O Prophet of Allah, may I be your ransom, you told us not to make this boy cry, and you commanded me not to let anyone enter upon you, but he came, so I let him go.' He did not answer her. He went out to his companions while they were sitting and said to them, 'My nation will kill this one.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and they were the boldest of the people toward him, so they said, 'O Prophet of Allah, they will kill him while they are believers?' He said, 'Yes, and this is his soil,' and he showed it to them.\""],[7987,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted.\""],[7988,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Three people whose prayer does not go beyond their ears until they return: the runaway slave, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and the imam of a people who dislike him."],[7989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Bahilah. I came to them while they were having a meal. They welcomed me and honored me and said, \"Come and eat.\" I said, \"I have come to forbid you from this food, and I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I have come to you so that you may believe in him.\" They disbelieved me and rebuked me, so I left while I was hungry and thirsty, having suffered severe hardship. I slept and was brought in my sleep a drink of milk, which I drank and quenched my thirst, and my stomach became full. The people said, \"A man from the best and noblest of you came to you, and you rejected him. Go to him and feed him of food and drink whatever he desires.\" They brought me food, but I said, \"I have no need of your food and drink, for Allah has fed me and given me drink.\" So look at the state I am in. They looked and so they believed in me and in what I brought from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7990,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Give me a servant.\" He said to him, \"There are three in the house; choose one of them.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you choose for me.\" He said, \"Take this boy, for I saw him praying since we left, for a while, and do not beat him, for we have been forbidden from beating the people of prayer.\""],[7991,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog.\""],[7992,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels sit at the doors of the mosques on Friday and write down the first, the second, and the third. When the imam comes out, the scrolls are raised.\""],[7993,"He said: \"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"The speech of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Quran, and he increased in remembrance, shortened the sermon, and lengthened the prayer. He did not disdain or feel too proud to go with the poor and the weak until he fulfilled their need.\""],[7994,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Abu Dharr a slave and said, \"Feed him from what you eat and clothe him from what you wear.\" Abu Dharr had a garment, so he tore it into two halves, wrapping himself in one half and giving the other half to the slave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Why do I see your garment like this?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you said: Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Should I free him?\" He said, \"May Allah reward you, O Abu Dharr.\""],[7995,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at midday, for at that time Hell is stoked.\""],[7996,"From the Prophet ﷺ, or from the brother of Abu Umamah, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at midday, for at that time Hell is stoked.\""],[7997,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He forbade prayer when the horn of the devil rises or sets.\""],[7998,"Abu Umamah asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"At what time is prayer disliked?\" He said, \"From the time you pray the dawn prayer until the sun rises a spear's length, and from the time the sun turns yellow until it sets.\""],[7999,"From Abu Umamah and his brother, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a people performing ablution and said, \"Woe to the heels from the Fire.\""],[8000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people performing ablution, and on the heel of one of them there was a spot the size of a dirham that the water did not reach. He said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the things I fear most for my ummah in its latter time are the stars, the denial of divine decree, and the injustice of rulers.”"],[8004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people performing ablution, and on their feet there remained a spot the size of a dirham that the water did not reach. So he said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8005,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he saw a man perform ablution for prayer, leaving a spot the size of a fingernail unwashed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to complete the ablution, then said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people, and on the heel of one of them there was a spot like a dirham or the size of a fingernail that the water did not reach. He began saying: “Woe to the heels from the Fire” twice."],[8007,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “My Lord came to me in the most beautiful form and said: ‘O Muhammad.’ I said: ‘At Your service, gladly.’ He said: ‘About what does the highest assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘I do not know.’ So He placed His hand between my chest and I came to know in that moment all that He asked me about concerning the affairs of this world and the Hereafter. He said: ‘About what does the highest assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘About degrees and expiations. As for degrees, they are performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous one.’ He said: ‘You have spoken truth. Whoever does that lives in good and dies in good, and his sins are removed as on the day his mother gave birth to him. As for expiations, they are feeding others, spreading peace, kind speech, and praying while people sleep.’ Then he said: ‘O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, abandonment of evil deeds, love for the poor, forgiveness, and that You accept my repentance. If You intend a trial for a people, deliver me from it without being afflicted.’”"],[8008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Learn the Qur’an, for it will intercede for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. Learn Surat al-Baqarah and Al ‘Imran. Learn the two radiant ones, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds or two canopies, or like two flocks of birds in rows, arguing in defense of their companion. And learn Surat al-Baqarah, for learning it is a blessing, abandoning it is a regret, and the idle cannot master it.” He meant by the idle the magicians."],[8009,"The Prophet ﷺ came out while I was sitting moving my lips, so he said, “What are you moving your lips for?” I said, “I am remembering Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Shall I not tell you something that, if you say it and then persist night and day, you would not reach it?” I said, “Yes, please.” He said, “Say: All praise is due to Allah, as many as His Book has enumerated; and all praise is due to Allah, as many as what is in His Book; and all praise is due to Allah, as many as His creation has enumerated; and all praise is due to Allah for what is in His creation; and all praise is due to Allah, filling His heavens and His earth; and all praise is due to Allah, the number of all things; and all praise is due to Allah, filling all things. And glorify Him similarly, and magnify Him similarly.”"],[8010,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “No household over whom a faddān (a yoke of oxen) arrives but they are humiliated.”"],[8011,"\"Be upright and well, if you persist in uprightness. No one can maintain their ablution except a believer.\""],[8012,"Abu ʿUbaydah Ḍirār b. al-Azwar took charge of killing Mālik b. Nuwayrah, and regarding that Mutammim b. Nuwayrah says, alluding to Khālid b. al-Walīd:"],[8013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me, or by a man milking, and said, “Leave the milk that remains in the udder (dawāʿī al-laban).” This is how Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Sinān, and the companions of al-Aʿmash disagreed with him, narrating it from al-Aʿmash, from Yaʿqūb b. Buḥayr."],[8014,"We gave a milch camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I milked it for him. When I took hold of it to exhaust the milk, he said, “Do not do that; leave the milk that remains in the udder.”"],[8015,"My family sent me with a milch camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, having given it to him as a gift. He said to me, “Milk it and leave the remaining milk in the udder,” and he supplicated for me."],[8016,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a she-camel as a gift. He said to me, “Get up and milk it.” So I got up and milked it. When I went to exhaust the milk, he said, “Leave the remaining milk in the udder.”"],[8017,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with the offspring of my camels. He said, “Milk it,” so I said, “Shall I exhaust the milk?” He said, “Do not exhaust it; leave the milk that remains in the udder.”"],[8018,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Stretch out your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.” Ḍirār said: Then I said..."],[8019,"I came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when I stood before him I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you.” He said, “Recite.” He said: I said..."],[8020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There will not cease to be a guardian (wālī) from Quraysh.”"],[8021,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of a dark night, tribulations like patches of smoke. In them a man's heart will die just as his body dies. In them a man will wake up as a believer and end the day as a disbeliever, and he will end the day as a believer and wake up as a disbeliever. In them some people will sell their morals and their religion for a paltry gain of this world.\" And indeed Yazid b. Mu'awiya has died, and you are our brothers and our full brothers, so do not precede us with anything until we choose for ourselves."],[8022,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"When a man comes to a people and they say, 'Welcome, welcome to him until the day he meets his Lord,' and when a man comes to a people and they say, 'Barren, barren for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[8023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Trim and do not exhaust, for it is more radiant for the face and more favorable with the husband.\""],[8024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Dahhak, what is your food?\" I said, \"Meat and milk.\" He said, \"Then what does it become?\" I said, \"Then it becomes what you know.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ has made what comes out of the son of Adam a parable for this world.\""],[8025,"\"I do not consider the blood money to belong to anyone but the male relatives, because they pay on his behalf. Does any of you have anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that?\" Dahhak b. Sufyan al-Kilabi, whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed over the Bedouins, said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me to give an inheritance to the wife of Ashim al-Dibabi from the blood money of her husband.\" 'Umar ؓ adopted that."],[8026,"\"Enter your dome so that I may inform you.\" He entered, and the [Prophet] came to him and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me that a woman from Ashyam Al-Dibabiy is to inherit from her husband’s mind.\""],[8027,"I do not know anything for you, then we call upon the people that anyone who has knowledge from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him stand up. Then Dhahhak bin Sufyan al-Kilabi stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me that I should inherit the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi from the blood money of her husband.\" So Umar inherited her."],[8028,"“The blood money is for the near male relatives from the father's side and the wife does not inherit anything from the blood money of her husband,” until Ad-Dahhak bin Sufyan wrote to him, and told him that the Prophet ﷺ ruled that the wife of Ashyam bin Dibabi should inherit from the blood money of her husband. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2642)"],[8029,"\"Ashim al-Dibabi had been killed by mistake.\""],[8030,"From 'Urwa, in naming those who attended the 'Aqaba pledge to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from the Banu Tha'laba b. 'Ubayd: al-Dahhak b. Haritha b. Zayd b. Tha'laba, and he \"witnessed Badr.\""],[8031,"When the Prophet ﷺ marched to Khaybar, he placed 'Ali ؓ in command of his vanguard and said: \"Whoever enters the palm grove is safe.\" When the Prophet ﷺ said that, 'Ali ؓ proclaimed it. The Prophet ﷺ looked at Jibril ﷺ and smiled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What makes you smile?\" He said: \"I love him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Jibril says he loves you.\" He said: \"It has reached me that Jibril loves me.\" He said: \"Yes, and one better than Jibril: Allah the Exalted.\""],[8032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young and does not recognize the right of our elders. And he is not one of us who deceives us. And a believer is not a believer until he loves for the believers what he loves for himself.\""],[8033,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing two fine Yemeni garments. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do you think these two garments of yours will admit you to Paradise?\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, if you seek forgiveness for me, I will not sit down until I take them off.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O God, forgive Damura b. Tha'laba.\" He went off quickly until he took them off."],[8034,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he would say, while folding his leg: \"Glory be to Allah and with His praise; I seek Allah's forgiveness. Indeed He is ever accepting of repentance\" seventy times."],[8035,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he would say, while folding his leg: \"Glory be to Allah and with His praise; I seek Allah's forgiveness. Indeed He is ever accepting of repentance\" seventy times."],[8036,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he would say, while folding his leg: \"Glory be to Allah and with His praise; I seek Allah's forgiveness. Indeed He is ever accepting of repentance\" seventy times."],[8037,"It is said to him: Dimam. He was in Yemen, and he used to treat people possessed by spirits. He came to Makkah and heard them saying about Muhammad ﷺ: a sorcerer, a soothsayer, and a madman. So he said: \"If I go to this man, perhaps Allah will heal him through my hands.\" He met him and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah heals through my hands, and I treat these spirits.\" He said: \"Praise be to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said: \"Repeat it to me.\" He repeated it to him three times. He said: \"I have heard the speech of soothsayers, the speech of sorcerers, and the poets, and I have never heard anything like these words. It has reached the depth of the sea. Stretch out your hand, I pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.\" He stretched out his hand and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and upon my people. So he pledged allegiance to him upon his people."],[8038,"Dimam b. Tha'laba came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Shall I not perform ruqya on you, O Muhammad?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Praise be to God; we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of our souls and the misdeeds of our actions. Whomever God guides, there is none to misguide him; and whomever He misguides, there is none to guide him. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\" Dimam said, \"I have read the scriptures — the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms — but I have never heard the like of this speech. Repeat them to me.\" So he repeated them to him. Then he said, \"Repeat them to me,\" and he repeated them to him. Then it was mentioned that he embraced Islam."],[8039,"Banu Sa'd b. Bakr sent Dimam b. Tha'laba to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came to him, made his camel kneel at the door of the mosque, then hobbled it, then entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting in the mosque. Dimam was a man with thick hair and two locks, until he stood over the Messenger of God ﷺ and his Companions and said, \"Which of you is of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said, \"Muhammad?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"O son of 'Abd al-Muttalib, I am going to question you and be harsh in my questioning, so do not take it personally.\" He said, \"I will not take it personally; ask about whatever comes to you.\" He said, \"I adjure you by God, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those after you: Has God commanded you to command us to worship God alone, not associating anything with Him, and to cast off these rivals that our fathers used to worship besides Him?\" He said, \"O God, yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by God, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those after you: Has God commanded you to command us to perform these five prayers?\" He said, \"O God, yes.\" Then he began mentioning the obligations of Islam one by one: zakat, fasting, Hajj, and all the laws of Islam, adjuring him at each obligation as he had adjured him in the previous one. When he finished, he said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. I will fulfill these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me, not adding to it or diminishing it.\" Then he turned away toward his camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If the one with the two locks is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8040,"A man from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had been nursed among them. He said, \"O son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said, \"I have answered you.\" He said, \"I am the envoy of my people and their messenger, and I am going to question you, and my questioning will be intense, and I will adjure you, and my adjuration will be intense, so do not be angry with me.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Tell me: Who created the heavens and the earth, Paradise and Hell?\" He said, \"God, may He be exalted.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Him: Is it He who sent you with what came to us of your letter and your messengers came to us, that we should bear witness that there is no god but God and that we should abandon al-Lat and al-'Uzza?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Him: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should pray five prayers every day and night. I adjure you by Him: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should fast one month every year. I adjure you: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should perform Hajj to it in Dhul-Hijjah. I adjure you: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"These are five, and I will not add to them.\" When he turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, if he does what he said, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8041,"A bedouin from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"And peace be upon you.\" He said, \"I am a man from your maternal uncles, from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their envoy. I am going to question you, so my questioning will be intense, and I will adjure you, so my adjuration will be intense.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go ahead, O brother of Banu Sa'd.\" He said, \"Who created you, and who created those before you, and who is the Creator of those after you?\" He said, \"God.\" He said, \"I adjure you by that: Is it He who sent you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Tell me: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths, and made provision flow between them?\" He said, \"God.\" He said, \"I adjure you by that: Is it He who sent you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should pray night and day five prayers at their times. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should fast the month of Ramadan. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that you should take from the surplus of our wealth and put it among our poor. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"As for the fifth, I am not asking about it, and I have no need of it\" — meaning obscene acts. Then he said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will act upon these and whoever obeys me among my people.\" Then he turned back. The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then said, \"If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8042,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Husayn b. 'Abd Allah b. Dumayra narrated to us from his father from his grandfather that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, marry me to so-and-so.\" He said, \"What do you have to give her as her dower?\" He said, \"I have nothing.\" He said, \"Whose is this ring?\" He said, \"Mine.\" He said, \"Then give it to her.\" And he married him to her. And he married another man on the basis of Surat al-Baqarah when he had nothing."],[8043,"From Damura b. Tha'laba al-Bahzi, a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"He used to charge into the enemy's camp until he broke through the ranks, then return until he stood back in his place.\""],[8044,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Pray to God for martyrdom for me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O God, I make the blood of Ibn Tha'laba forbidden to the polytheists and disbelievers.\" He said, \"I used to charge into the thick of the people, and the Prophet ﷺ would appear to me behind them.\" They said, \"O Ibn Tha'laba, you charge and attack the people.\" He said, \"The Prophet ﷺ appears to me behind them, so I charge at them until I stand beside him. Then he appears to me at my companions, so I charge until I am with my companions.\" He said, \"And he lived for a long time after that.\""],[8045,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they do not envy one another.\""],[8046,"Umm al-Harir, when a man of the Arabs died, it weighed heavily on her. It was said to her, \"Umm al-Harir, why do we see that when a man of the Arabs dies, it weighs heavily on you?\" She said, \"I heard my master say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Among the signs of the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs.'\" Muhammad b. Abi Razin said, \"Her master was Talha b. Malik.\""],[8047,"When a man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and had no acquaintance in Madinah with whom to stay, he stayed with the people of the Suffah. I had companions there, and we used to receive from the Messenger of God ﷺ each day, between every two of us, two mudds of dates. While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in one of the prayers, a caller from among his Companions called out, \"O Messenger of God, the dates have burned our stomachs and our guts are on fire.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he stood up, praised God, and extolled Him, then mentioned what he and his people had endured of hardship. He said, \"I and my two companions spent more than ten days with no food except wild berries, until we came to our brothers among the Ansar, and they shared their food with us. The bulk of their food was dates. By the One besides whom there is no god, if I could find bread and meat for you, I would feed you. Perhaps you will live to see a time — or whoever among you lives to see it — when people will wear garments like the covering of the Ka'bah, and bowls of food will be brought to you morning and evening.\""],[8048,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I desire to wage jihad in the path of God.\" He said, \"Is your mother alive?\" I said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Stay close to her feet, for there is Paradise.\""],[8049,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Extend your hand.\" He said, \"Even if I command you to sever ties with your mother?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then I returned to him and said, 'Extend your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you.' He said, 'Upon what?' I said, 'Upon Islam.' He said, 'Even if I command you to sever ties with your mother?' I said, 'No.' Then I returned to him a third time. He had a mother and was one of the most dutiful of people to her. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'O Talha, there is no severing of kinship ties in our religion, but I wished that there be no doubt in your faith.' So he embraced Islam and his Islam was excellent. Then he fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ visited him and found him unconscious. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I think Talha will pass away tonight. If he regains consciousness, send for me.' Talha regained consciousness in the middle of the night and said, 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ visit me?' They said, 'Yes,' and told him what he had said. He said, 'Do not send for him at this hour, lest an animal sting him or something befall him. But in the morning, convey my greetings to him and tell him to ask forgiveness for me.' Then he passed away. After the Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he asked about him, and they informed him of his death and what he had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands and said, 'O God, meet him while he smiles at You and You smile at him.'"],[8050,"A delegation of Qays came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: \"Begin with the Ahmasiyyin before the Qaysiyyin. O God, bless the Ahmasiyyin and their men.\""],[8051,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, in our land we have grapes that we press and drink from.' He said: 'No.' I repeated it and he said: 'No.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, we seek healing with it.' He said: 'That is not a cure, but it is a disease.'"],[8052,"On the authority of a brother of 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from her mother's side, from Banu Daws, he said: I saw in a dream that I met a group of Jews, so I asked them and they asked me. I said: 'You are a people, were it not that you say 'Uzayr is the son of God.' They said: 'And you, you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' Then I met their counterparts among the Christians, so I asked them and they asked me. I said: 'You are a people, were it not that you say the Messiah is the son of God.' They said: 'And you, you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' So I told the Messenger of God ﷺ about it. He said: 'Did you tell anyone about it before me?' I said: 'Yes, O Prophet of God.' Then the Prophet of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said: 'Your brother saw a dream and has told you what he saw. What prevented me from forbidding you from that was shyness. So when you speak, say: What God wills alone.'"],[8053,"“O Prophet of Allah, what do you think about praying in a single garment?” So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ untied his lower garment, folded his cloak over it, wrapped himself in both, and led us in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said, “Does every one of you find two garments?”"],[8054,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions while they were building the mosque. When I saw their work, I began skillfully handling the shovel and mixed the clay with it. It was as if he was pleased with my handling of the shovel and their work. He said, “Leave the Hanafi and the clay, for he is the most skilled of you with clay.” The wording is from the hadith of Asim b. Ali."],[8055,"He witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man asked him about a man praying in a single garment, but he said nothing. When the prayer was called, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ matched his two garments and prayed in them."],[8056,"We sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the delegation of Abd al-Qays came. He said, \"Why have your complexions turned yellow, your bellies grown large, and your veins become prominent?\" They said, \"Our leader came to you and asked you about a drink that suited us, and you forbade him from it. We were in a land that was unhealthy and feverish.\" He said, \"Then drink whatever seems good to you.\""],[8057,"He was brought in, so we entered. I served him tharid, meat, and nabidh. He ate and drank, and he pressed me, so I ate and drank with him, though I was afraid of the dawn. Then he said, \"My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Eat and drink, and do not let the spreading, rising light alarm you. Eat and drink until the red glow appears before you,'\" and he gestured with his hand."],[8058,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he forbade us to start fasting a day before Ramadan until we see the crescent or complete the count, and we should not break the fast until we see it or complete the count."],[8059,"The Messenger of God said, \"Excellent foster parents are the people of Oman.\""],[8060,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When you pray, do not spit in front of you or to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty; otherwise, under your foot.\" He gestured with his foot and scraped the ground."],[8061,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you are in prayer, do not spit in the direction of your face or to your right, but to your left if it is empty; otherwise, under your foot.\""],[8062,"Tariq b. Abdullah al-Muharibi, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"When you pray, do not spit in front of you or to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty or under your foot.\""],[8063,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When one of you stands in prayer, let him not spit in front of him or to his right, but to his left if it is empty or under his left foot.\""],[8064,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When you pray, do not spit in front of you or to your right, but to your left or under your left foot.\""],[8065,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When you spit, do not spit in front of you or to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty or under your foot.\""],[8066,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"When you pray, do not spit in front of you or to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty or under your foot.\""],[8067,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When you are in prayer, do not spit in front of you or to your right. Spit to your left; if it is not empty, then under your left foot.\" Then he said, \"Like this,\" and wiped the ground."],[8068,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"When you use stones for cleansing, use an odd number, and when you perform ablution, sniff water into the nose and expel it.\""],[8069,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Tariq, prepare for death before death.\""],[8070,"I was in the market of Dhu al-Majaz when a young man passed by wearing a red striped cloak, saying, \"O people, say: There is no god but God, and you will prosper.\" A man behind him was pelting him, having bloodied his heels and legs, saying, \"O people, he is a liar, so do not obey him.\" I asked, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"This is the youth of Banu Hashim who claims that he is the Messenger of God ﷺ, and this is his uncle Abd al-Uzza.\" When Muhammad ﷺ emigrated to Madinah and the people embraced Islam, we departed from al-Rabadhah that day with a woman of ours in a howdah. When we came to Madinah and approached its walls, we put on clothes other than our own, and there was a man in the road. He said, \"From where are the people coming?\" We said, \"We are bringing provisions for our families from its dates. We have a red camel standing, tied with a nose rope.\" He said, \"Will you sell me your camel?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"For how much?\" We said, \"For such and such saa of dates.\" He did not reduce anything from what we said, and he struck with his hand and took the camel's nose rope, then turned away with it. When he disappeared from us behind the walls, we said, \"By God, we have done nothing; we have traded with someone we do not know.\" A woman sitting said, \"I have seen a man whose face was like the full moon on the night of al-Badr. By God, he will not wrong you nor deceive you; I guarantee your camel.\" Then a man came and said, \"I am the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ to you. This is your dates, so eat and be satisfied and measure out.\" He said, \"We ate and were satisfied and measured out and received in full.\" Then we entered Madinah and came to the mosque, and there he was, delivering a sermon on the pulpit. We heard from his speech: \"Give charity, for charity is better for you. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Begin with those you support: your father, your mother, your sister, your brother, and then those nearest to you, then those nearest to you.\" A man from the Ansar stood and said, \"O Messenger of God, these are Banu Yarbu; they killed a man of ours in the pre-Islamic era, so aid us against them.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, a father does not bear the crime of his child. Indeed, a father does not bear the crime of his child. Indeed, a father does not bear the crime of his child.'\" three times."],[8071,"Our dye during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ was wars and saffron."],[8072,"\"O my son, I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and I did not see any of them perform qunut. O my son, it is an innovation.\" He said it three times."],[8073,"\"I prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ؓ, and Ali here in al-Kufah for about five years, and they did not perform qunut in the Fajr prayer.\" Then he said, \"O my son, it is a newly invented matter.\""],[8074,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Name yourselves after me (by my name), but do not call yourselves by my Kuniya, and whoever sees me in a dream, he surely sees me, for Satan cannot impersonate me (appear in my figure). And whoever intentionally ascribes something to me falsely, he will surely take his place in the (Hell) Fire. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6197)"],[8075,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[8076,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a nabidh in a stone vessel."],[8077,"We used to go early to the Prophet ﷺ, and a man would come and a woman would come, and he would say, \"O Messenger of God, what should I say when I pray?\" He would say, \"O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me, for these have gathered for you your worldly life and your Hereafter.\""],[8078,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ teaching one who had embraced Islam, saying, \"Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, and provide for me.\" Then he said, \"These have gathered the good of this world and the Hereafter.\""],[8079,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came to him and said, \"O Messenger of God, what should I say when I ask my Lord?\" He said, \"Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being, and provide for me,\" and he gathered his four fingers except the thumb, \"for these gather for you your religion and your worldly life.\""],[8080,"When a man embraced Islam during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, they taught him the prayer."],[8081,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulating the House, and when the people crowded around the Black Stone, he touched it with a hooked staff in his hand."],[8082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever prays Fajr is under Allah's protection, and his reckoning is with Allah.”"],[8083,"“I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Ali, and none of them had a lighter prayer than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, yet it was complete.”"],[8084,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says La ilaha illallah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and blood inviolable, and his reckoning is with Allah.”"],[8085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say La ilaha illallah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.”"],[8086,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever affirms the oneness of Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and blood inviolable, and his reckoning is with Allah.”"],[8087,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever affirms the oneness of Allah and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Allah, Allah has made his wealth and blood inviolable, and his reckoning is with Allah.”"],[8088,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Slaughter is sufficient for my companions.”"],[8089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Slaughter is sufficient for my companions.”"],[8090,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no servant who prostrates and says, 'My Lord, forgive me' three times, except that he is forgiven before he raises his head.”"],[8091,"“We used to sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were boys, and I did not see a man with longer silence than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When his companions spoke and talked at length, he would smile.”"],[8092,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is three days; whatever is beyond that is a kindness.”"],[8093,"The Prophet ﷺ said, Enjoining, all that is good is a Sadaqa.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6021)"],[8094,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the lightest of people in prayer, yet it was complete.”"],[8095,"That tranquility descends upon the tongue of 'Umar."],[8096,"A man from Banu Tamim or Banu 'Utarid said: 'O you slave with the cut ear, do you want to share in our spoils?' His ear had been cut off while with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: 'The better of my two ears you insulted.' So he wrote to 'Umar ؓ and wrote: 'The spoils belong to those who witnessed the battle.'"],[8097,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ and I fought in the caliphate of Abu Bakr ؓ'"],[8098,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and participated in battles during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar. Thirty-three or thirty-four battles from Ghazwat to Sariyah."],[8099,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Friday prayer is obligatory upon every Muslim except a slave, a sick person, a woman, or a child.\""],[8100,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: \"About what do the highest assembly dispute?\" He said: \"About degrees and expiations. As for degrees, they are feeding food, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep. As for expiations, they are completing ablution in the cold, walking heavily to the Friday prayers, and waiting for prayer after prayer.\""],[8101,"The Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Tell us, what is the first thing the people of Paradise will eat when they enter?\" He said, \"The first thing they will eat is the liver of a whale.\""],[8102,"\"We used to sell an ornamented sword and buy it with silver.\""],[8103,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to mention the Hour a great deal until it was revealed: {About what are you asking? Its knowledge is with your Lord}"],[8104,"\"The Prophet ﷺ, when he came to a place near the house of Ya'la b. Munabbih, would face the House and supplicate.\""],[8105,"I saw in what a sleeping person sees, as if I passed by a group of Jews. I said: 'Who are you?' They said: 'We are the Jews.' I said: 'You are indeed a people, were it not that you say 'Uzayr is the son of God.' They said: 'And you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' Then I passed by a group of Christians. I said: 'You are indeed a people, were it not that you say the Messiah is the son of God.' They said: 'And you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' When morning came, I told some people about it. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said: 'Did you tell anyone about it?' I said: 'Yes.' When he prayed the noon prayer, he stood as a preacher, praised God and extolled Him, then said: 'Indeed Tufayl saw a dream and told those of you whom he told. Indeed you used to say a word that shyness from you prevented me from forbidding you. So do not say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.'"],[8106,"From ʿUrwa regarding the naming of those from the Ansar who attended the ʿAqaba pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, then from the Banū Salima b. Zayd b. Khaytham: Ṭufayl b. al-Nuʿmān b. Khansāʾ, and he participated in Badr."],[8107,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Daws has perished—they have disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8108,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions arrived and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8109,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions arrived and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8110,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ faced the qibla and raised his hands. The people said, \"Daws is ruined.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8111,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8112,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8113,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions arrived and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8114,"That the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sent Tufayl ibn Amr and another person to Daws. They came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to destroy Daws.\" He said, \"O Allah, guide Daws and bring them to us.\""],[8115,"He hosted the Messenger of God ﷺ among a group of people. They spent the night at his place, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came out at night and found him lying on his stomach. He nudged him with his foot and woke him, then said, \"Do not lie like this, for it is the lying posture of the people of the Fire.\""],[8116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave instructions, and one man went with another man, and one man went with two men, until I was left as the fifth of five. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Go.\" We went with him to ʿĀʾisha ؓ, and he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought hashīsha and we ate. Then she brought ḥaysa like a small bird and we ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, give us something to drink.\" She brought a small cup of milk and we drank. Then he said, \"If you wish, you may stay the night; and if you wish, go to the mosque.\" We said, \"We will go to the mosque.\" While I was lying on my stomach, a man moved me with his foot and said, \"This is a lying posture that God hates.\" I looked and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would look at the common people and say, \"So-and-so, take so-and-so and host him.\" He continued until I remained with the Messenger of God ﷺ as the fifth of five. He said to us, \"Go to the house.\" We went with him and entered the house of ʿĀʾisha ؓ—that was before the veil was imposed on them. He said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought hashīsha and we ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought ḥaysa like a small bird and they ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, give us something to drink.\" She brought a bowl with ḍiyāḥ and they drank. Then he said to us, \"If you wish, stay here; and if you wish, go to the mosque.\" We said, \"No, rather we will go to the mosque,\" and we disliked burdening the Messenger of God ﷺ. I slept in the mosque, and while I was lying on my stomach, a man came to me and moved me with his foot and said, \"Turn over like this, for it is a sleeping posture that God Almighty hates.\" I looked and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque while I was sleeping on my stomach. He moved me with his foot and said, \"This is a sleeping posture that God hates.\" I raised my head and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8119,"While I was lying down in the mosque, a man nudged me with his foot, saying, “[Lie] like this, for this is a posture that Allah ﷻ hates.” I raised my head and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O so-and-so, take this one with you; O so-and-so, take this one with you.” I remained the fourth of four. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “Go.” We set out until we came to the house of 'A'ishah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O 'A'ishah, feed us.” She brought some herbs, and we ate. Then he said, “O 'A'ishah, feed us.” She brought some hais the size of a small bird. Then he said, “O 'A'ishah, give us something to drink.” She brought a small cup of milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “If you wish, stay the night here, or if you wish, go to the mosque.” We said, “Rather, we will go to the mosque.” While I was sleeping on my stomach before dawn, a man pushed me with his foot and said, “[Lie] like this, for this is a posture that Allah ﷻ hates.” I raised my head and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8121,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who performs ablution and then lowers his hand and touches his penis, or should I sprinkle water on it?” He said, “It is a part of you.”"],[8122,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am in prayer and I touch my penis with my hand.” He said, “It is a piece of you.”"],[8123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you desires his wife, let him come to her even if she is at the oven.”"],[8124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fajr is not the white light that rises vertically, but rather the red glow that spreads horizontally.”"],[8125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fajr is not the white light that rises vertically, but rather the red glow that spreads horizontally.”"],[8126,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If it is cloudy for you, then complete the count as thirty.”"],[8127,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was laying the foundations of the mosque of Madinah. I began carrying stones as they were carrying. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You people of al-Yamamah are the most skilled at mixing clay, so mix the clay for us.” I mixed the clay for them, and they carried it."],[8128,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say, “When a man calls his wife to his need, she should respond, even if she is at the oven.”"],[8129,"We set out, six of us, as a delegation to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: five from Banu Hanifah and the sixth a man from Banu Dab'ah b. Rabi'ah. We came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, prayed with him, and told him that in our land there was a church of ours. We asked him for some of the leftover water of his purification. He called for water, performed ablution with it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a water skin. He said, “Take this water, and when you reach your town, demolish your church, then sprinkle its place with the water, and take that place as a mosque.” We said, “O Prophet of Allah, the town is far and the water will dry up.” He said, “Then add water to it, for that will only increase its goodness.” We set out with it until we reached our town and did as he commanded. That day a monk from Tayyi' saw us, and when we called the adhan for prayer, the monk said, “A call of truth.” Then he fled, and we never saw him again."],[8130,"I built the mosque of Madinah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would say, “Let the Yamami handle the clay, for he is the best of you at kneading it.”"],[8131,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man, as if he were a Bedouin, asked him, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who touches his private part after performing ablution?” He said, “Is it anything but a piece of flesh from you or a morsel?”"],[8132,"“A scorpion stung me while I was with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and he recited ruqyah over me.”"],[8133,"“When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ gave the salam in prayer, we would see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek.”"],[8134,"Qays ibn Talq said: Talq ibn Ali visited us on a certain day during Ramadan. He remained with us till evening and broke fast with us. He then stood up and led us in the witr prayer. He then went to his mosque and led them in prayer. When the witr remained, he put forward another man and said: Lead your companions in the witr prayer, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There are no two witrs during one night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1439)"],[8135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A woman must not refuse her husband, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle.”"],[8136,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think: if one of us touches his private part, should he perform ablution?” He said, “No, it is only a piece of flesh from you.”"],[8137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A believer is not one whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful actions.”"],[8138,"From his father Talq b. Ali, who was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[8139,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution.” This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub b. Utbah except by Hammad b. Muhammad, and Hammad b. Muhammad also narrated the other hadith. Both are authentic according to me. It seems likely that he heard the first hadith from the Prophet ﷺ before this one, then heard this one later. Thus it agrees with the hadith of Busrah, Umm Habibah, Abu Hurayrah, Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, and others who narrated from the Prophet ﷺ the command to perform ablution from touching the private part. So he heard both the abrogated and the abrogating."],[8140,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He remained silent until the time of Asr prayer arrived, then he matched his lower garment with his outer sheet, wrapped himself in them like this, and led the Asr prayer. When he finished, he said, “Where is the one who asked about praying in a single garment?” The man said, “O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Does every one of the people find two garments?”"],[8141,"We sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Mukhtar b. Abd al-Qays came and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, what do you think about a drink we make from our fruits?\" The Prophet ﷺ turned away from him until he asked him three times. Then he stood and led us in prayer. When he finished the prayer, he said, \"Who is the one asking about the intoxicant? You ask me: do not drink it and do not give it to your Muslim brother. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no man ever drinks it seeking to become intoxicated but that Allah will give him wine to drink on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8142,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to us, \"Soon there will come a people who recite the Qur'an but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes through the game. Blessed is the one who kills them, and blessed is the one whom they kill.\" Then he turned to me and said, \"Indeed, they will emerge in your land, O Tihami, fighting between the rivers.\" I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, it has no rivers.\" He said, \"Indeed, it will.\""],[8143,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his back in his bowing and prostration.\""],[8144,"\"I was mixing clay in Madinah when a scorpion stung me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and recited an incantation over me until I recovered.\""],[8145,"\"A scorpion stung Talq in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ recited a ruqyah over him and wiped him with his hand.\""],[8146,"From Urwah, in the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Zuhayr b. Rafi."],[8147,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Zuhayr b. Rafi."],[8148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us something that was beneficial to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said, \"What do you do with your cultivated fields?\" I said, \"We lease them for a quarter and an eighth.\" He said, \"Do not do that. Either cultivate them or keep them.\" I said, \"We hear and obey.\""],[8149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us something that was convenient for us. I said, \"What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said is true.\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you do with your cultivated fields?' We said, 'We lease them for a quarter, a third, and loads of straw and barley.' He said, 'Do not do that. Cultivate them or give them to be cultivated.'\""],[8150,"From ʿUrwah, regarding naming those who made the first emigration to the land of Abyssinia: Abū Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Asad, and with him was his wife Umm Salamah. She gave birth in the land of Abyssinia to ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah."],[8151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ seated me with him at a meal and said to me: “Mention the name of God, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.”"],[8152,"Abu Quhafa was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, his head and beard like thaghama. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Take him to some of his women to change it.\" He said, \"So they took him and dyed it red.\""],[8153,"By Allah, I did not marry her when I married her out of desire for wealth or children, but I wanted her to tell me about ʿUmar’s night. So he asked her: How was ʿUmar’s prayer at night? She said: He would pray ʿatamah, then he would order us to place a basin of water at his head and cover it. He would wake during the night, put his hand in the water, wipe his face and hands, then remember Allah Almighty as much as he willed. Then he would wake again several times until he came to the hour in which he would stand for his prayer. Ibn Buraydah said to him: Who told you this? He said: The daughter of ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ told me. He said: Trustworthy, by Allah."],[8154,"The last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “When you lead people in prayer, lighten the prayer for them.”"],[8155,"When the north wind blew strongly, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have sent.'"],[8156,"The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon me was that I make the prayer light for the people."],[8157,"He informed him that the last thing upon which the Messenger of God ﷺ parted from him was: 'Make the prayer light for the people.'"],[8158,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to place the mosque of al-Ṭāʾif where their idol had been."],[8159,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who drinks it and the one who sells it,\" meaning wine."],[8160,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “The gates of heaven are opened halfway through the night, and a caller calls out: Is there any supplicant, that he may be answered? Is there any asker, that he may be given? Is there any distressed person, that he may be relieved? No Muslim remains supplicating with a supplication but Allah answers him, except an adulteress who goes about with her private parts or a tax collector.”"],[8161,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to the Muslims, \"There are three Egypt's: one at the meeting point of the two seas, one in the Nile Delta, and one in Sham (Syria). The Muslims will be terrified by three terrifying events: the emergence of the Dajjal (Antichrist) in the East, which will be defeated by the first Egypt (meeting point of the two seas) with an army of seventy thousand, accompanied by a group of Jews and women. The people of Egypt will be divided into three groups: one group will stay in Egypt and say, 'We will defend ourselves,' one group will join the Bedouins, and one group will join the second Egypt (in the Nile Delta). Then the Dajjal will proceed to Sham, while its people take refuge in the mountain pass of Afiq. They will send a detachment to confront him, but they will be defeated. They will face severe famine and hardships, to the extent that one of them will burn his bow and eat it. While they are in that state, a caller from the sky will announce, 'O people, here comes your help!' They will say, 'This is the voice of a well-fed person.' Then Jesus the son of Mary ﷺ will descend while leading the Fajr prayer, and the people will say to him, 'O Spirit of Allah, come forward and lead us in prayer.' He will reply, 'You are all leaders of Muhammad's nation, some of you leading others. So, you should come forward and lead the prayer.' The leader will then perform the prayer, and Jesus will take his weaponry and head towards the Dajjal. When the Dajjal sees Jesus, he will dissolve like salt in water, and Jesus will place his spear in the ground between the two horns of the Dajjal and kill him. The companions of the Dajjal will be defeated, and there will not be a single one among them without being killed. Even the trees and rocks will say, 'O believer, there is a disbeliever behind me, so kill him!'\""],[8162,"That ʿUthman b. Abi al-ʿAs came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some people of Thaqif. They entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: “Guard our goods, or our mounts, for us.” He said: “On condition that when you leave, you wait for me until I come out from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a copy of the Qur'an that he had, and he gave it to me. He appointed me over them and made me their imam, though I was the youngest of them.”"],[8163,"“The Islam of ʿAmr b. al-ʿAs, Khalid b. al-Walid, and ʿUthman b. Talha took place with the Negus, and they came to Madinah in Safar of the year eight of the Hijrah.”"],[8164,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in the House."],[8165,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever steps over people’s necks on Friday after the imam has come out, or separates between two people, is like one who drags his intestines into the Fire.”"],[8166,"O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind in Kufa a man dictating the codices from memory. ʿUmar became angry until his face swelled, then said, “Who is he?” He said, “ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud.” So he said, “May your father be for Allah’s sake, and who is more deserving of that than him? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.’”"],[8167,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"Umar surpassed the people in four things: his mention of the captives on the day of Badr, when he ordered their execution and God, exalted is He, sent down {Were it not for a prior decree from God, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took}; his mention of the veil, when Zaynab said, 'And you are jealous of us while revelation descends in our houses,' so God, exalted is He, sent down {And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil}; the supplication of God's Prophet ﷺ, 'O God, support Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab' ؓ; and his judgment concerning Abu Bakr, for he was the first of the people to pledge allegiance to him.\""],[8168,"“ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah and I were with the women on the day of the Trench, in the fort of Ḥassān. He would stoop down for me once and I would look, and I would stoop down for him and he would look.”"],[8169,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping himself in it with its two ends crossed.”"],[8170,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a single garment, with its two ends crossed.”"],[8171,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik. Ḥ And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik reported to us. Ḥ And ʿAlī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl b. Abī Uways narrated to us: Mālik narrated to me, from Hishām b. ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah, that he “saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment in the house of Umm Salamah, placing its two ends on his shoulder.”"],[8172,"I heard ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah say: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in my mother’s house in a single garment, wrapping himself in it.”"],[8173,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, with its two ends crossed.”"],[8174,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, placing its end on his shoulders in the house of Umm Salamah.”"],[8175,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, covering himself with it in the house of Umm Salamah.”"],[8176,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in a single garment.”"],[8177,"That he “saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a garment whose end he had thrown over his shoulders.”"],[8178,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapping himself in it.”"],[8179,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[8180,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in my mother's house praying in a single garment, having put its two ends on opposite sides."],[8181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed in the house of Umm Salamah in a garment, having wrapped himself with it (putting it over both shoulders)."],[8182,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment."],[8183,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Hisham b. ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿUmar b. Abi Salamah, that he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a garment, wrapping himself with it, placing its two ends upon his shoulders, in the house of Umm Salamah."],[8184,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapping himself with it, placing its two ends upon his shoulders."],[8185,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapping himself with it."],[8186,"It was narrated from Umar bin Abi Salamah that he saw Messenger of Allah ﷺpraying in a single garment in the house of Umm Salamah, putting the ends of it on his shoulders.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 764)"],[8187,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; Ibn Lahiʿah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from ʿUrwah, who said: I heard ʿUmar b. Abi Salamah say: 'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment, having put its two ends on opposite sides.'"],[8188,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment."],[8189,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in a single garment."],[8190,"That he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapping himself with it, having put its two ends on opposite sides."],[8191,"That he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment, having put its two ends on opposite sides."],[8192,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, having placed its two ends on opposite shoulders."],[8193,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether a fasting person may kiss. He said, \"Ask this one,\" referring to Umm Salamah, who was sitting there. She said, \"He indeed does that.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.\" He said, \"By Allah, I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most mindful of Him.\""],[8194,"This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salamah: {Indeed, Allah only intends to remove from you impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with thorough purification.} He called al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and Fatimah and seated them in front of him, and he called Ali and seated him behind his back. Then he and they were covered with the cloak. Then he said, \"O Allah, these are my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\" Umm Salamah said, \"Am I with them, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You stay in your place, and you are upon good.\""],[8195,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abdullah b. Mas'ud: The scriptures used to descend from heaven from a single gate, but the Quran was revealed from seven gates upon seven modes: lawful and unlawful, clear and ambiguous, parables, command and prohibition. So declare lawful what it makes lawful, declare unlawful what it makes unlawful, act upon its clear verses, refrain from its ambiguous ones, and take lesson from its parables. Indeed, all of it is from Allah, and none takes heed except those of understanding."],[8196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of Umm Salamah and saw with them an effeminate man, who was saying, \"O Abdullah b. Abi Umayyah, if al-Ta'if is conquered, I will show you Badiyah bt. Ghaylan. She advances with four and retreats with eight.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"These must never enter upon you.\""],[8197,"Food was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, \"O Umar, my son, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\""],[8198,"While I was a boy in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, my hand was moving about in the dish. He said, \"O boy, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\""],[8199,"Umar b. Abi Salamah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited me to a meal and said, \"Come near, my son, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\""],[8200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said, \"O boy.\" I said, \"At your service.\" He said, \"Sit, my son, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\""],[8201,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while food was in front of him. He said to me, \"Come near, eat, and mention the name of Allah, from what is near you.\""],[8202,"Umar b. Abi Salamah, the stepson of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported: Food was served to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I came and began moving my hand about, eating from here and there. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my hand and said, \"Stop, my son, eat from what is near you.\""],[8203,"I was a boy in the lap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my hand was moving about in the dish. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O boy, when you eat, say 'In the name of Allah,' eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.\" He said, \"That remained my manner of eating thereafter.\""],[8204,"One day I ate with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I started taking from around the dish. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Eat from what is near you.”"],[8205,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I command you with three and forbid you from three. I command you not to associate anything with God, to hold firmly to obedience all together until God's command comes to you while you are upon that, and to give sincere counsel to the rulers from those who command you with God's command. I forbid you from ‘he said, she said,’ excessive questioning, and squandering wealth.”"],[8206,"“Let this not alarm you, O Commander of the Believers, for by God, my violation toward the one whose affair you entrusted to me is no more severe than your violation toward me.” He said: It was as if that pleased Umar from him, and it increased him in good."],[8207,"“Peace be upon you, O Commander,” while a group from the people of Syria was with him. They said: “Who is this hypocrite who fell short in greeting the Commander of the Believers?” Uthman said to Muawiyah: “These have found fault with me for something you know better. Indeed, I greeted Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may God have mercy on them, with it.” Muawiyah said: “I think part of what he says did happen, but the people of Syria, when the turmoil occurred, said: By God, we will know our religion and not fall short in greeting our caliph. I think you, O people of Madinah, say to the collector of zakah ‘Commander.’”"],[8208,"Hani': We performed Hajj in the time of Uthman b. Affan ؓ. I sat in a gathering in the Prophet's Mosque ﷺ, and there was a man narrating to them: “We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ one day when a man came and prayed toward this pillar. He hurried before completing his prayer, then left. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘If this man were to die, he would die without being upon anything of the religion. A man may make it light and complete it.’” I asked about this man and was told: “Uthman b. Hunayf al-Ansari.”"],[8209,"Hani': We performed Hajj in the time of Uthman b. Affan ؓ. I sat in a gathering in the Prophet's Mosque ﷺ, and there was a man narrating to them: “We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ one day when a man came and prayed toward this pillar. He hurried before completing his prayer, then left. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘If this man were to die, he would die without being upon anything of the religion. A man may make it light and complete it.’” I asked about this man and was told: “Uthman b. Hunayf al-Ansari.”"],[8210,"On the authority of his grandfather Uthman b. Sahl b. Hunayf: “Before he came from Makkah, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to call people to faith in God and belief in Him by word without action, and the qiblah was toward Jerusalem. When he migrated to us, the obligations were revealed, Madinah abrogated Makkah and what was said in it, and the Sacred House abrogated Jerusalem. Thus faith became word and action.”"],[8211,"I heard Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ rejected celibacy for Uthman b. Maz'un. Had he permitted it, we would have castrated ourselves.”"],[8212,"...that he should practice celibacy, but the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade him.” Sa'd said: “Had he allowed that, we would have castrated ourselves.”"],[8213,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ rejected celibacy for Uthman b. Maz'un,” and had he permitted celibacy for him, we would have castrated ourselves."],[8215,"His wife said: “Congratulations on Paradise to you.” The Prophet ﷺ looked at her with an angry look and said: “What do you know?” She said: “Your horseman and your companion.” The Messenger ﷺ said: “By God, I do not know what will be done with me.” That weighed heavily on the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ because of his statement about Uthman, who was among the best of them. When Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, he said: “Join our predecessor Uthman b. Maz'un.”"],[8216,"Uthman b. Maz'un came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I feel ashamed for my family to see my private parts.\" He said, \"Why? When He has made you a covering for them and made them a covering for you.\" He said, \"I dislike that.\" He said, \"They see it from me and I see it from them.\" He said, \"You are the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said, \"I am.\" He said, \"You? Then who after you?\" He said, \"When Uthman turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Uthman b. Maz'un is indeed modest and veiling.'\""],[8217,"The wife of Uthman b. Maz'un, whose name was Khawla bt. Hakim, entered upon A'isha looking disheveled in appearance. She asked her, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"My husband stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ entered, and A'isha mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ met Uthman and said, \"O Uthman, monasticism was not prescribed for us. Do I not serve as an example for you? By God, the most fearful of you of God and the most careful of you regarding His limits is me.\""],[8218,"He said, \"O Messenger of God, I am a man who finds this celibacy during military campaigns difficult. Will you permit me to castrate myself?\" He said, \"No, but upon you, O Ibn Maz'un, is fasting, for it is a restrainer.\""],[8219,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ caught up with Uthman b. Maz'un while they were on their mounts at the pass of al-Uthaya from al-Arj. His mount pressed against Uthman's mount, and the Messenger of God's ﷺ mount had already gone ahead of the group. Uthman b. Maz'un said, \"You hurt me, O lock of trial.\" When the mounts set off, Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ approached him and said, \"May God forgive you, Abu al-Sa'ib, what is this name you called me?\" He said, \"No, by God, I am not the one who named you. The Messenger of God ﷺ named you. He is ahead of the group, leading the people. One day you passed by us while we were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, 'This is the lock of trial,' and he pointed with his hand. 'There will remain between you and trial a strongly locked door as long as this man lives among you.'\""],[8220,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting in the courtyard of his house in Makkah, Uthman b. Maz'un passed by and smiled at the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Will you not sit?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ sat facing him. While he was speaking with him, the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky and looked at it for a while. Then he began to lower his gaze to where he placed it on his right, on the ground. The Messenger of God ﷺ turned from his companion Uthman to where he placed his gaze, and he began to nod his head as if trying to understand what was being said to him, while Ibn Maz'un was looking. When he finished his matter and understood it, he said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his gaze until it disappeared into the sky, then returned to Uthman with his former sitting position.\" He said, \"O Muhammad, what was I sitting with you about? I have never seen you do what you did this morning.\" He said, \"Did you notice that?\" Uthman said, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A messenger of God came to me while you were sitting.\" He said, \"A messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What did he say to you?\" He said, \"{Indeed God commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrongdoing, and oppression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.}\" Uthman said, \"That was when faith settled in my heart and I loved Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[8221,"Abu Bakr ؓ brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of God ﷺ, leading him, an old blind man, on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Why did you not leave the old man until we came to him?\" He said, \"I wanted him to receive the reward. By God, I was more delighted by the Islam of Abu Talib than by the Islam of my father, seeking thereby the delight of your eye.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You have spoken the truth.\""],[8222,"Abu Quhafa was brought to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest, his head like white thaghama (a white plant). He said, \"Change it and keep him away from black.\""],[8223,"Abu Quhafa was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, his head and beard like thaghama, like this white cotton. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Take him to some of his women to change it and keep him away from black.\""],[8224,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought Abu Quhafa on the day of the conquest of Makkah, his beard and head like thaghama. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Change it with something and keep him away from black.\""],[8225,"Abu Quhafa was brought, or he came, in the year of the conquest, his head and beard like thagham or thaghama. He was ordered to his women, and they said, \"Change it with something.\""],[8226,"Uthman b. Abi al-'As, and Abu al-'As's name is — and he is Abu al-'As b. Bishr b. 'Abd b. 'Abd Allah b. Hammam b. Aban b. Bashshar b. Malik b. Hutayt b. Jusham b. Qasiyy b. Munabbih b. Bakr b. Hawazin b. Mansur b. 'Ikrima b. Khasafa b. Qays b. Ghaylan b. Mudar."],[8227,"With twelve dirhams. I said: If I had twelve dirhams with me, I would buy a ram with it, sacrifice it, and feed my family. When I stood up, ʿUthmān’s messenger followed me with a purse containing fifty dirhams. I never saw dirhams with greater blessing than those. He gave it to me while he sought reward for it, and I was in need of it."],[8228,"ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ had a room that he had emptied for ḥadīth. We used to come to him there, and he would say: “An hour for this world and an hour for the Hereafter, and Allah knows best which of the two hours prevails.”"],[8229,"I have found the Muslim man between two needs: a need of this world that is indispensable for him, and a need of the Hereafter that is indispensable for him. Allah knows best which of the two needs prevails."],[8230,"I saw ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ having water sprinkled on him on the day of ʿArafah while he was fasting."],[8231,"He carried people who had nothing between them and the water except the planks. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they perish — or a word like that — I will certainly take their number from Thaqīf."],[8232,"ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, and he was a young man: We came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ, and he found me the best of them in taking the Qurʾān, and I had surpassed them by Sūrat al-Baqarah. The Prophet ﷺ said: “I have appointed you over your companions, though you are the youngest of them. When you lead people in prayer, lead them according to the weakest of them, for behind you are the old, the young, the weak, and the one with a need. When you are a tax collector, do not take the shāfiʿ — that is, the pregnant one — nor the rubbā, nor the ram of the flock. And the man’s prized possession is more entitled to it than you. Do not touch the Qurʾān unless you are pure. Know that ʿumrah is the lesser ḥajj, that an ʿumrah is better than this world and what is in it, and that a ḥajj is better than an ʿumrah.”"],[8233,"The last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “When you lead people in prayer, make the prayer light for them.”"],[8234,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿUthmān, lead your people. Whoever leads people should lighten, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the one with a need.”"],[8235,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik from Yazīd b. Khuṣayfah that ʿAmr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb al-Sulamī informed him that Nāfiʿ b. Jubayr b. Muṭʿim informed him from ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ that he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUthmān said: I had a pain that was about to destroy me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wipe it with your right hand seven times and say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find.” He said: I did that, and Allah removed what was in me. I continued to enjoin it upon my family and others."],[8236,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a pain. He said: “Place your right hand on it, then say: In the name of Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find — seven times.” I did that, and Allah sufficed me, may He be exalted."],[8237,"He complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ of a pain. He said: 'Whoever of you feels a pain, let him place his right hand upon it and mention the name of God three times, and let him say: \"I seek refuge in the might of God and His power from the evil of what I find and fear\" seven times.'"],[8238,"He informed him that ʿUthman b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while a pain had seized him and nearly disabled him. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Place your right hand on the place that hurts, wipe over it seven times, and say in each wiping: \"I seek refuge in the might of God and His power from the evil of what I find.\"'"],[8239,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, and he mentioned snakes: 'Whoever fears their vengeance is not of me.'"],[8240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A man for whom three of his own loins have preceded him in Islam has indeed entered a well-fortified shield against the Fire.'"],[8241,"I heard ʿUthman b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ say: I complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about forgetting the Qurʾān. He struck my chest with his hand and said: 'O Satan, come out of the chest of ʿUthman.' ʿUthman said: 'After that I never forgot anything of it that I wished to remember.'"],[8242,"From ʿUthman b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ al-Thaqafī, whom the Prophet ﷺ appointed over al-Ṭāʾif, he said: 'The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon me was: \"Make the prayer light for the people.\"'"],[8243,"The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ instructed me was: 'You will lead a people in prayer, and behind you are the old, the weak, and the needy, so keep the prayer brief.'"],[8244,"The last words the Messenger of God ﷺ spoke to me when he appointed me over al-Ṭāʾif were: 'Make the prayer light for the people,' until he specified: 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and 'Recite in the name of your Lord who created' and similar surahs of the Qurʾān."],[8245,"I arrived in the delegation of Thaqif when they went as a delegation to the Messenger of God ﷺ. We put on our fine garments at the door of the Prophet ﷺ, and they said, 'Who will hold our riding camels for us?' Everyone wanted to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ and disliked staying back from him. Uthman said, 'I was the youngest of the group, so I said, \"If you wish, I will hold them for you on condition that you have God's covenant that you will hold mine for me when you come out.\" They said, \"That is yours.\" So they entered upon him, then came out and said, \"Come with us.\" I said, \"Where?\" They said, \"To your family.\" I said, \"I journeyed from my family until, when I set down at the door of the Prophet ﷺ, I should turn back and not enter upon him, after you gave me the covenant that you know?\" They said, \"Then hurry, for we have spared you the asking; we did not leave anything without asking him about it.\" So I entered and said, \"O Messenger of God, ask God to give me understanding in religion and to teach me.\" He said, \"What did you say?\" I repeated the words, and he said, \"You have asked me something no one of your companions has asked me. Go, for you are their commander as well as over those of your people you come to, and lead the people in prayer considering their weakest.\" Then I left, and I came to him again another time and said, \"O Messenger of God, I have been in pain since I left you.\" He said, \"Place your right hand on the place that hurts and say seven times: I seek refuge in the might and power of God from the evil of what I feel.\" I did that, and God, may He be glorified and exalted, healed me."],[8246,"The last instruction the Messenger of God ﷺ gave me when he sent me as commander over al-Taif was: \"Accommodate the people according to their weakest, for among them are the sick, the old, the young, and those with needs.\""],[8247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Lead your people in prayer and accommodate them according to their weakest, for among them are the old, the weak, and those with needs.\""],[8248,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Fasting is a shield from the Fire, like the shield of one of you in battle.\""],[8249,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Fasting is a shield from the Fire, like the shield of one of you in battle.\""],[8250,"'Uthman bin Abi Al-As called for milk to be given to him (Mutarrif) to drink. Mutarrif said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Fasting is a shield like the shield of any one of you in battle.\"' Abu Hurairah said: \"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Fasting is a shield.\"' (Sahih (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2230)"],[8251,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"A good fast is fasting three days of every month.\""],[8252,"O Messenger of God, make me the imam of my people. He said, \"You are their imam, and follow the example of their weakest, and appoint a muadhdhin who does not take wages for his adhan.\""],[8253,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, Satan comes between me and my prayer and recitation.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"That is a devil called Khinzab. When you sense him, seek refuge with God from Satan and spit to your left.\""],[8254,"He complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about whispering during prayer. He said, \"That is a devil called Khinzab. When one of you feels something of him, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge with God from him.\""],[8255,"On the authority of Uthman b. Abi al-As and a woman of Quraysh, that they both heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O God, forgive me my sins, my error, and my deliberate acts.\""],[8256,"On the authority of Uthman b. Abi al-As and a woman of Quraysh, that they both heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O God, forgive me my sins, my error, and my deliberate acts.\""],[8257,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed Allah draws near to His creation and forgives the one who seeks forgiveness, except for a fornicatress with her private parts or a tax collector.”"],[8258,"When the delegation of Thaqif came to the Prophet ﷺ, he lodged them in the mosque so that their hearts might be softened. They stipulated to the Prophet ﷺ that they would not be gathered (for military service), nor subjected to tithe, nor circumcised, nor that anyone other than themselves be appointed over them. The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no good in a religion that has no bowing (prayer).”"],[8259,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ descends to the lowest heaven every night and says: ‘Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?’”"],[8260,"O Abu Harun, what has seated you here? He said: “This person appointed me over al-Ubulla.” He said: “Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: ‘Indeed the Prophet of Allah Dawud ﷺ used to say to his family at an hour of the night: O family of Dawud, arise and pray, for this is an hour in which supplication is answered except for a sorcerer or a tax collector.’” Then he boarded a ship in his place, then returned to Ziyad and asked to be excused."],[8261,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed in the night there is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened and He says: ‘Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?’”"],[8262,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed in the night there is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened and He says: ‘Is there any asker that I may give him? Is there any supplicant that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness that I may forgive him?’”"],[8263,"Among what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was that I not take any wages for the call to prayer."],[8264,"The last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “Pray with your companions the prayer of the weakest among them, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and the one with a need.”"],[8265,"The last thing the Prophet ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “Pray with your companions the prayer of the weakest among them, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and the one with a need. And appoint a mu’adhdhin who does not take wages for the call to prayer.”"],[8266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me when he sent me to Thaqif: “Be moderate in prayer, O Uthman, and measure the people by the weakest among them, for among them are the weak, the one with a need, the pregnant, and the nursing. Indeed I hear the cry of a child and I shorten (the prayer).”"],[8267,"Indeed the last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “When you pray with your companions, pray with them the prayer of the weakest among them, for among them are the weak and the sick.”"],[8268,"Indeed we would not attend circumcision during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor were we invited to it."],[8269,"“This is something we did not see in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So he refused to eat."],[8270,"“A period of forty days was set for the postpartum woman.”"],[8271,"A period of forty days was set for the postpartum woman."],[8272,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: Allah, mighty is His mention, says: “Whoever does a good deed shall have ten times its like, except fasting, for it is Mine and I shall reward for it.”"],[8273,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “Fasting is a shield with which the servant shields himself from the Fire.”"],[8274,"That he gave him wealth to trade with, the profit to be shared between them. He gave him twenty thousand dirhams, and with it he bought wine. Then he brought it to al-Ubulla, and ʿUthman went out to him and did not leave a single jar or anything else but smashed it. ʿUthman said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “cursed wine, its drinker, its buyer, its seller, its presser, and its carrier.”"],[8275,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, the torment of the grave, the trial of life, and the trial of death.”"],[8276,"That he used to prefer fasting while traveling, saying: “It was a concession.”"],[8277,"“Breaking the fast while traveling is a concession.”"],[8278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUthmān b. Ṭalḥah on the day of conquest: “Bring me the key of the Kaʿbah.” He was slow in bringing it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood waiting for him until sweat like pearls dripped from him, and he said: “What is delaying him?” A man hastened to him, while the woman who had the key—and it was thought that he said Umm ʿUthmān—said: “If he takes it from you, he will never give it back to you.” ʿUthmān kept after her until she gave him the key, and he went with it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He opened the door, then entered the House, then came out with the people with him and sat by the drinking place. ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, if we have been given prophethood, and we have been given the siqāyah, and we have been given the ḥijābah, no people have a greater share than us.” He said: It was as if the Prophet ﷺ disliked his statement. Then he called ʿUthmān b. Ṭalḥah and handed the key to him and said: “Keep it hidden.” ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: I narrated this to Ibn ʿUyaynah, and he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me—I think from Ibn Abī Mulaykah—that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī that day when he spoke to him about the key: “I have only given you what you bear as a burden, and I have not given you what you will be burdened by.” He means: I gave you the siqāyah because you incur expense in it, and I did not give you the House—that is, they take from its gift. This is the statement of ʿAbd al-Razzāq."],[8279,"I asked ʿUthmān: Why did the Prophet ﷺ send for you after he came out of the Kaʿbah? He said: He said to me: “I saw the two horns of the ram and forgot to command you to cover them, for nothing should be in the House that distracts a person praying.”"],[8280,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying behind the middle pillar of the House, two rakʿahs. And in the House—or he said the Kaʿbah—there were three pillars."],[8281,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār: ʿUthmān b. ʿAmr b. Rifāʿah b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād."],[8282,"Mūsā b. ʿAwn b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd dictated to me the lineage of ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd: ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. Kāhil b. Ḥabīb b. Tāmir b. Makhzūm b. Ṣāhilah b. Kāhil b. al-Ḥārith b. Tamīm b. Saʿd b. Hudhayl b. Mudrikah b. Ilyās b. Muḍar b. Nizār."],[8283,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. al-Ḥārith b. Shamkh b. Makhzūm b. Ṣāhilah b. al-Ḥārith b. Tamīm b. Hudhayl b. Mudrikah b. Ilyās b. Muḍar b. Nizār b. Maʿd b. ʿAdnān, an ally of Banū Zuhrah, witnessed Badr."],[8284,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. al-Ḥārith b. Shamkh b. Makhzūm b. Kāhil b. al-Ḥārith b. Saʿd b. Hudhayl, from the allies of Banū Zuhrah."],[8285,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd died; he was nicknamed Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and he was some sixty-odd years old, in the year thirty-two in Madinah. He bequeathed to al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām, who prayed over him, and he was buried in al-Baqīʿ."],[8286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ nicknamed him Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, though no child was born to him."],[8287,"I saw myself as the sixth of six when there was no Muslim on the face of the earth other than us."],[8288,"Ibn Mas'ud used to wash his head, then leave his hair behind his ears."],[8289,"\"I saw Abdullah Ibn Masood throwing stones.\""],[8290,"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ had two braids and bore the mark of the people of the Jahiliyyah, and he had thin shins."],[8291,"We used to go to Abdullah b. 'Amr and talk to him, Ibn Numair said: One day we made a mention of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, whereupon he said: You have made mention of a person whom I love more than anything else. I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn Qur'an from four persons: Ibn Umm 'Abd (i. e. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud) he started from him-then Mu'adh b. Jabal and Ubayya b. Ka'b, then Salim the ally of Abu Hudhaifa. (Using translation from Muslim 2464a)"],[8292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek the Qur'an from four: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal, 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Khudhayfah.\""],[8293,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Take the Qur'an from four: from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud\"—and he began with him—\"and from Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah.\""],[8294,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by with Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and they passed by 'Abdullah while he was praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Umm 'Abd, ask, and you will be given.\" 'Umar ؓ said: \"Abu Bakr and I raced, and we never raced to any good but that he beat me to it, so he gave him the good news.\" 'Abdullah said: \"I do not know except that among my supplications, which I can hardly leave off in my prayer, is: O Allah, I ask You for bliss that never ends, coolness of eyes that never perishes, and the companionship of Muhammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternity.\""],[8295,"The Prophet ﷺ went out with Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ. Abu Bakr ؓ had invited them, so they went out from his house to the mosque, the mosque of Madinah. 'Abdullah was standing in it, praying and reciting. Then he sat down, recited the testimony of faith, praised Allah as He deserves, with the best praise a man can offer, and sent blessings upon His Prophet ﷺ. Then he earnestly supplicated, while the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"Who is this, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"This is 'Abdullah, the son of Umm 'Abd. Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm 'Abd recited.\" Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ hastened to him, and Abu Bakr ؓ beat him. 'Umar mentioned that Abu Bakr beat him. 'Umar said: \"He was always first in good deeds.\""],[8296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and they had supper with him. When they finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out between Abu Bakr and 'Umar and came upon Ibn Mas'ud while he was standing praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\""],[8297,"'Abdullah was asked: \"What was it you supplicated for on the night when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to you: 'Ask, and you will be given'?\" He said: \"O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that never ends, and the companionship of Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest degree of eternity.\""],[8298,"The Prophet ﷺ came to him between Abu Bakr and 'Umar while 'Abdullah was praying. He began reciting Surat al-Nisa', and he recited it in full. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\" Then he sat down and supplicated, and the Prophet ﷺ kept saying: \"Ask, and you will be given. Ask, and you will be given.\" Among what he asked was: \"O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that never ends, and the companionship of Your Prophet ﷺ in the garden of eternity.\" 'Umar went to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud to give him the good news and found Abu Bakr ؓ already leaving, having beaten him to it. He said: \"If you did, you were indeed always first in good deeds.\""],[8299,"While he was reciting in the mosque, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ passed by as he was supplicating. The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar ؓ had gone out. When they drew parallel to him, the Prophet ﷺ heard his supplication but did not recognize him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr ؓ went back to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \"What was the supplication you were making?\" He said: \"I praised and glorified Allah, then I said: O Allah, there is no god but You. Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, Your messengers are true, the prophets are true, and Muhammad ﷺ is true.\""],[8300,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik b. 'Abdullah b. Abi Namir, from 'Awn b. 'Abdullah b. 'Utbah, from his father, who said: While Ibn Mas'ud was in the mosque supplicating, the Prophet ﷺ passed by with Abu Bakr. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew parallel to him, he heard his supplication, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recognize him. He said: \"Who is this? Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr went back to 'Abdullah and said: \"What was the supplication you were making?\" He said: \"I praised and glorified Allah, then I said: O Allah, there is no god but You. Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Your Book is true, the prophets are true, Muhammad ﷺ is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and Your messengers are true.\""],[8301,"A man came to 'Umar ؓ and said: \"I have come to you from a man who dictates the masahif from memory.\" He said: 'Umar was alarmed and said: \"Woe to you! Watch what you say,\" and he became angry. The man said: \"I have come to you only with the truth.\" 'Umar said: \"Who is he?\" He said: \"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud.\" 'Umar said: \"I know no one more entitled to that than him. I will tell you about 'Abdullah. We stayed up one night in a house with Abu Bakr ؓ for some need of the Prophet ﷺ. Then we went out, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking between me and Abu Bakr. When we reached the mosque, there was a man reciting. The Prophet ﷺ stood to listen to him. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is late,' but he nudged me with his hand, saying: 'Be quiet.' He recited, bowed, prostrated, sat down supplicating and seeking forgiveness. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Ask, and you will be given.' Then he said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.' So my companion and I knew that it was 'Abdullah. When morning came, I went to him to give him the good news, but he said: 'Abu Bakr beat you to it.' And I never raced him to any good but that he beat me to it.\""],[8302,"ʿWhoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.ʿ Umar bin al-Khattab narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said... a similar report, in which he said: crisp or fresh. (Using translation from Aḥmad 35)"],[8303,"O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind in Iraq a man dictating the codices from memory. ʿUmar ؓ became angry until his face reddened. ʿUmar said to him repeatedly, “Do you know what you are saying?” He said, “I only inform you of the truth.” ʿUmar ؓ said, “Who is he?” He said, “Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” He said, “He became calm until the anger left him, then he said: There is no one on the face of the earth more deserving of that than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed up one night in the house of Abu Bakr ؓ for some need until it became dark, then he returned walking between me and Abu Bakr until we reached the mosque, and there was a man from the Emigrants praying. He stood listening to his recitation. I and my companion did not know who he was. He said: When he had stood for a while, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Emigrants is praying; if you would return, for it has become dark.” He said: He poked me, and the Prophet ﷺ kept listening to his recitation. He said: He bowed and prostrated, then sat supplicating, and the Prophet ﷺ began saying, “Ask, you shall be given; ask, you shall be given.” Neither I nor my companion knew who he was until we heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm ʿAbd recites.” He said: “That is when I and my companion learned who he was.” He said: “I went early to ʿAbdullah to give him the good news, and he said: Abu Bakr has preceded you. By Allah, I never vied with Abu Bakr for any good except that he preceded me.”"],[8304,"Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ gave him the good news that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Masʿud.”"],[8305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while I was with him and Abu Bakr, near Ibn Masʿud while he was reciting. He stood listening to his recitation. Then ʿAbdullah bowed and prostrated, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran as it was revealed, let him recite from Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” He said: I went early to Ibn Masʿud to give him the good news of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. When I knocked on the door, he heard my voice and said, “What brings you?” I said, “I came to give you glad tidings of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.” He said, “Abu Bakr has preceded you.” I said, “If he did, he is indeed foremost in good deeds. We never raced to any good except that Abu Bakr preceded me to it.”"],[8306,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, and be guided by the guidance of ʿAmmar, and hold fast to the covenant of ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud.”"],[8307,"ʿAbdullah addressed us when the codices were being torn, and the mosque was full of the people of Badr. He said, “The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ know that I am the most knowledgeable among them concerning the Book of Allah.” Shaqiq said: Then I saw that he felt ashamed of what he said, so he said, “But I am not the best of them. If I knew a man more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would go to him.” Shaqiq said: “When ʿAbdullah finished his sermon, I sat in the circles to listen to what they said, and I heard no one disapproving of that.”"],[8308,"When Uthman commanded regarding the copies of the Quran as he was commanded, Abdullah stood up and praised Allah. Then he said, \"O people, surely Allah says, 'And whoever commits a sin only earns it against himself. And Allah is ever Knowing and Wise.' So commit transgression with the copies of the Quran upon the recitation of the one whom I command to recite it upon the recitation of Zaid bin Thabit. By He in whose hands is my soul, I have taken from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs. And Zaid bin Thabit has two things, he plays with the boys, and by He in whose hands is my soul, if I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, I would come to him.\""],[8309,"“By Allah, no surah of the Quran was revealed except that I know where it was revealed, and no verse of it was revealed except that I know concerning what it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would go to him.”"],[8310,"“By the One besides whom there is no god, no surah of the Quran was revealed except that I know where it was revealed, and no verse, and I know concerning whom it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would ride to him.”"],[8311,"“There is no verse in the Book of Allah except that I know where it was revealed and concerning whom it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would journey to him.”"],[8312,"\"And there is none worthy of worship except Him. There is no surah (chapter) in the Book of Allah except that I know where it was revealed and there is no verse except that I know what it was revealed about.\""],[8313,"It was asked of Abdullah, \"Read according to the recitation of Zaid.\" He said, \"Should I abandon my recitation for the recitation of Zaid? I have read seventy Surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was a young boy and he had two twisted hairs.\""],[8314,"“...that he should embezzle a codex, let him do so, for whoever embezzles something will come with what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8315,"“...that he should embezzle a codex, let him do so, for whoever embezzles something will come with what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8316,"\"I have read seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and Zaid ibn Thabit has two scrolls in the Book.\""],[8317,"Abdullah said, \"I have read from the Prophet ﷺ seventy surahs,\" and Zaid bin Thabit, with a small bird, plays with the children."],[8318,"On whose reading am I ordered to read? \"I have read seventy surahs to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" And indeed, Zaid bin Thabit is a companion of the wolves who plays with the boys."],[8319,"“Do I not see you praying when the Book of Allah has been ordered and then torn apart? So I prayed hastily, and I was not detained. I entered the house and was not detained. I climbed up and was not detained. Then I found al-Ashʿari, Hudhayfah, and Ibn Masʿud disputing, with Hudhayfah saying to Ibn Masʿud, ‘Hand over this codex to them.’ He said, ‘No, by Allah, I will not hand it over to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it more than seventy times, and then I should hand it over to them? By Allah, I will not hand it over to them.’”"],[8320,"He heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ood say, \"I have received from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy Surahs.\" I memorized them before Zaid ibn Thabit, who had a stutter, had mastered them and was playing with the boys."],[8321,"\"Wondrous it is for people to abandon my recitation and prefer the recitation of Zaid ibn Thabit, even though I have received seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Zaid ibn Thabit is a young man with a lisp.\""],[8322,"\"Abdullah ibn Mas'ood said, 'I have read seventy-two surahs from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ .' And indeed, Zaid ibn Thabit had two notebooks.\""],[8323,"I have taken seventy chapters from the Prophet ﷺ in which no one disputes with me."],[8324,"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs."],[8325,"\"I have read seventy-two surahs during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. And Zaid ibn Thabit had two helpers who used to play with the children.\""],[8326,"\"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs. And indeed, Zaid bin Thabit is a disbeliever in Allah as he did not believe in it.\""],[8327,"I have read seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I completed the recitation of the Quran with the best of people, Ali ibn Abi Talib."],[8328,"He said to him: O my brother, we have a gathering, so come to us. I went to him in his gathering and learned from him seventy surahs. ʿAbd Allah said to me, “I took them from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Jibril ﷺ brought them down from the Lord of the worlds, Exalted is He.”"],[8329,"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy Surahs."],[8330,"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “Your permission with me is that you may raise the veil and hear my secret conversation until I forbid you.” Al-Hasan said: al-siwad means secret talk."],[8331,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your permission with me is that you may uncover the curtain.”"],[8332,"“ʿAbd Allah ؓ was the keeper of the cushion, the siwak, and the sandals.”"],[8333,"I used to pick a siwak for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the arak tree. The wind would bend him over, and there was thinness in his legs, so the people laughed. The Prophet ﷺ said, “What are you laughing at from the thinness of his legs? By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Balance than Uhud.”"],[8334,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the legs of Ibn Masʿud on the Day of Resurrection will be stronger and greater than Uhud.”"],[8335,"While he was walking behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his companions or some of them nudged him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, ʿAbd Allah in the Scales on the Day of Resurrection is heavier than Uhud,” as if they were amazed at his lightness."],[8336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ came to me after he had fled from the polytheists, while I was tending sheep belonging to Ibn Abi Muʿayt at Jiyad. He said, “O boy, do you have any milk to give us?” I said, “I am entrusted and I am not going to give you milk.” He said, “Do you have a young she-goat that no male has mounted?” I said, “Yes.” I brought it to him, and he wiped the udder, and the udder filled with milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought him a hollowed rock, and he milked and drank and gave drink, and he gave Abu Bakr ؓ to drink and gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink,” and it shrank."],[8337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ came to me after he had fled from the polytheists, while I was tending sheep belonging to Ibn Abi Muʿayt at Jiyad. He said, “O boy, do you have any milk to give us?” I said, “I am entrusted and I am not going to give you milk.” He said, “Do you have a young she-goat that no male has mounted?” I said, “Yes.” I brought it to him, and he wiped the udder, and the udder filled with milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought him a hollowed rock, and he milked and drank and gave drink, and he gave Abu Bakr ؓ to drink and gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink,” and it shrank."],[8338,"I was among the sheep of ʿUqbah b. Abi Muʿayt when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said, “O boy, do you have any milk?” I said, “Yes, but I am entrusted.” He said, “Then bring me a ewe that no male has mounted.” I brought him a young she-goat or a yearling, and he began wiping the udder and supplicating until it let down milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought a rock, and he milked into it, then he handed it to Abu Bakr and he drank, then the Prophet ﷺ drank after him. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink by Allah's permission,” and it shrank and returned to what it had been."],[8339,"I was among the sheep of ʿUqbah b. Abi Muʿayt when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said, “O boy, do you have any milk?” I said, “Yes, but I am entrusted.” He said, “Then bring me a ewe that no male has mounted.” I brought him a young she-goat or a yearling, and he began wiping the udder and supplicating until it let down milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought a rock, and he milked into it, then he handed it to Abu Bakr and he drank, then the Prophet ﷺ drank after him. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink by Allah's permission,” and it shrank and returned to what it had been."],[8340,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was herding sheep for Uqbah. He wiped my head and said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, for you are a diligent teacher.\""],[8341,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I am pleased for my community with what Ibn Umm ʿAbd was pleased with for it.”"],[8342,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Recite.” So he began Surat al-Nisaʾ until when he reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” (Q 4:41)—the verse—his eyes shed tears, and he said, “It is enough for us.”"],[8343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Recite.” He said: I said, “O Messenger of God, should I recite to you when it was revealed to you?” He said, “Yes.” So I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ until I reached this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” He said, “Enough for you now.” I turned to him and his eyes were flowing with tears."],[8344,"He recited to the Prophet ﷺ until he came to this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ wept, and he said in the hadith, “Whoever would like to recite the Qurʾan as fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.”"],[8345,"The Prophet ﷺ asked me to recite Surat al-Nisaʾ while he was on the pulpit, so I recited it until when I reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” the eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ filled with tears, and he said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Qurʾan as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.”"],[8346,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Recite the Qurʾan to me.” Ibn Masʿud said, “O Messenger of God, should I recite the Qurʾan to you when it was revealed to you?” He said, “I would love to hear it from someone other than myself.” So he recited to him until he reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” and the eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ filled with tears, and he said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Qurʾan as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” This is how it was narrated by ʿAmr b. Marzuq and the companions of Shuʿbah, and Sulayman b. Harb connected it."],[8347,"Ibn Masʿud said: I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when I came to this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” his eyes overflowed."],[8348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered me to recite to him while he was on the pulpit. I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ to him until when I reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” the Messenger of God ﷺ pressed me, so I looked at him and his eyes were shedding tears, shedding tears."],[8349,"ʿAbd Allah struck Abu Jahl but did nothing. He said, “A little shepherd boy of yesterday?” He said, “That is him.” So he took his sword and struck him until he killed him."],[8350,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr and said, “I have killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, did you kill him?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” Joy overwhelmed him, and he said, “Show me him.” So I went with him until I stood with him at his head, and he said, “Praise be to God who has disgraced you. This is the Pharaoh of this community. Drag him to the well.” He said: I had struck him with my sword but it did not cut him, so I took his sword and struck him with it until I killed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me his sword as booty."],[8351,"I reached Abu Jahl while he was thrown down, wearing his helmet, with a good sword, and with me a bad sword. I began to poke his head with my sword, remembering how he used to poke my head in Makkah, until his hand weakened. I took his sword, and he raised his head and said, “On whose side was the defeat—for us or against us? Are you not our little shepherd boy in Makkah?” I killed him. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” He made me swear three times, then he stood and went with me to them and supplicated against them."],[8352,"When God defeated the polytheists on the day of Badr, I passed by and saw Abu Jahl thrown down with his leg struck. I said, “O enemy of God, O Abu Jahl, God has disgraced the other.” He said, and I did not fear him at that time, “Get away from a man whom his own people have killed.” So I struck him with a useless sword of mine, but it availed me nothing until his sword fell from his hand. I took it and struck him until he became cold. Then I came running to the Messenger of God ﷺ, hurrying faster than any creature of God, until I reached him and said, “O Messenger of God, God has killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” He said, “How?” So I told him how the story went and how I found him. He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” He said “Allahu Akbar,” then said, “Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise and aided His servant.” Then he set out until he came to him and said, “This is the Pharaoh of this community.”"],[8353,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, God Almighty has killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and exalted His religion.”"],[8354,"I brought the head of Abu Jahl to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “This is the head of Abu Jahl.” He said, “By God, besides whom there is no god?”—and this was how he used to swear—so I said, “By God, besides whom there is no god, this is indeed the head of Abu Jahl.” He then said, “This is the Pharaoh of this nation.”"],[8355,"I came upon Abu Jahl at the Battle of Badr lying slain, and I said, “O enemy of God, God has disgraced you.” He said, “And how has God disgraced me by a man whom you killed while I had my sword with me?” I began striking him with my sword but it would not cut him, while he had a good sword of his own. Then I struck his hand, and the sword fell from his grip, so I took it. Then I uncovered the helmet from his head and struck his neck. After that I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him, and he said, “By God, besides whom there is no god?” I said, “By God, besides whom there is no god.” He said, “Go and verify.” So I went, hastening like a bird, then returned, hastening like a bird, laughing, and told him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Then go and show me.” So I went with him and showed him. When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood over him, he said, “This is the Pharaoh of this nation.” Thus it was narrated by Zayd b. Abi Unaysa from Abu Ishaq from ʿAmr b. Maymun, and Abu Wakiʿ concurred with him."],[8356,"I arrived at Abu Jahl on the day of Badr while he was dying, so I struck him with a sword that I had with me. His sword then slipped from his hand, so I took it and killed him. Then I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a hot day, as if I were carrying the Earth, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that Allah killed Abu Jahl?\" He said, \"Allah?\" I said, \"Yes, Allah, until he swore to me three times.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Go and show me.\" So I went to him, and when he looked at him, he said, \"This man was the Pharaoh of this nation.\""],[8357,"At the Battle of Badr I was pushed toward Abu Jahl, and I had been seated. I took his sword and struck his head with it. He said, “Our little shepherd in Makkah.” I struck him with his sword until he became cold. Then I came to the Prophet and said, “O Messenger of God, I have killed Abu Jahl.” ʿAqil, who was a captive with the Prophet ﷺ, said, “You lie; you did not kill him.” I said, “Rather you are the liar and the sinner, O enemy of God. By God, I have killed him.” He said, “What is his distinguishing mark?” I said, “On his thigh there is a ring like the ring of a hobbled camel.” He said, “You have spoken the truth.”"],[8358,"We were sitting with ʿUmar when ʿAbdullah came, and those seated nearly equaled him in height because of his shortness. ʿUmar laughed when he saw him. He began speaking with ʿUmar and joking with him while standing before him, then he turned away. ʿUmar followed him with his gaze until he disappeared, then said, “A little vessel filled with understanding.”"],[8359,"ʿUmar wrote to the people of Kufa: “I have sent ʿAmmar as commander and ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud as teacher and minister. They are among the noble ones of the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, from the people of Badr and Uhud. Follow them and listen to their words. I have preferred you over myself by sending ʿAbdullah to you.”"],[8360,"“May God have mercy on Ibn Masʿud. He was indeed a jurist, but I will give him the share of a maternal brother on account of his mother, then divide the property between them.”"],[8361,"Hudhayfa said: “The person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ in manner, bearing, moderation, and address from the time he leaves his house until he returns—though I do not know what he does with his family—is ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud. By God, the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad know that ʿAbdullah is among the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8362,"“The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Umm ʿAbd is the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8363,"“The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Masʿud is among the closest of them to God in nearness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8364,"Hudhayfa said: “The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Umm ʿAbd is among the closest of them to God in nearness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8365,"Hudhayfa said: “The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Umm ʿAbd is among the closest of them to God in nearness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8366,"“I have not seen a man more resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ in bearing, manner, and conduct from the time he leaves his house until he returns to it than this one”—meaning ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud. “And the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that he is among the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8367,"I was sitting with Hudhayfah when Ibn Mas'ud and Abu Musa passed by. Hudhayfah did not want to ignore them, so he said, \"The person who most resembles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he leaves his house until he returns to his family is Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and Allah knows best what he does.\""],[8368,"Hudhayfah said: \"Indeed, the closest of people in guidance, manner, judgment, and preaching to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the time he leaves his house until he returns – and I do not know what he does with his family – is ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud. By Allah, the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ surely know that Ibn Masʿud is among the closest of them in means (wasilah).\""],[8369,"\"Tell us of a man close in conduct, guidance, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"I do not know of anyone closer in guidance, conduct, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the wall of his house conceals him than Ibn Umm ʿAbd.\""],[8370,"\"Tell us of a man close in conduct, guidance, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"I do not know of anyone closer in guidance, conduct, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the wall of his house conceals him than Ibn Umm ʿAbd.\""],[8371,"We were with Hudhayfah opposite the house of ʿAbd Allah, and he said: \"I do not know of anyone more similar in manner and conduct to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the occupant of this house, from the time he leaves until he enters his home. When he is concealed, then Allah knows best. The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ certainly knew that he is among the closest of them in means (wasilah) to Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8372,"\"Shall I not tell you of the closest of people in resemblance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in guidance, manner, and conduct?\" We said: \"Yes, indeed.\" He said: \"ʿAbd Allah.\""],[8373,"\"Whoever wishes to look at the most similar of people in guidance, conduct, and bearing to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he leaves his home until he returns, let him look at ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8374,"\"And indeed, the one of you two most similar in guidance and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8375,"I was sitting with Hudhayfah and Abu Musa al-Ashʿari, and one of them said to his companion: \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say such-and-such a hadith?\" He said: \"No.\" The other said to him: \"Then did you hear it?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then the occupant of this house claims that he heard it.\" Abu Musa said: \"If he did, he used to enter when we were screened, and witness when we were absent.\" Sulayman al-Aʿmash said: \"He means ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8376,"Ibrahim said: ʿAbd Allah came to Abu Musa and conversed with him. When the prayer became due and the iqamah was called, Abu Musa stepped back. ʿAbd Allah said to him: \"You indeed know that it is part of the Sunnah for the owner of the house to lead.\" Abu Musa refused until a freedman of one of them went forward."],[8377,"We were in the house of Abu Musa with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they were looking into a mushaf. ʿAbd Allah stood up, and Abu Masʿud said: \"I do not know of anyone left after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more knowledgeable of what Allah, Exalted is He, revealed than this standing one.\" Abu Musa said: \"Since you have said that, he used to witness when we were absent and be granted permission when we were screened.\""],[8378,"\"I do not see any man more knowledgeable of what was revealed upon Muhammad ﷺ than ʿAbd Allah.\" Abu Musa said: \"If that is said, then indeed he used to hear when no one was heard, and enter when no one was allowed to enter.\""],[8379,"Abu Masʿud said: \"No, by Allah, I do not know of anyone left by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah than this standing one.\""],[8380,"That he heard Abu Musa say: \"My brother and I arrived from Yemen, and we stayed for some time, thinking that ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud was from the household of the Prophet ﷺ, because of his frequent entering upon the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[8381,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and I considered Ibn Masʿud to be from the household.\""],[8382,"\"My wife's milk was retained in her breast, so I began to suck it and then spit it out. Some of it then entered my stomach.\" He said: \"She has become forbidden to you.\" So he went to ʿAbdullah. Abu ʿAtiyyah said: So he stood, and we stood with him. He said: \"Suckle from the breast of this one, for suckling is only what grows the flesh and the blood.\" Then Abu Musa said: \"Do not ask me about anything as long as this learned man is among you.\""],[8383,"That his wife's breast became swollen, so he began to suck it and spit it out, and some of it entered his stomach. He said: \"I do not think she is suitable for him.\" So he went to Ibn Masʿud and asked him about that. He said: \"She has not become forbidden to you. Only that suckling which grows the flesh and strengthens the bone becomes prohibited, and there is no suckling after weaning.\" So it was said to Abu Musa, and he said: \"Do not ask us about anything as long as this learned man remains among us, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[8384,"From ʿAbdullah, regarding {Fear Allah as He should be feared}: He said: \"That He is obeyed and not disobeyed, remembered and not forgotten, thanked and not denied.\""],[8385,"In his saying \"Fear Allah as He should be feared,\" he said, \"That He is obeyed and not disobeyed, and that He is thanked and not ungrateful, and that He is remembered and not forgotten.\""],[8386,"From Murrah, regarding His saying {and gave wealth despite love for it}: He said: Ibn Masʿud said: \"That you give it while you are healthy and miserly, hopeful of life and fearful of poverty.\""],[8387,"From ʿAbdullah: \"The major sins are those between the beginning of Surat al-Nisaʾ and the beginning of its thirtieth verse.\""],[8388,"ʿAbdullah said: \"How excellent are the two detested things: death and poverty. By Allah, indeed wealth and poverty—I do not care with which of them I am tested. If it is wealth, indeed in it there is compassion; and if it is poverty, indeed in it there is patience.\""],[8389,"ʿAbdullah told us one day: \"Indeed, sickness does not have any reward written for the one who suffers it.\" That grieved us and weighed heavily upon us. Then he said: \"But Allah ﷻ expiates sins through it.\""],[8390,"ʿAbdullah said: \"Shall I warn you against excess in speech? It is enough for one of you to say only what achieves his need.\""],[8391,"\"That I remember Allah from morning until evening is more beloved to me than that I raid upon thoroughbred horses from morning until evening.\""],[8392,"ʿAbdullah said: \"Indeed I know households that the Dajjal will frighten.\" They said: \"Who, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman?\" He said: \"The houses of the people of Kufah.\""],[8393,"“Do not mention him excessively, for when the matter is decreed in heaven, it is quicker to descend to the earth that it appear on people's tongues.” He said: “Indeed, how will you be when the people are secure and you are fearful? And how will you be when the people are in shade and you are in the sun?”"],[8394,"ʿAbdullāh said: “If he were to wake up in Bābil, some of them would wake up complaining to him of sore feet from the speed.”"],[8395,"“Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; whoever seeks to be heard of, Allah will make him heard of; whoever acts arrogantly out of pride, Allah will abase him; and whoever humbles himself out of humility, Allah will raise him. People are either given ample provision in this world but constrained in the Hereafter, constrained in this world but given ample provision in the Hereafter, constrained in both this world and the Hereafter, or given ample provision in both this world and the Hereafter. And there is one who finds rest and one from whom rest is found.” We said: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what is the one who finds rest and the one from whom rest is found?” He said: “As for the one who finds rest, he is the believer; when he dies, he finds rest. As for the one from whom rest is found, he is the one who wrongs people and backbites them.”"],[8396,"I examined the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ and found that their knowledge ended with six: ʿUmar, ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, Abū al-Dardāʾ, and Zayd b. Thābit. Then I examined the six and found that their knowledge ended with ʿAlī and ʿAbdullāh."],[8397,"Indeed, knowledge and faith are in their place; whoever seeks them will find them. He said that three times. And seek knowledge from four: ʿUwaymir Abū al-Dardāʾ, Salmān al-Fārisī, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, and ʿAbdullāh b. Salām."],[8398,"“None remained with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uḥud except four, one of them being ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd.”"],[8399,"I heard ʿAlī say: The Prophet ﷺ ordered Ibn Masʿūd to climb a tree and bring him something from it. His Companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What makes you laugh? The leg of ʿAbdullāh in the Scale is heavier than Uḥud.”"],[8400,"I climbed a small arāk tree to pick some of its fruit, and my companions began to marvel at my lightness. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What do you marvel at? By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is heavier in the Scale on the Day of Resurrection than Uḥud.”"],[8401,"It is only two things: guidance and speech. The best speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad ﷺ. Beware of newly invented matters and innovations, for the worst of affairs are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is misguidance. Do not let the time span grow long for you, lest your hearts harden. Hope: what is coming is near. Indeed, what is far is what is not coming. Indeed, the wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who is admonished by others. The worst of mounts are the mounts of falsehood. Indeed, lying is not proper in seriousness or jest. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. It will be said of the truthful one: he spoke truth and was righteous; and it will be said of the liar: he lied and acted wickedly."],[8402,"It is only two things: guidance and speech. The best speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad ﷺ. Beware of newly invented matters and innovations, for the worst of affairs are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is misguidance. Do not let the time span grow long for you, lest your hearts harden. Hope: what is coming is near. Indeed, what is far is what is not coming. Indeed, the wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who is admonished by others. The worst of mounts are the mounts of falsehood. Indeed, lying is not proper in seriousness or jest. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. It will be said of the truthful one: he spoke truth and was righteous; and it will be said of the liar: he lied and acted wickedly."],[8403,"It is only two things: guidance and speech. The most truthful speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad ﷺ. The worst of affairs are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance, and every misguidance is in the Fire."],[8404,"He used to come every Thursday and stand, not sitting, and say: Do not put the people to trial, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need. He would say: They are two: the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad, the most truthful speech is the Book of Allah, and the worst of affairs are their newly invented ones. Every newly invented matter is misguidance. The wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who is admonished by others. Indeed, let not the time span grow long for you, nor let hope divert you, for all that is coming is near, and only what is not coming is far. Among the worst of people is the one who prolongs the day out of fear of the night. Killing a believer is disbelief and insulting him is wickedness. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. Indeed, the worst of mounts is falsehood. Lying is not proper in seriousness or jest, nor for a man to promise his child something and not fulfill it. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. It will be said of the truthful one: he spoke truth and was righteous; and it will be said of the liar: he lied and acted wickedly."],[8405,"That he would come every Thursday, standing upright, not sitting, and say: 'Do not cause tribulation for the people, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one in need.' Then he would say: 'There are two things, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the truest speech is the Book of God, and the worst of matters are their innovations, and every innovation is misguidance. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others. Beware, let not the long span of time delude you, nor let false hopes divert you, for all that is coming is near; indeed far is only what is not coming. Among the worst of people is he who lengthens the day in fear of the night. Indeed, killing a believer is disbelief, and insulting him is wickedness. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. Indeed, the worst of vessels is lying, and lying is not appropriate in seriousness or jest, nor may a man promise his child something and then not fulfill it. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire, and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. The truthful one is said of him: He was truthful and righteous, and the liar is said of him: He lied and was wicked.'"],[8406,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud said: 'All that is coming is near. Indeed, far is only what is not coming. God does not hasten for anyone's haste, nor is He light about people's affairs. What God wills, not what people will. God wills a matter and people will a matter. What God wills happens, even if people dislike it. There is no bringer near of what God has distanced, and no distancer of what God has brought near. Nothing occurs except by God's permission. The truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the worst of matters are their innovations, and every innovation is a heresy, and every heresy is misguidance.'"],[8407,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud said: 'All that is coming is near. Indeed, far is only what is not coming. God does not hasten for anyone's haste, nor is He light about people's affairs. What God wills, not what people will. God wills a matter and people will a matter. What God wills happens, even if people dislike it. There is no bringer near of what God has distanced, and no distancer of what God has brought near. Nothing occurs except by God's permission. The truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the worst of matters are their innovations, and every innovation is a heresy, and every heresy is misguidance.'"],[8408,"'Indeed, the truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the worst of matters are their innovations. Indeed, what you are promised is surely coming, and you are not able to escape. Indeed far is only what is not coming. Beware, hold fast to truthfulness, for it leads to Paradise. A man keeps being truthful until he is recorded with God as a true friend, and righteousness becomes firm in his heart, and wickedness does not have in his heart even the space of a needle to settle therein. Beware, and beware of lying, for it leads to the Fire. A man keeps lying until he is recorded with God as a liar, and wickedness settles in his heart until there is not in his heart the space of a needle for it to settle therein.'"],[8409,"'Lying is not appropriate in jest or seriousness, nor may one of you promise his child something and then not fulfill it for him.'"],[8410,"Abd Allah said: 'Lying is not appropriate in seriousness or jest.'"],[8411,"She was called Buraydah. We said: 'O Buraydah, tell Abu Wa'il to narrate to us.' She said: 'O Abu Wa'il, narrate to the people what you heard from Abd Allah.' He said: 'I heard Abd Allah say: O people, you will be gathered on a single plain where the caller will make you hear and your sight will penetrate you. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb' — he said, and I think he added — 'and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8412,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8413,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8414,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who was fortunate in his mother's womb.'"],[8415,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud used to address us every Thursday, saying: 'Indeed, the truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and every innovation is a heresy, and every heresy is misguidance, and the worst of matters are their innovations. Indeed, you will be gathered on a single plain where your sight will penetrate you and the caller will make you hear. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8416,"'O people, hold fast to truthfulness, for it brings near to righteousness, and righteousness brings near to Paradise. Beware of lying, for it brings near to wickedness, and wickedness brings near to the Fire. It is said of the truthful one: He was truthful and righteous, and of the liar: He lied and was wicked. Indeed, the angel has an inclination and the devil has an inclination. The angel's inclination is an admonition to good, and the devil's inclination is an admonition to evil. Whoever finds the angel's inclination, let him praise God, and whoever finds the devil's inclination, let him seek refuge from that, for God (may He be exalted) says: {Satan promises you poverty and commands you} until the end of the verse. He said: Indeed, God (may He be exalted) laughs at two men: a man who rises from his bed, his blanket, and his cover in a cold night, performs ablution, then stands for prayer. God says to His angels: What made My servant do what he did? They say: Our Lord, hope for what is with You and fear of what is with You. He says: I have given him what he hoped for and secured him from what he feared. And a man who was in a group, knew what he would gain from fleeing and knew what he would have with God, so he fought until he was killed. He says to the angels: What made My servant do what he did? They say: Our Lord, hope for what is with You and fear of what is with You. He says: I call you to witness that I have given him what he hoped for and secured him from what he feared — or a similar phrase.'"],[8417,"Abd Allah b. Masʿud said: “None of you is but a guest and a loaned item. The guest is departing, and the loan is to be returned to its owner.”"],[8418,"Abd Allah said: “Knowledge is not from abundant hadith; rather, knowledge is from fear (of Allah).”"],[8419,"That I be ashes."],[8420,"Ibn Masʿud instructed his son Abu ʿUbaydah with three statements: “O my son, I instruct you to fear Allah, let your house suffice you, weep over your sin, and hold back your tongue.”"],[8421,"A man said to Abd Allah: “Instruct me with comprehensive, beneficial words.” Abd Allah said to him: “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him. Remain with the Quran wherever it goes. Whoever brings you truth, accept it from him even if he is far away, and whoever brings you falsehood, reject it even if he is a beloved close one.”"],[8422,"That I see a man idle, neither engaged in work for this world nor the Hereafter.”"],[8423,"That I see a man idle, neither engaged in work for this world nor the Hereafter.”"],[8424,"“Whoever emigrates seeking something shall have what he sought.” He said, “A man emigrated to marry a woman called Umm Qays, and he was known as the emigrant of Umm Qays.”"],[8425,"\"A man should not say, 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence, and I repent to Him three times, except that his sins will be forgiven, even if he flees from crawling.'\""],[8426,"Indeed, the mountain calls out to the mountain by its name: “O so-and-so, did anyone pass by you today who remembered Allah?” When it says yes, it rejoices. ʿAwn said: “They listen to evil and do not listen to good, yet they are better at hearing good.” And he recited: {And they say, “The Most Merciful has taken a son.” You have done an atrocious thing. The heavens almost rupture therefrom, and the earth splits open, and the mountains collapse in devastation that they ascribe to the Most Merciful a son. And it is not appropriate for the Most Merciful that He should take a son.}"],[8427,"Abd Allah said: “Whoever his prayer does not enjoin him to what is right and forbid him from what is wrong, he only increases in distance from Allah.”"],[8428,"Abd Allah said: “Patience is half of faith, and certainty is faith.”"],[8429,"While I was with Abd Allah, I saw a crowd; it stirred and then settled. He said: “Beware of the clamor of the market, for it is the clamor of Satan.”"],[8430,"Abd Allah said: “Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires. Whoever peers through the veil will fall upon what lies behind it.”"],[8431,"ʿAbd Allah (said): “The people with the most sins on the Day of Resurrection will be those who most indulge in falsehood.”"],[8432,"“Yaʿqub delayed his sons until the pre-dawn time.”"],[8433,"And knowledge."],[8434,"Ibn Masʿud (said): “Beware of ‘Do you think?’ and ‘Do you think?’, for those before you were destroyed only by ‘Do you think?’ and ‘Do you think?’. Do not compare anything with anything, lest a foot slip after it was firm. When one of you is asked about what he does not know, let him say, ‘I do not know,’ for that is a third of knowledge.”"],[8435,"ʿAbd Allah (said): “There is no year but that the one after it is worse than it, and no year is better than another year, and no community is better than another community. Rather, it is the passing away of your best ones and your scholars, and people will come who judge matters by their own opinions, and Islam will be demolished and broken.”"],[8436,"“The righteous depart one after another, and there remain people of doubt who do not recognize good and do not reject evil.”"],[8437,"When he sat down, he used to say: “You are in the passage of the night, with diminished lifespans and recorded deeds. Death comes suddenly. Whoever sows good is likely to reap desire, and whoever sows evil is likely to reap regret. Every sower is such that a slow one does not miss his share, and a greedy one does not attain what was not decreed for him. Whoever is given good, it is Allah who gave it; whoever is protected from evil, it is Allah who protected him. The God-fearing are masters, the jurists are leaders, and their company is an increase.”"],[8438,"\"Do not fight against this night, for you will not be able to endure it. And if one of you becomes sleepy, let him go to his bed, for it is surrendered to him.\""],[8439,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty.”"],[8440,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty.”"],[8441,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty—the beauty of people in the face, whiteness, and other than that. When a woman came to him, he would cover his face for fear that she would be tempted.”"],[8442,"That he should report everything he hears.”"],[8443,"“When you invite a man, then you have given him permission.”"],[8444,"The most painful thing in a believer is obscenity."],[8445,"The most base of a believer's character traits is obscenity."],[8446,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"A man may go out with his religion and return with nothing of it. He comes to a man who possesses no benefit or harm for him or for himself, and swears to him by Allah, 'You have lied and committed sin,' and then he returns without having obtained anything of his need, and he has made Allah angry with him.\""],[8447,"He said: \"He is ruined who does not enjoin good and forbid evil.\" He said: \"Rather, he is ruined whose heart does not know the good and whose heart does not reject the evil.\""],[8448,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"Whoever desires the Hereafter harms his worldly life, and whoever desires the worldly life harms his Hereafter.\" And he commanded them to harm the perishable for the sake of the enduring. And he said: \"You are in a time in which its scholars are many and its orators are few, and its givers are many and its beggars are few. So lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon. And indeed some eloquence is magic. And after you will come a time in which its orators are many, its scholars are few, its beggars are many, and its givers are few.\""],[8449,"\"You are in a time in which the prayer is long and the sermon is short, and its scholars are many and its orators are few. And a time will come upon you in which the prayer is short and the sermon is long, its orators are many and its scholars are few. They will delay the ʿIsha prayer until the rising of the dead (i.e., very late). Whoever of you reaches that should pray the prayer at its proper time and make it with them as a supererogatory prayer. You are in a time in which a man is envied for the abundance of his wealth and the abundance of his dependents. And a time will come upon you in which a man is envied for the fewness of his dependents and the lightness of his burden. I do not leave behind in my family anyone dearer to me than their death, nor any household among the beetles. And indeed I love them as they love your families.\""],[8450,"ʿAbd Allah saw some children of his offspring playing in front of him, and he said: \"These are less important to me than their number of beetles.\""],[8451,"\"False testimony is equal to associating partners with Allah.\" And he recited: {And avoid false speech}."],[8452,"that He finds him with his face in the dust."],[8453,"\"Indeed charity falls into the hand of Allah before it falls into the hand of the beggar.\" Then ʿAbd Allah recited: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants} until the end of the verse."],[8454,"A man brought his nephew to ʿAbd Allah while he was drunk, and said: \"I found this one drunk.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Shake him, rinse his mouth, and smell his breath.\" He said: So he was shaken, his mouth was rinsed, and his breath was smelled, and the smell of wine was found on him. So ʿAbd Allah ordered him to prison, then released him the next day. Then he ordered a whip whose end was beaten until it became a light switch. Then he said to the flogger: \"Flog and draw back your hand, and give every limb its due.\" So he flogged him with a flogging that was not severe, and he was in a cloak and trousers, or a shirt and trousers. Then he said: \"By Allah, how bad is the guardian of the tribe! I did not discipline and improve the discipline, nor did I cover the disgrace.\" He said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, he is my nephew; I feel for him the same anguish I feel for my own son.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Indeed Allah Almighty loves pardon, but it is not appropriate for a guardian to be brought a prescribed punishment and not carry it out.\""],[8455,"A man brought his nephew to ʿAbd Allah while he was drunk, and said: \"I found this one drunk.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Shake him, rinse his mouth, and smell his breath.\" He said: So he was shaken, his mouth was rinsed, and his breath was smelled, and the smell of wine was found on him. So ʿAbd Allah ordered him to prison, then released him the next day. Then he ordered a whip whose end was beaten until it became a light switch. Then he said to the flogger: \"Flog and draw back your hand, and give every limb its due.\" So he flogged him with a flogging that was not severe, and he was in a cloak and trousers, or a shirt and trousers. Then he said: \"By Allah, how bad is the guardian of the tribe! I did not discipline and improve the discipline, nor did I cover the disgrace.\" He said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, he is my nephew; I feel for him the same anguish I feel for my own son.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Indeed Allah Almighty loves pardon, but it is not appropriate for a guardian to be brought a prescribed punishment and not carry it out.\""],[8456,"Abdullah said, \"If any of you is afflicted with a punishment, do not curse him, rather ask Allah to forgive him and have mercy on him.\""],[8457,"When you see your brother commit a sin, do not be helpers of Satan against him by saying, 'O Allah, disgrace him! O Allah, curse him!' Rather, ask Allah for pardon. For we, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, would not say anything about anyone until we knew upon what he would die. If he was sealed with good, we knew that he had attained good; and if he was sealed with evil, we feared for him because of his deeds."],[8458,"That I be provided with a whip in the path of Allah is dearer to me than that I perform Hajj after Hajj."],[8459,"Abdullah had permitted exchange (al-sarf) and permitted a man to marry a woman, then she died before he consummated the marriage, and to marry her mother. Then he came to Madinah and it was as if he met Umar, so he retracted. He then went to the money-changers and forbade them from that."],[8460,"Abdullah used to permit a dirham for two dirhams and a dinar for two dinars. Then he returned to Madinah and went to Umar, Ali, and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and they forbade him from that. When he returned, I saw him going around among the money-changers saying, 'Woe to you, O people! Do not consume usury, and do not buy a dirham for two dirhams, nor a dinar for two dinars.'"],[8461,"About his saying."],[8462,"He informed him that she is not lawful for him. When he returned to Kufa, he said to the man, 'She is forbidden to you,' so he separated from her."],[8463,"Abdullah said, 'When you meet the wicked man, meet him with a frowning face.'"],[8464,"That you should change it, so frown in his face."],[8465,"Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, looked into the hearts of His servants and found the heart of Muhammad ﷺ to be the best of the hearts of His servants, so He chose him for Himself and singled him out—or he said: He sent him with His message. Then He looked into the hearts of His servants after his heart and found the hearts of his companions to be the best of the hearts of His servants, so He made them the ministers of His Prophet ﷺ, fighting for His religion."],[8466,"Allah, may He be exalted, looked into the hearts of His servants and chose Muhammad ﷺ, so He sent him with His message and selected him with His knowledge. Then He looked into the hearts of the people and chose his companions, so He made them the ministers of His Prophet ﷺ and the supporters of His religion. Whatever the believers deem good is good in the sight of Allah, and whatever the believers deem ugly is ugly in the sight of Allah."],[8467,"Abdullah heard a man say, 'Where are those who abstain from this world and desire the Hereafter?' Abdullah said, 'Those are the people of al-Jabiyah. Five hundred Muslims stipulated that they would not return until they were killed.' So they shaved their heads, met the enemy, and were killed, except one who informed about them."],[8468,"The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people: those who do not recognize good and do not reject evil. They will copulate like beasts in the road. A woman will pass by a man in the road, and he will approach her and satisfy his need with her, then return to his companions and laugh to them and they laugh to him, like the foul, wormy dates that are not good to eat."],[8469,"The Hour will not be established except upon the worst of people, upon a people who do not enjoin good and do not forbid evil; they will copulate like donkeys copulate. A man will take a woman by the hand, be alone with her, and fulfill his need from her; then he will return laughing to them and they will laugh to him, like the putrid discarded dates that are not eaten."],[8470,"That a man says to his brother, 'Fear Allah,' and he replies, 'Mind yourself; you are commanding me?'"],[8471,"It is enough of a sin for a man that when it is said to him, 'Fear Allah,' he becomes angry."],[8472,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and from their elders. When knowledge comes from their young ones, that is when they perish."],[8473,"I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: People will remain righteous and cohesive as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and from their elders. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish."],[8474,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from their elders and those of their predecessors. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish. This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd b. Wahb, and Zayd b. Hibban concurred with him."],[8475,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and their elders. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish."],[8476,"Indeed Allah ﷻ looked into the hearts of the servants and found the heart of Muhammad ﷺ to be the best of hearts of the servants.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of 'Asim."],[8477,"“When you send peace and blessings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then do it well, for you do not know, that may be shown to him.” They said to him: “Teach us.” He said: “Say: ‘Allahumma aj’al salataka wa rahmataka wa barakatika ‘ala sayyidil-mursalin wa imamil-muttaqin wa khatamin- nabiyyin, Muhammad ‘abdika wa Rasulika imamil-khayri (wa qa’idil- khair), wa Rasulir-Rahmah. Allahummab’athhu maqaman mahmudan yaghbituhu bihil-awwaluna wal-akhirun. Allahumma salli ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama sallayta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim; Allahumma barik ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim, innaka Hamidum Majid (O Allah, send Your grace, honour, mercy and blessings upon the leader of the Messengers, the imam of the pious and the seal of the Prophets, Muhammad, Your slave and Messenger, the Imam of the good (and the leader) of the good, and the Messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a station of praise and glory that will be the envy of the first and the last. O Allah, send Your grace, honour and mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your grace, honour and mercy upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 906)"],[8478,"“When you send peace and blessings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then do it well, for you do not know, that may be shown to him.” They said to him: “Teach us.” He said: “Say: ‘Allahumma aj’al salataka wa rahmataka wa barakatika ‘ala sayyidil-mursalin wa imamil-muttaqin wa khatamin- nabiyyin, Muhammad ‘abdika wa Rasulika imamil-khayri (wa qa’idil- khair), wa Rasulir-Rahmah. Allahummab’athhu maqaman mahmudan yaghbituhu bihil-awwaluna wal-akhirun. Allahumma salli ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama sallayta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim; Allahumma barik ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim, innaka Hamidum Majid (O Allah, send Your grace, honour, mercy and blessings upon the leader of the Messengers, the imam of the pious and the seal of the Prophets, Muhammad, Your slave and Messenger, the Imam of the good (and the leader) of the good, and the Messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a station of praise and glory that will be the envy of the first and the last. O Allah, send Your grace, honour and mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your grace, honour and mercy upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 906)"],[8479,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. By my life, I do not think any of you has not taken a mosque in his house. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen us, and none would stay behind from them except a known hypocrite or one whose hypocrisy was recognized. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he is stood in the row. No man purifies himself and does it well, then takes a step intending to go to a mosque from the mosques, except Allah writes for him a good deed because of it, raises him a degree because of it, and removes from him a sin because of it—so much so that we used to take short steps."],[8480,"Whoever would like to meet Allah as a Muslim servant, let him guard these five prayers where the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. By my life, if every one of you prayed in his house as the one who stays in his house prays, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen us, and none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I have seen us, and indeed a man would be supported between two men until he is brought into the row. No Muslim servant performs ablution and does it well, intending to go to a congregational mosque and pray in it, and takes a step except Allah raises him a degree because of it or removes from him a sin because of it—so much so that we used to take short steps.\" And the wording is that of the hadith of Hajjaj."],[8481,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them in congregation, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah ﷻ has obligated for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he is brought and stood in the row. A time came upon us when none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. Indeed we used to take short steps between them."],[8482,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard the prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. A time came upon us when none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was clear. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he stands in the row."],[8483,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah has prescribed for your Prophet the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. By my life, if you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prays in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. A time came upon us when none stayed away from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I saw a man being supported between two men until he was stood in the row. No man purifies himself and perfects his purification, then heads to one of the mosques to pray in it, and takes a step except that Allah records for him a good deed by it, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a sin by it, until we used to take short steps."],[8484,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. By my life, if you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prays in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known."],[8485,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for His Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prayed in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. No man purifies himself and perfects the purification, then heads to one of these mosques except that Allah records for him for every step he takes a good deed, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a bad deed by it. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, and a man would be supported between two men until he was stood in the row."],[8486,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. I think there is no one among you except he has a mosque in which he prays. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. No Muslim servant performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then proceeds to prayer except that Allah records for him for every step a good deed, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a sin by it."],[8487,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers when the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of al-Mas'udi."],[8488,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers when the call is given for them, for Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. Each man among you has a mosque in his house. If you abandoned your mosques, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, you would go astray."],[8489,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays away from it prays, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I saw a man among us being supported between two men until he was stood in the row. No Muslim servant performs ablution in his house, perfects the ablution, then heads to a mosque, comes to it, lifting a foot and placing a foot, except that Allah records for him by it ten good deeds, erases from him ten bad deeds, and raises for him by it ten degrees, until we used to take short steps."],[8490,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known or a sick person, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8491,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known or a sick person, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8492,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8493,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8494,"Adhere to the five prayers in the mosque, for they are from the matter of guidance and the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ."],[8495,"He should meet Allah as a Muslim servant; so let him perform the prayers wherever the call is made for them, for they are the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ. Indeed, if every man prayed in his house, you would abandon the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and if you abandoned the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, you would go astray. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among us, and the prayer would not be commenced until the rows were made straight—or when our rows were made straight—whereas today the prayer is commenced and then one of them calls out, 'O slave girl, bring me water for ablution,' and he bares his forearms. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among us, and we used to speak that when a man performed ablution in his house and then went out to prayer, he would not lift a foot except that a degree was raised for him thereby, and he would not place the other except that Allah removed a sin from him thereby. So we used to take short steps."],[8496,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except that he spoke one day and the words 'The Messenger of Allah said' slipped from his tongue, and distress overcame him until I saw sweat rolling down him. He said, 'If Allah wills—either above this, or close to this, or below this.'"],[8497,"He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' and when he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' trembling overcame him and he would say, 'Like this, or something like this, or close to this, or whatever Allah wills.'"],[8498,"Abdullah would go a year without narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then one day he narrated while we were with him and said, 'Like this, or close to this.'"],[8499,"I sat with Abdullah for a year and did not hear him narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then one day he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then his face changed, then he said, 'Like this, or above this, or below this.'"],[8500,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one hadith, and he sweated, then said, 'This, or like this, or similar to this.'"],[8501,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—until one evening he said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' then he lowered his head. He raised his head and I saw that the buttons of his shirt were undone, his jugular veins had swollen, and his eyes had filled with tears. He said, 'Or above that, or below that, or close to that, or similar to that.'"],[8502,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then his face changed, then he said, 'Like this, or close to this.'"],[8503,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Like that, or similar.' He was not seen narrating after this hadith ever again."],[8504,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then trembling seized me, and he said, 'Like this, or similar to this.'"],[8505,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said' more than once. He said: I looked at him while he was leaning on a staff, and I saw the staff shaking."],[8506,"'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and his clothes trembled. He said, 'This, or like it, or similar to this.'"],[8507,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would change color and his complexion would alter, and he would say, “This or something close to this.”"],[8508,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, except a hadith I heard him narrate; then he shuddered like the shuddering of a palm branch, then he said, “This or something like it.”"],[8509,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ ever, except once; and indeed I saw him shudder like the shuddering of a palm branch, then he said, “Close to this or something like this.”"],[8510,"Abdullah stayed for a year without saying \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.\" And when he said \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,\" he was struck by a thunderbolt and his face changed, and he said, \"It is like this or like that or like this.\""],[8511,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ; and when he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ,” he said, “This or something like this, or close to this,” and indeed he was trembling."],[8512,"I left a people in the mosque saying, “Whoever glorifies such and such will have such and such.” He said, “Stand, O ‘Alqama.” When he saw them, he said, “O ‘Alqama, divert the people’s eyes from me.” When he heard them and what they were saying, he said, “Indeed you are clinging to the tail of misguidance, or indeed you are more guided than the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.”"],[8513,"A storyteller who sits at night and tells the people, “Say such and such,” was mentioned to Ibn Masʿūd. He said, “When you see him, inform me.” He said, so they informed him, and ʿAbdullāh came veiled and said, “Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd. Do you know that you are more guided than Muḥammad ﷺ and his companions, or indeed you are clinging to the tail of misguidance?”"],[8514,"A people would sit from sunset to nightfall glorifying, saying, “Say such and such, and say such and such.” ʿAbdullāh said, “If they sit, notify me.” When they sat, they came to him, and he set out, entered with them and sat wearing a burnoose. They began their glorification, and ʿAbdullāh uncovered the burnoose from his head and said, “I am ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd.” The people fell silent. He said, “You have brought a dark innovation, or you have surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” A man from Banū Tamīm said, “We have not brought a dark innovation, nor have we surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” ʿAmr b. ʿUtba b. Farqad said, “I seek forgiveness from God, O Ibn Masʿūd, and I repent to Him.” So he ordered them to disperse. He said: And Ibn Masʿūd saw two circles in the mosque of Kufa, so he stood between them and said, “Which of you was before its companion?” One of them said, “We were.” He said to the other, “Arise and go to it,” and he made them one."],[8515,"He said to the boy, “Go and see whether these were sitting before or those.” He came and said, “These.” He said, “The mosque only needs one innovator, for those before you perished only through mutual hatred.”"],[8516,"He informed him, “When they sit, notify me.” When they sat, he notified him, and ʿAbdullāh came wearing a burnoose until he entered upon them, uncovered the burnoose from his head, then said, “I am the son of Umm ʿAbd. By God, you have brought a dark innovation, or you have surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” Muʿaḍḍad, who was an eloquent man, said, “By God, we have not brought a dark innovation, nor have we surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.” ʿAbdullāh said, “If you follow the people, they have preceded you with a clear precedence; and if you deviate right and left, you have gone astray with a far misguidance.”"],[8517,"“Do not weary the people, lest they weary of the remembrance.”"],[8518,"“O warner, do not drive the people to despair.”"],[8519,"Abū Mūsā said, “What has brought you at this hour?” He said, “No, by God, except that I saw a matter that alarmed me, and indeed it is good, and indeed it alarmed me, and indeed it is good: a people sitting in the mosque and a man saying to them, ‘Glorify such and such, praise such and such.’” He said, so ʿAbdullāh set out, and we set out with him until he came to them and said, “How quickly you have gone astray, while the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ are alive, his wives are young, and his garments and vessels have not changed. Count your evil deeds, for I guarantee from God that He will count your good deeds.”"],[8520,"Abdullah stood by me while I was narrating stories in the mosque and said: O Amr, you have indeed introduced an innovation of misguidance. Are you more guided than Muhammad ﷺ and his companions? I saw them disperse from me until I saw my place with no one in it."],[8521,"Are you more guided or the companions of Muhammad ﷺ? Indeed you are clinging to a fringe of misguidance."],[8522,"They mentioned to him a man who narrates stories, so he came among the people and I heard him say: \"Glory be to Allah, such and such.\" When he heard that, he stood up and said: \"Do you not hear?\" When they looked at him, he said: \"Indeed you are more guided than Muhammad ﷺ and his companions. Indeed you are clinging to a fringe of misguidance.\""],[8523,"When people fall into evil, say: I have no example in evil."],[8524,"When people fall into trial and they say: Go out, you have an example in the people, then say: I have no example in evil."],[8525,"That he should learn something from it, let him do so, for the smallest of houses in good is the one in which there is nothing of the Book of Allah. Indeed the house in which there is nothing of the Book of Allah is like the ruin of a house that has no one to inhabit it, and indeed Satan leaves the house in which Surah al-Baqarah is heard."],[8526,"Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for Satan does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."],[8527,"\"Every thing has a peak and the peak of the Quran is Surah Al-Baqarah, and every thing has a core and the core of the Quran is the detailed explanation. Indeed, the devils flee from the house in which Surah Al-Baqarah is recited. And even the smallest houses have an inside that does not contain anything from the Book of Allah.\""],[8528,"Abdullah used to say: \"The smallest of houses is the one in which there is no Book of Allah, and indeed the house in which there is no Book of Allah is ruined like the ruin of a house that has no one to inhabit it.\""],[8529,"Indeed this Quran is the banquet of Allah, so learn from His banquet what you can. Indeed this Quran is the rope of Allah which He commanded, and it is the clear light and the beneficial healing, a protection for the one who holds fast to it and a salvation for the one who clings to it. It does not go crooked so that it would need to be straightened, and it does not deviate so that it would need to be corrected. Its wonders do not cease, and it does not wear out from repetition. Recite it, for indeed Allah ﷻ will reward you for every letter of it with ten good deeds. I do not say to you that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter."],[8530,"Whoever recites the Quran, for every letter of a verse he has ten good deeds, and I do not say Alif Lam Mim is ten, but Alif, Lam, and Mim are thirty good deeds."],[8531,"Learn the Quran and recite it, for you will be rewarded for it with a good deed for every letter of it. Indeed I do not say Alif Lam Mim is a good deed, but Alif, Lam, and Mim are thirty good deeds. That is because Allah ﷻ says: {Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times its like}."],[8532,"Learn the Quran and recite it, you will be rewarded for every letter with ten good deeds. Indeed I do not say Alif Lam Mim, but I say Alif, Lam, and Mim."],[8533,"A man died, so the angels of punishment came to him and sat by his head. They said, \"You have no way to escape from us. He used to recite Surah Al-Mulk.\" Then they sat by his feet and said the same. Finally, they sat by his abdomen and said, \"You have no way to escape from us. Indeed, he has passed away while Surah Al-Mulk was with him.\" Thus, he was given the name \"Al-Mani'ah\" (the Preventer)."],[8534,"A man is approached in his grave. His feet are approached, and they say: \"You have no way over what is before us; he used to recite Surat al-Mulk upon us.\" Then his torso is approached, and it says: \"You have no way over me; he had contained Surat al-Mulk within me.\" Then he is approached from his head, and it says: \"You have no way over what is before me; he used to recite Surat al-Mulk within me.\" Abdullah said: \"It is the preventer, preventing the punishment of the grave. And in the Torah it is: Surat al-Mulk—whoever recites it in a night has done much and good.\""],[8535,"Abdullah said: \"The Quran is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, and an advocate whose testimony is believed. Whoever makes it his guide, it leads him to Paradise; whoever puts it behind him, it drives him to the Fire.\""],[8536,"\"Whoever loves the Quran and is pleased with it, he is upon good.\""],[8537,"\"Whoever loves to know that he loves Allah and His Messenger, let him look: if he loves the Qur'an, then he loves Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[8538,"You heard Abdullah, and I confirm you—or I narrate and you confirm me. He said: I heard Abdullah say: The most comprehensive verse in the Quran for good and evil is a verse in Surat al-Nahl: {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrongdoing, and oppression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.} He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: I heard Abdullah say: The greatest verse in the Quran in bringing joy is a verse in Surat al-Ghuraf: {Say, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair} of the mercy of Allah. Indeed Allah forgives all sins, if He wills. He said: You have spoken the truth."],[8539,"Masruq said to Shutayr: These people have turned to us only for us to narrate to them. Either you narrate and I confirm you, or I narrate and you confirm me. Masruq said: Narrate, and I will confirm you. Shutayr said: Abdullah b. Mas'ud narrated to us that the greatest verse in the Book of Allah is {Allah—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. He narrated to us that Abdullah said: The most comprehensive verse in the Book of Allah is {Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. And he narrated to us that the most or greatest verse in the Book of Allah in bringing joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair} of the mercy of Allah to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. And he narrated to us that the verse in the Book of Allah conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth."],[8540,"We sat in the mosque, and the people surged toward the two of them. One of them said to his companion: They only stood up to us so that we narrate to them. Either I narrate to them and you confirm me, or you narrate and I confirm you. One of them said: I heard Abdullah say: \"The greatest verse in the Quran is the Verse of the Throne.\" The other said: You have spoken the truth. The other said: I heard Abdullah say: The most comprehensive verse in the Quran is {Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence}. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: And I heard him say: The verse in the Quran conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out}. He said: You have spoken the truth. The other said: And I heard him say: The greatest verse in the Quran in bringing joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves}. He said: You have spoken the truth."],[8541,"Masruq said: I do not think these people sat with us except to hear good from us. Either you narrate from Abdullah and I confirm you, or I narrate from Abdullah and you confirm me. He said: Narrate to us, Abu 'A'ishah. Masruq said: I heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say: \"The two eyes commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the private part confirms or denies that.\" He said: Yes, and I have also heard it. He said: Have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the most comprehensive verse in the Quran regarding lawful and unlawful, command and prohibition is {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality} to the end of the verse? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. He said: Have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the verse in the Quran conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect}? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. He said: And have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the verse in the Quran bringing the greatest joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah} to the end of the verse? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. The wording is from the hadith of Hammad b. Zayd."],[8542,"That if one of you goes out in the morning and learns a verse from the Book of Allah, it is better for him than forty-four, forty-four, forty-four—until he enumerated many things."],[8543,"That if one of you goes out in the morning and learns a verse from the Book of Allah, it is better for him than forty-four, forty-four, forty-four—until he enumerated many things."],[8544,"He used to recite a verse to a man and then say: \"It is better than what the sun has risen upon, or better than anything on the earth,\" until he would say that concerning the entire Quran."],[8545,"\"Whoever desires the good of the first and the last, let him stir the Quran, for in it is the good of the first and the last.\""],[8546,"Abdullah said, \"Whoever seeks knowledge should start with the Quran, for it is the best of all things, both in the beginning and in the end.\""],[8547,"\"Whoever desires knowledge, let him stir the Quran, for in it is the knowledge of the first and the last.\""],[8548,"For every letter there is a limit, and for every limit there is a point of ascent."],[8549,"Indeed, there is not a single letter of the Qur'an except that it has a limit, and for every limit there is a point of ascent."],[8550,"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' it is as if he has recited a third of the Qur'an."],[8551,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'The parable of one who recites the Qur'an but does not act upon it is like a fragrant herb whose scent is pleasant but has no taste. The parable of one who acts upon the Qur'an but does not recite it is like a date whose taste is pleasant but has no fragrance. The parable of one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it is like a citron whose taste is pleasant and whose fragrance is pleasant. The parable of one who does not recite the Qur'an nor act upon it is like a colocynth whose taste is bitter and whose smell is bitter.'"],[8552,"Whoever recites Surah al-Baqarah in a night has done much and has done well."],[8553,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'Whoever recites three verses from Surah al-Baqarah in a night has done much and has done well.'"],[8554,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'Whoever recites ten verses from Surah al-Baqarah in a house, no devil will enter that house that night until morning: four verses from its beginning, the Verse of the Throne, two verses after it, and its closing verses.'"],[8555,"He used to recite: {And all will come to Him in humility} (Q27:87)."],[8556,"I recited the Qur'an to ʿAbd Allah and he did not correct me except for two letters. I recited: {And all will come to Him in humility} (Q27:87). He said: {And all will come to Him in humility}. And I recited: {Until, when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied} (Q12:110). He said: {And thought that they had been lied to}."],[8557,"He used to recite: {This is nothing but the tales of the ancients} (Q68:15), saying: 'Something they fabricated.'"],[8558,"Ibn Masood used to recite the Quran to a man. The man recited the verse \"Verily, the sadaqat (charity) are only for the poor and the needy\" incorrectly. So Ibn Masood said, \"This is not how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to me. He recited it as 'Verily, the sadaqat are only for the poor and the needy'.\" And he elongated it."],[8559,"He recited: (Wherever He directs him, he brings only good)."],[8560,"That you worship none but Him.'"],[8561,"I heard the Quran reciters and I found their recitations close to one another, so recite as you have been taught, and beware of being overly meticulous and of disagreement, for it is only like one of you saying, 'Come here' and 'Come on.'"],[8562,"ʿAbdullah [said]: Do not say {hīt} [i.e., do not alter the reading]. We have already asked about that, and I prefer to recite as I was taught."],[8563,"He used to recite {majrāhā wa-mursāhā}."],[8564,"It is permitted to recite some of it [one variant] in place of some [another variant], but the error is to attach to it something that is not part of it."],[8565,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar, for it is Arabic."],[8566,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar."],[8567,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar, for it is Arabic, and there will come a people who will master it but they are not the best of you."],[8568,"Keep looking at the mushaf continuously."],[8569,"Keep reviewing the mushafs, for it slips away from men's chests more quickly than camels break free from their tethers."],[8570,"He recited it as {bal ʿajibtu wa-yaskharūn}."],[8571,"He used to recite it as \"al-Ḥayy al-Qayyām\"."],[8572,"He used to recite {ḥattā yalija al-jamalu fī sammi al-khiyāṭi} [until the camel goes through the eye of the needle], saying, \"It means the male camel.\""],[8573,"Abdullah said: \"When one of you asks his companion how he recites such-and-such a verse, let him ask him about what comes before it.\""],[8574,"Abdullah said: \"When one of you asks his brother about a verse, he should not say, 'Such-and-such,' for that is not upon him, but he should recite what comes before it, then let him come between him and his need.\""],[8575,"I recited to Abdullah and he was pleased with my voice, so he said: \"Recite in a measured tone, may my father and mother be your ransom.\""],[8576,"Ibn Masʿud said: \"Keep looking at the mushaf, and if you differ over a ya or a ta, make it ya; treat the Quran as masculine.\""],[8577,"He said: \"When you dispute over a ya or a ta, make it ya and treat the Quran as masculine, for it is masculine.\""],[8578,"He said: \"This Quran will surely be snatched away from among you.\" I said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, how can it be snatched away when we have fixed it in our mushafs?\" He said: \"It will be taken away by night, and nothing of it will remain in the heart of any servant or in any mushaf, and people will wake up poor like beasts.\" Then Abdullah recited: \"And if We willed, We could surely take away that which We have revealed to you, then you would find no guardian for you against Us.\""],[8579,"Abdullah said: \"The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing that will remain is prayer, and a people will surely pray who have no faith.\""],[8580,"And the Quran will surely be snatched away from among you.\" They said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, are we not reciting the Quran and have we not fixed it in our mushafs?\" He said: \"The Quran will be taken away by night and removed from the hearts of men, so that nothing of it will remain on the earth.\""],[8581,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8582,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8583,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8584,"\"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is negligent.\""],[8585,"\"He used to read the Quran on Fridays and he used to read it three times in Ramadan.\""],[8586,"Abdullah said: \"The Quran is not to be recited in less than three days. Recite it in seven, and let a man keep to his portion every day and night.\""],[8587,"Ibn Masʿūd used to recite the Qur’an in three [days], and he would only take a little help from the daytime."],[8588,"ʿAbdullāh used to recite the Qur’an every three [days], and he rarely took from it during the daytime."],[8589,"Our companions ʿAlqamah, al-Aswad, and al-Rabīʿ b. Khuthaym."],[8590,"Abū Isḥāq was asked, and it was said to him: “Do you remember from al-Aswad that ʿAbdullāh said: ‘When you recite a sūrah whose end is a prostration, then if you wish, bow, for the rakʿah is from the prostration; and if you wish, prostrate, then recite a sūrah after it?’” He said: “Yes.”"],[8591,"“When the prostration is the seal of the sūrah, then if you wish, bow; and if you wish, prostrate.”"],[8592,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd: “It is only the repentance of a prophet that is mentioned, so he would not prostrate in it,” meaning Ṣād."],[8593,"ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād."],[8594,"And he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8595,"He would not prostrate in Ṣād, and he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8596,"ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād."],[8597,"From al-Shaʿbī: They both said: ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād, and he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8598,"“Recite,” and he would prompt him while he was reciting."],[8599,"“Read,” and he began reading, and he began prompting him."],[8600,"Ibrahim: “ʿAbd Allah went aside to relieve himself, then a man asked him to open (the recitation), and he prompted him before touching water.”"],[8601,"“On Ibn Masʿud’s ring there was a tree, or something, between two flies.”"],[8602,"“Whoever recites five verses in a night will never be recorded that night among the heedless; whoever recites one hundred verses will be recorded among the devout; whoever recites three hundred will have a qintar recorded for him; and whoever recites seven hundred will succeed.”"],[8603,"ʿAbd Allah would prostrate in “When the sky is split open.”"],[8604,"I prostrated with ʿUmar and with ʿAbd Allah in “When the sky is split open.” Al-Aswad said, “As for one of them, I have no doubt about it.”"],[8605,"I saw ʿAbd Allah and ʿUmar, or one of them, prostrate in “When the sky is split open.”"],[8606,"“ʿAbd Allah would prostrate in (Surah) al-Najm and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created.’”"],[8607,"ʿAbd Allah: “Whoever recites Surah al-Aʿraf, or al-Najm, or ‘When the sky is split open,’ or the Children of Israel, or ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes to bow at the end of any of them, he may bow, and the prostration of bowing suffices him; and if he prostrates, let him add another surah to it.”"],[8608,"“Whoever recites al-Aʿraf, al-Najm, and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes to bow at the end of any of them, he may bow, and the prostration of bowing suffices him; and if he prostrates, let him add another surah to it.”"],[8609,"“Whoever recites al-Aʿraf, al-Najm, and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes he may bow with it and it suffices him; and if he wishes he may prostrate, then stand and recite the surah and bow and prostrate.”"],[8610,"When Ibn Masʿud recited al-Najm to the people, he prostrated with it; and when he recited it in prayer, he bowed with it and prostrated."],[8611,"There is nothing upon him regarding smiling in the prayer."],[8612,"Abdullah b. Masʿud used to prostrate in the first verse of Ḥā Mīm Tanzīl from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."],[8613,"Abdullah said: Indeed, the prayers are the good deeds and an expiation for what is between the first to the afternoon prayer is the afternoon prayer, and an expiation for what is between the afternoon prayer to the sunset prayer is the sunset prayer, and an expiation for what is between the sunset to the night prayer is the night prayer, then the Muslim retires to his bed with no sin upon him as long as he avoids major sins. Then he recited: {Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds}."],[8614,"Abdullah b. Masʿud said: You burn until when they pray the dawn prayer, they are washed; then you burn until when they pray the noon prayer, they are washed; you burn until when they pray the afternoon prayer, they are washed; until he counted all the prayers like this."],[8615,"Indeed, these prayers are the true expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided."],[8616,"The prayers are expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided."],[8617,"We used to recite to Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī while he was walking. When we came to a prostration verse, he said Allahu Akbar and we said Allahu Akbar, and he prostrated and we prostrated, gesturing. He would raise his head and say, 'Peace be upon you,' and we would say, 'And upon you be peace.' Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān claimed that Abdullah used to do that with them."],[8618,"Whoever among you recites the Quran, let him learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, for if a bedouin meets him and says, 'O Muhājir, do you recite the Quran?' and he says, 'Yes,' then the bedouin says, 'And I recite,' then the bedouin says, 'Do you assign the shares, O Muhājir?' If he says, 'Yes,' he says, 'An addition and good.' But if he says, 'I do not know it well,' he says, 'Then what is your superiority over me, O Muhājir?'"],[8619,"Abdullah said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, there is nothing on the face of the earth more in need of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8620,"Abdullah said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, there is nothing on the back of the earth more in need of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8621,"Abdullah said: There is nothing on the earth more deserving of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8622,"I heard Abdullah b. Masʿud say: There is nothing more deserving of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8623,"“Sin is what scratches the hearts; whatever scratches the heart of any of you, let him leave it.”"],[8624,"“Whatever is from a glance, the devil has a share of desire in it, and sin is what scratches the hearts.”"],[8625,"ʿAbd Allah: “Beware of the whisperings of the chests.”"],[8626,"“Whoever lets others hear of his deeds, Allah will expose him; whoever shows off, Allah will expose him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever humbles himself before Allah out of humility, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8627,"“Go forth as a scholar or a learner, and do not go forth between that; if you do not, then love the scholars and do not hate them.”"],[8628,"ʿAbd Allah counseled his son ʿAbd al-Rahman, saying: “I counsel you to be mindful of Allah, let your house suffice you, weep over your sin, and control your tongue.”"],[8629,"“A man who hoards will be cauterized; a dirham will touch another dirham and no dinar another dinar; his skin will be expanded until every dinar and dirham is placed separately on it.”"],[8630,"“Accustom yourselves to good, for good comes by habit, and guard your intentions in prayer.”"],[8631,"“Whoever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.”"],[8632,"“Whoever desires the Hereafter harms his worldly life, and whoever desires the world harms his Hereafter, so He commanded them to harm the perishable for the everlasting.”"],[8633,"I was at Shuraf, and ʿAbd Allah stopped with us. My family sent me to him with some things, and some slave boys of ours who were with the camels came from a journey of four nights with a bird. I took it to him. When I took it to him, he asked me, “From where did you bring me this bird?” I said, “Some slave boys of ours who were with the camels brought it from a journey of four nights.” ʿAbd Allah said, “I wish that I were where it was hunted, not speaking to any human about anything, and no one speaking to me until I meet Allah.”"],[8634,"By Allah, other than whom there is no god, there is no living soul but that death is better for it: if it is righteous, for Allah ﷻ says, “And what is with Allah is better for the righteous,” and if it is wicked, for Allah ﷻ says, “And let not those who disbelieve think that Our granting them respite is better for themselves; We only grant them respite that they may increase in sin.”"],[8635,"O people, learn! Whoever knows, let him act."],[8636,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “A people will come who drink knowledge as one drinks.”"],[8637,"“You have spoken the truth, by the One besides whom there is no god.”"],[8638,"\"Abdullah said, 'I do not know any of you who has the endurance of a camel in the darkness of the night and the heat of the day.'\""],[8639,"\"Do not imitate the religion of anyone among you, for if he believes, he will believe, and if he disbelieves, he will disbelieve. If you are to follow anyone, follow the one who has passed away, for the living are not safe from trials.\""],[8640,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “None of you should be an immaʿa (one who blindly follows others).” They said, “What is an immaʿa, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “He says, ‘I am only with the people: if they are guided, I am guided; and if they go astray, I go astray.’ Indeed, let each of you resolve in himself that even if the people disbelieve, he will not disbelieve.”"],[8641,"“In the Age of Ignorance we used to call the immaʿa the one who comes to food without being invited. Indeed, the immaʿa among you is the one who makes his religion a mount for others.”"],[8642,"“In the Age of Ignorance we used to call the immaʿa a man who is invited to food and another man follows him. Today it is the one who makes his religion a mount for people. And we used to call slander sorcery; today it is ‘it was said and he said.’”"],[8643,"“You pray more and strive more than the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ, yet they were better than you.” They said, “Why is that, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “Because they were more abstinent from this world and more desirous of the Hereafter.”"],[8644,"\"Follow and do not innovate, for you have been sufficed with every innovation of misguidance.\""],[8645,"“The whole earth will be fire on the Day of Resurrection, and Paradise will be beyond it. They will see its maidens with swelling breasts and its goblets. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of ʿAbd Allāh, a man will sweat so profusely that his sweat will flow over the earth up to his own height, then it will rise until it reaches his nose, while the reckoning has not touched him.” They said, “Why is that?” He said, “Because of what he sees people suffering.”"],[8646,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “By the One besides whom there is no god, no servant thinks well of Allah except that He gives him what he thought, and that is because all good is in His hand.”"],[8647,"ʿAbd Allāh said to his wife: “Is today better or yesterday?” She said, “I do not know.” He said, “But I know: yesterday is better than today, and today is better than tomorrow, and so on until the Hour comes.”"],[8648,"ʿAbd Allāh came out to us one day while he was weak. We said, “What is the matter with you?” He said, “The pure part of this world is gone, and nothing remains but its dregs. Today death is a gift for every Muslim.”"],[8649,"“The pure part of this world is gone, and nothing remains but its dregs. Today death is a gift for every Muslim.”"],[8650,"The likeness of this world is that of a water-hole (thaghab).\" We said, \"What is a thaghab?\" He said, \"A pool whose clear water has gone and whose dregs remain. So death is a gift for every believer.\""],[8651,"The people of affliction will wish on the Day of Resurrection, when they behold the reward, that their skins had been cut with scissors."],[8652,"that their bodies had been cut with scissors.\""],[8653,"The disbeliever will be bridled with his sweat on the Day of Resurrection, because of the length of that day, until he says, \"My Lord, relieve me, even if it be to the Fire.\""],[8654,"that he should ask, let him begin with praising and extolling Allah as He deserves, then let him invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then let him ask afterwards, for that is more likely to succeed.\""],[8655,"When a man mounts a riding beast and does not remember Allah, Satan rides behind him and says to him, \"Sing.\" If he is not good at it, he says to him, \"Wish.\""],[8656,"The Satan of a believer meets the Satan of a disbeliever. The Satan of the believer appears pale, dusty, and emaciated, so the Satan of the disbeliever says, \"What is the matter with you? Woe to you, you are ruined.\" The Satan of the believer says, \"No, by Allah, I cannot get at him with anything. When he eats, he mentions the name of Allah; when he drinks, he mentions the name of Allah; and when he enters his house, he mentions the name of Allah.\" The other one says, \"But I eat from his food, drink from his drink, and sleep on his bed.\" So this one is fat and that one is emaciated."],[8657,"Abdullah, the major sins are associating partners with Allah, despairing of Allah's relief, despondency of Allah's mercy, and feeling secure from Allah's plan."],[8658,"that he said: The greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, feeling secure from Allah's plan, despondency of Allah's mercy, and despairing of Allah's relief."],[8659,"The greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, despairing of Allah's relief, despondency of Allah's mercy, and feeling secure from Allah's plan."],[8660,"Go to your mother and tell her to dress you in a shirt other than this one.\""],[8661,"We were with Abdullah when a son of his came wearing a silk shirt. He said, \"Who clothed you in this?\" He said, \"My mother.\" He said, \"So he tore it.\" He said, \"Tell your mother to clothe you in something other than this.\""],[8662,"He said: “A man will never find the taste of faith until he believes in divine decree and knows that he will die and that he will be resurrected.”"],[8663,"That he will die and then be resurrected after death.”"],[8664,"Three qualities: whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith—abandoning disputation in what is true, avoiding lying in jest, and knowing that what befalls him could not have missed him and what misses him could not have befallen him."],[8665,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Did they say, ‘We are the people of Paradise’?”"],[8666,"A man said in the presence of ʿAbd Allāh, “I am a believer.” ʿAbd Allāh said, “Say, ‘I am in Paradise,’ but we believe in God, His angels, and His messengers.”"],[8667,"“I adjure by God any one who has severed ties of kinship to leave us, for we wish to call upon our Lord while the gates of heaven are closed to the one who severs ties of kinship.”"],[8668,"“When a man among the Children of Israel committed a sin, he would wake to find written on his door, ‘You have committed such-and-such a sin, and its expiation is such-and-such a deed,’ so perhaps he would be eager to make it known.” Ibn Masʿūd said, “I would not love that God ﷻ gave us that in place of this verse: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks God’s forgiveness will find God Forgiving, Merciful}.”"],[8669,"A man passed by another man while he was prostrating and stepped on his neck. He said, “You step on my neck while I am prostrating? By God, God will never forgive you, ever.” God said, “Do you swear by Me? Indeed, I have forgiven him.”"],[8670,"“Indeed, the likeness of the belittled (minor) sins is like the likeness of a group of travelers who camped in a barren land. With them was food that could not be cooked except with fire. So they scattered: one came bringing dung, another came bringing a bone, and another came bringing a stick, until they gathered from that enough with which to cook their food. Likewise is the one who commits the belittled sins: he tells a lie, and commits a sin, and gathers from that what may cause God to cast him on his face into the Fire of Hell.”"],[8671,"He said: We asked permission to enter upon ʿAbd Allāh after the dawn prayer, and he gave us permission, casting a velvet cloak over his wife and saying, “I disliked keeping you waiting.”"],[8672,"Two men at whom God laughs: a man upon a horse among the finest horses of his companions; when they meet the enemy, they flee, but he remains firm—if he is killed, he is killed as a martyr, so God laughs at him. And a man who rises in the night when no one knows of him, performs ablution thoroughly, prays for Muḥammad ﷺ, praises God, and begins the recitation—God laughs at him, saying, ‘Look at My servant; no one sees him but Me.’"],[8673,"Three things I swear by, and a fourth—if I swore by it, I would be truthful: God will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes God as his protector in this world but that God entrusts him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no man loves a people but that he will come with them. The fourth, which if I swore by it I would be truthful: God does not conceal a servant in this world but that God will conceal him in the Hereafter."],[8674,"ʿAbd Allāh said: Three things I swear by, and a fourth—if I swore by it, I would hope not to sin and would be truthful: God will not make one who has a share in submission like one who has no share; no Muslim servant takes God as his protector but that God will entrust him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no man loves a people but that God will resurrect him with them. The shares of Islam are three: prayer, alms, and fasting. The fourth, if I swore by it, I would hope not to sin: God does not conceal a servant in this world but that God will conceal him in the Hereafter."],[8675,"I went with a man to ʿAbdullāh, and found him standing in prayer while two men had flanked him. When he said the salutation, they asked him about a verse. He said to one of them, \"Who taught you to recite?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" He said to the other, \"Who taught you to recite?\" He said, \"Abū Ḥakīm\"—or he said \"Abū ʿAmrah.\" He said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then he wept until his tears soaked the pebbles. Then he said, \"ʿUmar ؓ was a strong fortress for Islam: people entered Islam and did not leave it. When ʿUmar was struck, the fortress was breached.\""],[8676,"And the other said, \"ʿUmar taught it to me.\" When ʿUmar was mentioned, ʿAbdullāh wept while standing, wiped his eyes, and shook his hand over the pebbles. Then he said, \"It is clearer than the road of al-Saylaḥīn.\" Then he said, \"Recite it as ʿUmar taught you. Any household of the Muslims that was not entered by grief for ʿUmar on the day he was struck is a household of evil. ʿUmar was the most God-fearing of us and the best reciter of the Book of Allah among us.\""],[8677,"Two men disputed about a verse. While we were in that state, ʿAbdullāh approached from the direction of his in-laws. They went to him, and I went with them. They said, \"We have disputed about a verse.\" ʿAbdullāh said to one of them, \"Recite.\" He recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"Abū ʿAmrah Maʿqil b. Muqarrin.\" Then he said to the other, \"Recite it.\" He recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" His eyes brought forth four [streams of tears], and he wept until I saw him take some of his tears in his palm and gesture with it like this. I saw two marks in the pebbles from ʿAbdullāh's tears. Then ʿAbdullāh said, \"I do not think any household of the Muslims that was not entered by grief for ʿUmar on the day he was struck is anything but a household of evil. ʿUmar was the most knowledgeable of us about Allah, the best reciter of the Book of Allah among us, and the most understanding of the religion of Allah among us. Recite it as ʿUmar taught you, for by Allah it is clearer than the road of al-Saylaḥīn.\""],[8678,"Two men came to ʿAbdullāh while we were with him. One said, \"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, how should we recite this verse?\" ʿAbdullāh recited it to him. The man said, \"Abū Ḥakīm taught it to me in such-and-such a way.\" The other recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" ʿAbdullāh said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then ʿAbdullāh wept until I saw his tears flowing down onto the pebbles. Then he said, \"ʿUmar was a strong fortress over Islam: people entered it and did not leave. The fortress has now become breached, so people leave it and do not enter.\""],[8679,"Abū Ḥakīm al-Muzanī taught me. He asked the other to recite, then said, \"Who taught you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb taught me.\" ʿAbdullāh wept until his tears dyed the pebbles. Then he said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then he traced a circle with his hand and said, \"ʿUmar was a strong fortress for Islam: people entered through it and did not leave it. When ʿUmar died, the fortress was breached, so people leave it and do not enter.\""],[8680,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"ʿUmar's acceptance of Islam was a conquest, his emigration was a victory, and his rule was a mercy. By Allah, we were not able to pray at the Kaʿbah openly until ʿUmar accepted Islam.\""],[8681,"From Qatādah and Ḥammād, who said: I heard them saying—he heard the two of them saying—that Ibn Masʿūd used to say, \"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was a strong fortress for Islam: one entered Islam and did not leave it. When ʿUmar died, a breach was made in the fortress, so one leaves it and does not enter it. When he took a path, we found it easy. When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar. He was the dividing line between increase and decrease. By Allah, I wish I could serve someone like him until I die.\""],[8682,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"By Allah, I think that if ʿUmar's knowledge were placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of the rest of the living people of the earth were placed in the other pan, ʿUmar's knowledge ؓ would outweigh it.\" Sulaymān said: I mentioned that, and he said, \"ʿAbdullāh said something even better than that. He said, 'I think ʿUmar went away with nine-tenths of knowledge.'\""],[8683,"ʿUmar's knowledge was placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of the people of the earth in the other pan, his knowledge would outweigh their knowledge.\" Wakīʿ said: al-Aʿmash said: I found that objectionable, so I went to Ibrāhīm and mentioned it to him. He said, \"What do you find objectionable in that? By Allah, ʿAbdullāh said something even better than that. He said, 'I think nine-tenths of knowledge went away on the day ʿUmar ؓ went away.'\""],[8684,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"I think nine-tenths of knowledge was raised with ʿUmar on the day he died. I think that if ʿUmar's knowledge were placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of those after him in the other, ʿUmar's knowledge ؓ would outweigh it.\""],[8685,"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. Where is he? He said, \"He is in Paradise.\" He said, \"Abū Bakr passed away. Where is he?\" He said, \"That is al-Awwāh; with every good he is sought.\" He said, \"ʿUmar passed away. Where is he?\" He said, \"When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar.\""],[8686,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar.\""],[8687,"When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar. His acceptance of Islam was a victory, and his rule was a conquest. By God, I know of nothing on the earth except that it felt the loss of ʿUmar—even the thorny trees. By God, I reckon that between his eyes there is an angel who guides him and directs him aright. By God, I reckon that Satan is afraid of him, lest he introduce something new into Islam and ʿUmar refute him. By God, if I knew of a dog that loved ʿUmar, I would love it."],[8688,"I loved ʿUmar so much that I feared God, and if I knew that a dog loved ʿUmar, I would love it. I wish I had been a servant to ʿUmar ؓ . Everything felt his loss, even the thorny trees. His migration was a victory, and his authority was a mercy."],[8689,"If ʿUmar loved a dog, that dog would be the most beloved of dogs to me."],[8690,"ʿAbdullāh said: “I feared God in my love for ʿUmar ؓ .”"],[8691,"ʿAbdullāh said: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar.”"],[8692,"ʿAbdullāh used to say: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar. I wish I were a servant to someone like ʿUmar until I die.”"],[8693,"ʿAbdullāh said: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar.”"],[8694,"ʿAbdullāh said: “ʿUmar’s acceptance of Islam was a conquest, and his rule was a mercy. By God, we were not able to pray at the House until ʿUmar accepted Islam. When ʿUmar accepted Islam, he confronted them until they called us, and we prayed.”"],[8695,"“We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8696,"I heard Ibn Masʿūd say: “We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8697,"“We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8698,"ʿAbdullāh said: Satan met a man from among the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ and wrestled with him. The Muslim threw him down and pressed his thumb. He said: “Let me go and I will teach you a verse that none of us hears except that he turns away.” So he released him, but he refused to teach him. He returned and wrestled with him again, and the Muslim threw him down and pressed his thumb. He said: “Tell me it.” But he refused to teach him. When he returned the third time, he said: “The verse in Sūrat al-Baqarah: {Allāh—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining} to its end.” It was said to ʿAbdullāh: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who was that man?” He said: “Who could it be except ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ ?”"],[8699,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"I think that Satan flees from Umar's perception.\""],[8700,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud met a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , who was struggling with a jinn. The man was able to overpower the jinn, and the jinn asked the man to let him go. The man agreed on the condition that the jinn teach him something beneficial if he overpowered him for a third time. The man overpowered the jinn again, and the jinn said, \"I see you as weak and thin, like the offspring of a dog. That is how you and the jinn are.\" The man replied, \"No, by Allah, I am not one of them. Rather, let me overpower you for the third time, and if I do, you must teach me something beneficial.\" The man overpowered the jinn again, and then he asked the jinn to teach him. The man asked, \"Can you recite the Ayat al-Kursi?\" The jinn replied, \"Yes.\" The man said, \"You will not recite it inside a house, but the Shaytan will leave the house with a noise like that of a donkey. It will not enter the house until morning.\" A man from the people asked, \"O Abu Abdullah! Who is that man from the companions of Muhammad ﷺ ?\" Abdullah ibn Mas'ud frowned and approached him, saying, \"Who could it be but Umar?\""],[8701,"That tranquility speaks upon the tongue of Umar.\""],[8702,"The most perceptive of people are three: the companion of Musa who said, {O my father, hire him. Indeed, the best you can hire is the strong and the trustworthy}. He said, \"What did you see of his strength?\" She said, \"He came to the well with a rock over it that so-and-so many could not lift, and he lifted it.\" He said, \"What did you see of his trustworthiness?\" She said, \"I was walking in front of him and he put me behind him.\" And the companion of Yusuf when he said, {Make his stay comfortable; perhaps he will benefit us or we will take him as a son}. And Abu Bakr when he appointed Umar as successor."],[8703,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"I think that between Umar's eyes there is an angel guiding him.\""],[8704,"And as if an angel between his eyes was guiding him.\""],[8705,"That between his eyes there was an angel guiding him.\""],[8706,"\"Umar disliked praying after the afternoon prayer, and I dislike what Umar disliked.\""],[8707,"We, the companions of Muhammad, gathered and appointed the best of us, one with superiority."],[8708,"From the best of us, one with superiority, so we pledged allegiance to him; so pledge allegiance to the Commander of the Believers, Uthman b. Affan.\""],[8709,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"It would not please me to shoot Uthman with an arrow that missed him—I think he said—intending to kill him, even if I had the like of Uhud in gold.\""],[8710,"ʿAbd Allah came announcing Umar's death and Uthman's appointment as successor. ʿAbd Allah said, \"By God, we did not fall short regarding our highest one, the one with superiority.\""],[8711,"From its highest—that is above.”"],[8712,"When ʿUthmān ؓ was appointed caliph, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said, “We have placed in authority the best of those who remain, and we have not been remiss.”"],[8713,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said, “We have placed in authority the best of those who remain, and we have not been remiss.”"],[8714,"That he announced the death of ʿUmar, and weeping choked him once or twice. Then he said, “ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was a strong fortress for Islam, into which people entered and from which they did not leave. The fortress has now crumbled.” Then he announced his death, and then said, “And ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān was appointed caliph, and we have not been remiss concerning the best of it—that is above.”"],[8715,"That his soul be taken, and his taking is the departure of his people. And you must hold to knowledge, for one of you does not know when he will need what he has. And you must hold to knowledge, and beware of excessive precision and going too deep. And you must hold to the old, for a people will come who recite the Book of Allah and cast it behind their backs.”"],[8716,"“O people, learn, for one of you does not know when he will be in need of it.” Then a man came to him and said, “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what do you think of a man who recites the Quran in reverse order?” He said, “That is one whose heart is reversed.” Then a muṣḥaf was brought to him that had been adorned and gilded, and ʿAbdullāh said, “The best adornment of a muṣḥaf is its recitation in truth.”"],[8717,"That he used to say, “O Allah, if You have written me among the people of wretchedness, then erase me and establish me among the people of felicity.”"],[8718,"That Ibn Masʿūd would sometimes quote a line of poetry from the events of the Arabs."],[8719,"I heard ʿAbdullāh say, “There is no word I can speak to a person of authority by which I can ward off from myself two lashes of the whip but that I would speak it.”"],[8720,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “A man may relate a hadith, and someone whose intellect cannot reach the understanding of that hadith hears it, and it becomes a trial for him.”"],[8721,"There were two towns, one righteous and the other wicked. A man left the wicked town intending to go to the righteous town, and death came to him wherever Allah willed. The angel and the devil disputed over him. The devil said, “By Allah, he never disobeyed me.” The angel said, “He had set out intending repentance.” It was decided between them that they should see to which of the two towns he was closer. They found him closer to the righteous town by a span, so he was forgiven. Maʿmar said, “And I heard someone say, ‘Allah brought the righteous town closer to him.’”"],[8722,"“One who forbids what is lawful is like one who permits what is unlawful.”"],[8723,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd say: 'The one who forbids the lawful is like the one who makes the unlawful lawful.'"],[8724,"'I do not leave behind me anything dearer to me than camels I give water to.'"],[8725,"'Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will question every guardian about what He entrusted to him: did he establish Allah's command among them or did he neglect it? Even a man will be questioned about his own household.'"],[8726,"that it would burst upon us, so if you sent someone to dam it... ʿAbd Allah said: 'We will not dam it. By Allah, a time will come upon people when, if they sought a basin of water, you would not find it. Every water will return to its source, and the water and the Muslims will be in Syria.'"],[8727,"The Euphrates River extended during the time of Abdullah, and the people disliked that. Abdullah said, \"Do not dislike it, for there will soon come a time when people will search for a cup of water and will not find it, as all water will return to its source, and the remainder of the water will be with the believers in Sham.\""],[8728,"'When the year thirty-five comes, a great event will occur. If they perish, then it is fitting; if they survive, then perhaps. And when the year seventy comes, you will see what you disapprove of.'"],[8729,"'It is as if I see the Turks coming to you on horses with cropped ears until they tether them at the bank of the Euphrates.'"],[8730,"that a man should love his brother, loving him only for the sake of Allah, and in it..."],[8731,"'...from idolatry.'"],[8732,"'Amulets, incantations, and love charms are idolatry, or a portion of idolatry.'"],[8733,"He saw on the neck of a woman of his household a leather strap containing amulets. He pulled it firmly until he cut the strap and said: 'The family of ʿAbd Allah is indeed free of need from idolatry.' Then he said: 'Love charms, amulets, and incantations are indeed idolatry.' A woman said: 'One of us gets a headache and seeks a ruqya. When she seeks a ruqya, it is thought to have helped her.' ʿAbd Allah said: 'Satan comes to one of you and inserts into her head. When she seeks a ruqya, he withdraws; when she does not, he pricks. If one of you were to call for water and sprinkle it on her head and face, then say, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,\" then recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" \"Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind,\" that would benefit her, if Allah wills.'"],[8734,"'The marrow of the leg of a woman of the houris will be seen through the flesh and bone and from beneath seventy garments, just as red wine is seen in a white glass.'"],[8735,"'Sudden death is a relief for the believer and a regret for the disbeliever.'"],[8736,"Indeed, the soul of the believer comes out as a sweat, and indeed the soul of the disbeliever comes out through the sides of his mouth like the breath of a donkey comes out."],[8737,"O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter, I ask You for the good of it and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it."],[8738,"ʿAbdullāh used to fast little. That was mentioned to him, so he said, “When I fast, I become too weak to recite, and reciting the Qur’an is more beloved to me.”"],[8739,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.” If he fasted, he fasted three days of the month."],[8740,"ʿAbdullāh used to fast little, so we said to him, “You fast little.” He said, “When I fast, I become too weak for prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.”"],[8741,"“Prayer is more beloved to me than fasting,” and he used not to pray the ḍuḥā (forenoon prayer)."],[8742,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.”"],[8743,"I heard al-Shaʿbī say, “ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd used not to pray the ḍuḥā, and he would pray between ẓuhr and ʿaṣr along with a long portion of the night.”"],[8744,"The matter of those two days."],[8745,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting. If he fasted, he fasted three days of the month.”"],[8746,"I used to go to Ibn Masʿūd for a year, “and I never saw him fasting on any day at all except in Ramadan, and he used to drink strong nabīdh from a green jar.”"],[8747,"I used to go to Ibn Masʿūd for a year, “and I did not see him praying the ḍuḥā, nor did I see him fasting voluntarily except on the day of ʿĀshūrā’.”"],[8748,"We were with ʿAbd Allah when a drink was brought to him. He said, \"Pass it to the people.\" They said, \"We are fasting.\" He said, \"But I am not fasting.\" So he drank, then recited: {They fear a day in which the hearts and eyes will turn about}."],[8749,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud saying: \"The righteous depart one after another, and there remain people of doubt who do not recognize what is good and do not reject what is evil.\""],[8750,"\"Allah ﷻ divided good and made it into ten parts, placing nine parts in Syria and the remainder in the rest of the earth. And He divided evil and made it into ten parts, placing one part of it in Syria and the remainder in the rest of the earth.\""],[8751,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. And death comes before meeting Allah.\""],[8752,"\"When one of you seeks a need, let him seek it privately; for he will only have what has been decreed for him. And let none of you go to his companion and praise him, thereby breaking his back.\""],[8753,"We were sitting with ʿAbd Allah when the people mentioned a man and spoke of his character. ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do you think that if you cut off his head you could restore it?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"His hand?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"His leg?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"You will never be able to change his character until you change his physical creation. The drop of semen settles in the womb for forty nights, then descends as blood, then becomes a clot, then becomes a lump of flesh. Then the angel is sent to it and writes down its provision, its character, and whether it is wretched or blessed.\""],[8754,"The people said, \"Is there no one to restrain him?\" ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do you think that if his head were cut off you could make a head for him? Or if his hands were cut off you could make a hand for him? Or if his leg were cut off you could make a leg for him?\" They said, \"No.\" ʿAbd Allah said, \"When the drop of semen falls into the woman, it remains for forty days, then descends as blood, then becomes a clot, then becomes a lump of flesh like that. Then Allah sends the angel and says, 'Write down his term, his deeds, his provision, his effect, and whether he is wretched or blessed.' You will never be able to change his character until you change his physical creation.\""],[8755,"Indeed, your Lord—Exalted is He—has neither night nor day; the light of the heavens and the earth is from the light of His Face. And the measure of each day of your days with Him is twelve hours. So your deeds from yesterday are presented to Him at the beginning of today’s day, and He looks into them for three hours; then He sees in them what He dislikes, and that angers Him. The first to know of His غضب (wrath) are the Bearers of the Throne; they praise Him, and it weighs heavily upon them. Then the Bearers of the Throne, the curtains/canopies of the Throne, the angels brought near, and the rest of the angels glorify Him. Then Jibrīl ﷺ blows the horn, and nothing remains except that it hears its sound, and they glorify the Most Merciful—Exalted is He—for three hours, until the Most Merciful is filled with mercy; that makes six hours. Then the wombs are brought, and He looks into them for three hours. That is His saying in His Book: “He is the One who shapes you in the wombs however He wills,” and: “He grants to whom He wills females, and He grants to whom He wills males; or He couples them—males and females—and He makes whom He wills barren. Indeed, He is Knowing, Powerful.” That makes nine hours. Then provision is brought, and He looks into it for three hours—His saying in His Book: “He expands provision for whom He wills and restricts it,” and: “Every day He is upon a matter.” He said: This is from your affair and the affair of your Lord."],[8756,"ʿAbd Allah used to say: \"Servants are in a state of ease under Allah's ﷻ covering as long as they maintain worship and do not shed forbidden blood.\""],[8757,"I said to ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAziz, \"Ibn Masʿud used to say: 'There will be ambiguous matters. Whoever among those absent from them approves of them is like one who witnessed them, and whoever among those who witness them detests them is like one who was absent from them.'\" This pleased him."],[8758,"When ʿAbd Allah left his house he would say, \"In the name of Allah, I rely upon Allah. There is no power and no strength except with Allah.\" Muhammad b. Kaʿb al-Qurazi said: This is in the Quran: {Embark therein: in the name of Allah} and He said: Upon Allah we rely."],[8759,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do not swear by the swearing of Satan, that one of you says, 'By the might of Allah.' Rather, say as Allah said: Allah, Lord of might.\""],[8760,"\"If you were a hypocrite, you would not fear that.\""],[8761,"When Uqbah's death came to Abdullah, he wept. It was said to him: 'You weep?' He said: 'He was my brother in lineage and my companion with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Along with that, I would not love that I was before him — that he die and I seek reward for him is dearer to me than that I die and he seek reward for me.'"],[8762,"Ibn Mas'ud used to say: 'O Beginner with no beginning before You, O Everlasting with no end to You, O Living, Reviver of the dead, You are the One standing over every soul with what it has earned.'"],[8763,"Abdullah said: 'Whoever has a handsome appearance, is in a position that does not disgrace him, and is granted ample provision, then is humble — he is among the pure ones of Allah.'"],[8764,"O Allah, I ask You for the good of it and the good of its people, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people."],[8765,"against wrongdoing, and a man who recognized the truth with his heart."],[8766,"Ibn Mas'ud said: 'Guarantee for me intentional killing, and I will guarantee for you accidental killing.'"],[8767,"Abdullah passed by me while I was selling some of my goods and swearing about them. He began to raise my head with something in his hand and said: 'Do not swear, for an oath profits the goods but erases blessing.'"],[8768,"His Lord will meet with him privately just as one of you meets with the moon on the night of the full moon. He will say: 'Son of Adam, what deceived you concerning Me? Son of Adam, what deceived you concerning Me? Son of Adam, what did you answer the messengers? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew?'"],[8769,"By Allah, there is none among you except that Allah will meet with him privately on the Day of Resurrection just as one of you meets with the moon on the night of the full moon. He will say: 'What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you answer the messengers?'"],[8770,"He said: 'Enter.' We said: 'We will wait a little; perhaps some of the people of the house have a need.' He began to glorify Allah, then said: 'You thought the family of Abdullah to be heedless.' Then he said: 'O slave girl, see whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' Then he said to her a second time: 'See whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' Then he said to her a third time: 'See whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Praise be to Allah who granted us this day and pardoned our slips in it.' And I think he said: 'And did not punish us with the Fire.'"],[8771,"To swear by Allah falsely is dearer to me than to swear by other than Him truthfully."],[8772,"The height of Musa ﷺ was twelve cubits, his staff was twelve cubits, and his leap was twelve; he struck Uj ibn Unuq and struck nothing but his ankle."],[8773,"That he should come to him and greet him »"],[8774,"«The souls of the martyrs are inside green birds that roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, then they take shelter in lanterns hanging from the Throne»"],[8775,"«Whoever of you comes seeking a fatwa, let him sit until we give it to him. Whoever of you comes as a litigant, let him keep hold of his opponent until we judge between them. And whoever of you comes to inform us of a shameful act that God has concealed, let him conceal himself with God’s concealment and entrust it privately to the One who possesses its forgiveness, for we do not possess its forgiveness and would impose a legal penalty on him; and with their dung»"],[8776,"ʿAbd Allah was brought an udder, and a man withdrew, saying, “I have forbidden it.” ʿAbd Allah said: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things God has made lawful for you} Eat and offer expiation."],[8777,"ʿAbd Allah was brought an udder, and he began eating from it. He said to the people, “Come close.” The people came close, but a man among them withdrew. ʿAbd Allah said, «What is the matter with you?» He replied, “I have forbidden the udder.” He said, “This is from the steps of Satan. Come close, eat, and expiate your oath.” Then he recited: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things God has made lawful for you}"],[8778,"«Every trait a believer may be folded upon except treachery and lying»"],[8779,"“My brother is ill; he complains of his stomach, and wine has been prescribed for him. Should I give it to him to drink?” ʿAbd Allah said, “Glory be to God! God has not placed healing in filth. Healing is only in two things: honey is a healing for people, and the Qurʾan is a healing for what is in the chests.”"],[8780,"People set out early in two ways: a seller of his own soul, so he destroys it, and a redeemer of it, so he sets it free. Charity is a proof, fasting is a shield, prayer is a light, tranquility is a gain, and abandoning it is a loss."],[8781,"«Souls are troops that have been marshaled. Those among them that recognize one another come together, and those that reject one another differ»"],[8782,"«Indeed God supports the religion through the sinful man»"],[8783,"Women are only a private part. A woman goes out of her house while there is no harm in her, but Satan looks up at her and says, ‘You will not pass by anyone but that you please him.’ And a woman puts on her clothes and it is said, ‘Where do you intend to go?’ She says, ‘I am visiting a sick person, or attending a funeral, or praying in a mosque.’ No woman has worshiped her Lord like worshiping Him in her house."],[8784,"«When you are three on a journey, appoint one of you as your leader, and let no two of you converse privately apart from their companion»"],[8785,"Abd Allah [said]: \"That is Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq, the sacrifice of Allah, son of Ibrahim, the friend of Allah.\""],[8786,"I heard Abd Allah supplicate with this supplication: \"O Allah, I ask You by Your abundant blessing which You bestowed upon me, and by Your trial which You tested me with, and by Your grace which You granted me, that You admit me to Paradise. O Allah, admit me to Paradise by Your grace, Your favor, and Your mercy.\""],[8787,"Abd Allah recited: {Except him who has taken a covenant with the Most Merciful} (19:87). He said: Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'Whoever has a covenant with Me, let him stand.' They said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, teach us.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, I covenant with You in this worldly life that if You entrust me to myself, You bring me near evil and distance me from good. I trust only in Your mercy, so make it for me a covenant with You that You fulfill to me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break the promise.' He said: Zakariyya Abu Yahya added in it from al-Qasim: 'Fearful, seeking refuge, seeking forgiveness, desirous of You.'"],[8788,"\"Assess people by their close companions.\""],[8789,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud [said]: \"O people, a time has come upon us when we do not judge and we are not there. Indeed, Allah has brought us to what you see. So whoever of you is presented with a judgment after today, let him judge in it according to what is in the Book of Allah. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, let him judge in it according to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge in it, let him judge according to what the righteous judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge in it, and the righteous did not judge in it, let him exercise his judgment. Let none of you say: 'I fear' or 'I think.' Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. So leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.\""],[8790,"Abd Allah [said]: \"If a matter confronts you that is unavoidable, look at what is in the Book of Allah and judge by it. If you are unable, then by what the Messenger ﷺ judged. If you are unable, then by what the righteous judged. If you are unable, then head toward it and do not be remiss. If you are unable, then acknowledge and do not be ashamed.\""],[8791,"\"Illness does not earn reward; reward is only for deeds, but Allah expiates sins by it.\""],[8792,"\"The one who gives legal verdicts to people in everything they ask him about is insane.\""],[8793,"Al-Hawdi said in his narration: \"in everything they ask him about.\""],[8794,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud [said]: \"What an excellent assembly is the assembly in which wisdom spreads.\""],[8795,"That a man becomes poor in knowledge he once had, or remains among people who do not know.\""],[8796,"Abd Allah [said]: \"Sufficient as knowledge is fear of Allah, and sufficient as ignorance is being deceived regarding Allah.\""],[8797,"ʿAbd Allah: When a commander is appointed, he will have two inner circles from his own people: one inner circle that commands him to obey Allah, and one inner circle that commands him to disobey. He is with whichever of the two he obeys."],[8798,"ʿAbd Allah: Do not hasten to praise people or to blame them. For perhaps you see something from your brother today that pleases you, and perhaps it will displease you tomorrow. And perhaps you see something from him today that displeases you, and perhaps it will please you tomorrow. People find fault, but Allah alone forgives sins on the Day of Resurrection. Allah is more merciful to His servant on the day he meets Him than a mother who spread out for him on the ground, then touched him: if there was a thorn, she would be struck by it before him; and if there was a sting, she would be struck by it before him."],[8799,"ʿAbd Allah: I think that a man does not forget knowledge that he once knew except because of a sin that he commits."],[8800,"ʿAbd Allah: Let none of you say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from tribulation,' for there is none among you who is not surrounded by tribulation. But whoever seeks refuge, let him seek refuge from its difficult entanglements. For Allah, may He be exalted, says: 'Your wealth and your children are but a trial' [Q 64:15]."],[8801,"ʿAbd Allah: Let none of you say: 'I am a sarurah.' For a Muslim is not a sarurah. And let none of you say: 'I am a hajj performer,' for the hajj performer is the one in ihram. But let him say: 'I intend to go to Makkah.'"],[8802,"There is no prescribed punishment except for two: a man who is disowned from his father, or who slanders a chaste woman."],[8803,"ʿAbd Allah: There is no prescribed punishment except for two: that he slanders a chaste woman, or a man is disowned from his father."],[8804,"ʿAbd Allah: Repentance is offered to the son of Adam as long as one of three things has not occurred: as long as the sun has not risen from its west, or the beast has not emerged, or Yaʾjuj and Maʾjuj have not come out."],[8805,"It was said to ʿAbd Allah: 'Allah the Exalted mentions prayer often in the Qurʾān: \"Those who are constant in their prayer\" [Q 70:23], \"And those who are mindful of their prayer\" [Q 70:34].' ʿAbd Allah said: 'That refers to its proper times.' They said: 'O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, we thought it meant abandoning it.' ʿAbd Allah said: 'Abandoning it is disbelief.'"],[8806,"Whoever abandons prayer has disbelieved."],[8807,"It was said to ʿAbd Allah: 'Allah the Exalted mentions prayer often: \"Those who are constant in their prayer\" [Q 70:23], \"And those who are mindful of their prayer\" [Q 70:34].' ʿAbd Allah said: 'That refers to its prescribed times.' We said: 'We thought it meant abandoning it.' He said: 'Abandoning it is disbelief.'"],[8808,"Whoever does not pray has no religion."],[8809,"“Whoever does not pray has no religion.”"],[8810,"That ʿAbd Allah went out for the dawn prayer after some people had leaned their backs against the qiblah side of the mosque, and he said: “Move back like this from the faces of the angels.”"],[8811,"That he saw some people leaning their backs against the qiblah between the dawn call to prayer and the iqamah, and he said: “Do not come between the angels and their prayer.”"],[8812,"Abdullah came at dawn and found a group of people with their backs facing the qibla. He said, \"Delay your prayers to avoid standing between the angels and the qibla, for it is the prayer of the angels.\""],[8813,"“As much as you are able to, O servants of Allah.”"],[8814,"ʿAbd Allah: “The two months are fifty-nine days.”"],[8815,"ʿAbd Allah arrived after Saʿd had built the palace and had made a mosque among the date-palm growers; he used to go out to it for the prayers. When ʿAbd Allah was put in charge of the treasury, someone made a breach in the treasury and the man was caught. ʿAbd Allah wrote to ʿUmar, and ʿUmar wrote back: “Do not cut off his hand, but move the mosque and put the treasury on the side facing the qiblah, for there is always someone in the mosque praying.” So ʿAbd Allah moved it and drew this plan. The palace that Saʿd had built was a shadhara, and when the imam stood upon it, ʿAbd Allah ordered it demolished until the imam’s standing place was level with the people."],[8816,"That ʿAbd Allah lent some money to maternal uncles of his from Banu Saʿd. When their stipends were distributed, they chose for him their property, and when it was brought to him, ʿAbd Allah said: “This is better than our money that we gave you, so gather your stipends and give us from its goods.”"],[8817,"ʿAbd Allah: “By the One besides whom there is no god, Allah apportioned this fayʾ upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ before Persia and Rome were conquered.”"],[8818,"ʿAbd Allah: “Four things have been finished: creation, character, provision, and the appointed term.”"],[8819,"Four things have been finished: creation, character, provision, and the appointed term. None of us can earn anything on behalf of another."],[8820,"Four things have been finished: creation, character, provision, and the appointed term. None of us can earn anything on behalf of another."],[8821,"ʿAbd Allah had a Christian scribe. ʿAbd Allah entered the palace and the Christian returned, so ʿAbd Allah followed him with the greeting of salam."],[8822,"Some people from among the polytheists walked with ʿAbd Allāh, and when he reached the gate of the palace he greeted them."],[8823,"ʿUmar (?) said: I passed by one of the mosques of Banū Ḥanīfah and heard them reciting something God had not sent down: the grinders grinding, the kneaders kneading, the bakers baking, the morsel-eaters eating morsels. He said: So Ibn Masʿūd put Ibn al-Nawwāḥah forward as their leader and killed him, and found the rest to be many, and said: “I will not slaughter them today for the devil. Send them to Syria so that God may grant them repentance or the plague may destroy them.”"],[8824,"ʿUmar (?) said: I passed by one of the mosques of Banū Ḥanīfah and heard them reciting something God had not sent down: the grinders grinding, the kneaders kneading, the bakers baking, the morsel-eaters eating morsels. He said: So Ibn Masʿūd put Ibn al-Nawwāḥah forward as their leader and killed him, and found the rest to be many, and said: “I will not slaughter them today for the devil. Send them to Syria so that God may grant them repentance or the plague may destroy them.”"],[8825,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Were it not that you are a messenger, I would strike your neck.” So today you are not a messenger. Then he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb, and he struck his neck in the market. Then he said: “Whoever wants to look at Ibn al-Nawwāḥah killed in the market.”"],[8826,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"If it were not for the fact that you are a messenger, I would have killed you.\" As for today, O Harashah, you are not a messenger. Stand up and strike his neck. So he got up and struck his neck."],[8827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn al-Nawwaha, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Do you bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah?\" The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"If it was not for the fact that you are a messenger, I would have killed you.\""],[8828,"ʿAbd Allāh was approached and it was said to him: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, there are people here reciting the recitation of Musaylimah. ʿAbd Allāh sent him back, and he stayed as long as God willed him to stay. Then he came to him and said: By the One by whom I swear, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I have left them now in a house, and that muṣḥaf is indeed with them. So he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb, and he set out with the people with him, and said: “Bring them.” When they were brought, ʿAbd Allāh said: “What is this after the spread of Islam?” They said: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, we ask God's forgiveness and repent to Him, and we bear witness that Musaylimah is the liar who fabricated against God and His Messenger. He said: So ʿAbd Allāh asked them to repent and sent them to Syria, and they were nearly eighty men. Ibn al-Nawwāḥah refused to repent, so he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb concerning him, and he took him out to the market and struck his neck, and ordered him to take his head and throw it into his mother's lap. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh said: I met an old man among them later in Syria, and he said: May God have mercy on your father. By God, if he had killed us that day, we would all have entered the Fire."],[8829,"The first to spread the Quran among the companions of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was Abdullah ibn Masood. The first to build a mosque for prayer was Ammar ibn Yasir. The first to give the call to prayer was Bilal. The first to ride his horse in the way of Allah was Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad. The first Muslim to throw a spear in the way of Allah was Saad. The first Muslim to be martyred on the day of Badr was Mahja, the servant of Umar ibn Khattab. The first group of people who pledged allegiance to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were the people of Juhayna. And the first to give voluntary charity from their own selves were the sons of Uthra ibn Saad."],[8830,"I stood next to Abdullah during the afternoon or evening, and I heard him reciting."],[8831,"\"It is as if I am looking at him while he is prostrating and he leaned on his elbows, to the point that I almost saw the whiteness of his armpits.\""],[8832,"I entered the mosque and said: I will pray at every pillar. Then I came to ʿAbd Allāh while he was sitting and his companions were with him, and they were talking about me (?). He said: “If he knew that his Lord is at the first pillar, he would not leave it until he finished his prayer.”"],[8833,"That God ﷻ is at the nearest pillar, he would not pass it until he finished his prayer.”"],[8834,"“If I were to tread on a live coal, it would be dearer to me than to tread on the grave of a Muslim.”"],[8835,"“The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, on the second is a virtue, and on the third is showing off and reputation. Whoever seeks to be heard, God will make him heard.”"],[8836,"There was an argument between a man from among the companions of ʿAbd Allāh and his wife. She said: Your food and the food of your family is nothing but from the milk of my ewe. So he swore that he would not eat anything from its milk. Then a guest came to them, and she prepared food for him with the milk of her ewe. The man said: You know that I do not eat it. The woman said: By God, if you do not eat, I will not eat. The guest said: By God, if you two do not eat, I will not eat. So they spent the night without dinner. The talk reached ʿAbd Allāh, and the man came to ʿAbd Allāh. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “What came between you and your family?” He said: There was no divorce, no ẓihār, and no īlāʾ. Then he told him the story. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “I adjure you, when you return to your family, that the first thing you do is eat from the milk of this ewe. And I think it would be better for yourself to expiate for your oath.”"],[8837,"I heard Abdullah bin Mas'ood saying, \"Indeed, Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for death.\""],[8838,"“Then adhere to the community of the people.”"],[8839,"“O people, fear God, and you must adhere to obedience and the community, for they are the rope of God which He commanded. What you dislike in obedience and the community is better than what you love in division. God did not create anything of this world but that He made for it an end point at which it stops, and then it decreases until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, the bonds of Islam have been established, and it is about to decrease and retreat until the Day of Resurrection. The sign of that is that you sever your ties of kinship, and that poverty becomes widespread, so that the rich fears nothing but poverty, and the poor finds no one who shows compassion to him, and the beggar stands between the two Friday prayers and nothing falls into his hand. While the people are like that, the earth will low a lowing like the lowing of a cow; every people will think that it lowed from their courtyard. Then there will be a return, and it will low a second time with pieces of its liver.” It was said to him: And what are pieces of its liver? He said: “Like these pillars, of gold and silver. From that day gold and silver will not benefit until the Day of Resurrection, and he will find no one to accept the charity of his wealth.”"],[8840,"He said: “O people, upon you is obedience and the community, for they are the rope of Allah which He commanded. Indeed, what you dislike in obedience and the community is better than what you love in division. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has not created a thing except that He made for it a limit at which it stops. Indeed, Islam has advanced and has stability. It is about to reach its limit, then it will recede and decrease until the Day of Resurrection. The sign of that is that poverty will increase, ties of kinship will be severed so that the poor will not find anyone to return to him, until the rich will think that what he has is not enough for him, and until a man will complain to his brother and his cousin and they will not give him anything, and until the beggar will walk between the two Fridays with nothing placed in his hand. Then, when that happens, the earth will bellow a bellowing: the people of every tract will think that it bellowed in their tract. Then it will calm upon them as long as Allah wills. Then the earth will surprise them vomiting the pieces of its liver.” It was said: “O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, what are the pieces of its liver?” He said: “Pillars of gold and silver. From that day, neither gold nor silver will be of benefit until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8841,"“Adhere to this community, for it is the rope of Allah which He commanded. Indeed, what you dislike in the community is better than what you love in division. Indeed, Allah has never created a thing except that He made for it an end. Indeed, this religion has been completed, and it is going to decrease. The sign of that is that kinship ties will be severed, wealth will be taken without its right, blood will be shed, a relative will complain to his relatives and they will not give him anything, and the beggar will go around between the two Fridays with nothing placed in his hand. While they are like that, the earth will bellow like the bellowing of a cow, then it will throw out the pieces of its liver. After that, neither gold nor silver will be of benefit.”"],[8842,"“Whoever establishes the prayer but does not give zakah, there is no prayer for him.”"],[8843,"ʿAbd Allah entered upon him while he had set up goods in his house. ʿAbd Allah said: “Conceal the furnishings of your house, for the people are about to be people of the pack-saddle.”"],[8844,"Abdullah said, \"Indeed, a believer is amiable, and there is no good in someone who is not amiable and is not befriended.\""],[8845,"ʿAbd Allah used to seek refuge from four things, saying: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that makes me tyrannical, from poverty that makes me forget, from desire that destroys me, and from deeds that grieve me.”"],[8846,"ʿAbd Allah used to say: “Beware of the difficult modes of speech.”"],[8847,"ʿAbd Allah said to his companions when they came to him: “Do you sit together?” They said: “We do not abandon that.” He said: “Do you visit one another?” They said: “Yes, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman. Indeed, a man among us misses his brother, so he walks seeking him to the farthest end of Kufa until he meets him.” He said: “You will remain in good as long as you do that.”"],[8848,"“Do not eat from cheese except what the Muslims and the People of the Book have made.”"],[8849,"“When ʿAbd Allah stood in prayer, he lowered his voice, his hand, and his gaze.”"],[8850,"ʿAbd Allah did not give a sermon in Kufa except that I attended it. I heard him one day when he was asked about a man who divorces eight times and similar things. He said: “It is as it is said.” Then he said: “Indeed, Allah ﷻ sent down His Book and clarified its clarification. Whoever comes to the matter from its proper direction, it is clarified for him. Whoever opposes, then by Allah, we cannot endure all your opposition.”"],[8851,"And he said: “Fasting three days of every month.”"],[8852,"“Fasting three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest.”"],[8853,"Abdullah used to say after the rukuʿ: “O Allah, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever else You will. O You worthy of praise and glory. There is none to withhold what You give and none to give what You withhold, and no possessor of riches can benefit from You his riches.”"],[8854,"“The distance between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years.”"],[8855,"That he said: “Between the lowest heaven and the one above it is a journey of five hundred years, and between each heaven is a journey of five hundred years, and between the seventh heaven and the Footstool (Kursi) is a journey of five hundred years, and between the Footstool and the water is a journey of five hundred years, and the Throne is above the water, and Allah ﷻ is above the Throne, and He knows what you are upon.”"],[8856,"The sun rises from the depths of hell between two devil horns, and it does not rise in the sky as a cinder unless a gate from the gates of fire is opened. When the heat intensifies, all of its gates are opened."],[8857,"Abdullah saw a man with some dirhams and said: “What will you do with them?” He replied: “I will buy some clarified butter with them.” He said: “Give them to your wife to place under her mattress, then buy meat with a dirham every day.”"],[8858,"“Indeed Allah ﷻ has distributed your characters among you just as He has distributed your provisions among you. And indeed Allah gives wealth to those He loves and those He does not love, but He does not give faith except to those He loves. So if Allah loves a servant, He grants him faith. So whoever is not guaranteed to spend his wealth, and fears the enemy to fight him, and fears the night to endure it, let him increase in saying: There is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah.”"],[8859,"Abdullah said: “Do you know how Islam diminishes?” They said: “As the dye of a garment fades, as a mount loses weight, and as a dirham becomes worn from long use.” He said: “That is part of it, but more than that is the death or departure of the scholars.”"],[8860,"The Bridge (Sirat) will be placed across the surface of Hell, like the edge of a sharpened sword, slippery and treacherous. Upon it will be hooks of fire by which people will be snatched. Some will be held back and fall into it, and some will be thrown down. Among them are those who will pass like lightning and will not be caught, and that one will be saved. Then like the wind and will not be caught, and that one will be saved. Then like the galloping of a horse, then like the running of a man, then like the quick walking of a man, then like the walking of a man, until the last of them will be a man whom the Fire has scorched and has met with evil in it, until Allah admits him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy. Then it will be said to him: ‘Wish and ask.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might?’ Then it will be said to him: ‘Wish and ask.’ He said: Until when his wishes are exhausted, He will say: ‘You shall have what you asked for and the like of it along with it.’ He said: And Abu Salih narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah who said: ‘And ten times the like of it along with it.’”"],[8861,"A man from Bajilah came to Abdullah and said: “I have married a virgin slave girl, and I fear that she may dislike me.” Abdullah said: “Indeed affection is from Allah, and dislike is from Satan, so that he may make hateful to him what Allah has made lawful for him. So when you enter upon her, tell her to pray two rakʿahs behind you.” Al-Aʿmash said: I mentioned this to Ibrahim, and he said: Abdullah said: “And say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me. O Allah, provide me from them and provide them from me. O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in good, and separate us when You separate us to good.”"],[8862,"“I have married a woman and I fear dislike.” He said: “When you bring her, pray two rakʿahs and say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me. O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in good, and separate us when You separate us to good.”"],[8863,"That he says: “Indeed Allah has commanded such and such and forbidden such and such,” and Allah ﷻ will say to him: “You have lied,” or he says: “Indeed Allah has forbidden such and such and made lawful such and such,” and Allah will say to him: “You have lied.”"],[8864,"“The example of one who persists in prayer is like one who knocks at a door. Whoever persists in knocking at the door, it is likely to be opened for him.”"],[8865,"Abdullah said: “As long as you are in prayer, you are knocking at the door of the King. Whoever knocks often at the door of the King, it is likely to be opened for him.”"],[8866,"\"The virtue of night prayer over day prayer is like the virtue of secret charity over public charity.\""],[8867,"ʿAbdullah: \"The virtue of night prayer over day prayer is like the virtue of secret charity over public charity.\""],[8868,"ʿAbdullah: \"The master of months is Ramadan, and the master of days is Friday.\""],[8869,"ʿAbdullah recited this verse: {On the day the earth will be changed to a different earth, and the heavens, and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Subduer.} He said: \"An earth will be brought like an ingot of silver, on which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed. The first matter judged among people on it will be regarding blood.\""],[8870,"\"Al-awwāh means the merciful.\""],[8871,"On the authority of ʿAbdullah regarding His saying: {Indeed Abraham was compassionate (awwāh), forbearing.} He said: \"Al-awwāh means the merciful.\""],[8872,"\"It means the one who supplicates much.\""],[8873,"\"O Abu Abdurrahman, what is lamentation?\" said Ar-Raheem. He replied, \"What is extravagant?\" He said, \"What is wasteful expenditure.\" He then asked, \"What is aid?\" He replied, \"What do people cooperate with each other in, meaning the difficulties.\""],[8874,"\"Spending wealth in an unlawful way,\" and he asked him about al-awwāh; he said: \"The merciful.\""],[8875,"To ʿAbdullah: \"Whom should we ask if we do not ask you?\" So ʿAbdullah felt compassion for him and said: \"What is al-awwāh?\" He said: \"The merciful.\" He said: \"What is al-ummah?\" He said: \"The one who knows good.\" He said: \"What is al-qānit?\" He said: \"The obedient.\" He said: \"What is al-māʿūn?\" He said: \"What people share among themselves.\" He said: \"What is al-tabdhīr?\" He said: \"Spending wealth in something other than its rightful due.\""],[8876,"\"Spending in something other than what is right.\""],[8877,"\"It is spending in something other than what is right.\""],[8878,"We, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, used to say that al-māʿūn is the bucket, the cooking pot, and the axe, which are indispensable to them."],[8879,"In his saying, \"Al-Ma'un\", he said: \"the axe, the pot, and the bucket.\""],[8880,"Regarding His saying {and withhold the small kindnesses}, he said: \"It is wealth whose right is not given.\" I said: \"Ibn Masʿūd says: 'It is the good things people exchange among themselves.'\" He said: \"That is what I am telling you.\""],[8881,"\"Every good deed is charity. At the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to consider the small kindness to be lending the bucket and the cooking pot and the like of that.\""],[8882,"\"We used to consider the small kindness to be the axe, the cooking pot, and the bucket.\""],[8883,"Regarding His saying {Indeed the hypocrites are in the lowest depths of the Fire}, he said: \"Coffins of iron that close over them.\""],[8884,"Regarding His saying {a dwelling place and a repository}, he said: \"The dwelling is the womb and the repository is the earth in which one dies.\""],[8885,"ʿAbdullāh said: \"Its repository is in this world and its dwelling is in the womb.\""],[8886,"In his statement, \"and from the cattle as pack animals and bedding,\" he said, \"The pack animals are what are carried by camels, and the bedding refers to the young ones.\""],[8887,"In his saying, \"Do they wait except for the angels to come to them, or for your Lord to come, or for some signs of your Lord to come on the day when some signs of your Lord come? On that day, belief will not benefit a soul that did not believe before.\" He said, \"The rising of the sun with the moon from its setting place is like the meeting of two companions.\""],[8888,"In His statement {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord will come, no soul's faith will benefit it}, He said, \"The rising of the sun from its west.\""],[8889,"\"Spending on what is not its right.\""],[8890,"Regarding His saying {then there is no sin upon them if they lay aside their garments, not displaying adornment}, he said: \"The outer garment.\""],[8891,"About this verse: {And do not think those who have been killed in the way of Allah} up to {they are provided for}, he said: \"The souls of the martyrs are with Allah ﷻ like green birds with lanterns hanging from the Throne, roaming in Paradise wherever they wish.\" He said: Then your Lord looked over them and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Our Lord, are we not roaming in Paradise wherever we wish?\" He said: Then He looked over them a second time and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Our Lord, are we not roaming in Paradise wherever we wish?\" Then He looked over them a third time and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Restore our souls to our bodies so that we may fight in Your way and be killed once again.\" He said: \"So He fell silent regarding them.\""],[8892,"Regarding His saying {its fuel is people and stones}, he said: \"Stones of sulfur that Allah ﷻ keeps with Himself however He wills and as He wills.\""],[8893,"Regarding His saying {and say 'ḥiṭṭah'}, he said: They said 'ḥinṭah,' a red grain with a hair-like awn in it. That is His saying {But those who wronged changed the saying to other than what was said to them}."],[8894,"Regarding His saying {But whoever hastens on in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, then there is no sin upon him}, he said: \"He is forgiven.\""],[8895,"These verses were sent down from the end of al-Baqarah: {The Messenger believes} from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[8896,"The verse after it abrogated it: {To it belongs what it earns, and upon it is what it acquires}."],[8897,"Indeed this path is attended; devils attend it, saying: 'O servants of God, this is the way, so hold fast to the rope of God, for the straight path is the Book of God.'"],[8898,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying {And hold fast to the rope of God all together}: ʿAbdullāh said, 'The Qurʾan.'"],[8899,"'The rope of God ﷻ is the congregation.'"],[8900,"In his statement, \"Those who remember Allah while standing, sitting, and lying on their sides,\" he said, \"If you are unable to pray standing, then sitting, and if not, then lying down.\""],[8901,"ʿAbdullāh said: In the Book of God there are two verses; no servant commits a sin then recites them and seeks God's forgiveness except that God forgives him: {And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember God and seek forgiveness for their sins—and who forgives sins except God?} and His saying {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks God's forgiveness, will find God Forgiving, Merciful}."],[8902,"From ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd regarding His saying {And married women, except what your right hands possess}: ʿAlī said, 'The polytheist women, when they are taken captive, become lawful for him.' Ibn Masʿūd said, 'The polytheist women and the Muslim women.'"],[8903,"In his saying \"And the one on his side\" he said, \"The woman.\""],[8904,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying {And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment}: he said, 'The day of Badr,' and {the greater punishment, that they might return}: he said, 'Those of them who remain, that they might repent and return.'"],[8905,"Indeed it is written in the Torah for those whose sides forsake their beds: what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has conceived; and indeed it is in the Qurʾan: {No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for the eyes}."],[8906,"'Indeed the dung beetle is tormented in its burrow because of the sins of the children of Adam.' Then he recited: {If God were to take people to task for what they have earned, He would not leave upon its back any creature}."],[8907,"In His saying, \"And the angels lined up in rows\" He said, \"The angels.\" In His saying, \"And those who drive away with a firm command\" He said, \"The angels.\" In His saying, \"And those who recite the remembrance\" He said, \"The angels.\" He said, \"The angels.\""],[8908,"\"Indeed, in the seven heavens, there is not a single space the width of a handspan except that it has an angel's forehead or feet standing [in worship]. Then, He recited, 'Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an and indeed, We will be its guardian.'\""],[8909,"That he said: {Entrust her to me}."],[8910,"Regarding His saying {Our Lord, You have caused us to die twice and given us life twice}: he said, 'It is like the one in al-Baqarah: {You were dead, then He gave you life, then He will cause you to die, then He will give you life, then to Him you will be returned}.'"],[8911,"We were sitting in the mosque when a man entered narrating to us: He said, “On the Day of Resurrection a smoke will come and seize the hearing of the hypocrites, and it will seize the believers like a cold.” So we entered upon ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd and narrated it to him while he was reclining. He sat up and said, “O people, whoever knows something, let him speak it; and whoever does not know, let him say, ‘Allāh knows best,’ for it is part of a man’s knowledge to say about what he does not know, ‘Allāh knows best.’ Allāh said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of those who pretend} (38:86). I shall narrate to you about the smoke: when Quraysh became obstinate and delayed in accepting Islam, the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ supplicated against them, saying, ‘O Allāh, help me against them with seven years like the seven years of Yūsuf.’ Then a famine struck them until everything was destroyed, until they ate carrion and bones, until a man would see between him and the sky something like smoke. That is His saying: {So watch for the Day when the sky will bring a visible smoke, covering the people; this is a painful punishment. Our Lord, remove from us the punishment; indeed we are believers} (44:10–12). It was removed from them, but they returned to their disbelief, so He seized them on the Day of Badr. That is His saying: {The Day We shall seize with the greatest seizure; indeed We shall take retribution} (44:16). He said, ‘The greatest seizure is the Day of Badr.’”"],[8912,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd [said]: “Five have passed: the smoke, the moon, the Byzantines, the seizure, and the unavoidable punishment.”"],[8913,"Regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “That is Jibrīl ﷺ in a green silk robe that filled what is between the heaven and the earth.”"],[8914,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He saw a green silk canopy that blocked the horizon.”"],[8915,"Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, they said: Shuʿbah informed us, from Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He saw a green silk canopy that blocked the horizon of the sky.”"],[8916,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “A green silk canopy from Paradise that blocked the horizon.”"],[8917,"In his saying, \"{Indeed, he (Muhammad) saw of the greatest signs of his Lord],\" he said, \"Muhammad ﷺ saw Gabriel in his true form, with six hundred wings, and not one wing but it filled the space between the east and the west.\""],[8918,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He has six hundred wings.”"],[8919,"In his statement \"{§By the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary}\" he said, \"The reward of Paradise includes palaces of silk and brocade.\""],[8920,"“A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood. The poisonous wind from which the jinn were created is one of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam. This fire of yours is one of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam.”"],[8921,"“Coral is the red bead.”"],[8922,"From ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd regarding His saying: {O you who believe, do not take as allies a people with whom Allāh is angry; they have despaired of the Hereafter} (60:13): “They do not believe in it and will not be rewarded. This is the disbeliever when he dies and sees his reward and looks upon it.”"],[8923,"Regarding this verse: {And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his own soul — it is those who will be successful} (59:9). “I am a man who has not been able to prevent anything from coming out of me, and I feared that this verse might have afflicted me.” ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd said, “You have mentioned miserliness, and what an evil thing miserliness is. As for what Allāh mentioned, it is not as you said. That is when you deliberately take the wealth of another or the wealth of your brother and consume it.”"],[8924,"In his statement \"حُسُومًا,\" he said \"مُتَتَابِعَاتٌ.\""],[8925,"Regarding His saying: {Its seal is musk} (83:26), he said, “It is not a seal with which it is sealed, but rather its mixture is musk. Have you not seen a woman among your women say, ‘Its mixture is of such-and-such perfume’?”"],[8926,"From ʿAbd Allah [regarding] {the receding stars, the running [stars]} (Q 81:15–16): “What are they, O ʿAmr?” He said: I said, “Cattle.” He said, “And that is what I think.”"],[8927,"From ʿAbd Allah [regarding] {And recite to them the story of him to whom We gave Our signs} (Q 7:175): “He is Balʿam, and it is also said Balʿām.”"],[8928,"“The sky.”"],[8929,"I said, “As for the reward, we have come to know it. So what is the ghanīmah?” He said, “Forty dirhams from every person.”"],[8930,"ʿAbd Allah: “Indeed, before the Hour there will be the harj.” Abu al-Aḥwaṣ said: al-harj is killing."],[8931,"“The price for which Yūsuf was bought was twenty dirhams. And his family, when he sent for them while they were in Egypt, were ninety-three people: their men were prophets and their women were ṣiddīqāt. By God, they did not leave with Mūsā until they numbered six hundred and seventy thousand.”"],[8932,"ʿAbd Allah: “Indeed, among the women there are five verses [or signs] for which I would not trade the world and all it contains. And I have come to know that when the scholars come across them, they recognize them: {If you avoid the major sins that you are forbidden, We will expiate your evil deeds and admit you to a noble entrance} (Q 4:31); and His saying {Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] the weight of an atom; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward} (Q 4:40); and {Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners should be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills} (Q 4:48); and {If only they had, when they wronged themselves, come to you and asked Allah’s forgiveness, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Accepting of repentance, Merciful} (Q 4:64); and {Whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks Allah’s forgiveness will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful} (Q 4:110).”"],[8933,"Abdullah replied, \"Indeed, in the Qur'an there are two verses that if a servant commits a sin and then recites them and seeks forgiveness from Allah, he will be forgiven.\" They asked him about these verses, but he did not inform them. Alqamah and Al-Aswad said to each other, \"Let us go with him.\" So they went to the house, took the Mushaf (book), and started reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. They said, \"We did not see them.\" Then they continued reciting until they reached the verse, \"And whoever does evil or wrongs himself but then seeks forgiveness from Allah, he will find Allah forgiving and merciful.\" They said, \"This is one.\" Then they continued reciting Surah Al-Imran until they reached the verse, \"And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who can forgive sins except Allah? And [who] do not persist in what they have done while they know.\" They said, \"This is the other.\" Then they closed the book and went to Abdullah and asked, \"Are these the two verses?\" He replied, \"Yes.\""],[8934,"ʿAbd Allah: “A man will continue to be in spaciousness in his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood. When he sheds unlawful blood, modesty is stripped from him.”"],[8935,"In His saying \"upon yourselves be it\" He ﷻ said, \"This is not the time for it, so say it if it is accepted from you. But if it is rejected from you, then it is upon yourselves. It will not harm you if someone goes astray.\""],[8936,"In his saying {On the day of Furqan, the day the two groups met}, he said, \"It was on the seventeenth night of Ramadan.\""],[8937,"Seek the night of Al-Qadr in the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first nights of Ramadan, during the pre-dawn of the day of Badr, the day of the great distinction, the day the two groups met. It cannot occur except in an odd-numbered night."],[8938,"ʿAbd Allah: “Test the hypocrites by three things: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he makes a covenant he betrays it. And Allah sent down confirmation of that in His Book: {And among them are those who made a covenant with Allah: if He gives us from His bounty} (Q 9:75) to the end of the verse.”"],[8939,"“The Qur’an and honey are two cures.”"],[8940,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {Those whom they call upon seek the means of nearness to their Lord} (Q 17:57): “There were people who used to worship them. Then those who had been worshipping them accepted Islam, while those who had been worshipped did not know. So Allah ﷻ rebuked them for that,” and he said: {Those whom they call upon seek the means of nearness to their Lord} (Q 17:57)."],[8941,"In His saying \"And whoever desires other than Islam as a religion - never will it be accepted from him, and he, in the Hereafter, will be among the losers\" (Quran 3:85), Allah warns against deviation and wrongdoing. He declares that those who plan or intend to commit a sin, but have not executed it, will not be held accountable until they actually commit the sin. Likewise, those who plan or intend to commit a sin and execute it only in private will not be punished by death until they are given a taste of painful punishment by Allah."],[8942,"\"Allah [God] ﷻ [may He be exalted] [has created] men [who are] not distracted by trade or selling [from] the remembrance of Allah.\""],[8943,"“Allah sends the wind, and it carries the water, and a cloud passes and lets it down as a milch camel lets down its milk, then it rains.”"],[8944,"“I do not analogize anything with anything. No foot slips after it has been firmly planted.”"],[8945,"From Salama b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak, that ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud ؓ melted silver from the public treasury, then sent word to the people of the mosque and said: “Whoever wants to look at molten metal, let him look at this.”"],[8946,"He entered the public treasury and called for the scraps that were in it. He lit a fire under them until they melted, then said: “Where is the one asking about al-muhl (molten metal)? This is al-muhl.”"],[8947,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding {And there is none of you but will pass over it}: “Passing over it means the sirat (bridge).”"],[8948,"That Marwan said regarding {And We gave him his family and the like of them with them}: “He received a family other than his own.” Ibn Masʿud said: “Rather, he received his own family themselves and the like of them with them.”"],[8949,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding {And Dhū al-Nūn, when he went away in anger}: “He was a slave who fled from his master.”"],[8950,"When those who will remain in the Fire forever are left, they will be placed in coffins of Fire containing nails of Fire. He said that two or three times. They will see no one in the Fire being punished besides them. Then ʿAbd Allah recited: {For them therein is sighing, and they therein will not hear.}"],[8951,"“They are the akhtān (sons-in-law / in-laws).”"],[8952,"“Al-hafada are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[8953,"“They are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[8954,"ʿAbd Allah said to me: “Do you know what hafada are?” I said, “Yes, they are a man’s helpers from his children and his children’s children.” He said, “No, they are the aṣhār (in-laws).”"],[8955,"I used to hold the mushaf for ʿAbd Allah. When he came to this verse: {And He has made for you from your spouses sons and hafada}, ʿAbd Allah said to me: “Do you know what al-hafada are?” I said, “A man’s servants.” He said, “No, they are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[8956,"In his saying \"{He had sons and daughters},\" he said \"The sisters are the daughters of the paternal uncle.\""],[8957,"God ﷻ indeed supports the religion with the wicked man."],[8958,"{The devouts}[Quran 9:112] – “the fasting ones.”"],[8959,"From ʿAbdullah regarding {And how many a prophet there was with whom fought many devoted men}[Quran 3:146]. He said, “Thousands.”"],[8960,"“The path of good and evil.”"],[8961,"\"That disbelief.\""],[8962,"“The unlawful is bribery in religion.”"],[8963,"“Bribery in judgment is disbelief, and among the people it is unlawful.”"],[8964,"“That is disbelief.”"],[8965,"From ʿAbdullah regarding their saying {Our Lord, whoever brought this upon us, increase for him a double punishment in the Fire}[Quran 38:61]. He said, “Vipers and snakes.”"],[8966,"In his saying \"{زِدْنَاهُمْ عَذَابًا فَوْقَ الْعَذَابِ}\", he said, \"Increase their punishment with the extension of their fangs, like the long palm tree.\""],[8967,"Regarding His saying {We increased them with punishment over punishment}[Quran 16:88]. He said, “Scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees.”"],[8968,"Regarding the saying of the Blessed and Exalted {Then they will meet deviation}[Quran 19:59]. He said, “A valley in Hell.”"],[8969,"“A river in Hell.”"],[8970,"“Al-Ghayy is a river in Hell into which those who followed lusts are thrown.”"],[8971,"A valley in Jahannam of pus."],[8972,"A river in Jahannam and a valley in Jahannam."],[8973,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they will soon meet ghayyā}: \"A valley in Jahannam, deep-bottomed, foul in food.\""],[8974,"It is a river in the Fire; it has a ghayy."],[8975,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they will soon meet ghayyā}: \"A river in Jahannam called Ghayy.\""],[8976,"Wayl is a valley in Jahannam of pus."],[8977,"From ʿAbd Allah: {and not to display their adornment except what is apparent of it}—he said: \"Clothing.\""],[8978,"From ʿAbd Allah: {and not to display their adornment except what is apparent of it}—he said: \"Adornment is the earring, the armlet, the anklet, and the necklace.\""],[8979,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {and not to display their adornment}: \"Adornment is the bracelet, the armlet, the anklet, the ring, the earring, and the necklace; and what is apparent of it is clothing and the outer wrap.\""],[8980,"From ʿAbd Allah: {they put their hands into their mouths}—he said: \"They bit them.\""],[8981,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they put their hands into their mouths}: \"They bit their fingers in rage.\""],[8982,"From Abdullah with regards to his statement \"And there is none of you except that he will come to it,\" he said, \"The path.\""],[8983,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {the Fire will scorch their faces while they are grimacing therein}: \"Have you not seen the heads, singed, with their teeth showing and their lips shriveled?\""],[8984,"About this verse: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “He will be collared with a bald-headed serpent that pecks at his head.”"],[8985,"Whoever has wealth and does not pay its zakat, on the Day of Resurrection it will be made into a collar for him — a bald-headed serpent that pecks at his head, saying: “I am your wealth with which you were miserly. {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection}.”"],[8986,"His wealth will come as a huge serpent that pecks at his head, saying: “I am your wealth with which you were miserly,” and he will be collared with it."],[8987,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Sublime: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “He will be collared with a bald-headed serpent with two fangs that pecks at his head, and he will say: ‘What have I to do with you?’ It will say: ‘I am your wealth with which you were miserly.’”"],[8988,"About His saying: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “A serpent that bites his jaw.”"],[8989,"\"Allah says, 'Establish the prayer at the decline of the sun.'\""],[8990,"The sun’s dulūk is its setting. The Arabs say, when the sun has set, idhā dalakat al-shams: the sun has declined and departed."],[8991,"“Its dulūk is its setting.”"],[8992,"“The sun’s dulūk is its setting.”"],[8993,"ʿAbdullāh prayed Maghrib and when he finished we kept turning around. He said: “Why are you turning around?” We said: “We think the sun is still risen.” He said: “This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer.” Then he recited: {Establish the prayer at the sun’s dulūk until the darkness of the night} — so this is the sun’s dulūk and this is the darkness of the night."],[8994,"ʿAbdullāh prayed one day and a man kept looking to see whether the sun had set. ʿAbdullāh said: “What are you looking at? This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer. Allah, Mighty and Sublime, says: {Establish the prayer at the sun’s dulūk until the darkness of the night} — so this is the sun’s dulūk and this is the darkness of the night.”"],[8995,"We were with Abdullah when he finished and he said, \"By the One besides whom there is no deity, this is the time for this prayer to be performed wherever the sun sets.\""],[8996,"“This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is where the sun has declined and the time of prayer has arrived.”"],[8997,"“The sun’s dulūk is its setting.”"],[8998,"The sun's declining is when it sets."],[8999,"Abdullah used to say: The two guards from the angels of Allah meet – the guard of the night and the guard of the day – at the rising of dawn. And recite if you wish: {And the Qur'an of dawn – indeed, the Qur'an of dawn is ever witnessed}."],[9000,"We were with Abdullah on the road to Makkah. When the sun set, he said: \"This is the darkness of the night.\" Then the call to prayer was given. Then he said: \"This, by Allah besides whom there is no deity, is the time of this prayer.\""],[9001,"The later evening prayer."],[9002,"The later evening prayer."],[9003,"From Abdullah regarding {Indeed, for him is a narrow livelihood}: He said: \"The punishment of the grave.\""],[9004,"Abdullah used to say: When I narrate to you a hadith, I bring you its confirmation from the Book of Allah. Indeed, when a Muslim servant says: 'Praise be to Allah, glory be to Allah, there is no deity but Allah, Allah is greatest, and blessed is Allah,' an angel takes hold of them and places them beneath his wing. Then he ascends with them and does not pass by any assembly of angels except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them until he brings them before the face of the Most Merciful, Exalted is He. Then Abdullah recited: {To Him ascends the good word, and righteous action raises it}."],[9005,"\"When Abdullah informs you of a narration, I confirm it to you. Indeed, when a Muslim servant dies, he is made to sit in his grave and it is said to him, 'Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet?' Allah will make him firm and he will say, 'My Lord is Allah, my religion is Islam, and my Prophet is Muhammad ﷺ .' Then his grave will be expanded for him and illuminated, and it will be opened for him. Then Abdullah recited, 'Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in worldly life and in the Hereafter. And Allah sends astray the wrongdoers.'\""],[9006,"He said: 'Write.' He says: 'O Lord, what should I write?' He says: 'Write whether he is wretched or blessed, male or female, his provision, his trace, and his term.' Then Allah, mighty and sublime is He, reveals to him whatever He wills, and the angel writes. Then Abdullah recited: {Indeed, We created man from a mixed drop to test him}. He said: And Abdullah said: \"The mixed (amshaj) are the veins.\""],[9007,"From Abdullah, he recited this verse: {But you prefer the worldly life}. Then he said: \"Do you know by what thing the worldly life began? For what thing did it prefer the worldly life? The world was hastened for us, and we were given its pleasure and its splendor, while the Hereafter was hidden from us and withheld from us. So we answered the immediate and abandoned the delayed.\""],[9008,"I saw Abdullah scratching out the two protective surahs and saying: \"Why do you add what is not in it?\""],[9009,"He used to scratch out the two protective surahs from his mushaf and say: \"Indeed, they have mixed into it what is not in it.\""],[9010,"He used to scratch out the two protective surahs from the mushaf, saying: \"They are not from the Book of Allah.\""],[9011,"He used to say: Do not mix into the Quran what is not in it. They are only two surahs of seeking refuge with which the Prophet ﷺ sought refuge: “Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak” and “Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind.” And ʿAbdullah used to erase them from the mushaf."],[9012,"He used to scratch out the two muʿawwidhatayn from the mushafs and say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only commanded that refuge be sought by means of them, and he did not use to recite them.”"],[9013,"ʿAbdullah said to him: “It was not proper for it to take hold of you. Atone for your oath and speak of it.” He said: Take the urine of camels that eat arak, meaning that eat arak, and cook it until it thickens, then drink it. And take arak leaves, pound them, and sprinkle them on it. He said: He did so and was cured."],[9014,"ʿAbdullah said: “The people of the lowest part are rulers over the people of its highest part.”"],[9015,"“Guard your children with regard to prayer, and accustom them to good, for good is a habit.”"],[9016,"“Accustom yourselves to good, for good comes only by habit.”"],[9017,"“Indeed your wealth is mine, but I have left it for you.”"],[9018,"“That I equip a whip in the path of Allah is more beloved to me than a Hajj after the Hajj of Islam.”"],[9019,"“The millstone of Islam will turn upon the head of thirty-five, then a great event will occur. If their destruction is in it, then it is likely; otherwise it will be delayed from them for seventy years. Whoever reaches that will see what he disapproves of.” Thus Abu al-Ahwas narrated it as mawquf, and Masruq, ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAbdullah, and al-Baraʾ b. Najiyah raised it."],[9020,"“A man may speak a word to make his companions laugh, and he does not return to his family with anything from it; he falls by it farther than from heaven to earth.”"],[9021,"That he wanted to bequeath more than one-third, so they permitted him. Then they retracted it after he died. ʿAbdullah was asked about that, and he said: “That is the objectionable thing; it is not permissible.”"],[9022,"From ʿAbdullah concerning a man who makes a bequest and the heirs approve, then they retract. ʿAbdullah said: “That is the objectionable thing; it is not permissible.”"],[9023,"Indeed, Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down with it a cure. So adhere to the milk of cows, for they graze upon every kind of tree."],[9024,"Abdullah said, \"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for one disease, the old age. So you should take the milk of cows, as it comes from the entire tree.\""],[9025,"Abdullah used to not consistently observe any act of worship except for performing the Witr prayer before the rak'ah."],[9026,"Abdullah used to not perform the morning prayer regularly, and when he did, he would perform the Witr prayer before the last unit."],[9027,"From two men among the companions of ʿAbd Allah that they used to bring their heads close to ʿAbd Allah in order to hear what he said in his prostration. One of them said: I heard him say, “Glory be to You, there is no god besides You.” The other said: I heard him say, “Glory be to You, there is no Lord besides You.”"],[9028,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say, “The one who is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[9029,"ʿAbd Allah said, “Hasten to the Friday prayers, for Allah ﷻ appears to the people of Paradise every Friday on a hill of camphor, and they will be close to Him according to how quickly they hastened to the Friday prayer. Allah ﷻ will bring about for them something of honor that they had not seen before. Then they will return to their families and narrate to them what Allah has brought about for them.” He said: Then ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque, and there were two men on Friday who had preceded him. So ʿAbd Allah said, “Two men, and I am the third, if Allah wills to bless the third.”"],[9030,"ʿAbd Allah said, “A Muslim man does not mock any state of the world he wakes up in or spends the evening in, without there being distress in his soul.”"],[9031,"\"It is better for one of you to bite on a live coal until it cools down or to hold on to it until it cools down than to say something that Allah has decreed, 'I wish it had not happened'.\""],[9032,"If only ten nights remained of my appointed term, I would love for a woman not to part from me during them."],[9033,"ʿAbd Allah said, “The one who raises his head before the imam raises his head is not safe from his head turning into the head of a dog. And let people who raise their eyes to the sky desist, or their eyesight will be snatched away.”"],[9034,"That he raise his head in prayer before the imam, lest his head turn into the head of a dog. And let people who raise their eyes in prayer desist, or their eyesight will not return to them."],[9035,"ʿAbd Allah said, “A man is not safe, if he raises his head before the imam, from his head turning into the head of a dog. Let people who raise their eyes to the sky desist, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[9036,"“ʿAbd Allah was one of the most generous of people in white garment and one of the best of people in fragrance.”"],[9037,"“ʿAbd Allah was pleased by perfume.”"],[9038,"ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque on Friday wearing clean, beautiful white clothes. He looked at a place where there was space and sat down, not stepping over anyone. He said: The imam came out, and there were two men talking. So he took some pebbles and threw them at them. They looked at him and fell silent. When the imam descended, he said, “Did you not know that you are in prayer?”"],[9039,"that he should take a stipend for it, while the keeper of their spoils...\""],[9040,"ʿAbd Allāh said: \"We are more entitled to it.\" He then sat conversing for a while, then rose and departed. ʿAlqamah went off, and when he reached the bearers of the coffers, he sent after him and summoned him back. He said: \"Are you in need?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Take the wealth.\" When he took it, ʿAbd Allāh said: \"That I should lend wealth twice is dearer to me than that I should give it once in charity.\""],[9041,"“Eat you and your companions a third, send to our Bedouin a third, and give a third in charity.”"],[9042,"“When one of you errs in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct within himself, then complete it accordingly, then prostrate two prostrations after the salutation while seated.”"],[9043,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Whoever doubts or errs in his prayer, let him strive, then prostrate two prostrations.”"],[9044,"Ibn Masʿūd used to say after “Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God”: “Peace be upon us from our Lord.”"],[9045,"About nabīdh? He said: “I do not drink except in something stoppered.” His son said: “Did not Ibn Masʿūd used to drink among you from the green jar?” He said: “Indeed.”"],[9046,"He heard Abdullah bin Mas'ud saying, \"How do you react when you see a group of people or when a group with dirty faces comes to you?\""],[9047,"“This is not the misleading trial, but rather this is a horn of the Devil.”"],[9048,"He said to him: “Rise and enter Paradise.” He turned to him frowning and said: “Have you left me anything?” He said: “Yes, for you is the like of what the sun has risen upon or set upon.”"],[9049,"“Do I not see you, a young man, reciting these two sūrahs in this prayer, while you are young?”"],[9050,"A man came to ʿAbd Allāh perfumed with ḥanūṭ. When he saw him and detected the scent of the perfume, he said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from his evil.” He said: Then he came to him and mentioned to him that he had had intercourse with his wife’s slave-girl. He said: “Apply the legal punishment to me.” He said: “Ask God’s forgiveness and repent to Him, and conceal it upon yourself; and if you are able to free her, then free her.”"],[9051,"ʿAbd Allāh used to pronounce the takbīr when he finished the recitation, then when he finished the qunūt he pronounced the takbīr and bowed."],[9052,"until the shadow of every thing becomes its like,” and he asked him about the time of ʿAsr, and he said, “Pray it while the sun is white and alive,” and he asked about the time of Maghrib, and he said, “When the sun has set.”"],[9053,"ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, “I warm myself with her in winter and cool myself with her in summer.”"],[9054,"Ibn Masʿud “would warm himself with his wife in winter while he was junub and had already performed ghusl, and he would cool himself with her in summer while they were in that state.”"],[9055,"A paternal cousin of his made ilaʾ from his wife for ten days, then he went out and returned after four months had passed, and he had intercourse with his wife. Then he met a man who reminded him of his oath, so he came to Ibn Masʿud and asked him. He made him swear by Allah, “I did not know,” then he sent for his wife and made her swear by Allah ﷻ, “I did not know,” then he ordered him, and he proposed to her on his own behalf."],[9056,"About a man who made a vow and did not name anything, he said, “He frees a slave.”"],[9057,"A young girl was brought to ʿAbd Allah who had stolen and had not yet menstruated, and he did not cut off her hand."],[9058,"ʿAbd Allah: Whoever swears an oath and then says, “If Allah wills,” has made an exception."],[9059,"ʿAbd Allah bought a slave girl from his wife – or from one of his wives – and he stipulated a condition for her, and she stipulated her service. ʿUmar ؓ said, “None of your property is that in which someone else has a stipulation of service.”"],[9060,"ʿAbd Allah said the takbir when he began the prayer, and he said, “Like this,” and Misʿar raised his hands above his chest."],[9061,"ʿAbd Allah stood up in the two rakʿahs and did not sit."],[9062,"My paternal uncle married me to his slave girl, and she bore me children, and now he wants to enslave them. He said, “He has no right to that.”"],[9063,"“He has no right to that.”"],[9064,"“ʿAbd Allāh continued proclaiming the talbiyah until he threw the pebble.”"],[9065,"That he heard ʿAbd Allāh say, while he was bowing: “There is no might and no power except with Allāh.”"],[9066,"ʿAbd Allāh said to a man: “When you ask your Lord for good, do not ask while there is a stone in your hand.”"],[9067,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Enter the morning anointed with oil, fasting.”"],[9068,"That she intended to combine an ʿumrah with her Hajj. She asked ʿAbd Allāh, and he said: “I find these to be only the months of Hajj. Allāh, exalted is He, said: {well-known months}.”"],[9069,"His statement refers to washing the two feet in His saying: {and your feet up to the ankles}."],[9070,"“A man must certainly rub between his fingers in ablution, or the Fire will certainly rub between them.”"],[9071,"“A man must certainly rub between his fingers with purification, or the Fire will certainly rub between them.”"],[9072,"That he said: “Rub between the five fingers, lest Allāh fill them with Fire.”"],[9073,"He said to me: “Cut it off,” while laughing: “Where will you isolate it from yourself? It is only a piece of you.”"],[9074,"“Is it anything but like the tip of your nose?”"],[9075,"“I do not care whether I touched it or the tip of my nose.”"],[9076,"He said: “I do not care whether I touch it or my knee.”"],[9077,"One of them said: “I do not care whether I touch my penis or the tip of my nose,” another said, “my ear,” another said, “my thigh,” and another said, “my knee.”"],[9078,"Ibn Masʿūd prayed while on his stomach there were rumen contents and blood from a slaughtered camel he had slaughtered, and he did not perform ablution."],[9079,"Ibn Masʿūd slaughtered a camel and became smeared with its blood and rumen contents, then the prayer was called, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."],[9080,"Regarding the hide of a dead animal, its tanning is its purification."],[9081,"That I perform ablution from an evil word is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from good food."],[9082,"That I perform ablution from an evil word is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from a good morsel."],[9083,"I perform ablution from an evil word: that is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from good food."],[9084,"ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd, and al-Shaʿbī said regarding a man who sleeps while sitting: “He does not have to perform ablution.”"],[9085,"A man performs ablution on account of intimate touching, touching with his hand, and kissing when he kisses his wife. He used to say regarding this verse: “or you have touched women” — it is groping."],[9086,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said: “Kissing is one of the forms of touching, and from it ablution is required.”"],[9087,"“Touching (mulāmasa) is whatever falls short of intercourse.”"],[9088,"That a man touches his wife's body with desire, there is wudu' required for it."],[9089,"Indeed, Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and takes hold of a hair from his backside, so he thinks that he has broken wind. He should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9090,"he hears a sound."],[9091,"Indeed, Satan surrounds a man during prayer to cut off his prayer from him. When he is unable, he blows in his backside to make him think that he has broken wind. So if he feels any of that, he should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9092,"he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9093,"that he washed the tips of his fingers and rinsed his mouth, then prayed."],[9094,"We were brought a bowl from the house of Ibn Mas'ud containing bread and meat, and we ate while Ibn Mas'ud was with us. He rinsed his mouth and washed his fingers before Maghrib."],[9095,"We were brought a bowl and we ate while 'Abdullah was with us. Then 'Abdullah rinsed his mouth and washed his fingers, then we set off to the Maghrib prayer."],[9096,"Wudu' is only from what comes out, not from what goes in; and fasting is from what goes in, not from what comes out."],[9097,"That 'Abdullah used to wear his leather socks at Fajr prayer and would not remove them until he retired to his bed."],[9098,"That he used to wipe over the socks and the sandals."],[9099,"'Abdullah made the wiping three days for the traveler and one day for the resident."],[9100,"I traveled with Abdullah b. Masud for three days to Madinah, and he did not remove his leather socks."],[9101,"I traveled with Abdullah to Madinah, and he did not remove his leather socks for three days and their nights. Sulayman said: I narrated this hadith of Shaqiq to Ibrahim, and he said: Abu Ubaydah narrated to me from Amr b. al-Harith this hadith."],[9102,"I traveled with Abdullah b. Masud, and he used to wipe over his leather socks for three [days]."],[9103,"For the traveler [is] three days to wipe over the leather socks, and for the resident, a day and a night. And I traveled with Abdullah, and he remained for three days wiping over the leather socks."],[9104,"For the traveler [is] three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night."],[9105,"The traveler wipes over the leather socks for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night."],[9106,"The traveler wipes for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night."],[9107,"A man had smallpox, so Ibn Masud ordered that dust be brought near in a basin or a bowl, and he wiped himself with the dust."],[9108,"If I were in a state of major ritual impurity and then did not find water for a month, I would not pray. Sufyan said: This is not to be acted upon."],[9109,"That he does not perform the major ablution."],[9110,"From Aishah, they said: When the two circumcised parts meet, the major ablution becomes obligatory. Masruq said: She was the most knowledgeable of them regarding that."],[9111,"Sufyan said: And the majority hold that the major ablution is obligatory."],[9112,"As for me, when I reach that point with the woman, I perform ghusl."],[9113,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say: “Any person in a state of janābah who washes with khiṭmī has done what is sufficient.”"],[9114,"If he washes his head while in a state of janābah with khiṭmī, he has done what is sufficient, and it does not harm him not to pour water over it."],[9115,"When one of you washes his head while in a state of janābah with khiṭmī and then performs ghusl after that, let him wash his head with water if he wishes."],[9116,"Ibn Masʿūd used to wash his head with khiṭmī while in a state of janābah, then perform ghusl, and he would not wash his head [with water]."],[9117,"If a person in a state of janābah washes his head with khiṭmī, that suffices him from washing it with water."],[9118,"What I strove to catch first was the opening takbīr at the beginning of the prayer."],[9119,"I strove to catch the beginning of the prayer."],[9120,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī led them in prayer and took off his sandals. ʿAbd Allah said to him: “Why did you take off your sandals? Are you in the sacred valley?”"],[9121,"Abū Mūsā said to him: “Go forward, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, for you are older in age and more learned.” He said: “No, rather you go forward, for we came to you in your home and your mosque.” So Abū Mūsā went forward and took off his sandals. When he had prayed, he said: “What did you intend by taking them off? Are you in the sacred valley of Ṭuwā? I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in leather socks and sandals.”"],[9122,"And he would not prostrate except on the ground."],[9123,"He used to stand on the burdī and prostrate on the ground. We said: “What is the burdī?” He said: “The mat.”"],[9124,"Ibn Masʿud performed prayer over (i.e., wiped over) a leather sock."],[9125,"Ibn Masʿud used to patrol the mosque and would not leave any darkness (person) in it except he would remove him, except a man praying."],[9126,"on his right, and he was not in prayer.”"],[9127,"from this.”"],[9128,"nor your Quran reciters."],[9129,"The prohibition of prayer is the takbir and its release is the taslim. When you have said the salam and a need hastens you, then depart before he turns his face back."],[9130,"He prayed with his companions in his house without an iqamah and said, “The iqamah of the townsman is sufficient.”"],[9131,"Sufyan said, “The iqamah of the town was sufficient for them.”"],[9132,"Abdullah bin Mas'ood saw a man raising his hands to the sky, supplicating while in his prayer. So, Abdullah bin Mas'ood said, \"What does he know? Perhaps his sight may be dazzled before it returns to him.\""],[9133,"When the prayer has been made obligatory, do not leave it for something else."],[9134,"when the sun had declined."],[9135,"ʿAbdullah prayed when the sun had declined. I said to Sulayman, “Zuhr?” He said, “Yes.” Then ʿAbdullah said, “This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the appointed time of this prayer.”"],[9136,"ʿAbdullah used to pray Zuhr while the grasshoppers were leaping in the heat of the sun-baked ground."],[9137,"Ibn Masʿūd used to delay the ʿAṣr prayer."],[9138,"The sun rises between the two horns of a devil. It does not rise even a spear’s length before a gate of the gates of Hell is opened for it. When the day reaches its midpoint, the gates of Hell are opened for it.” He said: So ʿAbdullāh used to forbid us from two prayers during these two times: when it rises until it has risen, and at midday."],[9139,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd used to brighten the dawn prayer (perform it a bit late when light appeared)."],[9140,"ʿAbdullāh used to say: “Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs.” We would pray behind our imam while wearing our clothes, and he would recite a surah from the miʾīn (the long surahs of about a hundred verses), then we would go to ʿAbdullāh and find him still in prayer."],[9141,"Allah the Exalted said: {until the darkness of the night, and the recitation of dawn. Indeed, the recitation of dawn is ever witnessed}."],[9142,"Someone who saw Ibn Masʿūd told me: He prayed Fajr, then sat and did not stand for any prayer until the call for Ẓuhr was made. Then he stood and prayed four (rakʿahs)."],[9143,"None of you should pray with an open gap between him and the qiblah — meaning an opening."],[9144,"Do not pray while there is an open gap between you and the qiblah."],[9145,"...that no one should pass in front of him while he is praying, let him do (what he can to prevent it); for the one passing in front of the praying person has a lesser reward than the one he passes in front of."],[9146,"...that no one should pass in front of him, let him do (what he can); for the one passing in front of the praying person has a lesser reward than the one he passes in front of."],[9147,"...that no one should cause someone to pass in front of him while he is praying, let him do (what he can); for the one passing in front of the praying person is less (in reward) than the one he passes in front of."],[9148,"...that someone should pass in front of you while you are praying, do not let him; for he throws away half of his prayer."],[9149,"that he should prostrate while saying in his prostration, “Labbayka wa saʿdayka (Here I am at Your service, and blessed are You).”"],[9150,"\"Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who take their place in the first rows (of prayer), meaning the advanced row.\""],[9151,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “Do not form rows between the columns, and do not follow a group as your imam while they are conversing.”"],[9152,"ʿAbdullāh said, “Do not follow as your imam a people who are disputing, and do not pray between the columns.”"],[9153,"I heard Ibn Masʿūd saying, “Do not form rows between the pillars, and do not pray while there are people passing in front of you.”"],[9154,"\"I hated praying between the pillars, single or double.\""],[9155,"Ibn Masʿūd used to say the takbīr every time he lowered and raised."],[9156,"Ibn Masʿūd used to raise his hands at the first instance, then did not raise them after that."],[9157,"ʿAbdullāh did not raise his hands in any part of the prayer except in the first takbīrah."],[9158,"When he entered the prayer, he raised his hands, then did not raise them after that."],[9159,"From Ibn Masʿūd ؓ: When they began the prayer, they used to say, “Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You,” before the recitation."],[9160,"He used to say, “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his arrogance, and his poetry.”"],[9161,"His whisper means Satan, his sneezing means madness, his snorting means arrogance, and his breath means poetry."],[9162,"\"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud did not pronounce aloud 'Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Rahim' (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) nor 'A'udhu billahi min ash-Shaytan ir-Rajim' (I seek refuge in Allah from Satan, the accursed) nor 'Ameen'.\""],[9163,"Ibn Masʿūd used to begin his prayer with {All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."],[9164,"Ibn Masʿūd used to recite in the first two rakʿahs of the noon and afternoon prayers the Opening of the Book and a surah in each rakʿah, and in the last two rakʿahs the Opening of the Book."],[9165,"Ibn Masʿūd led them in the ʿIshāʾ prayer and recited forty verses of al-Anfāl, then in the second rakʿah he recited a sūrah from the Mufaṣṣal."],[9166,"Ibn Masʿūd led us in the ʿIshāʾ prayer. He began with Sūrat al-Anfāl until when he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, he bowed. Then in the second rakʿah he recited two sūrahs from the Mufaṣṣal."],[9167,"ʿAbdullāh recited in the later ʿIshāʾ in the first rakʿah {They ask you about the spoils of war} until he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, then he bowed. Then in the second he recited a sūrah from the Mufaṣṣal? He said: Yes."],[9168,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd led us in the later ʿIshāʾ prayer. He began al-Anfāl and recited until when he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, he bowed. Then he stood and in the second rakʿah recited a sūrah."],[9169,"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, should I recite behind the imam? He said: “Listen attentively to the Qurʾān, for in the prayer there is enough preoccupation, and the imam will suffice you for that.”"],[9170,"That he should be an imam who does not recite.”"],[9171,"Ibn Masʿūd would not recite behind the imam,” and Ibrāhīm used to follow that."],[9172,"Ibn Masʿūd would not recite behind the imam,” and Ibrāhīm used to follow that."],[9173,"“When the imam falters, do not correct him, for that is speech.”"],[9174,"He said, \"It is a statement.\""],[9175,"Alqamah and Al-Aswad said: \"We prayed behind Abdullah, and when he went into the bowing position, he placed his hands on his knees and struck our hands.\" So we did the same."],[9176,"Ibn Masʿūd bowed and placed his hands together, putting them between his knees.”"],[9177,"ʿAbdullāh would place his hands together when bowing, putting his hands between his knees and spreading his forearms on his thighs.”"],[9178,"ʿAbdullāh would say in his bowing: My Lord, forgive me.”"],[9179,"To say in his bowing and prostration, \"Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, la ilaha ghairuka.\""],[9180,"Abū al-Aswad said: ʿAbd Allāh used to say in his prostration: “Glory be to You; there is no lord other than You.” Shaddād said: He used to say: “Glory be to You; there is no god other than You.”"],[9181,"“I entered the mosque and found ʿAbd Allāh praying. He bowed, and I began [reciting] Sūrat al-Aʿrāf and finished it before he prostrated.”"],[9182,"When [the imam] says: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” then let the one behind him say: “Our Lord, to You belongs praise.”"],[9183,"When [the imam] says: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” then let the one behind him say: “Our Lord, to You belongs praise.”"],[9184,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate resting on his hip or lying on his side, for if he perfects the prostration, all his bones prostrate.”"],[9185,"“When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate lying on his side or resting on his hip, for if he perfects the prostration, every limb of his prostrates.”"],[9186,"“He rises on the balls of his feet in the first and second rakʿah.”"],[9187,"“ʿAbd Allāh used to rise on the balls of his feet.”"],[9188,"That Ibn Mas'ood used to do it."],[9189,"“ʿAbd Allāh, when he said takbīr upon raising his head from the prostration, would stand up with it.”"],[9190,"ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “Do not tie back [your hair], for your hair prostrates, and for every hair you have a reward.” He said: “I only tied it back so that it would not get dusty.” He said: “If it gets dusty, that is better for you.”"],[9191,"ʿAbd Allāh passed by a man prostrating who had tied back his hair. He undid his tied hair and let it loose, then waited until he finished praying. ʿAbd Allāh said: “Indeed your hair prostrates with you, so do not tie it back, for for every hair of it you have a reward.” The man said: “I feared it would get dusty.” ʿAbd Allāh said: “If it gets dusty, that is better for you.”"],[9192,"“ʿAbd Allāh would not turn around in prayer. If his need was to his right, he would turn away to his right, and if his need was to his left, he would turn away to his left.”"],[9193,"He used to say: 'When the imam has said the salam, then depart wherever your need takes you, to the right or to the left, and do not turn around like the turning around of a donkey.'"],[9194,"on his right.'"],[9195,"'When the imam has said the salam, then let him stand or turn away from his place.' I said: Is it sufficient for him to turn away from his place while facing the qiblah? He said: 'The turning away is to go west or east, according to more than one.'"],[9196,"that he 'when he had said the salam, he would get up from his place or turn away to the east or to the west.'"],[9197,"'When the imam has said the salam and a man has a need, he should not wait for him, once he has said the salam, to turn his face toward him, for the ending of the prayer is the salam.' And ʿAbdullah, when he had said the salam, would not delay in getting up or moving from his place and turning his face toward them."],[9198,"'When you are behind the imam, do not bow until he bows, and do not prostrate until he prostrates, and do not raise your head before him. Then when the imam has finished and has not gotten up or turned away, and you have a need, go and leave him, for your prayer is complete.'"],[9199,"From Abu Khalid, one of the companions of ʿAbdullah: A man came to ʿAbdullah and said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, so-and-so recites the Quran while bowing, and he recites while prostrating. ʿAbdullah said: 'Indeed, there are men who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. When it enters the heart and becomes firmly rooted in it, then it benefits.'"],[9200,"as if it were a thrown garment."],[9201,"'Make the prayer settled.' Mansur was asked what he meant by that, and he said: 'That one should be still in his prayer when he bows and when he prostrates.'"],[9202,"ʿAbdullah: 'Be settled in the prayer,' meaning: be still and at ease."],[9203,"\"God continues to look favorably upon His servant with His face as long as he does not turn away or speak.\""],[9204,"'As for this man, he has deviated from the Sunnah. If he had alternated between the two, it would have been more beloved to me.'"],[9205,"'Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught the prayer.'"],[9206,"\"Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught [the prayer].\""],[9207,"He informed him from ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud that they both said, \"Whoever does not catch the rakʿah should not count the prostration.\""],[9208,"\"Whoever misses the bowing should not count the prostration.\""],[9209,"I and ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque while the people were bowing, so we bowed, then we walked until we joined the people. They raised their heads and we raised [ours] with them. When we finished the prayer, I stood up to make up [what I missed], but ʿAbd Allah spoke to me and said, \"You have completed the prayer.\""],[9210,"I and Ibn Masʿud entered the mosque while the imam was bowing, so we bowed, then we moved on until we stood in line with the row. When the imam finished, I stood up to make up [the prayer], but he said, \"You caught it.\""],[9211,"And he said, \"Indeed you caught it.\""],[9212,"\"... that you bow before reaching the row.\""],[9213,"\"When one of you bows and then walks to the row before they raise their heads, he counts it; but if they raise their heads before he reaches the row, he does not count it.\""],[9214,"\"You have caught it, if Allah wills.\""],[9215,"ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque and [someone] entered with him. The imam bowed, so we bowed before we reached the row, then we reached the row when the imam said 'Samʿa Allahu li-man hamidah.' When the imam said the taslim, ʿAbd Allah's companion stood up to make up [the prayer], but ʿAbd Allah grabbed his garment and said, \"Sit down, for you have caught the prayer.\""],[9216,"\"Is not the prayer the most worthy thing I hasten to?\""],[9217,"\"When a man doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he prayed three or two [rakʿahs], he should base it on the more certain of the two, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[9218,"He said: 'He should seek the most correct course and prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness.'"],[9219,"That ʿAbd Allah used to say regarding forgetfulness: He should seek the correct course and prostrate two prostrations while seated after the taslim."],[9220,"Forgetfulness is when one stands where one should sit, or sits where one should stand, or says the salam after two rakʿahs. Then he should complete his prayer and prostrate two prostrations while seated, reciting the tashahhud in them."],[9221,"When you stand or sit or say the salam, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recite the tashahhud, then say the salam."],[9222,"I am amazed at these two men. As for the one who lets his lower garment hang down, Allah will not look at him; and as for the other, Allah will not accept his prayer."],[9223,"Yes. As for this one, Allah will not look at him, meaning the one who lets his lower garment hang down; and as for this one, Allah will not accept from him, meaning the one who does not complete his bowing or his prostration."],[9224,"That he saw a bedouin praying with his lower garment hanging down, and he said: 'The one who lets his lower garment hang down in prayer is not in a state of what is lawful or unlawful with Allah ﷻ.'"],[9225,"He should make what he catches with the imam the end of his prayer."],[9226,"Each has done well, and we will do as Masruq did."],[9227,"Both are good, and I will do as the one who recited in the two rakʿahs did."],[9228,"That Jundub and Masruq caught one rakʿah of the Maghrib prayer. When the imam said the salam, they stood to make up the remaining rakʿahs. Jundub stood in the second rakʿah, while Masruq sat in both of them. They mentioned this to Ibn Masʿud, and he said: 'Both of you have done well, and I will do as Masruq did.'"],[9229,"Jundub and Masruq prayed Maghrib in a mosque, having caught only one rakʿah with the imam. They stood to make up the rest. Masruq sat in the second rakʿah, and Jundub stood in the first rakʿah of the make-up. They came to ʿAbd Allah and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Both of you have done well, and do as Masruq did.'"],[9230,"Masruq and Jundab reached the imam after they had missed a rakʿah. Masruq did not recite, while Jundab recited. They mentioned that to ʿAbd Allah, and he said: \"Neither of you has fallen short in the matter, but the correct course is what Masruq did.\""],[9231,"Prayer has an appointed time, like the appointed time of Hajj."],[9232,"Straighten your rows, for Satan passes through them like small pebbles, or like the young of pebbles."],[9233,"Do not bow before the imam, do not rise before him, do not prostrate before him, and do not raise [your head] before him."],[9234,"The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he rises, rise. Do not get ahead of him when he bows, nor when he rises, nor when he prostrates. If you are concerned about catching up with what he has preceded you in, then he prostrates before you and rises before you, so you will catch up with that."],[9235,"We perform Hajj to the House of our Lord and settle debts, and he is like the sandgrouse swooping down. ʿAbd Allah said: \"We have not heard of this in the latter religion; this is nothing but fabrication.\" Then ʿAbd Allah left."],[9236,"He turned towards the north and then prayed with them."],[9237,"ʿAbd Allah prayed with ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad. One stood on his right and the other on his left, then he stood between them."],[9238,"Ibn Masʿud prayed with him and with al-Aswad, and he stood between them."],[9239,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"When they are three, let them all stand in a row. When they are more than that, let one of them go forward.\""],[9240,"Ibn Masʿud came while the imam was praying the morning prayer, and he prayed two rakʿahs facing a pillar, and he had not yet prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr."],[9241,"The prayer was called, and ʿAbd Allah went to the mosque and prayed two rakʿahs, then he entered the mosque."],[9242,"Ibn Masʿud used to say: \"Attach your needs to the obligatory prayer.\""],[9243,"I heard the recitation of ʿAbd Allah in one of the two daytime prayers."],[9244,"I prayed beside ʿAbd Allah, and I did not realize he was reciting anything until I heard him say, “My Lord, increase me in knowledge” (Q 20:114), so I knew he was in Sūrat Ṭā Hā."],[9245,"For one of you to sit on two embers would be better for him than to sit cross-legged in prayer."],[9246,"\"Because for a man to sit on two cushions is better for him than to sit cross-legged during prayer.\" Abdul Razzaq said, \"If he prays standing, then he should not sit in a cross-legged position during the tashahhud (a part of the prayer) and if he prays sitting, then he should sit cross-legged.\""],[9247,"About a sick person, when he prays, he said: “If he cannot reach the ground, let him gesture; and let him make his prostration lower than his bowing.”"],[9248,"“Gesture, and let your bowing be higher than your prostration.”"],[9249,"ʿAlqama and al-Aswad entered upon ʿAbd Allah and said, “Al-Aswad’s mother has been bedridden, and he props up a palm-frond fan stick for her to pray on. What do you think?” He said, “I think Satan presents the stick to her; she should prostrate on the ground if she can, and if not, she should gesture.”"],[9250,"I said to ʿAlqama, “How was ʿAbd Allah’s recitation?” He said, “The people of the house could hear his voice.”"],[9251,"He made himself hear."],[9252,"He made his ears hear."],[9253,"We asked ʿAlqama, “How was ʿAbd Allah’s recitation at night, when he used to stay overnight with him?” He said, “He would make the household of his brother ʿUtba hear him, while they were in a room in front of him.”"],[9254,"He narrated to us, so we asked him, “How did ʿAbd Allah use to recite?” He said, “He would make the household of ʿUtba hear him, while they were in a room in front of him.”"],[9255,"\"He used to perform Tahajjud (night prayer) when there was still time left in the night, just as he used to perform the Maghrib prayer before the nightfall.\""],[9256,"He would make those around him hear, but he did not raise his voice, until there remained of the pre-dawn darkness only about the interval between the call to prayer for Maghrib and finishing it; then he performed Witr."],[9257,"Abdullah used to perform the Sunnah prayer after returning from the Maghrib prayer when a portion of the night remained."],[9258,"\"The Witr is the prayer between the two regular prayers.\""],[9259,"Abdullah: \"Al-Witr is the prayer between the two obligatory prayers.\""],[9260,"Abdullah said, \"Al-Witr is the prayer that is performed between Isha prayer and Fajr prayer.\""],[9261,"\"The period between the two prayers is considered to be a voluntary prayer, and specifically the period between the Isha (Night) prayer and the Fajr (Dawn) prayer.\""],[9262,"\"The Witr is the prayer performed between the two prayers.\""],[9263,"I bear witness that Abdullah ibn Mas'ood, indeed I heard him calling out with it as a call: \"Witr is the prayer that is between the two prayers, the last prayer of the night which you call Al Atamah, and the prayer of Fajr, when do you pray Witr, it is good.\""],[9264,"Ibn Mas'ood used to perform the night prayer after Fajr, and my father used to perform the night prayer before Fajr."],[9265,"\"The Fajr prayer was called and I was performing Witr.\""],[9266,"\"To call the iqamah for Fajr prayer while I was still in my nightly recitation, having not yet performed Witr.\""],[9267,"\"O Abu Abdurrahman, is there a prayer after the adhan (call to prayer)?\" He said, \"Yes, and after the iqama (call to commence prayer).\""],[9268,"\"That Abdullah used to perform the voluntary prayers of night (Tahajjud) in sets of three.\""],[9269,"\"Abdullah used to perform the voluntary night prayer in sets of three, and then he would end with one additional unit.\""],[9270,"Ibn Mas'ud said: \"The night prayer is like the day prayer, (meaning they both hold equal importance and reward) and the Maghrib prayer should be performed three times (meaning one should perform three units of prayer for Maghrib).\""],[9271,"\"The Witr prayer is three, like the Witr of the daytime prayer.\""],[9272,"\"Witr is three units of prayer, similar to the prayer of Maghrib.\""],[9273,"\"A rak'ah cannot be divided.\""],[9274,"Abdullah replied, \"Yes, but three are better.\" Saad then said, \"I can't add anything more to it.\" This made Abdullah angry, and Saad said, \"Are you angry with me for praying one additional unit of prayer while you inherit three grandmothers? Won't you also leave a share for Hawwa, the wife of Adam?\" Yahya informed me about this from Thawri."],[9275,"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman stayed up conversing at al-Walid b. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt's, then left his company and stood talking until they saw the first glimmers of dawn. Then each of them performed Witr with one rak'ah."],[9276,"Abdullah used to recite \"Qul Huwallahu Ahad\" in the last Rak'ah of Witr, then he would raise his hands and make supplication before the Rak'ah."],[9277,"Ibnu Mas'ud used to observe voluntary night prayers throughout the year."],[9278,"From more than one of the companions of 'Abdullah that Ibn Mas'ud used to say, \"When one of you performs Witr, then sleeps, then wakes, let him break his Witr and pray an additional rak'ah, then perform Witr after that.\""],[9279,"\"That Ibn Mas'ud would not perform qunut in Fajr prayer.\""],[9280,"\"That Ibn Mas'ud would not perform qunut in the morning prayer.\""],[9281,"Abdullah used to not pray the Fajr prayer regularly, but when he did, he would pray the Witr prayer before the Rak'ah."],[9282,"\"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud did not perform qunut in the morning prayer.\""],[9283,"He used to offer voluntary prayers before the bowing (rak'ahs) in a prayer, but he did not offer voluntary prayers before the morning prayer."],[9284,"Regarding the prayer on the day of Eid, the Fajr prayer was called, so Ibn Mas'ud stood behind a pillar and prayed two rak'ahs, then joined them."],[9285,"\"That the morning prayer be performed.\""],[9286,"That he \"disliked speaking after praying the two rak'ahs before Fajr.\""],[9287,"\"To speak after Fajr except with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[9288,"\"To hear anyone speaking in it from the break of dawn until sunrise.\""],[9289,"that you should keep silent.”"],[9290,"that you two should keep silent.”"],[9291,"“Ibn Masʿud disliked speaking after praying the two rakʿahs of Fajr.”"],[9292,"“ʿAbd Allah’s prayer during the day was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Fajr. He did not pray before ʿAsr or after it.”"],[9293,"ʿAbd Allah’s voluntary prayer, which he would not abandon, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Subh."],[9294,"“ʿAbd Allah’s voluntary prayer, from which he did not diminish, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before the morning prayer.”"],[9295,"“ʿAbd Allah’s prayer, which he would not leave, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Fajr.”"],[9296,"he used to say: “When the sun declined, he would stand and pray four rakʿahs, reciting in them two surahs from the Miʾin (the long surahs). When the muʾadhdhins called one another, he would tighten his garment and then go out to the prayer.”"],[9297,"ʿAbd Allah [said]: “Nothing equals the night prayer among the daytime prayers except four rakʿahs before Zuhr, and their virtue over the daytime prayer is like the virtue of congregational prayer over praying alone.”"],[9298,"that his father “did not pray the Duha prayer.”"],[9299,"“I never came to him at any hour except that I found him standing in prayer between Maghrib and ʿIsha” — meaning ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud."],[9300,"“It is an hour of heedlessness.”"],[9301,"ʿAbd Allah: “Yes, the hour of heedlessness,” meaning the prayer between Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[9302,"“Drowsiness during fighting is security from Allah, and drowsiness during prayer is from Satan.”"],[9303,"ʿAbd Allah: “Drowsiness during prayer is from Satan, and drowsiness during fighting is security from Allah.”"],[9304,"“Yawning and sneezing during prayer are from Satan.”"],[9305,"“Prayer is not shortened except in Hajj or Jihad.”"],[9306,"He said, \"Do not decrease from your prayers in your homes, nor take part in your affairs, nor travel in the valleys of the lowlands for your needs, and then say that you are travelers, for a traveler is only one who travels from horizon to horizon.\""],[9307,"He said: “Do not be deluded by your trades and your gatherings, and travel to the villages of the Sawad, and say, ‘We are a people on a journey.’ The traveler is only one from horizon to horizon.”"],[9308,"“Do not be deluded by your Sawad, for the gathering place of any of you and his family is one thing, unless he chooses otherwise.”"],[9309,"“Whoever prays four rakʿahs while traveling must repeat the prayer.”"],[9310,"About a man who lies on his side at the two rakʿahs of Duha? He said: “What is the matter with one of you that he rolls around like the rolling of a donkey?”"],[9311,"“Do you burden people with what Allah has not burdened them? They see you praying and then consider that obligatory upon them. If you must do it, then in the houses.”"],[9312,"When ʿAbd Allah stood, we would sit after him and help people with the recitation. Then when we stood, we prayed. That reached him, so we entered upon him and he said: “Do you burden people with what they are not burdened? They see you and think it is a Sunnah. If you must do it, then in your houses.” Sulayman said: ʿAmr b. Murrah also narrated to us from Abu ʿUbaydah from ʿAbd Allah."],[9313,"That I prostrate, so I disobeyed, and to me is the Fire."],[9314,"A man, while he was irrigating a field of his, saw a cloud raining. He heard a voice in it saying, 'Irrigate the land of So-and-so.' He followed the voice until he reached the land that was named. He asked its owner, 'What is your practice regarding it?' He said, 'I return one-third [of its produce to the land], I give one-third in charity, and I reserve one-third for my family.'"],[9315,"\"May Allah curse the women who tattoo, those who have themselves tattooed, those who file their teeth for the sake of beauty, altering Allah's creation.\" This reached a woman of Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub. She said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I heard that you cursed such and such.' He said, 'Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed and who are mentioned in the Book of Allah?' She said, 'Indeed I read what is between the two covers, but I do not find it.' He said, 'If you were a reader, you would have found it. Have you not read, \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it\"?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it.' She said, 'I think your family does some of that.' He said, 'Go and look.' She entered and did not see anything of what she sought. 'Abd Allah said, 'If she was like that, she would not have been intimate with us.' Al-Dabari said: We said to Abu Bakr, 'What is al-namisa?' He said, 'The one who plucks her hair.'"],[9316,"\"The Messenger of Allah cursed, so a woman from the Banu Asad said to him, 'I think he is cursing your family.' He said, 'Go and look.' So she went and then came back and said, 'I did not see anything in them (i.e., his family), and I did not see him (i.e., the curse) in the Quran.' Abdullah said to her, 'Indeed, yes, the Messenger of Allah said that.'\""],[9317,"Something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or you find it in the Book of Allah? He said, 'Rather, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I find it in the Book of Allah.' She said, 'By Allah, I have read what is between the two covers of the mushaf, and I did not find it.' He said, 'Do you not find in it, \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it\"?' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'By Allah, I think the one in your house does it.' He said, 'Then I have not kept the advice of my brother Shu'ayb.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah: enter upon her and look at her hair.' She entered and looked at a bald woman and saw nothing in her hair. She came out and said, 'I found nothing.' He said, 'Then I have not kept the advice of Shu'ayb.'"],[9318,"\"May Allah curse the women who file their teeth, pluck their eyebrows, tattoo themselves, altering Allah's creation.\" A woman of Banu Asad called Umm al-Mustawrid came to him and said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I heard that you cursed the women who file their teeth, pluck their eyebrows, and tattoo themselves.' He said, 'Should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah?' She said, 'I have read what is between the two covers, and I did not find it in it.' He said, 'If you have read what is between the two covers, indeed it is in the Book of Allah: \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it.\"' She said, 'By Allah, I think your family does it.' He said, 'Enter and look. If they do it, they will not spend a night with me.' She entered and looked, then came out saying, 'I saw nothing. I saw nothing.'"],[9319,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, \"May the one who connects (= tribal affiliations) be cursed, as well as the tattooer, the fortune-teller, and those who pluck their facial hairs.\" This statement was said by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[9320,"\"By Him besides whom there is no god, a woman never prays a prayer better for her than a prayer she prays in her house, except in the Sacred Mosque or the Mosque of the Messenger, except for an old woman in her manqalayha.\""],[9321,"\"A woman does not pray in any place that is better for her than her house, except in the Sacred Mosque or the Mosque of the Prophet ﷺ, except a woman who goes out in her manqalayha,\" meaning her khuffs."],[9322,"I heard the Lord of this house swearing an oath and going far in the oath: \"There is no prayer place for a woman better for her than her house, except in Hajj or 'Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of marriage, for she is in her manqalayha.\" I said, \"What is her manqalayha?\" He said, \"An old woman whose steps have become short.\""],[9323,"'Abd Allah swore an oath and went far in the oath: \"There is no prayer place for a woman better than her house, except in Hajj or 'Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of marriage, for she is in her manqalayha.\""],[9324,"He saw Ibn Mas'ud driving women out of the mosque on Friday and saying, \"Go out to your houses; that is better for you.\""],[9325,"\"I saw Ibn Mas'ud driving women out of the mosque on Friday.\""],[9326,"He used to drive women out of the mosque on Friday and say, \"Pray in your houses.\""],[9327,"That she sits in the depth of her house worshipping her Lord. One of them says, 'I will go to my family,' and the Shaytan seeks to make her look attractive until she says, 'No one saw me except that I pleased him.'"],[9328,"Women are but ʿawrah. Indeed, a woman leaves her house while there is nothing wrong with her, and Satan seeks to raise himself up for her, saying: “You will not pass by anyone but that you will charm him.” And indeed, a woman puts on her clothes, and it is said: “Where do you intend to go?” She replies: “I am visiting a sick person, attending a funeral, or praying in a mosque.” But a woman has not worshipped her Lord with anything like worshipping Him in her home."],[9329,"Indeed, a woman is ʿawrah. When she leaves her house, Satan raises himself up for her, and she says: “No one sees me but that I charm him.” The closest she is to Allah is when she is in the innermost part of her home."],[9330,"“A woman’s prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her chamber, and her prayer in her chamber is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer anywhere else.” Then he said: “Indeed, when a woman goes out, Satan raises himself up for her.”"],[9331,"“A woman’s prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer outside it.”"],[9332,"“Two wooden dancers (i.e., two clogs or stilts).”"],[9333,"“A woman of the Children of Israel used to wear two wooden clogs and stand upon them to set a tryst with her lover, so menstruation was imposed upon them.” And ʿAbd Allah (i.e., Ibn Masʿūd) used to say: “Keep them back where Allah has kept them back.”"],[9334,"“Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” When he finished, he said: “It used to be said: among the signs of the Hour are that a man will greet another man only because he knows him, that mosques will be taken as thoroughfares, that women and horses will become expensive and then become cheap and will not become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection, and that a man and a woman will trade together.”"],[9335,"“That mosques be taken as thoroughfares.”"],[9336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the signs of the Hour are that a man will pass through the length and breadth of the mosque without praying two rakʿahs in it.” This is how Mansūr narrated it, and Qatādah connected it."],[9337,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Allah and His Messenger ﷺ have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Among the signs of the Hour are that a man will pass through the mosque without praying two rakʿahs in it, that a man will not greet anyone except one he knows, and that a young boy will make an old man cool (i.e., will relieve him or act as his superior).’”"],[9338,"“Peace be upon you, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” He laughed and said: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The Hour will not come until greeting is only upon acquaintance; indeed this man recognized me from among you and greeted me, and until mosques are taken as thoroughfares so that no prostration is made to Allah in them, and until a young boy sends an old man as a messenger between the two horizons, and until a merchant travels between the two horizons and finds no profit.’”"],[9339,"The prayer was commenced in the mosque, and we came walking with ʿAbd Allah. When the people bowed, ʿAbd Allah bowed and we bowed with him while we were walking. A man passed in front of him and said: “Peace be upon you, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” ʿAbd Allah said while bowing: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” When he finished, some of the people asked him: “Why did you say, when the man greeted you, ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth’?” He replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Among the signs of the Hour are when greeting is upon acquaintance.’”"],[9340,"ʿAbdullah used to say: “Perform this prayer well and shorten these sermons.”"],[9341,"“Lengthy prayer and short sermon are an indication of a man’s understanding.”"],[9342,"“Lengthy prayer and short sermon are an indication of a man’s understanding.”"],[9343,"“There will be rulers over you who kill the prayer. Whoever of you reaches that should pray it at its proper time and make his prayer with them a supererogatory prayer.”"],[9344,"“You are in a time whose preachers are few and scholars many; they make the prayer long and the sermon short. There will come upon you a time whose preachers are many and scholars few; they make the sermon long and delay the prayer until it is said: ‘This is the glow of the dead.’” I said to him: “What is the glow of the dead?” He said: “When the sun turns very yellow. Whoever of you reaches that should pray the prayer at its proper time; if he is detained, let him pray with them and make his prayer alone the obligatory one and his prayer with them voluntary.”"],[9345,"“There will be rulers who abandon practices like this. If you abandon them, they will make them like this. If you abandon them, they will bring the great calamity.”"],[9346,"“Do not be a tax collector, nor a headman, nor a policeman, nor a courier, and pray the prayer at its appointed time.”"],[9347,"“ʿAbdullah would pray with them when they delayed it a little, and he held that they bore the sin of that.”"],[9348,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “None of that was done, and Allah and His Messenger ﷺ did not command us to wait for you with our prayer while you are attending to your need.”"],[9349,"That he hears the muezzin say: “Allah is most great, Allah is most great; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,” and he does not say the like of what he says, and that he wipes his face before finishing his prayer, and that he urinates standing, and that he prays when there is nothing between him and the qiblah to screen him."],[9350,"From al-Musayyab, who traced the hadith back to ʿAbdullah, who said: “Four things are from coarseness: that a man hears the muezzin say ‘Allah is most great’ and does not say it, and hears the testimony of faith and does not say it, and wipes dust from his forehead while praying, and prays in open ground with no screen between him and the qiblah.”"],[9351,"And that you hear the muezzin and do not say what he says."],[9352,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah said to him: Perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray. He saw that ʿAbd Allah did not understand the gravity of what he had done. He then repeated: O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah said to him: «Perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray.» He remained silent, and when those with him had departed, he said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah took hold of his finger and pressed it, then said: «It was only said to you so that you would understand: perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray.»"],[9353,"«Does every one of you find two garments? He may pray in a single garment.»"],[9354,"«Ibn Masʿūd and ʿĀʾishah used to offer voluntary prayers while traveling before the prayer and after it.»"],[9355,"He said to Ibn Masʿūd: Are you not amazed at people between your house and the house of Abū Mūsā who claim that they are observing iʿtikāf? He said: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong.»"],[9356,"\"Do not be surprised by the people between your house and the house of Abu Musa who claim that they are in seclusion,\" Ibn Mas'ood said. \"Perhaps they have succeeded and you have failed, or they have remembered and you have forgotten.\" He said, \"As for me, I have learned that seclusion is only in the congregational mosque.\""],[9357,"He said: Shall I not amaze you at people observing iʿtikāf between your house and the house of al-Ashʿarī? ʿAbd Allah said: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong.» Ḥudhayfah said: I do not care whether I observe iʿtikāf in it or in this market of yours. Iʿtikāf is only in these three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Aqsa Mosque. Those who observed iʿtikāf and whom Ḥudhayfah criticized were in the great mosque of Kufa."],[9358,"Ḥudhayfah said to ʿAbd Allah: There are people observing iʿtikāf between your house and the house of Abū Mūsā. Will you not forbid them? ʿAbd Allah said to him: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong, and they have remembered while you have forgotten.» Ḥudhayfah said: There is no iʿtikāf except in these three mosques: the Mosque of Madinah, the Mosque of Makkah, and the Mosque of Iliya."],[9359,"A man observed iʿtikāf in a tent of his, and people pelted him with pebbles. The man sent for ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd, and ʿAbd Allah came, «drove the people away, and deemed that commendable.»"],[9360,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud used to make nine takbirs for both Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr, starting by making four takbirs, then reciting Quran, then making one takbir and performing the bowing position (Ruk'u), then standing back up for the second unit of prayer and starting by reciting Quran, then making four takbirs and performing the bowing position with one of them."],[9361,"This is the festival of the Muslims, so how is the prayer? They said: Ask Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. So he asked him, and he said: «He stands and says takbīr four times, then recites the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah from the mufaṣṣal, then says takbīr and bows; that makes five. Then he stands and recites the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah from the mufaṣṣal, then says takbīr four times and bows at the last of them; that makes nine in the two festival prayers.» None of them objected to that."],[9362,"Al-Walīd said: The festival has arrived, so what should I do? Ibn Masʿūd said: «Say Allāhu akbar, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate to Allah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate to Allah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate; then say takbīr and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah; then say takbīr and bow and prostrate. Then stand and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and bow and prostrate.» Ḥudhayfah and Abū Mūsā said: He is correct."],[9363,"About the takbīr in prayer on the day of Fiṭr and Aḍḥā. One said: Ask this one, and the other said: Ask this one, until Ḥudhayfah said to him: Ask this one, meaning ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd. So he asked him, and Ibn Masʿūd said: «He says takbīr four times, then recites, then says takbīr and bows, then says takbīr in the second, then recites, then says takbīr four times after the recitation.»"],[9364,"«Ibn Masʿūd used to say takbīr nine times in the two festival prayers: four before the recitation, then he would say takbīr and bow; and in the second he would recite, and when he finished he would say takbīr four times, then bow.»"],[9365,"He «used to say takbīr nine times on Aḍḥā and Fiṭr: he would stand and say takbīr four times, then recite, then say one takbīr and bow with it, then stand and recite and say four takbīrs, bowing with one.»"],[9366,"He used to say the takbir in the first (rakʿah) five times: with the takbir of the rakʿah and the takbir of commencement, and in the other four times, with the takbir of the rakʿah."],[9367,"Al-Ashʿari said: Ask ʿAbd Allah, for he is the most learned and the earliest of us. So he asked him, and he said: You begin with four, and you finish with four, and you say one takbir, then you add three to it, then you say takbir and bow. When you raise from the prostration, you recite, then you say four takbirs, then you bow."],[9368,"The takbir in the two ʿIds is four, like the prayer over the deceased."],[9369,"Indeed between every two takbirs there is the measure of a word."],[9370,"They both would make anyone they saw praying before the imam's departure on the ʿId sit down."],[9371,"About the prayer before the imam's departure."],[9372,"That anyone should pray before the imam."],[9373,"\"About the prayer on the day of Eid before the Imam's departure.\""],[9374,"Ibn Masʿud would not pray before it (the ʿId prayer) and would pray after it four rakʿahs."],[9375,"Ibn Masʿud would pray after it four rakʿahs or eight, and he would not pray before it."],[9376,"Ibn Masʿud would pray four (rakʿahs) after the two ʿIds."],[9377,"He would pray four (rakʿahs) after the two ʿIds."],[9378,"ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud said: Whoever misses the ʿId, let him pray four (rakʿahs)."],[9379,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: \"Whoever misses the Eid prayer should pray four rak'ahs.\""],[9380,"He used to say the takbir from the dawn prayer on the Day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice."],[9381,"A mudd of wheat or a sa' of dates or barley."],[9382,"I performed ghusl with Ibn Mas'ud on the Day of Arafah under the arak tree."],[9383,"Abdullah used to say: \"The takbir during the days of Tashriq is after the dawn prayer from the Day of Arafah until after the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice.\""],[9384,"He used to say the takbir in the dawn prayer on the Day of Arafah and stop after the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice, saying takbir when he prayed the afternoon prayer.\" He said: And he used to say: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illa Allah, wa Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, wa lillahi al-hamd."],[9385,"Abdullah: \"If I had recited it as 'fas'a' (walk briskly), I would have walked briskly until my cloak fell off. And he used to recite it 'famdu' (proceed).\""],[9386,"In the words of Ibn Mas'ood, \"Proceed to the remembrance of Allah, which is like His saying: 'Indeed, your efforts are diverse.'”"],[9387,"He asked Ubayy b. Ka'b, while the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon, about a verse from the Book of Allah. Ubayy turned away from him and did not reply. When he finished his prayer, he said: \"You did not perform the Friday prayer properly.\" So Ibn Mas'ud asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Ubayy spoke the truth.\""],[9388,"Abdullah said to him: \"What you asked about is your share of the Friday prayer.\""],[9389,"To say to your companion 'Be quiet' when the imam has come out for the Friday prayer."],[9390,"I prayed with Zirr and he led me, but we missed the Friday prayer. I asked Ibrahim, and he said: \"Abdullah did that with 'Alqamah and al-Aswad.\" Sufyan said: \"Sometimes I and al-A'mash did it.\""],[9391,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer should add another to it, and whoever misses the two rak'ahs should pray four."],[9392,"Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught Jumuʿah, and whoever does not catch the rakʿah should pray four."],[9393,"Whoever catches the two rakʿahs or one of them has caught Jumuʿah, and whoever misses the two rakʿahs should pray four? He said: \"Yes.\""],[9394,"Whoever catches the khutbah, then Jumuʿah is two rakʿahs, and whoever does not catch it should pray four, and whoever does not catch the rakʿah should not rely on the prostration until he catches the rakʿah."],[9395,"\"Whoever misses the last rakʿah should pray four.\" Maʿmar said: Qatādah said: He prays four. It was said to Qatādah that Ibn Masʿūd came while they were sitting at the end of the prayer, and he said to his companions: \"Sit, you have caught it, if Allah wills.\" Qatādah said: \"He only means: 'You have caught the reward.'\""],[9396,"that we should pray four rakʿahs after Jumuʿah, until we heard the statement of ʿAlī: \"Pray six.\" Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \"So we pray six.\" ʿAṭāʾ said: \"Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān prays two rakʿahs then four.\""],[9397,"that we should pray four before Jumuʿah and four after it, until ʿAlī ؓ came and ordered us to pray two rakʿahs after it, then four."],[9398,"that we should pray four before Jumuʿah and four after it, until ʿAlī came and ordered us to pray two rakʿahs after it, then four."],[9399,"\"Make it six.\""],[9400,"\"Ibn Masʿūd prayed on the day of Jumuʿah, after the imam had said the salām, four rakʿahs.\""],[9401,"Abū Isḥāq: \"ʿAlī used to pray six rakʿahs after Jumuʿah.\""],[9402,"\"Ibn Masʿūd used to pray four after Jumuʿah.\""],[9403,"\"We used to pray Jumuʿah with ʿAbd Allah, then return and take a siesta.\""],[9404,"We used to gather with Ibn Masʿūd, then we would return and take a midday nap."],[9405,"I saw ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd patrolling the mosque at night. He would remove anyone he saw in it as a dark figure, except a man standing in prayer."],[9406,"\"Your imam should come forward.\" We said, \"Our imam is not here.\" He said, \"Let one of you come forward.\" So a man came forward and stood on a bench in the qiblah of the mosque, and ʿAbd Allāh forbade him."],[9407,"that he lead them from an elevated place.\""],[9408,"ʿAbd Allāh said, \"The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing to remain is prayer. There will surely be people who pray yet have no religion.\""],[9409,"Fasting is from the sighting of the crescent to its sighting; if it is obscured from you, then thirty days."],[9410,"I came to Abdullah bin Masood and said, \"Some people in the neighborhood and some of our neighbors are fasting today.\" He asked, \"Did they see the crescent?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Because it is more beloved to me to break my fast for a day in Ramadan and then make it up, than to fast for a day in Sha'ban.\""],[9411,"\"You had been in a state of major ritual impurity, so prayer was not lawful for you. Then you performed ghusl, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you, so fast.\""],[9412,"He came to the mosque of the neighborhood after they had prayed Fajr and said to them—that was in Ramadan—\"I had intercourse with my wife, then sleep overcame me, and I entered the morning without having performed ghusl. What do you think?\" The people said to him, \"We think you have broken your fast.\" So he went to ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd and said to them, \"I have come to one who is better than you or more knowledgeable.\" He said, \"Breaking the fast is only from food and drink, so complete your fast.\""],[9413,"\"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I was in a state of major ritual impurity and did not perform ghusl until morning.\" ʿAbd Allāh said, \"You had been in a state of major ritual impurity, so prayer was not lawful for you. Then you performed ghusl, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you.\" That was in Ramadan."],[9414,"\"If I had intercourse with a woman at night, then deliberately left the ghusl until morning, it would not prevent me from fasting. I only had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9415,"\"If I had intercourse with a woman at night, then deliberately left the ghusl until morning, that would not prevent me from fasting, because I only had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9416,"\"If I had intercourse with my wife at the beginning of the night, then entered the morning in a state of major ritual impurity, I would still fast, because I had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9417,"If I were in a state of major ritual impurity and stayed for a month not finding water, I would not pray until I found water."],[9418,"Sufyān: This is not to be taken."],[9419,"Ibn Masʿūd would fondle his wife in the middle of the day while he was fasting."],[9420,"Ibn Masʿūd: Whoever breaks his fast on a day in Ramadan without a dispensation will meet Allah with that, even if he fasts the entire age; if He wills He will forgive him, and if He wills He will punish him."],[9421,"Fasting is only from what enters, and not from what exits; and ablution is from what exits, and not from what enters."],[9422,"We had the predawn meal with ʿAbd Allāh, then we went out and the prayer was called."],[9423,"If food or drink is offered to one of you while he is fasting, he should say: I am fasting."],[9424,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd: Seek the Night of Decree on the night of the seventeenth, the morning of Badr, or the twenty-first night, or the twenty-third."],[9425,"May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He knew that it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from the people so that they would not rely on it. By the One who sent down the Book to Muḥammad ﷺ, it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. We observed and memorized it. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception. I said to Zirr: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises on that morning like a basin, with no rays."],[9426,"May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. By Allah, he knew that it is in Ramadan, but he disliked that they should rely on it, or he loved that they should not rely on it. By Allah, it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night—he swore without making an exception. He said: I said: O Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. Ḥammād said: I said to ʿĀṣim: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises on the morning after that night without rays, like a basin, until it rises high."],[9427,"Tell me about the Night of Decree, for ʿAbd Allāh says: Whoever stands in prayer the whole year will attain it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He knows that it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from the people so that they would not rely on it. By Allah, it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us. We counted and memorized that it is indeed it. ʿĀṣim said: I said to Zirr: What is that sign? He said: The sun rises white like a basin, with no rays, until it rises high. He said: I observed it many times like that."],[9428,"It is in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: How did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. We counted and memorized. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception."],[9429,"\"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh.\" I said, \"O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that?\" He said, \"By the verse about which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, so I memorized it and counted it. By the One who sent down the Book upon Muhammad, it is the night of the twenty-seventh.\""],[9430,"\"Narrate to me, for I used to love meeting you, and I did not come except to meet you. So narrate to me about the Night of Decree, for Ibn Masʿud says: 'Whoever stands the whole year in prayer will attain it or reach it.' Ubayy said: 'He knew that it is in Ramadan, but he loved to keep it hidden from you. It is the night of the twenty-seventh, based on the verse about which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, so we memorized it and learned it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would continue it until dawn, and when it was one day before or one day after, he would ascend and look at the sun and say: \"The sun rises on its morning without rays until it rises high.\"'\","],[9431,"Ubayy said, \"May Allah have mercy on Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman. He knew that it is in the month of Ramadan on the night of the twenty-seventh, but he loved that they not rely on it.\""],[9432,"\"Whoever stands the entire month of Ramadan in prayer will attain it.\" He said, \"Then I came to Madinah and mentioned that to Ubayy. He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I know which night it is - the night that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to stand in prayer.' He said, 'So I asked him about it, and he said: \"The night of the twenty-seventh.\"' Abda said, 'So when the month was thirty days, we stood three nights after it, and when it was twenty-nine, we stood two nights after it.'\""],[9433,"\"Abdullah used to lead us in prayer during the month of Ramadan and would leave while it was still night.\""],[9434,"That he said, \"For twenty-five camels, a bint makhad; if not available, then a male ibn labun?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[9435,"\"You have no stipend from me. Your stipend is only from your fay' and your jizya, and charity is for its people.\" When they kept coming back to him, he brought the keys to ʿUthman and threw them, saying, \"I am not a treasurer.\""],[9436,"\"When they reach the age of maturity, inform them about the obligation of paying Zakat. If they wish, guide them to fulfill it, and if they wish to leave it, then let them.\""],[9437,"He said to him, \"You owe zakat of such-and-such for a year.\""],[9438,"\"He used to give us the stipend, then take its zakat.\""],[9439,"\"In my care are orphans, so shall I give it to them?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[9440,"\"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, is there zakat on my jewelry?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"I have a nephew who is an orphan, so shall I put it for them?\" He said, \"Put it for them.\""],[9441,"\"Whoever earns lawfully, withholding zakat corrupts it, and whoever earns unlawfully, zakat does not purify it.\""],[9442,"“When one of you follows a funeral, let him take hold of all sides of the bier, for that is from the Sunnah; then afterwards let him volunteer or leave off.” And the wording is that of the hadith of Abū Nuʿaym."],[9443,"\"If one of you follows a funeral procession, let him take hold of the sides of the bier completely, for it is from the Sunnah, then let him either perform voluntary acts of worship after it or leave.\" And the wording is from the hadith of Abu Nuaim."],[9444,"“When one of you follows a funeral, let him take hold of all sides of the bier, for that is from the Sunnah; then afterwards let him volunteer or leave off.” And the wording is that of the hadith of Abū Nuʿaym."],[9445,"“That you carry by the four sides of the bier, then volunteer or leave off.”"],[9446,"“That you take hold of the four sides of the bier, then volunteer afterwards or leave off.”"],[9447,"“Indeed your companion is impure, so perform ghusl from it; otherwise, wudu suffices you.”"],[9448,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “No recitation or speech has been prescribed for us over the funeral. Say takbir as the imam says takbir, and increase in the best of speech.”"],[9449,"“To tread on a live coal is more beloved to me than to tread on the grave of a Muslim man.”"],[9450,"“No recitation or speech has been prescribed for us in the funeral prayer. Say takbir as the imam says takbir, and increase in good speech.”"],[9451,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Do not buy fish in water, for it is uncertainty.”"],[9452,"“Riba is seventy-some odd doors.”"],[9453,"“A transaction within two transactions is riba.”"],[9454,"“Pure, without intercourse.”"],[9455,"“(She must be) pure without intercourse. If he wishes to divorce her according to the Sunnah three times, he divorces her once in a period of purity, then she must observe a menstrual period after the final divorce.”"],[9456,"“That he divorce according to the Sunnah as Allah ﷻ commanded him: let him divorce her when she is pure without intercourse.”"],[9457,"Abd Allah b. Masʿud said regarding {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at their prescribed periods}: “The divorce at the prescribed period is that you divorce her when she is pure, then leave her until she completes her waiting period, or take her back if you wish.” Shuʿbah said: The people of Kufa say: “without intercourse.”"],[9458,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {divorce them at their prescribed periods}: He said: “Whoever intends the divorce that is truly a divorce should give her time, so that when the woman becomes pure from menses he divorces her while pure without intercourse.”"],[9459,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {divorce them at their prescribed periods}: He said: Whoever intends the divorce that is truly a divorce should give the woman time until she becomes pure without intercourse. He says to her: “Observe your waiting period.” If he regrets it and his soul follows her, he calls two men to witness her return; otherwise he leaves her until her waiting period ends. He should not divorce her three times while she is pregnant, for Allah would cause him to regret it, and he would have to spend on her during her pregnancy and breastfeeding.”"],[9460,"O Commander of the Believers, my husband divorced me, and my bleeding ceased for three menstrual periods. Then he came to me after I had placed my water (for ghusl), closed my door, and taken off my clothes, and said: “I have taken you back, I have taken you back.” Umar said to Ibn Masʿud: “What do you think about her?” He said: “I think she is his wife as long as prayer has not become lawful for her.” Umar said: “And I think that too.”"],[9461,"The woman said: “Indeed, what happened from you did not make me report the matter as it really was.” Umar said: “Tell me.” She said: “He divorced me, then left me until I was in the last of three menstrual periods and my bleeding stopped. I prepared my ghusl, closed my door, and took off my clothes. Then he knocked on the door and said: ‘I have taken you back, I have taken you back.’ So I left my ghusl and put on my clothes.” Umar said: “What do you say about her, O Ibn Umm ʿAbd?” I said: “I see that he has more right to her as long as prayer has not become lawful for her.” Umar said: “What a good opinion you have, and I think that too.”"],[9462,"Uthman sent to my father asking him about her. My father said: “How can a hypocrite give a fatwa?” Uthman said: “We seek refuge in Allah from your being a hypocrite, and we seek refuge in Allah from calling you a hypocrite. We seek refuge in Allah that such a thing should exist in Islam, then he should die without clarifying it.” He said: “I think he has more right to her until she performs ghusl after the third menses and prayer becomes lawful for her.” I do not know but that Uthman adopted that."],[9463,"A man divorced his wife once. She menstruated three times. When she sat down to perform ghusl, her husband came and took her back. She said: “You have no right to that.” They went to Ibn Masʿud, and he made her swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, that he had taken her back after prayer had become lawful for her. She did not swear, so he returned her to him."],[9464,"If she has been entered upon, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."],[9465,"If she has been entered upon, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."],[9466,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding a man who divorces his wife three times before consummating the marriage. He said: “ʿAbd Allah considered her in the position of one with whom the marriage has been consummated.”"],[9467,"That the menstruation had ceased from her but that was not clear, she should wait a year; if she does not menstruate during it, she observes the waiting period after the year of three months. If she menstruates during the three months, she observes the waiting period by menstruation. If she menstruates but her menstruation is not completed after she has observed those three months following the year, he said: “Do not hasten against her until you know whether her menstruation is completed or not.”"],[9468,"Yes, so he married her and she bore him a child. Then he came to Umar and asked him, and he said: “Separate between them.” He said: She has borne him a child. He said: “Even if she bears ten, separate between them.”"],[9469,"Concerning the woman gifted (in marriage): “If they accept her, it is one (divorce), and she is more entitled to herself; if they do not accept her, it is nothing.”"],[9470,"\"If they accept it, then it is a clear one.\""],[9471,"A man says to his wife: “Your affair is in your hand,” or “Seek success in your affair,” or he gifts her to her family and they accept it: it is one irrevocable divorce."],[9472,"\"Allah ﷻ has clearly explained divorce, so whoever divorces as Allah ﷻ has commanded, it has been made clear to him. And whoever took upon himself the clothing of someone else, we made it his clothing, and Allah is not burdening you with what you say upon yourselves.\" He said, \"And we see the statement of Ibn Sirin as an expression that I do not remember well, as he said, 'If he had the women of the people of the earth, then he said, 'All of them have gone away.'\""],[9473,"“It is as you said.” Then a man came to him and said: I divorced my wife the number of the stars. He said: “Did you say it once?” He said: Yes. He said: “Do you want her to be separated from you?” He said: Yes. He said: Then Abdullah mentioned at that point the women of the people of the earth with something I do not remember. Then Abdullah said: “Allah has made clear to you how divorce is. Whoever divorces as Allah commanded him, it has been made clear to him. Whoever confuses, we assign to him his confusion. By Allah, you will not confuse yourselves and we will bear it for you. It is as you say.”"],[9474,"I divorced my wife ninety-nine times, and I asked and was told that she has become separated from me. Ibn Mas'ud said: “They loved that separation be made between you and her.” He said: What do you say, may Allah have mercy on you? He thought that he would grant him a concession. He said: “Three separate her from you, and the rest of them are aggression.”"],[9475,"I divorced my wife ninety times, and I have a child from her, and some people want to separate me and my family. Abdullah said: “Three are sufficient for you, and the rest of them are aggression.”"],[9476,"“Concerning the prohibited (utterance), it is an oath that he expiates.”"],[9477,"“Concerning the prohibited (utterance), it is an oath that he expiates.”"],[9478,"“Concerning the prohibited (utterance), the expiation of an oath.”"],[9479,"Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: “Concerning the prohibited (utterance), the expiation of an oath.”"],[9480,"That you touch them, and he did not say: When you divorce the believing women then you marry them."],[9481,"God has indeed made clear. Whoever approaches the matter from its proper aspect, it has been made clear to him; and whoever opposes, then by God, we cannot oppose you."],[9482,"If four months have passed, it is īlāʾ."],[9483,"And he said: When four months have passed, then acknowledge one pronouncement of divorce."],[9484,"ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd and Ibn ʿAbbās said: When the four months have passed, it is one pronouncement of divorce and she is more entitled to herself. Qatādah said: ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd said: She observes the waiting period of a divorced woman."],[9485,"She has become irrevocably separated from you, so propose to her on her own behalf. So he proposed to her on her own behalf and gave her a riṭl of silver as a bridal gift."],[9486,"This verse which is in the shorter Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden}, was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah, {And those of you who die and leave behind wives}, the verse. He said: And it reached him that ʿAlī said: It is the later of the two terms. And he said that."],[9487,"Whoever wishes, I will invoke mutual cursing with him: The verse {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden} was not revealed except after the verse of the woman whose husband died, {And those of you who die and leave behind wives, they shall wait concerning themselves four months and ten days}."],[9488,"The shorter Sūrat al-Nisāʾ was revealed after four months and ten days."],[9489,"The waiting period of a divorced woman is from the time she is divorced, and of a woman whose husband has died from the time he dies. And whoever wishes, I will swear with him that the shorter sūrah was revealed after al-Baqarah."],[9490,"The shorter sūrah was revealed after the longer one, meaning al-Nisāʾ."],[9491,"{...that they deliver their burden} after the one in al-Baqarah {And those of you who die and leave behind wives, they shall wait concerning themselves}."],[9492,"ʿAbd Allāh said: Do you think that if four months and ten days pass and she has not delivered her burden? They said: Until she delivers. Then ʿAbd Allāh said: So you impose hardship on her and do not give her the concession. The verse of the shorter sūrah was revealed after the longer one: {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden}. When she delivers her burden, the waiting period has ended."],[9493,"\"But his paternal uncle did not say this.\" He said: \"So I met Malik b. ʿAmir al-Hamdani and asked him, and he began to recall the hadith of Subayʿah. I said: 'I am not asking you about that. Did you hear Ibn Masʿud say anything about it?' He said: 'Yes. They mentioned that in his presence, and he said: \"What do you say if she gives birth before the end of four months and ten days?\" We said: \"She must wait until the four months and ten days have passed.\" He said: \"And what do you say if the four months and ten days pass before she gives birth?\" We said: \"Until she gives birth.\" He said: \"You impose the strict ruling upon her but do not grant her the concession. The shorter Surah al-Nisaʾ was revealed after the longer one: {And those who are pregnant}\" '\""],[9494,"\"There was between me and my wife what occurs between people. She said: 'If the authority you have over my affair were in my hand, you would know what I would do.' He said: 'Then the authority I have over your affair is in your hand.' She said: 'Then you are divorced three times.' He said: 'I consider it one, and you are more entitled to take her back.' And I will meet the Commander of the Believers ʿUmar. So he met him and related the story to him. He said: 'May God do to the men, may God do to the men! They take what God placed in their hands and put it into the hands of women. May dust fill her mouth! What did you say?' He said: 'I said: \"I consider it one, and he is more entitled to her.\"' He said: 'And I think that. If you had thought otherwise, I would have considered that you were wrong.'\" Mansur said: \"I said to Ibrahim: 'But Ibn ʿAbbas used to say: May God cause her star to err; if she had said, \"I have divorced myself.\"' Ibrahim said: 'They are the same.'\""],[9495,"\"There was between me and my wife some words. She said: 'If the authority over my affair were in my hand, you would know what I would do.' I said: 'Then I call you to witness that the authority you have over your affair, which I possess, is in your hand.' She said: 'Then you are divorced three times.' Ibn Masʿud said: 'So it is one, and you are more entitled to her. And I will ask the Commander of the Believers about that.' So he rode and met ʿUmar and related the story to him. He said: 'May stones fill her mouth! May God do to the men and do—they take what God placed in their hands regarding the affair of women and place it in their hands. What do you think?' I said: 'I consider it one, and he is more entitled to her.' He said: 'Yes, what you have considered is good. Had you considered otherwise, you would have been wrong.'\""],[9496,"ʿUmar: \"And I think that.\""],[9497,"\"If she decides something, then she has no authority.\""],[9498,"\"If she chooses her husband, it is nothing; and if she chooses herself, then it is one.\""],[9499,"ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud: \"If she chooses herself, then it is one; and if she chooses her husband, then it is nothing.\""],[9500,"That ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud said regarding \"your affair is in your hand\": \"If she chooses herself, then it is one, and he is more entitled to her; and if she chooses her husband, then it is nothing.\""],[9501,"ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud: \"If she chooses her husband, there is no harm; and if she chooses herself, then it is one, and he has the right of return over her.\""],[9502,"\"It is three.\""],[9503,"\"They gather during the day, then each one of them returns to her house at night.\""],[9504,"ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud: \"If he slanders her after having divorced her while he has the right of return over her, he invokes the liʿan against her; and if he slanders her after having divorced her with a final divorce, he does not invoke the liʿan against her.\""],[9505,"The two who invoke curses upon one another will never come together."],[9506,"The entire inheritance of the child of a woman who has invoked curses belongs to his mother."],[9507,"From 'Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, they said: \"The paternal relatives of the child of a woman who has invoked curses are the paternal relatives of his mother.\""],[9508,"\"If Allah took a covenant for a soul in the loins of a man and then poured it upon a rock, He would bring it out from that rock. So if you wish, complete it; and if you wish, do not practice coitus interruptus.\""],[9509,"Regarding coitus interruptus: \"It is the hidden female infant buried alive.\""],[9510,"\"Ibn Mas'ud disliked combining two sisters in the possession of one's right hand.\""],[9511,"\"Ibn Mas'ud disliked a slave woman and her mother.\""],[9512,"\"Ibn Mas'ud disliked a slave woman and her mother.\""],[9513,"\"And I dislike that your slave woman be a polytheist.\""],[9514,"We disagreed about the recitation of this letter: {And He knows what you do} or do you do? So I came to Ibn Mas'ud to ask him about that. While I was with him, a man came to him and said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, a man committed adultery with his wife, then they repented and made amends.\" So 'Abdullah recited this verse: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds, and He knows what you do}."],[9515,"\"They are fornicators as long as they are together.\" It was said to Ibn Mas'ud: \"What if they repent?\" He said: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds}. Ibn Mas'ud kept repeating it until I said: \"Indeed, he sees no harm in it.\""],[9516,"About misdeeds} the verse"],[9517,"that he said, “They are two fornicators as long as they are together.”"],[9518,"Ibn Mas'ud and Aisha both said, \"They will continue to be adulterers as long as they continue to meet.\""],[9519,"that a man should have intercourse with his slave woman as fornication.”"],[9520,"“Half the punishment will be upon her, but she will not receive half the concession.”"],[9521,"“The slave woman is to be confirmed free of pregnancy by one menstrual period.”"],[9522,"“Divorce and the waiting period pertain to the woman.”"],[9523,"“Divorce pertains to men, and the waiting period pertains to women.”"],[9524,"“If she is freed while married to a slave and does not know that she has the option, or is not given the choice until her husband is freed or until he dies or she dies, they inherit from one another.”"],[9525,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “The likeness of the one who frees his concubine and then marries her is like the likeness of the one who offers his camel as a sacrificial animal and then rides it.”"],[9526,"“Selling her is her divorce.”"],[9527,"“If you must do it, then place it in the share of her child.”"],[9528,"Omar, we definitely find this to be true. I don't desire anything, and yet I am told that I only go to the daughters of so-and-so to look at them. At this point, Abdullah bin Mas'ood said to him, \"Didn't you know that Ibrahim complained to Allah about the nature of Sarah's womb? It was said to him, 'She was created from a rib, so wear her according to what she had in her, as long as it does not bring disgrace upon her in her religion.'\" Upon hearing this, Omar said, \"Indeed, Allah has filled your heart with much knowledge.\""],[9529,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd said concerning a virgin who fornicates with a virgin, “They are each to be flogged one hundred lashes and banished for a year.”"],[9530,"Ibn Masʿūd said concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, “If he forced her, she is freed and he is fined her equivalent; and if she willingly obeyed him, he keeps her and is fined her equivalent.”"],[9531,"Then we will stone you if you have been married before. They said, 'He only came to his wife's slave woman.' ʿAbd Allah said, 'If you forced her, then set her free and give your wife a slave woman in her place.' He said, 'By Allah, I forced her and struck her.' He did not stone him, and he ordered that he be flogged below the prescribed punishment."],[9532,"It is not lawful for this slave woman to be stripped, stretched out, shackled, or fettered."],[9533,"Her embracing Islam is her marital chastity."],[9534,"ʿAbd Allah: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you} Set free a slave."],[9535,"ʿAbd Allah: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you} Set free a slave."],[9536,"ʿAbd Allah: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you} Set free a slave."],[9537,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I swore that I would not sleep on my bed for a year. ʿAbd Allah recited this verse: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors.} Expiate your oath and sleep on your bed. He said, 'I am wealthy.' He said, 'Set free a slave.'"],[9538,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I swore that I would not sleep on my bed for a year. ʿAbd Allah recited this verse: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors.} Expiate your oath and sleep on your bed. He said, 'I am wealthy.' He said, 'Set free a slave.'"],[9539,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I swore that I would not sleep on my bed for a year. ʿAbd Allah recited this verse: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors.} Expiate your oath and sleep on your bed. He said, 'I am wealthy.' He said, 'Set free a slave.'"],[9540,"Umar said to Ibn Masʿud, 'What are these people saying?' He said, 'I did that.' He said, 'Did you see that?' He said, 'Yes.' They said, 'We came to summon him, and there he was asking him.'"],[9541,"On the servants of Allah, as much as you are able."],[9542,"From ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud regarding a virgin who is coerced: A virgin is entitled to the equivalent of the dower of one of her women, and a previously married woman is entitled to the equivalent dower of someone like her."],[9543,"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said regarding a slave woman who is forced: \"If she was a virgin, then one-tenth of her price, and if she was previously married, then half of one-tenth of her price.\""],[9544,"From Ali and Ibn Mas'ud: they said: \"A small or large amount of suckling makes marriage unlawful.\""],[9545,"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said regarding suckling: \"A small or large amount of it makes marriage unlawful.\""],[9546,"Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: \"A woman given three divorces is entitled to lodging and maintenance.\""],[9547,"\"Like the departure of people who leave at dawn after the Fajr prayer.\""],[9548,"\"You and your companions eat one-third, give one-third as charity, and send one-third to the family of my brother Utbah.\" It was said to Sufyan: \"Is it voluntary?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[9549,"You hear Allah say: {The Hajj is in months well-known}. I do not consider these except to be the months of Hajj."],[9550,"\"The impotent man is given a year's delay; if he consummates with her, then fine, otherwise they are separated.\""],[9551,"\"The impotent man is given a year's delay.\""],[9552,"\"The engagement will be postponed for a year, if they agree to it. Otherwise, they will be separated and she will get the alimony.\""],[9553,"\"Whoever divorces in jest or marries in jest, it is valid.\""],[9554,"He used to say: \"The sexual intercourse of her master does not make her lawful for her husband until she marries another husband.\""],[9555,"Allah ﷻ has prohibited twelve women, and I dislike twelve: the slave woman and her mother; the two sisters being combined; the slave woman when your father has had intercourse with her; the slave woman when your son has had intercourse with her; the slave woman when she commits adultery; the slave woman in the waiting period of another; the slave woman who has a husband; your slave woman who is a polytheist; your paternal aunt and maternal aunt through suckling."],[9556,"He gave him nabīdh to drink from a green jar. Abu Wāʾil said: “I have seen that jar.”"],[9557,"“I used to prepare nabīdh for ʿAbdullāh in a green jar while he watched it, and he would drink from it.”"],[9558,"\"A man from the people said, 'Has it really been revealed like this?' So Abdullah said, 'Woe to you! I have indeed recited it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said to me, \"You have done well.\"' While he was talking, he smelled the odor of alcohol from him. So Abdullah said, 'Do you drink alcohol and deny the Quran? I will not stand until you are lashed with the punishment.'\""],[9559,"A man said, “It was not revealed like that.” I drew close to him and detected the smell of wine from him. I said, “Do you deny the truth and drink impurity? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it like this. I will not leave you until I impose the prescribed punishment on you.” So he imposed the prescribed punishment on him."],[9560,"ʿAbdullāh said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, would not place your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9561,"One of us fell ill, and suk r was prescribed for him. We came to ʿAbdullāh and asked him. He said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has not placed your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9562,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Do not give your children [nabīdh] to drink. They were born upon the fiṭrah. Would you give them to drink what is not lawful for them? Their sin is upon the one who gave it to them to drink, for Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has not placed your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9563,"“Those who fall from mountaintops, are eaten by wild beasts, or drown in the seas are martyrs in the sight of Allah.”"],[9564,"About a man who manumitted his slave at death while he had no other wealth and owed a debt, he said: “He should work to earn his value.”"],[9565,"“A slave girl of mine nursed a son of mine, and I want to sell her.” Ibn Masʿūd detested that and said: “Would that the one to whom I sell her were called the mother of my child.”"],[9566,"From its owner: “If its owner comes, he is given the choice: if he chooses the reward, it is his; if he chooses his property, his property is his.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “Thus do with lost property.” The wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq."],[9567,"“Those are the two times: withholding during life and squandering at death.”"],[9568,"“That one of you should die leaving neither kin nor relatives. What prevents him, when that is the case, from placing his wealth among the poor or the needy?”"],[9569,"My uncle bequeathed his estate to me, and this is part of his estate. May I buy it? He said: \"No, and do not borrow anything from their wealth.\""],[9570,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, shall I buy this horse? He said: \"What is the matter with it?\" He said: Its owner bequeathed it to me. He said: \"Do not buy it, and do not borrow anything from his wealth.\""],[9571,"Quasi-intentional killing is with a stone, a stick, a whip, a push, or a throw, and everything with which you deliberately strike someone; in it there is aggravation in the blood money. And mistake is when you throw something and miss with it."],[9572,"Quasi-intentional killing is with a stone and a stick."],[9573,"From ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud, they said: \"Aggravation in quasi-intentional killing; one is not killed for it.\""],[9574,"Quasi-intentional killing is twenty-five hiqqahs, twenty-five jadhaʿahs, twenty-five bint makhads, and twenty-five bint labuns."],[9575,"“The blood money of one who killed by mistake is twenty Hiqqah (three-year-old she camels), twenty Jadha'ah (four year old she camels), twenty Bint Makhad (one year old she camel), twenty Bint Labun (two year old she camels), and twenty Bani Makhad (one year old she camels).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2631)"],[9576,"Ibn Masʿud: \"For every pair of organs, the full blood money is due, and for every single organ, the full blood money is due.\""],[9577,"The two eyes are equal, the two testicles are equal, the fingers are equal, the teeth are equal, the two hands are equal, and the two feet are equal."],[9578,"Regarding a man and a woman: \"They are equal up to five camels.\" He said: And ʿAli said: \"Half of everything.\""],[9579,"Regarding a man from whom retaliation is taken and then he dies. He said: \"Upon the one who exacted retaliation is his blood money, then the blood money for his wound is deducted from it.\""],[9580,"ʿUmar said to Ibn Masʿud, while he was beside him: \"What do you say?\" Ibn Masʿud said: \"I say to him: He has been secured from execution.\" He said: Then he struck his shoulder and said: \"A vessel filled with knowledge.\""],[9581,"When death comes, it wipes out everything."],[9582,"Ibn Masʿūd [said]: \"The people of faith are the most restrained in killing.\""],[9583,"And ʿAlī also said it."],[9584,"He said: \"For every covenanted person, Magian or otherwise, the blood-money is payable in full.\""],[9585,"\"A slave of mine stole a cloak from another slave of mine. Is his hand to be amputated?\" He said: \"No. Your property, one part of it from another.\""],[9586,"Regarding spying: \"If it becomes clear to us\"—meaning, \"we shall enforce the punishment upon him.\""],[9587,"\"The hand is not to be amputated except for a dinar or ten dirhams.\""],[9588,"ʿAbd Allāh [said]: \"The hand is not to be amputated except for a dinar or ten dirhams.\""],[9589,"\"The shroud is to be taken from the entire estate.\""],[9590,"ʿAbd Allāh [said]: \"Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever.\" Al-Masʿūdī did not say it on the authority of his father."],[9591,"\"Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever.\" Isrāʾīl did not trace it back to the Prophet, but Sharīk did trace it back."],[9592,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Kill snakes, for whoever fears their retaliation is not of me.\""],[9593,"A Muslim has six duties of kindness toward another Muslim: he greets him with salām when he meets him, answers him when he invites him, says \"May God have mercy on you\" when he sneezes, attends his funeral when he dies, gives him sincere counsel in his absence, and loves for him what he loves for himself. Abū Jaʿfar al-Farrāʾ did not trace it back to the Prophet, but Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī did trace it back."],[9594,"A time will come upon people when a man will come to a grave and say, “Would that I were in the place of its occupant.” It is not out of love for meeting Allah, but because of the affliction he sees."],[9595,"A time will certainly come upon you when a man will pass by a grave and say, “Would that I were in the place of this one,” while he has no love for meeting Allah, but because of the severity of the affliction he sees. It was said, “What is best at that time?” He said, “A sturdy horse and a weapon with which a man can go wherever he goes.”"],[9596,"“For a camel smeared with tar to crowd against me is more beloved to me than for a perfumed woman to crowd against me.”"],[9597,"“For a man to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry.”"],[9598,"Abdullah: “Strip the Quran bare, and do not mix with it what is not part of it.”"],[9599,"“The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose of your religion is prayer.”"],[9600,"“The trumpet is like a horn into which it is blown.”"],[9601,"Abdullah: “Mix with people and keep away from them.”"],[9602,"“Mix with people and be sincere with them regarding what they desire, but as for your religion, do not let them touch it.”"],[9603,"There was a man who had wealth and never did any good with it. When death came to him, he said to his family, “When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind.” So that was done to him. Then Allah gathered him and said, “What made you do what you did?” He said, “Out of fear of You.” So Allah’s mercy reached him."],[9604,"Abdullah: “Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will never guide you when they have already led themselves astray. Either they will tell you something true and you will disbelieve them, or something false and you will believe them.”"],[9605,"“Then your Prophet ﷺ will stand as the fourth of four.” Shuʿba said, “I only heard this in this hadith.”"],[9607,"\"Allah ﷻ will punish a people from among the people of faith, then remove them through the intercession of the intercessors.\" Then he said: \"These are those whom the intercession of the intercessors will not benefit.\""],[9610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: People will stand before the Lord of the Worlds for forty years, their eyes fixed, awaiting the decisive judgment, until sweat engulfs them from the severity of the distress. Then Allah ﷻ will descend, and the nations will kneel, and He will call out: O people, are you not content with your Lord who created you and commanded you to worship Him, then you turned away from Him and denied His favor, that He leaves you and what you turned to? Every person will turn to what he turned to. Then a caller will call out: Whoever used to turn to something, let him stick to it. He said: Then those who turned to a stone, or a piece of wood, or a riding animal will depart. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Zayd b. Abi Unaysa."],[9611,"We conversed one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the talk kept us up. When morning came, we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: The prophets were presented to me with their followers from their nations. There was a prophet ﷺ with a small group from his nation, and a prophet with no one. Allah has informed you about the people of Lot, for He said: {Is there not among you a man of right judgment?} He said: Until Moses b. Imran ﷺ passed by with those with him from the Children of Israel. I said: My Lord, where is my nation? He said: Look to your right. I looked and there were the hills, the hills of Makkah, filled with the faces of men. He said: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? I said: I am pleased, my Lord. He said: Look to your left. I looked and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. He said: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? I said: I am pleased, my Lord. He said: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan al-Asadi came and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me one of them. He said: \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me one of them. He said: \"ʿUkkasha has preceded you to it.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"If you can, may my father and mother be your ransom, be among the seventy thousand, then be so. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the hills. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I have seen many people crowding together.\" Then he said: \"I hope that those who follow me from my nation will be a quarter of Paradise.\" The people said takbir. Then he said: \"I hope that they will be half of the people of Paradise.\" The people said takbir. Then he recited this verse: {A multitude of those from among the first, and a few from those of later times.} They discussed among themselves who these seventy thousand were. Some said: People born in Islam and died upon it. Then the matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not practice tiyarah, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[9612,"We spoke at length one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we went to him in the morning. He said: The prophets were presented to me with their nations. A prophet ﷺ would pass by with a small group, a prophet with a band, a prophet with a few, and a prophet with no one. Until Moses ﷺ passed by me with a large throng from the Children of Israel, and they impressed me. I said: Who are these? It was said: This is your brother Moses, and with him are the Children of Israel. I said: Where is my nation? It was said: Look to your right. I looked and the hills were filled with the faces of men. Then it was said to me: Look to your left. I looked and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. It was said to me: Are you pleased? I said: I am pleased, O Lord, I am pleased, O Lord. It was said to me: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom. If you can be among the seventy thousand, then do so. If you fall short, then be among the people of the hills. If you fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I have seen people crowding together.\" Then ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan al-Asadi stood and said: Supplicate for me, O Messenger of Allah, that He make me among the seventy. So he supplicated for him. Then another man stood and said: Supplicate to Allah, O Messenger of Allah, that He make me among them. He said: \"ʿUkkasha has preceded you to it.\" He said: Then we discussed among ourselves who these seventy thousand were: People born in Islam until they died upon it. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not practice tiyarah, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[9613,"By Allah, I am not more grieved over these two if they died than my grief over these two birds if they fell dead. Indeed I find for them what a parent finds for his child. But I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Hour will not be established until every tribe is ruled by its hypocrites.\" That is why I desired that we die before that time."],[9614,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The feet of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection from before his Lord until he is asked about five things: his life, in what he spent it; his youth, in what he wore it away; his wealth, from where he earned it and on what he spent it; and what he did with what he knew."],[9615,"That this verse was revealed with Allah reproaching them except for four years: {And do not be like those who were given the Scripture before, and a long period passed over them, so their hearts hardened; and many of them are defiantly disobedient.}"],[9616,"The day seemed long to me, so I tried to remember whom I could talk to. He said: He began to narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I narrated to him. Then he started to narrate to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be a fitnah in which the one lying down is better than the one reclining, the one reclining is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one galloping. Its slain are all in the Fire.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when will that be? He said: \"That will be in the days of al-harj.\" I said: When are the days of al-harj? He said: \"When a man does not trust his companion.\" I said: What do you command me to do if I live to see that time? He said: \"Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he enters my house? He said: \"Then enter your room.\" I said: What do you think if he enters my room? He said: \"Then enter your mosque and do like this,\" and he grasped his right hand on his wrist, \"and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that.\""],[9617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The last person to enter Paradise will walk on the bridge and will walk one step and then kneel. The fire will surround him, and when he surpasses it, he will turn towards it and say, 'Blessed is He who saved me from you. He has given me something that He has not given to anyone among the earlier and later people.' A tree will be raised for him, and he will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to this tree so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything other than this?' He will say, 'Yes, my Lord, but I will not ask You for anything other than this.' Allah will excuse him because He will see something that he cannot bear, and he will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to it so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Then a tree will be raised for him at the gate of Paradise, which is better than the first one. He will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to this tree so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything other than this?' He will say, 'Yes, my Lord, but I will not ask You for anything other than this.' Allah will excuse him because He will see something that he cannot bear, and He will bring him closer to it. He will then hear the voices of the people of Paradise, and he will say, 'O Lord, admit me to it.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, would it please you if I were to give you the entire world and a similar world along with it?' He will say, 'Are You making fun of me, though You are the Lord of all the worlds?' The Messenger of Allah laughed and then said, 'Do you not ask me why I laughed?' The person asked, 'Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'I laughed at the laughter of the Lord of the worlds when He said, 'Do you make fun of Me, though You are the Lord of all the worlds?' He said, 'No, I am not making fun of you, but I can do whatever I will.'\""],[9618,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The deeds of the children of Adam are presented every Monday and every Thursday. He has mercy on those who show mercy and forgives those who seek forgiveness, then He leaves the people of rancor with their rancor.\""],[9619,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A time will surely come upon the people when you will envy a man for a light burden as you envy him today for abundant wealth and children, until one of you passes by the grave of his brother and rolls upon it as an animal rolls in its pasture, saying: Would that I were in his place. It is not out of longing for Allah nor for righteous deeds he has sent ahead, but only because of the affliction that befalls him."],[9620,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When a servant prays but does not complete his prayer—its humility and its bowing—and frequently turns around, it is not accepted from him. And whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, even if he is honorable in the sight of Allah.\""],[9621,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\""],[9622,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A person is with the one he loves.”"],[9623,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was a witness over them as long as I was among them.”"],[9624,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to pray at the eclipse of the sun and the moon. And when you see that it has afflicted them, then hasten to prayer; for if it is the one you fear, it will occur while you are not heedless, and if it is not, you will have attained good and earned it."],[9625,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying and greeted him, and he gestured to me."],[9626,"From Abu Rafiʿ, the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, from ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, that the Prophet of God ﷺ said: “There was no prophet but he had disciples who guided by his guidance and followed his way. Then after them came successors who say what they do not do and do what you disapprove of. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer. Beyond that there is not even a mustard seed’s weight of faith.”"],[9627,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever has a need and brings it to people, his poverty will not be relieved; but if he brings it to God, may He be exalted, God will soon grant him sufficiency, either a delayed reward or immediate wealth.”"],[9628,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Hour has drawn near, and they only increase in distance from it.”"],[9629,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Treat yourselves with cow’s milk, for I hope that God will place healing in it, for it grazes on trees.”"],[9630,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who, when he hears the call to prayer, says the takbir and bears witness that there is no god but God and bears witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then says: ‘O God, give Muhammad the wasilah and the excellence, and place him in the highest rank, and in the chosen ones his love, and in those brought near his remembrance,’ but that intercession will be assured for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[9631,"I heard Ibn Masʿud say: “When the Messenger of God ﷺ became angry, his cheeks would turn red.”"],[9632,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “God, may He be exalted, is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.”"],[9633,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, I think he was ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, that the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to delay the noon prayer until cooler, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell."],[9634,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying in the midday heat, but he did not complain to us."],[9635,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When one of you fears the ruler, let him say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, be a protector for me from the evil of so-and-so son of so-and-so—meaning the one he fears—and from the evil of the jinn and mankind and their followers, lest any of them transgress against me. Mighty is Your protection, and exalted is Your praise, and there is no god besides You."],[9636,"A rooster crowed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and a man said: O Allah, curse him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not curse it and do not revile it, for it calls to prayer.\""],[9637,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The one who remembers Allah among the heedless is like the one who stands firm among those who flee.\""],[9638,"It was revealed concerning a group of Arabs who used to worship a group of jinn. The jinn accepted Islam, but the group of Arabs were unaware of it, regarding His saying: {Those whom they call upon seek means of access to their Lord}."],[9639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no believing servant from whose eyes tears flow, even if it were the size of a fly's head, out of fear of Allah, except that Allah will forbid him from the Fire.\""],[9640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The closest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who sends the most blessings upon me.\""],[9641,"From ʿAbdullah, I do not know but that he raised it [to the Prophet]: \"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt, and she may not stipulate the divorce of her sister in order to empty what is in her plate.\""],[9642,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most virtuous? He said: \"Prayer at its appointed time.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Kindness to parents.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"That people are safe from your tongue.\" Then he fell silent, and if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9643,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which deeds are most virtuous. He said: \"Prayer at its proper time.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Then kindness to parents.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Jihad in the path of Allah.\" Then he fell silent, and if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9644,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? Or: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: \"Prayer at its proper time.\" I said: Then which? He said: \"Kindness to parents.\" I said: Then which? He said: \"Then jihad in the path of Allah.\" And if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9645,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ which deeds are most virtuous, and he said: \"Prayer at its proper time, then jihad in the path of Allah.\""],[9646,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time, then dutifulness to parents, then jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9647,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which deed is best?” He said, “The prayer at the beginning of its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.” It was said, “Then which?” He said, “Dutifulness to parents.” It was said, “Then which?” He said, “Jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9649,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its appointed time.” I said, “Then which?” He said, “Dutifulness to parents.” I said, “Then which?” He said, “Jihad in the cause of Allah.” Then he fell silent with me, and if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9650,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, that Ibn Masʿud said: “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Establishing the prayer at its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9651,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, that Ibn Masʿud said: “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Establishing the prayer at its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9652,"You asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “The prayer at its proper time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9653,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.”"],[9654,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.”"],[9655,"The prescribed prayer at its time and dutifulness to parents."],[9656,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayers at their times, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And the wording is from the hadith of Maʿmar, and the others are similar."],[9657,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9658,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ‘Which deeds are best?’ He said: ‘That you perform the prayer at its proper times.’ He said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ He said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ And if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me. The wording is that of the hadith of Ibrahim b. Tahman, and the others are similar to it."],[9659,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah and closest to Him?’ He said: ‘Prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then what comes after that?’ He said: ‘Then kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then what comes after that?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ And if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me."],[9660,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah and closest to Him?’ He said: ‘Prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then what comes after that?’ He said: ‘Then kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then what comes after that?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ And if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me."],[9661,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ‘Which deeds are best?’ He said: ‘Prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ By Allah, if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me. I said: ‘Then which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?’ He said: ‘That you set up a rival to Allah, while He created you.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘That you kill your child for fear that he will eat with you.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘That you commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife.’ It was not long before Allah sent down the confirmation of it: ‘And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery. And whoever does that will meet a penalty.’ Yazid b. Mu‘awiyah transmitted it well, while Hammad b. Salamah did not transmit it well."],[9662,"I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?’ He said: ‘Establishing prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Then kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Then struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ Then he fell silent, and if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me."],[9663,"I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?’ He said: ‘Establishing prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Then kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Then struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ Then he fell silent, and if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me."],[9664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, ‘Which deed is best?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents and prayer at its time.’ Za’idah traced it back to the Prophet, while Shu‘bah and Hammad b. Salamah stopped it at the companion."],[9665,"‘The prayers at their times.’"],[9666,"‘O Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, which of the degrees of Islam is best?’ He said: ‘Prayer.’ He said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Zakat.’ He said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ He said: ‘Then with whom is a person (to be)?’ He said: ‘I think he said: ‘With the one he loves.’’"],[9667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us and then increased in his prayer or decreased. Mansur said, ‘It is Ibrahim who forgot, whether from ‘Alqamah or ‘Alqamah from ‘Abdullah b. Mas‘ud.’ ‘Abdullah said: ‘When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer and turned his face toward us, we said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?’ He said, ‘No.’ Then what he had done was mentioned to him, so he bent his leg, faced the qiblah, and prostrated twice. Then he turned away and said, ‘If something new had occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you. But I am a human being like you; I forget as you forget. So if I forget, remind me. And if any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek what is right, complete it upon that, then say the salam and prostrate twice.’’"],[9668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us a prayer in which he added or subtracted. When he finished his prayer, we said, ‘Has something been added to the prayer?’ He said, ‘What is that?’ We said, ‘You prayed with us such and such.’ So he turned, bent his legs, and prostrated twice. Then he turned his face toward us and said, ‘I am only a human being like you. So if I forget, remind me. And if any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek the right course, complete it, then prostrate twice.’"],[9669,"The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek what he thinks is right, complete it, then prostrate twice.’"],[9670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted something. When he finished, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'If something had occurred, I would have informed you. I am only a human being; I forget just as you forget. So whoever among you prays and adds or omits something, let him seek what is correct, complete it, and prostrate twice for forgetfulness.'"],[9671,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and either he added or omitted something. Ibrahim said: 'By Allah, that came only from me.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'No.' We told him what he had done. He said: 'When a man adds or omits something, he should prostrate twice.' He then prostrated twice."],[9672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If one of you doubts in the obligatory prayer, let him seek what is correct, then prostrate twice for forgetfulness.'"],[9673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what is correct and prostrate twice for forgetfulness while sitting.'"],[9674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted something. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' We said: 'You prayed such-and-such.' He then faced the qiblah, prostrated twice, and then said the salam."],[9675,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the 'Asr prayer and rose in the fourth rak'ah without sitting until he prayed a fifth with us. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five with us.' He then faced the qiblah, said the takbir, and prostrated twice."],[9676,"'Alqamah prayed the 'Asr prayer with five rak'ahs. When he said the salam, we said: 'You prayed five.' He said to a man from al-Nakha' called Ibrahim b. Suwayd: 'Is that so, O one-eyed?' He said: 'Yes.' He then prostrated with us twice while standing, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam. Then he said: ''Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the 'Asr prayer with five rak'ahs. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' We said: 'You prayed five.' He said to a man called Dhu al-Shimalayn: 'Is that so, O Dhu al-Yadayn?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He then prostrated with us twice while sitting, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam. Then he said: 'O people, I am only a human being like you; I forget just as you forget. So if I forget, remind me. And if one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he added or omitted something, let him seek what is correct in that, complete it, and prostrate twice. For if anything were added to your prayer, I would have informed you.'"],[9677,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr. When he finished his prayer, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' He then faced the qiblah and prostrated twice. Then he said: 'I am only a human being; I forget just as you forget. So if one of you errs in his prayer, let him prostrate twice.'"],[9678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' He then prostrated twice."],[9679,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed five rak'ahs and prostrated twice."],[9680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs. They said to him: 'O Prophet of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He then said the salam and prostrated twice for forgetfulness."],[9681,"He led the people in five rak'ahs. When he finished, they said: 'You prayed five rak'ahs.' 'Alqamah said: 'Do you say that, O one-eyed?' meaning Ibrahim. He said: 'Yes.' 'Alqamah then prostrated twice for forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud and said the salam. Then he turned to them and informed them from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud from the Prophet ﷺ that he did that."],[9682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five rakʿahs with them. When he said the salam, he was told about that, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice while seated."],[9683,"ʿAlqamah led us in Zuhr prayer with five rakʿahs. When he finished, they said to him, “You prayed five.” He said, “I did not.” Then he said, “Is that so, O one-eyed man?” He said, “I said, ‘Yes.’” So he turned and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said the salam. Then he mentioned from ʿAbdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prayed five rakʿahs and saw them whispering to one another. He said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “And what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” He said, “No, but I forgot.” So he turned and prostrated twice."],[9684,"ʿAlqamah led us in prayer with five rakʿahs. He was told, so he said, “I did not.” I said, “Yes, you did.” He said, “And you, O one-eyed man?” I said, “Yes.” So he prostrated twice, then narrated to us from ʿAbdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prayed five rakʿahs, and the people whispered to one another, saying, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No.” They told him, so he bent his leg and prostrated twice, then said, “I am only a human being; I forget as you forget.”"],[9685,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he did something similar."],[9686,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr or ʿAsr with five rakʿahs, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “These two prostrations are for whoever of you thinks that he added or omitted something.”"],[9687,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rakʿahs and then prostrated twice."],[9688,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed five rakʿahs. When he finished, it was said, “O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No, and what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” He said, “I am only a human being like you; I remember as you remember and forget as you forget.” Then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[9689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in Zuhr or ʿAsr prayer with five rakʿahs. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No, and what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” So he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice, then said, “These two prostrations are for whoever of you thinks that he added or omitted something.”"],[9690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer, then entered [his house]. Some of the people said to others, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “And what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” So he took him by the hand and went out to the mosque, where there was a circle in which Abu Bakr and Umar were present. He said, “Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true?” They said, “Yes, O Prophet of Allah.” So he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice."],[9691,"ʿAbdullah: “Rather, you have recited quickly, like the recitation of poetry and the scattering of bad dates. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite pairs of similar surahs in one rakʿah.” Then he mentioned ten rakʿahs with twenty surahs, according to the arrangement of ʿAbdullah, the last of them being “When the sun is wrapped up [in darkness]” (al-Takwir) and al-Dukhan."],[9692,"Give every surah its due share of bowing and prostration, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recite twenty surahs in ten rakʿahs."],[9693,"Reciting quickly like the recitation of poetry? Recite as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: two surahs from the Mufassal in one rakʿah."],[9694,"I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine, two surahs in a rakʿah."],[9695,"Rapid recitation like the rapid recitation of poetry? Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the analogous surahs, two surahs, twenty surahs."],[9696,"I recited the mufassal last night in a single rakʿah. He said, 'Scattered [recitation] like scattering poor dates, and rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair together, two surahs in a rakʿah.' The wording is that of the hadith of Abu ʿUbayd."],[9697,"ʿAbd Allah [said]: I certainly knew the analogous surahs with which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray: al-Dhariyat and al-Tur, and Iqtarabat and al-Najm, and al-Rahman and al-Waqiʿah, and Nun and al-Haqqah, and al-Muzzammil and La Uqsimu bi-Yawm al-Qiyamah, and Hal Ata ʿala al-Insan and al-Mursalat, and ʿAmma Yatasaʾalun and al-Naziʿat, and ʿAbasa and Waylun li-l-Mutaffifin, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat and Ha Mim al-Dukhan."],[9698,"I recited the mufassal tonight in a single rakʿah. ʿAbd Allah said, 'Rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in a single rakʿah,' and he mentioned twenty surahs from the beginning of the mufassal, pairing two surahs [in each rakʿah]."],[9699,"I certainly know the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in a single rakʿah. Then ʿAbd Allah stood, took ʿAlqamah by the hand, and ʿAlqamah came out to us. We said to him, 'Did he tell you the analogous surahs?' He said, 'He said the first twenty of the mufassal, among them a surah from the Al Ha Mim family: al-Dukhan, and its counterpart ʿAmma Yatasaʾalun.'"],[9700,"I certainly memorize the paired surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: eighteen from the mufassal and two surahs from the Al Ha Mim family."],[9701,"I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair together, two surahs in a rakʿah."],[9702,"Rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair: twenty surahs in ten rakʿahs."],[9703,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a man who left behind his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister. He assigned to the daughter one half, to the son's daughter one sixth, and what remained to the sister."],[9704,"To the daughter one half and to the sister one half, and he did not assign anything to the son's daughter. He said, 'Ask Ibn Masʿud, for he will agree with me.' So they asked Ibn Masʿud and informed him of al-Ashʿari's statement. He said, 'Then I have gone astray and I am not among the rightly guided. I judge among you by the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"To the daughter one half, to the son's daughter one sixth, and to the sister one third.\"' This reached al-Ashʿari, and he said, 'Do not ask me about anything as long as this learned man is among you.'"],[9705,"Then I have gone astray and I am not among the rightly guided, but I judge concerning it by the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"To the daughter one half, to the son's daughter a share to complete the two thirds, and what remains to the full sister.\""],[9706,"From a man who died leaving his daughter, his son's daughter, and his full sister. He said: 'To the daughter belongs half, and whatever remains goes to the full sister.' He said to us: 'Ibn Masʿūd will surely say the same as I said.' So they asked Ibn Masʿūd, then they told him what Abū Mūsā had said. He said: 'How could I say what he said when I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"To the daughter belongs half, to the son's daughter one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and whatever remains goes to the full sister.\"'"],[9707,"I would then have gone astray and I am not of the rightly guided. But I will judge in it as the Prophet ﷺ judged in it: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9708,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9709,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who is tattooed, the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who has them joined, the one who consumes ribā and the one who enables it, and the one who makes a woman lawful (for her previous husband) and the one for whom it is done."],[9711,"He said: 'I had a slave, so I freed him and made him a sāʾibah for the sake of God.' ʿAbd Allāh said to him: 'The people of Islam do not set slaves free as sāʾibah; only the people of the Jāhiliyyah used to do that. You are the patron of his favor and the most entitled of people to his inheritance. If you feel uneasy about anything, show it to us and we will place it in the public treasury.'"],[9712,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ, delaying the latter to the end of its time and performing the former at the beginning of its time."],[9713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine the two prayers while traveling."],[9714,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You are the most similar of nations to the Children of Israel. You will surely follow their way closely, step by step, until there is nothing among them but there will be something like it among you, to the point that if one of them were to pass by a woman, one of them would stand with her and have intercourse, then return to his companions laughing to them and they would laugh back to him.'"],[9715,"That he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[9716,"They used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ. One of them said: 'Peace be upon God.' He said: 'Who said \"Peace be upon God\"? Indeed God is al-Salām (the Source of Peace), but say: \"Greetings, prayers, and good things are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\"'"],[9717,"When we sat (in prayer), we used to say: 'Peace be upon God, peace be upon Jibrīl.' The Prophet ﷺ heard us and said: 'Indeed God is al-Salām (the Source of Peace). So when one of you sits in prayer, let him say: \"Greetings, prayers, and good things are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God.\"'"],[9718,"When we sat down in the prayer, we used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon us from our Lord; peace be upon Jibril and Mika'il; peace be upon so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam (the Source of Peace). When you sit in the prayer, say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. When he says that, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens or on the earth. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.' Then he chooses whatever words he wishes."],[9719,"From Hammad, Mansur, Husayn, al-A'mash, and Abu Hashim, from Abu Wa'il and Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, who said: We did not know what to say in the prayer; we used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon Mika'il.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud and said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam. When you sit after two rak'ahs, say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin.' Abu Wa'il said in the hadith of 'Abdullah from the Prophet ﷺ: 'When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and the earth.' Abu Ishaq said in the hadith of 'Abdullah: 'When you say it, it reaches every angel brought near, or every prophet sent, or every righteous servant. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9720,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ heard that and said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9721,"They used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9722,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril and Mika'il and every angel whose name we know.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught us: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu. When you say this, every angel, every prophet, and every righteous servant is included in your words.'"],[9723,"The Prophet ﷺ turned to them and taught them the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9724,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon so-and-so; peace be upon so-and-so,' naming those from the angels and prophets whom we knew. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught us the tashahhud, and we used to learn it as one of us would learn a surah from the Qur'an. He said: 'Say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9725,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people would say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon Mika'il; peace be upon the angels brought near.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught them the tashahhud and said: 'Say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9727,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril,' until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9729,"'Abdullah said: We used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say, 'Peace be upon Allah.' He said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9730,"From Mansur, Sulayman, Hammad, Abu Hashim, and Mughira, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, who said: We used to say in the prayer: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Allah Himself is Peace. But say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9731,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to teach us the Tashahhud and the Khutbah, just as he would teach us a Surah from the Quran, beginning with \"All greetings, prayers, and good words belong to Allah\" until his saying, \"His servant and Messenger.\""],[9732,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9733,"We, when we sat, used to say: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il, peace be upon the angels.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us words which, if we say them, we greet every angel in the heaven and every righteous servant on the earth: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9734,"The translation of the passage into English is: \"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , taught us to recite the Tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and good acts are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' \""],[9735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer just as he taught us a surah from the Qur'an: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9736,"We did not know what to say in every rak'ah; we glorified, magnified, and praised our Lord. Muhammad ﷺ was given the openings of good and its endings—or he said: its comprehensive words. He said to us: 'When you sit after every two rak'ahs, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then let him choose of supplication what pleases him most and supplicate with it.'\""],[9737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud in prayer: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' The wording is that of the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Ishaq, and the others are similar."],[9738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said] to us: 'When you sit after every two rak'ahs, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he chooses of supplication what pleases him most.'\""],[9739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Qur'an: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9740,"We did not know what to say in every two rak'ahs of prayer except that we magnified, glorified, and praised our Lord. Muhammad ﷺ was given the openings of good and its endings. He said: 'When you sit for the tashahhud, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9741,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud and said: 'Say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'Say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9744,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran, and he would say: “Learn it, for there is no prayer without the tashahhud.”"],[9745,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and taught me the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9746,"He heard him say: ʿAlqama took me by the hand, ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud took ʿAlqama by the hand, and the Prophet ﷺ took Ibn Masʿud by the hand, and he taught him the tashahhud in prayer: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9747,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9748,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the tashahhud in prayer. He said: We used to memorize it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as we would memorize the letters of the Quran, the waws and the alifs. He said: When he sat on his left hip, he said: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” Then he would supplicate to his Lord, then he would say the salam and depart."],[9750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: When one of you sits in his prayer, let him say: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9751,"We used to say in prayer: “Peace be upon our Lord.” It was said to us: Say: “Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah,” for when you say that, you greet everyone in the heavens and the earth."],[9752,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran.”"],[9753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9754,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. O Allah, bless Muhammad and his household as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless us with them. O Allah, bless Muhammad and his household as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless us with them. The prayers of Allah and the prayers of the believers upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, ﷺ and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\""],[9755,"The Prophet ﷺ taught them the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” Al-Ajlaḥ raised it, but Ḥammād b. Salama did not raise it."],[9757,"O Allah, I ask You for all that is good, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your righteous servants have asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants have sought refuge. O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[9758,"I heard ʿAbdullah say: When one of you sits in prayer, let him say the greetings — and he mentioned the tashahhud — then he said: Let him say: O Allah, I ask You for all that is good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the best of what Your righteous servants have asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants have sought refuge. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. Our Lord, we believe, so forgive us our sins and expiate our evil deeds, and cause us to die with the righteous. Our Lord, grant us what You have promised us through Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise."],[9759,"He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given concise speech. He would teach us what to say in prayer when we sit in it: “Greetings to Allah, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.” Then he would ask for whatever came to mind after that and would desire His mercy and forgiveness with a few brief phrases, not prolonging the sitting. And he would say: I love that the request you make to Allah, when one of you sits in prayer and finishes the greeting, should be to say after that: Glory be to You, there is no god but You. Forgive my sin and set right my deeds; indeed You forgive sins to whom You will, and You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. O Forgiver, forgive me; O Accepter of repentance, accept my repentance; O Merciful, have mercy on me; O Pardoner, pardon me; O Kind, be kind to me. O Lord, enable me to be grateful for Your blessing which You have bestowed upon me, and grant me excellence in worshiping You. O Lord, I ask You for all good, and I seek refuge in You from all evil. O Lord, open for me with good and seal for me with good, and grant me a longing to meet You without harmful distress or misleading trial. Protect me from evil deeds, and whoever You protect from evil deeds, You have shown him mercy, and that is the great triumph. Then whatever supplication you make should be in humility and sincerity, for He loves His servant's humble entreaty to Him."],[9760,"He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given concise speech. He would teach us what to say in prayer when we sit in it: “Greetings to Allah, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.” Then he would ask for whatever came to mind after that and would desire His mercy and forgiveness with a few brief phrases, not prolonging the sitting. And he would say: I love that the request you make to Allah, when one of you sits in prayer and finishes the greeting, should be to say after that: Glory be to You, there is no god but You. Forgive my sin and set right my deeds; indeed You forgive sins to whom You will, and You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. O Forgiver, forgive me; O Accepter of repentance, accept my repentance; O Merciful, have mercy on me; O Pardoner, pardon me; O Kind, be kind to me. O Lord, enable me to be grateful for Your blessing which You have bestowed upon me, and grant me excellence in worshiping You. O Lord, I ask You for all good, and I seek refuge in You from all evil. O Lord, open for me with good and seal for me with good, and grant me a longing to meet You without harmful distress or misleading trial. Protect me from evil deeds, and whoever You protect from evil deeds, You have shown him mercy, and that is the great triumph. Then whatever supplication you make should be in humility and sincerity, for He loves His servant's humble entreaty to Him."],[9761,"It was recited in his presence, or he recited it: {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} Then ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient. They said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} Then ʿAbdullah said: Do you know what the nation is? The one who teaches people good, and the devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger."],[9762,"ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif, and he was not of the polytheists. Farwah, a man from Ashjaʿ, said: You forgot — indeed it is Ibrahim. He said: Who forgot? We used to liken Muʿadh to Ibrahim. He was asked about the nation and said: A teacher of good. And he was asked about the devoutly obedient and said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9763,"Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif. It was said to him: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif.} He said: Did you hear me mention Ibrahim? Then he said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif. He said: We used to liken Muʿadh to Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[9764,"ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient. Farwah said: It is a mistake; {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} He said: We used to liken him to him. He was asked about the nation and said: A teacher of good. And he was asked about the devoutly obedient and said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9765,"The nation is the one who teaches people good, and the devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger. And such was Muʿadh b. Jabal: he used to teach good and was obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9766,"A man said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, we do not see you narrating to us anything you do not know. Allah ﷻ says {Indeed Ibrahim} but you say: Indeed Muʿadh. He said: They keep hearing truth from me and rejecting it. The devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah, and Muʿadh was like that."],[9767,"On the authority of ʿAbdullah: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah. Do you know what the nation is? It is the one who teaches people good."],[9768,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself and told Ibn Masʿud to bring him three stones. He came with two stones and a piece of dung. He threw away the dung and said: “This is filth; bring me a stone.”"],[9769,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the jinn, and he said to me: “Find me three stones.” I found him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: “This is filth.”"],[9770,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and he wanted to fulfill his need, so he said, \"Bring me three stones.\" I looked for them and found two stones, but I didn't find the third stone. So, I found a small piece of dung and brought it to him. He said, \"Didn't you know that it is impure?\""],[9771,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to relieve himself and said: “Bring me three stones with which to clean myself.” I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, saying: “It is filth.”"],[9772,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ so he could relieve himself. He ordered me to bring him three stones. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and discarded the dung, saying: “This is filth.”"],[9773,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered me to bring him three stones. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and discarded the dung, saying: “It is filth.”"],[9774,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring me three stones.” He performed ablution without touching water. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He said: “Throw away the dung, for it is filth.”"],[9775,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself and said: “Bring me something with which to clean myself, but do not bring me anything that is a barrier or dung.” I did so, then he performed ablution and prayed."],[9776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set off for his need and said, \"Bring me something and do not bring me a bone or a reed.\" So I did, and he performed ablution and then prayed."],[9777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me three stones.” I brought him two stones and the dung of a donkey. He took the two stones and cast away the dung, saying: “It is impure.”"],[9778,"He made ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with nabīdh, so he performed ablution and said: “A drink that is purifying.”"],[9779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: “I have been commanded to recite to your brethren among the jinn. Let a man from you stand with me, and let no man stand who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride.” I stood with him and took a water-skin containing nabīdh and went with him. When he went out, he drew a line for me and said: “Do not step out of it, for if you step out, you will not see me nor I you until the Day of Resurrection.” Then he went and disappeared from me until I could not see him. When dawn broke, he came back and said to me: “I see you standing?” I said, “I have not sat down.” He said: “It would not have harmed you if you had.” I said, “I feared I might step out of it.” He said: “Indeed, if you had stepped out, you would not have seen me nor I you until the Day of Resurrection. Do you have water for ablution?” I said, “No.” He said, “What is this water-skin?” I said, “It contains nabīdh.” He said, “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution and began the prayer. When he finished the prayer, two men from the jinn came to him and asked him for provisions. He said, “Did I not command provisions for you and your people with what is good for you?” They said, “Yes, but we wanted some of us to witness the prayer with you.” He said, “Which people are you from?” They said, “From the people of Naṣībīn.” He said, “These two have succeeded and their people have succeeded,” and he commanded for them dung and bones as food and meat. The Prophet ﷺ forbade cleaning oneself with bone or dung."],[9780,"On the night of the jinn, two of them stayed behind and said, “We will witness the dawn prayer with you, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you have water?” I said, “I have no water, but I have a water-skin containing nabīdh.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “A good date and purifying water,” and he performed ablution. Isrāʾīl said in his version: Then he prayed the morning prayer."],[9781,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the night of the jinn: “What is in your water-skin?” He said, “Nabīdh.” He said, “A good date and purifying water.”"],[9782,"ʿAbd al-Wārith Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaqarī narrated to us, from Sharīk, from Abū Fizāra, from Abū Zayd, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought water for ablution on the night of the jinn. I said, “I have nothing but nabīdh in a water-skin.” He said, “A good date and purifying water,” and he performed ablution with it."],[9783,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was among a group of his companions, he said: “Let a man from among you stand with me, but let no man stand with me in whose heart is an atom’s weight of deceit.” So I stood with him and took the water-skin, which I thought contained only water. I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we were in upper Makkah, and I saw dark shapes gathered together. He drew a line for me and then said: “Stand here until I come to you.” I stood while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to them, and I saw them rushing toward him. The Messenger of Allah stayed away for a long part of the night, then came to me at dawn and said: “Have you been standing all this time, O Ibn Masʿud?” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not tell me to stand until I come to you?” Then he said to me: “Do you have any water for ablution?” I said: “Yes.” I opened the water-skin and found it was nabīdh. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I took it thinking it was only water, but it turned out to be nabīdh.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution with it. When he stood to pray, two figures from among them came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we would like you to lead us in our prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lined them up behind him and then prayed with us. When he finished, I said to him: “Who are these, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “These are jinn of Nasībīn; they asked me for provision, so I gave them the refuse as provision. Whatever dung they find becomes barley for them, and whatever bone they find becomes meat for them.” At that point the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade using dung and bone for istinja."],[9784,"On the night of the jinn, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you have something for purification?” I said: “Nothing but nabīdh in a water-skin.” He said: “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution."],[9785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out before the Hijrah to the outskirts of Makkah. He drew a line for me and said: “Do not do anything until I come to you.” Then he said: “Let nothing you see alarm or frighten you.” He went forward a little and sat down, and there were black men like the men of the Zutt. They were as Allah Almighty said: {They almost crowded upon him}. I wanted to get up and defend him as much as I could, but then I remembered the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed still. Then they dispersed from him, and I heard them saying: “O Messenger of Allah, our route is long and we are leaving, so give us provision.” He said: “You may have the dung and any bone you come upon—there is meat for you on it, and any dung you come upon is dates for you.” When they left, I said: “Who are these?” He said: “These are jinn of Nusaybīn.”"],[9786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to accompany him on the night of the jinn. I went with him until we reached upper Makkah. He drew a line for me and said: “Do not leave.” Then he went off into the mountains. I saw men descending upon him from the mountain tops until they came between me and him. I drew my sword and said: “I will strike until I rescue the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then I remembered his words: “Do not leave until I come to you.” I remained like that until dawn came. The Prophet ﷺ came while I was standing. He said: “Have you been in this state all along?” I said: “If you had stayed a month, I would not have left until you came to me.” Then I told him what I had intended to do. He said: “If you had left, neither I nor you would have met until the Day of Resurrection.” Then he intertwined his fingers with mine and said: “I was promised that the jinn and mankind would believe in me. As for mankind, they have believed in me; and as for the jinn, you have seen.” He said: “I think my appointed time has drawn near.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Abu Bakr as successor?” He turned away from me, and I saw that he did not agree. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Umar as successor?” He turned away from me, and I saw that he did not agree. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Ali as successor?” He said: “That one—by the One besides whom there is no god—if you pledge allegiance to him and obey him, he will admit you all into Paradise, completely.”"],[9787,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the delegation of jinn. He sighed, so I said: “What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Abu Bakr.” He remained silent for a while, then moved on. Then he sighed again, so I said: “What is the matter with you, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Then appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Umar.” He remained silent for a while, then moved on. Then he sighed again, so I said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Then appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Ali b. Abi Talib.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they obey him, they will all enter Paradise, completely.”"],[9788,"I was not with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but I wish I were with him. (Using translation from Muslim 450d)"],[9789,"The Prophet ﷺ removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed their sandals. He said: “What made you remove your sandals?” They said: “We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours.” He said: “Jibril ﷺ informed me that there was something unclean on one of them, so I removed them for that reason. Do not remove your sandals.”"],[9790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform qunūt except for one month; he did not perform qunūt before it or after it."],[9791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt for thirty days, supplicating, then he abandoned it."],[9792,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his houses on his left. When he finished the prayer, he would go to his houses on his left."],[9793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the Burāq and he mounted it with Jibril, may Allah bless them both. They traveled, and whenever he came to a mountain, his legs would rise, and when he descended, his hands would rise, until they reached a land that was dark and stinking, then a land that was spacious and fragrant. I said: “O Jibril, we were traveling in a dark, stinking land, then to a spacious, fragrant land.” He said: “That is the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.” Then I came upon a man standing in prayer. He said: “Who is this with you, O Jibril?” I said: “Your brother Muhammad.” He welcomed him and prayed for blessing. He said: “Ask for ease for your ummah.” I said: “Who is this, O Jibril?” He said: “Your brother Musa.” I said: “Was his voice and his complaining to his Lord like that?” He said: “Yes, that was known of him and his intensity.” Then we traveled on, and I saw lamps and light. I said: “Who is this, O Jibril?” He said: “This is the tree of your father Ibrahim.” I said: “Shall I approach it?” He said: “Yes.” So we approached it, and he prayed for blessing for me and welcomed me. Then we went on to Bayt al-Maqdis, and I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie their animals. Then I entered the mosque, and the prophets were gathered for me—those whom Allah named in His Book and those He did not name. I prayed with them, except for the possessors of the cow: Isa, Musa, and Ibrahim, may Allah bless them and grant them peace."],[9794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If hardship were in a hole, ease would enter upon it until it brought it out.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Indeed, with hardship comes ease}."],[9795,"Announcing death is from the affairs of the Jāhiliyyah."],[9796,"I used to see the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said the salam to his right and to his left."],[9797,"\"We were not commanded to fast on Ashura except before Ramadan was revealed, so when Ramadan was revealed we were not commanded or forbidden from it.\""],[9798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I had resolved to order Bilal to call the prayer, then go to people who hear the call but do not respond, and burn their houses down upon them.\""],[9799,"Regarding the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[9800,"No concession was given for abandoning the congregation except for one who is afraid or ill."],[9801,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Hasan and Husain passed by, and they were young children. He said, \"Bring me my two sons, I seek refuge for them with the same protection that Ibrahim sought for his two sons, Ismail and Ishaq.\" He said, \"I seek refuge for you both in the perfect words of Allah, from every evil eye, harmful thing, and Satan.\""],[9802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is the equal of his father.\""],[9803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is the equal of his father.\""],[9804,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no forgetfulness in the prayer of fear.\""],[9805,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the two parties to a sale disagree about the sale, they should rescind the sale.\""],[9806,"We used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ and would hear the glorification of the food."],[9807,"\"Yes, we used to fast it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before the month of Ramadan was made obligatory. When the month of Ramadan was made obligatory, it abrogated it.\" Then he said, \"Sit down,\" so I sat and ate."],[9808,"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet ﷺ while traveling, and with Abu Bakr and Umar."],[9809,"When the Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit, we would face him."],[9810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that a man be named Harith, or Walid, or Hakam, or Abu al-Hakam, or Aflah, or Najih, or Yasar. And he said: “The most beloved of names to God ﷻ is that by which one is rendered a servant (of Him).”"],[9811,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seeking the lawful is an obligation after the obligatory.”"],[9812,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for thirty nights, supplicating against the tribes of Banu Sulaym, Riʿl, Dhakwan, and ʿUsayya, who had disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[9813,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would sleep in his prostration, and his sleep was not recognized except by his breathing; then he would rise for his prayer."],[9814,"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[9815,"I saw the moon split into two, with Hiraʾ between them."],[9816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us, when one of us sneezed, to say ‘yarhamuka Allah’ to him."],[9817,"Tell us when the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer? He said, \"When a portion of the night remains after the previous prayers until the Maghrib prayer, he was asked about his recitation, and he said, 'He used to recite aloud for the people of the household.'\""],[9818,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard seed of faith.”"],[9819,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: “And whoever does that will meet a penalty.”"],[9820,"I asked Abdullah b. Masud: Did the Prophet ﷺ deliver the sermon standing or sitting? He said: Do you not recite: “And they left you standing”?"],[9821,"On the day of Badr, Saʿd fought the fighting of both a horseman and an infantryman."],[9822,"Whoever goes to a diviner or a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[9823,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Looking at the face of ʿAlī is an act of worship.”"],[9824,"from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever is generous with his family on the day of Ashura will remain in abundance throughout the rest of his year.\""],[9825,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every prophet has a special group among his companions, and my special group among my companions are Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ.”"],[9826,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the moon split, and one part went behind the mountain. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bear witness, bear witness.”"],[9827,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not clean yourselves after defecation with dung or bones, for they are the provision of your brothers among the jinn.”"],[9828,"The Jews said: “Are not your brothers who died the ones who used to drink it?” Then God ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten} (Qur'an 5:93). The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It was said to me, 'You are one of them.'”"],[9829,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us the istikhārah (prayer for guidance). He said: “When one of you wants to do something, let him say: 'O God, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You know and I do not know, and You have power and I have no power, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If this matter which I intend is good for my religion and for the outcome of my affairs, then make it easy for me. And if something else is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be.' He says that, then he resolves.”"],[9830,"“The fourth of four—and what is the fourth of four? It is not far from God. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'People will sit with God on the Day of Resurrection according to their going early to the Friday prayers: the first, then the second, then the third, then the fourth.'” Then he said: “The fourth of four—and what is the fourth of four? It is not far from God.”"],[9831,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The closest a servant is to God is when he is prostrating.”"],[9832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The soul of a believer comes out as sweat, while the soul of a disbeliever flows out as the soul of a donkey. A believer may commit a sin, and it is intensified for him at death so that he may be expiated by it. And a disbeliever may do a good deed, and it is made easy for him at death so that he may be rewarded for it.”"],[9833,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Khaybar. He wanted to relieve himself, and when he wanted that, he would go far away so that no one could see him. He said: “Look, O ʿAbd Allāh, do you see anything?” I looked and saw a single tree, and I told him. He said to me: “Look, do you see anything?” I looked and saw another tree far from its companion, and I told him. He said: “Say to them: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together.'” I said that to them, and they came together. Then he came to them and screened himself with them. Then he stood up, and each of them went back to its place."],[9834,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Khaybar. He wanted to relieve himself, and when he wanted that, he would go far away so that no one could see him. He said: “Look, O ʿAbd Allāh, do you see anything?” I looked and saw a single tree, and I told him. He said to me: “Look, do you see anything?” I looked and saw another tree far from its companion, and I told him. He said: “Say to them: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together.'” I said that to them, and they came together. Then he came to them and screened himself with them. Then he stood up, and each of them went back to its place."],[9835,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Khaybar. He wanted to relieve himself, and when he wanted that, he would go far away so that no one could see him. He said: “Look, O ʿAbd Allāh, do you see anything?” I looked and saw a single tree, and I told him. He said to me: “Look, do you see anything?” I looked and saw another tree far from its companion, and I told him. He said: “Say to them: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together.'” I said that to them, and they came together. Then he came to them and screened himself with them. Then he stood up, and each of them went back to its place."],[9836,"The two sons of Mulaykah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, our mother used to honor the husband, show affection to the child,” and he mentioned the guest, “except that she buried a daughter alive in the Jahiliyyah.” He said, “Your mother is in the Fire.” They turned away, and evil could be seen in their faces. He ordered that they be brought back, and joy could be seen in their faces hoping that something had happened. He said, “My mother is with your mother.” A man from the hypocrites said, “What does this avail his mother while we tread on his heels?” A man from the Ansar—and I have never seen a man who asked more questions than him—said, “O Messenger of God, has your Lord promised concerning her or both of them?” He said, “Do you think it is from something?” He said, “I have not asked my Lord, and indeed I will stand at the Praised Station on the Day of Resurrection.” The Ansari said, “And what is that Praised Station?” He said, “That is when you are brought barefoot and naked, and the first to be clothed will be Ibrahim ﷺ , who will say, ‘Clothe my friend.’ Then two white garments will be brought, and he will put them on, then sit facing the Throne. Then my clothing will be brought, and I will put it on, and I will stand at his right in a station that no one other than me will stand; the first and the last will envy me for it. And my river Kawthar will be opened to the Pool.” A man from the hypocrites said, “For it, no water ever flowed over pebbles or pebbles but it had a quality or pebbles.” He said, “O Messenger of God, what quality and pebbles?” He said, “Its quality is musk and its pebbles are pearls.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard like today: water that flows over quality or pebbles but it has vegetation.” The Ansari said, “O Messenger of God, does it have vegetation?” He said, “Yes, rods of gold.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard like today; for no rod grows but it leaves and has fruit.” The Ansari said, “Does it have fruit?” He said, “Yes, colors of jewels, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst again, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after it.” This hadith was also narrated by al-Saʿiq b. Hazn from ʿAli b. al-Hakam, and he differed from Saʿid b. Zayd in its chain."],[9837,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, “You and your wealth belong to your father.”"],[9838,"The Prophet ﷺ clasped his hands together."],[9839,"“We did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of God ﷺ more often than we fasted thirty.”"],[9840,"“Traits that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do and people have abandoned, one of them is the imam’s salam in the funeral prayer like his salam in the prayer.”"],[9841,"“Add more of this for us, may my father and mother be your ransom; for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘A beautiful voice is an adornment of the Quran.’”"],[9842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about whispering, and he said, “That is pure faith.”"],[9843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[9844,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A cow is for seven and a camel is for seven in the sacrificial animals.”"],[9845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O young people, marry, for it is the best way to guard one's chastity and lower one's gaze. Whoever is not able to marry, then he should observe fasting, for it will be a shield for him.\""],[9846,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me to begin the day of my fast with oiled and combed hair, and not to begin the day of your fast frowning. And answer the invitation of whoever invites you from the Muslims as long as they do not display musical instruments; if they display musical instruments, then do not answer them. And pray over whoever dies from the people of our qiblah, even if he was killed crucified or stoned; for if you meet God with the like of the earth’s fill of sins, it is better for you than to affirm martyrdom for anyone from the people of the qiblah.”"],[9847,"“Do you know which charity is best?” They said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The best charity is a grant: to grant a dirham or the back of a mount.”"],[9848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed God ﷻ loves that His dispensations be accepted, just as He loves that His obligatory duties be fulfilled.”"],[9849,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a group of Banu Hashim approached. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them, his face reddened and his eyes welled up. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing something in your face that we dislike.” He said, “We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and my household will face trials and expulsion after me.”"],[9850,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say Takbeer (Allahu Akbar) during every lifting and lowering, and would greet (say salaam) to his right and left until the whiteness of his face could be seen from both sides."],[9851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"All of creation are the family of Allah, and the dearest of them to Allah are those who benefit His family the most.\""],[9852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever dies and has a male or female child is granted peace or does not grant peace, is pleased or is not pleased, will have no reward except Paradise.\""],[9853,"Abdullah stood at al-Safa next to a crevice in it and said, “Here, by the One besides whom there is no god, stood the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down.”"],[9854,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever buys a sheep that has been left unmilked, if he is pleased with it, he keeps it; otherwise he returns it along with a saa‘ of dates.”"],[9855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not go out to meet the trade caravans.”"],[9856,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Injury caused by a beast is without liability, and [injury caused by falling into] a well is without liability, and [injury caused by] a grazing animal is without liability, and on buried treasure the fifth is due.”"],[9857,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a naked woman approached. This distressed the Prophet ﷺ and he closed his eyes. A man from the group stood up, threw a garment over her, and held her close. Some of his companions said, “O Messenger of Allah, I think she is his wife.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you think her jealous? Allah ﷻ has decreed jealousy for women and jihad for men. Whoever among them bears it patiently with faith and seeking reward will have the like of the reward of the martyrs.”"],[9858,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Let those of maturity and wisdom stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Beware of the commotion of the marketplaces.”"],[9859,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes twist the forelock of his horse with his hand."],[9860,"From Ibrahim, and ‘Umarah had gone out to Makkah, so I hired a donkey and brought him to al-Qadisiyyah. He narrated to me from Ibrahim, from ‘Alqamah, from Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have young men from his household pass by him and his complexion would change because of that. One day some young men from his household passed by him and his complexion changed because of that. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing from you what distresses us: young men from your household pass by you and your complexion changes because of that.” He said, “These members of my household: Allah has chosen the Hereafter for them and has not chosen this world for them.”"],[9861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no retaliation except with the sword.”"],[9862,"Five signs have passed and five remain. Among them: the splitting of the moon, which we have seen; the smoke has passed; the great seizure has passed; the barren day has passed; and the inevitable punishment has passed."],[9863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “My description is Ahmad, the one who relies on Allah; he is neither harsh nor coarse. He repays a good deed with a good deed and does not repay an evil deed in kind. His birthplace is Makkah, his migration is to Taybah, and his nation is the praisers. They tie their lower garments at their waists and wash their limbs. Their gospels are in their breasts. They line up for prayer as they line up for battle. Their sacrifice by which they draw near to Me is their blood. They are monks by night and lions by day.”"],[9864,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Every act of kindness is charity, whether the giver is rich or poor.”"],[9865,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “You will not be an ascetic until you are humble.”"],[9866,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The soul of a believer comes out like sweat, and I do not love a death like the death of a donkey.” It was said: “What is the death of a donkey?” He said: “The soul of a disbeliever comes out from the corners of his mouth.”"],[9867,"A ruqya for fever was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “Present it to me.” They presented it: “In the name of Allah, a cleft, a horned, a salty, a sea, Qifta.” He said: “These are covenants which Sulayman b. Dawud ﷺ took upon the vermin, and I see no harm in it.”"],[9868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on three days: the day before the Day of Tarwiyah, the day of Fitr, and the day of Adha."],[9869,"From the Prophet ﷺ that when he sought guidance in a matter he wanted to undertake, he would say: “O Allah, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your ability through Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You have power and I have none, and You know and I know not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this affair is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my livelihood, and good for me in what I seek good through, then decree it for me in well-being and make it easy, then bless me in it. And if other than that is better for me, then decree for me what is good wherever it may be.”"],[9870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded fighting the breakers of allegiance, the wrongdoers, and the renegades."],[9871,"Ali commanded fighting the breakers of allegiance, the wrongdoers, and the renegades."],[9872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith is Yemeni, and Mudar is at the tails of camels.”"],[9873,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wine is cursed, and its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one who has it pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the consumer of its price.”"],[9874,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed riba (usury), the one who consumes it, the one who pays it, its scribe, and its two witnesses if they know, and the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who asks for it, the one who asks for tattooing, the woman who plucks eyebrows and the one who asks for it, and he forbade wailing."],[9875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of people are my generation, then the second, then the third. Then there will come a people in whom there is no good.”"],[9876,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The woman who buries her daughter alive and the girl buried alive will both be in the Fire.”"],[9877,"That he should read the scroll of Muhammad ﷺ that bore his seal, let him read: “Say, come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden you” up to His saying, “so that you may become righteous”."],[9878,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying, “O you who believe, do not consume one another’s wealth wrongfully, unless it be trade by mutual consent among you” – he said, “It is definitive; it has not been abrogated.”"],[9879,"While we were with the Prophet ﷺ, we heard a caller calling out: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Upon the natural disposition.” Then he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allāh.” He said, “He has brought it out of the Fire.” So we hurried to him and found a shepherd among his sheep, and prayer time had arrived, so he called it out."],[9880,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he heard a caller saying: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Upon the natural disposition.” Then he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allāh.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He has come out of the Fire.”"],[9881,"When Ibrāhīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, the sun was eclipsed. The people said, “It was eclipsed because of the death of Ibrāhīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings of Allah be upon them both.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. When you see that, pray until it clears.”"],[9882,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “No one who has an atom’s weight of pride will enter Paradise, and no one who has an atom’s weight of faith will enter the Fire.”"],[9883,"Ṭalḥah said: I recited to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb; Yaḥyā b. Waththāb recited to ʿAlqamah b. Qays; ʿAlqamah b. Qays recited to ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd; and ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Māliki yawmi al-dīn” with alif, and “ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim” with kasrah."],[9884,"O Muhammad, you will ascend one heaven after another."],[9885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This dinar and this dirham destroyed those before you, and I do not think they will do anything but destroy you.”"],[9886,"I said to al-Aʿmash, “From whom did you recite ‘wal-rujza fahjur’?” He said, “I recited to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb; Yaḥyā recited to ʿAlqamah; ʿAlqamah recited to ʿAbdullāh; and ʿAbdullāh recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[9887,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “When people differ, Ibn Sumayyah will be with the truth.”"],[9888,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"You will certainly see after me favoritism and matters you will disapprove of.\" We said, \"What do you command us?\" He said, \"Give them their due and ask Allah for your due.\""],[9889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[9890,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: A man will come holding another man by the hand and say, \"O Lord, this one killed me.\" Allah ﷻ will say, \"Why did you kill him?\" He will say, \"So that glory might be Yours.\" He will say, \"It is indeed Mine.\" He said: And a man will come holding another man by the hand and say, \"O Lord, this one killed me.\" Allah will say, \"Why did you kill this one?\" He will say, \"I killed him so that glory might be for so-and-so.\" He will say, \"It is not his. Bear your sin.\""],[9891,"People from Kufa came to him, and he greeted them with salam and enjoined them to fear Allah, and not to differ about the Quran or dispute over it, for it does not differ, nor does it fall away, nor does it change through much repetition. Do you not see that the law of Islam in it is one—its prescribed punishments, its recitation, and Allah's command in it? If one of the two readings commanded something and the other prohibited it, that would be difference, but it combines all of that. I hope that there has come to be among you of understanding and knowledge the best of what is among people. If I knew anyone whom camels could reach who knew better than I what Allah revealed to Muhammad ﷺ, I would seek him out until I added his knowledge to my knowledge. I know that the Quran used to be presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once every year, and it was presented to him twice in the year he passed away. Whenever I recited the Quran to him, he told me I was doing well. So whoever recites according to my recitation, let him not abandon it out of aversion to it; for whoever denies a single letter of it denies all of it."],[9892,"From Ibn Mas'ud, tracing it to the Prophet ﷺ: \"The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the bad breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk.\""],[9893,"Allah ﷻ said: \"Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the bad breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk.\""],[9894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud for a need: \"Indeed, all praise is due to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead; and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\""],[9895,"Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sermon for a need: \"All praise is due to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead; and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. 'O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word' (to the end of the verse). 'O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims.' 'O people, fear your Lord who created you' to the end of the verse. To proceed.\""],[9896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, Islam began as something strange, so glad tidings to the strangers.\""],[9897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than the Isha and Fajr prayers. If they knew the merit in them, they would come to them even crawling.\""],[9898,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A man will be bridled by his sweat on the Day of Resurrection and will say, 'My Lord, relieve me even if it is to the Fire.'\""],[9899,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and say: \"My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[9900,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal ata 'ala al-insan."],[9901,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: There was a man who was praying, and when he prostrated, another man came and stepped on his neck. So the one underneath said, “By Allah, he will never be forgiven!” Allah ﷻ said: “My servant swore by Me that I would not forgive My servant. Indeed, I have forgiven him.”"],[9902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two fasts, two prayers, two garments, two foods, two marriages, and two sales. As for the two days, they are the day of Fitr and the day of Adha. As for the two prayers, they are a prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and a prayer after Asr until the sun sets. As for the two garments, they are wrapping oneself in a single garment with nothing between one's private parts and the sky; that is called al-summa. As for the two foods, they are eating with one's left hand while one's right hand is sound, and eating while reclining. As for the two sales, they are a man saying, “You sell for me and I will sell for you.” As for the two marriages, they are marrying a prostitute, and marrying a woman along with her maternal aunt or paternal aunt."],[9903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ask Allah of His bounty, for Allah ﷻ loves to be asked. And the best of worship is awaiting relief.”"],[9904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[9905,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Quran was revealed in seven dialects.”"],[9906,"Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ, “What has made you gray, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Hud and al-Waqiah.”"],[9907,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man stood up and accidentally stepped on another man's foot. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Make space.\" The man asked, \"What does 'make space' mean, O Messenger of Allah? Did I eat my brother's flesh?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Indeed, you have eaten your brother's flesh.\""],[9908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of one person is enough for two, and the food of two is enough for four.”"],[9909,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[9910,"“We have been commanded to establish prayer and give zakat. Whoever does not give zakat has no prayer.”"],[9911,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate with these words: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and self-sufficiency.”"],[9912,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people.”"],[9913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man's prayer in congregation surpasses his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees, each like his prayer in his house.”"],[9914,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers.”"],[9915,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees.”"],[9916,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds a man’s prayer alone by twenty-some prayers.”"],[9917,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees.”"],[9918,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[9919,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but he is my brother and companion. God has taken your companion as an intimate friend.”"],[9920,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: \"If I were to take a close friend, I would have chosen Abu Bakr as my close friend. However, your close friend is Allah.\""],[9921,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but your companion is the intimate friend of God.”"],[9922,"The reading of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was known in the afternoon and the evening by the movement of his beard."],[9923,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he has killed a polytheist man whose blood has become lawful.”"],[9924,"We asked the Messenger of God ﷺ whether apes and pigs are from the lineage of the Jews. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, may He be exalted, has never cursed a people and then transformed them so that they had descendants until He destroyed them. Rather, this was a creation that existed, and when God, may He be exalted, became angry with the Jews, He transformed them and made them like them.”"],[9925,"\"He does not like the wide/uncrowded space of the two arms with blood; for it has a killer in the sight of God who does not die. And it does not please you that a person earns money from forbidden (illegitimate) means, so if he spends from it, it will not be accepted from him, and if he withholds it, it will not be blessed for him. And if he dies and leaves it, it will become his provision for the fire.\""],[9926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, the disbeliever will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he says, ‘O Lord, grant me relief, even if it is to the Fire.’”"],[9927,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever swears a solemn oath deliberately to seize the property of a Muslim unjustly will meet God on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him.” Then he recited, “Indeed, those who purchase a small price with the covenant of God and their oaths…” [Al ʿImran 3:77]. Yazid b. Ibrahim traced it back to the Prophet, but Hammad b. Zayd did not trace it back."],[9928,"“Whoever swears a solemn oath, deliberately committing a sin in it, in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim, will meet God while He is angry with him.”"],[9929,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The woman is ʿawrah, and when she goes out, the Shayṭān seeks to tempt her, and she is closest to God when she is in the depths of her house.\""],[9930,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: 'Alif-Lām-Mīm, the sending down of the Book' (Sūrat al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man' (Sūrat al-Insān)."],[9931,"When the Prophet ﷺ began the prayer, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You; blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You.'"],[9932,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever is moderate will not be in need.'"],[9933,"\"I swear by nine that the Ibn Sayyad is the Dajjal is more beloved to me than swearing by one, and I swear by nine that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was martyred is more beloved to me than swearing by one that he was not martyred because Allah made him a prophet and took him as a martyr.\""],[9934,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. When he finished his prayer, he said: 'Indeed, God ﷻ brings about for His Prophet whatever He wills, and one of the things He has brought about for him is that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[9935,"We used to talk during the prayer; some of us would greet others, and one of us would gesture to his companion about a need. One day I came while the Prophet ﷺ was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what had newly occurred. When he finished, he said: 'Indeed, God ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[9936,"Ibn Masʿūd ؓ said: 'We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to us. But when I came from the land of Abyssinia, I greeted him and he did not respond to us. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what would come after. Then I waited for him, and when he finished his prayer, I mentioned that to him. He said: \"Indeed, God brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has decreed—or he said: He has brought about—that you should not talk during the prayer.\""],[9937,"We used to talk during the prayer; some of us would greet others, and one of us would gesture to his companion about a need. One day I came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what had newly occurred. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'Indeed, God brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[9938,"People used to return the greeting to one another during the prayer, until Ibn Masʿūd ؓ greeted the Prophet ﷺ and he did not respond to him. He sat down sad, imagining that something had been revealed concerning him. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, Ibn Masʿūd mentioned that to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is enough occupation, and the prayer suffices as an occupation.'"],[9939,"That he had gone out to the land of Abyssinia, and the people used to greet one another during the prayer. When ʿAbdullāh returned, he greeted the Prophet ﷺ and he did not respond. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger. I greeted you and you did not respond to me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[9940,"We used to greet the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to us. But when we returned from the Negus, we greeted him and he did not respond to us. We said: 'O Messenger of God, we used to greet you during the prayer and you would respond to us.' He said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[9941,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[9942,"He used to send greetings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would respond to him with greetings. Then, he sent greetings upon him while he was praying, but he did not respond to him. Abdullah thought this was due to a reason from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . When he finished, Abdullah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I used to send greetings upon you while you were praying and you would respond to me, but today I sent greetings upon you and you did not respond to me. I thought there might be a reason for that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but we were forbidden from speaking during prayer except with the Quran and remembrance.\""],[9943,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ during the prayer, and he would respond to us. Then one day I greeted him and he did not respond to me. I asked him about that, and he said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills.\""],[9944,"We used to speak during the prayer, some of us greeting others. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not speak during the prayer.\""],[9945,"Mu'awiya said to one of his associates, 'He will certainly grieve.' When he sat with him on his bed, he said, 'O Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah reward you in [the loss of] al-Hasan b. 'Ali.' He said, 'Has he died?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'May the mercy and good pleasure of Allah be upon him, and may He join him with his righteous predecessors. By Allah, O Mu'awiya, it will not fill your grave, nor will you consume his provision, nor will you live forever after him. We have been afflicted with a greater loss than him—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—yet Allah did not forsake us after him.'"],[9946,"Some people of the Zutt were brought to ʿAli ؓ who worshipped an idol, and he burned them with fire. Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"],[9947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly."],[9948,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: “A rabbit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while ʿA’ishah was asleep, so he set aside the hindquarter for her. When she woke up, he gave it to her and she ate it.”"],[9949,"On the day the sun eclipsed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed four rakʿahs in two rakʿahs, with four prostrations."],[9950,"About mutʿah in the Hajj, Ibn ʿAbbās called out to him, “We know better about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that, and men exited the state of iḥrām and performed tamattuʿ with the ʿUmrah. They had no sacrificial animals with them, and they circumambulated the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and they had intercourse with women.” Then Ibn ʿAbbās said, “Indeed, I give this ruling based on what was done during the time of the Leader of the God-fearing.” Ibn al-Zubayr said, “Then be content with yourself, for by Allah, if you do that, I will surely stone you with your own stones.” Then their speech ended."],[9951,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded zakāt al-fiṭr: one ṣāʿ of dates, or one ṣāʿ of barley, or two mudds of wheat, for every present person and Bedouin, young or old, free or slave."],[9952,"Qasama in pre-Islamic times served as a barrier between people, and whoever swore a decisive oath in which he was sinful would be shown a punishment from Allah by which he would be made an example, due to his audacity against sacred things. So they used to be cautious about decisive oaths and fear them. When Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ, he confirmed qasama, and the Muslims held it in greater awe because of what Allah had taught them about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled by qasama between two clans of the Ansar called Banu Haritha. That was because some Jews killed Muhayyisa and the Jews denied it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned the Jews for their qasama, because they were the ones who claimed the blood, and he commanded them to have fifty men swear fifty oaths that they were innocent of his killing. The Jews declined to swear the oaths. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned Banu Haritha and commanded them to have fifty men swear fifty oaths that the Jews had killed him treacherously, and that they were entitled thereby to what they claimed from the one who killed their companion. Banu Haritha declined the oaths. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he ruled that his blood money was owed by the Jews, because he was found among them and in their dwellings."],[9953,"Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said: “Jibril ﷺ led me in prayer at the House twice. He prayed Zuhr with me when the sun had declined, by the measure of a sandal strap. Then he prayed Asr with me when the shadow of every object was equal to its length. Then he prayed Maghrib with me when the fasting person breaks his fast. Then he prayed Isha with me when the twilight had disappeared. Then he prayed Fajr with me when food and drink became forbidden for the fasting person. Then the next day he prayed Zuhr with me when the shadow of every object was equal to its length. Then he prayed Asr with me when the shadow of every object was twice its length. Then he prayed Maghrib with me at the same time, when the fasting person breaks his fast. Then he prayed Isha with me when the first third of the night had passed. Then he prayed Fajr with me.” Abu Nu’aym said, “I do not know what he said regarding Fajr.” Then he said, “He turned to me and said, ‘O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you; the time is what lies between these two times.’”"],[9954,"Ibn Abbas said: I will only inform you of what I saw from Allah’s Messenger ﷺ. He and his companions were in his house when the muezzin came, so he stood up for the prayer. When he reached the door, a platter containing bread and meat was brought to him, so he returned with his companions and he ate and they ate. Then he went back to the prayer and did not perform ablution. The maternal uncle of Ibn Ishaq, Musa b. Yasar, [was present]."],[9955,"Mutʿah was in the beginning of Islam, and they used to recite this verse: “And those from whom you seek enjoyment, give them their due” up to a specified term. A man would come to a town where he had no acquaintance and would marry for as long as he thought he would finish his need, so that she would guard his belongings and set his affairs aright — until this verse was revealed: “Forbidden to you are your mothers…” to the end of the verse, and the term was abrogated and mutʿah was forbidden. Its confirmation in the Qur’an is: “Except from their spouses or what their right hands possess, for indeed they are not blameworthy.” So anything other than this private part is forbidden."],[9956,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The first to change the religion of Abraham ﷺ was Amr b. Luhayy b. Qama'ah b. Khindif, Abu Khuza'ah.\""],[9957,"Ibn Abbas: Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that."],[9958,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn: in the first rak'ah, the Opening of the Book and two verses from the end of al-Baqarah: {The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord}; and in the second rak'ah, the Opening of the Book and one verse from Al Imran: {Say, O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you} to the end of the verse."],[9959,"O son of my brother, ask him how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the prayer for rain on the day he prayed for rain with the people. Ishaq said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: O Abu Abbas, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the prayer for rain on the day he prayed for rain with the people? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out humbly and in worn clothes, and he performed it as he performed on the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha."],[9960,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had been married, and they asked him to judge between them by stoning, so he stoned them in the courtyard of the mosque."],[9961,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Wudu is once, once.\""],[9962,"Na'im, Abu Abdullah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, narrated to him that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey branded on the face and disapproved of that. The man said: By Allah, I will not brand it except on the farthest part of the face. So he ordered for a donkey of his, and it was cauterized on its two haunches."],[9963,"It is the Sunnah."],[9964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever falls into them is likely to sin, and whoever avoids them is more secure for his religion, like a shepherd grazing near a sanctuary, soon to fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is the unlawful.\""],[9965,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to us, from Jaʿfar b. Muḥammad, from his father, from Yazīd b. Hurmuz, that Najdah wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ asking him about five matters. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Were it not that I would be concealing knowledge, I would not write to him. Najdah wrote to him: To proceed: Inform me, did the Messenger of God ﷺ go on raids with women? Did he assign them a share? Did he kill children? When does the orphanhood of an orphan end? And about the fifth, to whom does it belong? Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to him: You wrote asking me: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ go on raids with women? He did go on raids with them, and they treated the wounded and were given gifts from the spoils. As for a share, he did not assign them one. The Messenger of God ﷺ did not kill children. You wrote: When does the orphanhood of an orphan end? By my life, a man's beard may grow while he is weak in taking for himself and weak in giving from it. When he takes for himself from what is best that people take, then orphanhood has gone from him. You wrote asking me about the fifth, to whom does it belong? We say it is for us, but our people refused us that."],[9966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no emigration after the conquest, but jihad and intention. And when you are called to march, then march.\""],[9967,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on his garment."],[9968,"It was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that the Jews fast on the day of ʿAshura. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If we live, we will differ from them and fast the ninth day.”"],[9969,"He heard Ibn ʿAbbas saying: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating a bone with meat, the muʾadhdhin came to him. He put it down, then stood for prayer and did not touch water."],[9970,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fought a people until he called them (to Islam).”"],[9971,"I was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Prophet ﷺ stood to pray at night, so I stood on his left. He took my hand and placed me on his right, then he prayed thirteen rakʿahs. I gauged his standing in each rakʿah as the length of (Surah) “O you wrapped in garments.”"],[9972,"If you want to look at the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ, then follow the prayer of Ibn al-Zubayr."],[9973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has pardoned for my Ummah their mistakes, their forgetfulness, and what they are coerced into.”"],[9974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four things, whoever is given them has been given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient in affliction, and a wife who does not seek to betray him in herself or his wealth.”"],[9975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to recite in the morning prayer (Surahs) “When the night covers” and “By the sun and its brightness.”"],[9976,"The Prophet ﷺ had promised al-Abbas a small herd of camels, so he sent me to him, and I stayed the night with him. It was the night of Maymunah bint al-Harith. The Prophet ﷺ arose after a short while, and I leaned on the pillow that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had leaned on. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and performed ablution, making it complete while using very little water, then he stood and began the prayer. I got up, performed ablution, and stood to his left. He reached behind with his hand, took hold of my ear, and placed me on his right. Maymunah was menstruating, so she got up, performed ablution, then sat behind him remembering Allah."],[9977,"When the Prophet ﷺ overlooked the graveyard while on its first path, he gestured with his hand behind the ridge or the high ground and said: \"What an excellent graveyard this is.\" I said to the one informing me: He singled out the mountain pass? He said: This is how we heard that the Prophet ﷺ singled out the pass facing the House."],[9978,"I heard Ibn Abbas ؓ reciting: dārastu, talawtu, khāṣamtu, jādaltu."],[9979,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from al-Ta'if, he halted at al-Ji'ranah and distributed the spoils there, then performed Umrah from there, and that was when two nights remained of Shawwal.\""],[9980,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Gabriel ﷺ was slow in coming to him, so he mentioned that to him. He said: \"How could he not be, when you do not use the siwak, do not trim your nails, do not clip your moustaches, and do not clean your finger joints?\""],[9981,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and stopped to rest at night, and nothing woke him but the sun. He got up and ordered the mu'adhdhin, who gave the adhan and the iqama, then he prayed."],[9982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped; a freedman of Banu Bayadah cupped him, and he gave him his wage. Had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."],[9983,"I stood beside the Prophet ﷺ on his left, and he turned me around and placed me on his right."],[9984,"In his statement {§It was as close as two bows or even closer}, the word \"al-qaab\" means restriction and \"al-qawsayn\" refers to the two arms."],[9985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah divided creation into two divisions and placed me in the better of them as a division: the companions of the right, and I am the best of the companions of the right. Then He made the two divisions into houses and placed me in the better of them as a house. That is His saying: {So the companions of the right—what are the companions of the right? And the companions of the left—what are the companions of the left? And the foremost, the foremost.} I am of the best of the foremost. Then He made the house into tribes and placed me in the better of them as a tribe. That is His saying: {into peoples and tribes}—the verse. I am the most God-fearing of the children of Adam and the most noble of them in the sight of Allah, without boasting. Then He made the tribes into houses and placed me in the better of them as a house. That is His saying: {Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly.}"],[9986,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What deed, if I do it, will make me enter Paradise? He said: \"Are you in a land to which water is brought?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then buy with it a new waterskin, then draw water in it until you wear it out, for you will not wear it out until you reach the deeds of Paradise.\""],[9987,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs Hajj from Makkah walking until he returns to it, for every step he has seven hundred good deeds of the good deeds of the Haram.\" Some of them said: And what are the good deeds of the Haram? He said: \"Every good deed there is a thousand good deeds.\""],[9988,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of dates until they are eaten from and until they are stored.\" I said, 'What is \"stored\"?' A man from the people said, 'Until they are cut or gathered.'"],[9989,"Al-Saʿb b. Jaththama gifted the Prophet ﷺ a haunch of wild donkey, but he returned it to him and said, \"We are in a state of ihram.\""],[9990,"I witnessed Ibn ʿAbbas saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to use the toothstick at night two or three times.\""],[9991,"A man asked Ibn 'Abbas: \"Did you meet the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, I met him while I was a boy. His purpose was to attend an Eid, so he went out and ordered a spear to be brought and it was planted for him near the house of Kathir b. al-Salt. He prayed facing it. Then he reminded the people and admonished them. Then he went up to the women, with no male with him except Bilal. He reminded them and admonished them with verses of the Qur'an and urged them to give charity. I saw them leaning toward their ears and throats to hand charity to Bilal. Then he returned to his family.\""],[9992,"The Prophet ﷺ did not give the kawdan (a slow packhorse) anything, and he gave it less than the share of the unmarried in strength and quality. The kawdan is a slow, non-Arabian horse."],[9993,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to open the prayer with 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[9994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us nothing but a yellow thing on a white thing except what is between its two covers (i.e., the Qur'an). I stood up to the hilt of his sword and found in the sword's shoulder strap a scroll on which was written: 'Whoever commits a crime, or shelters a criminal, or claims descent from other than his father, or claims a patron other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.'"],[9995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best charity is that which leaves the giver self-sufficient, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.”"],[9996,"When {Indeed, you and what you worship besides Allah are the firewood of Hell; you will enter it} was revealed, ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zibaʿrā said: “I will contend with Muḥammad on your behalf.” He said: “O Muḥammad, is it not in what Allah has revealed to you: {Indeed, you and what you worship besides Allah are the firewood of Hell; you will enter it}?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “These Christians worship ʿĪsā, these Jews worship ʿUzayr, and these Banū Tamīm worship the angels—are they all in the Fire?” Then Allah, may He be exalted, revealed: {Indeed, those for whom the best has preceded from Us, they will be far removed from it.}"],[9997,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Quraysh: \"O assembly of Quraysh, there is no good in anyone who worships besides Allah.\" They said: \"Do you not claim that ʿĪsā was a prophet and a righteous servant? If you are truthful, he is indeed one of their deities.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {And when the son of Maryam was set forth as an example, at once your people clamor about it}—they raise an outcry—{And indeed he is a sign of the Hour}: the coming forth of ʿĪsā before the Day of Resurrection."],[9998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer is not one who eats his fill while his neighbor is hungry.\""],[9999,"\"Allah did not send any prophet but that after him there was a halt, with whom He fills Jahannam.\""],[10000,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about one who performed some of the rites of Hajj out of order due to ignorance, not intentionally. He said: \"There is no harm upon him.\""],[10001,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a camel of ours has broken loose into a garden.\" The Prophet ﷺ went to it and said: \"Come here.\" It came with its head lowered until he put a halter on it, and he gave it to its owners. Abu Bakr said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, it was as if it knew you are a prophet.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no one between its two lava tracts but that he knows I am a prophet, except the disbelievers among the jinn and mankind.\""],[10002,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[10003,"\"I am a man whose livelihood comes only from the work of my hands, and I make these images.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"I find nothing for you except what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever makes an image, Allah will punish him on the Day of Resurrection until he breathes into it, and he will never breathe into it.'\" The man became very distressed and his face turned yellow. Then he said: \"Woe to you! If you insist on making them, then make trees and everything that has no soul.\""],[10004,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, does medicine benefit against destiny?\" He said, \"Medicine is from destiny, and it may benefit by Allah's permission.\""],[10005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five."],[10006,"The Muslims would not look at Abu Sufyan or initiate conversation with him. He said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three things I will give you: I have the finest and most beautiful Arab woman, Umm Habibah; I will give her to you in marriage.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And make Muāwiyah a scribe before you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And appoint me as a commander to fight the disbelievers just as I used to fight the Muslims.” He said: “Yes.”"],[10007,"“We used to recite this:” {The heavens are almost rent asunder from above them}"],[10008,"“I came on a donkey, with a rider behind me from Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying in an open area. We dismounted and then came and joined the prayer, leaving the donkey in front of them, and he did not mind that. Then two slave girls from Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib came running, one chasing the other, until they reached the Prophet ﷺ during the prayer while he was praying, and he separated them, and he did not mind that.”"],[10009,"You have asked one who knows. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent so-and-so al-Aslamī along with eighteen sacrificial camels. He said: “O Messenger of God ﷺ, what do you think if one of them becomes too exhausted to walk?” He said: “Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood and strike its side with it. Do not eat from it yourself, nor anyone from your traveling companions or your party.”"],[10010,"Ibn ʿAbbas: \"You are teaching me the Sunnah? May you be bereft of your mother! I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ combine ʿasr with zuhr and maghrib with ʿisha. Then I met Abu Hurayra and he agreed with him.\""],[10011,"That he should remove his sandals and place them beside him."],[10012,"It was like the tar of camels, and we would drink it and see no harm in it."],[10013,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done at al-Qaha while he was in ihram."],[10014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ says: \"I will not look into the right of My servant until My servant looks into My right.\""],[10015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars."],[10016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among the people there is none like a man who takes hold of his horse's head, striving in the path of Allah and restraining his evil from people; and like a man in the desert with livestock who honors his guest and gives him his due.\""],[10017,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever leads a blind person until he reaches a safe place, God Almighty will forgive him forty major sins and four grave sins that would necessitate the Fire.\""],[10018,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive ʿAbd al-Qays,” three times."],[10019,"Al-Fadl b. al-Abbas was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ. The young man began glancing at the women and looking at them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning his face away with his hand from behind him, while the young man kept glancing at them. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “This is a day on which whoever controls his hearing, his sight, and his tongue will be forgiven.”"],[10020,"On the day Saʿd b. Muʿadh died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at his grave, then he said, “Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return.” Then he said: “If anyone could be saved from the squeezing of the grave, Saʿd would have been saved. It squeezed him, then relief was granted to him.”"],[10021,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: ‘O Muhammad, Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, its server, and the one who asks for it to be served.’”"],[10022,"We raid this Maghrib, and they are people of idols, and they have water skins in which there is milk and water. Ibn Abbas said: “Tanning is purification.” Ibn Waʿla said: “From your own opinion or something you heard?” He said: “Rather, something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10023,"To al-Abbas and al-Fadl b. Abbas: Mention to the Prophet ﷺ that he order for you from the alms, and I will attend with you. So al-Fadl mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Have patience with yourselves, O Banu Hashim, for the alms are but the washings of people.”"],[10024,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever says in the morning: {Glory be to Allah when you reach evening and when you rise in the morning; and to Him is praise in the heavens and the earth, and at night and when you are at noon} — the entire verse — he will attain what he missed during his day. And whoever says it in the evening will attain what he missed during his night.'"],[10025,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rak‘ahs in which he recited the Mother of the Book and did not add anything to them.”"],[10026,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he commanded five things and forbade ten. He commanded parting the hair, the toothstick, trimming the mustache, rinsing the nose, and rinsing the mouth. He forbade that a woman be married in addition to her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt, that two women be together in one garment, shighar marriage, selling dogs, the dower of a prostitute, the earnings of a cupper, the skins of wild beasts, wearing Qassi cloth, and the stud fee of a stallion."],[10027,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said, “Women are not required to shave; upon women is only shortening.”"],[10028,"Ibn ʿUmar would sometimes break his fast with sexual intercourse."],[10029,"“We dislike that—this muḥāqalah [sharecropping arrangement].” I said, “Should we give the land for a third or a quarter?” He said, “There is no harm in that; we used to do that.”"],[10030,"The Prophet ﷺ was in a garden. Abu Bakr asked permission, so he said, “Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise.” Then ʿUmar asked permission, so he said, “Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise and martyrdom.” Then ʿUthman asked permission, so he said, “Give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise and martyrdom.”"],[10031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent your women from coming to the mosques.”"],[10032,"And he said: “I pray as I saw my companions praying, and I am not one to prevent anyone from seeking more good if he desires it.”"],[10033,"“...that the truth is someone else, so we believe them, and they judge unjustly, so we strengthen them in it and make it seem good to them. So what do you think about that?” He said: “O son of my brother, we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we used to consider this hypocrisy.”"],[10034,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[10035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sends one prayer upon me, Allah sends ten prayers upon him because of it.”"],[10036,"And upon you be peace and God’s mercy, and welcome, and greetings to Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Place a cushion for him. Ibn ʿUmar said: “Were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Three things are not refused: milk, a cushion, and perfume,’ I would not have sat on it.”"],[10037,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Your lifespan compared to the nations before you is only like the time between the afternoon prayer and the setting of the sun.”"],[10038,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Everyone entrusted with something will be asked about what he was entrusted with, even a man will be asked about his wife, his slave, and his child.”"],[10039,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling fruits until their defect has passed.” Ibn Surāqah said: “When is that, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said: “At the rising of the Pleiades.”"],[10040,"Ibn ʿUmar said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say that.”"],[10041,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding misguidance, he used to say, \"O Allah, the One who returns misguidance and guides those who are astray. Guide me from my astrayness by Your power and authority, for it is from Your gifts and favors.\""],[10042,"The Prophet صَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ said, \"Iblis entered Iraq and achieved his goal, then he entered Syria and was expelled from it, then he entered Egypt and caused turmoil and spread mischief.\""],[10043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were praying after dawn and said, “There is no prayer after dawn except two rakʿahs.”"],[10044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The believer’s lower garment reaches to mid-calf, and there is no blame on him for what is between that and the ankles. Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him.”"],[10045,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The parable of the believer is like that of a tree whose leaves do not fall—the date palm.”"],[10046,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in his supplication when he entered the morning and when he entered the evening, and he never abandoned it until he departed this world and until he died: “O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly affairs, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and calm my fears. O Allah, protect me from before me, from behind me, from my right, from my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in You from being swallowed up from beneath me.” Jubayr said, “And that is the earth swallowing.” I do not know whether it is the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the statement of Jubayr."],[10047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them that a servant among the servants of Allah said, “O Lord, to You belongs praise as befits the majesty of Your face and the greatness of Your authority.” The two angels found it difficult and did not know how to record it. They ascended to the heaven and said, “O our Lord, Your servant said a statement that we do not know how to record.” Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, said—and He is most knowing of what His servant said—“What did My servant say?” They said, “O Lord, he said: O Lord, to You belongs praise as befits the majesty of Your face and the greatness of Your authority.” Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, said to them, “Write it down as My servant said it, until My servant meets Me and I reward him for it.”"],[10048,"We used to count, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions were numerous: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān; then we would fall silent."],[10049,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise.'"],[10050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I saw Jesus, son of Mary, upon him a striped garment, circumambulating the House.' They said, 'Who resembles him?' He said, ''Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. And I saw Moses, son of 'Imran, a dark-skinned, sturdy man from the people, as if he were one of the men of Shanu'ah. And I saw the Dajjal.' We said, 'Who resembles him, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, ''Abd al-'Uzza b. Qatan al-Mustaliqi.'"],[10051,"He said, 'I adjure you, unless you go and judge.' He said, 'Do not be hasty. Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought refuge in a protector\"?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then I seek refuge in Allah from being a judge.' He said, 'And what prevents you, when your father used to judge?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever is a judge and judges ignorantly will be among the people of the Fire. And whoever is a knowledgeable judge and judges with truth or justice will seek release as an equal recompense.\" So what hope do I have after this?' Abu al-Qasim 'Abdullah b. Wahb said, 'This, in my view, is 'Abdullah b. Wahb b. Zam'ah, and Allah knows best.'"],[10052,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer, he would say, 'I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, uprightly and in submission, and I am not of the polytheists. Glory be to You, O Allah, with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, with no partner. With that I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims.'"],[10053,"It is a Sunnah: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar made their camels kneel."],[10054,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Which of the people is best?' He said, 'The one with the best character.'"],[10055,"He heard 'Abdullah b. 'Umar say, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit saying, \"The Compeller will take His heavens and His earth in His hands,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ closed his hand and began clenching and opening it. Then he said, \"I am the Most Merciful, I am the King. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ swayed to his right and to his left until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lowest part, to the point that I said, \"Will it fall with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"'"],[10056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you performs wudu and does it well, then goes out to the mosque, nothing removes him except the prayer, his left foot does not cease wiping away a sin while the other records a good deed until he enters the mosque.”"],[10057,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, he would say: “O Allah, do not cause our deaths to occur in it until You bring us out of it.”"],[10058,"\"I have not seen anyone among the people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who is darker than Mu'awiyah.\""],[10059,"I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed me with a Qubtiyyah garment, and he clothed Usamah b. Zayd with a striped silk hullah. He looked and saw that I had let my garment hang low, so he came and took hold of my shoulder and said: “O Ibn ʿUmar, everything of the clothing that touches the ground is in the Fire.” Then I saw Ibn ʿUmar wear his izar up to the middle of his shin."],[10060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the most beloved of houses to Allah is a house in which there is an orphan who is honored.”"],[10061,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man from the desert came to him wearing a jubbah of Sijan, fastened with silk brocade. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wants to elevate every horseman son of a horseman and lower every shepherd son of a shepherd.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the collar of his jubbah and said, \"He is wearing the clothing of one who does not understand.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Prophet of Allah, Nuh, was near death, he said to his son, 'O my son, I am giving you my final instructions.' He then briefed him on the instruction: 'I command you with two things and forbid you from two things. I command you with 'There is no god but Allah,' for if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed on one side of a scale and 'There is no god but Allah' on the other, it would outweigh them. And if the seven heavens and the seven earths were a closed ring, 'There is no god but Allah' would break it. And I command you with 'Glory be to Allah and with His praise,' for it is the prayer of creation, and by it creation is given provision. And I forbid you from disbelief and arrogance.'\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know what disbelief is; what is arrogance? Is it that a man has two fine sandals which he wears, and two fine straps that please him?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Is it that he has a fine garment which he wears?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Is it that he has a beautiful horse whose beauty pleases him?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Is it that he has companions who sit with him?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then what is arrogance?\" He said, \"To reject the truth and look down on people.\""],[10062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and able-bodied.\""],[10063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the minbar and said, \"I will not swear, I will not swear, I will not swear.\" Then he descended and said, \"Rejoice, rejoice! Indeed, whoever prays the five prayers and avoids the major sins will enter through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes.\" Al-Muttalib said: I heard a man ask Abdullah b. Amr, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention them?\" He said, \"Yes: disobedience to parents, associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, slandering chaste women, consuming the orphan's property, fleeing from the battlefield, and consuming usury.\""],[10064,"I went out for a need while some of us were greeting one another during the prayer. Then I returned and greeted, but he did not respond to me, and he said: \"Indeed, in the prayer there is enough occupation.\""],[10065,"Abdullah [Ibn Masud] said: While I was concealed behind the curtains of the Ka'bah, three persons came: a Thaqafi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts. They conversed among themselves. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears what we say?\" Another said, \"If we raise our voices, He hears; and if we lower them, He does not hear.\" The third said, \"If He hears when we raise our voices, then He hears when we lower them.\" I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight, or your skins; but you thought that Allah does not know much of what you do} up to His saying {among the losers}. This is how Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it, and Abu Mu'awiyah and the companions of al-A'mash differed from him."],[10066,"Abdullah [Ibn Masud] said: I was concealing myself behind the curtains of the Ka'bah. Three persons came, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts: a Qurayshi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Thaqafis, or a Thaqafi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis. They spoke words I did not understand. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears our words?\" Another said, \"If we raise our voices, He hears them; if we do not raise them, He does not hear them.\" The third said, \"If He hears anything from it, He hears all of it.\" I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight} – the verse."],[10067,"I was concealing myself behind the curtain of the Ka'bah, and in the mosque there was a man from Thaqif and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis. He said, \"Do you think Allah hears our murmur?\" One of the two said, \"He hears when we raise our voices.\" The other said, \"If He hears when we raise our voices, He will surely hear when we lower them.\" Ibn Mas'ud said: I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of their words, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight, or your skins} to the end of the verse. And al-Mas'udi differed from them."],[10068,"Three persons sat at the gate of the Ka'bah: two Qurayshis and a Thaqafi, or two Thaqafis and a Qurayshi. Some of them whispered to others about a matter. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears what we say?\" Another said, \"As for what we say aloud, He hears it.\" The third said, \"If He hears what we say aloud, then He hears what we whisper.\" Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves} – the verse."],[10069,"Abdullah [Ibn Mas'ud] said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; and with Umar two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you. Would that my share of four rak'ahs were two accepted rak'ahs."],[10070,"Abdullah [Ibn Mas'ud] said: I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you. Would that I had, for four rak'ahs, two accepted rak'ahs."],[10071,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you."],[10072,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs. This is how the companions of al-A'mash narrated it, and Shu'bah differed from them."],[10073,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prayed at Mina two rak'ahs; with Abu Bakr, and he prayed two rak'ahs; and with Umar, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Would that my share were two accepted rak'ahs. And Qays b. al-Rabi' differed from them."],[10074,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar at Mina two rak'ahs, and Muhammad b. Ubaydillah al-Arzami contradicted them."],[10075,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs, and Isra'il contradicted them."],[10076,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs."],[10077,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} descended upon him. He said: I was receiving it from his mouth while it was still fresh, and his mouth was indeed moist, when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it,\" but it eluded us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10078,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave at Mina when a snake sprang upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" We rushed toward it, but it outran us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10079,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of a snake in the Haram."],[10080,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of a snake in Mina.\""],[10081,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when a snake came out. He said, \"Kill it,\" but it outran us, and he said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10082,"Abdullah said: The Mursalat was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were in a cave, and he taught it to me. I am indeed reciting it close to what he taught me, and I do not know with which of its two endings it ends: {When it is said to them, 'Bow down,' they do not bow} or {Then in what statement after it will they believe?}"],[10083,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} descended upon him. I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was indeed moist with it, and I do not know with which of the two it is ended: {Then in what statement after it will they believe?} or {When it is said to them, 'Bow down,' they do not bow}. He said: And a snake escaped him into a hole, so he said, \"You were protected from its evil and it was protected from your evil.\""],[10084,"It was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the snake. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the night of the snake? He said: I was with him when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seek it.\" We sought it, but it eluded us until it entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your evil and protected you from its evil.\""],[10085,"From Abdullah: We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} was sent down upon him. We were indeed receiving it from his mouth while it was fresh, when a snake came out upon us. We rushed to kill it, but it slipped away. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil and you were protected from its evil.\""],[10086,"While we were in the mosque of al-Khayf on the night of Arafah, we heard the sound of a snake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" It entered a crack of a hole, so he brought a palm frond and lit a fire in it, then we emptied part of the hole but did not find it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your evil and protected you from its evil.\""],[10087,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina when al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and suddenly there was a snake. They sought it, but it eluded them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have been protected from its evil just as it was protected from your evil.\""],[10088,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and we were receiving it from his mouth when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" We rushed toward it, but it entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10089,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, nor should he see it as a right upon himself to turn away only from his right side. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10090,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, seeing only that it is a right upon him to turn away only from his right side. Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10091,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, seeing only that it is a right upon him to turn away from his right side. Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10092,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left. And this is how the companions of al-A'mash narrated it, but al-Hajjaj b. Arta'ah differed from them."],[10093,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10094,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever is capable of marriage should get married; otherwise, let them fast, for fasting will be a shield for them.\""],[10095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O young men, whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding chastity. And whoever cannot, then upon him is fasting, for it is a shield for him.\""],[10096,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever among you can afford to get married, let him do so, and whoever cannot afford it should fast, for it will be a restraint (Wija) for him.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2241)"],[10097,"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ about being single, so he said, \"Marry, and if you are unable to, then observe fasting, as it will be a restraint for you.\""],[10098,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ say the takbir at every rising and lowering, standing and sitting, and he would give the greeting to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10099,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ say the takbir at every rising and lowering, standing and sitting, and he would give the greeting to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10100,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ say the takbir at every rising and lowering, standing and sitting, and he would give the greeting to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10101,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to give the greeting to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[10102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10103,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeting with salam, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and from the other side the like of that."],[10104,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to greet with salam to his right, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10105,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to greet with salam to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his face could be seen or appear. I have not forgotten, among what I have forgotten: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10107,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , that he used to give salutations with his left-hand."],[10108,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' and to his left the like of that, until his cheek appeared to them."],[10109,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us from Hajjaj from al-Shaʿbi and Abu al-Duha from Masruq from ʿAbdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left, turning the side of his face toward them."],[10110,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and his left hand until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, saying 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah'.\""],[10111,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10112,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and left hand until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, saying \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.\""],[10113,"Whatever I have forgotten, I have not forgotten the salam of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer: to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10114,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left."],[10115,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and left hand."],[10116,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeting with salam to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer. When he finished, we said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'No. I am only a human like you. When I forget, remind me.' He then faced the qiblah with them and said takbir, and they said takbir. Then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then he said takbir and prostrated, and they prostrated. Then he greeted with salam to his right and to his left."],[10118,"It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he gave the salam to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,” and to his left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.”"],[10119,"I prayed with ʿAli and ʿAbdullah, and I saw them give the salam to their right and to their left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.” He claimed that they both prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave the salam to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” and to his left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” until the whiteness of his cheek was seen from both sides."],[10120,"It was said to Abdullah, \"A man in Makkah greets with two greetings, so how should he respond?\" He said, \"How should he attach them?\""],[10121,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform two salutations (i.e., the act of greeting by saying 'As-Salamu Alaikum').\""],[10122,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give the salam to his right and to his left.”"],[10123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fortify your wealth with zakat, treat your sick with charity, and prepare for affliction with supplication.”"],[10124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any man whom Allah has given knowledge and he conceals it, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[10125,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When one of you is fasting, let him not be obscene or ignorant. If someone insults him, let him say: ‘I am fasting.’”"],[10126,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When one of you is fasting, let him not be obscene or ignorant. If someone insults him, let him say: ‘I am fasting.’”"],[10127,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When one of you is fasting, let him not be obscene or ignorant. If someone insults him, let him say: ‘I am fasting.’”"],[10128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks for something while he is self-sufficient regarding it, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches on his face.”"],[10129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks for something while he is self-sufficient regarding it, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches on his face.”"],[10130,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever gives a loan twice, he will have the like of the reward of one of them had he given it as charity.”"],[10131,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought captives, and he began to give each household as a whole, and he disliked separating them.”"],[10132,"\"We used to perform ablution with the water of a leper's basin.\""],[10133,"«Seek it on the night of the seventeenth, for it is the morning of the Day of Furqan, the day the two hosts met.»"],[10134,"«The duration of the noon prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in summer was three feet to five feet, and in winter five feet to seven feet.»"],[10135,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: «Allah does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from stolen spoils; and begin with those you support.»"],[10136,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: «There will be rulers who kill the prayer and strangle it to the point of the death rattle; indeed it is the prayer of one worse than a donkey, and the prayer of one who finds no alternative. Whoever of you reaches that time, let him perform the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory one.»"],[10137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade anyone from monopolizing from the children of Adam."],[10138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name.»"],[10139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was detained one night with one of his wives, and he did not come to us for the later evening prayer until the night had passed. Then he came to us, and among us were those praying and those lying down. He gave us glad tidings and said: «Indeed no one from the People of the Book performs this prayer.» Then it was revealed: {They are not all alike; among the People of the Book is an upright community who recite the verses of Allah during the hours of the night while they prostrate.}"],[10140,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «People must have a leadership, whether righteous or wicked. As for the righteous one, it is just in distribution and your spoils are divided among you equally. As for the wicked one, the believer is tested therein; and a wicked leadership is better than harj.» It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is harj?\" He said: «Killing and lying.»"],[10141,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about these two suras, and he said: «It was said to me and I said, so say as I said.»"],[10142,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ praising Nakhaʿ until I wished I were a man from Nakhaʿ."],[10143,"From Abdullah b. Masud, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: «The world will not pass away until Allah sends a man from my household whose name matches my name and whose father's name matches my father's name.»"],[10144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The Hour will not come until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name, and he will fill the earth with justice and fairness as it was filled with injustice and oppression.»"],[10145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The nights and days will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name.»"],[10146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there remained of this world but one night, a man from the household of the Prophet ﷺ would still rule during it.”"],[10147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name.”"],[10148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The world will not come to an end until a man from my family, whose name matches my name, becomes the ruler of the Arabs.\" And this wording is from the hadith of Musaddad."],[10149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The days and nights will not pass until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name. He will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with tyranny and oppression.”"],[10150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household assumes authority. He will fill the earth with fairness and justice as it was filled with oppression and tyranny. His name matches my name.”"],[10151,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household assumes authority whose name matches my name.”"],[10152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If only one day of this world remained, Allah would lengthen that day until He sends in it a man from me — or from my family, my household — whose name matches my name and whose father’s name matches my father’s name.”"],[10153,"\"For me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The world will not pass away, nor will the days end, until a man from my family controls the Arabs, and his name matches mine.'\""],[10154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If only one night of this world remained, Allah would lengthen that night until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name and whose father’s name matches my father’s name. He will fill it with fairness and justice as it was filled with oppression and tyranny.”"],[10155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name. He will fill the earth with fairness and justice as it was filled with tyranny and oppression.”"],[10156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name.” He said: Yes."],[10157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name.” He said: Yes."],[10158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name.” He said: Yes."],[10159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The days and nights will not pass until a man from my household rules.”"],[10160,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man from my family will come forth whose name matches my name and whose character matches my character. He will fill it with justice and fairness as it was filled with oppression and tyranny.\""],[10161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The days and nights will not pass—even if only one day remains of this world—until Allah sends a man from my ummah whose name matches my name.\""],[10162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Keep reviewing the Qur'an, for it is more prone to escape from the hearts of men than a camel from its hobbles. None of you should say, 'I forgot such-and-such a verse,' but rather he was made to forget.\""],[10163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth is the fasting of the entire age and its breaking of the fast.\""],[10164,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.\""],[10165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever deceives us is not of us; scheming and deceiving are in the Fire.\""],[10166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal.\""],[10167,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"The woman who buries her daughter alive and the girl who is buried alive are in the Fire.\""],[10168,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr were three hundred."],[10169,"About prayer at sunrise and at sunset.\""],[10170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \"What is richness?\" He said, \"Despairing of what is in people's hands.\""],[10171,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are no two Muslims who have two children of theirs die between them except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.\""],[10172,"\"The first to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sa'd.\""],[10173,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"As for me, I prostrate on seven bones and I do not tie back hair or a garment.\""],[10174,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Abu Bakr, verily I saw myself last night at a well drawing water. You came and drew water, and you were weak, and may Allah forgive you. Then 'Umar came and it turned into a large bucket, and the people struck at the watering trough.\""],[10175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Marry virgins, for they have sweeter mouths, more productive wombs, and are more content with little.\""],[10176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say: He is Allah, the One (Qur'an 112) equals one-third of the Qur'an.\""],[10177,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When three are gathered, let not two converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that will grieve him.\""],[10178,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A woman must not describe another woman to her husband as if he were looking at her.\""],[10179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him.\""],[10180,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"],[10181,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn: 'Say: O disbelievers' (Qur'an 109) and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Qur'an 112).\""],[10182,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs after sunset: 'Say: O disbelievers' (Qur'an 109) and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Qur'an 112).\""],[10183,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"A caller is sent at the time of every prayer and says: O children of Adam, arise and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves. So they arise, purify themselves, and their sins fall from their eyes. They pray, and they are forgiven for what is between the two prayers. Then they kindle again in between. When the first prayer comes, he calls: O children of Adam, arise and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves. So they arise, purify themselves, pray, and they are forgiven for what is between the two prayers. When the afternoon prayer comes, the same, and when the sunset prayer comes, the same, and when the night prayer comes, the same. Then they sleep, having been forgiven.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"So one travels in the night for good and one travels in the night for evil.\""],[10184,"\"We used to call it in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ 'the protector', and in the Book of Allah it is a surah; whoever recites it every night has indeed done much and good.\""],[10185,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is as if I am looking at Musa in this valley, in ihram, between two Qatwani cloaks.”"],[10186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ took Ibrahim as a close friend, and your companion is the close friend of Allah, and Muhammad ﷺ is the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he recited: {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station}."],[10187,"On the day of Badr, when they brought the captives, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Abu Bakr and said: “What do you think about these?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are your people. If you kill them, they will enter the Fire. If you take ransom from them, then whoever accepts Islam will be a support for us, and whoever refuses we will take his ransom.” He said: “What do you think, O Umar?” He said: “I think you should present them and strike their necks. These are the leaders of disbelief and the commanders of disbelief. By Allah, they were not satisfied until they expelled us, and they were the first of the Arabs to raid us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abu Bakr, your likeness is that of Ibrahim ﷺ when he said: {Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me—indeed You are Forgiving and Merciful}. As for you, O Umar, your likeness is that of Nuh when he said: {My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any inhabitant from among the disbelievers}.”"],[10188,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the captives and said: “What do you think?” Umar said: “O Messenger of Allah, they belied you and expelled you; strike their necks.” Abdullah b. Rawahah said: “O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley with much firewood; set it ablaze and throw them into it.” Al-Abbas said: “May Allah sever your kinship.” Abu Bakr said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are your kin, your root, and your people. Overlook them; Allah will save them from the Fire through you.” He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and some said the opinion was what Abu Bakr said, and others said the opinion was what Umar said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: “What do you say about these two men? Their likeness is that of brothers they had before them. Nuh said: {My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any inhabitant from among the disbelievers}. Musa said: {Our Lord, obliterate their wealth}. Isa said: {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise}. Ibrahim said: {Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me—indeed You are Forgiving and Merciful}. Allah hardens the hearts of men in it until they are harder than stones, and He softens the hearts of men in it until they are softer than softness. You are in need, and none of them will depart except with ransom or a blow to the neck.” Abdullah said: I said: “Except Suhayl b. Bayda'.” Abdullah said: I had heard him mention Islam, so he fell silent. I kept looking at the sky, waiting for stones to fall on me. I said: I put the words before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he said: “Except Suhayl b. Bayda'.”"],[10189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would find a man's shoulder leaning away from his companion's shoulder and would straighten it, saying: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[10190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform the night prayer, O People of the Quran.\" An Arab man asked, \"What does the Prophet ﷺ say?\" He replied, \"You are not one of its people.\""],[10191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite the Night Prayer, O people of the Quran.\""],[10192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the Children of Israel acted in disobedience, their reciters and scholars forbade them from what they were doing, but they disobeyed them. Then they mixed with them in their livelihoods, and Allah struck their hearts one upon another, then He cursed them on the tongue of Dawud and Isa son of Maryam.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up, having been reclining, and said: “No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until you bend them to the truth completely.”"],[10193,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “When the Children of Israel took to acts of disobedience, their scholars forbade them, but they did not desist. Then they sat with them and associated with them, so Allah struck their hearts one upon another.” Then he said: {Those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel were cursed}—the verse."],[10194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you must enjoin good and forbid evil, and you must seize the hand of the wrongdoer and bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will strike your hearts one upon another and curse you as He cursed them.”"],[10195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people before you, when one of them committed a sin, the one who forbade him would forbid him as a mere excuse. Then the next day, he would sit with him, eat with him, and drink with him, as if he had not seen him commit the sin yesterday. When Allah saw that from them, He struck their hearts one upon another, then He cursed them on the tongue of their Prophet Dawud and Isa son of Maryam. That was because they disobeyed and transgressed. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you must enjoin good and forbid evil, and you must seize the hands of the wrongdoer and bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will strike your hearts one upon another, then He will curse you as He cursed them.” Khalaf said: “ta'tirunahu” means “you subdue him.”"],[10196,"They were made to appear few in our eyes on the day of Badr, until I said to my companion beside me: “How many do you think they are? Do you think they are seventy?” He said: “I think they are a hundred.” Then we captured a man from them and asked him, and he said: “We were a thousand.”"],[10197,"We heard a singer singing a song that had a stronger melody than Muhammad's ﷺ melody on the day of Badr when he said, \"O Allah, I sing to you what you promised me. O Allah, if you destroy this group, they will not be worshiped.\" Then he turned around as if his face was the moon, and said, \"It's as if I'm watching the people's wrestling match at night.\""],[10198,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , performed the prayer of fear (Salat al-Khawf), so he arranged them in rows, facing the enemy, row after row. He prayed one rak'ah with them, then the row that followed him stayed behind, and they stood in the position of those who were facing the enemy. Those people advanced and prayed behind him one rak'ah, then he said the salutation to them. Then those who were behind him stood up and prayed one rak'ah, then those people advanced and stood in the position of those people, and they prayed one rak'ah.\""],[10199,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Quran was revealed in seven modes. Whoever recites according to one of them should not turn to another out of aversion to it.”"],[10200,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a donkey named Ufayr.”"],[10201,"Some people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Our companion is ill; shall we cauterize him?' He remained silent for a while, then said: 'If you wish, cauterize him; and if you wish, treat him with heated stones.'"],[10202,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from fraud.'"],[10203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heaven will show mercy to you.'"],[10204,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Who is the noblest of people?' He said, 'Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq, Allah's sacrifice.'"],[10205,"\"The Prophet ﷺ married Aisha when she was six years old, and consummated the marriage when she was nine years old, and he passed away when she was eighteen years old.\""],[10206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to instruct us, when we began the prayer, to say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. Blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You.'"],[10207,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The one who repents from sin is like one who has no sin.'"],[10208,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.'"],[10209,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we were delayed from the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha prayers. That was difficult for us, so we said, 'We are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in the path of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called the iqama for prayer, and we prayed with each prayer's iqama. Then he said: 'There is no group on earth remembering Allah other than you.'"],[10210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat during the two rak'ahs as if on hot stones."],[10211,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he was in the two rak'ahs, was as if on hot stones. I would say, 'Until he stands,' and he would say, 'Until he stands.'"],[10212,"And Abdullah said, \"O Aba Yazid, if the Messenger of Allah saw you, he would love you. And whenever I see you, I am reminded of the sincere worshippers.\""],[10213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever builds beyond what suffices him will be burdened to carry it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[10214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in Surat al-Najm, he and the polytheists all together."],[10215,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree, and he said, \"Which of you remembers al-Sahbawat?\" ʿAbdullah said, \"I do, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, when the moon rose, and that was the night of the twenty-seventh.\""],[10216,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Be truly modest before God.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, we are indeed modest, and praise be to God.\" He said, \"It is not that. But whoever is truly modest before God must guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it holds, and remember death and decay. Whoever desires the Hereafter abandons the adornment of this world. Whoever does that has been truly modest before God.\""],[10217,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to al-Mundhir b. Sawa: \"Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat, that one is a Muslim, having the protection of God and the protection of the Messenger ﷺ.\""],[10218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If one of you points a spear at a man, and its tip is at the hollow of his throat, and he says, 'There is no god but God,' then let him lift the spear away from him.\""],[10219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and they were killed. They said, \"When you meet your people, convey to them from us that we met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.\""],[10220,"\"Beware of testimonies; if you must, then testify for an expedition the Messenger of God ﷺ sent out, who were killed, and it was revealed about them: 'Convey from us to our people that we met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.'\""],[10221,"God Almighty sent His Prophet ﷺ to cause a man to enter Paradise. He entered a synagogue and found Jews reading the Torah. When they came to the description of the Prophet ﷺ, they stopped. In a corner there was a sick man. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Why did you stop?\" The sick man said, \"They came to the description of a prophet and stopped.\" The sick man came crawling until he took the Torah and read it until he reached the description of the Prophet ﷺ and his community, then said, \"This is your description and the description of your community. I bear witness that there is no god but God and that you are the Messenger of God.\" Then he died. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Attend to your brother.\""],[10222,"\"We did not have a festival except at the beginning of the day, and I saw us praying the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the shade of al-Hatim.\""],[10223,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade slapping the cheeks and tearing the garments."],[10224,"ʿAbdullah: \"You have been commanded with four things: establishing prayer, giving zakah, performing Hajj and ʿUmrah to the House; Hajj is the greater Hajj and ʿUmrah is the lesser Hajj.\""],[10225,"You have been commanded in the Book of God with four things: establishing prayer, giving zakah, Hajj, and ʿUmrah to the House.\" He did not mention Ibn Masʿud."],[10226,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Bilal, and he had a heap of dates. He said, \"What is this, O Bilal?\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, it is for you and your guests.\" He said, \"Do you not fear that it will have a vapor from the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear diminution from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[10227,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not return after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\""],[10228,"Your Prophet ﷺ, when he was bowing or prostrating, would say: \"Glory be to You and praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\""],[10229,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery.\""],[10230,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I had forbidden you from nabidh in certain vessels. Indeed, no vessel makes anything unlawful. Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[10231,"The passage translates to: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah has commanded me to marry Fatimah to Ali.'\""],[10232,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers.\""],[10233,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes an oath on a false matter, let him use it to take away the wealth of a Muslim and meet Allah while He is angry with him.\""],[10234,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Abusing a Muslim is Fusuq (an evil doing) and killing him is Kufr (disbelief).\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 48)"],[10235,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for that, and the tattooer and the one who asks for tattooing."],[10236,"We were sitting with Abdullah bin Mas'ood when a man asked him, \"O Abu Abdullah, did you ask your prophet ﷺ how many caliphs would this ummah have?\" Ibn Mas'ood replied, \"No one has asked me about it since I arrived in Iraq before you did. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'The caliphs of the Children of Israel were twelve in number.'\" The wording is from a narration by Hujjaj."],[10237,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The mill of Islam will turn for five and thirty years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; if they survive, they will remain for seventy years.\""],[10238,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ looked at the slain on the day of Badr, he said to Abu Bakr: \"If Abu Talib were alive, he would know that our swords have taken hold of the chiefs.\" And that is why Abu Talib says:"],[10239,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No judge judges between people except that he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with an angel holding him by the back of his neck until he is made to stand over Hell. Then he will raise his head to the sky; if God says, 'Throw him,' then his fall will be for forty autumns.\""],[10240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, strengthen Islam with 'Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.\" Then God made the supplication of His Messenger for 'Umar b. al-Khattab come true, and through him He built Islam and destroyed idols."],[10241,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[10242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his property is like the sanctity of his blood.\""],[10243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like to supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."],[10244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: He is Allah, the One (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad) is one third of the Qur’an.”"],[10245,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “Ammā baʿd (to proceed).”"],[10246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over the people of the well and said: “O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, do they hear?” He said: “You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, but today they cannot answer.”"],[10247,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the light of the moon on the night of the full moon. The second group will be like the color of the most beautiful shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives from the ḥūr al-ʿīn, each wife wearing seventy robes. The marrow of their shins will be visible from behind their flesh and robes, just as red drink is seen in a white glass.”"],[10248,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from five things: cowardice, miserliness, bad old age, the trial of the chest, and the punishment of the grave."],[10249,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying: {On the Day the earth will be changed to another earth} (Qur’an 14:48), he said: “A white earth, as if it is silver, in which no unlawful blood has been shed and no sin has been committed.”"],[10250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The houses of Allah on earth are the mosques, and it is incumbent upon Allah to honor the one who visits Him in them.”"],[10251,"He said: “The best of you is the one who learns the Qur’an and teaches it.”"],[10252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us: When one of you sneezes, let him say: “Al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds).” When he says that, let those near him say: “Yarḥamuka Allah (May Allah have mercy on you).” When they say that, let him say: “Yaghfiru Allahu lī wa lakum (May Allah forgive me and you).”"],[10253,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in an upper room that was like a bathhouse, and he was sleeping on a mat that had left marks on his side. I wept. He said: “What makes you weep, O ʿAbd Allah?” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, Kisrā and Caesar walk on silk, brocade, and fine silk, while you sleep on this mat that has left marks on your side.” He said: “Do not weep, O ʿAbd Allah, for they have this world and we have the Hereafter. What have I to do with this world? My likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who stops under a tree, then moves on and leaves it.”"],[10254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever makes his heart drink the love of this world will cleave to three things from it: misery whose weariness never ends, greed whose wealth is never attained, and hope whose end is never reached. This world is both pursuing and pursued. Whoever pursues the world, the Hereafter pursues him until death comes and seizes him. Whoever pursues the Hereafter, the world pursues him until he receives his provision from it in full.”"],[10255,"No people of prophethood were ever destroyed until fornication and usury appeared among them."],[10256,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A camel [slaughtered] on the Day of Sacrifice is for ten.\""],[10257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No disease has been placed on earth except that a cure for it has been provided. It is known to those who know and unknown to those who do not know.\""],[10258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Food for one day is a right, food for two days is a sunnah, and food for the third day is showing off. Whoever seeks to be heard, God will make him heard.\""],[10259,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The expiation for a gathering is for the servant to say: 'Glory be to You, O God, and praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.'\""],[10260,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, God places the heavens on one finger, the mountains on one finger, the trees on one finger, and the water and the earth on one finger, then says: 'I am the King.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then recited: {They did not estimate God with His true estimation}."],[10261,"A scholar from among the Jewish rabbis came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"On the Day of Resurrection, God will place the heavens on this, the creatures on this, the mountains on this, and the earth on this.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and recited: {They did not estimate God with His true estimation} up to His saying: {from what they associate with Him}."],[10262,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best of this community is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimonies and whose testimonies precede their oaths.\""],[10263,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"Which people are best?\" He said: \"My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people where the testimony of one of them will precede his oath and his oath will precede his testimony.\""],[10264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The last person to exit the Fire and enter Paradise is a man who will be pushed into Paradise. He will think that it is already full, so he will say, 'O Allah! It is already full!' It will be said to him, 'Enter, for you have ten times the world or ten times what the world contains.' He will say, 'Are You laughing at me though You are the King?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars became visible.\""],[10265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Have you not seen the last person to enter Paradise and the last person to exit Hell? A man who has been touched by the flames of Hell will pass by his Lord and say, 'O Lord, take me out of this fire and put me under the shade of a tree.' When his soul leaves his body, he will look at the tree of Paradise and say, 'O Lord, let me enter Paradise.' But there will be no deeds for him to rise with, so he will depart, crawling until he reaches them. However, he will not find a place for himself there and will return to his Lord, saying, 'O Lord, I did not find a place for myself there.' The Lord will say, 'Go, for you have the equivalent of the whole world and ten times its size.' The man will say, 'Are you making fun of me when You are my Lord?' At this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars and incisors appeared.\""],[10266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and I brought him water. He said, \"Who ordered you to do this?\" I said, \"No one ordered me.\" He said, \"You have done well; rejoice in Paradise.\" Then Ali came and he gave him glad tidings of Paradise."],[10267,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you.\" Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ entered, greeted, and ascended."],[10268,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you.\" Then Abu Bakr appeared, then Umar ؓ."],[10269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in a garden and said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Abu Bakr entered. Then he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Umar entered. Then he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Ali ؓ entered."],[10270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom, and some eloquence is magic.\""],[10271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.\""],[10272,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Keep refreshing your knowledge of the Qur'an, for it slips away from men's chests more readily than camels escape to their homelands.\""],[10273,"When the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" he would say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will. You are worthy of praise and glory.\""],[10274,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. The people said, \"Stop for us to rest,\" so he said, \"Who will wake us?\" I said, \"I will guard you and wake you.\" Then I slept and they slept, and we did not wake up except by the heat of the sun on our heads. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the last of us, so he got up, performed ablution along with the people, prayed two rak'ahs, then prayed the dawn prayer."],[10275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"How will you be when a quarter of the people of Paradise is yours, while the rest of mankind has three-quarters?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"How will you be when a third is yours?\" They said, \"That is more.\" He said, \"How will you be when half is yours?\" They said, \"That is more.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will be one hundred and twenty rows, of which you are eighty rows.\""],[10276,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. The people fled from him, and I remained with him along with eighty of the Muhajirun and Ansar. We retreated on our feet about eighty steps, but we did not turn our backs to them. They are the ones upon whom Allah sent down tranquility. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept moving forward on his mule. His mule swerved, so he leaned off the saddle, and I rushed toward him and said, \"Lift yourself up, may Allah raise you.\" He said, \"Hand me a handful of dust.\" He threw it in their faces, and their eyes filled with dust. He said, \"Where are the Muhajirun and the Ansar?\" I said, \"They are near.\" He said, \"Call them.\" So I called them, and they came with their swords in their right hands, like shooting stars, and the polytheists turned their backs and fled."],[10277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No Muslim is ever afflicted with any worry, grief, or distress, and says: 'Allahumma inni 'abduka, wa ibn 'abdika, wa ibn amatika, nasīyatī bi-yadika, mādin fiyya hukmuka, 'adlun fiyya qadā'uka, as'aluka bi kulli ismin huwa laka sammayta bihi nafsaka, aw anzaltahu fi kitabika, aw 'allamtahu ahadan min khalqika, awi ista'tharta bihi fi 'ilmil-ghaybi 'indaka an taj'alal-Qur'āna rabī'a qalbi, wa nūra basari, wa jalā'a huznī wa dhahāba hammi', Illa adhhaba Allahu hamahu wa abadala hu makan huznih farahan.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn these words?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Yes, whoever hears them should learn them.\""],[10278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let your house be sufficient for you, weep over the remembrance of your sin, and control your tongue.\""],[10279,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets to mention the name of Allah at the beginning of his meal should say when he remembers: 'In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end.' For he starts a new meal and the evil one is prevented from partaking of it.\""],[10280,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Kill all snakes. Whoever leaves them out of fear of their revenge is not of me.\""],[10281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The millstone of Islam will turn at the head of thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; and if they remain, they will remain for seventy years.\""],[10282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Mas'ud.\" I said, \"At your service,\" three times. He said, \"Do you know which bond of faith is most firm?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Alliance for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.\""],[10283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Masʿūd!\" I said, \"At your service,\" three times. He said, \"Do you know which of the bonds of faith is most firm?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Loyalty for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.\""],[10284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Masʿūd!\" I said, \"At your service,\" three times. He said, \"Do you know which of the bonds of faith is most firm?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Loyalty for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.\""],[10285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Masʿūd!\" I said, \"At your service,\" three times. He said, \"Do you know which of the bonds of faith is most firm?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Loyalty for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah.\""],[10286,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place his right hand over his left hand in prayer.\""],[10287,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought captives, he would give the members of a household all together, out of dislike of separating them.\""],[10288,"ʿAbdullah [b. Masʿūd ؓ ] said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by, and the people began saying, \"This is the Messenger of Allah.\" A Jew said, \"If he is the Messenger of Allah, I will ask him about something, and if he is a prophet, he will know it.\" He said, \"O Abu al-Qāsim, tell me: is a human being created from the man's semen or from the woman's semen?\" He replied, \"The man's semen is white and thick; from it come the bones and the nerves. The woman's semen is yellow and thin; from it come the blood and the flesh.\""],[10289,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer beyond its times and introduce innovations.\" He [Ibn Masʿūd] said, \"What should I do if I live to see them?\" He replied, \"You ask me, O son of Umm ʿAbd, what you should do? There is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah.\""],[10290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the glance is a poisoned arrow from among the arrows of Iblīs. Whoever abandons it out of fear of Me, I will replace it for him with faith whose sweetness he will find in his heart.\""],[10291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I saw Ibrāhīm ﷺ on the night I was taken on the Night Journey. He said, 'O Muhammad, convey greetings from me to your community, and tell them that Paradise has good soil and sweet water, and that it is a plain, and its plants are: Subḥān Allāh (Glory be to Allah), al-Ḥamdu lillāh (Praise be to Allah), Lā ilāha illā Allāh (There is no god but Allah), Allāhu akbar (Allah is Greatest), and Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh (There is no might or power except with Allah).'\""],[10292,"\"There were two men from Juhaynah who jointly owned a slave, and one of them freed him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he made him liable for it. He had a small flock of nearly one hundred sheep, so he sold them and paid his companion.\""],[10293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When two parties to a transaction differ, and the commodity is still present, then the word is the word of the seller, or they may return it.\""],[10294,"\"I have not lied since I became Muslim except for one lie. I was saddling the mount for the Prophet ﷺ when a man from the people of al-Ṭāʾif came and asked me, 'Which saddle is most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said, 'The Ṭāʾifī turned-down one,' but he disliked it. When it was brought to him, he said, 'Who saddled this?' They said, 'Your saddle-maker.' He said, 'Tell Ibn Umm ʿAbd to saddle it.' So the saddle was returned to me.\""],[10295,"That it was in the handwriting of his father ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, written with his own hand, and in it ʿAbdullāh said: “By Allah, besides Whom there is no deity, I have not seen anyone harsher against the overly scrupulous than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10296,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Verily the overly scrupulous are destroyed.”"],[10297,"ʿAbdullāh said: “It is only a day we used to fast before Ramaḍān.”"],[10298,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The Children of Israel appointed a successor over themselves, and he stood praying in the moonlight above Bayt al-Maqdis. He mentioned things he had done, then he lowered himself by a rope, and in the morning the rope was hanging from the mosque while he had gone. He set off until he came to a people on the seashore, and he found them making bricks. He asked them, ‘How much do you charge for these bricks?’ They told him, so he made bricks with them and ate from the work of his own hands. When prayer time came, he purified himself and prayed. That worker reported him to their village chief, saying, ‘Among us is a man who does such and such.’ So he sent for him, but he refused to come to him. Then he came riding on his mount, and when he saw him he fled. He pursued him and overtook him and said, ‘Wait, let me speak a word to you.’ He stood until he spoke to him and told him that he had been a king and that he had fled from fear of his sin. He said, ‘I will join you in that.’ So they both worshipped Allah and asked Allah to cause them to die together, and they both died.” ʿAbdullāh said: “If I were at the sands of Egypt, I would show you their graves,” describing it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did."],[10299,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has servants whom He withholds from being killed; He lengthens their lives in excellence of deeds, gives them good provision, keeps them alive in well-being, and takes their souls in well-being upon their beds, and He grants them the stations of martyrs.”"],[10300,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered the state of iḥrām when his mount set off with him."],[10301,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he passed by an anthill that had been burned with fire. He said: “It is not appropriate for anyone to punish with the punishment of Allah.”"],[10302,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a small bird fluttering over the heads of his Companions and said: “Who has disturbed this one?” A man from the Anṣār said: “I took its eggs, or its chicks.” So he ordered him to return them."],[10303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the two parties to a sale disagree, the word is that of the seller.”"],[10304,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"No one is more jealous than Allah, because He has forbidden indecencies. And no one loves praise more than Allah, because He has praised Himself. And no one loves excuses more than Allah, because He accepts excuses from His creation. And no one loves praise more than Allah, because He praises Himself.\""],[10305,"The Prophet ﷺ went hungry, so he sent a message to his wives to bring him some food, but none of them had any. He then said, \"O Allah, I ask you for your bounty and mercy, for no one possesses them except you.\" He was then given a praying sheep and he said, \"This is from the bounty of Allah, and we are awaiting His mercy.\""],[10306,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[10307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform the dawn prayer when it is bright, for that is greater for the reward.”"],[10308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The excellence of the night prayer over the day prayer is like the excellence of secret charity over open charity.”"],[10309,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Our Lord marvels at two men: a man who rises from his bed and cover, leaving his beloved and family for his prayer. Allah ﷻ says to His angels, 'Look at My servant; he rose from his bed and cover, leaving his beloved and family for his prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me.' And a man who goes out to fight in the cause of Allah and flees, then knows the consequence of fleeing and the reward of returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah, the Exalted, says to His angels, 'Look at My servant; he returned out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me until his blood was shed.'"],[10310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If it were said to the people of the Fire, 'You will remain in the Fire for the number of every pebble in the world,' they would rejoice. And if it were said to the people of Paradise, 'You will remain in Paradise for the number of every pebble in the world,' they would grieve. But eternity has been decreed for them."],[10311,"He said: Won't you come near, O Abu Muhammad, for the midday meal? He said: Did you fast this day? He said: 'We used to fast this day before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, we fasted it and abandoned what was other than it.'"],[10312,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'Allah will gather the nations on the Day of Resurrection, then He will descend from His Throne to His Footstool, and His Footstool encompasses the heavens and the earth.'"],[10313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments: a San'ani striped cloak and two Hibara striped cloaks."],[10314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Two types of people are insatiable and never satisfied: the seeker of knowledge and the seeker of this world."],[10315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone, for the first to seize the dominion of my community and what Allah has granted them will be the Banu Qantura'.'"],[10316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will always be forty men of my community whose hearts are like the heart of Abraham; Allah repels harm from the people of the earth through them. They are called al-Abdal.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They did not attain this through prayer, fasting, or charity.' They said: O Messenger of Allah, how did they attain it? He said: 'Through generosity and sincere counsel to the Muslims.'"],[10317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, al-Salam (peace) is one of the names of Allah which He placed on earth, so spread it among yourselves. When a man greets a group and they respond, he has a degree of superiority over them because he reminded them. If they do not respond, then one better and purer than them responds to him.'"],[10318,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The Fire has been kindled and Paradise has been brought near. O people of the rooms! If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[10319,"From the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"Indeed, after you there will come a time of patience for those who adhere to it, their reward will be equivalent to that of fifty martyrs.\" So, 'Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, from us or from them?\" He said, \"From among you.\""],[10320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a horse that he rode at a flowing pace, and it pleased him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This horse of mine is indeed a sea.'"],[10321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among yourselves.'"],[10322,"The first thing I learned of the affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ: I came to Makkah with some uncles of mine, and we were directed to al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. We reached him while he was sitting at Zamzam, so we sat with him. While we were with him, a man approached from the gate of al-Safa, white with a redness over him, having thick, curly hair reaching halfway down his ears, aquiline-nosed, with a slight projection at the bridge, bright front teeth, dark wide eyes, a full beard, a thin line of hair from chest to navel, rough hands and feet, wearing two white garments, as though he were the moon on the night of the full moon. Walking on his right was a beardless youth of handsome face, near puberty or having reached it, and behind them came a woman who had covered her beauty until he made for the Black Stone and touched it, then the youth touched it, then the woman touched it. Then he circumambulated the House seven times, with the youth and the woman circumambulating with him. Then he touched the corner, raised his hands and said takbir, and the youth stood at his right and raised his hands, and the woman stood behind them, raised her hands and said takbir. He prolonged the qunut, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head from bowing and performed qunut while standing, then prostrated, and the youth and the woman prostrated with him, doing as he did and following him. He said: We saw something we did not recognize in Makkah, so we found it strange. We turned to al-Abbas and said: O Abu al-Fadl, this religion we did not know among you—has something new occurred? He said: Yes, by God. Do you not know this one? We said: No. He said: This is my nephew, Muhammad b. Abd Allah, and the youth is Ali b. Abi Talib, and the woman is Khadija bt. Khuwaylid. By God, there is no one on the face of the earth who worships God by this religion except these three."],[10323,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my community from them are eighty rows.”"],[10324,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days.”"],[10325,"Aisha had an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma'il. Captives from Bal'anbar arrived, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to free from among them, and he said: “Whoever has an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma'il, let him not free anyone from Himyar.” Ali b. 'Abis said: I said to Isma'il b. Abi Khalid: What was Himyar? He said: He is greater than Isma'il."],[10326,"They said: O Messenger of God, you have forgotten? He said: “Why should I not forget when the groove of one of you is between his nail and his fingertips?”"],[10327,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I am your forerunner at the Pool, and I will vie with the nations by you, so do not fight one another after me.”"],[10328,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When the appointed term of one of you is in a land, he is brought to it for a need.”"],[10329,"“We have been commanded to fulfill an oath.”"],[10330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and then the nearest, then the next nearest.”"],[10331,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Perform Hajj and 'Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sin as the bellows removes impurity from iron and gold and silver, and Hajj Al-Mabrur brings no less a reward than Paradise.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2631)"],[10332,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The slain person will come, grasping his killer, while his veins gush blood before the Possessor of Might, and he will say: O Lord, ask this one why he killed me. Then He will say: Why did you kill him? If he says: I killed him so that glory would be for so-and-so, He will say: It is God's.”"],[10333,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The Emigrants, the Helpers, the freed ones of Quraysh, and the freed ones of Thaqif—some of them are allies of others in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[10334,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am your forerunner at the Pool.”"],[10335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will place him in the Fire.”"],[10336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever dies while associating partners with Allah, Allah will make him enter the Fire.\""],[10337,"To wash your hands until they are clean, then enter your right hand into the container and pour with your right hand onto your left hand to wash your private parts until they are clean. Then hit the wall and the ground with your left hand and rub them, then pour water onto them with your right hand to wash them. Then perform ablution for prayer."],[10338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[10339,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while they are still alive, and those who take graves as places of prostration.”"],[10340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, and there were some women of the Ansar in it. He admonished them and reminded them, and said: “There is no woman among you who loses three of her children but that she will enter Paradise.” One of the women said: “Is it not [also] for those who lose two, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “And for those who lose two.”"],[10341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How bad it is for one of you to say, ‘I forgot a verse, such-and-such,’ but rather he was made to forget. Keep reviewing the Quran, for it is wild and flees more swiftly from the chests of men than camels from their hobbles.”"],[10342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies setting up a rival to Allah will enter the Fire. And the five prescribed prayers are expiations for what occurs between them, as long as major sins are avoided.”"],[10343,"“Instruct your dying ones to say: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ for the soul of the believer comes out like sweat, while the soul of the disbeliever comes out from the side of his mouth like the breath of a donkey.”"],[10344,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Keep reviewing the Quran, for it flees more swiftly from the chests of men than cattle from their hobbles.”"],[10345,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman must not have skin-to-skin contact with another woman, for she will describe her to her husband or to a man as if he is looking at her.”"],[10346,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman must not have skin-to-skin contact with another woman, for she will describe her to her husband or to a man as if he is looking at her.”"],[10347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you are three,” and he mentioned something similar, and he added to it: “Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[10348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the prayer of seeking guidance: “O Allah, I ask You to choose for me by Your knowledge and to decree for me by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty, for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion and good for me in my livelihood and good for me in what I seek good through, then decree it for me in well-being, make it easy for me, and bless it for me. And if You know that something other than it is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be.”"],[10349,"The Prophet ﷺ only forbade the meat of domesticated donkeys because they were used for work."],[10350,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I saw Jibril ﷺ , and he had six hundred wings.\""],[10351,"\"The most beloved of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the best of you in character, and the most hateful of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the boastful and the arrogant.\" I said to Ibn Bahdalah, \"What are the arrogant?\" He replied, \"The proud.\""],[10352,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection is bloodshed, and the first thing for which a servant will be called to account is prayer.\""],[10353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us these words: \"O Allah, reconcile our hearts and bring harmony between us, guide us to the paths of peace, deliver us from darkness to light, keep us away from immoralities, both apparent and hidden. O Allah, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our spouses, and our offspring, and turn to us in mercy. Indeed, You are the Ever-Relenting, the Merciful. Make us grateful for Your blessings, praising You for them, and proclaiming them, and complete them upon us.\""],[10354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah while there were three hundred and sixty idols around the House. He began striking them with a stick he had, saying: \"Truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish. Truth has come, and falsehood can neither originate nor repeat.\""],[10355,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Hell will be brought, led by seventy thousand reins; with each rein, seventy thousand angels pulling it.\""],[10356,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one is killed unjustly without a share of the sin falling upon the son of Adam.\" This is how Sulayman al-Taymi narrated it from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah b. Murrah, from Shaqiq; but others narrated from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah b. Murrah, from Masruq."],[10357,"'Abdullah said: \"Indeed, I am informed of where you are, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except the dislike of boring you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to space out his admonitions to us over the days, fearing we would become weary.\""],[10358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with people who honor the extravagant and belittle the worshipers, and who act according to the Qur'an when it aligns with their desires and abandon it when it contradicts their desires? At that point, they believe in some things and disbelieve in others. They strive for what can be attained without effort, without taking into account predestined fate, appointed time, and allotted sustenance. And they do not strive for what cannot be attained except through effort, hoping for a fully rewarded return, a deserving effort, and a trade that does not perish.\""],[10359,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, how can I know when I have done well and when I have done wrong?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"When you hear your neighbors saying, 'You have done well,' then you have done well; and when you hear them saying, 'You have done wrong,' then you have done wrong.\""],[10360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer, and he either added to it or omitted from it. Some of them asked him, \"Has something new occurred in the prayer?\" He replied, \"Nothing new has occurred in it. Had something new occurred, I would have told you; but I am a human being and I forget. So when I forget, remind me.\" He then completed what remained of his prayer, performed two prostrations of forgetfulness, and said, \"When one of you prays and does not know whether he has added or omitted, let him strive to determine what is correct, then let him prostrate twice while sitting.\""],[10361,"\"He said about reading behind the imam, listen to the recitation as you have been commanded; for in prayer, there is fulfillment and that imam will suffice you.\""],[10362,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"How bad it is for a man or a woman to say, 'I forgot such-and-such a Surah' or 'such-and-such a verse.' Rather, he was made to forget.\""],[10363,"From Ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the Prophet ﷺ saying: 'Let none of you say: I forgot such-and-such a verse, for he did not forget; rather, he was made to forget.'"],[10364,"I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud on the day of 'Ashura' while he was eating fresh dates. He said: 'This is the day of 'Ashura', a day we were commanded to fast before Ramadan was revealed.'"],[10365,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim.'"],[10366,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, the drop of semen remains in the womb for forty days, then it becomes a clinging clot for a similar period, then it becomes a lump of flesh for a similar period. Then God sends the angel with four words, and he writes its provision, its lifespan, and whether it is wretched or blessed.'"],[10367,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, the drop of semen remains in the womb for forty days, then it becomes a clinging clot for a similar period, then it becomes a lump of flesh for a similar period. Then God sends the angel with four words, and he writes its provision, its lifespan, and whether it is wretched or blessed.'"],[10368,"'None is more jealous than God; that is why He forbade immorality, both open and secret.'"],[10369,"O daughter of the Messenger of God, did the Messenger of God ﷺ leave with you anything that you could gift me? She said: 'O servant girl, bring that leaf.' She searched for it but could not find it. She said: 'Woe to you, search for it; for it is equal in my sight to Hasan and Husayn.' She searched for it, and behold, she had swept it away with her sweepings. In it was written: Muhammad ﷺ said: 'He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his harm. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. God loves the modest, forbearing, chaste, self-restrained one, and He hates the obscene, foul-mouthed, persistent beggar. Indeed, modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise, while obscenity is from vulgarity, and vulgarity is in the Fire.'"],[10370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip completely like two donkeys.'"],[10371,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Accept the invitation, do not reject the gift, and do not strike the people'—or 'the Muslims.'"],[10372,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever God wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.'"],[10373,"O tongue, speak good and you will gain, and be silent from evil and you will be safe, before you regret. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Most of the sins of the son of Adam are from his tongue.'"],[10374,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever has a daughter and disciplines her well, teaches her well, and gives her generously from the blessings of God that He has bestowed upon him, she will be a protection and a shield for him from the Fire.'"],[10375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When my companions are mentioned, remain silent. And when the stars are mentioned, remain silent. And when fate is mentioned, remain silent.\""],[10376,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Keep revising the Qurʾān, for it escapes from the hearts of men more quickly than camels escape from their hobbles. How bad it is for any of you to say, \"I forgot such-and-such a verse,\" when in fact he was made to forget.'"],[10377,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The Qurʾān is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted and a disputant whose argument is confirmed. Whoever places it before him, it leads him to Paradise; whoever places it behind him, it drives him to the Fire.'"],[10378,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Among the signs of the Hour's approach is the swelling of the new moons.'"],[10379,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'In the last days there will be people who sit in the mosques in circles, their focus being this world. Do not sit with them, for God has no need of them.'"],[10380,"\"I came to Kufa for trade and I stayed near Al-A'mash. When it was night, I intended to descend, but he stood up and performed Tahajjud prayer. I passed by him reciting this verse: 'Allah bears witness that there is no deity except Him, and [so do] the angels and those of knowledge - [that He is] maintaining [creation] in justice. There is no deity except Him, the Exalted in Might, the Wise. Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.' Then Al-A'mash said, 'I bear witness to what Allah has borne witness to, and I entrust this testimony to Allah, and it is in His custody: 'Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.' He repeated it several times. I said, 'Indeed, I heard something in it,' so I went to him the next morning and bid him farewell. Then I said, 'O Abu Muhammad, I heard you reciting this verse repeatedly.' He said, 'So, you did not understand its meaning?' I said, 'I have been with you for a month and you have not informed me.' He said, 'By Allah, I will inform you of its meaning after a year.' So, I stayed for a year, and I was at his door. When the year passed, I said, 'O Abu Muhammad, the year has passed.' He said, 'Abu Wa'il informed me from Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one who brings this verse with its companion on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will say: My servant fulfilled his covenant, and I am more entitled to fulfill the covenant. Bring My servant into Paradise.'\""],[10381,"'The straight path upon which the Messenger of God ﷺ left us.'"],[10382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah than these ten days.\" It was said, \"Not even Jihad in the cause of Allah?\" He said, \"Not even Jihad in the cause of Allah.\""],[10383,"that we prostrate on seven bones and that we do not gather up our hair or our garment."],[10384,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend.'"],[10385,"'We used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ and we did not perform ablution from wherever our feet trod.'"],[10386,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The dead are tormented in their graves, so much so that even the beasts hear their cries.'"],[10387,"'A Muslim man may do good in the last third of his life at the time of his death, and God will thereby render his zakat complete.'"],[10388,"From ʿAbdullāh, who attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ: 'People are of two kinds: a scholar and a learner, and there is no good in anyone else.'"],[10389,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding His saying, \"He will pay them their rewards in full and give them more from His bounty\": 'Their rewards: He will admit them to Paradise; and He will give them more from His bounty: intercession for those for whom intercession is due, who did good to them in this world.'"],[10390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[10391,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a rider came and made his camel kneel by the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to you from a journey of nine days; I have exhausted my body, stayed awake through my nights, and gone thirsty through my days to ask you about two traits that keep me awake. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What is your name?” He said: I am Zayd al-Khayl. He said: “Rather, you are Zayd al-Khayr.” He said: I ask you about God's sign regarding one whom He wills good for and His sign regarding one whom He does not will good for. I love good and its people and those who act upon it, and if I act upon it I am certain of its reward, and if I miss anything of it I long for it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “God's sign regarding one whom He wills good for and His sign regarding one whom He does not will good for is: if He willed good for you in the Hereafter, He would prepare you for it, then He would not care in which valley you go.”"],[10392,"'Abdullah: divorce is in a period of purity without intercourse."],[10393,"The eighteen men from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who were killed on the day of Badr: God placed their souls in Paradise in green birds that roam freely in Paradise. He said: While they were like that, your Lord looked upon them with a glance and said: “O My servants, what do you desire?” They said: “Our Lord, there is nothing above this.” He said: “O My servants, what do you desire?” They said on the fourth time: “Return our souls to our bodies so that we may be killed as we were killed.”"],[10394,"He said to his family: If you follow what I command you, I will hand over my wealth to you; otherwise I will not. They said: We will follow what you command us. He said: When I die, burn me with fire, then crush my bones thoroughly, and when you see a day of strong wind, climb to the top of a mountain and scatter me in the wind. He said: They did it. 'Abdullah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He fell into God's hand, and He said to him: “What carried you to do what you did?” He said: “Fear of You.” He said: “I have forgiven you.”"],[10395,"A Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: How excellent a community is your community, were it not that they associate equals. He said: “How do they associate equals?” He said: They say, “What God wills and you will.” He said: “He is saying something. Say: What God wills, then you will.”"],[10396,"A Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: How excellent a community is your community, were it not that they associate equals. He said: “How do they associate equals?” He said: They say, “What God wills and you will.” He said: “He is saying something. Say: What God wills, then you will.”"],[10397,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I want to go out to Bahrayn for trade. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Pray two rak'ahs.”"],[10398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Were the religion suspended from the Pleiades, men from the sons of Persia would reach it.”"],[10399,"“Indeed, before the Hour there will be days of turmoil in which knowledge will be lifted and ignorance will descend.”"],[10400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to place his hands between his knees in prayer."],[10401,"He sent to his brothers among the people of Kufa and ordered them to gather so that he could bid them farewell. They gathered in the portico of the mosque. He came to them, greeted them, and ordered them not to dispute about the Qur'an. He informed them that whoever rejects anything of it has rejected all of it. He told them that they used to dispute about it in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ and that they used to recite to him, and he would tell all of them that they were excellent. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Tongues do not differ over it, nor does it wear out from much repetition. That is because the law of Islam in it is one: its prescribed punishments and its obligations. If one of the two readings commanded something the other forbade, the obligations and prescribed punishments would differ in it.” And he mentioned a word: “If I knew that anyone had more knowledge than me of what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ, whom camels could reach, I would go to him until I joined his knowledge to my knowledge. I read seventy suras from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Qur'an was presented to him every year, and I would present it to him and he would tell me that I was excellent, until the year in which he was taken, when it was presented to him twice, then I recited to him. I will not abandon it out of aversion to it.”"],[10402,"«I saw the Prophet ﷺ apply kohl to the eye of ʿAlī ؓ with his saliva.»"],[10403,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ used to breathe three breaths into the vessel, pronouncing the Name of God at each breath and expressing gratitude at the last of them.»"],[10404,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «Among people are keys to the remembrance of God—when they are seen, God is remembered.»"],[10405,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the words of God ﷻ, {For God is his protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous believers}: He said, “The righteous believers are Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ.”"],[10406,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd: This verse was revealed—{Those who purchase a small price with God’s covenant and their oaths}—nothing abrogated it. So any man who seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath is among the people of this verse."],[10407,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «Paradise has eight gates: seven closed and one open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction.»"],[10408,"I performed Hajj with Ibn Masʿud , and saw him doing Rami of the big Jamra (Jamrat-ul-Aqaba) with seven small pebbles, keeping the Kaʿba on his left side and Mina on his right. He then said, \"This is the place where the one on whom Surat-al-Baqara was revealed (i.e. Messenger of Allah ﷺ ) stood.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1749)"],[10409,"Here, I saw the one upon whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed, responding."],[10410,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I did everything with her except intercourse,” meaning with a woman. Then God ﷻ revealed: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds.}"],[10411,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «The believer is not a slanderer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor indecent.»"],[10412,"From the Prophet ﷺ: «Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qurʾān in one night?» They said, “Who could bear that?” He said, «Yes: Say, “He is God, the One.”»"],[10413,"From the Prophet ﷺ: «Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qurʾān in one night?» They said, “Who could bear that?” He said, «Yes: Say, “He is God, the One.”»"],[10414,"From the Prophet ﷺ: «Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qurʾān in one night?» They said, “Who could bear that?” He said, «Yes: Say, “He is God, the One.”»"],[10415,"From the Prophet ﷺ: «Would any of you be unable to recite a third of the Qurʾān in one night?» They said, “Who could bear that?” He said, «Yes: Say, “He is God, the One.”»"],[10416,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?\" They said, \"Who can do that?\" He said, \"Yes: Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[10417,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?\" They said, \"Who can do that?\" He said, \"Yes: Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[10418,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?\" They said, \"Who can do that?\" He said, \"Yes: Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[10419,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?\" They said, \"Who can do that?\" He said, \"Yes: Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[10420,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is any of you unable to recite one third of the Quran in a night?\" They said, \"Who can do that?\" He said, \"Yes: Say, He is Allah, [who is] One.\""],[10421,"From al-tabaqqur.\""],[10422,"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade a gold ring or a gold circle."],[10423,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold rings.\""],[10424,"That Abu Bakr went out, and nothing brought him out but hunger, and that Umar went out, and nothing brought him out but hunger, and that the Prophet ﷺ came out to them, and they told him that nothing had brought them out but hunger. He said, \"Come with us to the house of a man from the Ansar called Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan.\" When he was not at home—he had gone to fetch water—the woman welcomed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his two companions and spread something for them, and they sat on it. The Prophet ﷺ asked her, \"Where has Abu al-Haytham gone?\" She said, \"He has gone to fetch fresh water for us.\" He did not wait long before he came with a water-skin containing water and hung it up. He wanted to slaughter a sheep for them, but it was as if the Prophet ﷺ disliked that for them. So he slaughtered a young she-goat for them. Then he went off and came with clusters of dates. They ate of that meat, unripe dates, and ripe dates, and drank from the water. One of the two—either Abu Bakr or Umar—said, \"This is part of the bliss about which we will be asked.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The believer is not reproached for anything he obtains in this world; only the disbeliever is reproached.\""],[10425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are a man who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, or a man who leads people astray without knowledge, or an image-maker who makes images.\""],[10426,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: \"They have diminished it, may Allah diminish them. By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years and he never diminished it by even one.\""],[10427,"\"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ that he used to say in the sermon of necessity, 'Praise be to Allah, we seek His help and ask for His forgiveness. We seek refuge in Allah from the evil within ourselves. Whoever Allah guides, there is no one who can lead him astray, and whoever He leads astray, there is no guide for him. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. Whoever obeys Allah and His messenger has been guided, and whoever disobeys them harms only themselves. Allah will not be harmed by anyone.'\""],[10428,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Beware of the sins that are considered insignificant, for they gather against a man until they destroy him. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave an example for them: like a man in a desolate land who was preparing food for a group. One man began bringing a stick and another man began bringing a stick until they gathered a great heap and lit a fire, and cooked what was in it.\""],[10429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Bathing on Friday is sunnah.\""],[10430,"\"That it be for me is dearer than what the sun has risen upon.\" He stood before the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr and said: \"We do not say to you as the people of Musa said, 'So go, you and your Lord'\" - the verse - \"but we will fight on your right and on your left.\" And I saw the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, its features beaming."],[10431,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Indeed, incantations, amulets, and love charms are shirk.\""],[10432,"A man said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, this is the camel we used to hear about.\" He said: \"Then where is the she-camel with the blaze?\""],[10433,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah and Hudhayfah when a woman and a man passed by them on a camel, their faces turned away. One of them said to his companion: \"This is the one we used to talk about.\" He said: \"No, with that one there is the she-camel with the blaze.\""],[10434,"Some people came to the Prophet of God ﷺ with their companion and said: \"O Prophet of God, our companion here has been ruined by shyness.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, shyness is part of the laws of Islam, and obscenity is from a person's baseness.\""],[10435,"My father had stopped praying with us. I said: \"What is the matter with you that you have stopped praying with us?\" He said: \"You make it too light.\" I said: \"What about the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: 'Among you are the old, the weak, and those with needs'?\" He said: \"I heard 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that.\" Then he prayed three times as much as you pray."],[10436,"\"About the private parts of women.\""],[10437,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People among the Muslims who were punished in the Fire will certainly enter Paradise by God's mercy and the intercession of the intercessors.\""],[10438,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ was not imagined by anyone who saw him.\""],[10439,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, God ﷻ has not made anything sacred except that He knew someone among you would come to know of it. Verily, I am holding you by your waists to keep you from tumbling into the Fire as moths and flies tumble.\""],[10440,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no man who is among a people who disobey God while they are more numerous and stronger than him, then they flatter regarding his affair, except that God punishes them.\""],[10441,"Intercession will continue for people as they are coming out of the Fire, until even Iblis, the most deceitful, will stretch his neck hoping that it may reach him."],[10442,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not ever seek to please anyone by displeasing Allah, and do not praise anyone for a favor that is from Allah, and do not blame anyone for what Allah has not given you. For the provision of Allah is not brought to you by the greed of a greedy person, nor is it repelled from you by the dislike of one who dislikes it. And indeed Allah, exalted is He, in His justice and fairness placed ease and joy in contentment and certainty, and placed worry and grief in displeasure.\""],[10443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of the Fire with the most severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection are one who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, a tyrannical imam, and these image-makers.\""],[10444,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wrongdoing is greatest? He said: \"A cubit of land that a believer diminishes from his brother's right, not a single pebble of it except that he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first of this ummah are its best, and the last of them are its worst, differing and divided. So whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then let his death come to him while he treats people as he would love to be treated.\""],[10446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the riding beast of one of you runs loose in a desert land, let him call: 'O servants of Allah, restrain it for me! O servants of Allah, restrain it for me! For indeed Allah has in the earth someone present who will restrain it for you.'\""],[10447,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no night talk except for one who is praying or for a traveler.\""],[10448,"A group of the nobles of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some Muslims, including Suhayb and Khabbab, were with him. They said: \"O Muhammad, are these the ones Allah has favored from among us? If you were to drive these away, we would follow you.\" Then Allah, glorified and exalted, revealed: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face} up to His saying: {Is not Allah most knowing of the thankful?}"],[10449,"\"Eat, for this is a day that used to be fasted before Ramadan was revealed; then Ramadan was revealed and this day was abandoned.\""],[10450,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"There is none among you but has been assigned a companion from the jinn.\" It was asked, \"Even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Even me. However, Allah has helped me against him, so he has embraced Islam and does not command me except with good.\""],[10451,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Dhuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha; so it was said to him (why), and he said: \"I did it so that my ummah may not be in hardship.\""],[10452,"He said to me: \"Come closer,\" so he brought me close until he seated me on his carpet, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Parents will have a debt owed to them by their child, and on the Day of Resurrection they will cling to him and he will say: I am your child; then they would wish, or they will desire, that he had been more than that.\""],[10453,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Being killed in the cause of Allah expiates all sins\" or he said \"everything except the trust. And the trust is in prayer, the trust is in fasting, and the trust is in speech; but the most severe of that is deposits.\" Sharik said: ʿAyyash al-ʿAmiri narrated to me from Zadhan from ʿAbdullah from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[10454,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) has angels on the earth who roam about, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10455,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) has angels who roam about on the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10456,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God has angels who roam about on the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me and said: “O Ibn Masʿūd!” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said it three times: “Do you know which of the bonds of faith is firmest?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the firmest bond of Islam is allegiance for God: loving for His sake and hating for His sake.”"],[10458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me and said: “O Ibn Masʿūd!” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said it three times: “Do you know which of the bonds of faith is firmest?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the firmest bond of Islam is allegiance for God: loving for His sake and hating for His sake.”"],[10459,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to me and said: “O Ibn Masʿūd!” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said it three times: “Do you know which of the bonds of faith is firmest?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the firmest bond of Islam is allegiance for God: loving for His sake and hating for His sake.”"],[10460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Dreams are glad tidings from Allah, and they are part of Prophet-hood, seventy parts of it. Verily, this fire of yours [in the light of the sun] is one of seventy parts of the heat of Hell.\" And he also said, \"Whoever goes to the mosque and waits for the prayer, he is considered to be in prayer as long as he does not commit any impurity. And whoever observes prayer after the prayer, he is considered to be in prayer as long as he does not commit any impurity.\""],[10461,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, and no one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride.” A man said: “O Messenger of God, I like my garment to be clean, my head to be oiled, my sandal strap to be new”—and he mentioned things, until he mentioned the whip's loop—“is that from pride, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No, that is beauty. Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) is beautiful and loves beauty. But pride is to disregard the truth and look down on people.”"],[10462,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he allotted dwellings, and he allotted to Ibn Masʿūd among those he allotted. His companions said to him: “O Messenger of God, turn him away from us.” He said: “Why then did God send me? Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) does not sanctify a community that does not give its weak ones their right.”"],[10463,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of Conquest, and around the Kaʿbah there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began piercing them and saying: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is ever vanishing.”"],[10464,"He heard ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd say: “I did not fast with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine days more often than I fasted with him thirty.”"],[10465,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever commits a sin and then regrets it, that is its expiation.”"],[10466,"“Indeed, usury, even if it becomes abundant, its outcome leads to scarcity.”"],[10467,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Riba does not become widespread except that its outcome leads to scarcity.”"],[10468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A true, righteous dream is one of seventy-six parts of prophethood.”"],[10469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is sufficient for a person, when he sees an evil that he is unable to change, that Allah knows that he disapproves of it.”"],[10470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant may be born a believer, live as a believer, and die a disbeliever; and a servant may be born a disbeliever, live as a disbeliever, and die a believer. A servant may act for a period of his life with felicity, then what is written for him overtakes him and he dies wretched; and a servant may act for a period of his life with wretchedness, then what is written for him overtakes him and he dies happy.”"],[10471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created Yahya b. Zakariyya in his mother’s womb a believer, and created Pharaoh in his mother’s womb a disbeliever.”"],[10472,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are no two Muslims except that between them is a veil from Allah. When one of them says to his companion something offensive, he tears his veil, and when he says, ‘O disbeliever,’ then one of them has disbelieved.”"],[10473,"I used to greet the Prophet ﷺ and he would return my greeting, but I greeted him and he did not return it. I said: I used to greet you and you would return my greeting, but I greeted you and you did not return it. He said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings about whatever He wills in His command.”"],[10474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed your companion is the Khalil of Allah,” meaning himself ﷺ."],[10475,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he did not see Jibril in his true form except twice. He said: As for one time, he asked him to show himself in his true form, so he showed himself to him, and he came filling the horizon. As for the second, he was with him when he ascended, regarding His saying: “Then he drew near and came down, and was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer, and He revealed to His servant what He revealed” [53:8–10]. When Jibril sensed his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, he returned to his form, and that is His saying: “And he certainly saw him in another descent at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, near which is the Garden of Refuge… He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord” [53:13–18]. He said: “The creation of Jibril.”"],[10476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will guard us tonight?” Abdullah said: I said, “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will sleep.” Then he repeated: “Who will guard us tonight?” I said, “I will,” until he repeated it three times, and I said, “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then you.” So I guarded them until near dawn, when the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ overtook me, “You will sleep,” and I slept. Nothing woke us except the heat of the sun on our backs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and performed ablution as he used to do and prayed the two rak‘ahs of Fajr, then led us in the Fajr prayer. When he finished, he said: “If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had willed that you not sleep through it, you would not have slept, but He willed it to be—or he said, it will be—for those after you. So this is for anyone who sleeps or forgets.” Then the Prophet’s she-camel and the people’s camels scattered. The people went out searching for them and brought back their camels except the Prophet’s she-camel. Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Take this direction.” I took the direction he indicated and found its halter tangled around a tree. By Allah, nothing could have untied it except a hand. He said: I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I found its halter tangled around a tree, nothing could have untied it except a hand. He said: And upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was revealed: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [48:1]."],[10477,"I heard Abdullah b. Mas‘ud say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram from al-Hudaybiyyah. We traveled at night and stopped in soft sandy ground. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who will guard us?” Bilal said: “I will.” He said: “Then you will sleep.” He said: They slept until the sun rose, and so-and-so and so-and-so woke up, among them Umar, but the Prophet ﷺ did not wake. Someone said: “Dismount,” and the Prophet ﷺ woke up and said: “Do as you used to do.” When they did, he said: “Thus is it for anyone among you who sleeps or forgets.”"],[10478,"“With us on the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose, there were two camel-drivers.”"],[10479,"From the Prophet ﷺ: When he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he would say, “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling whatever is between them and filling whatever You will after that—Lord of praise and Lord of majesty and glory. There is none to withhold what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against You.”"],[10480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no faith for him who has no trustworthiness, and there is no religion for him who has no covenant. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the religion of a servant will not be correct until his tongue is correct, and his tongue will not be correct until his heart is correct. And he will not enter Paradise who does not feel secure from his neighbor's harms.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the harms?\" He said, \"His cheating and his oppression. And whatever man acquires wealth from unlawful sources and then he spends from it, it will not be blessed for him, and if he gives charity, it will not be accepted from him. And what remains will only increase him in the Fire. Verily, the impure does not remove the impure, but rather the pure removes the impure.\""],[10481,"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? He replied, \"Like the flowing water, yes.\""],[10482,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by his companions one day and said to them, “Do you know what your Lord, Mighty and Sublime, is saying?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said it three times. He said, “By My might and My majesty, no servant performs it at its proper time except that I enter him into Paradise, and whoever performs it other than at its proper time, if I will I have mercy on him, and if I will I punish him.”"],[10483,"“From which people is the man?” I said, “A man from the people of Basra.” He said, “From which tribe?” I said, “From this clan of Banu Saʿd.” He said to me, “O Saʿdi, I will narrate to you a hadith about you which I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, shall I not guide you to a people of great wealth and great strength, from whom you may take abundant property—or he said, much property?’ He said, ‘Who are they?’ He said, ‘They are this clan of Banu Saʿd from the people of the sands.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Indeed Banu Saʿd have a great share with Allah.’ Ask, O Saʿdi.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, is there any knowledge by which the Hour is known?” He was reclining, and he sat up straight and said, “O Saʿdi, you have asked me about something I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, is there any knowledge by which the Hour is known?’ He said to me, ‘O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed the Hour has signs, and indeed the Hour has portents. Indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the child becomes a source of anger, and that the rain becomes scorching heat, and that the wicked overflow in abundance. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the liar is believed and the truthful is rejected. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the treacherous is entrusted and the trustworthy is betrayed. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that close relatives sever ties and wombs are cut off. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that every tribe is ruled by its hypocrites and every market by its wicked. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mosques are adorned and hearts are ruined. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that a believer in his tribe is more humiliated than a stray sheep. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that men suffice with men and women with women. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mosques become crowded and pulpits are raised. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the ruins of the world are built up and its inhabited places are ruined. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that musical instruments appear and wine is drunk. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is the drinking of wine. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour are the police, the slanderers, and the backbiters. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that children born of fornication become many.’” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, while they are Muslims?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, while the Qur’an is among them?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, how can that be?” He said, “A time will come upon people when a man divorces his wife, then denies her divorce and remains upon her private part, so the two of them are fornicators as long as they remain.”"],[10484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Souls are troops assembled together; those that recognized one another came together, and those that disavowed one another differed.”"],[10485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Let not the call of Bilal prevent any of you from his pre-dawn meal, for he only calls the adhan so that your sleeper may wake, and your standing one may return, and the dawn appears like this.”"],[10486,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever drags his garments out of pride, Allah will not look at him, neither in what is lawful nor in what is unlawful.” This Ismaʿil is Ibn Abi Khalid, and Allah knows best."],[10487,"A man kissed a woman and then went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have done such and such.\" So Allah revealed the verse, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove the evil deeds.\" The man asked, \"Is it for me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"No, it is for my Ummah (nation).\""],[10488,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a man who performs ghusl from janabah and water misses part of his body. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He should wash that place, then pray.”"],[10489,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Shall I not inform you of those for whom the Fire is forbidden?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Every gentle, soft, near, and easy person.”"],[10490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you is invited to a meal, let him respond. If he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him supplicate for blessing.”"],[10491,"I argued with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me, so I came to ʿImran b. al-Husayn al-Khuzaʿi, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said, “O Abu Nujayd, I argued with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me. Is there a hadith you can narrate to me, perhaps Allah will benefit me by it?” He said, “Perhaps if I narrate a hadith to you, you will cover your ears as if you did not hear it.” I said, “I came only for that.” He said, “If Allah were to punish the people of the heavens and the people of the earth, He would punish them and He would not be unjust; and if He were to admit them into His mercy, His mercy would be more expansive for them than their sins. It is as Allah, Mighty and Sublime, said: {He punishes whom He wills and forgives whom He wills}. Whoever is punished, it is the truth; and whoever is shown mercy, it is the truth. If the mountains were gold or silver for one of you and he spent them in the path of Allah, then did not believe in qadar, its good and its evil, that would not benefit him.” Then I came to ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud and asked him. ʿAbd Allah said to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, “O Abu al-Mundhir, narrate to him.” Ubayy said, “O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥman, narrate to him.” So Ibn Masʿud narrated the like of the hadith of ʿImran b. Husayn from the Prophet ﷺ, and upon his family, with abundant, good, blessed peace."],[10492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I hope that Allah will brighten our faces with a boy,” and she gave birth to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas."],[10493,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: When the Prophet ﷺ and his family were in the mountain pass, my father came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, I think Umm al-Fadl has conceived.” He said, “Perhaps Allah will delight our eyes from her with a boy.” I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ while I was in my swaddling cloth, and he chewed and gave me from his mouth. Mujahid said, “We do not know anyone who was given tahnik with the saliva of prophethood other than him.”"],[10494,"I was born three years before the Hijrah, while the Prophet ﷺ was still alive, and I was thirteen years old."],[10495,"Abdullah ibn Abbas died in the year seventy-eight."],[10496,"I heard Abu Nuʿaym say, \"Ibn ʿAbbas died in the year sixty-eight.\""],[10497,"Ibn ʿAbbas was tall, tinged with yellowness, corpulent, handsome, with a beautiful face, and he had two braids."],[10498,"I saw Ibn ʿAbbas and he had a jumma (hair reaching the shoulders)."],[10499,"I saw Ibn ʿAbbas during the days of Mina with long hair, wearing a waist-wrapper that had some trailing, and over it a yellow cloak."],[10500,"I witnessed Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya when Ibn ʿAbbas died in al-Taʾif. He said the takbir over him four times, took him from the qibla side when he placed him in the grave, and set up a tent over him for three days."],[10501,"I witnessed the death of Ibn ʿAbbas in al-Taʾif. Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya took charge of him, said the takbir over him four times, placed him in the grave from the side of his feet, and set up a tent over him."],[10502,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when I was ten years old."],[10503,"\"I recited the muhkam (i.e., the mufassal) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" and he was then twelve years old."],[10504,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I had recited the muhkam of the Qurʾan.\" Shuʿba said: I asked Abu Bishr, \"What is the muhkam?\" He said, \"The mufassal.\""],[10505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was fifteen years old, and I had been circumcised."],[10506,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while I was still a young boy.\""],[10507,"While I was passing by, and the Prophet ﷺ was in the Hijr, he said, \"O Umm al-Fadl.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"You are pregnant with a boy.\" She said, \"How, when Quraysh have sworn that women will not give birth?\" He said, \"It is as I tell you. When you give birth to him, bring him to me.\" When she gave birth to him, she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he named him ʿAbd Allah, and he fed him from his saliva. Then he said, \"Take him away, and you will surely find him to be clever.\" She said: I went to al-ʿAbbas and told him, and he dressed and then came to the Prophet ﷺ. He was a handsome man, tall in stature. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he stood up to him, kissed him between the eyes, then seated him on his right, and then said, \"This is my uncle, so whoever wishes may boast of his uncle to him.\" Al-ʿAbbas said some words: \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Why should I not say it, when you are my uncle and the remnant of my forefathers, and the uncle is a father?\""],[10508,"Ibn ʿAbbas died in al-Taʾif, and I attended his funeral. A white bird came, the like of which had not been seen, and entered his bier, then was not seen leaving it. When he was buried, this verse was recited at the edge of the grave, and we did not know who recited it: \"O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing, and enter among My servants and enter My Paradise.\""],[10509,"It is said to be a crane [ghurnūq] until it entered into the interior of the bier and was not seen."],[10510,"It is said to be a crane [ghurnūq], then it entered into the bier and was not seen after that."],[10511,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and with the Prophet ﷺ there was a man confiding privately with him, and he seemed to be turning away from my father. So we left him, and my father said, “Did you not see your cousin seeming to turn away from me?” I said, “O my father, there was a man with him confiding privately with him.” He said, “Was there anyone with him?” I said, “Yes.” So we went back, and he said, “O Messenger of God, I said to ʿAbd Allāh such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such. Was there anyone with you?” He said, “Yes. Did you see him, O ʿAbd Allāh?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “That was Gabriel ﷺ ; he is the one who occupied me from you.”"],[10512,"The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand on the head of ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās and said, “O God, grant him wisdom and teach him interpretation.” He placed his hand on his chest, and ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās felt its coolness in his back. Then he said, “O God, fill his interior with judgment and knowledge.” So he never felt uneasy in himself about asking anyone among the people, and he remained the ḥabr (learned man) of this community until God took him to Himself."],[10513,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was wearing white clothes, and he was confiding privately with Diḥya b. Khalīfa al-Kalbī, who was Gabriel ﷺ , and I did not know. I did not greet them. Gabriel said, “O Muḥammad, who is this?” He said, “This is my cousin, this is Ibn ʿAbbās.” He said, “How intensely white his clothes are! Indeed, his descendants will prevail after him. If he had greeted us, we would have returned his greeting.” When I returned, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, “O Ibn ʿAbbās, what prevented you from greeting?” I said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, I saw you confiding privately with Diḥya b. Khalīfa, and I disliked interrupting your private conversation.” He said, “And you saw him?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, your sight will go and will be restored to you at your death.” ʿIkrima said: When Ibn ʿAbbās died and was placed on his bier, a bird of intense radiance came and entered into his shrouds. They wanted to unfold his shrouds, but ʿIkrima said, “What are you doing? This is the glad tidings of the Messenger of God ﷺ that he told him.” When he was placed in his grave, he was met with words that were heard by those at the edge of his grave: {O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing, and enter among My servants and enter My garden}."],[10514,"I was in the house of Maymūna bt. al-Ḥārith, and I placed ablution water for the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Who placed this?” Maymūna said, “ʿAbd Allāh placed it.” He said, “O God, teach him interpretation and give him understanding in religion.”"],[10515,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced me and said, “O God, teach him wisdom.”"],[10516,"Muʿāwiya said to him, “What do you say about Abū Bakr?” He said, “May God have mercy on Abū Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Qurʾān, remote from inclination, heedless of indecency, forbidding the wrong, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, turning away from destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly desires, resolute upon justice for creation, commanding the good, patient toward it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God in mornings and evenings, overpowering his soul toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, sufficiency, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, carefulness, abstemiousness, and competence. May God cause those who slander him to be followed by curses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10517,"Muʿāwiya said to him, “What do you say about Abū Bakr?” He said, “May God have mercy on Abū Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Qurʾān, remote from inclination, heedless of indecency, forbidding the wrong, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, turning away from destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly desires, resolute upon justice for creation, commanding the good, patient toward it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God in mornings and evenings, overpowering his soul toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, sufficiency, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, carefulness, abstemiousness, and competence. May God cause those who slander him to be followed by curses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10518,"Muʿāwiya said to him, “What do you say about Abū Bakr?” He said, “May God have mercy on Abū Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Qurʾān, remote from inclination, heedless of indecency, forbidding the wrong, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, turning away from destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly desires, resolute upon justice for creation, commanding the good, patient toward it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God in mornings and evenings, overpowering his soul toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, sufficiency, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, carefulness, abstemiousness, and competence. May God cause those who slander him to be followed by curses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10519,"Muʿāwiya said to him, “What do you say about Abū Bakr?” He said, “May God have mercy on Abū Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Qurʾān, remote from inclination, heedless of indecency, forbidding the wrong, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, turning away from destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly desires, resolute upon justice for creation, commanding the good, patient toward it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God in mornings and evenings, overpowering his soul toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, sufficiency, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, carefulness, abstemiousness, and competence. May God cause those who slander him to be followed by curses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10520,"Muʿāwiya said to him, “What do you say about Abū Bakr?” He said, “May God have mercy on Abū Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Qurʾān, remote from inclination, heedless of indecency, forbidding the wrong, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, turning away from destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly desires, resolute upon justice for creation, commanding the good, patient toward it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God in mornings and evenings, overpowering his soul toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, sufficiency, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, carefulness, abstemiousness, and competence. May God cause those who slander him to be followed by curses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10521,"What do you say about Abu Bakr?\" He said, \"May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr. By Allah, he was a devoted follower of the Quran, distant from desires, free from indecency, forbidding evil, knowledgeable in religion, fearing Allah, abstaining from destructive temptations, standing in prayer at night, fasting during the day, detached from worldly possessions, resolute in upholding justice, commanding good, patient in hardship, grateful in all situations, remembering Allah in the morning and evening, conquering his own desires in favor of others, showing righteousness, guarding his chastity, practicing asceticism, contentment, sufficiency. Allah has honored and elevated his companions with piety, contentment, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, protection, asceticism, sufficiency. Allah has avenged those who curse him until the Day of Judgment.\""],[10522,"Mu'awiya said to him: 'What do you say about Abu Bakr?' He said: 'May God have mercy on Abu Bakr. By God, he was a reciter of the Quran, distant from deviation, heedless of obscenity, a forbidder of wrongdoing, knowledgeable of his religion, fearful of God, avoiding destructive things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his worldly concerns, resolute upon justice for all creation, enjoining good, patient in it, thankful in all circumstances, remembering God morning and evening, and compelling himself toward what is beneficial. He surpassed and excelled his companions in piety, contentment, asceticism, chastity, righteousness, prudence, abstinence, and competence. May God inflict curses until the Day of Resurrection upon anyone who slanders him.'"],[10524,"And he said: 'If any prophethood remained among them, he would inform me of what I ask them about.' So he wrote to him asking about the galaxy, the rainbow, and the place the sun had not touched except for one hour. When the letter and messenger reached Mu'awiya, he said: 'This is something I never thought I would be asked about until this day of mine. Who is this for?' It was said: 'Ibn Abbas.' So Mu'awiya folded up Heraclius' letter and sent it to Ibn Abbas. Ibn Abbas wrote back to him: 'The rainbow is a safeguard for the people of the earth from drowning. The galaxy is the gate of the sky through which it will split open. As for the place the sun had not touched except for one hour of the day, it is the sea that was parted for the Children of Israel.'"],[10525,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to a man: 'Come, let us learn from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask them, for they are many.' He said: 'How strange, by God, O Ibn Abbas! Do you think people will need you when among the people are those you see from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' So I left that and devoted myself to asking and seeking out the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I heard of a man who had a hadith he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would go to him and find him taking a midday nap. I would use my cloak as a pillow at his door while the wind blew dust onto my face until he came out to me. When he saw me he would say: 'O cousin of the Messenger of Allah, what is the matter?' I would say: 'A hadith has reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I wanted to hear it from you.' He would say: 'Why did you not send for me so that I could come to you?' I would say: 'I was more deserving of coming to you.' Then that man would see me when the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away and people needed me, and he would say: 'You were more deserving than me.'"],[10526,"I sat with seventy or eighty individuals from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Not one of them differed with Ibn Abbas and then met him except that he said: 'The saying is as you said' or 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[10527,"The man is not lying, but rather disagreeing. Ibn Abbas said, \"So what do you say about what happened in yourself?\" And the man said to him, \"May Allah tell you, He says, 'So there will be no blood relations among them on that day, nor will they ask about one another.'\" And he said in another verse, \"And some of them will come to others questioning.\" And he said in another verse, \"They do not conceal from Allah anything.\" And he said in another verse, \"And Allah is our Lord, we have not associated anything with Him.\" They have concealed in this verse and in His saying, \"He constructed the heavens and extended its scope and perfected it and created the night and formed the light and spread the earth.\" So He mentioned in this verse the creation of the heavens before the creation of the earth, then He said in this other verse, \"Do you deny the One who created the earth in two days and make for Him equals? That is the Lord of the worlds. And He placed on it firmly set mountains over its surface and blessed it and determined therein its [creatures'] sustenance in four days without distinction - for [the information] of those who ask. Then He directed Himself to the heaven while it was smoke and said to it and to the earth, 'Come into being, willingly or by compulsion.' They said, 'We have come willingly.'\" So He mentioned in this verse the creation of the earth before the creation of the heavens, \"And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\" \"And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\" \"And Allah is Hearing and Seeing.\" And it is as if it was then that Ibn Abbas said, \"Tell me what is in yourself.\" The questioner said, \"If you inform me about this, it is enough for me.\" And Ibn Abbas said, \"His saying, 'So there will be no blood relations among them on that day, nor will they ask about one another.' This is in the first blowing of the trumpet, the statues will be blown off and those in the heavens and on the earth except whoever Allah wills.\" \"So there will be no blood relations among them at that time, nor will they ask about one another. Then when it is in the second blowing of the trumpet, they will rise.\" \"So as for His saying, 'And Allah is our"],[10528,"Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us in the year two hundred and twenty-three, saying: Hayyan b. Ubayd Allah b. Zuhayr al-Misri, Abu Zuhayr, narrated to us sixty years ago, saying: I asked al-Dahhak b. Muzahim about His saying: {No disaster strikes upon the earth or among yourselves except that it is in a register before We bring it into being; indeed that, for God, is easy}, and about His saying: {Indeed We were copying what you used to do}, and about His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}. He said: Ibn Abbas said: God, exalted is He, created the Throne and settled upon it. Then He created the Pen and commanded it to flow by His permission, and He magnified the Pen to the extent of what is between heaven and earth. The Pen said: 'With what, O Lord, shall I flow?' He said: 'With what I am creating, whether in My creation of a drop, a plant, a soul, or a trace—meaning by that deed, provision, or term.' So the Pen flowed with what is to be until the Day of Resurrection, and God recorded it in the hidden Book with Him beneath the Throne. As for His saying: {Indeed We were copying what you used to do}, God entrusted angels who copy from that Book every year in Ramadan on the Night of Decree what will occur on earth from one event until the like of it in the coming year. They compare it with the guardian angels over the servants every Thursday evening, and they find what the guardians have raised to match what is in their Book, with no addition or subtraction. As for His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}, God created for everything what suits it from His creation and what benefits it from His provision. He created the camel with a form that is not suitable for anything from His creation other than it among the animals. Likewise is every thing from His creatures. He created for the beasts of the land and its birds from provision what benefits them on land, and He created for the beasts of the sea and its birds from provision what benefits them in the sea. That is His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}."],[10529,"Do you find the five prayers in the Book of God? He said: 'Yes.' He recited to him: {So glory be to God when you reach the evening} — that is Maghrib; {and when you reach the morning} — that is Subh; {and in the afternoon} — that is Asr; {and when you reach midday} — he said: that is Zuhr; {and after the Isha prayer} — he said: that is the Isha prayer."],[10530,"A man who speaks about what he has no knowledge of, and a man who conceals knowledge that he has.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth, O Ibn Abbas. I came to ask you.' He said: 'Ask, O Ibn al-Azraq.' He said: 'Tell me about the saying of God, exalted is He: {A flame of fire will be sent upon you both}. What is shuwaz?' He said: 'A flame without smoke.' He said: 'Did the Arabs know that before the Book was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes. Did you not hear the saying of Umayya b. Abi al-Salt?'"],[10531,"When the Haruriyya seceded and were in a separate abode on their own, I said to Ali: 'O Commander of the Faithful, delay the prayer a little so that perhaps I may go to these people and speak with them.' He said: 'I fear them for you.' I said: 'Not at all, if God wills.' So I put on the best Yemeni garment I could, then entered upon them while they were resting during midday. I entered upon a people more intense in worship than any I had ever seen. Their hands were like the calloused knees of camels, and their faces were marked from the traces of prostration. I entered and they said: 'Welcome, O Ibn Abbas. What brings you?' I said: 'I have come to tell you about the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Revelation came down while they were more knowledgeable of its interpretation.' Some of them said: 'Do not speak to him,' while others said: 'We will certainly speak with him.' I said: 'Tell me what you hold against the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his son-in-law, the first to believe in him, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who were with him?' They said: 'We hold three things against him.' I said: 'What are they?' They said: 'The first is that he appointed men as arbiters in the religion of God, while God has said: {Judgment belongs to none but God}.' I said: 'And what else?' They said: 'He fought but did not take captives or war spoils. If they were disbelievers, their wealth would be lawful to him; and if they were believers, their blood would be forbidden to him.' I said: 'And what else?' They said: 'He erased his own title as Commander of the Faithful. If he is not the Commander of the Faithful, then he is the commander of the disbelievers.' I said: 'Tell me, if I recite to you from the clear Book of God and narrate to you from the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ that which you cannot deny, will you return?' They said: 'Yes.' I said: 'As for your saying that he appointed men as arbiters in the religion of God, God says: {O you who believe, do not kill game while you are in the state of ihram} up to His saying: {two just men among you shall judge it}. And He said about a woman and her husband: {And if you fear a breach between them, send an arbitrator from his people and an arbitrator from her people}. I adjure you by God: is the judgment of men in the sparing of their blood and their lives and the rectification of their relations more worthy, or in a rabbit whose value is a quarter of a dirham?' They said: 'O God, in the sparing of their blood and the rectification of their relations.' He said: 'Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' 'As for your saying that he fought but did not take captives or war spoils: would you take your mother captive and make lawful from her what you make lawful from other women? If you claim she is not your mother, then you have disbelieved and left Islam. God, exalted is He, says: {The Prophet is closer to the believers than their own selves, and his wives are their mothers}. So you are wavering between two errors. Choose whichever you wish. Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' 'As for your saying that he erased his own title as Commander of the Faithful: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Quraysh on the day of Hudaybiyya to write a document between him and them. He said: \"Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has agreed upon.\" They said: \"By God, if we knew that you were the Messenger of God, we would not have turned you away from the House nor fought you. But write: Muhammad b. Abd Allah.\" He said: \"By God, I am indeed the Messenger of God even if you deny me. Write, O Ali, Muhammad b. Abd Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was superior to Ali. Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' Then twenty thousand of them returned, and four thousand remained and were killed."],[10532,"If you fear that he may overpower you, then say: 'God is greater, God is greater than all His creation. God is mightier than what I fear and am wary of. I seek refuge in God, besides whom there is no deity, the Holder of the seven heavens lest they fall upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of Your servant so-and-so and his soldiers and followers from jinn and mankind. O my God, be for me a protector from their evil. Great is Your praise, mighty is Your protection, blessed is Your name, and there is no deity other than You.' Three times."],[10533,"Ibn Abbas used to say: 'O Allah, I ask You by the light of Your Face, by which the heavens and the earth are illuminated, that You place me in Your fortress, Your protection, Your refuge, and under Your care.'"],[10534,"I said to Ibn Abbas: 'Do you know what you have done and what you have ruled? Your fatwa has been carried far and wide by the riders, and poets have spoken about it.' He said: 'And what did they say?' I said: 'They said...'"],[10535,"I saw on Ibn Abbas's bed—or in Ibn Abbas's gathering—a cushion of silk."],[10536,"Salamah b. Nubayt al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Muzāḥim narrated to us, saying: Ibn ʿAbbās passed by a storyteller and kicked him with his foot, saying: “Do you know the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “And what is the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “You do not know the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “No.” He said: “You have perished and caused others to perish.”"],[10537,"The young man asked you if he can kiss while he is fasting, and you said no. Then he asked you if he can be kissed while he is fasting, and you said yes. So how can it be permissible for him to do what is forbidden for me, while we are on the same religion? Ibn Abbas said to him, \"The veins of the testicles are connected to the nose. When the nose smells something, the male reproductive organ moves, and when it moves, it calls for something bigger. And the elder one is in control of his desires, while the other person has lost his vision and has a woman behind him.\" It was said to Ibn Abbas, \"O Ibn Abbas, there is a woman behind you.\" He said, \"Woe to you! What a bad company you have!\""],[10538,"That with me there was a man from the people of qadar (fatalism/denial of divine decree), so I struck his head. They said: “And why that?” He said: “Because Allah created a preserved tablet of a white pearl; its covers are of red ruby, its pen is light, its writing is light, and its width is what is between heaven and earth. He looks into it every day three hundred and sixty looks; with each look He creates, gives life, honours, humiliates, and does whatever He wills.”"],[10539,"When Allah ﷻ sent Mūsā ﷺ and revealed to him the Torah, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” So Mūsā ﷺ desisted. Then when Allah ﷻ sent ʿUzayr and revealed to him the Torah after He had raised it from the Children of Israel, until some said that he was the son of Allah, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” But his soul refused until he asked again, saying: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” But his soul refused until he asked again. He said: “Can you tie up a bundle of the sun?” He said: “No.” He said: “Can you bring a measure of wind?” He said: “No.” He said: “Can you bring a mithqāl of light?” He said: “No. Can you bring a qīrāṭ of light?” He said: “No.” He said: “Thus you are not able to do what you asked about. I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked. Indeed, I will not make your punishment except that I erase your name from the prophets, so you will not be mentioned among them.” So He erased his name from the prophets, and he is not mentioned among them, though he is a prophet. Then when Allah sent ʿĪsā ﷺ , and he saw his station with his Lord, and He taught him the Book, the wisdom, the Torah, and the Gospel, and he healed the blind and the leper, and raised the dead, and informed them of what they ate and what they stored in their houses, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked. And you are My servant, My messenger, and My word which I cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Me. I created you from dust, then said to you ‘Be,’ and you were. If you do not desist, I will surely do to you as I did to your companion before you. I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” So ʿĪsā ﷺ gathered his followers and said: “Divine decree is the secret of Allah, so do not burden yourselves with it.”"],[10540,"“I found that the most correct of people concerning it in speech is the most ignorant of them of it, and the weakest of them concerning it in speech is the most knowledgeable of them of it. And I found the one who looks into it like one who looks into the rays of the sun: the more he increases his looking into it, the more his sight increases in bewilderment.”"],[10541,"“The mosques are the houses of Allah on earth, shining for the inhabitants of heaven just as the stars of heaven shine for the inhabitants of the earth.”"],[10542,"May Allah bless you, I said to Pharaoh, and may he bless you too, and Pharaoh has died."],[10543,"\"Whenever a year comes to mankind, they introduce innovations in it and abandon the traditions until innovations thrive and traditions die.\""],[10544,"That there is not on earth a pomegranate that is pollinated except with a grain from the grains of Paradise, and perhaps it is this one.”"],[10545,"“Whoever wears yellow sandals will remain in happiness as long as he wears them.”"],[10546,"I will tell you a discourse that is neither secret nor open. When there happened concerning this man what happened—meaning ʿUthmān—I said to ʿAlī: “Withdraw; for if you were in a hole, you would be sought until you are brought out.” But he disobeyed me. By Allah, Muʿāwiyah will surely rule over you, and that is because Allah ﷻ says: {And whoever is killed unjustly, We have given his heir authority, so let him not exceed in killing; indeed he is helped}. And the Quraysh will surely make you follow the way of Persia and Rome, and the Christians, the Jews, and the Magians will surely wish for you. So whoever among you then holds to what he knows will be saved, and whoever leaves it—and you will leave it—you will be like a generation among the generations that perished.”"],[10547,"That he was in the house of Maymūnah, and he placed water for the Prophet ﷺ's purification. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who placed it?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “I did.” So he struck me on my shoulder and said: “O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation.”"],[10548,"“I saw Jibrīl twice, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me for wisdom twice.”"],[10549,"ʿUmar used to ask me along with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf said to him: “You ask him?” He said: “He is from where you know.” So he asked them about {When the help of Allah comes and the victory}. I said: “It is only the appointed term of the Prophet ﷺ.” And he recited the surah to its end up to {He is ever accepting of repentance}. ʿUmar said: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[10550,"ʿUmar used to admit me with the elders of Badr. Some of them said: “Why do you admit this youth with us, when we have sons like him?” He said: “He is among those you know.” He said: One day he called them and called me, and I did not see him call me that day except to show them from me. He said: “What do you say about {When the help of Allah comes and the victory, and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in multitudes}”—until he finished the surah. Some of them said: “He commanded us to praise Allah and seek His forgiveness when we are helped and victory is granted to us.” Others said: “We do not know,” and some said nothing. Then he said to me: “O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you say the same?” I said: “No.” He said: “Then what do you say?” I said: “It is the appointed term of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah taught him: when the help of Allah comes and the victory—the conquest of Makkah—that is the sign of your term, so glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever accepting of repentance.” ʿUmar said: “I know nothing from it except what you know.”"],[10551,"From Qatada and 'Asim, that they heard 'Ikrima say: Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab summoned the companions of Muhammad ﷺ and asked them about Laylat al-Qadr, and they agreed that it is in the last ten nights. Ibn 'Abbas said: I said to 'Umar, 'Indeed I know, and I think, which night it is.' 'Umar said, 'And which night is it?' I said, 'The seventh that passes or the seventh that remains of the last ten.' 'Umar said, 'And from where did you know that?' Ibn 'Abbas said: I said, 'Allah created seven heavens and seven earths and seven days, and the month revolves in seven, and He created man from seven, and he eats from seven, and he prostrates on seven, and the circumambulation of the House is seven, and the stoning of the jamarat is seven—for things he mentioned.' 'Umar said, 'You have perceived a matter we did not perceive.' Qatada used to add on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas regarding his saying 'and he eats from seven': he said, 'It is the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {And We caused to grow therein grain, and grapes, and green fodder} [Quran 80:27-28], to the end of the verse.'"],[10552,"Al-'Abbas said to me: 'O my son, the Commander of the Believers is summoning you, bringing you near, and consulting you along with the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So preserve from me three traits: be wary—let him never test a lie on you; do not reveal a secret of his; and do not backbite anyone in his presence.' 'Amir said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Each one of these is better than ten thousand.'"],[10553,"On the evening of 'Arafah he would recite Surat al-Baqarah and Surat Al 'Imran, then explain them verse by verse. He was a copious, resourceful, far-reaching [scholar].\""],[10554,"That all the people know of it what I know of it, and indeed I hear of a judge among the judges of the Muslims who is just in his judgment and I rejoice for him, though perhaps I will never bring a case before him; and indeed I hear of rain that has fallen on a land of the Muslims and I rejoice, though I have no livestock there."],[10555,"Ibn 'Abbas said to him: 'O Commander of the Believers, may Allah reward you well. Rejoice, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated that Allah would strengthen the religion through you while the people were in disagreement. When you accepted Islam, your Islam became a source of honor, and Allah brought Islam, the Messenger of Allah, and his companions to prominence through you. You migrated to Madinah, and your migration was a conquest. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while he was pleased with you.'"],[10556,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Makkah: 'How good you are, and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that your people expelled me from you, I would not dwell in any other than you.'"],[10557,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal, and that it is a sunnah. He said: They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood. He did perform ramal, but it is not a sunnah. Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived while the polytheists were on the mountain of Qu'ayqi'an, and it reached him that they were saying that he and his companions were weak, so he commanded them to perform ramal to show them that they had strength."],[10558,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Your people claim that the Prophet ﷺ performed ramal around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood; it is not a sunnah.'"],[10559,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal around the House, and that it is a sunnah. He said: They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood. I said, 'What have they spoken truth about, and what falsehood?' He said, 'They spoke truth that he performed ramal, and falsehood that it is not a sunnah. Quraysh said, \"Leave Muhammad and his companions from al-Hudaybiyyah until they die the death of maggots.\" When they made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he would come the following year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came the following year while the polytheists were on the side of Qu'ayqi'an. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Perform ramal around the House,\" and it is not a sunnah.' I said, 'Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood.' I said, 'What have they spoken truth about, and what falsehood?' He said, 'They spoke truth that he performed tawaf on a camel, and falsehood that it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have people pushed away from him, nor would they be struck away from him, so he performed tawaf on a camel so that they could hear his words and see his place, and their hands would not reach him.' I said, 'Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth. When Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded with the rites, Satan confronted him at the place of sa'i, and he raced with him, and Ibrahim ﷺ outran him. Then Jibril ﷺ took him to Jamrat al-'Aqabah, and Satan confronted him, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he confronted him at the middle jamrah, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he laid him down on his forehead, and Isma'il had a white shirt on. He said to him, \"O my father, it is not a shirt, so shroud me in it.\" Ibrahim ﷺ turned around, and there was a white, big-eyed, horned ram, so he slaughtered it. Then Jibril ﷺ took him to the farthest jamrah, and Satan confronted him, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he took him to Mina and said, \"This is al-Mash'ar al-Haram.\" Then he took him to 'Arafah.' Ibn 'Abbas said, 'Do you know why it is called 'Arafah?' I said, 'Why is it called 'Arafah?' He said, 'Jibril ﷺ said, \"Have you come to know?\" He said, \"Yes.\"' Then Ibn 'Abbas said, 'Do you know how the talbiyah was?' I said, 'And how was the talbiyah?' He said, 'When Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded to proclaim the pilgrimage to the people, the mountains lowered their heads for him, and the towns were raised for him, so he proclaimed to the people.'"],[10560,"That when the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah, he said: 'The people have claimed that you have perished from weakness and hunger, so perform ramal when you enter and when you touch [the corner] for three circuits.' So they did. The people of Makkah said, 'We do not see the people except as strong, yet you claimed that they had perished from weakness.'"],[10561,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah and performed tawaf around the House on foot."],[10562,"Ibn ʿAbbas [said]: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to touch [in tawaf] anything except the Yamani Corner. Muʿawiya ؓ said: Nothing of the House is forsaken."],[10563,"He said: I could hear their words. Muʿawiya began to touch the two corners of the Black Stone, so Ibn ʿAbbas said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not used to touch these two corners. Muʿawiya said: Leave me alone, O Ibn ʿAbbas; for nothing of it is forsaken."],[10564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Makkah: “How good you are and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt in other than you.”"],[10565,"Muʿawiya and Ibn ʿAbbas performed Hajj. Muʿawiya began to touch all the corners, so Ibn ʿAbbas said: I only saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch these two corners."],[10566,"He narrated to him that he heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: “I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch other than the two Yamani corners.”"],[10567,"Muʿawiya performed Hajj and did not come to any corner of the House except that he touched it. Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used only to touch the Yamani Corner and the Black Stone. Muʿawiya said: Nothing of the corners of the House is forsaken."],[10568,"I heard him say: “We used to call it Shabbaʿa—meaning Zamzam—and we used to find it an excellent aid for the family.”"],[10569,"The people herded sheep and slaughtered them, then they started cooking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and ordered for the pots to be overturned and said, \"Do not partake in plundering.\""],[10570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any believer who frees a believer, Allah will ransom by every limb of him a limb of him from the Fire.” This is how al-Nadr narrated it from Muhammad b. Abi Humayd from ʿAmra bt. ʿUbayd Allah b. al-ʿAbbas, and Abu ʿAmir al-ʿAqadi disagreed with him, saying: from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas."],[10571,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever frees a believer in this world, Allah will ransom by every limb of him a limb from the Fire.”"],[10572,"We were sitting with Ibn ʿAbbas among a group of young men of Banu Hashim, and a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in Zuhr and ʿAsr? He said: No. He said: Perhaps he used to recite within himself."],[10573,"We were sitting with Ibn ʿAbbas among a group of young men of Banu Hashim, and a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in Zuhr and ʿAsr? He said: No. He said: Perhaps he used to recite within himself."],[10574,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the courtyard of his house in Makkah, ʿUthman b. Mazʿun passed by him and smiled broadly at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Do not sit.” He said, “Indeed I will.” So the Messenger of Allah sat facing him. While he was speaking with him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky, looked at the sky for a while, then began lowering his gaze until he fixed it on the ground to his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from his companion ʿUthman toward where he had fixed his gaze, and began nodding his head as if he were trying to understand what was being said to him. Ibn Mazʿun was watching. When he had accomplished what he needed and understood what was being said to him, the Messenger of Allah raised his gaze until it disappeared into the sky. Then he returned to ʿUthman in his original sitting posture and said, “O Muhammad, what was it that I was sitting with you for? I have never seen you do what you did this morning.” He said, “Did you notice that?” ʿUthman said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A messenger from Allah ﷺ came to me.” “While you were sitting?” He said, “Yes.” “What did he say to you?” He said, “{Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrong, and oppression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.}” ʿUthman said, “That was when faith became firmly established in my heart, and I loved Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[10575,"From ʿAli b. Abi Hamalah and al-Awzaʿi, they said: ʿAli b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbbas used to prostrate a thousand times every day."],[10576,"I spent the night at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ’s. He went to the mosque and led the people in the last ʿisha prayer until no one remained in the mosque except him. Then he passed by me and said, “Who is this?” I said, “ʿAbdullah.” He said, “What is it?” I said, “Al-ʿAbbas ordered me to spend the night with you tonight.” He said, “Then come along.” When he left, he entered and said, “Spread a bed for ʿAbdullah.” I was brought a cushion of coarse cloth. Al-ʿAbbas had instructed me, “Do not sleep until you have memorized his prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed, raised his head to the sky, and said, “Glory be to the King, the Most Holy,” three times. Then he recited this verse from the end of Surah Al ʿImran until he completed it: {Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth...}. Then he got up, cleaned his teeth with a siwak, performed ablution, entered his prayer place, and prayed two rakʿahs that were neither short nor long. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed and did as he had done the first time. Then he cleaned his teeth with a siwak, performed ablution, entered his prayer place, and prayed two rakʿahs that were neither long nor short. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed and did as he had done, prayed, then performed witr. When he finished his prayer, I heard him say: “O Allah, place light in my sight, place light in my hearing, place light in my tongue, place light in my heart, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light in front of me, place light behind me, place light above me, place light below me, and grant me light on the Day of Resurrection, and make my light great.”"],[10577,"That his father sent him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need. He said, \"So I found him sitting among his companions in the mosque, and I was unable to speak to him. When he finished praying Maghrib, he stood up and bowed until the Muezzin called the Isha prayer, and the people followed. Then he prayed the prayer and stood in bowing until those who remained in the mosque left. Then he went to his house, and I followed him. When he heard my footsteps, he said, 'Who is this?' and turned to me. I said, 'Ibn Abbas.' He said, 'The cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?' I said, 'The cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' He said, 'Welcome, the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . What brought you?' I said, 'My father sent me with something and something.' He said, 'Did you come at this time?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'If you did not come to your appointment at this time, then you are not leaving.' He entered his house, and I entered with him. I said, 'I would like to see the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' So he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and threw his gaze towards the sky and recited these verses from Surah Ali Imran, 'Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth,' until the end of the five verses, until he reached, 'Indeed, You do not fail in [Your] promise.' Then he said, 'O Allah, make light in my hearing, light in my sight, light beneath me, and give me light with You.' And beside him was a container filled with tooth stick from Arak, and he sharpened it, then rinsed, then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, and again he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and recited verses and invoked supplications, then he washed, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and recited verses and invoked supplications, then he washed, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he slept until I heard him snore, and he recited the verses, then he invoked with the invocation, then he washed, then he stood and prayed a prayer I recognized he performs more rak'ahs in it. So I came to his left corner, and he took me by the ear and turned me until he positioned me to his right corner. Then he prayed two rak'ahs of Fajr, then he went out to the prayer."],[10578,"What would be conquered for his ummah after him, generation after generation, was shown to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was pleased with that. Then Allah ﷻ revealed {And your Lord will surely give you, and you will be pleased.} So Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in each palace whatever befits it of youths and servants."],[10579,"Al-Mahdi led us in prayer and recited “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” aloud. I said something to him about that, and he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn ʿAbbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” aloud."],[10580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your Lord said: “By My might and majesty, I will surely exact retribution from the wrongdoer in this life and the next, and I will surely exact retribution from one who sees a wronged person and is able to help him but does not do so.”"],[10581,"When the Prophet ﷺ woke up at night, he would clean his teeth with a siwak, then perform ablution and recite {Indeed in the alternation of night and day...} to the end of the two verses. Then he would stand and pray two rakʿahs, then leave and sleep until he breathed deeply in sleep. Then he would get up and do the same again. Then he would return to his bed. Then he would get up and pray two rakʿahs, then do the same as he did the first time. Then he would perform witr with three."],[10582,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray during the day in pairs, two by two."],[10583,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while there were three hundred and sixty idols on the Kaʿbah; Iblis had fastened their feet with lead. He came with his staff and began striking each idol with it, and it would fall on its face, and he would say, “Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish,” until he had passed by all of them."],[10584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder or meat, then prayed and neither rinsed his mouth nor touched water."],[10585,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a limb and prayed without performing ablution."],[10586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a moist shoulder in the house of Ḍubāʿah bt. al-Ḥārith, then prayed and did not touch water."],[10587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate meat and prayed without performing ablution."],[10588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder in the house of Ḍubāʿah bt. al-Ḥārith."],[10589,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder, then went out to prayer and did not renew his ablution."],[10590,"He saw the Prophet of Allah ﷺ eat from a roasted shoulder, then pray, and he did not perform ablution because of that."],[10591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Love Allah for the blessings with which He nourishes you, love me for the love of Allah, and love the people of my household for love of me.\""],[10592,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone continually asks pardon, Allah will appoint for him a way out of every distress, and a relief from every anxiety, and will provide for him from where he did not reckon. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1518)"],[10593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer is created susceptible to trials, oft-repentant, forgetting; when reminded, he remembers.\""],[10594,"A bird was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You.\" Then ʿAlī came, and he said: \"O Allah, and to me.\""],[10595,"Al-ʿAbbās sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I came to him in the evening while he was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymūnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray during the night. When he had prayed the two rakʿahs before dawn, he said: \"O Allah, I ask You for mercy from You by which You guide my heart, gather my affairs, mend my brokenness, restore my affection, set right my religion, protect my absent ones, elevate my present ones, purify my deeds, whiten my face, inspire me with right guidance, and protect me from every evil. O Allah, grant me true faith and certainty after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your generosity in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for success at the time of decree, the hospitality of the martyrs, the life of the fortunate, the company of the prophets, and victory over the enemies. O Allah, I bring my need to You even if my judgment is short and my deeds are weak, for I am in need of Your mercy. So I ask You, O Decider of affairs, O Healer of hearts, as You make a way between the seas, to protect me from the punishment of the Blaze, from the cry of destruction, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever good my judgment falls short of, my deeds are too weak for, and my hopes do not reach—good that You have promised to any of Your servants or good that You bestow upon any of Your creation—I desire it from You and I ask You, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah, make us guides who are guided, not astray and not leading astray, at war with Your enemies and at peace with Your friends. We love people through Your love and we show enmity, through Your enmity, to those among Your creation who oppose You. O Allah, this is the supplication, and upon You is the response. O Allah, this is the effort, and upon You is the reliance. There is no power and no strength except with Allah. O Allah, Possessor of the strong rope and the right command, I ask You for security on the Day of Warning and Paradise on the Day of Eternity with the favored witnesses, those who bow and prostrate, and those who fulfill the covenants. Indeed, You are Merciful and Loving, and You do whatever You will. Glory be to the One who is clothed in might and has spoken it. Glory be to the One to whom praise is due alone. Glory be to the Possessor of the Throne and splendor. Glory be to the Possessor of power and generosity. Glory be to the One who has enumerated everything by His knowledge. O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my grave, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, and light below me. O Allah, increase me in light, grant me greater light, and place light for me.\""],[10596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hang the whip where the people of the household can see it.\""],[10597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it.”"],[10598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it, for it is a means of discipline for them.”"],[10599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang your whip where your family can see it.”"],[10600,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain, saying: “O Allah, grant us a downpour that is relieving, abundant, widespread, swift, not delayed, beneficial, and not harmful.” Before long we were rained upon until everything flowed, until they came to him and said: “We have been flooded.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, around us and not upon us.”"],[10601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The child of zina is the worst of the three if he acts according to the deeds of his parents.”"],[10602,"Abu Bakr ؓ had a seat near the Prophet ﷺ from which he would not rise except for al-ʿAbbas, and that pleased the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day al-ʿAbbas approached, so Abu Bakr moved aside from his seat for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, your uncle has approached.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him, then turned to Abu Bakr smiling and said: “This al-ʿAbbas has approached wearing white garments, and his descendants after him will wear black, and twelve men from among them will rule.”"],[10603,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blessing of horses is in their chestnut color.”"],[10604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blessing of horses is in their chestnut color, and the most auspicious of them in forelock is that which has a white blaze, white stockings, and a free right foreleg.”"],[10605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever holds the stirrup of his Muslim brother, not seeking anything from him and not fearing him, will be forgiven.”"],[10606,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning on Thursday.”"],[10607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Buy slaves and share with them in their provisions, meaning their earnings. Beware of the Zanj, for their lifespans are short and their provisions are little.”"],[10608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting for the whole of the month of Rajab."],[10609,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, eighty of which are from my ummah.”"],[10610,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When I was taken on the Night Journey, I reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its lote fruits were like large earthenware jars.”"],[10611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, wala' (patronage) does not transfer and does not change.\""],[10612,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For one of you to raise a puppy after the year one hundred and fifty-four is better for him than to raise a child of his own loins.\""],[10613,"Allah sent to the Prophet ﷺ an angel from among the angels together with the angel Jibril ﷺ . The angel said to him: \"O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives you the choice between being a prophet-servant or a prophet-king.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to Jibril as if seeking counsel, and he gestured to him to be humble. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, a prophet-servant.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen eating while reclining until he met his Lord."],[10614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever separates from the Muslims by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck. Whoever dies without having an imam over him, his death is a death of ignorance. And whoever dies under a blind banner, rallying to a faction or supporting a faction, his killing is a killing of ignorance.\""],[10615,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are a tribe of Rabiʿa, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar. We cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a matter which, if we act upon it, we will enter Paradise, and we will call those behind us to it.\" He commanded them with four things and forbade them from four things. He commanded them to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to establish the prayer, to give the zakat, to perform Hajj to the House, and to give the khums from the spoils of war. He forbade them from four things: drinking from hantam jars, dubba' gourds, naqir vessels, and muzaffat vessels. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, from what should we drink?\" He said: \"Use these water-skins whose mouths are tied.\""],[10616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in the darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10617,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Those who love one another [for Allah's sake] are in the shade of Allah.\""],[10618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' before everything, and 'There is no god but Allah' after everything, will be protected from anxiety and grief.\""],[10619,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\" Hammam added: Qatada said: \"We do not know vomit except as something forbidden.\""],[10620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\""],[10621,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The example of one who takes back his charity is like the dog that vomits and then returns to its vomit and eats it.\""],[10622,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"We do not have the evil example: the example of one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit and eats it.\""],[10623,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit.”"],[10624,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was told about the daughter of Hamzah, and her beauty was mentioned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you not know that she is the daughter of my brother through suckling? Do you not know that Allah has made unlawful through suckling what He made unlawful through lineage?”"],[10625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man’s paternal uncle is the twin of his father.”"],[10626,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for the fingers ten (camels) each, and for the hand fifty as an obligatory compensation.”"],[10627,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking a ruling. He had obligated upon himself a sacrificial camel in an oath he swore. He ruled for him a camel from the camels, and he rebuked the man from returning to it."],[10628,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon to the people, a man came, stepped over the people until he drew near to him, and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “Sit.” He sat. Then he stood a second time and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “Sit.” He sat. Then he stood a third time and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “And what is your punishment?” He said: “I came to a woman unlawfully.” The Prophet ﷺ said to men among his companions, among them ʿAlī, Ibn ʿAbbās, Zayd b. Ḥārithah, and ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān: “Go and flog him one hundred lashes.” He had not been married. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, should we not flog the one with whom he committed it?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring him to me.” When he was brought, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Who is your partner?” He said: “So-and-so woman.” The Prophet ﷺ sent for her and called her, and asked her about that. She said: “He has lied, by Allah. I do not know him, and I am innocent of what he said. Allah is witness to what I say.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is your witness that you did it with her? For she denies that you did it with her. If you have a witness, I will flog her; otherwise I will flog you the punishment for slander.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have no witness.” So he ordered him to be flogged the punishment for slander, eighty lashes."],[10629,"A woman asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward for a woman's participation in battle?\" He replied, \"Obeying her husband and acknowledging his rights.\""],[10630,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The likeness of the one who takes back his gift is like the likeness of the dog that vomits then returns to its vomit.”"],[10631,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"The example of the one who gives charity and then takes it back is like that of a person who vomits and then consumes it again.\""],[10632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The likeness of the one who gives charity then takes back his charity is like the likeness of the dog that vomits then eats its vomit.”"],[10633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept while prostrating until he snored, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution."],[10634,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[10635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbīr in the two ʿĪd prayers twelve times: in the first seven, and in the second five. He would go by one route and return by another."],[10636,"“The Prophet ﷺ would not drink nabīdh more than three days.”"],[10637,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted the liʿān between the ʿAjlānī man and his wife, and she was pregnant. Her husband said, “By Allah, I have not approached her since we pollinated the palm trees — al-ʿafr is the watering of palm trees after the watering from the wells is left off for two months.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, “O Allah, make it clear.” They claimed that the woman’s husband was thin in the forearms and shins, with reddish hair, and that the one with whom she was accused was Ibn al-Saḥmāʾ. She said, “Then she gave birth to a boy who was black, clear-skinned, with curly, tightly coiled hair, thick forearms, and plump shins.”"],[10638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned her.” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No, but that was a woman who had become notorious in Islam.”"],[10639,"To Ibn ʿAbbās, mentioning the two who engaged in liʿān: “Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned her’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No. That was a woman who had become notorious.”"],[10640,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted the liʿān between a man and his wife.”"],[10641,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have not had contact with my wife since the pollination of the palm trees — its pollination is that they are fertilized and then left unwatered for forty days after fertilization. I then found a man with my wife.” Her husband was pale-skinned, thin, with lank hair, while the one with whom she was accused was plump, tending towards darkness, with curly, tightly coiled hair, and had large buttocks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, make it clear; O Allah, make it clear.” Then he conducted the liʿān between them, and she gave birth to a child resembling the one with whom she was accused."],[10642,"That he mentioned the two who engaged in liʿān in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and ʿĀṣim said something about that, then left. A man from his people came to him and mentioned that he had found a man with his wife. ʿĀṣim said, “I was not afflicted with this except because of my own statement.” So he took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what he had found with his wife. That man was pale-skinned, thin-fleshed, with lank hair, while the one he claimed to have found with his wife was reddish, fleshy. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Allah, make it clear.” She gave birth to a child resembling the one her husband mentioned he had found with her, so the Messenger of Allah conducted the liʿān between them. A man said to Ibn ʿAbbās in the gathering, “Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If I were to stone a woman without clear evidence, I would have stoned this one’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No. That was a woman who used to display herself openly in Islam.”"],[10643,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned so-and-so. Suspicion has become apparent from her in her appearance, her speech, and those who enter upon her.”"],[10644,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forgot the Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr prayers on the day of the Confederates. He remembered after Maghrib, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “They distracted us from the prayer until the day departed. May Allah fill their graves with fire.” Then he prayed them after Maghrib."],[10645,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with a forelock and said, “The women of the Children of Israel used to put this on their heads, and they were cursed and the mosques were forbidden to them.”"],[10646,"I wish that people would allocate between a third to a quarter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A third, and a third is a lot or significant.\""],[10647,"“Mutʿah was indeed practiced during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10648,"Ibn ʿAbbās: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymūnah bt. al-Ḥārith while he was in iḥrām.”"],[10649,"Abu Bakr uncovered the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was covered with a cloth, looked at the face of the Prophet ﷺ, then leaned over him and kissed him."],[10650,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat meat from the shoulder of a sheep, then pray without performing ablution."],[10651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about khaṭṭ (geomancy), and he said: \"It is a remnant of knowledge.\""],[10652,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for ten years while the Qur'an was revealed to him, and in Madinah for ten years while it was revealed to him."],[10653,"He saw his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."],[10654,"Women have no say in the marriage contract. Maymūnah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Faḍl, and Umm al-Faḍl entrusted it to al-ʿAbbās, who married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[10655,"...to be praised for what he does — as one being punished? We shall surely be punished, all together. Ibn ʿAbbās said: What is the matter with you and this? It was revealed about the People of the Book. Then Ibn ʿAbbās recited: {And when God took a covenant from those who were given the Scripture: 'You shall make it clear to the people'} up to His saying: {Think not that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they have not done}. And Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet ﷺ asked them about something, but they envied him and concealed it, telling him something else. They rejoiced and went out having made him think they had told him what he asked about, and they sought praise from him for that, rejoicing in what they had done in concealing from him what he asked about."],[10656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given victory in any battle like he was at Uḥud. That was denied, so Ibn ʿAbbās said: Between me and the one who denies it is the Book of God. God says: {And God did indeed fulfil His promise to you when you were slaying them by His permission}. Ibn ʿAbbās said: al-ḥass means killing. {Until when you lost courage} up to His saying: {And God has pardoned you, and God is bountiful to the believers}. He meant by this the archers. The Prophet ﷺ stationed them at a lookout and said: \"Protect our backs. If you see us being killed, do not come to our aid; and if you see us gaining spoils, do not share with us.\" When God granted the Prophet ﷺ spoils and allowed him the camp of the polytheists, the archers all turned away and entered the camp to plunder, while the ranks of the Prophet's companions had become interlocked — and he interlaced his right and left fingers. When the archers abandoned that position where they had been, the cavalry entered from that point upon the Prophet's companions, and they struck one another, and many Muslims were killed. From the beginning of the day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions had killed seven or nine of the standard-bearers of the polytheists. The Muslims made a retreat toward the mountain, but did not reach the place people call al-Ghār; they were below al-Mihrās. Satan cried out, \"Muḥammad has been killed!\" and we had no doubt it was true. We remained so, not doubting he had been killed, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared between the two mountain passes. I recognized him by the way he swayed when he walked. We rejoiced as if nothing had befallen us. He climbed toward us saying: \"God's anger is intense against a people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" And another time he said: \"O God, it is not for them to overcome us until they reach us.\" He stayed for a while, and then Abu Sufyān shouted from the foot of the mountain: \"Exalted be Hubal!\" — meaning his gods. \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not answer him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" When he said, \"Exalted be Hubal,\" ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: \"God is more exalted and more majestic.\" Abu Sufyān said: \"O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, you have done well.\" Then he repeated the same: \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, here is Abu Bakr, and here am I, ʿUmar.\" Abu Sufyān said: \"A day for the day of Badr. Days alternate, and war is a matter of give and take.\" ʿUmar said: \"No, they are not equal. Our slain are in Paradise and your slain are in the Fire.\" He said: \"You claim that. We would then be disappointed and losers.\" Then Abu Sufyān said: \"You will find mutilation among your slain, and that was not by the decision of our leaders.\" Then tribal pride overtook him, and he said: \"Indeed it happened, but we did not disapprove of it.\""],[10657,"God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed — those are the disbelievers}, {the wrongdoers}, {the transgressors}. Ibn ʿAbbās said: He revealed them concerning two groups of the Jews. One of them had subdued the other in pre-Islamic times, until they agreed and made a settlement that every slain person killed by the powerful group from the weak group would have a blood money of fifty wasq, and every slain person killed by the weak group from the powerful group would have a blood money of one hundred wasq. They remained on that until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived. Then the two groups submitted to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — though the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not yet prevailed over them or subdued them, and there was a truce. The weak group killed a man from the powerful group, so the powerful group sent to the weak group: \"Send us one hundred wasq.\" The weak group said: \"Has this ever been so when their religion is one and their lineage is one? The blood money of some of them is half that of others. We only gave you this out of oppression and fear of you. But now that Muḥammad ﷺ has come, we will not give you that.\" War was about to break out between them, but then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a judge between them. The powerful group thought and said: \"By God, Muḥammad will not give you from them double what he gives them from you. They spoke the truth: they only gave us this out of oppression and subjugation. So send someone secretly to Muḥammad ﷺ to find out his opinion. If he gives you what you want, you will accept his judgment; but if he does not, you will be wary and not accept it.\" So they secretly sent people from the hypocrites to test the opinion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, God informed His Messenger of their entire affair and what they intended. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {O Messenger, let not those who hasten into disbelief grieve you, from those who say} up to His saying: {And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed — those are the transgressors}. Then he said: By God, it was revealed concerning them, and God meant them."],[10658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his sword Dhū al-Faqār as booty on the day of Badr, and it was the one about which he saw the vision on the day of Uḥud."],[10659,"\"The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[10660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah in the year of the conquest for fifteen [days] shortening the prayer."],[10661,"The last surah of the Qur'an to be revealed in full was {When the help of Allah comes and the victory} [Q 110:1]."],[10662,"When Ali's companions, as they were marching to Basra, learned that the people of Basra had gathered in support of Talha and al-Zubayr, it distressed them and it weighed on their hearts. Ali said, 'By the One besides whom there is no god, he will surely prevail over the people of Basra, Talha and al-Zubayr will surely be killed, and there will surely come out to you from Kufa six thousand five hundred fifty men' - or 'five thousand five hundred fifty men,' al-Ajlah was unsure. Ibn Abbas said: That stayed in my mind. When the people of Kufa came, I went out and said, 'I will certainly see. If it is as he says, then it is a matter he heard; otherwise it is a trick of war.' I met a man from the army and asked him, and by Allah he did not delay in saying what Ali had said. Ibn Abbas said: And it was among the things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tell him."],[10663,"Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it."],[10664,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring could be heard, then he got up and prayed without performing ablution.\""],[10665,"The Prophet ﷺ went out intending to pray and passed by a cooking pot. He took a bone from it and ate it, then went on to pray without performing ablution."],[10666,"\"O Abu Al-Abbas, does the killer have a chance for repentance?\" Ibn Abbas replied, \"I'm amazed by your question. What do you say?\" He repeated the question to him again, and Ibn Abbas asked him, \"What do you say?\" After repeating the question two or three times, Ibn Abbas said, \"How can he repent? I heard your Prophet ﷺ say, 'The slain person will come on the Day of Resurrection, with his head held in one hand and his killer in the other, covered in blood until he reaches the throne. Then, the slain person will say to Allah, 'My Lord, this person killed me,' and Allah ﷻ will say to the killer, 'You are doomed,' and he will be taken to Hell.'\""],[10667,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and for a virgin her consent is her silence.\""],[10668,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and for a virgin her father seeks her consent, and her silence is her acknowledgment.\""],[10669,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A previously married woman has more authority over her own person, and a virgin is asked for her consent, and her consent is her silence.\""],[10670,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and a virgin is asked for her consent, and her silence is her acknowledgment.\""],[10671,"A woman from Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has become senile. Allah's obligation of Hajj has overtaken him, but he is unable to perform it. Is it sufficient for him if I perform it on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[10672,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The most hateful people to Allah are those who seek the ways of ignorance in Islam and those who unlawfully seek the blood of a person to spill his blood.\""],[10673,"Musaylimah the Liar came during the era of Allah’s Messenger ﷺ and began saying, “If Muhammad grants me the authority after him, I will follow him.” He arrived with a large number of his people. Allah’s Messenger ﷺ came to him, accompanied by Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, and in the hand of Allah’s Messenger ﷺ was a piece of a palm branch. He stood before Musaylimah among his companions and said, “If you were to ask me for this piece, I would not give it to you, and you will not go beyond what Allah has decreed for you. If you turn back, Allah will surely hamstring you. I see in you what I was shown, and this is Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas; he will answer you on my behalf.” Then he departed."],[10674,"Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said: Allah, Exalted is He, said: “The son of Adam belied Me, though it was not proper for him to belie Me, and he reviled Me, though it was not proper for him to do that. As for his belying Me, it is his claim that I am not able to recreate him as he was. As for his reviling Me, he says I have a son. Glorified am I above taking a consort or a son.”"],[10675,"Ibn Abbas said: I do not care about what you perform ablution for. I bear witness that I saw Allah’s Messenger ﷺ eat a meat shoulder and then stand up to pray without performing ablution. He said: Sulayman was present for that from both of them."],[10676,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to the prayer, and a meat shoulder was brought to him. He took a bite from it and then proceeded to the prayer without rinsing his mouth or purifying. The wording is from the hadith of Rawh b. al-Qasim."],[10677,"Ibn Abbas said: Shall I show you how Allah’s Messenger ﷺ used to perform ablution? He called for a vessel containing water, scooped a handful, and rinsed his mouth and nose. Then he took another handful, joined his hands with it, and washed his face. Then he took another and washed his right hand. Then he scooped another handful and washed his left hand. Then he took a handful of water, lowered his hand, and wiped his head and ears with it. Then he scooped another handful and sprinkled it on his feet while he had sandals on, and the left likewise, and he wiped the bottom of the sandals. Then he said, “Like this.”"],[10678,"Arbad b. Qays b. Juzayy b. Khalid b. Ja’far b. Kilab and Amir b. al-Tufayl b. Malik came to Madinah to Allah’s Messenger ﷺ. They reached Allah’s Messenger ﷺ while he was sitting, and they sat before him. Amir b. al-Tufayl said, “O Muhammad, what will you grant me if I accept Islam?” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “You will have what the Muslims have and you will bear what they bear.” Amir b. al-Tufayl said, “Will you grant me the authority after you if I accept Islam?” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “That is not for you nor for your people, but you may have the reins of the horses.” He said, “I am now in charge of the reins of the horses of Najd. Give me the desert and leave the settled land to you.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “No.” When they turned away from Allah’s Messenger ﷺ, Amir said, “By Allah, I will fill it against you with horses and men.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “Allah will prevent you.” When Arbad and Amir left, Amir said, “O Arbad, I will distract Muhammad with talk while you strike him with the sword. If you kill Muhammad, the people will only accept blood money and dislike war, and we will give them the blood money.” Arbad said, “I will do it.” They returned to him, and Amir said, “O Muhammad, stand with me so I may speak to you.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ stood with him, and they withdrew to the wall, and Allah’s Messenger ﷺ stood speaking with him while Arbad drew the sword. When he placed his hand on the hilt of the sword, it stuck to the hilt, and he could not draw the sword. Arbad delayed striking Amir, so Allah’s Messenger ﷺ turned and saw Arbad and what he was doing, and he departed from them. When Amir and Arbad left Allah’s Messenger ﷺ and reached the harrat Waqim, they dismounted. Sa’d b. Mu’adh and Usayd b. Hudayr came out to them and said, “Depart, O enemies of Allah! May Allah curse you both.” Amir said, “Who is this, O Sa’d?” He said, “This is Usayd b. Hudayr, the one of the battalions.” They went on until they reached al-Raqm, where Allah, Exalted is He, sent a thunderbolt upon Arbad and killed him. Amir went on until he was at al-Harr, and then Allah sent a gland infection upon him. Night overtook him in the house of a woman from Banu Salul. He began touching the gland in his throat and saying, “A gland like the gland of a camel in the house of a Saluli woman,” wishing to die in her house. Then he mounted his horse and urged it on until he died upon it on his way back. Allah, Exalted is He, revealed concerning them: “Allah knows what every female carries and what the wombs decrease” up to His saying, “You have no protector besides Him.” He said: “The guardian angels” from Allah’s command protect Muhammad. Then he mentioned Arbad and what preceded him regarding it. He said: “It is He who shows you the lightning, causing fear and hope,” up to His saying, “And He is severe in stratagem.”"],[10679,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought fruit, he would give it to the youngest child present."],[10680,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from the shoulder of a sheep and then prayed without performing ablution."],[10681,"Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said: “A distinguishing sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill of Zamzam.”"],[10682,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no racing prize except for camels, horses, or arrows.”"],[10683,"O Messenger of God, what may I do with my wife while she is menstruating? He said: “Tie her waist-wrapper firmly, then do what you wish with her.”"],[10684,"The English translation of the given passage would be: \"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked in the mirror, he would say, 'Praise be to Allah who has beautified my appearance and adorned me with what He has not bestowed upon others.'\""],[10685,"The Prophet ﷺ came out while they were sitting and said: “Shall I not tell you who has the best standing among people?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “A man who holds the bridle of his horse” – or he said – “a horse in the path of God, until he is killed.” He said: “Shall I tell you who comes after him?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “A man isolated in a mountain pass who establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, and keeps away from the evils of people. Shall I tell you who is the worst of people?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The one who is asked by God but does not give by Him.”"],[10686,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Shall I not tell you who the best of people is? Among the best of people is a man holding the bridle of his horse in the path of God. Shall I tell you who comes after him? A man isolated with his flock, fulfilling God’s right concerning it. And shall I tell you who the worst of people is? A man who is asked by God but does not give by Him.”"],[10687,"May God forgive Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. By my life, this verse troubled the Muslims before him until God, exalted is He, sent down: “God does not burden any soul beyond its capacity. It has what it earned and against it what it incurred.” He said: Intrusive thoughts are what people cannot control, and God has decreed for every soul its recompense according to what it earned."],[10688,"May God forgive Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. The Muslims found from this verse the same distress he found, so they complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Thus your Lord has said, so say: ‘We believe in what He has sent down, and we hear and obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return.’” They said it as long as God willed them to say it, until God, exalted is He, sent down: “The Messenger has believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord” up to His saying “God does not burden any soul beyond its capacity.”"],[10689,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Pulpits of gold will be set up for the prophets, on which they will sit, while my pulpit will remain without me sitting on it” – or he said, “without me taking a seat on it – standing upright before my Lord because of my community, fearing that I might be sent to Paradise while my community remains behind me. So I will say: ‘My Lord, my community, my community!’ Then God Most High will say: ‘O Muhammad, what do you wish Me to do with your community?’ I will say: ‘My Lord, make their reckoning just.’ They will be summoned and their accounts will be settled. Some will enter Paradise by God’s mercy, and some will enter Paradise by my intercession. I will not cease interceding until I am given writs for men who had been dispatched to the Fire, until even Malik, the keeper of the Fire, says: ‘O Muhammad, you have left no one from your community for your Lord’s wrath to punish.’”"],[10690,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas on this pulpit narrating that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say these words at times of distress: “There is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing. There is no god but God, Lord of the Great Throne. There is no god but God, Lord of the heavens and the earth and Lord of the Great Throne. Avert from me the evil of so-and-so.”"],[10691,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"It is permissible for a man to look at the slave girl he intends to purchase, other than her private parts, from her knees to the end of her garment.\""],[10692,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Jesus son of Mary ﷺ said: “Matters are only three: a matter whose right guidance has become clear to you, so follow it; a matter whose error has become clear to you, so avoid it; and a matter about which people differ, so refer it back to the one who has knowledge of it.”"],[10693,"The Prophet ﷺ said from the pulpit: “Shall I not tell you about the worst of you?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The worst of you is the one who travels alone, flogs his slave, and withholds his aid.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “One who hates people and they hate him.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Those who do not accept a slip, nor accept an excuse, nor forgive a sin.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “One whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe.”"],[10694,"On the authority of ʿAʾishah, they both said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque and there were voices like the buzzing of bees reciting the Quran. He said: “Islam will spread, then there will be a period of weakness for it. Whoever’s period of weakness leads to extremism and innovation, those are the people of the Fire.”"],[10695,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Good character melts away sins as water melts ice, and bad character spoils deeds as vinegar spoils honey.”"],[10696,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Two hungry wolves let loose among a flock of sheep are not more destructive to it than the son of Adam’s love of honor and wealth.”"],[10697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you ask by Allah, ask with the palms of your hands, and do not ask with their backs, and wipe your faces with them.”"],[10698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Verily, everything has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty.”"],[10699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Verily, everything has an honor, and the honor of gatherings is to face the qiblah. Whoever looks into his brother’s book without his permission, it is as if he looks into the Fire.”"],[10700,"She said: “Permit him if you wish,” so I let him in. When he sat down, he said: “Rejoice.” She said: “Also,” and he said: “There is nothing between you and meeting Muhammad ﷺ except that the soul leaves the body. You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved only what is pure. Your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwāʾ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained until morning at the campsite, and the people woke up without water with them. So Allah ﷻ revealed: “And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth.” That was because of you, and Allah did not send down this concession for this Ummah except for you. And Allah the Exalted sent down your exoneration from above seven heavens, brought by the Trustworthy Spirit. Morning came and there was no mosque among the mosques of Allah in which Allah is remembered except that it was recited in it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.” She said: “Leave me from you, Ibn ʿAbbās. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I wish I had been something utterly forgotten.”"],[10701,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Sniff water into the nostrils twice, and the ears are part of the head.”"],[10702,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ and commanded fasting on it.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is a day that the Jews and Christians venerate.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the coming year comes, God willing, we will fast the ninth.” But the coming year did not arrive until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away."],[10703,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Health and free time are two blessings in which many people are deceived.”"],[10704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.”"],[10705,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ʿĪd prayers: in the first rakʿah, the Opening of the Book and “Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High,” and in the second, the Opening of the Book and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[10706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder, then prayed without touching water — the wording is that of the hadith of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān."],[10707,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder and did not perform ablution."],[10708,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, then he went out for prayer. A large dish containing meat and bread was brought to him and he ate from it and did not perform ablution (again)."],[10709,"I entered the house of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and found 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas there. We discussed ablution after eating food touched by fire. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat food touched by fire, then pray without performing ablution. We said, 'Did you see him yourself?' He pointed to his eyes and said, 'My eyes saw it.'"],[10710,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from a shoulder (of meat), then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10711,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a shoulder or a foreleg, then lead the people in prayer without performing ablution.'"],[10712,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage: a bone with meat was brought to him while he was circumambulating the House on the Day of Sacrifice; he took a bite from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10713,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for prayer and a gift met him—a limb of a sheep. He ate a morsel or two from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever eats any of this vegetable of yours (garlic) should not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what harms the children of Adam.'"],[10715,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'The Messenger of Allah was washed (after death) in his shirt, and 'Ali, al-Fadl b. 'Abbas, Salih b. 'Abbas, and Salih b. Shuqran, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, descended into his grave.'"],[10716,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated on his camel during the Farewell Pilgrimage and touched the corner with his staff, disliking that the people be pushed away from him.'"],[10717,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated during the Farewell Pilgrimage on his she-camel al-Qaswa'."],[10718,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman who was insane and said: 'Which is dearer to you: that you be cured of this, or that you be patient and have Paradise?' She said, 'Paradise.'"],[10719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' in Madinah without fear or rain. I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Why do you think he did that?' He said, 'He wanted to make things easy for his community.'"],[10720,"Umm al-Fadl sent milk to the Prophet ﷺ and he drank it while he was addressing the people at Arafah."],[10721,"From the Prophet ﷺ."],[10722,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"The womb has a hook that clings to the waist of the Most Merciful; it joins whoever joins it and cuts off whoever cuts it off.\""],[10723,"It is from the Sunnah."],[10724,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old, Abu Bakr when he was at the same age, Umar b. al-Khattab when he was fifty-six, and Uthman when he was eighty-one."],[10725,"If the land is fertile, then aim for exploration and give the travelers their rights; for indeed, Allah is Kind who loves kindness. But if it is arid, then flee and rely on the camel (for transportation); for indeed, the land folds at night and be cautious of the wild animals on the road; for indeed, it is the abode of snakes and the hunting ground of predators."],[10726,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Nothing from the slaughter of the people of Jahiliyyah has given birth to me, and I have been born only from marriage, just like the marriage in Islam.\" Abu Al-Qasim Al-Madini said, \"He is Fulayh bin Sulayman, according to me.\""],[10727,"Ibn Abbas: Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that."],[10728,"About a slave who divorced his wife twice, then both were freed: may he marry her again? He said: Yes. It was asked: On whose authority? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ issued that ruling."],[10729,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If I live, God willing, until next year, I will fast the ninth, for fear of missing the day of Ashura.\""],[10730,"That he should come to me and ask me? The Messenger of God ﷺ went out humble, beseeching, and plainly dressed; he did not deliver a sermon like this one of yours, and he prayed two rak'ahs as he prayed on the Eid."],[10731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The martyrs are on a shining river at the gate of Paradise; their provision comes out to them morning and evening.\""],[10732,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Uthman b. Maz'un on the day he died and leaned over him as if advising him, then raised his head and they saw traces of weeping in his eyes, then leaned over him a second time, then raised his head and they saw him weeping, then leaned over him a third time, then raised his head with a sob. So they knew that he had died, and the people wept. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Stop; this is from Satan, so seek forgiveness from Allah.\" Then he said: \"Go away from you, Abu al-Sa'ib, for you have departed and have not been soiled by anything of it.\""],[10733,"The Prophet ﷺ, on the day Sa'd b. Mu'adh was buried, while sitting at his grave, said: \"If anyone were to be saved from the trial of the grave, Sa'd b. Mu'adh would have been saved, but he was squeezed with a squeeze, then released.\""],[10734,"Ibn Abbas: It is for the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[10735,"About the share of the near of kin, and he says: To whom does he think it should go? Ibn Abbas said: It is for the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it among them. Umar had offered us something from that which we considered less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it. He had offered to help their newlyweds, pay off their debtors, and give to their poor, but he refused to give them more than that."],[10736,"About the near of kin whom Allah mentioned in the Qur'an, about killing the children of the polytheists, and whether the Prophet ﷺ used to kill them, about when the orphanhood of an orphan ends, and about the slave and the woman who witness battle. He said: If I did not fear that he would fall into something evil, I would not write to him. So he wrote regarding the near of kin: We used to consider the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be them, but our people denied us that. As for the orphan, when he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is observed in them, his property is handed over to him, and his orphanhood has ended. As for the children, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not kill the children of the polytheists, and you should not kill them unless you know what al-Khidr knew about the boy when he killed him. Regarding the slave and the woman, do they have a share if they witness battle? He wrote to him that they have no fixed share, unless they are given something from the spoils of the people."],[10737,"That he commit an imprudence; I did not write to him. Then he wrote to him: As for the orphan, when he has a wet dream and sound judgment is perceived from him, orphanhood has ceased for him. As for the children, if you know about them what al-Khiḍr knew, then otherwise do not kill them. As for the slave, he used to be given a share. As for the women, they used to treat the wounded and give water. As for the fifth, we claim that it is for us, and our people claim that it is not for us."],[10738,"And about the slave and the woman who attend the spoils: is there anything for them from it? And about the orphan: when is the name of orphan removed from him? And about killing children. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Were it not that I hope that God will benefit him through my writing, I would not write to him. Then he said: Write, O Yazīd: As for the fifth, we used to hold that it was for us, but our people refused us that. As for the slave and the woman who attend the spoils, there is nothing for them from it, but they are given a small gift. As for the orphan, orphanhood is removed from him when he reaches puberty, and he becomes one of the poor Muslims. As for the children, do not kill them until you know from them the like of what al-Khiḍr knew about the boy before he killed him. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī."],[10739,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no one who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him and he accompanies them, except that they will admit him to Paradise.\""],[10740,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, and the intoxicant from every drink.\""],[10741,"\"O Messenger of God, I sometimes think to myself about something concerning the Lord that I would rather be a cinder than speak of it.\" Shuʿbah said: One of them said: \"Praise be to God, who has only given you power over whispering.\" The other said: \"Praise be to God, who has turned its matter back to whispering.\""],[10742,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, a little of it and a lot, and intoxication from every drink.\""],[10743,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, a little of it and a lot, and intoxication from every drink.\""],[10744,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of God, shall we not sell it? He said: \"The One who forbade drinking it also forbade selling it.\""],[10745,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.\""],[10746,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever conceals knowledge that he knows will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.\" He said: \"It is the testimony about a man: it is requested of him or not requested of him, and he knows it but does not guide its owner to it. So the knowledge is exactly this.\""],[10747,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The hudud punishments are not to be carried out in mosques, nor is retaliation to be taken against a parent for [killing] his child.”"],[10748,"“Indeed three [divorces] used to be made one during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[10749,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever is killed in the blind or by something thrown, while between them is a rock, a wipe, or a stick, then the blood money of be paid for him is the blood money for accidental killing. Whoever kills deliberately, then retaliation is upon him, and whoever tries to prevent that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the Angels, and all the people, and neither Sarf nor Adl will be accepted from him.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4789)"],[10750,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten the iftar, to delay the suhur, and to place our right hands upon our left [in prayer].”"],[10751,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed the best reciter among people is one who, when he recites, shows sorrow.”"],[10752,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram.”"],[10753,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in ihram.”"],[10754,"“The Prophet ﷺ was commanded that we prostrate on seven [parts] and that we not gather back our hair or clothing.”"],[10755,"The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven: his face, his palms, his knees, and his feet, and he was forbidden to gather back hair or clothing."],[10756,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven and was forbidden to gather back his hair and garments.”"],[10757,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was commanded that we prostrate on seven bones and was forbidden to gather back hair or clothing.”"],[10758,"“The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven and that he gather back his hair or garments.”"],[10759,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven body parts: the nose, the forehead, the palms, and the tips of the fingers, and not to gather back hair or clothing.”"],[10760,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I have been forbidden to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I have been forbidden to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10764,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven (bones), and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if it is a hundred conditions.\""],[10768,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fruit until it is fit to eat.\""],[10769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes possession of it.\""],[10770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you buy food, do not sell it until you take possession of it.\" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"I consider that other than that in sales is like food.\""],[10771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he receives it in full.\" And I think that everything is like it."],[10772,"The food that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited to be sold until it is received (taken possession of)."],[10773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of food before it is received."],[10774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you buys food, he should not sell it until he receives it.\""],[10775,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He who buys foodstuff should not sell it till he is satisfied with the measure with which he has bought it. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2126)"],[10776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of food until it is fully received."],[10777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid sharecropping (muzāraʿa), but he commanded that they be kind to one another."],[10778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to grant his brother [the use of] his land is better for him than taking a fixed remuneration.\""],[10779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit leasing land, but he said: \"For one of you to grant [the use of] his land to his brother is better for him than taking a remuneration for it.\""],[10780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For a man to grant his brother [the use of] his land is better for him than taking a fixed rent (kharj) for it.\""],[10781,"The Prophet ﷺ once said on earth, \"Giving it as a gift to your brother is better than collecting rent for it.\""],[10782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to grant it to his brother is better for him,\" and he did not prohibit leasing it."],[10783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For a man to let his brother cultivate [his land] is better for him than taking a rent (kharāj) for it.\""],[10784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of Madinah enter ihrām from Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, the people of Shām from al-Juḥfah, the people of Yemen from Yalamlam, and the people of Najd from Qarn.\""],[10785,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I made ẓihār from my wife, and her anklet pleased me last night, so I had intercourse with her before I made expiation.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Did not Allah, Mighty and Sublime, say: {before they touch one another}? Refrain until you make expiation.\""],[10786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited wearing silk, but there is no harm in wearing cotton or linen fabric."],[10787,"The Prophet ﷺ took in his hand a piece of gold and a piece of silk and said, \"Verily, these two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah and permissible for their females.\""],[10788,"The first to proclaim Islam openly was Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ"],[10789,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"If I remain until next year, I will certainly fast the ninth.\""],[10790,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to take back his gift, except a father.\""],[10791,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said: \"Horses belonging to the Muslims attacked a people among the polytheists, and they fought them and killed their children.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are with their fathers.\""],[10792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Silver has not been spent on anything more beloved to Allah than a sacrificial animal slaughtered on the day of Eid.\""],[10793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing is seen better for two who love each other than marriage.\""],[10794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in his sermon, \"Verily, he guides to the best of manners, and indeed, he repels their evil.\""],[10795,"A man gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a she-camel as a gift, and he gave him a reward for it. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" So he gave him more. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" So he gave him more. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I had resolved not to accept a gift except from an Ansari, a Qurashi, or a Thaqafi.\""],[10796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Remain in your places of dwelling, for emigration has ceased, but there remains jihad and intention. When you are called out, go forth.\""],[10797,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah, \"Shall we act according to what has been decreed and rely on it, or should we depend on something we strive for?\" He said, \"No, rather act according to what has been decreed, for the pens have dried.\" He said, \"Then what is the point of striving?\" He said, \"Act, for everyone will be facilitated (in their actions).\""],[10798,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Surat Tanzeel (al-Sajdah) and ten verses from the al-Mufassal, and sometimes he would say, \"Has there come upon man...\""],[10799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attach the fixed shares to the estate, and whatever the fixed shares leave goes to the nearest male.\""],[10800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Divide the estate among the heirs of the fixed shares according to the Book of Allah, and whatever the fixed shares leave goes to the nearest male.\""],[10801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attach the fixed shares to the Book of Allah, and what I have left goes to the nearest male.\""],[10802,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Give the Fara'id (the shares of the inheritance that are prescribed in the Qur'an) to those who are entitled to receive it. Then whatever remains, should be given to the closest male relative of the deceased .\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6732)"],[10803,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The evil eye is real. If anything could outstrip destiny, the evil eye would do so. And if you are asked to wash (for it), then wash.”"],[10804,"They used to consider performing ʿUmrah during the months of Hajj as one of the most wicked acts on earth. They used to call Muharram Safar and say: “When the wounds of the camel’s back heal, and the tracks fade away, and Safar passes, then ʿUmrah becomes permissible for the one intending it.”"],[10805,"And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform Umrah with Aisha in Dhu al-Hijjah except to refute the statements of the polytheists. For this place is from Quraish, and whoever criticizes their religion, they used to say, \"When the Yam (a type of fly) urinates and the donkey's tail is raised, then the Umrah is considered. So they used to prohibit Umrah until Dhu al-Hijjah and Muharram would pass. And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform Umrah with Aisha except to fulfill their statement."],[10806,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped, gave the cupper his fee, and used medication in the nose."],[10807,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he was asked about the slaughtering and the shaving, regarding which comes first and which comes later. He said: “There is no harm.”"],[10808,"“The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that goes back to its vomit.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2386)"],[10809,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fixed Dhul-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, Qarn for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. These are for their residents and for those who come to them intending Hajj or ʿUmrah. Anyone who is nearer than that should assume ihram from his starting point, even the people of Makkah from Makkah.”"],[10810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding Allah’s ﷻ statement {Then there is no rafath, no fusuq, and no jidal in Hajj}: “Rafath is lewd speech and soliciting women for intercourse; fusuq is all acts of disobedience; and jidal is a man arguing with his companion.”"],[10811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from selling food until he had taken full possession of it."],[10812,"“Triple divorce was considered one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and the first two years of ʿUmar’s caliphate.” Then ʿUmar said: “The people have become hasty in a matter in which they had been given respite. If only we could enforce it upon them.” So he enforced it upon them."],[10813,"“The three pronouncements were made one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, and three during the first part of ʿUmar’s rule.” Ibn ʿAbbas said: “Yes.”"],[10814,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[10815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather the hair or the clothes.”"],[10816,"About mutʿah marriage: because they used to trade in the middle of the year.”"],[10817,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who had dyed (his beard) with henna and said, \"How good this is.\" Then another passed by him who had dyed with henna and katam, and he said, \"How good this is.\" Then another passed by him who had dyed with saffron, and he said, \"This is better than all of that.\" And Tawus used to dye with saffron."],[10818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade intercepting the caravans and a resident selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[10819,"\"The first to embrace Islam was Ali ؓ.\""],[10820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever splits the staff of the Muslims while the Muslims are in a complete state of Islam has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck.\""],[10821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The worst house is the bathhouse; voices are raised in it and private parts are exposed.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the sick are treated in it and filth is removed in it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever enters it, let him enter only covered.\""],[10822,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned wine, and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we make a drink from this millet.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[10823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A one-eyed or emaciated animal is not permissible as a sacrificial camel, and beware of the one that has been deliberately weakened.\""],[10824,"The Prophet ﷺ was given some game meat, but he returned it and said, \"We are forbidden to eat it.\""],[10825,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque on Friday and saw Abu Isra'il standing in the sun without seeking shade. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with him?\" They said, \"He vowed to stand and not seek shade and not break his fast.\" He said, \"Command him to sit, seek shade, and break his fast.\""],[10826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived on the morning of the fourth day, pronouncing talbiyah for Hajj. He ordered them to make it an Umrah, but that seemed grave to them. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what kind of exiting from ihram?\" He said, \"Complete exiting.\""],[10827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Beware of a house called the bathhouse.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt and benefits the sick.\" He said, \"Whoever enters it, let him cover himself.\""],[10828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no vow except in that in which Allah is obeyed, and no vow involving severing ties of kinship, and no divorce or manumission regarding what one does not own.\""],[10829,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a khamisa."],[10830,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever revives dead land, he has the most right to it.”"],[10831,"The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his hands in every rak'ah, and the righteous said to do so after every takbirah."],[10832,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a woolen cloak alone."],[10833,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Cupping on the head is a cure for seven things, if the one performing it intends them: madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, toothache, headache, and a darkness he finds in his eyes.”"],[10834,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say after the tashahhud: “O God, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge with You from the trial of the Dajjal, and I seek refuge with You from the trials of life and death.”"],[10835,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {So recite what is easy of the Qur'an}: He said: “A hundred verses.”"],[10836,"“There is no divorce except with a waiting period, and no manumission except for the sake of God the Exalted.”"],[10837,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer without an adhan or iqamah, then he came to the women and admonished them and urged them to give charity. So how many necklaces and rings were thrown into Bilal's garment until it was filled, or as God willed."],[10838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “This city is sacred; God made it sacred, and killing was not made lawful in it for anyone before me, but it was made lawful for me, so it is sacred by God's sanctity.”"],[10839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “There is no emigration after the conquest, but there is jihad and intention. And when you are called to mobilize, then mobilize.”"],[10840,"I traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel and drank from it so that the people could see him. Then he broke his fast when he entered Makkah and conquered Makkah in Ramadan. Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted while traveling and broke his fast, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break his fast.”"],[10841,"“The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ was ten dirhams.”"],[10842,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Ghusl is obligatory on every Muslim every seven days, for his hair and his skin”—meaning for Friday. “Sa'id b. Miqlas is Sa'id b. Abi Ayyub.”"],[10843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of Sacrifice: “No deed of the son of Adam on this day is more excellent than blood that is shed, except a severed womb that is reconnected.”"],[10844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “One is not a believer of complete faith who does not regard affliction as a blessing and ease as a misfortune.” They said, “How is that, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Because affliction is followed only by ease, and likewise ease is followed only by misfortune. And one is not a believer of complete faith who is not in sorrow whenever he is not in prayer.” They said, “And why, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Because the one praying converses intimately with his Lord, and when he is not in prayer he only converses with the son of Adam.”"],[10845,"That you touch your buttocks to your heels in prayer.”"],[10846,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give good tidings and do not drive people away; and when you become angry, be silent.”"],[10847,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ shared among his companions on the day of Hudaybiyyah seven people in a cow.”"],[10848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am holding you by your waist-wrappers, saying, ‘Guard against the Fire, guard against the prescribed punishments.’ When I die, I will leave you, and I will be your forerunner at the cistern. Whoever reaches it will have succeeded. Then some people will be brought and will be taken to the left. I will say, ‘My Lord,’ and He will say, ‘They kept turning back on their heels after you.’”"],[10849,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man circumambulating the House while another man was leading him by a nose-ring due to a vow he had made, so he cut it and said: “Lead him by his hand.” And he passed by a man who had tied his hand to another person with a strap or a thread or something else, so he cut it and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Lead him by his hand.”"],[10850,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Circumambulation of the House is prayer, but God Almighty has permitted speech therein. So whoever speaks should speak only good.”"],[10851,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you stands in prayer, let him not close his eyes.”"],[10852,"The Prophet ﷺ used to call the Farewell Pilgrimage the Pilgrimage of Islam.”"],[10853,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ ramaled at the House and between Safā and Marwah only because the polytheists had seen hardship in him and his companions, so he ramaled.”"],[10854,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The pilgrim in ihram may kill the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the vicious dog, and the mouse.”"],[10855,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The son of Adam has been commanded to prostrate on seven bones.”"],[10856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a shoulder blade and said: “Bring me a shoulder blade so that I may write for you a document after which you will never differ.” Those with him among the people began to make a clamor, so a woman among those present said: “Woe to you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is making a covenant with you.” Some of the people said: “Be quiet, for you have no intellect.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are the ones with no forbearance.”"],[10857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me a shoulder blade and an inkpot so that I may write for you a document concerning which no two men will differ.” He said: “They were slow in bringing the shoulder blade and the inkpot, so Allah took him.”"],[10858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night prayer should be performed in pairs of two, and the Witr prayer should be a single unit of prayer at the end of the night.\""],[10859,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the Day of the Conquest the meat of jallāla animals, their milk, and their backs.”"],[10860,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tamattuʿ until he died, and Abu Bakr ؓ performed tamattuʿ until he died, and ʿUmar and ʿUthman ؓ” — meaning the tamattuʿ of Hajj."],[10861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the Kaʿba and said: “There is no god but Allah. How good you are, and how good your fragrance, and how great your sanctity! Yet the believer is greater in sanctity than you. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has made you sacred, and He has made inviolable from the believer his wealth, his blood, his honor, and that we should think ill of him.”"],[10862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “recited the talbiya in ʿUmra until he touched the Black Stone, and in Hajj until he threw the jamra.”"],[10863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “gave a grandmother one-sixth.”"],[10864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The excellence of knowledge is superior to worship, and the essence of the religion is piety.”"],[10865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard the voices of two men while they were saying:"],[10866,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Ruqbā is not lawful, nor ʿumrā. Whoever is given something as ruqbā or ʿumrā, it belongs to him.”"],[10867,"We arrived with the Prophet ﷺ intending only Hajj, so we entered iḥrām for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated on his mount, touching the corner with a staff he had with him. Then he turned to the watering place and said: “Draw some water for me from it.” They drew a bucket for him, and he took a sip, rinsed his mouth, then spat it back into the bucket and said: “Return it to the well.” Then he said: “O Banū Hāshim, you are engaged in a righteous work. Were it not that you would be overcome for it or it would be taken as a sunna, I would have taken part with you.” Then he went to his dwelling and addressed his companions, saying: “ʿUmra has entered into your Hajj, so release yourselves from iḥrām, except those who have a sacrificial animal with them.” And he said: “Were it not that I have a sacrificial animal with me, I would have released myself from iḥrām with you.” Surāqa b. Mālik stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever?” He said: “Rather, forever.” They were pleased by whatever conformed to the practice of the people of the Jāhiliyya. The people of the Jāhiliyya used to say: when Ṣafar has passed, the fur has grown, and the wound has healed, then ʿUmra is lawful for the one performing ʿUmra."],[10868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be rulers who are recognized and denounced. Whoever opposes them is saved, whoever keeps away from them is safe, and whoever mixes with them is ruined.”"],[10869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no zakah on working oxen, but for every thirty cattle there is a tabiʿ (a one-year-old male calf), and for every forty there is a musinn (a two-year-old cow or bull).”"],[10870,"“At the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, three were made one.”"],[10871,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Tawaf is prayer, so speak little during it.”"],[10872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever imitates in poetry, he has no morals with Allah.\""],[10873,"Safwan b. Umayyah came to Madinah and slept in the mosque, placing a khamisah (a striped cloak) of his under his head. A thief came and stole it. He went to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that the thief's hand be cut off. Safwan said: “O Messenger of God, it is his.” He said: “Why did you not say so before you brought him to me?”"],[10874,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and said: “Pay him his fee.”"],[10875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Many a teacher of the letters of Abu Jad, who is learned in the stars, will have no share with God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10876,"He mentioned the Prophet's ﷺ statement about the Friday ghusl. I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: “Should he also apply perfume or oil if he has it for his family?” He said: “I do not know.”"],[10877,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ prescribed the prayer of travel as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs, and prescribed the prayer of residence as four rakʿahs.”"],[10878,"I attended the Eid prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he began with the prayer before the sermon."],[10879,"The Prophet ﷺ passed while circumambulating the Kaʿbah and saw a man leading another man by a nose ring in his nose. The Prophet ﷺ cut it off, then ordered him to lead him by his hand."],[10880,"The Prophet ﷺ passed while circumambulating the Kaʿbah and saw a man whose hand was tied to another man with a strap, a string, or something else. The Prophet ﷺ cut it and said: “Lead him by your hand.”"],[10881,"The people used to leave in every direction, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you should depart until his last act is at the House.”"],[10882,"When the Prophet ﷺ got up at night to perform tahajjud, he would say: “O God, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Maintainer of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the King of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Truth, Your speech is true, the meeting with You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, the Hour is true, Muhammad ﷺ is true, and the prophets are true. O God, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have contended, and to You I have made judgment, so forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer. There is no god but You.”"],[10883,"God says: “And let them circumambulate the Ancient House” [Qurʾan 22:29]. And the Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated from behind it."],[10884,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever takes back his gift is like one who returns to his own vomit.”"],[10885,"The Messenger of God ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʻAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[10886,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one introduces into this community an innovation that did not exist before without dying while afflicted by it.” I myself saw Ibn Hishām when he was deposed and the agents of al-Walīd came and put a collar around his neck."],[10887,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Five things are met with five.” They said: “O Messenger of God, what are five met with five?” He said: “No people break a covenant but their enemy is given power over them; none judge by other than what God has sent down but poverty spreads among them; indecency does not appear among them but death spreads among them; none give short measure but vegetation is withheld from them and they are seized with years of drought; and none withhold the zakah but rain is withheld from them.”"],[10888,"After the takbir and after saying “I have turned my face toward Him who originated the heavens and the earth as a ḥanīf, a Muslim,” the Messenger of God ﷺ would say: “O God, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. You are the Truth, Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. O God, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have contended, and to You I have made judgment, so forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. O God, You are my God; there is no god but You.” Then after this the Messenger of God ﷺ would recite."],[10889,"A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ at Kurāʻ al-Ghamīm, but he returned it to its owner and apologised to him, saying: “We are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[10890,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his own vomit.”"],[10891,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us the Qurʾan, and he would say: “Greetings, blessed words, prayers, and good things belong to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” Yaḥyā b. Bukayr said: Al-Layth used to adopt this."],[10892,"He heard Ṭāwūs say: I said to Ibn ʻAbbās about sitting on the two heels, and he said: “It is the Sunnah.” I said: “We consider it harsh for a man.” He said: “It is the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.”"],[10893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[10894,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “Do not impose conditions of ruqba on your property; for whoever is given something as a ruqba, it belongs to the one to whom it is given.” Ruqba is when a man says: “This is for so-and-so as long as he lives; and if so-and-so dies, then it is for so-and-so.”"],[10895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of Muzdalifah is a place of standing; and keep away from the interior of Muhassir. And all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.”"],[10896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever recites the surah in which the family of ʿImran is mentioned on Friday, ﷺ and His angels bless him until the sun sets.”"],[10897,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “Allah ﷻ created this city on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and fashioned it when He fashioned the sun and the moon. Whatever faces it from the sky is sacred. It was not lawful for anyone before me; it was made lawful for me only for an hour of a day, then it returned to being as it was.” It was said to him: “This is Khalid b. al-Walid killing people.” He said: “Arise, O so-and-so, and go to Khalid b. al-Walid and tell him to restrain his hand from killing.” The man went to him and said: “The Prophet of Allah ﷺ says: ‘Kill whom you are able to overpower.’” So he killed seventy people. Then someone came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He sent for Khalid and said: “Did I not forbid you from killing?” He replied: “So-and-so came to me and ordered me to kill whom I was able to overpower.” He sent to him: “Did I not command you?” He said: “You wanted one thing, and Allah wanted something else. Allah’s command prevailed over your command, and I could not do anything except what happened.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not respond to him at all."],[10898,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: “There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership.”"],[10899,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “All of ʿArafah is a place of standing; and keep away from the interior of ʿUranah.”"],[10900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather up my garment or my hair.”"],[10901,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We were commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and we were ordered not to gather up a garment or hair.”"],[10902,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother.”"],[10903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We have not seen anything like marriage for two people who love each other.”"],[10904,"“…that your heels touch your buttocks.”"],[10905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck up hair or clothing.”"],[10906,"From the Prophet ﷺ that when he stood for the night prayer, he would say the takbīr and then say: “O Allah, Yours is the praise, the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth; Yours is the praise, the Light of the heavens and the earth; Yours is the praise, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all within them. You are the Truth, Your word is the truth, Your promise is the truth, the meeting with You is true, the Garden is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, by You I have disputed, and to You I have brought judgment. You are our Lord, and to You is the return. My Lord, forgive me what I have kept secret and what I have made public, what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed. You are my God; there is no god but You.”"],[10907,"“I scraped it off with idhkhir and wool”—that is, semen."],[10908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We were commanded to prostrate on seven limbs and not to tuck up hair or clothing.”"],[10909,"… that you place your buttocks on your heels between the two prostrations.”"],[10910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman in her howdah, and she brought out a child and said, “O Prophet of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?” He said, “Yes, and you have a reward.”"],[10911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed in blind fighting or in a stoning with a stone or a stick, his blood money is the heaviest upon his ʿāqila. Whoever is killed by his own hand, retribution is on his hand. Whoever intervenes between him and that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither ṣarf nor ʿadl will be accepted from him.”"],[10912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymūna while he was in iḥrām."],[10913,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the eclipse prayer, he said: “He recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed; and the other rakʿah was the same.”"],[10914,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a supplication that is not heard, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is not satisfied. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from these four.”"],[10915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while at Minā: “If the people of the gathering knew with whom they had settled, or among whom they had alighted, they would rejoice at the bounty from their Lord after forgiveness.”"],[10916,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while at Minā: “If the people of the gathering knew with whom they had settled, they would rejoice at the bounty after forgiveness.”"],[10917,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the ʿisha prayer one night until the people of the mosque had left, except ʿUthman b. Mazʿun—one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—and fifteen or sixteen men, not reaching seventeen. ʿUthman said, “I will not leave tonight until the Prophet ﷺ comes out, so that I may pray with him and learn what his matter is.” The Prophet ﷺ came out near the first third of the night, with Bilal, and he did not see anyone in the mosque when he heard the murmur of their speech in a corner of the mosque. He walked to them until he greeted them and said, “What keeps you sitting at this hour?” They said, “O Prophet of God, we waited for you to witness the prayer with you.” He said to them, “No nation before you has ever prayed this prayer of yours, and you have continued to be in prayer ever since.” And he said, “Indeed the stars are a safeguard for the sky; when the stars are effaced, what you are promised will come to the sky. I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I go, what my Companions are promised will come to them. My Companions are a safeguard for my nation; when my Companions go, what my nation is promised will come to it.”"],[10918,"“No one do I vouch for except the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[10919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever his prayer does not restrain from indecency and wrong does not increase from God except in distance.”"],[10920,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions “did not perform tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwa except a single tawaf, for their hajj and their ʿumra.”"],[10921,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The son of Adam has three hundred and sixty joints; for each one of them, each day, is a charity.” He said, “The good word a man speaks is charity; a man’s helping his brother with something is charity; the drink of water he gives is charity; and removing harm from the road is charity.”"],[10922,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Were it not that the Rukn has been imprinted with the impurities of the Jahiliyya and its filths, and the hands of wrongdoers and sinners, it would be used to seek healing for every ailment, and it would remain today as it was on the day God created it. God only changed it to blackness so that the people of this world would not look upon the adornment of Paradise and that it will return to it. Indeed it is a sapphire from the sapphires of Paradise, which God placed when He sent down Adam at the site of the Kaʿba, before the Kaʿba existed. The earth then was pure, and no acts of disobedience had been done on it, and it had no inhabitants to defile it. A row of angels was placed for it on the boundaries of the sanctuary, guarding it from the inhabitants of the earth—its inhabitants then being the jinn, for whom it was not appropriate to look at it because it is something from Paradise. The angels were keeping them away from it, standing on the boundaries of the sanctuary, surrounding it on every side. For that reason it was called the sanctuary, because they form a barrier between them and it.”"],[10923,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Twelve thousand will come out of ʿAdan Abyan, supporting God and His Messenger. They are the best of those between me and them.”"],[10924,"“Whoever dwells in the desert becomes coarse; whoever follows the hunt becomes heedless; and whoever goes to the ruler is put to trial.”"],[10925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “No one who commits incest with a mahram will enter Paradise.”"],[10926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is enough sin for you that you never cease to be quarrelsome.”"],[10927,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Jibril ﷺ to show himself in his true form. He said, “Call upon your Lord.” So he called upon his Lord, and a blackness appeared before him from the direction of the east, and it began to rise and spread. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, he fell down in a faint. Then he came to him, revived him, and wiped the spittle from the corner of his mouth."],[10928,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The death of a stranger is martyrdom. When he is at the point of death, he casts his gaze to his right and to his left and sees no one but strangers. He remembers his family and children and takes a breath; for every breath he takes, God erases two thousand thousand sins and records for him two thousand thousand good deeds.”"],[10929,"Ibn ʿAbbās said regarding the prostration in Ṣād: \"It is the repentance of a prophet; Allah commanded His prophet to follow him.\""],[10930,"{Those are they whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance.}"],[10931,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while on a journey and he was reciting Sūrat Ṣād, \"and he prostrated in it.\""],[10932,"In His saying \"And indeed, We have given you, [O Muhammad], seven of the often repeated [verses]\", He said, \"These are the seven often repeated [verses]\"."],[10933,"The Prophet ﷺ \"performed cupping on the top of his foot while he was fasting.\""],[10934,"\"Concession was given to the elderly man while he is fasting, and the young man was forbidden.\""],[10935,"\"Allah, may He be exalted, made the prayer obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rakʿahs when resident, two rakʿahs when travelling, and one rakʿah in fear.\""],[10936,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The prayer of residence is four rakʿahs, of travel is two rakʿahs, and of fear is one rakʿah.\""],[10937,"\"Allah made the prayer obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rakʿahs when resident, two rakʿahs when travelling, and one rakʿah in fear.\""],[10938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was aided by the east wind, and ʿĀd was destroyed by the west wind.\""],[10939,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"This is an ʿumrah from which we have benefited. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should come out of iḥrām completely. The ʿumrah has been incorporated into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10940,"The Prophet ﷺ made it an ʿumrah. They had arrived in Makkah four nights before ʿArafah, and he disliked that the Muslims should remain for four nights without circumambulating the House. He knew that if they circumambulated the House they would come out of iḥrām, except for those who had brought sacrificial animals. So he said three times: \"An ʿumrah from which we have benefited. Then the ʿumrah was incorporated into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10941,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was sent to the red and the black, while the Prophet ﷺ was sent only to his own people specifically. I was aided by fear, so that the enemy would fear me from a distance of a month or two months' journey. War booty was made lawful for me, and it was not lawful for anyone before me. The earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification. And it was said to me, 'Ask and you shall be given,' so I reserved my supplication as intercession for my community. It will reach, if Allah wills, whoever died without associating anything with Allah.\""],[10942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day before the Tarwiyah: “Our resting place tomorrow, if Allah wills, will be at al-Khayf al-Ayman where the polytheists used to draw lots.”"],[10943,"Al-Fadl was older than me, and he used to let me ride behind him, so I would be in front of him. Once my brother and I rode behind on a female donkey and reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying with the people at Arafah. We dismounted in front of him and joined the prayer, leaving her to graze in front of him, and he did not interrupt his prayer."],[10944,"He instructed that a man should not pray more than one prayer with a single tayammum; then he should perform tayammum again for the next prayer."],[10945,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over Hamzah and saw what had been done to his body, he said, \"If it weren't for the sadness that it would cause the women, I would have left him until he was consumed by the stomachs of animals and the beaks of birds, until Allah resurrects him from there.\" He was saddened by what he saw, so he said, \"If I am victorious over the Quraysh, I will mutilate thirty of their men.\" Allah then revealed in this regard, \"So if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted\" until His saying, \"They are plotting.\" He then ordered that he be prepared for burial, so his body was prepared facing the qiblah, and the takbir (saying Allahu Akbar) was pronounced over him nine times. Then all the martyrs were gathered around him, and whenever a martyr was brought, he was placed next to Hamzah and the funeral prayer was performed for him and the martyrs together with him. This continued until the funeral prayer was performed for him and the martyrs seventy-two times. Then he stood up and faced his Companions until he saw them, and when the Quran was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pardoned and forgave and left the mutilation."],[10946,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Go on military expeditions and you will gain the daughters of the yellow ones.” Some of the hypocrites said: “He is tempting you with women.” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: “Among them are those who say, ‘Grant me leave and do not tempt me.’”"],[10947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled during Ramadan and both fasted and broke his fast. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke his fast."],[10948,"Two verses of Surat al-Maʾidah were abrogated: the verse of the sacrificial animal and the garlands, and the other verse: “So judge between them or turn away from them.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given a choice in that matter: if he wished, he could judge between them, and if he wished, he could refer them to someone else’s judgment, until it was revealed: “So judge between them by what Allah has sent down.”"],[10949,"He forbade drinking from the ear of the cup and from its crack."],[10950,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was helped against his enemy with terror casting a distance of two months’ journey."],[10951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Jesus, Moses, and Abraham (peace be upon them all). As for Jesus, he was reddish, with curly hair and a broad chest. As for Moses, he was dark-skinned, large-bodied, and straight-haired, as if he were from the men of the Zutt.” They said to him: “And Abraham?” He said: “Look at your companion.”"],[10952,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”"],[10953,"A man from the people of al-Awali would sometimes invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at midnight to share barley bread, and he would accept."],[10954,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on his mount, touching the corner with his staff."],[10955,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am the city of knowledge and ʿAlī is its gate, so whoever wants knowledge should come to its gate.”"],[10956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out when he went to the Banu Qurayzah on a donkey, and with him was Jibril (Gabriel) ﷺ on a white mule with a saddle made of silk. The flag-bearer led the way and they set off for an hour, then Jibril ﷺ said, \"O Muhammad, by the One Who sent you with the truth, I will not dismount from it until it is opened for you.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So he did not go back until it was opened for him.\""],[10957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ali and Fatima while they were laughing. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ , they remained silent. The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"Why were you both laughing, but when you saw me, you remained silent?\" Fatima replied, \"By my father, are you more beloved to the Messenger of Allah?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"This is Ali, who is dearer to me than you.\""],[10958,"“We are the family of Muḥammad ﷺ.”"],[10959,"When the verse “In it are men who love to purify themselves” was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ sent for ʿUwaymir b. Sāʿidah and said: “What is this purification for which God ﷻ has praised you?” They said: “O Messenger of God, no man or woman among us comes out of the privy without washing his private part—or he said his posterior.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is it.”"],[10960,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while he was in Makkah facing toward the Sacred House, and the Kaʿbah was between his hands, and after he emigrated for sixteen months, then he turned to the Kaʿbah.”"],[10961,"On the day of Khaibar, Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the eating of donkey meat. (Using translation from Bukhārī 4217)"],[10962,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “Fear God with the fear due to Him...” (the verse), and said: “If a drop of zaqqūm were dropped into the seas of this world, it would corrupt their livelihoods. How much worse for the one whose food it will be?”"],[10963,"That he used to consider the exception valid even after a year. Then he recited: “And never say of anything, ‘I will do that tomorrow,’ except [saying], ‘If God wills.’ And remember your Lord when you forget.” He said: “When you remember.” It was said to al-Aʿmash: “Did you hear this from Mujāhid?” He said: “Al-Layth related it to me from Mujāhid.”"],[10964,"A group of young men from the Banu Hashim came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, allow us to participate in this charity. We want our share to be distributed among the people, and we will fulfill our obligations just like everyone else.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"We, the family of Muhammad, are not allowed to receive charity. It is the impurities of people. But what would you think if I were to hold onto the ring of Paradise? Would anyone be preferred over you?\""],[10965,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ “used to combine Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ during travel, without any urgent matter, or an enemy pursuing him, or fear of anything.”"],[10966,"I was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymūnah, and the Prophet ﷺ got up at night and performed ablution. I stood at his left side, and he turned me around with his hands and placed me on his right side."],[10967,"That the Prophet ﷺ “combined between Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ, in travel and in residence.”"],[10968,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange, so blessed are the strangers.”"],[10969,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night, in which a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever at night, and a believer at night and a disbeliever in the morning, and a people will sell their religion for a portion of this world.”"],[10970,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Have yourselves cupped on the fifteenth, seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first, lest the blood surge within you and kill you.”"],[10971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has three children born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant.”"],[10972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter.”"],[10973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the most beloved of deeds to Allah after the obligatory ones is bringing joy to a Muslim.”"],[10974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of the conquest of Makkah (eating) the jallālah and (taking) spoils unlawfully."],[10975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts the day of ʿArafah, it will be an expiation for two years.”"],[10976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts two days of al-Muḥarram, for each day he will have thirty good deeds.”"],[10977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not one of us who does not honor the elderly, show mercy to the young, enjoin good, and forbid evil.”"],[10978,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ and ʿAlī ؓ among the gardens of Madinah. We passed by a garden, and ʿAlī ؓ said: “How beautiful this garden is, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Your garden in Paradise is more beautiful than it.” Then he gestured with his hand to his head and beard, then wept until his weeping grew loud. It was said: “What makes you weep?” He said: “Grudges in the hearts of a people that they will not show you until they lose me.”"],[10979,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"I have been given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was given the red and black camels, and indeed the prophets were sent only to their own people, while I was sent to all people. I was granted victory through fear, as the enemy would be afraid of me from the distance it takes to travel for a month. I was given the spoils of war, and the land was made for me a place of prayer and purification. And I was given intercession, and I have saved it for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10980,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said on the night he was taken on the Night Journey: “I saw Ibrāhīm and he resembled me. I saw Mūsā, tall with curly hair, as if he were from the men of Shanūʾah. I saw ʿĪsā, fair with a medium build and straight hair, as if his head were dripping with oil.”"],[10981,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī: “You are to me in the position of Hārūn to Mūsā.”"],[10982,"The Prophet ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “I will surely kill the ʿAmāliqah in a battalion.” Then Jibrīl ﷺ said: “Or ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ.”"],[10983,"He used to recite this variant: “{Mustakbirīna bihi sāmiran tahjurūn}.” He said: “The polytheists used to satirize the Messenger of Allah in their poetry.”"],[10984,"Speech is disliked in four situations: on the day of Friday (Jumuʿah), on the day of Fiṭr, on the day of Aḍḥā, and during the prayer for rain, when the imam ascends the pulpit; he speaks until he descends."],[10985,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, how is ablution performed?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water for ablution and washed his right hand three times, then he put his hand into the vessel, then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, each three times, then he wiped his head and the outer part of his ears along with his head, then he washed his feet three times. Then he said, “This is ablution. Whoever adds to this has transgressed and wronged.”"],[10986,"When the Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between his companions, between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, and did not establish brotherhood between ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and anyone among them, ʿAlī ؓ went out angry until he came to a small watercourse and lay on his arm, and the wind blew dust over him. The Prophet ﷺ searched for him until he found him, then poked him with his foot and said to him, “Get up, for you are not fit to be called anything but Abū Turāb (father of dust). Are you angry with me because I established brotherhood between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār and did not establish brotherhood between you and anyone among them? Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Hārūn to Mūsā, except that there is no prophet after me? Indeed, whoever loves you will be surrounded by security and faith, and whoever hates you, Allah will cause him to die the death of the Age of Ignorance, and he will be reckoned for his deeds in Islam.”"],[10987,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In Paradise there is a tree,” or “There is no tree in Paradise” – ʿAlī b. Jamīl was uncertain – “that does not have a leaf except that it is written on it: There is no god but Allah, Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, ʿUmar al-Fārūq, ʿUthmān Dhū al-Nūrayn.”"],[10988,"“When the sun sets, restrain your children, for it is an hour in which the devils spread out.”"],[10989,"From Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ – I think he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ – he said: “There are two insatiable ones whose craving is never satisfied: one insatiable in seeking knowledge, and one insatiable in seeking worldly gain.”"],[10990,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Ṣād (Sūrah 38)."],[10991,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: This tribe of Quraysh used to approach women in Makkah and enjoy them in every position, facing and from behind. When they came to Madinah and married among the Anṣār, and tried to do the same with them, they objected and said, “This is something we have never been approached with.” The matter spread until it reached the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah, exalted be He, revealed concerning that: “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” [Qurʾān 2:223] – facing or, if you wish, on her back, meaning by that the place of childbirth for the tilth; he says: come to the tilth from wherever you wish. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Ibn ʿUmar said, “In her back passage,” and Ibn ʿUmar erred, may Allah forgive him, for the matter was as I have explained."],[10992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever gives the call to prayer for seven years seeking Allah’s reward, a clearance from the Fire will be written for him.”"],[10993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A single jurist is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers.”"],[10994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best of them (women) is the one with the easiest dowry.”"],[10995,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The best of them (women) is the one with the easiest dowry.”"],[10996,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever participates in forbidden bloodshed by even half a word will come on the Day of Resurrection with it written between his eyes: 'Despairing of God's mercy.'\""],[10997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in a state of ihram."],[10998,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so cleanse yourselves from it.\""],[10999,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Muslims are partners in three things: water, pasture, and fire. Its price is unlawful.\""],[11000,"A man with a wound was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, seeking his permission to lance it. He permitted him."],[11001,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Treat my uncle al-ʿAbbas well, for he is the remnant of my forefathers. Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is his father's counterpart.\""],[11002,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for me and said: \"What an excellent interpreter you are.\" And Gabriel prayed for me twice."],[11003,"When ʿUmar embraced Islam, Gabriel ﷺ descended and said: \"O Muhammad, the inhabitants of heaven have rejoiced at ʿUmar's Islam.\""],[11004,"Seek goodness and needs from people of handsome faces."],[11005,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O people, ask God for your dead, and do not announce their deaths to people.\""],[11006,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar used to place the deceased in the grave from the direction of the qiblah."],[11007,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Adorn your voices with the Quran.\""],[11008,"\"They are people who disbelieved in ʿĪsā and then believed in Muḥammad.\" {And those who disbelieve—their allies are ṭāghūt; they bring them out of the light into darkness.} \"They are people who believed in ʿĪsā, then when Muḥammad was sent, they disbelieved in him.\""],[11009,"While the Prophet ﷺ was on the pulpit, he said \"Ameen\" three times. When asked about it, he said that Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, \"Whoever you are mentioned in front of and they do not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen. Jibril ﷺ continued, \"Whoever reaches the age where their parents, or one of them, are alive and they do not earn their forgiveness, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen. He further said, \"Whoever witnesses the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen."],[11010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah and in which deeds are more virtuous than the ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah). So increase in these days the saying of Tahleel, Takbeer, and Tahmeed.\""],[11011,"We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as pilgrims, and he commanded them, so they made it an ʿUmrah. Then he said, \"If I could go back and change what I have done, I would do as they have done, but the ʿUmrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he interlaced his fingers together. So the people exited ihrām except those who had the sacrificial animal with them. ʿAlī arrived from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"With what did you enter ihrām?\" He said, \"I entered ihrām with the same as you entered ihrām with.\" He said, \"Do you have a sacrificial animal with you?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then remain as you are, and you shall have a third of my sacrificial animal.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had brought one hundred camels as sacrificial animals."],[11012,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihrām for Hajj. When he arrived, he performed ṭawāf around the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and he did not shorten his hair, and he did not exit ihrām, those who had brought the sacrificial animal. And he commanded those who had not brought the sacrificial animal to perform ṭawāf and saʿy and to shorten their hair or shave, and then to exit ihrām.\""],[11013,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man whose thigh was exposed, so he said, \"Cover it, for the thigh of a man is part of his nakedness.\""],[11014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the majority of the punishment in the grave is due to urine, so protect yourselves from urine.\""],[11015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever among you is unable to fight the enemy, or to endure the night in worship, let him remember Allah often.\""],[11016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better in the sight of Allah than Yūnus b. Mattā.'\""],[11017,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade inciting animals against one another.\""],[11018,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born on Monday, revelation came down to him on Monday, and he died on Monday.\""],[11019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk at every prayer.\""],[11020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to perform ghusl behind the rooms, and no one ever saw his private parts.\""],[11021,"\"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a ring of silver.\""],[11022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"slaughtered his sacrificial animal on the day he was prevented, at al-Tanʿīm.\""],[11023,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on a mat.\""],[11024,"From Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His saying, {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you}, he said, \"He forbade himself his concubine.\""],[11025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled in Ramadan and fasted one day until the afternoon, then broke his fast, then fasted and completed the fast until night."],[11026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf and walked briskly in the first three rounds to show the polytheists that he and his companions had strength, and walked the remaining four."],[11027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not that my community would be burdened, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer.\""],[11028,"Regarding His saying {And those who commit immorality from among your women} up to His saying {until death takes them}, he said: \"They used to be confined in houses; if she died, she died, and if she lived, she lived,\" until this verse in Surat al-Nur was revealed: {The fornicatress and the fornicator, flog each one of them with a hundred lashes}, and Surat al-Hudud was revealed. So whoever committed something was flogged and released."],[11029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a dead person is buried, he hears the sound of their sandals when they turn away from him departing.\""],[11030,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wear a shirt with short sleeves and length."],[11031,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿumrah in Ramadan."],[11032,"Allah's Messenger ﷺ said, “The first part of this matter (i.e., Islam) is prophethood accompanied by mercy; then there will caliphates accompanied by mercy; then there will be kingdoms accompanied by mercy; then there will be emirates accompanied by mercy; then they will bite at it like donkeys (i.e., they will fight over it.) So jihād is enjoined upon you; the best jihād is guarding the frontiers, and the best garrison is the one in ʿAsqalān.'"],[11033,"\"O Abu Abbas, I divorced my wife three times.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"You have disobeyed your Lord and your wife has become unlawful for you.\" Allah said, \"O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their prescribed waiting period.\""],[11034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did wipe [over the khuffs], but did he wipe after Surat al-Maʾidah was revealed?"],[11035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the pen is lifted from three individuals: the sleeping person until they wake up, the insane person until they regain sanity, and the child until they reach understanding or reach puberty."],[11036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The ruin of my community lies in three things: tribalism, belief in predestination (al-qadariyyah), and narrating reports without verification.\""],[11037,"\"If you forget the exception, then make the exception when you remember. This is specific to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it is not for us to make an exception except in the connection of an oath.\""],[11038,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I do not ask you for any reward for the clear proofs and guidance I have brought you, except that you love Allah and draw near to Him through obedience to Him.\""],[11039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the sale of spoils of war before they were distributed."],[11040,"\"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited on the day of Khaybar the use of ropes for watering one's fields, and he said, 'Water your crops,not the crops of others. He also prohibited the selling of spoils of war before they are divided, and the consumption of the meat of domestic donkeys, as well as the consumption of any animals with fangs among the wild beasts.\""],[11041,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifted a camel in his presents to Abu Jahl, with a piece of silver attached to its head, to provoke the polytheists with it."],[11042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered as a sacrificial animal during the ‘Umrah of Hudaybiyyah the camel of Abu Jahl b. Hisham, which had a nose ring of gold — that is, the rein — and he did that only to enrage Quraysh."],[11043,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to go on a military expedition in the path of Allah.” He said, “Go to Syria, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has guaranteed Syria and its people for me. And keep to Ascalon in Syria, for when the mill turns in my nation, its people will be in goodness and well-being.”"],[11044,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.\" They said, \"What about those who cut their hair short?\" He said the same in the third time, \"And those who cut their hair short.\""],[11045,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever flees from two has indeed fled, but whoever flees from three has not fled.”"],[11046,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The forerunners are three: the forerunner to Moses was Joshua b. Nun, the forerunner to Jesus was the companion of Yasin, and the forerunner to Muhammad ﷺ was Ali b. Abi Talib.”"],[11047,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Fatimah to Ali, Fatimah said, “O Messenger of Allah, you have married me to a poor man who has nothing.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Are you not pleased, O Fatimah, that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose from the people of the earth two men, one of them your father and the other your husband?”"],[11048,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Ali to Fatimah, she said, “You have married me to a poor man who has no wealth.” He said to her, “Are you not pleased that Allah looked upon the earth and chose from it two men, making one of them your father and the other your husband?”"],[11049,"The Children of Israel, when one of them was killed intentionally, nothing was lawful for them except retaliation, but for you, blood money has been made lawful. Thus this one is commanded to pursue in a fair manner, and this one is commanded to pay with kindness. “That is a concession from your Lord.”"],[11050,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Ali to distribute his sacrificial animals, so he distributed them in portions. Then he came to him and said, “Distribute their saddle blankets and hides.”"],[11051,"You disobeyed your Lord, and your wife has become separated from you. So you did not fear Allah, that He might make a way out for you and provide for you from where you do not expect. And he recited: “O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their prescribed waiting period.”"],[11052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When you pass by the meadows of Paradise, graze therein.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are the meadows of Paradise?” He said, “Gatherings of knowledge.”"],[11053,"The Prophet ﷺ would not fight a people until he had called them to Islam."],[11054,"The Jews used to say, “This world is seven thousand years, and we will be punished only one day in the Fire for every thousand years, so it will be only seven counted days.” Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: “And they say, ‘The Fire will not touch us except for counted days’” up to His saying “abiding therein forever.”"],[11055,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade sleeping before the ʿIshāʾ prayer and engaging in conversation after it."],[11056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people of Makkah, do not shorten the prayer for a distance of less than four barīd from Makkah to ʿUsfān.\""],[11057,"This verse was revealed concerning the Qadariyyah: {The Day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces: \"Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, We have created everything by measure.\"}"],[11058,"\"It was revealed concerning ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib. He had four dirhams, and he spent one at night, one by day, one secretly, and one openly.\""],[11059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Zamzam. We drew a bucket for him, and he drank, then he spat into the bucket, then we poured it back into Zamzam. Then he said: \"Were it not that you would be overcome, I would have drawn it with my own hand.\""],[11060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man will enter Paradise in which there will be no remaining people or rooms except they will say, 'Welcome, welcome to us.' Abu Bakr asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of that man on that day?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, 'Indeed, you are that man, O Abu Bakr.'\""],[11061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam. In it is food that nourishes and a healing for illness. The worst water on the face of the earth is water in the valley of Barahūt, the remnant of Hadramawt, like the leg of a locust among creeping things. In the morning it flows abundantly, and by evening it has no moisture.\""],[11062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A habitual drinker of wine, an undutiful child, and one who constantly reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise.\""],[11063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In the last days there will come people whose faces are the faces of humans but whose hearts are the hearts of devils, like ravenous wolves. There is no mercy in their hearts. They shed blood and do not refrain from any evil. If you follow them they will deceive you; if you stay away from them they will backbite you; if they speak to you they will lie to you; if you entrust them they will betray you. Their young are arrogant, their youth are reckless, and their old do not enjoin good nor forbid evil. Seeking honor among them is humiliation, and seeking what is in their hands is poverty. The forbearing among them is led astray, and the one who enjoins good among them is accused. The believer among them is deemed weak, and the sinner among them is honored. The Sunnah among them is considered innovation, and innovation among them is considered Sunnah. At that time, their worst will be given power over them, and their best will supplicate but will not be answered.\""],[11064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A habitual drinker of wine, an undutiful child, and one who constantly reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise.\" Ibn ʿAbbās said: This distressed me because believers commit sins, until I found that in the Book of Allah: regarding the undutiful child, {So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship?}; regarding the one who reminds of favors, {Do not invalidate your charities with reminders or injury}; and regarding wine, {Indeed, wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are only defilement} up to His saying {so avoid it}."],[11065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The angels rejoice at the departure of winter out of mercy for the hardship that befalls the poor believers.\""],[11066,"Al-Fadl and I ran ahead of the Prophet ﷺ, riding together on a donkey, while he was praying on the Day of ʿArafah, with no one between us and him to screen us from him."],[11067,"Muhammad ﷺ"],[11068,"He used to recite: “It is not for a prophet to be dishonest” [Quran 3:161]. “And how could it not be for him to be dishonest when he could be killed?” Allah said: “And they kill the prophets” [Quran 2:61]. “But the hypocrites accused the Prophet ﷺ of something,” so Allah revealed: “It is not for a prophet to be dishonest.”"],[11069,"“Whatever in the Quran is ‘qattala’ with a doubled letter, it is punishment; and whatever is ‘qatala’ with a single letter, it is mercy.”"],[11070,"About nabidh from earthen jars. Ibn ʿAbbās put his fingers in his ears and said: “May they be deaf if I have lied about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard him say: ‘All clay vessels are unlawful—white, red, black, and green.’”"],[11071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his life and how he spent it; about his body and how he wore it out; about his wealth and how he spent it and from where he earned it; and about love for us, the People of the House.”"],[11072,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Perhaps you will remain after me until you meet a people who deny Allah’s decree and attribute sins to His servants. They derived their speech from Christianity. When that happens, disassociate yourselves from them before Allah.” Ibn ʿAbbās would raise his hands and say: “O Allah, I disassociate myself from them before You, as Your Prophet ﷺ commanded.”"],[11073,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The son of Adam has been commanded to prostrate on seven bones.”"],[11074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Iblis said to his Lord: “My Lord, Adam has been sent down, and I know that there will be a scripture and messengers. What are their scriptures and messengers?” He said: “Their messengers are the angels and the prophets among them, and their scriptures are the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, and the Criterion.” He said: “Then what is my scripture?” He said: “Your scripture is tattoo; your Quran is poetry; your messengers are soothsayers; your food is that over which Allah’s name is not mentioned; your drink is every intoxicant; your truth is lying; your house is the bathhouse; your traps are women; your muezzin is the flute; and your mosque is the markets.”"],[11075,"The history was in the year in which the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Medina and in which Abdullah Ibn Zubayr was born."],[11076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is given a gift while a group of people are with him, they are his partners in it.”"],[11077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sees a gap in a row should fill it himself. If he does not, and someone passes by, let him step over his neck, for he has no sanctity.”"],[11078,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath and one witness."],[11079,"“The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dye with henna while in ihram and wear garments dyed with safflower while in ihram.”"],[11080,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its goodness appeared."],[11081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not sell fruit until its ripeness appears.”"],[11082,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ attended a funeral, gloom and deep thoughtfulness were seen upon him."],[11083,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Uthāya, he was brought rose-henna, and he said: “It resembles the sweet basil of Paradise.”"],[11084,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by this verse: {And by the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness} (Q 91:7–8), he would stop and then say: “O Allah, grant my soul its righteousness; You are its Guardian and Master, and the best to purify it.”"],[11085,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him and without having killed a soul, he will meet Allah light of back (i.e., unburdened).”"],[11086,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Do not keep staring at lepers.”"],[11087,"The Prophet ﷺ consummated marriage with his maternal aunt Maymūna at Sarif, and she died at Sarif.” Al-Layth b. Saʿd said: “Zayn b. Shuʿayb was as he was named Zayn (i.e., a fine man).”"],[11088,"A man manumitted a slave of his, and the freedman died, so the Prophet ﷺ gave inheritance to the manumitter."],[11089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and ʿUmrah consecutively, for they eliminate sins just as the bellows eliminate the dross of iron.”"],[11090,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, a man fought in the path of Allah, seeking reward, until he was killed. Will he be in Paradise?” He said: “Yes.” When the man turned away, he called him back and said: “Jibrīl ﷺ came to me and said: ‘Unless he has a debt.’”"],[11091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Religion is sincere counsel.” It was said: “To whom, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “To Allah, to His Book, to His Prophet, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people.”"],[11092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts one day of Ramadan, seeking reward, his fast will be such that if all the people of the world were to gather from the time the world began until it ends and give him food and drink to the fullest, he would not seek from the people of Paradise any of that.”"],[11093,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj. May I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Yes. Do you not think that if he owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would that not suffice him? For this is just like that.\""],[11094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Treat goats well, for they are a delicate asset and they are in Paradise. The wealth most beloved to Allah is sheep. And you should wear white, for Allah created Paradise white, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it. And the blood of a white sheep is greater in the sight of Allah than the blood of the two black ones.\""],[11095,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a fistula from which I constantly discharge. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When you perform ablution from your head to your feet, then no further ablution is required of you.\""],[11096,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Budayl b. Warqāʾ to Minā and he called out: \"These are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them.\""],[11097,"I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to perform ablution, and he said: \"O Allah, give him understanding of the religion and teach him interpretation.\""],[11098,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years and died at the age of sixty-three."],[11099,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted a menstruating woman to depart before performing the farewell circumambulation if she had already performed it."],[11100,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by the grave of Prophet Moses ﷺ while he was praying at his grave."],[11101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a sword whose hilt was of silver and whose pommel was of silver, and it was called Dhū al-Faqār. He had a bow called al-Sadād. He had a quiver called al-Jumʿ. He had a coat of mail adorned with copper called Dhāt al-Fuḍūl. He had a spear called al-Nabʿāʾ. He had a shield called al-Dhaqan. He had a white buckler called al-Mūjiz. He had a black horse called al-Sakb. He had a saddle called al-Dāj. He had a gray mule called Duldul. He had a she-camel called al-Qaṣwāʾ. He had a donkey called Yaʿfūr. He had a carpet called al-Kurr. He had a short spear called al-Namir. He had a water-skin called al-Ṣādir. He had a mirror called al-Mudillah. He had scissors called al-Jāmiʿ. He had a staff of shawḥaṭ wood called al-Mushawwiq."],[11102,"Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh came to the Prophet ﷺ with a basket of fresh dates that he had brought from al-Ṭāʾif and handed it to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It removes the heaviness of the chest and clears the heart.\""],[11103,"Visiting the sick on the first day is a Sunnah, and after that it is voluntary."],[11104,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \"It was prescribed for them that ten should not flee from two hundred. Then it was lightened for them,\" and he recited: \"Now Allah has lightened [your burden] for you, and He knows that there is weakness among you\" (8:66). So it was prescribed \"that one hundred should not flee from two hundred.\""],[11105,"I was among those whom the Prophet ﷺ sent ahead from Muzdalifah to Minā with the women and children."],[11106,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿUkāẓ, Mijannah, and Dhū al-Majāz were markets in the Jāhiliyyah. When Islam came, they felt sinful [about trading there during Hajj], so Allah ﷻ sent down: {There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord} during the Hajj seasons."],[11107,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever sees a gap in a row, let him fill it with himself. If he does not do so, and someone passes by him, let him step on his neck, for he has no sanctity.\""],[11108,"\"All of them were killed at Badr by death or illness, and al-Ḥārith b. Qays, who was from the Hayāṭilah.\""],[11109,"From Abū Muḥammad al-Jazarī, who is Ḥamzah al-Naṣībī, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever supports falsehood to thereby invalidate a truth has disowned the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. Whoever walks to the authority of Allah to humiliate it, Allah will humiliate him along with the disgrace He stores for him on the Day of Resurrection. The authority of Allah is the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet. Whoever is given authority over any matter of the Muslims and appoints over them a man while knowing that among them there is someone more deserving of it and more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger than him, has betrayed Allah, His Messenger, and all the believers. Whoever abandons the needs of the people, Allah will not look into his need until he fulfills their needs and gives them their due. Whoever consumes a dirham of ribā, it is like thirty-three acts of zinā. Whoever's flesh is nourished by unlawful gain, the Fire is more fitting for him.\""],[11110,"That he heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating a meaty bone, the muʾadhdhin came for the prayer, so he put it down and stood for prayer without touching water.\""],[11111,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"It is only a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alighted,\" meaning al-Abṭaḥ."],[11112,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only walked briskly in the ʿumrah because of the polytheists.\""],[11113,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"No one is given any authority except that well-being is spread out before him. If he accepts it, it is completed for him, but if he breaches it, there is opened for him that which he has no strength to bear.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: What does 'breaches it' mean? He said: \"He seeks out slips and private faults.\""],[11114,"We used to recognize the conclusion of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ [prayer] by his saying: \"Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[11115,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the first fruits of the season, he would place them over his eyes and then say: \"O Allah, as You have fed us its first, feed us its last.\" Then he would order it to be given to the youngest child of his household."],[11116,"From two women who were stitching leather. One of them went out and claimed that her companion had struck her with an awl, while the other denied it. Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled: \"The oath is upon the defendant. If people were given what they claimed, men would claim the wealth of other men and their blood. But call her\" – so recite to her: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain with the covenant of Allah and their oaths – those will have no share in the Hereafter}. He said: So I did that, and she confessed. That reached him, and he was pleased with it."],[11117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If people were given what they claimed, men would claim the wealth of other men and their blood, but the oath is upon the defendant.\""],[11118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If people were given whatever they claimed, men would claim the wealth and lives of other people.”"],[11119,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to drink honey at Sawdah’s house, then he would enter upon ʿĀʾishah. She said: “I smell an odor from you.” Then he entered upon Ḥafṣah, and she said: “I smell an odor from you.” He said: “I think it is from a drink I had at Sawdah’s. By God, I will not drink it.” Then this verse was revealed: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what God has made lawful for you?}"],[11120,"The dawn prayer was called, so I got up to pray the two rakʿahs before dawn. The Messenger of God ﷺ took my hand and pulled me, saying: “Will you pray dawn as four?”"],[11121,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “My community will drink wine in the end of time, and they will call it by another name.”"],[11122,"The Prophet ﷺ used to travel from Madinah to Makkah, fearing none but God, praying two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs."],[11123,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How can a community be sanctified when the rights of its weak are not taken from its strong?”"],[11124,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “All of ʿArafah is a standing place, but keep away from the hollow of ʿUranah. And all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from the hollow of Muḥassir.”"],[11125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Two supplications are not veiled from God: the supplication of the oppressed, and a person’s supplication for their brother in his absence.”"],[11126,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed inside the Kaʿbah. Bilāl and al-Faḍl were at the door. Bilāl said: “He prostrated,” and al-Faḍl said: “He bowed.”"],[11127,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take it, O Banī Ṭalḥah, as a permanent, enduring trust; none but an oppressor will take it from you” – meaning the guardianship of the Kaʿbah."],[11128,"The Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[11129,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were invited to a trotter I would accept.”"],[11130,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed the people with his back toward the Kaaba, between the Black Stone and the door."],[11131,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is as if I am looking at a bow-legged black man, tearing it down stone by stone,” meaning the Kaaba."],[11132,"(The narrator Qutaibah said: This tradition has been narrated by Sa'id b. Abu Sa'id in my collection): The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who does not chant the Qur'an is not one of us. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1469)"],[11133,"“My mother and I were among those whom God excused.”"],[11134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from the privy and was presented to him. They (the people) asked: Should we bring you water for ablution? He replied: I have been commanded to perform ablution when I get up for prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3760)"],[11135,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, will summon people on the Day of Resurrection by their names as a covering from Him upon His servants. But at the bridge (ṣirāṭ), God ﷻ will give every believing man a light and every believing woman a light and every hypocrite a light. When they are level upon the bridge, God will strip the light of the hypocrites, men and women. Then the hypocrites will say, ‘Wait for us so that we may take from your light,’ and the believers will say, ‘Our Lord, perfect for us our light.’ Then no one will remember anyone.”"],[11136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O boy, preserve God and He will preserve you. Preserve God and you will find Him before you. Know God in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship. Know that what missed you was not going to befall you, and what befell you was not going to miss you. Know that creation, if they were to gather to give you something that God did not will to give you, they would have no power over it, or to turn away from you something that He willed to befall you, they would have no power over that. When you ask, ask God, and when you seek help, seek help from God. Know that victory comes with patience, relief with distress, and with hardship comes ease. Know that the pen has already run with what is to be.”"],[11137,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The partner is an intercessor, and the right of pre-emption (shufʿa) is in everything.”"],[11138,"Regarding His saying: “Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied” (12:110), he said: “They were human, so they weakened and thought that they had been given a false promise.” He recited: “Until the messenger says” (12:110)."],[11139,"ʿAbd al-Razzāq said—and I do not think that al-Thawrī did not inform us—from ʿUthmān b. al-Aswad, from Ibn Abī Mulayka, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill from Zamzam.”"],[11140,"It was said to Ibn ʿAbbās: “Muʿāwiya performed witr with one rakʿa.” He said: “Leave Muʿāwiya aside, for he was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11141,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God sends down every day one hundred and twenty mercies: sixty of them for those circumambulating, forty for those performing iʿtikāf around the House, and twenty of them for those looking at the House.”"],[11142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “My basin is a month’s journey; its corners are equal, its drinking vessels are as numerous as the stars of the sky. Its water is whiter than snow, sweeter than honey, and more fragrant than musk. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst after that, ever.”"],[11143,"Some of them said: “It is inherited magic.” Their opinion settled on it being inherited magic. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he grieved, covered his head, and wrapped himself. Then God sent down: “O you enveloped in garments, arise and warn, and magnify your Lord, and purify your garments, and shun idolatry, and do not grant favor to acquire more, and for your Lord be patient” (74:1–7)."],[11144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered a walled garden belonging to one of the Ansar and began taking fresh dates and eating them while walking, and I was with him. He turned to me and said, \"O Ibn Abbas, do not eat with two fingers, for that is the eating of Satan; rather eat with three fingers.\""],[11145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered a walled garden belonging to one of the Ansar and began taking fresh dates and eating them while walking, and I was with him. He turned to me and said, \"O Ibn Abbas, do not eat with two fingers, for that is the eating of Satan; rather eat with three fingers.\""],[11146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered a walled garden belonging to one of the Ansar and began taking fresh dates and eating them while walking, and I was with him. He turned to me and said, \"O Ibn Abbas, do not eat with two fingers, for that is the eating of Satan; rather eat with three fingers.\""],[11147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no day more virtuous than another in fasting except the month of Ramadan and the day of Ashura.\""],[11148,"\"I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ prefer any day over another except the day of Ashura.\""],[11149,"The Prophet ﷺ \"did not seek the superiority of any day over another after Ramadan except the day of Ashura.\""],[11150,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not fast any day seeking its superiority over another after Ramadan except the day of Ashura.\""],[11151,"The Prophet ﷺ \"performed ablution with one mudd of water and took the ritual bath with one sa' of water.\""],[11152,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"would sprinkle water on his family on the night of the twenty-third.\""],[11153,"\"I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led from the weak members of his family, from Muzdalifah to Mina.\""],[11154,"I heard Ibn Abbas say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me ahead among the weak ones or among the heavy baggage from Muzdalifah at night.\""],[11155,"He heard Ibn Abbas ؓ say: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I saw myself last night in what a sleeper sees, as if I was praying near a tree, and as if I recited Surah al-Sajdah and prostrated, and I saw the tree as if it prostrated along with my prostration, and as if I heard it saying, 'O God, record for me thereby a reward with You, remove from me thereby a burden, make it for me a treasure with You, and accept it from me as You accepted it from Your servant Dawud.'\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So the Messenger of God ﷺ recited Surah al-Sajdah, and I heard him saying in his prostration the same as what the man reported from the words of the tree.\""],[11156,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while they were lending in dates for one year, two years, and three. He said, \"Whoever lends, let him lend in a known measure and a known weight for a known term.\""],[11157,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, Sufyan b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from ʿAbdullah b. Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while they used to give advance payments for fruits for two and three years. He said: “Whoever gives an advance payment, let him give it in a known measure and a known weight, for a known term.”"],[11158,"“I travel, should I shorten the prayer during travel?” Ibn ʿAbbas ؓ said: “It is not shortening; rather it is its complete form and the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out secure, fearing none but Allah, and prayed two rakʿahs until he returned.”"],[11159,"“The Prophet ﷺ never fought a people until he called them (to Islam).”"],[11160,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fought a people except that he called them (to Islam).”"],[11161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever learns a branch of astrology has learned a branch of sorcery; the more he increases, the more he increases.\""],[11162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent his wives ahead from Jamʿ on the night before the crowding."],[11163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send the families and the weak ahead to Mina from al-Muzdalifah."],[11164,"He informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to say that Al-Inakhah with Al-Muhasab is nothing. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only waited for it until Aisha comes."],[11165,"A Bedouin came to him and asked for a drink, so he was given nabīdh to drink. He said: What is the matter with your brothers? They serve honey and milk, while you serve nabīdh? He said: It is not out of stinginess on our part, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for a drink, so we gave him nabīdh. He said: You have done well and been generous; so do likewise."],[11166,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him ahead from Muzdalifah among the weak members of his family."],[11167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[11168,"The Prophet ﷺ sent the weak members of his family ahead from Jamʿ at night."],[11169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that only to show the polytheists his strength; so whoever wishes may do it, and whoever wishes may leave it—meaning raml."],[11170,"The Prophet ﷺ continued to say the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[11171,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I am the guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in its highest part, and a house in its lowest part for the one who gives up disputation while being in the right, gives up lying while joking, and improves his character toward people.”"],[11172,"I spent the night in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up during the night, loosened the water skin, performed wudu, then stood for prayer. I got up, performed wudu, then came and stood on his left. He took me by his right hand, turned me around from behind him, and placed me on his right, so I prayed with him."],[11173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Arafah with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him. The she-camel swerved with him while he raised his hands, not letting them go above his head. Then he continued in the same manner until Muzdalifah, with al-Fadl riding behind him. He did not stop reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrah."],[11174,"The Prophet ﷺ performed a single tawaf for both his Hajj and his Umrah."],[11175,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take good omens and did not take bad ones, and he liked good names."],[11176,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take good omens and did not take bad ones, and he liked good names."],[11177,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take good omens and did not take bad ones, and he liked good names."],[11178,"Do not go out on the day of Fitr until you have given the sadaqah and eaten something before going out."],[11179,"Ibn ‘Abbas said The Prophet ﷺ married Maimunah while he was in the sacred state(wearing ihram). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1844)"],[11180,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"],[11181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.” Abu Muawiyah added in his narration: with me."],[11182,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who among you has begun this day fasting?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Who among you has visited a sick person?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Who among you has accompanied a funeral?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Whoever combines them in one day will enter Paradise.”"],[11183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, said takbir in its corners, supplicated, then came out and prayed behind the Maqam."],[11184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you wishes to give his brother his land, let him grant it to him as a gift, or let him let him cultivate it; and let him not give it to him for a third or a quarter.”"],[11185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11186,"A man complained to the Prophet ﷺ about celibacy and said, “Should I not castrate myself?” He said: “No. He who castrates or has himself castrated is not of us, but fast and let the hair of your body grow.”"],[11187,"Many a time I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while donkeys were braying in front of him."],[11188,"On the left of the Prophet ﷺ; then he took my hand and made me stand on his right, and he wiped over my head."],[11189,"That they should spend the nights in Makkah during the nights at Mina—meaning the family of Shaybah and the family of al-ʿAbbas."],[11190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk on the day of ʿArafah, and he drank it and gave it to the one on his right to drink."],[11191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the wailing woman and the woman who listens to her, and he said: “Women have no share in the funeral procession.”"],[11192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire.”"],[11193,"Tamattuʿ in Hajj is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[11194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hating Banu Hashim and the Ansar is disbelief, and hating the Arabs is hypocrisy.”"],[11195,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: “We are the people, apart from other people.”"],[11196,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise, and there is nothing on earth from Paradise besides it. It was whiter than crystal, and were it not for the impurity of the pre-Islamic era that touched it, no afflicted person would touch it but that he would be healed.\""],[11197,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The thorns of the Haram are not to be cut, its game is not to be killed, its fresh herbage is not to be uprooted, and its lost property is not lawful to pick up except for one who announces it.\""],[11198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut in the Fajr prayer, supplicating against some people and for some people."],[11199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives a gift has more right to his gift as long as he is not recompensed for it. But if he takes back his gift, he is like one who vomits and then eats his own vomit.\""],[11200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no jalab in Islam.\""],[11201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to wipe over the leather socks until Allah took him."],[11202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting and in ihram, and he fainted. So he forbade people that day from a fasting person being cupped, out of dislike for weakness."],[11203,"From Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about semen that gets on a garment. He said: \"It is only like spittle or mucus; remove it from it with a piece of cloth or with idhkhir (a type of grass).\""],[11204,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah and his son went on Hajj on their camel and left me.\" He said: \"O Umm Sulaym, an Umrah in Ramadan suffices for a Hajj.\""],[11205,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has not performed Hajj. Can I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"What do you think if your father had a debt, would you pay it off?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[11206,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah for Umrah until he touched the Black Stone, and he recited the talbiyah for Hajj until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[11207,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ went out from Madinah to Makkah when he conquered it, and that was in Ramadan while he was fasting. He fasted until he reached Qudayd, and it reached him that the people were suffering from thirst and hardship. So he called for water and drank, and he broke his fast. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke his fast."],[11208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine two prayers while traveling: Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[11209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"For a boy, two ʿaqiqahs; for a girl, one ʿaqiqah.\""],[11210,"\"He is Muhammad ﷺ. He drew near and came down to his Lord, exalted be He.\""],[11211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two horned rams that were white with black markings. He would place his foot on their sides when he intended to slaughter them and say: \"In the name of Allah, from You and for You. O Allah, accept from Muhammad.\""],[11212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever grants a respite to a person in difficulty until he can pay, Allah will grant him respite for his sin until he repents.\""],[11213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Food on the wedding day for one day is a sunnah, food for two days is a virtue, and food for three days is showing off and seeking reputation.\""],[11214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Vehemence affects the best of my community.\""],[11215,"The Prophet ﷺ held gold and silk in his hand, moving them and saying, \"This is forbidden for the males of my Ummah.\""],[11216,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying sitting cross-legged with his buttons unfastened."],[11219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon ʿUmar while some of his companions were with him and said: \"Are you believers?\" They remained silent three times. Then ʿUmar said at the last of them: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And why is that?\" ʿUmar said: \"We hope for reward from Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Believers, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.\""],[11220,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O people, seek medical treatment, for Allah has not created a disease except that He has created a cure for it except for death.\""],[11221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Vinegar is an excellent condiment.\""],[11222,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet ﷺ entered the Kaʿbah and there were six pillars inside. \"He stood at each pillar and supplicated, but he did not pray.\""],[11223,"And Ibn Abbas said, \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , went out on the day of Eid al-Fitr and performed two units of prayer, then he went to the women and Bilal was with him. He commanded them to give charity, and they began to throw it.\""],[11224,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade uncertain transactions.\""],[11225,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no marriage except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, whether small or large.\""],[11227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly."],[11228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the last ʿIsha prayer one night until the people slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. Then ʿUmar came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the prayer.\" So they prayed, and it was not mentioned that they performed ablution again."],[11229,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he would say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that.\""],[11230,"That you perform tawaf, and if it is easy, then touch the Black Stone. The stray one who had gone astray on the road to Makkah died missing. He said: Maʿmar b. Rashid and Salm b. Abi al-Dhayyal were lost and no trace of them was seen."],[11231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal on a night of wind and rain, and he called out: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[11232,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about someone who shaved before slaughtering, and he said: \"There is no harm.\""],[11233,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted the pilgrim in ihram to wear trousers if he cannot find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks if he cannot find sandals."],[11234,"This black woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I suffer from epileptic fits and I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah for me.\" He said: \"If you wish, be patient and Paradise will be yours, and if you wish, I will supplicate to Allah to heal you.\" She said, \"I will be patient,\" then said, \"But I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah that I do not become uncovered.\" So he supplicated for her."],[11235,"I was among those who hurried in the baggage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of Muzdalifah."],[11236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family ahead on the night of Muzdalifah and commanded them not to stone the Jamrah until the sun rose."],[11237,"The beginning of hastening (al-īḍāʿ) was only from the side of the desert people. They would stand at the edges of the people, having hung their bows and quivers. When they departed, they would rattle. The Messenger of God ﷺ was seen while the base of his she-camel's ear appeared to touch her withers, and he was saying: “O people, you must maintain calm. O people, you must maintain calm.”"],[11238,"“The īlāʾ of the people of the Jāhiliyyah was a year or two years. Then God set a time limit for īlāʾ. Whoever's īlāʾ is less than four months is not īlāʾ.” The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Saʿīd b. Manṣūr."],[11239,"“The Prophet of God ﷺ prayed with the people on the day of Fiṭr two rakʿahs without adhān or iqāmah. Then he delivered a sermon after the prayer. Then he took Bilāl by the hand and went to the women and preached to them. Then, after he had left them, he ordered Bilāl to go to them and order them to give charity.”"],[11240,"They waited for the prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque, and they slept. Then we woke up three times. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and prayed ʿIshāʾ, and he said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for the people, I would command them to delay this prayer until this time.” We looked, and it was the middle of the night."],[11241,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ said, 'O sons of Abdul Muttalib, if you are given authority over this matter after me, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this house or praying at any hour they wish, whether during the day or night.'\""],[11242,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to send the baggage ahead at saḥar (the last part of the night). I was among those who were sent, meaning from Muzdalifah."],[11243,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the best of the angels? Jibrīl ﷺ . And the best of the prophets is Ādam, and the best of women is Maryam bt. ʿImrān.”"],[11244,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say seven takbīrs over the people of Badr, and five takbīrs over Banū Hāshim. Then the last of his prayer was four takbīrs until he departed this world."],[11245,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Two qīrāṭs will be placed in his balance, each qīrāṭ like Mount Uḥud,” meaning for one who follows a funeral procession."],[11246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out to some walls of the city when the day became hot, and it would be easy for him to perform purification there. If he had a need, he would fulfill it, otherwise he would perform ablution. When the sun disappeared from the horizon by the distance of a lance, he would stand up and pray four units of prayer without sitting in between, and then he would stand up and go to the mosque. Ibn Abbas said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer that you pray and we do not pray it?\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Whoever from my nation prays it, he has revived his night, during which the doors of the heavens are opened and supplication is answered.\""],[11247,"Al-ʿAbbās came to the Prophet ﷺ at a time when he did not usually come to him. It was said: “O Messenger of God, this is your uncle at the door.” He said: “Give him permission, for he has come for some matter.” When he entered upon him, he said: “What has brought you, O uncle, at this hour, and it is not your usual time when you come?” He said: “O son of my brother, I remembered the Jāhiliyyah and its ignorance, and the world seemed narrow to me despite its vastness. I said: Who will relieve me? And I knew that no one would relieve me except God, then you.” He said: “Praise be to God who put this in your heart. I wish Abū Ṭālib had taken his share, but God does what He wills.” He said: “Shall I grant you a gift?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I give you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Shall I grant you a gift?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “When there is an hour in which prayer is offered, not after ʿAṣr nor after sunrise, but between those, then perform your ablution thoroughly. Then stand before God and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah, if you wish make it from the beginning of the Mufaṣṣal. When you finish the sūrah, say: Subḥān Allāh, wa-l-ḥamdu li-llāh, wa lā ilāha illā llāh, wa-llāhu akbar fifteen times. Then when you bow, say that ten times. Then when you raise your head, say that ten times.”"],[11248,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was being cupped on Tuesday. I said: “You are being cupped on this day?” He said: “Yes. And whoever among you coincides with Tuesday, the night of the seventeenth of the month, let him not let it pass without being cupped. So be cupped.”"],[11249,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I did not pass by any group of angels except that they ordered me to perform cupping.”"],[11250,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, Iblīs has rebellious devils among the shayāṭīn. He says to them: ‘Go after the pilgrims and the mujāhidūn, and lead them astray from the path.’”"],[11251,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The key to prayer is purification, and its sanctification is the takbir, and its release is the taslim.”"],[11252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine two prayers during travel: Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha, while not pursuing an enemy nor being pursued by one."],[11253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear thunder, remember Allah, for it does not strike one who remembers.”"],[11254,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Wine is the mother of indecencies and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it may fall upon his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt.”"],[11255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Makkah to Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah when the sun had declined, and he prayed Zuhr, ʿAsr, Maghrib, and ʿIsha, then spent the night there until morning on the Day of ʿArafah. Then he went to ʿArafah and prayed Zuhr and ʿAsr when the sun had declined, then he proceeded to Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and ʿIsha there together, with no voluntary prayer between them."],[11256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you has a nosebleed during his prayer, let him leave, wash the blood off, then repeat his ablution and restart his prayer.”"],[11257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the farewell tawaf at night, or by night."],[11258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning Marwah: “This is the place of sacrifice, and every ravine and path of Makkah is a place of sacrifice in the ʿUmrah.”"],[11259,"The angels did not fight alongside the Prophet ﷺ except on the Day of Badr, and on other occasions they were reinforcements. The Prophet ﷺ had only two horses with him: one belonging to al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad and the other to Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi."],[11260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not drink as a camel drinks; rather drink in two or three breaths, mention Allah’s name when you drink, and praise Allah when you finish.”"],[11261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed the shepherds to throw the pebbles at night."],[11262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked.”"],[11263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only walked briskly between al-Safa and al-Marwa to show the polytheists his strength."],[11264,"Al-Muhassab is not a ritual; it is merely a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped."],[11265,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymuna and said: \"Why did they not take its hide, tan it, and make use of it?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion.\" He said: \"Only eating it is forbidden.\""],[11266,"A sheep died in the possession of one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not tan its hide and make it into a water skin?\""],[11267,"The Prophet ﷺ sent the weak members of his family from Muzdalifa at night."],[11268,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while fasting and in the state of ihram."],[11269,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while in the state of ihram."],[11270,"In his statement \"and upon those who are capable of it,\" he said \"they are required to do it.\" \"It is a ransom of feeding a poor person,\" \"only one.\" \"So whoever voluntarily does good,\" \"he increases the feeding of another poor person that is not obligated.\" \"So it is better for him.\" \"No one is exempted from this except for the elderly person who is not capable of fasting, or a sick person who knows that they will not recover.\""],[11271,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade al-ightiyal, then said: \"If it harmed anyone, it would harm the Persians and the Byzantines.\" Ibn Bukayr said: Al-ightiyal is for a man to have intercourse with his wife while she is breastfeeding."],[11272,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer one night, then came out with his head dripping water, and said: \"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have loved for this prayer to be performed at this time.\""],[11273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the prayer one night until part of the night had passed. Umar came out and called to him: \"The prayer, O Messenger of Allah! The women and children have slept.\" He came out with water dripping from his side, wiping the water from his side, and saying: \"It is the time, were it not that I would burden my community.\""],[11274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever sells food should not sell it until they receive it in full.\" This was narrated by Qabeessah from Hammad ibn Salamah from Amr from Ata. It was also narrated by the companions of Hammad from Hammad from Amr from Tawoos. Similarly, it was narrated by the companions of Amr ibn Dinar, and this is the correct narration."],[11275,"A man bit the hand of another man during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and the latter pulled out his front tooth. The Prophet ﷺ declared it void. This is how Sa'id b. Amr narrated it from Sufyan from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas, and he erred in it. The companions of Ibn Uyayna narrated it from Ibn Uyayna from Amr from Ata from Safwan b. Ya'la b. Umayya from his father, and likewise the companions of Ata narrated it, which is the correct version."],[11276,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once."],[11277,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that the plate be licked."],[11278,"That one should fight ten; but that was hard for them, so He removed that from them and it was reduced to fighting the enemy when they were twice as many."],[11279,"From Ibn Abbas: {It is not for a prophet to have captives} he recited until he reached {a great punishment}, meaning the spoils of Badr before He made them lawful for them, saying: \"Were it not that I do not punish those who disobey me until I have given them prior warning,\" {a great punishment would have touched you for what you took}."],[11280,"Al-Abbas used to say: \"By God, it was revealed concerning me when I told the Messenger of God ﷺ about my Islam and asked him to settle with me for the twenty uqiyyas that were found with me, but he refused to settle with me for them. So God gave me for the twenty uqiyyas twenty slaves, all of whom traded with my wealth in their hands, along with what I hope for of God's forgiveness.\""],[11281,"Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed spoils among his companions that day, and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas received a goat, which he slaughtered for himself. When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood at ʿArafa, he ordered Rabiʿa b. Umayya b. Khalaf, who stood beneath the bridle of his she-camel and was a man with a loud voice, saying: \"Cry out, O people, do you know which month this is?\" So he cried out and the people said: \"The sacred month.\" Then he said: \"Cry out, do you know which land this is?\" They said: \"The sacred land.\" He said: \"Cry out, do you know which day this is?\" They said: \"The greater pilgrimage.\" He said: \"Cry out.\" So he said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ says: God ﷻ has made your blood and your property sacred, like the sanctity of this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours, and like the sanctity of this day of yours.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ completed his pilgrimage and said when he stood at ʿArafa: \"This is the standing place, and all of ʿArafa is a standing place.\" And he said when he stood at Quzah: \"This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifa is a standing place.\""],[11282,"This verse abrogated her waiting period: she observes it in her family wherever she wishes, the words of God ﷻ {without being expelled}. ʿAtaʾ said: If she wishes, she observes the waiting period with her family, and if she wishes, she leaves, because of the words of God ﷻ {but if they leave, there is no blame upon you for what they do with themselves}."],[11283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Maymuna bt. al-Harith during that journey of his while he was in a state of ihram. The one who married him to her was al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Makkah for three days. Then Huwayṭib b. Abd al-Uzza b. Abi Qays b. Abd Wadd b. Naṣr b. Malik b. Ḥasal came to him on the third day with a group of Quraysh. Quraysh had entrusted him with expelling the Prophet ﷺ from Makkah. They said: \"Your term has ended, so leave us.\" He said to them: \"What harm would it do you if you left me to consummate the marriage among you and we prepared food for you, and you attended it?\" They said: \"We have no need of your food. Leave us.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ departed."],[11284,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray inside the House, but when he entered, he fell down in prostration, then raised his head and supplicated.\""],[11285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, saying takbir over them nine times, nine times, then seven times, seven times, then four times, four times, until he met God ﷻ."],[11286,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For a virgin, seven days; for a previously married woman, three days.\""],[11287,"Among what the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated with during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O God, You hear my words and see my place and know my secret and my open affairs; nothing of my matter is hidden from You. I am the miserable, the poor, the seeker of help, the seeker of protection, the fearful, the apprehensive, the one who confesses and acknowledges his sin. I ask You as a humble beggar asks, and I beseech You as a sinful, abased person beseeches, and I call upon You as a fearful, blind person calls upon You, one whose neck is humbled before You, whose eyes overflow for You, whose body is humiliated, and whose nose is rubbed in the dust for You. O God, do not make me wretched in my supplication to You, and be always merciful to me, O Best of those who are asked and O Best of those who give.\""],[11288,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: \"Greetings, good words, and prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\""],[11289,"He may circumambulate the House and walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa before going out to Arafah; and it is the sunnah of the people of Makkah to circumambulate the House and walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa after returning from Mina."],[11290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"All of Arafat is a standing place, but keep above the valley of ʿUrana; and all of Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) is a standing place, but keep above the valley of Muhassir.\""],[11291,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is old and cannot perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Would you pay off a debt if he owed it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being paid; perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[11292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"An ʿUmrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[11293,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not make use of its skin?\" They said: \"It is carrion.\" He said: \"Tanning the hide purifies it.\""],[11294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, I asked Allah for three things for you: I asked Him to make your standing firm, to teach your ignorant, and to guide your astray; and I asked Him to make you generous, noble, and merciful. If a man were to stand between the Corner and the Maqam, pray, and fast, and then die hating the family of Muhammad ﷺ and being pleased with them, he would enter the Fire.\""],[11295,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of snakes while in ihram and within the Haram."],[11296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters the House, he leaves forgiven.\""],[11297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection it will be called out: Where are those who reached sixty?—that is the lifespan about which Allah ﷻ said: 'Did We not give you life long enough for whoever would remember to take heed?'\""],[11298,"While I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to me: \"O boy, preserve Allah and He will preserve you; preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.\""],[11299,"O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated the House before I threw the pebbles. He said: \"No harm.\""],[11300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When people differ, justice is with Mudar.\""],[11301,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The bad example is not for us: the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[11302,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “When you sight the crescent of the month of Ramadan, fast; then when you sight it, break the fast.”"],[11303,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not see his Lord with his eyes; he saw Him only with his heart.”"],[11304,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, supported me with four ministers, chiefs.” We said, ‘O Messenger of God, who are these four?’ He said: “Two from the people of heaven and two from the people of earth.” I said, ‘Who are the two from the people of heaven?’ He said: “Gabriel and Michael.” We said, ‘Who are the two from the people of earth?’ He said: “Abu Bakr and ʿUmar.”"],[11305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and God relents toward whoever repents.”"],[11306,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the night prayer one night until people slept and woke, and slept and woke. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab stood and said, ‘The prayer.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ came out with water dripping from his head and said: “Were it not that it would be difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to pray it at this time.”"],[11307,"I said to ʿAtaʾ: A man vowed to circumambulate on his knees seven times. He said: Ibn ʿAbbas said: “They were not commanded to circumambulate crawling, but let him circumambulate for his knee seven times and for his foot seven times.” I said: Did he not command him an expiation? He said: “No.”"],[11308,"We attended with Ibn ʿAbbas the funeral of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: When you lift her bier, do not jolt or shake it, and be gentle, for “the Messenger of God ﷺ had nine wives; he used to apportion for eight and not apportion for one.” ʿAtaʾ said: The one for whom he did not apportion was Safiyyah bt. Huyayy."],[11309,"That no one should go out on the day of Fitr until he has eaten, let him do so. He said: I have not failed to eat before going out since I heard that from Ibn ʿAbbas; I eat from the edge of the tariqah. I said: What is the tariqah? He said: Thin bread, or I drink milk, or nabidh, or water. I said: How do you interpret this? He said: I heard him, I think from the Prophet ﷺ, say: They used not to go out until the forenoon had extended, and they would say: We eat so that we are not rushed from the prayer. He said: “Sometimes I went out having tasted nothing but water.” Ibn ʿAbbas is the speaker."],[11310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and ʿUmrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron.”"],[11311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A valid Hajj has no reward except Paradise.\""],[11312,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked one day at ʿUmar b. al-Khattab and smiled at him, then said: “O Ibn al-Khattab, do you know why I smiled at you?” He said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “God boasted to His angels on the night of ʿArafah about the people of ʿArafah in general, and He boasted about you in particular.”"],[11313,"O Messenger of God, I owe God a sacrificial animal, and I am wealthy, but I cannot find it. He said: “Slaughter a sheep.”"],[11314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will raise the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner on the Day of Resurrection, and they will have two eyes, a tongue, and two lips, testifying for whoever touched them with fidelity.”"],[11315,"The Prophet ﷺ applied perfume before entering the state of ihram."],[11316,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.”"],[11317,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over the prayer and other affairs of Madinah."],[11318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cover the faces of your dead, and do not imitate the Jews.”"],[11319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage about the ramy (stoning of the jamrah). He said: “Allah has prescribed the saʿy for you, so perform the saʿy.”"],[11320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or his body and conceals it without complaining to people, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him.”"],[11321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah created the Garden of ʿAdn, He created in it what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. Then He said to it: ‘Speak.’ It said: ‘The believers have succeeded.’”"],[11322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing weapons in the lands of Islam or on the two Eid days unless in the presence of an enemy."],[11323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Love the Arabs for three reasons: because I am an Arab, the Quran is Arabic, and the speech of the people of Paradise is Arabic.”"],[11324,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite aloud “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."],[11325,"Ibn Abbas said: “You have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example,” then he recited: “And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.”"],[11326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon that made the young women in their chambers hear it, and he said: \"O company of those who have submitted with their tongues but faith has not entered their hearts! Do not harm the believers, and do not pursue their faults, for whoever pursues the fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his fault, and whoever Allah pursues his fault, He will expose him, even if he is in the interior of his house.\""],[11327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Five are among the practices of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, perfuming, and marriage.\""],[11328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Cupping is for pain in the molars and for drowsiness.\""],[11329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.\""],[11330,"to leave when she menstruates.\""],[11331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides food for a fasting person will receive the same reward.\""],[11332,"\"O Abu al-Abbas, what do you say about me?\" He said: \"What could I possibly say about you?\" He said: \"I am a clerk with a pen.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The possessor of the pen will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in a coffin of fire, locked upon it with locks of fire. Then he will look at his pen: in what did he cause it to run? If he caused it to run in obedience to Allah and His good pleasure, the coffin will be unlocked from him, and if he caused it to run in disobedience to Allah, the coffin will plummet with him for seventy autumns, until the maker of the pen and the solderer of the inkpot.'\""],[11333,"about perfume and adornment.\""],[11334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of gaps,\" meaning in prayer."],[11335,"\"Beware of gaps,\" meaning in prayer, and he did not attribute it to the Prophet."],[11338,"that he heard Ibn Abbas say: \"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord, the Exalted, twice.\""],[11339,"that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him that she had been married off while she was unwilling, so she was separated from her husband. She had been previously married, and after that she married Abu Lubabah."],[11340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When my community wears light shoes with patches, men and women, and patches their sandals, Allah will disown them.\""],[11341,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade slaughtering sacrificial animals at night."],[11342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever keeps the left side of the mosque inhabited due to the fewness of its people, he will have two rewards.\""],[11343,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter.\""],[11344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr ؓ. He supported me with his own self and his wealth, and he married his daughter to me.\""],[11345,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not drink wine. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is drunk. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not be alone with a woman who is not a mahram to him.\""],[11346,"The blacks were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Leave me alone regarding the blacks; indeed the black one is concerned only with his stomach and his private parts.\""],[11347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted for eighty horses on the day of Hunayn two shares each."],[11348,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever drinks a sip of wine, Allah will not accept from him his prayers and good deeds for three days. And whoever drinks a cup (of wine), Allah will not accept from him his prayers and good deeds for forty mornings. And the habitual drinker of wine, it is a right upon Allah that He gives him to drink from the river of Al-Khabal.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the river of Al-Khabal?\" He said, \"It is the pus of the people of Hellfire.\""],[11349,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to dye (his beard), he would take some oil and saffron, rub it between his hands, then rub it on his beard."],[11350,"ʿAtaʾ said: \"There is no divorce for one who does not possess the authority to dissolve his marriage, and no emancipation for one who does not own the slave,\" mentioning that from Ibn ʿAbbas and attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[11351,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform a ritual bath.\""],[11352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding His saying {marked} [Quran 3:125]: \"It means 'distinguished.' The distinguishing mark of the angels on the day of Badr was black turbans, and on the day of Uhud red turbans.\""],[11353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no piece of land in which Allah is remembered with prayer except that it boasts over the lands surrounding it and rejoices at the remembrance of Allah, its extent reaching to the seven earths.\""],[11354,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Harshness afflicts the best of my community.”"],[11355,"A man contracted chickenpox, so he isolated himself. He washed and then covered himself, but he passed away. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, and he said, \"They killed him. May Allah kill them! Wasn't the cure for skin diseases to ask for it to be rubbed on him?\""],[11356,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"Those who willingly accept Islam are from the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth, and those who do so reluctantly are those who are captured and brought to Islam from the prisoners of the nations, wearing chains and shackles. They will be led to Paradise while they are filled with hatred.\""],[11357,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off the access to the valleys and came with the sacrificial animal, but he was unable to perform tawaf around the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwa. As for you, the people of Mecca, delay your tawaf until you return."],[11358,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, sends down every day and night one hundred and twenty mercies. Upon this House descend sixty, for those circumambulating; forty, for those praying; and twenty, for those gazing at it.”"],[11359,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “God has an angel who, if he were told to swallow the seven heavens and the earths in a single morsel, he would do it. His glorification is: ‘Glory be to You, wherever You are.’”"],[11360,"From ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas and ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the istikhārah (prayer for seeking guidance) just as he taught us a sūrah from the Qur’an: “O God, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek Your decree by Your power. You have power and I have none, and You know and I do not know. You are the Knower of the unseen. O God, whatever You have decreed for me, make its outcome good.”"],[11361,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image of a statue, and the image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection in the Fire. The Most Merciful will say to them: ‘Give life to what you created,’ and they will remain in punishment until the image speaks, but it will not speak.”"],[11362,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A safeguard for the people of the earth from drowning is the rainbow, and a safeguard for the people of the earth from dissension is allegiance to Quraysh, the people of God. When any Arab tribe opposes them, they become a party of Iblīs.”"],[11363,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Waḥshī, the killer of Ḥamzah, inviting him to Islam. He sent back: “O Muḥammad, how can you call me to your religion while you claim that whoever kills, associates partners, or commits adultery meets a great punishment, with the torment doubled for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will remain in it disgraced—and I have done all that? Do you find any concession for me?” Then God, may He be glorified, revealed: “Except him who repents, believes, and works righteousness. For those, God will change their evil deeds into good deeds, and God is ever Forgiving, Merciful.” Waḥshī said: “O Muḥammad, this is a severe condition—‘except him who repents, believes, and works righteousness’—perhaps I cannot do this.” Then God revealed: “Indeed, God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.” Waḥshī said: “O Muḥammad, I see there is a will after that, so I do not know whether I will be forgiven or not. Is there anything other than this?” Then God revealed: “O My servants who have transgressed against yourselves, do not despair of God’s mercy. Indeed, God forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.” Waḥshī said: “This is it,” and he came and embraced Islam. So the people said: “O Messenger of God, if we commit what Waḥshī committed [will we be forgiven too]?” He said: “This is for all Muslims generally.”"],[11364,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him, mercy overwhelms him. If he visits at the beginning of the day, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him until evening, and if he visits at the end of the day, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him until morning.” It was said: “O Messenger of God, this is for the visitor, but what is for the sick person?” He said: “Multiples of this.”"],[11365,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take the blacks [as brothers], for three of them are among the leaders of the people of Paradise: Luqmān the wise, the Najāshī, and Bilāl the muezzin.” Abū al-Qāsim said: “He meant the Abyssinians.”"],[11366,"“Whoever arrives as a pilgrim and circumambulates the House and walks between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, his Hajj is completed and it becomes an ʿUmrah. Such is the practice of God and the practice of His Messenger ﷺ.”"],[11367,"From the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ."],[11368,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say: “We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking the fast, to delay our predawn meal, and to place our right hands upon our left hands in prayer.”"],[11369,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “A gift to the ruler is embezzlement.”"],[11370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, ‘There is no god but God.’ When they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with God.”"],[11371,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Every inheritance that Islam found and was not divided is to be divided according to the Islamic division.”"],[11372,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives and the weak among his family, and they were moved from Muzdalifah at night; then they went on until they threw the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah.”"],[11373,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever enters the House enters into a good deed and exits from an evil deed, forgiven.”"],[11374,"That the Prophet ﷺ requested Suhail bin Amr to bring Zamzam water."],[11375,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God have mercy on those who shave.” They said, “And those who shorten, O Messenger of God?” He said, after three times: “And those who shorten.”"],[11376,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ came with the sacrificial animal and circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah before standing at ʿArafah.” As for you, O people of Makkah, delay your circumambulation until you return."],[11377,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is invalid; her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated the marriage with her, she is entitled to the dower for what he made lawful of her private part. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"],[11378,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, ʿUmar b. Qays narrated to us, from ʿAtaʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Kill the gecko, even if it is inside the Kaʿbah.”"],[11379,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, ʿUmar b. Qays narrated to us, from ʿAtaʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches ʿArafah before dawn has caught the Hajj.”"],[11380,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best rows for men are the first ones, and the worst are the last. The best rows for women are the last ones, and the worst are the first.”"],[11381,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Wine is the mother of abominations and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it may commit incest with his mother, his maternal aunt, or his paternal aunt.”"],[11382,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his wives and the weak members of his family when they departed from Muzdalifah to leave at night and then continue until they passed Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[11383,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was in ihram because of a pain he had, and he used the siwak while he was in ihram."],[11387,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died from the meat which a Jewish woman had poisoned for him, his aorta was severed by the poison at the beginning of the year, and he would say: “I have not ceased to feel pain from it.”"],[11388,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Saad ibn Abi Waqqas a piece of meat from a goat and ordered him to sacrifice it."],[11389,"Some Muslims were with the polytheists and they swelled the ranks of the polytheists. An arrow would come and strike one of them and kill him, or he would be struck and killed. So God ﷻ revealed concerning them: {Indeed, those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves – they say, “In what condition were you?” They say, “We were oppressed in the land.”} – the verse."],[11390,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were to stone anyone without evidence, I would stone so-and-so, for suspicion has appeared in her appearance, her speech, and those who enter upon her.”"],[11391,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate a shoulder in the house of Maymunah bt. al-Harith, then he went out to the prayer and did not perform wudu."],[11392,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘May God reward Muhammad on our behalf as he deserves,’ exhausts seventy scribes for a thousand mornings.”"],[11393,"The Prophet ﷺ changed the two garments of ihram at al-Tanʿim when he entered Makkah."],[11394,"The Messenger of God ﷺ assigned shares among his wives for a cow on the occasion of the sacrifice."],[11395,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11396,"The wife of Thabit b. Qays obtained a divorce, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to observe a waiting period of one menstrual period."],[11397,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Menstrual bleeding has spurts, and the blood of menstruation has an odor unlike anything else. When the menstrual period has ended, one of you should perform ghusl and then wash away the blood.”"],[11398,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was placed in his grave, Shuqran, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, took a velvet cloth that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear and buried it with him in the grave. He said, “No one will wear it after the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[11399,"Those who went down into the grave of the Messenger of God ﷺ were Ali, al-Fadl and Qutham the two sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Aws b. Khawli said to Ali ؓ, “O Ali, I adjure you by God concerning our share of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said, “Come down with the people.” So he went down, and they were five."],[11400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would deliver two sermons on Friday while standing, sitting between them."],[11401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would deliver the sermon on Friday, on the day of Fitr, and on the day of Adha from the minbar. When the mu'adhdhin fell silent on Friday, he would stand and deliver the sermon."],[11402,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any female slave who bears a child to her master is free after his death.”"],[11403,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapped in it, using its extra part to guard against the heat of the ground."],[11404,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would pray in a single garment, using its extra part to guard against the heat and cold of the ground."],[11405,"Concerning the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. We said, “Yes.” He said, “When the sun declined from its meridian while he was at his home, he would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting. If it had not declined while he was at his home, he would travel until it was time for Asr, then dismount and combine Zuhr and Asr. When Maghrib became due while he was at his home, he would combine it with Isha. If it had not become due while he was at his home, he would ride until Isha became due, then dismount and combine them.” Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn al-Miqdam said to me, “We have not heard this from Ibn Jurayj, and no one but you has brought it.”"],[11406,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey and set out when the sun declined, he would combine Zuhr and Asr. If he set out before that, he would combine them at the time of Asr."],[11407,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to mount before the sun declined, he would mount and delay Zuhr until he combined it with Asr. When he wanted to mount after the sun had declined, he would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting. When he wanted to mount at the time of Maghrib, he would pray Maghrib and Isha before mounting. When he wanted to mount before the time of Maghrib, he would delay Maghrib until he combined it with Isha."],[11408,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lot, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done.”"],[11409,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would encourage night prayer, to the extent that he said, “Even if it is one rak'ah.” Then he went out for the prayer, and there was a man praying while the prayer was being established. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two prayers together?”"],[11410,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the night prayer and encouraged it until he said: “Hold fast to the night prayer, even if it be one rakʿah.” And the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and found a man praying after the prayer had been established. And he also said: “Will you not desist? Two prayers together?”"],[11411,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “O God, grant Ibn ʿAbbās wisdom and teach him the interpretation.”"],[11412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and said, \"Indeed, Allah has given everyone their rights. Know that Allah has prescribed obligations, established practices, set limits, made certain things permissible and others forbidden, and has ordained the religion, making it easy, lenient, and comprehensive, and not burdensome. Know that there is no faith for those who do not have trustworthiness, and no religion for those who do not have covenants. Whoever breaks his promise will not receive my intercession, and he will not have access to my pond. Know that Allah has only allowed killing in three cases: a person who turns back from his faith, a married person who commits adultery, and one who kills another person, and he shall be killed in return. Have I conveyed the message?\""],[11413,"When the wind blew, the Prophet ﷺ would face it, kneel down, stretch out his hands, and say: “O God, I ask You for the good of this wind and the good of what it was sent with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was sent with. O God, make it a mercy and do not make it a punishment. O God, make it winds and do not make it a wind.”"],[11414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever goes to the authority of God on earth to humiliate him, God will humiliate his neck on the Day of Resurrection, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter.” Muslim added: “And the authority of God is the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11415,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to those who measure and weigh: “You have been put in charge of a matter in which the previous nations perished.”"],[11416,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Satan sends the strongest and most powerful of his companions against the one who does good with his wealth.”"],[11417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abū Dharr: “Which of the bonds of faith, I think he said, is most firm?” He said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Loyalty for the sake of God, enmity for the sake of God, love for the sake of God, and hatred for the sake of God.”"],[11418,"“Whoever drinks a drink that removes from him the intellect that he was given has come to one of the doors of major sins.”"],[11419,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever supports falsehood in order to defeat truth with his falsehood, the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger ﷺ are absolved from him.”"],[11420,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever combines two prayers without an excuse has come to one of the doors of major sins.”"],[11421,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever gives testimony by which the wealth of a Muslim man is made lawful to be taken or blood is shed, he has made the Fire obligatory upon himself.”"],[11422,"Narrated Ibn Abbas: The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no Muslim who takes care of an orphan between two Muslims, providing him with food and drink, except that he will enter Paradise immediately, except for the one who commits a sin that cannot be forgiven. And whoever takes care of my two dependents (i.e., his daughters), and treats them well, then he will enter Paradise.\" It was said, \"And who are his two dependents?\" He replied, \"His two eyes.\" And it was also narrated, \"And whoever takes care of three daughters, supports them, and treats them well, Allah will admit him into Paradise.\" Then a man from the Bedouins said, \"And what about two?\" He (Ibn Abbas) said, \"Two as well.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"This is the best of the hadiths, and it contains jewels and pearls.\""],[11423,"Nawfal b. al-Ḥārith sent his two sons to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to them: “Go to your uncle; perhaps he will use you for the ṣadaqāt and you may obtain something with which to marry.” They met ʿAlī, who said: “Where are you heading?” They told him of their need, and he said to them: “Go back.” So they went back. When evening came, he ordered them to go to the Prophet of God ﷺ. When they reached the door and asked permission, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: “Let down your curtain; my two cousins are coming in to me.” They told the Prophet of God ﷺ their need, and the Prophet of God ﷺ said to them: “Nothing of the ṣadaqāt is lawful for you, the people of the household, not even the water in which hands have been washed. In the fifth of the fifth there is what will suffice you, or be enough for you.”"],[11424,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No flesh that grew from ill-gotten gain will enter Paradise.”"],[11425,"“The recitation of the Messenger of God ﷺ was loud enough for whoever was in the chamber to hear.”"],[11426,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God curse whoever takes as allies other than his true patrons. May God curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land. May God curse whoever leads a blind man away from the road. May God curse whoever curses his parents. May God curse whoever slaughters for other than God. May God curse whoever has intercourse with an animal. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot.”"],[11427,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Abi ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbas, that a man clung to a debtor of his for ten dinars and said: “By God, I have no payment to give you today.” He said: “By God, I will not part from you until you pay or bring a guarantor who will pay on your behalf.” He said: “By God, I have no payment and I cannot find anyone to carry it for me.” So he dragged him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, this man clung to me, and I asked him to wait one month, but he refused unless I pay him or bring him a guarantor. I said: By God, I cannot find a guarantor and I have no payment today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will you not give him respite except for one month?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then I will carry it on your behalf.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ took it upon himself. The man went and brought him the amount he had promised. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Where did you get this gold?” He said: “From a mine.” He said: “Go, for we have no need of it, and there is no good in it.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ paid it on his behalf."],[11428,"That I should bathe, and whoever does not bathe is not obligated, and I shall tell you how this is: The people were hard-pressed, wearing wool and working on their backs. Their mosque was narrow, and the roof was only a bower. The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one hot day and had sweated in that wool until odors arose, and they harmed one another. The Prophet ﷺ noticed those odors, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O people, when this day comes, bathe, and let each of you apply the best oil and perfume he can find.”"],[11429,"“Twenty men from the clients fought at Badr alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[11430,"“Drinkers were beaten in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ with hands, sandals, and sticks.”"],[11431,"On the day of Hunayn, the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ caught on a tree while the people were gathered around him asking him for spoils. The Prophet ﷺ thought they had seized his cloak and said: “Let go of my cloak. Do you want me to be miserly? By God, if God were to give you spoils as numerous as the trees of Tihamah in livestock, I would distribute them among you, and you would not find me miserly, cowardly, or lying.” They said: “It was only a samurah tree that caught his clothes,” so they freed him."],[11432,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him in the mosque, then left. He stood, spread his legs, and urinated. The people rushed at him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not interrupt the man’s urination.” Then he said: “Are you not a Muslim?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “What made you urinate in our mosque?” He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I thought it was just one of the open grounds, so I urinated in it.” The Prophet ﷺ ordered a bucket of water to be poured over his urine."],[11433,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever cheats us is not one of us, and whoever shoots at us at night is not one of us.”"],[11434,"The Messenger of God ﷺ walked with them to Baqiʿ al-Gharqad, then sent them off and said: “Go in the name of God. O God, help them.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ returned to his house — meaning regarding the killing of Ibn al-Ashraf."],[11435,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a man who imagines during his prayer that he has broken his ablution when he has not. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Satan comes to one of you while he is praying until he opens his anus, making him imagine that he has broken his ablution when he has not. If one of you experiences that, he should not leave until he hears its sound with his ear or smells its odor with his nose.”"],[11436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a woman with irregular bleeding, and he said, \"That is a kick from Satan in her womb.\""],[11437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever brings [a horse] to the race on the day of betting is not one of us.\""],[11438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would glance to the right and left during prayer without turning his neck behind his back."],[11439,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said, \"O young man, shall I teach you something through which Allah will benefit you?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Preserve Allah, and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah, and you will find Him before you. Become acquainted with Allah in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship. When you ask, ask Allah. When you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pen has dried concerning what will be on the Day of Resurrection. If all creation strove to benefit you with something that Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to, and if all creation strove to harm you with something that Allah has not decreed upon you, they would not be able to.\""],[11440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent some sheep to Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas to distribute among his companions, and they were performing tamattuʿ. There remained a billy goat, so Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas sacrificed it for his tamattuʿ."],[11441,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that when he would dispatch his armies he would say, \"Go forth in the name of Allah, fighting in the path of Allah those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not transgress, do not mutilate, do not kill children or those in monasteries.\""],[11442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them, for all ailments and for fever, this supplication: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Great. I seek refuge in Allah, the Magnificent, from the evil of every throbbing vein and from the evil of the heat of the Fire.\""],[11443,"\"No prophet has ever had a wet dream; rather, wet dreams are from Satan.\""],[11444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever has sexual intercourse with a woman forbidden to him by close kinship, kill him.\""],[11445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If a dog laps from a vessel, it is to be washed seven times.\""],[11446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the one who makes a woman lawful for her previous husband. He said, \"There is no marriage except a marriage of desire, not a marriage of deception, nor of one who mocks the Book of Allah; and the one who has not tasted the small amount of sweetness [of intercourse] has not [validly married].\""],[11447,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever has sexual intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal. Whoever has sexual intercourse with a man, kill him,\" meaning the act of the people of Lot."],[11448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill the doer and the one it is done to: the act of the people of Lut, and the one who comes to an animal, and the one who comes to a woman within the prohibited degrees.”"],[11449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of Arafah is a standing place, and move up from the mountain pass of Safah.”"],[11450,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is more superior?\" He said, \"A gentle and lenient Hanifiyyah\"."],[11451,"Ibn Abbas asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Which religion is more beloved to Allah?\" He replied, \"The gentle Hanifiyyah religion.\""],[11452,"The verses in al-Ma'idah, {So judge between them with justice; indeed, Allah loves those who act justly}, were revealed concerning blood money among Banu Qurayzah and Banu al-Nadir. That is because the tribe of Banu al-Nadir had a higher status, so they used to pay the full blood money, while Banu Qurayzah used to pay half the blood money. They brought their dispute about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah revealed that concerning them. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them adhere to the truth in that matter and made the blood money equal."],[11453,"This verse {And do not pray loudly, nor too softly, but seek a way between that} was revealed because of those people. He said: “Do not pray loudly, lest they disperse from you, nor too softly, so that one who loves to hear it by eavesdropping without them may not hear it, perhaps they will call to some of what they hear and benefit from it.”"],[11454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his daughter Zaynab to her husband based on her first marriage, and he did not introduce anything new."],[11455,"“There is no harm and no reciprocation of harm.”"],[11456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a horned, large-eyed, virile ram."],[11457,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “A believer does not steal from the spoils.”"],[11458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered the Friday sermon standing."],[11459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man says to another man, ‘O effeminate one,’ then flog him with twenty lashes. And if a man says to another man, ‘O Jew,’ then flog him with twenty lashes.”"],[11460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of unborn fetuses in the womb, the sale of semen, and the sale of a fetus that is itself pregnant."],[11461,"The pilgrim in ihram is given a concession to kill the snake, the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, and the biting dog."],[11462,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on the two Eids before the sermon."],[11466,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sought the permission of the Quraysh regarding Al-Atirah. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we engage in Al-Atirah during the month of Rajab.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said to them, \"Engage in Al-Atirah as it was practiced during the time of ignorance (pre-Islamic era), but whoever among you desires to sacrifice for the sake of Allah, eat from it and give charity, then let them do so.\" Their practice of Al-Atirah was that they would slaughter animals and then rub the blood on the heads of their idols."],[11467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a call during the days of Mina, saying: \"Do not fast during these days, as they are days of eating, drinking, and sexual relations.\""],[11468,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The south wind does not stir a pool of rain in a valley but that it causes it to flow.\""],[11469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wear his ring on his right hand."],[11470,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honorable practice for women.\""],[11471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ affirmed Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt in two verses of his poetry, his saying:"],[11472,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting."],[11473,"Amr b. al-As ؓ led the people in prayer while he was junub. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and asked him about that. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I feared that the cold would kill me, and Allah ﷻ has said: {And do not kill yourselves. Indeed, Allah is ever Merciful to you}.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent about him."],[11474,"To a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Jew.\" The Prophet ﷺ had him flogged with twenty lashes."],[11475,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no sarurah in Islam.\""],[11476,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Provision is mount and riding camel.\""],[11477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fix a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: A man drank an intoxicant and was found disgracing himself in a pit, so he was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he was opposite the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and entered al-Abbas, who embraced him. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he laughed and said: \"Did he do that?\" And he did not ask about him."],[11478,"Ibn Abbas said: When the illness of Abdullah b. Ubayy in which he died occurred, the Prophet ﷺ came to him and they spoke words between them. Abdullah said: \"I have understood what you say. Grant me a favor: shroud me in your shirt and pray over me.\" So the Prophet ﷺ shrouded him in that shirt of his and prayed over him. Ibn Abbas said: And Allah knows best what kind of prayer it was. Muhammad ﷺ never deceived any person."],[11479,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I declared zihar upon my wife and then had intercourse with her before making expiation.” He said, “What led you to do that?” He said, “I saw her lower leg in the moonlight, and I fell upon her.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Keep away from her until you make expiation.”"],[11480,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ having declared zihar upon his wife and then had intercourse with her. He said, “O Messenger of God, I declared zihar upon my wife and then had intercourse with her before making expiation.” He said, “What led you to do that, may God have mercy on you?” He said, “I saw her anklet in the moonlight.” He said, “Do not approach her until you do what God ﷻ has commanded you.”"],[11481,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My mother died without performing Hajj and without leaving a will. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?” He said, “Tell me, if your mother had a debt and you paid it off?”"],[11482,"While Umm Salamah was one night lying beside the Messenger of God ﷺ, she got up as if she were concealing herself. He said, “What is the matter with you? Have you given birth?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “No harm. Perform your ablution and return to your place.”"],[11483,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Let the best among you give the call to prayer, and let your reciters lead you in prayer.”"],[11484,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ and ʿAʾishah ؓ used to bathe from a single vessel, and they would contend over the water.”"],[11485,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no contagion.” A Bedouin said, “O Messenger of God, we take a mangy sheep and cast it among the flock, and then the flock becomes mangy.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Bedouin, who made the first one mangy?”"],[11486,"He said, “There is no recitation in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers except the Opening of the Book.” Ibn ʿAbbas said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to recite, and the Messenger of God ﷺ indeed conveyed what was sent down to him from the messages of his Lord.”"],[11487,"A woman used to pick up dirt from the mosque, and she died. The Prophet ﷺ was not informed of her burial, so he said, “When one of you dies, inform me.” Then he prayed over her and said, “I saw her in Paradise because she used to pick up dirt from the mosque.”"],[11488,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When a parent looks at his child and it pleases him, the child has the reward of freeing a soul.” It was said, “O Messenger of God, what if he looks three hundred and sixty times?” He said, “God is greater.”"],[11489,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The mother of a child is free, even if it is a miscarriage.”"],[11490,"“Indeed God ﷻ favored Muhammad over the inhabitants of the heavens and over the inhabitants of the earth.” A man said to him, “O Abu ʿAbbas, what is his favor over the inhabitants of the heavens?” He said, “God ﷻ says to the inhabitants of the heavens, {And whoever of them says, ‘I am a god besides Him,’ that one We shall recompense with Hell. Thus do We recompense the wrongdoers.} And God ﷻ said to Muhammad ﷺ, {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that God may forgive you your past and future sins.} — the verse. It was said to him, “O Abu ʿAbbas, what is his favor over the prophets?” He said, “God ﷻ says, {And We did not send any messenger except with the tongue of his people.} And God ﷻ said to Muhammad ﷺ, {And We have not sent you except as a bringer of good tidings and a warner to all mankind.} So God sent him to humans and jinn.”"],[11491,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers, and he did not command us, though he had conveyed [the message]."],[11492,"I was at the side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day the sun eclipsed, and I did not hear him recite."],[11493,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood for a long while, then bowed for a long while, then stood for a long while, then bowed for a long while, then prostrated, then repeated the same."],[11494,"When this verse was revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}, Persia sent to Quraysh: 'Dispute with Muhammad and say to him: What you slaughter with your own hand using a knife is lawful, but what Allah slaughters with a sword of gold is unlawful.' Then this verse was revealed: {And indeed the devils inspire their allies to dispute with you}. He said: 'The devils are from Persia and their allies are from Quraysh.'"],[11495,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: Allah ﷻ said: 'Whoever knows that I have power to forgive sins, I forgive him and do not care, as long as he does not associate anything with Me.'"],[11496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I would love for it to be in the heart of every person of my Ummah,' meaning Tabāraka alladhī bi-yadihi al-mulk."],[11497,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever's religion differs from the religion of the Muslims, strike his neck.' And he said: 'When he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no way against him unless he commits something for which his prescribed punishment is carried out.'"],[11498,"One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ died. Ishaq said: I think he named her Safiyyah bt. Huyayy in Madinah. So I went to Ibn Abbas and informed him, and he prostrated. I said to him: 'Do you prostrate when the sun has not yet risen?' Ibn Abbas said: 'May you have no mother! Do you not know that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"When you see a sign, prostrate\"? And what sign is greater than the Mothers of the Believers departing from among us while we are still alive?'"],[11499,"\"Indeed, Muhammad ﷺ has seen his Lord.\" Ikrimah said, \"O Abu Abbas, does Allah not say: 'Vision perceives Him not, but He perceives [all] vision'?\" Ibn Abbas replied, \"I swear by your mother, that is only when He is in a manner that cannot be comprehended by sight.\""],[11500,"The spear was planted in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and he prayed toward it while women on camels passed beyond it."],[11501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every bond and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my bond and lineage.'"],[11502,"The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Abbas: 'O my uncle, shall I not teach you? Shall I not grant you? Shall I not tell you? Shall I not do for you ten qualities which, if you do them, Allah will forgive your sins: the first of them and the last, the old and the new, the secret and the open, the small and the great, the erroneous and the deliberate. You should pray four rakʿahs, reciting in each rakʿah the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation in the first rakʿah, say while standing: \"Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great\" fifteen times. Then bow and say it ten times while bowing. Then raise your head and say it ten times while standing. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times while sitting. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five. You do that in four rakʿahs. If your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of ʿAlij, Allah would forgive them for you.'"],[11503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does one plunder a valuable plunder while he is a believer.'"],[11504,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on a carpet."],[11505,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Seek help through the midday nap for standing in prayer at night, and through eating the pre-dawn meal for fasting during the day.\""],[11506,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not come to women at night,\" meaning when one of you returns from a journey, he should not come to his wife except during the day. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey, and two men went ahead after the statement of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they came to their wives, and each one found a man with his wife."],[11507,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood.\""],[11508,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The death of a stranger is martyrdom.\""],[11509,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs: the ʿumrah of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, the ʿumrah of al-Qaḍāʾ the following year, his third ʿumrah from al-Jiʿrānah, and his fourth ʿumrah which was with his ḥajj."],[11510,"\"O Messenger of God, my mother died without making a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[11511,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ that his mother had died, \"Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I have a garden of palms, and I call you as witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf.\" Rawḥ said: Al-makhrafah is palm trees."],[11512,"About one [group], they reached al-Rawḥāʾ and said, \"You did not kill Muḥammad, nor did you mount the maidens with full breasts behind you. Evil is what you did.\" That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called the people to arms, and they responded until they reached Ḥamrāʾ al-Asad or Biʾr Abī ʿUyaynah. Then God, blessed and exalted, revealed: {Those who responded to God and the Messenger after the wound had befallen them}. Abū Sufyān had said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Your appointment is the season of Badr, where you killed our companions.\" So as for the coward, he turned back, and as for the brave one, he took up the equipment of fighting and trade. They came to him and found no one there, and they engaged in trading. Then God, blessed and exalted, revealed: {So they returned with favor from God and bounty, no harm having touched them}."],[11513,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Its thorny trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be startled, its fresh herbage shall not be cut, and its lost property is not lawful except to one who announces it.\" Al-ʿAbbās said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\" He said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\""],[11514,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God has made Makkah sacred, and it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day, then it is sacred by God's sanctity. Its trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be startled, and its fresh herbage shall not be cut.\" Al-ʿAbbās said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\" He said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\""],[11515,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God's anger is severe against the one whom the Messenger of God ﷺ has killed, and against the one who made the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ bleed.\""],[11516,"Ali paid Fatimah's mahr with an iron coat of mail."],[11517,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever listens to a people’s conversation while they dislike it will have molten lead poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever pretends to have seen a dream that he did not see will be charged with tying a knot between two grains of barley.”"],[11518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked a man, “Where did you stay?” He said, “With so-and-so (a woman).” He said, “Did she close her door on you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that."],[11519,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you stay with so-and-so and enter upon her?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that."],[11520,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “I marvel at the patience and generosity of my brother Yusuf, may Allah forgive him. When they sent to him to ask about the dream, had I been in his place I would not have done so until I came out. And I marvel at his patience and generosity, may Allah forgive him: he was summoned to come out, but he did not come out until he told them his excuse. Had I been in his place I would have hurried to the door. Were it not for the word, he would not have stayed in prison so long when he sought deliverance from other than Allah, in His saying: {Mention me in the presence of your lord}.”"],[11521,"In His saying {And We appointed not the vision which We showed thee but as a trial for mankind}, He said, \"It is a vision that the Prophet ﷺ saw on the night of his ascension, and it is not a dream.\""],[11522,"The moon was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: “The moon has been bewitched.” Then the verse was revealed: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split} up to His saying {continuing}."],[11523,"Ali entered upon Fatimah on the day of Uhud and said: “Take this sword, it is not blameworthy.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “If you fought well, Sahl b. Hunayf and Abu Dujanah Simak b. Kharashah also fought well.”"],[11524,"Huyayy b. Akhtab and Kaʿb b. al-Ashraf came to Makkah to Quraysh and made a pact with them to fight the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said to them: “You are the people of ancient knowledge and the people of the Book, so tell us about us and about Muhammad.” They said: “What are you and what is Muhammad?” They said: “We slaughter the humped camels, give milk to drink mixed with water, free the captives, give water to the pilgrims, and maintain ties of kinship.” They said: “And what is Muhammad?” They said: “A solitary man who cut off our ties of kinship, and the thieves of the pilgrims, the Banu Ghifar, followed him.” They said: “Rather, you are better than him and more guided in the path.” Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Book, believing in jibt and taghut} to the end of the verse."],[11525,"“May you have no mother! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is sufficed by someone better than you.”"],[11526,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah curse the men who imitate women and the women who imitate men.”"],[11527,"“We used to eat, drink, bathe, and go out, then go out to the prayer place.”"],[11528,"I saw ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas eating at Arafah for some time, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fast it, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar.”"],[11529,"that he should make himself steadfast — one man against ten — when the Muslims were few. When the Muslims became many, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded a man to be steadfast against two men, ten against twenty, and one hundred against two hundred.”"],[11530,"The first thing revealed to the Prophet ﷺ was that it was said to him: Cover yourself. After that his private parts were never seen."],[11531,"The Prophet ﷺ went out happily and said, \"Indeed, Allah has increased for you a prayer, and it is the Witr prayer.\""],[11532,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say anything improper. I forbade you from the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat and keep some. I forbade you from nabīdh, so drink, but do not drink anything intoxicating.”"],[11533,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed while wearing his sandals.\""],[11534,"that the Prophet ﷺ forbade sales involving uncertainty (gharar)."],[11535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in a house wearing only a waist-wrapper, which he had thrown between his legs, with his thighs exposed. Abu Bakr came seeking permission to enter, so he granted him permission and he entered. Then Umar came, so he granted him permission and he entered. Then Uthman came, so he granted him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he rose quickly and entered the inner room. That was hard for Aisha. When the people left, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar entered and you did not change your state, but when Uthman entered you stood up. He said: “O Aisha, should I not feel shy before one before whom the angels feel shy? Indeed the angels feel shy before Uthman.”"],[11536,"that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.” Abu Kurayb added in his hadith: Then Umar woke up and went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam that day. Abu Kurayb said in his hadith: “O Allah, make Islam mighty.”"],[11537,"that a man prayed alone behind the rows, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to repeat the prayer."],[11538,"The people �— the people took their due from us."],[11539,"“They were nine men from the people of Nasibin.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them messengers to their people."],[11540,"“The last funeral prayer over which the Prophet ﷺ prayed, he said four takbirs over it.”"],[11541,"their elders hear from their young.” It was said to Ibn Abbas: Why is that? He said: “Because the young heard and the elders did not hear.”"],[11542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be guarded, so his uncle, Abu Talib, would send men from the Banu Hashim to guard him every day until this verse was revealed: \"O Messenger, convey that which has been revealed to you from your Lord\" until the statement of Allah: \"And Allah will protect you from the people.\" So his uncle wanted to send someone to guard him, but he said, \"O uncle, Allah has protected me from the jinn and mankind.\""],[11543,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted the testimony of a Bedouin regarding the sighting of the crescent of Ramadan."],[11544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting and in ihram. A man called Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage and interceded for him with his masters."],[11545,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Loyalty (wala') belongs to the one who sets free.\""],[11546,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Loyalty (wala') belongs to the one who sets free.\""],[11547,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The best with which you can dye gray hair is henna and katam.\""],[11548,"\"Visiting a sick person once is a sunnah; anything more is supererogatory.\""],[11549,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar and cooked their meat. \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots to be overturned and forbade their meat that day.\""],[11550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Mount Hira and the mountain began to shake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stay firm, O Hira, for there is nothing upon you but a prophet, a truthful one or a martyr.\" With him were the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Zubayr, Abdul Rahman ibn Awf, Saad, and Sa'id ibn Zaid ibn Amr ibn Nufayl."],[11551,"\"The Prophet ﷺ stayed after the conquest for seventeen days praying two rak'ahs.\""],[11552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the 'Asr prayer with three rak'ahs and forgot one. He left and entered upon one of his wives. Then a man from his Companions called Dhu al-Shimalayn entered upon him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened?\" He said: \"What is that?\" He said: \"You prayed three.\" So he took him by the hand and went out to the people who had been with him and said: \"Did Dhu al-Yadayn speak the truth?\" They said: \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"He claims that I prayed three.\" They said: \"He has spoken truthfully. We thought that you had been commanded something regarding that.\" \"So he led them in one rak'ah, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[11553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The sacrificial animal (adha) is obligatory on me and sunnah for you.\""],[11554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let none of you stand in a place where a man is killed unjustly, for the curse descends upon those who are present when they do not defend him. And let none of you stand in a place where someone is struck unjustly, for the curse descends upon those who are present when they do not defend him.\""],[11555,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions were swimming in a pool. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Let each man among you swim to his companion.\" So each man swam to his companion, and the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr remained. The Prophet ﷺ swam to Abu Bakr until he embraced him and said: \"I am to my companion, I am to my companion.\""],[11556,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you pray, raise your lower garments, for whatever of your lower garments touches the ground is in the Fire.\""],[11557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and the masculine women, and the woman who tattoos and the woman who asks to be tattooed, and the woman who extends hair and the woman who asks to have it extended."],[11558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A believer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he drink alcohol while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer.\""],[11559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of qadar, for it is a branch of Christianity.\""],[11560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring was heard, then he got up and prayed without performing ablution."],[11561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two groups of my community have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.\""],[11562,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the women who imitate men and the effeminate men."],[11563,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , ascended the pulpit with a thick bandage wrapped around his head. He praised and extolled Allah, then he said, \"Indeed, people are increasing in number while the Ansar (the helpers) are decreasing to the point where they will be like salt in a dish. So whoever among you assumes a position of authority and benefits some people while harming others, let him accept the good deeds of the righteous and overlook the mistakes of others.\" This was the last sermon that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , delivered before he passed away."],[11564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah: \"Allah, may He be glorified, will not punish you nor your child.\""],[11565,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day to his companions: \"Whom do you count as martyrs among you?\" They said: \"Whoever is killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, is a martyr.\" He said: \"The martyrs of my community would then be few. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the man who dies on his bed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the one who dies of a stomach ailment is a martyr; the one who is bitten is a martyr; the drowned one is a martyr; the one who suffocates is a martyr; the one mauled by a wild beast is a martyr; the one who falls from his mount is a martyr; the one killed by a collapsing building is a martyr; the one with pleurisy is a martyr; and the woman in childbirth whom her child kills, her child will drag her by her umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[11566,"Allah did not reveal {O you who believe} except that Ali is its chief and its noble one. And Allah reproached the companions of Muhammad ﷺ in more than one place, and He mentioned Ali only with good."],[11567,"When the women pledged not to display themselves as in the first ignorance, a woman said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I see you impose on us that we not display ourselves, but so-and-so has helped me and her brother has died.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go and help her, then come and pledge to me.\""],[11568,"\"I see that you have been made forbidden to me, so go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; perhaps you may seek something to return you to me.\" So she went, and he sat waiting for her at the edge of the well. She came to the Prophet ﷺ while a hairdresser was combing his head. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Aws b. al-Samit, as you know, is weak in judgment and unable, and he has declared zihar from me, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The most deserving of being shown kindness for good, if it were I, or to show kindness for good, if it were him, is he. He has declared zihar from me, O Messenger of Allah, so seek something to return me to him, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He said: \"O Khuwaylah, we have not been commanded anything regarding your matter, and if we are commanded, I will inform you.\" While his hairdresser had finished one side of his head and started the other, Allah, may He be glorified, revealed, and when revelation came upon him his face would turn dark until he felt its coolness, and when it was lifted his face returned white like a heart. Then he spoke with what he was commanded. The hairdresser said to her: \"O Khuwaylah, I think it is now about your matter.\" She was seized by a shiver; a trembling overcame her, then she said: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from anything being sent down about me except good, for I sought from Your Messenger only good.\" When it was lifted from him, he said: \"O Khuwaylah, Allah has revealed about you and your husband: {Allah has heard the words of the woman who argues with you concerning her husband} up to His words {then return to what they said, then freeing a slave before they touch each other}.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no servant other than me, and I have no servant other than him.\" He said: {And whoever does not find, then fasting two consecutive months}. She said: \"By Allah, if he does not eat twice a day his sight dims.\" He said: {And whoever is unable, then feeding sixty poor people}. She said: \"By Allah, we have nothing in a day except an uqiyyah.\" He said: \"Then tell him to go to so-and-so and take from him half a wasq of dates and give it in charity to sixty poor people and take you back.\" She said: \"So I came, and when he saw me he said: 'What is with you?' I said: 'Good, and you are blameworthy. You have been commanded to go to so-and-so and take from him half a wasq of dates and give it in charity to sixty poor people and take me back.' So he went running until he brought it.\" She said: \"And I knew him before that as unable to carry on his back five sa's due to weakness.\""],[11569,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us in the mosque of al-Khayf. He praised Allah and mentioned Him as He deserves, then said: \"Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah will gather his affairs, place his richness before his eyes, and the world will come to him submissively. And whoever makes the world his concern, Allah will scatter his affairs, place his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world will come to him except what is written.\""],[11570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution after the full bath is not one of us.\""],[11571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallālah sheep, the price of a dog, the stud fee of a stallion, and the earnings of a cupper."],[11572,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the people who are satiated in this world will be the people of hunger in the Hereafter tomorrow.\""],[11573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Adhere to sorrow, for it is the key to the heart.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how is sorrow?\" He said: \"Make yourselves hungry with hunger and thirsty.\""],[11574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Mūsā b. ʿImrān passed by a man while he was writhing, so he stood calling upon Allah to heal him. It was said to him: 'O Mūsā, what afflicts him is not a share from Iblīs; rather, he made himself hungry for Me. He is the one who sees that I look at him every day many times. I marvel at his obedience to Me. So command him to supplicate for you, for he has with Me every day a supplication.'\""],[11575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever angers Allah in pleasing people, Allah will be angry with him and make those whom he pleased angry with him in His displeasure. And whoever pleases Allah in angering people ؓ, He will be pleased with him and make those whom he angered pleased with him in His pleasure, until He beautifies him and beautifies his speech and action in his eye.\""],[11578,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have committed adultery with my wife while she was menstruating.\" So he ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."],[11579,"\"There is no harm in cupping for the fasting person; it was only disliked because of weakness.\""],[11580,"\"It is the Mother of the Book.\""],[11581,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be sincere to one another in knowledge, for the betrayal of one of you in his knowledge is more severe than his betrayal in his wealth, and indeed Allah, exalted is He, will question you on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11582,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will a town be destroyed while the righteous are in it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" It was said: \"Why, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Because of their negligence and their silence regarding the disobedience of Allah.\""],[11583,"While Ṣafwān b. Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque with his cloak under his head, a man came and pulled out his cloak and took it. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that his hand be cut. He said: \"I did not think that my cloak would cause the hand of a Muslim to be cut because of it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why not before you brought him to me?\""],[11584,"The Prophet ﷺ left Madinah for Makkah and fasted until he reached Qudayd. A vessel of milk was brought to him, so he broke his fast while on his mount, and it was Ramadan, and the people broke their fast. Those who broke their fast said to those who had not broken their fast: \"Break your fast, O disobedient ones.\""],[11585,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ that he was asked about a woman who made a vow upon herself that she would certainly perform Hajj walking. He ordered her to perform Hajj riding."],[11586,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not fast before Ramadan; fast at its sighting and break your fast at its sighting. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty days.\""],[11587,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the circuit between al-Safa and al-Marwa on his mount."],[11588,"\"Those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves\" — they [the angels] said, \"In what condition were you?\" They said, \"We were oppressed in the land.\" They said, \"Was not God's earth spacious enough for you to emigrate therein?\" Those — their abode is Hell, and evil is the destination. He said: They were a group of Muslims in Makkah who went out with a group of the polytheists to fight and were killed alongside them, so this verse was revealed: \"Except the oppressed among men, women, and children who cannot devise a plan and are not directed to a way — for those, perhaps God will pardon them.\" Thus God excused those among them who had an excuse and destroyed those who had no excuse. Ibn Abbas said: I and my mother were among those who had an excuse."],[11589,"He said to his family: Carry me and take me out of the land of the polytheists to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: He died on the way before reaching the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Then the revelation came down: \"And whoever leaves his home emigrating to God and His Messenger,\" until he reached \"God is Forgiving, Merciful.\""],[11590,"In His saying ﷻ {And do not raise your voice in your prayer, nor be silent therein}, He said, \"Whenever he prayed, he raised his voice.\""],[11591,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: \"He is one-eyed, with curly hair, of a fair ruddy complexion, glowing white, as if his head is a serpent. He most resembles ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan among the people. But the utmost destruction — the utmost destruction — is that he is one-eyed, and that your Lord, Exalted is He, is not one-eyed.\""],[11592,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Dajjal has curly hair, is of a fair ruddy complexion, moon-like in brightness, as if his head is a branch of a tree. His left eye is obliterated, and the other is like a floating grape. The person who most resembles him is ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan. As for the utter destruction — the utter destruction — he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed.\""],[11593,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Dajjal has curly hair, is of a fair ruddy complexion, moon-like in brightness, as if his head is a branch of a tree. His left eye is obliterated, and the other is like a floating grape. The person who most resembles him is ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan. As for the utter destruction — the utter destruction — he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed.\""],[11594,"A woman from among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed a full bath after major ritual impurity. The Prophet ﷺ came and performed ablution from the leftover water of her bath. She said, \"I bathed from it.\" He said: \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[11595,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came one day to bathe, and one of his wives said, \"O Messenger of God, it is the leftover of my bath.\" He said: \"Water does not become impure.\""],[11596,"One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ bathed in a large basin. The Prophet ﷺ came to perform ablution from it, or to bathe. She said to him, \"O Messenger of God, I was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Water is not made impure.\""],[11597,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade taking a living creature as a target."],[11598,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a people who had set up a pigeon and were shooting at it, and he said: \"Do not take a living creature as a target.\""],[11599,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar who had set up a pigeon as a target and were shooting at it. He said: “Do not take anything possessed of a soul as a target.”"],[11600,"These were men who had embraced Islam from the people of Makkah and wanted to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gained understanding of the religion, they wanted to punish them, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, indeed among your spouses and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them. But if you pardon, and overlook, and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.}"],[11601,"A woman embraced Islam during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. Then her first husband came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I embraced Islam along with her, and she knew of my embracing Islam along with her.” So the Prophet ﷺ took her away from her second husband and returned her to her first husband."],[11602,"“Amusing themselves and turning away from it.”"],[11603,"“The prophets were from the Children of Israel except for ten: Nuh, Hud, Lut, Shuʿayb, Ibrahim, Ismaʿil, Ishaq, ʿIsa, and Muhammad ﷺ and upon them all be peace. And there is no prophet who had two names except ʿIsa and Yaʿqub (peace be upon them).”"],[11604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let the beards grow full and trim the moustaches.” He said: “And Ibrahim ﷺ , the intimate friend of the Most Merciful, used to let his beard grow full and trim his moustache.”"],[11605,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to trim his mustache, and that Ibrahim Al-Khalil (Abraham) used to trim his mustache."],[11606,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that on buried treasure one-fifth is due.”"],[11607,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘A righteous dream is one of the seventy parts of prophecy.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3897)"],[11608,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A man should not have skin-to-skin contact with a man, nor a woman with a woman.”"],[11609,"They said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of those who died while they were praying toward Jerusalem?” So Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah would never let your faith be lost. Indeed Allah is to all people Kind and Merciful.}"],[11610,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, what of those who died while drinking wine?” So it was revealed: {There is no sin upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they have eaten} the verse."],[11611,"A man from Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ with a flock of sheep, and he greeted them. They said: “He only greeted you to seek protection.” So they went to him, killed him, and took his sheep. Then they brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, when you travel in the way of Allah, verify} up to His saying {Thus you were before.}"],[11612,"Regarding His saying {Our Lord, we have believed, so write us down among the witnesses}, he said: “With Muhammad and his nation, for they have borne witness that he conveyed, and they have borne witness for the messengers that they conveyed.”"],[11613,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ after he finished at Badr, “Take the caravan; there is nothing beyond it.” Al-ʿAbbas said, while he was a captive in his bonds, “It is not fitting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Why?” He said, “Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you.”"],[11614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “People of my community will certainly recite the Qurʾan, and they will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game.”"],[11615,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to set out on a journey, he would say, “O Allah, You are the companion in the journey and the successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from difficulty in the journey and sorrow on the return. O Allah, contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us.” And when he returned, he would say, “Returning, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord.” And when he entered upon his family, he would say, “A return, a return to our Lord, a repentance that leaves no sin upon us.”"],[11616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever builds a wall, let him support it against his brother’s wall.”"],[11617,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “If you disagree about the path, then measure seven cubits, and do not make it less than that.”"],[11618,"The Prophet ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep and said it was well-cooked. Then he wiped his hand with a wipe and prayed."],[11619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand on a cloth that was beneath him, then stood and prayed."],[11620,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Yes.” He said, “There is no alliance in Islam, and every alliance made in the Jahiliyyah is only strengthened by Islam in intensity and force.”"],[11621,"“When you prostrate, press your hands to the ground.” Sharik added, “For you have been commanded to do that.”"],[11622,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “By Allah, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by Allah, I will certainly raid Quraysh.” Then he said the third time, “If Allah wills.”"],[11623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a caravan that had arrived containing some awqiyah of gold, and he gave it as charity to the widows of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib. He said, “I will not buy something for which I do not have its price.”"],[11624,"ʿAʾishah bought Barīrah from the Ansar to set her free, and they stipulated her walaʾ for themselves. She granted them that. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she informed him, and he said, “Walaʾ is only for the one who sets free.” Then he ascended the pulpit and said, “What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Any condition not in the Book of Allah is rejected, even if it is a hundred conditions.” Barīrah had a husband, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice: if she wished, she could remain with her husband as she was, and if she wished, she could separate from him. She separated from him. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered and saw a leg of a sheep and said to ʿAʾishah, “Will you not cook this meat for us?” She said, “It was given as charity to Barīrah, and she gave it to us as a gift.” He said, “Cook it, for it is charity for her and a gift for us.”"],[11625,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and said, “Expel them from your homes.”"],[11626,"The Prophet ﷺ decided to divorce her. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to Aisha.' He did so, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame} upon them both if they make terms of peace between themselves; and peace is better. And whatever they agree upon by mutual consent is permissible."],[11627,"No, by Allah, I will never commit adultery. Then was revealed: {And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution}."],[11628,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ formed brotherhood among his Companions, so they began inheriting from each other because of that, until the verse was revealed: \"And those with close relationship are more entitled to inheritance from one another.\" So they started inheriting based on kinship."],[11629,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted during travel and broke his fast."],[11630,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, 'Give me a handful of pebbles.' He gave him the handful of pebbles, and the Prophet threw them at the faces of the people until none of them remained except that their eyes were filled with pebbles, and then the verse was revealed, 'And you did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw.'\""],[11631,"The Prophet ﷺ and those with him prayed towards Jerusalem for sixteen months, then the qiblah was changed afterwards."],[11632,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah (small palm-fiber mat)."],[11633,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a reed mat."],[11634,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete the number, and the month is twenty-nine.'"],[11635,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not precede the month. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If there is an obstruction between you and it, then complete the number.'"],[11636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty.'"],[11637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not anticipate the month. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete the number.'"],[11638,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began speaking with clear speech. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11641,"“Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom, and part of eloquence is sorcery.”"],[11642,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom.”"],[11643,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom, and indeed, part of eloquence is sorcery.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to quote verses of poetry."],[11644,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no contagion, no bad omen in birds, no hāmah, and no ṣafar.” A man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and throw it among the flock, and then the flock becomes mangy.” He said, “Then who infected the first one?”"],[11645,"“O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died,” meaning a sheep. He said, “Why did you not take its skin?” They said, “Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “Allah only said: {Say, ‘I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it, unless it is carrion, or flowing blood, or the flesh of swine.’} You would not eat it; rather, you would tan it and benefit from it.” So she sent for it, skinned its hide, tanned it, and made a water skin from it until it wore out at her place."],[11646,"A sheep belonging to Umm al-Aswad died, and she informed the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: {Say, ‘I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it, unless it is carrion, or blood’} up to the end of the verse, and he said: “You are not going to eat it.” So she sent for it and skinned it. Ibn ʿAbbas said: They made its hide into a water skin, and I saw it after a year. Abu al-Ahwas said: “Umm al-Aswad” is a mistake; the correct is Sawdah."],[11647,"There were two co-wives, and there was a quarrel between them. One of them threw a stone at the other and caused her to miscarry a dead boy, and the woman died. He ruled that the diyah be paid by the ʿāqilah. Her paternal uncle said, “She miscarried, O Messenger of Allah, a boy whose hair had grown.” The father of the killer said, “He is lying. By Allah, he neither cried, nor reasoned, nor drank, nor ate. Such a one is not entitled to blood money.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is it the rhymed prose of the Age of Ignorance and its soothsaying? I prescribe for the boy a ghurrah (a slave, male or female).” Ibn ʿAbbas said: The name of one of them was Mulaykah and the other was Umm ʿUṭayf."],[11648,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while he was in iḥrām.”"],[11649,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Avoid drinking from gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels, and drink from water skins. If you fear its fermentation, then dilute it with water.”"],[11650,"A cooked lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and she sent it to the Prophet ﷺ. The people ate, but the Prophet ﷺ did not eat. Khālid b. al-Walīd said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it forbidden, so we should leave it?” He said, “No, but I find it repulsive.”"],[11651,"A lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and she sent it to the Prophet ﷺ. The people ate, except the Prophet ﷺ. Khālid b. al-Walīd said, “Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah, so we should leave it?” He said, “No, but I find it repulsive.”"],[11652,"\"In his statement 'Your mothers are forbidden for you', he said 'Seven prohibitions come from lineage and seven from marriage through affinity.' And in his statement 'and what is beyond that is lawful for you', he said 'from lineage.' And in his statement 'the Book of Allah upon you', he said 'the four books.'\""],[11653,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered ʿAlī to prepare a bath for him, then he gave him a garment and said, “Cover me, and turn your back to me.”"],[11654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not intercept caravans outside the market, do not leave animals unmilked [to deceive buyers], and do not bid against one another [merely to raise the price].”"],[11655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A group of people from my community will recite the Quran but they will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game.”"],[11656,"“They used to talk during prayer; a man’s servant would come to him while he was praying and speak to him about his need, so they were forbidden from speaking [during prayer].”"],[11657,"I was sleeping, and I was approached and told: “Tonight is the Night of Decree.” So I got up while drowsy, and my foot caught on one of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing praying. Ibn Abbas said: I looked into the night, and it was the twenty-third night. “The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi.”"],[11658,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It would not please me to have the red camels if I were to break the pact that is in Dar al-Nadwah.”"],[11659,"“The slaughtered animals of the Jews and Christians were only made lawful because they believed in the Torah and the Gospel.”"],[11660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has land and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his neighbour.”"],[11661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “did not prohibit leasing land, but he commanded [us] to adhere to noble character.”"],[11662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever abandons a prayer will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[11663,"The Prophet ﷺ “forbade buying fruit until it is ripe [and ready to be eaten].”"],[11664,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “I was aided by the east wind, and ʿAd was destroyed by the west wind.”"],[11665,"The Prophet ﷺ “used to prostrate on a mat.” Husayn — meaning al-Muʿallim — [narrated it]."],[11666,"The people disputed about the new moon during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then a Bedouin came and testified that he had seen it. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do you testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said, “Yes.” So the Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he proclaimed, “Fasting is tomorrow.”"],[11667,"\"There was no woman who offered herself to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[11668,"\"They were merchants who were not distracted by trade or selling from the remembrance of Allah.\""],[11669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade blowing into food, drink, and fruit."],[11670,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Do not revile Tubbaʿ, for he had embraced Islam.”"],[11671,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “On every joint of a person there is a charity due each day.” Some of the people said, “This is difficult, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a charity; helping a weak person is a charity; and every step one of you takes to prayer is a charity.”"],[11672,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Every Muslim has a prayer due, and every step one of you takes to prayer is itself a prayer.”"],[11673,"He said to his people, “I will extinguish for you the fire of al-ḥadathān.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād, a man from his people, said, “By God, O Khālid, you have never said anything to us but the truth. So what is your affair and the affair of the fire of al-ḥadathān? You claim that you will extinguish it.” So ʿUmārah b. Ziyād went with him along with some people from his people until they came to it while it was emerging from a cleft in a mountain in a ḥarrah called Ḥarrat Ashjaʿ. Khālid drew a line for them and seated them inside it, and he said, “If I am delayed from you, do not call me by my name.” Then it came out as if it were reddish horses, following one another. Khālid faced it and began striking it with his staff, saying, “Bada bada, all is guidance, raw youths. The son of the shepherd of goats claimed that I would not come out of it while my clothes were still moist.” He entered the cleft with it and was delayed from them. ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said, “By God, if your companion were alive, he would have come out to you by now.” They said, “He forbade us to call him by his name.” He said, “Call him by his name.” So he came out to them, holding his head, and said, “Did I not forbid you to call me by my name? By God, you have killed me. So bury me, and when donkeys pass by you, including a dock-tailed donkey, then dig me up, for you will find me alive.” Then donkeys passed by them, including a dock-tailed donkey, and they said, “Dig him up, for he commanded us to dig him up.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said to them, “Do not let Muḍar say that we dig up our dead. By God, you will never dig him up.” Khālid had informed them that in his wife’s saddlebag there were two tablets, and if any matter became difficult for them, they should look at them, for they would see what they asked about. He also said, “Let no menstruating woman touch them.” When they returned to his wife, they asked her about them, and she brought them out while she was menstruating, so the knowledge that was in them departed. Abū Yūnus said: Simāk said: The son of Khālid b. Sinān came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Welcome to the son of my brother.” And Abū Yūnus is Ḥātim b. Abī Ṣaghīrah."],[11674,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to have skin-to-skin contact with a man, and a woman with a woman."],[11675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade muḥāqalah and muzābanah. And ʿIkrimah used to dislike selling green fodder."],[11676,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan.”"],[11677,"The Prophet ﷺ had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he did not find anything with which to redeem it until he died."],[11678,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man from his companions to a Jew to kill him. He said, “O Messenger of God, give me permission to say something.” He said, “Say whatever seems appropriate to you, for war is deceit.”"],[11679,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer.” ʿIkrimah said: I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, “How is faith removed?” He said, “Like this,” and he described it by interlacing his fingers, then he pulled them apart. “And if he repents, it returns to him.”"],[11680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave whom his master gives in marriage. He said, \"In whose hand is the divorce?\" He said, \"In the hand of the one who takes hold of the shank.\""],[11681,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves off [hunting] snakes for fear of seeking them is not of us.\""],[11682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Sacrificial slaughter and ritual slaughter were prescribed for me but not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer but you were not commanded to do it.\""],[11683,"\"Sacrificial slaughter was prescribed for me but not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer but you were not commanded to do it.\""],[11684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a village at the distance of four farsakhs or two farsakhs on the day of Ashura: \"Whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast, and whoever has eaten, let him not eat for the rest of his day.\""],[11685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt.\""],[11686,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There should be no harming or reciprocating harm. A person should secure a piece of wood on the wall of his neighbor. And if you have doubts about the road, then make it seven cubits.\""],[11687,"A cheese was brought to the Prophet ﷺ during the expedition of al-Ta'if, and his companions began striking it with their sticks and saying, \"We fear that it may contain carrion.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Put the knife into it and mention the name of Allah over it.\""],[11688,"The Prophet ﷺ did not enter the House during the Hajj, but he entered it in the year of the conquest. When he dismounted, he prayed four rak'ahs—or he said two rak'ahs—between the Stone and the door, facing the House, and said, \"This is the qiblah.\""],[11689,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed three [rak'ahs] and gave the salam. Dhu al-Shimalayn said, \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Prophet ﷺ prayed one rak'ah and prostrated twice."],[11690,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There is no believing servant except that he has a sin that he repeatedly falls into from time to time, or a sin upon which he persists and does not part with it until he departs from this world. Indeed the believer is created as one who is tried, repentant, and forgetful: when he is reminded, he remembers.\""],[11691,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.\""],[11692,"\"Water is required by water, in the case of a wet dream.\""],[11693,"“Prayer by anyone upon anyone is not appropriate except upon the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11694,"“The Prophet ﷺ had raisin nabidh, and he would drink it that day and the next day; and if it was the third day, he would drink it, otherwise he would pour it out.”"],[11695,"The Prophet ﷺ “used to wear a ring on his right hand.”"],[11696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether for themselves or for someone else, Paradise is guaranteed for them except if they commit an unforgivable act. And whoever loses their two honorable possessions, Paradise is guaranteed for them except if they commit an unforgivable act.\" \"Abu Sufyan is him, as far as I know, Sa'id bin Masruq, and Allah knows best.\""],[11697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ singled us out with three things: that we perform wudu thoroughly, that we do not consume charity, and that we do not make donkeys cover horses."],[11698,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Khadijah, Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, “O Muhammad, convey my greetings of peace to Khadijah and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, with no noise in it and no fatigue.”"],[11699,"That the Prophet ﷺ “forbade eating mujaththamah, jallalah, and drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.”"],[11700,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade eating mujaththamah, jallalah, and drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.”"],[11701,"That the Prophet ﷺ “forbade drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin, eating mujaththamah, and drinking the milk of a jallalah.”"],[11702,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wishes his lifespan to be extended and his provision increased, let him maintain ties of kinship.”"],[11703,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “cursed men who imitate women and women who imitate men.”"],[11704,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “This and this are equal” – meaning the thumb and the little finger – “their blood money is equal.”"],[11705,"“The husband of Barirah was a slave.”"],[11706,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: I saw him in the streets of Madinah pressing his eyes shut. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning it with four—her masters stipulated the walaʾ for themselves. The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the walaʾ belongs to the one who manumits, and he gave her the choice, so she chose herself. He ordered her to observe the waiting period and gave her charity. She sent some of it to ʿAʾishah as a gift, and ʿAʾishah asked the Prophet ﷺ about it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is charity for her, but for us it is a gift.”"],[11707,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated seven times, and he did so at a brisk pace because he loved to show the people his strength."],[11708,"ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My sister has vowed to walk to the House.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah is in no need of your sister’s vow. Let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel.”"],[11709,"In his statement \"Mankind used to be one nation,\" he said, \"upon Islam.\""],[11710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever forms an image will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection with blowing the soul into it. Whoever eavesdrops on people’s speech while they dislike that will have molten lead poured into his ear. And whoever falsely claims a dream will be tasked with tying together two grains of barley.”"],[11711,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: “I saw in al-Abtah an old foolish man who says the takbir when he prostrates and when he raises his head.” He said: “Is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? May your mother lose you!”"],[11712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah bt. al-Harith while he was in ihram and consummated the marriage after he returned, at a place of water called Sarif."],[11713,"Jamilah bt. Salul came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I do not fault Thabit b. Qays in character or religion, but I cannot bear him, and I hate disbelief after Islam.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you return his garden to him?” She said: “Yes.” So the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take back from her what he had given her and not to take any more."],[11714,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"],[11715,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, my father is a very old, sick man for whom standing is difficult. Tell me which night I should seek so that Allah may grant me success in it—the Night of Decree.” He said: “Look for the seventh.”"],[11716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays from muzzy, and I fear it may be the unripe dates."],[11717,"That the Prophet ﷺ bookmarked Hassan and Hussein."],[11718,"The Quran was sent down on the Night of Decree in Ramadan to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was sent down in stages."],[11719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made two rakʿahs obligatory during travel just as He made four obligatory while settled."],[11720,"When the verse was revealed: “O Prophet, indeed We have sent you as a witness and a bringer of good tidings and a warner” [Qur’an 33:45], the Prophet ﷺ called ‘Ali and Mu‘adh, and he had already ordered them to go out to Yemen. He said: “Go forth, give good tidings and do not repel, make things easy and do not make them difficult, for it has been revealed to me: ‘O Prophet, indeed We have sent you as a witness’ over your nation, ‘and a bringer of good tidings’ of Paradise, ‘and a warner’ from the Fire, ‘and a caller’ to the testimony that there is no god but God, ‘and an illuminating lamp’ with the Qur’an.”"],[11721,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with his face dripping blood and said: “O Messenger of God, I followed a woman, then a man met me and did to me what you see.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God, may He be exalted, intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment of his sin in this world; and when He intends evil for a servant, He withholds his sin until He confronts him with it on the Day of Resurrection, as if he were a donkey.”"],[11722,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “I saw the Dajjal as a fair-skinned, white, stout, curly-haired man, as if the hair of his head were branches of a tree, one-eyed, as if his eye were the morning star. I liken him to ‘Abd al-‘Uzza, a man of Khuza‘ah.”"],[11723,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Learn the two radiant suras, al-Baqarah and Al ‘Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for their companion. Learn al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the idle cannot master it.”"],[11724,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the images in the house—meaning the Ka‘bah—he did not enter until he ordered them erased. He saw Ibrahim and Isma‘il with divination arrows in their hands and said: “May God fight them! By God, they never sought omens with divination arrows at all.”"],[11725,"He said: “Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of vengeance is not of us.” He said: And Ibn ‘Abbas said: “Snakes are the transformed jinn, just as apes were transformed from the Children of Israel.”"],[11726,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11727,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11728,"I witnessed Eid with the Prophet ﷺ and he delivered a sermon. He thought that the women hadn't heard, so he called them and advised them, saying, \"Give in charity.\" Then, the women started giving their rings, earrings, necklaces, and even their garments. The Prophet commanded Bilal to collect them in his garment until he distributed them."],[11729,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever changes his religion—or he said: reverts from his religion—kill him.” And he said: “Do not punish with God’s punishment,” meaning fire."],[11730,"“The husband of Barirah was a slave belonging to Banu So-and-so, people of the Ansar, called Mughith. By God, it is as if I am looking at him now, following her through the streets of Madinah, weeping.”"],[11731,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The evil example is not for us: the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit.”"],[11732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit. The evil example is not for us.”"],[11733,"“It is not abrogated. He used to recite it: ‘They will be collared with it.’ It is concerning the very old man who is obliged to fast but cannot bear it, so he breaks the fast and feeds.”"],[11734,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever makes an image will be required on the Day of Resurrection to blow the spirit into it, and he will never be able to blow, and he will be punished for it. Whoever listens to the speech of a people while they dislike that, molten lead will be poured into his ears. Whoever lies about his dream will be required to tie a knot in a barley grain” — or he said “between two barley grains” — “and he will be punished for it, and he will not do it.”"],[11735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered an ʿaqiqah for al-Hasan with a ram, and for al-Husayn with a ram."],[11736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a mukatab dies and leaves an inheritance, or becomes liable to a prescribed punishment, he inherits according to the portion of him that has been freed, and the prescribed punishment is carried out on him according to the portion of him that has been freed.”"],[11737,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the Night of Decree, he said: “Seek it in the ninth remaining, the seventh remaining, and the fifth remaining.”"],[11738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram."],[11739,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting."],[11740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boast about your forefathers who passed away during the Jahiliyyah. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the dung that the beetle rolls with its nose is better than them.”"],[11741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boast about your forefathers who died during the Jahiliyyah. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, what the beetle rolls with its nose is better than your forefathers who died during the Jahiliyyah.”"],[11742,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram, and consummated the marriage with her at Sarif when he was out of ihram."],[11743,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in Sad, and it is not one of the prescribed prostrations."],[11744,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in Sad."],[11745,"That the Prophet ﷺ prostrated while he was in Makkah at [the recitation of] al-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and the humans prostrated with him. And Hafs b. ʿUmar said in his hadith: Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Makkah, and the Jews, the Christians, and the polytheists prostrated with him."],[11746,"ʿAʾishah said to her: \"In disappointment! I see you are detaining us.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what is that?\" Safiyyah said, \"She has menstruated.\" It was said, \"She has already performed the ifadah.\" He said, \"Then no.\""],[11747,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to take from the heads while he was fasting—meaning kissing."],[11748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped and paid the cupper; and if it had been impure, he would not have fed him."],[11749,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I threw [the pebbles].\" He motioned with his hand and said, \"No harm.\" And he was not asked that day about anything regarding advancing or delaying except that he motioned with his hand and said, \"No harm.\""],[11750,"That he should not speak, nor seek shade, nor sit, and that he should fast his day. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Order him to speak, seek shade, sit, and fast his day.\""],[11751,"The Prophet ﷺ was traveling when he passed by a woman with her hair uncovered. He said, \"What is this?\" It was mentioned that it was a woman from the Quraysh tribe who had vowed to perform Hajj with her hair uncovered. He said, \"Tell her to cover her hair.\""],[11752,"The Prophet (PBUH) said, \"Between the pillar and the station, there is a binding obligation that relieves the person with a disability from making it.\""],[11753,"That a group of people came to the Prophet ﷺ with a woman and said, \"O Muhammad! What has been revealed to you regarding adultery?\" He replied, \"Go and bring me two men from the learned scholars of the Children of Israel.\" So they brought him two men, one of them was a young man with a good voice, while the other had his eyebrow covering his eye, and he had to raise it with a string. The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"I adjure both of you by Allah, do you know what Allah revealed to Moses regarding the adulterer?\" They replied, \"You have adjured us by a great oath. Indeed, we inform you that Allah revealed to Moses the punishment of stoning for the adulterer, and we were a youthful and attractive group, and our women were beautiful. This sin became widespread among us, so we did not enforce the punishment. Instead, we would flog (the adulterer).\" The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"Go and bring your companion and when she gives birth, stone her.\""],[11754,"That the Prophet ﷺ went out to a people who had set up a live pigeon as a target and were throwing it. He said, \"It is not permissible to eat its meat.\""],[11755,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to drink from a vessel in three breaths."],[11756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever of the izār extends below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[11757,"That the Prophet ﷺ would not blow into the drink."],[11758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His firm obligations be taken.\""],[11759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His firm obligations be taken.\""],[11760,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the dominion of debts, the dominion of enemies, the destruction of blessings, and the trials of the false Messiah.\""],[11761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"You will surely bring clear proof for what you say, or you will be flogged with the prescribed punishment.\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I am truthful, and Allah will surely send down my excuse.\" Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him, and they performed mutual cursing. When the fifth [oath] remained, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is binding, and I wished that you be shown mercy.\" Then she said, \"By Allah, I will not disgrace my people,\" and she proceeded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Observe her. If she gives birth to a white child with lank hair and short eyes, then it is for Hilal b. Umayyah; and if she gives birth to a dark-skinned child with curly hair and kohl-lined eyes, then it is for Sharīk b. al-Sahmāʾ.\" Then she gave birth to one for Sharīk."],[11762,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever listens to the conversation of a people, molten lead will be poured into his ear; and whoever falsely claims a dream will be tasked with tying together two grains of barley, and he will not be able to tie them.\""],[11763,"That the husband of Barirah was a slave, and I saw him striking his head against the walls in pursuit of her."],[11764,"Permission was granted for drinking from the mouths of water-skins."],[11765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I did not pass by any group of angels except that they commanded me to practice cupping.\""],[11766,"The Prophet ﷺ used to apply kohl with ithmid before sleeping every night."],[11767,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, it weighed heavily upon him and people refrained from speaking to him."],[11768,"I spent the night at the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when the first dawn appeared, he got up and performed Witr with nine units, saying the salam between every two units."],[11769,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever spends a night with light food and drink, praying, the wide-eyed houris will crowd around him until morning.\""],[11770,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for seventeen days shortening the prayer."],[11771,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What an excellent servant is the cupper! He removes blood, lightens the back, and sharpens the eyesight.\""],[11772,"The Prophet ﷺ placed a purple velvet cloth in his grave."],[11773,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting."],[11774,"The Prophet ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah at night, and he cupped him and gave him his fee."],[11775,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[11776,"Umar b. al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side, and he said: “O Messenger of God, if only you would take a bed softer than this.” He replied: “What have I to do with this world? By Him in Whose hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who travels on a scorching day, seeks shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then moves on and leaves it.”"],[11777,"The Prophet ﷺ turned toward Uhud and said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, it would not please me if this Uhud were turned into gold for the family of Muhammad, which I would spend in the way of God, and then I die on the day I die leaving two dinars of it—except for two dinars I set aside for a debt, if I owe any.”"],[11778,"The Prophet ﷺ would pass consecutive nights on an empty stomach, while his family could find no evening meal. He said: “Most of their bread was barley bread.”"],[11779,"The Prophet ﷺ died “leaving neither dinar nor dirham, neither slave nor slave-girl; he left his coat of mail pawned to a Jew for thirty measures of barley.”"],[11780,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You are a third of the people of Paradise, or half of the people of Paradise.”"],[11781,"When {When comes the help of God and the victory} was revealed until the end of the surah, he said: “The Prophet’s own soul was announced to him when it was revealed.” He said: “He then devoted himself to the utmost striving in the matter of the Hereafter that he had ever done.” After that, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Victory and the help of God have come, and the people of Yemen have come.” A man said: “O Messenger of God, who are the people of Yemen?” He said: “A people with tender hearts and soft hearts; faith is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni.”"],[11782,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went on a military expedition and had not finished with the enemy until the afternoon prayer was delayed past its usual time. When he had finished with them, he looked and saw that the afternoon prayer had been delayed into the evening, so he prayed. When he had finished his prayer, he called upon his enemy and said: “O God, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire.”"],[11783,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on one of his expeditions, and a man said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about the children [of the polytheists]?” The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent and did not answer him a word until he had finished his expedition and went around. Then he saw a boy who had fallen from a litter, and it was him. His caller announced: “Where is the one who asked about the children?” The man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he forbade killing their children and said: “God knows best what they would have done.”"],[11784,"When {When the help of Allah and the conquest comes (i.e., the victory over Makkah)},the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah and said, \"I have been informed of my death.\"So she cried, and he said to her, \"Do not cry, for you will be the first of my family to join me.\"So she smiled, and some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saw her and said, \"We saw you cry and smile.\"She said, \"He told me, 'I have been informed of my death,'\" so I cried.He then said, \"Do not cry, for you will be the first of my family to join me.\"So I smiled."],[11785,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his uncle al-Abbas: “O uncle, make much supplication for well-being.”"],[11786,"Dubaa bt. al-Zubayr b. Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I intend to perform Hajj; should I make a condition?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “How should I say it?” He said: “Say: At Your service, O God, at Your service; my place of ending is wherever You detain me on the earth.”"],[11787,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The month of Sha'ban is a month of prayers, all of them are performed at Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha.\""],[11788,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Aslam—may God grant them peace—and Ghifar—may God forgive them.”"],[11789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah for seventeen nights shortening the prayer."],[11790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once passed by a piece of food, picked up a bone from it, ate from it, then performed prayer without performing ablution (wudu)."],[11791,"Indeed, Allah has chosen Ibrahim for His intimate friendship, and He has chosen Musa for His direct speech, and He has chosen Muhammad for His visions."],[11792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in ihram, and he said, \"Ihram is more stringent than fasting.\""],[11793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who had put his foot on the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him with its eyes. He said, \"Why not before this? Do you want to kill it twice?\""],[11794,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever does not press his nose with his forehead to the ground when he prostrates, his prayer is not acceptable.\""],[11795,"He used to say the takbir when rising and when placing. I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said, \"May you have no mother! Is that not the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ?\""],[11796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while they were in ihram."],[11797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring was heard, then prayed and did not repeat the ablution."],[11798,"About the Prophet ﷺ regarding a situation where a woman becomes unconscious while she is menstruating, he said, \"Give charity with a dinar, and if you cannot find that, then with half a dinar.\""],[11799,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah when he was not in ihram."],[11800,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever claims to have seen a dream he did not see will be ordered to tie a knot between two barley grains, and whoever makes an image will be ordered to blow into it, and whoever eavesdrops on people's conversation while they flee from him will have molten lead poured into his ear.\""],[11801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prostrate in anything of the mufassal since he moved to Madinah."],[11802,"A man from the Bedouins died and had no male relatives, but he had a freedman whom he had set free. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Was he not angry when he was angry and pleased when he was pleased?\" They said, \"Yes,\" so he made his freedman inherit his wealth."],[11803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who brands on the face."],[11804,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Mecca's conquest, 'Indeed, Allah, may His remembrance be glorified, made Mecca sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth. It is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Judgment. Its game should not be disturbed, its trees should not be cut, its grass should not be uprooted, and its prey should not be chased except by a skilled poet.' So Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said, 'Except for the incense, O Messenger of Allah, the needs of the people and homes require it.' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent for a while and then said, 'Except for incense, for it is permissible.'\""],[11805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground, then said: \"Do you know what this is?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. ʿImran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.\""],[11806,"\"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the time of sacrifice came, so we shared in a cow seven [people] and in a camel ten [people].\""],[11807,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt.\""],[11808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be given in marriage upon the paternal aunt and upon the maternal aunt, and he said: \"If you do that, you sever your ties of kinship.\""],[11809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"One day of a just ruler is better than sixty years of worship, and a legal punishment carried out justly on earth is more purifying for it than forty years of rain.\""],[11810,"I am not a mother for you, that is the prayer of my father Al-Qasim ﷺ ."],[11811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"had cupping done and gave the cupper a dinar.\""],[11812,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that fruit be sold until it is edible, nor wool on the back, nor milk in the udder.\""],[11813,"Maʿiz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: \"Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or pressed?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Did you do such and such?\" without using a euphemism. He said: \"Yes.\" So he ordered him to be stoned."],[11814,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was \"praying, a sheep came running in front of him, and he raced it until he pressed his belly against the wall.\""],[11815,"The Prophet ﷺ came out during his illness with his head bandaged with a cloth, sat on the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: \"There is no one among the people who is more generous to me with his self and his wealth than Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. If I were to take a close friend from among the people, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam is better.\" Then he said: \"No small door shall remain in the mosque but it shall be closed, except the small door of Abu Bakr.\""],[11816,"\"From al-musmat [the solid, compact one].\""],[11817,"\"Whoever dies with the scandalous wind in his belly, Allah will disgrace him before the witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11818,"There is no one from whose words some are not taken and some left except the Prophet ﷺ."],[11819,"from the food of two people competing to show off to each other.\""],[11820,"Beware of rhymed prose in supplication and avoid it, for I knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions not doing that."],[11821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[11822,"Maʿiz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that he had committed zina. He turned away from him. Then he asked his people, \"Is he insane?\" They said, \"There is nothing wrong with him.\" He said, \"Did you do it with her?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he ordered that he be stoned. He was taken away, and he did not pray over him."],[11823,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Snakes are the metamorphosed jinn, just as apes and pigs were metamorphosed from the Children of Israel.\""],[11824,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Safiyyah, \"Make it a condition that my place (of residence) is wherever you confine me.\""],[11825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever imagines in his prayer that he has broken his ablution should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell.\""],[11826,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj walking.\" He said, \"Let her ride, for Allah ﷻ is not in need of her walking.\""],[11827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying when Abu Jahl came and forbade him from praying. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: 'And let him call his associates; We will call the zabaniyah.' Ibn ʿAbbas said: \"If he had done so, the zabaniyah would have seized him.\""],[11828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a bedouin to visit him when he was ill. When he entered upon a sick person to visit him, he would say: \"No harm, purification if Allah wills.\" The bedouin said, \"You say purification? No, rather it is a fever boiling on an old man, visiting him will be the graves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then yes, then.\" The wording is from the hadith of ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. al-Mukhtar."],[11829,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Badr: \"This is Jibril ﷺ , holding the head of a horse with him, upon him the implements of war.\""],[11830,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from Makkah, some young boys from Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib met him. He carried one in front of him and another behind him."],[11831,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage; had he known it to be impure, he would not have given it."],[11832,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated on a camel, and whenever he came to the corner, he pointed to it."],[11833,"Seven [relations] are prohibited by lineage and seven by marriage, and he recited this verse in Surah al-Nisa."],[11834,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God made Makkah sacred; it was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. It was made lawful for me only for an hour of the day. Its fresh vegetation is not to be cut, its trees not to be felled, its game not to be startled, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it.\" Al-Abbas said: \"O Messenger of God, except for idhkhir, for our goldsmiths.\" He said: \"Except for idhkhir.\""],[11835,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Islam is ten portions, and he who has no portion has lost: the testimony that there is no god but God, and it is the creed; the second is prayer, and it is the fitrah; the third is zakat, and it is purification; the fourth is fasting, and it is the shield; the fifth is Hajj, and it is the law; the sixth is jihad, and it is warfare; the seventh is commanding the right, and it is faithfulness; the eighth is forbidding the wrong, and it is the proof; the ninth is the community, and it is affection; and the tenth is obedience, and it is protection.\""],[11836,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"We have no bad example: one who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit.\""],[11837,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they dislike him, molten lead will be poured into his ears. Whoever claims to have seen a dream he did not see will be charged to tie a knot between two grains of barley and will be punished, though he will not be able to tie it. And whoever makes an image will be punished until he blows the spirit into it, though he will never blow.\""],[11838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ embraced me and said: \"O God, teach him wisdom.\""],[11839,"He was called Mughith; it is as if I see him going around behind her weeping, his tears flowing onto his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Abbas: \"O Abbas, are you not amazed at the intensity of Mughith's love for Barirah and the intensity of Barirah's hatred for Mughith?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"If only you would take him back, for he is the father of your child.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, do you command me?\" He said: \"I am only an intercessor.\" She said: \"Then I have no need of him.\""],[11840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to the watering place and asked for a drink. Al-Abbas said to al-Fadl: \"Go to your mother and bring the Messenger of God ﷺ a drink from her.\" He said: \"Give me to drink.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, they put their hands in it.\" He said: \"Give me to drink.\" So he drank from it. Then he came to Zamzam while they were giving water and working in it. He said: \"Work, for you are engaged in righteous work.\" Then he said: \"Were it not that you would be overcome, I would go down and place the rope on this,\" meaning his shoulder, and he pointed to his shoulder."],[11841,"\"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ recited aloud, we recited aloud; and whenever he was silent, we were silent.\""],[11842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out in Ramadan to Hunayn while the people differed, some fasting and some not. When he was settled on his mount, he called for a vessel of milk or water and drank it. He said: \"Then he placed it on his mount, and the people saw him. Those not fasting said to those fasting: 'Break your fast.'\""],[11843,"that he should enter upon Fatimah. They said, 'Bring something.' He said, 'I do not find anything.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Where is your Hutamiyyah coat of mail?'"],[11844,"The Prophet ﷺ was not asked about anything on the Day of Sacrifice except that he said, 'No harm, no harm.'"],[11845,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What is forbidden by lineage is also forbidden by breastfeeding.'\""],[11846,"The wife of Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'By Allah, I do not find fault with him in character or religion, but I dislike disbelief after Islam.' He said, 'Will you return his garden to him?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'O Thabit, accept the garden and divorce her with one divorce.'"],[11847,"that he should eat it."],[11848,"that the Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram."],[11850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No one among the people has been more excellent to me in the blessing of family and wealth than Abu Bakr. If I were to take a close friend, I would take him, but there is the brotherhood of Islam or faith.'"],[11851,"the Prophet ﷺ: 'If you marry her, then return our daughter to us.'"],[11852,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr while he was in his tent, 'O Allah, I adjure You by Your covenant and Your promise. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today.' Abu Bakr took him by the hand and said, 'Enough, O Messenger of Allah, for you have implored your Lord persistently.' He was wearing the coat of mail, and he came out saying, 'The assembly will be defeated, and they will turn their backs. Nay, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter.'"],[11853,"that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the jallalah (an animal that eats filth), the mujaththamah (an animal tied and used as a target), and drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[11854,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin and breathing into a vessel."],[11855,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have ordered the killing of every solid black one. So kill the muʿayyanah (the one with two spots above its eyes) among dogs, for it is the accursed one from the jinn.'"],[11856,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the battle if he did not encounter the enemy early in the day, until the wind would blow and it would be time for the prayers. He used to say, \"O Allah, with You is the provision, with You is the movement, and there is no power or strength except with Allah.\""],[11857,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, when I eat meat I become aroused toward women and desire takes hold of me, so I have forbidden meat upon myself.” Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Surely Allah does not love the transgressors. And eat of what Allah has provided for you, lawful and good}."],[11858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited an-naqīr, al-muzaffat, ad-dubbāʾ, al-jarr, and al-ḥantam."],[11859,"Al-ʿAbbās was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ on a camel that he had branded on its face with fire. He said, “What is this brand, O ʿAbbās?” He said, “A brand we used to apply in the pre-Islamic era.” He said, “Do not brand with fire.”"],[11860,"A blind man had a slave woman who was the mother of his child. She used to revile the Prophet ﷺ and speak much against him. He would forbid her but she would not stop, and he would rebuke her but she would not be deterred. One night she mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and he could not endure it, so he got up to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned on it until he killed her. In the morning her two children were between her legs, smeared with blood. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he stood and gathered the people, then said, “I adjure by Allah: a man who has a right upon me and did what he did, let him stand.” The blind man came forward wailing and said, “By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, I am the one who did it. She was the mother of my child, and I had from her two sons like pearls. She was indeed a gentle, kind companion to me, but she used to mention you and revile you. I would forbid her but she would not stop, and I would rebuke her but she would not be deterred. Last night she mentioned you and attacked you, and I could not endure it, so I got up to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned on it until I killed her.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I bear witness that her blood is wasted.”"],[11861,"“Our wine on that day was faḍīkh, and it was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and it is nothing but your faḍīkh.”"],[11862,"That the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to recite in the Fajr prayer."],[11863,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11864,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men."],[11865,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men, and he expelled so-and-so."],[11866,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Expel the effeminate men from your houses.” He said: And the Prophet ﷺ expelled an effeminate man, and ʿUmar expelled an effeminate man."],[11867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The blood money of a mukātab is according to the portion of him that has been freed: the blood money of a free man, and according to the portion of him that remains enslaved: the blood money of a slave.”"],[11868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a mukātab that he should pay according to the portion of him that has been freed the blood money of a free man."],[11869,"A mukātab was brought before the Prophet ﷺ and he said, “He pays for what he has paid of his kitāba the blood money of a free man, and for what he has not paid the blood money of a slave.”"],[11870,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The blood money of a mukatab (a slave who has contracted to purchase his freedom) is according to the extent of his freedom: the blood money of a free man for the portion that he has paid toward his freedom, and the blood money of a slave for the portion that remains in slavery.”"],[11871,"that he should slaughter himself or his child, then let him slaughter a ram.” Then he recited: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.”"],[11872,"that the Prophet ﷺ “forbade selling animals on credit.”"],[11873,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Treat your children equally in gift-giving; if I were to prefer anyone, I would have preferred women.”"],[11874,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed his ihram garment at al-Tanʿim while he was in a state of ihram.”"],[11875,"When one of his daughters was proposed to, the Prophet ﷺ would come to her private chamber and say: “So-and-so is proposing to so-and-so.” If she stabbed the wall, he would not marry her off; but if she did not stab the wall, he would give her in marriage."],[11876,"that when the Prophet ﷺ married off Fatimah, he said: “O ʿAli, do not go in to your wife until you give them something.” ʿAli said: “I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Give her your Hutamiyyah armor.”"],[11877,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “annulled the marriage of a virgin and a previously married woman whose fathers married them off against their will.”"],[11878,"that the Prophet ﷺ “was cupped and gave the cupper his wages.” “The name of Abu ʿAzzah is al-Hakam b. Tahman.”"],[11879,"A man from the Ansar had two stallions, and he brought them into a wall and closed the door on them. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ and wanted him to pray for him. The Prophet ﷺ was sitting, and there were some Ansar with him. He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have come with a need, and I had two stallions that I brought into a wall and closed the door on them. I would like you to pray that Allah makes them obedient to me.\" He said to his companions, \"Get up with us.\" So he went until he came to the door, and he said, \"Open.\" The man hesitated because he was worried about the Prophet ﷺ , but he said, \"Open.\" So he opened the door, and one of the stallions was close to the door. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, he prostrated to it and said, \"Bring me something more powerful than it, and I will grant you what you want.\" So he brought some rubbish and he held it against the stallion's head, and the stallion submitted to him. Then he walked to the farthest corner of the wall to the other stallion, and when he saw it, it fell prostrate to him. He said to the man, \"Bring me something more powerful than it.\" So he held its head against something and it submitted to him. He said, \"Go, for they will not disobey you.\" When the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw this, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, these two stallions that do not have reason prostrated to you, should we not then prostrate to you?\" He said, \"I do not command anyone to prostrate to another. Even if I were to command someone to prostrate to another, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[11880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You must keep to the first row and the right side, and beware of praying between the pillars.”"],[11881,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud in some prayers and remained silent in others. So we recite in the prayers in which the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited, and we remain silent in the prayers in which he remained silent.” It was said to him: “Perhaps the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited to himself.” He became angry and said: “Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be suspected? Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be suspected?”"],[11882,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “that he fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam.”"],[11883,"Three men came to the Prophet ﷺ. The first said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you, and the mercy of Allah.' Then the second came and said, 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.' Then the third came and said, 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you.' Abu al-Fata was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you gave more to so-and-so and so-and-so, but you did not give my son anything.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We did not find any addition for him, so we replied to him with the like of what he said.'"],[11886,"He said: “Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honor for women.”"],[11887,"From Ibn Abbas, I do not think but that he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ; he said: “The prayer is in the dwellings.”"],[11888,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed a man seeks a need, and Allah withholds it from him because what is better for him, and he accuses people, wronging them, and says, 'Who will satisfy me?'”"],[11889,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Three have no reckoning regarding what they eat, if it is lawful: the fasting person, the one who partakes of the pre-dawn meal, and the one stationed in the path of Allah.”"],[11890,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Soon you will see human devils; one of them hears a hadith and spreads it to others, and so he turns the people away from listening to it from the companion who narrated it.”"],[11891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Exalted is He, supported me with the sharpest-tongued and strongest-armed of the Arabs, the Banu Qaylah, the Aws and the Khazraj.”"],[11895,"“Allah gave speech to Musa, intimate friendship to Ibrahim, and the vision of Him to Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[11896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not from us who performs ablution after the ritual bath.”"],[11897,"When the news of the death of Ja'far b. Abi Talib came, the Prophet ﷺ entered upon Asma' bt. 'Umays and placed 'Abdullah and Muhammad, the two sons of Ja'far, on his thigh, then said: “Jibril informed me that Allah, Exalted is He, caused Ja'far to be martyred, and that he has two wings with which he flies among the angels in Paradise.” Then he said: “O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his children.”"],[11898,"“From prophet to prophet until I was brought forth as a prophet.”"],[11899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the privy, then came out, and there was a covered vessel of water. He said, 'Who did this?' 'Abdullah said, 'I did.' He said, 'O Allah, teach him the interpretation of the Qur'an.'"],[11900,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Dubāʿa: “Perform Hajj and stipulate conditions and say: My place of dissolution is wherever You withhold me.”"],[11901,"That the Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[11902,"“A man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give half a dinar in charity.”"],[11903,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he disliked combining (in marriage) a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt, and two paternal aunts, and two maternal aunts."],[11904,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aisha and Hafsah while they were fasting. Then he left and came back while they were eating. He asked, \"Were you not fasting?\" They replied, \"Yes, we were, but we were given this food as a gift and we liked it, so we ate from it.\" He said, \"Fast for a day in its place.\""],[11905,"This verse was revealed on the day of Badr, \"And it is not for a prophet to take captives\". It was revealed regarding a red camel that was lost on the day of Badr. Some people said, \"Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it.\" So Allah revealed, \"And it is not for a prophet to take captives.\""],[11906,"From Ibn ʿAbbās regarding {It is not for a prophet to be dishonest}: He said: It concerned a red velvet cloak that was lost on the day of Badr, and they said he took it, so there was revealed {And it is not for a prophet to be dishonest}."],[11907,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning a woman in post-natal bleeding: “She performs ghusl, then enters ihrām, and carries out all the rites except the tawāf of the House.”"],[11908,"The poor people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Indeed, the rich people fast as we fast and pray as we pray, but they also have wealth from which they give charity and free slaves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"When you pray, say 'Subhanallah' thirty-three times, 'Alhamdulillah' thirty-three times, and 'Allahu Akbar' thirty-four times.\""],[11909,"“Your return is to Paradise.”"],[11910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no confinement after Sūrat al-Nisāʾ.”"],[11911,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited {A day that will make children grey-haired} and said: That is the Day of Resurrection, and that is a day when Allah, glorified be His mention, says to Adam: “Arise and send a delegation from your progeny to the Fire.” He said: “Of how many, O Lord?” He said: “From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and one will be saved.” That weighed heavily on the Muslims, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perceived that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he saw that in their faces: “The children of Adam are many, and Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj are from the children of Adam, and none of them dies until a thousand men from his own loins inherit from him. In them and their like is a shield for you.”"],[11912,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was consoled for his daughter Ruqayya, the wife of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān, he said: “Praise be to Allah; burying daughters is from the noble deeds.”"],[11913,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib said: “O Messenger of Allah, the Qurʾān slips away from my chest.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I teach you words by which Allah will benefit you and benefit whom you teach?” He said: “Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.” He said: “Pray on the night of Friday four rakʿahs. In the first rakʿah recite the Opening of the Book and Yā Sīn; in the second, the Opening of the Book and Ḥā Mīm al-Dukhān; in the third, the Opening of the Book and Alif Lām Mīm Tanzīl al-Sajdah; and in the fourth, the Opening of the Book and Tabārak al-Mufaṣṣal. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah and extol Him, send blessings upon the prophets, and seek forgiveness for the believers. Then say: O Allah, have mercy on me by abandonment of sins forever as long as You keep me alive, and have mercy on me from burdening myself with what does not concern me, and grant me good insight into what pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honour and might that is not sought, I ask You, O Allah, O Merciful, by Your majesty and the light of Your countenance, to make my heart adhere to love of Your Book as You taught me, and grant me to recite it in the manner that pleases You from me. I ask You to illuminate my sight with the Book, loosen my tongue by it, relieve my heart through it, expand my chest by it, employ my body with it, strengthen me for that, and help me in it, for none helps me to good other than You, and none grants success to it except You. Do that for three Fridays, or five, or seven, and you will memorise it by Allah’s permission, and it never misses a believer.” Afterwards he came to the Prophet ﷺ after seven Fridays and informed him of his memorisation of the Qurʾān and the hadith. The Prophet ﷺ said: “A believer, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah! Teach Abū Ḥasan, teach Abū Ḥasan!”"],[11914,"That the Prophet ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, and they took booty. Among them was a man who said to them: “I am not one of you. I fell in love with a woman and followed her, so let me look at her, then do whatever seems right to you.” There was a tall, dark-complexioned woman. He said to her: “Accept Islam, Ḥubaysh, before life runs out. Have you considered, if I followed you and caught up with you with ornaments, or reached you at al-Khawāniq, was it not right that a lover should attain, one who undertook the night journeys and the midday heat?” She said: “Yes, may I be your ransom.” He said: They brought him forward and struck his neck. Then the woman came, fell upon him, let out one or two gasps, and died. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the news, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Was there not among you a merciful man?”"],[11915,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, I adjure you by God and kinship: we have eaten 'ilhiz'—meaning hair and blood.\" Then God ﷻ sent down: {And We seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves to their Lord, nor did they entreat Him}."],[11916,"One thousand men from Banu Sulaym witnessed with the Messenger of God ﷺ the day of the conquest of Makkah."],[11917,"Regarding His saying {And fear a day in which you will be returned to God}, \"It is the last verse that was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[11918,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, they were among the most dishonest people in measuring, so God ﷻ sent down {Woe to those who give short measure}, and after that they measured well."],[11919,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Khaybar, {When the victory of God and the conquest comes} was revealed to him, to the end of the story. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O 'Ali b. Abi Talib, O Fatimah, the victory of God and the conquest has come. {And you see people entering the religion of God in multitudes, then glorify the praise of your Lord and ask His forgiveness. Indeed, He is ever accepting of repentance}—bearing in mind that after me there will be jihad among the believers.\" He said, \"Against what shall we fight the believers who say, 'We believe'?\" He said, \"Against innovations in religion when they act according to opinion, and there is no opinion in religion. Religion is only from the Lord—His commands and His prohibitions.\" 'Ali said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you think if a matter arises for which no Qur'an was revealed and no Sunnah was specified from you?\" He said, \"Make it a consultation among the worshippers among the believers, and do not decide it by the opinion of a single individual. If I were to appoint a successor, no one would be more entitled to it than you because of your early entry into Islam, your kinship to the Messenger of God ﷺ, your being his son-in-law, and with you is the mistress of the women of the believers. And before that, there was the kindness of Abu Talib toward me; the Qur'an was revealed while I was keen to care for his children in return.\""],[11920,"'Ali said, \"O Messenger of God, you said to me on the day of Uhud, when I was kept from martyrdom and those who were martyred were martyred, 'Martyrdom is behind you.' He said, 'How will you be patient when this is dyed from this?' and he gestured with his hand to his beard and head.\" 'Ali said, \"Since you have made clear what you have made clear, that is not among the occasions of patience but rather among the occasions of glad tidings and honor.\""],[11921,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The sacrificial animal was prescribed for me and not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer and you were not commanded to.\""],[11922,"Abu Barzah al-Aslami was a soothsayer who judged among the Jews in matters they brought to him for arbitration. Some Muslims brought a dispute to him for arbitration, so God ﷻ sent down: {Have you not seen those who claim that they believed in what was revealed to you and what was revealed before you, wishing to take their disputes to the tyrant while they were commanded to reject him} up to His saying {We intended nothing but good}."],[11923,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who drinks from a vessel of gold only pours into his belly the fire of Hell.\""],[11924,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God ﷻ created one hundred mercies, one of which He distributed among creation, and ninety-nine remain until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The barefoot person has more right to the middle of the road than the one wearing sandals.\""],[11926,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Tabuk and performed 'Umrah, and when he descended from the pass of 'Usfan, he commanded his companions to lean back against the mountain pass until he returned to them. He went and stopped at his mother's grave, and he conversed privately with his Lord for a long time. Then he wept, and his weeping intensified, and they wept because of his weeping. They said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has not wept in this place except that something has happened in his community that they cannot bear.\" When they wept, he stood and returned to them and said, \"What makes you weep?\" They said, \"O Prophet of God, we wept because of your weeping. We thought that perhaps something had happened in your community that they cannot bear.\" He said, \"No, though some of it has occurred. But I stopped at my mother's grave and asked God to permit me to intercede for her on the Day of Resurrection, but God refused to permit me. So I felt mercy for her—she is my mother—and I wept. Then Jibril ﷺ came to me and said, {And Abraham's seeking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of God, he disowned him}. So disown your mother as Abraham disowned his father. I felt mercy for her—she is my mother—and I called upon my Lord to lift four things from my community. He lifted two and refused to lift two. I called upon my Lord to lift from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, and that He not divide them into factions, and that He not make them taste the might of one another. God lifted from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, but God refused to lift two: killing and chaos. He turned to his mother's grave only because she was buried under such-and-such, and 'Usfan was theirs.\""],[11927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the two prostrations of forgetfulness al-Murāghamatayn (the two that make Satan choke with rage)."],[11928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not pray facing a grave, and do not pray upon a grave.\""],[11929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dug the trench while his companions had tied stones to their bellies out of hunger. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said: \"Have you been shown a man who can give us a meal?\" A man said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"As for no, go ahead and show us to him.\" So they went to the man, and there he was in the trench working on his portion of it. His wife sent word: \"Come, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come to us.\" The man came running and said: \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for him.\" He had a she-goat with her kid, so he jumped to her. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The kid is behind us.\" So he slaughtered the kid. The woman went to some flour she had, kneaded it, and baked it. She brought the pot and crumbled her large bowl, then brought it near to the Prophet ﷺ and his companions. The Prophet ﷺ placed his finger in it and said: \"In the name of Allah. O Allah, bless it. Eat.\" They ate from it until they had their fill, yet they ate only a third of it and two-thirds remained. Then he sent those ten who were with him: \"Go and send us your number.\" So they went, and those ten came in their place. They ate from it until they were full. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood and supplicated for the lady of the house, and pronounced blessings upon her and her household. Then they walked to the trench, and he said: \"Take us to Salman.\" There was a rock in front of him that he had been unable to break. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Leave me, so that I may be the first to strike it.\" He said: \"In the name of Allah,\" and struck it, and a piece, a third of it, fell off. He said: \"Allah is greatest! The palaces of Rome, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\" Then he struck again, and another piece fell off. He said: \"Allah is greatest! The palaces of Persia, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\" At that point the hypocrites said: \"We are digging a trench for our own protection, and he is promising us the palaces of Persia and Rome!\""],[11930,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting."],[11931,"The Prophet ﷺ set out in Ramadan at the time of the conquest and fasted until, when he was at Qudayd, he broke the fast, and his companions broke their fast, until they entered Makkah. The wording is that of Sulayman b. Harb."],[11932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked at a brisk pace (ramal) in his Hajj for the first three rounds from the Black Stone to the Black Stone, and walked the [remaining] four."],[11933,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in two white garments and a red one."],[11934,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gifted one hundred camels to Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, with a silver nose ring.\""],[11935,"The Muslims captured one of the prominent men of the idolaters and killed him. Then they asked to ransom him, but the Prophet ﷺ forbade them to sell his corpse."],[11936,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam al-Zuhri over the collection of zakah. He took Abu Rafiʿ with him as a follower. Abu Rafiʿ came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about it. He said: \"O Abu Rafiʿ, charity is unlawful for Muhammad and for the family of Muhammad, and the client of a people is one of them.\""],[11937,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave Abu Qatadah and his spoils.\""],[11938,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Jibril ﷺ conversing privately with him, the horizon of the sky split open. Jibril began to draw near to the earth and sway. Suddenly an angel appeared before the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah commands you to choose between being a prophet-servant and a king-prophet.\" The narrator said: Jibril motioned to me with his hand to be humble, and I knew that he was a sincere adviser to me, so I said: \"A servant-prophet.\" That angel then ascended to the sky. I said: \"O Jibril, I had wanted to ask you about this, but I saw in your state something that distracted me from asking. Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is Israfil. Allah created him, on the day He created him, standing before Him with his feet together, not raising his gaze. Between him and the Lord are seventy veils of light, any of which, if he drew near to it, would burn him. Before him is a tablet. When Allah, may He be exalted, decrees something in the heaven or in the earth, that revelation ascends and strikes his forehead. He looks: if it pertains to my duty, He commands me with it; if it pertains to Mikhaʾil's duty, He commands him with it; and if it pertains to the Angel of Death's duty, He commands him with it.\" I said: \"O Jibril, what are you in charge of?\" He said: \"The wind and the hosts.\" I said: \"What is Mikhaʾil in charge of?\" He said: \"Vegetation and rain.\" I said: \"What is the Angel of Death in charge of?\" He said: \"Taking souls. I did not think he had descended except for the coming of the Hour. What you saw from me was only out of fear of the Hour's coming.\""],[11939,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he stipulated that the land, and all that was yellow and white, meaning gold and silver, belonged to him. The people of Khaybar said to him: \"We know the land better, so give it to us on condition that we work it and have half of the fruit, and you have the other half.\" He mentioned that he gave it to them on that condition. When the time came for the dates to be cut, he sent Ibn Rawahah to them, and he estimated the dates—this is what the people of Madinah call khars (estimation). He said: \"In this there is such-and-such and such-and-such.\" They said: \"You have demanded too much from us, O Ibn Rawahah.\" He said: \"Then I will undertake the estimation of the dates and give you half of what I have said.\" They said: \"This is the truth, and by it the heavens and the earth are established. We are satisfied that you take what you have said.\""],[11940,"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen."],[11941,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"Whatever of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[11942,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and claimed that he had had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give a dinar in charity; if he could not find one, then half a dinar.\""],[11943,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding \"the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: he should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[11944,"The Prophet ﷺ stood over the slain of Badr and said: \"May Allah reward you on my behalf, O band, with evil. You betrayed me though I was trustworthy, and you called me a liar though I was truthful.\" Then he turned to Abu Jahl b. Hisham and said: \"This one was more insolent toward Allah than Pharaoh. When Pharaoh was certain of destruction, he declared Allah's oneness, but when this one was certain of death, he called upon al-Lat and al-'Uzza.\""],[11945,"Salih, the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , seized the property of the people of Khaybar, except for themselves and their children. The Prophet then asked for the whereabouts of their utensils that were used in their weddings, to which they replied that the Prophet had expelled them and they had spent it. The Prophet said, \"See what you say, for if you hide it from me, I will consider it as your blood and that of your descendants.\" Then he called two men from the Ansar and said to them, \"Go to such and such a place and look for a hut with a patch on its roof. Remove the patch and bring me the utensils.\" They went and returned with the utensils. The Messenger of Allah struck their necks and sent for their offspring. Safiyya, who was their bride, was brought to him. He ordered Bilal to take her to his house. Bilal went with her to the house of the Messenger of Allah. He passed by her husband and brother, who were killed. When he returned to the Messenger of Allah, he said, \"Glory be to Allah! O Bilal, why did you bring a virgin girl and pass by two killed men while she saw them? Don't you have any mercy?\" Bilal replied, \"I intended to burn her chest.\" The Messenger of Allah then entered with her and spent the night with her. Abu Ayub brought his sword and sat next to the mattress. He said, \"If I had heard a shepherd or a monk, I would have been close to the Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet then went to Bilal's house and asked, \"Who is this?\" Abu Ayub said, \"I am Abu Ayub.\" The Prophet asked, \"Why are you here at this time?\" Abu Ayub replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, I brought a virgin girl and you had killed her husband and brother, so I was concerned for your safety. I thought I would be close to the Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, Abu Ayub,\" three times. The people then discussed this matter, with some saying it was his secret and others saying she was his wife. When they were leaving, they said, \"Look at the Messenger of Allah, if he covers her, then she is his wife, and if he doesn't cover her, then she is his secret.\" The Messenger of Allah covered her, put her on his knee, and said, \"Mount.\" The Messenger of Allah honored her by putting her foot on his knee, and he put his knee on her thigh, and they rode off together. Before that, he had offered her the choice to either be set free or be married to him, and she chose to be set free and married. And so he did."],[11946,"The Prophet ﷺ was distracted from the 'Asr prayer until the sun had set. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They distracted us from the middle prayer. May Allah fill their graves and their homes with fire.\""],[11947,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on a camel and touched the corner with his staff."],[11948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered one hundred camels as sacrificial animals. He slaughtered sixty of them himself and commanded a man from among his companions, who slaughtered the remaining forty. He ordered him to take a piece from each camel, string them on a thread, cook them in a pot, and then he ate from it and drank the broth."],[11949,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"Do not raise your hands except at seven places; when starting the prayer, when entering Al-Masjid Al-Haram and looking at the Kaaba, when standing on Safa and Marwa, when standing with the people on 'Arafah night and during the Stoning of the Jamarat.\""],[11950,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak members of his household. He took hold of the upper arm of each one of us and said: \"Do not throw the pebbles at the Jamrah until the sun has risen.\""],[11951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled during the month of Ramadan. His companions complained to him of thirst, so he called for water and drank, and then some of the people broke their fast while others continued to fast. Neither of the two groups criticized what the other had done."],[11952,"Regarding His saying: \"They ask you what they should spend. Say: 'The surplus'\" (Q 2:219), he said: \"What is beyond the needs of one's dependents.\""],[11953,"\"The first of them will be detained for the last of them.\""],[11954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived during the truce that was between him and the polytheists, while the polytheists were at the door of the assembly house, near the Black Stone. They had been saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions were suffering from hardship and weakness. When they touched the Black Stone, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"They have been saying that you are suffering from hardship and weakness, so walk briskly (ramal) for three circuits so that they may see that you have strength.\" When they touched the Black Stone, they lifted their legs and walked briskly. Then some of them said to others: \"Do they claim that they are suffering from hardship and weakness? They are not content with walking until they run at a fast pace.\""],[11955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family from Muzdalifah at night, then he came to us one by one, striking us on our thighs. I was one of those he struck on the thigh. Then he said: \"O my son, do not throw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah until the sun has risen.\""],[11956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set free on the day of Taʾif those slaves of the polytheists who came out to him."],[11957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House on his camel and touched the corner with his staff. Then he came to the water station, and his paternal cousins were drawing water from it. He called for a drink, so a bucket was raised to him and he drank from it. Then he said: \"Were it not that people might think it and adopt it as a ritual, and then fight you over it, I would draw water with you.\" Then he went to Safa and Marwah and circumambulated them on his camel."],[11958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah al-Ansari, Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib, and Zayd b. Harithah. ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah lagged behind, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What kept you?\" He said: \"Friday, O Messenger of Allah—I am attending the Friday prayer, then I will set out.\" He said: \"A single morning or evening journey in the path of Allah is better than this world and all it contains.\" So he set out immediately."],[11959,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman who had been killed on the day of the Trench and said: \"Who killed this woman?\" A man said: \"I did, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Why?\" He said: \"She fought me for my sword.\" He then remained silent."],[11960,"\"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen. The Emigrants were sixty-odd men, and the Helpers were two hundred and thirty-six men. The bearer of the banner of the Emigrants was ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ, and the bearer of the banner of the Helpers was Saʿd b. ʿUbadah ؓ.\""],[11961,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: \"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen. The Emigrants were sixty-odd men, and the Helpers were two hundred and thirty-six men. The bearer of the banner of the Emigrants was ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ, and the bearer of the banner of the Helpers was Saʿd b. ʿUbadah ؓ.\""],[11962,"ʿAmmar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: my father narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: \"The distinguishing mark of the angels on the day of Badr was white turbans, which they had let down to their backs, and on the day of Hunayn it was red turbans. The angels did not fight on any day except the day of Badr; they were only there as numbers and reinforcement, not striking.\""],[11963,"ʿAmmar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: my father narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas ؓ who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped during Ramadan and fainted, and for that reason he disliked it.\""],[11964,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting and in a state of ihram.\""],[11965,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles at the Jamrah on the day of sacrifice, then slaughtered, then shaved his head.\""],[11966,"The day of Badr was on the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."],[11967,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who has intercourse with a pregnant woman.\""],[11968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon."],[11969,"Two slaves went out on the day of al-Ta'if while the Prophet ﷺ was besieging them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set them free."],[11970,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Maymunah bt. al-Harith, and she delegated her affair to al-Abbas, so he gave her to him in marriage."],[11971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"I saw the angels washing them (the two of them).\""],[11972,"Regarding His saying: \"The month of Ramadan in which the Qur'an was sent down\" and His saying: \"Indeed, We sent it down on a blessed night,\" he said: \"It was sent down in Ramadan on the Night of Decree, on a blessed night, all at once, then it was sent down gradually at the positions of the stars over the months and days.\""],[11973,"When the Messenger of Allah returned from Uhud, the women of the Ansar cried over their martyrs. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of this and he said, \"But Hamza has no one to mourn him.\" So, the women of the Ansar returned and said to their womenfolk, \"Do not cry for anyone until you lament for Hamza.\" He said about them until this day, \"Do not cry except for Hamza.\""],[11974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us and took off his sandals, so we took off our sandals. When he finished the prayer, he said: \"Why did you take off your sandals?\" They said: \"We saw you take them off, so we took ours off.\" He said: \"I found wetness in them.\""],[11975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver sermons to them while traveling, leaning on his bow."],[11976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver sermons to them while traveling, leaning on his bow."],[11977,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite the Opening of the Book (Surah al-Fatihah) over the funeral prayer."],[11978,"Ali b. Abi Talib was the standard-bearer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr. The standard-bearer of the Muhajirun was Ali, in all the battles, and Qays b. Sa'd b. Ubadah was the standard-bearer of Ali."],[11979,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray twenty units (rak'ahs) and the odd (witr) during Ramadan."],[11980,"That the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ to the disbelievers was: {Come to a word that is equitable between us and you} until the end of the verse."],[11981,"When Abu Sufyan and his companions descended upon the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud, he said to his companions, \"I saw in a dream my sword Dhu al-Faqar broke, and I saw cows being slaughtered, and that is a calamity, and I saw upon me my coat of mail, and it is your city—they will not reach it, God willing.\""],[11982,"That on the day of Badr, the Messenger of God ﷺ had one hundred camels, and with him were two horsemen: one ridden by al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad and the other by Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and Sahl b. Hunayf. He said: His companions took turns riding the camels along the way, and the Messenger of God ﷺ and Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, \"took turns riding a camel.\""],[11983,"\"Al-'Uzza was in Batn Nahlah, al-Lat was in al-Ta'if, and Manat was in Qudayd.\" He said: 'Ali b. al-Ja'd said, \"Batn Nahlah is the garden of Banu 'Amir.\""],[11984,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about that, \"so he ordered him to cover his head and to take for him some trees from this 'aljan and place it upon his legs.\""],[11985,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw Hanzala b. al-Rahib and Hamza being washed by the angels.\""],[11986,"From Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Khalid b. al-Walid and 'Ali b. Abi Talib to Yemen. He placed 'Ali in command of the Muhajirun and placed Khalid in command of the Bedouins. He said: \"And if there is fighting, 'Ali is in command of all the people.\""],[11987,"That the Prophet ﷺ would \"throw the pebbles when the sun had declined, such that when he finished throwing them, he prayed Zuhr.\""],[11988,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the stoning of Ma'iz b. Malik, they came to him and informed him that they had done so. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"He has repented with such a repentance that if a tax-collector had repented with it, it would have been accepted from him.\""],[11989,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib in Paradise with two wings, flying wherever he wished.\""],[11990,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The anger of God Almighty has intensified upon the one who claims that he is the king of kings.\""],[11991,"\"The Conquest was witnessed by one thousand eight hundred from Juhayna, one thousand from Muzayna, nine hundred from Banu Sulaym, four hundred and some from Banu Ghifar, and four hundred and some from Aslam.\""],[11992,"«Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ six children: ʿAbd Allah, al-Qasim, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum, and Fatimah; and Mariyah the Copt bore him Ibrahim.»"],[11993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «O company of the Ansar, who is your chief?» They said: Jadd b. Qays, and we honor him. He said: «He is not your chief; rather, your chief is ʿAmr b. al-Jamuh.» And he was generous."],[11994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to «throw the pebbles at the time of the sun’s decline, such that when he finished his throwing he prayed Zuhr.»"],[11995,"When the Prophet ﷺ stopped at al-Taʾif, he ordered a caller, and he called out: «Any slave who comes out is free.» Two slaves came out to him, and he set them free."],[11996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «O company of merchants, is any one of you unable, when he returns from his market, to recite ten verses, so that Allah writes for him a good deed for each verse?»"],[11997,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to throw the pebbles until the sun rose.»"],[11998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family on from Muzdalifah, then he said: «Do not throw the Jamrah until the sun rises.»"],[11999,"The Prophet ﷺ used to «wipe the sweat from his face during prayer.»"],[12000,"«ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud came upon Abu Jahl on the day of Badr while he was fallen, and he drew his sword and struck his neck, and his head flew off. Then he took his spoils and came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that he had killed Abu Jahl. He made him swear by Allah three times, and he swore, and he gave him his spoils.»"],[12001,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed with tranquility upon him.» And he mentioned the hadith."],[12002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to «pray Zuhr and ʿAsr at Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah.»"],[12003,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five prayers at Mina.»"],[12004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr with [Surat] Bara'ah, then he sent Ali after him and he took it. Abu Bakr said, \"Has something happened concerning me?\" He said, \"No, you are my companion in the cave and at the Pond, and no one should deliver [it] on my behalf except me or Ali.\""],[12005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr and ordered him to proclaim these words, then he sent Ali after him. While Abu Bakr was on part of the road, he heard the grumbling sound of the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr came out startled, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behold it was Ali. He handed him the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He appointed him over the pilgrimage season and ordered Ali to proclaim these words. They both set off and performed the Hajj. Ali stood during the days of Tashriq and proclaimed, \"The protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger is free from every polytheist. So travel freely in the land for four months. No polytheist should perform Hajj after this year, and no one should circumambulate the House naked, and none will enter Paradise except a believer.\" Ali kept proclaiming it, and when his voice became hoarse, Abu Hurayrah stood up and proclaimed it."],[12006,"A man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."],[12007,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12009,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has intercourse with his wife during her menstruation should give a dinar in charity, and whoever has intercourse with her when the blood has stopped but she has not bathed should give half a dinar.\" All of that is from the Prophet ﷺ."],[12011,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating: \"If it was fresh blood, he should give a dinar in charity, and if it was yellowish, then half a dinar.\""],[12012,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying while donkeys were fighting in front of him."],[12013,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in ihram."],[12014,"That the Prophet ﷺ has been cupped while fasting."],[12015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram and fasting."],[12016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while he was in ihram and had cupping done while he was fasting."],[12017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in ihram."],[12018,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is established, begin with the evening meal."],[12019,"Al-Sa'b b. Jaththamah gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a wild donkey as a gift. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Return it to him, for we are in ihram.'"],[12020,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A woman may not grant permission in her husband's house except with his permission, nor may she leave her bed to pray voluntarily except with his permission.'"],[12021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in a red Najrani suit that he used to wear and a shirt."],[12022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments: in his shirt in which he died and an Anbijani suit."],[12023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in a suit that he used to wear and a shirt. Al-Fadl and a man from the Ansar washed him, and the Ansari was pouring water on them and washing under the garment. He was washed while wearing his shirt, which was not removed from him until he had been washed."],[12024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and mannish women."],[12025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' A man said, 'And those who shorten?' He said, 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' A man said, 'And those who shorten?' He said the third or fourth time, 'And those who shorten.'"],[12026,"\"A donation of money never decreases, nor does a servant extend his hand with a charity except that it falls into the hand of Allah before it reaches the beggar, and a servant does not open a door of asking for something out of wealth except that Allah opens a door of poverty on him.\""],[12027,"The first to embrace Islam was Ali."],[12028,"From Ibn Abbas: Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, and a man from the Ansar was killed with him. Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib came with two garments to shroud Hamzah in, but there was no shroud for the Ansari. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots between the two garments, then each of them was shrouded in one garment."],[12029,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House and supplicated in its corners, then he came out and prayed two rak'ahs."],[12030,"The Prophet ﷺ ransomed the captives of Badr, and the ransom for each one of them was four thousand. ʿUqbah b. Abī Muʿayṭ was killed before the ransom. ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib went to him and executed him in retaliation. He said, 'Who will care for the children, O Muḥammad?' He said, 'The Fire.'"],[12031,"In His statement, \"And [remember] when those who disbelieved plotted against you to restrain you or kill you or evict you [from Makkah]. But they plan, and Allah plans. And Allah is the best of planners.\" Quraysh consulted one night in Makkah. Some of them said, \"Let's establish a case against him with evidence, seeking to discredit the Prophet ﷺ.\" Some of them said, \"Kill him!\" And some of them said, \"Expel him!\" Allah informed His Prophet ﷺ about this. Ali stayed in the bed of the Prophet ﷺ that night while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left until he reached the cave. The polytheists guarded it, thinking he was the Prophet ﷺ. When they woke up in the morning, they went after him and when they saw Ali, Allah foiled their plan. They asked, \"Where is your companion?\" He replied, \"I do not know.\" They searched for his footprints and when they reached the mountain, they became disoriented. They climbed the mountain and passed by the cave where they found spider webs covering its entrance. They stayed there for three [days]."],[12032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd to al-Ṭāʾif, and a man shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'How similar this is to the companion of Yā Sīn.'"],[12033,"A man would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from those who had set out, having mentioned only the Ḥajj, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, 'Go and exit the state of iḥrām with an ʿUmrah after he had performed ṭawāf.' The man would say, 'O Messenger of Allah, I set out intending only the Ḥajj.' He would say, 'It is not the Ḥajj, but rather it is an ʿUmrah.'"],[12034,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There are no forty people who intercede for a believer except that Allah accepts their intercession.'"],[12035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us this supplication as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qur'an: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Jahannam, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah al-Dajjāl, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave.'"],[12036,"He said to him, 'O young man, beware of reviling the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for it is destructive.'"],[12037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the illness of the sick, I would have delayed the ʿatamah prayer.'"],[12038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted.'"],[12042,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he drank, would breathe twice."],[12043,"\"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and then stood on his left side, so he took hold of me and made me stand on his right side.\""],[12044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no leader appointed over ten people except that he will be questioned about them on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[12045,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the water distribution point, and a woman came with a son of hers and said, 'My son wants to go on a military expedition, and I am preventing him.' He said, 'Do not leave your mother until she gives you permission, or death takes her, for that is greater for your reward.'"],[12046,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Prayer is not to be performed facing a grave, nor upon a grave.'"],[12047,"\"Narrated by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Whoever makes a vow but does not specify it, then its expiation is like the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow in disobedience to Allah, then its expiation is like the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that they cannot afford, then its expiation is the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that they can afford, then let them fulfill it.'\""],[12048,"Ibn Abbas, Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Azhar, and Miswar ibn Makhrama said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade praying after Asr prayer.\""],[12049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house and found a picture of Ibrahim and Maryam in it, so he said, \"As for them, they know that the angels do not enter a house with a picture. This is Ibrahim portrayed, so what is the matter with him that he is splitting?\""],[12050,"I spent the night with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He got up, performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs until that amounted to ten rak'ahs, then he performed Witr with three rak'ahs, then he lay down and slept until he snored; his sleep was with snoring. Then the muezzin called him to the Morning Prayer, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."],[12051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer after 'Asr."],[12052,"Ibn Abbas saw 'Abd Allah b. al-Harith praying while his head was tied up behind him, so he went and stood behind him and began to undo it, while the other remained still for him. Then when he finished, he came to Ibn Abbas and said, 'What do you have against my head?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The likeness of this is the likeness of one who prays while bound hand and foot.\"\""],[12053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gold ring on the hand of a man, so he removed it and threw it away, and said: “Would one of you deliberately take an ember of fire and place it in his hand?” After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, it was said to the man, “Take your ring and benefit from it.” He said, “No, by Allah, I will not take it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has thrown it away.”"],[12054,"A woman lifted up a child to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'Is there Hajj for this one?' He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12055,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was traveling on the road to Makkah, a woman spoke to him from her howdah, and she took hold of the upper arm of a child and lifted him up, saying, 'Is there Hajj for this one, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'For him is a Hajj, and for you is a reward.'"],[12056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The sisters are believers: Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith, Salma the wife of Hamzah, and Asma' bt. 'Umays - she is their sister through their mother."],[12057,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The foremost women of the people of Paradise after Maryam bt. 'Imran are Fatimah, Khadijah, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.'"],[12058,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Abu Bakr to lead the Hajj, and he did not approach the Ka'bah, but rather he headed to Dhu al-Majaz informing the people of their rites and conveying to them from the Messenger of God ﷺ, until they came to 'Arafah before Dhu al-Majaz. That was because they had not performed 'Umrah along with Hajj."],[12059,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a gap between his front teeth; when he spoke, it was seen as light between his two front teeth."],[12060,"O Messenger of God, is there Hajj for this one? He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12061,"O Messenger of God, is there Hajj for this one? He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12062,"I slept in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, while the Prophet ﷺ was with her, so that I might see how the Prophet ﷺ prayed at night. The Prophet ﷺ spoke with his family for a while, then slept. When it was the last third of the night or half of it, he got up and looked at the sky and recited: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding} until he recited these verses. Then he got up, performed ablution, and used the toothstick. Then he prayed eleven rak'ahs. Then Bilal called the Adhan for prayer, so he prayed two rak'ahs, then went out and led the people in the Morning Prayer."],[12063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Frequented House (al-Bayt al-Ma'mur) in the sky is called al-Surah, and it is aligned with the Sacred House, directly above it; if it fell, it would fall upon it. Every day seventy thousand angels enter it, never having seen it before. And it has in the sky a sanctity equal to the sanctity of Makkah.\" He said: \"And every day seventy thousand angels enter the House, never to enter it again ever.\""],[12064,"Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was forty years old. He remained in Makkah for thirteen years thereafter, then migrated to Madinah and stayed there for ten years, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[12065,"When the Prophet ﷺ commanded the people to exit the state of ihram by performing an 'umrah during the Farewell Hajj, a man would come and say, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is the Hajj,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, \"It is not the Hajj; it is only an 'umrah.\""],[12066,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. I saw him get up during the night, relieve himself, then go to the water skin, untie its strap, and perform a wudu that was between two wudus. Then he returned to his bed and slept. Then he went to the water skin, untied its strap, performed the full wudu, and prayed. So I got up and did as he had done, then I came to him and stood on his left. He turned me around and placed me on his right. He prayed either eleven or thirteen rak'ahs, then slept until he snored. I heard him say in his prostration: \"O Allah, place light in my heart, place light in my hearing, place light in my sight, place light behind me, place light in front of me, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light above me, place light below me, and grant me great light.\" Then he slept until he snored, and Bilal came to him and called him to the prayer, and he went out."],[12067,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith. The Prophet ﷺ got up during the night, went to relieve himself, then came and washed his face and hands. Then he stood to pray during the night. He went to the water skin and performed a wudu between two wudus, not using much water but making it complete. Then he stood to pray. He said: I stepped aside, disliking that he should see that I was observing him, meaning I was watching him. Then I got up and did as he had done, and I stood on his left. He took hold of the part next to my ear and turned me around until I was on his right, while he was praying. His prayer was completed at thirteen rak'ahs, including the two rak'ahs of Fajr. Then he lay down and slept until he snored. Then Bilal came and called him to the prayer, and he got up and prayed without renewing his wudu."],[12068,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and I said, \"I will certainly memorize the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and how he performs it.\" He came from the mosque, went to a corner of the house, relieved himself, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and washed his face and hands. Then he lay down and remained as long as Allah willed. Then he got up, went to a corner of the house, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and performed a wudu between two wudus, not using much water but making the wudu complete. Then he came to the mosque. He said: I did as he had done, then I came and stood on his left. He took my hand, pulled it from behind me, and placed me on his right. He prayed eight rak'ahs, then prayed three rak'ahs of witr, then prayed two rak'ahs, then said: \"O Allah, grant me light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in front of me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light below me, and light above me. O Allah, give me light, grant me light, and magnify light for me.\""],[12069,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, and I observed how many rak'ahs the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He got up, urinated, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and poured water into a bowl or a large dish. He washed his face and forearms, then slept. Then he got up and performed a good wudu between two wudus, then stood to pray. I came and stood on his left. He took hold of me and placed me on his right. The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night was completed at thirteen rak'ahs. Then he slept, and his sleep was known by his snoring. He slept until he snored, then went out for the prayer. He used to say in his prayer or in his supplication: \"O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my heart, light on my right, light on my left, light in front of me, light behind me, light above me, and light below me, and grant me light.\""],[12070,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, both from Malik b. Anas, from Makhramah b. Sulayman, from Kurayb, that Ibn 'Abbas informed him that he spent the night at the house of his maternal aunt Maymunah. He said: \"She lay down across the width of the cushion, and the Prophet ﷺ and his family lay along its length. The Prophet ﷺ slept until midnight, or a little before it, or a little after it. Then he woke up, sat up, and wiped the sleep from his face with his hands. Then he recited the ten concluding verses of Surah Al 'Imran. Then he went to a hanging water skin, performed wudu from it and made his wudu excellent. Then he stood to pray. I did as he had done, then I went and stood at his side. He placed his hand on my head and took hold of my ear, twisting it. He prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then performed witr, and lay down until the mu'adhdhin came to him. He got up and prayed two light rak'ahs, then prayed the Fajr prayer.\""],[12071,"I spent the night at Maymunah's house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her that night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu and stood to pray. I stood on his left, and he took hold of me and placed me on his right. He prayed thirteen rak'ahs that night, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until he snored, and when he slept he would snore. Then the mu'adhdhin came to him, and he went out and prayed without renewing his wudu."],[12072,"My father sent me to the Prophet ﷺ with a gift. I came to him while he was in the house of Maymunah. He made me lie down on the rest of the cushion. When it was the middle of the night, he got up, looked at the sky, then recited the end of Surah Al 'Imran: 'Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth...' until he finished it. Then he went to a hanging water container, used the siwak, performed wudu and made it complete, and did not pour out much water. Then he moved me, so I got up and performed wudu. I stood on his left, and he turned me around, so I stood on his right. He began to recite while twisting my ear. He prayed ten rak'ahs, then performed witr, then slept, and when he slept he would snore. Then Bilal came to him and woke him for the prayer. He got up and prayed two light rak'ahs, then went out for the prayer."],[12073,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no one who, when they want to be intimate with their spouse, says: 'In the name of Allah, O Allah, protect us from Satan and keep Satan away from what You have blessed us with.' Then, if they are blessed with a child, Satan will not harm that child.\""],[12074,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of one who prays with his head tied back is that of one who prays while bound.\""],[12075,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of one who prays with his head tied back is only that of one who prays while bound.\""],[12076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House and found in it an image of Ibrahim and an image of Maryam. He said, “As for them, they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so what is the matter with him that he is seeking divination by arrows?”"],[12077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “All of Muzdalifah is a standing place, and keep away from the interior of Muhassir, and use pebbles like those thrown in khadhf.”"],[12078,"“We did not know the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except by his takbir.”"],[12079,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of Allah, I have been enlisted in such-and-such an expedition, while my wife intends to perform Hajj.” He said, “Return and perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man should not be alone with a woman, nor should he travel with her unless she has a mahram with her.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to join such-and-such an army, while my wife intends to perform Hajj.” He said, “Then perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A woman should not travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her unless she has a mahram with her.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to go out in such-and-such an army, while my wife wants to perform Hajj.” He said, “Go out with her.”"],[12082,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon: “A woman should not travel unless she has a mahram with her.” A man stood up and said, “I have been enlisted in the expedition, and I want to send my wife for Hajj.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12083,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “A man should never be alone with a woman unless she has a mahram with her, and she should not travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her except with a mahram.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, my wife has set out for Hajj, and I have been enlisted in such-and-such an expedition.” He said, “Then turn back and perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12084,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on a carpet.”"],[12085,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muadh to Yemen, he said, “You will come upon a people of the Book. Let the first thing to which you call them be the worship of Allah. When they acknowledge that, then inform them that Allah ﷻ has obligated upon them five prayers in their day and night. When they do that, then inform them that Allah has obligated upon them a zakah to be taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. When they do that, then take from them, and beware of taking the best of their wealth.”"],[12086,"A man died and left no inheritance for anyone. So the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seek out [relatives].\" They could not find anyone to inherit him, so the Prophet ﷺ gave his inheritance to his freed slave who was loyal to him and the one who freed him."],[12087,"“A man died in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and left no heir except a slave of his. He freed him and ﷺ gave him his inheritance.”"],[12088,"A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no heir was found to inherit from him, while he had a client whom the deceased had freed. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Give him his wealth.”"],[12089,"Do people raise their voices with dhikr upon finishing the prescribed prayer? Did the Prophet ﷺ do it? Ibn Abbas said: \"I knew it when I heard it.\""],[12090,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevents the Ethiopians of Banu al-Mughira from coming to you except that they fear you will reject them.\" He said: \"There is no good in the Ethiopians: when they are hungry they steal, and when they are full they fornicate. Yet they have two good qualities: feeding food and courage in battle.\""],[12091,"\"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, then woke up, performed ablution, and used the siwak. He did that several times during the night.\""],[12092,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"The siwak cleanses the mouth and pleases the Lord.\""],[12093,"From the Prophet ﷺ is it? If the Prophet ﷺ recited it, I recites it; and if the Prophet ﷺ did not recite it, I do not recite it. Then the man left and said to me: \"O Shu'bah, he rejected it.\" So I rejected it, and he said: \"Woe to you! If he had recited it, the people would have known it.\""],[12094,"\"I passed with al-Fadl b. al-Abbas on a donkey before the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he neither forbade us nor turned us back.\""],[12095,"\"I know of no harm in it, and I do not think the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it when he forbade except due to arrogance and pride, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that.\" He said: \"What are these birds in the brazier?\" He said: \"Do you not see how we burned them with fire?\" When al-Miswar left, he said: \"Remove this garment from me and cut off the heads of these statues, or images.\""],[12096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"would show the whiteness of his armpits when he prostrated.\""],[12097,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"sent him with his family to Mina on the Day of Sacrifice, and they threw the jamrah at dawn.\""],[12098,"\"He said, 'When he purifies himself from sexual impurity, he pours water with his right hand onto his left hand seven times.'\" Then he said, \"How many times have you poured water onto my hands, O Shu'bah?\" I said, \"I don't know.\" He said, \"You have no mother and what prevents you from knowing?\" Then he performed ablution for prayer and poured water over himself, and said, \"This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to purify himself.\""],[12099,"\"Seven are forbidden by lineage and seven by marriage.\" Then he recited: {Forbidden to you are your mothers} until he reached {and daughters of the sister}. Then he said: \"This is lineage.\" Then he recited: {And your mothers who nursed you} until he reached {and that you gather between two sisters}. Then he recited: {And do not marry what your fathers married of women}. Then he said: \"This is marriage.\""],[12100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only forbade domestic donkeys for fear of a shortage of riding animals."],[12101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the first thing that Allah created was the pen and the fish.\" He was asked, \"What is being written?\" He replied, \"Everything that will exist until the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he recited the letter \"Nun\" (which refers to a chapter of the Quran) and said, \"By the pen and by what they write.\" It was not lifted from Hammad ibn Zaid except by Muammal ibn Isma'il."],[12102,"Al-ʿAbbas came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"You have left rancor among us since you did what you did.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"They will not attain good until they love you for Allah and for my kinship. Do you hope—Sulayb, a tribe of Murad—for my intercession, while Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib do not hope for it?\""],[12103,"One day we woke up and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were weeping, with each woman's family around her. I went out to the mosque and found it filled with people. Then ʿUmar came and went up to the Prophet ﷺ, who was in an upper room. He greeted him but he did not answer. He said, \"Have you divorced your wives?\" He said, \"No, but I have made an oath of abstention.\" He stayed away for twenty-nine days, then came down to his family."],[12104,"The Prophet ﷺ entered into ihram after the prayer."],[12105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Security and well-being are two blessings in which many people are deceived.\""],[12108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"I do not ask you for any reward for it, except that you fulfill my right in regard to my kinship with you, and that you maintain the ties of kinship between me and you.\""],[12109,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated, he would turn the inside of his palms toward his face."],[12110,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"No one who has an atom's weight of pride will enter Paradise.\""],[12111,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not pass the miqat except in a state of ihram.\""],[12112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his leather socks, and his companions wiped over theirs. But did he wipe after Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed?"],[12113,"There was no clan of Quraysh except that the Prophet ﷺ was born of it or had kinship among them. Say, 'I do not ask you for any reward for it, except that you restrain me and refrain from me for my kinship with you.'"],[12114,"A man was thrown by his she-camel and died while in a state of ihram. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Wash him with water and sidr, shroud him in his two garments, and do not apply perfume to him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12115,"From Ibn Abbas, tracing it back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs after the last evening prayer (al-'isha al-akhirah), reciting in the first two rak'ahs 'Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun' and 'Qul huwa Allahu ahad,' and reciting in the last two rak'ahs 'Tanzil al-Sajdah' and 'Tabaraka alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk,' they will be recorded for him as four rak'ahs from the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr).\""],[12116,"Healing is in three things: a drink of honey, a cupping incision, and cauterization with fire. And I forbid my community from cauterization."],[12117,"The passage translates to: \"Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet? And in the Hereafter, there is something similar to that.\""],[12118,"\"The Quran was sent down all at once, then it was sent down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in stages (as stars).\""],[12119,"His father said to him: \"O my son, ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a garment from his clothes to shroud me in, and ask him to pray over me.\" Abdullah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you know the honor of Abdullah, and he has commanded me to ask you for a garment to shroud him in and for you to pray over him.\" So he gave him a garment from his clothes and intended to pray over him. Umar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you know Abdullah and his hypocrisy. Will you pray over him when Allah has forbidden you to pray over him?\" He said: \"And where?\" He said: \"{If you seek forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.}\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then I will increase beyond seventy.\" Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {And do not pray over any one of them who has died, ever, nor stand at his grave} and Allah revealed: {It is all the same for them whether you seek forgiveness for them or do not seek forgiveness for them; Allah will never forgive them.} He said: A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prolonged his sitting. The Prophet ﷺ went out three times so that the man would follow him, but he did not. Then Umar ؓ entered and saw the man, and he recognized the displeasure in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his staying. He said: \"Perhaps you have annoyed the Prophet ﷺ.\" The man understood and stood up. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I stood up three times so that you would follow me, but you did not.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would appoint a doorkeeper, for your wives are not like other women, and it is purer for their hearts.\" Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you} to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Umar and informed him of that. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about the captives. Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, spare your people and take ransom from them, and use it to strengthen yourselves.\" Umar b. al-Khattab said: \"Kill them.\" He said: \"If you two were in agreement, I would not disobey you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ followed the advice of Abu Bakr. Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land. You desire the goods of this world, but Allah desires the Hereafter.} He said: Then it was revealed: {And certainly We created man from an extract of clay} to the end of the verses. Umar said: \"Blessed be Allah, the best of creators.\" Then it was revealed: {So blessed be Allah, the best of creators.}"],[12120,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,\" the polytheists mocked him and said: \"Muhammad mentions the god of al-Yamamah.\" Musaylimah used to call himself al-Rahman. When this verse was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded not to recite it aloud."],[12121,"\"It is not forbidden for you.\" Then he recited: {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you?} \"But you owe the most severe of expiations: a slave.\""],[12122,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that an animal be made a target (by tying it and shooting at it).\""],[12123,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"When a man enters paradise, he will ask about his parents, his wife, and his children. It will be said to him that they have not reached your level of righteousness and deeds. He will then say, 'O Lord, I have done good for myself and for them.' He will be commanded to join them with him (in paradise). And Ibn Abbas recited the verse: 'And those who believed and their descendants followed them in faith...' until the end of the verse.\""],[12124,"In his saying, \"O man,\" Taha said."],[12125,"The daughter of Khalid b. Sinan came to the Prophet ﷺ. He spread his garment for her and said, \"The daughter of a prophet whom his people neglected.\""],[12126,"The Prophet ﷺ would not pray on the two Eids before the prayer or after it."],[12127,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Hajj is the jihad, and the Umrah is voluntary.\""],[12128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank while standing."],[12129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be at the end of time people who dye with black like the crops of birds; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[12130,"While Jibril ﷺ was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a creaking sound from above him. He raised his head and said: “This is a gate of heaven that has been opened today, never opened before except today.” An angel descended from it, and he said: “This is an angel who has descended to the earth, never descended except today.” He greeted and said: “Rejoice in two lights that you have been given, which no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah. You will not recite a single letter of them without being given it.”"],[12131,"O Messenger of Allah, I had intercourse with my wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to free a slave. The value of a slave on that day was a dinar."],[12132,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Be independent of people even with the stem of a toothbrush.\""],[12133,"A barren wind seized them on the Day of Badr."],[12134,"When the verse {Say: I ask of you no reward for it, save love of the near of kin} was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, who are your kin whose love has become obligatory upon us? He said: “Ali, Fatimah, and their two sons ؓ.”"],[12135,"When the verse {Those whom the angels take while they are wronging themselves} up to the end of the verse was revealed, he said: “There were people in Makkah who had embraced Islam. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Madinah, they disliked migrating and were afraid.” Then Allah, Exalted is He, revealed {Those whom the angels take} up to His saying {except the oppressed}."],[12136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me a sheet and an inkwell, so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.” They said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is delirious.” Then they fell silent, and he fell silent. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall we not bring it to you afterwards?” He said: “After what?”"],[12137,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He was forbidden to use any living thing as a target."],[12138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not take any living thing as a target.”"],[12139,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed on the day of Eid Al-Fitr and did not pray before or after it, then he went to the women with Bilal, and he commanded them to give charity. So the woman threw her jewelry and her worn-out clothes.\""],[12140,"He heard the call, then did not come to it – then there is no prayer for him, except with an excuse."],[12141,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever hears the call and does not answer it without an excuse, then there is no prayer for him.”"],[12142,"The Prophet ﷺ interjected in the middle of his speech and said: “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[12143,"Death or to Makkah."],[12144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not take anything with a soul as a target.\""],[12145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ expiated with a sa' of dates and commanded the people to do that; whoever could not find it, then half a sa'."],[12146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to seek protection for Hasan and Husayn: \"I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of God from every devil, venomous creature, and every evil eye.\""],[12147,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters upon a sick person whose appointed time has not come and says in his presence seven times: 'I ask God, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,' he will be granted well-being.\""],[12148,"\"I spent the night with the Prophet ﷺ, and he called for a cushion of haircloth for me and placed it under my head.\""],[12149,"That He not make them into sects, and not make some of them taste the might of others, but He refused.\""],[12150,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Three persons whose prayer God does not accept: a leader of a people while they dislike him, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who have severed relations.\""],[12151,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not have mercy on our young, respect our old, and recognize our right.\""],[12152,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"There is no man who visits a sick person and says: 'I ask God, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you' seven times, while his appointed time has a delay, except that it is lightened for him.\""],[12153,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no deed more beloved to God than a deed performed during these ten days, except a man who goes out as a warrior with his own self and his wealth, then does not return.\""],[12154,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the night in which I was taken on the Night Journey, I found a pleasant fragrance. So I said, 'O Jibril, what is this pleasant fragrance?' He said, 'This is the fragrance of the comb of the daughter of Fir'awn and her children.' I asked, 'What is the matter with her?' He said, 'While she was combing the daughter of Fir'awn, the comb fell from her hand, so she said, 'In the name of Allah.' Fir'awn's daughter said to her, 'Is it my father or your Lord that you seek?' She said, 'Rather, my Lord and your Lord and the Lord of your father is Allah.' She said, 'Do you have a Lord other than my father?' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Then I will inform him about that.' She said, 'Yes.' So she informed him, and he called her and said, 'O so-and-so, do you have a Lord other than me?' She said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' So he commanded for a cow made of copper to be taken, and it was heated and her children were thrown into it one by one. She said, 'I have a request for you.' He said, 'What is it?' She said, 'I want my bones and the bones of my child to be gathered together and placed in one shroud, and we be buried together.' He said, 'That is upon you.' So her children continued to be thrown into the cow until it reached her infant son. It was as if she hesitated for his sake, so he said to her, 'O mother, go ahead, for the punishment of this world is easier than the punishment of the Hereafter.' Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Then four people stood up to speak, 'Eesa ibn Maryam, the companion of Jurayj, the witness of Yusuf, and the son of Fir'awn's maid. And the narration is from the Hadith of Abu 'Umar ad-Dariri.\""],[12155,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Sulayman, the Prophet of God ﷺ, when he stood in his place of prayer, saw a tree standing firmly before him. He said to it: 'What is your name?' It replied: 'The carob.' He said: 'For what purpose are you?' It replied: 'For the ruin of this house.' So Sulayman said: 'O God, conceal my death from the jinn so that humans know that the jinn do not know the unseen.' He carved it into a staff upon which he leaned, and the woodworm ate it, so it fell, and he collapsed. They estimated its consumption by the woodworm and found it to be a year. Thus it became clear to humans that if the jinn had known the unseen, they would not have remained in the humiliating punishment for a year. Ibn Abbas used to recite it thus: 'The jinn thanked the woodworm, and it used to bring water to it wherever it was.'\""],[12156,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Prostration is on seven body parts: the two hands, the two feet, the two knees, and the forehead; and raising the hands when you see the House, and on al-Safa and al-Marwa, and at ʿArafa, and at Jamʿ, and when throwing the jamarat, and when the prayer is called."],[12157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Seventy prophets prayed in the Mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa — it is as if I am looking at him, wearing two Qatwani cloaks, in a state of ihram, on a camel of the Shanu'a camels, muzzled with a fiber nose-rein that had two braids."],[12158,"From the Prophet ﷺ: When one of you sneezes and says 'al-hamdu lillah', the angels say 'Rabb al-ʿalamin'. Then when he says 'Rabb al-ʿalamin', the angels say 'May Allah have mercy on you'."],[12159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Black Stone was whiter than snow, but the sins of the children of Adam made it black.\""],[12160,"From the Prophet ﷺ: I was commanded to use the siwak so much that I feared for my teeth."],[12161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs, then said: Ask these people who claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs after Surah al-Ma'ida. By Allah, he did not wipe after al-Ma'ida. To wipe over the back of a piebald camel would be more beloved to me than to wipe over them."],[12162,"I have not seen a people better than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They did not ask him except about thirteen matters until he passed away, all of them in the Qur'an. Among them: {They ask you about the sacred month}, {They ask you about wine and gambling}, {They ask you about orphans}, {They ask you about menstruation}, {They ask you about the spoils of war}, {They ask you what they should spend}. They would not ask except about what benefited them. He said: The first to circumambulate the House were the angels. Between the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner are graves of the prophets. When his people harmed him, a prophet would leave from among them and worship Allah in that place until he died."],[12163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabiʿ al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from ʿAta' b. al-Sa'ib, from Saʿid b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbas ؓ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I asked my Lord a question that I wish I had not asked. I said: O Lord, before me there were messengers, some of whom You subjected the winds to, and some of whom used to revive the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and give you shelter? Did I not find you astray and guide you? Did I not find you poor and enrich you? Did I not expand your chest for you and remove from you your burden? I said: Yes, O Lord. And their wording is the same.[1]"],[12164,"A bowl of tharid was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Eat from its sides and do not eat from its middle, for the blessing descends in its middle."],[12165,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ to show him the rites. Thabir split open for him, and he entered Mina and showed him the jamarat, then showed him Jamʿ and showed him ʿArafat. When he was at the first jamra, Iblis appeared to him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank. Then he appeared to him again — until he mentioned Jamrat al-ʿAqaba — and he sank and went away."],[12168,"Jibril went with the Prophet ﷺ to show him the rites. He brought him to Jamrat al-ʿAqaba, and there was Iblis upon it. He commanded him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank into the earth. Then he came to the middle jamra, and there was Iblis, so he commanded him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank into the earth. Then he came to the third one and did the same to him. Then he brought him to Jamʿ, then he performed talbiya from ʿArafat."],[12169,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Eid, and he began praying before the sermon, without calling the adhan or iqamah. Then he rode his mount and delivered a sermon on it. After that, he approached the women and gave a sermon to them and urged them to give charity. He said, \"O women, give charity.\" So, women started throwing their garments, rings, and earrings into Bilal's garment."],[12170,"The Jews disputed with the Prophet ﷺ, saying: You eat from what we kill but do not eat from what Allah kills. Then Allah, exalted be He, sent down: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."],[12171,"When it was revealed, it became difficult for the Muslims and hard on them, so Allah abrogated it and sent down: {Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity}."],[12172,"When the Quran descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would receive it with his tongue and lips, and from that he endured great hardship. Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it} (Q 75:16), meaning: to hasten to take it. He says: {Indeed upon Us is its collection and its recitation} (Q 75:17), meaning: to collect it in your heart and that you recite it. {So when We have recited it} (Q 75:18), meaning: when We have sent it down, {then follow its recitation} (Q 75:18), meaning: listen and be silent. {Then indeed upon Us is its explanation} (Q 75:19), meaning: to make it clear by your tongue. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found relief."],[12173,"Regarding the words of Allah ﷻ: {Woe to you, and woe! Then woe to you, and woe!} (Q 75:34-35), is it something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, or something Allah sent down? He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it, then Allah sent it down.\""],[12174,"While I was circumambulating with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a man say: 'O Allah, forgive so-and-so son of so-and-so.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is this?' He said: 'A man asked me to supplicate for him.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Your companion has been forgiven.'"],[12175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We wish that Musa had been patient with him, so that he would relate to us of their affair.'"],[12176,"The Prophet ﷺ married while in a state of ihram."],[12177,"Dreams of the prophets are revelation."],[12178,"Regarding His words: {You are the best nation produced for mankind} (Q 3:110), he said: 'They are those who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Madinah.'"],[12179,"Ma'iz came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed twice. Then he said: 'Take him away.' Then he said: 'Bring him back,' and he confessed twice more, until he confessed four times. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Take him away and stone him.'"],[12180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ma'iz b. Malik: 'Is what has reached me about you true?' He said: 'What has reached you about me?' He said: 'It has reached me that you committed intercourse with the slave girl of the Banu So-and-so.' He said: 'Yes.' Then he testified four times, and he ordered that he be stoned."],[12181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the shade of a chamber, and the shade was about to recede from him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man will come to you looking at you with the eyes of a devil. When he comes to you, do not speak to him.' They had not waited long before a man appeared before them. He called him and said: 'Why do you and your companions revile me?' He said: 'Call them.' So he called them, and they began swearing by Allah that they had not said or done anything, until he pardoned them. Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {On the Day when Allah will resurrect them all, and they will swear to Him as they swear to you} (Q 58:18), to the end of the verse."],[12182,"The Ansar's houses were far from the mosque, and they wanted to move closer to the mosque. Then the verse was sent down: {And We record what they have sent ahead and their traces} (Q 36:12), so they remained in their houses."],[12183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform qunut in the dawn prayer, supplicating against a clan of Banu Sulaym."],[12184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” Then he recited: {As We began the first creation, We will repeat it. [That is] a promise binding upon Us. Indeed, We will do it.} The first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, and men from my companions will be taken to the right and to the left. I will say, “My companions!” It will be said, “They kept turning back on their heels since you left them.” I will say as the righteous servant Isa ibn Maryam said: {I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me up, You were the Observer over them, and You are, over all things, Witness.} {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, indeed it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.}"],[12185,"“Marry, for the best of this nation had the most wives.”"],[12186,"“There is no repentance for the murderer of a believer; no verse has abrogated it since it was revealed.”"],[12187,"“It was revealed among the last of what was revealed, and nothing has abrogated it.”"],[12188,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you?” No one answered him. Then he said: “Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you?” A man said, “I am,” and a man from them had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What prevented you from speaking when I spoke?” He said, “I thought, O Messenger of Allah, that something had been revealed about my people, and I disliked being the one to bring it to them.” He said: “No, indeed your companion is being detained by his debt.”"],[12189,"Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined.” He said, “What has ruined you?” He said, “I turned my saddle [i.e., changed position during intercourse].” He did not reply to him until it was revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish;} he said, “From the front or the back, but avoid the anus and menstruation.”"],[12190,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, Iblis let out a wail at which his troops gathered to him. He said, “Despair of ever bringing the nation of Muhammad back to polytheism after this day of yours; but tempt them in their religion and spread wailing among them.”"],[12191,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while fasting and in ihram.”"],[12192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “would not omit fasting on the White Days, whether traveling or resident.”"],[12193,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a man from the Ansar. When he approached his house, he heard him speaking inside. When he asked permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “I heard you speaking to someone else.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I entered the room distressed by people’s talk because of the fever I had. Then a visitor came in to me, a man whose sitting I have never seen more noble nor whose speech finer, after you.” He said, “That was Jibril ﷺ . Indeed, among you are men such that if one of them swore by Allah, He would fulfill his oath.”"],[12194,"Quraysh came to the Jews and asked, “With what did Musa bring to you?” They said, “His staff and his hand white for the beholders.” They came to the Christians and asked, “How was Isa?” They said, “He healed the blind and the leper, and revived the dead.” Then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Call upon your Lord to make Safa gold for us.” He called upon his Lord, and this verse was revealed: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding.} So let them reflect on them."],[12195,"The Prophet ﷺ “would pray two rak‘ahs after Maghrib, prolonging the recitation in them until the people of the mosque dispersed.”"],[12196,"The Quraysh used to circumambulate the House naked, whistling and clapping, so Allah ﷻ revealed {Say, 'Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah?'} and they were commanded to wear clothes."],[12197,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {Verily, the friends of Allah—no fear shall be upon them, nor shall they grieve}: he said, \"Allah is remembered by seeing them.\""],[12198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which good deeds are more beloved to Allah or in which the good deed is better than the ten days.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad?\" He said, \"Not even jihad, except for a man who goes out with himself and his wealth and does not return with anything.\""],[12199,"Narrated by the Prophet, ﷺ , \"There are no deeds during the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah that are more beloved to Allah than performing Jihad in His cause, except for a man who goes out with his life and his wealth and does not return with anything from that.\""],[12200,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said, \"There are no days of this world in which deeds are more excellent than the ten days.\" A man said, \"Not even the like of them in the path of Allah?\" three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the third time, \"Except one who does not return.\""],[12201,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him that her sister had vowed to fast for a month, but she had embarked on the sea and died without fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fast on behalf of your sister.\""],[12202,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother died with a month's fast owed by her; shall I make it up on her behalf?\" He said, \"If your mother had a debt, would you pay it on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\" Sulayman said: al-Hakam and Salamah b. Kuhayl, while we were all sitting when Muslim narrated this hadith, said: We heard Mujahid mention this hadith from Ibn Abbas."],[12203,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother made a month's fast obligatory upon herself and she died.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you think if she had a debt, you would pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12204,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My father died without performing Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said, \"If your father had a debt, would you pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12205,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[12206,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan; and he used to recite in the Friday prayer: Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la and Hal Ataka Hadith al-Ghashiyah."],[12207,"When the Prophet ﷺ recited Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la, he said, \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.\""],[12208,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, Abu Bakr said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been expelled—we will all surely perish.\" When this verse was revealed: {Permission is given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and Allah is surely able to give them victory} {Those who have been expelled from their homes}, Abu Bakr knew that there would be fighting."],[12209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs at night, then leave and use the siwak."],[12210,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be brief in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need.”"],[12211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man hates the Ansar while believing in Allah and the Last Day, and no man loves Thaqif while believing in Allah and the Last Day.”"],[12212,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five prayers at Mina."],[12213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Umm Salamah: “This is ʿAli b. Abi Talib; his flesh is my flesh and his blood is my blood. He is to me of the station of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.”"],[12214,"Al-Saʿb b. Jaththamah gifted the Prophet ﷺ — while he was at Qudayd — the hindquarter of a wild donkey, but he returned it while it was dripping blood."],[12215,"Al-Saʿb b. Jaththamah gifted the Prophet ﷺ the hindquarter of a wild donkey, dripping blood, but he returned it and said: “We are in a state of ihram.”"],[12216,"\"He heard the call but did not respond, so he has no prayer.\" This was narrated by Al-Qattarani from Sulaiman ibn Harb in a standing position, and it was also narrated by Ismail ibn Ishaq Al-Qadi from Sulaiman ibn Harb in a raised position."],[12217,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The first to be called to Paradise are the ḥammādūn — those who praise Allah in prosperity and adversity.”"],[12218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ said: “O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you, and I do not mind. Even if you were to come to Me with sins nearly filling the earth, I would meet you with nearly as much forgiveness, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. Even if your sins reached the height of the sky, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you.”"],[12219,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , entered the Kaaba and offered two rak'ahs (units of prayer) in between the Sariyatayn (the two pillars in the Kaaba), then he left and offered two rak'ahs between the door of the Kaaba and the Hajar (the stone). Then he said, 'This is the qibla (direction of prayer).' Then he entered again and stood up to supplicate but did not offer prayer.\""],[12220,"“The polytheists used to say in the talbiyah: ‘Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka illa sharikan huwa laka tamlikuhu wa ma malak.’ Then Allah ﷻ revealed: ‘Do you have among those whom your right hands possess partners in what We have provided for you, so that you are equal in it, and you fear them as you fear yourselves?’”"],[12221,"I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up, startled, asked for water, performed wudu, then recited: “Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth…” to the end of the surah. Then he began al-Baqarah and recited it letter by letter until he completed it. Then he bowed and said: “Subhana Rabbiya al-ʿAzim.” Then he prostrated and said: “Subhana Rabbiya al-Aʿla.” Then he raised his head and said between the two prostrations: “Rabbi ighfir li wa-rhamni wa-jburni wa-rfaʿni wa-rzuqni wa-hdini.” Then he stood and recited in the second rakʿah Al ʿImran until he completed it. Then he bowed and prostrated, then he did as he had done in the first. Then he lay down. Then he got up, startled, and did as he had done in the first two, reciting letter by letter, until he had prayed eight rakʿahs, lying down between every two rakʿahs, and he performed witr with three. Then he prayed two rakʿahs of fajr. Then he said: “Allahumma ajʿal fi nafsi nuran wa fi qalbi nuran wa fi basari nuran wa fi samʿi nuran wa-jʿal bayna yadayya nuran wa min khalfi nuran wa ʿan yamini nuran wa ʿan shimali nuran wa min tahti nuran wa min fawqi nuran wa aʿzim li nuran.”"],[12222,"The Prophet ﷺ performed saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[12223,"The Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at the Jamrah."],[12224,"When {And warn your closest kindred} was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ climbed al-Safa and said, \"Woe to the morning!\""],[12225,"\"Allah took the covenant of the prophets for their people.\""],[12226,"\"The borrowed item.\""],[12227,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, green jars, and wooden vessels, and that dates and raisins be mixed.\""],[12228,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I vowed to slaughter at Buwanah.\" He said, \"Perhaps there is something of the pre-Islamic era in your heart?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Fulfill your vow.\""],[12229,"\"The last verse revealed was {And fear a day when you will be returned to Allah}.\""],[12230,"\"Whoever followed him had mercy in this world and the hereafter, and whoever did not follow him was spared from what the rest of the nations were tested with: metamorphosis, sinking into the earth, and being pelted.\""],[12231,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade walking in a single sandal or a single leather sock, sleeping alone in a house, or relieving oneself in open land unless one bends down or faces an enemy unless he moves away from himself."],[12232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abu Isra'il while he was standing in the sun, and said, \"What is wrong with this man?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he vowed not to speak, not to sit, and to fast.\" He said, \"Tell him to speak, seek shade, sit, and complete his fast.\" He did not instruct him to offer expiation."],[12233,"He fell from his mount and his neck was broken, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Wash him with lote-tree leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12234,"The Prophet ﷺ came and found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. He asked, \"What is the significance of this day?\" They replied, \"This is the day when Allah saved Moses and drowned the people of Israel, so we fast it out of gratitude and commemorate it.\""],[12235,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say between the two prostrations, \"O Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me.\""],[12236,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother vowed to fast for a month, but she died before she could fast.\" He said, \"Do you think that if your mother had a debt, you would pay it?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12237,"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's house. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then came and prayed four rak'ahs, then slept, then woke up and said, \"Did the boy wake up? Did the boy stand?\" I came and stood on his left, so he turned me to his right. He prayed five rak'ahs, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring—or he said, his heavy breathing—then he went out for the prayer."],[12238,"That al-Saʿb b. Jaththama sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was at Qudayd, a haunch of a wild donkey—or he said a hindquarter of a wild donkey—but he returned it (to him) while it was dripping blood, as he was in a state of ihram."],[12239,"That al-Saʿb b. Jaththama sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was in a state of ihram at Qudayd, and he returned it while it was dripping blood."],[12240,"That the Prophet ﷺ said on the day of the Trench: “They have distracted us from the middle prayer—may God fill their graves and their bellies with fire.”"],[12241,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I owe (the freeing of) a slave, and I have a black non-Arab slave girl.” He said: “Bring her to me.” Then he said: “Do you testify that there is no god but God?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then free her.”"],[12242,"A black slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"A traveler passing by me while I am with my master's camels, can I give him some milk without their permission?\" The Prophet replied, \"No.\" The slave said, \"If I throw and hit myself, and continue to do so?\" The Prophet replied, \"Whatever you hit, leave what you don't hit.\""],[12243,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever shows off (riyaʾ), God will expose him; and whoever makes a show (sumʿa), God will make a show of him.”"],[12244,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray witr with three rak'ahs. In the first he would recite \"Glorify the Name of Your Lord, the Most High;\" in the second: \"Say: O You disbelievers!\" and in the third: \"Say: He is Allah, (the) One.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1702)"],[12245,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Friday (prayer) Surat al-Jumuʿa and Surat al-Munafiqun."],[12246,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Friday (prayer) Surat al-Jumuʿa and Surat al-Munafiqun."],[12247,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata ʿala al-Insan."],[12250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God cursed the Jews; fat was made forbidden for them, but they sold it and consumed its price.”"],[12251,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a military expedition that included al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad. When they reached the people, they found that they had dispersed, but one man with a great deal of wealth remained and did not leave. He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” Al-Miqdad, however, leaned toward him and killed him. A man among his companions said to him: “You killed a man who said ‘there is no god but God’? By God, this will surely be mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ.” When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they said: “O Messenger of God, a man bore witness that there is no god but God, but al-Miqdad killed him.” He said: “Summon al-Miqdad for me.” Then he said: “O Miqdad, did you kill a man who said ‘there is no god but God’? What will you do with ‘there is no god but God’?” He said: Then God revealed: “O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of God, investigate, and do not say to one who offers you peace, ‘You are not a believer,’ seeking the goods of the life of this world; for with God are abundant gains. Thus you were before, and God conferred favor upon you.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He was a believing man who concealed his faith among a disbelieving people, and you killed him. Likewise, you yourself used to conceal your faith in Makkah.”"],[12252,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Majid b. Suhayl, from Yahya b. ʿAbbad, from Saʿid b. Jubayr, that Ibn ʿAbbas narrated to him that his father ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib sent him on an errand of his to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Maymuna bt. al-Harith was the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbas, so he entered upon her and found the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque. Ibn ʿAbbas said: I lay down in her room and resolved to count how many (rakʿas) the Messenger of God ﷺ would pray. He said: He came while I was lying down in the room after part of the night had passed and said: “Has the boy gone to sleep?” Then he took hold of a covering that was on Maymuna, threw part of it over himself, with part of it remaining on her. Then he stood and prayed two rakʿas at a time until he had prayed eight rakʿas. Then he performed witr with five, without sitting between them. Then he sat and praised God as He deserves, praising Him at length. Then the last of his words was: “O God, place for me a light in my heart, and place for me a light in my hearing, and place for me a light in my sight, and place for me a light on my right and a light on my left, and place for me a light before me and a light behind me, and increase me in light, and increase me in light, and increase me in light.”"],[12253,"“The Qur'an was separated from the Reminder and placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven, then Gabriel began to bring it down to the Prophet ﷺ, reciting it in a measured way.”"],[12254,"In his statement \"Indeed, We have sent it down in the night of decree,\" he said, \"The Quran was revealed as a whole and it was placed in the House of Honor in the lowest heaven. Jibril (Gabriel), ﷺ , revealed it to Muhammad, ﷺ , in response to the words in the lowest heaven and he revealed it to Muhammad, ﷺ , in response to the words of the people and their actions.\""],[12255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first call to prayer was only instituted to make it easy for the people of prayer to prepare for their prayer. So when you hear the call to prayer, perform the ablution thoroughly; and when you hear the iqamah, hasten to the first takbir, for it is the beginning and completion of the prayer; and do not rush the reciter in bowing and prostrating.\""],[12256,"The Ansar said among themselves: \"If we were to gather wealth for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would stretch out his hand and no one could come between him and it.\" So they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we intended to gather for you from our wealth.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Say: I do not ask you for it any reward, except love for the near of kin.} They went out disagreeing. Some of them said: \"Did you not see what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said?\" Others said: \"He only said this so that we fight for his family and support them.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Or do they say: He has fabricated a lie against Allah?} up to His saying: {And He it is who accepts repentance from His servants.} The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered them repentance, up to His saying: {And He responds to those who believe and do righteous deeds, and increases them from His bounty.} They are the ones who said this, that you should repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness."],[12257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jibril ﷺ : \"What prevents you from visiting us more often than you do?\" Then this verse was revealed: {And we do not descend except by the command of your Lord.}"],[12258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Regarding the prostration in Sad: Dawud prostrated it in repentance, and we prostrate it in thankfulness.\""],[12259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my family is the likeness of the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns.\""],[12260,"Wine itself has been prohibited, and intoxication from every drink."],[12261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family at night to Muzdalifah and said to them: \"Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun has risen.\""],[12262,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[12263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever speaks about the Book of Allah without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12266,"A man insulted a father of al-Abbas from the pre-Islamic era, so al-Abbas slapped him. His people came and said: \"By Allah, we will surely slap him,\" and they took up arms. News of that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he ascended the pulpit and said: \"O people, which people of the earth do you consider most honorable in the sight of Allah?\" They said: \"You.\" He said: \"Indeed al-Abbas is of me and I am of him. Do not revile our dead, for you would harm our living.\" Then the people came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we seek refuge in Allah from your anger. Seek forgiveness for us.\""],[12267,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others.”"],[12268,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What becomes prohibited by suckling is what becomes prohibited by lineage.”"],[12269,"“Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives.”"],[12270,"When wine was forbidden, the companions of the Messenger of God went to one another and said: “Wine has been forbidden and made equivalent to idolatry.”"],[12271,"“He saw him.”"],[12272,"When God revealed {Except the oppressed among men, women, and children who cannot devise a plan and are not directed to a way} [Q 4:98], “the going out to the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[12273,"Regarding His saying {My Lord, make this a secure city and provide its people with fruits—whoever of them believes in God and the Last Day} [Q 2:126], Ibn ʿAbbas said: Abraham ﷺ had reserved it exclusively for the people, so God ﷻ revealed “and whoever disbelieves as well—I will provide for them just as I provide for the believers. I create a creation and do not provide for them; I give them enjoyment for a little while, then I will compel them to the punishment of the Fire.” Then Ibn ʿAbbas recited {To each We extend, these and these, from the gift of your Lord, and the gift of your Lord is not restricted} [Q 17:20]."],[12274,"“Whoever sees me in a dream has (really) seen me, for Satan cannot appear in my form.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3901)"],[12275,"“The place of the two feet, and the extent of His Throne cannot be measured.”"],[12276,"“Concession was given to the elderly man, the one afflicted by severe thirst, and the pregnant woman to break the fast in Ramadan.”"],[12277,"“I enjoin you to fear God, and beware of mentioning the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, for you do not know what has preceded for them.”"],[12278,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If one does not find a lower garment (izār), he should wear trousers (sarāwīl) and whoever does not find shoes (na'alayn), should wear sandals (khuffayn).\""],[12279,"The Prophet ﷺ took a ring and wore it, then said: “This has distracted me from you since today—to it a glance and to you a glance.” Then he threw it away."],[12280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[12281,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to circumambulate the House wearing red outer garments, and it was not the misha'a."],[12282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My community has been given something that no other community was given at the time of calamity: {Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return}.\""],[12283,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas: \"{I swear by this city} - Makkah, {and you are free in this city} - Makkah, {and [by] a parent and what he fathered, We have certainly created man in hardship} - in uprightness and in erectness.\""],[12284,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah does not look at the one who lets his garment hang low.\""],[12285,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ does not look at the one who lets his lower garment hang low.\""],[12286,"\"A sheep passed in front of the Messenger ﷺ while he was praying, between him and the qibla, and it did not interrupt his prayer.\""],[12287,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid and Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas ؓ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing of the wind was released against 'Ad except the size of the ring's opening; then it was sent upon them and carried them from the desert to the settled area. When the people of the settled area saw it, {they said, 'This is a cloud bringing us rain'} facing our valleys; the desert people were in it, so the desert people were thrown upon the settled people until they perished.\" He said: \"It raged against its keepers until it burst forth from the doors.\""],[12288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: \"Alif-Lam-Meem. The revelation of the Prostration and has there come to you the story of the dispute?\""],[12289,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer Surat al-Jumu'ah and al-Munafiqun."],[12290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying \"Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah,\" so he said: \"Who is Shubrumah?\" He said: \"My brother or a relative of mine.\" He said: \"Have you performed Hajj for yourself?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.\""],[12291,"I heard Ibn Umar say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh in earthenware jars.\" So I went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: \"Ibn Umar spoke the truth.\" I said: \"What is the jar?\" He said: \"Made of clay.\""],[12292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best gift is a word of truth that you hear, then carry it to a Muslim brother of yours and teach it to him.\""],[12293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in every Friday morning prayer the chapter of \"Alif Lam Meem Tanzeel\" and \"Has there not come upon man a period of time.\""],[12294,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Wiping over the two socks is for the resident for one day and night, and for the traveler for three days and their nights.\""],[12295,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind.\""],[12296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr on the day of ʿAshura. When he finished, he said: \"Whoever among you has begun the day fasting, let him complete his fast; and whoever has not begun the day fasting, let him not eat anything. For this is a day on which Musa was given victory over Pharaoh, so the Jews fasted it in gratitude, and we have a greater right to gratitude.\""],[12297,"The Quran was sent down all at once to the nearest heaven, then it was sent down in portions afterwards to the Prophet ﷺ."],[12298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of your garments is white, so shroud your dead in it and clothe your living with it. And the best of your kohls is ithmid: it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight.\""],[12299,"From Ibn ʿAbbas, who raised the hadith to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever dies addicted to wine will meet Allah as a worshipper of an idol.\""],[12300,"Some Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Abu al-Qasim, we will ask you about some things. If you answer us correctly, we will follow you, believe you, and have faith in you.\" He then took from them the covenant that Isra'il took upon himself. They said: \"Allah is guardian over what we say.\" They said: \"Tell us about the sign of the Prophet ﷺ.\" He said: \"His eyes sleep, but his heart does not sleep.\" They said: \"Tell us how a woman conceives a female and how she conceives a male.\" He said: \"The two fluids meet. If the woman's fluid rises above the man's fluid, she conceives a female; and if the man's fluid rises above the woman's fluid, she conceives a male.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us about thunder: what is it?\" He said: \"An angel among the angels, entrusted with the clouds. He drives them wherever Allah wills.\" They said: \"What is this sound that is heard?\" He said: \"The angel's rebuke of the cloud when he drives it until it reaches where he commands it.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us what Isra'il forbade upon himself.\" He said: \"He lived in the desert and suffered from an ailment, and he found nothing that suited him except camel meat and their milk, so for that reason he forbade them.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us who comes to you from the angels. For there is no prophet but an angel from among the angels comes to him with the message and revelation. So who is your companion? For only this remains.\" He said: \"Jibril ﷺ .\" They said: \"That is the one who descends with war and fighting. That is our enemy. If you had said Mika'il, the one who descends with rain, we would have followed you.\" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Say: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril...} the verse."],[12301,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he \"forbade killing any animal by tying it up and shooting it.\""],[12302,"The jinn used to ascend to the heaven to listen to the revelation. When they heard a word, they would add nine falsehoods to it. As for the word, it would be true, but what they added was false. When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, they were prevented from their listening posts. That was mentioned to Iblis, and before that stars were not thrown at them. Iblis said to them: \"This is because of something that has happened on the earth.\" So he sent his troops, and they found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing praying between two mountains. They came to him and told him, and he said: \"This is the event that has happened on the earth.\""],[12303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant."],[12304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to recite on Friday in the Fajr prayer: 'Alif Lam Mim. The Revelation of the Book...' (al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man...' (al-Insan).\""],[12305,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with reciting \"Subhan\" and \"Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun\" and \"Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad\" in every unit (rak'ah) [of the prayer]."],[12306,"Nabidh was made for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of my maternal aunt in a water-skin."],[12307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are no days in which drawing near to Allah with a deed is more excellent than these ten days.\" It was said: \"Not even jihad?\" He said: \"Not even jihad, unless a man goes out with his own self and his wealth and returns with none of it.\""],[12308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever follows the Book of Allah, Allah will guide him from misguidance and protect him from an evil reckoning on the Day of Resurrection.\" That is because Allah says: {So whoever follows My guidance will not go astray or suffer.}"],[12309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no concubinage in Islam. Whoever engaged in concubinage during the pre-Islamic era, I have attached him to his ʿaṣaba. And whoever claims a child from an illegitimate union, he neither inherits nor is inherited from.”"],[12310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.”"],[12311,"“Umm Ḥufayd, my maternal aunt, sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. He ate from the clarified butter and the dried curd, and left the dabb lizards out of disgust. Had they been unlawful, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[12312,"“Umm Ḥufayd bt. al-Ḥārith b. Jazʾ, the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbās, sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for them, and they were eaten at his table, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left them like one who feels aversion to them. Had they been unlawful, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor would he have ordered that they be eaten.”"],[12313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and the Jews were fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What is this?” They said: “This is a day on which Allah drowned Pharaoh and saved Moses.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am closer to Moses ﷺ than you,” and he ordered that it be fasted."],[12314,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj, and she died without performing it.” He said: “Do you think that if your sister had a debt, you would pay it off?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “The debt owed to Allah is more worthy of being paid. Perform Hajj on behalf of your sister.”"],[12315,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My mother vowed to perform Hajj, but she died before performing it. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?” He said: “Do you think that if your mother had a debt, you would pay it off?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then perform Hajj on her behalf and settle what is owed by her, for Allah ﷻ is more deserving of fulfillment.”"],[12316,"“The death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was announced to him.” It was revealed to him: “When there comes the help of Allah and the victory”—the conquest of Makkah—“then ask forgiveness of your Lord, and know that your term has drawn near.”"],[12317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fasted a complete month other than Ramadan. When he fasted, he would continue fasting so that one would say: “By Allah, he will not break his fast.” And when he broke his fast, he would continue not fasting so that one would say: “By Allah, he will not fast.”"],[12318,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, and al-muzaffat.”"],[12319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: “Allah knows best what they would have done, since He created them.”"],[12320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with a group of his companions heading to the market of ʿUkāẓ. The devils had been prevented from hearing the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against them. The devils returned to their people, who said: “What is the matter with you?” They said: “We have been prevented from hearing the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against us.” They said: “Nothing has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven except something that has happened. So travel throughout the east and west of the earth and see what it is that has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven.” So they set out traveling the east and west of the earth, seeking what had prevented them from hearing the news of heaven. Those who had headed toward Tihāmah turned back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he and his companions were at Nakhlah, heading to the market of ʿUkāẓ, and he was “leading his companions in the dawn prayer.” When they heard the Quran, they listened and said: “By Allah, this is what has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven.” Then and there they returned to their people and said: “O our people, we have heard a wondrous Quran, guiding to right conduct, and we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.” Then Allah revealed to His Prophet: “Say: It has been revealed to me”—and what was revealed to him was only the speech of the jinn."],[12321,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited al-Najm, and when he reached, \"Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza\" \"and Manat, the third, the other,\" Satan cast onto his tongue: Those are the exalted gharaiq (cranes), and their intercession is surely hoped for. When he prostrated, the Muslims and the polytheists prostrated, so Allah ﷻ revealed, \"And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet except that, when he recited, Satan cast,\" up to His saying, \"the punishment of a barren day\"; the Day of Badr."],[12322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seeing is not like being told.\" Allah said to Musa: \"Your people have been tested,\" but he did not throw down the Tablets. When he saw [them], he threw down the Tablets and broke them."],[12323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ said: \"If I take the two precious things of My servant (his eyes) and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[12324,"\"...that they should give something to their relatives among the polytheists, so they asked, and permission was granted to them.\" Then this verse was revealed: {It is not your responsibility to guide them, but Allah guides whom He wills. And whatever good you spend is for yourselves} until His saying {and you will not be wronged}."],[12325,"\"In His saying, 'And do not make your prayer too loud or too low, but seek between that a way.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the Qur'an with a loud voice during prayer. When the polytheists heard him, they insulted him and those who brought him. So Allah revealed to him, 'And do not make your prayer too loud.' Then the polytheists would hear him and insult him. 'And do not make your prayer too low.' He said, 'Inform your companions.' 'But seek between that a way.'\""],[12326,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {And when they hear what has been revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears} he said: \"They were sailors - meaning seamen - who came with Ja'far b. Abi Talib from Abyssinia. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Qur'an, they believed and their eyes overflowed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps when you return to your land you will change your religion.' They said: 'We will never change our religion.' So Allah ﷻ revealed that about their statement.\""],[12327,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymuna, and it was her night. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray, and I stood on his left. He took hold of my forelock or my hair and made me stand on his right."],[12328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no Muslim but he has a sin that afflicts him time after time. Indeed the believer is forgetful: when he is reminded, he remembers.\""],[12329,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to her: \"What prevents you from performing Hajj?\" She said: \"We only have a camel used for carrying water, and my father and husband went on a military expedition with it.\" He said to her: \"Perform 'Umrah in Ramadan, for it is equal to a Hajj for you.\""],[12330,"The prohibition of wine was revealed concerning two tribes of the Ansar. They drank until, when they became intoxicated, they started playing with one another. When they sobered up, a man would see the marks on his face, his head, and his beard, and say: \"My brother So-and-so did this to me. By Allah, if he had been kind and merciful to me, he would not have done this to me.\" They had been brothers with no rancor in their hearts, but rancor fell into their hearts. So Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, wine, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through wine and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?} Then some people who were scrupulous said: \"It is defilement, and it is in the belly of So-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and So-and-so who was killed on the day of Uhud.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is not upon those who believe and do righteousness [any] blame concerning what they have eaten} [the rest of] the verse."],[12331,"A woman brought her son to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my son has madness, and it seizes him at our lunch and dinner, and he becomes troublesome to us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his chest and supplicated. He vomited a vomit, and out of his belly came something like a black puppy, and he was healed."],[12334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[12335,"Allah made the prayer obligatory through the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ: four rak'ahs when resident, and two rak'ahs when traveling."],[12336,"Ibn Abbas said: \"Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives.\""],[12337,"The Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[12338,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray during the night, so I got up on his left side. He took me by the hand and placed me on his right side, wiped my chest, and said: “O Allah, grant him wisdom.”"],[12339,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the men among you who will be from the people of this world in Paradise?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ is in Paradise, the Siddiq is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn born into Islam is in Paradise, and a man who is in a remote part of a city and visits his brother only for the sake of Allah is in Paradise. Shall I inform you of your women who will be among the people of Paradise?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The loving, child-bearing woman who, when she becomes angry or is made angry, says: 'My hand is in your hand; I will not close my eyes in sleep.'”"],[12340,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Death has a terror. When one of you experiences the death of his brother, let him say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. And indeed to our Lord we are returning. O Allah, record him among the doers of good, place his record in ʿIlliyyin, and grant a righteous successor for his offspring among those who remain. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward and do not test us after him.'”"],[12341,"Thirty-nine men and a woman embraced Islam with the Prophet ﷺ. ʿUmar embraced Islam as the completion of forty, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O Prophet, sufficient for you is Allah and whoever follows you of the believers.}"],[12342,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. When the Prophet ﷺ prayed ʿIsha, he returned to her, and it was her night. He prayed two rakʿahs, then turned and said: “Has the boy slept?” I was listening. He said in his prayer: “O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my tongue, and grant me light.”"],[12343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'Convey greetings of peace to ʿUmar and tell him that his approval is judgment and his anger is honor.'”"],[12344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever acts for the sake of Allah within the community and does what is correct, Allah accepts it from him; and if he errs, He forgives him. But whoever acts seeking to cause division and does what is correct, Allah does not accept it from him; and if he errs, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[12345,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station}, he said: “He will seat him between Himself and Jibril, and he will intercede for his Ummah. That is the praised station.”"],[12346,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or affirms loyalty to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[12347,"The Prophet ﷺ married while in a state of ihram and cupped while in a state of ihram."],[12348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while in a state of ihram and cupped while in a state of ihram."],[12349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions performed ʿumrah from al-Jiʿrānah, so they uncovered their right shoulders and placed their cloaks under their armpits, then threw them over their left shoulders, and then they did ramal."],[12350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will surely raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, bearing witness for whoever touched it in truth.”"],[12351,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {in a muddy spring}."],[12352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are a kind of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[12353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are a kind of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[12354,"I found in my father’s book. Abu al-Ashjaʿ gave us his father’s book, so we copied from it from Sufyān, from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUthmān b. Khuthaym, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I slaughtered before I threw.” He said: “Throw, and there is no harm.” Then he said, “I shaved before I threw.” He said: “Throw, and there is no harm.”"],[12355,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"],[12356,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who mentioned his Lord, Exalted is He, saying: “When My servant remembers Me in private, I remember him in private; and when he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than the gathering in which he remembered Me.”"],[12359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of your garments is white, so dress your living in it and shroud your dead in it.”"],[12372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sit on the ground, eat on the ground, milk the ewe, and accept the invitation of a slave to barley bread."],[12373,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I engaged with a woman in what is short of intercourse.” So Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night}."],[12374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The resident and the visitor are equal therein.” He said: “Equal are the one who stays and the one who departs.”"],[12375,"The Jews said: 'Allah's hand is tied up.' May their hands be tied up and may they be cursed for what they said. Rather, both His hands are spread out, He spends as He wills."],[12376,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was diverted from Sham (Greater Syria) to Qibla (Kaaba), and he performed Salah toward the Kaaba in Rajab, during the first seventeen months of his stay in Madinah.\""],[12377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a group of traders and said, \"O group of traders.\" They responded to him and raised their necks. He said, \"Verily, Allah will resurrect you on the Day of Judgment as wicked except for those who are truthful, righteous, and fulfill their trust.\""],[12378,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'When Allah created the Pen, He said to it: Write. So it wrote everything that will occur until the Hour comes.'"],[12379,"I said to Ibn Abbas: 'Is there repentance for someone who intentionally kills a believer?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then what about His saying: {And those who do not call upon another god besides Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery; and whoever does that will meet a penalty multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will abide therein humiliated — except for those who repent, believe, and do righteous work; then Allah will replace their evil deeds with good deeds}?' He said: 'This is a Makkan verse, which was abrogated by a Madinan verse: {But whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein forever, and Allah's wrath is upon him and He has cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment}.'"],[12380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, and a bucket of Zamzam was brought to him. He drank from it while standing."],[12381,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, when he raised his head from bowing he would say: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.'"],[12382,"I stayed overnight at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up during the night, performed ablution three times each, then stood to pray. I got up and did as he did, then I stood on his left, so he positioned me on his right."],[12383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade solid silk (garments)."],[12384,"He poured water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ablution at his maternal aunt Maymunah's house. When he came out, he said: 'Who placed my ablution water for me?' She said: 'My sister's son, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'O Allah, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation.'"],[12385,"Thursday, and what a day Thursday was! A day on which the Prophet's ﷺ pain intensified.' And he mentioned the hadith."],[12386,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'I am holding you back by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, saying: Beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments. When I die, I will be your forerunner, and your appointed place is at the Pond. Whoever reaches it will succeed. And some people will come and be taken to the left. I will say: O Lord, my community. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you, turning back on their heels.'"],[12387,"Adiyy b. Badda' and Tamim al-Dari used to travel to Makkah for trade. A man from Banu Sahm went out with them and died in a land where there was no Muslim. He entrusted his belongings to them, so they delivered his inheritance to his family but kept a silver cup inlaid with gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them swear by Allah that they had not concealed it or disclosed it. Then they found the cup in Makkah, and they said: 'We bought it from Tamim al-Dari and Adiyy.' Two men from the heirs of the Sahmi stood up, swore, and took the cup. Concerning them, this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, testimony among you...} the verse."],[12388,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Moses ﷺ performed Hajj on a red camel, wearing a Qatwani cloak.'"],[12389,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah created a preserved tablet made of a white pearl, its pages are made of red ruby, and His pen is light for Him. Every day, He creates and provides sustenance, causes death and gives life, honors and humiliates, and does whatever He wills.\""],[12390,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and had not performed Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on her behalf?\" He said, \"Tell me, if your mother had a debt and you paid it off, would that settle it for her?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being settled.\""],[12391,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah.\""],[12392,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not send a prophet to a people and take him back except that He makes a period of slackness after him, then He fills Hell from that period of slackness.\""],[12393,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not send a prophet among a people and then take him back except that He makes a period of slackness after him and fills Hell from that period of slackness.\""],[12394,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr in Madinah without travel or fear.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbas, \"Why do you think he did that?\" He said, \"He wanted not to cause hardship to anyone of his Ummah.\""],[12395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and combined Maghrib and ʿIsha in Madinah while he was resident, without fear or anything that compelled him to do so.\" They said, \"Why, O Abu ʿAbbas?\" He said, \"He wanted not to cause hardship to his Ummah.\""],[12396,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr and ʿAsr together in Madinah without fear or travel."],[12397,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[12398,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha, on a journey or on the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[12399,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and between Maghrib and ʿIsha, during travel."],[12400,"He said to his sons, \"O my sons, go out from Makkah for Hajj on foot, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'For the pilgrim who rides, for every step his mount takes there are seventy good deeds; and for the one who walks, for every step there are seven hundred good deeds.'\""],[12401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said], \"Wash him with water and lote tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12402,"A man in ihram was thrown by his mount and his neck broke, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah."],[12403,"A man among us was thrown from his mount while he was in ihram, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey when a man's she-camel threw him and broke his neck, and he died while in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12405,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, and with him was a Muslim man in ihram, his camel stumbled and he fell from it, and his neck was broken. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in the two garments in which he entered ihram, and do not cover his face, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12406,"A man's she-camel threw him and killed him while he was in ihram, and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12407,"A man's camel threw him and broke his neck while he was in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Clothe him in two garments, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his head, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12408,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12409,"While a man was on his she-camel, it threw him and broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with lote leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah\" or he said \"with matted hair.\""],[12411,"Mohammad said, \"Wash him and don't bring him near anything that he was prohibited from. Shroud him in his two garments, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection wearing them.\""],[12412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him and shroud him in his two garments, and do not touch him with anything that was forbidden to him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12413,"A Muslim man died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that he be washed and wrapped in two garments and not touched with perfume. And I am uncertain whether his head was covered or not. He said: \"This one will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12414,"A man was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he fell from his mount and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be shrouded and washed, and that his face not be covered, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah, or he said uttering the talbiyah."],[12415,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"My brother’s camel threw him, and he died while he was in ihram.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, and do not perfume him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection in ihram.\""],[12416,"A she-camel trampled a man in ihram and killed him, so the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought, and he said: \"Wash him and shroud him, but do not wash his head and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be resurrected uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12417,"He fell off his mount while he was in ihram, and it trampled him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought, and that was mentioned to him, so he said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his face, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12418,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ on a camel while he was in ihram, and it killed him — Shuʿbah said, meaning he died — so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments with his head uncovered, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with matted hair.\""],[12420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not know the end of a surah until \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim\" was sent down upon him."],[12421,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a revelation with the phrase \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful\", he knew that the previous Surah had ended and he would then begin reciting the next one."],[12422,"Jibril ﷺ used to send down revelation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he said \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,\" he began another surah."],[12423,"The Prophet ﷺ came out from the privy, then sat down and ate. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not perform ablution?\" He said: \"I have only been commanded to perform ablution for prayer; as for eating, no.\""],[12424,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram.\" This is how Muʿawiyah b. Hisham narrated it. But the companions of al-Thawri narrated it from al-Thawri, from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbas, and that is the correct version."],[12425,"\"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight rakʿahs together and five rakʿahs together without rain or fear.\" This is how al-Juʿfi Husayn narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah. But the companions of Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah, from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, and likewise the companions of ʿAmr b. Dinar narrated it from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd."],[12426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, walking, and uncircumcised.\""],[12427,"\"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and repeated it three times, then he said, 'Do you know why I gave the guarantee?' They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'Gabriel came to me and informed me that whoever you are mentioned in his presence and he does not send blessings upon you, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.' And whoever reaches both his parents or one of them in old age and does not enter Paradise through them, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.' And whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.'\""],[12428,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with the people around him, and he said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ has given every prophet a desire, and my desire is in standing in this night [prayer], so let no one pray behind me. And Allah has given every prophet a provision, and my provision is this fifth; so when I am taken, it belongs to the rulers of affairs after me.\""],[12429,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated, saying, “O Allah, bless us in our sa’ and our mudd, and bless us in our Makkah and our Madinah, and bless us in our Sham and our Yemen.” A man among the people said, “O Prophet of Allah, and our Iraq?” He said, “Therein is the horn of Satan and the barking of tribulations, and indeed coarseness is in the east.”"],[12430,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever hears the call and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O Allah, bless him and convey him to the station of intercession (wasīlah) with You, and make us among those for whom he intercedes on the Day of Resurrection, intercession becomes incumbent for him.”"],[12431,"Amr b. Abi Asim al-Nabil reported to us: My father reported to us from Thawr b. Yazid: Maslama b. Abi Ata reported to me from Sa'id b. Jubayr, who said: Abdullah b. Abbas and Abdullah b. Umar testified before me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade (using) gourds, vessels coated with pitch, vessels coated with tar, and hantam jars.” I said, “What is hantam?” He said, “Every (vessel made of) clay.”"],[12432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ makes lands flourish for a people and makes wealth fruitful for them, and He has not looked at them since He created them out of hatred for them.” It was said, “How is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Because of their maintaining ties of kinship.”"],[12433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf, then returned and came to the watering place, and said: “Give me a drink of what the people drink.”"],[12434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “combined between Zuhr and Asr in Madinah without fear.”"],[12435,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, indeed I love you so much that I remember you, and were it not that I come and look at you, I would think that my soul would depart. Then I remember that if I enter Paradise, I will be below you in station, and that distresses me, and I would love to be with you in rank.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not reply anything, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, they will be with those whom Allah has favored} (the verse). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and recited it to him."],[12438,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Which of you knows Quss b. Sa'ida al-Iyadi?” They said, “All of us know him, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “What became of him?” They said, “He perished.” He said: “I will not forget him at Ukaz in the sacred month, while he was on a red camel, addressing the people, saying: O people, gather, listen, and understand. Whoever lives dies, and whoever dies is gone, and everything that is to come will come. Indeed in the sky there is news, and in the earth there are lessons: a bed laid out, a ceiling raised, stars that move, and seas that do not diminish. Quss swore a true oath: if there is contentment on earth, there will certainly be discontent after it. Indeed Allah has a religion that is dearer to Him than the religion you follow. Why do I see people going and not returning? Are they pleased and staying, or are they left and sleeping?” Then he ﷺ said, “Is there among you anyone who can recite his poetry?” So some of them recited it."],[12439,"I heard the words of Hassan b. Thabit: “”"],[12440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like a donkey carrying books, and the one who says to him ‘listen’ has no Jumu'ah.”"],[12441,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord ﷻ twice: once with his sight and once with his heart."],[12442,"He used to say regarding His saying, {And he certainly saw him on the clear horizon}: “I only mean Jibril ﷺ , that Muhammad ﷺ saw him in his form at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary.”"],[12443,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting and in ihram."],[12444,"I stood one night to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, and I stood on his left, so he gestured with his hand from behind him and took my hand—or my upper arm—until he made me stand on his right."],[12445,"I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar how the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was. They said, \"He would pray thirteen rakats, and he would perform witr with three rakats after the 'Isha prayer.\""],[12446,"\"In his saying 'Say, I do not ask you for it any payment, except for love of [my] relatives', he ﷺ said, 'Maintain my kinship ties and do not deny me.'\""],[12447,"Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer and the two units of prayer while traveling.\""],[12448,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet?” He said, “When Adam was between the spirit and the body.”"],[12449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a sheep’s shoulder in the mosque, and he ate it; then he stood for prayer and did not touch water."],[12450,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade us to take anything with a soul as a target."],[12451,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking standing from Zamzam—and the wording is from the hadith of Abu Nuʿaym."],[12452,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water, so we gave him Zamzam water. He drank while standing."],[12453,"I handed the Prophet ﷺ a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water and was brought a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12455,"I gave the Prophet ﷺ water from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12456,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral after it had been buried."],[12458,"He told me that he witnessed the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"He came to a desolate grave, so he aligned them and loudly proclaimed Allahu Akbar four times.\" Sulaiman said, \"I asked Ash-Sha'bi, 'O Abu Amr, who informed you of this?' He said, 'Ibn Abbas.'\""],[12459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a grave and said, “What is this?” They said, “He—or she—was buried last night.” Ibn ʿAbbas said, “So he lined us up behind him, then he prayed over it.”"],[12460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a grave and said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"Someone was buried last night.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said, \"We formed rows behind him, then he prayed over him.\""],[12461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins, and he gave the cupper his wage. Had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."],[12462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah, and he cupped him, and he reduced his tax by half a saʿ or more."],[12463,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be cupped three times: on the two jugular veins or between the shoulder blades. A servant of his from Bayadah, called Abu Hind, cupped him. He used to pay his family a mudd and a half every day, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ interceded for him, so they reduced it by half a mudd. After that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."],[12464,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins and the withers."],[12465,"The Prophet ﷺ used to be cupped on the two jugular veins and the withers."],[12466,"A questioner asked while Ibn ʿAbbas was praying, and Ibn ʿAbbas said to him: O questioner. He said: At your service. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And do you pray the five prayers? He said: Yes. He said: And do you fast Ramadan? He said: Yes. He said: It is incumbent upon us to help you. So he took off a garment he was wearing and clothed him with it. Then he said: At that, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Any Muslim who clothes a Muslim with a garment remains in Allah's protection as long as a patch of it remains on him.\""],[12467,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will surely send a man whom Allah will not disgrace.\" He sent for ʿAli while he was at the mill grinding, and none of you would have been grinding. They brought him with sore eyes, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, I can hardly see. He blew into his eyes, shook the banner three times, then handed it to him. Victory was granted to him, and he brought Safiyyah bt. Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins: \"Which of you will be my protector in this world and the Hereafter?\" three times, until he passed by the last of them. ʿAli said: O Prophet of Allah, I am your protector in this world and the Hereafter. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter.\" He said: And he sent Abu Bakr with Surat al-Tawbah, and he sent ʿAli after him. Abu Bakr said: O ʿAli, perhaps Allah and His Prophet are displeased with me. ʿAli said: No, but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting that anyone should convey from me except a man from me, and I am from him.\" He said: And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ placed his garment over ʿAli, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, and said: \"Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.\" And he was the first to embrace Islam after Khadijah among the people. He said: And ʿAli purchased his own life; he wore the Prophet's ﷺ garment, then stood in his place. He said: The polytheists were throwing stones at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr came and said: Come to me, O Messenger of Allah—Abu Bakr thought he was the Prophet of Allah. ʿAli said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ has set out toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him. Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him. ʿAli kept throwing stones as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to throw, writhing with his head wrapped in the garment, not removing it until morning. Then he uncovered his head when morning came, and they said: You are indeed despicable. Your companion, when we throw stones at him, does not writhe, but you writhe. We found that strange. He said: Then he set out with the people on the expedition of Tabuk. ʿAli said to him: Shall I go out with you? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No.\" So ʿAli wept. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that you are not a prophet? It is not fitting that I should go unless you are my deputy.\" He said: And he said to him: \"You are the protector of every believer after me.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ closed the doors of the mosque except ʿAli's door, so he could enter the mosque while in a state of major ritual impurity, since it was his path and he had no other path. He said: And he said: \"Whoever's mawla I am, ʿAli is his mawla.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said: Allah has informed us in the Quran that He is pleased with them, with the companions of the tree, knowing what is in their hearts. Did He tell us that He became displeased with them afterwards? And he said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar when he said: Will you permit me to strike his neck—meaning Hatib: \"Would you have done it? And what do you know? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish?\""],[12468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered all the doors to be closed except ʿAli's door ؓ."],[12469,"A man from the Banu 'Amir came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was a healer and a physician, so he said, \"O Muhammad, you utter certain words. Can I heal you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then called him to Allah ﷻ and asked, \"Would you like me to show you a sign?\" He had some date-palms and a tree with him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called forth a stalk from it. The man approached him while he was prostrating and raising his head until he reached him. Then he stood in front of him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Return to your place.\" So he returned to his place. Al-'Amiri swore, \"By Allah, I will never deny what you say.\" Then he said, \"O people of Banu Sa'sa'a, by Allah, I will never deny anything he says.\""],[12470,"While we were washing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man came and knocked on the door, saying: I remind you of Allah—will you not give me today a share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? ʿAli said: Let him in and place him behind the curtain; he will hand us the water. We let him in, and he handed us the water. And ʿAli said: By Allah, I did not turn him except that another was with me turning him. He said: And I heard in the house: Do not remove the shirt from him."],[12471,"Do you see one who killed a believer deliberately, then repented, believed, and did righteous deeds, then was guided? He said: And how can repentance be his, when I heard your Prophet ﷺ say: The closest of creation to the Throne of the Merciful on the Day of Resurrection will be the believer who was killed unjustly, his head on his right and his killer on his left, and his jugular veins gushing blood, saying: My Lord, ask this one why he killed me? Why did he come between me and the prayer?"],[12472,"The first to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about nabidh were the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays. They came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of abundant vegetation, and we obtain fresh herbs, so he ordered us to prepare a drink. He said: \"Soak [dates or raisins] in waterskins, but do not soak in earthenware jars, nor in gourds, nor in vessels smeared with pitch, nor in hollowed-out stumps, for I have been forbidden wine, gambling, and the kubah, which is the drum, and every intoxicant is unlawful.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it becomes strong? He said: \"Pour water over it.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it becomes strong? He said: \"Pour water over it.\" He said on the third or fourth time: \"When it becomes strong, then pour it out.\""],[12473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[12474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The price of wine is unlawful, the dower of a prostitute is unlawful, the price of a dog is unlawful, and the kubah is unlawful. If the owner of a dog comes to you seeking its price, then fill his hands with dust. Wine, gambling, and every intoxicant are unlawful.\""],[12475,"For Jibril ﷺ used to present the Quran to the Prophet ﷺ every year in Ramadan. He said: So he presented the Quran to him in the year in which the Prophet ﷺ passed away twice. Thus ʿAbdullah witnessed what was abrogated from it and what was changed. So the final recitation of ʿAbdullah is the latter one."],[12476,"This verse was revealed: {And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe.} \"So the people refrained from marrying them until the verse after it was revealed.\" {This day good things have been made lawful to you. The food of those given the Scripture is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them. And chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those given the Scripture. This day good things have been made lawful to you. The food of those given the Scripture is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them. And chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those given the Scripture.} \"So the people married women of the People of the Scripture.\""],[12477,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Good conduct and good appearance are one part of seventy parts of prophethood.\""],[12478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Good conduct, good appearance, and moderation are one part of forty-five parts of prophethood.\""],[12479,"He said: We said to Ibn ʿAbbas: Have you considered the saying of Allah (glorified and exalted be He): {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his chest}? He said: \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood one day to pray, and a thought crossed his mind.\" The hypocrites who were praying with him said: Do you not see that he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them? So Allah (glorified and exalted be He) revealed: {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his chest}."],[12480,"Two men came to the Prophet of God ﷺ with one need. One of them greeted, and the Messenger of God ﷺ noticed an unpleasant odor from his mouth. He said to him, \"Do you not use the tooth stick (siwāk)?\" He replied, \"I do, but I have not eaten any food for three days.\" So he ordered a man to host him and fulfill his need."],[12481,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not one of us who steals, robs, or indicates towards theft.\""],[12484,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ spread apart the thighs of al-Ḥusayn and kiss his private part.\""],[12485,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If the one who begs knew what he incurs from it, he would not beg.\""],[12486,"\"If a Qur'an with which mountains were moved, or the earth were split asunder, or the dead were made to speak...\" He said: They said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"If it is as you say, then show us our forefathers from among the dead so we may speak to them, and open for us these mountains—the mountains of Makkah that have enclosed us.\" Then it was revealed: \"And if there had been a Qur'an with which mountains were moved, or the earth were split asunder, or the dead were made to speak...\""],[12487,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Mecca for ten years, then descended [to the verse]: \"{Say: 'My Lord, admit me with an entrance of truth and exit me with an exit of truth.'}\" Then, he migrated to Medina."],[12488,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The man who has nothing of the Qur'an inside him is like a ruined house.\""],[12489,"\"The Messenger ﷺ said, 'There is no one among you except that he has been assigned a companion from the jinn.' They asked, 'Even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, but Allah has helped me against him, so he has become a Muslim.'\""],[12490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us in haste while we were sitting, and his haste startled us. When he reached us, he greeted and then said: \"I came to you in haste to inform you about the Night of Decree, but I forgot it between me and you, so seek it in the last ten nights.\""],[12491,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"How can I know that you are the Messenger of God?\" He said, \"If I call this cluster from this palm tree, will you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The cluster came down from the palm tree until it fell to the ground, and it began to hop until it came to the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said to it, \"Return,\" and it returned until it went back to its place. The Bedouin said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God,\" and he believed."],[12492,"\"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of God ﷺ at night, and he would drink it the next day, and that night, and the next day, and that night, and the next day, until when evening came he would drink it and give it to others to drink, or he would order it and it would be poured out.\""],[12493,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to have raisins soaked for him, and he would drink it that day, the next day, and the day after that, until the evening of that night. Then he would order that it be given to others to drink or poured out.\""],[12494,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to have nabīdh soaked for him, and he would drink it the next day and the day after. When it was the third day, he would order it to be poured out.\""],[12495,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to have raisins soaked for him in a water-skin, and he would drink it from the evening, and the next day, and the day after that. If any remained, he would order it to be poured out or drunk.\""],[12496,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"used to have nabīdh soaked for him, and he would drink it that day and its night, and the next day and its night. When it was the third day, he would order that it be poured out or given to the servants to drink.\""],[12497,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a waterskin, and he would drink it the next day and its night, and the day after and its night. When it was the third day, he would order that it be poured out or he would give it to the servants to drink."],[12498,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would drink it that day and the next day and the third day. When evening came, he would pour it out or give it to the servants to drink, and he would not give the servants anything forbidden to drink."],[12499,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would drink it the next day and the day after. When the evening of the third day came, he would pour it out or order that it be poured out."],[12500,"I heard Ibn Abbas saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, green jars, and hollowed wood.\""],[12501,"Wine itself was forbidden, the little of it and the much of it, and intoxication from every drink."],[12502,"I traveled with Ibn Abbas from Madinah to Syria and asked him: Did the Prophet ﷺ leave a will? He said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of Aishah. He said: 'Call Ali for me.' She said: 'Shall we not call Abu Bakr, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Call him.' Then Hafsah said: 'Shall we not call Umar?' He said: 'Call him.' Then Umm al-Fadl said: 'Shall we not call al-Abbas, your uncle?' He said: 'Call him.' When they had gathered, he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he remained silent and did not speak. Umar said: 'Rise and leave the Prophet ﷺ, for if he had a need from us he would have mentioned it.' He did that three times, then said: 'Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.' Aishah said: 'Abu Bakr was present, so Abu Bakr came forward to lead the people in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief, so he went out leaning between two men. When the people sensed him, they glorified Allah, and Abu Bakr moved to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: 'Stay where you are.' The Prophet ﷺ began the recitation from where Abu Bakr had ended, with Abu Bakr standing and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting. Abu Bakr followed the Prophet ﷺ, and the people followed Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah did not finish the prayer until he became very heavy, so he went out leaning between two men, with his feet dragging on the ground. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and he did not leave a will.\""],[12503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever has enough to reach the Sacred House of Allah for Hajj but does not perform Hajj, and whoever has wealth that reaches the threshold of zakah but does not pay it, will ask to be sent back at the time of death.' A man said to him: 'Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas! Only the disbeliever asks to be sent back!' He said: 'I will recite to you the Qur'an: {O you who believe, spend from what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a short while}.'"],[12504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever has enough to perform Hajj but does not perform Hajj, or enough to pay zakah but does not pay it, will ask to be sent back at the time of death.' A man said to him: 'Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas! Only the disbeliever asks to be sent back!' He said: 'I will recite to you the Qur'an: {O you who believe, spend from what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a short while, so that I may give charity and be among the righteous}.'"],[12505,"Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed on the day of Khaybar. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered it, the Muslims captured women from the People of the Book who had husbands. When a man wanted to approach one of these women, she would say: 'I have a husband.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about that, and Allah, glorified be He, sent down this verse: {And protected women among women} - the verse - meaning the captive women from the polytheists who are captured: there is no harm in that. I mentioned this to Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and he said: 'He spoke the truth.'"],[12506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Goodness reaches the house in which food is eaten faster than a knife reaches the hump of a camel.'"],[12507,"My father narrated to me, dictating from his original book: Muhammad b. Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Umar Abu Yahya, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, who said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing any living creature unless it harms.'"],[12508,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah, glorified be He: {And when the Prophet confided a matter to one of his wives}: He said: Hafsah entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in her house while he was having intercourse with Mariyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Do not tell Aishah until I give you glad tidings: your father will take charge after Abu Bakr when I die.' Hafsah went and told Aishah that she saw the Prophet ﷺ having intercourse with Mariyah, and she told her that the Prophet ﷺ informed her that Abu Bakr would take charge after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umar after him. Aishah said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Who told you this?' He said: 'The All-Knowing, the All-Aware told me.' Aishah said: 'I will not look at you until you make Mariyah forbidden to yourself.' So he made her forbidden, and Allah, glorified be He, sent down: {O Prophet, why do you forbid}."],[12509,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The one killed defending his wealth is a martyr, the one killed defending his family is a martyr, and the one killed defending his own life is a martyr.\""],[12510,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Beautify your voices with the Qur'an.\""],[12511,"\"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' in Madinah without any reason.\" It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: \"What did he intend by that?\" He said: \"To make things easier for his Ummah.\""],[12512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Today is the pledge, tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire. I am the first, Abu Bakr is the second, 'Umar is the third, and the people after that are in the race: the first, then the next.\""],[12513,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, when was your covenant taken?\" He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[12514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one has done me more favors than Abu Bakr. He gave me his daughter in marriage, helped me migrate to the abode of emigration, and if I were to take a close friend (khalil), I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but instead there is the brotherhood of affection until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12515,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey called Ya'fur, and I began to sweat, so he ordered me to perform ghusl.\""],[12516,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"When Jibril ﷺ brought revelation to the Prophet ﷺ, he would not finish until the Prophet ﷺ began to speak the first of it, out of fear that he would faint. Jibril said to him: 'Why do you do that?' He said: 'Out of fear that I might forget.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {We will make you recite, so you will not forget}.\""],[12517,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah ﷻ spoke to Musa in one hundred and forty thousand words over three days. When Musa ﷺ heard the speech of human beings, he despised them because of what had entered his ears from the speech of the Lord ﷻ. Among what He confided to him was: \"O Musa, those who put on a show have not put on a show with anything like asceticism in this world, and those who seek closeness to Me have not drawn near with anything like piety from what I have forbidden them, and those who worship have not worshipped with anything like weeping out of fear of Me.\" Musa said: \"O Lord of all creation, O Master of the Day of Judgment, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, what have You prepared for them and how have You rewarded them?\" He said: \"As for the ascetics in this world, I will permit them to enter My Paradise, and they will settle wherever they wish. As for the pious who abstain from what I have forbidden them, on the Day of Resurrection, no servant will remain but that I will take him to account and scrutinize him, except the pious, for I will be shy of them, honor them, and admit them to Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep out of fear of Me, they will have the highest station, in which they will not be shared with.\"\""],[12518,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who is killed in the path of Allah facing forward, not turning back, will reach Paradise seventy years before the one killed while retreating. The sick of my Ummah will reach Paradise seventy years before their healthy ones. And the prophets before Sulayman b. Dawud will reach Paradise forty years before him because of the kingdom he had.\""],[12519,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A woman should not travel three miles except with a husband or with a mahram.' It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'People say three days.' He said: 'That is a mistake on their part.'\""],[12520,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied the banner for 'Ali on the day of Khaybar, he supplicated for him for a little while and said: 'O Allah, help him and grant victory through him, have mercy on him and have mercy through him, support him and support through him. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy.'\""],[12521,"When the Prophet ﷺ intended to go out for the expedition of Tabuk, he said to Jadd Ibn Qais, \"O Jadd Ibn Qais, what do you say about fighting Bani Asfar (the yellow people)?\" Jadd replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who has companionship with women, and whenever I see the women of Bani Asfar (the yellow people), I become tempted. Therefore, grant me permission to stay behind and do not include me in the expedition, so that I do not become tempted.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed the verse {And among them are those who say, \"Grant me permission [to be exempted from fighting] and do not put me to trial.\" Unquestionably, they have fallen into trial.}"],[12522,"In His saying \"{Allah shall give them love}\" He said, \"Love in the hearts of the believers was revealed concerning Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah honor his face.\""],[12523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A thrifty person is never destitute.”"],[12524,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They are two veils: the husband and the grave.”"],[12525,"Regarding His statement {For they do not lie to you} lightly — and thus he used to recite it — he said: “They are not able to not be a messenger, nor to not be the Qur’an as Qur’an. If they were to lie to you with their tongues, they would be lying to you, and that is nothing but a liar, and that is the denial.”"],[12526,"Regarding His statement {Do not say “ra’ina”}, he said: “They used to say to the Prophet ﷺ ‘attend to us, let us hear you,’ but ‘ra’ina’ is like your saying ‘give us.’ {And listen without being made to hear} — for the Prophet ﷺ — he said: “They say, ‘May you not hear.’ And ‘listen’ — for the Prophet ﷺ — ‘may you not hear.’ He said: {And if they had said, ‘We hear and obey’ and ‘listen and consider us,’ it would have been better for them.}”"],[12527,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party and they gained spoils, he would divide the spoils into fifths, then strike that fifth into five parts. Then he recited: {And know that whatever you gain as spoils, for Allah is one fifth of it} up to His saying {for Allah} — the key of the statement — {To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth}. He made the share of Allah and the share of the Messenger one. {And to the near relatives} — he made these two shares a source of strength in horses and weapons. He made the share of the orphans, the needy, and the wayfarer such that he would not give it to anyone else. He made the remaining four shares: for a horse two shares, for its rider one share, and for a foot soldier one share."],[12528,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A safeguard for my community from drowning, when they board ships, is to say: ‘In the name of Allah, the King. {They have not estimated Allah with His true estimation. The earth, all of it, will be in His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Glorified and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.} {In the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful.}’”"],[12529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The nobles of my community are the bearers of the Qur’an.”"],[12530,"I said to Ibn Abbas: “What do you think about coitus interruptus?” He said: “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said anything about it, then it is as he said. Otherwise, I say about it: {Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish.} Whoever wishes may practice coitus interruptus, and whoever wishes may leave it.”"],[12531,"\"Two units, two units, the sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[12532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hesitated in a verse during the dawn prayer. When he finished the prayer, he turned his face to the people and said: “Did Ubayy b. Kaʿb attend the prayer with you?” They said: “No.” He said: “The people thought he missed him only so that he could prompt him.”"],[12533,"“The Aws and the Khazraj had enmity between them in the pre-Islamic era. While they were sitting one day, they mentioned what was between them until they became angry, and some of them rose against others with weapons.” So the verse was revealed: {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you?} — the entire verse and the two verses after it up to {And remember the favor of Allah upon you when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together.}"],[12534,"From Ibn Abbas regarding {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you?} He said: “The Aws were conversing when they mentioned the affairs of the pre-Islamic era, and they became angry until there was war between them. They took up weapons and some of them advanced against others.” So the verse was revealed: {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you} up to His saying {then He saved you from it.}"],[12535,"Ibn Abbas was asked: “How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ test women?” He said: “When a woman came to him to accept Islam, he made her swear by Allah that she had not left out of hatred for a husband, and by Allah that she had not left to acquire a dinar, and by Allah that she had not left out of desire for one land over another, and by Allah that she had left only out of love for Allah and His Messenger.”"],[12536,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed three ʿumrahs in Dhu al-Qaʿdah."],[12537,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"How can I be at ease when the Companion of the Horn has already taken the horn in his mouth?\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ inclined his forehead, \"waiting for when he is commanded, then he blows.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, what shall we say?\" He said: \"{Sufficient for us is God, and how excellent a Trustee is He}.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: {So when the trumpet is blown}."],[12538,"\"In his saying, 'When the trumpet is blown', he (the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ) said, 'How can I feel comfortable while the companion of the horn has already taken the horn?' And he pointed to his forehead saying, 'Does he listen to when he is commanded?' So his companions asked, 'Then what should we say?' He said, 'Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'\""],[12539,"\"...that He will give you more than it.\""],[12540,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the earnings of slave women.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbas, \"And why did he forbid it?\" He said: \"Out of fear that they would be unable, and then you would be unable.\""],[12541,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray four (rakʿahs) before Jumuʿah and four after it, not separating between them."],[12542,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on his way out to Badr: \"God ﷻ has promised me Badr and to grant me their camp as spoils. Whoever kills an enemy shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if God wills, and whoever captures a captive shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if God wills.\" When they faced each other, God cast terror into the hearts of the polytheists. When they fought, God defeated them, and the swift among the people pursued them; they killed seventy and captured seventy."],[12543,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ: \"He has not fasted, the one who fasts forever.\""],[12544,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, by God, I have come to you from a people for whom no shepherd sets out provisions and no stallion passes by them.\" So he ascended the pulpit, praised God, and then said: \"O God, give us a rain that rescues, makes fruitful, abundant, covering (the earth), swift, and not delayed.\" Then he descended, and no one came to us from any direction except that he said, \"You have revived us.\""],[12545,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Makkah is the sacred sanctuary of God: its fresh herbage is not to be cut, its trees are not to be felled, and its game is not to be startled.\" Al-ʿAbbas said, \"O Messenger of God, except idhkhir, for it is for our blacksmiths and for the roofs of our houses.\" He said, \"Except idhkhir.\""],[12546,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave a young she-camel to Abu Bakr as a gift, but he deemed it too young. Then he said to me: \"Take it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, my son, and say: We are working people; if you have one older than it, send it to us.\" So I brought it, and he said: \"O son of my uncle, direct it to the camels of zakat.\" Then I came to him in the mosque and prayed ʿisha with him. He said: \"Do you want to spend the night at your maternal aunt's? It has become evening.\" And it coincided with her night with the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I went to her, and she fed me supper and spread for me a cloak folded four times, which I used as a mattress. I said to myself: I will certainly observe what the Prophet ﷺ does tonight. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ entered and said: \"O Maymunah.\" She said, \"At your service, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Has your nephew come to you?\" She said, \"Yes, here he is.\" He said: \"Did you give him supper if you had anything?\" She said, \"I did.\" He said: \"And you spread for him?\" She said, \"Yes.\" Then he turned to his bed, but did not lie on it; he lay down beside it and placed his head on the bed. He remained for a while, and I heard him snore in sleep. I said: He has slept, and he is not awake, and he will not stand tonight. Then he got up when I thought a quarter or a third of the night had passed. He went to his siwak and a water vessel, and used the siwak until I heard the grating of his front teeth under the siwak, while he was reciting these verses: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth...}"],[12547,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed over a deceased person, he would say: \"O God, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our females and our males. Whoever You keep alive from among us, keep him alive upon Islam; and whoever You take from among us, take him upon faith. O God, Your pardon, Your pardon.\""],[12548,"A slain person was killed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ whose killer was unknown. So he ascended his pulpit and said: \"O people, shall a person be killed while I am among you and it is not known who killed him? If the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth were to gather to kill a Muslim man, God would punish them without number or reckoning.\""],[12549,"About [avoiding] harming the Prophet ﷺ and refraining from following him."],[12550,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father has died; should I free a slave on his behalf?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[12551,"The Prophet ﷺ sent an army and its flag was returned, so he sent another and its flag was returned with the head of a golden deer. And then the verse was revealed (And it is not for any prophet to embezzle)."],[12552,"From [the prohibition of] solid silk."],[12553,"On the right of the Throne—and both of Allah's hands are right—upon pulpits of light, their faces of light; they are not prophets, nor martyrs, nor truthful ones.\" It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who are they?' He said, \"Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah, the Exalted.\""],[12554,"We set out as pilgrims, and when we camped at Batn Nakhl, we sighted the crescent. Some of the people said, 'It is three nights old,' and others said, 'It is two nights old.' We came to Ibn Abbas and said, 'We sighted the crescent; some of the people said it is three nights old, and others said it is two nights old.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended it for its sighting, so it is [counted] on the night you sighted it.'"],[12555,"\"There is no man who is put in charge of ten people but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand fettered to his neck until judgment is passed between him and them.\""],[12556,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray eight rak'ahs at night and then he would pray three rak'ahs of witr."],[12557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever hears the sound of a bell, or enters a church, or a synagogue, or a fire temple, or a place of idols, and says: 'There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah,' Allah will record for him a reward equal to the number of those who did not say it, or he will be recorded with Allah as a truthful one.\""],[12558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever establishes prayer, gives Zakat, performs Hajj, fasts during Ramadan, and treats guests kindly will enter Paradise.\""],[12559,"Abu Jahl said, 'If Muhammad returns to pray behind the Maqam, I will certainly assault him.' It was said, 'There he is, praying behind the Maqam.' So he went toward him, then turned back and said, 'By al-Lat and al-Uzza, battalions of [angels] came between me and him.' Ibn Abbas said, 'Had he moved, the guards of Hell would have seized him.' Then he recited: {Let him call his associates; We will call the guards of Hell}."],[12560,"\"Muhammad ﷺ preceded [in declaring] badhaq [intoxicating]. What intoxicates is forbidden.\""],[12561,"\"Do you know why this verse was revealed? O you who have believed, do not ask about things that, if they are shown to you, will distress you. There were people who used to mock the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by saying, 'Who is my father?' And he would also say, 'My camel has gone astray, where is my camel?' So Allah revealed this verse.\""],[12562,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying, and a kid went to pass in front of him, so he hurried to block it. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while a she-donkey belonging to al-Fadl b. al-Abbas was grazing that day in front of him."],[12563,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five [units] and prostrated twice for forgetfulness while sitting.\""],[12564,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted Usama b. Zayd behind him on the Day of ʿArafa until he reached Muzdalifa, then he mounted al-Fadl behind him until he reached Jamrat al-ʿAqaba, and he did not cease reciting the talbiya until he threw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba.\""],[12565,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, the young boys of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, ahead on donkeys on the night of Muzdalifa, and he began patting our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw the jamra until the sun rises.\""],[12566,"\"I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers or not, but we recite.\""],[12567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hurried us at night from Muzdalifa to Mina and carried us to the jamarat, and he began striking our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba until the sun rises.\""],[12568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, the young boys of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, ahead on donkeys, patting our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba until the sun rises.\""],[12569,"\"I came with a boy from Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib on a donkey while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in prayer, so we sent the donkey away and entered the row, and two slave girls came racing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them.\""],[12570,"What do you say about the grandfather? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying and his grandfather passed by in front of him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastened to face the Qibla. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one day and there was a donkey belonging to Al-Fadl ibn Abbas grazing in front of him."],[12571,"When you throw the jamra, everything becomes permissible for you except women. He said, \"As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perfuming his head with musk. Is that perfume or not?\""],[12572,"The Angel of Death came to the Prophet ﷺ during the illness in which he passed away, and he asked permission while his head was in the lap of ʿAli. He said, \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\" ʿAli ؓ said, \"Go back, for we are busy with you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you know who this is, O Abu al-Hasan? This is the Angel of Death. Enter, rightly guided.\" When he entered, he said, \"Your Lord ﷻ sends you greetings of peace.\" He said, \"Where is Jibril?\" He said, \"He is not near me now; he will come.\" The Angel of Death left until Jibril descended upon him. Jibril ﷺ said to him while he was standing at the door, \"What brought you out, O Angel of Death?\" He said, \"Muhammad ﷺ requested you.\" When they both sat, Jibril said, \"Peace be upon you, O Abu al-Qasim. This is a farewell from me and from you.\" It has reached me that the Angel of Death did not greet any household before him, nor will he greet anyone after him."],[12573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever curses my companions, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.\""],[12574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let every man eat from his sacrificial animal.\""],[12575,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to pray two rakʿas, two rakʿas whenever he left his house until he returned.\""],[12576,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from his family as a traveler, he would pray two rak'ahs until he returned to his family."],[12577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his family on the two Eids."],[12578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."],[12579,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."],[12580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, may He be exalted, says: 'Whoever shows enmity to a friend of Mine, I have declared war on him. I have never hesitated about anything I am going to do as I hesitate about the death of a believer: he dislikes death, and I dislike distressing him. Sometimes My believing friend asks Me for wealth, but I turn him from wealth to poverty; if I turned him to wealth, it would be bad for him. Sometimes My believing friend asks Me for poverty, but I turn him to wealth; if I turned him to poverty, it would be bad for him. Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, said: By My might, My majesty, My loftiness, My splendor, My beauty, and the elevation of My station, no servant gives preference to My desire over his own desire except that I fix his term before his eyes, and the heaven and earth guarantee his provision, and I am behind the trade of every trader for him.'"],[12581,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast, he would say: 'For You I have fasted, and upon Your provision I have broken my fast, so accept from me; indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.'"],[12582,"When the people of the mosque were expelled and 'Ali was left, the people talked about that. It reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'I did not expel you of my own accord, nor did I leave him; rather, Allah expelled you and left him. I am only a commanded servant; whatever I am commanded, I do. I follow only what is revealed to me.'"],[12583,"Allah created the Garden of Eden with His hand, lowered its fruits into it, and split its rivers in it. Then He looked into it and said: 'The believers have succeeded.' He said: 'By My might, no miser shall be My neighbor in it.'"],[12584,"The Prophet ﷺ only banished al-Ḥakam b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ from Madinah to al-Ṭāʾif. While the Prophet ﷺ was in his room, he saw a person peeking at him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “The gecko, the gecko.” He looked, and it was al-Ḥakam. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave; do not live with me in Madinah as long as I remain.” So he banished him to al-Ṭāʾif."],[12585,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He cursed the women who visit graves, those who build mosques over them, and those who place lamps on them.”"],[12586,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating grapes by pulling them off the stem."],[12587,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in an open area with nothing in front of him.”"],[12588,"“The Prophet’s ﷺ share that Allah fed him is the fifth of the fifth.”"],[12589,"It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"],[12590,"From Yazīd Abū Khālid al-Dālānī al-Wāsiṭī, from al-Minhāl b. ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ḥārith, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever enters upon a sick person and says: ‘I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,’ then he will be cured as long as his appointed time has not arrived.” Shuʿbah said: “He raised it once and did not raise it twice.”"],[12591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever enters upon a sick person and says: ‘I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,’ then he will be cured as long as his appointed time has not come.”"],[12592,"The Prophet ﷺ “prayed over a deceased person after he had been buried.”"],[12593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A prophet among the prophets complained to his Lord, may He be exalted, saying: ‘O Lord, one of Your servants believes in You and acts in obedience to You, yet You withhold the world from him and expose him to affliction, while another of Your servants disbelieves in You and acts in disobedience to You, yet You withhold affliction from him and present the world to him.’ So Allah, may He be exalted, revealed to him: ‘Affliction and servants belong to Me. There is nothing except that it glorifies Me, declares My oneness, and magnifies Me. As for My believing servant, he has sins, so I withhold the world from him and expose him to affliction until he comes to Me and I reward him with good deeds. As for My disbelieving servant, he has good deeds, so I withhold affliction from him and present the world to him until he comes to Me and I requite him for his sins.’”"],[12594,"Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Call upon your Lord to turn al-Ṣafā into gold for us; if it becomes gold by morning, we will follow you.” So he called upon his Lord, may He be exalted, and Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: “Your Lord sends you greetings of peace and says: If you wish, al-Ṣafā will become gold for them, and whoever among them disbelieves I will punish with a punishment I have not inflicted on anyone in the worlds; or if you wish, I will open for them the gate of repentance and mercy.” He said: “Rather, the gate of repentance and mercy.”"],[12595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gabriel told me that the month has ended, it was twenty-nine days.\""],[12598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sodom and the surrounding towns were not destroyed until they used tooth-sticks and chewed gum in their gatherings.\""],[12601,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray two rakʿahs before dawn, then sleep until he snored and breathed heavily while prostrating or sitting, then he got up and prayed. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you slept.\" He said: \"Ablution is required only for one who sleeps lying down, for when he lies down his joints relax.\""],[12602,"The cousin of your Prophet ﷺ—meaning Ibn ʿAbbās—told me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw Mūsā b. ʿImrān ﷺ : a tall, curly-haired, brown-skinned man, as if from the men of Shanūʾah. And I saw ʿĪsā b. Maryam: a man of medium build, tending toward reddish-white, with straight hair. And I saw Mālik, the keeper of the Fire, and I saw the Dajjāl in signs that Allah ﷻ showed me.\""],[12603,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say at times of distress: \"There is no god but Allah, the Magnificent, the Forbearing. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the Great Throne.\""],[12604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the illness of the sick, I would have delayed the last evening prayer.\""],[12605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting for a servant to say, 'I am better than Yūnus b. Mattā.'\""],[12606,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The worst food is the food of a walīmah, to which the well-fed are invited while the hungry are turned away.\""],[12607,"He used to teach us the ruku' (bowing) as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them, then he would become still for us while bowing, such that if a drop of water were to be dripped between his shoulders, it would not move forward or backward."],[12608,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon the valley of Ibn al-Azraq and said, \"What is this valley?\" They said, \"The valley of Ibn al-Azraq.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Musa ﷺ descending, and he has a loud voice, calling upon his Lord with the talbiyah.\" Then he came upon a mountain pass and said, \"What is this mountain pass?\" It was said, \"The mountain pass of such and such.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Yunus b. Matta on a red camel with short hair, its halter made of palm fiber, wearing a woolen jubbah, and he is reciting the talbiyah.\" Abu al-Qasim said: Hammad b. Salama said \"Ibn al-Azraq,\" but it is actually \"al-Azraq.\""],[12609,"The Prophet ﷺ [said]: \"Do not curse it, for it is commanded, and whoever curses something that does not deserve it, the curse falls back upon him.\""],[12610,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying {And We made it a guidance for the Children of Israel}: He said, \"He made Musa a guidance for the Children of Israel.\" And regarding His saying {So do not be in doubt about meeting Him}: He said, \"About Musa's meeting his Lord, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[12611,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever sees something from his ruler that he dislikes, let him be patient, for there is no one who separates from the community and then dies except that he dies a death of Jahiliyyah.\""],[12612,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed your Lord is Merciful. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, it is written for him as ten times up to seven hundred times, up to many multiples. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, it is written for him as one good deed. But if he does it, it is written against him as one evil deed, or He erases it. And no one is destroyed upon Allah except the one who is destroyed.\""],[12613,"He said on a rainy day: \"Pray in your dwellings.\" Then he said, \"Are you surprised? The one who is better than us, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, did it.\""],[12614,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Sa'id, 'I have hidden a treasure for you, so what is it?'\" He said, \"Humility.\" He said, \"Go away.\""],[12615,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The affair of this ummah will continue to be moderate or favorable until they speak about children and qadar.\""],[12616,"Muhammad ﷺ [said]: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor and the destitute, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12618,"Muhammad ﷺ [said]: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12619,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12620,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women.\""],[12621,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah.\""],[12622,"Al-Zubayr donated a horse in the path of Allah, then he found a foal from its progeny being sold, and he was forbidden to buy it."],[12623,"\"They were a people who, during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, did not go on military expeditions with him due to illnesses, diseases, and pains, while others who were healthy also did not go with him. The sick ones were excused in contrast to the healthy.\""],[12624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O young men of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Whoever guards his private parts will have Paradise.\""],[12625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first from whom the earth will split open, and this is no boast.\""],[12626,"\"...to prohibit what Allah and His Messenger have prohibited, then let him prohibit nabidh made in earthenware jars.\""],[12627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four things, saying: \"I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the Fire, I seek refuge in Allah from trials, both apparent and hidden, and I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the one-eyed liar.\""],[12628,"\"I visited my maternal aunt, and it coincided with the night of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for a long portion of the night, performed ablution thoroughly, then stood to pray. I stood up, performed ablution, and came to his side. When he knew that I wanted to pray, he took my hand and placed me on his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and performed witr with seven or nine rak'ahs, then he performed two rak'ahs, then he lay on his side until I heard his breathing. Then the prayer was called, and he went out for the prayer.\""],[12629,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, he kept his back straight; if water were poured on his back, it would have stayed."],[12630,"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was taken on the night journey and morning came upon him in Makkah, he sat apart in sorrow. The enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, came to him and said, as if mocking, \"Did anything happen?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He (i.e., the Prophet) said: 'I was taken by night to the Sacred House (Bayt al-Maqdis).'\" He said, \"Then you woke up among us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He did not show him that he was denying him, fearing that if he called his people to it they would reject it—the hadith. He said, \"What do you think if I call your people to you? Will you tell them what you told me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Abu Jahl said, \"O Banu Ka'b b. Lu'ayy, come!\" The gatherings dispersed until they sat down before them. Abu Jahl said, \"Tell your people what you told me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I was taken by night.\" He said, \"To where?\" He said, \"To the Sacred House (Bayt al-Maqdis).\" They said, \"Then you woke up among us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Some clapped, and some placed his hand on his head in astonishment, saying, \"A lie, he claims.\" Among the people were those who had traveled to that mosque and seen it. They said, \"Can you describe the mosque to us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"I described it to them until some of the description became confused for me.\" He said, \"The mosque was brought forth while I was looking at it, until it was placed near the house of 'Aqil or the house of 'Iqal. I began to describe it while I was looking at it.\" The people said, \"As for the description, by Allah, he has hit the mark.\""],[12631,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"Which speech is most beloved to Allah?\" He said, \"The one who alights and departs (al-hāll al-murtaḥil).\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is al-hāll al-murtaḥil?\" He said, \"The companion of the Quran who strikes through its beginning until he reaches its end, and through its end until he reaches its beginning.\""],[12632,"The Prophet ﷺ passed wind from his shoulder and then prayed without performing ablution."],[12633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Remember Allah with a remembrance such that the hypocrites say, 'You are showing off.'\""],[12634,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The people of Paradise are those who fill their ears with praise of people for good while he listens, and the people of the Fire are those who fill their ears with praise of people for evil while he listens.\""],[12635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the two side-posts of the door while we were in the house and said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, is there anyone among you from other than you?\" They said, \"A son of our sister.\" He said, \"The son of a people's sister is from them.\" Then he said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, if distress, fever, hardship, or adversity befalls you, say: Allah, Allah, our Lord, He has no partner.\""],[12636,"Regarding His saying: {For him are successive [angels] before him and behind him} (Quran 13:11), he said, \"It refers to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[12637,"Regarding His saying: {On the Day when We will fold the heaven like the folding of a scroll for the records} (Quran 21:104), he said, \"The Prophet ﷺ had a scribe called al-Sijill.\""],[12638,"\"There was a beautiful woman who used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ. Some people would advance and some would delay in order to look at her.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {And We have already known the foremost among you, and We have already known the ones who lag behind} (Quran 15:24)."],[12639,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"The Greatest Name of Allah, when invoked with it, He answers, is in this verse from the family of Imran, 'Say: O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You wills.' until the end of it.\""],[12640,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that, for it is its expiation—except for divorce or manumission.\""],[12641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin, and He would forgive them.\""],[12642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The expiation of sin is remorse.\""],[12643,"When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You, for all fortune is Yours.”"],[12644,"\"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Allah said, 'I have created good and evil, so blessed is the one upon whose hands good is determined, and woe to the one upon whose hands evil is determined.'\""],[12645,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I have never seen anything more excellent in seeking or swifter in attaining than a good deed that is recent for an old sin. {Indeed, good deeds do away with evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.}”"],[12646,"“Glory be to Allah and with His praise. I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him”—it is recorded as he said it, then it is hung upon the Throne, and no sin committed by its utterer can erase it until he meets Allah, and it remains sealed just as he said it."],[12647,"From Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ, and we do not know it except as a marfūʿ narration attributed to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the prayer, and fasting Ramadan. Whoever abandons any one of them is a disbeliever whose blood is lawful.”"],[12648,"One of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ pitched a tent over a grave, not knowing it was a grave. Then suddenly a person inside was reciting “Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion” until he completed it. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I pitched my tent over a grave, not knowing it was a grave, and suddenly a person was reciting ‘Blessed is He’ until he completed it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is the preventer, it is the deliverer; it delivers him from the punishment of the grave.”"],[12649,"\"The demons.\""],[12650,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “In Hell there is a valley from which Hell seeks refuge four hundred times every day. That valley has been prepared for the ostentatious of the community of Muhammad ﷺ: for one who carries the Book of Allah, for one who gives charity for other than Allah’s sake, for those who perform pilgrimage to the House of Allah, and for one who goes out in the path of Allah.”"],[12651,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A slave who obeys Allah and obeys his masters—Allah will admit him to Paradise seventy autumns before his masters. The master will say: ‘O Lord, this was my slave in this world.’ He will say: ‘I rewarded him for his deeds and rewarded you for your deeds.’”"],[12652,"He informed him, saying: “I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight [rakʿahs] combined and seven [rakʿahs] combined.”"],[12653,"“I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight and seven combined.”"],[12654,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed eight rakʿahs combined and seven rakʿahs combined, without illness or ailment.”"],[12655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “prayed in Madinah seven and eight: Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.”"],[12656,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever cannot find an izār may wear sirwāl, and whoever cannot find sandals may wear khuffayn.”"],[12657,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Trousers are for one who does not find a waist cloth, and leather socks are for one who does not find sandals\"—meaning the pilgrim in ihram."],[12658,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers; and if he does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks.\""],[12659,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"If the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers; and if he does not find sandals, then leather socks.\""],[12660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon to the people at Arafah and said: \"Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers.\""],[12661,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ giving a sermon at Arafat, saying: \"Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers.\""],[12662,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever does not find a waist cloth but finds trousers, let him wear them; and whoever does not find sandals but finds leather socks, let him wear them.\""],[12663,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masʿud."],[12664,"\"...that Allah may will, and remember your Lord when you forget\" [Quran 18:24]—meaning to say 'if Allah wills.'"],[12665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Muhajirun because they migrated away from the polytheists; and among the Ansar there were also Muhajirun, because Madinah was a place where revelation descended, and they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-ʿAqabah."],[12666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets to send blessings upon me has missed the path to Paradise.\""],[12667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the meat of horses be eaten."],[12668,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached regarding the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: \"She is not permissible for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and the same prohibitions apply through suckling as apply through blood relations.\""],[12669,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sought for the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: \"She is not lawful for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and whatever is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling.\""],[12670,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Will you not marry the daughter of Hamzah?\" He said: \"She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.\""],[12671,"\"The black dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer.\""],[12672,"The Prophet ﷺ combined two prayers during the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq."],[12673,"\"It is from the Sunnah to combine two prayers while traveling.\""],[12674,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The prostitutes are those who give themselves in marriage without evidence.\""],[12675,"Circumcision is a Sunnah for men and a noble act for women."],[12676,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The martyr will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and set up for reckoning, and the charitable person will be brought and set up for reckoning, then the people of affliction will be brought, and no scale will be set up for them and no register will be spread out for them; rather, reward will be poured upon them abundantly, until the people of well-being in the standing place will wish that their bodies had been cut with shears, because of the excellence of God's reward for them.\""],[12677,"Ibn Abbas said: \"The Fajr prayer is between the break of dawn and the rising of the sun's rays. Its time ends once the sun has risen. The Messenger of God ﷺ once set out at night and then stopped to rest, and he did not wake until the sun had risen, or part of it had risen. He did not pray until it had risen high, then he prayed, and it is the middle prayer.\""],[12678,"The Prophet ﷺ set the ransom for the people of Badr at four hundred."],[12679,"From the Prophet ﷺ, from the Trustworthy Spirit ﷺ , he said: \"The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'The servant's good deeds and bad deeds will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and some will be subtracted from others. If one good deed remains, God will admit him into Paradise.'\" He said: I said: \"What if no good deed remains?\" He said: \"Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they did and overlook their misdeeds, among the companions of Paradise.\" He said: I said: \"What do you think of His saying: 'No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for their eyes'?\" He said: \"It is the servant who does a deed in secret, and God conceals it for him on the Day of Resurrection, so he sees comfort for his eyes.\""],[12680,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The evil eye is real; the evil eye is real. It brings down the high mountain.\""],[12681,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best door of righteousness is charity.\""],[12682,"\"If this verse was revealed to us, we would not take that day as a celebration.\" Ibn Abbas said: \"Indeed, it was revealed on two occasions: on the day of Jumu'ah (Friday) and on the day of Arafah.\""],[12683,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a man with the Prophet ﷺ speaking to him in confidence. He seemed to be turning away from my father. We left him, and my father said to me, \"Did you not see your cousin? He was as if turning away from me.\" I said, \"O father, there was a man with him speaking to him in confidence.\" He said, \"Was there someone with him?\" I said, \"Yes.\" We returned and my father said, \"O Messenger of God, I said to ʿAbd Allah such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such. Was there someone with you?\" He said, \"Yes. And did you see him, O ʿAbd Allah?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That was Jibrīl. It was he who occupied me from you.\""],[12684,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream one day at midday, disheveled and dust-colored, with a bottle in his hand containing blood. I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, what is this?\" He said, \"This is the blood of al-Ḥusayn and his companions. I have been collecting it since today.\" That day was counted, and it was found that he was killed on that day."],[12685,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid. Her father was reluctant to marry her to him, so she prepared food and drink and invited her father and some people from Quraysh. They ate and drank. Khadījah said to her father, \"Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allah is asking for my hand in marriage. Stand up and marry me to him.\" He married her to him, and she perfumed him and dressed him in a fine garment. That is how they used to treat fathers when they married off their daughters. When the intoxication left him, he looked and saw that he was perfumed and wearing a fine garment. He said, \"What is the matter with me?\" She said, \"You married me to Muḥammad.\" He said, \"I married you to the orphan of Abū Ṭālib? No, by my life!\" Khadījah said, \"Are you not ashamed? Do you want to make a fool of yourself? You would tell Quraysh and the people that you were drunk?\" She kept at him until he consented."],[12686,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Khadījah, \"I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear that I may be possessed.\" Khadījah said, \"God would not do that to you, O son of ʿAbd Allah.\" Then she went to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said, \"If he is truthful, this is a nāmūs like the nāmūs of Mūsā. If he is sent while I am alive, I will support him, help him, and assist him.\""],[12687,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for fifteen years: seven or eight seeing the light and hearing the voice, and eight receiving revelation. He stayed in Madinah for ten years."],[12688,"The Prophet ﷺ used to give the sermon standing by a palm trunk before he took a pulpit. When he took the pulpit and moved to it, the trunk yearned for him. He embraced it, and it became still. He said, \"If I had not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12689,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, \"How old was the Messenger of God ﷺ when he died?\" He said, \"I did not think someone like you among a people would be unaware of that.\" I said, \"I asked, and people differed, so I wanted to know your statement about it.\" He said, \"Can you calculate?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Take forty: he was sent at that age, and fifteen: his stay in Makkah, feeling secure and fearing, and ten: his emigration in Madinah.\""],[12690,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five.\" Al-Ḥasan used to say, \"He died at the age of sixty.\""],[12691,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken at the age of sixty-five."],[12692,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had himself cupped and gave the cupper his wage. If it had been unlawful, he would not have given it."],[12693,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Abū Hilāl narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. Sīrīn, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ had himself cupped and paid him. If it had been impure, he would not have paid him.\""],[12694,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had he known it to be impure, he would not have given it."],[12695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and gave the cupper his fee. Had it been unlawful gain, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have given it."],[12696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had it been impure, he would not have given it."],[12697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and would not wrong a hired worker his wage."],[12698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had he known that there was harm in it, he would not have given it."],[12702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to shorten the prayer between Madinah and Makkah, fearing none but God."],[12703,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to shorten the prayer between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but God."],[12704,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled from Makkah to Madinah and prayed two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but God — or he said: fearing none but God — and prayed two rakʿahs."],[12706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to travel from Madinah to Makkah fearing none but God, and prayed two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs."],[12707,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed between Makkah and Madinah two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed between Makkah and Madinah two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12709,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out from Madinah to Makkah fearing none but God, and he prayed two rakʿahs until he went out."],[12710,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but God."],[12711,"Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn ʿAbbas: \"The Prophet ﷺ ate the meat off a shoulder bone, then stood and prayed and did not perform wudu.\""],[12712,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate the meat off a bone, then prayed and did not touch water."],[12713,"The Prophet ﷺ ate the meat off a shoulder bone, then stood and prayed and did not perform wudu."],[12714,"I was among those who hastened in the heavy baggage of the Prophet ﷺ from Jamʿ to Mina."],[12715,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Dhul-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Najd."],[12716,"Revelation came down to the Prophet ﷺ when he was forty years old. He stayed in Makkah thirteen years and in Madinah ten, and he died when he was sixty-three years old."],[12717,"The Messenger of God ﷺ extended his hand to Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah held back until he went and performed ghusl and came. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I was junub.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Muslim does not become impure.\""],[12718,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a caller, and he called out on a rainy day: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[12719,"Al-Hasan: Did not the Prophet ﷺ stand for the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess that passed by him? Ibn ʿAbbas said: Indeed, and he sat down."],[12720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood? The other said: Indeed, and he sat down."],[12721,"Regarding this verse: “And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person.” He said: “Then the other verse abrogated it: ‘So whoever among you witnesses the month, let him fast it.’”"],[12722,"Abu Ayyub ؓ divorced his wife. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the divorce of Umm Ayyub was a sin (ḥūb).” Ibn Sīrīn said: “al-ḥūb means sin.”"],[12723,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “When the first part of al-Muzzammil was revealed, their standing in prayer was like their standing in Ramadan, or similar to their standing in Ramadan, and there was a year between its beginning and its end.”"],[12724,"“I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a cloak of the finest Yemeni cloth.”"],[12725,"I heard him say: The Prophet ﷺ obtained spoils on the day of Hunayn and distributed them to the people. The Ansar said: “We fight, but the spoils go to others.” That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent word to them to gather. He came to them and said: “O assembly of Ansar, is there anyone among you other than yourselves?” They said: “No, except a son of a sister of ours and a client of ours.” He said: “The son of a people’s sister is one of them, and the client of a people is one of them.” He said: “O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that the people take away sheep and cattle, while you take Muhammad ﷺ?” They said: “We are pleased.”"],[12726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever among my ummah loses two children who die before him, Allah will admit him to Paradise.” ʿĀʾishah asked: “And someone who loses one child?” He said: “And whoever loses one child, O fortunate one.” She asked: “And one who has no child die before him?” He said: “I am the one who dies before my ummah; they have not been afflicted with the like of me.”"],[12727,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, and people were rained upon until the canal flowed for forty days.” In the morning people said: “The star of such-and-such has proven true,” and among them were those who said: “This is a mercy that Allah has sent down.”"],[12728,"People were rained upon during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the people this morning there is one who is grateful and one who is ungrateful. They said: ‘This is a mercy that Allah has sent down,’ while others said: ‘The star of such-and-such has proven true.’ Then this verse was revealed: ‘Nay, I swear by the locations of the stars’ up to ‘You make your provision that you deny.’”"],[12729,"The polytheists used to say: “Labbayk, no partner has You.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “Woe to you, enough, enough.” Then they would say: “Except a partner who is Yours; You own Him and what He owns.” They said this while circumambulating the House."],[12730,"“I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the finest of Yemeni garments.”"],[12731,"The people would not look at Abu Sufyan or sit with him. He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Three things I will give you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I have the finest and most beautiful Arab woman, Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan; I will give her to you in marriage.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And Muāwiyah – make him a scribe, place him before you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And appoint me as a commander to fight the disbelievers just as I used to fight the Muslims.” He said: “Yes.”"],[12732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God cursed the Jews. Fats were forbidden to them, but they sold them and consumed their price. When God, exalted is He, forbids eating something, He forbids its price.”"],[12733,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Some poetry contains wisdom, and some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[12734,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to delay the evening prayer (al-ʿatamah) until one third of the night. That is why it is called al-ʿatamah, because he used to delay it (yuʿtim) into the darkness.”"],[12735,"\"I passed by, along with a young boy from the Quraysh, riding a donkey in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying. He did not finish his prayer and two young girls from the Bani Abdul Mutallib clan came and took hold of his knees. He spread his arms between them and did not finish.\" This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Al-Hakam, from Yahya bin Al-Jazzaar, from Suhaib. Mansur contradicted this narration."],[12736,"That he said to ʿUmar: “You accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ with the best companionship, and he is pleased with you.”"],[12737,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas: How should I say prayer when I am in Mecca, and when I do not pray along with the Imam? He said: Two rak'ahs (of prayer) is the Sunnah of Abu'l-Qasim ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 688a)"],[12738,"\"That is the Sunnah of Abi Al-Qasim ﷺ , even if you feel reluctant.\""],[12739,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas: How should I say prayer when I am in Mecca, and when I do not pray along with the Imam? He said: Two rak'ahs (of prayer) is the Sunnah of Abu'l-Qasim ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 688a)"],[12740,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the spirit into it, but he will not be able to.”"],[12741,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, then called for a sacrificial camel and marked the right side of its hump. Then he wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals. Then his mount was brought, and when he sat on it and it stood upright with him at al-Baydāʾ, he entered the state of iḥrām."],[12742,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the state of iḥrām after the noon prayer from al-Baydāʾ."],[12743,"That God made it lawful and revealed regarding it the longest verse in the Book of God: {O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a fixed term, write it down}."],[12744,"The Prophet ﷺ used to visit the House every night during the nights of Minā."],[12745,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about the Witr prayer. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is a rak'ah at the end of the night prayer. (Using translation from Muslim 753)"],[12746,"I do not know whether the Messenger of God ﷺ stoned it with six or seven."],[12749,"The banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ was black and his standard was white."],[12750,"To Ibn ʿAbbas, and he pointed to Muʿawiya: \"They serve water and honey, and the family of so-and-so serve milk, and you serve nabidh. Is it out of stinginess on your part or out of need?\" He said: \"We are neither stingy nor in need, but the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him, and we gave him some of this nabidh to drink. He drank from it and said: 'Do likewise.'\""],[12751,"The Messenger of God ﷺ intended to perform Hajj. A woman said to her husband: \"Take me on Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said to her: \"I do not have anything on which to take you on Hajj.\" She said: \"Take me on Hajj on your camel so-and-so.\" He said: \"That is dedicated to the cause of God.\" She said: \"Take me on Hajj on your water-carrying camel.\" He said: \"That one you and I use alternately.\" She said: \"Then sell your dates.\" He said: \"That is my food and yours.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived, the woman sent her husband to him and said: \"Convey to him my greeting of peace and God's mercy, and ask him what equals a Hajj with you.\" He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my wife conveys to you the greeting of peace and God's mercy. She had asked me to take her on Hajj with you, and I said: I do not have anything on which to take you on Hajj. She said: Take me on Hajj on your camel so-and-so. I said: That is dedicated to the cause of God.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If you had taken her on Hajj on it, it would have been in the cause of God.\" He continued: \"She said: Take me on Hajj on your water-carrying camel. I said: That one you and I use alternately. She said: Then sell your dates. I said: That is my food and yours.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at her eagerness for Hajj. He said: \"She instructed me to ask you what suffices as a Hajj with you.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Convey to her the greeting of peace and God's mercy, and tell her that an ʿumra in Ramadan equals a Hajj with me.\""],[12752,"From Ayyub, ʿAsim, and ʿAbd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Ziyadi, from ʿAbd Allah b. al-Harith, who said: Ibn ʿAbbas delivered a sermon to us on a rainy day. When the muezzin reached 'Come to prayer,' he ordered him to call out: 'Pray in your dwellings.' Some of them looked at one another, so he said: \"It seems you disapprove of this? One better than me did this, and it is a firm practice.\""],[12753,"When you reach 'Come to success,' say: 'Indeed, pray in your dwellings.' It was said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"One better than me did it.\""],[12754,"Because he sat on a white hide and it turned green and vibrated.\" Saʿid b. Bashir said: \"And Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to me that Qatada used to raise this hadith to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[12755,"May you be bereft of your mother! You are teaching us about its time? We used to combine the two prayers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[12756,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Among a man's happiness is a light beard.\""],[12757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever takes a span of Makkah without right, it is as if he has taken it from beneath the foot of the Most Merciful; and whoever takes anything from the rest of the earth without right will come on the Day of Resurrection with it hung around his neck from seven earths.\""],[12758,"\"When you see the crescent of Muharram, then count; when it is the ninth day, then enter the morning fasting.\" I said: \"Is that how Muhammad ﷺ used to fast?\" He said: \"That is how Muhammad ﷺ used to fast.\""],[12759,"“Whoever sees me in a dream has (really) seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3903)"],[12760,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: \"What reports have spread among the people saying, 'Whoever circumambulates the House has become free of ihram'?\" He said: \"That is the sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, even if you dislike it.\""],[12761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first to deny was Adam. When Allah ﷻ created him, He wiped his back and brought forth his offspring and all that He would create until the Day of Resurrection. He began presenting them to him, and he saw among them a radiant man. He said: 'O Lord, which of my sons is this?' He said: 'This is your son Dawud.' He said: 'O Lord, how long is his life?' He said: 'Sixty years.' He said: 'O Lord, increase his life.' He said: 'No, unless you give him from your own life.' Adam's life was a thousand years, and he gave him forty years from his life. He said: 'So He wrote a document for him regarding that and made the angels witnesses.' When Adam was dying, the angels came to take his soul. He said: 'Forty years of my life remain.' They said: 'You gave them to your son Dawud.' He said: 'I did not do that; I did not give him anything.' Then Allah brought down the document and the angels testified against him. So Allah completed for Adam a thousand years and completed for Dawud a hundred years.\""],[12762,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Jibril ﷺ said: 'Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish.'\""],[12763,"\"Surat al-An'am was revealed all at once in Makkah at night, with seventy thousand angels around it glorifying Allah.\""],[12764,"A woman came to me seeking my allegiance. I took her to an enclosed place and I hit her with my hand and attempted to seduce her. I did everything with her except sexual intercourse. Umar said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is pregnant.\" He replied, \"Yes.\" Umar said to him, \"Go to Abu Bakr and ask him.\" So he went to him and told him what he had said to Umar. Abu Bakr said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is pregnant.\" He then went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the same thing he had told Abu Bakr and Umar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is fighting for the cause of Allah.\" He replied, \"Yes.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and the Quran was revealed, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night.\" until the end of the verse. The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is this command specific to me or for the general public?\" Umar raised his hand and struck his own chest and said, \"No, by Allah, not for the sake of power, but for the general public.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said, \"Umar has spoken the truth.\""],[12765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah drowned Pharaoh, he said: 'I believe that there is no god except the One in whom the Children of Israel believe.' Jibril ﷺ said: 'O Muhammad, if you had seen me, I was taking mud from the sea and stuffing it into his mouth, fearing that mercy might reach him.'\""],[12766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no one among the children of Adam except that he has erred or thought of a sin, except Yahya b. Zakariyya.\""],[12767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him, and we gave him some of this drink—meaning the drink of the siqaya—and he said, \"You have done well; do it like this.\""],[12768,"We recited it in the time of the Prophet ﷺ for two years: “And those who do not call upon another god besides God, and do not kill the soul which God has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery” [Q 25:68]—the verse—then was revealed “except for one who repents” [Q 25:70]. I never saw the Prophet ﷺ rejoice with any joy more intense than his joy at this verse and at “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [Q 48:1]."],[12769,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on his riding camel, touching the corner with his staff."],[12770,"We were in a circle in the mosque discussing the virtues of the prophets, which of them is best. We mentioned Noah and the length of his worship of his Lord, and we mentioned Abraham, the friend of the Merciful, and we mentioned Moses, God's interlocutor, and we mentioned Jesus son of Mary, and we mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ. While we were doing that, the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, \"What are you discussing among yourselves?\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, we were discussing the virtues of the prophets, which of them is best. We mentioned Noah and the length of his worship, we mentioned Abraham, the friend of the Merciful, we mentioned Moses, the interlocutor of the Merciful, we mentioned Jesus son of Mary, and we mentioned you, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"So whom did you prefer?\" We said, \"We preferred you, O Messenger of God, because God sent you to all mankind, forgave you your past and future sins, and you are the seal of the prophets.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, it is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better than Yahya b. Zakariyya.'\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, how so?\" He said, \"Did you not hear how God described him in the Qur'an? He said: 'O Yahya, take the Scripture with strength.' And We gave him judgment while yet a boy' [Q 19:12]. Then he recited until he reached: 'a master, chaste, and a prophet from among the righteous' [Q 19:13–14]. He never committed an evil deed, nor did he intend one.\""],[12771,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he said, \"There is no human being but has in his head a wisdom held by an angel. When he humbles himself, it is said to the angel, 'Raise his wisdom,' and when he becomes arrogant, it is said to the angel, 'Lay his wisdom low.'\""],[12772,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was visited by two angels as a sleeping person sees. One of them sat at his feet and the other at his head. The one at his feet said to the one at his head, \"Strike a parable for this man and his community.\" He said, \"The example of this man and his community is like a group of travellers who reached the edge of a desert, but they had no provisions with which to cross the desert or return. While they were in that state, a man came to them wearing a striped robe and said, 'What do you think: if I bring you to lush meadows and full watering places, will you follow me?' They said, 'Yes.' So he set off with them and brought them to lush meadows and full watering places. They ate, drank, and grew fat. Then he said to them, 'Did I not find you in that earlier condition?' They said, 'Yes.' 'But did you not agree that if I brought you to lush meadows and full watering places you would follow me?' They said, 'Yes.' So one group among them said, 'By God, he has spoken truth; we will certainly follow him.' And another group said, 'We have accepted this place; we will stay here.'\""],[12773,"He saw his Lord, exalted is He, with his heart."],[12774,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping at al-Qahah while he was in a state of ihram."],[12775,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years receiving revelation, and in Madinah for ten years, and he died at the age of sixty-three."],[12776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out saying, \"Part of the decline of religion is inspecting the Nabataeans and their building of palaces in the garrison towns.\""],[12777,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Wear turbans and you will increase in forbearance.\""],[12778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to a clan of the Arabs calling them to Islam, but they did not accept the letter and returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: “Indeed, if I had sent it to a people on the shore of Oman from the Azd Shanu’ah, and they submitted, they would have accepted it.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to al-Julanda calling him to Islam, and he accepted it and submitted, and he sent a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It arrived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away, so Abu Bakr made the gift an inheritance and divided it between Fatimah and the people."],[12779,"Four hundred men from Daws came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Welcome! The finest of people in faces, the sweetest of them in mouths, and the greatest of them in trustworthiness.”"],[12780,"When the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Who are the people?” They said: “Rabiʿah.” He said: “Welcome to the delegation, not disgraced nor regretful.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are a clan of Rabiʿah, and we come to you from a distant land. Between us and you lies this clan of the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a decisive matter to which you call and to which we call those behind us, and by which we may enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four. I command you with faith in Allah, the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Do you know what faith is? It is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you give one-fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from four: from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.” He said: “And perhaps he said: and the muqayyar. Memorize them and call to them those behind you.”"],[12781,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this clan of Rabiʿah has been separated from you by the disbelievers of Mudar, so we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. Command us with a matter that we may adopt and to which we may call those behind us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: faith in Allah, the testimony that there is no god but Allah” — and he counted on his hand — “the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you pay one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade the dubba’, the muzaffat, the naqir, and the hantam.”"],[12783,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, there are disbelievers from the tribe of Mudar between us and you, and we can only come to you during the sacred months. So give us a command that we can convey to those behind us and invite them to it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Tell them that there are four testimonies: There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting in Ramadan, and paying one-fifth of what you have acquired. And I prohibit you from drinking the wine of grapes, and from the wine of dates, and from the wine of barley and wheat.\""],[12784,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are this clan of Rabiʿah, and the disbelievers of Mudar have come between us and you, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a matter that we may act upon and to which we may call those behind us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: faith” — and he explained it to them — “the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, and that you pay one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muqayyar.”"],[12785,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Greetings, O Messenger of Allah. We are from the tribe of Rabi'ah, but there are disbelievers from the tribe of Mudar among us. We can only come to you in the sacred month, so guide us and call those behind us to the same. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I command you to do four things: to have faith in Allah, bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and Muhammad is His Messenger, establish prayer, give zakat (charity), and pay one-fifth of the war booty. I forbid you from five things: do not consume carrion, blood, pork, or wine.\""],[12786,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot come to you whenever we wish. So inform us of what is lawful for us and what is forbidden to us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: that you establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, and give one-fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12787,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with what is lawful for us and what is forbidden to us.” He said: “I command you with one matter and forbid you from four. I command you with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you give one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12788,"“The first Friday prayer established after the Friday prayer in Madinah was a Friday prayer in al-Bahrayn, in a village belonging to ʿAbd al-Qays called Juatha.”"],[12789,"From Ibn ʿAbbas: “The first Friday prayer was established in Madinah, then the Friday prayer of Juatha.”"],[12790,"He was a prophet who sent his brother and said: “Go to Makkah until you hear from him and bring me news of him.” His brother went to Makkah and heard news of the Prophet ﷺ, then returned to Abu Dharr and informed him that he enjoins good, forbids evil, and enjoins noble character. He said: “You have not satisfied me.” Then he took a waterskin containing water and a leather bucket, and set out until he came to Makkah. He was afraid to ask anyone about anything, and he did not meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until night fell. When it became dark, ʿAli b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: “Who is the man?” He said: “A man from Ghifar.” He said: “Come to your lodging,” and took him to his lodging, neither of them asking the other about anything. When morning came, he went out but did not meet him, so he stood aside in the mosque. ʿAli b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: “Is it not time for the man to know his lodging?” He took him along, neither of them asking the other about anything. On the third day, Abu Dharr made ʿAli promise that if he told him what he wanted, he would keep it secret and conceal it from others. He did so, and said: “It has reached me that a man has appeared in Makkah claiming to be a prophet. I sent my brother, but he did not bring me what would satisfy me, so I came myself to learn his news.” ʿAli b. Abi Talib said: “Then follow my tracks, for if I see something I fear for you, I will stand as if to urinate and return to you. If I see nothing, then follow my tracks.” So ʿAli went out, and Abu Dharr followed his tracks until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Dharr told him his news and heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then submitted. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, command me with your command.” He said: “Return to your people until my news reaches you.” He said: “No, by Allah, I will not return until I proclaim Islam openly.” He went out to the mosque and called out with the prayer, saying: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.” The polytheists said: “The man has turned Sabian! The man has turned Sabian!” and they beat him until he fell. Al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib passed by him, leaned over him, then said: “O people of Quraysh, you are merchants and your route passes by Ghifar. Do you want us to cut off the route from you?” So they left him alone. On the second day, he repeated the same words, and they beat him. Al-ʿAbbas passed by him and said the same to them, so they left him alone. This was the beginning of Islam for Abu Dharr ؓ."],[12791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The ʿumrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[12792,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Gabriel came to me during the final ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and said, \"The Umrah (lesser pilgrimage) during Hajj is valid until the Day of Resurrection.\" Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If I had known beforehand what I know now, I would have not brought the sacrificial animals and performed the Hajj rites.\""],[12793,"Allah is greater—the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, or he said: the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ."],[12794,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: “A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[12795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rakʿahs at night."],[12796,"His freedman said to him: “Mutʿah was only when people were in need and women were few.” Ibn Abbas said to him: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[12797,"Do not seek a need from a blind man, and do not seek it at night. When you seek a need, face the man directly, for modesty is in the eyes. And seek your need early in the morning, for the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early mornings.”"],[12798,"For the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.”"],[12799,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Muhammad b. Maslamah a sword and said: “Fight the polytheists as long as they are fought. When you see two swords drawn among the Muslims, strike with it until it is notched, then stay in your house until a decisive death or a stray hand comes to you.” Then I came to Ibn Umar and he narrated to me the like of it from the Prophet ﷺ."],[12800,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ashajj ʿAbd al-Qays: “You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.”"],[12801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the people of the East are ʿAbd al-Qays.”"],[12802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the advocate of whoever wrongs ʿAbd al-Qays.”"],[12803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive ʿAbd al-Qays,” three times."],[12804,"Regarding wine: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque. While he was talking intimately, he undid his wrap, then said: “Whoever has any wine, let him inform me.” The people began coming to him; one said, “I have a wineskin of wine”; another said, “I have a waterskin”; another said, “I have a small skin,” and whatever Allah willed that they had. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gather it in Baqiʿ of such-and-such, then inform me.” He stood and I stood with him, walking on his right, while he leaned on me. Abu Bakr caught up with us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me and placed me on his left and put Abu Bakr in my place. Then Umar b. al-Khattab caught up with us, and he took him and placed him on his left, so he walked between the two of them until, when he stood over the wine, he said to the people: “Do you recognize this?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, this is wine.” He said: “You have spoken the truth. Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its server, and the one who consumes its price.” Then he called for a knife and said: “Sharpen it.” They did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and began slashing the wine skins. The people said: “There is benefit in these skins.” He said: “Yes, but I only do this out of anger for Allah because of the displeasure that is in it.” He said: “And some of them add to this in the hadith more than others.”"],[12805,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: “Rather, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[12806,"Fulfill my need, O Commander of the Believers, for by Allah, my burden is great. I have become the father of ten, the brother of ten, and the uncle of ten. When Marwan turned away, while Ibn Abbas was sitting with Muawiya on his couch, Muawiya said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When the Banu al-Hakam reach thirty men, they will take the signs of Allah among them as a gain, His servants as slaves, and His Book as deceit. When they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be swifter than fruit’?” Ibn Abbas said: “O Allah, yes.” Then Marwan mentioned a need he had, and Marwan b. Abd al-Malik returned to Muawiya and spoke to him about it. When he turned away, Muawiya said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned this and said: ‘Abu al-Jababirah the four’?” Ibn Abbas said: “O Allah, yes.” For that reason Muawiya claimed Ziyad."],[12807,"Some people from Himyar came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about things. One of them said: “I love women, and I love to come to my wife from behind, so what do you think about that?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish} [Quran 2:223]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Come to her from the front or from the back, as long as it is in the vagina.”"],[12808,"Your Prophet ﷺ was born on Monday, and on Monday he left Makkah, and he entered Madinah on Monday, and he conquered Badr on Monday, and Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed on Monday: {This day I have perfected for you your religion} [Quran 5:3], and he raised the corner on Monday, and he died on Monday."],[12809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam consists of three hundred and thirteen ways. There is no way by which its adherent meets Allah except that he enters Paradise by it.”"],[12810,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In the urine and milk of camels there is healing for those whose stomachs are afflicted with chronic diarrhea.”"],[12811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out to urinate and then wipe himself with dust. I would say, 'O Messenger of Allah, water is near you.' He would say, 'Perhaps I will not reach it.'"],[12812,"He was behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me while I was riding behind him: 'O boy, I will teach you some words. Preserve them: Preserve Allah and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. Know that if the nation gathered to benefit you, they would not benefit you except with something Allah has already written for you. The pens have dried and the pages have been folded.'"],[12813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Marry off the unmarried — three times — according to what the families agree upon, even if it is a handful of toothstick twigs (arak).'"],[12814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Sabaʾ — what is it? A man, a woman, or a land?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man who fathered ten sons. Six settled in Yemen and four in Syria. As for the Yemenis: Madhhij, Kindah, al-Azd, al-Ashʿariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar. As for the Syrians: Lakhm, Judham, ʿAmilah, and Ghassan.'"],[12815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not guide you to a word that will save you from associating partners with Allah? {Say: O disbelievers} at the time of your sleep.'"],[12816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every bird with talons and every beast of prey with fangs."],[12817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every beast of prey with fangs and every bird with talons."],[12818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every predatory animal with fangs."],[12819,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'There will be a people at the end of time called the Rafidah, who reject Islam and cast it off. Kill them, for they are polytheists.'"],[12820,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and ʿAli was with him. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O ʿAli, there will be among my community a people who claim love for us, the People of the House. They will have a nickname and be called the Rafidah. Kill them, for they are polytheists.'"],[12821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes perform ghusl on Friday and sometimes he would leave it occasionally."],[12822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12823,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12824,"“I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques,” and he did not mention Layth."],[12826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things—if a person is free from even one of them, then surely Allah will forgive him whatever else He wills: he who dies without associating anything with Allah, and is not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and does not bear malice against his brother.”"],[12827,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Whatever Allah wills and you will.” He said: “You have set up a rival to Allah. Rather, say: Whatever Allah alone wills.”"],[12828,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Whatever Allah wills and you will.” He said: “You have made me an equal [to Allah]. Say: Whatever Allah wills.”"],[12829,"Some of his companions said: It was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he neither declared it lawful nor unlawful. Ibn Abbas said: “How bad is what you say! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent only as one who makes lawful and makes unlawful. Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith came to visit her sister Maymunah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. They brought with them food containing the meat of a dabb lizard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after it had grown dark—meaning it had become night. Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dabb meat. So he held back from it, and Maymunah held back from it. Ibn Abbas said: And those with him ate it. If it had been unlawful, he would have forbidden them from it, and he said: “It is not found in our land, and we find it distasteful.”"],[12830,"Some of them said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I do not make it lawful, nor do I make it unlawful.” Ibn Abbas said: “How bad is what you said! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent only as one who makes lawful and makes unlawful. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Maymunah, and with him were al-Fadl b. al-Abbas, Khalid b. al-Walid, and a woman, and Maymunah. A table was brought with bread and dabb meat on it. He held back his hand and said: ‘This is meat I have not eaten, but eat.’ So Khalid b. al-Walid, al-Fadl b. al-Abbas, and the woman ate. Maymunah said: I will not eat food from which the Prophet ﷺ did not eat. So Maymunah did not eat.”"],[12831,"My father narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Yazid b. al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, should I perform Hajj on behalf of my father?” He said: “Yes, if you do not add any good to him, you will not add any harm to him.”"],[12832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are a kind of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[12833,"Ibn Abbas said: “Any man who claims descent from other than his parents, or claims allegiance to other than his masters who freed him, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels until the Day of Resurrection; neither turning away nor justice will be accepted from him.”"],[12834,"A group of Jews came to the Prophet of God ﷺ one day and said, “O Abu al-Qasim, tell us about matters we will ask you that none knows but a prophet.” He said, “Ask me whatever you wish, but grant me the covenant of God and what Jacob took upon his children: if I tell you something and you recognize it, you will follow me.” They said, “That is yours.” They said, “Four matters we ask you about: tell us which food Israel forbade upon himself before the Torah was sent down; tell us how the fluid of the woman is from the fluid of the man, and how the female and the male come from it; tell us how this unlettered prophet is among his people; and who is his guardian among the angels?” He said, “Upon you is the covenant of God: if I tell you, you will follow me.” So they gave him whatever covenant and pact he wished. He said, “I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah to Moses: do you know that Israel fell severely ill and his sickness lasted long, and he vowed that if God healed him, he would forbid the most beloved drink to him and the most beloved food to him, and the most beloved food to him was camel meat and the most beloved drink to him was its milk?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” He said, “I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god: do you know that the fluid of the man is thick and the fluid of the woman is yellow and thin, and whichever of the two prevails, the child and resemblance are by God’s permission; if the man’s fluid prevails, it is male by God’s permission, and if the woman’s fluid prevails, it is female by God’s permission?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” He said, “I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah to Moses: do you know that this unlettered prophet’s two eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” They said, “Now then, tell us who your guardian among the angels is, for at this point we will either join you or part from you.” He said, “My guardian is Gabriel ﷺ , and God ﷻ has never sent any prophet except that he was his guardian.” They said, “At this point we part from you. Had your guardian been other than him among the angels, we would have followed you and believed you.” He said, “What prevents you from believing him?” They said, “He is our enemy.” At that, God ﷻ said: {Whoever is an enemy to Gabriel—for it is he who brought it down upon your heart by God’s permission, confirming what was before it and as guidance and good tidings to the believers. Whoever is an enemy to God} up to {behind their backs as if they do not know}. Thus they incurred wrath upon wrath."],[12837,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah. She had children—five or six from a husband of hers who had died—so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “What prevents you from me?” She said, “By God, O Prophet of God, nothing prevents me from you except that you are the most beloved of creation to me, but I honor you too much for these children to clamor at your head morning and evening.” He said, “Does anything other than that prevent you from me?” She said, “No, by God.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “May God have mercy on you. The best women who ever rode the backs of camels are the righteous women of Quraysh—the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most protective of a husband in what he possesses.”"],[12838,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said, “Whoever drinks wine is impure for forty days. If he repents from it, God turns to him. If he returns, he returns impure. If he repents, God turns to him. If he returns, he returns impure for forty days. If he repents from it, God turns to him. If he goes back to it, it is a right upon God to make him drink from the pus of the people of Hell.” They said, “O Abu al-Abbas, what is the pus of the people of Hell?” He said, “The fats of the people of the Fire and their ichor.”"],[12839,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he stood one night in Makkah during the night and said, “O God, have I conveyed?—three times.” Then ‘Umar b. al-Khattab stood up—he was compassionate—and said, “O God, yes. You have been eager, striven, and given sincere counsel. O God, yes. You have been eager, striven, and given sincere counsel.” In the morning he said, “Faith will certainly prevail until it drives disbelief back to its homelands, and the seas will certainly be crossed with Islam, and there will certainly come upon people a time when they learn the Quran, teach it, and recite it, then say, ‘We have recited and taught, so who is better than us?’ Is there any good in those?” They said, “No, O Messenger of God, and who are those?” He said, “Those are from you, and those are the fuel of the Fire.”"],[12840,"In His saying \"They ask you about orphans. Say, 'Improvement for them is better,'\" and this was before the revelation of \"Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly are only consuming into their bellies fire. And they will be burned in a Blaze.\" The Muslims disliked eating with orphans and felt uncomfortable if they were to mix with them in any way, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. So Allah revealed, \"Say, 'Improvement for them is better. And if you mix your affairs with them, then they are your brothers. And Allah knows the corrupter from the amender. And if Allah had willed, He could have put you in difficulty. However, He chose to facilitate for you.\"' He says, \"It is not to restrict you but [to promote] virtue;\" and He says, \"Whoever is rich, let him be abstinent, and whoever is poor, let him eat [only] in a fair manner.\" He says, \"The poor person may consume the wealth of the orphan to the extent of his needs, according to the standard of his living and his benefit from it, as long as he does not exceed [his needs].\""],[12841,"From Ibn ‘Abbas regarding His saying {When you are among them and lead them in prayer, let a group of them stand with you}: this is the prayer at times of fear. The imam stands, and with him stands a group of them, while a group takes their weapons and stands facing the enemy. The imam prays one rak‘ah with those with him, then remains seated in his position. They stand and pray the second rak‘ah for themselves while the imam remains seated. Then they depart until they come to their companions and stand in their position. Then the others come forward, and the imam prays the second rak‘ah for them. Thus “the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with the people on the day of Batn Nakhlah.”"],[12842,"\"In his statement 'there is no sin upon you to seek provision from your Lord,' it means that there is no harm for you in trade and business before and after Ihram. As for Ihram, the Messenger of Allah forbade getting married, arranging a marriage or sacrificing until he completes his Ihram.\""],[12843,"Regarding His saying {Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities}, he said: the greatest of major sins is associating partners with God, for God says {Whoever associates partners with God, God has forbidden Paradise to him}; and despairing of the mercy of God, for God says {No one despairs of the mercy of God except the disbelieving people}; and feeling secure from the plan of God, for God ﷻ says {No one feels secure from the plan of God except the losing people}. Among them is disobedience to parents, for God ﷻ made the disobedient a tyrannical wretch; killing the soul that God has forbidden except by right, for God, Blessed and Exalted, says {His recompense is Hell} the verse; slandering chaste women, for God, exalted is His mention, says {They are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment}; consuming the orphan’s property, for God ﷻ says {They only consume fire in their bellies, and they will burn in a blaze}; fleeing from battle, for God, Exalted, says {Whoever turns his back to them that day—unless swerving to fight or withdrawing to a company—has incurred wrath from God, and his abode is Hell, and wretched is the destination}; consuming usury, for God, Exalted, says {Those who consume usury do not stand except as one whom Satan has confounded by touch}; magic, for God, Exalted, says {And they certainly knew that whoever bought it would have no share in the Hereafter}; fornication, for God says {He will meet a penalty}—the punishment will be multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection and he will abide therein humiliated; the false, sinful oath, for God says {Those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price} the verse; embezzlement, for God, Exalted, says {Whoever embezzles} will bring what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection; withholding the obligatory zakat, for God, Exalted, says {Their foreheads, sides, and backs will be branded with it}; false testimony, for God ﷻ says {Whoever conceals it, his heart is sinful}; drinking wine, for God ﷻ equated it with idols; deliberately abandoning prayer or anything God has obligated, for the Messenger ﷺ says, “Whoever deliberately abandons prayer has freed himself from the protection of God and His Messenger”; breaking covenants; and severing ties of kinship."],[12844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Prompt your dying ones to say the testimony that there is no god but God. Whoever says it at his death, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what about one who says it in good health?” He said, “That is more obligatory and more obligatory.” Then he said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if the heavens and the earths and all who are in them and between them and beneath them were brought and placed in one pan of the scale, and the testimony that there is no god but God were placed in the other pan, it would outweigh them.”"],[12845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was eager for all people to believe and follow him in guidance, but God informed him that none believes except one for whom happiness had preceded in the first decree, and none goes astray except one for whom wretchedness had preceded in the first decree. Then God ﷻ said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Perhaps you would kill yourself with grief that they will not be believers}, meaning {If We willed, We could send down to them a sign from the sky, and their necks would remain bowed before it}."],[12846,"In his statement, \"Say, I do not ask of you any reward for it except love for my close relatives,\" he ﷺ said that the Messenger of Allah had kinship ties with all the Quraysh tribe. But when they denied him and refused to follow him, he said, \"O people! If you refuse to follow me, then protect my kinship ties among you. Let no one from the Arabs have a greater responsibility in protecting me and supporting me than you.\""],[12847,"In His saying {Those who, when afflicted with a calamity, say, \"Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.\" It is those who will be awarded blessings and mercy from their Lord and it is those who are [rightly] guided.} Allah informs us that when a believer submits to the command of Allah and returns to Him, and then turns back to Him in times of affliction, three qualities of goodness are written for Him: prayer, mercy, and the realization of the path of guidance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever turns back to Allah in times of calamity, Allah will mend his calamity, better his outcome, and make for him a righteous successor that pleases Him.\""],[12848,"In his statement \"so that they may increase in faith with their faith,\" he said, \"Indeed Allah sent His Prophet with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, so when they believed in it, their pilgrimage increased, and when they believed in it, their jihad increased, and then He completed their religion for them.\" He said, \"This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So the firmest and most truthful faith of the people of the heavens and the people of the earth and the most complete of it is the testimony that there is no god but Allah.\""],[12849,"From Ibn ‘Abbas regarding His saying {And do not recite your prayer loudly nor in a whisper}: he said, “He does not pray ostentatiously for the people, nor does he abandon it out of fear of the people.”"],[12850,"In His saying \"And indeed, it is a reminder for you and your people,\" He said, \"It is an honor for you and your people.\""],[12851,"In his statement \"And remember the favor of Allah upon you and His covenant with which He bound you when you said, 'We hear and we obey'; and fear Allah. Indeed, Allah is Knowing of that within the breasts,\" it means that when Allah sent the Prophet ﷺ and revealed the Book to him, they said, \"We believe in the Prophet ﷺ and in the Book, and we affirm what is in the Torah.\" So Allah reminded them of His covenant with which they had bound themselves and commanded them to fulfill it."],[12852,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive to make corruption in the land} (Qur'an 5:33): He said, \"A group from the People of the Book who had a covenant and pact with the Prophet ﷺ, but they broke the covenant and caused corruption in the land. So Allah gave His Prophet ﷺ the choice: if he wished, to kill them; if he wished, to crucify them; if he wished, to cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides. As for banishment, it is fleeing in the land. If one comes repentant and enters Islam, it is accepted from him and he is not taken to account for what came before him from him.\""],[12853,"In his saying, \"{If you are given this, take it, and if you are not given it, be cautious},\" they were the Jews. A woman among them committed adultery, and Allah had ruled in the Torah regarding stoning for adultery. So, they wanted to stone her. They said, \"Go to Muhammad, perhaps he has a dispensation in this matter.\" So, they went to him and said, \"O Abu al-Qasim, a woman among us has committed adultery. What do you say about her?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"How did Allah rule in the Torah regarding adultery?\" They said, \"Leave the Torah aside, what do you have in that matter?\" He said, \"Bring me your most knowledgeable person about the Torah that was revealed to Moses ﷺ.\" So, they brought him a man, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"By the One who saved you from the people of Pharaoh and split the sea for you and saved you, and drowned the people of Pharaoh, has Allah informed you about the ruling in the Torah regarding adultery?\" They said, \"He ruled for stoning.\""],[12854,"Abdullah b. Umar, whose kunya was Abu Abd al-Rahman, died in Makkah after the Hajj and was buried at al-Muhassab; and some people say at Fakhkh. His age when the Prophet ﷺ permitted him on the Day of the Trench to fight was fifteen years. The Trench was in Shawwal of the year four, so his age on the day he died was eighty-four."],[12855,"\"Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet ﷺ for sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him.\""],[12856,"\"Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet ﷺ for sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him.\""],[12857,"\"The age of Ibn Umar on the day he died was eighty-four.\""],[12858,"\"Abdullah b. Umar died in the year seventy-four and was buried at Fakhkh, and he was eighty-four years old.\""],[12859,"A spear of a man from the people of Syria struck him in his leg. Al-Hajjaj entered upon him to visit him and said, \"If I knew who struck you, I would strike his neck.\" He said, \"You are the one who struck me.\" He said, \"How?\" He said, \"On the day you brought weapons into the sanctuary of Allah.\""],[12860,"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, who did this to you so that I may take retribution for you from him? He said, \"By Allah, will you take retribution from him?\" He said, by Allah, I will take retribution for you from him. He said, \"What is the matter with the sanctuary of Allah and its security, that weapons are carried in it?\" He said, so he died from it."],[12861,"\"My father brought me on the day of Uhud to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was fourteen years old, and the Prophet ﷺ did not permit me. Then he brought me on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share for me.\" Nafi' said, \"I narrated this to Umar b. Abd al-Aziz, and he ordered that no one be allotted a share except one who was fifteen years old.\""],[12862,"\"He used to spend the night in prayer.\" Then he would say, \"O Nafi', has dawn broken?\" He would say no. \"Then he would resume prayer.\" Then he would say, \"O Nafi', has dawn broken?\" I would say yes. \"Then he would sit and seek forgiveness and supplicate until morning.\""],[12863,"\"I haven't been satisfied since I converted to Islam.\""],[12864,"A cloak. I said to Nafi', \"Did he eat meat?\" He said, \"When he fasted or traveled, it was the most common of his food.\""],[12865,"What prevents you from this matter when you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the son of the Commander of the Believers? He said, \"What prevents me from it is that Allah, Mighty and Sublime, has forbidden me the blood of my Muslim brother.\" He said, for Allah, Mighty and Sublime, says, {And fight them until there is no fitnah and the religion is entirely for Allah} (Qur'an 8:39). He said, so Ibn Umar said, \"We fought them until there was no fitnah and the religion was entirely for Allah, and you want me to fight until there is fitnah and the religion is for other than Allah.\""],[12866,"\"You are loved by the people, so go to Syria,\" Ibn Umar said, \"By my close proximity and companionship with the Prophet ﷺ, and the bond of kinship between us, he did not befriend him.\""],[12867,"that he should associate anyone else with me in it.”"],[12868,"“I saw on ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar two Maʿafiri garments, and his garment was halfway down his shins.”"],[12869,"“Ibn ʿUmar was given a gift of cloaks of silk brocade, among them a red cloak, and he divided them among his sons.”"],[12870,"“What the foolish will not despise you for, and the wise will not fault you for.” He said, “What is that?” He said, “What is between five dirhams and twenty dirhams.”"],[12871,"that a man should accompany him on a journey, and he stipulated that he should not accompany him on a jallal camel, “and do not vie with us for the call to prayer, and do not fast except with our permission.”"],[12872,"and that we should prepare his pre-dawn meal for him.”"],[12873,"“O shepherd of the sheep, is there any sheep to be slaughtered?” The shepherd said, “Its owner is not here.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “Say, ‘The wolf ate it.’” The shepherd raised his head to the sky and said, “Then where is God?” Ibn ʿUmar bought the shepherd and bought the sheep, then freed him and gave him the sheep."],[12874,"“Peace be upon you, O son of the one with two wings.”"],[12875,"“Isn’t it the best of your perfumes?”"],[12876,"and he said, “Indeed God is one God.”"],[12877,"About the Witr prayer, he began to say \"At the end of the night.\" So I said, \"Do you mean, do you mean?\" He said, \"Make your meaning at that star, and he pointed towards the sky. The night prayer is done in pairs, in pairs, and the Witr prayer is a single unit at the end of the night.\""],[12878,"A man said to Ibn ʿUmar, “I love you for the sake of God.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “But I hate you for the sake of God.” He said, “Why?” He said, “Because you embellish your call to prayer and take a wage for it.”"],[12879,"His son said to him, “What is this one saying?” He said, “This one says, ‘Know me, know me.’”"],[12880,"People have never exchanged anything among themselves better than covering a male. A man covers his horse, and its reward runs for him; a man covers his stallion, and its reward runs for him; a man covers his ram, and its reward runs for him."],[12881,"“O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I have entered ihram and I have gathered my hair.” He said, “Did you not hear ʿUmar during his caliphate say: Whoever braids his head or mats it should shave it?” He said, “O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I did not braid it, but I gathered it.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “A she-goat and a he-goat, and the he-goat of a she-goat.”"],[12882,"No one curses anyone unless it's just one man."],[12883,"Garlic used to be crushed for Ibn ʿUmar, then strung on a thread and placed in the broth on a thread, and taken out on a thread, then thrown away, and he would eat."],[12884,"Ibn Umar said, \"Indeed, the best food is that which is free from harm to the teeth.\""],[12885,"I said to Ibn Sirin, “Did they used to joke?” He said, “They were only like other people. Ibn ʿUmar used to joke, recite poetry, and say, ‘...’ ”"],[12886,"“Give it to him.” But a man opposed it and bought it from him for a dirham, then brought it to him. Then the poor man came asking, and he said, “Give it to him.” But a man opposed him and bought it from him for a dirham. Then he wanted to return it but was prevented. “Had Ibn ʿUmar known about that bunch of grapes, he would not have tasted it.”"],[12887,"He used to enter the bathhouse, and the bath attendant would apply depilatory paste to him. When it reached his waist, he would say to the bath attendant, “Leave.”"],[12888,"Depilatory paste thins the skin."],[12889,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he performed ghusl, opened his eyes and inserted his fingers into his navel."],[12890,"Any surplus in it is a gift for you from me."],[12891,"“O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, take it for what you gave me.” He said, “I swore an oath, and I would not help Satan against you by making you break your oath.”"],[12892,"I fear suspicion."],[12893,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he prayed alone during the days of tashriq, did not say the takbir after the prayer."],[12894,"“O Nafiʿ! Spend on us from our own wealth, for we have no need that charity be given to us.”"],[12895,"He used to recite this variant: “What! When we are decayed bones?” (79:11)"],[12896,"He saw Ibn ʿUmar with his waist-wrapper reaching halfway down his shins, his shirt above that, and his cloak above the shirt."],[12897,"I saw Ibn ʿUmar hastening between the two markers, saying, “I am doing it, I am doing it.”"],[12898,"“O Allah, make me among Your servants with the greatest share in every good You distribute this morning: light by which You guide, mercy You spread, provision You extend, harm You remove, affliction You lift, and tribulation You avert.”"],[12899,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The deceased is surely punished by his family’s weeping over him.”"],[12900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick man from among his companions while I was with him. He entered upon him while he was praying on a piece of wood, placing his forehead on the wood. He gestured to him, so he cast aside the wood and took a cushion. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Put it away from you. If you are able to prostrate on the ground, then do so; otherwise, gesture with a nod, and make your prostration lower than your bowing.”"],[12901,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever intercedes to block one of the prescribed punishments of Allah has opposed Allah in His command.”"],[12902,"When we missed a man at Fajr and ʿIshāʾ, we would think ill of him."],[12903,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding a man who has a wife, then divorces her, then another man marries her and divorces her before consummating the marriage: is she lawful for the first? He said: “No, not until she tastes the honey [i.e., consummates the marriage with the second husband].” Abu al-Qasim said: Shuʿbah erred in this hadith in two places: in saying “from Salim b. Razin,” whereas it is Sulayman b. Razin, and in adding Saʿid b. al-Musayyib to the chain. It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri and Qays b. al-Rabiʿ from ʿAlqamah b. Marthad, from Sulayman b. Razin al-Ahmar, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, and that is correct."],[12904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The deceased is tormented because of the wailing over him.”"],[12905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Refrain from (harming) the people of Lā ilāha illā Allāh; do not declare them disbelievers for a sin, for whoever declares the people of Lā ilāha illā Allāh disbelievers is closer to disbelief.”"],[12906,"“I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ, with Abu Bakr, with Umar, and with Uthman ؓ, and all of them did not fast it, meaning the Day of Arafah.”"],[12907,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever mutilates his brother, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.” Al-Aṣamm, meaning Yazid b. Hurmuz, and Allah knows best."],[12908,"The Prophet ﷺ “prayed the fear prayer with these (group) one rakʿah and with these (group) one rakʿah.”"],[12909,"I heard Ibn Umar say: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came with al-Ashajj, and they asked the Prophet of Allah ﷺ about drinks, and he said: “Do not drink from ḥantamah, nor from dubbāʾ, nor from naqīr.”"],[12910,"“In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah.” Then when he began placing the bricks upon the laḥd, he said: “O Allah, protect her from Satan and from the torment of the grave.” Then when they leveled the mound over her, he stood beside the grave and said: “O Allah, make the earth withdraw from her sides, raise her soul, and grant her Your pleasure.” I said: “Are these things you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or things you said from your own opinion?” He said: “If I were capable of saying it, rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[12911,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see them, pray.”"],[12912,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The night prayer is two by two, and when you want to finish, pray one rakʿah, which will make odd for you what you have prayed.”"],[12913,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it.”"],[12914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “prohibited selling food purchased by measure until he takes full possession of it.”"],[12915,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The pilgrim in ihram should not wear the shirt, nor the qabāʾ, nor the trousers, nor the turban, nor the burnūs, nor anything touched by saffron or wars.”"],[12916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You should wear white garments, so wear them and shroud your dead in them.”"],[12917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option (to cancel) as long as they have not separated.”"],[12918,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and it was a dark night. The Prophet’s ﷺ mu’adhdhin called the adhan, and he prayed. Then he ordered a crier to announce: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[12919,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and it was a dark night. The Prophet’s ﷺ mu’adhdhin called the adhan, and he prayed. Then he ordered a crier to announce: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[12920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two people should not hold secret counsel apart from the third.”"],[12921,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People are like a hundred camels; you will hardly find among them a suitable riding camel.”"],[12922,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bilal gives the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan.”"],[12923,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when he was in a hurry on a journey, he would delay Maghrib until he combined it with the Isha prayer."],[12924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever misses the Asr (afternoon) prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been lost.\""],[12925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the zakah on crops watered by rain and rivers one tenth, and on those watered by artificial irrigation half of one tenth."],[12926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Isha in the last part of his life. When he said the salam, he said: “Do you see this night of yours? After a hundred years, no one on the face of the earth today will remain.”"],[12927,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin the prayer with the takbir and raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders. Then when he said the takbir for bowing, he did the same. Then when he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he did the same. Then he said, “Our Lord, to You is praise,” and did the same."],[12928,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir in prayer, he would raise his hands level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he did the same. When he raised his head, he did the same. And when he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he said, “Our Lord, to You is praise,” and did the same. He did not do that in prostration."],[12929,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs all praise,” then before prostrating he would say: “O God, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,” then he would say the takbir and prostrate—until God, exalted is He, sent down: “You have no part in the matter.”"],[12930,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups for one rakʿah while the other group faced the enemy. Then they left and stood in the position of their companions facing the enemy, and the others came and the Prophet ﷺ prayed one rakʿah with them. Then the Prophet ﷺ said the salam. Then these made up one rakʿah and those made up one rakʿah."],[12931,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Perform ablution after (eating) that which has been changed by fire.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 486)"],[12932,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.”"],[12933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to look at the private part of his brother."],[12934,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade praying in the middle of the road, relieving oneself there, or urinating there."],[12935,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[12936,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The prayer of one sitting is like half the prayer of one standing.”"],[12937,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is God, the One.”"],[12938,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar did not wear rings or seal letters, until Ziyad b. Abi Sufyan wrote to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab: “You write to us about matters that have no seals.” So at that point he adopted a ring and sealed with it."],[12939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever preserves me regarding my Companions will come to me at my basin, and whoever does not preserve me regarding my Companions will not see me on the Day of Resurrection except from afar.”"],[12940,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it begins to yellow or redden."],[12941,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a white shirt on ʿUmar and said: “Is this shirt of yours new or washed?” He said: “Rather, washed.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wear new, live praiseworthy, die as a martyr, and may God grant you the delight of your eye in this world and the Hereafter.” He said: “And you, O Messenger of God.”"],[12942,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when travel in a journey hurried him, he would delay the Maghrib prayer until he combined it with the Isha prayer."],[12943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform glorification (subhanAllah) while on his mount, not caring which direction he was facing."],[12944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever sells a slave who has property, the property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""],[12945,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[12948,"He would walk in front of the funeral while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman walked ahead of it. My father narrated this Hadith, and indeed, the Hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is only from Zubair. It is the Hadith of Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and the Hadith of Ibn Uyaynah seems like a fabrication."],[12949,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ , Abu Bakr, and Umar used to walk in front of the funeral.\""],[12950,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[12951,"And he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to walk in front of it, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman.\""],[12952,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim: he does not wrong him nor hand him over. Whoever is engaged in the need of his brother, Allah is engaged in his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress in this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever conceals a Muslim, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12953,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A believer is not stung from the same hole twice.\""],[12955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted the Muslims regarding what would gather them for prayer. They suggested the trumpet, but he disliked it because of the Jews. Then the bell was mentioned, but he disliked it because of the Christians. That night, Abdullah b. Zayd, a man from the Ansar, and Umar b. al-Khattab were shown the call (adhan) in a vision. The Ansari went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, who then gave the call to prayer with it."],[12956,"Two men from the Ansar recited a surah which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taught them, and they used to recite it. One night they stood to pray and could not recall a single letter of it. In the morning they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is among what has been abrogated and caused to be forgotten, so turn away from it.\" Al-Zuhri used to recite it as {ma nansakh min ayatin aw nunsiha} with a damma on the nun and lightly (pronounced)."],[12957,"The most frequent oath of the Prophet ﷺ was: \"No, by the Turner of hearts.\""],[12958,"No head was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor on the day of Badr to Madinah."],[12959,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"commanded the sharpening of blades and that they be concealed from the animals.\""],[12960,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it on the Day of Hunayn, and we were not fornicators.\""],[12961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and he struck him with his foot and said, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" Ibn Sayyad said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered ones.\" He said, \"Then do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\""],[12962,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"I saw a black woman with disheveled hair coming out of Madinah until she stood at Mahya'ah, which is al-Juhfah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I interpreted it to mean that the plague of Madinah was transferred to al-Juhfah.\""],[12963,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him with his foot and said, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" Ibn Sayyad said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered ones.\" Ibn Sayyad said to him, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\""],[12964,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever comes to me as a visitor, with no known need except to visit me, it is incumbent upon me to be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cupping on the head is for insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and toothache.\""],[12966,"A boy came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I intend to go to this region for Hajj.\" He said, \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked with him and said, 'O boy, may Allah provide you with piety, direct you toward good, and suffice you against worry.'\" When the boy returned and greeted the Prophet ﷺ, he raised his head toward him and said, \"O boy, may your Hajj be accepted, your sin forgiven, and your expenditure replaced.\""],[12967,"He informed him that it was said to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Mu'arras, the resting place of the tree, \"Ask, for it is the blessed stony ground of Makkah.\""],[12968,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, Allah will build for him a house in the Fire.\""],[12969,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12970,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw in a dream that I was given a large wooden cup full of milk, and I drank from it until I was filled, until I saw it flowing in my veins between the skin and the flesh. Some remained, and I gave it to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" They said, \"Interpret it, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said, \"This is knowledge that Allah gave you and filled you with, and some remained, so you gave it to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said, \"You have spoken correctly.\""],[12971,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Between my grave and my pulpit, there is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my pond.\" So, he quoted its foundation and said, \"I have written it from Muhammad ibn Bishr.\""],[12972,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful.”"],[12973,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A dog indeed diminishes two qirats every day, except a hunting dog or a sheepdog.” Abu al-Qasim said: “Diminishes, meaning from the reward of its owner.”"],[12974,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “From grapes comes khamr, from honey comes khamr, from raisins comes khamr, from dates comes khamr, and from wheat comes khamr. I forbid every intoxicant.”"],[12975,"When a deceased person died, the Messenger of God ﷺ would say: “Send him ahead to our forerunner. How excellent a forerunner for my community is Uthman b. Maz‘un.”"],[12976,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Kill snakes. Whoever finds the one with two stripes or the short-tailed one and does not kill them is not of us, for they are the two that snatch away sight and cause what is in women’s wombs to miscarry.”"],[12977,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom God has taught the Quran and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom God has given wealth and he spends it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.”"],[12978,"The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[12979,"The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[12980,"Ibn Umar said: “The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: ‘No, by the Turner of hearts.’”"],[12981,"The oath by which the Messenger of God ﷺ used to swear was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[12982,"He used to curse al-Bayda’ or intended to curse it, and he said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not enter ihram except from Dhu al-Hulayfah.”"],[12983,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not enter ihram except from near the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah.”"],[12984,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: that he met Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah, and that was before revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ offered him a leather dining mat with meat on it, but he refused to eat. He said: 'I do not eat from what they slaughter for their idols. I eat only from that over which the name of God has been mentioned.'"],[12985,"From Zayd b. Harithah al-Kalbi, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'We used not to call him anything but Zayd b. Muhammad until the Qur'an came down: \"Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of God.\"'"],[12986,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he appointed Usamah b. Zayd as commander, and it reached him that the people were finding fault with Usamah b. Zayd and criticizing his command. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among the people and said: 'Indeed, you are finding fault with Usamah and criticizing his command, and you did the same with his father before. He was indeed worthy of command, and he was indeed the most beloved of all people to me. And this one after him is the most beloved of people to me, so treat him well, for he is among the best of you.' Salim said: 'I never heard ʿAbd Allah relate this hadith without saying: \"except Fatimah.\"'"],[12987,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ was approached while he was at al-Muʿarras in Dhu al-Hulayfah, in the belly of the valley, and he said: 'You are in a blessed pebbly plain.'"],[12988,"Regarding the dream of the Messenger of God ﷺ about Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, he said: 'I saw people gathered, and Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and God forgives him. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab stood and it turned into a large bucket. I have never seen a champion among people do what he did, until the people settled by the watering place.'"],[12989,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.' Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of God, one side of my lower garment hangs loose unless I take care of it.' He said: 'You are not one of those who do it out of pride.'"],[12990,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever says in any marketplace: 'There is no god but Allah, alone without partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him belongs all praise, and He is capable of all things,' Allah will write for him a thousand thousand good deeds.\""],[12991,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is below the ankles is in the Fire.'"],[12992,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'I saw in a dream that people were gathered, and Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and God forgives him. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab took it, and it turned into a large bucket. I have never seen a champion do what he did, until the people settled by the watering place.'"],[12993,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.' Salim said: 'My father narrated to me that Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of God, one side of my lower garment hangs loose unless I take care of it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"You are not one of those who do it out of pride.\"'"],[12994,"While ʿUmar b. al-Khattab was riding in a group, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard him swearing by his father. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by God or remain silent.'"],[12995,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Three will not enter Paradise and three God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection. As for those who will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the woman who imitates men, and the cuckold. As for the three whom God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of what he has given.'"],[12996,"You know that we used to say during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman—meaning in the caliphate."],[12997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was pressed for time on a journey, would combine Maghrib and ʿIshaʾ after the twilight had disappeared by an hour."],[12998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned ʿAshuraʾ and said: \"It was a fast of the people of the Jahiliyyah, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break the fast.\""],[12999,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The night prayer is two rakʿahs at a time, two rakʿahs at a time; so when you fear the arrival of dawn, perform Witr with one rakʿah.\""],[13000,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Everything has a source, and the source of taqwa is the hearts of those who know Allah.\""],[13001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The deceased is punished by the weeping of the living.\""],[13002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallalah (an animal that eats filth), its milk, and its riding."],[13003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you can be like the companion of the measure of rice, let him be like him.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is the companion of the measure of rice?\" He said: \"Three men went out, and the sky became cloudy over them, so they entered a cave. A rock came until it sealed the entrance over them. They tried to move it but could not. Some of them said to the others: 'You have fallen into a grave matter; let each man among you supplicate with the best deed he has performed, perhaps Allah will rescue us from this.'\" Then he mentioned the hadith of the cave in full."],[13004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not right for a Muslim who has wealth enough to make a will to spend even one night without his will being with him.\""],[13005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first from whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, then Abu Bakr, then ʿUmar. Then the people of al-Baqiʿ will come and be gathered with me, then I will wait for the people of Makkah and they will be gathered with me.\""],[13006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the chest of ʿUmar b. al-Khattab with his hand three times when he accepted Islam, saying: \"O Allah, remove what is in his chest of rancor and replace it with faith,\" saying that three times."],[13007,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When it is his seventh day, pour blood away from him and remove harm from him.\""],[13008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for livestock or hunting, two qirats are deducted from his good deeds each day.\""],[13009,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command us to be brief, and he used to lead us in prayer with (the surah) al-Saffat."],[13010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not look at a gray-haired adulterer, nor at a poor man who is arrogant, nor at one who drags his lower garment out of pride.\""],[13011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he returned from Hajj or ʿUmrah, would say whenever he ascended a mountain pass or a hillock: 'Allahu Akbar' three times, then say: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. We are returning, repenting, worshiping, prostrating, to our Lord praising. Allah has been true to His promise, helped His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.'"],[13012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Dajjal will descend at this salt-marsh, and the last to go out to him will be women, so much so that a man will return to his mother, his sister, and his paternal aunt and tie her up securely, fearing that she might go out to him. Then Allah will enable the Muslims over him, and they will kill him and kill his followers, so much so that the Jew will hide under a tree or a stone, and the stone or the tree will say: \"O Muslim, here is a Jew under me, so kill him.\"'"],[13013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man from Qahtan will surely drive the people with a stick.'"],[13014,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No servant makes an image except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Bring to life what you have created.'"],[13015,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Allah loves the skilled worker.'"],[13016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ʿArafat while saying: 'To You it hastens, its girth strap trembling, its religion differing from the Christians' religion.' Abu al-Qasim said: 'Abu al-Rabiʿ al-Samman, in my view, erred in raising this hadith to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, because what is well-known in the narration from Ibn ʿUmar is: from ʿArafat while he was saying...' then he mentioned the rajaz verse."],[13017,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'No servant makes an image except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Bring to life what you have created.'"],[13018,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Islam is built on five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakat, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House.'"],[13019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds.'"],[13020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage. So whoever does not kill them is not one of us.'"],[13021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds, and a qirat is like Uhud.'"],[13022,"Woe to you, O Ashʿab, do not beg, for my father narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'There will surely come people on the Day of Resurrection with no morsel of flesh on their faces, having worn it away.'"],[13023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray before the sermon on the two Eids."],[13024,"\"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Al-Isbal may apply to the Izar, the Qamis and the turban. Whoever drags any one of these out of vanity, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5334)"],[13025,"Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'Stand and strike the neck of this man.' Salim took the sword, took the man, and headed toward the gate of the palace. His father saw him heading off with the man and said: 'Do you think he will do it?' He sent someone after him twice or three times. When he brought him out, Salim said to him: 'Have you prayed the dawn prayer?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then take whichever road you wish.' Then he came back and threw down the sword. Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'Did you strike his neck?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'I heard my father here saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection until evening.\"' Ibn Umar said: 'He is shrewd. We named you Salim only so that you would remain safe.'"],[13026,"Al-Hajjaj said to him, \"What prevented you from killing him?\" Salim replied, \"My father informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, 'Whoever prays the Fajr prayer is in the protection of Allah throughout his day.' So I disliked killing a man whom Allah has protected.\" Al-Hajjaj then asked Ibn 'Umar, \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ ?\" Ibn 'Umar replied, \"Yes.\""],[13027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[13028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[13029,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ doing that."],[13030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'How is the night prayer?' He said: \"Two by two. Then when you fear dawn, pray witr with one.\""],[13031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer and became confused during it. When he finished, he said to Ubayy b. Ka'b: \"Did you pray with us?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What prevented you from prompting me?\""],[13032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None may touch the Quran except one who is pure.\""],[13033,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought nabidh and he drank some of it."],[13034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not make mosques thoroughfares, except for remembrance or prayer.\""],[13035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram when his mount set off with him."],[13036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Choose four of them.\""],[13037,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts the days of Hajj and does not find a sacrificial animal when he performs tamattuʿ, then it is between the ihram of one of you until the Day of ʿArafah, and that is the last of them.\""],[13038,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The poor of my Ummah will enter Paradise before their rich by forty autumns.\" I said: \"Describe them to us.\" He said: \"They are those whose clothes are greasy, whose heads are disheveled, who are not granted permission at the gates, and who do not marry the protected women. The easts and wests of the earth are entrusted to them; they give all that is upon them and are not given all that is due to them.\""],[13039,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Jews were asked about Musa and they went to excess, adding and subtracting until they disbelieved. And the Christians were asked about ʿIsa and they went to excess concerning him, adding and subtracting until they disbelieved. And it will soon spread from me hadiths. So whatever comes to you of my hadith, recite the Book of Allah and test it. Whatever agrees with the Book of Allah, then I said it, and whatever does not agree with the Book of Allah, then I did not say it.\""],[13040,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah has forbidden wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[13041,"In his saying \"{§as a shining lamp},\" Muhammad's heart is the cavity, and the bottle is his heart, and the lamp is the light that is in his heart, it is lit from a blessed tree. The tree is Ibrahim, an olive tree that is not eastern nor western, neither Jewish nor Christian. Then he recited \"{Ibrahim was neither Jewish nor Christian, but he was a pure monotheist, Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists}\""],[13042,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer, and a man was turning the pebbles with his hand. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he turned to us and said: \"Which of you was turning the pebbles with his hand?\" A man stood up and said: \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said to him: \"That is your share from your prayer.\""],[13043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no good in the gathering of women, nor at a deceased person, for when they gather, they say and say.\""],[13044,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus until it wastes him away is better for him than to have it filled with poetry.\" And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna attributed Abu ʿUbaydah, saying: \"Abu ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar.\""],[13045,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard thunder and lightning, he would say: \"O Allah, do not kill us with Your wrath, and do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that.\""],[13046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed, would raise his hands when he began, when he said takbir for bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[13047,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Muslims looked at the best of them and appointed him as successor, and he was Abu Bakr. When Abu Bakr died, the people looked at the best of the Muslims and appointed him as successor, and he was ʿUmar. When he died or was killed, the Muslims looked at the best of them and appointed him as successor, and he was ʿUthman. If you kill him, then bring me someone better than him, and by Allah, I do not think that you will do it.\" Abu al-Qasim said: \"Al-Qasim, from whom Qurrah b. Khalid narrated this hadith, is Abu Nuhayk of Basra, who is Ibn Muhammad.\""],[13048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If one of you is faced with a matter that he fears will escape him, then let him pray this prayer,\" meaning combining the two prayers."],[13049,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No parent has ever endowed their child with anything better than good manners.\""],[13050,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I forbade you from nabidh in earthenware jars, and I had forbidden you from visiting graves, and I had forbidden you from sacrificial meats. Now, containers do not make anything lawful or unlawful. Now, visit graves, for they soften the hearts.\" ʿAbdan added in his hadith: \"Now, I had forbidden you from the meats of sacrificial animals, so eat and store whatever you wish.\""],[13051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight, so gather together over it and do not separate from it.\""],[13052,"The Prophet ﷺ asked about a man and said, \"Who knows him?\" A man among them said, \"I do.\" He asked, \"What is his name?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" He asked, \"What is his father's name?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" He asked, \"What is his clan?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" The Prophet said, \"You should not be acquainted with him until you know his name, his father's name, and his clan. If he falls ill, you should visit him, and if he dies, you should follow his funeral procession.\""],[13053,"He was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ among a group of his companions, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O these people, do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" They said: \"Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do you not know that Allah has sent down in His Book that whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah?\" They said: \"Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and that obedience to you is part of obedience to Allah.\" He said: \"And obedience to Allah is that you obey me, and part of obeying me is that you obey your leaders. And if they pray sitting, then pray sitting, all of you.\""],[13054,"Narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Indeed the Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, nor betray him, nor abandon him in a calamity that befalls him. And if he encounters the best of the Arabs and the mawali, they will love one another with a love from which they find no escape. And if he encounters the worst of the two groups, they will hate one another with a hatred from which they find no escape.\""],[13055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People are like a hundred camels: one seeks a mount suitable for travel among them, but finds only one.\""],[13056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on my brother ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah. Wherever the prayer overtook him, he would make his camel kneel.\""],[13057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Eid and began by praying without any adhan or iqamah, then he delivered the sermon."],[13058,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he started the prayer, raised his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he did not raise them above his ears."],[13059,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a camel, facing whatever direction it took him."],[13060,"Umar b. al-Khattab gave a horse in charity to a man for the sake of Allah. Then Umar found him selling it, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I gave a horse in charity to so-and-so, and I found him selling it. Should I buy it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity.\""],[13061,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The keys of the unseen are five,\" then he recited this verse: {Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. And no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware.}"],[13062,"Some people raided the camels of the Prophet ﷺ, drove them away, apostatized from Islam, and killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a believer. The Prophet ﷺ sent after them, and they were captured. He cut off their hands and feet and put out their eyes. It is said that this is ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, and it is said ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUtbah, and Allah knows best."],[13063,"The Prophet ﷺ put out the eyes of the ʿUraynis only because they had put out the eyes of the shepherds."],[13064,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Bad omens are in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse.”"],[13065,"There was a wife under my care whom I loved, but my father disliked her. He ordered me to divorce her, but I refused. Then ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿAbd Allah, divorce her.”"],[13066,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques.” I said, “As for me, I shall prevent my family; so whoever wishes may let his family go.” He turned to me and said: “May Allah curse you! May Allah curse you! May Allah curse you! You hear me say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they not be prevented, and you say this?” Then he wept and stood up in anger."],[13067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques when they ask your permission.” Bilal said, “By Allah, we shall prevent them.” Then ʿAbd Allah said, “O enemy of Allah, I say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and you say we shall prevent them?”"],[13068,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar say: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with ʿAʾishah behind him, Abu Bakr asked permission and entered. Then ʿUmar asked permission and entered. Then Saʿd b. Malik entered. Then ʿUthman b. ʿAffan asked permission while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was talking with his knee uncovered. He pulled his garment over his knee when ʿUthman asked permission, and said to his wife, “Move back.” They conversed for a while, then left. ʿAʾishah said, “O Prophet of Allah, my father and his companions entered and you did not adjust your garment over your knee, nor did you move me back from you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O ʿAʾishah, should I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy? By the One in whose hand is the soul of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the angels feel shy of ʿUthman just as they feel shy of Allah and His Messenger. Had he entered while you were close to me, he would not have spoken or raised his head until you left.”"],[13069,"“I only do as I saw the Prophet ﷺ do.”"],[13070,"When the rim of the sun starts appearing defer prayer till it completely appears, and when the rim of the sun disappears defer prayer till it completely disappears. (Using translation from Muslim 829)"],[13071,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not deliberately aim your prayers at the rising of the sun or its setting, for it rises between the two horns of Satan.”"],[13072,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs, as did Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman for part of his rule.”"],[13073,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gentleness is not given to the people of a household except that it benefits them.”"],[13074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the deceased is punished by the weeping of his family.”"],[13075,"“As for us, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to consider it hypocrisy. I do not know what you consider it to be?”"],[13076,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzled wealth.” And you were in Basra."],[13077,"“I prayed with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ the prayer of fear. He arranged a group of us behind him, and another group faced the enemy. He said the takbir, then bowed with them and prostrated twice. Then the group that was with him departed and faced the enemy, and the other group came and lined up behind him. Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said the salam, and each man of the two groups stood and completed for himself one rakʿah and two prostrations.”"],[13078,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not pray the same prayer twice in a day.”"],[13079,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik who narrated to us from Ali bin al-Mubarak al-Sanaani that Ismail bin Abi Uwais narrated to me from Malik who narrated to us from Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi who narrated from Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Umar from Saeed bin Yasar that he said: \"I was traveling with Abdullah bin Umar on the road to Mecca. Saeed said: When I feared dawn, I stopped and performed the Witr prayer.\" Abdullah said: \"Is there not a good example in the Messenger of Allah?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer on a camel.\""],[13080,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying voluntarily on his donkey while he was heading to Khaybar.”"],[13081,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and ʿAli b. al-Mubarak al-Sanʿani narrated to me; Ismaʿil b. Abi Uways narrated to us; Malik narrated to me, from ʿAmr b. Yahya, from Saʿid b. Yasar, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on his donkey while he was heading to Khaybar.”"],[13082,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while he was on a donkey, heading toward Khaybar.” ʿAmr b. Yahya said: “That is facing toward Syria.”"],[13083,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on his donkey while his donkey was heading toward Khaybar, making gestures (with his head)."],[13084,"Saʿīd b. Yasār, the freed slave of Shuqrān, the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to me. He said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar say: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying on a donkey while heading toward Khaybar.”"],[13085,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on a donkey while he was heading toward Khaybar.”"],[13086,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever dies separated from the community dies a death of the Age of Ignorance.”"],[13087,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade meeting caravans (before they reach the market), a resident selling on behalf of a bedouin, and any of you proposing to a woman already betrothed to his brother until he marries her or gives her up.”"],[13088,"That no day he had named would come upon him except that he fasted on it, and that coincided with the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast. Ibn ʿUmar said: “You have a good example in the Messenger of God.” “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not fast on the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast, nor did he command fasting them.”"],[13089,"That that day would not pass him except that he fasted, and that day coincided with the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast. Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “You have a good example in the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then he said: “He did not fast the day of breaking the fast or the day of sacrifice, nor did he consider fasting them a right.”"],[13090,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Mosque of Jerusalem.”"],[13091,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Every shepherd is responsible for his flock.”"],[13092,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever strikes his slave with a punishment he did not deserve, its expiation is to set him free.”"],[13093,"He said to the young man, “What do you need, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “Woe to you! Do you love that Allah should look at you on the Day of Resurrection?” He said, “Glory be to Allah! What prevents me from loving that?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Allah will not look at a servant on the Day of Resurrection who drags his lower garment out of pride.’” He said, “That young man was never seen except with his garment raised until he died.”"],[13094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No amputation for livestock except what is beyond the enclosure, and no amputation for fruit except what the drying-floor has gathered.”"],[13095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The dead person is tormented by the weeping of the living.”"],[13096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting for three days. They said, “But you fast continuously.” He said, “I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[13097,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to Arafah; among us were those reciting the talbiyah and among us were those saying takbir. The one saying takbir was not reproached for his takbir, nor was the one reciting the talbiyah reproached for his talbiyah. Abdullah ibn Umar was among those who said takbir."],[13098,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The small stream which God, Exalted is He, mentioned, {Your Lord has placed beneath you a small stream} (Q 19:24), is a river God brought forth for her to drink from.'"],[13099,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The fornicator does not commit fornication at the time he fornicates while he is a believer, nor does the wine-drinker drink wine at the time he drinks it while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal at the time he steals while he is a believer, nor does one seize a notable plunder while he is a believer.'"],[13100,"I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: 'Command him to take her back.'"],[13101,"Al-Qanabi narrated to us from Malik, from Qatan ibn Wahb, that Yuhannas, the freed slave of al-Zubayr, informed him that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar during the fitnah when a freed woman of his came to greet him and said: 'O Abu Abdir-Rahman, I wanted to leave, and times have become hard for us.' Abdullah ibn Umar said to her: 'Stay, you wretched one! For I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"No one endures its hardship and severity except that it will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection.\"'"],[13102,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever fasts on Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, then gives charity on Friday from the little of his wealth, every sin he has committed will be forgiven for him until he becomes like the day his mother gave birth to him, free from sins.'"],[13103,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'An angel descended upon me from heaven who had never descended upon any prophet before me and will not descend upon anyone after me. It was Israfil, and Gabriel was with him. He said: \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.\" Then he said: \"I am the messenger of your Lord to you. He commanded me to inform you: if you wish, you will be a prophet servant; and if you wish, a prophet king.\" I looked at Gabriel, and Gabriel gestured to me to be humble. The Prophet ﷺ then said: \"A prophet servant.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Had I said a prophet king, then if I wished, the mountains would have moved with me as gold.\"'"],[13104,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, this world is more insignificant to God than this lamb is to its owners. Were the world to equal the weight of a mustard seed with God, He would not have given it to anyone except His friends and beloved ones among His creation.'"],[13105,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever says: \"There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is the Ever-Living who does not die; in His hand is all good, and He is capable of everything,\" desiring by it only His Face, God will admit him by it into the gardens of bliss.'"],[13106,"I climbed onto a roof and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Hafsah's house relieving himself between two bricks, facing toward the Holy House."],[13107,"About the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'When he prayed, he would say \"God is greatest\" every time he raised and every time he lowered, in bowing and prostration. When he finished, he would say: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of God\" to his right and to his left.'"],[13108,"I said to Ibn 'Umar, 'I saw you wearing these sandals of tanned leather.' He said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing them and performing ablution while wearing them.'"],[13109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dye with it."],[13110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We have not loved anything from your world except your women.'"],[13111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse while on the pulpit: \"And they did not appraise Allah with true appraisal\" to the end of the verse. The pulpit swayed like this and like that, meaning it shook."],[13112,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever guides a blind person forty steps, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"],[13113,"He said to him, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, will you perform Hajj on this?' He said, 'Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Do not abandon Hajj, even if on an old, broken-tusked camel worth ten dirhams.\" By Allah, no mount has come to me except this one, and I would not abandon Hajj.'"],[13114,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the new moon, he would say: “O Allah, let it appear upon us with security, faith, safety, Islam, and success in what You love and are pleased with. Our Lord and your Lord is Allah.”"],[13115,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing an izar that was rustling, and he said: “Who is this?” I said, ‘Abdullah. He said: “If you are Abdullah, then raise your izar.” So I raised my izar to the middle of my shins, and his izar remained like that until he died."],[13116,"When the verses that obligate punishment were revealed, such as His saying: “Those who devour the property of orphans unjustly” to the end of the verse, and like “Those who consume riba,” and like His saying: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell,” he said: We used to testify that whoever did any of this was in the Fire. But when His saying was revealed: “Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills,” we refrained from testifying, and we feared for them because of what Allah had made obligatory for them."],[13117,"From Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Every creature of the sea and land that does not have flowing blood, no zakat is due on it.”"],[13118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ has creatures whom He created for the needs of people. People turn to them in their needs. Those are the ones secure from the punishment of Allah.”"],[13119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed them during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: “Verily, Allah has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed?” They said, “Yes.” He said: “O Allah, bear witness.” He said that three times, then said: “Beware, do not revert after me to disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"],[13121,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call out: ‘O people of Paradise, there is no death; O people of the Fire, there is no death.’ So the people of Paradise will increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in sorrow upon their sorrow.”"],[13122,"We were talking about the Farewell Pilgrimage while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, but we did not know what the Farewell Pilgrimage was. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood as a preacher, praised and extolled Allah, then mentioned the false messiah, the Dajjal, and expounded at length about him. Then he said: “Allah has not sent any prophet except that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Noah warned of him, and the prophets after him. He will emerge among you, and if any of his affairs is unclear to you, it should not be unclear that he is one-eyed in the right eye, as if it is a floating grape.”"],[13123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If people knew what is in solitude, no one would travel alone at night.”"],[13124,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Jibril kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.\""],[13125,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house.\""],[13126,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water,\" or he said: \"Make it cool with water.\""],[13127,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.\""],[13128,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I have been given the keys of everything except five: {Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain} and He knows what is in the wombs; and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.\""],[13129,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking help against his father. He said: \"He has taken from my wealth.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Do you not know that you and your wealth belong to your father?\""],[13130,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a black-and-white ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise, do you recognize this?' They will crane their necks and look. And it will be said: 'O people of Hell, do you recognize this?' They will crane their necks and look. Then it will be slaughtered. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise, eternity, and no more death; and O people of Hell, eternity, and no more death.'\""],[13131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I know that the most beloved land to Allah is Mecca, and if it were not for my people forcing me out, I would not have left. O Allah, make the love of Medina in our hearts as you have made the love of Mecca in our hearts.\" And whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached Medina, his face would be recognized with delight and joy."],[13132,"We heard of the Farewell Pilgrimage while the Messenger of God ﷺ was alive among us, and we did not think it was his farewell. The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and mentioned the Dajjal, speaking at length about him. Then he mentioned of his affair what God willed him to mention. Then he said: \"Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, never sent a prophet but that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Nuh warned his nation of him, then the prophets after him, one prophet after another.\" Then he said: \"Now, whoever of you is unclear about his affair, and the Messenger of God ﷺ hesitated to say it,\" then he said: \"except whoever of you is unclear about his affair, let it not be unclear to you that your Lord is not one-eyed, while he is one-eyed in the right eye, as if it were a floating grape. Now, have I conveyed?\" They shouted from the sides: \"Yes.\" He said: \"O God, bear witness,\" three times. Then he said: \"Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\""],[13133,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"They will pass out of Islam as an arrow passes through the game.\""],[13134,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God.\""],[13135,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Only two are envied, or as God willed him to say: a man whom God gave the Quran and he stands in prayer during the hours of night and day, and a man whom God gave wealth and he spends it.\""],[13136,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted to al-Zubayr the run of his horse in a land called Tharira. He let his horse run until it stopped, then threw his whip and said: \"Give him as far as his whip reached.\""],[13137,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied kohl, he would put three (drops/applications) in the right eye and two in the left, making it an odd number."],[13138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Increase in planting (the trees of) Paradise, for its water is sweet and its soil is good. So increase in planting it (by saying): ‘There is no might nor power except with Allah (La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah).’”"],[13139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to spend the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and when he had prayed Fajr he would sit on his mount and enter the state of ihram (by saying the talbiyah)."],[13140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prostrate (for forgetfulness) on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn."],[13141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times.”"],[13142,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surat al-Najm in Makkah, and the people prostrated with him, such that a man would raise some earth to his forehead and prostrate on it, and even a man would prostrate on another man."],[13143,"\"From the Prophet, ﷺ , that he said, 'There is no surah, whether small or large, except that I have heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , recite it in its entirety during prayer.'\""],[13144,"ʿAmr b. Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿUmar, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: A woman used to borrow jewelry in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and then keep it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let the woman repent to Allah (Mighty and Sublime) and to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and let her return what she has,” while she was listening. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Stand, O so-and-so, take her hand and cut it off.”"],[13145,"I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came, greeted him, and then turned away. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love this man.” He said: “Have you told him?” I said: “No.” He said: “Tell your brother.” So I went to him, greeted him, took hold of his shoulder, and said: “By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He said: “And I love you for the sake of Allah.” And I said: “Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ commanded me to tell you, I would not have done so.”"],[13146,"Make haste to observe the witr prayer before morning. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1436)"],[13147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a horse race, and he raced the jadhāʿ (young horses) to the goal."],[13148,"We used to withhold (judgment) regarding the killer (whether he would be forgiven) until the verse was revealed: “Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.”"],[13149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mudabbar (a slave freed upon the owner’s death) is (counted) from the third (of the estate).”"],[13150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Tayammum is two strikes; one strike on the face and one strike on the hands up to the elbows.\""],[13151,"\"We ate a lizard in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found it repulsive. And we refrain from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finds repulsive.\""],[13152,"While the Prophet ﷺ was at al-ʿAqiq, it was said to him: “You are in the blessed valley,” or “in a blessed sandy plain.”"],[13153,"My maternal uncle ʿUthman b. Mazʿun sent me to bring him a blanket. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission while he was at the trench. He gave me permission and said to me, 'Whoever you meet, tell them that the Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to return.' That was during severe cold. I went out and met the people and said to them, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to return.' He said: 'By God, no two or even one of them turned back for me.'"],[13154,"Ibn ʿUmar was asked, 'Where did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray on the Day of the Confederates?' He said, 'He prayed in the heart of the mountain pass, near a ruin there. And the Messenger of God ﷺ granted permission for the people to leave, then he ordered me to call them, so I called them.'"],[13155,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey and passed over high ground or an elevated spot, he would say the takbir three times, then say: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things.' Then he would say: 'Returning, repenting, worshiping, prostrating, praising our Lord. God has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and alone defeated the confederates.'"],[13156,"A raiding party seized food and honey as spoils during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the fifth was not taken from them."],[13157,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Let one of you pray in his own mosque, and not chase after the mosques.'"],[13158,"Ibn Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah (servant of Allah) and Abdur Rahman (servant of the Most Merciful).\""],[13159,"A woman has no sacredness except in her face."],[13160,"The Prophet ﷺ designated al-Rabadhah as a protected reserve for the owners of the charity camels."],[13161,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about performing ablution after a full-body bath, and he said: 'What ablution is more comprehensive than the full-body bath?'"],[13162,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution after eating what fire has changed.'"],[13163,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call.' He asserted that Bilal used to give the call, and when Bilal came down, Ibn Umm Maktum would give the call."],[13164,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the Maghrib prayer: 'Those who disbelieved and obstructed from the way of God.'"],[13165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out from the mosque to al-Safa by the gate of Banu Makhzum."],[13166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to the cemetery walking and return walking, as did Abu Bakr and Umar."],[13167,"Abu Bakr As-Siddiq received something from Umar, then he said, \"Seek forgiveness for me, O my brother.\" This made Umar angry, and he said the same thing to him repeatedly, which made Umar even angrier. Abu Bakr mentioned this incident to the Prophet ﷺ, and they went to him and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your brother asks you to seek forgiveness for him, so do not do so.\" Abu Bakr swore, \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, every time he asks me I seek forgiveness for him.\" Then he said, \"There is no creation of Allah after you who is dearer to me than him.\" Abu Bakr said, \"And by the One who sent you with the truth, there is no one after you dearer to me than him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not hurt me with regard to my companion. Verily, Allah has sent me with guidance and the true religion. You said, 'You have lied,' and Abu Bakr said, 'You have spoken the truth.' If Allah had not named him my companion, I would not have taken him as a close friend. But the brotherhood of Allah is sufficient. So calm down, every fruit has gone bad except the fruit of the son of Abu Quhafa.\""],[13168,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bidding farewell to someone who was departing, then Abdullah said: \"I entrust to Allah your trust, your religion, and the conclusion of your deeds.\""],[13169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The right of pre-emption applies only where boundaries have not been set; once boundaries have been set, there is no pre-emption.\""],[13170,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received the leaders, he said, \"A person does not find anything within himself except that I take it as a sign from Gabriel, ﷺ .\""],[13171,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.\""],[13172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ specified the miqat for their own people and for those who come upon them from among those who intend Hajj and Umrah: for the people of Madinah, Dhu al-Hulayfah; for the people of Sham, al-Juhfah; and for the people of Najd, Qarn."],[13173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not that I would impose difficulty on my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer.\""],[13174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, bless my community in its early morning.\""],[13175,"During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to say: 'Who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter [the caliphate]?' We would say: 'Abu Bakr.' Then we would say: 'What do you think, if Abu Bakr dies, who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter?' We would say: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' Then we would say: 'What do you think, if Umar b. al-Khattab dies, who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter?' We would say: 'Uthman.'"],[13176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while on the pulpit: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform ghusl.\""],[13177,"Whoever performs Hajj should make the last of his rites at the House, except for menstruating women, for whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession."],[13178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In the prayer of fear, the imam stands with a group of people with him, and they prostrate one prostration while another group stands between them and the enemy. Then those who prostrated with their leader withdraw and take the place of those who have not prayed, and those who have not prayed come forward and pray with their leader one prostration. Then their leader departs, having completed his prayer, and each of the two groups prays one prostration for itself. If the fear is more severe than that, then on foot or mounted—and by 'prostration' he meant one rak'ah.\""],[13179,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Maghrib prayer: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[13180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the Friday sermon twice, with a sitting between them."],[13181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the zakat al-fitr for every Muslim, free or slave, young or old: a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley."],[13182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, Allah will grasp the heavens with His right hand and the earths with His other hand'—I think he said: the other—'then He will say: I am the King.'"],[13183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while fasting and gave the cupper his wage. Had it been forbidden, he would not have given it."],[13184,"The Prophet ﷺ acquired a ring and wore it on his right hand."],[13185,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Allah, give us water.'"],[13186,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he saw no harm in women wearing silk brocade and silk."],[13187,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.'"],[13188,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed facing a camel."],[13189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to let his turban hang between his shoulder blades."],[13190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and wishes to break his fast, he may break it, unless his fast is that of Ramadan, making up Ramadan, or a vow.'"],[13191,"The Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ with a man and a woman from among them who had committed adultery. He said to them, \"How do you deal with someone who has committed adultery among you?\" They replied, \"We strike them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what do you find in the Torah?\" They said, \"We do not find anything in it regarding this matter.\" Abdullah ibn Salam said to them, \"You have lied; in the Torah, there is stoning. Bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful.\" So the Torah was brought, and the part that he had studied from them was placed on his hand while he covered the verse about stoning. He then asked, \"What is this?\" When they saw that, they said, \"It is stoning.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they be stoned where the graves were. Abdullah said, \"I saw her companion leaning over her to protect her from the stones.\""],[13192,"That unripe dates and fresh dates be steeped together, and dried dates and raisins together."],[13193,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited prayer at sunrise and at sunset."],[13194,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed [the spoils of] the Trench except to six individuals: four from the Muhajirun—Talhah, al-Zubayr, Ali, and Sa'd—and from the Ansar, Abu Dujanah and al-Harith b. al-Simmah."],[13195,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful.\""],[13196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ shaved his head during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[13197,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Many a fasting person obtains nothing from his fasting but hunger and thirst, and many a person standing in prayer obtains nothing from his standing but sleeplessness.\""],[13198,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is enough sin for a man to neglect those whom he is responsible to feed.\""],[13199,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah and prostrate on it."],[13200,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a slain woman during one of his military expeditions and prohibited the killing of women and children."],[13201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited a man from approaching two men who are conversing privately unless he seeks their permission."],[13202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You must wear turbans, for they are the mark of the angels; and let them hang down behind your backs.\""],[13203,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform the ritual bath.\""],[13204,"He intended to enter the state of consecration, came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, and spent the night there. When morning came, he mounted his riding camel, and when it stood upright with him, he pronounced the talbiyah. He asserted that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do that."],[13205,"About the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[13206,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless us in our Sham. O Allah, bless us in our Yemen.” He said it several times. When it was the third or fourth time, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, and in our Iraq?” He said: “Therein are earthquakes and trials, and from there the horn of Satan will rise.”"],[13207,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs except a hunting dog or a livestock dog.”"],[13208,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he observed iʿtikaf, his bed and his cot would be placed for him at the pillar of repentance on the side facing the qiblah, then he would lean against it."],[13209,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah has chosen ones among His creation whom He keeps alive in well-being, and when He takes their souls, He takes them to His Paradise. Those are the ones upon whom trials pass like patches of dark night while they remain in well-being from it.”"],[13210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military expedition toward Najd, and ʿAbd Allah was in it. We captured many camels, and our shares reached twelve camels each, and the Messenger of Allah gave us an extra camel each as booty."],[13211,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin the talbiyah when his riding camel stood upright with him.”"],[13212,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over an adulteress who died during her postpartum bleeding along with her child.”"],[13213,"“A woman divorced three times is not lawful for her first husband until she marries another husband, he has intercourse with her, and she tastes his sweetness.”"],[13214,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar used to perform ablution washing each part three times, tracing that back to the Prophet ﷺ."],[13215,"\"The Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, this refers to the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger ﷺ .\""],[13216,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great, ten good deeds are written for him for every letter. Whoever aids in a false dispute remains in Allah's displeasure until he withdraws. Whoever intercedes to prevent one of Allah's prescribed punishments has opposed Allah in His command. Whoever falsely accuses a believing man or woman, Allah will confine him in the mud of pus on the Day of Resurrection until he comes out of what he said, and he will not come out.'"],[13217,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'All flies are in the Fire except the bee.' And he used to forbid killing them and burning food. Sufyan said: 'It seems that burning food was in the land of the enemy.'"],[13218,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit saying: 'The Compeller will take His heavens and His earths in His hand.' And he clenched his hand and began clenching and opening them, then he said: 'I am the Compeller. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned to his right and to his left until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lowest part, so much so that I said: 'Is it going to fall with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'"],[13219,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Wiping the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner removes sins completely.'"],[13220,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: 'I see you jostling at these two corners.' He said: 'If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Wiping them removes sins.\"'"],[13221,"And I heard him saying, \"Whoever circumambulates this house for a week, counting every step, will have a good deed written for him with each step, and a bad deed will be forgiven for him, and he will be raised in status, and it will be as if he has emancipated a slave.\""],[13222,"\"And I heard him saying, 'Whoever drinks alcohol, his prayer will not be accepted by Allah for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But if he returns to it, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But if he returns to it again, his prayer will not be accepted. And it was the right of Allah to make him drink from the river of impurities.' We said, 'O Abu Abdullah, what is the river of impurities?' He said, 'It is the pus of the people of Hell.'\""],[13223,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There are three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who reminds others of his gifts, the one who drags his lower garment out of pride, and the one addicted to wine.' It was said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what is the one addicted to wine?' He said: 'Persisting in it.'"],[13224,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I joke but I speak only truth'? He said: 'Yes.'"],[13225,"And he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ jostling at it, and I heard him say: 'He does not put down a foot nor raise it except that a good deed is written for him for it.'"],[13226,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever drinks alcohol, his prayers will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. He said it three times. If he repeats the sin, it is upon Allah to make him drink from the river of filth.\" It was asked, \"What is the river of filth?\" He said, \"It is the pus of the people of Hell.\""],[13227,"A man said to Ibn Umar, \"O Abu Abdul-Rahman, why do I see you touching the two corners and not leaving them?\" Ibn Umar used to do that. He replied, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Indeed, touching them removes sins.'\""],[13228,"And I heard him saying, \"Whoever circumambulates this house for a week will have a reward for it.\""],[13229,"And I heard him say, \"Whoever drinks alcohol in this world, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he returns [to drinking], his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he returns [again], his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks it for the fourth time, it is the right of Allah to make him drink from the mud of Khabeel.\" It was asked, \"What is the mud of Khabeel?\" He said, \"The pus of the people of Hell.\""],[13230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The measure is the measure of the people of Madinah, and the weight is the weight of the people of Makkah.'"],[13231,"About nabidh made in earthenware jars, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh in earthenware jars.' And Sulayman b. Harb said in his narration: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited.'"],[13232,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh in earthenware jars? He said: 'Yes.'"],[13233,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh in earthenware jars? He said: 'Yes. Tawus swore to us by Allah that he heard it from Ibn 'Umar.'"],[13234,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade hunting with dogs and predatory animals.\""],[13235,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid soaking (nabidh) in earthenware jars and gourds? He said: Yes."],[13236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars."],[13237,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So Umar went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the news. He commanded him to take her back. He said: I did not hear him add anything to that."],[13238,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have made them fond of Ammar; he calls them to Paradise while they call him to the Fire.\""],[13239,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Part of the honor of a believer before Allah is the cleanliness of his garment and his contentment with little.\""],[13240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a horse race, sending them from al-Hayfa' and its course ended at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. He also raced horses that had not been trained, and their course was from the thaniyya to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."],[13241,"I heard Ibn Umar say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from departing until his last visit is to the House, except menstruating women; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them a concession to depart.\""],[13242,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The night prayer is in pairs, and when you fear dawn, then one (rak'ah).\""],[13243,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"It is not lawful for a man to give a gift or grant and then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The likeness of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is that of a dog that eats until it is full, and then vomits and returns to its vomit.\""],[13244,"Fruit is not to be sold until its ripeness is apparent."],[13245,"Regarding the jallalah (animal that eats filth)."],[13246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, respond to him; and whoever does you a favor, repay him. If you do not find anything with which to repay him, then supplicate for him until he sees that you have repaid him.\""],[13247,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Flies are in the Fire, and he forbade killing bees and that food be burned in the land of the enemy.”"],[13248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except bees.”"],[13249,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mu’adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him.”"],[13250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my shoulders and said: “Be in this world as a stranger or a passer-by.”"],[13251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Permit women to go to the mosque at night.” His son said: “By Allah, we will not permit them, lest they take that as a means of deceit.” He said: “May Allah do such-and-such to you! You hear me say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and you say no?” Layth said in his hadith: “And they would go out unperfumed.”"],[13252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women from the mosques at night.” His son said: “By Allah, we will prevent them.” So he stretched out his hand and slapped him, and said: “I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you say what you say!”"],[13253,"“The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not witness any of your pastimes except racing and archery.”"],[13255,"“O Messenger of Allah, if only we were to take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.” Then it was revealed: {And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer}."],[13256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take from this and leave this,” meaning he takes from the hair below his lower lip and leaves his beard."],[13257,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and masculine women.”"],[13258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever disowns his child in order to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of witnesses, retaliation for retaliation.”"],[13259,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about throwing the pebbles (ramy al-jimār), what is in it for him? I heard him say: “You will find that with your Lord when you are most in need of it.”"],[13260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, respond to him; and whoever gives you a gift of a sheep’s trotter, accept it.”"],[13261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿishāʾ prayer until the one praying had prayed, the one waking had awakened, the sleepers had slept, and those who perform tahajjud had performed it. Then he came out and said: “Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have ordered them to pray at this time—or this prayer,” or something similar."],[13262,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The people of the Fire will be made huge in the Fire until the distance between the lobe of one of their ears and his shoulder becomes a journey of seven hundred years, the thickness of the skin of one of them becomes forty cubits, and his molar tooth becomes greater than Mount Uhud.” Their wording is one."],[13263,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand for the funeral of a Jew that passed by him."],[13264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to follow a funeral that has a wailing woman with it."],[13265,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mutilation."],[13266,"It is an innovation. Come out with us, for this is an innovation."],[13267,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions arrived as pilgrims. He said: “O people, enter iḥrām for ʿumrah, except those who have a sacrificial animal with them, for the ʿumrah has entered into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[13269,"We and he: when we met him we said to him what you like, and when we left him we said something else. He said: “That is what we used to consider hypocrisy while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13270,"We crush unripe dates, then add ripe dates to it, then leave it and drink it. He said: “That is faḍūkh, and wine was forbidden while the majority of their drink was what you mention.”"],[13271,"That is al-faḍūkh. Wine was forbidden while it was our drink."],[13272,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ : \"Whoever drinks alcohol and lets it enter his stomach, his prayers will not be accepted from him for seven days. And if he dies while in that state, he dies as disbeliever. And if his mind is distracted from fulfilling any of the obligatory duties, his prayers will not be accepted from him for forty days. And if he dies during that time, he dies as disbeliever.\""],[13273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: He is Allah, the One (Q 112) equals one third of the Qur'an, and Say: O disbelievers (Q 109) equals one quarter of the Qur'an.” He used to recite them in the two rakʿahs of Fajr, and he said: “These two rakʿahs are what time has desired.”"],[13274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer.”"],[13275,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and shook his hand. He did not withdraw his hand from the man’s hand until the man withdrew his own hand. Then the man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, what about ʿUthman?” He said: “That is a man from the people of Paradise.”"],[13276,"My grandmother ʿAʾishah bt. Yunus, the wife of al-Layth, narrated to me from Layth b. Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me during my lifetime.”"],[13277,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever performs Hajj and visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me during my lifetime.”"],[13278,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to follow a funeral procession in which there is a wailing woman.”"],[13279,"“that we pray in an elevated mosque.”"],[13280,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O son of Adam, guarantee me two rakʿahs at the beginning of the day and I will suffice you for the rest of it.”"],[13281,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever drags his lower garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13282,"And I heard him say: “Do not abandon the two rakʿahs before the Fajr prayer, for in them are the ragāʾib (desirable rewards).”"],[13283,"And I heard him say: “Never disown your child, lest Allah disgrace you before all creation as you disgraced him in this world.”"],[13284,"And I heard him say: \"Do not die while you have a debt upon you, for there are only good deeds and bad deeds; there is no dinar or dirham there, as recompense and settlement, and He does not wrong anyone.\""],[13285,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"None of you should prevent his family from coming to the mosque.\""],[13286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the Day of the Conquest the meat of jallālah camels and their milk."],[13287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not befitting for a believer to humiliate himself.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself?\" He said, \"By exposing himself to trials that he cannot bear.\""],[13288,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one hadith. He said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"Indeed among trees there is a tree whose likeness is that of the Muslim man.\" I wanted to say it is the date palm, but I looked and found that I was the youngest of the people, so I remained silent."],[13289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his wives to perform tamattuʿ and commanded them to depart."],[13290,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House, and with him was al-Faḍl, and Bilāl stood at the door."],[13291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banū ʿAbd Manāf, let me not find you preventing anyone from circumambulating this House at any hour of the night or day.\""],[13292,"Ibn ʿUmar said: \"I have been given from it something that I do not think anyone has been given except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — meaning sexual intercourse.\""],[13293,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Among trees there is indeed a tree like the believing man.\" I wanted to say it is the date palm, but I looked at the faces of the people and found that I was the youngest of them in age, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm.\""],[13294,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of the believer is that of the date palm: whatever you take from it benefits you.\""],[13295,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating the heart of a palm tree."],[13296,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he sneezed and praised Allah. They said, 'May Allah have mercy on you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'May Allah guide you and set your affairs aright.'"],[13297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Tell me about a tree whose example is like that of a believer.\" So, people started mentioning a tree from the trees of the valleys, and I thought to myself that it is the date palm tree. I wanted to say it, but then saw the people's teeth, so I hesitated, fearing that they may detest it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm tree.\""],[13298,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakat, fasting Ramadan, and the Hajj to the House, and the Hajj to this House—twice.'"],[13299,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ while the sun was on Quʿayqiʿan after the afternoon prayer. He said, 'Your lifespans compared to the lifespans of those who have passed are only like what remains of this day compared to what has passed of it.'"],[13300,"On the authority of the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"The example of a believer is like that of a palm tree.\""],[13301,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was eating heart of palm along with the people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Among the trees there is a tree like the Muslim man.' The people fell silent until I was about to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, as I was the youngest of the people. Then he said, 'It is the date palm.'"],[13302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have been given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was sent to all people, the red and the black, whereas each prophet was sent only to his own people. I was aided with fear—my enemy is struck with terror at a distance of a month's journey. I was granted the spoils of war. The earth was made a mosque and a means of purification for me. And I was granted intercession, which I have reserved for my community.'"],[13303,"The Messenger of Allah performed Umrah four times, one of them in the month of Rajab."],[13304,"The forenoon (Duha) prayer is an innovation."],[13305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In the mosque of al-Khaif lies the grave of seventy prophets.\""],[13306,"I was sitting with Abdullah bin Umar, along with Urwah bin Zubair. Urwah asked him in which month did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Umrah? He replied, \"He used to perform Umrah in the month of Rajab.\""],[13307,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than twenty-five times—or he said, more than twenty times—recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[13308,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ reciting in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[13309,"He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿumrah twice before performing Hajj.' News of that reached ʿAʾishah, and she said: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs. ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar knew that; one of them was combined with his Hajj.'"],[13310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever asks you in the name of Allah, give to him, and whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him protection, and whoever presents you with a leadership, accept it.\""],[13311,"He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined us to be good to the neighbor, until we thought he would make him an heir.'"],[13312,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a gathering seeking Allah's forgiveness one hundred times, saying: 'My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, and accept my repentance; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.'"],[13313,"He was asked: 'What do you say about ʿAli ؓ?' He replied: 'He is that one—his house.' Then he was asked: 'What do you say about ʿUthman?' He said: 'What can I say about a man who sinned in a matter between him and his Lord, and He forgave him; and sinned in a matter between you and him, and you killed him?'"],[13314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"],[13315,"He relied on Aisha's room and was asked in which month did the Prophet ﷺ perform Umrah? He said, \"In the month of Rajab.\""],[13316,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ as the tenth of ten. A man from the Ansar came and said, “O Prophet of Allah, who is the most astute of people and the most resolute of people?” He said, “The one among them who remembers death most, and the one who prepares for death most intensely before death descends. Those are the astute ones; they have gone with the honor of this world and the Hereafter.”"],[13320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of part of my body and said, “O Ibn Umar, be in this world like a stranger or a wayfarer, and count yourself among the occupants of the graves.”"],[13321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever gives you a gift, accept it.”"],[13322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever gives you a gift of a foreleg or a shank, accept it.”"],[13323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The likeness of a believer is like that of a perfume seller: if you sit with him, he benefits you; if you walk with him, he benefits you; and if you partner with him, he benefits you.”"],[13324,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”"],[13325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.” He used to forbid killing them and burning food."],[13326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Flies are in the Fire except the bee.” And they used to dislike killing it and burning food."],[13327,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A settled person should not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[13328,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A settled person should not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[13329,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A settled person should not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[13330,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A resident must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[13331,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A resident must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin.”"],[13332,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to intercept trade goods on the roads and forbade a resident to sell on behalf of a Bedouin."],[13333,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A resident must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin, nor buy for him.”"],[13334,"It was said to him: “When we enter upon the rulers, we say to them what we do not say when we leave them.” He said: “We used to consider that hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[13335,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ in some shade in Madinah, and he was looking for ʿAli ؓ, we came to a wall and looked into it. He saw ʿAli lying on the ground, covered in dust, and said: “I do not blame people for calling you Abu Turab.” I saw ʿAli’s face change and he was distressed by that. Then he said: “Shall I not please you, O ʿAli?” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “You are my brother and my minister. You will settle my debts, fulfill my promises, and discharge my obligations. Whoever loves you during my lifetime has fulfilled his vow. Whoever loves you during a lifetime from you after me, God will seal for him with security and faith. Whoever loves you after me but did not see you, God will seal for him with security and faith and grant him safety on the day of the greatest terror. And whoever dies hating you, O ʿAli, dies a death of the Jahiliyyah; God will call him to account for what he did in Islam.”"],[13336,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The first for whom I shall intercede on the Day of Resurrection are the people of my household, then the nearest of Quraysh, then the Ansar, then those who believed in me and followed me from Yemen, then the rest of the Arabs, then the non-Arabs. And the first for whom I shall intercede are the people of virtue.”"],[13337,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever dies in the morning, let him not take a midday nap except in his grave; and whoever dies in the evening, let him not spend the night except in his grave.”"],[13338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade letting the lower garment hang below the ankles."],[13339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God did not open upon ʿAd any of the wind with which they were destroyed except an amount like the place of a ring. It passed by the desert dwellers and carried off their livestock and their wealth, lifting them between the sky and the earth. When the settled people saw the wind and what was in it, they said: ‘This is a cloud bringing us rain.’ Then it cast the desert dwellers and their livestock upon the settled people.”"],[13340,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The muʾadhdhin who seeks God’s reward is like a martyr writhing in his blood until he finishes his call to prayer, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him. And when he dies, worms do not consume him in his grave.”"],[13341,"The Throne shook out of love for meeting God with Saʿd, and he was the last to come out of his grave. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Saʿd was squeezed in his grave, so I asked God to lighten it for him.”"],[13342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The warrior in the path of Allah and the pilgrim to the House of Allah are the delegation of Allah: He called them and they answered Him.”"],[13343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, your Lord is Modest and Generous. He is too Modest to let His servant raise his hands in supplication and then return them empty. So when one of you raises his hands, let him say, 'O Ever-Living, there is no god but You, O Most Merciful of the merciful,' three times. Then, when he lowers his hands, let him pour out that goodness upon his face.\""],[13344,"“Emigration ceased after the conquest.”"],[13345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever parts with ʿAli has parted with me, and whoever parts with me has parted with Allah.”"],[13346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The giver from abundance is not more virtuous than the taker when he is in need.”"],[13347,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him pay the zakat of his wealth. Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him say what is good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him honor his guest.”"],[13348,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says: ‘Praise be to Allah, before Whose greatness all things humble themselves; praise be to Allah, before Whose might all things abase themselves; praise be to Allah, before Whose dominion all things submit; praise be to Allah, before Whose power all things surrender,’ and says it seeking nothing of what He has, Allah will record for him a thousand good deeds, raise him a thousand degrees by it, and entrust to him seventy thousand angels who seek forgiveness for him until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13349,"“The Duha prayer is an innovation, and what an excellent innovation it is.”"],[13350,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is Allah, the One.”"],[13351,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah.”"],[13352,"Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ, one of them from the Ansar and the other from Thaqif. The Ansari preceded him, so the Prophet ﷺ said to the Thaqafi: “O brother of Thaqif, the Ansari has preceded you.” The Ansari said: “I will start with him, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said to him: “O brother of Thaqif, ask about your need, and if you wish, I will tell you what you have come to ask about.” He said: “That would be more pleasing to me for you to do.” He said: “You ask me about your prayer, your bowing, your prostration, and your fasting, and you say: What is in it for me?” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth.” He said: “Pray the first part of the night and its last part, and sleep in its middle.” He said: “What if I pray in its middle?” He said: “You then…” He said: “When you stand for prayer and bow, place your hands on your knees, spread your fingers, then raise your head until every limb returns to its joint. When you prostrate, place your forehead firmly on the ground and do not peck. Fast the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.” Then he turned to the Ansari and said: “Ask about your need, and if you wish, I will tell you.” He said: “That would be more pleasing to me.” He said: “You have come to ask me about your leaving your house heading for the Sacred House, and you say: What is in it for me? You have come to ask about your standing at ʿArafah, and you say: What is in it for me? About your throwing the pebbles, and you say: What is in it for me? About your circumambulation of the House, and you say: What is in it for me? About your shaving your head, and you say: What is in it for me?” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth.” He said: “As for your leaving your house heading for the House, for every step your mount takes, Allah records a good deed for you and wipes away a sin from you. As for your standing at ʿArafah, Allah ﷻ descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of them to the angels, saying: ‘These are My servants who have come to Me disheveled and dusty from every deep ravine, hoping for My mercy and fearing My punishment, though they have not seen Me. How would it be if they had seen Me? If you had sins like the sand of ʿAlij, or like the days of the world, or like the drops of rain, Allah would wash them away from you.’ As for your throwing the pebbles, it is stored up for you. As for your shaving your head, for every hair that falls you have a good deed. When you circumambulate the House, you come out of your sins as on the day your mother gave birth to you.”"],[13353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The storyteller awaits wrath, the listener awaits mercy, the merchant awaits provision, the hoarder awaits curse, and the wailing woman and those around her of women—upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[13354,"The Prophet ﷺ came out and spread his right palm and said: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans. No one is added to them or subtracted from them.” Then he spread his left palm and said: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, for the people of the Fire, with their names, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans. No one is added to them or subtracted from them.”"],[13355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone, and he did not touch anything besides them."],[13356,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Permit women to go to the mosques at night.\""],[13357,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When something is entrusted to Allah, He protects it. I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the final deeds of your actions.\""],[13358,"The Prophet ﷺ secluded himself and addressed the people, saying, \"Indeed, when one of you stands in prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let each of you know what he is conversing with his Lord about, and let not one of you pronounce his recitation in prayer loudly over another.\""],[13359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him. If the person refuses, he should fight him, for with him is a qarin (companion).\""],[13360,"He saw the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, mounting his riding animal."],[13361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam."],[13362,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"To proceed (amma baʿd).\""],[13363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl.\""],[13364,"I said to Ibn Umar: \"Did you witness the Pledge of Ridwan with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"What was he wearing?\" He said: \"A cotton shirt, a padded jubba, a cloak, and a sword. And I saw al-Nuʿman b. Muqarrin al-Muzani standing by his head, holding up the branches of the tree away from his head while the people were pledging allegiance to him.\""],[13365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram when his mount stood upright with him."],[13366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not revile the face, for the son of Adam was created in the image of the Most Merciful, Exalted is He.\""],[13367,"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, indeed we are traveling and we meet people who say there is no predestination. So, if you meet them, inform them that Ibn Umar is innocent from them. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him, handsome in appearance, with a pleasant fragrance and clean clothes. He greeted the Prophet ﷺ and asked, \"Can I come close to you?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Approach.\" So, he came closer until his knees touched the knees of the Prophet ﷺ . Then he asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? \"The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It is to testify that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to perform Hajj pilgrimage to the House of Allah, fasting in the month of Ramadan, and to perform ablution from impurity.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a Muslim?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" The man asked again, \"Tell me about faith (Iman).\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Day of Judgment, and destiny, both its good and bad aspects.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a believer?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" The man then asked, \"Tell me about excellence (Ihsan).\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then know that He sees you.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a person of excellence?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" We said, \"We have never seen anyone more virtuous in appearance, with a better fragrance, and showing more respect to the Prophet ﷺ than this man. When the man left, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"Do you know who this man was?\" We replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This was Gabriel ﷺ . He came to teach you your religion.\""],[13368,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a Bedouin approached. When he drew near, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Where do you intend to go?\" He said: \"To my family.\" He said: \"Would you like something good?\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said: \"Who will testify to what you say?\" He said: \"This tree.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came, plowing through the ground, until it stood before him. He asked it to testify three times, and it testified that he was as he said. Then it returned to its place of growth, and the Bedouin went back to his people and said: \"If they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will return to you and stay with you.\""],[13369,"A time came upon us when none of us thought that he was more entitled to the dinar and the dirham than his Muslim brother. Yet I am in a time when the dinar and the dirham are dearer to us than our Muslim brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When people are stingy with the dinar and the dirham, abandon jihad in the path of Allah, cling to the tails of cattle, and engage in ʿinah transactions, Allah will impose upon them a trial that He will not lift until they return.\""],[13370,"If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not once, not twice, not three times” — he counted seven times — “I would not have narrated it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Three will be on mounds of musk on the Day of Resurrection: grief will not terrify them, nor will they be frightened when people are frightened: a man who learned the Qur’an and stood with it, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and what is with Him; a man who called out every day and night five prayers, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and what is with Him; and a slave whom the bondage of this world did not prevent from obeying his Lord."],[13371,"A time came upon us when none of us thought he was more entitled to the dinar and the dirham than his Muslim brother. Then, when we reached the latter part of it, we awoke and the dinar and the dirham became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When people become miserly with the dinar and the dirham, deal in ʿīnah, and follow the tails of cattle, Allah will send upon them humiliation that He will not lift from them until they return to their religion.”"],[13372,"\"Regarding the sale of booty until it is divided.\""],[13373,"\"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ praying twenty-five times, and he used to recite in the two units of prayer before Fajr and the two units of prayer before Maghrib, 'Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun' and 'Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad'.\""],[13374,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah has cursed whoever reviles my Companions.”"],[13375,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you see those who praise people to their faces, throw dust in their faces.”"],[13376,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he looked for Bilal to give the call to prayer for them, but he was not found. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man, and he gave the call to prayer in place of Bilal. After that, he wanted to give the iqamah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only the one who gave the call to prayer gives the iqamah.”"],[13377,"Two festivals coincided during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: the day of Fitr and a Friday. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the Eid prayer, then turned to face them and said: “O people, you have attained good and reward. We shall hold the Friday prayer, so whoever wishes to attend the Friday prayer with us let him attend, and whoever wishes to return to his family let him return.”"],[13378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would make things difficult for my ummah, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"],[13379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not sit for any part of the night except that he passed the siwak over his mouth."],[13380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The least of my ummah are those who reach seventy.”"],[13381,"A man from Ethiopia came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ask and inquire.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have been favored over us with appearance, colors, and prophethood. Have you considered that if I believed in what you believe in and did what you did, would I be with you in Paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have been favored over us with appearance, colors, and prophethood. Have you considered that if I believed in what you believe in and knew what you knew, would I be with you in Paradise?\" The man said, \"Yes.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the whiteness of blackness in Paradise can be seen from a distance of a thousand years' travel.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah' will have a covenant with Allah. And whoever says, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,' one hundred thousand good deeds will be written for him, and four and twenty thousand good deeds more.\" A man asked, \"How can one be destroyed after this, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, a man will come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds as great as a mountain, but Allah will render them insignificant as dust. The blessings from the blessings of Allah will almost expire, except by the grace of Allah.\" This Surah was revealed, \"Has there not come upon man a period of time when he was not a thing mentioned?\" until His saying, \"And a great kingdom.\" Al-Habashi said, \"Indeed, my two eyes have seen what your two eyes cannot see in Paradise.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" Then he wept until his soul passed away. Ibn 'Umar said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placing him in his grave with his own hand.\""],[13382,"The Prophet ﷺ performed Umrah in the month of Rajab."],[13383,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever says, ‘Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,’ one hundred and twenty-four thousand good deeds are written for him. And whoever says, ‘There is no god but Allah,’ he will have a covenant with Allah on the Day of Resurrection by it.”"],[13384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not wake up from any part of the night except that he passed the siwak over his mouth."],[13385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Mention the good qualities of your dead and refrain from their faults.”"],[13386,"The Messenger of God ﷺ once led us in prayer. When he raised his head from the bowing, he said, “God hears the one who praises Him.” A man behind him said, “Our Lord, to You belongs abundant, good, blessed praise.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said three times, “Who was the speaker just now?” The man said, “I, O Messenger of God.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw more than thirty angels rushing to it, each of them striving to be the first to write it down.”"],[13387,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw in a dream as if there were two bracelets of gold on his forearms, and he blew on them and they flew away. He said, “They are the two liars of my community: the one of Yemen and the one of Yamamah. They will not harm my community in anything.”"],[13388,"I went early in the afternoon to the Prophet ﷺ. Abu al-Hasan came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Come close to me, O Abu al-Hasan.” He kept drawing him near until he took his ear between his lips. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ leaned to his left until the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head like one startled, and said, “The wicked one knocked on his hearing at the door.” He said, “Go, O Abu al-Hasan, and lead him as a sheep is led to its milker.” Then there was ʿAli, who had brought al-Hakam, taking hold of both his ear and his cheek, until he made him stand before the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet of God ﷺ cursed him three times. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ said to ʿAli, “Sit aside.” Then some people from the Emigrants and the Helpers came to the Prophet of God ﷺ, and then the Prophet of God ﷺ called for him and said, “Indeed, this one will oppose the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ, and from his loins will emerge trials whose smoke reaches the sky.” A man among the Muslims said, “God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He is too insignificant and contemptible for that to come from him.” He said, “Yes, and some of you will be his partisans on that day.”"],[13389,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims, God will not look into his need until he looks into their needs.”"],[13390,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was gesturing with his palm like this, as if measuring something: “Whoever separates from the community of the Muslims by a handspan has removed the noose of Islam from his neck. And the dissidents will have their banners, which they will be reaching for from behind their backs on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever dies without an imam of the community dies a death of ignorance.”"],[13391,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say: “Do not revile your dead, for reviling them is not lawful.”"],[13392,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say when he visited Abu Salamah while he was ill, and he heard the words of Umm Salamah while she was weeping. The Prophet of God refrained from entering when he heard her weeping over him with the Book of God, saying: “And the throes of death will come with the truth; that is what you used to turn away from.” Then he entered, greeted, and said, “May God compensate you, O Umm Salamah.” When he went out with Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr said to him, “I saw you, O Messenger of God, disliking to enter because they are wailing.” He said, “I do not enter a house in which there is wailing or a black dog.”"],[13393,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ: he came to a cloth merchant and bought a shirt from him for four dirhams. He went out wearing it, and there was a man from the Helpers who said, “O Messenger of God ﷺ, clothe me with a shirt; may God clothe you from the garments of Paradise.” So he took off the shirt and clothed him with it. Then he returned to the shopkeeper and bought a shirt from him for four dirhams, and two dirhams remained with him. Then he came upon a girl in the road weeping, and he said, “What makes you weep?” She said, “O Messenger of God, my family gave me two dirhams to buy flour with them, and I lost them.” The Prophet ﷺ gave her the remaining two dirhams. Then she turned away weeping, and he called her and said, “What makes you weep, when you have taken the two dirhams?” She said, “I fear they will beat me.” So he walked with her to her family, gave the greeting, and they recognized his voice. Then he returned and gave the greeting, then returned and gave the greeting, then returned a third time, and they responded. He said, “Did you hear the first greeting?” They said, “Yes, but we loved that you increase us in greeting. What has brought you here, may our father and mother be ransom for you?” He said, “This girl feared that you would beat her.” Her master said, “She is free for the sake of God, because of your walking with her.” The Prophet of God ﷺ gave them glad tidings of good and Paradise, then said, “God has indeed blessed the ten dirhams: God clothed His Prophet with a shirt, and a man from the Helpers with a shirt, and God freed a neck through them. I praise God, for it is He who provided us this by His power.”"],[13394,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Who will take this letter of mine to the tyrant of Byzantium?” He presented it to them three times. Then he said, “Who will go and have Paradise?” A man from the Helpers called ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Khaliq said, “I will take it, and I will have Paradise if I perish in that cause?” He said, “Yes, you will have Paradise whether you deliver it, or are killed, or perish. God has made Paradise obligatory for you.” He set out with the letter of the Prophet ﷺ until he reached the tyrant and said, “I am a messenger of the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds.” He was granted permission and entered upon him. The tyrant of Byzantium recognized that he had brought the truth from a sent prophet. Then he presented to him the letter of the Prophet ﷺ. He gathered the Byzantines before him and presented it to them, but they disliked what he brought. One man among them believed in it and was killed upon his belief. Then the man returned to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what had happened with him and the killing of the man. The Prophet ﷺ said at that: “God will raise him as a nation alone,” referring to that slain man."],[13395,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no believing servant who turns to God in repentance before death by a month except that God accepts it from him. And even less than that—before his death by a day or an hour, if God knows repentance and sincerity from him—except that God accepts it from him.”"],[13396,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day a man was placed in his grave: two angels came to him and said, “We will strike you with a blow.” He said to them, “For what will you strike me?” They struck him with a blow that filled his grave with fire. Then they left him until he recovered and the terror left him. He said to them, “For what did you strike me?” They said, “You prayed a prayer while not in a state of purity, and you passed by a wronged man and did not help him.”"],[13397,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on a Friday when he prayed the afternoon prayer with the people while seated in the first two rakʿahs: a dog passed by to cut across his prayer, and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas feared that it would pass in front of him, so he supplicated against the dog, and God destroyed it by His power. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer and saw that the dog had perished, he said, “Who among you supplicated against this dog?” No one spoke. The Prophet of God ﷺ repeated, and Saʿd said then, “I supplicated against it, O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be ransom for you. I feared that it would cut across your prayer, so I supplicated against it.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “How did you supplicate against it, O Saʿd?” Saʿd said, “Glory be to You, there is no god but You, O Possessor of majesty and honor. Destroy this dog lest it cut across the prayer of Your prophet.” The Prophet of God ﷺ said, “O Saʿd, you have supplicated on a day and in an hour with words that, had you supplicated against all that is between the heavens, it would have been answered for you. Rejoice, O Saʿd.”"],[13400,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When any of you dies, do not hold him back, and hasten with him to his grave, and let the opening of the Book (al-Fātiḥah) be recited at his head and the closing of al-Baqarah at his feet in his grave.”"],[13401,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no prayer for one who enters the mosque while the imam is standing praying; let him not pray alone by himself, but let him join the imam in the prayer.”"],[13402,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Slander, revilement, and fanatical pride are in the Fire, and they will never combine in the breast of a believer.”"],[13403,"“The Messenger of Allah performed ablution three times, three times.”"],[13404,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever fasts perpetually has neither fasted nor broken his fast.”"],[13405,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[13406,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: “No people withhold the zakāh of their wealth except that they are deprived of rain from the sky, and were it not for the beasts, they would not be given rain.”"],[13407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you, for there is no servant who spends the night pure except that an angel spends the night with him in his undergarment; he does not turn over at any hour of the night except that he says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night pure.”"],[13408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you. There is no servant who spends the night pure except that an angel spends the night in his undergarment; whenever he turns over at any hour of the night, the angel says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, as he spent the night pure.”"],[13409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pray over whoever says lā ilāha illā Allāh, and pray behind whoever says lā ilāha illā Allāh.”"],[13410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My Ummah will never unite upon misguidance. So, hold fast to the [united] group (the majority), for indeed, the Hand of Allah is with the [united] group.\""],[13411,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling the right of patronage (walāʾ) and giving it as a gift.”"],[13412,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling the right of patronage (walāʾ) and giving it as a gift.”"],[13413,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in whatever direction his mount faced."],[13414,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on his mount."],[13415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any two parties to a sale have no sale between them until they separate, except a sale with an option.”"],[13416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven times. Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have an excellent example."],[13417,"The Prophet ﷺ came and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have an excellent example."],[13418,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” Then he said: Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example."],[13419,"I heard Ibn 'Umar say: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa through the gate by which one goes out to it, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” Ghundar added in his narration: Shu'bah said: Ayyub informed me, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, that it is a Sunnah."],[13420,"As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he came and circumambulated the House, then prayed two rak'ahs, then went between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[13421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should make his brother get up from his seat in order to sit in his place.”"],[13422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to relieve himself at al-Maghmas. Nafi' said: “About two miles from Makkah.”"],[13423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs except a livestock dog or a hunting dog."],[13424,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever has a slave jointly owned between him and another, and he frees his share, then it is assessed for him and he frees him.”"],[13425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the drinker of wine and the one who serves it."],[13426,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its goodness becomes apparent."],[13427,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah and in it there were three hundred and eighty idols. In his hand was a staff, and he began pointing at them and saying: “Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish.” And the idols fell down."],[13428,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade (using) gourds and vessels smeared with pitch."],[13429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed on us the sadaqah of Ramadan: one sa' of barley or one sa' of dates."],[13430,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the most beloved people to Allah? And what are the most beloved deeds to Allah?\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"The most beloved people to Allah are those who are most beneficial to others, and the most beloved deeds to Allah are bringing happiness to a Muslim or removing a distress from him, settling his debt or relieving his hunger. And I would prefer to walk with my brother in fulfilling his need over staying in itkaf in this Masjid (al-Nabawi) for a month.Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will cover his faults, and whoever suppresses his rage even though he could fulfill it, Allah will fill his heart with hope on the Day of Judgment. And whoever walks with his brother in fulfilling his need until he secures it, Allah will make his footing firm on the Day when feet will slip.\""],[13431,"\"The Prophet ﷺ made the date palm's boundaries extend to the length of its branches.\""],[13432,"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sun rises between the two horns of a devil.”"],[13433,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not wiping other than these two (the two khuffs)."],[13434,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not wiping other than these two (the two khuffs)."],[13435,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not wiping other than these two (the two khuffs)."],[13436,"While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a woman passed by. Some of the people said, “This is the daughter of Muhammad.” A man said, “Indeed the likeness of Muhammad among Banu Hashim is that of a fragrant herb in the midst of stench.” The woman went and informed the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ came, anger recognizable in his face, until he stood over the people and said: “What is the matter with statements that reach me from certain people? Indeed Allah, may He be exalted, created the heavens and the earth in seven (layers). He chose the highest of them and dwelt in it, and He settled whomever He willed of His creation in His heavens. He created the earth in seven (layers) and chose the highest of them, and He settled whomever He willed of His creation in it. He created the creation and chose from the creation the children of Adam, and chose from the children of Adam the Arabs, and chose from the Arabs Mudar, and chose from Mudar Quraysh, and chose from Quraysh Banu Hashim, and chose me from Banu Hashim. I am from the best to the best. So whoever loves the Arabs, it is out of love for me that he loves them, and whoever hates the Arabs, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.”"],[13437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and 'Umrah consecutively, for they remove sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron.”"],[13438,"He said to a man: “Sell me the fruit of your land for the measure you used to measure from it.” Ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade this, and it is muzabanah.”"],[13439,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after Isha."],[13440,"I heard Ibn Umar say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at al-Hijr, he said, \"Do not enter upon these punished people.\" Then he ordered the dough, and it was thrown away."],[13441,"While we were around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he mentioned the fitnah or it was mentioned in his presence. He said, \"When you see that people's covenants have become corrupted, their trusts have become light, and they have become like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers. I stood up to him and said, \"How should I act at that time, may Allah make me your ransom?\" He said, \"Stay in your house, control your tongue, take what you know, leave what you reject, keep to the affairs of your own self, and leave the affairs of the common people.\""],[13442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How will you be in a time—or a time is about to come—when people will be sifted with a thorough sifting, and the dregs of people will remain, their covenants and trusts having become corrupted, and they will differ, and they will become like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers. They said, \"How should we be, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, and attend to the affairs of your own selves, and leave the affairs of your common people.\""],[13443,"He reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"How will you be when a time comes in which people will be sifted with a thorough sifting, and you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants have become corrupted and who have neglected their trusts, and they return to being like this\"—and he inserted his fingers into one another. They said, \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, and keep to your own special affairs, and leave the affairs of your common people.\""],[13444,"“I retained from the Messenger of God ﷺ a thousand proverbs.”"],[13445,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.” Then he said: “God, Mighty and Exalted, and His Messenger ﷺ have forbidden wine, gambling, the kubah (drum), and al-ghubayra (a fermented drink).”"],[13446,"One day I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in his house and he said: “Do you know who is with us in the house?” I said: “Who, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Jibril ﷺ .” I said: “Peace be upon you, O Jibril, and the mercy of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He has returned your greeting.”"],[13447,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Knowledge is three things, and whatever is beyond that is surplus: a decisive verse, an established sunnah, and a just obligatory share.”"],[13448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever feeds his brother until he is full and gives him water to drink until he is quenched, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seven trenches, each trench being a distance of five hundred years.”"],[13449,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There will be a caliph, he and his descendants are from the people of the Fire.”"],[13450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a man to marry a woman by divorcing another, nor is it lawful for a man to outbid a fellow man’s transaction until he gives it up, nor is it lawful for three people in open land to appoint one of themselves as their leader, nor is it lawful for three people in open land for two of them to hold private conversation without their companion.”"],[13451,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever stands up (in prayer) and recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad (Surah Al-Ikhlas) and Al-Lahus-Samad (Surah Al-Falaq), then he has recited a third of the Quran.\""],[13452,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which Islam is best? He said: \"That you feed food and greet with peace those you know and those you do not know.\""],[13453,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The first group to enter Paradise will be the poor among the emigrants who are boycotted by others. When they are commanded, they listen and obey, even if there is a person among them who has a need but it is not fulfilled until he dies while it is still in his chest. Indeed, Allah invites Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and it comes with its splendor and beautification. Allah will say, 'Where are My servants who fought in My cause, were harmed in My cause, and strived in My cause? Enter Paradise with no punishment, no accounting.' The angels will come and prostrate and say, 'Our Lord, we glorify You night and day, and who are these whom You have made superior to us?' The Lord, blessed and exalted be He, will say, 'These are My servants who fought in My cause, were harmed in My cause, and strived in My cause.' The angels will enter upon them from every gate, saying, 'Peace be upon you, for your patience. How excellent is the final home!'\""],[13454,"And he narrated that a man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: I pledge allegiance to you for emigration and jihad, and I seek reward from Allah. He said: \"Is either of your parents alive?\" He said: Yes, both of them. He said: \"So do you seek reward from Allah?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Return to your parents and keep their company well.\""],[13455,"A man asked me, so I said: This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so go and ask him, then come back and tell me. He asked him, then returned and told me that he had asked him, and he said: \"It is the greatest of major sins and the mother of indecencies. Whoever drinks wine abandons prayer and may fall upon his mother, his paternal aunt, and his maternal aunt.\""],[13456,"The Prophet ﷺ seated him behind him and said: “O young man, shall I not grant you something? Shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you? Safeguard Allah and He will safeguard you; safeguard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that the pen has already dried with what is to be, and know that if the creatures were to intend something for you that was not written upon you, they would not be able to do it. And know that victory is with patience, relief is with distress, and with hardship comes ease.”"],[13457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"ʿAli is my root and Jaʿfar is my branch\" or \"Jaʿfar is my root and ʿAli is my branch.\""],[13458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Congratulations to you, O ʿAbd Allah. Your father is flying with the angels in the sky.\""],[13459,"From his father, regarding these words: \"There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Magnificent. Glory be to God, Lord of the Noble Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"Prompt your dying with them.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, what about for the living?\" He said: \"Better and better.\""],[13460,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent an army and appointed Zayd b. Harithah as their commander. He said: \"If he is killed or martyred, your commander is Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib. If he is killed or martyred, your commander is ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah.\" They set off and met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Jaʿfar took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of God, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and God granted victory through him. Their news came to the Prophet ﷺ. He went out and ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: \"To proceed: your brothers met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Jaʿfar took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of God, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and God granted victory through him.\" Then he gave the family of Jaʿfar three days before coming to them. Then he came to them and said: \"Do not weep for him after today.\" Then he said: \"Summon for me the sons of my brother.\" We were brought as if we were chicks. He said: \"Summon for me the barber.\" He ordered him, and he shaved our heads. Then he said: \"As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib. As for ʿAwn and ʿAbd Allah, they resemble me in my appearance and character.\" Then he took my hand and raised it, saying: \"O God, be a successor to Jaʿfar in his family, and bless ʿAbd Allah in the transaction of his right hand.\" He said this three times. Then our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?\""],[13461,"About killing them—meaning the snakes that are in houses."],[13462,"Sahl entered upon al-Hajjaj while leaning on his hand, and said to him: The Prophet ﷺ said concerning the Ansar: “Be good to their good-doers and pardon their wrongdoers.” He said: Who will testify for you? He said: These two at your sides, Abdullah b. Ja'far and Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Talhah. They said: Yes."],[13463,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped his head three times and said: “O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his family.”"],[13464,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he praised Allah. It was said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. He said: “May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.”"],[13465,"I saw the ring of the Prophet ﷺ on his right hand."],[13466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best meat is the meat of the back.”"],[13467,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed ʿIsha, he would perform four rakʿahs and make witr with one prostration, then sleep until he prayed after his prayer during the night."],[13468,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple from my nation.'"],[13469,"About the Prophet ﷺ , it was mentioned that he appointed an inheritance for himself because he was born on the bed of Zama'ah. He said to Sawda, \"As for you, seclude yourself from him.\""],[13470,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his uncle al-ʿAbbas to order his sons to cultivate clover, for it repels poverty. He said, “And al-qadb is lucerne.”"],[13471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever draws his sword then strikes with it, his blood is forfeited,” meaning he struck with it."],[13472,"About nabidh, he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade earthenware jars and gourds.”"],[13473,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “If I were to take an intimate friend other than my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but he is my brother and my companion in the cave.”"],[13474,"\"The Prophet ﷺ cursed so-and-so and his son from this pulpit.\""],[13475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.\""],[13476,"'Utbah b. Farqad wrote to 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr asking his legal opinion about the grandfather. He wrote back: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If I were to take a close friend from my nation other than my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave.\" And Abu Bakr used to treat him like a father."],[13477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Hajj: \"Which city is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"Mecca.\" He said, \"Which month is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"The month of Dhul-Hijjah.\" He said, \"Which day is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"The day of Sacrifice, the greatest day of Hajj.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours, until you meet your Lord.\""],[13478,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: \"This is the day of 'Ashura', so fast it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded its fasting.\""],[13479,"\"I saw Ibn al-Zubayr performing tawaf wearing a bartalah.\""],[13480,"\"And take provisions, for the best provision is God-consciousness.\""],[13481,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ curse al-Hakam and his offspring."],[13482,"Al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwam: \"O Messenger of God, which comfort will we be asked about? They are only the two black ones: water and dates.\" He said: \"Indeed that will be.\""],[13483,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is more virtuous than a thousand prayers in any other mosque.\""],[13484,"\"We ate grilled food with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while we were in the mosque. Then the prayer was called, so we did not increase or add anything except that we wiped with pebbles.\""],[13485,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: After the prayer, when he had said the salam, before standing, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, raising his voice: \"There is no god but God, alone without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no might nor power except by God; we worship none but Him. His is grace, His is bounty, and His is good praise. There is no god but God, sincere to Him in religion, even if the disbelievers hate it.\""],[13486,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting the verse: “They said: Two sorcerers supporting one another.”"],[13487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken him as a close friend.” He made the grandfather a father, to whom wealth may pass."],[13488,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed before the Hour there will be thirty liars, among them al-Aswad al-‘Ansi, the man of San‘a’, and the man of al-Yamama.”"],[13489,"I heard ‘Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: The Prophet ﷺ recited the tashahhud: “In the name of Allah and by Allah, the Best of names. All greetings, pure words, and prayers are due to Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, and that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. O Allah, forgive me and guide me.” This was in the first two rak‘ahs."],[13490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"],[13491,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of Umm Salamah praying in a single garment, draping its two ends over opposite shoulders."],[13492,"Al-Mustanir b. Rizam the Jew struck my face with a hooked staff of shawhat wood and wounded me with a wound that reached the membrane of the brain or fractured the skull. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he uncovered it and spat into it, and nothing from it ever harmed me."],[13493,"That he said: O Messenger of God, we are in our desert, and by God's praise I pray there, so command me to one night of this month that I should descend to the mosque and pray in it. He said: \"Descend on the night of the twenty-third and pray it, and if you like to continue to the end of the month, then do so, and if you like to return to your family, then do so.\""],[13494,"That he said: O Messenger of God, tell me a night in which the Night of Decree is sought. He said: \"Were it not that people would only descend for the prayer except on that night, I would have told you, but seek it in the twenty-third of the month.\""],[13495,"From Damra b. Abdullah b. Unays and Abd al-Rahman b. Ka'b that they both heard Abdullah b. Unays say: I sat in the gathering of Banu Salima, and I was the youngest of them, on the morning of the twenty-first of Ramadan. They said: Who will ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for us when the Night of Decree is? I said: I will. So I went until I arrived at Maghrib on the night of the twenty-second, and I prayed the prayer with him. Then I stood for him at his door until he passed by me, and he brought me into his house. He called for supper for me and said to me: \"Eat supper.\" Indeed I saw myself holding back from it because of its scarcity. Then he called for his sandals and stood up and said: \"It seems you have a need?\" I said: Yes, men from Banu Salima sent me to you asking you when the Night of Decree is. He said: \"How many nights of the month have passed?\" I said: Twenty-two. He said: \"It is tonight.\" Then he returned and said: \"Or the next one, or the next one.\""],[13496,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Night of Decree. He said: \"I saw myself prostrating in water and mud.\" I said: Make it clear to me so that I may seek it out? He said: \"Seek it in the latter half.\" I said: In which part of the latter half? He said: \"In the twenty-third.\""],[13497,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the Night of Decree. He said: \"I saw it and then was made to forget it, so seek it in the latter half.\" Then he returned and asked him, and he said: \"In the twenty-third that passes of the month.\" Abd al-Aziz said: My mother told me that Abdullah b. Unays used to keep alive the night of the sixteenth until the night of the twenty-third."],[13498,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The greatest of major sins are associating partners with God, disobedience to parents, and the false oath. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one swears, even if it is about the like of a mosquito's wing, except that it becomes a black spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[13499,"\"That the Messenger of God ﷺ sent him on a military expedition alone.\""],[13500,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I saw myself on Laylat al-Qadr prostrating in water and mud.” Then the Prophet ﷺ led us in prayer on the night of the twenty-third, and I saw him prostrating in water and mud."],[13501,"From ʿAbd Allāh b. Unays, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he was asked about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Seek it tonight.” And that night was the night of the twenty-third. A man said: O Messenger of God, then it is the first of eight? He said: “Rather, the first of seven, since the month does not complete [thirty days].”"],[13502,"He narrated to us from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim coincides while he is in prayer, asking God for good, except that He gives it to him.” Abū Hurayrah indicated with his hand that it was a small amount. When Abū Hurayrah died, I said: If only I went to Abū Saʿīd and asked him. So I went to him and asked him. Then I left him and entered upon ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām and asked him. He said: God created Adam on Friday and took him [in death] on Friday, and on it the Hour will occur, and it is the last hour. I said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said “in prayer,” but that is not an hour of prayer. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one waiting for prayer is in prayer”? I said: Yes. He said: Then by God, it is it."],[13503,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām: O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim, and I would like to ask you about some things. He said: “Ask about whatever occurs to you.” I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about a man's resemblance to his mother, when the fluid is from the man. He said: “The man's fluid is white and thick, and the woman's fluid is red and thin. Whichever of them prevails over the other, the resemblance belongs to it.” I said: O Messenger of God, what will the people of Paradise eat when they enter it? He said: “An extra portion of fish liver.” I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about the signs of the Hour. He said: “A fire that emerges from the east and drives the people to their gathering place.” He said: I bear witness that you are a prophet."],[13504,"“Jesus ﷺ will be buried with the Messenger of God ﷺ and his two companions, and his grave will be the fourth.”"],[13505,"I entered the mosque of Madinah, and a man came and prayed two rakʿahs, making them brief, with a trace of humility upon him. A man said: Whoever would like to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this one. I followed him and told him, and he said: Glory be to God; no one should say what he does not know. I will tell you why that is. I saw a vision and related it to the Prophet ﷺ. I saw as if I were in a garden—and he mentioned its vastness, beauty, and greenness—with in its middle an iron pillar whose base was in the earth and its top in the sky. At its top was a handle. He said to me: Climb. I said: I cannot. Then a servant came to me and took hold of my clothes—that is, from behind me—and struck at the top of it, saying: Hold fast. I awoke with it in my hand. I related it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “The garden is Islam, the pillar is the pillar of Islam, and the handle is the firm handhold, so you are upon Islam.” And behold, he was ʿAbdullah b. Salam."],[13506,"“Shall I not relate to you a hadith that is in the Book of God?” Then he mentioned a people who will come out of the Fire. Ibrahim will say, “O Lord, You have burned my children,” and they will come out of it."],[13507,"“Indeed we find the description of the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good tidings, and a warner, and a protection for the unlettered. You are My servant and His messenger. I have named you al-Mutawakkil. He is not harsh, nor hard-hearted, nor clamorous in the markets, nor does he repay evil with its like; rather he pardons, forgives, and overlooks. And I will not take you until I have straightened the crooked creed by your testifying that there is no god but God, by which He opens blind eyes, deaf ears, and covered hearts.’” ʿAtaʾ b. Yasar said: Abu Waqid al-Laythi informed me that he heard Kaʿb al-Ahbar say the like of what Ibn Salam said."],[13508,"“By Him in whose hand is my soul, the nearest of people on the Day of Resurrection will be Muhammad ﷺ, sitting at His right upon the Throne.”"],[13509,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the pulpit: “It would not be difficult for you, if you could manage, to take two garments for Friday other than the two garments of work.”"],[13510,"He said: We discussed among ourselves and said, 'Which of us will go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him which deeds are most beloved to God?' We were in awe that any one of us should stand up. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a man to us. Some of us began gesturing to one another, and he recited to us: 'Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies God' from its beginning to its end. Hilal said: 'Ata' b. Yasar recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: Hilal recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awza'i said: Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end."],[13511,"What is between ʿAyr and Uhud is sacred. The Messenger of God ﷺ declared it sacred. I would never cut a tree from it or hunt a bird."],[13512,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When the prayer is due and one of you has the need to defecate, let him begin with that, then pray afterwards, and let him not come to prayer while he is holding it back.”"],[13513,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, saying: Dawud b. Qays narrated to us. And Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Razzaq from Dawud b. Qays, who said: I heard ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. Aqram narrating from his father that he was with his father at al-Qaʿ in Namirah, and a mounted party passed by us, and they made their camels kneel at the side of the road. He said to me, “My son, stay with our lambs until I approach these riders.” He said, so he approached them and I approached with him. Then the prayer was established, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among them, and I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ every time he prostrated."],[13514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man may free from his slave whatever he wishes—if he wishes, two-thirds, and if he wishes, a quarter.”"],[13515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “For camels there is a farʿ, and for sheep there is a farʿ. And the ʿaqiqah is performed for a boy, and his head is not touched with blood.”"],[13516,"The Messenger of God ﷺ approached until he was in the midst of the dwellings of the Ansar and noticed the smell of roasting meat. He said: \"Who is this who has slaughtered?\" A man came out and said: \"O Messenger of God, this is a day on which food is undesirable.\" He said: \"Slaughter again.\" He said: \"By God, I have nothing but a jadhaʿah or a lamb of sheep.\" He said: \"Slaughter again\" three times, then said: \"Then slaughter it, and it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[13517,"I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ as his people embraced Islam. He advised us, saying, \"Let the one among you who knows the most Qur'an lead you in prayer.\" As I knew the most Qur'an, they made me lead them."],[13518,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"O God, whoever believes in me, attests to my truthfulness, and knows that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth and children few, endear to him meeting You, and hasten for him the decree. And whoever does not believe in me, does not attest to my truthfulness, and does not know that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth abundant and prolong his life.\""],[13519,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “O people, it is not lawful for me nor for anyone else of the spoils of the Muslims even the weight of this hair.” He took a hair from the withers of his she-camel, after what God had apportioned for me."],[13520,"The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned me when he wanted to send me with wealth to Abu Sufyan to distribute among Quraysh in Makkah after the conquest. He said: “Find a companion.” ʿAmr b. Umayya al-Damri came to me and said: “I have heard that you intend to set out and are seeking a companion, and I am your companion.” The Messenger of God ﷺ had said: “When you find a companion, inform me.” So I informed him, and he said: “Who?” I said: “ʿAmr b. Umayya al-Damri.” He said: “When he descends into the land of his people, beware of him, for the poet said: ‘Your brother al-Bakri, so do not trust him.’” We set out until we reached al-Abwaʾ. He said: “I need something from my people, so wait for me.” I said: “Go rightly guided.” When he turned away, I remembered the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I tied my camel tightly, then set off urging it quickly. When I was at al-ʿAsafir, there he was confronting me with a group. He said: “I urged my camel on, and I heard him, and when he saw that I had outdistanced him, they turned back, and he came to me and said: ‘I had a need from my people.’ I said: ‘Indeed.’ Then we went on until we arrived in Makkah, and I handed over the wealth to Abu Sufyan.”"],[13521,"O Messenger of God, you forbade incantations, but I use incantations for snakebite. He said: \"Recite them to me.\" So I recited them to him, and he said: \"There is no harm in these; these are covenants.\" He said: Then a man from the Ansar came who used incantations for scorpion stings, and he said: \"Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so.\""],[13522,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God (mighty and sublime) may support the religion through a wicked man.\""],[13523,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"O God, support ʿAli; O God, honor whoever honors ʿAli; O God, abandon whoever abandons ʿAli ؓ.\""],[13524,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif. He used to come out to us at night and narrate to us. One night he was late in coming to us; then he came out to us. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, you were late in coming to us tonight.” He said: “A portion (hizb) of the Qur’an came to me, and I disliked to interrupt it until I had finished it.” When morning came, we asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “How do you divide the Qur’an into portions?” They said: “Three, five, seven, nine, eleven, thirteen (surahs); and what is between Qaf and ‘al-Qur’an al-Majid’ to the end of the Mufassal is a good portion.” Thus narrated al-Walid b. Muslim from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Rahman al-Ta’ifi, from ʿUthman b. ʿAmr b. Aws, from his father; but Wakiʿ, Qurran b. Tammam and others disagreed with him, and narrated it from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Rahman, from ʿUthman b. ʿAbd Allah b. Aws, from his grandfather Aws b. Hudhayfa."],[13525,"The Prophet ﷺ sent with me a sacrificial animal as a voluntary offering and said: “If any of it is injured, then slaughter it, then dip its shoe in its blood and strike it on its side, and leave it between the people and it.”"],[13526,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day he died left nothing except his weapon, his white mule, and a piece of land which he made as charity.”"],[13527,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, “and he recited Surat al-Najm and prostrated, and I prostrated with him.”"],[13528,"So he ordered that he be made thirsty. Then he called for a basin of water and called for the young horses, and they drank. Then 'Amr's horse came and folded its legs and drank. This is the behavior of a half-breed. He said, 'Do you not see?' He said, 'Yes, a half-breed recognizes a half-breed.' It reached 'Umar, and he wrote to him: 'It has reached me what you said to your commander, and it has reached me that you have a sword you call al-Sim'ama, and I have a sharp sword. By Allah, if I place it on your head, I will not lift it until I reach something with it.' He mentioned something from his inside. 'If it pleases you to know whether what I say is true, then return.'"],[13529,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed them and said: 'May Allah brighten [the face of] a person who hears my words and retains them. For many a bearer of jurisprudence has no understanding, and many a bearer of jurisprudence conveys it to one more understanding than himself.'"],[13530,"A letter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to 'Umayr Dhu Murran and whoever accepts Islam from Hamdan. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah to you, besides whom there is no deity. Now then, your acceptance of Islam reached us upon our arrival from the land of the Romans. So rejoice, for Allah has guided you with His guidance. If you bear witness that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, and give zakat, then you have the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger over your blood, your wealth, and the land of Alyun upon which you accepted Islam, its plains, mountains, springs, and pastures, without being wronged or restricted. For charity is not lawful for Muhammad nor for his household. Malik b. Murara al-Rahawi has guarded the unseen, fulfilled the trust, and conveyed the message. I command you, O Dhu Murran, to treat him well, for he is regarded with respect among his people, and may your Lord love you.'"],[13531,"Abu al-Darda': 'As for me, I will not abandon them. Whoever wishes to humble himself, let him humble himself.'"],[13532,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hama.'"],[13533,"From 'Urwa regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar, then from Banu Khansa' b. Mabdhul b. 'Amr b. Ghanm b. Mazin: 'Umayr, and he is given the kunya Abu Dawud b. 'Amir b. Malik b. Khansa' b. Mabdhul."],[13534,"From Abu ʿImran al-Jawni, I think only from Anas b. Malik, he said: Wahb b. ʿUmayr was present at Uhud as a disbeliever and was wounded, so he was among the slain. A man from the Ansar passed by him, recognized him, placed his sword in his belly until it came out of his back, then left him. When night fell and the cold struck him, he made his way to Makkah and recovered. He and Safwan b. Umayyah gathered in the Hijr, and Wahb said, 'Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would love to be the one who kills Muhammad myself.' Safwan said to him, 'How would you do it?' He said, 'I am a swift man whom no one can catch. I will come to him and deceive him, then strike him with the sword and join the horses, and no one will catch me.' Safwan said to him, 'Your dependents with my dependents, and your debt upon me.' So he went out, sharpening his sword and poisoning it, then set out for Madinah, intending only to kill the Prophet ﷺ. When he reached Madinah, ʿUmar b. al-Khattab saw him and was troubled and distressed. He said to the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, 'I have seen Wahb, and his arrival alarms me, for he is a treacherous man. Surround your Prophet.' The Muslims surrounded the Prophet ﷺ. Wahb came and stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'May you have a pleasant morning, O Muhammad.' He said, 'Allah has replaced it for us with something better.' He said, 'I recall you used to say it while you were pleased.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'What has brought you here?' He said, 'I came to ransom your captives.' He said, 'What is the matter with the sword?' He said, 'Indeed, we carried it on the Day of Badr but did not succeed or prevail.' He said, 'What is the thing you said to Safwan in the Hijr: \"Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would be the one who killed Muhammad myself\"?' The Prophet ﷺ informed him of his affair. Wahb said, 'Hah! How did you say?' He repeated it to him. Wahb said, 'You used to tell us news of the people of the earth, and we disbelieved you. Now I see you tell news of the people of heaven. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give me your turban.' The Prophet ﷺ gave him his turban. Then he went out to Makkah. ʿUmar said, 'He came while he was more hateful to me than a pig, then he returned while he was dearer to me than some of my own children.'"],[13535,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ. When they wanted to leave, they said, 'You have memorized everything you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so ask him about nabidh.' So they came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land with bad water that does not suit us except with drink.' He said, 'What is your drink?' They said, 'Nabidh.' He said, 'In what do you drink it?' They said, 'In naqir (a hollowed-out palm trunk).' He said, 'Do not drink in naqir.' They said, 'By Allah, our people will not agree with us on this.' So they returned and asked him, and he told them the same. Then they came again, and he said, 'Do not drink in naqir, lest one of you strikes a blow from which he remains lame until the Day of Resurrection.' They laughed. He said, 'What are you laughing about?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with the truth, we drank in a naqir of ours, and some of us rose against others, and one struck a blow from which he is lame until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[13536,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah, exalted is He, has promised me to admit three hundred thousand of my community into Paradise.' ʿUmayr said, 'O Prophet of Allah, increase for us.' ʿUmar said, 'That is enough for you, O ʿUmayr.' He said, 'What is it to you and me, O Ibn al-Khattab? What harm is it to you if Allah admits us into Paradise?' ʿUmar said, 'Allah, Majestic and Mighty, if He wills, will admit people into Paradise with a single handful or a single scoop.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'ʿUmar has spoken the truth.'"],[13537,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while Adi b. Hatim was in charge of the alms of his people—that is, an agent of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[13538,"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was sent with prophethood, and I do not know any of the Arabs who was more hateful or more averse to him than I, until I joined the Romans and became a Christian among them. When I heard about the good character he called people to and the people who had gathered around him, I traveled until I came to him and stood before him while Suhayb, Bilal, and Salman were with him. He said, 'O Adi b. Hatim, submit and you will be safe.' I said, 'Ah! Ah!' So I made my camel kneel, sat down, pressed my knee against his knee, and said, 'O Messenger of God, what is Islam?' He said, 'You believe in God, His angels, His Books, and His Messengers, and you believe in the divine decree, its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until the treasures of Kisra and Caesar are opened. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until a woman travels from al-Harrah—and there was no Kufah on that day—and circumambulates this Kaʿbah with no protector. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until a money bag goes around seeking someone to accept it, and finds no one, and strikes it against the ground and says, 'Would that you had never existed; would that you were dust.'"],[13539,"A man said, 'When Uthman was killed, no two goats butted heads over it.' I said, 'Rather, many eyes were gouged out over it.'"],[13540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman must not travel more than three [days] except with a dhu mahram.”"],[13541,"“Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Yes. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: ‘O ʿAdī b. Ḥātim, submit and you will be safe.’ I said: ‘What is Islam?’ He said: ‘Testify that there is no god but Allah, and testify that I am the Messenger of Allah, and believe in the divine decrees, all of them: their good and their evil, their sweet and their bitter.’”"],[13542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will not come upon you but a short time until a woman travels in a litter between Makkah and al-Ḥīrah, and no one takes hold of her halter. And there will not come upon one of you but a short time until a man walks with a handful of gold and does not find anyone to accept it. And there is none of you but will be presented to Allah ﷻ with no interpreter between him and Him. So whoever is able to shield himself from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so.'"],[13543,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we do not ask you about the obedience of one who fears Allah and does right, but about one who does such and such, mentioning evil.' He said: 'Fear Allah, and hear and obey.'"],[13544,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs that we send after game, and we eat from what they catch for us?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[13545,"I said: O Messenger of God, I ask you about food that I leave only out of scrupulousness. He said: “Do not leave anything in which you have imitated Christianity.”"],[13546,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O ʿAdi, do not belittle my Companions. The treasures of Kisra will surely be opened, and a woman in a howdah will set out from al-Hirah under the protection of this House, and this wealth will surely be made lawful at the beginning of the day, then it will be cast aside at its end and no one will accept it.” ʿAdi said: I have indeed seen two of these, and the third will surely come to pass."],[13547,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a person in a state of major ritual impurity who sleeps. He said: “He should perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[13548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A time is near when it will be hard for a man to give out the zakat of his wealth.”"],[13549,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever swears an oath over the property of a Muslim man will meet God while He is angry with him.” It was said, “And what about the one who gives it up, O Messenger of God?” He said, “For him is Paradise.”"],[13550,"He threw a stone at a wife of his, and she died. He followed the Messenger of God ﷺ to Tabuk and told him his story. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You pay her blood money, and you do not inherit from her.”"],[13551,"The Messenger of God ﷺ made a protected area around every side of Madinah a barid in extent: its trees are not to be beaten, nor its branches cut, except for a stick used to drive animals."],[13552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his companions to fight, and a man from his companions was struck by an arrow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'This one has made it obligatory.' And they said when he ordered them to fight, 'Then, O Messenger of God, we will not say as the Children of Israel said to Moses: \"Go, you and your Lord, and fight\" to the end of the verse, but we say: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; indeed, we are with you, among the fighters.'"],[13553,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for clothing, and he clothed me with two coarse garments. I saw myself wearing them, being among the most clothed of my companions."],[13554,"When he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said to him, 'What is your name?' He said, 'Nashbah.' He said, 'You are ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd.'"],[13555,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about Paradise, and he mentioned the pool. He said, 'Is there fruit in it?' He said, 'Yes, and in it is a tree called Ṭūbā.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, which tree of our land does it resemble?' He said, 'It does not resemble any tree of your land. Have you been to Syria? There is a tree there called the walnut, which grows on a single trunk and whose top spreads out.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the size of its root?' He said, 'If a young she-camel of your family's camels were to travel, you would not encompass its root until its collarbone breaks from old age.' He said, 'Are there grapes in it?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What is the size of a cluster from it?' He said, 'A month's journey for the piebald crow, without tiring.' He said, 'What is the size of a single grape from it?' He said, 'Your father and mother took a young she-camel, slaughtered it, and skinned its hide, then said, \"Make for us a bucket from it.\"' He said, 'O Messenger of God, will that grape suffice me and my family?' He said, 'Yes, and the generality of your clan.'"],[13556,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a bedouin came and said, “O Messenger of God, I hear you mention a tree in Paradise, and I know of no tree with more thorns than it — meaning the talh (acacia).” He replied, “The mottled buck — meaning the castrated one — in it are seventy colors of food, no one color resembling another.”"],[13557,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade clipping the tails, forelocks, and manes of horses. As for their tails, they are their fly whisks; as for their manes, they are for their warmth; and as for their forelocks, good is tied within them."],[13558,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No servant leaves his house in the morning or evening heading to the mosque except that his steps are — one step an expiation and one step a good deed.”"],[13559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal (sahur) at the end of the night.” And he used to say: “It is the blessed meal.”"],[13560,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, “How was the beginning of your affair?” And he mentioned the hadith."],[13561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rebuked a man who had a Persian bow, saying, \"Throw it away.\" Then he pointed to the Arab bow and said, \"With this and with the spear of qana, you will gain power in the lands and be victorious over your enemy.\""],[13562,"Arfajah’s nose was injured on the Day of al-Kulāb, so he made a nose of silver, but it became foul, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to make a nose of gold."],[13563,"I came to Madinah and entered the mosque while the people were waiting for the prayer. A man came out to us with his head dripping from the ablution he had performed or from a bath he had taken. He led us in prayer. When we had prayed, the people began going to him saying, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about such-and-such? O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about such-and-such?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Thus, O people: indeed the religion of Allah is ease,” three times. Then I went out from the door and departed."],[13564,"When Abu Bakr returned and the people had completed their Hajj, ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd al-Thaqafī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. Then he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to return to his people. He said, \"I fear that they will kill you.\" He replied, \"If they found me sleeping, they would not wake me.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him. He returned to al-Ṭāʾif and served dinner. Thaqīf came to greet him, so he called them to Islam and advised them sincerely. They accused him, disobeyed him, and made him hear such harm as he had not feared from them. They left him, and when the last part of the night came and dawn broke, he stood on an upper room in his house, called the adhān for prayer, and pronounced the shahādah. A man from Quraysh shot him with an arrow and killed him."],[13565,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave him a dinar to buy a sacrificial animal for him. ʿUrwah said: I bought two sheep for him with it, then sold one of them for a dinar and a sheep. “He prayed for blessing for me in trade.” And when he bought dust, he profited from it."],[13566,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ twist the forelock of his horse between his two fingers, then said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13567,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13569,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a market and gave him a dinar, then said: “Buy a sheep for us.” So he went and bought two sheep for a dinar. Then a man met him and he sold him one sheep for a dinar. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ with a dinar and a sheep. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “May Allah bless you in the transaction of your right hand.” He said: “I would stand in the marketplace and not return to my family until I had profited forty thousand.”"],[13570,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A woman may not be married in addition to her maternal aunt or her paternal aunt.”"],[13571,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a delegation of his people. When they entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Has anyone else come to you besides you?” They said: “Yes, a youth of ours whom we left behind with our baggage.” He said: “Send for him.” When I entered upon him while they were with him, he turned to me and said: “The giving hand is the upper one, and the begging hand is the lower one. And what suffices you, then do not ask. For God’s wealth is both asked for and given.”"],[13572,"“A delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Ramadan, and he set up a tent for them in the mosque. When they embraced Islam, they fasted with him.”"],[13573,"Ata' narrated to me, a man from Banu Shaybah, and he was a very old man. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying at this station wearing two sandals of tanned leather.”"],[13574,"The Prophet ﷺ sent ten men as scouts and appointed over them 'Asim b. Thabit al-Ansari, the grandfather of 'Asim b. 'Amr. He mentioned it in full."],[13575,"'Umar b. al-Khattab sent for him to seek his help with some of the sadaqah, but he refused to work for him. Then he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When the Day of Resurrection comes, the ruler will be commanded and made to stand on the bridge of Jahannam. The bridge will be commanded and it will shake violently, and every bone in him will be dislocated from its place. Then Allah will command the bones and they will return to their places. Then He will question him. If he was obedient to Allah, He will seize him and give him a double portion of reward. But if he was disobedient to Allah, the bridge will twist with him and he will fall into Jahannam for seventy autumns.'\""],[13576,"I entered the mosque of Madinah, and the people were saying, \"We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger.\" He said: I said, \"What did they say?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a khutbah on his minbar when a man stood up, took his son by the hand, and led him out of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah curse the leader and the led. Woe to this one one day—to this ummah from so-and-so, the one with the buttocks.\""],[13577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah bt. 'Umar once, then took her back."],[13578,"From ʿIsmah b. Qays, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that he used to seek refuge in his prayer from the trial of the west."],[13579,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq met a man from the Arabs called ʿUfayr b. Abi ʿUfayr. Abu Bakr said to him: Did you hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ anything about love? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Love is inherited, and enmity is inherited.”"],[13580,"One of his paternal uncles came to the Prophet ﷺ and embraced Islam. When he returned, he passed by a mad Bedouin bound in iron. Some of them said to him: Do you have anything with which to treat him, for your companion has brought good? He said yes. He said: I then recited ruqya over him using the Mother of the Book for three days, twice each day, and he recovered. They gave me a hundred sheep, but I did not take them until I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said: Did you say anything other than this? I said no. He said, “Eat them, in the name of God. By my life, whoever eats by a false ruqya—you have eaten by a true ruqya.”"],[13581,"When ʿAli went out to Siffin, he appointed Abu Masʿud as his deputy over Kufah. There were men from the people of Kufah who had hidden themselves from ʿAli, and when he departed they appeared. People would come to Abu Masʿud and say, \"By Allah, Allah has destroyed his enemies and granted victory to the believers.\" Abu Masʿud would say, \"By Allah, I do not consider it a victory or well-being that one of the two parties prevails over the other.\" They said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"There will be reconciliation between the people.\" When ʿAli arrived, they mentioned that to him, and ʿAli said, \"Withdraw from our work.\" He said, \"And why is that?\" He said, \"We have found you not understanding a sound understanding.\" He said, \"As for me, there remains from my understanding what lets me know that the latter is worse.\""],[13582,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: A man from those before you was brought to account, and no good was found for him except that he used to mix with people and was wealthy. He would order his servant to be lenient with the one in difficulty. Allah ﷻ said: We are more entitled to that than him, so be lenient with him. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said in his hadith: We are more entitled than him to be lenient with him, so He was lenient with him."],[13583,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: Men from my companions will surely be raised for me, until when I see them they will be snatched away before me. I will say: My companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."],[13584,"A man from the Ansar, whose kunya was Abu Shu'ayb, prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ and said: Bring with you five. The Prophet ﷺ said: Do you permit the sixth?"],[13585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “What harm would it have done to the owners of this one if they had benefited from its hide?”"],[13586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Every act of kindness is charity.”"],[13587,"While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice from behind me: \"Know, Abā Masʿūd!\" I turned and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ. The whip fell from my hand out of awe of him. He said: \"Indeed, by God, God has more power over you than you have over this one.\""],[13588,"I attended a feast in which Abu Mas‘ud and Qurazah b. Ka‘b were present, and slave girls were singing. I said, “Glory be to Allah! Do you do this while you are companions of Muhammad ﷺ and people of Badr?” They said, “We were granted a dispensation for singing at weddings and for weeping without wailing.”"],[13589,"“It is not from the Sunnah to pray before the imam comes out on the day of Eid.”"],[13590,"We were with Ali when Abu Mas‘ud came to him. Ali said to him, “I see that you give legal opinions to the people.” He said, “Indeed I tell them that the last ones are worse.” Ali said, “Tell us what you heard the Prophet ﷺ saying about the hundred.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘A hundred years will not pass over the people while on the earth there is a blinking eye.’” Ali said, “You erred. He only said, ‘For whoever is on the face of the earth on that day – and there is no ease or joy except after the hundred.’”"],[13591,"Abu Mas‘ud said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military campaign, and the people were afflicted with hardship until I saw gloom on the faces of the Muslims and joy on the faces of the hypocrites. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he said, “By Allah, the sun will not set until Allah brings you provision.” Then Uthman knew that Allah and His Messenger would be truthful, so Uthman purchased forty camels with the food that was on them and sent nine of them to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said, “What is this?” They said, “Uthman has gifted it to you.” Then joy was recognized on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gloom on the faces of the hypocrites. I saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was visible, supplicating for Uthman with a supplication I never heard him make for anyone before or after him: “O Allah, give Uthman; O Allah, do for Uthman.”"],[13592,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a garden and then said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you.” Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered. Then he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you.” Then Umar entered. Then he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you. O Allah, make him Ali.” Then Ali ؓ entered."],[13593,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat down in front of him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, as for greeting you with peace, we know it, but as for invoking blessings upon you, tell us how we should invoke blessings upon you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until we wished that the man who asked him had not asked him. Then he said, “When you invoke blessings upon me, say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[13594,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night?\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, can we bear a third of the Qur'an? He said: \"Is one of you unable to do so with Qul huwa Allahu ahad?\""],[13595,"Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari or Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud narrated that both of them said that they accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and that Jibril (Gabriel) came to the Prophet ﷺ after the sun had set. Jibril said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Dhuhr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the shadow of everything was equal to its height and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Asr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the sun had disappeared and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Maghrib prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the red twilight vanished and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Isha prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the dawn broke and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Fajr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him the next day when the shadow of everything was similar to its previous day's length and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Dhuhr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Dhuhr prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the shadow of everything was similar to its length the previous day and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Asr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Asr prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the sun had set at a particular time and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Maghrib prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when a portion of the night had passed and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Isha prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Isha prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when it was dawn and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Fajr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril said, \"There is a time period between these two (Fajr and sunrise).\""],[13596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh, \"This affair will continue to be among you, and you will be its guardians, as long as you do not introduce innovations. Then He will set upon you the worst of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped.\""],[13597,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I perform a deed and keep it secret, but it becomes known, and I am pleased about that.\" He said, \"Two rewards are written for you: the reward of the secret and the reward of the open.\""],[13598,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and that was at the sun's decline. He said, \"Stand and pray,\" so he stood and prayed Zuhr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when his shadow was equal to his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed ʿAsr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when the sun had set and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Maghrib as three rakʿahs. Then he came to him when the twilight had disappeared and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed the later ʿIsha' as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when dawn broke and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Fajr as two rakʿahs. Then he came to him the next day for Zuhr when his shadow was equal to his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Zuhr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when his shadow was twice his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed ʿAsr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him at the first time when the sun had set and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Maghrib as three rakʿahs. Then he came to him after the twilight had disappeared and it had become dark and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed the later ʿIsha' as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him after dawn had risen and it had become bright and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Subh as two rakʿahs. Then Jibril ﷺ said to him, \"Between these two is the time for prayer.\""],[13599,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ should come forward and lead them in prayer.”"],[13600,"I heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir say: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The two things I fear most for my community are their pursuit of signs and desires and their abandonment of the Qur'an and prayers; that the hypocrites learn it and argue with it against the people of knowledge.”"],[13601,"He heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir al-Juhani say: “For every gesture a man makes with his hand during prayer, a good deed or a degree is recorded for each finger.”"],[13602,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wickedness is seventy parts: for the Berbers sixty-nine parts, and for jinn and humans one part.”"],[13603,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People are three: one who is safe, one who gains, and one who is ruined.”"],[13604,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Abu Bakr, \"When do you perform the Witr prayer?\" He replied, \"I pray two by two units of prayer, and then I perform the Witr prayer before I sleep.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"A cautious believer.\" The Prophet ﷺ asked Umar bin Khattab, \"How do you perform the Witr prayer?\" He replied, \"I pray two by two units of prayer, and then I sleep until I perform the Witr prayer at the end of the night.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"A strong believer.\""],[13605,"Abu Ayyub said to him: \"Why do you delay this prayer when you are one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Someone who did not accompany him will see you and think that this is its time.\" So we said: \"O Abu Ayyub, how did you use to pray it?\" He said: \"We used to pray it when the sun declines, hastening before the stars appear.\" \"Is that so, ʿUqbah?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[13606,"When {So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great} (Quran 56:96) was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Place it in your bowing.” And when “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” (Quran 87:1) was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Place it in your prostration.”"],[13607,"She vowed to perform Hajj walking barefoot and unveiled. ʿUqbah asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Tell her to cover her head, ride, and fast for three days.”"],[13608,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whenever a person embarks on a journey alone, while remembering and mentioning Allah, an angel accompanies him. And whenever a person is alone with his hair or something similar, a devil accompanies him.\""],[13609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Let her ride, wear clothes, and fast.”"],[13610,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: He saw Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left hand and said: “What is the matter with her that she eats with her left hand?” She said: “O Prophet of Allah, there is a sore on my right hand.” He said to her: “Even if it were a cow’s death?” Then the plague seized her and killed her."],[13611,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wears silk in this world, it will be forbidden for him in the Hereafter.”"],[13612,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Lands will be opened for you, and God will suffice you, so let none of you be too weak to play with his arrow.”"],[13613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and completes his ablution, then raises his head to the sky and says, ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God alone with no partner, and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger,’ eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter from whichever of them he wishes.”"],[13614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he applied kohl, applied it an odd number of times, and when he cleaned himself with stones, he cleaned himself an odd number of times."],[13615,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then prays a prayer in which he is mindful until he completes it, he will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[13616,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, will admit to Paradise because of a single arrow: its maker, who seeks reward in his craft for good, and the one who shoots it, and the one who gifts it.\" And he said: \"Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. Everything a man amuses himself with is false except training his horse, shooting with his bow, and playing with his wife.\""],[13617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated it to me, so I went to him and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, will admit three people to Paradise: its maker, who seeks reward in his craft for good, the one who shoots it, and the one who hands it to him. Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. And there is no amusement except three: a man training his horse, playing with his wife, and shooting with his bow. And whoever abandons archery after having learned it, out of aversion to it, then it is a blessing he has rejected—or he abandoned it.\""],[13618,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you of the best thing with which those who seek refuge seek refuge? Say: 'I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,' and say: 'I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.'\""],[13619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions. ʿUqba said: A jadhaʿa fell to my share. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a jadhaʿa has fallen to my share. He said: \"Sacrifice it.\""],[13620,"While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between al-Juhfa and al-Abwāʾ, a wind and darkness overtook us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began seeking refuge with \"I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak\" and \"I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,\" and he said: \"O ʿUqba, seek refuge, for no one has sought refuge with the like of them.\" He said: Then I heard him leading us in prayer with them."],[13621,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will never recite a surah more beloved to me, nor more effective, than 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.' So if you can manage not to abandon it in any prayer, do so.\""],[13622,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh b. Salmān from Muʿādh b. ʿAbdullāh b. Khubayb from his father from ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī that he said: While I was leading the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his mount during a military expedition, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say, O ʿUqba.\" I said: What shall I say? He said it a third time. I said: What shall I say? He said: \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" and he recited the surah until he completed it. Then he recited, \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,\" and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he recited, \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,\" and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he said: \"Refuge has never been sought with the like of them.\""],[13623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be rulers after me who will lead you in prayer. If they complete its bowing and prostration, it is for you and for them. If they fall short in it, it is for you and against them.\""],[13624,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we used to take turns herding the animals. When it was my turn, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was addressing the people, and I heard him say: \"There is no Muslim who performs ablution and does it well, then stands in his prayer and understands what he is saying in it, except that he departs as on the day his mother gave birth to him, free of sins, with no sin upon him.\" I could not contain myself at that and said: Excellent! Excellent!"],[13625,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Any woman married off by two guardians belongs to the first of them.”"],[13626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tonight verses were sent down to me, the like of which have never been seen: ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak’ and ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of people.’”"],[13627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit during Ramadan and said, \"I have stood on this pulpit and I know the Night of Qadr. So seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.\""],[13628,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ being gifted a leather container of honey. He accepted it and said: 'Protect my mountain pass,' so he protected it for him and wrote a document for him."],[13629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Preserve me in my Companions and my in-laws. Whoever preserves me in them, Allah will preserve him in this world and the Hereafter. And whoever does not preserve me in them, Allah will turn away from him, and whoever Allah turns away from is near to being seized.\""],[13630,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Upon you is the remembrance of your Lord, and pray your prayers at their earliest times, for Allah, exalted be He, will multiply for you.\""],[13631,"ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl b. Hishām, and he had no offspring. He had fled on the Day of the Conquest, until his wife asked the Prophet ﷺ for safe-conduct for him—she was Umm Ḥakīm bt. al-Ḥārith b. Hishām—and he granted him safety. She caught up with him in Yemen and brought him back to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he stood up, embraced him, and said: \"Welcome to the emigrant rider.\""],[13632,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day I came to him: \"Welcome to the emigrant rider, welcome to the emigrant rider.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I will not leave any expense I spent against you without spending the like of it in the way of God.\""],[13633,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ to Bahrain. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went out on a military expedition and we went out with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ dozed, then woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" We discussed who the ʿAmr might be. Then he dozed a second time, woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" Then he dozed a third time, woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" We said: \"Who is ʿAmr, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ.\" They said: \"What is the matter with him?\" He said: \"I remembered him. When I called people to give charity, he would come with charity and give generously. I would say: 'Where did you get this, O ʿAmr?' He would say: 'From God.' ʿAmr spoke the truth. ʿAmr has much good with God.\" Zuhayr said: \"When the strife occurred, I said I will follow this man about whom the Messenger of God said what he said, and I did not part from him.\""],[13634,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to them in the year of al-Muraysīʿ when they became Muslim: \"Part of the completeness of your Islam is that you pay the zakah on your wealth.\""],[13635,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar ؓ died while the quarters of Makkah were only called 'the freed ones': whoever was in need dwelled, and whoever was well-off housed others.\""],[13636,"I heard ʿAlqamah b. al-Ḥuwayrith, one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The fornication of the two eyes is looking.'\""],[13637,"\"I was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He built a dome for us near the house of Al-Mughirah. Bilal used to bring our iftar during Ramadan while we were traveling excessively.\""],[13638,"\"May you not be alarmed, may you be fatherless. The Messenger of God ﷺ had been employing you, and may you not be alarmed.\"… the hadith."],[13639,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for me his grant from him concerning this water where I am.”"],[13640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, during the expedition of Tabuk, said, “If the plague occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if you are elsewhere, do not advance into it.”"],[13641,"Ziyād said to him: \"You are of the bran of the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.\""],[13642,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on an expedition. When we returned heading back to Madinah, the wife of a man who had been martyred with the Messenger of God ﷺ wept. He said: \"Who is this weeping woman?\" They said: \"Fāṭimah bt. ʿAdī.\" He said: \"You belong to ʿAʾidh b. ʿAmr.\" So he married her to his father and entrusted her to him."],[13643,"Sumayr b. Zuhayr al-Jasri said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother Salamah b. Zuhayr went out as an emigrant to Allah ﷻ and His Messenger, and the shepherds of your riding camels from Banu Ghifar met him and killed him during the sacred month. There had been blood between us and them in the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and asked them about that. They said: We found him driving your riding camels, so we wanted to seize him, but he resisted us, so we killed him. I do not know whether he made them swear an oath or believed them, except that he asked him about his brother's Islam but found no proof, so he paid him the blood money for the sanctity of the sacred month: fifty camels. He said: Those camels remained in his family's possession as the best livestock and the greatest in blessing."],[13644,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ expressing fear for his ummah regarding six traits: the rule of youths, the proliferation of police, bribery in judgment, the severing of family ties, the cheapening of blood, and a generation that takes the Qur'an as musical instruments, putting forward a man who is not the most knowledgeable among them nor the most virtuous, so that he may sing to them."],[13645,"So he informed him, and he gathered us together. He kept pressuring the Christian until he confessed. Then he ordered a piece of wood for him, and it was carved. Then he said: 'These people have a covenant, so fulfill your covenant with them as long as they fulfill theirs with you. But if they break it, then they have no covenant.' And he ordered for him to be crucified."],[13646,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us at midday, frightened, and said: 'Obey me as long as I am among you, and hold fast to the Book of God: make lawful what it makes lawful and forbid what it forbids.'"],[13647,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Visit the sick and follow funerals.'"],[13648,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “War is deception.”"],[13649,"To the Messenger of God ﷺ: “My companion whom you saw with me bought a bow and gave it to me as a gift—should I take it from him?” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “No.” Then he waited until the beginning of the year, came back to him and said, “O Messenger of God ﷺ, should I take it?” He said: “No.” Then he waited until the beginning of the next year and said, “Should I take that bow, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No.” He said, “Should I not take it, O Messenger of God, so that it remains with him?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do you want to meet God, O ʿAwf, on the Day of Resurrection with an ember from Hell between your shoulder blades?”"],[13650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ judged between two men. The one against whom judgment was given said, “God is sufficient for me, and how excellent a Trustee is He.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring him back”—or he said, “Call the man to me?”—and said: “God praises prudence and blames incapacity. When something”—or he said, “a matter”—“overwhelms you, say, ‘God is sufficient for me, and how excellent a Trustee is He.’”"],[13651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of sins that are not forgiven: misappropriation—whoever misappropriates anything will bring it on the Day of Resurrection—and consuming usury. Whoever consumes usury will be raised on the Day of Resurrection insane, thrashing about.” Then he recited: “Those who consume usury do not stand except as one stands whom Satan has touched with madness.”"],[13652,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was observing iʿtikaf in the last ten nights of Ramadan. When it was the night of the twenty-third, he said: “Whoever would like to stand in prayer with us this night, let him stand in my place until a third of the night had passed.” Then he left, and I walked with him to Qutaybah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would lead us in prayer this night? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is enough for a man to stand with the imam until he departs; the standing of a night will be recorded for him.”"],[13653,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Storytellers are three: a ruler, one commanded, or a conceited boaster.”"],[13654,"I heard ʿAwf b. Malik say: I stood with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he began by using the toothstick, then performed ablution, then stood and prayed. I stood with him. He began and opened the recitation from al-Baqarah; he did not pass by a verse of mercy without stopping and asking, nor pass by a verse of punishment without stopping and seeking refuge. Then he bowed and remained bowing for the length of his standing, saying in his bowing: “Glory be to the Possessor of might, dominion, pride, and greatness.” Then he recited Al ʿImran, then surah by surah, doing the same."],[13655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and upon whom you invoke blessings and who invoke blessings upon you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not then oppose them in that case? He said: “No, as long as they establish the prayer among you. Whoever has a ruler appointed over him and sees from him something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he does of disobedience to Allah, but he should not withdraw his hand from obedience.”"],[13656,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Dreams are of three kinds: among them are terrifying things from Satan to sadden the son of Adam; among them are what a man is concerned with in his waking state and sees in his sleep; and among them is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood.” I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: “I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O ʿAwf, count six things before the Hour: the first of them is my death; then the one that follows it is the conquest of Jerusalem; then the one that follows it is a death that will befall my ummah in Syria and will consume them like the sudden death of sheep; then the one that follows it is that wealth will overflow among you until a man is given a hundred dinars and remains dissatisfied with them; then the one that follows it is a trial that will occur among you and no Arab household will remain but it will enter it; then the one that follows it is that the Banu al-Asfar will make a peace treaty with you, and at the end of it they will gather eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand men.”"],[13658,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among them are the abdal, and by them you are granted victory and by them you are given provision.\""],[13659,"He entered the mosque leaning on Dhu Kalaʿ while Kaʿb was telling stories to the people. ʿAwf said to Dhu Kalaʿ: \"Will you not forbid this nephew of yours from what he is doing? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one tells stories to the people except a ruler, one commanded, or a boaster.'\""],[13660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Before the Dajjal there will be years of deception, in which rain will be abundant and vegetation will be scarce, the truthful will be disbelieved, the liar will be believed, the treacherous will be trusted, the trustworthy will be suspected, and the ruwaybidah will speak in them.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?\" He said: \"One to whom no heed is paid.\""],[13661,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to avarice, and from a desire that reverts to greed, and from greed that leads to what is not desired.\""],[13662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Jews split into seventy-one sects, the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, my ummah will certainly split into seventy-three sects: one in Paradise and seventy-two in the Fire.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they?\" He said: \"The main body.\""],[13663,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with six or seven or eight men. He said: \"Give me your pledge.\" We pledged to him, and he took from us what he took from the women. Then he followed that with a light word and said: \"Do not ask people for anything.\""],[13664,"You have hastened its reward, and I will not eat it. Abu ʿUbaydah said the same. The Prophet ﷺ preceded me, and when he saw me he said: \"O owner of the camel.\""],[13665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted with us for rest one night, and each one of us spread out his forearm on his mount's forearm. I woke up part of the night, and there was the Prophet's she-camel with no one in front of it. I set out looking for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and found Muadh b. Jabal and Abdullah b. Qays standing. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said, 'We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley,' like the sound of a millstone. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of intercession.' He said, 'You are among the people of my intercession.' Then we went together racing to the people, and found the people alarmed and missing their Prophet. He said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of your intercession.' When they gathered around him, he said: 'I call you to witness that my intercession is for whoever of my nation dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[13666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My intercession is for whoever of my nation dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[13667,"The Prophet ﷺ judged between two men, and the one against whom judgment was given said, 'Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Bring the man back to me,' and said, 'What did you say?' So he told him. Then he said: 'Allah blames for incapacity, but you must be diligent. If a matter overwhelms you, say: Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'"],[13668,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day: 'I have come to know the last person of Paradise to enter Paradise. He used to ask Allah to keep him away from the Fire, but he did not ask for Paradise. When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, and he remains between that, he will say, \"O Lord, what is there for me here?\" He will say, \"This is what you used to ask Me for, O son of Adam.\" He will say, \"Yes, O Lord.\" While he is like that, a tree from the gate of Paradise appears to him, extending inside Paradise. He will say, \"O Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may eat from its fruit and shade myself in its shade.\" He will say, \"O son of Adam, did you not used to ask Me?\" He will say, \"O Lord, who is like You?\" He will keep seeing something better than something else and asking, until it is said to him, \"Go, and you will have what your feet walk over and what your eyes see.\" So he will walk until his feet are tired. He gestured with his hand and said, \"This and this.\" Then it is said, \"This is for you, and the like of it with it.\" He said: He will be pleased, so much so that He will give him something He has not given anyone among the people of Paradise. He will say, \"If I were permitted, I would feed the people of Paradise food and drink and clothing from what Allah has given me, and it would not diminish anything for me.\""],[13669,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus from his pubic area to his throat, churning, is better for him than to have it filled with poetry.\""],[13670,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one should relate stories to the people except a commander, one commanded to do so, or a schemer.\""],[13671,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military expedition. A man said, 'I will go out with you on condition that you give me a share of the spoils.' Then he said, 'By Allah, I do not know whether you will gain spoils or not, but give me something fixed.' So I gave him three dinars. We went on the expedition and obtained spoils. I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'I find for him in this world and the Hereafter nothing but these three dinars that he took.'"],[13672,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said to him: \"Hold on to six things before the Hour\" - the hadith."],[13673,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “My community is three thirds: a third will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment; a third will be given an easy reckoning, then will enter Paradise; and a third will be purged and exposed. Then the angels will come and say, ‘We found them saying, “There is no god but Allah alone,”’ and Allah will say, ‘They have spoken the truth; there is no god but Me. Admit them into Paradise for saying, “There is no god but Allah alone.” And carry their sins upon the people who denied the truth.’ This is the verse in which Allah, Exalted is He, said: {and they will surely carry their own burdens and other burdens along with their own burdens} and its confirmation is in the verse in which He mentioned the angels. Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, said: {Then We made those whom We chose from among Our servants inherit the Book} and He made them three groups, and they are all categories: {among them is one who wrongs himself}—this is the one who is exposed and purged; {and among them is one who is moderate}—he is the one given an easy reckoning; {and among them is one who is foremost in good deeds by Allah’s permission}—this is the one who enters Paradise without reckoning or punishment. By Allah’s permission they will all enter it together, with no distinction made between them. {They will be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their clothing therein will be silk. And they will say, “Praise be to Allah who has removed from us sorrow. Indeed, our Lord is Forgiving and Appreciative—He who has settled us in the home of permanence out of His bounty. Neither fatigue will touch us therein, nor will weariness touch us therein.” And those who disbelieve will have the fire of Hell; neither will it be decreed for them that they die, nor will its punishment be lightened for them. Thus do We recompense every ungrateful one.}”"],[13674,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a tent of his and said, “O Messenger of Allah, may I enter?” He said, “Enter.” I said, “All of me?” He said, “All of you.” Then he said: “Hold fast to six things that will occur before the Hour. The first of them is the death of your Prophet,” and I wept. “Then the conquest of the Holy House (Jerusalem); then a tribulation that will enter every house of hair and clay; then wealth will overflow among you until a man will be given a hundred dinars and will be displeased with it; then a plague that will be among people like the quʿāṣ of sheep; and then a truce between you and the Banū al-Aṣfar, but they will betray you and march against you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.”"],[13675,"My father’s delegation came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him as a young boy. He ordered two cloaks for each man and ordered one cloak for me. When we departed, one of the men sold me one of his two cloaks, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing two cloaks. He looked at me and said, “Where did you get this?” I said, “I bought them from so-and-so.” He said, “You were more entitled to it than he, since he squandered what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given him.”"],[13676,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the sons of the Anṣār, the sons of the sons of the Anṣār, and the clients of the Anṣār.”"],[13677,"The Banū Murra sent me with the zakāt of their wealth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I arrived before him in Madinah and found him sitting among the Emigrants and the Anṣār. I came to him with camels that were like the roots of the arṭā tree. He said, “Who is the man?” I said, “ʿIkrāsh b. Dhuʾayb.” He said, “Trace your lineage upward.” I said, “Son of Ḥurqūṣ b. Jaʿd b. ʿAmr b. al-Nazzāl b. Murra b. ʿUbayd, and these are the zakāt camels of the Banū Murra b. ʿUbayd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled then said, “These are the camels of my people; this is the zakāt of my people.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be branded with the brand of zakāt camels and added to them. Then he took my hand and went with me to the house of Umm Salama and said, “Is there any food?” A large bowl with tharīd and meat was brought to us, and we began to eat from it. I began to move my hand around its sides, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his left hand over my right hand and said, “O ʿIkrāsh, eat from one place, for it is one food.” Then a tray was brought to us containing different kinds of fresh dates. I began eating from what was in front of me, while the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved about the tray. Then he said, “O ʿIkrāsh, eat from wherever you wish, for it is not one kind.” Then water was brought to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his hands and wiped his face, forearms, and head with the moisture of his palms, then said, “O ʿIkrāsh, this is the ablution for what fire has changed.”"],[13678,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Hour will not come until a man from the clients rules over the people; he will be called Jahjāh.”"],[13679,"ʿAkkāf b. Wadāʿa al-Hilālī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?” He said, “No.” He said, “Nor a slave girl?” He said, “No.” He said, “And you are healthy and well-off?” He said, “Yes, praise be to Allah.” He said, “Then you are among the brothers of the devils. Either you will be one of the monks of the Christians, and then you are one of them, or you will be one of us, and then do as we do. For part of our sunna is marriage. The worst of you are your unmarried, and the most contemptible of your dead are your unmarried. Do you seek to entice the devils? He has no weapon against the righteous among men and women more effective than celibacy, except for the married—those are the purified, the ones kept free from indecency. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf! They are the female companions of David, the female companions of Joseph, and the female companions of Kursuf.” ʿAṭiyya said, “Who is Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “A man among the Children of Israel who lived on one of the coasts of the sea, fasting by day and standing in prayer by night, never slackening in fasting or prayer. After that he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty because of a woman he fell in love with, and he abandoned the worship of his Lord, Mighty and Exalted. Then Allah reached him despite what had passed from him, and Allah turned to him in mercy. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf! Marry, for you are among the sinners.” ʿAkkāf said, “I will not leave, O Messenger of Allah, until you marry me to whomever you wish.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have married you, in the name of Allah and with His blessing, to Karīma bt. Kulthūm al-Ḥimyarī.”"],[13680,"Some people made noise near the Prophet ﷺ, and one of his companions said, “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would send someone to them to forbid them from this.” He said, “If I sent someone to them and forbade them from going to al-Ḥajūn, some of them would still go there even if they had no need of it.”"],[13681,"He requested a piece of land from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Wādī al-Qurā, and today it is called Buwayra of ʿUtayr.” He said, “And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he camped at Tabūk and prayed in Wādī al-Qurā.”"],[13682,"He wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and began with himself."],[13683,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Learn from your lineage that which connects you to your relatives, for maintaining family ties is a source of love for your family, wealth, and a means of prolonging your life.\""],[13684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this foul tree should not come near our mosque,\" meaning garlic."],[13685,"To his right, and I did not wait long before a woman came and stood behind the two of them. The young man said the takbir, so the two of them said the takbir. Then he bowed, so the two of them bowed. Then he prostrated, so the two of them prostrated. I said: \"O Abbas, a great matter!\" Al-Abbas said: \"A great matter indeed. Do you know the young man?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"He is Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew. Do you know who the woman is?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"This is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. Abd al-Uzza, the mistress of the women of Quraysh, the wife of my nephew. And this is Ali b. Abi Talib, my nephew.\" My nephew claims that his Lord, the Lord of the heavens and the earth, commanded him with this religion. By Allah, I do not know anyone on the face of the earth upon this religion other than these three.\""],[13686,"We entered upon al-Hasan during the severe pain that had afflicted him. A man said to him, 'I feel sorry for you for what I see.' He said, 'Brother, do not. By Allah, whatever is dearer to me is dearer to Allah. He said: {Whatever affliction befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.} So this is what my hands have earned. Then afterward the pardon of my Lord ﷻ will come to me in what remains.'"],[13687,"From Sabrah b. Ma'bad, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: A group of people from the common folk gathered with Mu'awiyah. He said, 'Let each man among you narrate a noble deed of his people and what virtue was among them.' The people narrated until the narration reached a young man from Juhaynah, and he narrated a narration but was unable to complete it. 'Imran b. al-Husayn turned to him and said, 'Speak, O brother of Juhaynah, with your mouth entirely, and I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Juhaynah are from me and I am from them. They became angry for my anger and pleased for my pleasure. I become angry for their anger and pleased for their pleasure. Whoever angers them has angered me, and whoever angers me has angered Allah.\"' Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan said, 'You have lied. The narration only came concerning Quraysh.' He said..."],[13688,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said to a man: “Did you fast any of the middle days of this month, meaning Shaʿbān?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then when you break your fast of Ramadan, fast one or two days.”"],[13689,"Part of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: “O Allah, forgive me for what I have done mistakenly, what I have done deliberately, what I have concealed, what I have declared openly, and what I have done out of ignorance.”"],[13690,"“Mutʿah is in the Book of Allah; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid it, and no prohibition concerning it was revealed.” He said: “A man expressed his opinion about it to whatever extent he did.” The wording is that of the hadith of ʿĀrim. ʿĀrim and Khālid b. Khidāsh said: Saʿīd al-Barrād, and he is Ibn Abī Khayrah. Ibrāhīm b. al-Ḥasan said in his hadith: “He did not forbid it,” and did not mention the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[13691,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves and neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[13692,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proclaimed the talbiyah for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah.”"],[13693,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said: “We performed Tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice.” He said: “A man expressed his opinion as he wished.”"],[13694,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, sincerely from his heart”—and he gestured with his hand toward the skin of his chest—“Allah will make his flesh forbidden to the Fire.”"],[13695,"\"On the Day of Judgment, the best of Allah's servants are those who constantly praise Him, and then a group of my ummah will never cease to fight against those who provoke them from the people of polytheism until they fight against the Dajjal.\""],[13696,"“I am narrating to you a hadith. If I recover from this pain of mine, do not relate it; and if I pass on my way, then relate it if you see fit, or leave it. We performed Tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not forbid it to us until he died.” He said: “A man sees it according to his own opinion.”"],[13697,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “Then for what do the workers act?” He said, “Act, for everyone is facilitated toward that for which he was created.”"],[13698,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum.” He returned the greeting, and the man sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Ten.” Then another came and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Llāh.” He returned the greeting, and the man sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Twenty.” Then another came and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Llāh wa barakātuh.” He returned the greeting and said, “Thirty.”"],[13699,"He said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see the effect of His blessing upon him.”"],[13700,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “People will come out of the Fire through the intercession of the intercessors and enter Paradise, and they will be called the Jahannamīs.”"],[13701,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will bring out of the Fire a people by my intercession; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun.\""],[13702,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ, and they traveled through the night until, when they were near dawn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted for a rest, and sleep overcame them until the sun rose. The first to wake from his sleep was Abu Bakr, and no one would wake the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his sleep until the Prophet ﷺ woke on his own. Then ʿUmar woke and did something near his head; he began saying takbir and raising his voice until the Prophet ﷺ woke. When he saw that the sun had risen, he said: \"Depart.\" He traveled with us until the sun became bright, then he dismounted and led us in prayer. One man from the group withdrew and did not pray with us. When he finished, he said: \"O so-and-so, what prevented you from praying with us?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" So he commanded him to perform tayammum with clean earth, and he prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead with a small group of riders to search for water, for we had become severely thirsty. While we were traveling, we came upon a woman with her legs dangling between two water skins. We said to her: \"Where is water?\" She said: \"Alas, alas, there is no water.\" We said: \"How far are you from water?\" She said: \"A day and a night.\" We said: \"Come with us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said: \"And what is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" We did not give her any choice in the matter until we brought her before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We opened the two spouts and drank, forty thirsty men, until we were satisfied, and we filled every water skin and vessel we had. Then he said to us: \"Bring whatever you have.\" We gathered for her bits of bread and dates until we made a bundle for her. He said: \"Go and feed this to your family, and know that we have not taken anything from your water.\" When she came to her people, she said: \"We have met the most enchanting of people, or he is a prophet as they claimed.\" So Allah guided that tribe through that woman, and she and they embraced Islam."],[13703,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor and needy, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[13704,"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ate his fill of a morning or evening meal until he met Allah, Mighty and Exalted."],[13705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Dajjal will emerge from the direction of Isfahan.”"],[13706,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Dajjal has eaten food and walked in the markets.”"],[13707,"This verse was revealed: “O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing,” while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Some of the people were dozing and some had dispersed, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his voice reciting it, and they gathered around the Prophet ﷺ, saying the Hour had come. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it and said, “Do you know which day that is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That is when Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, says to Adam: ‘Arise, O Adam, and send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He says, ‘What is the delegation of the Fire?’ He says, ‘Send forth from every thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.’” The people were struck silent, none of them showing even a tooth. He then said, “Work and rejoice, for you are among mankind but like a black mark on a camel’s back, or like a spot on a beast’s foreleg.” Then he said, “Know that you are alongside two creations that never enter anything without multiplying it: Yaʾjuj and Maʾjuj, along with those of the children of Iblis who perished.”"],[13708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[13709,"A man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them and freed two of them."],[13710,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mutilation. He would say: “Mutilation includes a man’s swearing that he will perform Hajj walking barefoot and on foot. Whoever swears to any of that, let him expiate for his oath and then ride.”"],[13711,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he made a stop for us to rest until the end of the night. We awoke with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the sun had risen. He said, “Depart! Depart!” So we departed until the sun was in the middle of the sky; then he dismounted, ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer. Each man among us prayed two rakʿahs, then he led us in prayer. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, should we repeat it tomorrow at its proper time?” He said, “Allah forbids us from riba, and would He accept it from us?”"],[13712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah ﷻ has chosen this religion for Himself, and nothing befits your religion except generosity and good character, so adorn your religion with both of them.”"],[13713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not deliver a sermon to us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[13714,"From ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn and Abū Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about His saying: {And pleasant dwellings in the Gardens of ʿAdn}. He said, \"A palace in Paradise of pearl, in which are seventy mansions of red ruby; in every mansion seventy rooms of green emerald; in every room seventy couches; on every couch seventy beddings of every color; on every bedding a woman; in every room seventy tables; on every table seventy kinds of food; in every room seventy serving boys and serving girls. And the believer will be given strength enough to come to all of that in a single morning.\""],[13715,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ spoke truth, and you lied.\""],[13716,"A man freed six slaves during his illness, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and enslaved four."],[13717,"A man from the Ansar freed six heads at his death, and he did not own any others. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he called them and cast lots among them; he allowed two and returned four to slavery."],[13718,"He passed by a storyteller who was telling stories. When he finished, he asked him, and he said: Verily we belong to God and to Him we return. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Recite the Qur’an and ask God by it before a people come who recite the Qur’an and ask people by it.\""],[13719,"We performed tamattuʿ during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not forbid us from it, and God ﷻ did not reveal anything concerning it."],[13720,"A man freed six of his slaves at the time of his death, and he had no wealth besides them. “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery.”"],[13721,"“Indeed the Prophet ﷺ flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals, forty lashes.”"],[13722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[13723,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no obedience to a creature in disobeying Allah.\""],[13724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it.'"],[13725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be four tribulations: a tribulation in which blood is deemed lawful, a second in which blood and wealth are deemed lawful, and a third in which blood, wealth, and private parts are deemed lawful.”"],[13726,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A man standing in a row in the cause of Allah is better than the worship of sixty years.”"],[13727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears a binding oath falsely and deliberately, let him take his place in the Fire with his face.\""],[13728,"A man freed six slaves at his death when he had no property besides them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ drew lots among them: he kept four as slaves and freed two."],[13729,"That when the death of the Negus reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, “Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.” He stood and prayed over him with the people behind him."],[13730,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him.”"],[13731,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade hantam jars."],[13732,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from stolen wealth.\""],[13733,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would narrate to us at night about the Children of Israel, and we would not get up except for a great prayer."],[13734,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Makkah, he stayed there for eighteen nights praying with the people of Makkah two rak'ahs except for Maghrib. Then he would say: \"O people of Makkah, complete your prayer, for we are a traveling people.\""],[13735,"We were with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his voice with these two verses: “O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nurses.” When we heard that, we urged on our mounts, knowing he was about to say something. When they gathered around him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know which day that is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That is the day when Adam will call out, and his Lord will call him, saying, ‘Adam, arise and send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He will say, ‘O Lord, how many are to be sent to the Fire?’ He will say, ‘Of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.’” When they heard that, they were struck speechless, so much so that none of them showed a smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what had come upon them, he smiled and said, “Work and receive glad tidings, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, with you are two creatures that have never been with anyone except that they made them numerous.” They said, “Who, O Prophet of Allah?” He said, “Gog and Magog, and those who perished among the children of Adam, and Iblis.” Then he said, “Work and receive glad tidings, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among the people only like a mole on the side of a camel, or a mark on the foreleg of a beast.”"],[13736,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “All of modesty is good.”"],[13737,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “What do you think about what people do today and toil in — is it something that was decreed for them and has passed from a predestination that preceded, or is it in what they will face from what their Prophet brought them and with which the proof was established against them?” He said, “Rather, it is something that was decreed for them and has passed.” He said, “Then why do they work?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever Allah created for one of the two stations, He grants him success for its action.” He said, “The confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah: ‘By the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness.’”"],[13738,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said: We were discussing righteousness in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began to narrate to us, saying: “Among the nations before you there was a devoted worshiper, an owner of a hermitage, called Jurayj. He had a mother who would come to him and call him, and he would look down at her and speak to her. One day she came to him while he was in his prayer, facing it, and she called him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imitated her, placing his hand on his forehead. She kept calling him, raising her head and placing her hand on her forehead: “O Jurayj, O Jurayj,” three times, each time three times. All the while Jurayj said, “O Lord, my mother or my prayer?” She became angry and said, “O Allah, do not let Jurayj die until he looks at the faces of prostitutes.” He said, “The daughter of the king of the village became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said to her, ‘Who did this to you? Who is your companion?’ She said, ‘He is the owner of the hermitage, Jurayj.’ He was unaware until he heard the axes at the base of his hermitage. He began asking them, ‘Woe to you, what is the matter with you?’ but they did not answer him. When he saw that, he took a rope and let himself down, and they began dragging him by the nose, beating him, and saying, ‘Hypocrite, you deceive people with your deeds!’ He said to them, ‘Woe to you, what is the matter with you?’ They said, ‘You are the companion of the king’s daughter whom you got pregnant.’ He said, ‘What did she do?’ They said, ‘She gave birth to a boy.’ He said, ‘Is the boy alive?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Turn away from me.’ So they turned away, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then went to a tree, took a branch from it, then came to the boy while he was in his cradle, struck him with that branch, and said, ‘O tyrant, who is your father?’ He said, ‘My father is so-and-so the shepherd.’ They said, ‘If you wish, we will rebuild your hermitage with gold, and if you wish, with silver.’ He said, ‘Restore it as it was.’ Abū Ḥarb claimed that none spoke in the cradle except three: ʿĪsā ibn Maryam, the witness of Yūsuf, and the companion of Jurayj.”"],[13739,"A man freed six slaves at his death, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him, so he freed two and kept four as slaves."],[13740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of al-khadhf (throwing pebbles with the fingers), for it breaks the tooth, puts out the eye, and does not harm the enemy.”"],[13741,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to God.”"],[13742,"He informed me of the people most hated by the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Keep it secret for me until I die? I said: Yes. He said: “The people most hated by the Messenger of God ﷺ were Banū Ḥanīfah, Banū Umayyah, and Thaqīf.”"],[13743,"The Prophet ﷺ died while he disliked three tribes: Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."],[13744,"Husayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muhammad, ʿAbd al-Muttalib was better for his people than you: he fed them liver and hump, while you slaughter them.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What did Allah will that you say?” He said: “What do you command me to say?” He said: “Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul, and resolve for me the most upright of my affairs.”"],[13745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man has a right over another man and grants him a delay until its term, it is charity for him. If he grants him a delay after its term, then for each day it is charity for him.”"],[13746,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Indeed, I do not fear for Quraysh except their own selves.” I said: “And what is that?” He said: “Greedy and arrogant. If you live long, you will see them as the most greedy and arrogant of people, until you see the people among them like sheep between two watering-troughs: once to this one and once to that one.”"],[13747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: “The prophets were presented to me. A prophet would come with no one but one man, and a prophet would come with no one but two men, and a prophet would come with no one but a small group. Then I looked and saw a great multitude, and I thought they were my community. When they drew near, they were the people of Musa. Then it was said to me: 'Look.' I looked and said: 'Who are these?' It was said: 'These are your community.' I rejoiced and was glad. Then it was said: 'Look.' I looked and saw another great multitude. It was said: 'These are your community.' I rejoiced and was glad. Then it was said to me: 'With these are seventy thousand of your community who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and the Muslims said: 'Who are these seventy thousand?' They agreed that they were those who were born in Islam and had not known anything of shirk. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while we were on that, and he said: “They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not practice augury from birds, and upon their Lord they rely.” Then ʿUkkashah stood and said: “Invoke Allah to make me one of them.” He said: “O Allah, make him one of them.” Then another man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, invoke Allah to make me one of them.” He said: “ʿUkkashah has preceded you to it.”"],[13748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves the chaste, abstaining from begging, who has dependents.\""],[13749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Go raid the tribe of so-and-so with so-and-so.\" He said: We lined up the men, and the women were behind the men. Then when they returned, a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, may Allah forgive you.\" He said, \"Have you done something new?\" He said, \"When the people were defeated, I caught a man from the people and the women, and he said, 'I am a Muslim,' or he said, 'I have embraced Islam,' but I killed him. By Allah, I did not do it.\" He did not seek forgiveness for him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For what do I fight the people except for Islam? By Allah, I will not seek forgiveness for you,\" or as he said. He said: He died later, and his clan buried him, but in the morning the earth threw him out. Then they buried him again and guarded him, but the earth threw him out a second time. Then they said, \"Perhaps someone came while you were sleeping and took him out.\" So they buried him a third time and guarded him, but the earth threw him out a third time. When they saw that, they left him, or as he said."],[13750,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and admonished the people, encouraged them, and warned them, and said what God willed to be. He said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him. Obey those whom God has placed in authority over you, and do not dispute authority with its people, even if he is a black slave. Hold fast to what you know of the Sunnah of your Prophet and the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs, and bite onto it with the molar teeth.”"],[13751,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us one morning and admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said, “O Messenger of God, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever remains after me will see severe disagreement. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs, bite onto it with the molar teeth, and beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is misguidance.”"],[13752,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The martyrs and those who died on their beds will dispute before our Lord concerning those who died in the plague. The martyrs will say, ‘Our brothers, they were killed as we were killed.’ Those who died on their beds will say, ‘Our brothers, they died on their beds as we died.’ God will judge between them and say, ‘Look at the wounds of the plague-stricken.’ If their wounds resemble the wounds of the martyrs, they are of them and with them. So they look at the wounds of the plague-stricken and find that they resemble the wounds of the martyrs, and they join them.”"],[13753,"From the Prophet ﷺ that one day he stood among the people and said: “O people, soon you will be made into armies: an army in Syria, an army in Iraq, and an army in Yemen.” Ibn Ḥawāla said, “O Messenger of God, if I reach that time, choose for me.” He said: “I choose Syria for you, for it is the best land of the Muslims and the chosen portion of God from His lands. He gathers to it His chosen ones from His creation. Whoever refuses, let him go to his Yemen and drink from its ponds, for God has guaranteed me Syria and its people.”"],[13754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise. One of you says to his shepherd, ‘Go to the middle of the valley, for it is the most fertile and the most grassy.’”"],[13755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ admonished us one day with an eloquent admonition that made eyes shed tears and hearts tremble. A man among the Muslims said, “This seems like the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “I have left you upon the clear path; its night is like its day. No one among you will deviate from it after me except one who is destroyed. Whoever among you lives will see much disagreement, so beware of innovations, and adhere to my sunnah and the sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth, and adhere to hearing and obedience, even if a slave is an Abyssinian.”"],[13756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ says: ‘If I take the two precious ones of My servant while he is attached to them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise if he praises Me for them.’”"],[13757,"\"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said: Allah the Almighty says, 'Those who love one another for My glory will be in my shade on a day when there is no shade except My shade.'\""],[13758,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, 'It is not lawful for you among predatory animals: any that has fangs, nor the domestic donkeys. And do not enter the houses of the People of the Book, and do not consume their wealth except what they give willingly. And do not strike—does any man among you think that he has become full, until he supposes, while reclining on his couch, saying: \"Allah ﷻ has not forbidden anything except in the Qur'an\"? Verily, by Allah, I have indeed narrated, commanded, and admonished.'"],[13759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, when a man gives water to his wife, he is rewarded.' He (the narrator) said: 'So I went to her and gave her water, and I informed her of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[13760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How will it be when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, whose necks are in disagreement, and they have become like this\"—and he separated his fingers. He said, \"How is the way out, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, keep to your own self, and beware of their common people.\""],[13761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"How will you be when you are among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have become corrupted, and they have differed and become like this\"—then he inserted his fingers into one another. I said, \"How will it be for me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, keep to your own special affairs, and beware of their common people.\""],[13762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants have become corrupted, whose trusts have become corrupted, and whose hearts have differed?\"—and he interlaced his fingers. He said, \"What should I do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Keep to what you know and leave what you reject, keep to the special affairs of your own self, and beware of their common people.\""],[13763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abdullah b. Amr: \"How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose hearts and trusts have become corrupted, and whose hearts have differed?\"—and he interlaced his fingers. He said, \"What should I do?\" He said, \"Keep to what you know and leave what you reject, keep to the special affairs of your own self, and beware of their common people.\""],[13764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people—a people whose pledges and trusts have become corrupted, and who have differed and become like this?” And he interlaced his fingers. He said: “What do you command me, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Keep to what you know and abandon what you disapprove of; attend to your own self and leave their common folk.”"],[13765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks wine, flog him. Then if he drinks again, flog him. Then if he drinks again, flog him. Then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him.” He said: ‘Abdullah b. ‘Amr used to say: “Bring me a man who has drunk wine three times, and I will strike his neck.”"],[13766,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The warrior has his reward, and the one who equips him has his reward and the reward of the warrior.”"],[13767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with two books in his hand and said: “Do you know what these two books are?” We said: “No, unless you tell us, O Messenger of God.” He said: “This is the book of the Lord of the Worlds, in it are the names of the people of Paradise and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then they are totaled at the last of them, so none are added to them or subtracted from them ever. And this is the book of the people of the Fire, with their names and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then they are totaled at the last of them, so none are added to them or subtracted from them ever.” The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Then what is the point of action if this is a matter already finished?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Rather, aim aright and draw near, for the person of Paradise is sealed with the deeds of Paradise even if he does any deed, and the person of the Fire is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire even if he does any deed. Your Lord, Mighty and Exalted, has finished with the servants.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ made a gesture with his hands and cast them aside: “Your Lord has finished with creation: a party in Paradise and a party in the Blaze.”"],[13768,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “A return from a military expedition is like a military expedition,” meaning the return from an expedition."],[13769,"From the Prophet ﷺ: the same."],[13770,"I said: “O Messenger of God, do you feel the revelation?” He said: “Yes, I hear sounds like bells, then I fall silent at that. And there is no time revelation comes to me except that I think my soul is about to depart.”"],[13771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do you know who is with us in the house? It is Jibril ﷺ , and he has greeted you.”"],[13772,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The greatest hypocrites of my community are its reciters.”"],[13773,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do you know who the Muslim is?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\" They said, \"Then who is the believer?\" He said, \"One whom the believers trust with their selves and their wealth.\" They said, \"Then who is the emigrant?\" He said, \"One who emigrates from evil and avoids it.\" Abu al-Qasim said: The people of Egypt say Musa b. ʿAli b. Rabah, while the rest of the people say Musa b. ʿUlayy, and he forbade anyone who called him ʿUlayy."],[13774,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Envy is only in two cases: a man to whom God has given the Quran and who stands by it, making lawful what it makes lawful and forbidding what it forbids, and a man to whom God has given wealth and who uses it to maintain his relatives and kin and acts according to the word of God.\""],[13775,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The weak and the downtrodden.\""],[13776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A man from my nation will be called out on the Day of Resurrection in front of all creation, and ninety-nine scrolls will be spread out before him, each scroll as far as the eye can see. Then He will say, \"Do you deny anything of this?\" He will say, \"No, my Lord.\" He will say, \"We have no good deeds recorded for you with Us, and there is no injustice for you today.\" Then a card will be brought out for him containing, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\" Then he will say, \"My Lord, what is this card compared to these scrolls?\" The scrolls will be placed in one pan and the card in the other, and the scrolls will be light and the card will weigh heavy."],[13777,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The best charity is reconciling between people.\""],[13778,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was never obscene nor given to obscenity."],[13779,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.\""],[13780,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The martyr is forgiven every sin except debt.\""],[13781,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Being killed in the path of God expiates everything except debt.\""],[13782,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the booty of the gatherings of remembrance?\" He said, \"Paradise.\""],[13783,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to a man, \"How have you entered the morning, O so-and-so?\" He said, \"I praise God to you, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This is what I wanted from you.\""],[13784,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever is turned back from his need by an omen has associated partners with God.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the expiation for that?\" He said, \"You say: O God, there is no omen but Your omen, and no good but Your good, and there is no god but You.\""],[13785,"A man said: O Messenger of God, the muezzins surpass us. So the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Say as the muezzin says, then when you finish, ask and you will be given.\""],[13786,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The world is a provision, and the best of its provision is the righteous wife.\""],[13787,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said, \"The best of companions in the sight of God is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of God is the one who is best to his neighbor.\""],[13788,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The poor among the emigrants will precede the rich on the Day of Resurrection by forty autumns.\""],[13789,"He heard Abdullah b. Amr say, \"Indeed, the good I do today is more beloved to me than twice as much with the Messenger of God ﷺ, because when we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, our concern was the Hereafter and the world did not concern us, but today the world has drawn us in.\""],[13790,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"He has succeeded whom God has provided with sufficiency and made content with what He has given him.\""],[13791,"We buried a man with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we returned and reached his door, there was a woman approaching. We do not think he recognized her. He said, \"O Fatimah, from where have you come?\" She said, \"From the family of this deceased; I showed mercy to them for their deceased and offered my condolences.\" He said, \"Perhaps you reached the graves with them?\" She said, \"God forbid that I should reach the graves with them, since I heard you mention about them what you mention.\" He said, \"If you had reached the graves with them, you would not have seen Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it.\" The graves are the burial grounds."],[13792,"A man said: O Messenger of God, a funeral of an unbeliever passes by us, and you stand for it? He said, \"Yes, stand for it, for you are not standing for it; you are only standing for the angels who are with it.\""],[13793,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask God for well-being. But when you meet them, be steadfast. If they shout and cry out, hold to silence.\""],[13794,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The world is a provision, and the best of its provision is the righteous woman.\""],[13795,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask God for well-being. But when you meet them, be steadfast and remember God much. If they shout and cry out, hold to silence.\""],[13796,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man from the Ansar, \"What do you say when you go to sleep?\" He said, \"I say: In Your name, O God, I lay down my side, so forgive me.\" He said, \"May God forgive you.\""],[13797,"Should I not teach you words that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach Abu Bakr when he wanted to sleep? We said, 'Yes.' He said, 'O God, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You are the Lord of everything and its Sovereign. I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, with no partner, and the angels bear witness. O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan and his shirk, and I seek refuge in You from bringing evil upon myself or bringing it upon a Muslim.'"],[13798,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever's head is struck in the path of God and he seeks reward, God forgives him for whatever sins came before that.'"],[13799,"When the Prophet ﷺ ordered the trench to be dug, and it was dug around Madinah, they said, 'O Messenger of God, we have found a rock that we cannot dig.' The Prophet ﷺ stood up and we stood with him. When he came, he took the pickaxe and struck with it once, saying 'Allahu Akbar.' I heard a crash the like of which I had never heard. He said, 'Persia has been opened.' Then he struck again and said 'Allahu Akbar.' I heard a crash the like of which I had never heard. He said, 'Rome has been opened.' Then he struck again and said 'Allahu Akbar.' I heard a crash the like of which I had never heard. He said, 'God has brought Himyar as helpers and supporters.'"],[13800,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever loves a man for the sake of God has loved God, and they will both enter Paradise together, but the one who loved for the sake of God will be higher in rank than the other who was loved for the sake of God.'"],[13801,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'God strengthens Islam with men who are not from its people.'"],[13802,"The Messenger of God said, 'The world is a provision, and the best provision of it is a righteous woman.'"],[13803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The world is a provision, and the best provision of it is a righteous wife.'"],[13804,"From Abdullah b. Amr, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'You will gain victory over the non-Arabs and will take houses called hammams. No man should enter them except with an izar' – or he said 'a waist wrapper' – 'and women should not enter them except after childbirth or due to illness.'"],[13805,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to supplicate, 'O God, I ask You for health, chastity, trustworthiness, good character, and contentment with destiny.'"],[13806,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, then the scale will be brought, then ninety-nine scrolls will be brought, each scroll as far as the eye can see, containing his sins and errors. They will be placed on one pan of the scale. Then a piece of paper like this will be brought' – and he gestured with his hand, holding his thumb – 'on it is the testimony that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. It will be placed on the other pan, and it will outweigh his sins and errors.'"],[13807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What happened to the Children of Israel shall happen to my nation. They divided into seventy-two sects, and my nation shall divide into seventy-three sects, all of them in Hellfire except for one sect.\" It was asked, \"Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Those who are upon what I and my companions are upon.\""],[13808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not marry women for their lineage, for perhaps their lineage will harm them, and do not marry them for their wealth, for perhaps their wealth will make them tyrannical. A black slave woman with a pierced ear who has religion is better.'"],[13809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'There is no prayer after the Fajr prayer except two rak'ahs.'"],[13810,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Ghānim narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ziyād b. Anʿum, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Yazīd, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The likeness of my community is like that of rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.”"],[13811,"The Messenger ﷺ came out to us and said: “Who do you count as a martyr among you?” We said: “The one who is killed in the path of God.” He said: “The one who is killed in the path of God is a martyr, and the one who drowns in the path of God is a martyr, and the one whom a stomach ailment kills is a martyr, and the woman whom childbirth kills is a martyr.”"],[13812,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The martyr has six qualities: he is forgiven with the first spurt of his blood, he is safeguarded from the terror, he sees his seat in Paradise, he is married to the wide-eyed houris, and he is protected from the punishment of the grave.”"],[13813,"A man belched in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “Restrain your belching, for the people who will be hungry longest on the Day of Resurrection are those who were most satiated in this world.”"],[13814,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “The best charity is reconciling between people.”"],[13815,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever looks at a Muslim with a look by which he frightens him without right, God will frighten him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13816,"\"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The gatherings of the believers are a guarantee from Allah for whatever is in them, whether it be in a mosque or in the presence of a sick person, or at a funeral, or in the presence of a just leader to console and honor them.\""],[13817,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Knowledge is three things; whatever is beyond that is surplus: a decisive verse, an established sunnah, and a just obligatory share.”"],[13818,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Glorification is half of the Scale, praise of God fills the Scale, and ‘there is no god but God’ has no veil until it reaches the Most Merciful, exalted is He.”"],[13819,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The quickest supplication to be answered is the supplication of an absent person for an absent person.”"],[13820,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Nothing is quicker to be answered than the supplication of an absent person for an absent person.”"],[13821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out and said: “God, exalted is He, is not made great by any sin He forgives. A man from among those before you killed ninety-eight people. He came to a monk and said: ‘I have killed ninety-eight people; do you find any repentance for me?’ He said to him: ‘You have gone too far.’ So he rose against him and killed him. Then he came to another monk and said: ‘I have killed ninety-nine people; do you find any repentance for me?’ He said: ‘No, you have gone too far.’ So he rose against him and killed him. Then he came to another monk and said: ‘I have killed one hundred people; do you find any repentance for me?’ He said: ‘You have gone too far, and I do not know. But here are two villages: one village called Naḍrah and the other called Kufrah. As for Naḍrah, its people do the deeds of Paradise, and no one else settles there. As for Kufrah, its people do the deeds of the people of the Fire, and no one else settles there. Go to Naḍrah, and if you settle there and act like its people, there is no doubt about your repentance.’ So he set out intending it, until when he was between the two villages death overtook him. The angels asked their Lord about him, and He said: ‘Look to which of the two villages he was closer, and record him as one of its people.’ They found him closer to Naḍrah by a fingertip, and he was recorded as one of its people.”"],[13822,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no raiding party that raids in the path of God and obtains spoils except that they hasten two-thirds of their reward, while one-third remains. But if they do not obtain spoils, their reward is complete for them.”"],[13823,"Verily, the hearts of all the sons of Adam are between the two fingers out of the fingers of the Compassionate Lord as one heart. He turns that to any (direction) He likes. Then Allahs Messenger ﷺ said: 0 Allah, the Turner of the hearts, turn our hearts to Thine obedience. (Using translation from Muslim 2655)"],[13824,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Verily God (Exalted is He) decreed the measures fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth.”"],[13825,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God finished with the decrees and the affairs of the world fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth.” Al-Layth did not mention “the affairs of the world,” but rather said: “the measures of everything.”"],[13826,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will surely come upon people a time when their hearts are hearts of the foreigners.” I said, “And what are the hearts of the foreigners?” He said: “Love of the world. Their custom will be the custom of the Bedouins. Whatever provision comes to them, they put it into livestock, considering struggle to be harm and zakat a fine.”"],[13827,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The poor among the emigrants will outstrip the rich on the Day of Resurrection by forty autumns.”"],[13828,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Faith wears out within one of you as a garment wears out, so recite the Quran, renewing faith in your hearts.”"],[13829,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ reciting this verse: {The Day when people will stand before the Lord of the worlds}. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How will you be when God (Mighty and Majestic) gathers you as arrows are gathered in a quiver for fifty thousand years without looking at you?”"],[13830,"On the day of the Trench, while they were digging a trench around Madinah, the Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of a pickaxe and struck with it one blow, and said: “With this blow, God will open the treasures of the Romans.” Then he struck a second blow and said: “With this, God will open the treasures of Persia.” Then he struck a third blow and said: “With this blow, God will bring the people of Yemen as supporters and helpers.”"],[13831,"When {When the earth is shaken with its earthquake} was revealed, Abu Bakr ؓ was sitting and he wept. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What makes you weep, O Abu Bakr?” He said: “This surah has made me weep.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If you did not err or sin, God would create after you a people who sin and err, and He would forgive them.”"],[13832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Fasting and the Quran will intercede for the servant on the Day of Resurrection. Fasting says: ‘Lord, I prevented him from food and drink during the day, so let me intercede for him.’ And the Quran says: ‘Lord, I prevented him from sleep at night, so let me intercede for him.’ Then they will be allowed to intercede.”"],[13833,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the two rakʿahs of dawn, he would lie down on his right side."],[13834,"A man died in Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed over him, then said: “Would that he had died away from his birthplace.” A man said, “Why, O Messenger of God?” He replied: “When a man dies away from his birthplace, it is measured for him from his birthplace to the end of his footsteps in Paradise.”"],[13835,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him say what is good or remain silent. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor.”"],[13836,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to supplicate, saying: “O God, forgive us our sins, our wrongdoing, our jesting, our seriousness, our deliberate acts—and all of that is with us.”"],[13837,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to supplicate with these words: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the domination of debt, the domination of the enemy, and the gloating of enemies.”"],[13838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say when he wanted to sleep: “O God, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and God of everything, I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and messenger—and the angels bear witness. O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan and his association, and I seek refuge in You from bringing upon myself a sin or turning it back upon a Muslim.”"],[13839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out on the day of Badr with three hundred and twenty-five fighting men, just as Saul went out. The Messenger of God supplicated for them when they went out: “O God, they are barefoot, so carry them; O God, they are naked, so clothe them; O God, they are hungry, so satisfy them.” Then God granted him victory at Badr, and they returned when they returned, and there was not a man among them but that he came back with a camel or two camels, and they were clothed and satisfied."],[13840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Faith is Yemeni, and they are from me and to me, even if their abode is far. It is near that they will come to you as helpers and supporters, so command you well.”"],[13841,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My husband is poor; he is not capable of anything.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her husband, “Do you recite any of the Qur’an?” He said, “I recite such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Excellent, excellent! Your husband is rich, so stick to him.” The woman stuck to her husband, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of God, God has expanded upon us and provided for us.”"],[13842,"Seven men came to the Prophet ﷺ, and each man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ took one man, and the Prophet ﷺ took one man. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “What is your name?” He said, “Abu Ghazwan.” He said: He milked seven sheep for him, and he drank all their milk. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Would you like, O Abu Ghazwan, to become Muslim?” He said, “Yes,” and he became Muslim. The Prophet ﷺ wiped his chest. When morning came, the Prophet ﷺ milked a single sheep for him, and he did not finish its milk. He said, “What is the matter with you, O Abu Ghazwan?” He said, “By the One who sent you as a prophet, I have drunk my fill.” He said, “Yesterday you had seven intestines, and today you have only one.”"],[13843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever goes to the mosque of the congregation, then one step wipes away a bad deed and one step writes a good deed, going and returning.”"],[13844,"The Prophet ﷺ sent out a raiding party, and they took booty and hastened their return. The people talked about how close their expedition was, how abundant their booty was, and how quick their return was. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I not point you to something closer in expedition than yours, more abundant in booty, and quicker in return? Whoever performs ablution then goes early to the mosque for the voluntary prayer of dawn—he is closer in expedition, more abundant in booty, and quicker in return.”"],[13845,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: “The muezzins surpass us.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Say as they say, and when you finish, ask and you will be given.”"],[13846,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk, he traveled with them through the night until it was near dawn, then he stopped with them at dawn and said: “O Bilal, guard the prayer for us.” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” But sleep overcame Bilal and he slept, and they slept until the sun pained them. The Messenger of God ﷺ got up and performed dry ablution, then said to Bilal, “Give the call to prayer and the iqamah.” Bilal said, “Now?” He said, “Yes.” So they prayed after the morning had come."],[13847,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “In Paradise there are chambers whose outside can be seen from their inside and whose inside can be seen from their outside.” Abu Malik al-Ashʿari said, “For whom are they, O Messenger of God?” He said, “For the one who softens speech, feeds food, and spends the night standing in prayer while people are asleep.”"],[13848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a man to lead the people in the noon prayer, and he spat toward the qiblah while leading the people. When it was time for the afternoon prayer, he sent for another man. The first man became anxious, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, was something revealed about me?\" He said, \"No, but you spat in front of you while leading the people, and you offended God and His angels.\""],[13849,"\"O Messenger of God, my father slaughters before he prays.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Tell your father to pray, then slaughter.\""],[13850,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the two trialers of the grave. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab said, \"Will our minds be returned to us, O Messenger of God?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Yes, just as you are today.\" ʿUmar said, \"Then stone in his mouth!\" (i.e., he was silenced)."],[13851,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When a man comes to visit a sick person, let him say: O God, heal Your servant so-and-so, that he may wound an enemy for You or walk to prayer for You.\""],[13852,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, allow me to castrate myself.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The castration of my community is fasting and standing in prayer.\""],[13853,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled and stopped with his companions. There were people who had made a shade over their companion, and he was fasting. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by them and said, \"What is the matter with your companion? Is he ill?\" They said, \"No, O Messenger of God, but he is fasting,\" and that was on a scorching day. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"It is not righteousness to fast while traveling.\""],[13854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the noon prayer and found a hobbled mount. He said, \"Where is the owner of this mount?\" No one answered him. He entered the mosque and prayed until he finished, then came out and found the mount as it was. He said, \"Where is the owner of this mount?\" Its owner answered him, saying, \"I am its owner, O Prophet of God.\" He said, \"Will you not fear God regarding it? Either feed it or release it so that it may seek for itself.\""],[13855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When the sun rises from the west, Iblis will fall down prostrating, calling out and raising his voice: 'My God, command me to prostrate to whomever You will.'\" He said: \"His attendants will gather to him and say, 'O their master, what is this supplication?' He will say, 'I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, to grant me respite until the appointed time, and this is the appointed time.'\" He said: \"The beast of the earth will emerge from a fissure in al-Safa. Its first step will land in Antioch, then it will come to Iblis and slap him.\""],[13856,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to Badr with three hundred fifteen, the number of the companions of Talut. When they appeared, he saw them as infantry, barefoot, and naked. He said, \"O God, they are hungry, so feed them; they are on foot, so carry them; they are naked, so clothe them.\" They returned from Badr, and there was not one among them who was not holding the head of one or two camels, and they were clothed and fed."],[13857,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever is silent, he is saved."],[13858,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever is silent, he is saved."],[13859,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning the womb and placing one of his fingers on top of the other, saying, \"Whoever maintains ties with you, I will maintain ties with him, and whoever severs ties with you, I will sever ties with him.\""],[13860,"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked a man, \"What do you say when you retire to your bed?\" He said, \"I say: In Your name I lay down my side, so forgive me my sin.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have hit the mark; may God grant you success.\""],[13861,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever meets God on the Day of Resurrection with the five prayers, the fasting of Ramadan, and the major ablution from impurity will be a true servant of God, and whoever omits any of them will be an enemy of God.\""],[13862,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man milking a ewe and said, \"O so-and-so, when you milk, leave some for its young, for they are among the offspring of animals.\""],[13863,"A man complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about bad livelihood, so he said: “May he raise a small one.” I asked him, and he said: “A foal or a servant boy.”"],[13864,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks a mouthful of wine, flog him with eighty lashes.”"],[13865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Heedlessness is in three things: from the remembrance of God, may He be exalted; from when one prays the dawn prayer until sunrise; and a man’s heedlessness of himself regarding debt until it overwhelms him.”"],[13866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while we were sitting, so we made room for him and he sat down. Then he said: “Where are my companions who are from me and I am from them, and I will enter Paradise and they will enter it with me?” He said it three times. We said: “Is it other than us, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Yes, the people of Yemen, those cast aside at the ends of the earth, turned away from the doors of rulers. One of them dies while his need is still in his chest, unfulfilled.”"],[13867,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the time of the dawn prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer in the dark, then he prayed it the next day when it was bright. Then he said: “Where is the questioner?” He said: “I am here.” He said: “The time is between yesterday and today.”"],[13868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and saw two groups. One group was supplicating to Allah and seeking closeness to Him, while the other group was learning and teaching Islamic jurisprudence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Both of these groups are on good and righteous path. However, the group that supplicates to Allah and seeks closeness to Him, if He wills, He gives them what they ask for, and if He wills, He withholds it from them. As for the group that learns and teaches the ignorant, I have been sent as a teacher, and these are better.\" So, he went and sat down with them."],[13869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: “These two are forbidden for the males of my community and lawful for its females.”"],[13870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has forbidden my Ummah (community) from consuming alcohol, gambling, impure slaughtered animals, and al-Kubba and al-Ghubayra, and He has increased me with the obligation of performing the Witr prayer.\""],[13871,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The lands of the non-Arabs will be conquered for you after me, and in them there are houses called bathhouses. Indeed, they are forbidden for men except with waist-wrappers, and for the women of my community except those who have just given birth or are ill.”"],[13872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no remembrance more excellent than ‘There is no god but God,’ and no supplication more excellent than seeking forgiveness.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: “So know that there is no god but God, and ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women” (Q 47:19)."],[13873,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If the imam experiences ritual impurity at the end of his prayer until he sits upright, then his prayer is complete, and the prayer of those behind him is like his prayer.”"],[13874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I do not care what I have done or leaned upon as long as I have hung an amulet, drunk a theriac, or recited poetry from myself.”"],[13875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When the treasuries of Persia and Byzantium are opened for you, what kind of people will you be?” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf said: “We will be as God has commanded.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Or other than that: you will vie with one another, then envy one another, then turn your backs on one another and hate one another, or something like that; then you will go to the dwellings of the emigrants and put some of them in charge of others.”"],[13876,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Nuh ﷺ fasted the entire time except the Day of Fitr and the Day of Adha, Dawud ﷺ fasted half the time, and Ibrahim ﷺ fasted three days of every month — he fasted the entire time and broke the fast the entire time.”"],[13877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should pray with his garment over his nose, for that is the snout of the Shaytan.”"],[13878,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when an old man asked him about kissing for the one fasting, and he gave him permission. Then a young man asked him about kissing for the one fasting, and he forbade him. Some of the people looked at the faces of others, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “The old man controls himself.” Musa b. Dawud added in his version: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I already knew why you looked at one another. The old man controls himself.”"],[13879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful to marry a woman by divorcing another.”"],[13880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who deliberately passes in front of a man while he is praying will wish on the Day of Resurrection that he were a dry tree.”"],[13881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four things, if they are in you, then what you miss of this world will not harm you: fulfilling the trust, truthful speech, good character, and purity of food.”"],[13882,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The rightly guided Muslim will attain the rank of those who fast and stand much in prayer, by the signs of Allah, through his good character and the nobility of his disposition.”"],[13883,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he says: “Whoever stands in prayer reciting ten verses will not be recorded among the heedless; whoever stands with a hundred verses will be recorded among the devout; and whoever stands with a thousand verses will be recorded among the thankful.”"],[13884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Ibrahim, Mariyah the Copt, the mother of his son, while she was pregnant from him with Ibrahim. He found with her a relative of hers who had come with her from Egypt, had embraced Islam, and whose Islam was good. He used to visit Umm Ibrahim. Because he was content with his position in relation to the mother of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ child, he castrated himself and cut what was between his legs until he left himself neither little nor much. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Ibrahim and found her relative with her, and something fell into his heart concerning that, as happens in people's hearts. He returned with changed color and met Umar, telling him what had fallen into his heart about Umm Ibrahim's relative. Umar took his sword and hurried until he entered upon Mariyah and found that relative of hers with her. He swung the sword at him to kill him, but when the man saw that, he uncovered himself. When Umar saw him, he went back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you that Jibril ﷺ came to me and informed me that Allah ﷻ has cleared her and her relative of what fell into my heart, and he gave me glad tidings that in her womb is a boy from me and he is the most resembling of creation to me, and he commanded me to name him Ibrahim and gave me the kunya Abu Ibrahim. Were it not that I dislike changing my kunya by which I am known, I would have taken the kunya Abu Ibrahim as Jibril ﷺ gave me.”"],[13885,"O Messenger of Allah, which of the Muslims is best? He said: \"One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""],[13886,"O Messenger of Allah, which of the Muslims is best? He said: \"One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""],[13887,"O Messenger of Allah, which of the Muslims is best? He said: \"One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\""],[13888,"Abdullah b. Amr was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man from the Bedouins came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love jihad and Umrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you have parents?\" He said: Yes, both of them. He said: \"Then go back and keep their company often.\""],[13889,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Do you know who will be the first to enter Paradise?\" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"The poor among the Emigrants, by whom hardships are warded off. One of them dies while his need is still in his chest, unable to fulfill it. The angels say: Our Lord, we are Your angels, Your keepers, and the inhabitants of Your heavens; do not admit them to Paradise before us. He says: My servants, they do not associate anything with Me. By them hardships are warded off. One of them dies while his need is still in his chest, unable to fulfill it. At that point, the angels enter upon them from every gate: {Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. And excellent is the final home} (13:24).\""],[13890,"I said to Abdullah b. Amr: We are in a land where there is no gold or silver. May we sell a camel for two camels, a cow for two cows, and a sheep for two sheep? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to equip an army, and the camels ran out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the camels have run out. He said: \"Take for me the young she-camels of zakat.\" So I began taking a camel for two camels up to the zakat camels."],[13891,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be among my nation men whose women ride on saddles like men, clothed yet naked, on their heads like the humps of bukhti camels. Curse them, for they are cursed. If there were a nation behind you from among the nations, their women would serve them as they serve you, like the women of the nations before you.\""],[13892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was commanded with the Day of Sacrifice as a festival which Allah made for this nation.\" A man said: What if I find only the milk-giving animal of my family? Should I sacrifice it? He said: \"No, but trim your nails, shave your pubic hair, and trim your mustache. That is the completion of your sacrifice.\""],[13893,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite. He said: \"I will teach you from the surahs beginning with Ha Mim.\" The man said: O Messenger of Allah, my tongue is heavy and my liver is thick. He said: \"I will teach you from the surahs beginning with Alif Lam Ra.\" The man said the same as before. He said: \"I will teach you from the surahs beginning with al-Musabbihat.\" The man said the same as his first statement. He said: \"Upon you is the comprehensive, unique surah.\" So he taught him When the earth is shaken with its [final] earthquake. The Bedouin said: Enough for me. Then he turned away, and the Prophet ﷺ called him back. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"I was commanded with the sacrifice, so offer a sacrifice on the Day of Sacrifice.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I find only the sheep of my family? He said: \"No, but trim your mustache and clip your nails, for that is part of the completion of your sacrifice.\" Al-Muqri added in his narration: \"And shave your pubic hair.\""],[13894,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “Indeed a servant may be recorded as a believer for ages upon ages, then he dies while God is wrathful with him; and indeed a believer may be recorded as a disbeliever for ages upon ages, then he dies while God is pleased with him. Whoever dies as a slanderer, a backbiter of people, his mark on the Day of Resurrection will be that God brands him on the snout from both lips.”"],[13895,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed the souls of the believers meet over a distance of a day and a night’s journey, even though neither of them has seen the face of his companion.”"],[13896,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If a lead ball like this”—and he pointed to something like a pearl, a skull—“were sent from heaven to earth, a journey of five hundred years, it would reach the earth before nightfall. And if it were sent from the top of the chain, it would travel for forty autumns, night and day, before reaching the earth’s base or its bottom.”"],[13897,"He mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Whoever guards it, it will be for him a light and a proof; and whoever does not guard it, it will not be for him a light or a proof, and he will be with Pharaoh, Haman, and Ubayy b. Khalaf.”"],[13898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever dies on Friday or the night of Friday will be protected from the trial of the grave.”"],[13899,"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ sought refuge from seven things: from sudden death, from the bite of a snake, from being eaten by a wild beast, from burning, from drowning, from something falling on him, and from being killed while fleeing from the battle line."],[13900,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ writing down what we heard from him, and we said: “Which of the two cities will be conquered first, O Messenger of God?” He said: “The city of Heraclius,” meaning Constantinople."],[13901,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “When the two freed ones rule—the freed one of the Arabs and the freed one of the Romans—the great battles will be at their hands.”"],[13902,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The battle cry of my community, when they are driven onto the Bridge, will be: ‘There is no god but You.’”"],[13903,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves those who love dates.\""],[13904,"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be a trial in which a man will part from his brother and his father. The trial will fly into the hearts of men among them until the Day of Resurrection, until a man is reproached by it as an adulteress is reproached by her adultery.”"],[13905,"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The qurayʿāʾ has come to you.” We said: “What is it, O Messenger of God?” He said: “A trial in which it is like an egg.”"],[13906,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Love your beloved moderately, for perhaps he may become hateful to you one day; and hate your adversary moderately, for perhaps he may become beloved to you one day.”"],[13907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Visit occasionally and you will increase in love.”"],[13908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every debt is rewarded from the good deeds of its owner except for one who incurred debt in three cases: a man whose strength weakened in the path of Allah, so he strengthened himself against fighting his enemy by a debt, then died without repaying it; a man who feared celibacy for himself, so he remained chaste by marrying a woman with a debt, then died without repaying it; and a man with whom a Muslim man died, and he found nothing to shroud him except by a debt, then he died without repaying it. It will be repaid on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three persons: whoever incurs debt among them and then dies without repaying it, Allah ﷻ will repay it on his behalf: a man who is in the path of Allah and his strength weakens, so he strengthens himself by a debt against his enemy, then dies without repaying it; a man with whom a man from among you dies and he finds nothing to shroud him or bury him except by a debt, then he dies without repaying it; and a man who fears temptation for himself in celibacy, so he remains chaste by marrying a woman with a debt, then dies without repaying it. Allah ﷻ will repay it on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three persons whose prayer is not accepted: one who goes ahead of a people while they dislike him, a man who comes to the prayer dibāran — and dibār is to come after the time — and a man who enslaves his freed slave.”"],[13911,"“In it ʿAbdullāh b. Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib died in al-Madīnah, and he was given the kunyah Abū Jaʿfar — meaning in the year eighty.”"],[13912,"“ʿAbdullāh b. Jaʿfar used to dye with henna.”"],[13913,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was commanded to give Khadījah good tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds, with no noise in it and no fatigue.”"],[13914,"From ʿAbdullāh b. Jaʿfar and ʿAbdullāh b. al-Zubayr: “They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when they were both seven years old, and when he saw them he smiled and extended his hand and accepted their pledge of allegiance.”"],[13915,"When Abu Talib died, the Prophet ﷺ set out for Taif on foot. He called them to Islam, but they did not respond to him, so he turned away. He came to the shade of a tree and prayed two rak‘ahs, then said: “O Allah, to You I complain of my weakness, my lack of resources, and my humiliation before people. Most Merciful of the merciful, You are the Most Merciful of the merciful. To whom will You entrust me? To an enemy who meets me with a scowling face, or to a relative to whom You have given authority over my affairs?\" \"If You are not angry with me, then I do not mind; Your forgiveness is more expansive for me. I seek refuge in the nur of Your Face by which the darknesses are illuminated and by which the affairs of this world and the Hereafter are set aright, lest You send down upon me Your anger or cause Your displeasure to befall me. To You belongs the right to pleasure until You are pleased. There is no power except through You.”"],[13916,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating watermelon with fresh dates.”"],[13917,"“The Prophet ﷺ was cupped after he was poisoned.”"],[13918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah ﷻ is with the debtor until he repays his debt, as long as his debt is not in something Allah dislikes.”"],[13919,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing two garments dyed with saffron, or a turban."],[13920,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a people shooting arrows at a ram. He said: \"Do not mutilate animals.\""],[13921,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood over Hamzah on the day of Uhud while burying him. He was wrapped in a striped cloak, and his feet became exposed when they covered his head. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered sand, and it was placed over his feet. He said: \"Were it not that our women would grieve, we would have left Hamzah in the open for the scavenging of beasts and birds.\""],[13922,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man asked him about what you asked me about. He said: \"Ask God for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[13923,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ seated me behind him and confided to me a secret that I would not tell anyone. He said: The most beloved things the Messenger of God ﷺ would conceal himself behind were a target and a wall of palm trees. He entered a garden belonging to a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel. When it saw the Prophet ﷺ, it yearned and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and wiped its hump and the back of its neck, and it became calm. Then he said: \"Whose camel is this?\" A young man of the Ansar came and said: \"It is mine, O Messenger of God.\" He said to him: \"Will you not fear God regarding this animal that God has put in your possession? It has complained to me that you starve it and overwork it.\""],[13924,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating cucumber with fresh dates."],[13925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting for a prophet to say, 'I am better than Yunus b. Matta.'\""],[13926,"To Ibn Abbas and Abdullah b. Ja'far: Do you both remember the day we met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They said: “Yes, he carried us and left you.”"],[13927,"“The Prophet ﷺ carried a boy from the Banu Hashim and Ibn Ja'far on a camel.”"],[13928,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would be met by the children of his household. He returned from a journey, and I was brought to him first, so he carried me in front of him. Then one of Fatimah's two sons was brought, and he carried him behind him. We entered Madinah, three of us on one mount.”"],[13929,"“The Prophet ﷺ carried a boy from the Banu Hashim on a mount.”"],[13930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for a matter has come to them that preoccupies them.”"],[13931,"“The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was with some boys of the Banu Abdul-Muttalib, and he carried me and another boy on a mount he was riding, so we were three on it.”"],[13932,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever doubts something in his prayer should prostrate twice as long as he has not said the salam.”"],[13933,"“The Prophet ﷺ wore a silver ring on his right hand.”"],[13934,"To his daughter when she entered upon al-Hajjaj: When he enters upon you, say: “There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.” And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say it when hardship befell him. She said it, and he did not reach her."],[13935,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing a ring on his right hand."],[13936,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a ring on his right hand."],[13937,"Abdullah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named it Taybah, and you name it Khubthah?”"],[13938,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The best meat is the meat of the back.”"],[13939,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever shoots at night is not one of us, and whoever sleeps on a roof without a parapet and dies, his blood is wasted.”"],[13940,"“Abdullah b. al-Zubayr was killed in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year seventy-three, and on the day he was killed he was seventy-two years old.”"],[13941,"“Abdullah b. al-Zubayr was born in Madinah twenty months after the Hijrah, and he was four months and seven days older than al-Miswar and Marwan.”"],[13942,"“Ibn al-Zubayr was killed in the year seventy-two.”"],[13943,"Asma, the daughter of Abu Bakr, immigrated to the Prophet ﷺ while she was pregnant with Abdullah bin Zubair. She gave birth and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ to rub his gums. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him and placed him in his lap, then he was brought a date and he sucked on it. The Prophet ﷺ then put it in his mouth and rubbed his gums with it. If the first thing to enter his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Asma said. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his body and named him Abdullah. Later, when he was seven or eight years old, he came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. Zubair ordered him to do so, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled when he saw him approaching and giving allegiance. He was the first person born in Madinah after the advent of Islam, and the Jews used to say that no child is born to them in Madinah. When Abdullah was born, the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised their voices in takbeer. Abdullah bin Umar, the son of Umar ibn Khattab, said when he heard the takbeer of the people of Sham (Greater Syria) after they killed Abdullah bin Zubair, who they considered to be better than those who celebrated his birth, and said, \"They are better than those who celebrated his death.\""],[13944,"Asma' bt. Abi Bakr set out when she emigrated while pregnant with Abdullah b. al-Zubayr. She arrived at Quba' and gave birth to Abdullah at Quba'. Then she brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after giving birth so that he might chew a date for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him from her, placed him in his lap, then asked for a date. A'ishah said: We spent a while looking for one before we found it. He chewed it, then placed it in his mouth. The first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Asma' said: Then he wiped him, prayed for him, and named him Abdullah. Then he came later when he was seven or eight years old to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Zubayr had ordered him to do that. He smiled when he saw him coming toward him, then accepted his pledge."],[13945,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, all my companions have kunyahs, so give me a kunyah. He said: “Take the kunyah of your son, Abdullah b. al-Zubayr.” She was called Umm Abdullah until she died."],[13946,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'All your wives have a kunyah except me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, 'Take the kunyah Umm ʿAbd Allah.' So she was called Umm ʿAbd Allah until she died, though she never gave birth at all."],[13947,"ʿAbd Allah b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, saying: My father Maslamah b. Qaʿnab narrated to me from Hisham b. ʿUrwah from ʿAbbad b. Hamzah b. ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr that ʿAʾishah said, 'O Messenger of God, will you not give me a kunyah?' He said, 'Take the kunyah of ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr.' So she was called Umm ʿAbd Allah."],[13948,"The Commander of the Faithful instructed me during his illness that if anything from the people of the Hijaz alarmed me, I should send you to them. And indeed something has alarmed me. So he said, 'I am as the Commander of the Faithful thought. Bind a banner for me and prepare the armies.' He said, 'He reached Madinah and permitted it for three days. Then he summoned them to pledge allegiance to Yazid on condition that they be slaves, owned property, in obedience to God and in disobedience to Him.' They answered him to that except one man from Quraysh whose mother was an umm walad (a slave woman who bore her master's child). He said to him, 'Pledge allegiance to Yazid on condition that you are a slave in obedience to God and in disobedience to Him.' He said, 'No, rather in obedience to God.' He refused to accept that from him and killed him. His mother swore an oath: if God gives her power over Muslim, alive or dead, she will burn him with fire. He said, 'When Muslim b. ʿUqbah left Madinah, his illness worsened and he died. The mother of the Qurayshi man went out with slaves of hers to Muslim's grave and ordered that it be dug up from the side of his head. When they reached him, there was a serpent coiled around his neck, gripping the tip of his nose and sucking it.' He said, 'The people recoiled from him and said, \"O our mistress, turn back, for God has sufficed you against his evil.\" And they told her the news. She said, \"No, not until I fulfill for God what I promised Him.\" Then she said, \"Dig for me from the side of his legs.\" So they dug, and there was the serpent with its tail wrapped around his legs. He said, 'She withdrew and prayed two rakʿahs, then said, \"O God, if You know that I was angry at Muslim b. ʿUqbah today only for Your sake, then leave me and him.\" Then she took hold of a stick and went to the serpent's tail and moved it, and it slipped away from the back of his head and came out of the grave. Then she ordered that he be taken out of the grave and burned with fire.'"],[13949,"I was present at the killing of Ibn al-Zubayr on the day he was killed in the Sacred Mosque. The armies began entering from the gates of the mosque, and whenever a group entered from a gate, he charged them alone until he drove them out. While he was in that state, a battlement from the battlements of the mosque fell on his head and knocked him down, while he was reciting these verses."],[13950,"Kaʿb used to narrate to us, and everything he said has come to pass except his saying: 'A young man of Thaqif will kill me.' And this is his head before me—meaning al-Mukhtar. Ibn Sirin said, 'He did not realize that Abu Muhammad—meaning al-Hajjaj—had been hidden for him.'"],[13951,"So I will not fulfill, by God, his oath. Then he said."],[13952,"Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubayb—he said it three times. Then he said, 'I forbade you from this'—he said it three times. 'You were indeed one who fasted much, prayed much, and maintained family ties.' That reached al-Hajjaj—the stance of ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar—so he had him brought down and threw him into the graves of the Jews. He sent to Asmaʾ bt. Abi Bakr, whose sight had gone, ordering her to come to him, but she refused. He sent to her: 'You will come, or I will send someone to drag you by your hair.' She said, 'By God, I will not come to you until you send someone to drag me by my hair.' His messenger came and told him, so he said, 'O boy, hand me my two sandals.' He handed him his sandals, and he went, blazing with anger, until he came to her and said, 'Have you seen what God did to the enemy of God?' She said, 'I see that you have ruined his worldly life, and he has ruined your afterlife. As for what you reproach him with—Dhat al-Nitaqayn (the one with two girdles)—yes, I had two girdles: a girdle with which the food of the Messenger of God ﷺ was covered from ants, and my other girdle which women cannot do without. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"In Thaqif there will be a destroyer and a liar.\" As for the liar, we have seen him; and as for the destroyer, you are he.' He said, 'Then he left.'"],[13953,"No, by God, he was not a hypocrite. He was indeed one who fasted much and prayed much. He said, 'Be quiet, for you are an old woman who has become senile.' She said, 'I have not become senile since I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"From Thaqif will come a liar and a destroyer.\" As for the liar, we have seen him—meaning al-Mukhtar—and as for the destroyer, you are he.'"],[13954,"Asmaʾ bt. Abi Bakr came with some of her slave girls, and her sight had gone. She said, 'Where is al-Hajjaj?' We said, 'He is not here.' She said, 'Then tell him to order for us these bones, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding mutilation.' We said, 'When he comes, we will tell him.' She said, 'When he comes, tell him that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer.\"'"],[13955,"He said, 'Tell her: al-Hajjaj says to you, \"Separate what wealth you have from the wealth of ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr.\"' She said, 'Do it with the son of Asmaʾ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"From this tribe of Thaqif will come two men: one of them a liar and the other a destroyer.\" As for the liar, we have known him, and I do not think he is other than the destroyer.' I returned to him and told him, and he did not dislike that."],[13956,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Proclaim marriages publicly.'"],[13957,"Abu Bakr's name was ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUthman, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named him ʿAtiq (freed) from the Fire."],[13958,"It was revealed concerning Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: “And no one has with him any favor to be repaid, except seeking the face of his Lord, the Most High. And he will surely be satisfied.”"],[13959,"“The Prophet ﷺ would point with his finger when he supplicated, without moving it.” Ibn Jurayj said: And ʿAmr b. Dinar added: ʿAmir b. ʿAbdullah b. al-Zubayr informed me, from his father, that he saw the Prophet ﷺ supplicating like that, and he was leaning with his left hand on his left leg."],[13960,"“When the Prophet ﷺ sat in prayer, he would place his left foot between his thigh and shin, and place his left hand on his left thigh, and place his right hand on his right thigh.”"],[13961,"“He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed and sat in the second or fourth [rakʿah], place his left hand on his left thigh and place his right hand on his right thigh, and point with the finger next to the thumb.”"],[13962,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that “when he prayed, he would place his left hand on his left thigh and the other on his right thigh, and raise his finger like this, pointing.”"],[13963,"He said: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ when he began the prayer raise his hands until they passed his ears.”"],[13964,"“Where were you?” I said: “I found people such that I have not seen better than them. They remember Allah, and one of them trembles until he faints from fear of Allah, so I sat with them.” He said: “Do not sit with them after this.” He saw that I was not convinced, so he said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the Quran, and I saw Abu Bakr and ʿUmar reciting the Quran, and this did not befall them. Do you consider them more humble before Allah than Abu Bakr and ʿUmar?” So I realized that was the case, and I left them.”"],[13965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever attends Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.”"],[13966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has a son in Makkah, a shrewd merchant with wealth. It is as if I can see him coming to you for his father’s ransom.” When Quraysh said what they said about the ransom, al-Muttalib said: “You have spoken truthfully. By Allah, if you do that, he will certainly seek revenge upon you.” Then he slipped away at night and arrived in Madinah, and ransomed his father for four thousand dirhams."],[13967,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the two litigants sit before the judge.”"],[13968,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast with a people, he would say: “May the fasting break their fast with you, and may the angels pray for you.”"],[13969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group of his companions when something had occurred that made them laugh, and he said: “Do you laugh while the mention of Paradise and Hell is before you?” Then this verse was revealed: “Inform My servants that I am the Forgiving, the Merciful, and that My punishment is the painful punishment.”"],[13970,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ twice or thrice."],[13971,"The Messenger of God ﷺ allotted four shares in the year of Khaybar: a share for al-Zubayr, a share for the near relative, a share for his mother, and a share for his horse."],[13972,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'A single suckle from breastfeeding does not make [marriage] unlawful, nor do two suckles.'"],[13973,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A single suckle does not make [marriage] unlawful, nor do two suckles.'"],[13974,"'The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us the call [to prayer].' I said, 'Why that?' He said, 'Because they will have the longest necks of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[13975,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'ʿUmra is valid for the one to whom it is given, and ruqba is for the one to whom it is granted; its course is the course of inheritance.'"],[13976,"'God commanded His Prophet to accept the pardoning aspect of people's character.'"],[13977,"This verse was revealed concerning the Negus: 'And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears.'"],[13978,"'Who would eat the crow, when the Messenger of God ﷺ has called it a transgressor?'"],[13979,"A man from the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of God ﷺ about the channels of the Harrah that they used to water the palm trees. The Ansari said, 'Let the water flow,' but al-Zubayr refused. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Water, O Zubayr, then send [the water] to your neighbor.' The Ansari became angry and said, 'O Messenger of God, is it because he is your aunt's son?' The face of the Messenger of God ﷺ changed color, then he said, 'Water, O Zubayr, then hold back the water until it returns to the root.' Al-Zubayr said, 'By God, I think this verse was revealed concerning that: \"But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what arises between them.\"'"],[13980,"Because Allah freed him from the tyrants.”"],[13981,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of Allah, should I perform Hajj on behalf of my father?” He said, “Are you his eldest child?” He replied, “Yes.” He said, “Then perform Hajj on his behalf.”"],[13982,"Zam‘ah had a slave woman with whom he used to have intercourse, and they accused her. She gave birth. The Prophet ﷺ said: “As for the inheritance, it belongs to him, and as for you, veil yourself from him, O Sawdah, for he is not a brother to you.”"],[13983,"To pray on the Day of Tarwiyah the Zhuhr, ‘Asr, Maghrib, ‘Isha’ and Subh in Mina, then to go forth and take a midday nap wherever Allah has decreed for him, then to depart when the sun declines and address the people, then descend and combine for me the two prayers, Zhuhr and ‘Asr, then stand at ‘Arafah and depart when the sun sets, then pray Maghrib wherever Allah has decreed for him to pray it, then stand at Muzdalifah, and when dawn breaks, pray Subh, then depart when it becomes morning, and when he has thrown the pebbles at the Jamrah, everything that was forbidden to him becomes permissible except women, until he circumambulates the House."],[13984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than a thousand prayers in any other except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is more excellent than a prayer in my mosque by a thousand prayers.”"],[13985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Sacred Mosque has been preferred over my mosque by a hundred prayers.”"],[13986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque.”"],[13987,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “An ‘Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.”"],[13988,"“They did not used to wash their private parts with water.”"],[13989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “If I were to take a close friend until I meet Allah besides Allah, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend.” He used to treat the grandfather as a father."],[13990,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever recites the Qur’an by heart or looking at it will be given a tree in Paradise; if a crow were to hatch its young under one of its leaves, and then that young crow reached old age and tried to fly, old age would overtake it before it could cut through that leaf.”"],[13991,"Al-Aqra‘ b. Habis came to the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, appoint him over his people.” ‘Umar said, “Do not appoint him, O Messenger of Allah.” They argued in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ until their voices rose. Abu Bakr said to ‘Umar, “You only intend to oppose me.” He said, “I do not intend to oppose you.” Then the verse was revealed: {O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet}. After that, when ‘Umar spoke in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, his speech was not heard until he asked him to repeat it."],[13992,"A delegation of riders from Banu Tamim came to the Prophet ﷺ, among them al-Aqraʿ b. Habis. Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, appoint al-Aqraʿ over his people.” ʿUmar said, “O Messenger of Allah, do not appoint him.” They disputed until their voices became loud. Then there was revealed concerning that: {O you who believe, do not put yourselves forward before Allah and His Messenger} until the verse was completed."],[13993,"ʿAli mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said, “Fatimah is but a part of me; what hurts her hurts me, and what exhausts her exhausts me.”"],[13994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no owner of camels but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection if he did not pay their due, and they will walk over him in a wide open plain, trampling him with their padded feet. The owner of cattle will be brought if he did not pay their due, and they will walk over him in a wide open plain, trampling him with their cloven hooves and goring him with their horns. The owner of sheep will be brought if he did not pay their due, and they will walk over him in a wide open plain, goring him with their horns and trampling him with their cloven hooves, none among them without horns or with broken horns. The owner of treasure will be brought, and a bald-headed venomous snake will be made to appear to him, and he will find nothing but to insert his hand into its mouth.” ʿAmr b. Dinar narrated it from ʿUbayd b. ʿUmar al-Laythi from the Prophet ﷺ as a mursal hadith."],[13995,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning will be destroyed.”"],[13996,"“It is not from the Sunnah to invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ on Friday on the pulpit.”"],[13997,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr on the pulpit of Makkah say in his sermon: O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “If the son of Adam were given a valley of gold, he would love a second; if he were given a second, he would love a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.”"],[13998,"About nabidh, he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars and gourds.”"],[13999,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A man swore by Allah, besides whom there is no deity, falsely, and He forgave him.”"],[14000,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and 'Ali b. 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us saying: Abu Nu'aym Dirar b. Surad narrated to us; and Yahya b. 'Uthman b. Salih narrated to us saying: Asbagh b. al-Faraj narrated to us. They said: 'Ali b. 'Abis narrated to us from Yazid b. Abi Ziyad from al-Bahi, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr who said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating until al-Hasan b. 'Ali came and climbed onto his back, and he did not make him get down until he himself got down. He would spread his legs for him so that he could enter from this side and exit from the other side.\""],[14001,"About 'umrah before Hajj? They said: \"It is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: you come forward and perform tawaf of the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then you exit ihram, even if it is one day before 'Arafah, then you enter ihram for Hajj, so you will have combined an 'umrah and a Hajj.\""],[14002,"And he said: \"You were not commanded to wipe; you were only commanded to pray.\""],[14003,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: \"Aligning the feet and placing the hand upon the hand in prayer is from the Sunnah.\""],[14004,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed al-Hakam and his offspring.\""],[14005,"Abu Malik al-Janabi narrated to us from Isma'il b. Abi Khalid from al-Sha'bi from 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr that he said while on the pulpit: \"By the Lord of this Sacred House and the Sacred Land, al-Hakam b. Abi al-'As and his offspring are cursed upon the tongue of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[14006,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one consulted is entrusted.\""],[14007,"When {Indeed you are to die, and indeed they are to die; then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord, will dispute} was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ, al-Zubayr said: \"Will what occurred between us in this world be repeated for us?\" He said: \"Yes, it will be repeated for you until every rightful claimant is given his due.\" Al-Zubayr said: \"By God, the matter is indeed grave.\""],[14008,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"He is not of us who raises weapons against us.\""],[14009,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: After the prayer, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"There is no god but God, we worship none but Him, Lord of grace, bounty, and good praise. There is no god but God, sincere to Him in religion, even if the disbelievers hate it.\""],[14010,"At the conclusion of his prayer, before standing, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"There is no god but God, alone without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no might nor power except by God; we worship none but Him. His is grace, His is bounty, and His is good praise. There is no god but God, sincere to Him in religion.\""],[14011,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\""],[14012,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\""],[14013,"A man said to Ibn al-Zubayr: \"Give us a ruling about nabidh made in earthenware jars.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid nabidh made in earthenware jars.\""],[14014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no obligatory prayer except that before it are two rak‘ahs.”"],[14015,"“Indeed Ibn ‘Abbas permits mut‘ah, but it is forbidden by Allah and His Messenger.”"],[14016,"“All are the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; so-and-so changed even the prayer.”"],[14017,"...that he finish his prayer. When he had finished it, he said: “Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not raise his hands until he had finished his prayer.”"],[14018,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"],[14019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a Muslim reaches fifty years of age, Allah turns away from him three types of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches sixty, Allah grants him turning to Him in repentance. When he reaches seventy, his evil deeds are erased and his good deeds are recorded. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives his sins, the earlier and the later, and he becomes a prisoner of Allah on earth and intercedes for his household.”"],[14020,"“He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment, wrapped in it, with its two ends placed on opposite sides.”"],[14021,"That Safwan b. Umayyah b. Khalaf al-Jumahi came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Upon whom have you stayed, O Abu Wahb?” He said, “I stayed upon al-ʿAbbas.” He said, “You have stayed upon the one who has the greatest love for Quraysh among Quraysh.”"],[14022,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ a hadith he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and which I had not heard from him. I feared that he might die or I might die before I heard it. So I purchased a camel, tied my saddle upon it, then traveled on it for a month until I reached Syria. I came to ʿAbdullah b. Unays al-Ansari, stood, and asked permission to enter, saying, “Jabir b. ʿAbdullah.” He came out to me and embraced me, and I embraced him. He said, “I said, ‘A hadith has reached me that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning wrongs. I feared that you might die or I might die before I heard it.’” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Allah will gather the servants’ — and he gestured with his hand toward Syria — ‘naked, barefoot, uncircumcised, and buhman.’” He said, “I said, ‘What is buhman?’” He said, “They will have nothing with them. A caller will call out with a voice that those far away hear just as those near hear: ‘I am the King, the Judge. It is not proper for anyone of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while someone of the people of the Fire seeks recompense from him for a wrong, nor is it proper for anyone of the people of the Fire to enter the Fire while someone of the people of Paradise seeks recompense from him for a wrong — even for a slap.’” He said, “I said, ‘How can that be, when we will come naked, uncircumcised, and buhman?’” He said, “By good deeds and bad deeds.”"],[14023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who will deal with Sufyan al-Hudhali? He satirizes me, reviles me, and harms me.” I said to him, “I will, O Messenger of Allah. Send me against him.” So he sent him. When he came to him at night, he entered his house and called out, “Where is Sufyan?” Someone from his family looked out at him and said, “What do you want?” He said, “I want Sufyan. Tell him to look out at me.” Sufyan looked out at him and said, “What do you want?” He said, “I want you to come down to me, for I have a coat of mail that I want to show you.” He said, “Where is it?” He said, “Here it is. Come down to me in your tent, and come out with me so I can show it to you.” He came out with him, and he drew his sword and struck him until he fell dead. Then he returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in his gathering and informed him that he had killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a staff on which he leaned. He handed it to him and said, “Lean on this, for those who lean on staffs on the Day of Resurrection will be few.” It remained with him until he died, and it was buried with him."],[14024,"That the group whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to ʿAbdullah b. Abi al-Huqayq to kill him were ʿAbdullah b. ʿAtik, ʿAbdullah b. Unays, Abu Qatadah, an ally of theirs, and a man from the Ansar. They arrived at Khaybar at night and went to their doors, locking them from outside. The wife of Ibn Abi al-Huqayq said, “This is the voice of ʿAbdullah b. ʿAtik.” He said, “Open up.” She opened, and I and ʿAbdullah b. ʿAtik entered. ʿAbdullah said, “Go ahead.” I went to strike her with the sword, but I remembered the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against killing women and children, so I refrained from her. ʿAli b. al-Madini said: This is ʿAbdullah b. Unays al-Ansari, not al-Juhani. This is the ʿAbdullah b. Unays al-Ansari from whom Jabir b. ʿAbdullah narrated."],[14025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “Who will deal with Khalid b. Nubayh, a man of Hudhayl?” He was at that time at ʿArafah. ʿAbdullah said: I said, “I will, O Messenger of Allah. Describe him to me.” He said, “If you saw him, you would fear him.” I said, “By the One who has honored you, I have never feared anything.” So I went out until I met him in the mountains of ʿArafah before the sun set. I met him and was struck with fear of him, and I knew then, when I feared him, what the Prophet ﷺ had said. He said, “Who is the man?” I said, “One seeking a need. Is there a place to spend the night?” He said, “Yes, follow me.” He said: I went out following his trail, prayed ʿAsr as two light rakʿahs, then went out, fearing that he would see me. Then I caught up with him and struck him with the sword. Then I entered the mountain and hid until the people had gone. Then I came out and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah and informed him of the news. Muhammad b. Kaʿb said: The Prophet ﷺ gave him a short staff and said, “Lean on this until you meet me with it on the Day of Resurrection. The fewest people on that day will be those who lean on staffs.” Muhammad b. Kaʿb said: When ʿAbdullah b. Unays died, he ordered that it be placed on his stomach, and he was shrouded over it, and it was buried with him."],[14026,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him on the night of the twenty-third."],[14027,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come to a water-skin, fold its mouth, and drink while standing."],[14028,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Seek it on the night of the twenty-third.”"],[14029,"The Prophet ﷺ said to your father regarding the Night of Decree? He said: My father was a man of the desert, so he said, “O Messenger of Allah, command me with a night in which I may come down.” He said, “Come down on the night of the twenty-third.” He said: When he turned away, he said, “Seek it in the last ten days.”"],[14030,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am at the encampment and, by the praise of Allah, I pray there. So command me with a night in which I may come down to this mosque and pray in it.” He said, “Come down on the night of the twenty-third.”"],[14031,"That a group of the Ansar said: Who is a man we can send to the Messenger of God ﷺ? Abdullah said: I said, I am. They said: Then go and ask him for us when the Night of Decree is. So I went out until I arrived at sunset at some of the dwellings of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then the Prophet ﷺ came out to pray Maghrib, so he prayed, and then he went out, and I went out with him until he entered his house and I was with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ called for a little food. Abdullah b. Unays said: I saw myself being invited by the Messenger of God ﷺ because of the scarcity of his food. When he finished, he called for his sandals, then said: \"I think you have a need.\" I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so-and-so and so-and-so sent me to you asking you when the Night of Decree is. He said: \"Tonight.\" And that night was the night of the twenty-second of Ramadan. Then he said: \"What night is it?\" I said: The night of the twenty-second. He said: \"No, rather the coming night, the night of the twenty-third.\""],[14032,"That we should descend with our families and women, and we fear for them neglect if we descend and leave them, and we dislike that this night should pass us by. Would you then send to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mention this to him and ask him to command us to a night we should descend to? Abdullah said: So they sent me, and I used to talk with them, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him and asked him to command us to a night we should descend to. He said: \"Descend on the night of the twenty-third.\" So Abdullah used to descend on that night, and when morning came he returned."],[14033,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying, and I stood on his left. The Messenger of God ﷺ took me and made me stand on his right. I had on a torn garment that did not cover me properly, so every time I prostrated I held it with my hand fearing that my private parts might be exposed, and behind me were women. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he called for a garment for me and clothed me with it, and said: \"Use it until this one wears out for you.\" Abu al-Hasan: this one from whom Sulayman b. Kathir narrated is Muhajir Abu al-Hasan; the one from whom Shu'ba narrated is a Kufan. And Abdullah b. Abd al-Rahman is Abdullah b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, the brother of Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla."],[14034,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: \"Among the greatest of major sins are associating partners with God, disobedience to parents, and the false oath. No person swears by God a binding oath in which he includes the like of a mosquito's wing except that it becomes a black spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[14035,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ mention the pilfering of charity: \"Whoever pilfers from it a camel or a sheep will be brought carrying it on the Day of Resurrection\"? Abdullah b. Unays said: Yes."],[14036,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then I was made to forget it. And I saw myself prostrating in water and mud.” Then I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrating in water and mud on the morning of the twenty-third."],[14037,"“My name in the Jāhiliyyah was so-and-so, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named me ʿAbd Allāh.”"],[14038,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever sits waiting for prayer is in prayer.”"],[14039,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer until he prays.”"],[14040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer until he prays.”"],[14041,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us, all from Mālik, from Yazīd b. al-Hād, from Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām, from the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer.”"],[14042,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart a mustard seed of arrogance.”"],[14043,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah while ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām was in a palm grove. ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “I will ask you about things that no one knows except a prophet. If you tell me about them, I will believe in you.” — the ḥadīth."],[14044,"He said, when the people stirred up trouble concerning ʿUthman's affair: 'O people, do not kill this old man but demand that he rectify matters, for no nation kills its prophet and then enjoys sound affairs until the blood of seventy thousand of its people is shed, and no nation kills its caliph and then enjoys sound affairs until the blood of forty thousand of its people is shed.' But they paid no heed to what he said and killed him. Then he sat in ʿAli's path and said: 'Where are you heading?' He replied: 'I am heading to the land of Iraq.' He said: 'Do not go to Iraq. Stick to the pulpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ.' Then the people from among ʿAli's companions sprang at him and were about to harm him, but ʿAli said: 'Leave him, for he is a man from us, the People of the House.' When ʿAli was killed, Ibn Salam said to Ibn Maʿqil: 'This is the head of the forty thousand, and upon it there will be a reconciliation. No nation kills its prophet except that seventy thousand are killed because of him, and no nation kills its caliph except that forty thousand are killed because of him.'"],[14045,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O God, bless my community in its early morning.'"],[14046,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'War is deception.'"],[14047,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he heard the people asking: 'Which deeds are best, O Messenger of God?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Faith in God and His Messenger, striving in the path of God, and an accepted pilgrimage.' Then he heard a call in the valley saying: 'I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And I bear witness, and I bear witness: no one bears witness to it except that he is free from polytheism.' The wording is that of the hadith of Ahmad b. Salih."],[14048,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ among a group of his companions when ʿUthman b. ʿAffan approached with a mount carrying two sacks, having tucked up his garment with the rope of his camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'What is in the two sacks?' He replied: 'Flour, ghee, and honey.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Make it kneel.' So he made it kneel. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ called for a cooking pot and put into it some of that flour, ghee, and honey, then ate. Then he said to his companions: 'Eat this, which the Persians call khabis.'"],[14049,"Zaid bin Sa'na went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day from the chambers, and with him was Ali bin Abi Talib. Then a man came to him riding a camel like a Bedouin, and he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, the people of the village of Banu Fulan have embraced Islam and entered into Islam, and I have told them that if they embrace Islam, provision will come to them in abundance. However, they have been afflicted with a year of drought, hardship, and scarcity of rain. So, I fear, O Messenger of Allah, that they will leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed. If you see fit to send something to them that will help them, then do so.\" Then the Messenger of Allah glanced at a man beside him, whom I think was Ali, and said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, there is nothing left of it.\" So, Zaid bin Sa'na approached him and said: \"O Muhammad, can you sell me some dates for a known time in the wall of Banu Fulan for such and such a period?\" He responded: \"No, O Jew, but I will sell you some dates for a known time for such and such a period, and do not mention the wall of Banu Fulan.\" So, I said, \"Yes,\" then he took my hand and I abandoned what I was doing. I gave him eighty mithqals of gold in known dates for such and such a period, and the man accepted them and said: \"Do justice to them and announce it to them.\" Zaid bin Sa'na said: \"So, when two or three days remained before the appointed time, the Messenger of Allah went out and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman came out with him in a group of his companions. So, when he finished the funeral prayer, and came close to a wall to sit down, I went to him and took hold of the edges of his shirt and his cloak, and I looked at him with a stern face. I said to him, \"Will you not fulfill my right, O Muhammad? By Allah, I know your clan, the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, very well. Rather, I have known you through my association with you. I looked at Umar, and his eyes were rolling in his head like a revolving wheel. Then he cast a quick glance at me with his eye and said: \"O enemy of Allah! Do you say to the Messenger of Allah what I hear and do what I see? By the One Who sent him with the truth, had I not feared that I would miss out on something, I would have struck you on the head with this sword of mine.\" The Messenger of Allah remained silent, looking at Umar calmly and with a sweet smile on his face. Then he said: \"O Umar, he and I were in more need of something other than this. You should have commanded me to do well, and commanded him to follow well. O Umar, go to him and give him his right, and add twenty sa's of dates to the place where they were kept.\" Zaid said: \"So Umar went with me and gave me my right and added twenty sa's of dates to the place where they were kept. I said: \"What is this increase, O Umar?\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah has ordered me to increase it to the place where it was kept.\" I asked him, \"Do you know me, O Umar?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"What led you to treat the Messenger of Allah as you did?\" He asked, \"O Umar, whenever something occurred to him from among the signs of Prophethood, I recognized it in his face when I looked at it, except for two signs that I did not tell him about which his forbearance outweighed his ignorance, nor would an increase in his ignorance cause his forbearance to decrease. I have informed him of both of them, and I bear witness to you, O Umar, that I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, Islam as my religion, and Muhammad as my Prophet. And I bear witness to you that half of my wealth, even though most of it comes in the form of charity given to the Ummah of Muhammad.\" Umar said, \"Or to some of them, for it is not suitable for all of them.\" I said, \"Or to some of them.\" So Umar and Zaid returned to the Messenger of Allah, and Zaid said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger. I believed in him, confirmed him, followed him, and witnessed many things with him.\" Then he died"],[14050,"\"For the Jewish scholars, I am a visitor to the mosque of our father Ibrahim and Ismail, making a covenant. I went to the messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in Makkah, and I met him when he had just finished performing Hajj. The messenger of Allah ﷺ found me in Mina with the people, and I stood among them. When the messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at me, he said, 'Are you Abdullah ibn Salam?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Come closer.' So, I approached him. He asked, 'By Allah, I ask you, O Abdullah ibn Salam, do you find me in the Torah as the messenger of Allah?' I said, 'Our Lord, describe him.' He said, 'Then Jibril came to him until he stood in front of the messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he recited to him, \"Say: He is Allah, [who is] One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent.\"' Then the messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to us. Ibn Salam said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the messenger of Allah.' Then he went to Madinah and kept his Islam hidden. When the messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Madinah, I was on top of a palm tree, and I heard a noise in the city. I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'It is the messenger of Allah who has arrived.' So, I threw myself down from the top of the palm tree and then I approached him and greeted him. Then I went back, and my mother said, 'By Allah, if Musa ibn Imran (Moses) was here, he would not have thrown himself down from the top of the palm tree like that.' I said, 'By Allah, I went down because I am eager for the arrival of the messenger of Allah ﷺ, just as Musa ibn Imran was sent.'\""],[14051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and said: 'What harm is there if one of you takes two garments for his Friday prayer besides his two work garments?'"],[14052,"We asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, are we better or those who came after us?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If one of them had the equivalent of a mountain of gold that he spends in the cause of Allah, it would not reach the level of one of you or even half of it.\""],[14053,"We used to be with the Prophet, and when he spoke he would raise his head toward the sky."],[14054,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'There is no prayer for one who turns away.'"],[14055,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'There is no prayer for one who turns away.'"],[14056,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, I have read the Quran, the Torah, and the Gospel.' He said: 'Recite this one night and that one night.'"],[14057,"Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'For God's sake, may your father be a ransom for you! Do you know a hadith that your father ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwan narrated from your grandfather ʿAbd Allah b. Salam?' He replied: 'Which hadith, may God have mercy on you? There are many hadiths.' He said: 'The hadith of the Egyptians when they besieged ʿUthman.' He said: 'I know that hadith. ʿAbd Allah b. Salam came while ʿUthman was under siege. He went and entered upon him, and they made way for him until he entered. He said: \"Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers.\" He replied: \"And upon you be peace. What brought you here, O ʿAbd Allah b. Salam?\" He said: \"I have come to remain until you are martyred or God grants you victory. I do not think these people are other than your killers. If they kill you, that is better for you and worse for them.\" ʿUthman said to him: \"I ask you by the right I have over you, go out to them, whether good that God brings about through you or evil that God repels through you.\" So he heard and obeyed, and went out to them. When they saw him, they gathered, thinking that he had come to them with something that would please them. He stood as a speaker, praised God, and extolled Him, then said: \"To proceed: God sent Muhammad ﷺ as a bearer of good tidings and a warner, giving glad tidings of Paradise to those who obey him and warning of the Fire those who disobey him. He made those who followed him prevail over all religion, even if the polytheists dislike it. Then He chose for him the dwelling places, and chose for him Madinah, making it the abode of emigration and the abode of faith. By God, the angels have continued to surround this city since the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in it, and the sword of God has continued to be sheathed from you since the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in it until this day.\" Then he said: \"God sent Muhammad with the truth. Whoever is guided is guided by God's guidance, and whoever goes astray goes astray after clear evidence and proof. No prophet was ever killed in the past except that seventy thousand warriors were killed because of him, all killed for his sake, and no caliph was ever killed except that thirty-five thousand warriors were killed because of him, all killed for his sake. So do not hasten to kill this old man. By God, no man among you kills him except that he will meet God on the Day of Resurrection with his hand cut off and paralyzed. Know that there is no right of a father over his son except that this old man has the like of it over you.\" He said: They stood up and said: \"The Jew has lied! The Jew has lied!\" He said: \"You have lied, by God, and you are sinful. I am not a Jew. I am one of the Muslims. God knows that, and His Messenger, and the believers. Quran has been revealed concerning me.\" Then he recited this verse: {Say: 'God is sufficient as witness between me and you, and whoever has knowledge of the Book.'} And God revealed the other verse: {Say: 'Have you considered: if it is from God and you disbelieve in it, and a witness from the Children of Israel bears witness to the like of it and believes, while you are arrogant?'}\" He said: Then they rose and entered upon ʿUthman and slaughtered him as a hullan is slaughtered. Shuʿayb said: I said to ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr: \"What is hullan?\" He said: \"A lamb.\" He said: ʿUthman had said before that to Kathir b. al-Salt: \"O Kathir, I, by God, will be killed tomorrow.\" He replied: \"Rather, may God raise your standing and thwart your enemy.\" He said: Then he repeated it a third time, and he said the like of that to him. He said: \"Why do you say that, O Commander of the Believers?\" He said: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him were Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, and he said to me: 'O ʿUthman, you will be with us tomorrow, and you will be killed tomorrow.' So I, by God, will be killed.\" He said: And he was killed. He said: Then ʿAbd Allah b. Salam went out to the people before they dispersed, while they were in the mosque, and stood on his feet and said: \"O people of Egypt, O killers of ʿUthman, you have killed the Commander of the Believers. By God, a pact broken, blood shed, and wealth divided will never cease, and it will not be divided.\""],[14058,"The people will remain after the Dajjal for forty years: markets will flourish and palm trees will be planted."],[14059,"My father: The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and said: “God ﷻ has praised you well regarding purification, O people of Quba. Will you not inform me?” We said: O Messenger of God, in the Torah we are required to clean ourselves with water after relieving ourselves."],[14060,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us at the mosque founded on piety, the mosque of Quba. He stood at its gate and said: “God has praised you well regarding purification. What is your purification?” We said: O Messenger of God, we are people of the scriptures and we find that using water for cleansing is required of us, and we do it today. He said: God has praised you well regarding purification. Then he recited: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and God loves those who purify themselves}."],[14061,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he passed by al-Hulaymah on his journey to Tabuk, his companions said to him: The stopping place, O Messenger of God—shade and water. It had doom trees and water. He said: “It is a land of crops and cattle; leave it, for it is commanded,” meaning his she-camel. She went on until she knelt beneath the doom tree that was in the mosque of Dhu al-Marwah."],[14062,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina, the people gathered to see him. I was among those who came out, and when I saw his face, I recognized that it was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was, \"Feed the hungry, spread peace, and pray while people are sleeping. You will enter paradise in peace.\""],[14063,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best of women is she who pleases you when you look at her, gives you what you ask when you command her, and guards your secret in her own self and your property.”"],[14064,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The distance between the two gateposts of Paradise is forty years, and a day will surely come upon it when it will be crowded like the crowding of camels that have come to water after five days, thirsty.”"],[14065,"\"To say something without knowledge, I have only seen something like a column that was placed in a green garden. In it, a rope was tied, and in its middle, there was a knot, and at its bottom, there was a halfway mark like that of a spear. It was said to me to climb it, so I climbed it and then I took hold of the rope and cut it upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Abdullah bin Salam will die while holding firmly onto the trustworthy rope.'\""],[14066,"From a revealed book or a sent prophet: There is no soul that repents one day before the illness in which it dies but that God accepts its repentance, until the sun rises from the west.”"],[14067,"“Come with me to the house so that you may pray in a mosque in which the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed and drink from a cup from which the Messenger of God ﷺ drank.” So I went with him to his house, prayed in his mosque, and he fed me dates and gave me sawiq to drink."],[14068,"“Will you not come to the house and pray in a mosque in which the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed and drink from a cup from which the Messenger of God ﷺ drank?” I went with him, and he said to me: “You are in a land where ostentation is widespread. Indeed, part of ostentation is that a man greets with salam and a gift is presented to him, and he accepts it.”"],[14069,"I came to Madinah and sat among some elders in the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ. An old man came leaning on a staff, and some of the people said: This is a man of the people of Paradise. He went behind a pillar and prayed two rakʿahs. I went to him and said: Some of the people claimed that you are a man of the people of Paradise. He said: Paradise belongs to God; He admits whomever He wills. I saw a vision in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. I saw as if a man came to me and said: Go. He took me along a great highway. A path appeared on my left, and I wanted to take it, but he said: You are not one of its people. Then another path appeared on my right, and I took it until I came to a slippery mountain. He took my hand and threw me up, and there I was on its summit, unable to settle or control myself. Then I saw a pillar with a handle of gold at its top. He took my hand and threw me up until I grasped the handle. I related it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “You have seen good. The great highway is the gathering place. The path that appeared on your left is the path of the people of the Fire, and you are not one of its people. The path that appeared on your right is the path of the people of Paradise. The slippery mountain is the abode of the martyrs. The handle you held fast to is the handhold of Islam, and you will remain holding it, God willing, until you die. I hope to be one of the people of Paradise.” And he was ʿAbdullah b. Salam."],[14070,"Whoever would like to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this one. I said: By God, I will follow him and find out where his house is. He said: I followed him until he nearly left Madinah; then he entered his house. I asked permission, and he permitted me. He said: What is your need, O nephew? I said to him: I heard the people say about you when you stood: Whoever would like to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this one, and I would like to be with you. He said: God knows best who are the people of Paradise. I will tell you why they said that. While I was sleeping, a visitor came to me and said: Rise. He took my hand and I went with him. There appeared broad paths on my left, and I started to take one, but he said to me: Do not take it, for it is the path of the companions of the left. Then there were broad paths on my right, and he said: Take this way. We came to a mountain, and he said: Climb up this. Whenever I tried to climb, I fell on my face; I did that many times. Then he took me until he brought me to a pillar whose top was in the sky and its base in the earth, with a ring at its top. He said to me: Climb to the top of this. I said: How can I climb to the top of this when its top is in the sky? He took my hand and threw me up, and there I was clinging to the ring. Then he toppled the pillar, and it fell, while I remained clinging to the ring until morning. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, relating the vision. He said: “As for the paths you saw on your left, they are the paths of the companions of the left. As for the paths you saw on your right, they are the paths of the companions of the right. The mountain is the abode of the martyrs, and you will not attain it. The pillar is the pillar of Islam, and the handle is the handhold of Islam. You will never cease holding to it until you die.” Then he said to me: “Do you know how God created creation?” I said: No. He said: God created Adam and said: You will beget so-and-so, and so-and-so will beget so-and-so, and so-and-so will beget so-and-so, and so-and-so will beget so-and-so—his term of life is such, his deeds are such and such, and his provision is such and such. Then the spirit is breathed into him."],[14071,"From a sent prophet or from a revealed book: if a servant committed every sin, then repented to God one day before his death, it would be accepted from him.”"],[14072,"“My name in the Jahiliyyah was so-and-so, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named me ʿAbd Allah.”"],[14073,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. I am the first from whom the earth will split open, and no boast. I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted. The banner of praise will be in my hand on the Day of Resurrection; beneath me will be Adam and all those after him.”"],[14074,"“Indeed the most honored of God’s creation before God is Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.”"],[14075,"ʿAbd Allah b. Salam said: “Indeed the most honored of creation before God on the Day of Resurrection is Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.”"],[14076,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever relates a speech that he would not like to be spread about him is a trust, even if its owner did not ask him to keep it secret.”"],[14077,"I said, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting: “Indeed we find in the Book of God that on Friday there is an hour in which no believing servant who is praying and asking God for something coincides with it except that He grants him his need.” ʿAbd Allah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ gestured to me, saying: “A part of an hour.” I said: “You have spoken the truth, a part of an hour.” I said: “Which hour is it?” He said: “The last hours of the day.” I said: “But it is not an hour of prayer.” He said: “Yes, indeed. When a believing servant prays and then sits, nothing keeps him except the prayer, so he is in prayer.”"],[14078,"I sat among a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and they said: “Which of you will go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him which deeds are most beloved to God?” Then it was revealed: {O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do?} Abu Salama said: ʿAbd Allah b. Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. Yahya said: Abu Salama recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. Al-Awzaʿi said: Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. Al-Walid said: Al-Awzaʿi recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. Duhaym said: Al-Walid recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. Ibrahim said: He recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept. And Ibrahim recited it to us from its beginning to its end, then wept."],[14079,"That he said: 'O Messenger of God, we find you in the Book of God: a community that praises much, the birthplace of their Prophet is Makkah, his emigration is to Taybah, and their striving is in Syria. They tie their lower garments at their waists and expose their limbs. They have a hum at night in the mosques like the hum of bees in their hives. On the Day of Resurrection they will come with radiant faces and limbs.'"],[14080,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever prays a prayer and then waits for the next one is in a state of prayer until he finishes it.'"],[14081,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'A dirham a man acquires from usury is greater in the sight of God than thirty-three acts of adultery he commits in Islam.'"],[14082,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'A dirham a man acquires from usury is greater in the sight of God than thirty-three acts of adultery he commits in Islam.'"],[14083,"On the authority of ʿUrwah: 'In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, from the Banu Imri' al-Qays b. Thaʿlabah b. Kaʿb b. al-Khazraj b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah b. Imri' al-Qays.'"],[14084,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab: 'In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah b. Imri' al-Qays.'"],[14085,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , entered in the Umrah of Al-Qadaa' with Abdullah ibn Rawahah in front of him, and he said:[Al-Bahr Al-Rajz]Let the disbelievers refrain from his way ... The Most Merciful has revealed in his revelationThat the best killing is in his way."],[14086,"That when the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah, ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah walked in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ, reciting:"],[14087,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he entered Makkah for that ʿUmrah, entered it while ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah al-Ansari was holding the nose-rein of his she-camel, reciting:"],[14088,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his companions during the Umrah of al-Qada', saying: 'Uncover your shoulders and hasten in circumambulation,' so that the polytheists would see their vigor and strength; and he plotted against them with all he could. The people of Makkah—men, women, and children—flocked out to look at the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions while they were circumambulating the House, and ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah was reciting rajaz verses before the Messenger of God ﷺ, girded with a sword, saying:"],[14089,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he conquered Khaybar, stipulated for himself the land and all yellow and white—meaning gold and silver. The people of Khaybar said to him: 'We know the land better.' So he gave it to them on condition that we work it and that we have half of the fruit and you have half. He mentioned that he gave it to them on that basis. When the time came for the date palms to be harvested, he sent Ibn Rawahah to them, and he estimated the crop—the people of Madinah call it khars. He said: 'This much and this much.' They said: 'You have overestimated for us, O Ibn Rawahah.' He said: 'I will take charge of estimating the palms and give you half of what I said.' They said: 'This is the truth, and upon it the heavens and the earth stand. We accept to take what you said.'"],[14090,"The affair of Khaybar: \"The Prophet ﷺ used to send Ibn Rawahah to the Jews, and he would estimate the date palms when they ripened, before any of it was eaten. Then the Jews would be given the choice to take it according to that estimate, or to hand it over to them for that amount. The Prophet ﷺ only ordered the estimation so that the zakah might be calculated before the fruits were eaten and dispersed.\""],[14091,"When Ibn Rawahah gave the Jews the choice, they took the dates, and they owed twenty thousand wasqs."],[14092,"The Prophet ﷺ conquered it, and it was a collection (of land) belonging to him—its cultivated fields and its palm trees. The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions had no slaves, so the Prophet ﷺ made a settlement with the Jews on condition that they do the work for us, and you have half of the dates, on condition that I will let you remain as long as Allah and His Messenger see fit. That was when the Prophet ﷺ sent Ibn Rawahah to assess the crop for them. When he gave them the choice, the Jews took the dates, and Khaybar remained in the hands of the Jews under the Prophet ﷺ's settlement until ʿUmar came and expelled them. The Jews said, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ not make a settlement with us on such and such?\" He replied, \"Yes, on condition that he would let you remain as long as Allah and His Messenger saw fit. Now it has become my view to expel you.\" So he expelled them, then divided it among the Muslims who had conquered it with the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not give any of it to anyone who had not been present at its conquest. He said: So its people now are the Muslims; there are no Jews in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only ordered the estimation so that he might calculate the zakah before the fruits were eaten and dispersed. They continued on that basis."],[14093,"About the Prophet ﷺ's agreement with the Jews of Khaybar, that we have half of the fruit and you have half, and you do the work for us. When their fruit ripened, they came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Our fruit has ripened, so send an assessor to assess between us and you.\" The Prophet ﷺ sent ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah. When he went around among their palm trees and looked at them, he said, \"By Allah, I do not know any of Allah's creation who fabricates more against Allah and is more hostile to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you. By Allah, Allah has not created anyone more hateful to me than you. By Allah, that does not cause me to wrong you by the weight of a single grain, as I know it.\" He said: Then he assessed all of it—what was for them and what was for the Jews—as eighty thousand wasqs. The Jews said, \"You have given us a choice.\" Ibn Rawahah said, \"If you wish, give us forty thousand wasqs and depart from us.\" They looked at one another, then said, \"By this the heavens and the earth are upheld, and by this they will overcome you.\""],[14094,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he sent ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah to divide the fruit with the Jews. When he came to them, they began offering him gifts of food, and he disliked to take anything from them. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only sent me to act justly between him and you, so I have no need for your gift.\" Then he assessed the palm trees. When he completed the assessment, ʿAbd Allah gave them a choice. He said, \"If you wish, I will guarantee your share and take charge of it, and if you wish, you will guarantee our share and take charge of it.\" They chose to guarantee it and take charge of it. They said, \"O Ibn Rawahah, this that you offer us and act upon is what upholds the heavens and the earth; they are only upheld by truth.\" Khaybar belonged to those who were present at Hudaybiyyah; no one else shared in it, none of them stayed behind from it, no one other than them attended it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not permit anyone who had stayed behind from his departure to Hudaybiyyah to be present at Khaybar."],[14095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah to divide the fruit with the Jews. When he came to them, they began offering him gifts of food and speaking to him, and they gathered for him jewelry from their women's jewelry. They said, \"This is for you, and be lenient with us and overlook.\" Ibn Rawahah said, \"O company of Jews, by Allah, you are the most hateful of people to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only sent me to act justly between you and him, so I have no need for your worldly goods, and I will not wrong you. You have only offered me what is unlawful (suht), and we do not consume it.\" Then he assessed the palm trees. When he completed the assessment, he gave them a choice. He said, \"If you wish, I will guarantee your share, and if you wish, you will guarantee our share and take charge of it.\" They chose to guarantee it and take charge of it. They said, \"O Ibn Rawahah, this that you act upon is what upholds the heavens and the earth; they are only upheld by truth.\""],[14096,"I said to Ata' that this incident occurred during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he informed me about Ibn Rawaha that he mediated between the Prophet ﷺ and the Jews, and they said, \"If you want, it is for us, and if you want, it is for you.\" They said this and the heavens and the earth were established."],[14097,"\"O company of Jews, you are the most hateful of Allah's creation to me, but that will not cause me to wrong you. As for what you have offered us of this bribe, it is unlawful (suht), and we do not consume it.\" Then he assessed the crop for them, then gave them the choice to take it or for him to take it. They said, \"By this the heavens and the earth are upheld,\" and they took it according to that assessment."],[14098,"The Prophet ﷺ had no workers to work on the palm trees and crops of Khaybar, so the Prophet ﷺ summoned the Jews of Khaybar and handed Khaybar over to them on condition that they work it for half, and that they deliver it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions. The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"I will let you remain in it as long as Allah permits you to remain.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah to them, and he would assess the palm trees when the first fruits ripened, before any of it was eaten, then he would give the Jews the choice to take it according to that estimate or to hand it over to them according to that estimate."],[14099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Muʾtah in Jumada al-Ula of the year eight, and he placed Zayd b. Harithah in command over them. He said to them, \"If Zayd is struck down, then Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib is in command of the people; and if Jaʿfar is struck down, then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah is in command of the people.\" The people equipped themselves and prepared to depart, and they were three thousand. When their departure was near, the people bade farewell to the commanders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted them. When ʿAbd Allah bade farewell along with those who bade farewell, he wept. It was said to him, \"What makes you weep, O Ibn Rawahah?\" He said, \"By Allah, it is not love of this world or longing for you; but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite a verse from the Book of Allah in which the Fire is mentioned: 'There is none of you but will pass over it; this is, upon your Lord, a decree that must be accomplished.' So I do not know how it will be with the crossing after the passing over?\" The Muslims said to them, \"May Allah accompany you, defend you, and return you to us righteous.\" Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah said:"],[14100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Muʾtah in Jumada al-Ula of the year eight, and he placed Zayd b. Harithah in command over them. He said to them, \"If Zayd is struck down, then Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib is in command of the people; and if Jaʿfar is struck down, then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah is in command of the people.\" The people equipped themselves and prepared to depart, and they were three thousand. When their departure was near, the people bade farewell to the commanders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted them. When ʿAbd Allah bade farewell along with those who bade farewell, he wept. It was said to him, \"What makes you weep, O Ibn Rawahah?\" He said, \"By Allah, it is not love of this world or longing for you; but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite a verse from the Book of Allah in which the Fire is mentioned: 'There is none of you but will pass over it; this is, upon your Lord, a decree that must be accomplished.' So I do not know how it will be with the crossing after the passing over?\" The Muslims said to them, \"May Allah accompany you, defend you, and return you to us righteous.\" Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah said:"],[14101,"By Allah, it is as if I am looking at Jaʿfar when he plunged from a sorrel horse of his, then hamstrung it, then fought the people until he was killed. When Jaʿfar was killed, ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner, then advanced with it while he was on his horse. He began trying to make himself dismount, and he hesitated somewhat, then he said:"],[14102,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army to Mu'tah and appointed Zaid bin Haritha as their commander. If Zaid is killed, then their leader will be Jafar. If Jafar is killed, then Abdullah bin Rawaha al-Ansari will be their leader. They set out towards Mu'tah going towards Sham (Levant). Their commanders, who were appointed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , were killed. Khalid bin Walid then took the flag and the Muslims agreed to it. Allah granted the Muslims victory over the enemy."],[14103,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"They were shown to me in Paradise in a tent of pearl, each one of them on a couch.\" I saw Zayd and Ibn Rawahah with their necks turned away, but as for Jaʿfar, he was upright, with no turning away. He said: So I asked, or it was said to me, \"When death came upon them, it was as if they turned away or as if they averted their faces, but Jaʿfar did not do that.\" Ibn ʿUyaynah said: That is when Ibn Rawahah says:"],[14104,"Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent an army to Mu'ta and appointed Zayd b. Haritha over them; if he is struck, then Ja'far b. Abi Talib is their commander; if Ja'far is struck, then Abdullah b. Rawaha is their commander. They set out until they met Ibn Abi Sabra al-Ghassani at Mu'ta, where there were gatherings of Arab Christians and Romans, and there were Tanukh and Bahram. Ibn Abi Sabra closed the fortress before the Muslims for three days, then they came out and met on green crops and fought a fierce battle. Zayd b. Haritha took the banner and was killed, then Ja'far took it and was killed, then Ibn Rawaha took it and was killed. Then the Muslims, after the commanders of the Messenger of God ﷺ, agreed upon Khalid b. al-Walid, and God routed the enemy and granted victory to the Muslims. He sent them in Jumada al-Ula."],[14105,"Abu Hurayra used to say in his narratives: \"Your brother used to say poetry or words that were not of obscenity, and he is Abdullah b. Rawaha.\""],[14106,"Abu Hurayra used to say: \"A brother of yours used not to utter obscenity,\" meaning Abdullah b. Rawaha. And he said."],[14107,"He heard Abu Hurayra while he was saying in his narratives, mentioning the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Your brother used not to utter obscenity,\" meaning Abdullah b. Rawaha."],[14108,"He heard Abu Hurayra saying in his narratives: \"Your brother used not to utter obscenity,\" meaning Abdullah b. Rawaha."],[14109,"While I was passing by in the mosque and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with some of his companions, the people said, \"O Abdullah bin Rawaha, O Abdullah bin Rawaha.\" I thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was calling me, so I came to him and he said, \"Sit down, O Abdullah bin Rawaha, how do you say poetry when you want to speak?\" I said, \"I think and then I speak.\" He said, \"You should curse the polytheists.\" I hadn't prepared anything, so I said: [The Simple Ocean] Tell me the price of the cloak, when ... you were like penguins or did shields harm you?So I knew the hatred in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because I priced his people's cloaks, so I looked and then I said: O Hashim of goodness, indeed Allah has favored you ... over all creation, and He has no equal.I have thoroughly examined the goodness in you ... with a perception that they lacked in what they saw.And if you were to ask or seek help from some of them ... in your entire affair, they would not have given refuge or help.So may Allah make firm what He has granted you of good ... with the firmness of Musa and the help they had received.He said, \"And you may be firm as well, O Ibn Rawaha.\""],[14110,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from coming to his family at night unannounced."],[14111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[14112,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; he said: My father Maslama b. Qa'nab narrated to me, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Abdullah b. Zam'a, that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in his sermon, mentioning the she-camel and the one who hamstrung her. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, {When the most wretched of them was sent forth} God sent forth for her a man mighty, strong, and protected in his clan, like Abu Zam'a. Then he mentioned women and said: \"Why would one of you go and flog his wife like the flogging of a slave, then perhaps lie with her at the end of his day?\" Then I heard him admonishing them about their laughter at breaking wind. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What makes one of you laugh at what he does?\""],[14113,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ one day in his sermon mention the she-camel and the one who hamstrung her, and he said: {When the most wretched of them was sent forth} there was sent forth for her a man mighty, fierce, and protected in his people, like Abu Zam'a. Then he mentioned women and said: \"Why would one of you go to his wife and flog her like the flogging of a slave, and perhaps he may lie with her at the end of his day?\" Then he admonished them about their laughter at breaking wind and said: \"What makes one of you laugh at what he does?\""],[14114,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"One of you should flog his wife with the the skin of a slave, then have sexual intercourse with her at the end of the day.\""],[14115,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Sawda bt. Zam'a. Her brother Abd b. Zam'a came from the Hajj and began to pour dust on his head. When he embraced Islam, he said: \"I was foolish the day I poured dust on my head because the Messenger of God ﷺ married Sawda.\""],[14116,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ became gravely ill and I was with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called to prayer. He said: \"Tell someone to lead the people in prayer.\" I went out and found Umar among the people, while Abu Bakr was absent. I said: \"O Umar, stand up and lead the people in prayer.\" He stood up, and when he said the takbir, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard his voice, for Umar was a loud-voiced man. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Where is Abu Bakr? God and the Muslims refuse that.\" He sent for Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, then he led the people in prayer. Abdullah b. Zam'a said: Umar said to me: \"Woe to you, what have you done to me, O Ibn Zam'a? By God, when you commanded me, I only thought that the Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered you to do that. Had it not been for that, I would not have led the people in prayer.\" I said: \"By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not command me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I considered you the most deserving of those present to lead the people in prayer.\""],[14117,"When the Prophet's ﷺ illness became severe, and I was with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called to prayer. He said: \"Tell him to instruct the people to pray.\" He went out and came to Umar, while Abu Bakr was absent, and said: \"O Umar, stand up and lead the people in prayer.\" He stood up, and when he said the takbir, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard his voice, for Umar was loud-voiced. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Where is Abu Bakr? God and the Muslims refuse that.\" He repeated that several times. He sent for Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed that prayer, then Abu Bakr led the people in prayer. Abdullah b. Zam'a said: Umar said to me: \"What have you done to me, O Ibn Zam'a? By God, when you commanded me to lead the people in prayer, I only thought that the Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered you to do that. Had it not been for that, I would not have led the people in prayer.\" I said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not command me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr, I considered you the best of those present.\""],[14118,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; they said: Mujammiʿ b. Yaʿqub al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ismaʿil, who said: It was said to ʿAbdullah b. Abi Habiba, “What did you witness from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in our mosque, Qubaʾ. I came, and I was a young boy, until I sat on his right, and Abu Bakr sat on his left.” He said: “Then he called for a drink, drank, and handed it to me on his right.”"],[14119,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; they said: Mujammiʿ b. Yaʿqub al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ismaʿil, who said: It was said to ʿAbdullah b. Abi Habiba, “What did you witness from the Prophet ﷺ?” He said: “He stood to pray, and I saw him praying in his sandals.”"],[14120,"A letter of a man came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to ʿAbdullah b. al-Arqam, “Respond on my behalf.” So he wrote his reply, then read it to him, and he said, “You have been correct and done well. O Allah, grant him success.” When ʿUmar assumed the caliphate, he used to consult him."],[14121,"We were with him on a journey, and he used to lead them in prayer. When the prayer time arrived, he said to us, “Let one of you lead you in prayer, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When the prayer time arrives and one of you has a need, let him begin with the need.’”"],[14122,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When the prayer is called and one of you has to defecate, let him begin with defecating.”"],[14123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the prayer is called and one of you wants to defecate, let him begin with defecating.”"],[14124,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you wants to go to relieve himself and the prayer has started, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14125,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you feels the need to defecate, let him begin with it before the prayer.”"],[14126,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you has to relieve himself and the prayer has been called, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14127,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you wants to relieve himself and the prayer has been called, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you needs to relieve himself and the prayer time arrives, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14129,"He went out to Makkah, and he was their imam. He put forward a man to lead them in prayer, then said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When the prayer is called and one of you has to defecate, let him begin with it.’”"],[14130,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “When the prayer is established and one of you needs to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14131,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When the prayer is established and one of you finds the need to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14132,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When one of you finds the need to relieve himself and the prayer has been established, let him begin with relieving himself.”"],[14133,"I was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ʿAbd al-Qays, but I was not with them; I only came with my father. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the vessels that you have heard of: al-dubbaʾ, al-hantam, al-naqir, and al-muqayyar."],[14134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade breaking the coinage of the Muslims that is current among them, except for a valid reason—that one breaks a dirham and makes it into silver, or breaks a dinar and makes it into dirhams."],[14135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade breaking the coinage of the Muslims that is current among them, except for a valid reason."],[14136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you buys meat, let him increase its broth, for if one of you does not get meat, he gets broth, and it is one of the two meats.”"],[14137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When you are in reeds, snow, or mud, and prayer comes, then gesture with a gesture.”"],[14138,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade facing either of the two qiblahs when defecating or urinating."],[14139,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting with them. He entered his house and said, \"Come in to me, but let none enter upon me except a Qurayshi.\" So I slipped in and entered. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O assembly of Quraysh, is there anyone among you who is not from you?\" They said, \"We inform you, O Messenger of God, of our fathers and mothers. With us is the son of a sister and the client.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The ally of a people is one of them, the client of a people is one of them, and the son of a people's sister is one of them. O assembly of Quraysh, you are the guardians after me of this matter, so do not die except as believers. Hold fast to the rope of God all together and do not divide, and do not be like those who divided and differed after clear proofs came to them. They were commanded only to worship God, being sincere to Him in religion, as hanifs, and to establish prayer and give zakah. That is the religion of the upright. O assembly of Quraysh, preserve me in my companions and their sons and their sons' sons. May God have mercy on the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar.\""],[14140,"We were sitting around the Messenger of God ﷺ in his mosque in Madinah when Gabriel ﷺ came to him with revelation. He covered himself with his cloak and remained for a long time until he was relieved and uncovered his cloak. There he was, sweating profusely, holding something in his hand. He said, \"Which of you knows what comes out of date palms?\" The Ansar said, \"We do, O Messenger of God, may our fathers and mothers be your ransom. Nothing comes out of date palms but we know it; we are people of date palms.\" Then he opened his hand, and there were date pits in it. He said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"These are date pits, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Pits of what?\" They said, \"Pits of a year.\" He said, \"You have spoken truly. Gabriel ﷺ came to you to oversee your religion. You will surely follow the ways of those before you, step by step, and you will take as they took: if a span, then a span; if a cubit, then a cubit; if a fathom, then a fathom, so much so that if they entered a lizard's hole, you would enter it. Except that the Children of Israel split concerning Moses into seventy sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and their community. Then they split concerning Jesus, son of Mary, into seventy-one sects, all astray except one: Islam and their community. Then you will be upon seventy-two sects, all in the Fire except one: Islam and their community.\""],[14141,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah narrated to us. And ʿAli b. al-Mubarak al-Sanʿani narrated to us: Ismaʿil b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever revives dead land that does not belong to a Muslim, it is his, and there is no right for a wrongful root.\""],[14142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever revives dead land, it is his, and there is no right for a wrongful root.\""],[14143,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"The well is a loss, the injury of a dumb animal is a loss, the mine is a loss, and on buried treasure is a fifth.\""],[14144,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"On Friday there is an hour during the day in which a servant does not ask for anything but he is given it.\" It was said, \"Which hour is it, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"When the sun rises until it declines.\""],[14145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say the takbir in the two Eid prayers: in the first rakʿah seven takbirs and in the second rakʿah five takbirs, before the recitation."],[14146,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us. And ʿAli b. al-Mubarak al-Sanʿani narrated to us: Ismaʿil b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The world will not pass away until there is a detachment of Muslims at Bawlan. O Ali,\" meaning Ali b. Abi Talib. He said, \"At your service, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"You will fight the Banu al-Asfar, and those after you from the believers will fight them. Then the best of the Muslims, the people of Hijaz who strive in the path of God, whom no blame of a blamer affects regarding God, will go out to them, until God grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome through glorification and takbir. God will demolish its fortress, and they will seize great wealth such as they have never seized before, so much so that they will divide it by the shield. Then a crier will cry out: O people of Islam, the false messiah, the Dajjal, has appeared in your lands. The people will turn away from the wealth; some will take and some will leave, and the taker will regret and the leaver will regret. Then they will say, 'Who is this crier?' and they will not know who he is. They will say, 'Send a scouting party to Ludd. If the messiah has indeed appeared, he will bring you knowledge of it.' They will come and look, but they will see nothing, and they will see the people quiet. They will say, 'The crier cried out only to us, so resolve and be guided. We will all go out to Ludd. If the false messiah is there, we will fight him until God judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges. If it is otherwise, then it is your lands, your kinsmen, and your armies; you will have returned to them.'\""],[14147,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever revives a sunnah of mine that has been killed after me, he will have the like of the reward of those who act upon it from the people, without that diminishing anything from the rewards of the people. And whoever introduces an innovation that God and His Messenger are not pleased with, upon him will be the like of the sin of those who act upon it from the people, without that diminishing anything from the sins of the people.\""],[14148,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, religion will retreat to Hijaz just as a snake retreats to its hole. Religion will cling to Hijaz as the mountain goat clings to the mountain top. Religion began as something strange and will return as something strange, so blessed are the strangers who repair what people corrupt after me of my sunnah.\""],[14149,"We went on a raid with the Messenger of God ﷺ, the first raid he undertook, at al-Abwaʾ, until when we were at al-Rawhaʾ, he stopped at ʿIrq al-Zabyah and prayed. Then he said, \"Do you know what the name of this mountain is?\" They said, \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"This is a mountain from the mountains of Paradise. O God, bless it and bless its people in it.\" And he said of al-Rawhaʾ, \"This is Sajasij, a valley from the valleys of Paradise. Seventy prophets prayed in this mosque before me, and Moses passed through it wearing two Qatwani cloaks on a gray camel, among seventy thousand of the Children of Israel, performing pilgrimage to the Ancient House. The Hour will not come until Jesus, son of Mary, God's servant and messenger, passes through it as a pilgrim or in umrah, or God combines both for him.\""],[14150,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “I fear for my Ummah after me from three deeds.” They said, “What are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “The slip of a scholar, or a tyrannical judgment, or a followed whim.”"],[14151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No jalab, no janab, no iʿtirad, and no townsman selling for a Bedouin.”"],[14152,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “No sulul and no ghulul; and whoever commits ghulul will bring what he stole on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14153,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he arrived in Medina. We used to pray towards the direction of the Qibla of Jerusalem for seventeen months."],[14154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed the cutting of the waist belt, the anklet, and the one who carries the stick of the beast."],[14155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Four mountains from the mountains of Paradise, four rivers from the rivers of Paradise, and four battles from the battles of Paradise.” It was said, “What are the mountains?” He said, “Uhud, which loves us and we love it, is a mountain from the mountains of Paradise; al-Tur is a mountain from the mountains of Paradise; and Lubnan is a mountain from the mountains of Paradise. The four rivers are the Nile, the Euphrates, Sayhan, and Jayhan. The battles are Badr, Uhud, the Khandaq, and Hunayn.”"],[14156,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Kathir b. ʿAbd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Three things from the affair of Jahiliyyah that people will not abandon: defaming lineages, wailing, and their saying, ‘We were given rain by such-and-such a star.’”"],[14157,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.”"],[14158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Horses will be scattered on the day of their arrival at the water.”"],[14159,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man say, “Here it is, green!” The Prophet ﷺ said, “O at your service! We have taken your good omen from your mouth. Take us out to a green place.” So they went out to it, and no sword was drawn there."],[14160,"The Prophet ﷺ said the takbir over the Negus five times."],[14161,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A believer is not stung from the same hole twice.”"],[14162,"The Prophet ﷺ protected Madinah by a barid from every direction."],[14163,"We raided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Conquest, and we were a thousand and some. Allah granted us victory over Makkah and Hunayn, until when we were between Hunayn and al-Ta’if, he saw a tree on which weapons used to be hung; it was called Dhat Anwat and was worshiped besides Allah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he turned away from it on a summer day to a shade that was nearer than it. A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as they have a Dhat Anwat.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “These are the ways! You have said, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, just as the Children of Israel said to Musa, ‘Make for us a god as they have gods.’ He said, ‘Should I seek for you a god other than Allah, while He has favored you over all the worlds?’”"],[14164,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali b. Abi Talib: 'You will fight the Banu al-Asfar in a band of Muslims whom no critic's blame in God's cause will affect, until you conquer Constantinople with takbir and tasbih.'"],[14165,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Kathir b. 'Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You will fight the Banu al-Asfar and kill them, and after you the believers will fight them. The believers who strive in God's cause will go out to them—no critic's blame in God's cause will affect them—until God opens Constantinople and Rome for them with tasbih and takbir. Its fortress will be demolished, and they will seize great wealth there, so much that they will divide the wealth by shields. Then a crier will cry out: O people of Islam, the false messiah, the Dajjal, has appeared in your lands and among your offspring. They will say: Who is this crier? But they will not know who he is. They will say: Look and be guided. Send a vanguard to Ludd; if the messiah has appeared, he will bring you knowledge of him. So they will send the vanguard to Ludd. Then they will say: Let us march to them. If it is him, we will fight him until God judges between us, and He is the best of judges. If it is the other, then it is your land and your kinsfolk; you will have returned to it.'"],[14166,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Muslims are bound by their conditions, except a condition that forbids the lawful or permits the unlawful. Reconciliation between people is permissible, except a reconciliation that permits the unlawful or forbids the lawful.'"],[14167,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The charity of a Muslim increases lifespan, prevents an evil death, and through it God removes arrogance and pride.'"],[14168,"\"I have memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twelve principles from the principles of religion.\""],[14169,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever alters the boundary markers of land, upon him is the curse of God and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection; God will accept from him neither sarf nor 'adl.'"],[14170,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No usurpation and no plunder.'"],[14171,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever takes as patrons others than his mawali, upon him is the curse of God and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection; God will accept from him neither sarf nor 'adl. Whoever kills other than his killer, upon him is the curse of God and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection; He will accept from him neither sarf nor 'adl. Whoever commits an offence or shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of God and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection; God will accept from him neither sarf nor 'adl.'"],[14172,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No mufraj shall be left in Islam.' Ibn Numayr added in his narration: 'until he is joined to a tribe.'"],[14173,"From 'Urwah: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr: 'Amr b. 'Awf, client of Suhayl b. 'Amr.'"],[14174,"He informed him that 'Amr b. 'Awf, who was an ally of Banu 'Amir and had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizya. The Messenger of God ﷺ had made peace with al-Bahrayn and appointed al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami over them. Abu 'Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of his arrival, so they attended the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he had prayed, he left, and they approached him. He smiled when he saw them and said: 'I think you have heard of the arrival of Abu 'Ubaydah and that he has brought something?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Rejoice and hope for what pleases you. By God, it is not poverty that I fear for you, but I fear that the world will be spread out for you as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete for it as they competed for it, and it will distract you as it distracted them.'"],[14175,"He informed him that 'Amr b. 'Awf al-Ansari, who was an ally of Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy and had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizya. The Messenger of God ﷺ had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami over them. Abu 'Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu 'Ubaydah, so they attended the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had prayed with them, they left and approached him. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled when he saw them, then said: 'I think you have heard that Abu 'Ubaydah has brought something?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Rejoice and hope for what pleases you. By God, it is not poverty that I fear for you, but I fear that the world will be spread out for you as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete for it as they competed for it, and it will destroy you as it destroyed them.'"],[14176,"He informed him that 'Amr b. 'Awf, who was an ally of Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy and had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ, informed him that the Prophet ﷺ sent Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn, and he brought its jizya. The Prophet ﷺ had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami over them. Abu 'Ubaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu 'Ubaydah, so they attended the dawn prayer with the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had prayed, he left, and they approached him. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled when he saw them, then said: 'I think you have heard that Abu 'Ubaydah has brought something from al-Bahrayn?' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Rejoice in what pleases you. By God, it is not poverty that I fear for you, but I fear for you that the world will be spread out for you as it was spread out for those before you, and you will compete for it as they competed for it, and it will destroy you as it destroyed them.'"],[14177,"He informed him—and he had been present at Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ—that the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn and he brought back its jizyah. The Messenger of God ﷺ himself had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed al-ʿAlaʾ b. al-Hadrami as governor over them. Abu ʿUbaydah arrived with wealth from al-Bahrayn, and the Ansar heard of Abu ʿUbaydah's arrival, so they came to the Messenger of God ﷺ at the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had prayed, he turned away, and they presented themselves before him. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled when he saw them, then said: \"I think you have heard that Abu ʿUbaydah has arrived with something?\" They said: \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Rejoice and hope for what pleases you. For by God, it is not poverty that I fear for you, but I fear for you that the world will be spread out before you as it was spread out before those before you, and you will compete for it as they competed for it, and it will destroy you as it destroyed them.\""],[14178,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to me: \"May God make you beautiful.\" He was a very old man, and he was handsome."],[14179,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: \"Come near and wipe my back.\" So I came near and wiped his back, and I placed the Seal of Prophethood between my fingers. I said: \"And what is the Seal of Prophethood?\" He said: \"Hair between his shoulders.\""],[14180,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ wiped my face and prayed for beauty for me.\" ʿAzrah said: \"Some of my family informed me that he reached one hundred and seven years, and there was nothing in his head or beard except a few white hairs.\""],[14181,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer, then ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon to us until the noon prayer came. He descended and prayed, then ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon to us until the afternoon prayer came. Then he descended and prayed the afternoon prayer, then ascended the pulpit and delivered a sermon to us until the sun had set. He informed us of what would come to pass, and the one with the best memory among us retained it.\""],[14182,"I heard ʿAmr b. Akhtab Abu Zayd al-Ansari say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ asked for water, so I brought him a cup in which there was a hair. I removed it, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O God, make him beautiful.' He said: 'I certainly saw him after sixty years had passed, with not a single white hair on his head or in his beard.'\""],[14183,"I heard 'Amr bin Akhatab Abu Zaid al-Ansari saying, \"I saw the seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like this, appearing as if it were being embossed.\""],[14184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"They call to God, may He be exalted, but they have nothing to do with God. Whoever fights them is closer to God than they are\"—meaning the Kharijites."],[14185,"He \"went on nine military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[14186,"The Prophet ﷺ once passed by the houses of the Ansar and found a group of people gathered. He asked, \"Who slaughtered before we did?\" A man came forward and said, \"I did, O Messenger of Allah. Today is a day when food is disliked.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Prepare something.\" The man said, \"By Allah, I have nothing but a piece of mutton or a pregnant goat.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Go ahead and slaughter it, and it will not be counted as a sacrifice for anyone after you.\""],[14187,"The Prophet ﷺ passed through our dwellings and noticed the smell of roasting meat. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Who is this who has slaughtered?\" A man from among us came out and said: \"O Messenger of God, it is a day on which food is undesirable, so I slaughtered to eat and to feed my neighbors.\" He said: \"Slaughter again.\" He said: \"No, by God besides whom there is no god, I have nothing but a jadhaʿah of sheep or a lamb.\" He said it three times. He said: \"Then slaughter it, and a jadhaʿah will not suffice for anyone after you.\" He had slaughtered before the prayer."],[14188,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Forbid your people from nabidh of earthenware jars, for it is forbidden by God and His Messenger.\""],[14189,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: “Indeed, which day is most sacred?” They said: “The day of the greater pilgrimage.” He said: “Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor among you are sacred, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Indeed, no offender commits a crime except against himself. Indeed, a parent does not commit a crime against his child, nor a child against his parent. Indeed, Satan has despaired of ever being worshipped in this land of yours, but he will have obedience in some of the deeds you regard as insignificant, and he will be content with that. Indeed, every blood-claim of the age of ignorance is abolished, and the first blood-claim I abolish is that of al-Harith b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib. He had been placed in foster care among Banu Layth, and Hudhayl killed him.” Then he said: “O my community, have I conveyed?” three times. Then he said: “O God, bear witness” three times."],[14190,"He was present at the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “No offender commits a crime except against himself, nor a parent against his child, nor a child against his parent.”"],[14191,"I was at the side of the Prophet’s ﷺ she-camel while she was chewing her cud, and her saliva was dripping between my shoulders. I heard him say: “God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right. No bequest is permitted to an heir. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his masters desiring to turn away from them, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither a supererogatory deed nor a compulsory one will be accepted from him.”"],[14192,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us while he was on his she-camel, al-Jadʿaʾ, and I was holding its neck while she was chewing her cud. He said: “God has given every possessor of a right his right. No bequest to an heir. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither a supererogatory deed nor a compulsory one will be accepted from him.”"],[14193,"I witnessed the Pilgrimage with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I was indeed between the neck of the Messenger of God’s ﷺ she-camel while she was chewing her cud, and her saliva was flowing between my shoulders. I heard him say: “Indeed, God has given every possessor of a right his right. Indeed, no bequest is permitted to an heir. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither a supererogatory deed nor a compulsory one will be accepted from him.”"],[14194,"I was holding the rein of the Messenger of God’s ﷺ she-camel while she was chewing her cud, and her saliva was flowing between my shoulders. I heard him say: “Indeed, God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right. Indeed, no bequest is permitted to an heir. The child belongs to the marriage bed. And whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. Neither a supererogatory deed nor a compulsory one will be accepted from him.”"],[14195,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon while he was on his mount at Mina, and he was holding its nose-rein while she was chewing her cud, and her saliva was indeed flowing between my shoulders. The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “O people, God has apportioned to every person his share of inheritance, and no bequest is permitted to an heir. Indeed, the child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or takes as masters other than his own, desiring to turn away from them, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people.”"],[14196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has given every possessor of a right his right. No bequest to an heir is permitted. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or attaches himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God.” He did not mention a month nor ʿAbd al-Rahman b. Ghanm."],[14197,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No bequest to an heir.”"],[14198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us on the day of the conquest until those who were far away gathered to him, and he called out with a voice loud enough for them to hear: “O people, God has been good to you and restored to every possessor of a right his right. Indeed, no bequest to an heir after this station of mine. The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or takes as masters other than his own, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people on the Day of Resurrection. Neither a supererogatory deed nor a compulsory one will be accepted from him.” Then he departed, and the people departed."],[14199,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the naming of those who attended the ʿAqabah pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar: ʿAmr b. Ghaziyya b. Thaʿlaba b. Khansaʾ b. Mindul b. Ghanm b. Mazin."],[14200,"And that he was among those whose hearts were to be reconciled.\""],[14201,"Subayʿah gave birth twenty-three or twenty-five [days] after her husband's death. When she had recovered she desired [to marry], so it was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does so, her term has become lawful.\""],[14202,"Subayʿah bt. al-Harith gave birth twenty-three or twenty-seven nights after her husband's death. When she had recovered from her postpartum bleeding she desired marriage, but that was disapproved of for her. It was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If she does so, her term has become lawful.\""],[14203,"Subayʿah gave birth twenty-three nights after her husband's death, and she desired [to marry]. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, and he said: \"If she does so, her term has been completed.\""],[14204,"The Prophet ﷺ came to one of the gatherings of the Ansar, and among them was a man known for vulgar speech. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.\""],[14205,"ʿAmr b. Qays had [claims to] usury from the pre-Islamic period, and that usury prevented him from embracing Islam until he could collect it; then he would become Muslim. One day he came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was at Uhud. He said to his people, \"Where is Saʿd b. Muʿadh?\" They said, \"He is at Uhud.\" He said, \"Where is so-and-so?\" They said, \"At Uhud.\" He asked about his people, and they said, \"They are at Uhud.\" So he took his sword and spear, put on his armor, and went to Uhud. When the Muslims saw him, they said, \"Away from us, O ʿAmr!\" He said, \"I have believed.\" Then he charged and fought until he was killed. He was carried to his family wounded. Saʿd b. Muʿadh entered upon him and said to his brother, \"Call out to him: Did you come angry for God and His Messenger?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then he died and entered Paradise without ever having prayed."],[14206,"ʿAmr b. Qays had [claims to] usury from the pre-Islamic period, and that usury prevented him from embracing Islam until he could collect it; then he would become Muslim. One day he came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was at Uhud. He said to his people, \"Where is Saʿd b. Muʿadh?\" They said, \"He is at Uhud.\" He said, \"Where is so-and-so?\" They said, \"At Uhud.\" He asked about his people, and they said, \"They are at Uhud.\" So he took his sword and spear, put on his armor, and went to Uhud. When the Muslims saw him, they said, \"Away from us, O ʿAmr!\" He said, \"I have believed.\" Then he charged and fought until he was killed. He was carried to his family wounded. Saʿd b. Muʿadh entered upon him and said to his brother, \"Call out to him: Did you come angry for God and His Messenger?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then he died and entered Paradise without ever having prayed."],[14207,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The earth will be conquered for you, and you will be spared hardship, so let none of you fail to play with his arrows.\""],[14208,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever cuts down a lote-tree (sidr) except for cultivation, Allah will build for him a house in the Fire.”"],[14209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seven I have cursed, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who adds to the Book of Allah, the one who denies the decree of Allah, the one who makes lawful what Allah has forbidden, the one who makes lawful from my progeny what Allah has forbidden, the one who abandons my Sunnah, the one who appropriates the booty for himself, and the one who tyrannizes with his authority to honor whom Allah has humiliated and humiliate whom Allah has honored.”"],[14210,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you have rulers who command you to pray, give zakah and perform jihad, then Allah has forbidden you from insulting them and has permitted you to pray behind them.”"],[14211,"I came to Syria seeking the obligatory share; and I saw a man around whom people had gathered. I said: “Who is this?” They said: “ʿAmr al-Bikali, whose hand was wounded on the day of Yarmouk, the day the Romans were expelled from Syria.” I heard him say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When you have rulers who command you to pray, give zakah and perform jihad in the path of Allah, prayer behind them is permitted for you, and insulting them is forbidden for you.’”"],[14212,"From ʿAmr b. al-Harith, the son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the brother of his wife Juwayriyya bt. al-Harith: “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his death left neither a dirham nor a dinar, nor a slave, nor a slave-girl, nor anything except his white mule, his weapon, and a piece of land which he left as charity.”"],[14213,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left nothing except his weapon, his white mule, and a piece of land which he made as charity.”"],[14214,"Muhammad b. Sallam al-Jumahi said: “ʿAmr b. Maʿdi Karib b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAmr b. ʿAsim b. ʿAmr b. Zayd, who is Munabbih.”"],[14215,"Muhammad b. Sallam said: “ʿAmr b. Maʿdi Karib had battles in the pre-Islamic era and lived into Islam. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ sent him to Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ at al-Qadisiyyah. He showed excellent valor there. ʿUmar wrote to Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas: ‘With two thousand men: ʿAmr b. Maʿdi Karib and Talha b. Khuwaylid, who is Talha al-Asadi. Consult both of them in war but do not appoint them over anything.’”"],[14216,"While he was in that state, suddenly a horseman from the horsemen of Persia began aiming arrows at him. It was said to him, 'O Abu Thawr, this horseman has been aiming his arrows at you.' He said, 'So he shot at him and hit the tip of 'Amr's bow and broke it. Then 'Amr charged at him and stabbed him, breaking his backbone. He dismounted to him and took two bracelets that were on him, made of gold, and a garment of silk brocade.' He said, 'So he handed that over to him.'"],[14217,"That we, since recently, when we performed Hajj, we used to say."],[14218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Indeed, the friends of Allah are those who pray and who establish the five prayers that Allah has prescribed for His servants, fast Ramadan and seek reward for his fasting, give the zakat with a good heart, seeking reward for it, and avoid the major sins that Allah has forbidden.' A man from his companions said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how many are the major sins?' He said, 'They are nine. The greatest of them is associating partners with Allah, killing a believer without right, fleeing on the day of battle, accusing a chaste woman, sorcery, consuming the wealth of an orphan, consuming usury, disobedience to Muslim parents, and violating the Sacred House, your qiblah, whether alive or dead. No man dies who has not committed these major sins, and who establishes prayer and gives zakat, except that he will accompany Muhammad ﷺ in the midst of Paradise, whose gates are folding doors of gold.'"],[14219,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'The major sins are seven: associating partners with Allah, killing a believing soul, fleeing from battle, consuming usury, consuming the wealth of an orphan, disobedience to parents, and deviating from the Sacred House.'"],[14220,"\"O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is the best?\" He said, \"The one with the longest Qunut.\" He said, \"Which charity is the best?\" He said, \"The effort of the generous one.\" He said, \"Which believers are the most complete?\" He said, \"The ones with the best manners.\""],[14221,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to raise his hands with every takbir in the prescribed prayer."],[14222,"There was a question on my mind that had saddened me. I had not asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about it, nor had I heard anyone ask him about it, so I kept waiting for the right moment. One day I entered while he was performing ablution, and I found him in two circumstances I loved to find him in: free (unoccupied) and in good spirits. So I said, “O Messenger of God, give me permission to ask you.” He said, “Yes—ask whatever occurs to you.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what is faith?” He said, “Forbearance and patience.” I said, “Which of the believers is best in faith?” He said, “The one with the best character.” I said, “Then which of the Muslims is best in Islam?” He said, “The one from whose hand and tongue the Muslims are safe.” I said, “Then which jihad is best?” He lowered his head and remained silent for a long time, until I feared I had burdened him, and I wished I had not asked him. And I had heard him the day before saying, “Indeed the greatest in جرم (offense) among the Muslims is the one who asks about something that was not forbidden to them, and then it is forbidden because of his questioning.” So I said, “I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger.” He raised his head and said, “What did you say?” I said, “Which jihad is best?” He said, “A word of justice before a tyrannical ruler.”"],[14223,"His grandfather 'Umayr b. Habib b. Khumasha had companionship and pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ at his maturity. He advised his children, saying: 'Beware of sitting with fools, for sitting with them is a disease. Whoever shows forbearance toward a fool is pleased with his forbearance; whoever loves him will regret; whoever does not acknowledge the little of what a fool brings will be forced to acknowledge much; whoever is patient with what he dislikes will attain what he loves. If one of you wants to command good or forbid evil, let him prepare himself to be patient with harm and trust in the reward from Allah, exalted be He. For whoever trusts in the reward from Allah will not feel the pain of harm.'"],[14225,"From Abu Dawud al-Mazini, and Abu Dawud was one of the people of Badr, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he entered the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah and prayed four rak'ahs in it. Then he declared the talbiyah in the mosque, and those in the mosque heard him and said, 'He declared the talbiyah from the mosque.' He declared the talbiyah when he mounted his riding camel, and the one near the mosque said, 'He declared the talbiyah when his riding camel stood erect with him.' Then when he stood erect on al-Bayda', he declared the talbiyah, and those on al-Bayda' heard him and said, 'He declared the talbiyah from al-Bayda'.' And all of them spoke the truth."],[14226,"From ʿUrwah, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Badr among the Muslims from Quraysh, then from Banu Zuhrah: ʿUmayr b. Abi Waqqas."],[14227,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Badr among the Muslims, then from Quraysh, then from Banu Zuhrah b. Kilab: ʿUmayr b. Abi Waqqas b. Uhayb b. ʿAbd Manaf b. Zuhrah."],[14228,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the Muslims, then from Quraysh, then from Banu Zuhrah: ʿUmayr b. Abi Waqqas."],[14229,"Safwan said, 'May Allah make life ugly after the slain of Badr.' ʿUmayr said, 'Yes, by Allah, there is no good in life after them. Were it not for a debt upon me which I find no means to repay, and dependents behind me for whom I find nothing, I would go to Muhammad and kill him if I filled my eyes with him. For I have a pretext among them: I will say I came to visit this son of mine, the captive.' Safwan rejoiced at his words and said, 'Your debt is upon me, and your dependents are like my own dependents in maintenance; if anything suffices me, we shall not fail them.' So Safwan carried him and equipped him with Safwan's sword, which was polished and poisoned. ʿUmayr said to Safwan, 'Keep my affair secret for some nights.' Then ʿUmayr set out until he reached Madinah. He dismounted at the gate of the mosque, hobbled his mount, and took the sword, intending it for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab saw him while he was among a group of the Ansar talking about the event of Badr and thanking Allah for His blessing. When ʿUmar saw ʿUmayr b. Wahb with the sword, he was alarmed and said, 'Here is the dog! This is an enemy of Allah, the one who stirred up enmity between us and estimated our numbers for the people.' Then ʿUmar arose and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'This is ʿUmayr b. Wahb; he has entered the mosque carrying weapons. He is the wicked, treacherous one. O Messenger of Allah, do not trust him.' He said, 'Bring him in to me.' ʿUmar went out and ordered his companions to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then to guard against ʿUmayr when he entered upon them. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab and ʿUmayr b. Wahb came and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with ʿUmar was his sword. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar, 'Step back from him.' When ʿUmayr drew near, he greeted him, 'May you have a pleasant morning' — that being the greeting of the people of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has honored us above your greeting, and made our greeting the salam, which is the greeting of the people of Paradise.' ʿUmayr said, 'Your acquaintance with it is recent indeed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has replaced it for us with something better. So what has brought you here, O ʿUmayr?' He said, 'I have come concerning my captive among you, so treat me kindly regarding my captive, for you are kinsfolk and family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Then what is the matter with the sword on your neck?' ʿUmayr said, 'May Allah curse such swords! Have they availed us anything? I forgot it was on my neck when I dismounted. By my life, I do care for it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Tell me the truth: what has brought you here?' He said, 'I came only for my captive.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Then what did you stipulate with Safwan b. Umayyah al-Jumahi in the Hijr?' ʿUmayr was startled and said, 'What did I stipulate with him?' He said, 'You undertook to kill me in return for his supporting your sons and paying your debt. And Allah stands between you and that.' ʿUmayr said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. O Messenger of Allah, we used to deny you regarding the revelation and what came to you from heaven. This conversation between me and Safwan in the Hijr is just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: no one else knew of it except him and me. Then Allah informed you of it. So I believe in Allah and His Messenger. Praise be to Allah who has brought me to this station.' The Muslims rejoiced when Allah guided him. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ said, 'A pig was dearer to me than him when he appeared, but today he is dearer to me than some of my own sons.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Sit down, we will console you.' And he said, 'Teach your brother the Qur'an, and release his captive.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I used to strive as much as I could to extinguish the light of Allah. Praise be to Allah who has brought me to this course. Permit me to join Quraysh and call them to Islam; perhaps Allah will guide them and save them from destruction.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him, so he went to Makkah. Safwan began saying to Quraysh in their gatherings, 'Rejoice at a victory that will make you forget the event of Badr,' and he kept asking every rider who arrived from Madinah whether anything had happened there, hoping for what ʿUmayr b. Wahb had said. Then a man from Madinah arrived, and Safwan asked about him. The man said, 'He has accepted Islam.' The polytheists met him and said, 'He has apostatized.' Safwan said, 'It is incumbent upon me never to benefit him with any expenditure and never to speak to him a single word.' ʿUmayr came to them and called them to Islam and gave them sincere advice, and many people accepted Islam."],[14230,"ʿUmayr b. Wahb al-Jumahi sat with Safwan b. Umayyah after the affliction of the people of Badr from Quraysh in the Hijr, a short while later. He was one of those who used to harm the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions, and they suffered hardship from them while they were in Makkah. His son, Wahb b. ʿUmayr, was among the captives of the people of Badr. He said: They mentioned the people of the pit and their misfortunes. Safwan said, 'By Allah, there is no good in life after them.' ʿUmayr b. Wahb said, 'You have spoken the truth. By Allah, were it not for a debt upon me which I cannot repay, and dependents for whom I fear loss after me, I would ride to Muhammad until I kill him. For I have a pretext among them: my son is a captive in their hands.' Safwan seized the opportunity and said, 'Your debt is upon me; I will pay it for you, and your dependents will be with my dependents as their equals as long as they remain. Nothing will suffice them that we cannot provide.' ʿUmayr said, 'Keep my affair and yours secret.' He said, 'I will do so.' Then ʿUmayr ordered his sword to be sharpened and poisoned, then set out for Madinah. While ʿUmar b. al-Khattab was in Madinah among a group of Muslims, remembering the Day of Badr, how Allah had honored them, and what He had shown them of their enemy, he saw ʿUmayr b. Wahb, who had made his camel kneel at the gate of the mosque, wearing his sword across his shoulder. He said, 'This dog, the enemy of Allah, ʿUmayr b. Wahb, has come only for evil. This is the one who stirred up enmity between us and estimated our numbers for the people on the Day of Badr.' Then ʿUmar entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this enemy of Allah, ʿUmayr b. Wahb, has come wearing his sword across his shoulder.' He said, 'Bring him in.' ʿUmar went and took hold of the strap of his sword around his neck and seized him by it. ʿUmar said to some men from the Ansar who were with him, 'Enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sit with him, and beware of this dog, for he is not trustworthy.' Then he brought him in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while ʿUmar held the strap of his sword. He said, 'Release him, O ʿUmar. Come near, O ʿUmayr.' He drew near and said, 'May you have a pleasant morning' — which was the greeting of the people of the Jahiliyyah among them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has honored us with a greeting better than your greeting, O ʿUmayr: the salam, the greeting of the people of Paradise.' ʿUmayr said, 'By Allah, O Muhammad, your acquaintance with it is recent indeed.' He said, 'What has brought you here?' He said, 'I came for this captive who is in your hands; treat him well.' He said, 'Then what is the matter with the sword on your neck?' He said, 'May Allah curse such swords! Have they availed anything?' He said, 'Tell me the truth: what did you come for?' He said, 'I came only for this.' He said, 'Rather, you sat with Safwan b. Umayyah in the Hijr, and you two mentioned the people of the pit from Quraysh. You said, \"Were it not for a debt upon me and my dependents, I would go out to kill Muhammad.\" Safwan undertook to pay your debt and support your dependents on condition that you kill me. And Allah stands between you and that.' ʿUmayr said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. O Messenger of Allah, we used to deny you regarding what you brought us of news from heaven and the revelation that descended upon you. This is a matter attended by no one but me and Safwan. By Allah, I know that nothing informed you of it except Allah. Praise be to Allah who guided me to Islam and brought me to this course.' Then he bore witness to the testimony of truth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Instruct your brother in his religion, teach him the Qur'an, and release his captive.' Then he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I was striving to extinguish Allah's light and severely harming those who followed Allah's religion. I would like you to permit me to go to Makkah and call them to Allah and to Islam; perhaps Allah will guide them. Otherwise, I will harm them as I used to harm your companions in their religion.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him, and he went to Makkah. When ʿUmayr b. Wahb had set out, Safwan said to Quraysh, 'Rejoice at an event that will come to you now and make you forget the event of Badr.' Safwan kept asking travelers about him until a rider arrived and informed him of his acceptance of Islam. He swore never to speak to him again and never to benefit him in any way. When ʿUmayr arrived in Makkah, he stayed there calling to Islam and severely harming those who opposed him, and many people accepted Islam at his hands."],[14231,"He said: May Allah make life ugly after the slain of Badr. He said, 'Yes, by Allah, there is no good in life after them. Were it not for a debt upon me which I find no means to repay, and dependents for whom I leave nothing, I would travel to Muhammad and kill him if I filled my eyes with him. For I have a pretext with which to excuse myself to him: I will say I came to visit this son of mine, the captive.' Safwan rejoiced at his words and said, 'Your debt is upon me, and your dependents are like my own dependents in maintenance; if anything suffices me, I will not fail them.' So Safwan carried him and equipped him, and ordered ʿUmayr's sword to be polished and poisoned. ʿUmayr said to Safwan, 'Keep my affair secret for some days.' Then ʿUmayr set out until he reached Madinah. He dismounted at the gate of the mosque, hobbled his mount, took the sword, and headed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab ؓ saw him while he was among a group of the Ansar talking about the event of Badr and mentioning Allah's blessing in it. When ʿUmar saw him with the sword, he was alarmed and said, 'This is the dog! This is an enemy of Allah, the one who stirred up enmity between us on the Day of Badr and estimated our numbers for the people.' Then ʿUmar arose and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'This is ʿUmayr b. Wahb; he has entered the mosque carrying his sword. He is the treacherous, wicked one. O Prophet of Allah, do not trust him.' He said, 'Bring him in.' ʿUmar went out and ordered his companions to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then to guard against ʿUmayr when he entered upon them. Then ʿUmar and ʿUmayr entered until they came before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with ʿUmayr was his sword. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar, 'Step back from him.' When ʿUmayr drew near, he said, 'May you have a pleasant morning' — that being the greeting of the people of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has honored us above your greeting and made our greeting the greeting of the people of Paradise, which is the salam.' ʿUmayr said, 'Your acquaintance with it is recent indeed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has replaced it for us with something better. So what has brought you here, O ʿUmayr?' He said, 'I came concerning our captives, for you are kinsfolk and family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Then what is the matter with the sword on your neck?' ʿUmayr said, 'May Allah curse such swords! Have they availed us anything? I simply forgot it on my neck when I dismounted. By my life, I do care for it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Tell me the truth: what has brought you here?' He said, 'I came only for my captive.' He said, 'Then what did you stipulate with Safwan b. Umayyah in the Hijr?' ʿUmayr was startled and said, 'What did I stipulate with him?' He said, 'You undertook to kill me in return for his supporting your sons and paying your debt. And Allah stands between you and that.' ʿUmayr said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. O Messenger of Allah, we used to deny you regarding the revelation and what came to you from heaven. This conversation between me and Safwan in the Hijr was just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: no one knew of it except him and me. Then Allah informed you of it. So I believe in Allah and His Messenger. Praise be to Allah who has brought me to this course.' The Muslims rejoiced when Allah guided him. ʿUmar said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, a pig was dearer to me than ʿUmayr when he appeared, but he is dearer to me than some of my own sons.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Sit down, O ʿUmayr, we will console you.' And he said to his companions, 'Teach your brother the Qur'an, and release his captive.' ʿUmayr said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I used to strive as much as I could to extinguish the light of Allah. Praise be to Allah who has brought me and guided me. Permit me to join Quraysh and call them to Allah and to Islam; perhaps Allah will guide them and save them from destruction.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him, so he went to Makkah. Safwan b. Umayyah began saying to Quraysh in their gatherings, 'Rejoice at a victory that will make you forget the event of Badr,' and he kept asking every rider who arrived from Madinah whether anything had happened there, hoping for what he had said. Then a man from Madinah arrived, and Safwan b. Umayyah asked about him. He said, 'He has accepted Islam.' The polytheists cursed him and said, 'He has apostatized.' Safwan said, 'It is incumbent upon me before Allah never to benefit him with any expenditure and never to speak to him a single word of my own accord.' ʿUmayr came to them and called them to Islam and gave them sincere advice to the best of his effort, and many people accepted Islam."],[14232,"He had a sister, and when he went out to the Prophet ﷺ, she would harm him concerning it and revile the Prophet ﷺ, for she was a polytheist. One day he took up the sword against her, went to her, and placed it on her and killed her. Her sons arose and cried out, saying, 'We know who killed her. Will our mother be killed? These are a people whose fathers and mothers are polytheists.' When ʿUmayr feared they would kill someone other than her killer, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'Did you kill your sister?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Why?' He said, 'She used to harm me concerning you.' The Prophet ﷺ sent to her sons and asked them, and they named someone other than her killer. The Prophet ﷺ informed them of it and declared her blood forfeit. They said, 'We hear and obey.'"],[14233,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, he said: Hatim b. Ismaʿil narrated to us from Yazid b. Abi ʿUbayd, who said: I heard ʿUmayr, the freedman of Abu al-Lahm, say: My master ordered me to cut meat into strips. A poor man came to me, and I fed him some of it. My master learned of it and beat me. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He summoned him and said, 'Why did you beat him?' He said, 'He feeds food without my commanding him.' He said, 'The reward is between you two.'"],[14234,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ upon the stones of al-Zayt, praying for rain, raising the palms of his hands."],[14235,"I set out with my masters toward Madinah seeking to emigrate. When we drew near to Madinah, they left me behind with their baggage and departed. I was afflicted with severe hunger. Then one of those who had come out of Madinah passed by me and said, 'If you entered one of the walled gardens of Madinah, you would find some of its fruit.' Umayr said: So I entered one of the walled gardens of Madinah and cut off two bunches of dates from its palms. The owner of the garden came, took me, and brought me to the Prophet ﷺ. He asked me about my situation, so I told him. He said to me, 'Which of the two is better?' I pointed to one of them, and he commanded me, so I took it, and he commanded the owner of the garden, and he took the other, and he let me go."],[14236,"I was herding at Dhat al-Jaysh when I was struck by severe hunger. I mentioned that to one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he directed me to a walled garden belonging to one of the Ansar. I cut a bunch of dates from it, so they seized me and took me to the Prophet ﷺ. I informed him of my need, so he gave me one bunch of dates and returned the rest to its owners."],[14237,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, and I was a slave owned by someone. I said, 'Give me something.' He gave me a sword and said, 'Gird yourself with it.' I took it and girded myself with it, but it fell to the ground. Then he gave me some of the odds and ends of the baggage."],[14238,"I went on a campaign with my master at Khaybar and witnessed its conquest. I asked the Prophet ﷺ to apportion a share for me, but he gave me the odds and ends of the baggage and did not apportion a share for me."],[14239,"I witnessed Khaybar with my masters. The Prophet of God ﷺ commanded me to gird on a sword, and there I was dragging it. When he was told that I was a slave, he ordered that I be given something of the odds and ends of the baggage."],[14240,"I showed the Prophet ﷺ a healing invocation I used to use against insanity. He began to say, 'Take such-and-such from it, and add such-and-such to it.'"],[14241,"I showed him—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—a healing invocation I used to use for the insane in the Jāhiliyyah. He said, 'Remove such-and-such from it, and remove such-and-such from it, and use such-and-such from it.'"],[14242,"Hatim al-Ta'i b. Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. al-Hashraj b. Imri' al-Qays b. Adi b. Akhram."],[14243,"I heard my father say: 'Adi b. Hatim al-Ta'i, whose kunyah was Abu Tarif, died in Kufa during the time of al-Mukhtar in the year sixty-eight.'"],[14244,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the miʿrad (a blunt arrow or spearhead). He said: 'If it strikes with its edge, then eat; but if it strikes with its broad side and kills, then it is a waqidh (an animal killed by a blunt blow), so do not eat.' I said: 'I send my dog and it eats (from the game).' He said: 'If you send your dog and mention the name of Allah, then eat.' I said: 'What if it eats?' He said: 'Then do not eat, for it held it back for itself and did not hold it back for you.' I said: 'I send my dog and find another dog with it.' He said: 'Do not eat, for you invoked the name (of Allah) over your dog, but you did not invoke it over the other.' And the wording is from the hadith of Sulayman b. Harb."],[14245,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog and invoke the name (of Allah), and I find another dog with it, and I do not know which of them caught it.' He said: 'Do not eat, for you invoked the name over your dog, but you did not invoke it over the other.'"],[14246,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'I send my dog and find another dog with it, and I do not know which of them killed it.' He said: 'Do not eat, for you invoked the name over your dog, but you did not invoke it over the other.'"],[14247,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the game of the miʿrad. He said: 'What it strikes with its edge, then eat; and what it strikes with its broad side, it is a waqidh.' He said: And I asked him about the game of the dog. He said: 'What it holds back for you, then eat, for the dog's seizure is its slaughter. And if you find with your dog another dog, and you think that it may have seized it together with it and killed it, then do not eat, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog, but you did not mention it over the other.'"],[14248,"I heard ʿAdi b. Hatim say: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the game of the miʿrad. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What you strike with its edge, then eat; and what you strike with its broad side, it is a waqidh.' And I asked him about the game of the dog. He said: 'What it holds back for you and does not eat from it, then eat it, for its seizure is its slaughter. And if you find with your dog another dog, and you think that it may have seized it together with it and killed it, then do not eat it, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog, but you did not mention it over the other.'"],[14249,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs with which we hunt.' He said: 'Look at these hunting animals and train them from what Allah has taught you, and eat from what they hold back for you. If it kills and does not eat, then eat it; but if it eats, then do not eat it.' I said: 'What do you think if my dogs mix with other dogs? Do you think I may eat from it?' He forbade us from it. And the wording is from the hadith of Dawud."],[14250,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who hunt with these dogs and birds, so what is lawful for us from them?' He said: '{Hunting animals, trained as hounds, teaching them from what Allah has taught you}' until the end of the verse. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, even if it kills?' He said: 'Even if it kills.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, even if other dogs mix with them?' He said: 'Do not eat except that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we shoot (arrows).' He said: 'Eat what you pierce and over which you mention the name of Allah.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the miʿrad?' He said: 'Do not eat from the miʿrad except what you ritually slaughter.'"],[14251,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunting with a dog. He said, \"If you send your dog and name it, and it catches and kills prey, then eat from it. But if it eats from the prey, do not eat from it, for it has held it for itself.\""],[14252,"ʿAdi said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'We are people of two mountains, and most of our food is game.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'With what do you hunt it?' I said: 'With dogs and arrows.' He said: 'When your dogs seize it, then invoke the name (of Allah), and whatever they hold back, then eat. But if another trained dog joins them, then do not eat until you ritually slaughter it. And if you take it out of water, then do not eat it until you ritually slaughter it, for it is a waqidh.'"],[14253,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'I send my dog and find another dog with it, and I do not know which of them caught it.' He said: 'Do not eat, for you invoked the name over your dog, but you did not invoke it over the other.'"],[14254,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the game. I said: 'I send my dog and invoke the name, and I find another dog with it, and I do not know which of them caught it.' He said: 'Do not eat, for you invoked the name over your dog, but you did not invoke it over the other.'"],[14255,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'We are a people who hunt with these dogs.' He said: 'When you send your trained dogs and mention the name of Allah over them, then eat what they hold back for you, even if they kill, unless the dog eats (from it). But if it eats, then do not eat, for I fear that it held it back for itself. And if other dogs mix with them, then do not eat.'"],[14256,"that he asked the Prophet ﷺ about hunting. He said: “When you send your dog, invoke Allah’s name, and if you come upon it having killed and not eaten, then eat, for it has only held it for you. If you come upon it having killed and eaten from it, do not eat anything of it, for it has only held it for itself. If your dog mixes with other dogs and they kill and do not eat from it, do not eat anything of it, for you only invoked the name over your dog, not over another. When you shoot your arrow, remember Allah’s name, and if you find that it fell into water and died, do not eat it, for you do not know whether the water killed it or your arrow. If you find it after a night or two nights with no mark on it other than your arrow, then if you wish to eat, eat.”"],[14257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “When you send your dog, mention Allah’s name. If it holds it for you and you reach it alive, slaughter it. If you reach it having killed and not eaten, eat. If you find other dogs with it, do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it. When you shoot your arrow, mention Allah’s name over it. If it holds it for you, eat. If you find it after it has been absent from you for a day, with no mark on it except your arrow, then eat if you wish. If you find it drowned in water, do not eat.”"],[14258,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, my land is a land of hunting.” He said: “When you send your trained dog and invoke Allah’s name, eat what the dog holds for you. If it kills and eats from it, do not eat, for it has only held it for itself. When you send your dog and invoke the name, and other dogs you did not invoke over mix with it, do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and it disappears from me for a night.” He said: “If you find your arrow in it and nothing else, eat it.””"],[14259,"When I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunting with dogs, he did not know what to say to me until the verse was revealed: “And what you have trained of hunting animals, training them as hounds, teaching them from what Allah has taught you.”"],[14260,"We asked the Prophet ﷺ, and I said: “I send my dog and take another dog with me, and I do not know which of them caught it.” He said: “Do not eat, for you only invoked the name over your dog and not over another.”"],[14261,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of hunting, and we go out with arrows.” He mentioned the miʿrāḍ (a blunt arrow), and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “When you shoot with the miʿrāḍ and invoke the name, and it pierces, eat it, for that is its slaughter. If it strikes with its side, do not eat it unless you slaughter it. If you find only a stone, it will suffice for you.”"],[14262,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunting with the miʿrāḍ. He said: “If you strike with its edge, eat, and if you strike with its side, do not eat, for it is a waqīdh (one killed by a blunt blow).”"],[14263,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunting with the miʿrāḍ. He said: “Do not eat from it except what you slaughter.”"],[14264,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the miʿrāḍ. He said: “If it strikes with its edge and pierces, eat, and if it strikes with its side, do not eat.”"],[14265,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the miʿrāḍ. He said: “If it pierces, eat, and if it strikes with its side, do not eat.”"],[14266,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunting with the miʿrāḍ. He said: “If you strike with its edge, eat, and if you strike with its side and it kills, it is a waqīdh, so do not eat.”"],[14267,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “If your shot falls into water and drowns, do not eat it.”"],[14268,"I said: O Messenger of God, I shoot at game, then I find it after three [days]? He said: “Eat whatever you find on it the mark of your arrow, as long as you do not find in it a wild animal, or find it drowned.”"],[14269,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the game of the goshawk. He said: “Whatever it holds back for you, eat it.”"],[14270,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O ʿAdī b. Ḥātim, how will you be when a woman in a litter travels from the castles of Yemen until she reaches al-Ḥīrah, fearing nothing but God, and [fearing] the wolf for her sheep?” I said: “Ṭayy’ has its fighters and its men.” He said: “Then God will suffice her, and what is other than her.”"],[14271,"From the Prophet ﷺ with the like of it. He said: “The woman has indeed ridden, coming out from Yemen to al-Ḥīrah, fearing nothing but God.”"],[14272,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “When Ramadan comes, fast thirty [days], unless you sight the new moon before that.”"],[14273,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me prayer and fasting, and said: “Pray thus and pray thus, and fast thus. When the sun sets, eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct for you from the black thread of dawn. And fast thirty days, unless you sight the new moon before that.” So I took two threads of hair, one black and one white, and I would look at them, but it would not become distinct for me. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he laughed and said: “O Ibn Ḥātim, that is only the whiteness of day from the blackness of night.”"],[14274,"I said: O Messenger of God, I have memorized everything you enjoined upon me except the white thread from the black thread. Last night I slept with two threads, looking at this one once and at that one once. The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: “The white thread from the black thread is only that which is in the horizon of the sky.”"],[14275,"When this verse was revealed: “…until the white thread becomes distinct for you from the black thread of dawn,” I took a black rope and a white rope and placed them under my pillow. I looked, but it did not become distinct for me. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he laughed and said: “Your pillow is indeed wide and long. This is only night and day.”"],[14276,"I said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of His saying: “the white thread from the black thread”—are they two threads? The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: “No, but it is the whiteness of day and the blackness of night.”"],[14277,"I said: O Messenger of God, what is the white thread from the black thread? Are they two threads? He said: “You have a broad back of the neck, if you see the two threads.” Then he said: “No, rather it is the blackness of night and the whiteness of day.”"],[14278,"When this verse was revealed: “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct for you from the black thread of dawn,” I took two ropes, one black and the other white, and placed them under my pillow. I kept raising them in the night, but the white did not become distinct for me from the black. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “O Ibn Ḥātim, your pillow is indeed wide. He only said: Eat and drink until the whiteness of day becomes distinct for you from the blackness of night.”"],[14279,"When this verse was revealed: “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct for you from the black thread of dawn,” I took two ropes, one black and the other white, and placed them under my pillow. I kept raising them in the night, but the white did not become distinct for me from the black. I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “O Ibn Ḥātim, your pillow is indeed wide. He only said: Eat and drink until the whiteness of day becomes distinct for you from the blackness of night.”"],[14280,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent him as a collector of zakah to his people. When he collected their zakah, that coincided with the death of the Prophet ﷺ."],[14281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Ḥīrah was shown to me like the fangs of dogs, and you will conquer it.” A man stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, grant me the daughter of Buqaylah.” He said: “She is yours.” So they gave her to him. Then her brother came and he said: “Will you sell her?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Name whatever price you wish.” He said: “For a thousand dirhams.” He said: “I have taken her for a thousand.” They said: “If only you had said thirty thousand.” He said: “Is there a number greater than a thousand?”"],[14282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none of you but Allah ﷻ will speak to him with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and see only what he sent forth of his deeds. He will look to his left and see only what he sent forth of his deeds. He will look in front of him and see nothing but the Fire facing him. So guard against the Fire, even with half a date.”"],[14283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none of you but Allah will speak to him with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and see only his deeds. He will look to his left and see only his deeds. Then he will look in front of him and see the Fire. So whoever among you can protect his face from the Fire, [let him do so], even with half a date.”"],[14284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every one of you will be spoken to by Allah on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between him and Allah. He will look to his right and will not see anything but what he has done (in the world). Then he will look to his left and will not see anything but what he has done. Then he will look in front of him and will see the Fire. So, whoever can save himself from the Fire, even if it is with half a date (given in charity), let him do so.\""],[14285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is none of you but Allah will speak to him on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and see only what he sent forth. Then he will look in front of him and the Fire will meet him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “So whoever among you can protect his face from the Fire, let him do so, even with half a date.”"],[14286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said: “Guard against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word.” Jarīr, Fuḍayl b. ʿIyāḍ, Asbāṭ b. Muḥammad, and Abū Muʿāwiyah inserted ʿAmr b. Murrah into this hadith between al-Aʿmash and Khaythamah."],[14287,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Guard against the Fire.” Then he turned away and averted his face until we thought he was looking at it. Then he said: “Guard against the Fire, even with half a date, even with a good word.”"],[14288,"“Guard against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word.”"],[14289,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Fire and turned his face away, then sought refuge from it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Guard against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word.”"],[14290,"I never entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he made room for me, or he said: “He moved for me.” One day I entered upon him while he was in a house full of his companions. When he saw me, he made room for me until I sat down beside him."],[14291,"I said: O Messenger of God, we are people who hunt. What do you think about the broad-headed arrow? He said: “Whatever it pierces, eat it.” And I asked him about dogs. He said: “If you send out your dogs and they catch something, then eat it, unless another dog besides them joins in.”"],[14292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A person’s auspiciousness and inauspiciousness lie between his two jaws.”"],[14293,"Abu Junadah narrated to us, and he used to live among Banu Sulul. Al-Aʿmash narrated to us from Khaythama b. ʿAbd al-Rahman from ʿAdi b. Hatim, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: On the Day of Resurrection, some people will be commanded to go to Paradise, until when they draw near to it and smell its fragrance and look at its palaces and what God has prepared for its inhabitants therein, they will be called: Turn them away from it. There is no share for them in it. So they will return with a regret the like of which the first ones did not return with. They will say: Our Lord, if only You had admitted us to the Fire before showing us the reward and what You have prepared in it for Your friends, that would have been easier for us. He will say: That is what I intended for you. When you were alone, you confronted Me with grave sins, and when you met people, you met them humbly. You showed people the opposite of what you gave Me from your hearts. You feared people and did not fear Me. You held people in awe but did not revere Me. You left things for people but did not leave anything for Me. So today I will make you taste the painful punishment along with depriving you of the reward."],[14294,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he came back from Badr. A man from the Ansar said: Did we meet any but old women like hobbled camels, and so we slaughtered them? The face of the Messenger of God ﷺ changed until I saw it as if pomegranate seeds had burst on it. Then he said: “O son of my brother, do not say that. Those are the great assembly of Quraysh. If only you had seen them in their gatherings in Makkah, you would have feared them.” By God, I went to Makkah and saw them sitting in the mosque, and I was unable to greet them because of their awe. Then I remembered the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: “O people, love Quraysh, for whoever loves Quraysh has loved me, and whoever hates Quraysh has hated me. God has made my people beloved to me, so I do not hasten punishment for them, nor do I consider any favor too great for them. O God, You made the first of Quraysh taste exemplary punishment, so make the last of them taste Your bounty. Indeed, God knew what was in my heart of love for my people, and so He gladdened me regarding them.” God, exalted is He, said: {And warn, O Muhammad, your closest kindred, and lower your wing to those who follow you of the believers} – meaning my people. So praise be to God who made the Siddiq from my people, and the martyr from my people, and the imams from my people. Indeed, God turned the servants over from back to belly, and the best of the Arabs was Quraysh. It is the tree about which God said: {A good word is like a good tree} – meaning by it Quraysh – {its root firmly fixed} – He says: its root is nobility – {and its branches in the sky} – He says: the honor with which God honored them through Islam, to which He guided them and made them its people. Then He sent down concerning them a decisive surah from the Book of God: {For the accustomed security of Quraysh – their accustomed security in the caravan of winter and summer – let them worship the Lord of this House, who fed them against hunger and made them safe from fear}."],[14295,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he came back from Badr. A man from the Ansar said: Did we meet any but old women like hobbled camels, and so we slaughtered them? The face of the Messenger of God ﷺ changed until I saw it as if pomegranate seeds had burst on it. Then he said: “O son of my brother, do not say that. Those are the great assembly of Quraysh. If only you had seen them in their gatherings in Makkah, you would have feared them.” By God, I went to Makkah and saw them sitting in the mosque, and I was unable to greet them because of their awe. Then I remembered the saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: “O people, love Quraysh, for whoever loves Quraysh has loved me, and whoever hates Quraysh has hated me. God has made my people beloved to me, so I do not hasten punishment for them, nor do I consider any favor too great for them. O God, You made the first of Quraysh taste exemplary punishment, so make the last of them taste Your bounty. Indeed, God knew what was in my heart of love for my people, and so He gladdened me regarding them.” God, exalted is He, said: {And warn, O Muhammad, your closest kindred, and lower your wing to those who follow you of the believers} – meaning my people. So praise be to God who made the Siddiq from my people, and the martyr from my people, and the imams from my people. Indeed, God turned the servants over from back to belly, and the best of the Arabs was Quraysh. It is the tree about which God said: {A good word is like a good tree} – meaning by it Quraysh – {its root firmly fixed} – He says: its root is nobility – {and its branches in the sky} – He says: the honor with which God honored them through Islam, to which He guided them and made them its people. Then He sent down concerning them a decisive surah from the Book of God: {For the accustomed security of Quraysh – their accustomed security in the caravan of winter and summer – let them worship the Lord of this House, who fed them against hunger and made them safe from fear}."],[14296,"I said: O Messenger of God, we send out trained dogs for ourselves. He said: “Whatever they hold back for you, eat it.” I said: Even if it kills? He said: “Even if it kills, as long as no dog other than them joins in.”"],[14297,"I said: O Messenger of God, I send out my trained dogs and they hold back game for me. May I eat it? He said: “If you send out your trained dogs and they hold back game for you, then eat.” I said: Even if they kill it? He said: “Even if they kill it, as long as no dog besides them shares in it.” I said: I shoot with a broad-headed arrow and it pierces. He said: “If it pierces, eat; but if it strikes with its side, then do not eat.”"],[14298,"I said: O Messenger of God, we send out dogs and they hold back game for us. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: If they are trained and you mention the name of God, then eat. I said: O Messenger of God, even if they kill it? He said: “Even if they kill it, as long as no dogs other than them share in it.” I said: What do you think about what is shot with a broad-headed arrow? He said: “If you mention the name of God and it pierces, then eat; but if it kills, then do not eat.”"],[14299,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I send out my dogs and I mention the name of God. May I eat from what they hold back for me? He said: “Yes.” I said: Even if it kills? He said: “Even if it kills, unless another dog besides them joins in.” I said: What about the broad-headed arrow with which I shoot and I mention the name of God? He said: “If it pierces, eat; but if it strikes it with its side, then do not eat.”"],[14300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is able to protect himself from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so.”"],[14301,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Protect yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date.”"],[14302,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “Protect yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date.”"],[14303,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14305,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14306,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14307,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date.\""],[14309,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and then search for it, but I only find it after a night. He said: \"If you see your arrow in it and no predator has eaten from it, then eat it.\""],[14310,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and then search for it, but I only find it after a night. He said: \"If you see your arrow in it and no predator has eaten from it, then eat it.\""],[14311,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and then search for the trace after that. He said: \"If you find your arrow in it and no predator has eaten from it, then eat it.\""],[14312,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and then search for the trace after that. He said: \"If you find your arrow in it and no predator has eaten from it, then eat it.\""],[14313,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a gold cross on my neck. He said, \"O 'Adi, take off this idol from your neck.\" So I removed it and approached him while he was reciting Surah Al-Bara'ah (Chapter 9 of the Quran). He read this verse, \"They took their scholars and monks as lords besides Allah\" until he finished it. I said, \"We do not worship them.\" He said, \"Don't they make lawful what Allah has made unlawful, and you make it unlawful, and they make unlawful what Allah has made lawful, and you make it lawful?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So that is their worship.\""],[14314,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word.\""],[14315,"\"Protect yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2552)"],[14316,"He went out to their gathering, and the prayer was established. Their imam stepped forward and lengthened the prayer and the sitting. When he finished, he said: \"Whoever of you leads us in prayer should complete the bowing and prostration, for behind him are the young, the old, the sick, the traveler, and the one in need.\" When the prayer time came, ʿAdī stepped forward, completed the bowing and prostration, and shortened the prayer. When he finished, he said: \"This is how we used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Mahdī."],[14317,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and complained of poverty. Then another came and complained of highway robbery. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O 'Adi, have you seen al-Hirah?\" I said, \"No, but I have been told about it.\" He said, \"If you live long, you will surely see women travelers departing from al-Hirah until they circumambulate the Kaaba, secure and fearing none but Allah. And if you live long, the treasures of Kisra will surely be opened.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Kisra son of Hurmuz?\" He said, \"Kisra son of Hurmuz. And if you live long, you will surely see a man bring out a handful of dirhams or silver seeking someone to accept it.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date; if you cannot find it, then with a kind word.\""],[14318,"He heard 'Adi b. Hatim say: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when two men came, one complaining of poverty and the other complaining of highway robbery. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for highway robbery, it will not be long before a caravan departs from al-Hirah to Makkah without a guard. As for poverty, the Hour will not come until one of you goes around with his charity and finds no one to accept it. Then one of you will surely stand before Allah ﷻ with no veil between him and Him, nor an interpreter to translate for him. He will surely say, 'Did I not give you wealth?' He will say, 'Yes.' He will say, 'Did I not send a messenger to you?' He will say, 'Yes.' Then he will look to his right and see nothing but the Fire, then he will look to his left and see nothing but the Fire. So let one of you guard himself against the Fire, even with half a date; if he cannot find it, then with a kind word.\""],[14319,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is none of you but his Lord will speak to him, with no interpreter between him and Him, nor a doorkeeper to veil him. He will say, 'Did I not send a messenger to you?' He will say, 'Yes.' Then He will say, 'Did I not give you wealth and favor you?' He will say, 'Yes.' 'So let one of you guard himself against the Fire, even with half a date.'\""],[14320,"\"I have nothing with me to give you, but I have a coat of mail in Kufa, and it is yours.\" The Bedouin was dissatisfied with it, so he swore not to give it. Then he said, \"I only came to ask you for a servant to help me.\" 'Adi said, \"I ordered my coat of mail for you, and by Allah, it is dearer to me than three slaves.\" The Bedouin became pleased with it and said, \"I accept your kindness.\" 'Adi said, \"Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him do what is better,' I would not have given it to you.\""],[14321,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath.\""],[14322,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him do what is better.\""],[14323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him leave it and do what is better.\""],[14324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If one of you swears about something and then sees something better, let him expiate for it and do what is better.\""],[14325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him do what is better.\""],[14326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better, let him abandon his oath and do what is better, and expiate for his oath.\""],[14327,"\"I have nothing to give you except my coat of mail and my helmet, so I will write to my family to give them to you.\" He was not satisfied, so 'Adi became angry and said, \"By Allah, I will not give you anything.\" Then the man became satisfied, so 'Adi said, \"By Allah, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever swears an oath and then sees what is more God-fearing, let him do it,' but he did not break his oath.\""],[14328,"Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ and gave speeches. One of them said, \"Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Get up, for what a bad speaker you are!\""],[14329,"A man delivered a speech before the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been guided aright, and whoever disobeys them both has gone astray.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Be quiet! What a wretched speaker you are.' He disliked his saying 'and whoever disobeys them both.'"],[14330,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting in the mosque. The people said: 'This is ʿAdī b. Ḥātim,' and I was a Christian. I came without a safe-conduct or a letter. When I was brought to him, he took my hand. Before that he had said: 'I hope that Allah will place his hand in my hand.' He stood with me, and a woman met him with a boy. They said: 'We have a need for you.' He stood with her until he fulfilled her need, then took my hand until he came to his house. A cushion was placed for him, and he sat on it, and I sat before him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'You are only deluded because it is said \"There is no god but Allah.\" Do you know of any god besides Allah?' Then he spoke for a while, then said: 'Are you only deluded or harmed because it is said \"Allah is greater\"? Do you know anything greater than Allah?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'The Jews have incurred anger, and the Christians are astray.' I said: 'Then I am a ḥanīf, a Muslim.' I saw his face brighten with joy. Then he commanded me, and I stayed with a man of the Anṣār. I would come to him at the two ends of the day. While I was with him one evening, some people came to him in woolen clothes of these striped ones. He prayed, then stood and urged them, then said: 'With a ṣāʿ, or half a ṣāʿ, or half of that, or even with part of a handful, one of you can protect his face from the heat of Hell or the Fire. Even with half a date. For one of you will meet Allah, and He will say to him what I say to you: \"Did I not give you hearing and sight?\" He will say: \"Yes.\" He will say: \"Did I not give you wealth and children?\" He will say: \"Yes.\" He will say: \"Where is what you sent ahead for yourself?\" He will look in front of him, behind him, to his right, and to his left, and will not find anything with which to protect his face. So let one of you protect his face from the Fire, even with half a date. If he does not find that, then with a good word. I do not fear poverty for you, for Allah ﷻ will support you and give you, until a woman travels in a litter between Yathrib and al-Ḥīrah, and the greatest fear for her mount is theft.' I began saying to myself: 'Where are the thieves of Ṭayyiʾ?'"],[14331,"The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the messengers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to ʿAqrab. They took my aunt and some people. When they brought them to the Prophet ﷺ, they lined them up before him. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the visitors have gone far, the children have been cut off, and I am an old woman with no service to offer. Show favor to me, may Allah ﷻ show favor to you.' He said: 'Who is your visitor?' She said: 'ʿAdī b. Ḥātim.' He said: 'The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger?' She said: 'So show favor to me.' When he returned, and a man beside him, whom we think was ʿAlī, said: 'Ask him for a mount.' She said: 'I asked him, and he ordered a female donkey.' I said: 'You have done something your father would not have done.' She said: 'Go to him, whether desirous or fearful. So-and-so came to him and obtained from him, and so-and-so came to him and obtained from him.' So I went to him, and there was with him a woman and children or a child. He mentioned their closeness to the Prophet ﷺ, and I realized that he was not a king like Kisrā and Caesar. He said: 'O ʿAdī, what makes you flee from it being said \"There is no god but Allah\"? Is there any god besides Allah? What makes you flee from it being said \"Allah is greater\"? Is there anything greater than Allah?' So I became Muslim, and I saw his face rejoice. He said: 'Those who have incurred anger are the Jews, and those who are astray are the Christians.' Then some people came to him and asked him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Now then, you people should give from your surplus. Let a man give a ṣāʿ, part of a ṣāʿ, a handful.' Shuʿbah said: 'Most of my knowledge is that he said: \"A date, half a date. One of you will meet Allah, and He will say: \"Did I not make you hearing and seeing? Did I not give you wealth and children? What have you sent ahead?\" He will look in front of him, behind him, to his right, and to his left, and will not find anything, so he will not shield himself from the Fire except with his face. So shield yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date. If you do not find that, then with a good word. I do not fear poverty for you. Allah will surely support you and give you, or open for you, until a woman travels in a litter between al-Ḥīrah and Yathrib, and the greatest fear for her litter is theft.'"],[14332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will come upon people a time when a woman will travel in a litter from Makkah to al-Ḥīrah, and no one will take hold of the halter of her mount. And there will come upon people a time when a man will walk with a handful of gold to give as charity, but it will not be accepted from him.'"],[14333,"He led them in the noon prayer and recited something like 'When the sky is split asunder.' When he finished the prayer, he said: 'I have not fallen short in leading you compared to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[14334,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs that we send after game, and they eat from what they catch for us.' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Even if they kill?' He said: 'Even if they kill.'"],[14335,"'She is not better than the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So he married him for the prescribed dowry."],[14336,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if one of us catches game and has no knife with him? May he slaughter it with a flint or a piece of wood?' He said: 'Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of Allah.'"],[14337,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'May I slaughter with a flint and a stick?' He said: 'Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of Allah, and eat.'"],[14338,"I said: O Messenger of God, I send my dog and it seizes the game, but I find nothing to slaughter it with except a sharp stone or a stick. He said: “Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of God.”"],[14339,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about game that I hunt. He said: “Cause the blood to flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of God Almighty.”"],[14340,"I said: O Messenger of God, we send trained dogs. He said: “When you mention the name of God, then eat.” I said: Even if they kill? He said: “Even if they kill.”"],[14341,"I said: O Messenger of God, my father used to maintain ties of kinship and do such and such. He said: “Your father desired something and attained it,” meaning remembrance."],[14342,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: O Messenger of God, which charity is best? He said: “The service of a slave in the way of God, or the shade of a tent, or a stallion for breeding.”"],[14343,"\"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon in which he said, 'O people, whoever we employ for a task and they withhold anything from us, even a needle or something smaller, they will be sinning and will be brought to account on the Day of Judgment.' A man from the Ansar, who was dark-skinned and it is as if I can see him now, stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, consider me exempt from your statement.' The Prophet asked, 'What is the matter?' The man said, 'I heard you say what you said earlier.' The Prophet then clarified, 'I say that whoever we employ for a task, whether they bring little or a lot, they will be given what is due to them, and whatever is forbidden will be avoided.'\""],[14344,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever of you we appoint over a task, let him come with its little and its much. Whatever he is given of it he takes, and whatever he is forbidden he refrains from.”"],[14345,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever of you we appoint over a task and he embezzles from us a needle or more than that, it will be a shackle that he will bring on the Day of Resurrection.” A black man from the Azd stood up to him—it is as if I were looking at him—and said: O Messenger of God, take back from me your task. He said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: I heard you say such and such. He said: “And I say it now: whoever of you we appoint over a task, let him come with its little and its much. Whatever he is given of it he takes, and whatever he is forbidden he refrains from.”"],[14346,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he spread his arms so that the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."],[14347,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The previously married woman expresses her own consent, and the virgin’s consent is her silence.”"],[14348,"There was a dispute between Imruʾ al-Qays and another man, so they brought their case to the Prophet ﷺ. He asked the Hadrami for evidence, but he had no evidence, so he ruled that Imruʾ al-Qays should take an oath. The Hadrami said, “O Messenger of God, if you let him take the oath, by God, my land will be lost.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever swears a false oath will meet God while He is angry with him.” Rajaʾ b. Haywa said: The Messenger of God ﷺ then recited: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...} the verse. Imruʾ al-Qays said, “What will I get if I give it up, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Paradise.” He said, “Then I call you to witness that I give it up.”"],[14349,"Two men came to the Messenger of God ﷺ disputing over some land. One said, “It is my land,” and the other said, “It is my land; I plowed it and planted reeds in it.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ made the one in whose possession the land was swear an oath."],[14350,"A man from Banu Sahm went out with Tamim al-Dari and ʿAdi b. Baddaʾ, and the Sahmi died. When they brought his inheritance, they missed a silver bowl inlaid with gold, so the Messenger of God ﷺ made them swear an oath. Then it was found, and they said, “We bought it from ʿAdi b. Tamim.” Two men from the heirs of the Sahmi stood up and swore by God, “Our testimony is more worthy than their testimony, and the bowl belongs to your companion.” Concerning them was revealed: {O you who believe, testimony among you...}"],[14351,"He met the Messenger of God ﷺ during one of his journeys and said, “O Messenger of God, I had two wives who fought with each other, so I threw something at one of them and killed her.” He said, “Pay her blood money, and do not inherit from her.” It is as if I can see the Messenger of God ﷺ on a red camel with a cut ear, saying: “O people, learn! The hands are three: the hand of God is the highest, the hand of the giver is the middle, and the hand of the one given is the lowest. So be chaste, even if it be with bundles of firewood. Have I conveyed? Have I conveyed?”"],[14352,"He said: “I asked my father about what you asked me. He said: I set out as one of four men from Banu Tamim. I was one of them, along with Sufyan b. Mujashiʿ b. Darim, Usama b. Malik b. Jundub b. al-ʿAnbar, Yazid b. Rabiʿa b. Kinabiyya b. Hurqus b. Mazin, and Yazid b. Jafna b. Malik b. Ghassan in Syria. When we arrived in Syria, we stopped at a watering place with trees belonging to a hermit, meaning the owner of a monastic cell. We said: If only we could wash from this water, anoint ourselves, and put on our clothes, then go to our companion. The hermit looked down at us and said: This is a language that is not the language of the people of this land. We said: Yes, we are people from Mudar. He said: From which Mudar? We said: From Khindif. He said: Verily, a prophet will soon be sent from among you, so hasten and take your share from him and you will be rightly guided, for he is the seal of the prophets. We said: What is his name? He said: Muhammad. When we returned from the son of Jafna, a son was born to each one of us, and he named him Muhammad.” Al-ʿAlaʾ said: Qays b. ʿAsim said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Do you know who was the first of the Arabs to know about you before you were sent?” He said, “No.” He said, “Banu Tamim,” and he told him this story."],[14353,"From ʿUrwa b. al-Zubayr regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: ʿUtba b. Ghazwan b. Jabir b. Wahb b. Qabisa b. Malik b. al-Harith b. Mazin b. Mansur b. ʿIkrima b. Hissa b. Qays b. Ghaylan b. Matar, an ally of Nawfal b. ʿAbd Manaf."],[14354,"ʿUtba b. Ghazwan was given the kunya Abu ʿAbd Allah, and it was also said Abu Ghazwan. He was tall and handsome. He died in the year seventeen while on his way to Basra on his second journey, and he was buried at one of the watering places. He was fifty-five years old, an ally of Banu Nawfal b. ʿAbd Manat."],[14355,"ʿUtba b. Ghazwan died in the year seventeen on the road to Basra while he was governor for ʿUmar b. al-Khattab, at the age of fifty-seven. It has also been said that he died in the year twenty. He was the one who founded Basra, laid out its dwellings, and built its mosque. He was the one who conquered al-Ubulla. His governorship of Basra lasted six months, having been appointed by ʿUmar b. al-Khattab."],[14356,"We campaigned with ʿUtba b. Ghazwān, and we conquered al-Ubulla. There we found a thin shard of walnut. We said, \"We have never seen stones that we break and eat.\""],[14357,"“Indeed this world has announced its departure and turned away, and nothing of it remains except a remnant like the dregs of a vessel that its owner pours out. And behind you is an abode, so move to it with the best of what is present with you. By Allah, I have surely seen myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when our mouths had become sore from eating leaves. There is not a man among us today except he is a commander over one of the garrison towns. I have seen myself and Saʿd b. Mālik racing to a cloak: I took half of it and Saʿd took half of it. It has reached me that between two panels of the panels of Paradise is a distance of forty years, and there will surely come a day when it is crowded. No prophethood ever occurred except that it was abrogated until it became kingship. I seek refuge in Allah from being great in my own estimation and small in people’s eyes. You will soon test the rulers after me.”"],[14358,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ as seventh of seven, and we had no food except the bark of trees."],[14359,"“To proceed: Indeed this world has announced its departure and turned away, and nothing of it remains except a remnant like the dregs of a vessel that its owner pours out. You will move from it to an abode that has no cessation, so move with the best of what is present with you. It has been mentioned to us that a stone is thrown from the edge of Hell and falls for seventy years without reaching its bottom. By Allah, it will surely be filled. Are you astonished? It has been mentioned to us that between two panels of the panels of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will surely come upon it when it is packed with crowding. I have seen myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we had no food except tree leaves until the corners of our mouths became sore. I picked up a cloak and split it between myself and Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, the horseman of Islam. I wrapped myself in half of it. None of us has risen this morning alive except that he has become a commander of one of the garrison towns. I seek refuge in Allah from being great in my own estimation and small with Allah. No prophethood ever abided except that it was transformed until its outcome became kingship. You will soon test or be tried by the rulers after us.”"],[14360,"“Indeed this world has announced its departure and turned away, and nothing of it remains except a remnant like the dregs of a vessel. You are in an abode from which you will depart, so move with the best of what is present with you. I have seen myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no food to eat except tree leaves until the corners of our mouths became sore.” Qurra said: “And I found a cloak.” Abū Naʿāma said: “I picked up a cloak and tore it in two halves. I wore one half and gave Saʿd the other half. None of those seven today is except over one of the garrison towns. The rulers after me will surely be tested. By Allah, no prophethood ever occurred except that it was transformed until it became kingship and tyranny. It has been mentioned to me”—Qurra said: “that a stone”—and Abū Naʿāma said: “that a sheet is cast from the edge of Hell and falls to its bottom.” Qurra said: “for seventy autumns,” and Abū Naʿāma said: “seventy autumns, and it will surely be filled. Between the two panels of the gates of Paradise is a journey of forty days, and a day will come upon the gates of Paradise when there is no gate except that it is packed. I seek refuge in Allah from being great in my own estimation and small with Allah.”"],[14361,"“I have seen us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as seventh of seven, and we had no food except the leaves of the ḥabala until one of us would defecate as a sheep defecates.”"],[14362,"“Indeed this world has announced its departure and turned away, and nothing of it remains except a remnant like the dregs of a vessel that its owner pours out. And indeed you are moving on, so move with the best of what is present with you. I have seen myself as the seventh of seven with the Prophet ﷺ, and our mouths had become sore from eating the leaves of trees.”"],[14363,"We used to witness fighting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the sun declined, he said to us, “Charge!” and we charged."],[14364,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[14365,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed behind you are days of patience. Whoever holds fast during them to the like of what you are upon will have the reward of fifty of you.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, or of them?” He said, “Rather, of you.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, or of them?” He said, “No, rather of you,” three or four times."],[14366,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: “When one of you loses something or wants help while he is in a land with no companion, let him say, ‘O servants of Allah, help me! O servants of Allah, help me!’ For Allah has servants whom we do not see, and this has been tried.”"],[14367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to Quraysh, “Is there among you someone who is not from you?” They said, “Our sister’s son, ʿUtba b. Ghazwān.” He said, “The son of a people’s sister is from them, and the ally of a people is from them.”"],[14368,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The martyrs and those who die of the plague will come. The people of the plague will say, 'We are martyrs.' It will be said, 'Look: if their wounds are like the wounds of martyrs, flowing blood with the fragrance of musk, then they are martyrs.' They will find them to be so.\""],[14369,"ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd al-Sulami: When a man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a name he disliked, he would change it. We came to him—we were seven from Banu Sulaym, the eldest of us being al-ʿIrbad b. Sariyah—and we all pledged allegiance to him together.\""],[14370,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Any Muslim who loses three children who have not reached the age of sin will be met by them at any of the eight gates of Paradise he wishes to enter.\""],[14371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts one day in the path of Allah as an obligatory act, Allah will distance Hell from him as far as the seven heavens and the seven earths. Whoever fasts one day voluntarily, Allah will distance Hell from him a distance like that between the heaven and the earth.\""],[14372,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he called me while I was a young boy. He said, 'What is your name?' I said, 'ʿAtalah b. ʿAbd.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Rather, you are ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd. Show me your sword.' He unsheathed it, and when he looked at it, it was a sword with thinness and weakness. He said, 'Do not strike with this, but thrust with it, a thrust.'"],[14373,"On the day of Banu Qurayzah, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever lands an arrow will have Paradise.' ʿUtbah said: 'I landed three arrows.'"],[14374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Rule is in Quraysh, judgment is in the Ansar, the call is in the Abyssinians, and jihad and emigration are in the Muslims and the Emigrants thereafter.'"],[14375,"On the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever lands an arrow into this fortress, Paradise is assured for him.' ʿUtbah said: 'I landed three arrows.'"],[14376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me while I was a young boy and said, 'What is your name?' I said, 'ʿAtalah b. ʿAbd.' He said, 'You are ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd.'"],[14377,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Show me your sword.' He unsheathed it and looked at it, and there was thinness and weakness in it. He said, 'Do not strike with this, but thrust with it, a thrust.'"],[14378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When a governor seeks out suspicion among the people, he corrupts them.'"],[14379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If a man were to be dragged on his face from the day he was born until he dies of old age in the pleasure of Allah, he would consider it insignificant on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14380,"O Messenger of God, curse the people of Yemen, for their might is severe, their number is great, and their fortresses are strong. He said, 'No.' And the Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the two non-Arabs: Persia and Rome. And the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'When the people of Yemen pass by you, driving their women and carrying their sons on their shoulders, they are of me and I am of them.'"],[14381,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his companions, 'Rise and fight.' Then a man was struck by an arrow, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This one has made it obligatory.'"],[14382,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'There is no Muslim who loses three children who have not reached puberty but that they meet him from the eight gates of Paradise, entering from whichever he wishes.'"],[14383,"From ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'The slain are of three types. A believing man who strives with his wealth and his self in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that is the martyr who boasts in the tent of God beneath His Throne; they are not surpassed except by the rank of prophethood. And a believing man who has burdened himself with sins and errors, then strives with his self and his wealth in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that is a rinsing of his sins and errors, for the sword is a wiper away of errors, and he will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes, for it has eight gates, and Hell has seven gates, some being better than others. And a hypocritical man who strives with his self and his wealth in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that one is in the Fire, for the sword does not wipe away hypocrisy.'"],[14384,"From ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd al-Sulamī, one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The slain are three types of men. A believing man who strives with his wealth and his self in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that is the martyr who boasts in the tent of God beneath His Throne; the prophets do not surpass him except by the degree of prophethood. And a believing man who has burdened himself with sins and errors, then strives with his wealth and his self in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that is a rinsing of his sins and errors, for the sword is a wiper away of errors, and he will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes, for it has eight gates, some being better than others, and Hell has seven gates. And a hypocritical man who strives with his self and his wealth in the path of God, until when he meets the enemy and fights them until he is killed; that one is in the Fire, for the sword does not wipe away hypocrisy.'"],[14385,"He heard ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd al-Sulamī say: A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'What is this pool of yours that you speak about?' He said, 'It is like the distance between al-Bayḍāʾ and Buṣrā. God will extend for me therein a watering place whose two ends no human among God's creation knows.' ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ said, 'As for the pool, it will be approached by the poor emigrants who fight in the path of God, and I hope that God will show me the watering place and I will drink from it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'My Lord has promised me that He will admit into Paradise seventy thousand of my community without reckoning, then each thousand will intercede for seventy thousand, then my Lord will scoop for me with His two hands three scoops.' ʿUmar ؓ said, 'The first seventy thousand, God will make them intercede for their fathers and kinsfolk, and I hope that God will place me in one of the latter scoops.' The bedouin said, 'O Messenger of God, is there fruit in it?' He said, 'Yes, and in it is a tree called Ṭūbā, which corresponds to the highest Paradise.' He said, 'Which tree of our land does it resemble?' He said, 'It does not resemble any tree of your land, but have you been to Syria?' He said, 'No, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'It resembles a tree in Syria called the walnut, which grows on a single trunk and then spreads at its top.' He said, 'What is the size of its root?' He said, 'If a young she-camel of your family's camels were to travel, it would not encompass its root until its collarbone breaks from old age.' He said, 'Are there grapes in it?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What is the size of a cluster from it?' He said, 'A month's journey for the piebald crow, neither turning aside nor tiring.' He said, 'What is the size of a single grape from it?' He said, 'Did your father slaughter a large sheep?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And skinned its hide and gave it to your mother, saying, \"Tan this and cut for us a bucket from it to water our livestock\"?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'It is like that.' He said, 'Will that suffice me and my household?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'And the generality of your clan.'"],[14386,"I came to ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd al-Sulamī, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and said, 'O Abū al-Walīd, I went out seeking sacrificial animals and found only one with broken teeth, and I disliked it. What do you say?' He said, 'Why did you not bring it to me to sacrifice?' I said, 'Glory be to God, it is not valid from you or from me?' He said, 'Yes, because you doubt and I do not doubt. The Messenger of God ﷺ only forbade the yellow one, the one whose horn is uprooted from its base, the one whose eye is sunken, the one that lags behind the flock due to lameness and weakness, and the broken one.'"],[14387,"that the Messenger of Allah said: “When anyone of you has intercourse with his wife, let him cover himself and not be naked liked donkeys.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1921)"],[14388,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command changing the hair, as a distinction from the non-Arabs."],[14389,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: “Whoever prays the Morning Prayer in congregation and then remains in the mosque glorifying God with the glorification of the forenoon (Duha), shall have the reward of a complete pilgrim and one performing ‘Umrah, his Hajj and ‘Umrah being complete.”"],[14390,"from its owners. When evening came, his companions gathered, so he called him and said, “From whom did you purchase the land?” He said, “From its owners.” He said, “Did they sell you anything?” They said, “No.” He said, “These are its owners, so return the land to the one from whom you bought it and take back the money.”"],[14391,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “In it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, the devils are fettered, and a caller calls out every night: ‘O seeker of good, come forward; and O seeker of evil, desist.’”"],[14392,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, the devils are chained, and a caller cries out: ‘O seeker of good, come forward; and O seeker of evil, desist’ — until the month passes.”"],[14393,"The Prophet ﷺ saw among his companions some lagging, so he called out to them: “O companions of Surat al-Baqarah.”"],[14394,"We were with ‘Utbah — women — perfuming ourselves and going out, while he was the most fragrant of us, doing nothing more than applying oil. We said to him, “What is this fragrance?” He said, “The itch (al-sharā) afflicted me in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I complained to him. He ordered me to wrap my garment over me — meaning to cover his private parts — then he spat into his hand and wiped my back and belly with it.”"],[14395,"We were with ‘Utbah — women — and each of us wanted to be more fragrant than her companion, while ‘Utbah was the most fragrant. When he went out, he was recognized by a good scent. So she asked about that, and she said: “The itch (al-sharā) took hold of him in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He complained to him, so he ordered him, and he sat before him and placed his hand over his private parts. Then the Prophet ﷺ spat into his hand and wiped his back and belly.”"],[14396,"We were three wives of ‘Utbah, and we used to perfume ourselves, and he was the sweetest-scented of us, yet he would not do more than oil his head and beard. A man would say to him, “O son of Farqad, how sweet is your scent!” So one of us said to him, “We perfume ourselves, and you do not do more than oil your head and beard, yet you are the sweetest-scented of us. How is that?” He said, “I was afflicted with an itch, so the Prophet ﷺ said, ‘Come closer.’ I came close, and he took my lower garment by its bottom edge and placed it over my private parts, then spread his hands and blew into them. He then wiped one hand over the other, and wiped one over my belly and the other over my back. So this fragrance is from that.”"],[14397,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which of the two terms did Moses fulfill?” He said, “The better and more complete of them.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Moses ﷺ wanted to part from Shu‘ayb ﷺ , he told his wife to ask her father to give her from his sheep what she could live on. So he gave her what his sheep produced that year of one color. When the sheep came to the watering trough, Moses ﷺ stood at the edge of the trough, and none of them came out except that he struck its side, so it became pregnant. All of them then produced offspring of one color, among them no fashūsh, no ḍabūb, no na‘ūl, and no kamshah that escapes the hand.” He said: “If you conquer Syria, you will find remnants of them, so take them. They are the Sāmiriyyah.” Ibn Yaḥyā b. Bukayr said: My father said: “Al-fashūsh is the one whose milk scatters when milked; al-ḍabūb is the one whose udder withholds the milk at milking; and al-kamshah is the one that is difficult at milking.”"],[14398,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he recited Ṭā-Sīn until he reached the story of Moses ﷺ , then he said: “Moses hired himself out for eight or ten years in exchange for guarding his chastity and food for his stomach.”"],[14399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When your military expeditions become distant and war booty is considered lawful and vows become numerous, then the best of your jihad is ribāṭ (guarding the frontiers).”"],[14400,"“‘Utbah b. Mas‘ūd died in the year forty-four.”"],[14401,"I heard Al-Zuhri say, \"Abdullah ibn Mas'ood did not make the earliest migration, compared to his brother Utbah, but he died before him.\""],[14402,"“ ‘Utbah b. Mas‘ūd died during the time of ‘Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.”"],[14403,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a black slave girl and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave. Will this one suffice for me?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who is your Lord?” She said, “Allah is my Lord.” He said, “What is your religion?” She said, “Islam.” He said, “Who am I?” She said, “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?” She said, “Yes, I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Do you pray the five prayers?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you fast Ramadan?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you affirm what has come from Allah?” She said, “Yes.” He then patted her on the back and said, “Set her free, for she suffices for you.”"],[14404,"“My brother and companion with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the most beloved of people to me except for ‘Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ .”"],[14405,"I heard Al-Ars bin 'Umairah, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Verily, a person may perform the actions of the people of the Fire throughout his life, until there is only an arm's length between him and Hell, but then what has been written for him overcomes him and he does the actions of the people of Paradise and enters Paradise. And verily, a person may perform the actions of the people of Paradise throughout his life, until there is only an arm's length between him and Paradise, but then what has been written for him overcomes him and he does the actions of the people of the Fire and enters Hell.\""],[14406,"That a man from Hadramaut and Imru' al-Qays ibn 'Aabis had a dispute over land, so they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked the man from Hadramaut for evidence, but he had no evidence. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of Imru' al-Qays ibn 'Aabis by taking an oath. The man from Hadramaut said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have made him victorious by taking an oath, and by Allah, he has taken my land.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes a false oath in order to illegally take the wealth of a Muslim, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Imru' al-Qays ibn 'Aabis and recited this verse to him. Imru' al-Qays said, \"O Messenger of Allah, for whom did he leave it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Paradise.\" Imru' al-Qays said, \"Then I bear witness that I have left it.\""],[14407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Consult women, so that the previously married woman may express herself, and the permission of the virgin is her silence.” Sufyān b. ‘Āmir added in the chain: “the bride.” Al-Layth b. Sa‘d narrated it from Abū Ḥusayn without going beyond ‘Adī b. ‘Umayrah."],[14408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah does not punish the common people for the deeds of the elite until the elite do an act that the common people are able to change but do not change. Then Allah permits the destruction of both the common and the elite.”"],[14409,"I heard ‘Adī b. ‘Adī"],[14410,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[14411,"And it is said that he is one of their own."],[14412,"The Prophet ﷺ came to them in the mosque of Quba and said, \"Allah ﷻ has praised you highly for purification in the matter of your mosque. What is this purification with which you purify yourselves?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we do not know anything except that we had Jewish neighbors who used to wash their behinds after defecation, so we washed as they washed.\""],[14413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah chose me and chose for me companions, and made among them for me ministers, supporters, and in-laws. So whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither compensation nor ransom will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[14414,"his grandfather said: “The Messenger of Allah said: 'You should marry virgins, for their mouths are sweeter, their wombs are more prolific and they are satisfied with less.'” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1861)"],[14415,"She is called Umm Afif bint Masrooh, who was pregnant with the child of Al-Nabighah. Umm Afif struck Muleikah on the floor of her house, which caused her death along with her fetus. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ determined their blood money. The fetus turned out to be a desired child of Abdullah or Walid. Her brother, Al-Ala' bin Masrooh, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, am I to pay the blood money for someone who has not eaten, drunk, looked, or desired? Such a person should be penalized.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"He is ignorant like the ignorance of pre-Islamic times.\""],[14416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be troubles and tribulations. Whoever comes to the community of Muhammad ﷺ while they are united, intending to divide them, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14417,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever rebels against my community while they are united, intending to divide them, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"After me there will be troubles and tribulations. So whoever you see intending to divide the community of Muhammad ﷺ while they are united, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be troubles and tribulations. So whoever you see dividing the community of Muhammad ﷺ, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14420,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"After me there will be troubles and tribulations.\" He prolonged his voice with it. \"So whoever intends to divide the community of Muhammad ﷺ while their affair is united, then kill him, whoever he may be. He swore an oath and did not except anyone from the people.\""],[14421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will be troubles and tribulations. So whoever you see walking toward the community of Muhammad ﷺ to divide its unity, then kill him.\""],[14422,"From ʿArfajah, who raised the hadith to the Prophet ﷺ: \"There will be troubles and tribulations. So whoever you see walking toward the community of Muhammad ﷺ while they are united, intending to divide them, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever walks toward my community while they are united, intending to divide them, then kill him, whoever he may be.\""],[14424,"various corruptions will arise in my community, so strike with sword the one who tries to cause separation in the matter of Muslims when they are united, whoever he be. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4762)"],[14425,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will be after me troubles and troubles. Whoever you see separating from the community or intending to divide the community of Muhammad while their affair is united, kill him, whoever he may be. The hand of Allah is upon the community, and indeed Satan is with the one who separates from the community.”"],[14426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed there will be troubles and troubles. Whoever intends to divide the community of Muhammad ﷺ, kill him, whoever he may be.”"],[14427,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed there will be troubles and troubles; he will raise his voice with them. Whoever you see intending to divide the affair of my community while it is united, kill him, whoever he may be.”"],[14428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you are upon a community and someone comes to divide your community and break your staff, kill him, whoever he may be.”"],[14429,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever comes to you while your affair is united upon one man, intending to divide your community, kill him.”"],[14430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be troubles and troubles. Whoever comes to my community while they are united, intending to divide the affair of their community, kill him.”"],[14431,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The hand of Allah is upon the community, and Satan runs with the one who opposes the community.”"],[14432,"His nose was injured on the Day of al-Kulāb during the Jāhiliyyah, so he made a nose of silver, but it became foul, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to make a nose of gold."],[14433,"His nose was cut off at the battle of Al-Kulab during the Jahiliyyah, so he wore a nose made of silver, but it began to rot, so the Prophet [SAW] told him to wear a nose made of gold. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5161)"],[14434,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the owner of the riding beast is more entitled to its front."],[14435,"When the people began the Hajj in the year nine, ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a Muslim. He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to return to his people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I fear they will kill you.” He said, “If they found me sleeping, they would not wake me.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him. He returned to his people as a Muslim. He presented a dinner, and Thaqīf came to greet him. He called them to Islam, but they suspected him, angered him, and made him hear what he had not expected. Then they left him until, when they had traveled by night and dawn broke, he stood upon a room in his house and called the adhān for prayer and testified. A man from Thaqīf shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of ʿUrwah is the example of the companion of Yāsīn: he called his people to Allah, and they killed him.”"],[14436,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had water with him, and when it reached the women, he would dip their hands into it.\""],[14437,"He performed the Hajj during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people did not know except at night while they were in a gathering. He then set out for Arafat at night and overflowed from it, then returned to the gathering and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I have performed Tawaf and made my animal sacrifice, so do I have the duty of Hajj?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever prays Fajr with us in congregation, stays with us until we have left Arafat and has already overflowed from Arafat before that, either at night or during the day, then he has completed his Hajj and fulfilled his obligation.\""],[14438,"I heard ʿUrwah b. Muḍarris b. Ḥārithah b. Lām say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Muzdalifah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you this hour from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. I have exhausted my mount and worn out myself. Is there any Hajj for me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever attends this prayer with us and stands with us until we depart, and had previously stood at ʿArafah by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.\""],[14439,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at Jamʿ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any Hajj for me?\" He said, \"Whoever prays this prayer with us, stands at this station with us, and had departed from ʿArafāt before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.\" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Sulaymān b. Ḥarb."],[14440,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any Hajj for me?\" He said, \"Whoever prays this prayer with us, stands at these stations with us, and had departed from ʿArafāt before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.\""],[14441,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Jamʿ before he departed. When he looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I crossed the two mountains and encountered hardship.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches our departure has caught the Hajj.\""],[14442,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Jamʿ before he departed. When he looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I crossed the two mountains and encountered hardship.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches our departure has caught the Hajj.\""],[14443,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at Muzdalifah, and he said, \"Whoever prays this prayer of ours, then departs with us, and had previously stood at ʿArafah by night or day, his Hajj is complete.\""],[14444,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have tired myself, exhausted myself, and worn out my shoes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches Jamʿ with the people and the imam before they depart has caught the Hajj; and whoever does not catch the people and the imam at Jamʿ until they depart has not caught the Hajj.\""],[14445,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have worn out my shoes, exhausted myself, and done such and such.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches Jamʿ and stands with the people until they depart has caught the Hajj; and whoever does not catch that has no Hajj.\""],[14446,"I heard ʿUrwah b. Muḍarris b. Aws b. Ḥārithah b. Lām al-Ṭāʾī say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Muzdalifah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. By Allah, I did not come until I had tired myself and exhausted my mount. I did not descend any mountain without standing on it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever attends this prayer with us and had previously stood at ʿArafah before that by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.\""],[14447,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the standing place of Jamʿ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from the mountain of Ṭayyiʾ. I have exhausted my mount and tired myself. By Allah, I did not descend from any mountain without standing on it. Is there any Hajj for me, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever prays the morning prayer with us at Jamʿ and had come to ʿArafāt before that by night or day has fulfilled his rites and completed his Hajj.\""],[14448,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) and said, 'O Messenger of God, I have come from the mountain of Ṭayyiʾ. I have exhausted my mount and wearied myself. By God, I did not descend from any mountain except that I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever attends this prayer with us, and had already come to ʿArafāt before that, whether by night or day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete.'"],[14449,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at the standing place at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) and said, 'O Messenger of God, I have come from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. I have exhausted myself and wearied my mount. By God, I did not descend any mountain except that I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me, O Messenger of God?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever prays this prayer with us, and has already come to ʿArafah, whether by night or day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete.'"],[14450,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) and the people were around him, and said, 'O Messenger of God, I am a man from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. I have exhausted my mount. By God, I did not descend any mountain that you stopped at except that I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me, O Messenger of God?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever witnesses this prayer with us, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.'"],[14451,"ʿAbdān b. Aḥmad narrated to us."],[14452,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ at Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) and said, 'O Messenger of God, I have come from the two mountains of Ṭayyiʾ. I did not leave any mountain except that I stood upon it. Is there any Hajj for me?' He said, 'Whoever prays this prayer with us, and has already departed from ʿArafah, whether by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites.'"],[14453,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A person is with the one he loves.'"],[14454,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14455,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection: reward and booty.'"],[14456,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Goodness and reward are tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.' It was said, 'O Messenger of God, what is that?' He said, 'Reward and booty.'"],[14458,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14459,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14460,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.” Thus did ʿAmr al-Awdī narrate it from his father from Sufyān. People narrated it from Sufyān from Jābir from al-Shaʿbī from Wahb b. Khanbash, and it is the correct one."],[14461,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Camels are a source of might for their owners, and sheep are a blessing.”"],[14462,"ʿUrwah al-Bāriqī stood over us while we were in our gathering and narrated to us, saying: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14463,"From Abū Isḥāq."],[14464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses.”"],[14465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14466,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14467,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come to a chestnut horse in the market of Madinah with my uncles, its forelock appearing between his two fingers, and he said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14468,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14469,"From the Prophet ﷺ similarly, he said: “Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14471,"ʿUyaynah b. Badr and Ḥiṣn entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while Abu Bakr and ʿUmar were with him, all sitting on the ground. He called for a cushion for ʿUyaynah and seated him on it, and said: “When a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.”"],[14472,"I heard ʿAttāb b. Asīd while he was leaning his back against the House of Allah saying: “By Allah, I gained from this work which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted to me only two plain garments, and I clothed my freedman Kaysān with them.”"],[14473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the zakah of vineyards: “They are estimated just as palm trees are estimated, then their zakah is paid as raisins just as the zakah of palm trees is paid as dates.”"],[14474,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him when he appointed him over Makkah: “Will you convey from me to your people what I command you? Tell them: No one should combine a sale and a loan, no one should sell a sale involving uncertainty, and no one should sell what he does not have.”"],[14475,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: “I have an elderly father and brothers, so I will go to them hoping that they may become Muslims and I will bring them to you.” He said: “If they become Muslims, it is better for them, but if they remain, Islam is vast and wide.”"],[14476,"I was among those taken on the day of Qurayẓah. They were killing those who had reached puberty and leaving those who had not, so I was among those left."],[14477,"ʿAṭiyyah said: I was among the captives of Banū Qurayẓah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has not reached puberty, leave him.” So they looked at me, saw nothing, and let me go."],[14478,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of all those who reached the age of puberty from the tribe of Qurayzah. I was still a young boy, so they left me alone.\""],[14479,"I heard ʿAṭiyyah al-Quraẓī say: “On the day Saʿd b. Muʿādh passed judgment on Banū Qurayẓah, I was a boy. They looked at my lower garment but did not find that I had grown pubic hair; so here I am among you.”"],[14480,"I was among those against whom Saʿd passed judgment. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that their fighting men be killed and their women and children be taken captive. He said: I was brought forward, and I thought he would surely have me killed. He said: He uncovered my pubic area and they looked at it, and they found that it had not yet appeared, so they put me among the captives."],[14481,"I was among those against whom Saʿd passed judgment, and they were uncertain about me—whether I was one of the fighting men or one of the dependents. So they looked at my pubic area and found that it had not yet appeared, and they placed me among the dependents."],[14482,"I was brought before the Messenger of God ﷺ at the time of Qurayẓah. Whoever among us had reached puberty or had grown pubic hair was killed. They looked at me and found that my pubic hair had not grown, so I was left alone."],[14483,"I was among the captives—I was brought forward along with the other captives who were presented during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they did not find that I had grown pubic hair, so I was released."],[14484,"I was presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Qurayẓah, and they did not find that I had grown pubic hair, so they let me go."],[14485,"I was among those presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Qurayẓah, and they were uncertain about me. They looked at my pubic area and found that the hair had not grown, so my way was left open."],[14486,"I heard a man in the mosque of Kūfah say: “On the day Saʿd b. Muʿādh passed judgment on Banū Qurayẓah, I was a boy, and they were uncertain about me. They did not find that the razor had passed over me, so I was spared.”"],[14487,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed the wealth of God is both accountable and granted.”"],[14488,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The giving hand is better than the lower hand.”"],[14489,"I came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ among a group from Banū Saʿd, and I was the youngest of them. They left me behind with their baggage, and they went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and fulfilled their needs. He said: “Is anyone left?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, a boy who stayed with our baggage. He told them to call me, so I came to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whatever God has given you, do not ask people for anything. Indeed the upper hand is the giving hand, and the lower hand is the receiving hand, and indeed God is the One from whom to ask and the One who gives.” The Messenger of God ﷺ spoke to me in our dialect."],[14490,"On the authority of my grandfather ʿAṭiyyah, who was a Companion, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire, and fire is only extinguished by water. So if one of you becomes angry, let him perform ablution.”"],[14491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When the ruler boils with rage, Satan gains mastery.”"],[14492,"He was among those who spoke to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Hawazin captives. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Your kinsmen, your root, and all the sucklings.” And he said: “For this day we saved you, and they are your mothers, your sisters, and your aunts.” The Messenger of God ﷺ spoke to his Companions, so they returned their captives to them, except for two men. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Go and give them a choice.” One of them said: “I will leave him,” and the other said: “I will not leave him.” When the latter turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said: “His arrow has struck well.” He would pass by a virgin girl or a boy and leave him, until he passed by an old woman. Then he said: “I will take this one, for she is a living mother, and they will ransom her from me with whatever they are able.” Atiyyah exclaimed: “Take her, O Messenger of God! Her mouth is not cool, nor is her breast full, nor is her visitor content. She is an old woman, O Messenger of God, a freeborn captive with no one to care for her.” When he saw that no one was interested in her, he left her."],[14493,"From Atiyyah al-Saʿdi, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A servant does not attain the rank of the God-fearing until he gives up what is harmless out of caution against what is harmful.”"],[14494,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Face sandals (i.e., straighten them to face the qiblah).”"],[14495,"“Asim b. ʿAdi b. al-Jadd b. al-ʿAjlan went out to Badr, but the Messenger of God ﷺ sent him back and allotted him a share (of the spoils) as an arrow.”"],[14496,"Asim b. ʿAdi b. al-Jadd b. ʿAjlan b. Dubayʿah, who was from Bali and an ally of Banu ʿUbayd b. Zayd b. Malik b. ʿAwf b. ʿAmr b. ʿAwf b. Malik b. al-Aws, went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to Badr, but he sent him back and allotted him an arrow along with the people of Badr. And it is said that the Prophet ﷺ appointed him as his deputy over al-ʿAliyah, and it is said that he lived to be one hundred and fifteen years old."],[14497,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ granted a concession to camel herders regarding the overnight stay (at Mina): they may stone (the Jamrah) on the Day of Sacrifice, then stone the next day and the day after for two days, then stone on the Day of Departure."],[14498,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ granted a concession to camel herders to stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then omit a day and a night, then stone after that."],[14499,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ granted a concession to camel herders to take turns, and to stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then leave off."],[14500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah on Monday, twelve nights having passed of Rabi' al-Awwal, and he stayed in Madinah for ten years."],[14501,"He said: We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ soon after he arrived, and he said, \"Where is Habis Sayl?\" We said, \"We do not know.\" Then a man from Banu Sulaym passed by me, and I said, \"Where have you come from?\" He said, \"From Habis Sayl.\" I called for my sandals and hurried to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you asked us about Habis Sayl and we said we had no knowledge of it. This man passed by me, so I asked him, and he claimed that his family is there.\" The Messenger of Allah asked him, \"Where is your family?\" He said, \"At Habis Sayl.\" He said, \"Move your family out of it, for it is imminent that a fire will come out of it that will light up the necks of camels at Busra.\""],[14502,"I and my brother bought a hundred shares from the shares of Khaybar. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"O 'Asim, two hungry wolves that attack a flock whose owner has neglected it are not more destructive to it than a person's love of wealth and status is to his religion.\""],[14503,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this verse was revealed: {Then they did not bring four witnesses} (24:13). I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses? The betrayer has already gotten what he wanted.\" He said: He had not even stood up before his cousin, his father's brother, came with his wife carrying a child, and she was saying, \"He is from you,\" while he was saying, \"He is not from me.\" Then the verse of li'an was revealed, and I was the first to speak of it and the first to be tested by it."],[14504,"From al-Zuhri, regarding naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: 'Asim b. Thabit b. Abi al-Aflah."],[14505,"From Ibn Ishaq, regarding naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: 'Asim b. Thabit b. Qays b. al-Aflah b. 'Ismah b. Malik b. Umayyah b. Sa'sa'ah b. Zayd b. Malik b. 'Awf b. 'Amr b. 'Awf."],[14506,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out an army or expedition, he would say to them, \"If you see a mosque or hear a mu'adhdhin, do not kill anyone.\" The Prophet ﷺ sent us on an expedition and commanded us to do that. We went out traveling through the land of Tihamah, and a man driving women in camel litters caught up with us. We presented Islam to him and said, \"Are you a Muslim?\" He said, \"What is Islam?\" We told him, but he did not know it. He said, \"If I do not do it, what will you do?\" We said, \"We will kill you.\" He said, \"Will you wait for me until I reach the women?\" We said, \"Yes, and we will catch up with you.\" He went out, and there was a woman in her howdah. He said, \"Accept Islam, Hubaysh, before life is cut off.\" She said, \"I accept Islam ten or nine times in succession.\" Then he said."],[14507,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Some part of my body itched, so I put my hand in to scratch, and my hand touched my penis.\" He said, \"I too am affected by that.\""],[14508,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no protected pastureland in Islam, and no rigging of bids.”"],[14509,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited us at Quba. When he wanted to return, we brought him a sturdy, slow-paced donkey, and he mounted it. We said, “O Messenger of God, this is a servant who will come with you to return the animal.” He said: “The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front.” We said, “O Messenger of God, ride it and return it to us.” He went and returned it to us, and it was ambling—none could keep pace with it."],[14510,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The majority of the hypocrites of my community are its reciters.”"],[14511,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us in one of the lanes of Madinah and stopped at a rubbish heap of a people. He said: “O Hudhayfah, screen me.” The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and urinated standing, then called for water, performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed."],[14512,"A slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my master married me off and now wants to separate me and my wife.” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: “O people, divorce is only in the hand of the one who takes the calf.”"],[14513,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you should sleep in a garment dyed with safflower, for it is his shroud.”"],[14514,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Were there to be a prophet after me, it would be ʿUmar b. al-Khattab.”"],[14515,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The back of a believer is protected, except by its due right.”"],[14516,"A man from Khuzaʿah arrived and ʿAli met him and said, “What has brought you?” He said, “I have come to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ: to whom should we hand over the zakat of our wealth when God takes you?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “To Abu Bakr.” He said, “And when God takes Abu Bakr, then to whom?” He said: “ʿUmar.” He said, “And when God takes ʿUmar, then to whom?” He said: “To ʿUthman.” He said, “And when God takes ʿUthman, then to whom?” He said: “Look out for yourselves.”"],[14517,"A man from the desert arrived with some camels of his. The Messenger of God ﷺ met him and bought them from him. Then ʿAli met him and said, “What has brought you?” He said, “I arrived with camels, and the Messenger of God ﷺ bought them.” He said, “Did he pay you cash?” He said, “No, but you sold them to him on credit.” ʿAli said, “Go back and say to him: O Messenger of God, if something happens to you, who will pay me my money? And see what he says to you, then come back to me and tell me.” So he said, “O Messenger of God, if something happens to you, who will pay me?” He said: “Abu Bakr.” So he informed ʿAli, and ʿAli said to him, “Go back and ask him: if something happens to Abu Bakr, who will pay me?” So he asked him, and he said: “ʿUmar.” He came and informed ʿAli, and ʿAli said to him, “Go back and ask him: if ʿUmar dies, who will pay me?” So he came and asked him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Woe to you! If ʿUmar dies, then if you can die, then die.”"],[14518,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had prayed Zuhr and was sitting in the mosque when a man came and entered to pray. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Is there not a man who will give charity to this man by praying with him?”"],[14519,"The Messenger of God ﷺ: say, “May God not return your lost animal to you.” And he disliked saying it himself."],[14520,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you prays the Friday prayer, he should not pray anything after it until he speaks or leaves.”"],[14521,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with his eye having been gouged out. He said to him, “Who struck you?” He said, “The one-eyed man of the Banu so-and-so.” So he sent for him, and he came. He said, “Did you gouge out this man’s eye?” He said, “Yes.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled against him for the blood money and said, “His eye shall not be gouged out, leaving you without sight.”"],[14522,"A slave stole during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, but he let him go. Then he was brought to him a second time, having stolen, and he let him go. Then he was brought the third time, and he let him go. Then he was brought to him a fourth time, having stolen, and he let him go. Then he was brought to him a fifth time, having stolen, and he cut off his hand. Then he was brought to him a sixth time, and he cut off his foot. Then he was brought to him a seventh time, and he cut off his hand. Then he was brought to him an eighth time, and he cut off his foot. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Four for four.”"],[14523,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to begin the recitation with “{Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds},” and so did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ؓ."],[14524,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ had a spear with which he would walk in front of him, and when he prayed, he would plant it in front of him.”"],[14525,"A camel belonging to an orphan of the Ansar ran away from us, and we could not catch it. We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He got up with us until we came to the garden where the camel was. When the camel saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, it came forward and prostrated to him. We said, “O Messenger of God, if only you would command us to prostrate to you as kings are prostrated to.” He said, “That is not for my community. If I were to do such a thing, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.”"],[14526,"A group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, we pass through these markets and look at these fruits and long for them, but we have no coin to buy them. Is there any reward for us in that?” He said, “Is there any reward except in that?”"],[14527,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The gift takes away hearing and the heart.”"],[14528,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said three times: “The stray animal of a believer is the burning of fire.”"],[14529,"When the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ who was married to Uthman died, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Marry Uthman. If I had a third, I would marry him to her. I did not marry him except by revelation from God, exalted be He.”"],[14530,"The Messenger of God ﷺ rode a horse and it ran with him, then he returned to us and said, “I found it to be a sea.”"],[14531,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Three people God will not look at tomorrow: an old man who commits adultery, a man who makes oaths a commodity, swearing in every right and falsehood, and a poor man who is arrogant and conceited.”"],[14532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man over the sadaqah. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, choose for me.' He said, 'Sit in your house.'"],[14533,"Al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib entered the mosque one day and greeted them. He noticed dislike in their faces, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his house and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why is it that when I enter the mosque I see dislike in people's faces?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he entered the mosque and said, 'O people, you will never believe and you will never be believers until you love ʿAbbas.'"],[14534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man walking in his sandals among the graves and said, 'O owner of the sibtiyyah (sandals), take off your sandals.'"],[14535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The most beloved action to Allah ﷻ is subhat al-hadith, and the most hateful of actions to Allah is al-tahdif. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is subhat al-hadith?' He said, 'People conversing while a man glorifies Allah.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is al-tahdif?' He said, 'People being in a good state, then a neighbor or companion asks them, and they say, \"We are in a bad state,\" complaining.'"],[14536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever apostatizes from his religion, kill him.'"],[14537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If the Quran were gathered in a hide, fire would not burn it.'"],[14538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever endears himself to people with what they love and contends with Allah, he will meet Allah, the Exalted, while He is angry with him.'"],[14539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah ﷻ has created for you the game of the sea.'"],[14540,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the east. It was said to him, 'Then what about the trial of the west?' He said, 'That is greater and greater.'"],[14541,"From the Prophet ﷺ, a hadith\" but Muhammad b. Ismaʿil did not mention the hadith."],[14542,"From the Prophet ﷺ that this verse was revealed: {Those who spend their wealth by night and by day, secretly and openly} – that it was revealed concerning expenditures on horses."],[14543,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said, “Horses have goodness and nobility bound to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. Their people are aided because of them, and the one who spends on them is like one stretching out his hands in charity. Their urine and their dung, for their owners, on the Day of Resurrection, will be among the musk of Paradise.”"],[14544,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, {And others besides them whom you do not know, God knows them}: that they are the jinn. The Prophet ﷺ said, “No jinn will cause harm in a house containing a noble horse.”"],[14545,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ said to a man from the Arabs called ʿUfayr b. Abi ʿUfayr: How did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ speak about love? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Love is inherited, and hatred is inherited.”"],[14546,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿAqil b. Abi Talib, “O Abu Yazid, I love you with two loves: one because of your kinship to me, and one because of what I know of my uncle’s love for you.”"],[14547,"He said: O ʿAqil, go to Muhammad. So I went to him and brought him out of a kibs—Talha said: a small room. He came in the midday heat, walking in search of shade because of the intense heat of the pebbles. We came to them, and Abu Talib said: Your paternal cousins claim that you annoy them in their gathering place and in their assembly, so stop that. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky and said, “Do you see this sun?” They said yes. He said, “I am no more able to abandon that than you are able to kindle a flame from it.” Abu Talib said: My nephew has never lied to us, so go back."],[14548,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When one of you marries, let it be said to him, “May God bless you and bless upon you.”"],[14549,"He married a woman from Banu Jusham, and it was said to him, “With harmony and sons.” He said: Do not say that, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade it and commanded us to say, “May God bless you and bless upon you.”"],[14550,"Do not say that. They said: What should we say, O Abu Yazid? He said: Say, “May God bless you and may God bless upon you. We used to be commanded to do that.”"],[14551,"Do not say this, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to say “With harmony and sons,” and commanded us to say, “May God bless you and bless upon you.”"],[14552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “May God bless among you and bless for you.”"],[14553,"Do not say that, for the Prophet ﷺ forbade it and commanded us to say: \"May Allah bless you and shower blessings upon you.\""],[14554,"From ʿUrwah: \"Regarding the naming of those who attended al-ʿAqabah for the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj: ʿUqbah b. ʿAmr b. Thaʿlabah b. Yasir b. ʿAsirah, and he is given the kunyah Abu Masʿud.\""],[14555,"From Ibn Ishaq: \"Regarding the naming of those who attended al-ʿAqabah from the Ansar, then from al-Khazraj: Abu Masʿud ʿUqbah b. ʿAmr b. Thaʿlabah b. Yasir b. ʿAsirah b. Hadarah b. ʿAwf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.\""],[14556,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When a man spends on his family an expenditure while seeking reward for it, it is charity for him.\" I said, \"From the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said, \"From the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[14557,"He was called Abu Shuʿayb, and he had a slave who was a butcher. He said to his slave, \"Prepare food for me, perhaps I will invite the Prophet ﷺ as the fifth of five.\" He invited the Prophet ﷺ as the fifth of five, and a man followed him. The Prophet ﷺ said to the man, \"You invited me as the fifth of five, and this man has followed us. If you permit, he may enter; otherwise he will return.\" He said, \"Rather, we permit him.\""],[14558,"He was called Abu Shuʿayb, and he invited the Prophet ﷺ along with five others. \"The Prophet ﷺ asked his permission regarding the sixth.\""],[14559,"A man from the Ansar who was given the kunyah Abu Shuʿayb said to his slave, \"Woe to you, I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so prepare food sufficient for five.\" He prepared it, then sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and invited him. A man who had not been invited followed them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This man has followed us, so do you permit him?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[14560,"Abi Shuayb had a servant who was a welder. When he saw how exhausted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions were, he ordered his servant to bring enough meat for five people. So he sent a message to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to bring a fifth of five. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with a fifth for five people, and a sixth man followed them. When they reached the door of Abi Shuayb, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, you sent for five, and this man has joined us. If you allow him, he will enter, otherwise he will go back.\" Abi Shuayb replied, \"No, I have allowed him, so let him eat.\""],[14561,"He was called Abu Shuʿayb, and he had a slave who was a butcher. He said to his slave, \"I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Perhaps I will invite him as the fifth of five.\" He prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and invited him as the fifth of five. A man followed them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man has followed us, so if you wish to permit him, then permit him.\""],[14562,"Make enough food for our servant, five or six servings, so that I may invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the fifth serving. Accordingly, they invited him and a man followed them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, you invited me for the fifth serving, and this man has accompanied us. If you wish, you may allow him, and if you wish, you may leave him.\" He said, \"No, I will allow him.\""],[14563,"He was called Abu Shuʿayb, and he had a slave who was a butcher. He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and recognized hunger in his face, so he said to his slave, \"Woe to you, prepare food for me, for I want to invite the Prophet ﷺ as the fifth of five.\" He prepared it, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and invited him as the fifth of five. A man followed them, and when he reached the door, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"This man has followed us, so if you wish, permit him, and if you wish, he will return.\" He said, \"No, rather I permit him, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[14564,"A man called Abu Shuʿayb said to a slave of his who was a butcher, \"Prepare food sufficient for five, for I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He prepared food for him, then sent to the Prophet ﷺ and his companions who were with him. When the Prophet ﷺ stood up, a man who had not been with them when he invited them followed them. When they reached the door, he said to the owner of the house, \"A man has followed me who was not present when you invited us. If you permit him, he may enter.\" He said, \"We have permitted him, so let him enter.\""],[14565,"From a man of the Ansar who was given the kunyah Abu Shuʿayb: He said, \"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and recognized hunger in his face. I met a slave of mine who was a butcher and ordered him to prepare food for five men. Then I invited the Prophet ﷺ, and he came as the fifth of five. A man followed them, and when he reached the door, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'This man has followed us. If you wish, permit him; otherwise he will return.' So I permitted him.\""],[14566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command charity, so a man would go and exert himself, then come with a mudd. Indeed, some of them today have a hundred thousand. Shaqiq said: I saw that he was alluding to himself."],[14567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command charity, so a man would go and exert himself, then come with a mudd. Indeed, some of them today have a hundred thousand. Shaqiq said: I saw that he was alluding to himself."],[14568,"We used to exert ourselves, so one of us would come with a small charity, and a man would come with half a sa'. Then some people among the hypocrites would defame us, so it was revealed: {Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities} - the verse."],[14569,"We used to exert ourselves in charity, so one of us would come with a sa', and some people among the hypocrites would defame them, so it was revealed: {Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities}."],[14570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command charity, and none of us would find anything to give as charity until he would go to the market and carry on his back, then come with charity and give it to the Prophet ﷺ. Indeed, I know today a man who has a hundred thousand; on that day he did not have a dirham."],[14571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever recites them in a night, they will suffice him - the two verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah."],[14572,"Whoever recites the conclusion of Surat al-Baqarah, it will suffice him instead of reciting for a night. And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given the endings of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[14573,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: The two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah - whoever recites them in a night, they will suffice him."],[14574,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: If a man recites two verses from the end of al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him: {The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord}."],[14575,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites these two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him: {The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord} to the end of the surah.\" ʿAbd al-Rahman b. Yazid said: \"So I came to Abu Masʿud al-Ansari while he was circumambulating and asked him about it, and he narrated this hadith to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[14576,"I met Abu Masʿud while he was circumambulating the House, and I said: \"A hadith that ʿAlqamah narrated to me from you.\" He said: \"Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, whoever recites them in a night, they will suffice him: {The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord}.'\""],[14577,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.\""],[14578,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, whoever recites them in a night, they will suffice him.\""],[14579,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, whoever recites them in a night, they will suffice him.\" He did not mention ʿAlqamah."],[14580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.\" Al-Aʿmash said, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of ʿAbd al-Rahman b. Yazid, something similar."],[14581,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever recites in a night the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah, they will suffice him.\""],[14582,"I came to Abu Mas'ud and said, \"Abu Mas'ud, inform me about your recitation of the last two verses from Surah Al-Baqarah.\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever recites these two verses in one night, they will be sufficient for him.\""],[14583,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.\""],[14584,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"I hardly attend the prayer because so-and-so lengthens it for us.\" I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ angrier in an admonition than he was that day. Then he said: \"Whoever leads the people in prayer should lighten it for them, for behind him are the weak, the young, the elderly, and the one with a need.\""],[14585,"\"O Messenger of God, I pray behind so-and-so, and he lengthens the prayer, so sometimes I hold back.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry such as I never saw him angry in an admonition, and he said: \"Among you are those who drive people away. Whoever leads the people in prayer should lighten the prayer for them, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need.\""],[14586,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I stay away from the dawn prayer because so-and-so lengthens it for us.\" I never saw the Prophet ﷺ angrier in an admonition than he was that day. He said: \"O people, among you are those who drive people away. Whoever of you prays with the people should make it brief, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need.\""],[14587,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, I keep away from the dawn prayer because so-and-so lengthens the recitation for us.\" I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ angrier in an admonition he gave than he was that day. Then he said: \"Whoever prays with the people should lighten the prayer for them, for among them are the young, the elderly, the weak, and the one with a need.\""],[14588,"O Messenger of God, by God, I indeed stay away from the dawn prayer because of so-and-so, on account of how long he prolongs it for us. I never saw the Prophet ﷺ more intensely angry in an admonition than he was that day. He said, “O people, among you are those who drive others away. Whoever of you leads the people in prayer should be brief, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs.”"],[14589,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I stay away from the prayer because of so-and-so, on account of how long he prolongs it for us.” I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ more intensely angry in an admonition than he was that day. He said, “O people, among you are those who drive others away. Whoever of you leads the people in prayer should be brief, for among them are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs.”"]]);
